        StaticBook("* Note *", "Othello", "A wouldnt suggest ignoring me again, sir. Your locks were broken, and your valuable stolen. Sorry.\n\n[!] A smiley face is drawn here in a dark black dust, probably that of coal [!]\n\n-Othy.", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Dusty Scroll*", "Thurak'Yar", "*as you unfurl the length of the tattered, yellowing scroll before you, you would find that instead of runes or notes, pictures adorn the aged reed paper. It would seem to be the retelling of an event, or, perhaps, a prophecy.*\n*the first scrawling depicts a small, hunched figure warming himself by a crude fire. Around him is a scribbled, complete blackness, broken only by the light from his meagre flames*\n ////////////\n////// O////////\n//// # |-| //////\n*the campfire has grown to a bonfire, and around it figures dance and drink. The black of the night is all but gone in the presence of the light and merriment*\n  //////////////\n  //// # ////////\n //// ## {O} O| ///\n /// #### ||   |  ///\n*a hush seems to have fallen over the camp as the night grows longer, and the fire has withered significantly. The black creeps in once again as the weary rest*\n  ///////////\n/////////////\n///// # //////\n//// ### __o //\n*a sunrise is pictured further down, illuminating a flat, bleak landscape. The remains of a fire have been scattered, and corpses mingle among the dirt*\n///////////////// ((\n//////~///////////\n______#__ x__ x__\n*at the bottom of the scroll a small verse is scribbled- the only writing on the whole piece. It seems to be in some strange, dead language*\n\n Fiith slaium az dhog az zamal amut ângh- slaium;", ""),
        StaticBook("*A letter*", "Clover Orvir", "[!] The note is neatly folded inside the envelope\nyou notice the formality of the cursive and begin to read the letter.\nDue to recent actions in my life, i must resign my duties as a Sillumir.\nI have learned much, and have had many trials and errors during my time. I hope one day i can return with nothing to hold me back.                             -Clover Orvir\n[!] As you finish reading you spot a few odd stains at the botom of the page, they look like small water marks", ""),
        StaticBook("*a red scroll*", "Thurak'Yar", "*the parchment is hued a crimson red, making reading the encryption difficult. What you can make out, however, would seem to be some sort of prediction or preminition*\n§uThe Red Realm Will Open\n§uThe Floating Fortress will rise from the sea\n§uThe Organic Island is going to fall along with the Fringelands\n§uThe realm of the Black Wrym shall soon open up", ""),
        StaticBook("*a small note*", "~5", "*you find a small, neatly written note in front of you, penned out on a plain sheet of paper in a dark purple ink. It seems to make no sense, however, and is only signed by the number, 5...*\nN fr ymj rfs wmt xytqj owtr ytz. Nk ytz wfsy yt kqsi rj, n wjxnij ns ymj Kwnsij Ijxjwy, ns f mtzxj ozxy tzyxqij tk ymj rfns ifyj tk ymj Zzi- Vznyj mfwi yt rqxx, ns kfhy. Nk ytz’wj nsyqqnljsy jstzlm yt ijhnumjw ymnx, ytz’wj ijxjwvnsl tk wjywngzynts.\n~5", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Tablet*", "Thurak'Yar", "*A tablet sits before you; old, cracked and runic. Across it verses in some strange, long forgotten text are carved, each more twisted and odd than the last. After scanning for long enough, you come upon a verse in common runes*\nAgh Ulu Skaat'Uga,\nGrazadh'uga agh\nnar'gotl;\nLûk'z ob Dom,\nLûk'z ob Or'Ta,\nLûk'z ob Ixli;\nGrish agh matum\nSkaat'uga, naan nar ob\ngrishulub;\nUlu kramp'uga nar\ngrish' ûr ulub kû\nkrankûkz;", ""),
        StaticBook("*a torn scrap*", "Thurak'Yar", "*it seems to be a small, wrinkled scrap of paper, torn from what must have been a great tome. The writing is faded, though easily made out against the yellow parchment*\n... all forms one could imagine. They gathered about the great Traf accompanied by their Shamans as Frum'Staaz. they obeyed, but only in companionship, for these beasts were never to be controlled.\nBy one Uruk's side only a flat, grey shadow could be seen, trailing from his feet and blinking back at those that glared...", ""),
        StaticBook("*Ancient Tome*", "Thurak'Yar", "[!] This book looks ancient, as if it predated the arrival of the Aegean Exodus to Asulon. It is filled with indecipherable texts and strange diagrams. While the text is unreadable, the pictures seem to show a method of golem creation.\nThe first stage of golem creation seems to be the creation of the core. The images show a block of gold held aloft by a being no dissimilar in appearance to a dwarf. It could possibly have been one of the race that built Karik. The picture also\ncontains what looks like a shaman of some sort, but definitely not one of dwarven descent. At the centre of the drawing is a bolt of unnatural looking lightning. It seems as if the Shaman is summoning the magical lightning to strike the core.\nIn the next diagram, the golden core and the dwarf holding it seem enveloped in some sort of field of lightning. A third diagram shows the dwarf holding the core, which is now transparent, with a mist swirling inside it. It is possible that this is\nmaking an impression of the dwarf’s essence and soul onto the core, rather than the crude rituals used in Aegis to transfer the soul entirely. Further on in the book, there is a diagram of a golden body being forged by the same\ndwarf that held the core aloft. The anvil strongly resembles the anvil of Karik, albeit in better condition than the one in Karik today. The body  is far more intricate than the comparatively primitive golems of Aegis. The next diagram is\na cross section of the golem. It seems to be made of several interlocking parts, all either forged or carved from what looks like no more than common ore or stone. In the centre of the body is a large central cavity. The final images show\nthe craftsman placing the core into the cavity, the body being enveloped in the magical lightning, and then the golem sitting up and looking at its creator. This book seems to confirm that the Ancients of Karik had the power to make\ngolems, and used that power. Given that golems have the ability to live almost indefinitely, this raises the question: Where are they all?", ""),
        StaticBook("*jumbled notes*", "Thurak'Yar", "3, 9, 2, 4, 3, 7, 4, 6, 3, 5, 6, 7.\n8, 2, 4, 3, 4.\n1, 5, 4, 6, 1, 5, 4.\n1, 9, 4, 3, 4, 1, 4, 8, 11.\n5, 3, 7, 1, 4, 4, 3, 5.", ""),
        StaticBook("*signed note*", "Thurak'Yar", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~Whuevah hawldz dizz nowt mae rezeeve ash Zpirid Wulk ur Blezzin'\nfrum da zpirid ob der choize frum Thurak da Farzeer. Zend heem ah burd wehn lat wund tu kollekd id, agh zhuw heem dizz nowt.\n     *Thurak'Yar*\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("-=Love Poems=-", "Kiveck Irelia", "~-=Love Poems=-~\nIf you said you were cold, I would wrap my arms around you.\nIf you said you were thirsty, I would give you the ocean blue.\nI would give you anything: the moon, the stars, the sunest too. This heart in my hands I hold out to you.\nImagine me and you, I think about you day and night, it's only right to think about the girl you love and hold her tight. So happy, together.\nA million stars up in the sky, one shines brighter I can't deny. A love so precious, a love so true, a love that comes from me to you.\nTrue love is measured by how deep you fall. And judged by how low you are willing to crawl just to save it and make it last. It is determined by how willing you are to open up to offer trust.\nThere's a light inside my heart that always lights the way; a glimmer of hope that gets me through the day; A little ray of happiness, that sometimes gets me through the harsh and sad times.\nThat little light, is you.\nI stumbled upon these small poems in a very secret place. I believed that I should share them with others now.", ""),
        StaticBook("-Clover Orvir", "Clover Orvir", "[!] The letter is in bueatiful Cursive handwriting with a small blue flower pressed against the pages. You begin to read...\n\"To Elodie,\nIs has been a while and seen as my husband has gone missing i would have a request. As small as it seems i am wondering if i could borrow a flint and steel or some rashons of food. As much as i regret asking i need... to feed my daughter\nand my current two jobs will not cover.\nVan'ayla.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Clover Orvir", ""),
        StaticBook("-Fire and Smoke-", "Garsto 'Spark' Leaf", "{-----------------}\n       Fire and Smoke\n{-----------------}Fire and smoke... Dragons... will burn your soul,\nThey Pillage and blow... Keep a watch on... your foe...\nAnd if this tower ends up in flames... So will we... and the rest of Vai-lor\n[!]Notes for how to play it on guitar and Lute are written here. [!]\n\nOrigionally written by Garsto Leaf.\n\n((OOC: Thank you for reading, this is actually the first song Ive written. For LOTC and well, probably my life. and extended new version may come in\nthe future but for now that is the song. Thanks again!))\n\n[!]Garsto Leaf's signature is here.[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("-Fire Evocation-", "Garsto 'Spark' Leaf", "{-----------------}         Fire Evocation\n{-----------------}This book is about Fire evocation.\n\nThe Fire Evocationists conjure appears to be real. But it is fake. One does not have power over the elements. For an Evocationist to conjure fire from the\nvoid they have to understand the element in the real/physical world first. The easiest way of bringing Fire into the physical world would be to light a torch by using Evocation or by creating a fire which then lights a fire. As a mage becomes more\nexperienced they can eventually form balls of Fire which they could shape into objects of Fire.\n\n((The Next part of this book is OOC. Its mainly for ones who already know Magic but want to Emote it. It is OOC. Remember that...\nGarsto is focused on a spot on a hay bale in front of him.\n\nis twitching a tad with his eyes locked on the position of the hay bale. He is muttering something. \n\nA tiny faint orange flame appears on the hay bale.\nThe flame gets smaller and blows itself out.\n\nGarsto falls back into a chair in fatigue.\n\nThat was an example of a Tier 1.\n\nThe next is Tier two.\nGarsto is concentrating on an unlit torch in front of him.\n\nHis forehead is sweating and he is breathing heavily.\n\nA Spark flickers on the coal in the torch.\nThe Spark lights the coal which results in the torch being lighted.\n\nGarsto's kitchen is now lit by the torch.\n\nStumbles in Fatigue.\n\nThat was a Tier Two. Next is a Tier Four.\nGarsto is concentrating with his hand outstretched towards the cow.\n\nHe begins to breath heavily and his forehead is sweating.\n\nHe mutters something. Flames erupt from his hand spinning into a shape.\nThe Shape looks something like a small dagger. Its not clear though.\n\nOpens his eyes and mutters something sending the fiery dagger towards the cow. \n\nThat was all OOC remember.))\nIts suggest that you meditate to help your self connect to the void. This can help you improve and go through tier 1.  At Tier two the user is able to hit a target most of the time. At the end of tier two the mage will be experimenting with conjuring Fire\nballs. Its said by Tier three the mage can conjure small fire balls successfully which they can conjure as Explosive or just normal. They can also vary the temperature of their fire. \n\n((Ooc: If you dont emote Fatigue you aren't doing it right.))\nUnless you are tier five and you are conjuring a small Spark. Even if you are Tier five you can still have Fatigue depending on how big the flame. Attempting to summon white hot flames. eah, not a great idea. You would die of heat. Or lack of Mana.\nSummoning fire from a distance takes time. ((Ooc: Summoning fire ON or BENEATH someone isn't allowed.)) You cant mold flames until you start to reach the end of Tier two. Even then you can only just about mold it into a ball of fire. With difficulty.\n((Ooc: Controlling a flame that is in the Physical world and was made in the Physical world, not drawn from the void would be considered power gaming.)) You will have increased heart rate, breathing heavily and will still get sweaty at levels above tier 3\nFrom personal experiences I learnt that when pulling from the void it feels like 'tugging a rope to pull something from nothingness.'\n\nI hope this book helped you with what you were looking for about Fire Evocation.\n/Signed Garsto Leaf./\n((Ooc: If I find you use this for some description wether its for the lore of your magic application or anything else. I will make a comment on your post saying its a copy of what I wrote origionally for when I tried to apply for magic.))", ""),
        StaticBook("11 Commandments", "Kaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "===Hail Valdoria===\n\n\n\n      The 11 Doctrines\n          of Conduct\n\n\n\n        Approved by\n    The Reich Ministry\n           of Truth\n-------------------In the heart of the Kaiser's men lies a singular hope, a dream, that is for the conception of propserity through the devotion of the Kaiser and so be his will. Our souls are ready, let us rise my brothers, let us conceive together the\nchild of nationalism and holy power. For now we shall instigate 11 doctrines of conduct, for all who live and shall be must conform, else grasp the warted shaft of Iblees. We, the pure race, shall now impose upon the realm a New Order.\nThus follows, thou shalt obey.\n\n1. The rivaling nations of the Vander shall reunite under the banner of purity and fraternity so the Kaiser wills it.\n2. The purity of man shall here be enforced through the instigation of cultural and social engineering. Thus be that any and all who live under the light of man shall worship the grace of only he who shall be priased, our Lord and Savior, the Kaiser.\n3. The purity of man shall here be enforced through the insitgation of cultural and social engineering. Thus be that any and all who live under the light of man shall worship the grace of only he who shall be praised, our Lord and Savior, the Kaiser.\n4. The fowl plague of Serenism and the elfen threat shall be eliminated through the systematic cleansing of the inferior races and the salvation of the Kaiser. Let our grand armies crush any and all militants against the glory and prowess of man.\n5. In the prescence of the impure, let us enter the cavities of all who have not been touched by the Kaiser. Let our seed flow into the chambers of darkness and let the Kaiser's grace guide our path into the horrors of the black worms.\n6. In address to our recent quarrels, we as a race, as a hope, as a dream, shall and must mold a new world free of the fetters of the lies of the individual and that of which is birthed from the valves of the individual.\n7. The counsel of Kingdoms shall henceforth be dissolved in exchange for the Grace and will of Holy theocracy and the divine right of the Rector.\n8. The economic might of man must be revitalized in response to the recent morbid and relentless inflation caused undoubtedly by the dwarvish conspiracy. Hence forth, all citizens of human heritage who are not of or associated directly with the blood\nof pure humanity shall be taxed at a rate of which must exceed 10% in proportion to the latter.\n9. All territory under the light of the Kaiser and the true realm of men shall be renovated to fit the amenities of the pure and centralized of three. Therefore, all roadways must not exceed but must hence thereby not precede the holy\ngirth of three metersin accord to our Lord's grand and superior highway system.\n10. In response to the elfen Serenist indoctrination of our pure culture, all architectural and aesthetic features under the light of man shall henceforth reflect the purity and holy national pride of our pious and superior culture.\n11. Above all else, shall each and every man under the glory of the Kaiser be blessed with the pious and ethereal zeal of white nationalism and forth be orgasmed by the exuberant passion of the autocratic fervor and the divine trinity of\nGod, King and Father.\nHeil to thee Kaiser, for my only true and mighty ubermensch, for thee may touch my heart and body through man's mighty thrust. Hail to thee my Kaiser, the true father of Man, the boiler of goblins and the cruncher of Elves. May your reign be felt in the\nviscera of all men, and may your pure prowess obliterate the tyranny of the impure and the steam of the lesser race. I love you, mein pious Lord, Heil to be thee, may the glory of Priorism, and may our mighty Vander Empire thrive until eternity!", ""),
        StaticBook("12345", "Hagnik Rogan", "Onc upon a tiem\nay kay ay rit nao dere was weddin  with peepul everiwere.\nsuck romantec sniff sniff I cri everytim\nOMG ima steal ur wifes", ""),
        StaticBook("30 Strictures", "Ypres Signus", ";-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;\n        The Holy\n     Strictures of\n      Yeu Rthulu\n\n    As according to\nthe cannon which has been confirmed and past down by all servants of Yeu Rthulu. Blessings upon you.\nStricture 1: One must never find joy in the death of any man, woman, or child. \n\nStricture 2: It is right for one to be bound in matrimony as to create lifemates, but one must never force such a sacred act on another.\nStricture 3: One must never make love outside of marriage.\n\nStricture 4: One must restrict themselves from gluttony and drunkenness.\nStricture 5: One must restrict themselves from un-marital lust and intercourse.\n\nStricture 6: One must restrict themselves from taking what is not theirs.\nStricture 7: One must find peace and tolerance to deal with those whom're not enlightened, for they follow their own path.\n\nStricture 8: One must restrict themselves from needlessly striking out against someone.\nStricture 9: One must not allow one's lust for revenge overtake them. Just retribution may be needed, but vengeance is reserved for the Gods.\nStricture 10: One must not deceive or harm one another with words.\n\n \nStricture 11: One must not abandon those whom trust one for support.\nStricture 12: One must allow their hearts to not be apathetic to their brother's burdens.\n \nStricture 13: One must respect their family, for they're of same blood.\nStricture 14: One must not show hatred to anyone due to their race, their age, or gender.\n \nStricture 15: One must restrict from the use of substances which muffle and cloud the emotions as to use to deal with their pain.\nStricture 16: One must support all whom are widowed, lame, or otherwise unable to support themselves. \n\n \nStricture 16: One must support all whom are widowed, lame, or otherwise unable to support themselves.\nStricture 18: One must be submit under the discernment of others as to have a understanding of what is brought by justice, and what is brought by anger.\nStricture 19: One must keep themselves accountable to their spouses. And likewise hold their spouses accountable.\n\nStricture 20: One must not allow one's anger to provoke trouble, and pain.\nStricture 21: One must allow themselves to be counted as equal unless proven otherwise by content of character.\n\nStricture 22: One must not challenge or disobey those whom are appointed to authority.\nStricture 23: One must find mercy within themselves to be patient with the mistakes of others.\n\nStricture 24: One must find joy in whatever he has, whether little, or great.\nStricture 25: One must find the purest of joys from their spouse.\nStricture 26: It is in due right, and in way of nature that those bound in marriage should enjoy the privileges of sexual intercourse and relations. Yet, it is to be kept between the 2 lifemates,-\nnot extending to others and creating such things as orgies or brothels, for they are detestable and disgusting.\n\nStricture 27: One must support and nurture their spouse as they would themselves.\nStricture 28: One must love their spouse more than any worldly thing, or person.\n\nStricture 29: One must not hide their true nature from their spouse. For it is the true nature of lifemates that must be bound together.\nStricture 30: One must honor and follow the strictures if they wish to live a pure life, contented, and compassionately.\n\n\n-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;-;", ""),
        StaticBook("<3", "Elayne", "It's sweet like nectar of the garden flower,\n\nIt's soothing like the buzzing of bumble bee.\n\nIt's warm like the rays of the morning sun,\n\nIt's the search of love so pure which keeps me on the run.\nIt's the pulse in my vein,\n\nThe thoughts in my brain,\n\nIn every breath that I take,\n\nThe smile my lips make,\n\nIt's in the twinkle of my eye, till the day I die.\nIt's my dreams in my sleep,\n\nIt's springs freshest leaf;\n\nA love so rare like this will always be with me for keeps.\nIt's warmth of my blood,\n\nAs my feelings flood,\n\nAs says my heart's beat,\n\nIts depth touches the ocean's feet.\nEven if its heart searing pain,\n\nWith nothing to gain,\n\nI will feel it as the tear on my cheek,\n\nAnd without words my soul will speak.\nA feeling so sincere,\n\nA bond so strong,\n\nI know my soul will never guide me wrong.\nI would wait till my last sunset,\n\nTill my heart slows down with dull ache,\n\nTill my eyes are wet,\n\nDak, you are my soul's mate.\n\n-=Lain=-", ""),
        StaticBook("<> Our Love <>", "Kale", "<><><>.Our Love.<><><>\n\nWritten By: Dr. Kale\n\n   Finally, here we are on the balcony with the most delightful sunset.\n  There he was standing in front of me leaning in for the kiss, the all of a sudden my nightmare appeared.\n\"Awh look at that, how cute. Let me guess you're going to kiss her now?\" he said laughing. \n  My eyes narrowed. Who is this bigget that ruined my long awaited moment?!\n  He succeded in upsetting Zeliek, for he drew his sword to challenge him.\nThe other man simply laughed and disappeared so Zeliek and I went back to what was supposed to happen. Okay, finally here it goes. \"Pff, lad you sure do take a long time to plant one.\"\n\nThat was enough for Zeliek, he jumped down ready to fight this man.\n\"What's your name, you pompous fool?\" Zeliek asked, furry in his eyes. \"If you'd like to know, it's Mason!\" he shouts with a rather large laugh. Once Zeliek saw his state he decided to simply part ways... Never to hear from him again.\n\nAbout two months\npass, and nothing from Zeliek. As I was learning to stitch there he was. \"Where's your other half?\" he'd ask. Once I heard the familiar voice I grew livid! \n\"You ruined everything!\" I shouted as my heart beat pounded. His reaction at first seemed rather\nhostile, but then became soft.\n\n  \"Apologies Miss?\" I didn't like this man. Nor did I have intentions to speak to him any further. \"Ah, Mason just the man I was hopin' to see!\" My teacher shouted quite happily before he scolded me.\n\"Masie, don't be so rude.\"\n\n  After that day, it seemed that Mason came almost everyday to that particular spot just to see me. Our hatred turned into a light friendship. Until one night in a lively tavern.\nHe looked off, and stared at the table after glancing me in the eyes. \"Masie?\" he asked with a embarrassed look upon his face. \"Hmm\" I said taking a sip of rich wine.\n\n\"W- would you care to have dinner sometime?\"\n*Here would be a drawing of a wine goblet hitting the cold stone ground*\n\n\"Wh- what, are you serious?\" I asked in complete shock. \"How do I know you're not makin' fun?\" I then crossed my arms defensivly. He laughed with rosey cheeks.\n\"I erm.. I promise?\" For a moment I actually considered it fully. But seeing the wine hit the ground, just tore me inside.\n\n\"Only if there's wine.\" I'd state firmly with a smile. He seemed glad to hear this.\nWe saw each other almost everyday. Some say we were the 'Fools Lovers' with all the joy that filled our hearts. Years went by, but then everything changed on the voyage to Vailor. Rain poured down harder as the lightning struck. He stood before me, not-\nlooking into my eyes. \"Masie.. whatever we had leave it in Athera. We move from each other for now.\" Tears fell from my eyes. My heart ripped into small pieces.. \"Mas-\" I barely got out before he left me there alone, cold in this horrid dark rain.\nThere was nothing left but a hopeless love. As the years grew longer and more lonesome, I became very knowledgeable with medicine. Even got a clinic in the Caliphate as a head doctor.\n\nIt never seemed complete without him, for he held a piece\nof my torn heart. That night standing on my balcony breathing in the clear air, a dove dropped a letter that reads:\n\"My dearest Masie, after all these years I can't help but think of you. I think it's time you knew the truth. May we meet?\" - M\nHolding back the tears was hard. For they weren't tears of joy but of dark sorrow and pain.\n\nHe continued to write me until the Moon grew a size larger, then I decided that I'd meet with him.\n<><><><><><><><><><><>\n\n  Walking into that garden and seeing him. After all the years, he hasn't changed one bit. \n\n\"Masie, I haven't much time but you must know. I did what I did on the boat to protect you.\"\nHis words were soft but hushed. I stared into his eyes, his beautiful eyes.. \"Why did you? What are you protecting me from?\" I couldn't help but ask.\n\n  \"I can't tell you, or else I won't be able to protect you from them.\" His gaze turned to the sky.\n\"Ju- just know that we will be able to be together one day, but for now I remain in hiding.\" He then turned to me with a moment of bliss in his eyes as he grabbed my face and kissed me.\n\n \"We will be together soon, I promise.\n\"I love you, Masie.\" A tear fell from his eye as we stood there face to face. Not another word was spoken for he left quickly afterwards and I was chocked. One thing was for certain.\nOur fated, happy, disfuctional, but unique love was not at an end. For this was our beginning. Our love.", ""),
        StaticBook("=- Evocation -=", "PiercingDarkness", "-()-()-()-()-()-()-()\n\n() Magic: Evocation ()\n\nBy, Mythras Ardere\n\n\"Some magic's for fools, others are for the intelligent.\"\n\n\n()-()-()-()-()-()-()\nLesson 1: Study\n:---------:-------:\n\nStudy your element, notice it's uses and affects, meditate and learn your senses.\n\nYou must get to know your element currectly to begin to learn magic.\nLesson 2: The Void\n----:----:----:---:--:\n\nThe Void is a place of magic, essentially, it's the realm of \"nothing,\" as well as what's known as \"everything.\" It is a place of emptiness filled with \"mana,\" or life energies.\nEvocation draws mana from the Void, and as such because of the \"un natural way,\" it draws mana, or \"power,\" from. It can be counted as unnatural forms of magic.\nThe Void: Connecting\n]-------[!]---------[\n\nTo connect to the Void, takes a long time of study and preparation and as such leads into a lack of physical strength. People seem to think being a flashy mage-warrior's possible. Well, it's not.\nYou must realize upon entering your studies, you will become frail, and weak. You'll lose your strength. It'll get to a point of terrible physique, you may have issues with certain things required of the average healthy person.\nBut magic's expressive way of dealing you power, may lead to you being less powerful in the long run, magic's for the weak to use in defense. Not petty battle use as many seem to think because of how other's treat it.\nThe Void: Steps to connect.\n\nTo connect, you must be aware of nothing around you, quell all emotions, and be thinking of nothing, at all. Your mind must be cleared. It takes practice and time, but eventually you'll learn so.\nAs you grow more powerful with your element, you must begin to experiment more with the magic on your own, and therefore have less of the average Void Connection task. You will have issues from harming yourself while experimenting.\nMay this guide have helped you.\n\nSources:\n\n- History of Magic\n- Mage Guild Teachings\n- Average Magic teachings", ""),
        StaticBook("[!] A Flier", "Ayche Raven'kor", "DO YOU HATE YOUR NEIGHBOR? DO YOU WISH THEY WOULD JUST DROP DEAD? WELL NOW THEY CAN. FOR ONLY 2500 MINAS YOU CAN KEEP ANYONE QUIET FOREVER!! SEND A BIRD TO YOUR LOCAL EDGY WITH THE NAME OF YOUR TARGET AND THEY WILL BE DEALT WITH WITHIN THE DAY!! SEND NOW!", ""),
        StaticBook("[!] A letter.", "Eloh'ra Rohkea", "Dear Aeras,\n\nBy the time you are reading this, I will be somewhere where one could not possibly find me.\n\nI've come to the sudden realization that I do not only need to find myself but my strengths and weaknesses, alone.\nI plead you not look for me nor be saddened by the event for as I will be back soon.\n\nThis will give me the chance to finally understand myself and what I desire to be in the future. With or without someone.\nI will be back in due time, to hopefully find you waiting for me.\n\nI wish you not just great joy, but love for as you deserve all there is.\n\nMuch love,\n- Eloh'ra Rohkea.", ""),
        StaticBook("[!] A note [!]", "Swampgoth Shreck'Lak", "Walhk eezt ihn duh zwump, latz wihl fynd mi theyr.", ""),
