        StaticBook("[AMC] Flyer", "Judas Windsor", "Vist Francois d'Aumont' shop located in central Felsen.\n\nThe prices are affordable even if you minas deprived. \n\nIf you need anything, we'll be sure to have it in stock!", ""),
        StaticBook("[Old Book]", "Axel Burchoff", "*A letter would be encrypted in this book. Obviously important to Axel.*\n\n\n\n\n                   ----->\nMy dear boy, I speak of this proud and happy. Do have fun on your journeys through Vailor, do not worry about what will happen to me.. I will be in the 7 Skies waiting for you to come to me. My dear boy, I treasure you most, and I wish you a merry life.\nDo take these words in consideration, please do. You ought to become what you want to become, and I wish you will. Your pa will take care of you, you will grow up strong and tall like him. Treasure me with your life, fight for the good. Never give up..\nThis is because my dear boy, at one point.. One time in life.. You. You will be you, the you you want to be... \n\n-Love Ma, Kristeen.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Black Bounty", "Barrowlord Kozilek", "Locate the Wight named Kozilek and say unto him, \"hallowed pearls.\"\n\nOnly there does your opportunity lie.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Bloodied Day", "Eirik Colborn", "A few saints days ago a day where many a guards died within the hallowed gates of Felsen, I upon being present left into the alleyway with my bannerman known as 'Maulhawk' it was there that we were approached by a character vailed in shadows.\nAs the person came closer the female features grew more apparent, she donned a hue of brown any other features were hid by her scoweled clothes. The woman tried her hardest to recruit me and my man into her clandestine guild. Her main offer were to\nparticipate in 'shady buisness' and 'illegal matters' I simply sighed as any man with his head on his shoulders would. Upon calling her out for her insanity I asked Maulhawk to remove her from my pressence. She called upon \"the gods\" saying\nwere they to exist they should help her. A pitty I knew naught there was such filthy unbelievers amongst us. Nay matter upon a  minute or two I left abruptly what happened after I nay know.\n\nSigned, Count Eirik Colborn, Patriach\nof House Colborn", ""),
        StaticBook("A bloodied tome", "Jonathan Dunharrow", "Malghourn's mother was not a nice lady. She doesn't like blood magic.\nThis is, your knowledge of blood magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Book", "Anonymous", "It was the raw and wild duo of earth and natural growth: the Aenguls Cernunnos and Cerridwen. These two incorporeal beings are the patrons and deities of which Druids call upon for influence over nature. With the elven\npenchant for similar ideals as the Druidic Aspects, the two factions frequently blend. In this, the Druids exist.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Chance Meeting", "Ennulia", "I took a few steps into the sunny glade, each footfall sounding off with the hushed crunch of the green grass below me.  The wind blew through the nearby trees with a low howl, wafting the sweet scent of pine into my nostrils.\nThe sound of distant squirrels scurrying up and across branches echoed through the forest, their mischievous chattering bringing a faint smile to my face. The birds were oddly quiet this morning, perhaps they were sleeping in, just as I had.\nI took a seat at the top of a nearby hill, my pack having grown quite heavy, and peered down into the woods below. A bit farther into the trees I could sense movement.\nThe large, brown mass slowly lumbered out from the trees, revealing a light brown muzzle and four stocky legs.\nAs it drew further from the trees I noticed that it was being trailed by two much smaller bundles of fur. A mother and her cubs.\nI’ve always had a great respect for bears. They’re big, strong and protective. As often as I go out on camping excursions I’d rarely seen bears up until this point.\nWhile my ursine acquaintances were a ways down the hill, and likely hadn’t spotted me yet, I didn’t want to take any chances. I took my things and left in the opposite direction, giving them a very wide berth.", ""),
        StaticBook("A chance.", "samler", "Dear Moon.\nI do understand your fears yet if we never try, we will never find the answer.\n\nI will not judge you from how I have known you prior to the courting. I do hope such will help you step forward.\n\n-Your dearest Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Coin", "Miru", "I wish I wish:\n~For a special world for you and me,\nA special bond one cannot see,\nIt wraps us up in its cocoon,\nAnd holds us fiercely in its womb,\nIts fingers spread like fine spun silk,\nGently nestling us to the fold,\nLike silken threat it holds us fast,\nBonds like this are meant to last.~\n\nAnd a new clothes.", ""),
        StaticBook("A deathwish", "Geoboy66", "Dear wishing well, I hope these bindings hold this ink firm. \nI am nature's bane, a\nnecessary evil in a\nwar of morals and\ncycles.  I look after the dead and you look after the living.  I ask that we may work in harmony in the decades to come.\n\n- Naruntah", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dedication", "Hreidmar Strongbrow", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n Carve for Me a Rock\n \n      A Dedication      \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHreidmar Strongbrow\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI want to build a hearth\n\nA tribute for my new kin\n\nI need your help,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve again.\n\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI need a place of shelter\n\nBeneath the skies of blue\n\nI need desire,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve for you.\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI want to keep my craftsmanship\n\nWithin your holy\nfount\n\nI need the strength,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve your mount.\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI have to keep my heart\n\nSecured in my new home\n\nI need the will,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve a dome.\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI need to feed my\nmind\n\nAnd ensure it is overfilled\n\nI need knowledge,\noh Aspects,\n\nI want to carve the hill.\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI need to build a door to you\n\nAnd hold it with a\nlock\n\nI can't do it without you,\n\nCarve for Me a Rock.\n\n -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-", ""),
        StaticBook("A Denial of Hope", "Aerxuis", "A Denial of the Mystification of Hope\nBy Amras Yavelty\nCopied by Aerx\nIt is prudent to mention that my writing doesn’t intend to deny hope as a valuable emotion of the being but instead explain it as a natural occurring phenomena and\nnot a religion justifying emotion. It seems that hope arises whenever the ‘self is under siege’ from within or externally. When I use the phrase ‘self under siege’ I mean the being in which hope occurs is undergoing an emotional,\nphysical or mental conflict as a result of internal or external factors\nThe problem with hope is that it often misleads the being into identifying hope as an inner sixth sense that gives out or provides some kind information about divine entities and\ntheir bond with beings. Hope indeed is a strong emotion and is one that seems to arise even in the most direst of situations. This is explained easily because hope is, none the less, an impulse of the being to maintain it alive and relevant in the\nworld. It is, after all, a common use of hope in Druid religion in which it had been used to indirectly justify the beliefs and cults regarding their gods.\nIt is a foolish notion a sir tends to disregard that hope is not a product of the mind, but\ninstead an impulse of the being to survive, a reflex, therefore it cannot be used in the rational process. It is from this statement that I can conclude that any justification of religious beliefs and cults through the false definition of hope are\nirrational and untrustworthy in their nature and is by all cost all logic is to be avoided by the Mali’aheral.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Diary", "Anonymous", ". . .\n\nDay 832: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks.\n\nDay 833: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks. Chopped wood.\nDay 834: Had tea. Ran out of crumpets. Hunted rabbits successfully. Played with rocks. \n\nDay 835: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Rocks went missing. Tended farm.\nDay 836: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Rivel split apart, torn asunder by arcane forces and floated into the sky. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks.\n\nDay 837: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks.\nDay 838: Had tea. Ate crumpets. Hunted rabbits. Played with rocks. Tended farm.\n\n. . .", ""),
        StaticBook("A dream", "F.V.", "Last night I dreamt about Haelun'or. As it oftens goes in dreams, I had no reason to be there, I simply.. was. I took a few steps on the beautiful bridge to the citadel and paused for a moment.\nAs my gaze drifted to the entrance of the citadel, I swear that it looked perfect in the moonlight of my dreams. I turned my attention to the water surrounding the bridge, quite without reason to do so, as it often goes in dreams.\nAs I stared into the deep blue waters, I swear that for an instance, the reflection of the bridge was as it is now, broken and horrible. In my dreamlike state, I hardly even thought about the reflection as I raised my head to look at the citadel again.\nAs I walked slowly towards the citadel, I remember humming a tune. Unfortunately, this tune is utterly lost to me at the minute, though I remember it being one of peace and contentment.\nAnyhow, I soon reached the gate of the citadel in all it's glory. Without explanation, the gate opened itself, as though the citadel welcomed back it's citizens. I remember a sigh of happiness escaping me as I once again laid my gaze upon my old home.\nI didn't bother with checking the laboratories, or even who had opened the gates. I suppose I thought that I could get to them later. \nI then made my way to the centre of the entrance, resting a hand on the back of my favourite bench with fondness.\nThere I stood for several moments, as though I was taking it all in. It is strange, but it almost felt the same as seeing the citadel for the first time. Being filled with hope, peace and utter contentment, all at the same time.\nAfter a few moments of standing and taking it all in, I begun walking once more. This time, I made my way up the stairs to the right of the lumbershop. \n\nHow odd it is, to think that afer all of these years, I can still remember all of those little shops.\nMy pace quickened as I walked up those stairs, as though I couldn't quite wait to get there. At the top of several flights of stairs stood a few rooms, rooms that are now empty and free of the glory that they once contained. But in my dream..\nI couldn't put into words the amount of relief and joy I felt when I saw the eternal library once again. Books filled every shelf, and I traced my hand along the spines of the book as I walked along.\nNow that I have time to reconsider this, I find it rather amusing that the first place I check for injury is the library that I had spent so many months researching in.\nWith the assurance that the books were safe, I began to walk to my old home in the Citadel, much more calmly now. But as I walked down this corridor, I began to notice that the paintings weren't quite as they should be.\nVines grew over the paintings, and several of them had been knocked down. In my dreamlike state, I almost didn't notice this, well, until I reached my old home, anyhow. My pace would quicken slightly as I fumbled in my pockets for the key.\nThe area around the door was covered in vines, and some of the wall had been worn away with time. I fumbled to unlock the old door, but it simply fell from it's hinges at the pressure.\nThe rooms that I had once kept so neat, the rooms that I had spent so many hours decorating.. Gone. The floor had caved in, the chests almost empty. Flies and maggots occupied the room in my dream, their smell causing me to back away, back into the hall.\nAs I turned back around, the hall was as it is now. Overgrown. A ghost of it's old self. I remember looking around in horror, before I ran back to the gate. The citadel around me had seemingly caught up in it's timeline, looking to be as it is now.\nI exited the citadel, the gate falling shut behind me with a loud thud. As I made my way across the bridge, I looked back, now seeing the citadel for what it was. A shell. Though it looked to be perfect, and as glorious as it once was..\nIt could never return to that stage.\nAs soon as I thought of this, I awoke in Lin'sulan. I peered out of the window to check the weather, made a pot of tea and began to write.\nThat, dear readers, is where we are now.\n\nI suppose that the moral of this, is that you cannot allow yourself to focus on the past, as it is gone. We must focus on the future, of both the Mali'aheral and of Haelun'or.\n\n                 - F.V.", ""),
        StaticBook("A few notes", "Hans Von Ziegel", "The papers are neatly organized, and writen in the native Waldenian\nlanguage, as if to further mock whoever the notes were meant for.\nMein liebster Caliph Wächten,\n\nIch bin zutiefst leid, was ich tat.\n\nJedoch,\n\nDeine Mutter schwitzt beim Kacken.\n\n*signed*\nJohans Von Ziegel\nA wax seal is pressed to the paper...\n\n\n      ███████ \n     ████████\n   ██████████\n   ██████████\n   ██████████\n   ██████████ \n   ██████████\n    █████████ \n      ███████\n   Ziegel Mercenary", ""),
        StaticBook("A Forest Poem", "Nivndil Duskhollow", "Puerith'leyu.\n\nThe trees they stand,\nA clamour of souls.\n\nTheir voices born on\nWinds, are old.\n\nBoughs up high,\nFairy halls.\n\nRoots below,\nSilent foot-falls.\nThey stand and wait,\nFor times unborn.\n\nTo whisper secrets,\nBefore words were forged.\n\nAmongst their trunks,\nBeneath canopy dome.\n\nTo bathe in twilight,\nThe trees my home.", ""),
        StaticBook("A found Journal", ":", "An Itharel's journal:\nIt's interesting really, even after ascending to a height of Demi-Godhood that many a Valah would dream of and many a Mali, Uruk or Bortu might envy...I feel little difference and yet I still fear it. The loss of my soul...not the literal soul I remind\nyou...you being me in the future. I fear it because...well look at my cousin...I hardly see a scrap of him left in that hollow golden shell...\n\nSo starting from this day I'll note the simple things...the taste of bread, the trees...\nthe coitus, the masonry, the books I read and poems that made me cry...that way I'll have memories to cling to...the pile of experiences that define us as people and thus will save me. \n\nI pray my mortality does not leave me too quickly...I must also\ntell Mia...and Skale...and those ignorant of this matter. It's a saddening truth and a cruel one for them and myself...but alas it is so...\n\nI am bound by the chains of service until I'm cast aside.\nYet another is lost. I can't blame him, the stress is damaging and the sights can drive any man past sanity...or good...\n\nIt would have been me had I not *several words have been erased as if the reader couldn't decide*\nwell...if I wasn't what I am...\n\nSeems as soon as we lose one, we recieve a new one. One of Katari's creatures...now one of Hesh's....I named him grandmaster.\n\nThe new Cleric is Luna. Impure but...pretty...\nalas the frailty of mortality. Like a small sculpture of glass and china. Fascinating yet...so delicate.\n\nSo this Rose tavern is clearly going to be nutcase central, perhaps I can fix that....maybe not.\nI see interesting folk here, the Gwyn individual appears again...she seems less...brute-ish.\n\nAll sorts in here actually. Old faces and new...one of Ivanus' past.\nSo for those interested, this is how you can be an Itharel:\n1. Man up- Ivanus.\nWell...I would note that usually sitting on a Shrine's altar would be...most...cruel.\n\nHowever...this particular one is in Lenia's name...so I doubt she'd mind.\n\nBesides I'm a walking steamboat of Tahariae's favour\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("A Found Notebook", "Rajiya al-Shamrani", "\"Cheza and August used to be married. They have a son even. August tortured her in horrific ways. Forced a golden apple down her throat too, and tortured her more. Cheza has nothing but contempt for August, on top of the darkness present in her heart.\"\n\"I will help look for a teacher for you, sweetheart.\"\n\n\"Maln, Father.\nHaelun, Mother.\"\n\n\"Be careful about those purity obsessed aheral. They won't like me being your mother. Not that I'll ever stop being your Haelun.\"\n\"I only teach arcane evocation sadly. For now. But do not feel troubled if you wish to learn something else. I am very proud of you already. You're a model student. Go find a teacher for whatever magic you desire, we can resume our lessons whenever.\"\n\"I am the Steward of Avalon of Erochland. I would like to offer you a free home, in exchange of looking after this child. The city is clean and nice, pretty safe too.\nMy name is Salendys.\"\n\"I may not look like it, but I am a powerful mage. Perhaps I can help you.\"\n\n\"Master arcanist. Electrical evocationist.\"\n\"What Ramza said in our last council meeting. I rarely see him lately, he's never there for me. And he wasn't there for me when I was mutilated either. He didn't even seem to care. He's not my brother anymore. He's just another cleric.\"\n\"I want to talk to a golemancer.\"\n\n\"I just want to talk to one.\"\n\"Hello. I am Salendys. I'm sorry about what happened in Athera.\"\n\"I want to talk to a golemancer.\"\n\n\"I just want to ask some questions.\"\n\n\"Fine. I want to ask about the speech runes used in golems.\" §\n\"Guard at the gate opened a trapdoor below me for no reason and it hurt.\"\n\n\"I don't want their help.\"\n\"I just want some company, is all. Chatting is difficult for me, for obvious reasons.\"\n\n\"Not really. I can't juggle with real balls. I can only juggle with evoked ones because I am in full control of them. It's just a pretty fake.\"\n\"I don't really know about runes, so you'll have to explain to me how this works.\"\n\n\"Will I sound like a golem?\"\n\n\"Interesting. What must I give in return?\"\n\"There are ways to grow it back, but I do not want that. I'll remain this way for now. Silent.\"\n-------------------Book was donated to the Grand Library of the Caliphate of Khalestine unsigned.\n\n           ---\nRajiya al-Shamrani,\nTalaaba of the Caliphate of Khalestine", ""),
        StaticBook("A GUIDE: Hijabs", "Zahrah", "A GUIDE: HIJABS\n\n\nTen hijab tips and secrets.\n\nFor those who wear one, who may wear one, or are generally interested.\n1. There are so many ways to tie a hijab.\n\n\nTie around the back of your head? More volume? There are so many choices!\n2. We actually have really nice hair!\n\nJust because it's hidden doesn't mean it doesn't exist. \nSometimes, it's even pretty.\n3. Running is a no-no.\n\nTry running or doing anything that makes you warm. We heat up a lot faster than the rest of you.\n4. We get asked a lot of silly questions.\n\n\"Are you actually bald?\"\n5. Most days is bad Hijab day.\n\nJust like bad hair days, sometimes you can put on your hijab and look like you haven't slept in weeks.\n6. Wearing new clothes can't be done until you have a hijab to match.\n\nReally. Do not try and wear a blue dress with a lime green dress. Think about it!\n7. We own so many, but have none to wear.\n\nIt's like going to look for food when the pantry is full. It's there but it's not really /there/.\n8. Hijabs can block sound too.\n\nSo we're not ignoring you, we actually can't hear you.\n9. If you drop your food, it ends up in your hijab and not on the floor.\n\nNo more wasting food that you accidentally drop! Who could ask for more?\n10. But finally, we're really proud of our choice.\n\nWe may be looked at funny, asked why we cover up. Some races don't understand. But. . \n\n'When I wear my headscarf, I feel I have faith, and identity. . '\n'And that's also beauty.'\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/pxohds6", ""),
        StaticBook("A humble Request", "Brutus Fontaine", "Sir Orithur,\n\nMy name Is Brutus Fontaine, i am an adventurer, and collector. While i was travelling, i happened to come across two very peculiar items, which i will list now:\n-\"Billy Bob's Trusty hoe\"= It looks like a wooden hoe to the common\neye, but it is actually a souvenir, gifted by the Tater Lord himself. I wish to give it to the library, for it to be shown in the museum wing.\n\n-Crude Thanium ore: Whilist wondering, i also came across a chunk of crude Thanium. Now, i do not wish to sell\nor donate it, but transform it into powder. Since your library is the only place i know of containing a Thanium laboratory, i came to thee for help. Do not worry, the chunk is secured at the moment.\n\nSo, what do you say? I donate to you the wooden hoe of\na pseudo-god, and you help me turn this thanium into powder. Send me a bird if you are interested, please.\n\n\n\n              -Your humble,\n     Brutus Fontaine", ""),
        StaticBook("A Hunters Chant", "Damai Torena", "A Hunters Chant\n\nI'll hunt that wolf and hunt that deer\nEven though I lost most of my gear\nCernnunos will guide my arrow\nHopefully not to hit a high sparrow\nMany men will hunt that wolf, but fail and try\nBut I wont end up with a cry\nBecause I have a trusty arrow\nA arrow so light it will fly and fly\nI have Cernnunos' guide\nOn my arrow's sleek\nside\nI will use the wolfs meat\nAnd put it under very hot heat\nI will use every part for good use\nI will do it up near a large, old spruce\n\nAnd the cycle will start again\nAnd the hunt will not be in Vain\nBecause I have the guide of Cernnunos\nAnd will hit the Wolf with barely any blows\nI shall go back home with many pelts\nMany more to hang off my belts", ""),
        StaticBook("A Journal", "Anonymous", "Day 1: Today I begin my trek to Mount Thahn, the colossal mountain in the centre of the world. It is an intriguing target for scientific study as it is a frozen tundra, yet is surrounded by temperate to hot lands. This is a\nmystery I shall solve, and which will catapult me to recognition in the guild and that fool Havery will finally see me as a proper rival.\n\nDay 3: Arrived at Mount Thahn. Was rudely thrown out of the dwarven\ncity built upon the upper slopes for attempting to enter the Remembrancer's library. Apparently the dwarves take issue with having their doors broken open with axes, but they shouldn't lock their knowledge away like that! Not\nfrom me, anyway. They can lock it away from Havery all they like.\n\nDay 4: A little prospecting soon deduced why: the mountain stone is rich in thanhium, a heat-absorbing ore. The ore has many useful\nmagical properties, including use as a power source for enchantments. I will hire some miners at once!\n\nDay 5: Sadly, setting up a thanhium mining operation could prove difficult. The dwarves have\ndiscovered and claimed the thanhium. All of it. They haven't actually dug it up, but a foul smelling dwarf informed me at swordpoint that it's all theirs. Should I attempt to steal it from under their noses, they'll likely respond by\nby force of arms. I will search for a place where we could potentially mine the ore without them noticing.\n\nDay 8: I discovered a cavern today. It seemed to warm as I went down, as if the thanhium\nwere... missing. Surely there should be more of it as one goes down? It's as if it's already been dug up, but the dwarves live on top of the mountain, not below it. I will venture deeper tomorrow.\n\nDay 9: I found\na huge door at the end of the cavern. It looks dwarven, but different, like it's centuries of architectural development ahead. Could the dwarves have developed time travel and invaded the past? I wouldn't put it past them. That being\nsaid, stealing their time machine and claiming it as my own invention... Forget beating Havery, this could send me right to the top! I must open this door...\n\nDay 13: No luck opening the door.\nDay 17: Still no luck opening the door. This sure is a low technology door for future dwarves, though.\n\nDay 20: It has occurred to me that the future dwarf theory is, to put it as the orcs would, a load of\nskah. The door isn't a future door, it's an ancient one. Have the dwarves devolved? I could believe that, they must have lost their brilliance with their height. Still no luck opening the door, but I suppose we could tunnel around it. Heard\nwhat sounded like people skulking around.\n\nDay 21: This discovery is remarkable! I can't write it down in fear that I will lose these notes and Havery will steal my discovery. We collapsed the\ntunnel we dug and I will hire a full expedition to loot this place. We need to get out quietly though, as the dwarves are onto us. I've heard they can be so quiet that they can sne\n\n*The journal stops abruptly here.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Last Testimony", "Felix Pyre", "It was John Vilcan. He was the one who did this to me.\n\nI was helping Laurinia with something in her house when suddenly I blacked out. When I awoke I was on a bed in some basement, missing my tongue. I saw him face... John was there with a knife in hand.\nI was able to push him off me before he did anything more, but when I was about to tackle him, something struck my face, not sure what, not sure who did it. But I suspect Laurinia...\n\nI need you to do me a favor... I cannot live like this, I can't recover\nI need you to end my pain, my misery. But you need to make it look like a murder, otherwise the Monks will not heal me. There is a knife on the table beside me ((There's actually furniture down here lol)) When you're done, burn this note.\nBut memorize its contents in its entirety. I need you to explain everything that I've told you... Then we find this bastard and we end him.\n\n((Just erase everything and leave the book in my mail instead of actually burning it, I wanna keep atleast one.))\nFor- Alfred Orris", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Jentos", "----+--+-O-+--+----\n\nDear leader of the wizards guild. \nI would gladly enjoy to join your organisation. \n\nI have been a court wizard for many years.\n\n-Jentos Blackwood\n((Jentos))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Aeran", "Dear Taynuel\n\nI would like to apologize for how I've acted. Throughout the whole time I've known you, but more specifically recently. I messed up big time, and deserve a larger punishment than I got. There's no excuse for my actions, I won't try to give\nyou one.\n\nI hope I can be a better person, and a better Druid, in the future. You're one of the great Druids in my opinion, truly.\n\n\n-Aeran", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Elvira Naromis", "-The letter would be written on fine parchment and the writing is simple yet joint. It's easy to recognise as Elvira's writing-\n\nDear all I know from working at the Drunken Monk.\n\nAs stated in my last letter, I was planning-\n- on going on a journey for a while. I have now decided to go out on that journey for some time of training my fire evocation, ingredient gathering, and finding more about myself than what I already know.\nHowever, I will not be going alone. I will be-\n- joined by Ramza, his daughter Iris, and my huntress friend Farryn Aren. Turns out, Ramza and Iris need time to relax... apparently some trouble came up between Ramza and his wife which led to Ramza leaving her. He is struggling so he and his daughter-\n-will be coming with me.\n\nAs for Farryn. You all won't know her but she serves as a huntress, hunting down bandits and monsters with a lance! Plus, she knows how to sail which is good. We're going to be sailing for a few days or so. It's good I know\n- someone who can help us if we get in a tight spot.\n\nI'm not sure how long we will be on this journey for but I guess for a year or two.\nFirstly, I just want to set some things:\n\nDaniel. I will no longer be capable of teaching\n-my students: Nisus (o_daxton_o) and Damon (CountSictor). If you want, you can teach them if you like. They are both currently on learning back the ingredients, although Nisus just finished about the frost vines and Damon hasn't started yet. I hope you-\n-don't mind, I can teach them when I return.\n\nIf any of you need to get in contact with me. Just blow on this whistle three times and either Ventus or Aithne will appear to take any letters to me.\nIf something bad is happening and you need me, I will-\n-hurry back but please make sure it's for a valid reason.\n\nI hope (and prey) you all remain safe and sound during my absense. Trust me, I hate leaving you all for a while but I need this.\nSo, do take care! And be yourselves please!\nWith hugs and safe travels\n\n-Elvira Naromis\nYour dear blonde Alchemist, fire mage and bartender.\n\n-A wooden whistle would be included in the envelope.-", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Anonymous", "Fear the Old Dark as Ryder did.\n\nThis is only the beginning.\n\nThere shall be no end.\n\nGod is with us.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Shawn Telvin", "\"Dearest Oliver,\n\nMay we please take down the gigantic, bloody chimes in the dedicant housing area?\n\nIt smells rotten, and my chickens keep trying to drink the blood. Emmy is not happy, either.\n\n-Shawn Telvin\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Ashton", "\"Dear Dad,\n\nI baked some fresh pie for you! I hope you enjoy it.\n\nLove you,\n\nAshton", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "ThatWeirdGirl", "Hi, I have a diamond that won't stop screaming at me and I was told to talk to an ascended. I live in Sutica.\n\n-Johanna Downer", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Seth Calith", "My deepest apology for the time for my respond. As I wrote it and thought of your reaction I felt something I haven't felt for long, fear.\n\nThat you would reject me, that you wouldn't be pleased and that history would repeat.\nI have now after 3 years finished my poem with more than two hundred papers spilled in attempts to finish it, something to be you worthy.\n\nI would like to meet you, I am flatteret by your gestures so far and I hope my slow one has as well.\nIf I am not what you seek, at least leave me a simple letter so I do not have to live through days un-knowing of your respond.\n\nI hope you enjoyed the poem, my Moon.\n\n-Seth Calith.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter for Xus", "Elora Delevoye", "Dear Xusayne~\n\nAn Orc came by the city today claiming that there is a whitewashed Orc in the city. The Orc was sent by his kind. Do you still have that Orc in your cellar, i believe that is the one. I am just warning you, i lied to the Orc and told him no\nWhitewash is here. But if he finds out i lied i am in danger, so is my family. The Orc threatend to kill everyone. I am going to talk to a gaurd hopefully they know what to do. Best regards\n\n~Elora", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter to Ari", "underwhereknight", "Dear Ari,\n\n    It's been a long time since I've seen you. I apolgize for all the times I brought you into peril. And the things I said to you in these situations...\n\n    But If you still care for me, my right knee cap was broken by the Feslen guard\nand I don't think I'll ever walk again normally without a devoted healer. I Have been planning on creating a guild of those who face monsters and such. This dream may be for not.\n\n     Thanhium as you probably know has magical properties.\nI have read it can be used in armor agaisnt monsters. Since I lack the  minas to afford to buy such armor or many other magical items. I plan on getting them straight from the source. After months of searching I have refound the old Thanhium ruins.\nNow that my leg is as it is I will need more assistance than before.  I'm asking alot I suppose but if you could contact every living memeber of Nathan's crew and inform them, as well as join me I'd appreciate it. With those joining us and a bit more\nrecruiting through a newspaper I am running with a new friend and bussiness partner, Aldern Osgood. It is called the 'Informer' and talks about the news of Feslen.\n\n     I am currently living in a 12. Steel Lane, just off the path next to the wall.\nThe guard doesn't like me so much as of now but I am still alive, thankfully.\n\n     If you don't get this letter Ari... I guess there isn't much to say. I hope whatever keeps you from this letter you brings you bliss in some form.\nLet's not give up on what we started all thoses years ago. I'm not the same man as I was back then. I am learned to read and write. I am learning alchemey. And I have a goal for this Thanhium more than just to sell it.\n        -With care,\n       Adam\nP.S. Please do not think this Monster hunting Guild is an outlandish thought. At the very least meet with me to discuss it.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Lost Bet", "Judas Windsor", "This is a book about random questions asked to strangers, I have decided to record them down into my book.\n\n(This was a lost bet, and therefore I shall pay the price of myterious questions.)\nWhat do you think about my yellow outfit?\n\nHobbit: It's ugly.\nHave you lost your Virginity: \n\nHobbit: (He hesitated) Ummm yes (Lying)\nWhat do you think of these questions?\n\nHobbit: They're odd.\n\nCan I have your name?\n\nHobbit: No.\nQuestion 1: Have you lost your virginity?\n\nElric: No answer.\n\nQuestions two: Have you ever had any sexual relations with an animal?\n\nElric: No\nWhat is your favourite food?\n\nElric: Grapes\nHow would you describe yourself in one word?\n\nSammy: Really cool guy.\nWhat do you think of the St Amyas?\n\nSammy: Super Lame\n\nHow would you kill the girl hanging from the sign above you?\n\nSammy: Running her over with my four wheeler.\nWhat do you think of me and Arya (her sister) being together?\n\nElaine: She is desperate and I feel sorry for her.\nWhat is your favourite food?\n\nElaine: Cream Pancakes\n\nAre you Jealous of me and Arya being together?\n\nElaine: No thats disgusting (She is)\nHave you ever had a pet before?\n\nAxel: No, atleast I don't think so.\n\nWhat do you think of the order of St Amyas:\n\nI don't know...someone told me they're an Unholy group.\n(I corrected him)\nHave you ever lost your virginity?\n\nAxel: I don't want to answer that.\n\nWhat is your sexual fantasy?\n\nAndwise: Sitting on the docks fishing, reels in as fast as I can\nas I reel in the devoure cus I'm buff you know. \nAnd I'm terrified as I reel in a monster who's ten times my weight.\n\nThen Descending from the heavens is a glowing creature with a pumpkin helmet, it'd point at the beast. Sends out a shog, and it\nexplodes into taters. \nPasses him a potato, and has a glimmer in it's eyes.\n\nEats tater, and the creature and Andwise take the day and visit halfling lands in all of the realms until they reach Athera.\n\nHe'd show the creature his old home, and\nthey'd kiss outside of it.\n\nBut you'd expect the helmet to get in the way?\n\nbut the pumpkin is also kissing me.\nWe grow old and raise three or four proppah halflings on a farm.\nTill we grow old.\n\nWhat is your favourite food?\n\nAndwise:  The Peregin family has an old recipe for lamp chops absoloutley delicious.\nFavourite Sexual Position:\n\nPumpkin on my head\n\nPumpkin on their head\n\n'The old trombone'\na classic.\n\n-Andwise.\nIf you had to get a tattoo/another tattoo what would it be or say?\n\nYpres; A trampstamp over my chest saying \"Know where your heart is.\"\n\nOr a name of my married wife.\nWhat is your favourite tavern?\n\nYpres: Red-Rose tavern.\n\nHow often do you smoke Cactus green?\n\nYpres: Never.\nIf you could kill anyone in Vailor who would it be and why?\n\nDrak'lur: Kalenz, zhe wuz arzehule.\n\nWho do you most find attractive in Vailor: \n\nDrak'lur: Weyul.\nName one thing you hate about yourself using only one word.\n\nDrak'lur: Mi Uncomzy puntz.\nBreasts Or Thighs?\n\nJeremiah:\n\nThighs becaus' t'ey fer walkin'.\n\nDeepest Secret?\n\nJeremiah: A'h onc' lead a'h gian' crab t'uh me 'ome once, t'at clos' enough?\nHave you ever thought about having sexual relations with an animal?\n\nJeremiah: Neve'h though' abou' tha', wouldn' be useful ey?\nIf you could use only one word to describe yourself what would it be?\n\nUdarr: Grass.\nBreasts, thighs, Armpit on a women?\n\nUdarr: Thighs.\nWhat is your most embarrassing secret?\n\nUdarr: A'h loike t'uh eat me own toenail choppin's.\nIf you had to choose one to live without what would it be?\n\nNose\n\nEyes\n\nEars\n\nMouth\n\nNermir: My mouth I dont speak much.\nWhat is your sexual fantasy you one day hope to come true?\n\nNemir: I dont really have any sexual fantasies so it wouldn't come true.\nBreasts, thighs, eyes or armpit?\n\nNemir: I'd rather a person with eyes.\nThat is the last of the questions please put yes if you asked strangers all these questions.\n\nYes: Yes I did\n\nNo:", ""),
        StaticBook("A Love Story", "Orithur", "pandan, pandan,\nwe fell in love so quick\n\npandan, pandan,\nnow hop on my dick", ""),
        StaticBook("A Marked Tale", "Snuggle the Elf", "The Marked Man's \nCompendium of Beasts\n\n        Volume II\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n         Book II\n\"Not here, my love,\" she said. \"My chambers are ahead.\"\n\nThe Staunton Girl's heart skipped as she ran her hand through his ashen hair.\n\n\"My wolf,\" she said. \"My white wolf.\"\n\nThe man smirked.\nHe snaked his arm around her waist, and drew her close.\n\nThe Staunton Girl felt the throbbing heat of the White Wolf's breath on her moist, supple skin.\n\nHe brought his nose to the nape of her neck.\nThe sweet and sour of honey and vinegar filled the White Wolf's senses.\n\nThe White Wolf threw his head, and let out a howl. He lifted her arm, and buried his face in her armpit.\n\nHer skin as pale and delicate as fresh snow blushed an apple red.\n\"How is it, my dear?\" the Staunton Girl asked.\n\n\"Like Gauldrim's ass.\" the White Wolf said as he licked the armpit salt off her moist armpit skin.\n\nShe grew weak in her knees. If she fell, would he catch her?\n\"Say my name,\" the Staunton Girl said. \"Say it.\"\n\nSalt and sweat danced on the White Wolf's tongue. The interplay between salty and sour made for a perfect marriage for his keen senses. Was marriage too a thing on his mind?\n\n\"Jarzy.\" he said.\nThoughts and dreams raced through her head as the White Wolf ran his tongue against and across her supple skin.\n\n\"Easy now,\" she said. \"Save some for later.\" \n\nShe gazed into his eyes, and brushed an ashen strand over his ear.\n\nHe let out a whimper.\n\"There, there, cute puppy.\" the Staunton Girl said. She beamed at him, and raised her other arm.\n\nThe White Wolf lunged at the fruit. Aged cheese, vinegar and cat shit took hold of his senses. His mind spun, and his thoughts were a blur.\nThe White Wolf howled. He pushed the Staunton Girl, and pinned her to the floor.\n\n\"Savage,\" she said. \"Know what rhymes with 'savage?'\" \n\nShe licked her lips, and raised her arms. \n\n\"Ravage me.\"\n*The remaining pages are glued together by an odd, unidentified substance.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Merchants Tale", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "A Merchants Tale\n\nBy some unknown merchant\nBe Fat\n\nBuy low\n\nSell High\n\nEmploy slaves\n\nRent a Dunstan\n\n10/10", ""),
        StaticBook("A message", "Arcadius Aurelius", "Greetings, steward. I was wondering.. How would an educated man, as myself, be able to acquire a job within these graceful city walls? I have many qualifications in business matters, and other matters that I shan't discuss. If you should see that\nI am qualified for some kind of job, please do contact me.\n\n-Arcadius Aurelius. (Balthasar)", ""),
        StaticBook("A new day", "Arahael Eloem", "A new day\nby Arahael Eloem\nThe warmth is returning,\nAs the sky blushed and flushed.\nThe evil are smoldering,\nReceiving the justice of good.\nThe flowers are swaying,\nAs the branches wave at me.\nPearls of moisture stuck to petals,\nAs they bloom of renewal.\nThe wind crisp and clean,\nWith an air of importance.\nI swept the scene with a single gaze,\nIt was a new day.", ""),
        StaticBook("A new day", "Unknown", "A new day\n\nThe warmth is returning,\nAs the sky blushed and flushed.\nThe evil are smoldering,\nReceiving the justice of good.\nThe flowers are swaying,\nAs the branches wave at me.\nPearls of moisture stuck to petals,\nAs they bloom of renewal.\n\nThe wind crisp and clean,\nWith an air of importance.\nI swept the scene with a single gaze,\nIt was a new day.\nArahael Eloem (PianoEby)", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "underwhereknight", "*A note is left on the bedside in bad hand writing*\nIf I can get in here easily enough, I can get other things easily enough. Hang a red banner from the bank and I will reveal myself to talk further on this.\n*the letter is not signed*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Jule Farmer", "Dearest Lauren,\n\nI'm not sure what all you've been told about me or my comrades conderning our rebellion, or even if you're concious of it at all. Know that I care for you, and that this rebellion is not against Savlians, but Salvus' poor leadership.\nI'm currently staying behind Felsen in a small settlement, independant of Felsen. I would like to meet you, and speak with you in person. There are larger homes, and more room to grow in Felsen, if our rebellion should fail. If our rebellion succeeds,\nthen you will have no cause to fret, as we'll be able to have a nice home and lands in Salvus territory. I hope we're successful for that cause alone. Send me a bird when you feel it necessary. I'll answer any questions you may have at that time. ->\n[[ OOC: Long time no see! Also yes, questions to be answered, basically, Salvus had a town meeting where we stated our issues and they answered, and the leadership literally was shutting us down on everything. Whenever someone would point out the flaws in\nSalvus, they'd go,\"We're just DIFFERENT.\" Like no. Examples of those flaws include the lack of bridges to farm and military islands, NO JOBS like at all, yet citizens were still expected to pay taxes. Also, I paid the tax on your house for this year. ]]", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Lorena Faeliel", "*A note would be wedged into a crate of winebottles. The contents of each a viscious black liquid. The note reads:*\n\n\"Love, your 'friend' left this crate of. . what ever here for you. She spoke about a 'Loss of Independance'\nand how they would stall that. She also said, and I quote\n'Good luck with that whole payoff thing.'.\n\nI do not know what she is talking of and quite honestly, it is concerning.\n\n-Lorena.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A note for Wulf", "Adil", "Wulf,\n  Before I left the keep I saw your notice outside of your lab. At first, I thought it was crazy. But after your leg injury, until we can get you walking, I will pledge myself to being such Lab Assistant. I will acquire slimeballs and search for a\nhealer.\n          -Adil", ""),
