        StaticBook("A Page", "Anonymous", "The 5th of Snows Maiden, 1302\n\nWe, the Order of Nine close upon the sanctuary of the heretic known as Ezekiel Cunningham. He appears to have sealed himself in an underground cave of sorts.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Parchment Roll", "The Soothsayer of Argul", "I COME TO FOREWARN OF DEATH, FOR IT IS IMPENDING. [*The words are scratched into the parchment, the non-specific threat crudely scrawled.*]", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem", "Anonymous", "Thumbleweed's Tower\n\nThumbleweed the fool,\nSitting in his tower,\nPassing every hour,\nSearching for the sorcerer's tool,\n\nThumbleweed the failed,\nGazing into his book,\nLooki\n\n\n*Someone else's writing appears below*\n\nThis, Aldereki, is the poorest work I have seen in years. Your assignment\nis not even complete.\n-Iyathir Aereos", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem of Nature", "Baine", "Nature is what we see,\nGeese that form a V in the sky.\nThe pedal of a flower that wave good bye in the wind.\nA wood pecker that pecks to no end.\nThe wheat that waits to be harvest and sold at the untold shop.\nThe tree that can spare no more but a\npear. \nNature is what we hear\nThe tree's branch that falls on to the abandoned ranch.\nThe clucks of chickens when they see a wild dog in the fog.\nThe hiss of a cat when they've found their prey in the ray of light.\nNature is what we feel.\nThe thorns on a rose bush that over grows.\nThe moarnful rabbit that's fur rubs against your leg.\nThe tall grass that is vast.\nThe tree that maybe gone soon.\nThe roots that someone played the flute on.\nNature is beauty. \nThe flower that grows in the sight of delight.\nNature is life or death.\nThe vultures that threaten to end the rabbit's life with one nasty bite.\nThe deer that lies injured near a wild dog unable to see through the fog.\nThe luck that a duck has when a hunter can not swim.\nNature is everything.\nA tree in the meadow that is ready to be carved into a bow.\nThe bird that sings to all beings.\nThe giant mushroom that grows in harmony near ebony.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Proposition", "Theran", "Hello, Orithur. My name is Theran, and I am also a collector of books. I own a bookstore in Felsen, but I also am establishing a library there for the public to view official documents, Church works, and the likes of those. I have found many texts here\nthat would be extremely valuable to the well-being of the library in Felsen. Is there a way for me to make copies of these books and to bring them back for public viewing in Felsen? I have books to donate if that is the case, as I have already written\nsome for the public. I also have some Druidic poems and tales. Let us be in touch.\n\nTheran\n((InherentEssence))\n\n*A feather lies between the pages, seemingly for bird-tracking*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Report", "Alderiki", "The Advanced on a Door Forever Sealed\n\nWe advanced upon the great doors of Urguan last night to find them sealed entirely. Reports from our spies within the area assured us the dwarves would not\nseal the door for their strange soul rending machine they call “The Seal” had consumed all but a fraction of the city’s populace, by order of the dwarven government. These informants did tell us that some remained at the\ngate, a skeleton crew who they believed were to few in number to seal the great door. Evidently, they were wrong for when we arrived we came across a hall which was impenetrable. Those left inside had seemingly\nprefered to leave themselves to the horrors within, rather than answer to our eldritch might which would bring them justice for their crimes.\n\nBeyond the wall, sickening screams were heard for days, and then\nsilence. What brought them their final descent into death remains unknown to us. Was it thirst? Starvation? Or something far more sinister which lurked within?\n\nFor days the most powerful of my\nkindred assaulted the wall with the elements: Fire, earth, wind and water but nothing could break its eternal watch. And so, days later, we left. The war had been won, but the mysteries which lay within the walls had forever been\nlost.\n\n-Alderiki", ""),
        StaticBook("A report", "Aulfr af Eklund", "In this journal do I submit my musings.\n\nI have decided that the Raevir are in fact part Olog as was released in a document recently. It does in fact make sense.\n\nI must capture some of them for testings...\n--\nIt is true, I have sliced open members of the Raev and seen their very large organs and malignant black cancers rotting them.\n\nObviously their bodies are fighting themselves.\n--\nIt is worse than I feared. The Raevir actually put Olog Organs inside each other to become more like Hughes Sarkozic. This is... Heresy.\n\nI must do more tests.\n--\nI have concluded there can be no doubt; The Raevir people are trying to make a proto-human race. This is not good, I must war the Ser Garahel.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Request", "Avern'len", "===================\n\nDarkness, fear, even pain have long been foreign to me,\n\nNow I am just an unnatural stain, dead as a cut down tree.\n\n===================\n===================\n\nYet, friends, in the name of love, I've fought the stigmas set.\n\nFor the sake of my blue eyed dove, an oath I shall not easily forget.\n\n===================\n===================\n\nA promise made beneath the birch, upon our humble mountainside.\n\nAnd so I wish to resume my modest search, and overcome this unnatural divide.\n===================\n===================\nWhat proof is there beyod simple words, perhaps my protection over your woods.\n\nI stood against dragons, Harbingers, and Scourge hordes, a dire trial by simply mere swords.\n===================\n===================\nAllow me to retack the path, my former kin, to reach enlightenment, attunement, take a totem- even then.\n\nI wish to atone for my involuntary sin, and take the path to Druidism again.\n===================\nA Request\n\nAvern'len San'taelah", ""),
