        StaticBook("Azure's Entry", "Azure", "(-----------)\nI don't think I can see when you're here with me. It's like darkness has covered my eyes and sometimes it feels like I'm going to die. It feels like I'm high, and I can feel nothing but burning on the inside.\n\nContinue -------->\n(chorus) So now I sit here trying to just get near. You are my everything, the reason I sing, the reason I've been so keen on living.\n\nSo won't you please come see that I would give anything just to be around you.\n\n(chorus)\n\nContinue ---->\nThings get hard when you're alone, I know this because what I've been shown. So come with me and see what you and I have been missing.\n(free style song)\n\n        (-------------)\n\n\n(Ballad)\n------------------------>\nLife is beautiful\nas it gleams\nit revives your soul\nleaving you redeemed\n\nMy name is Azure\nand I sing for you,\nto tell how I miss her,\nso singing is what I do\n\n\n\nContinue ---------->\nThis girl is beautiful,\nand it's funny,\nher skin feels like wool\nso soft like a bunny\n\nMy name is Azure\nand I sing for you,\nto tell how I miss her,\nso singing is what I do\n\n\n\nContinue ------------>\nEven though its ending\nand we've had our fun\nalways remeber to sing\nunder the setting sun\n\nMy name is Azure\nand I sing for you,\nto tell how I miss her,\nso singing is what I do\n       (-------------)\n\nSonnet\n------------->\nBlood, hate, and pain leads to more blood red rain so beware the beast called war or you will die for sure\n\nYou can take this song\nand think all daylong\neither way its true\nwar is a pain statue\n\n\nContinue ------------>\nSo never forget\nwhat has been said\nthat war is pointless\ncreating a bloody mess\n\nI hope this meeting\nhas sent its meaning\nand now you understand\ndo not lend war a hand\n\n        (------------)\n\n      THE      END", ""),
        StaticBook("Babys First Wand", "Toxzero", "Baby's First Wand\n\nBy Sarrion Di'Pasali\nWhat is a wand?\n\nA wand is a tool made from a few simple materials but shaped together in an art and love for craftsmanship, then used as a focal point for any spell. They are used for users who find ease to use a point rather than one's palm,\nor users who use destructive magic and wish to have a distance between them and such. Advanced use for wands can be configured with external magic and crystals, allowing enchantments and the like to be added.\nSelecting your material:\n\nThe base for your wand has to be selected out of a material, one of the most common ones would be wood as it can be carved into one’s own design for originality and personality, easy to put a socket in for the focus crystal\nand any other gems, and very light to carry but easy to break. The next most popular type of material would be metal, harder to get designs engraved into and harder to get them forged, and much harder to get gems\nand the crystal socketed but much much more durable and will last longer.\nSelecting your Focus Crystal:\n\nThe tip of your wand is going to be tipped with a focus crystal, a crystal that naturally grows in the forest and used as a focus point for spells.\nThey vary in color and length, but they can be incorporated simply on the tip or as a neat-o design such as in the mouth of a dragon’s head on the tip of a wand. Once your wand is fully put together, have fun casting.", ""),
        StaticBook("Badlands 1552", "Lealenn", "Day 1\nAfter receiving my supplies from Laureh'lin, I set out on my way to take the carts from the Cloud Temple to Felsen, and then a transit from there to the Erochlands. How queer it is to see not a single\nliving soul present in this swampy area.\nDay 2\nWalking around the Erochlands seems to reveal an orcish shrine near a castle. I wonder if the inhabitants co-exist peacefully, although the wide moat and high walls may suggest otherwise.\nDay 3\nIn the vague directions the patron from Celenin gave me, I have started off the beaten path, hiking through the snow, heading Southwards to where-ever this Badlands is. The weather has turned for a worst, and it has started raining\nincessantly. Half the food I brought has been afflicted with rot.\nDay 7\nFor the past few days, I have trekked, I climbed, I fell, without seeing a single sign of a sign of civilization. No roads, no signs, not even a tree. I seem to be going on a wild goose chase.\nDay 8\nDuring my stumble down the side of a mountain, I saw the most beautiful scene during this trip so far. A wide frozen lake stretches as far as a town, criss crossing through the valley, gleaming in the morning sunlight. Its so cold, even in\nSummer the sun does not seem capable of melting it. As breath-taking it is, I cant replenish any supplies here. I hope I see a town soon, I doubt I can survive much more on potatoes and bitter rye.\nDay 10\nA green lush field expands right before my eyes, with tall pine trees unlike any I have seen, with slender leaves waving in the air. I stumble upon what I think is an Inn, only to find it belongs to the Bard's Guild. Why does it exist in such a\nremote location? It flies the colours of yellow and green.\n\nA quick search within shows only two people living within, Titania and Syndra Hawksong, I assume a family business. While few instruments lay about, it seems to be covered with empty\nshelves. It seems its more for formality than an actual base of operations. Whatever the reasoning, I still cant find food. What bad luck.\nDay 11\n\nI met someone known as  Orrineat Goldhand in a dwarven encampment, confirming my suspicioins that I have wandered into dwarven territories. He gave me fish soup, the first hot food in possibly 2 weeks.\nThe first sips were pure heaven. \n\nSome conversation flowed, between two lonely individuals. He tells of the capital being redesigned, that all dwarves were forced into camps outside the walls.\nHe does not appear to know anything else, having claimed ignorance from constant mining. How very dwarf-like. I soon part, looking for a new path to take, with soup in each of my hands. No one knows where this Badland is, or even these\nmali'fenns. I wonder why.....\nDay 13\n\nAfter more wandering, I seem to come upon a large stretch of a siege by nightfall upon the plain. A passerby nodded and confirmed this was the Badlands, where the Fenn state once lived, although I can see no traces of anyone possibly\nliving here now. The fort of wood is frozen, but the inside is bare of any food or cots. Death traps are scattered everywhere, as well as tall guard towers intersecting the plain every so often. It seems more like a mock war camp, than an actual\nsettlement. There is nothing to be gleaned from here, unless the colours of red and blue, black and yellow mean anything upon the tents.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bardmancy", "Ox Druid Popo", "The Art of Bardmancy is forming noises from the Void into the sound of words, and bringing it into our world. Through this act, the Bardmancer can influence (not force!) the emotions and feelings of those around him or her. It is important to note, while\nBardmancy is NOT in any way shape or form used for combat, it does require mana, as it requires a connection to the void. It should also be noted that an instrument can be enchanted with Bardmancy to amplify the Bard's magic, much like a staff to a mage.\nTo perform bardmancy, one must meditate while listening to any manner of music that involves words. Focus on how it makes you feel, what makes the sound, and how one moves their mouth in order to form these word. The next step is to connect to the Void.\nWhile Bardmancy does not require an awful lot of mana, connecting to the void regardless takes much time, and most of your time studying will be spent trying to connect to the void. Once you have said connection, the first thing one must to on the\nbeginning of their journey with Bardmancy is to make any noise come out of their mouth. Truly, any noise you can hear is suitable. Imagine drawing out from your mouth with an invisable hand. While this takes several tries to correctly perform,\nit does come easier with practice. The next step is to attempt to form this sound into a word. This is easier said than done, as it requires your mind to focus greatly on turning the sound into the sound of your very own voice.\nHowever, as you continue, connecting to the void and forming and singing the words, as well as putting emotions behind them, will become much easier. At the beginning, your sentances will have long pauses in them, taking a lot of concentration, and may\neven force you to quit your song lest you pass out due to using up your mana. However, as Bardmancy is not /too/ complex, it does not require much mana once you learn how to bring the words into our plane of existance. However, any Bardmancer, no matter\ntheir skill, can sing forever.", ""),
        StaticBook("Barn Invest.", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "Upon hearing rumor of some barn outside of the Library of Dragur, which was involved with some sort of magical anomaly, I set out to investigate it. Before that however, let me explain a bit further.\n   Without boring anyone with the minute details, I-\n-shall proceed. The barn is a little ways to the west of the library. As the story goes, Orithur and a few others went to this barn to open a tome of 'unknown power'. Soon afterwards, a large crackle of energy was sensed surging desperately from the barn.\nReturning to the barn, Orithur was reportedly seen 'radiating' with magical energy as he stormed away. Once getting to the scene, it's reported there was a 'magical washboard' that whisked a female away. What this means, I am unsure. The only other -\n-person left in the barn informed the newcomers that this was the scene of a summoning. The summoning of a Voidal Horror known as the 'Outvoker'. This being was spoken to have already perished during some unknown previous event, according to the paper.\nThat is all that is known of this story.\n   Eventually I found myself to this said barn, and I must say, there are quite a few strange details about it. I first noticed that there is a strange portion of the land just in front of the entrance which is -\n- accursed by some blight which is unknown to me. Following what may or may not be blood, I entered the barn. \n   The second thing I noticed was that the barn was left with only a single story remaining, the rest of the barn inexplicably vanished without-\n-a roof.\n   Next and thirdly, I realized there are many pits, holes, and divots within the barn's floor. There are also reportedly less foliage, but that may just be because this is a barn and wouldn't have much anyway.\n   Upon further inspection, it-\n-appears that several trees near the barn have also inexplicably been severed from the midsection up. No traces of the trees' upper half. \n   A peculiar note, I realized that this barn is quite in the middle of nowhere. What purpose does a barn serve if -\nthere is no farmland nearby, nor cattle. Why was this even here in the first place? Was this barn even always here?\n   It appears that there are certainly anomalies about this barn, and a void node, Voidal Horror, or a tome of 'unknown power' may be -\n-responsible for this. I shall continue my investigation and research in the future. Until then, that is all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Blah", "Glacio Nereus", "Basic Uruk Words and Phrases\n\nBlah - Common\n\nUg - Hello\nThrom'ka - Hello (Formal)\nYub - Yes\nNub - No\nRulg - Thanks\nKlomp - Fight\nFlat - Kill\nUruk - Orc\nLat - You\nMi - Me\nTwiggeh - Elf\nAlbai - Elf\nShara - Human (?)\nBub'hozh - Big, Good\nNub'hozh - Small, Bad\nStout - Dwarf\nNubded - Undead\nBuub - Pig\nBuurz - Black, Dark\nMojo - Magic\nBuurz Mojo - Dark Magic\nSkah - Fuck\nSnaga - Slave\nSkah Snaga - Charis Pre. Rescue\nAgh - And\nRex - King\nKub - Child\nAsh - One\nDub - Two\nGakh - Three", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking", "Lillian", "<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   A Guide To Basic\n         Cooking\n     \n            By\n       Lillian Hill\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~    <><><><><><><><><>\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Dough~~~~~~\nIngredients:\nTwo binds of wheat.\nCooking Pot.\n\nFind the granules of wheat and remove them, before grindng them and mixing them with a small amount of water. You now have a basic dough.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Bread~~~~~~Ingredients:\nOne lump of dough\n\nCut off a small amount of the dough made previously, and form it into a ball. Place it in your cooking pot over your hot water, and wait for it to cook.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~Pan-Cakes~~~~\nIngredients:\nTwo portions of dough.\nCut your dough into two portions, and then go to flatten them out, and place them in your cooking pot side by side over heated water.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Fish~~~~~~~\n\nIngredients:\nRaw fish of your choice.\n\nRemove the bones of the fish, and peel off one layer of scales, placing it in the cooking pot with the small amount of seasoning.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Meats~~~~~~\nIngredients: Your choice of raw meat.\n\nSeason the meat with your choice of herb or salt, and then place it in your cooking pot, with a small amount of fat, or water.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking V2", "Lillian Hill", "<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Basic Cooking V.2\n   Soups And Stews.\n          \n            By\n       Lillian Hill\n\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   <><><><><><><><><><>\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n\nFor each of these recipes a bowl will be needed. These can be easily brought from most stores, or if you feel skilled enough, easy to carve yourself from wood. This is the second installment of the 'Basic Cooking' books.\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~Sailor's delight~~~\nIngredients: A cooked fish of your choice. \n\nAdd a small amount of water to your cooking pot, and allow it to warm. Meanwhile, finely dice your fish, making sure to skin and bone it, removing the head. Place\nthe chunks of fish in the hot water, and allow it to reach boiling point. At this point, you may feel free to add herbs or salts of your choice, such as tarragon, dill weed or basil. After the broth has boiled for half an elven hour, take a ladle and pour\nit into a bowl, taking care not to spill any of the liquid, as it may burn. Fish are an easy ingredient to attain, making this the perfect recipe for an easy and cost effective meal that would satisfy the hunger of your whole family.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Mushroom Stew~~\nIngredients:\nOne red browncap shroom.\nOne brown browncap shroom.\n\nTo start with, add a large quantity of water to your cooking pot, lighting your fire underneath the\ncauldron of water. As the water warms, peel your mushrooms of the top layer, as this allows for flavour to soak into the water. Then continue to slice your mushrooms into a few reasonable size chunks. After the water has started to bubble, throw in the\nmushrooms, adding some salt and perhaps some butter or lard, if you have the resources to do so. Allow the mushrooms to cook, stirring the broth occasionally. Once the mushrooms have coloured slightly, and the aroma begins to fill the room, ladle the stew\ninto a bowl. An easy recipe, as this type of fungi are commonly found in the wild, or can be bought from a store. This recipe makes enough for one person, though can be easily changed to make enough for the whole family.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Chicken Stew~~~\nIngredients:\nOne large piece of roat chicken.\nStart by lighting your fire and pour some water into the cooking pot to halfway, allowing it to heat and boil. Take the chicken and remove the skin. Then, make sure to\ncut it into bite size chunks, making sure to carefully place them in the cooking pot to avoid the splashing of water. After doing this, allow the chicken to cook before adding any extra vegtables. Once the chicken has browned further and the aroma fills\nthe room, remove the pot of broth from the heat and pour into a dining bowl. Allow to cook slightly before eating.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ <><><><><><><><><><><>\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~Pork Soup~~~~\n\nIngredients: \nCooked Pork\n\nStart off by lighting your fire and heating your cauldron, before placing the cooking pot over the boiling water. This creates a Bain Marie.\nAfter doing this, fill your cooking pot halfway with water. Next, slice up the pork, removing the fat. Place the slices into the cooking pot with salt and rosemary or sage. Stir the soup occasionally. After leaving it to cook for about half an elven hour,\nremove the bowl from the heat. Pour the soup into a serving bowl, though allow it to cool as the water would be boiling.\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Vegtable Soup~~\n\nIngredients:\nTwo baked potatoes. \nFour carrots.\n\nCreate the Bain Marie once more and add your cooking pot. Fill the cooking pot with warm water to about\na quarter of the way. While the water is warming, slice your potatoes into chunks, and add them to the water. Next, cut your carrots into thin round disks. Add these to the water. If you wish, salt and rosemary can be added to give the soup some seasoning\nand flavour. Soon after, remove the cooking pot from the heat. Pour the contents into a serving bowl. \n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic supplies", "Jessie Boatwright", "Jessie Boatwrights medical supply list:\n\n1. One note book.\n2. A bottle of water.\n3. A bottle of Blissfoil.\n4. A bottle of disinfectant.\n5. Three vials of ink.\n6. Two quils.\n7. Surgical sponge\n8. Surgical needle.\n9. Cauterising set.", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle For CT", "Eenhoornheid", "Seth Calith's tell of the battle for the Cloud Temple of Anthos. The 29th of The Amber Cold in year 1452\nIt's early in the morning, the humans, dwarves, orcs and maybe even some elves are shouting about praising a squid, a spy bat, praising the sun, creator and many more things. Shouts of hatred towards one another is filling this small fort.\nThe forces are seemingly ready as the sun goes down once more. Wether or not this attack shall happen at night, I do not know. Many things is still shouted, speaks of herasy is heard as someone wish to dine in the Nethers while others wants in the Seven\nHavens, the must disturbing of all the shouts must be the 'Blood for coin' which is what House Flay shouted in times of old. A Disbute has started of what war-cry is the one they wish for. Instead of debating, they simply shout, someone even attempted to\nmix shouts to make this even worse. I hope this war shall soon start and close the mouth of theirs.\n\nThe war has started, the first footmen of the scourge has been sighted. They have sent few troops in advance to keep them at bay while the rest\nof the army uses crossbows and bows alike to end them. The sound of monsters is heard, most likely giving the chill to many men. A charge has started, explosions are seen on their charge, damaging the army. I will now move a bit forward to see what will\nhappen now. The battle is bloody in the ruins of an old fort. I avoided a magical spell by few inches from the 'friendly' side. This is indeed a chaos filled with blood and the screams of death. I know not whom will win yet.\nShous of retreat is heard while others seek to run head first into the battle, orders seemingly have little meaning now. \n\nThe soldiers are slowly pushing forward, many spells of death is fired to the only bridge allowing them to pass and\nattacking the enemy themself.\n\nSomeone is claiming the battle is on the losing end while others wish to scale the mountains and lastly, others give orders to kill the enemy mages on the mountains.\nI still wonder how this will end, I am without answer as this night surely will be long.\n\nA knight of Oren shouts of the retreat of the scourge, suddenly an ambush was revealed from the right flank. The fate is yet to be seen.\nIn the distance, I can see them hacking at the gate, seemlingly they managed to break it, allowing for a further attack. \n\nThe gate was a trap, attackers came from behind, some died while I managed to escape.\nThe Scourge has positioned guards at the gate, I can't enter to see the actual battle.\n\nThe ambushers was tricked into running into the allied fort, bringing them into a quick death.\n\nThe allied are\nadvancing now once more, I will follow.\n\nThe Scourge has placed mages and archers on top of a giant construct of some sort. Raining down fire on the allies, almost hitting me once more.\nSeemingly, the allies wants to enter the library, for what reason I do not know. Maybe the scourge is hiding there.\n\nI start to think that these arrows I have avoided is actualy from the allies, attempting to hit the\nmages.\nThey found a way to enter the library, now they need only to enter the floating tainted earth, chained to the earth of the Cloud Temple of Anthos.\n\nThe Library is swarmed by the monsters of the scourge and the allies of Anthos.\nLava also flows in the library, making this far too warm for comfort combined with the stench of dead.\n\nSeemingly a portal of some sort is placed on the second floor, it's frame made of ice and white shining light of some sort.\nSomeone now wants to dine in 'hell', I really wonder where they all get these names.\n\nWords are shouted of breaking the portal to the floating earth. Wether or not it will work, I do not know.\nA new plan is forged, everyone enters the portal at the same time to meet the powers of the magic at the same time. I must say one of the best plans to be heard, running head first into the fire.\nThe light of the day returns as the battle is still here. One of the red crystals from the tainted earth flew towards a warmechine on the mountain, what the result is, I do not know.\n\nI found the remains of a Billy Bob's award medal.\nLooking like a flower, on it, claiming this Billy Bob killed a dragon, most likely, it was a drake.\n\nAs I enter the library once more, the library is destroyed, sounds of cheer is heard yet the battle is now over.\nThey still need to destroy the chains to the tainted earth so it may float or crash, I do not know what will happen but hopefully one of the two options.\nWhile under attacks of the enemy, the allies managed to break the chains by hand.\n\nThe battle is almost over, they are going to finish off the rest of the Harbingers of the Setherins. Seemingly they are winning this war.\nIt's done, the war is won, Anthos won the war against the Scourge, hopefully. I shall now leave the lands which stinks of death, rot and fire.", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle Plans", "Ebonsquire", "Battle Plans (Classified)\n\n((Originally written by colwin1))\nThis book is only to be seen by the most trustworthy and highest ranked members of Guardian. If they, as a group, choose to let another party see the contents of these plans, then so be it. If one is to die with these plans, it is crucial that they are\nrecovered, no one else must lay eyes on them. Anyone who shares the content without an official vote shall be punished. As anyone could be a spy for the Undead.\nStep One - Preparation\n\nIt is important to keep in mind that the Undead are very powerful indeed. So do not take anything of much value with you. Some food, and stone swords would be best. This is because stone swords are\ninexpensive, yet more efficient than wood. Leather armor is also a good idea, if you have any. Protection is always valuable. Some ladders should be brought (See step 3, the attack) as well. And for others, an axe, and a pickaxe. This will also be\nexplained later. \n\nStep Two - The Road to Battle\n\nWe should start by travelling up the road to Oren, visiting other cities along the way. This is so we can gather other adventureres to aid us in our battle.\nOur last stop will be in Oren. We should have an Oren guard aid us, so that we may legally open the gate to the Snowy Fields if no one else will. Along with the benefit of gate access, the presence of a professional guard will raise morale and convince\nfar more people to aid us in our journey. Then, after we have entered the Snowy Fields, we should go to our base in the fields to make sure that everyone is clear on what they are to do,\nStep Three - Commencing the Battle\n\nOnce everyone knows what to do, a small party (3-5) should take ladders to lay on the enemy walls, while the rest of us travel by tunnel into the keep. Depending on how heavily guarded the tunnel is, we may need to dig\nand mine our own. This is why we need shovels and pickaxes. We need axes in case we need to gather wood to repair our base. We should bring wood with us anyways if that is the case. The Undead should be distract enough by our small ladder party that we\ncan easily slip in from behind, and devastate their ranks. Once the enemy notices that we are within their keep, we must get reinforcements to support the warriors that originally stormed the front. They will at this point, be too confused to react\nlogically to our attack, and thus retreat, or die trying to figure out what's going on. This is referring to the Undead, keep in mind. \n\nStep Four - The Upkeep\n\nOnce the keep is ours, we should send two messengers (for safety) to Oren to tell others of the news and bring more people to support the keep, and make sure it is not retaken by the enemy.\nAnyone that comes to help should bring their own armor and weapons, as well as food, etc., for everyone else. Obviously there are going to be injured men who need medical attention. For that purpose, we need beds for them to sleep in, and food for them\nto eat. Once this whole ordeal is done, if it goes according to plan, the Undead keep will be ours, and the Snowy Fields will once more be safe from the terror of the Undead. \n\nThese plans are to be seen by officers of Guardian, and can be changed at any\ntime. However, nothing MUST be changed unless a very fatal flaw is detected.\n\nWritten by Ardougnious ((colwin1))\n\nLookover 1: We will not bring random people off the streets, instead, we will gather forces from S.A.", ""),
        StaticBook("Beatae Memoriae", "Shinku", "Lost And Found:\nShade & Shinku\n\n~For My Dearest Shade\nMy shade, oh beautiful shade\nWhat mistake could be made?\nMy beautiful Ker who made the wonderful shade.\n\nEyes crisp gold.\nA treasure trove.\nThe only Ker, The only one whom her secrets were told.\nA veil of mystery whom no one could read into his eyes.\nWhere do those of evilness go in concern of lies?\nNone knows but the eyes of My shades eyes.\n\nShade the Ker with fur as black as night.\nWith posture as such as a knight,\nHis will, duty, and pleasure to protect the elven child with hair of a shadows night.\n\nThe Ker and Child part with due despair.\nWith hopes to repair the broken bridge on faithful promises.\nThe promises of once again to come\ntogether once again.\nJust maybe fate will be kind to forever partners.\n\nLooks matter naught.\nWhat matters is what minds taught.\nWhat memories wrought.\nWhat truth and companionship bought.\n\nMaybe. Just maybe. We can meet again-\n-My Dearest Shade\n\n~With love your Crimsion Rose", ""),
        StaticBook("Becoming Lunch", "Yden", "The crazy man who tried to feed us to Orc!\n\nOur story begins at Haeln'or, we prepared for a day out of the city, get to know the lands we now call home. So me and Clover packed our bags with food and supplies for the journey\nvarious meats and cheeses, bread and wine and set out to Fi'Ceru, the town was quite, the majority of the population seemed to be occupying the inn so we went into invistigate, we spoke with a tall man with brown hair and a battle-worn face\nhe spoke to us in a harsh and abrupt tone. He seemed to recognise Clover but when he turned to me he said in a rather rude tone \"And who is this then?\" I did not reply to his question but instead turned around and left the inn, Clover closely behind.\nThis part of the world seemed fairly hostile, perhaps it was because we were high elves or perhaps this man was just not very nice but we left the town only an hour after we entered and made our way to the docks, we discussed where we would visit next.\nnone of us really knew where we wanted to visit so we just went to the nearest cart we could find and traveled. We arrived at our destination in where ever we found ourselves. From here we picked a direction and walked, hand in hand following the path\nas if it were law, we spotted lots of people and plenty of structures along the way, various camps and farms, market stalls and homes. We arrived at the great cast iron gates of a city and called out and waited for a reply but none came, we waited for\nanother minute before following the path south back the way we came, picking another direction at a crossroad we did the same, following the path and taking in the sights. After a few minutes of walking we came to a mighty castle. In this castle were\nhighlanders, lots of them. At first they seemed friendly enough, they offered us some help so we hesitantly accepted and followed like sheep. He took us inside his home and he seemed fairly friendly until he unsheathed his blade and threatened us.\nAt first the man said he was going to make us his slaves but I think he changed his mind because before we knew it Clover was in my arms weeping as we were sentenced to death, the man tied us up and prepared to open the gates and turn us into lunch.\nWe kissed each other goodbye and closed our eyes. \"Stoooop!\" shouted a man with blond hair, the man who placed us there was in chains and we were being untied, a moment later and we would have been their next meal. He apologized on behalf of the\ncrazy man and let us on our way, we were just happy to be alive. \nThat was the time we almost become lunch.\n\nThe End\nBy Yden and Clover", ""),
        StaticBook("BEelEe", "Farmer Billy Bob", "*crudely written in mud on a dirtied crumpled page*\n\n\nbEElEe\n\n\n            bUB\n\n    wuS\n\n\n                   hEAR", ""),
        StaticBook("bEeLee bUB", "Farmer Billy Bob", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Beginning of End", "Leyu", "The Beginning of The End by Relgard\n22/First Seed/1328\nMy name is Relgard. I am a Deputy of the White Ravens. I am being hunted by the Wardens. They are hunting me because I am fighting their evil reign, with the help of others. This is the story, from the beginning, to now;\nThe Beginning of the End. I cannot write all things, and I cannot write perfectly as I sit here, waiting. Some ravens are talking to our allies, some keeping lookout. Our agent within the wardens is spying. :: It all started months ago, me and my loyal\nfriend Duncan were searching for an undead worshipper. We say commotion in Laurelin, and watched. There had been an arrest for two people, a boy named Sparrow, and a man named Caden. We tried following them, for Sparrow had been arrested\nfor worshipping the dead. We were outside the base of these people, the Wardens, when they took the first offense. They arrested Duncan. :: I tried to stop them, but couldn't. I had to run. I returned to the Raven base and alerted my allies. Duncan was\nlater released. Weeks later I met a couple called \"The Burkesters\". They were nice people. Good friends. They would soon play a vital role in all things. :: I was returning from a battle in Kramoroe, where I had fought orcs trying to toll\npeople when I saw commotion at the Burkesters's house. I investigated. Two sons wer ebeing born. :: Nothing big happened for a while, until one day, Duncan told me that Leka, Burk's wife, was arres ted. The wardens though she was a minion of\nIblees. She was not. Duncan and I set out to help our friend. While we were traveling, we met Caden again. He was, by then, leader of the Rebels against the Warde ns. We also came across Zoe, an Ex-Raven friend of mine. We continued and finally\nentered the keep. ::&lt;How to Enter&gt; Facing North Gate from North: Follow outer wall Counter-Clockwise Until you reach a desert. You can jump here. Follow inner wall same Direction Soon you will find trees. Some can be jumped on to get\nover the inner wall. End Instructions. :: We got in, but were caught. I was later returned to the wardens. mercy and gien to Seventh of the Ravens. Leka later died, and most of the world was against the Wardens. They tried, and failed, to attack Oren,\ndue to my warning them in time. I later heard some of the Druids speaking of the Wardens in a negative Tone I talked, and gained an alliance for the rebelion. I also heard unsettling news. Caden was captured, and the wardens were no longer\nletting prisoners leave. Then I recieved bird from the agent. The wardens were coming for me and a druid. I escaped to the ravens, the druid was captured. :: While hiding with the Ravens I began this book. Now we've started attacking. We did a\njailbreak and got the druid out. Now we are working to break the warden's alliances so we have all the men. Things are looking up, and the agent is still loyal. Relgard, 22/FirstSeed/1328\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bell's Diary", "liam_barnett", "Bell's Super Duper\n      Private Diary\n-------------------\n\nThis will be my log of important events, starting with me being the victim of guard brutality.\n10th of Sun's Smile, 1563:\n\nThis is the new chapter in my life; Skyfall has fallen to the hands of Vandoria, I'm out of my old teaching job, and I now run a junkyard.\nUpon walking into the tavern, I request that I buy a whole load of drinks. Six rum, three vodka, and a glass of water. The girl behind the counter, seeming to be in her twenties,  if even that, refused. Her heavy accent\nmade it quite difficult to understand her request, but she told me to buy only one drink. As I continued to demand that I be served multiple drinks, she told me to leave the tavern. So, as any alchohol deprived\nman would do, I came back with a knife. I asked one more time to be served, and when she refused, I pulled my knife out, demanding the drinks I had asked for. I instantly met the wrath of some man, abnormally tall, wearing heavy\nmetallic armour. He turned me into the guards, and recounted what had just happened. As I sat at a table in the barracks, almost five guards stood by. When they weren't looking, I easily hopped over the wall.\nI slept in the woods for just one night, then returned the next day, only to be grabbed by the same guards again. They proceeded to hang me upside down from a tower, beat me, and the like. But then I was taken into the basement.\nThat's where I was strapped to a chair, and one guard with mis-matched eyes retrived his own knife, asking if I wanted my left or right eye removed first. Struggling, I remained strapped down as the\nman continued to drill my left eye with the knife, my sockets full of blood. Afterwars, he cut me in various places, legs to chin. But it was nothing compared to the loss of my left eye. I'm now blinded and scarred,\nunable to see through that eye. \n\nAbuse by the Felsen guard at it's finest.\n12th of Malin's Welcome, 1566:\n\nUpdate since my last entry, which was quite some time ago; My daughter, Daisy, has been born, and I'm still living in at the same junkyard. Business is fine, I'm able to\nsupport us both. I'm just thankful that we live outside the walls, I'd hate to be within the same city as all those criminals or corrupted soldiers.\n\nToday is my birthday, and I just went out for a drink, then\nsat down with Daisy at home. It's raining outside.\n\nIt was a nice birthday, to say the least.\n2nd of Sun's Smile, 1566:\n\nIronically, I've joined the guard force. The junkyard has declined in sales, and we're losing more money than we're receiving. I've decided that I'll need to take up a second\njob, just to take care of Daisy and myself. I was swiftly accepted into the force, and shown how to operate the gate, given a copy of the rules, all that good stuff.\nI'm considering selling the house and the junkyard, and moving into a cheaper apartment in the city. It may be best for Daisy to live within the walls, as Orcs and the like have started showing up more frequently.\nAnd Kha. Kha are disgusting.\n11th of Snow's Maiden, 1567:\n\nOn the watch today, Mattington brought in two orcs, assisted by some of the Goldies. They stored a larger one upstairs, and the Goblin in a cell, monitored by myself.\nI was instructed to search all of his belongings, and confiscate any arms or armour it had on it's person. There were blades and the sort, which I took away for safety precautions. Mattington then\ndemanded a fine of one hundred mina from the Goblin, for whatever crime he had commited, and the Goblin declared that it had no money. And so, I was told to confiscate all of his items, to make up for the fine.\nThis included a journal, some spare ink, and some type of buckler of sorts. I placed all of his belongings on a desk, as the rest of the guards were handling the other orc. I was hissed at by the Goblin from behind the bars,\nas he declared that a, \"Swampguth\" had given the buckler to him. After flipping through his own journal, I found nothing of interest, so I allowed him to keep that. But, long story short, the other guards ended up killing\nhis friend by accident, in some type of brawl. The Goblin became upset, attacked me and Mattington, but was quickly aprehended. They threw him into the moat, leaving him to die.\nIn my eyes, this was, of course, appropriate punishment. However, it was not the appropriate solution. If he were to wake up, he would only cause trouble again. I hauled his resting body\nback to the Uzg, leaving him in the sand outside their city, hoping that somebody would find him. What I did was not out of respect, or care for this criminal, but out of fear. I wanted him out of Oren.\nSo this was, by far, a noble act, as I was caring for the empire, and not the individual-- But does the Lord applaud my actions? Have I satisfied him?\n11th of Malin's Welcome, 1567:\n\nThis is the first major attack, directed at Felsen as a whole, and not just an individual. These fire-related incidents are n-\n[!] Suddenly, the rest of the page is torn to a shred, and the other twenty or so pages have been removed as well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bell's Response", "Ebonsquire", "Arch Mage Bell's Response to the reports of Cataris' trial\n\n((Originally written by TehLulu))\nCataris was put on trial for breaking our laws and my direct orders. He did NOT uphold the 'balance' by attacking the undead. He put all of the MAge's Guild at risk by doing so. Everyone who participated in the attack, which he claimed to me personally he\ndid not \"lead,\" (though I have read differently in the Aegis Times newspaper) was nearly killed by the Prophet, including the Wizard. He has gained us an enemy. The undead want revenge on the Guild now. They will come after me first, as one of the\nArch Mages. I will likely be tortured more, as they have been doing recently, whenever I dare to venture up north to guard it. I may even be killed. Magic has not yet returned to us; the Veil which exists between this world and the one which magic seeps\nthrough from is not yet weak enough. The Veil is the reason why undead magic is so strong and Ascended magic seemingly less potent. I will write more on the subject, but to put it bluntly, the undead are closest to Iblees. He is imprisioned on the other\nside of the Veil, where the powers of magic wait. He has given his servants, the undead, a more direct connection to the other side of the Veil than Ascended or the rest of the world. That is why the Mage's Guild does not yet have magic yet . . . but we\ncan feel it coming.\n\nCataris, in attacking the undead base, broke our rules and my direct orders as Arch Mage. He betrayed my trust in doing so, but he was given simply a warning and sent on his way. But other evidence has appeared which\nshows our problems inside the Guild are not yet done. We will be working quietly to fix these. And we will be attempting not to make the undead irritated at us by attacking them for a very good reason... Should the guild fall before magic returns, we will\nnot be as well equipped. Magic will not be as useful to all of us as a whole, and our tomes upon tomes of knowledge will be destroyed, or used against us. That is why we put Cataris on trial for his actions. I sinecerely hope you understand and do not\ngive in to all the propaganda circulating at the moment. The Guild stands for the long-term defense of Aegis. If we fall even before magic returns, we will be of no use. But we will continue defending and working on collecting knowledge to better\nprepare Aegis for the return of magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Beo", "Edward York", "Beo is silly, silly Billy Beo.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bestiary V1", "Adeon of Rhoswen", "The Marked Man's Bestiary\n\nContents:\n1. Beasts of Nature\n2. Natural Monstrosities\n3. Sentient Supernaturals\n3. Supernatural Monstrosities\n4. Constructs\n-Beasts of Nature-\n\nThese creatures are the beasts commonly seen throughout the world and pose no real threat to the innocent mundane.\nCanines: Either intelligent pack hunters or less witty companion animals, the canine often possesses sharp teeth and fur- unlike their Ursidae cousins, they are not often large and do not possess significantly sharp claws. Canines are known to be tamable.\nRats: These creatures are the messengers of coming pestilence and death, they've the standard qualities expected of small rodents. Extended exposure to these creatures often leads to sickness, earning them the nickname \"Plague bearers\".\nBats: These creatures are physically quite similar to the common rat despite the fact that they have wings and do not possess a tail.\nThey're generally nocturnal and have an enhanced sense of hearing which makes up for their poor vision.\nBirds: Variations of these are seen far and wide. From the common pigeon to the barn owl. The creatures have near countless variations and are often used to carry messages over long distances. They are mostly harmless.\nSand Tortoise: These creatures are of staggering size. We've precious little information on the beasts and taking one down would require no less than a siege party. The creature grows in size rivaling a small keep. They are extremely rare.\nSand Lizard: A common sight within the Orcish deserts. These creatures are surprisingly fast and can topple a target with very little effort. Their hide is nothing worthy of note. Their bones are of decent density and genuinely sturdy.\n-Natural Monstrosities-\n\nThese are the creatures commonly found within nature but are considered perverse and diluted in purpose. They're to be hunted and their existence extinguished.\nThe Harpy: These monsters have the ability to fly and resemble ugly women- their skin is extremely oily and susceptible to fire. They're bones are quite brittle and will crack under pressure. Their feathers are fine for use in arrows and their pelts make-\n-for good middle class clothing. They've a cruel sense of humor. They are known to scoop up targets and drop them from lethal heights. If a Harpy nest is discovered it is suggested that it be burned immediately.\nKrummavisur: Resembling a Raven, though staggering in size. These beasts have awe-inspiring wing spans and considerable strength.\nThey scoop up their prey and toss them immeasurable distances. The beast is not to be fought alone. They can kick up dust-\n-with the density to block sight for yards. When effort is applied they can shove a man in full plate to his knees with the power of the air from their wings alone. It is suggested that the feet are struck, as they are quite thin and easy to amputate.\nCockatrice: An odd looking creature. Standing at the height of a small building with the width to match.\nThey are quite intimidating to fight up close and are able to fly, rendering close combat to be the inevitable result of an encounter.\nThe Cockatrice has the ability to exhale a thick gray smog that turns whoever comes in contact with it to stone. Being submerged in water will negate this effect.\nTheir skin is unholy in strength, steel will hardly damage it, an aurum blade is required.\nThe Beast's bones are strong as stone and they've the strength to topple a building with ease.\nLeaf Apes: Fundamentally illusive creatures that have flesh as hard as rock and bones like fresh timber. They possess decent strength for their size but struggle to penetrate leather. They tend to rush a target and make an effort to climb atop its face.\nOnce atop the victim's face, the Leaf Ape will tear at the flesh. Bladed steel weapons are practically useless against these creatures and will often break upon contact with their skin- blunt weapons are suggested as well as aurum swords.\nCave Leeches: A beast that drops down on it's targets and spews acid onto them, it has the strength to render armor useless. They only attack in complete darkness. \n\nNo one has survived an encounter thus far.\nDrakes: Creatures with bat-like wings, the ability to breathe flame, scaly hides, complete with muscular legs and tail-- these truly majestic beasts have captured the awe of men for centuries. Despite this, magical perversion has lead to the Drake species\nundergoing various mutations and become near extinct. It is expected that combat with a Drake be avoided and alternative methods to killing be used to neutralise the threat such a beast poses. The Drake's main weaknesses are its wings, mouth and eyes,\n-however this beast will continue fighting until the last drop of blood runs from it's wound. Decapitation and siege weaponry is suggested.\nEnlarged Arachnid:\n\nThe average spider, though colossal in size and extremely venomous- they are susceptible to fire and relatively easy to defeat compared to other beasts in this compendium.\n-Sentient Naturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with if possible and relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane population.\nTroll: Usually found lurking under bridges, in caves or forests. These beasts can be at times helpful and friendly-- at other times they are forces to be reckoned with. Trolls are generally quite intelligent and are capable of speech, complex emotion and-\n-co-operation. The best method of slaying a Troll is to use aurum and to disable it's method of movement, trolls are known to carry enormous amounts of weight in the form of fat around their waist and are unable to get up if any of their legs are damaged.\n-Sentient Supernaturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with and if possible relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane.\nSpecters: Spirits without bodies, these beings can be benevolent, neutral or malevolent, just like a living person. They can only be harmed by aurum as normal metals will pass straight through them.\nSpecters have the ability to wield enchanted weaponry\n-\n-and don enchanted armor, some have the ability to fly and cast spells, those that have this ability use it to deadly effect. It is suggested that aurum weaponry be used combined with a high-guard stance.\nSpecters are vulnerable to salt and it is-\n-suggested that the perimeter in which the spirit is manifesting be surrounded by lines of pure sea salt.\n-Constructs-\n\nThese are the result of spells or golemmancy, they are able to fit into the supernatural sentient category as well as the monstrous supernatural category depending on what they are- constructs usually have a master and a purpose to follow.\nHunters: \n\nSharing many traits with a specter, the Hunter has the ability to fly- it wears large, heavy armor but is not impeded in any way by this fact. The Hunters are apparently a sort of Golem gone rogue, they once served a holy order and sought to-\n-slay dangerous Magi. Now they slay any who wield magic, including Marked Men. Hunters explode when defeated and it is advised that those who have defeated it clear the area before it does so, as shrapnel is often projected.\nAurum seems to weaken the-\n-creature considerably, though it is probably wise to use steel in order to damage the armor before an aurum weapon is presented.\nHalf swording is suggested due to the armored nature of this foe.\nGolems: The result of powerful runes and magic, Golems can take many forms- from colossal lumbering humanoid to slithering metal snake, all Golems have an 'Impera' who dictates their every action-- Golems will attempt to protect these individuals at all-\n-costs. These constructs are often the result of a soul being bound to the magegold core, destroying this would most likely neutralise the threat. \nWays to destroy the Golem depend on a number of things including environment and the material the Golem is-\n-made of. Golems made of stronger materials may need to be cast from great heights, thrown into watery depths or toppled into a substance hot enough to melt metal.\n-Supernatural Monstrosities-\n\nThese creatures defy all reason. They serve no purpose in this world and are to be slain.\nNecrophages: These creatures come in two variations; Fleshed and Skeletal.\n\nFleshed typically maintain a slumped posture, they've considerable strength and an immunity to pain.\n\nAurum weaponry is recommended for these types of creatures.\nAlone, their presence is a joke, but when amassed it's often best to simply route.\nThe method of reanimation is unknown, however it is to be noted that they appear more frequently around areas of frequent fighting or wickedness.\nFire is a weakness.\nLich: The ultimate product of an individual's greed for power or knowledge. Liches are beings that have made a transformation into entities powered purely on arcane energies and a deep seated hatred for those that get in the way of more power.\nTypes of Liches vary broadly and improvisation is to be expected. One recurring trait seems to be the presence of a crystal known as the phylactery- it is where the Lich's soul is rumoured to be kept, destroying this crystal will kill the creature.\nBloodsuckers/Sangbriseur:\nThese creatures take the form of an obscene lump of slimey acid. Depending on their environment, the creature can absorb it's surroundings and become deadlier-- there are such things as Bloodsuckers who have absorbed fire,\nbecoming thrice as dangerous as their acidic counterparts. To dispose of the creature, it is suggested that it be cut into smaller pieces and set alight-- be sure that every chunk is burnt or else it will regenerate over time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bio: Mark I", "Unknown", "Name: Mirtok DeNurem\nAge: Unknown\nGender: Male\nRace: Human, Northern\nStatus: Unknown\n\nDescription\nHeight: 6'7\"\nWeight: 285lb\nBody Type: Mesomorph\nEyes: Green\nHair: White\nSkin: Fair\nSignificant Markings:\nNone known to the public.\nPersonality: Realist, more acceptive towards reason and logic in his decision making process.\nInventory: Warhammer augmented with the weapons of past Hocmeisters.\nTitle(s): Hochmeister, Emperoro's Chapmion, King of Hanseti\nWeaponry: Warhammer\n\nFamily\nFather: Unknown, presumed dead.\nMother: Unknown, presumed dead.\nDaughter: Winter DeNurem, presumed dead.\nMirtok DeNurem is thought to be born during Aegis. DeNurem's childhood was relativity normal but cut short when the undead destroyed everything he had known. Nothing else is known of his youthful years.\n\nAt some point during his life DeNurem\nfound himself in a Order of men, founded by Gaius Marius. Since that day Mirtok has been in that Order forged so long ago, rising the ranks each decade. He fought glorious and heroic wars but also bloody and gruesome ones. His leader Gaius remained a\nshining beacon of righteousness and hope that kept Mirtok on the right path of honor and chivalry. The Teutonic Order eventually became a harden force capable of mass devastation among the evil community. But as their power grew so did the man's ego and\ndesire for more. Mirtok tried to resist such temptations that would lead him away from ultimate dedication and loyalty, but every so often he took himself, allowing the seed wrong to root itself in his heart.\n\nTowards the death of his leader and the rise\nof his best friend Sam, the Order and even the nation they forged fell on hard times. The opposing human nation of Renatus lauched fierce and relentless attacks on the struggling nation of Hanseti, weakening the moral of Mirtok and his men. The cruelty\nthe renatus leaders showed to Mirtok gave water to the seed of evil that wished to grow inside him. He no longer saw others as people but mere numbers, he became harsh even to his own brothers in arms and even allowed the barbaric killings of others on\nthe field of battle. He nearly lost sight of himself as the temptation took over, but he banished himself to a snowy moutain and committed himself years of mining and gathering. After close to 12 years had past he returned to his Order bearing a massive\nsupply of material that gave his men a edge during combat.\n\nMirtok had grown passive and more prone towards talk than fighting to solve conflicts. HOwever his fellow soldiers became barbaric and blood thirsty, often calling Mirtok \"soft\" for his alternate\nmethod of finding a solution. Mirtok couldn't help but feel that Sam had failed him and his people, driving the desire to take the leader for himself so that he may steer the nation on the path towards its former glory. But Sam was assassinated before he\ncould fully insight a civil war, making him the new Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order and king of Hanseti.\n\nNow being the ruler of Hanseti he begins to act accordingly. He is a survivor of the old ways of the Order used to follow and a link to Gaius, as\nhe stood by him since day one. However it's said that Mirtok has suffered from an accident that transformed him physically and perhaps mentally. Usually talked about among his Sariants. For a long period of time, Mirtok kept his armor on, not once\nremoving it. \n\nMirtok became less compassionate for his fellow beings, only caring for his own men and their benefits. He became more daring and less cautious but maintained his speaking prowess. MIrtok died but a new Hochmeister rose in his tattered\nremains, one that shows no fear, no remorse, and no mercy.\n\nHe continued on that path for many years following the event, partaking in many wars and even being involved in a World War against the majority of Asulon. He tried his best to keep his\nnation intact but through countless lighting skirmishes conducted by the growing Renatian Empire, Mirtok laid down his kingship to the lands of Hanseti and contributed to the formation of the Oren Empire. Under Godfrey his power had been strengthened and\nhis purpose restored. He quickly became an altranationalist to Godfrey and a zealot progressor of his goals. He has since regain his Kingship and his Order has seen a drastic increase in stability and strength.\n\nMuch later into the rise of the Holy Oren\nEmpire, Mirtok gained strong political and militaristic footholds within the Empire. Obtaining titles such as King, Hochmeister, Grand Marshall, and the Emperor's Champion; As well as affirming the role of the Teutonic Order as a leading military power\nboth in and out of the Empires region of influence. He had an abundence of resourses at his disposal, tools of war and progression. It was in these tools that Mirtok along with his Sariants, were able to survive after the Cloud Calamity that struck\nHanseti with a deadly poisonous gas. The Cloud persisted for serveral years after the intial invasion, brought on by his own hands at the various dig sites along hte Eastern Peaks of Hanseti. He had found what he had been searching for but in return, he\nlost his very Motherland and the source of his Goddess' radiance. Using what had been stockpiled from the Emperor's supply lines. Mirtok had a variety of technologies created to help his soldiers move about the lost lands of Hanseti, eventually the Cloud\nbecame little of an issue to the Sariants and they were able to once more reach the Emperor during a time of heavy international stress, Mirtok had to complete the project the Emperor tasked him with, putting an end to the opposition and confirming the\nHoren name forever rules from the throne. With that, Mirtok launched a large scale research program that was hosted out of the cold halls of Fickloch. There he had people captured and experimented on, and with their use over he had their bodies\nrepurposed to feed his pipe dream of a doomsday device.\n\nThough, the events of Oren subsided and the only thing that began to threaten the Empire were the occasional peasant uprising. Mirtok faded from the limelight of Asulon's happenings, tended to his\nown inter Order rebellion with half his forces splitting off and betraying the brothers who were left under Mirtok's command. He quickly and personally visited each ofthe traitors and killed them without mercy. At the side of his brother, Lion, the\nrebels fell and the Order remained the surviving faction.\nThough security has a price. The Order began to pitter out, with memebers losing interest and recruitment at an all time low. The lack of war, battle and conflict took it's toll on the Order but\nMirtok tried to rise above it. He used the down time to rip and claw his way up, giving life to his Order and strength to his men. After a short lived but large rebellion attempt brought on by the mages and men of the west sectors of Oren, Mirtok's\nrecruitment numbers soared and the Order once more had itself a purpose to fulfill. All that has happened in his life has only furthered the strong ruthless nature that Mirtok has come to adopt, and in a world as unstable as Asulon, the death toll will\ncontinue to rise as the Order marches on with Mirtok at the helm.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bird Directions", "Seth Calith", "Two black hawks, one of my own breed of hawks, the other one semi-wild.\n\nFeed them with bits of meat, mice or fish.\n\nThe female is a calm one, responding to the name of Iheiuh; Wind.\n\nThe male one needs still some training, -\nonly reacting some of the time, still in training. Responding on the name Barbu. If he does try to bite any of you, hit him on top of the head, Iheiuh will not react and actualy be a boon for Barbu.\n\nThis is my gift, messanger hawks, partial of my own -\nbreed and one from the outside, to symbolize your marriage.\n\nShould you wish to continue the symbole, you should let your child have Iheiuh and Barbu's grand child, as age-wise it would fit better.\nI do hope for your best.\n\n-Seth Calith.", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Rose", "Telperian Faroar", ">---------------------<\nAtrim:Is a blonde man with green eyes. “Hey Louise, do you like like me?” He like likes me who tried to help me out with my mind. [!] A sketch of Atrim is here with a heart next to it. [!]\n>---------------------<\n\nCareful: William.\n>---------------------<\nTuvya: Is the Emperor of the lands of Orenia, can help me settle. Met him near the Cloud Temple.\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nJakir: Blue eyes, handlebar moustache, light brunette, man. Helped with the fight in the Standing Inn. [!] A sketch of Jakirs’ face is here. [!] Unloyal to a lover?\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nArtemis Carlyle: A man with darker brunette hair and dark blue eyes. Met him at the Standing Inn. Wants to help me find my admirer.\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nDaren Bonehill: Count of Nerezza. Is my boss. I work at his castle. From the start of the Stone Road, head towards Northern Wilderness. Then, take a left, then a right. [!] A sketch of Daren is here. [!]\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nTeleia Index: Supplied me 2 notebooks as I had lost mine. [!] A sketch of Teleia is here. [!]\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nKatari Stirling: Conversed with me in the Standing Inn. [!] A sketch of Katari is here. [!]\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nGilraen: [!] An image is here of her. [!] She helped me with monsters and hunger one night.\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nThor Faolain: Owner of Nerezza. Is also my boss. I work the farm for him. [!] Thors’ face is sketched here. [!]\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nJack: I gifted him 3 pancakes and he placed a kiss on the back of my hand. I think he fancies me. [!] A quick sketch of his face is here. [!]\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nCptn Harrison Shard: Is a privateer Captain that has a fancying of me. [!] A sketch of his head & Shoulders. [!]\n>---------------------<\n>---------------------<\nRagnar Faolain: 3rd leader of the Faolain along with Daren and Thor.\n>---------------------<\nX--------------------X\nI saw a dwarf get murdered. An accused thief took an axe to his head. I am still bad with blood. Rest In Peace. I then played DnD with Ulfrik Faolain. It was fun. \nX--------------------X\nIf he fixes my mind, I must play DnD with him\nX--------------------X\nToday, I received a fancy, brass-buttoned green dress, from “A secret admirer.” I think Ulfrik sent it but he was being cryptic about the answer.\nX--------------------X", ""),
        StaticBook("BlacksmithGuide", "willsiren", "A Blacksmithing General Handbook By Viscar Van'Eer Of Astfield.\nDISCLAIMER: I may be only proficient in the art of blacksmithing, however, my knowledge is unrivaled througout Oren.\n-------------------[!] There would be a drawing of two men dueling.\nHeavy armor must be designed to take a lot of punishment. It will receive direct blows from all sorts of weapons while protecting the wearer.wearer. Leather strips are used to make the straps and bindings in all armor.\nFerrum and steel are easy to work.\nFerrum armor requires a large number of Ferrum ingots. A smith might need a couple of dozen to complete a full set of Ferrum armor. Steel armor primarily uses steel ingots, but some Ferrum is used as well.\nOrcish armors require lots of bone and leathers m\nelded with a bit of Ferrum. Heat should be used sparingly, lest it become brittle. The Orcs are masters of this technique, but it can be learned by any smith with patience and skill.\nSteel plate mail is made by adding steel With Coal and Minerals.\nThe alloy is stronger than either metal by itself. Coal minerals can be a finicky material requiring the heat from the forge to be steady and not vary much. Bluesteel can only be worked when heated.It will develop small cracks that eventually shatter the\nmaterial if hammered cold. Unlike most other armors, Bluesteel will not alloy with iron. It must be used pure.\nI can only tell you tales of how to make Undead armor. I have never seen it myself, nor do I know anyone that has. The stories say that it shoul\nd always be worked on at night... ideally under a new or full moon, and never during an eclipse. A red harvest moon is best.Flesh and Bone is the principal materials, but at the right moment a heart of a pure person or animal must be thrown into the fire.\nI hope my blacksmithing demonstrations can help you too better your knowledge. \n-Viscar Van'Eer\n\n((This knowledge should be demonstrated Rp'ly not literally))", ""),
        StaticBook("Blackwood poetry", "Jentos Crazed-Blade", "Book O' poetry\nOoooooooooooooooooO\n\n\nBy Jentos Crazed-Blade of House Blackwood\n..................oooOooo..................\n\"In this book you shall read O' my ghazal's, haiku's and more! Now simply let yourselve's dragged by\nmy poem's.\"\n\n\nGhazal\nXxxooooooOooooooxxX\n\n\"Ti's a scar in the sky\"\n\n\"This very, deep poem was done in my early man-hood.\"\nXxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxX\"T'is a scar in the sky:\n\n\"Like a dark beast's growl! \n\nYou wonder what could be so fowl?. T'is a scar in the sky!\"\n\n\"It light's it strike's, it's a fallen star.\nT'is a scar in the sky\"\n\"You wait for the horrid drum.\n\nLike the devil's hum.\nT'is a scar in the sky!\"\n\n\"Thy withering light.\n\nWhich blind's your might! T'is a scar in the sky!\"\n\n\"It Blaze's your dream's.\n\nT'is what you have\nseen! T'is a scar in the sky!\"\n\nLike a god's hammer.\n\nThe world is it's banner. T'is a scar in the sky!\"\n\"It seek's as you weep.\n\nYou search your sleep. T'is a scar in the sky.\"\n\n\"As a beast O' myth.\n\nVainquished it seast.\nT'is a scar in the sky.\"\nXxxooooooOooooooxxX\nFor my second and shorter poem, an ode!\n=======oOOOo=======\n\nOde to the raven's flight! :\n\n\"Like thy fallen rain of grim.\n\nI see them bare the feather's of shadow.\n\"I see them rising the rim! \n\nBringing down the meadow.\n\nT'is like the flying ashe's O' death!\n\nIt's a dark ascendance.\nAnd it is nothing I have met!\"\n======oOOOo=======\nA song O' my family!\nIOOOxxXooooXxxOOOI\n\"This is a battle song from thy wild family O' north: Blackwood!\"\n\n\"Raven-Fall.\"\n\"Thy head's will roll and thy mountain's will fall!\"\n\n\"Until we choke on thy Dra-a-gon's HOooOard!\"\n\"Thy arrow's will fly and thy undead will rise!\"\n\n\"OooooooO! OooooO!\"\n\n\"Thy boooat's will row an' thy armie's will go!\"\n\n\"Thy blade's shall cling, the bell's will ring and WE SHALL SING!\" \"Hey!\"\n\"Thy prince will die... And thy raven will fly!\"\n\n\"Ho!\"\noooooooooOoooooooooThy one who ride's thy tempest storm!\"\n\n\"He ride's the sea's he tame's and see's!\nHe ride's the frosted storm.\"\n\"His word is thy wind!\nHis blade he will swing! He ride's thy tempest storm!\"\n\n\"Shall he rise! T'is nothing from his size! He ride's thy tempest storm!\"\n\n\"He storm's the night he light's thy might!\nHe ride's thy tempest storm!\"\n\"He bare's no helm...\nDAaaaaaaAvid BridgehelllM!\"\nXxxxxoooOOOoooxxxxX\n\"On this dear reader, I say good-bye.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Blah Dictionary", "Shreck", "Diz buuk tranzlatez wurds in blah tew kommon, writtun bi Shreck.\n\n-Ug ¦ Hello, Hi, Hail\n-Throm'ka ¦ Formal greeting\n-Yub ¦ Yes\n-Nub ¦ No\n-Gug'ye ¦ Goodbye\n-Lat ¦ You\n-Mi ¦ Me, I\n-Wi ¦ We, Us\n-Hi ¦ He\n-Rulg ¦ Thanks\n-Blah ¦ Talk, Speak, Orchish Language\n-Blah'er ¦ Mouth\n-Peepers ¦ Eyes\n-Skah'er ¦ Male Reproductive Organ\n-Gruk ¦ Think, Know, Understand\n-Dabu ¦ Yes, My Pleasure\n-Bubhosh ¦ Great, Big\n-Nubhosh ¦ Bad, Small\n-Snaga ¦ Slave\n-Buub ¦ Pig\n-Pushdug ¦ Stinky\n-Glob ¦ Fool, Shit, Poop\n-Klomp ¦ Fight, Attack\n-Flat ¦ Dead, Kill\n-Blarg ¦ Home\n-Brudda ¦ War Uzg Orc\n-Stout ¦ Dwarf\n-Twiggeh, Treehugger ¦ elf\n-Darkie ¦ Farfolk, Dark elf\n-Squeals, Snaaks ¦ Halflings\n-Quickspawn, Breeder, Shara, Pinkii ¦ Human\n-Nuutshara ¦ Ascended\n-Nubded ¦ Undead\n-Howlur ¦ Dog, Wolf\n-Skah ¦ Fuck\n-Agh ¦ And\n-Buurz ¦ Dark\n-Mojo ¦ Magic\n-Bi ¦ By\n-Krimp ¦ Stun, Capture\n-Uzg ¦ World\n-Goi ¦ City\n-Lusk ¦ Axe\n-O'lig ¦ Bow\n-Ligz ¦ Arrow\n-Zult ¦ Sword\n-Stik ¦ Staff\n-Steemiez ¦ Redstone\nNumburz!\n\nAsh ¦ One\nDub ¦ Two\nGakh ¦ Three\nFuth ¦ Four\nH' ¦ Five\nH'ash ¦ Six\nAshety ¦ Ten\nAshty ¦ Eleven\nDubty ¦ Twelve\nDubty ¦ Twenty", ""),
        StaticBook("Blind Man's Book", "The Blind Man", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Blood Cake", "Nugosaurus", "Blood Cake Recipe\nwritten by \"Puzhdug\"\n\nServes: 12 Orcs\n\nSupply List:\n\n3 cups of flour\n\n2 1/2 teaspoons of baking powder\n\n1/2 teaspoon of salt\n1 3/4 cups of sugar\n\n2/3 cup of butter\n\n2 eggs\n\n1 1/2 teaspoons of vanilla\n\n1 cup of milk\n\n1/4 cup of descendent blood\n2 hunks of descendent flesh (optional)\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. Light your furnace, make sure it is decently warm.\n\n2. Grease up the bottoms of two 8-inch round pans and line them with wax paper.\n3. Sift together flour, baking powder, and salt; set aside.\n\n4. Cream together the sugar and butter until light.\n\n5. Add eggs and vanilla to the creamy mixture and beat until thoroughly mixed.\n6. Add the flour mixture to the creamy mixture, mix in milk and blood.\n\n7. Continue to mix the mixture for 1 minute.\n\n8. Spread the batter mixture evenly in the prepared pans. Bake for 30 to 35 minutes.\n9. Allow to sit idle until cool.\n\n10. Put hunks of flesh inbetween the two cakes, frost and decorate as desired.\n\nSuggestions:\n\nFrost with a creamy blood frosting!\n\nDecorate with fingers!\nWrite names and messages in the center with blood or frosting!\n\nMake with your momo, popo, cubs, and family for a family-friendly fun time and a delicious, protein-filled treat!\n\nUse as a gift to Glutros!\n\nGift it to an Orc in need.\nLastly, feed to any disobedient slaves!\n\nWritten by \"Puzhdug\", good luck in your cooking adventures and praise Krug!", ""),
        StaticBook("Blood of Many", "Daniel Nodal", "With great might and ideals men have raised themselves to fight. Throughout the sands of time we have seen gigantic armies fall and tyrant kings still stand. And yet, where do these ideals, these admittedly impressive albeit unsuccessful ventures lead?\nDeath and destruction. The decay of rebellions, and the downfall of freedom. And yet where many have failed, it takes but one to succeed. Need one be reminded of any of the ancient kings and rules who have come to an, shall we say abrupt end? Indeed,\nAssassins shape the tide of history more than you know. And here you arem reading, seeking, learning. What is it that you wish to know I wonder?\nIt is true that we have our governments, it is true that they are what hold us together- And yet! It is also\nthat we have the power to sway the tide! Move the battlefield to our advantage! And even, end the rule of the horrendous” The power in the minority is greater than we think. And it is why today we live in a world DEFINED by the assassinations of\nyesterday! And were these the greatest historic decisions? Perhaps not. But while some were not the best, others changed history for the better, bringing Aegis to the place it is today-or was yesterday rather. Grand armies once again amass in a hopeless\neffort to combat the Undead forces.\nIt makes one question where the world will be left, with such meek enemies yet so strong.\nIt is high time we accept our history’s motive and ally ourselves with Iblees to bring salvation to our world.\nThis is where our powers are tested. We must remain resolute in the times to come if we are to become united. Otherwise we might as well let our blood spatter against the stone.\nThe Blood of Many, the Heart of One\n\nOriginal written in Aegis\nRewritten by Leyu’Maehr\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Blood of Many", "Leyu", "The Blood of Many, the Heart of One\nWith great might and ideals men have raised themselves to fight. Throughout the sands of time we have seen gigantic armies fall and tyrant kings still stand. And yet, where do these ideals, these admittedly impressive albeit\nunsuccessful ventures lead ? :: Death and destruction. The decay of rebellions, and the downfall of freedom. And yet where many have failed, it takes but one to succeed. Need one be reminded of any of the ancient kings and rules who have\ncome to an, shall we say abrupt end? Indeed, Assassins shape the tide of history more than you know. And here you are, reading, seeking, learning. What is it that you wish to know I wonder? ::It is true that we have our governments, it is true that\nthey are what hold us together- And yet! It is also true that we have the power to sway the tide! Move the battlefield to our advantage! And even, end the rule of the horrendous! The power in the minority is greater than we think. And it is why today we\nlive in a world DEFINED by the assassinations of yesterday! And were these the greatest historic decisions? Perhaps not. But while some were not the best, others changed history for the better, bringing Aegis to the place it is today-or was\nyesterday rather. Grand armies once again amass in a hopeless effort to combat the Undead forces. ::It makes one question where the world will be left, with such meek enemies yet so strong. ::It is high time we accept our history's motive and and ally\nourselves with Iblees to bring salvation to our world. This is where our powers are tested. We must remain resolute in the times to come if we are to become united. Otherwise we might as well let our blood spatter against the stone.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Blue Orchid A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "To inform the reader, this book is mainly existent for the purpose of containing diagrams of the anatomy of a blue orchid. Ultimately, this is for the use in conjuration.\n*All over this page there is an exquisitely detailed depiction and labelled analysis of a blue orchid. It involves things such as the roots, stem, pedals, and etcetera.*\nThe roots of the flower exist for several purposes. These include keeping it properly rooted into the ground as well as for gaining nutrients/water from the surrounding soil.\nNext, the stem of the blue orchid. The stem exists for the purpose of transporting nutrients throughout the flower for sustenance. This would include various materials for use in photosynthesis and water.\nThen there are the pedals and leaves of the plant. Much of the photosynthesis is done within these parts of the plant. By collecting sunlight, the orchid is capable of processing it into a form of sugar.\nWithin the flowers include reproductive organs as well, including things such as the ovules.\nAs for habitat, I have found that the blue orchid mainly grows in humid regions, such as swamplands and islands.\n*Finally, there are several closer depictions of the several different portions of the flower's form. They seem zoomed in closer than the initial picture from before and show slightly more detail.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Blue Steel", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "In the time of Anthos, when the name Steelwall was spoken with respect and awe, the smith Lark had spent decades as Kralta’s smith, honing his art and becoming renowned even amongst dwarven blacksmiths for his prowess and skill.\nTo solidify himself in human history as one of its greatest, Lark began to study the properties of Carbarum. Surely forging a strong set of Carbarum armor, of which the likes have not been seen since the times of Asulon,\nwould cement his status as a smith whose skills would be seen as mythical. So he set to work, draining his supply of carbarum ore until he only had a small portion left. Met with total and utter failure, Lark erupted in a frenzy,\niron and carbarum into his forge. The metals began to melt within the intense heat and the molten metal began to drip into the ingot cast, forming a new alloy. Bluesteel.\nUpon returning to his forge, Lark cried with glee at his success and set to work, testing the metal’s strength and durability, putting it through intense trial to better learn his creation. To his surprise, unlike previous carbarum ingots,\nthey did not break apart or shatter upon use. In-fact, the metal seemed stronger than normal steel, not quite the level of ancient carbarum, but strong enough to the point that it lasted longer than any previously known metal.\nWith this new metal, Lark used it to create his legendary weapons and armors that kept Orenian soldiers alive during the Dwarf vs Oren conflicts.\nWhen Lark met his untimely demise, he left the secrets to Bluesteel to his son Avgust Steelwall and close friend, Dared Starbreaker. Avgust in turn, left the secrets to the Cloud Temple Monks so that they might\nspread the alloy’s existence and so that the inhabitants of the realm may put it to use should the techniques to Carbarum smithing ever be lost once more.\n===================The Story of Blue Steel is told by Lark Steelwalls apprentice and retold in this book. \nRe-Written By:\nSarrion Zytiaear\nOOC: Bluesteel is a 4:2 alloy of iron and carbarum that is roughly the durability of Carbarum, but lacks its strength. The metal can be forged through intense heat (roughly 3000 degrees celsius, hot enough to melt\nLotC Carbarum and Ferrum into something entirely new.) It has a bluish tint and basically is used to create armor that is step up from Iron, but below or at diamond's durability. In terms of armor strength, it is the same as iron.", ""),
        StaticBook("Body Training.", "Dunstan Zytiaear", "Table of contents.\nPg3. Introduction.\npg5. Starting.\npg8. Self Dicipline\npg11. Endurance.\npg17. Strength.\npg22. Disease & Injury.\npg25. Pain & discomfort.\n\nIntroduction.\nIf one wants to harness their mind and body to its greatest ability they must face the challenge of their own willingness. Once you can overcome your own mind then you can over come your own body. All information in this book is\nuseless if one can not muster the will and humility to conquer themselfs.\nStarting.\nThe final statement of the introduction is the most important in this stage. You have been asked to embrace humility as it is the requirement to learn where you stand. If you believe your what you are not then you will fail. If you believe\nyou can throw a small tree but struggle to swing a stick how would you learn to move larger trees? You must come to terms with what you truly can do if you wish to change it. You must accept weakness to become strong. You must accept injury to recover.\nYou must accept to change. Find your self if you wish to better yourself.\nSelf Dicipline.\nOnce you have found where you stand you must embrace the emotions that come with it and use it. The pain, anger, frustration, and sadness that come form embraceing your own falts are your ultimant tools. But you must learn to wield\nthese tools with skill. You must controll yourself to drive your self. If you cannot learn to controll your tools you can not craft any quality. All you will do is destroy your self if you can not controll your emotions.\nYour emotions can be the most precise of tools and the most deadly of parasites. Unchecked rage has lead to the downfall of nations while honed rage has lead to the creation of nations.\nEndurance.\nA quite simply physically painfull aspect to hone. Training may seem simple but time will tell it is not. Pick a simple task and do it with repetition for an extended period of time. Running is a recommended task for this. When you start to\nrun you may feel fine. Within the first minute your hearts pulse will quicken and your breathing will heavy. Soon your legs and lungs will start to feel a burning sensation. This burning sensation will begin to slowly start to spread throughout your body.\nThe desire to stop will suck at your mind like a leech  and you will begin to take measures to attempt to make the action take less effort. You will begin to argue with your self whether or not or not you have done enough. You dont know what enough\ntruly feels like. You will need to excersise self dicipline to own your emotion and have it assist you into going farther. The moment you collapse is when you will know every thing. The moment you have collapsed is the moment that teaches you what\nenough is. At this moment you may puke and will be covered in sweat. Your body will be screaming for both rest and nutrient. Find where you stand as you have to make a decision on what you need more. My personal siggestion is to drag yourself to a tavern,\nembrace the humility of fumbling over your self to walk, and order a meal.\nStrength.\nIncreasing the ammount of pure phyisical power you can exert is a tasking process that will cause a great physical change on your body. You will require both a viraty of heavy movable objects and a signifigant ammount of nutrents. Find what\nyou are able to lift then find something lighter and heavier. You will start with the lighter and you will do it with the aim of repetition. Move to the middle weight and lift to a number that will be decided as your secess point. Once you have lifted the\nmiddle weight go to the heavy weight and lift with the goal of reaching your success point. If you reach your success point move to a heavier weight and go for your success point again. Do this untill you fail. Remember where you have failed for the next\ntime you will try to pass this. You will be sore on a regular basis. This is the feeling of your muscles growing. You will learn enjoy this feeling. As your muscles grow you must also feed them, thus you must eat more and you must eat with proper\nattention to nutrition.\nDisease & Injury.\nThese go hand in hand as injury can result in disease and disease can result in injury. It is more important to clean ones wounds than it is to heal them. If ones calf is sliced open it should be cleaned before any attempt to mend\nthe calf back together is done. An uncleaned injury can lead to infection which if left further unchecked can lead to organ failure which will come back around to further injury and possable death. Disease is an entire beast in its self as all you can do\nwith out extensive training is collect rest and eat healthy foods.\nPain & discomfort.\nMany mistake this as ones enemy when in reality it can be ones ultimate ally. It is the manner in which one is consciously alert to detail of their body which may not be the most apparent.\nYou must learn to befriend pain and discomfort if you want to be able to tame it. If you want to tame it you must embrace it. If you want to embrace it you must be familiar with it. Push your self. Endure the cold bare back. Run the extra mile and\ndo it upon blistering feet. Revel in the feeling and progress will be made.", ""),
