        StaticBook("BoulderBear Oath", "Haggis BoulderBear", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=      LEGAL DOCUMENT\nThis document states that in exchange for the treasures requested by the current ClanFather (Haggis BoulderBear) the BoulderBear clan will pledge their mercenary service to the holder of this contract, should they\nsuccessfully fulfill the ClanFather's requests, if the signature upon this document is NOT the current ClanFather then this contract shall be void; Other exeptions of this contract would be any act that goes against the Grand Kingdom or its people, The\nBoulderBear clan and its men or the allies of the BoulderBear (Depending on the ClanFather's say). \nThis Contract is to be instantly made void at the discression of the ClanFather, following BoulderBear tradition \"The BoulderBear's allegiance is with the\nhighest bidder.\" with the exception of the Grand Kingdom, taking supreme priority over any current contract bearer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Braduk Rhinos", "Thurak", "Braduk Rhinos    \n\n Discovery \nIn Aegis, when the Braduk Clan was just starting off, a village war had broken out between the Braduk village, Kenuk, and a rivalling village led by Braduk’s half-brother, Gorjol.\nDishonourable raids were leaving Kenuk in ruins, and the Braduks needed an edge. Braduk discovered rhinos roaming the mountain pass. The problem was that they only stood around the height of the average human, so they couldn't support the weight of most\nOrcs. Braduk, however, still saw potential in the beasts' sharp, sturdy horns and incredibly thick hides. After a short raid on Kenuk, Braduk decided to inspect the rhinos more closely. One was captured and brought to the village, and Braduk watched it\nstomp around in a pen for a while, pondering how the beasts could be used to their advantage.\nBreeding \nBraduk ordered for a few more to be captured, and started a breeding program in hopes of bigger, mountable rhinos to use in the Village Wars. He only bred the largest rhinos, which, at the time, weren't much bigger than the average ones.\nEach generation was slightly larger than its parents, and as such the progress was painstakingly slow. It wouldn't be until long after Braduk’s death that the rhinos would be big enough to ride. Two Chieftains after Braduk’s reign, Goregutz was finally\npleased with the size and tried to mount the first Braduk Rhino.\nTaming \nAt this point, the rhinos hadn't been properly tamed yet. The larger ones were dangerous, and were kept locked up in caves situated not too far from the clan fort. Smaller ones were usually killed for meat and leather, though\nthe clan was still eagerly awaiting the fruits of labour to be harvested from the massive Rhinos. Goregutz, as a show of strength and bravery, decided to try his luck with the only ten-foot rhino they had. He entered the pen with several other Orcs, and\nimmediately the animal went berserk. It began to smash around, killing many that stood in its path, impaling and crushing the slowest of the Orcs with no more than a turn of its head. Goregutz, being one of the biggest, jumped at the Rhino and mounted it.\nHe grabbed it by its two long horns, holding on for his life as the Rhino tried it’s best to throw the Orc off its back. It bucked around like this for several minutes until it threw Goregutz off. The beast was tenacious, but so was Goregutz.\nHe jumped back on the rhino, holding on even tighter, but even then he was bucked off multiple times. It took hours for it to tire out, and Goregutz barely outlasted it. Finally, the rhino grew tired and stopped.\nExhausted just as much as the Rhino, Goregutz relaxed a bit, sitting on it calmly.\n\n\"Mi kall lat Gurtog,\" said Goregutz.\n\nThe rhino grunted, and looked up at him with what resembled a look of respect.\nCharacteristics\nBraduk Rhinos have a diet consisting of grains, grasses and small plants. Usually the untamed rhinos are kept in a pen and fed their daily meals, but once paired with an Orc they are let free to roam and eat as they please.\nStunted Rhinos, a somewhat common occurrence in Braduk forts due to the lack of grasses, are usually killed and processed. Their hide is used in armour, their horns sometimes sharpened into daggers, and their meat is cooked up in casseroles, being too\ntough for any other meal.\n\nThe rhino’s most common colour is grey though rare sand coloured rhinos can be born. The very first rhinos were black, but as time went on their skin lightened through reproduction.\nIt is unknown if a black rhino remains, the last being Ghazkull’s, and there has only been one recording of a white rhino.\n\nDuring infancy, the Braduk rhino will have just a bump where the horns will develop. As they mature, they grow two horns;\none directly in front of the other. The front horn is longer than the back horn, and usually reaches an average length of 47 inches (120 cm), while the second horn usually reaches 35 inches (90 cm). If a horn is cut off, it will take decades to\nRe-develope, and during the first couple days, the hole will remain. It is a lethal spot, and if stabbed will result in a fatality. It's common practice for a Braduk to customize his rhino’s horns by sharpening them, overlaying them with iron, or\nsometimes carving his name or important symbols into them.\n\nTheir thick hides cover most of their body and legs. It’s too thick to be penetrated by arrows, but hard swung weapons are capable of breaking the bones of the beasts.\nOn some occasions, an Orc will use rhino hide as a moderate substitute for leather armour, and the clan mothers have been known to replace an Orc's flesh with a Rhino's in serious injuries to prevent infection.\nThe rhino's underbelly is loose fat, and is the weakest spot on their body, save for the soft flesh behind their large ears and underneath the horns. The average Braduk rhino stands from 9-10 ft tall, and can weigh between 8,000-8,500 lbs.\nAs a result of their incredible size, their speed is depressingly slow. Bursts of speed are not uncommon, however; a charging rhino is capable of reaching a maximum speed of 40 kmh (approx. 25 mph), with enough force to break through solid\nbrick walls. Additionally, what Braduk Rhinos lack in speed they definitely make up in stamina, being capable of maintaining a constant speed for as much as a day without rest.\nThe Braduk Rhinos grow at about the same rate as a normal Orc does. When an Orc cub is born into the Braduks, a rhino will already be chosen for him by one of the Elders of the clan, usually one born at around the same time.\nAt the age of ten an Orc is shown to the Rhino, and this is where they will be bonded for life. They must first gain each other’s honour by engaging in a klomp. The Orc must do as Goregutz did, and mount the rhino until it ceases retaliation.\nThe Orc will name the rhino, and in turn, the rhino will name the Orc. The Braduk Rhinos have their own respected contingents and have their own names; communicating to each other using a series of grunts, snarls, grumbles and roars.\nThe bond between a rhino and an Orc is strong, and one can rarely live without the other. After the two have been paired, the rhino will scar the Orc with its horn, and in turn the Orc will scar the rhino with his favoured weapon.\nThe Braduk rhino is extremely difficult to train and control due to their ferocity and their horrible eyesight. They're known to charge upon the slightest provocation, and it’s rare that a particular rhino can be approached\nby anyone other than its familiar rider. As a result, an Orc must spend tremendous amounts of time familiarizing himself with the rhino he wishes to ride. Due to their foul tempers, the rhino will commonly go into a bloodthirsty fit during battle,\nrequiring truly masterful skill for a rider to maintain control, and such fits can cause just as much damage to the rider's enemies as to his friends. Because of their poor eyesight, the rhino must also rely heavily on its strong sense of smell,\nthough this of course presents further difficulty in training and control; a stray scent sometimes causing a Braduk Rhino to plough through a nearby wall without warning.", ""),
        StaticBook("Braxus. II .", "Braxus Ni'leya", "===================\n\n----[ Braxus.II ]----\n\n~ This is part two of a two part series.\n\n===================\n===================\n\n Afraid of becoming impure, I made my home in a cave, I became reclusive and secluded for years. The burning sensation of being able to return kept me alive. I was allowed back and started on a trial of repent, hoping to -\n===================\n\n- restore my name and reputation. Such to this day is still proving hard to do.\n\n It is the 19th of the Deep Cold, 1512. I am 248 years of age. My name is Braxus Ni'leya and I seek to keep the flames of silver burning bright for -\n===================\n\n- as long as I draw breath.\n\n--[ Maehr'sae\n        Hiylun'ehya ]--\n\n~ Braxus Ni'leya.\n\n===================", ""),
        StaticBook("Brennus", "Reign Silverblade", "Target: Brennus Cedric ((W3IRDO))\n\nReason: Walking around Felsen, heard this man talk to another about killing a Flay, and wanting to kill more. Didnt get the other's name. \n\nBlack Hair,blue eyes.\nArmour. Tabard red\nand black.", ""),
        StaticBook("Brewing Ale", "Sofetios", "Brewing Ale\n\n          ~By Sofetios\n               Jayamen\nThis book is my experience brewing beer. \n\nIn this book, I will explain to the best of my ability the ways to brew beer. So without anymore introduction, here we go.\nTo start out with making some beer,  Here is what you will need to make 6 mug-fulls of ale, or a keg-full.\n\n((In OOC because of the materials.\n((\n7 iron ingots – Cauldron\n3 iron ingots - Bucket\n1 iron ingot and 3 logs – 3 kegs\n2 fences and 2 logs – 6 mugs\n))\n((\n2 sticks and 3 cobble(or better) - sickle\n2 hops of the same kind\n(optional) 2 of a brew able added ingredient.\n))\nNow, to start out you need to get some barley seeds. This will be what makes the hops for later on. Different types of land ((Biomes)) produce different types of Barley seed. To collect the barley seed, you will need a special tool called a Sickle.\n((To craft sickle, one stick bottom left, one stick middle, three other building materials bottom middle, middle right, and top middle.))\nWhen you have your sickle,  you can collect seeds from tall or short grass. Tall grass probably has a higher chance of getting good seeds. You can mix different seeds.\n. ((When mixing seeds, you can get nothing, one type or both types. I have found that you can’t get three types.))\nNow that you have your Barley seeds, it’s time to make them into hops. Find suitable farm ground and plant the seeds. When they are fully grown, harvest them. Now the fun part begins. Brewing.\nYou will want to be near a water source that won’t go out. Once you have one, place down your cauldron and fill it near the top with water. ((right click on the top of it with a water bucket)).\nNow add in the hops that you harvested and perhaps an additional brew able ingredient.\n((Some brewable ingrediants include but are not limited to: Carrots, Wheat, Pumpkins, Sugar cane, Mushrooms, Saplings, apples, cactus, and more.))\nNow its time to store your brew in a keg. ((to make three kegs, it is, one iron ingot on the middle left, and three logs on the bottom middle, right middle, and top middle.))\nYou will want to make your brew twice to fill up the keg. ((you transfer the ale with mugs. To make three mugs, it s a fence and a log next to each other. Left click on the top of the cauldron with the brew in it to get one mugful per time.\nThen right click the nozzle (tripwire hoop) of the keg to put it in.)) Each time you brew something will make three mugfulls or half a keg.\nNow comes the hard part. Waiting. I have heard it takes one elven week to fully age most brews. The longer you wait, the more tasty((less harmful, and more beneficial)) your brew will get.\n. Though don’t drink it straight from the start, or you will get sick.\n\nThere are many possibilities for mixing brews. All you have to do is test them out.\nThank you for reading and I hope this was helpful.\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Brewing Vol.I", "Siri", "Alcoholica Esoterica\n      by Siri Ihelia\nAlcohol is a commonly  found in beverages such as ale, beer, liquor, but also found in commonly in medicine to disinfect a wound. \n\nThis book explores the virtues, production, and sources of alcohol.\nAle\n\nAle is a beverage commonly associated with dwarves or humans. It is made from grains such as barley, rye, oats, and wheat. \n\nThe recipe to make ale requires yeast, grain, fire, water, hop.\nThe equipment needed is a large stove, a pot, and some oaken barrels to store the ale in. \n\nOne must first soak the grain in warm water to turn it into malt. \n\nNext, boil the malt, grain, with water, let the mixture simmer\nwithout boiling over. \n\nAdd the hop and cool, the mixture is now known as wort. \n\nStrain the wort into a barrel and add the yeast to ferment for a month. \n\nTap the barrel with a screw to drink.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bringing of Life", "Edwyn Lynderly", "The Bringing\n             of Life.\n\n\n\n  The Notes of Edwyn\n               Lynderly\n6th of Malin's Welcome.\n\nToday begins the endeavour to grow that of a tree, from nothing more than a sapling. I travelled  to the cloud temple, I came across a small store in which to purchase a sapling during my prior task.\nI settled on a spruce sapling, I've always admired how despite being present in the coldest of enviroments they can still flourish into something magnificent. Tomorow I shall attempt to plant my newly obtained sapling.\n7th of Malin's Welcome.\n\nWith sapling in hand, I left the druids grove in search of the perfect location. Wondering into the nearby woods, I soon settled on a small clearing that would be perfect for my tree. Grasping my shovel I dug a small hole, the\nperfect size for my small sapling. Bringing it to settle within it's new home, I brushed the dirt back towards it's original resting place.  It's oddly therapeutic this planting thing. Allowing it a drizzle of water I collected from the nearby river, I\nleft the sapling.\n14th of Malin's Welcome.\n\nA few days have passed since the planting of my sapling, it's growing well. Along with allowing it daily watering, I've been applying bonemeal to help fertilize it's growth. I used a small stick to support the\ngrowing tree. I was concerned it's size would soon cause it to collapse, better it be secure at the end of the day. I'll continue to monitor it's growth over the coming month, hopefully it'll grow into something sufficient soon.. The risk is holds against\nthat of natures  prey makes me anxious.. Once it grows more, that threat will hopefully disperse. I'd rather not have to buy another sapling.\n21st of Malin's Welcome.\n\n§II nearly lost the damned sapling today. I was returning from the river bank, collecting water within my pail when I saw the small critter edging closer towards it. It had a nibble, but dropping my bucket I managed\nto shoo it away from the plant.. It'll need some defense against this, cant sit here day in day out looking after the bloody thing.\n29th Malin's Welcome.\n\nAfter several days of heaving rocks back and forth, I've built a hefty wall around my sapling. It's nothing major but should keep those small bastards at bay, moreso thanks to the lighting.. Or does that\nattract more critters towards it.. Well, a splash late now. I've considered giving my tree a name, oddly. Never really held a 'connection' to anything other than another person.. For now however, I shall name it 'Edwyn's tree.' Very original, I know.\n3rd of The First Seed.\n\nA new month, never really noticed the months pass by until I actually went to record this journal. It's now grown to reach the height of my chest, quite interesting that it grows so quickly.. However, I have been\nfeeding it hefty amounts of bonemeal on a regular basis. Those creatures that lurk the shadows of the grove are awfully useful in obtaining the bones. I've considered stopping the bonemeal, allowing it to go naturally for some time.. Yet, I must admit my\ncuriosity only grasps at my conscious to see just how far I can push this plant.\n12th of The First Seed.\n\nAnother spurt of growth from the plant! It's spectacular to watch, every day I awake to a few new branchs.. It's almost become consuming of my life, keeping me awake as I continplate what I may\nfind in the morning.. Yet, along with this I also cannot concern over it.. A large bear, happy lumberjack or even just that of a strong wind can ruin my efforts. I've still not slowed my bonemeal additions, I figure the large my tree can grow the greater\nchance it stands against these threats.\n15th of The First Seed.\n\nIt's the early hours of the morning, I couldnt sleep. Had this gut feeling something was wrong with the tree, yet whilst trudging from the warmth of my bed I found little to be concerned about. Odd.\n24th of The First Seed.\n\nI can't even maintain it's growth at this point, it's gone far beyond what I even expected. It's already above my height I believe, and yet I cannot stop with the bonemeal. It's practically an\nobsession at this point, an addiction. Even though I admit it I still ignore my own pleas, having this burning desire for it to stretch far above it's surrounding brothers.\n30th of The First Seed.\n\nNearing the end of the second month.. The growth has halted slightly, I believe the earth it has rooted itself into fails to address it's constant need for water. I need a better means of relieving it's constant\nthirst.. Perhaps if I extend the river to run alongside it? However thats an awful amount of work, I'll have to consider it over the coming days.\n4th of The Grand Harvest.\n\nYet another month, and with it my small pond has been completed.. After heaving multiple buckets of water up the small incline leading towards my tree it began to rain.. A days work, completed in minutes by that of\nnature.. Perhaps the aspects noticed by struggle and gave me aid, or just merely a coincidence. Whatever it is, the tree should be able to feed from it's new source for some time.. I've already noticed a hint of growth again, which makes me happy.. I was\nconcerned it had reached its limit.. Yet no, my little sapling has only continued to grow.\n12th of The Grand Harvest.\n\nI woke today to be greeted by a slither of growth once again, and yet, despite such I only feel disappointment. A few local brethren to my tree had given in to the drought of water caused by the massive thirst of my own.\nTheir leaves went brown, and within a few days their trunks failed to sustain themselves as rot caused them to fall.  Perhaps the excess bonemeal has only came to punish me, yet now I fail to grant it such a privlidge and even so it grows..\n19th of The Grand Harvest.\n\nSoon will come the time to show my efforts to Arin. The tree continues to grow substainally, however it's yet to poison any more of the surrounding nature with thirst thankfully.  It's been  an interesting experiance, from\nthe small sapling which could hardly survive.. Requiring a wall for protection, which thanks to my shoddy building has since fallen into ruin.. Makes quite the pretty border however, I must admit.  Now the tree remains large, I doubt I shall leave it come\nthe end of my trial. It's almost like a child at this point, even though it's constantly threatening to destroy more of it's brethren for the precious supply of water, I cannot hate it nor bring the guts to save the others.. It's my tree, and with my care\nit has far outgrown the others.\n\nI suppose that also means this will be the last time I write within this journal, and probably see it. Oh well, fun whilst it lasted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Brown Bear A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "This book has been written for documenting the various systems within the common brown bear species for use in conjuration.\n   The systems being covered in this book include: cardiovascular, respiratory, nervous, skin, musculoskeletal, digestive, and-\n-urinary systems.\n*Flipping to this page, you find a rather detailed sketching of a brown bear's cardiovascular system. It includes the heart, veins, and arteries being spread throughout the entire body.*\nCardiovascular System:\n   This system is composed of the heart, veins, and arteries throughout the entire body.\n   The purpose of this system is to carry blood throughout the body and provide it with proper nutrients.\n   The brown bear's cardiovascular-\n-system is rather large, as it has a large body to provide with blood.\n*The next sketch is riddled with similar detail as before, but instead of a heart and veins, you are greeted with a sketching of lungs connected through the bear's throat.*\nRespiratory System:\n   This system is composed of the mouth connected via the throat into the bear's lungs.\n   The purpose of this system is to provide the blood stream with nutrients via oxygen and breathing.\n   The bear's respiratory system isn't -\n- particularly unique besides it being some what larger than a human's or otherwise.\n*The next sketching is displaying what appears to be the brain, connected and sprawling throughout the rest of the bear's body. Nerves branch out from the spinal cord.*\nNervous System:\n   This system includes the brain, the spinal cord, and all the nerves within the body.\n   The purpose of this system is to direct intentional actions, and enable thinking and emotions.\n   The brown bear isn't particularly self aware, -\n- much like other animals, but it is intelligent to a certain extent and with a plethora of instincts.\n*This sketch is a bit different than the others, as it displays three different figures. The first displays a shaved bear, the second shows the various layers within the skin, and the third shows a bear with its fur.*\nSkin:\n   This system is actually just one organ, but the organ is so expansive that it warrants itself as its own system.\n   The purpose of this system is to provide a barrier to the external environment and protect the inner workings of the body.\nThe brown bear has a rather dark brown hair covering its skin. Otherwise, the skin is rather similar in function to other animals.\n*A rather complicated sketch appears on this next page, showing two sketchings of a bear. The first is of the various muscles within, and the other shows the bear's skeleton.*\nMusculoskeletal System:\n   This system includes all the muscles, ligaments and tendons within the bear, as well as the entire skeleton.\n   The purpose of this system is to provide motion of the body and structure.\n   The brown bear is a huge, behemoth of-\n- a creature. Its body is rather massive, with large muscles and thick bones, allowing it to be a powerful hunter. Its claws and teeth are also rather sharp to add onto its dangerous nature.\n*This sketch shows the bear's mouth being connected through the throat into its stomach, then into the large/small intestines, then finally out through the back. It's quite noticably the digestive system.*\nDigestive System:\n   This system also includes the mouth connected through the throat into the stomach, the intestines, then finally excreting out the behind. It also includes the pancreas, gallbladder, and the liver. \n   The purpose of this system is to-\n- extract nutrients from food, then to excrete wastes.\n   The bear is rather similar to other animals in its digestive system.\n*The final sketching seems rather lacking compared to the others, with only displaying the kidneys, and bladder.*\nUrinary System:\n   For conjuration purposes, you only need to worry about the kidney and bladder within this system.\n   The purpose of this system is to filter wastes out from the blood stream.\n   For the brown bear, nothing is particularly unique.\nSide Notes:\n-Very defensive of their young, a mother brown bear is a force to be reckoned with.\n-They aren't immune to fire.\n-Sorry.\nList of Systems:\n-Cardiovascular\n-Respiratory\n-Nervous\n-Skin\n-Musculoskeletal\n-Digestive\n-Urinary\n*The final pages of this book are a compilation of miniature versions of all the sketches previously shown in the book. They are relatively close together for comparison.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Brown Fungi", "Aerxuis", "Brown Fungi \nBy Unknown \nCopied by Aerx \nThese fungi seem to sprout a lot slowly although grow with a top cap not bent over, this cap follows the sun blocking it out as mushrooms smaller would grow underneath and-\nspout out, although the brown mushroom would decay quicker than the toadstools they will kill or decay a lot more of its surroundings helping nature’s peace. These mushrooms are handy although not efficient in hot or cold climates-\n-since the stem would be too weak and break or burn in any hot or cold climate.\nThese mushrooms are also used for mushroom soup to counter the toadstools drugged effect and give a very tasteful and filling meal.\nThese mushrooms are great for around people, although try not to breath in most of the spores as they will endanger your life span or your life in general.", ""),
        StaticBook("Brown Recluse", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "The purpose of this book is in detailing the various systems and structures within a brown recluse spider.    The few systems within the brown recluse spider include its two sections. These are its abdomen and its cephalothorax.\n*The next page shows the intricately detailed sketching of a spider's back end. The abdomen. Within it shows the various workings within.*\nAbdomen:\n   The various parts within the abdomen include the heart gut, digestive gland, malpighian tubule, spinnerets, silk glands, and book rung.\n   The purpose of this system is in digesting nutrients, producing webbings, and reproduction.\n*The next sketching is equally detailed as it shows the various structures within the first segment of a spider. Showing its various inner workings, it is the cephalothorax.*\nCephalothorax:\n   The various structures within the cephalothorax are the legs, the brain, the main stomach, simple eyes, pedipalp, poison gland, chelicera, and mouth.\n   The purpose of this system is commanding any remote thought, digesting, -\ncatching pray, locomotion, and providing structure alongside the abdomen.\nSide Notes:\n-A single brown recluse's bite can kill you in about two days. The poison works in a conjuration, but only remains for as long as the conjuration does.\n-Damn this was scary to study.\n-Still not sorry.\nList of Systems:\n-Abdomen\n-Cephalothorax\n*You're met with the two previous sketchings shown within the book, with just as much detail as they are combined to show comparison and the sum of their parts.*", ""),
        StaticBook("CA Proclamation", "Ser Orgmar", "Carrot Proclamation\n-All farmfields must sustain atleast 2/5 of all crops, as carrots.\n\n-Any farmer, rancher, or farmhand who fails to plant atleast 2/5 of their crop as carrots shall receive 1 weeek in the stocks and if the offense is repeated shall face hanging.\nPurpose: To provide the people of Oren with more nutrient filled food.", ""),
        StaticBook("Carnival Diary", "HugTheWorld", "Make a right\nMake another right\nMake a left\nMake a right\nGo straight until wall\nMake another right\nFollow the path to a wall\nMake a left\nMake the right\nFollow the path\nMake a right\nTurn around\nGo straight\nuntil a wall\nMake a right\nMake the first right\nFollow the path\nMake the first left\nMake the second left\nFollow the path\nMake a right\nFollow the path\nMake the first left\nMake a right\nMake a left\nFollow the path\nTurn around\nMake a left\nTurn around\nGo straight until a wall\nFollow the path\nMake a left\nMake a right\nMake the right\nMake the first left\nFollow the path\nMake the first left\nMake the third left\nMake the first\nright\nGo straight to the wall\nMake the right\nFollow the path\nMake a left\nTurn around\nGo straight\nFollow the path\nMake the way final right\nTurn around\nGo straight\nMake a right\n[!] In the middle of all of the directions, some tired handwriting shows some numbers...\n\n2\n7\n8\n[!] A blank space is intentionally left for a fourth number.\nEnd of Directions\n\nI'm sorry, but I just can't keep writing the directions. I'm lost and it's driving me mad. The circus must've taught me something. I mean, it must've... I need to get out.\n\n[!] The name Sue is signed, almost unable to read.\nThe Soulstone\n\nI'm now going to grip my soulstone, sleepless and bitter, and head home. But I shall find this place again by marking the coordinates if I can track them properly. I assume they are...\nX: 1530\nZ: -1580\n[!] A crudely drawn sketch of the carnival is on this page. It reeks of a lack of sleep.\nReturn\n\nI've returned to the carnival, and I will continue to explore it. Somehow I find it unbearable to stay and yet worse to leave. Enter I will now.\n[!] Filling this page is a drawing of a pit of slime. It sits in the middle of the carnival, yet not much is drawn surrounding it.\n\n\n\n\nTHE MYSTERIOUS PIT OF GRIME\n[!] Various notes are scratched here, obviously taken from another source.\n\ndie rules fur bruno's uber fant\n\nastisch starker mann konkurrenz\n\ndie uberhammer!\nRe-entry\n\nI have re-entered the funhouse. I find my mind will never let me leave until I complete the monstrosity coming from said funhouse. The circus, the carnival, whatever it is brings back memories of my childhood and of my young adulthood. I wonder\nif this circus is ever still used or just abandoned, or if it is some sign for me to find. I'm running out of food, so that seems to be my main problem at the present moment. But onward for me, into the funhouse.\n[!] A sketch of a part of the maze, with multiple turns, is shown. The texture of the wool is drawn in well and glowstone is obvious above, but there is no color.\nPURPLE\n2 7 8 5\n\nThe code appears to be 2 7 8 5.\n\nNow I must simply find a way out of here...\n[!] There is a sketch of a strange glowstone exit. Next to it is a sign reading \"Exit for the Weak\".\n\n\nI refuse to go out this way, because I'm not even fully sure it would really take me out. I will continue on.\n[!] A sketch is here of a track through wool, with some diamond blocks above. It seemingly continues to descend.\n\n\nI've made it back now, and will soon be to my exit.\n[!] A sketch of a large room with many buttons and lamps matching numbers, surrounded by wool and quartz blocks, fills this page. There is also a RESET and a CLOSE DOOR button.\n[!] A sketch is made on this page of a tunnel leading out from the previous area sketched. Some blocks are shaded, while others are not, but they all appear the same texture.\n[!] A sketch fills the page of a quartz parkour map, over water. It goes up and down in different spots.\n\n\nThis is as far as I was able to get on my farthest journey. I got up pretty high before.\nThere's no exit! It doesn't go anywhere! I'm going to the exit for the weak now.\nConclusion\n\nStarving and weary, I did make it out of the funhouse. That carnival is a very odd place, but somehow I am still attracted to it. I know I will be returning, and it's likely I will start a text specifically about it but I'm not sure. I\ndo advise any who would themselves consider the funhouse think about it first. The overall vibe of the carnival is very strange, but yet somehow comfortable.\n\n\n\n\n-Sue", ""),
        StaticBook("Carry on . . .", "His Industrious Justice, Lathros", "\"Carry on My Wayward Dwarf\"\n\nCarry on my wayward Dwarf\nThere'll be peace when you are done\nLay your weary beard to rest\nWhy don't you drink some more\nAh\nOnce I rose above the noise an confusion Just to get a glimpse beyond this illusion \nI was digging ever deeper, but I dug too deep\nThough my eyes could see I still was a blind dwarf\nThough my mind could think I still was a stark dwarf\nI hear the voices when I'm dreaming,\nI can hear them say\nCarry on my wayward Dwarf,\nThere'll be peace when you are done\nLay your weary beard to rest\nWhy don't you drink soem more\nMasquerading as an alt with no reason\nMy charade is the event of the season\nAnd if I claim to be a wise man,\nWell, it surely means that I don't know\nOn a stormy sea of moving emotion\nTossed about, I'm like a ship on the ocean\nI set a course for winds of fortune,\nBut I hear the voices say\nCarry on my wayward Dwarf\nThere'll be peace when you are done\nLay your weary beard to rest\nWhy don't you drink some more, more!\nCarry on,\nYou will always industrialize\nCarry on,\nNothing equals the splendor\nNow your life's no longer empty\nSurely industry waits for you\nCarry on my wayward Dwarf\nThere'll be peace when you are done\nLay your weary beard to rest\nWhy don't you drink\nWhy don't you drink some more!\nDrink some more!", ""),
        StaticBook("Cataris's Trial", "Leyu", "Arch Mage Bell's Response to the reports of Cataris' trial\nCataris was put on trial for breaking our laws and my direct orders. He did NOT uphold the \"balance\" by attacking the undead. He put all of the Mage's Guild at risk by doing so. Everyone who\nparticipated in the attack, which he claimed to me personally he did not \"lead,\" (thoug h I have read differently in the Aegis Times newspaper) was nearly killed by the Prophet, including the Wizard. He has gained us an enemy. The\nundead want revenge on the Guild now. They will come after me first, as one of the Arch Mages. I will likely be tortured more, as they have been doing recently, whenever I dare to venture up nort h to guard it. I may even be killed. Magic has not yet\nreturned to us; the Veil which exists between this world and the one which magic seeps through from is not yet weak enough. The Veil is the reason why undead magic is so strong and Ascended magic seemingly less potent. I will write more on the\nsubject, but to put it bluntly, the undead are closest to Iblees. He is imp risoned on the other side of the Veil, where the powers of magic wait. He has given his servants, the undead, a more direct connection to the other side of the Veil than A\nscended or the rest of the world. That is why the Mage's Guild does not yet have magic yet...but we can feel it coming. :: Cataris, in attacking the undead base, broke our rules and my direct orders as Arch Mage. He betrayed my trust in doing so, but he\nwas given simply a warning and sent on his way. But other evidence has appeared which shows our problems inside the Guild are not yet done. We will be working quietly to fix these. And we will be attempting not to make the undead irritated at us by\nattacking them for a very good r eason... Should the guild fall before magic returns, we will not be as well equipped. Magic will not be as us eful to all of us as a whole, and our tomes upon tomes of knowledge will be destroyed, or used again st us.\nThat is why we put Cataris on trial for his actions. I sincerely hope you understand and do not give in to all the propaganda circulating at the moment. The Guild stands for the long-term defense of Aegis. If we fall even before magic\nreturns, we will b e of no use. But we will continue defending and working on collecting knowledge to better prepare Ae gis for the return of magic.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("CAUTION", "Maia", "ATTENTION ! ATTENTION ! \n-=-=- \nZaviel (Main Street 4) is a dark wizard Officialy. Elisa saw him killing a woman and she followed him near some ruins. I followed her. There was a talk. And Elisa got near him and CUT OFF HER OWN TONGUE WITH THE WORDS : \"I\nWOULD NOT NEED THAT BABE\"... \n\nTHIS WAS EXTREMELLY SCARY. \n\nWHEN YOU SEE ZAVIEL KILL HIM OR LOCK HIM IN CAGE. HE IS A DARK WIZARD. \n\nCaution! Be safe around dark wizards!\n            By: Anoniomus", ""),
        StaticBook("Cavalry report 3", "Titus de Sola", "1st of Amber Cold, 1518.\n\nHorse of 500 under command of Augustus the Iron Decurion led a cavalry maneuver around the Adrian Trident, armed with lance and mace, to flank around the north of Barrowyk.\n\nIt was hoped that assorted\nmilitia and lone knights would be encountered and lynched, but most were already within the safety of the Vladovic walls.  The Decurion's horse relocated to a position of flat ground whilst several scouts baited the castle garrison successfully.\nCocky and bringing their finest equipment, expecting imminent triumph, the Decurion's horse pincered and shred through their lines of hubris, slaying several members of House Vladov and taking their equipment for themselves.\n\nTo be stored in the archives.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cave Chickens", "Kirrekith", "Cave Chickens\n\n   Kirrekith Reffahc\n~                        ~\n       A Summary\n\nBooks to complete the set.\n\nEin eron Melkan\nRikkin eron da Ein\nMelkanrumm Ein\nAnnaein\nA cave chicken was once a domesticated animal, once an animal discovered within jungles and forests and once part of a larger food source for most of the races. Chickens were usually used for their source of food be that in meat, feathers\n--->\nfor arrows or their eggs.\n\nA cave chicken is however, far from this. These creatures developed within the walls of Kal’Akash. It was well documented to these dates that chickens bread and thrived in the dark\n--->\nwarm walls of dwarven society, only now have they changed.\n\nTerminology\n~                        ~\nAfter the outbreak, various states of cave chicken were witnessed, with many different traits and appearances. To begin with, there was the traditional chicken (fem or male), seeming as large as a normal\n--->\nchicken. Then came the Alpa Cave Chicken, which could control the flock around it, and was larger than a chicken, more to the height of 4ft or 5ft. Then came the behemoth, which rose to the height of at least 15ft or more. Above this… Is a\n--->\nunknown Cave chicken, of unknown size and origin, considered the first of its kind; the Brood Chicken, considering a behemoths size… This must be larger than that.\nBiology and Habit\n~                        ~\nCave chickens vary in sizes dependant on their stage of growth. These creatures are however, unmistakably carnivores, having a desire to eat anything that is easy prey, though… They will move up the\n--->\nfood chain with their size and also will change diet dependant on what is available. They can begin with mice, rats, cats, dogs… Then larger prey.\n\nUsually these creatures live for a few years, their lives shortened with their \n--->\nsize, the only exception being possibly the Brood Chicken, though we have no confirmation of her existence. The males of this species, grow to Alpha chickens, possessing a longer set of plumage and tail. However like with most cave\n--->\nchickens the tail feathers and nearly all other feathers have been lost, though a distinct fleshy stump remains. Of the cave chicken subspecies most lack any feathers, as to why is unknown, most taking on a thicker outer flesh or hide.\n--->\nAs well as this their feet bare sharper talons, with others either bearing carnivorous beaks or serrated beaks allowing for the ripping of flesh.\nBehaviour\n~                        ~\nSocial Behaviour,\n\nThe social dynamic of the cave chicken has been hard to observe due to most researchers or those misfortunate to be too close to them being eaten.\n--->\nWhat has been seen by most of the witnesses, is that, and alpha often leads a pack of these animals, though on occasion a alpha will be lead by a behemoth cave chicken. \n\nThe social attitude between the animals is --->\nless than friendly, should one fall victim to disease or ailment, they’re swiftly killed and eaten, to ensure the pack and colony remains strong. \n\nWe remain uncertain as to whether a Brood Cave Chicken or “Mother Hen” has\n--->\ninfluence upon these, a few researchers believe they do, as do I, however without sufficient material or research advancing in our understanding is hard.\n\nAn area we can clearly identify is power structure,\n--->\noften never question by chickens on the hunt, the animals power structure is.\n\nBrood Cave Chicken\n-\nBehemoth\n-\nAlpha\n-\nCave Chicken\nCourtship\n~                        ~\n\nThis remains an area we are uncertain of, speculation remains that the largest behemoth has breeding rights to a Brood Cave Chicken, though at this point is purely speculation.\nNesting and Laying\n        Behaviour\n~                        ~\n*UNKNOWN*\nBroodiness\n~                        ~\n*UNKNOWN*\nHatching and Early\n            Life\n~                        ~\n*UNKNOWN*\nBreeding\n~                        ~\n*UNKNOWN*\nOrigins\n~                        ~\nThe cave chicken is most certainly of relation to the domesticated chicken, baring all the similarities of origin species. However as described above, their appearances and nature has been\n--->\nsignificantly warped to one of a carnivorous and ruthless subspecies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cave Trees.", "[Yemekar's Pick] Elder Falent Ireheart", "After more exploration, me and my father have found what seems to be a forest, in a cave, underwater atop another cave full of trees underwater. It was a remarkable area with an astonishing site.\n\n        ~Falent Ireheart", ""),
