        StaticBook("Complete Job", "Ae'ris Leithwin", "Jobs - Assigned to\n\nFlapman - Lerald Vyronov. Ordered 250 Stacks of Oak / Spruce Logs.\n3 days deadline. started 13/11/15\n\nAccepted - payout 1250.\nMember pay 500\n\nGathered: 258/250\nGamerCrimson Delivered: 13\nGathered: 127\nItisme_\nGathered: 32\n\nVoid - Released from duty -\nNanoninja23 - Donated: 5.5\n\nDonated - Void payment\nDuckerDuck -\nGathered - 77\nPaid:\nDuckerduck: 154\nGamerCrimson: 254", ""),
        StaticBook("Conjuration", "Haadi Mubdee", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=           Conjuration\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=\nAh, Conjuration; the rarest Arcane Art known… well, it won’t be rare anytime soon. Of course, once you begin to learn the art, you will be referred to as a “Conjurer”. A conjurer is an individual who access the Void and construct living organisms which\nare fueled wholly by the mana of their creator. Through the depths of the void, a Conjuration user will be able to summon a mighty creatures of placid flowers into reality. Alas, as a conjurer you will be constantly delivering your mana for virtually\nvery second your ersatz summon exists. You will soon come to a realisation that Conjuration uses the most of your mana unlike any other Arcane Science. In order to uphold the existence of your faux creature in reality, you must feed it prescisely a great\nportion of mana to flow within it. As the creature you summon will be downright complex, the process of building it within the Void will be rather tiresome and there is a good chance you may be drained completely of your mana until you reach\nunconsciousness, as that happens, your beast will be removed from the physical realm and be sent back to the Void. Yes, you can decide to desist the flow of mana beforehand, in which case the fauna will vanish to no consequence. Now, for you to construct\nan organism within the Void, you must first have a sharp and great understanding of both the interior and exterior of the living you wish to formulate. This can be achieved by oftenly killing and dissecting the creature you wish to summon. However, it is\nalso best to keep very detailed anatomical diagrams of the beast you wish to conjure. Remember to have note son the animal’s exterior, interior and bone structure if you want to have an accurate understanding of it. In the opaque Void, the fabrics which\ngenerate the entity are summoned bone by bone, layer by layer, muscle by muscle and organ by organ the Conjurer crafts and sculpts their being into an exact copy of their previously existing self. As a result of poor research, the Conjurer may fail at\nthis point, producing a being unlike that of its true and real form will result in an uneven and revolting entity which would certainly turn to a sludge once conjured. After a while of practice, the Conjurer would be able to summon the creature exactly\nhow it was before it was slain and have it formed with sheer stability. As it will behave akin to the life form it represents, it will follow its creator’s commands. As a Conjurer myself, I would highly recommend you begin to study roses, then petite\ninsects until you grow stronger and confident enough to move on to study and conjure anything larger. Think of Conjuration as art. You are the painter and the Void is the frame. What you paint in that frame will need to look beautiful and make sense in\nthe judge’s eyes. Bear in mind that the “judge” is the physical realm. If the judge thinks your work of  art is good, it will be accepted and be brought into reality. However, if it’s horrible and ugly, it will be stamped on and crushed and it will appear\nas an abomination in the mortal plane, you will be smacked in the face for your poor efforts, that smack will tire you. Keep practicing and your artistic skills will improve and the judge will begin and continue to accept your art. Overtime, your frame\nwill expand and leave you open to produce which the judge can view. Be warned though, the larger the harder. And yes, you can fabricate hybrid fauna. I’ll leave that for you to grasp the concept of that alone.\nAuthor: Unknown\nCopied by Guildmaster Haadi Mubdee of the Mages Guild, 1461.", ""),
        StaticBook("Conjuration", "Mythras Sylvari", "Conjuration:\n          \nConjuration, is the bringing of life forms formed in the void by the conjurationist, into the world itself.\n\nThe three sub-magicks of Conjuration, are.\n- Primodrialism\n- Perenial\n- Morphonic\nMorphon, is the conjuring of animals, and the creating of them as a entity. \n\nIt's to bring a animal into existence, after lots of study put into the animals insides, and outsides, essentially, interior or exterior.\nPerenial, is the conjuring of plant life, after the study of the interior and exterior workings, to do such, is the arcane art of the conjuring of perenials.\n\nEssentially, the conjuring of a studied plant.\nPrimordial, is the bringing of elementals into the physical plain.\n\nYou must be learned in the art of evocation, and the added art of conjuration.\n\nIt's essentially summoning creatures made of your arcane element.\nConjuration, is as said, a hard art, the many theories enacted suggest slowness in the power of the art.\n\nTo evoke animals and plants, and even elementals, is a valuable skill.\nSources:\n\n- Goliath\n- Random Magician \n- Learnings in delver bas.\n\n- Inquisition\n- Theories", ""),
        StaticBook("Conspirators", "Siegfried de Jaeger", "Khendu Annunaki\nGambino's\nMayor of Felsen\n\nOwn majority of Felsens key buildings, Bank, Markets, Taverns, Cathedral?\nS.G Merchant group.\n\nAccess to the Imperial Palace. \n\nHigh risk.. Very Dangerous men, not to be underestimated", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 1", "Catarrh", "The Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHear what mi blah, young one, for mi blah lat h’dub honors by which the orc lives, agh h’dub pillars on which he stands.\n\nSTRENGTH\nVALOR\nBOLDNESS\nCONTENTMENT\nWISDOM\nFORTHRIGHTNESS\nDISCIPLINE\n\nStrength is the simplest honor. It is by nub means easy to attain, but very easy to lose. It comes with the weight of earth, yet drifts away on the currents of the river from the unwary. Yet, for he who keeps watch, it\nstands firm as iron. By it, the body stands strong. Without it, the bones fall as dry reeds. By the strong outer self, the strong inner self is protected.\n\nValor is that which compels us to stand. By it, we face our enemies agh conquer our fears. Turn nub\nfrom the challenges of life. Cower nub before latz foes. Stand agh face those who oppose lat.\n\nBoldness is that energy by which we charge into the flames. Be unafraid of risk. It is the gate to many rewards. As valor makes us stand our ground,\nboldness commands us to press forward.\n\nContentment is the key to satisfaction. Trust nub in wealth, for gold flees as the sands on the night winds. Trust nub in land, for many lands agh whole continents have been lost before this ash. Be content with\nlatz lusk agh latz bread. If you have a blarg, a mate, agh cubs, lat be truly blessed beyond measure.\n\nWisdom is born of a strong mind. It is more practical than philosophy, agh goes beyond mere knowledge. It is the ability for right living, common sense,\nwit, resolution of life’s problems, agh success beyond material gain. Gruk for latself, but heed the blahings of those more experienced with the respect agh consideration due them. Learn from life, agh apply latz learning in a way that means something.\nForthrightness is honesty agh directness. It is intentional clarity of blahing, agh the absence of deception. Blah truth. Blah to blah, nub to flatter. Do as lat blah, agh let latz blah be latz bond. If lat blah it, mean it. Live it\n\nDiscipline is that\nwhich keeps latz life in order. Without it, all other honors forsake lat, for honor demands that the honorable governs his life with the will of iron. Hard work agh control of the self hold body agh mind together.\n\nStand firm in all these things, agh lat\nwill stand indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 2", "Catarrh", "The second book of the Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka, agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHeed mi warning, all who are wise, for mi blah lat h’dub dishonors by which an orc is ruined, agh h’dub shames which may befall him.\n\nWEAKNESS\nIRRESOLUTION\nCOWARDICE\nAVARICE\nTHOUGHTLESSNESS\nDUPLICITY\nCOMPLACENCY\n\nWeakness, blah’d plainly, is the absence of strength. Be nub frail, agh neglect nub the body. He who can-nub defend himself, how can he defend that for which he stands? To give place to weakness is\nto keep latz bub’hoshest treasure in a fortress of straw.\n\nIrresolution is the way of he who falters in the presence of adversity. Do nub quail when the storm thunders. Do nub turn away when latz enemies roar. Be nub like the rabbit, who, when he is\nfrightened but a little, flees to his hole for safety. The rabbit is prey, agh the orc must never be prey.\n\nCowardice halts the feet, agh binds the spirit. Nub hosh thing comes to the coward, for the coward takes nub risk. The coward never takes the\ndifficult path. There is no success for such an ash. All his ways are worthless, agh his life profitless.\n\nAvarice is the heart of the empty spirit. Lust for gold blinds the eyes to truth, agh numbs the mind to wisdom. It makes the senses dull, such that\nhe whose life is governed by the mina can-nub perceive honor, agh hears nub the call of Krug.\n\nThoughtlessness is to the mind as weakness is to the body. The ash who gruks nub is nub’hosher than the blind or the deaf, for he chooses himself nub to gruk\nthe way to live rightly. He is blind to the way in which he should walk, agh the advice of the wise enters nub his ear. All his workings are senseless, agh his feet lead him to shame.\n\nDuplicity is the forked tongue of the dishonorable. The duplicitous\nash blahs “yub” with his mouth, but “nub” in his spirit. His blah can-nub be trusted, for he is a serpent agh a companion to serpents. With his face he grins agh flatters, but behind his back he bears a double-edged dagger to betray lat. Do nub be like\nsuch an ash, for the number of those who will hear him dwindles by the hour.\n\nComplacency is the quicksand upon which the glob builds a blarg. It is a hosh-smelling poison, agh a smooth road which leads to ruin. Complacency lulls lat to sleep with a soft\ntouch agh sweet songs, but, when lat have awoken, it has stolen latz strength, latz mate, agh all latz bread.\n\nThe ash who falls into any of these falls surely agh quickly to his destruction.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contract", "Iat", "Haadi Mudbee, Caliph Court Mage, is contracted to instruct Iatrilemar Elervathar on the arcane form known as voidal translocation. In return the Maheral of Haelun'or shall pass over his knowledge on the arcane form known as voidal shifting until a time\nthat he is able to instruct Haadi Mudbee on the subject.\n\nSigned,\n\nIatrilemar Elervathar,\nMaheral of Haelun'or\n\nHaadi Mubdee, Court Sahooru of the Caliphate", ""),
        StaticBook("Contract", "Lily Potter", "I, Lily Potter, sign here on the date of the 21st of the First Seed, 1570 stating that I am forever in the debt of Mr. Dan Cooper. In return for this agreement being signed, I will be given residence at Ross Road 4 in Felsen. If for any reason Dan Cooper\nchooses, he may evict me from the property which he owns. No matter through death, obstacle, or tragedy, I, Lily Potter, fall in the debt of Dan Cooper, the drafter of this contract and giver of this home. I still retain my freedom, but fall at the\nservice and good hand of Dan Cooper. I, Lily Potter, am not slave nor whore, and am not forced to break the laws of Felsen and the Empire of Oren under this contract. I still have control over my minas, though Dan Cooper can demand a reasonable sum\nspecifically for rent and for no other purposes, if he decides to. My soul and fate is now intertwined with Dan Cooper's, and with a drop of blood counting as a signature, this contract begins.\n\n[!] A drop of blood stains the page.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contract", "Fuze Yaander", "16th Snow Maiden, 1556, On this day I, Petyr Barbanov, sign this contract with the Dark Water Mercenary Guild.\n\n-The Dark Water Mercenary Guild will receive land to build a guild hall.\n-The Dark Water Mercenary Guild will receive 2 suits of armor\nevery Saint's week.\n-The Dark Water Mercenary Guild will not take on contracts against Petyr Barbanov's interests.\n-The Dark Water Mercenary Guild will put this contract before others so Petyr Barbanov may call upon them if needed.\nFailure to comply with the stated terms will result in a voided contract.\n\nSigned,\n\nPetyr Barbanov\nSigned,\n\nFuze Yaander", ""),
        StaticBook("COoK", "Harrrison", "mI     N aM e\n        i           Z\n\n        C O o K", ""),
        StaticBook("Copied Book", "Monk Scribe", "*Many parts of the book seem missing, but it appears to be a copy. Clearly the book it was coppied from was not complete.*\n\nWriten by the Third Elder Monk, in the year 109. Many pages are missing in the original.\n…..the female Aengul proceeded to leave, Aeriel and the Wizard were indeed distraught. The system collapsing before their own eyes…… Odion was called for guidance. It is reported that the Daemon’s stone halls spat flames like a baneslither when he heard\nof this dissent. They rushed to find that the portal had already closed, making it impossible to trace the followers of the Dark Lady, as Monk John was apt to call her.\n\nAeriel decreed that the ethereal spirits must refrain from the constant contact with\nthe Descendant Races as to avoid further mishaps such as this. Some of the Daemons who had befri…..d mortals were angered and left the realm as well, while the remaining Daemons and the majority of Aenguls decided to abide by thi….., each in their own way\nIt did seem that Aeriel, as well as the Wiz……………….which some did not……… ……and throughout Aegis, the monks destroyed all tomes other than……much to his dismay. The Wizard was quite upset with the actio………. though it was all for a grand cause, indeed.\nHe later came to be glad for Aeriel’s decision, for………… efforts were certainly successful for the most part, as is apparent in society, and the account o…………not fully untrue, naturally, yet th………… only to be preserved within this room by the Scarlet Monks", ""),
        StaticBook("Copy request", "Reeg", "Name: Jack Dolen\nDate:\n11th of the Deep Cold\n1565\nBook Donated: Alchemy Recipies ((by connor428))\nBook Copy wished for:\nIllusion Theory by Valmir Audane", ""),
        StaticBook("Cordal Paradiso1", "Farley III Stafyr", "Cordal's Paradiso\n\n   A Journey to the\n       Seven Skies\n\n  Written by Cordal\n             Winter\nCordal Winter was in a coma for many days. When he awoke, he had an amazing story to tell. You see, while his body remained in the mortal plane, his soul wandered the heavens. This is the story of his journey, written with the grace of God.\nI felt myself ascending suddenly. I no longer felt the blow to my head. I no longer felt anything at all. I looked down and saw my quivering, mortal form upon the floor of the basement, pooled with crimson.\nStrangely I felt no unhappiness or discomfort. No- rather I felt a feeling of elation and happiness. I floated further and further upward, into the sky. Past the sky, as the churches and apartments and shining palaces of Kaldonia\ndisappeared underneath me. The light slowly faded from my vision, and it was as if I was a child, floating within a vast womb. Darkness was everywhere. All of a sudden a white, pure light winked into existence, calling me.\nI floated towards it, drawn to its irresistible clarion call. As I was about to enter, Two pairs of hands grabbed me, stopping me from entering. I fought against the hands, but they gentled me, and I turned to see two aenguls.\nThey had one pair of wings each, so they were minor, not yet having earned more pairs of wings. One was blond of the purest honey, the other’s hair like polished silver. It was the only difference between the two. The blonde spoke first.\n“Halt your struggle, Cordal Winter. It is not your time yet. You have is a different purpose.”   Of course, I was greatly confused. The silver haired one then spoke in an equally melodious voice.\n“Our Creator has set to you a task- you must gaze upon the glories of the Seven Skies, and bring His message to the mortals He so cares for.”   My mind whirled.\n“Why has He chosen me, a lowly priest, for this great task? Why could not the good Bishop Henry, or his eminence have been chosen?”   The aenguls boomed in anger.\n“It is not yours to question your Creator! Do as His Blessed command states!”   If I were not stricken with panic, I surely would have whimpered. The golden haired aengul spoke.\n“Ah mortal… You are so young, and uncomprehending. I am Beatus, and this is the esteemed Armis. We will guide you through the Seven Skies, and return you to your mortal vessel when finished.”\nI could only nod as they bore me through the holy, sweet light. I felt euphoria as I went in, but this changed as I looked upon the First Sky. Aloft they held me by each arm as I looked across the  blasted, twisted landscape.\nEverywhere there were souls in torment. No torment in our mortal realm can compare to some of the things I have seen in the First Sky. I howled in terror.\n\n  “Why have you brought me to this place!”   I shrieked.\nArt thou aenguls unholy demons, taking me to the Nether!” The aenguls, perturbed, shook their heads. \n\n “This is the First Sky. All souls go to this place, for a certain amount of time. Their sins are washed clean in torment and\nand pain. Only the pure can ascend onwards.”   I passed a long line of what looked to be men of the Raev. They were being repeatedly dipped in boiling lead. I shuddered and inquired Armis about them. The silver haired aengul  happily answered my\nquestion.   “These are the traitors to the High Pontiff, who fought the Lucienists. They will be here longer than most… But not forever. Though they committed unholy treason, all of them were good and loyal men to their liege lord.\nSoon they will ascend, likely to the Fourth Sky.”   I nodded, pleased that these men would not be in torment forever. The Aenguls took me higher and higher, until the landscape of the First Sky dwindled to nothing.\nWe were in a sea of white light, it grew brighter and brighter until suddenly the aenguls shot upwards into the Second Sky.\nThe Second Sky was far different from the first. It was a land of rolling green plains, but no trees. It was also slightly gloomy, not well lit, as if from a rainy sky. There weren’t many people around. It was far less populous than the First Sky.\n“What is the nature of this Sky, O Beatus and Armis?” I asked. They set me down on the ground, which was as firm as that of the mortal world. I began to stride about as they alighted, walking behind me.\n“This is the plane for virtuous heathens,”   said Beatus, “Those who did not follow the True Faith, but still did courageous feats.” I began to walk, heading first for a muscular looking dwarf. He had a tough, mean look about him.\n“Hello.”   I said, interested. The dwarf grunted. “What is your name?” I asked.\n\n  “Urir Ireheart.”   he said. “This wasn’t what oi feckin expected when oi died. Where tae feck is Dungrimm’s halls?”\nI was taken aback. Urir Ireheart, the dwarf who plunged the Axe of Krug into the Nether and so saved Aegis. He refused to speak to me any further, so I moved on. There I saw a tall, proud, southern looking man.\nHe was surrounded by a few others that looked like him, and was clothed in leather, with some gold jewelry. He smiled at me as I approached.\n\n  “A visitawr! Welcawm to thar Secawnd Sky!”   he said.\nIt was quite a different reaction from before.\n\n  “What is your name?”   I asked. The man smiled.\n\n“Khagan Sauros, awf thar Subudai. How fare my people?” I frowned slightly. Sauros?\nThe Khagan that tormented Oren in its early days? Still, he seemed amiable, so I told him.\n\n  “The House Nicator has the blood of the Subudai in them, but your people are scattered or dead.” Sauros sighed.\n“Sertorious told me as much, I had hoped they were refawrged.”   he gestured to another man who looked much like him. I sighed and looked to the aenguls. They once again gently grabbed me by each arm, and their great wings flexed upwards.\nThe grassy plains of the Second Sky shrank beneath us as we went upwards into the Third Sky. \n\nWhen we suddenly appeared, I was rather intrigued to see a sprawling city, with a cloudy blue sky overhead.\n“What is this city?”   I asked. It was Armis who responded.\n\n“This is the eternal city of Vetus, in the Third Sky.” In the streets of the city I saw many mortal activities. People wandered through the streets, talking and laughing.\nIt looked a bit like Kaldonia, and Arethor. Very… normal. I inquired as to why it seemed so earthly.\n\n  “Vetus is a city for those who did nothing impious nor pious, good nor bad, in their lives.\nThey were content with just living, and this is their reward.”   said Beatus. We moved on quickly from this plane. There was certainly nobody of note here, and it was not very interesting.\nWhen we ascended into the Fourth Sky, I was completely overwhelmed by what I saw. This was the Seven Skies of prophecy. I had never before seen something like it. The entire place was a vast rolling grassland, not unlike the Second Sky.\nHowever, the earth was rich and smelled of fine new soil. Trees sprouted majestically every so often. Tables sprawled over the landscape, lit with many candles, for the entire place was bathed in the glow of the evening.\nFood, a grand feast, was laid out over all the tables, and peasant looking fellows feasted, drank, and laughed. As they ate and drank, the food and beverages reappeared. On a throne sat a man, surrounded by pigeons.\nThey chattered when they saw us approaching. Next to him sat a man covered in coal dust.\n\n  “What is this place?”   I asked the aenguls.\n“This is the Fourth Sky, home of those who were loyal to their masters, and those who worked hard to accomplish many great things. The Fourth Sky is inhabited by the hardworking peasants of Raevir blood, Auvergnian blood, and even a\nfew Easterners can be found here.”\n\n“Why is it the evening here?”\n\n  “Because,”   said Armis, “The evening is when the peasant man truly shows himself. It is when he is happiest.\nThe working day is over and he casts off his cloak and boots and makes merry with friends and family.”\n\n  “And the man on the throne?”   I inquired.\n\n\"That is Saint Bogdanistan. He was offered a place in\nthe Sixth Sky, but turned it down to join his people here. Next to him is Saint Hunwald.”   I was delighted to learn this, and spent many an hour drinking and making merry with the many peasants. I know a bit of Raev, and have a complete knowledge of\nAuvergnian, and was able to have a grand time. At one point in my feasting, I was pulled aside by Saint Bodganistan. I immediately bowed before him in piety, as was my duty. His son, Vladislavistan, beamed at me. I was surprised to see him.\n“Good Vladislav, why are you not in the First Sky with the rest of your brothers?”   I asked. Vladislav chuckled.   “Because our time is of up!”   I watched in amazement as the Raev men suddenly ascended into the Fourth Sky, popping up from holes in the\nthe ground. They seemed untouched by the horrible treatment they had received in the First Sky, joking and laughing with their friends in good humor. I was truly amazed by the Creator’s infinite mercy. The two aenguls laughed, a\ntinkling, joyous sound that I will remember forever. I feasted a while longer in the Fourth Sky, speaking with its hardworking inhabitants, before I turned to the aenguls and told them I was ready to depart.\nThey gave a nod and grabbed me once more, taking me up into the Fifth Sky. The Fifth Sky was more of what I had expected of the Seven Skies. It was an endless ivory palace, with majestic red carpets and flowing tapestries telling the deeds of the\ninhabitants. The greatest heroes who had ever followed the True Faith gathered in the great hall and chatted with each other, reminiscing about times long past. I saw the High Pontiffs. Lucienists mingled with Oren guard.\nMost prevalent was the banner of the White Rose. So many men had fought and died under that banner as to make almost any man who was once a member of that hallowed brotherhood worthy of the Fifth Sky.\nI first sought out the company of one who was wearing the High Pontiff’s miter. I introduced myself as Father Cordal Winter, and he laughed.   “So, one of the Winters is a priest? Never thought I’d see the day. I am High Pontiff Lucien. The first one,\nused to be called Velwyn Ashford. Har! I’m glad to see my brothers here with me.”   at this the hallowed man gestured to the many White Roses strewn about the room. “I’ve been watching the church from here, my son.”\n“You can see all that?”   I asked in surprise. Lucien laughed.\n\n“Indeed! We on the Fifth Sky can watch the mortal realm, unlike those in the Fourth Sky and below. It’s a part of our reward.”", ""),
        StaticBook("Cordal Paradiso2", "Farley III Stafyr", "I knelt and kissed the Pontiff’s ring in submission and farewell, and he bid me to continue. On my way traversing the court I accidentally bumped into a particular white rose member.\n“Yeesh! Watch where yer goin!”   he said. I nodded, making an apology. He looked me over, then bowed. “Sorry, fathah. Didn’t know you were a man of the cloth.” The White Rose member himself was a rather scarred individual with a large... mohawk, I\nbelieve the word was. He stuck out his callused hand.e… mohawk, I believe the word was. He stuck out his callused hand. “I’m Arthal Lowedge. Good to meet you Fathah…”\n\n “Cordal Winter, Father Cordal Winter, good Ser.”\nArthal chuckled, then I went on my way. The aenguls awaited me. I felt a knot of apprehension in my stomach as we flew away from the ivory palace of the Fifth Sky. We were heading to the Sixth Sky. What would lie in the Seventh?\nI was almost done with my journey.\n\nWe shot into the Sixth Sky, and I was immediately enveloped in a feeling of euphoria. Golden light shone everywhere.\nA choir of aenguls and daemons sang, lifting their voices. Armis and Beatus joined in, and my head felt as if it were to split from happiness. Flowing rivers of milk and fine wine poured in an unending torrent.\nGemstones and rich pearls dotted the riverbanks. Ripe fruit hang from magnificent trees. We touched down on a cloud. It was solid, but soft, like the wool of a sheep. I could jump very high here, and I bounced from cloud to cloud\nas a child would bounce from one bed to another. A large cloud held a good number of folk, so I went there. They seemed ready to greet me. At the front stood an elderly man with a majestic crown, and white flowing beard and hair.\n“Welcome to the Sixth Sky, Cordal Winter.”   he said gravely. My knees immediately bent. I was unable to think as I was confronted with Saint Godfrey, the First Emperor, the Uniter of Mankind. He smiled slightly at me as another being strode forward,\na white glowing stag. It’s presence made me feel as comforted and healed as Saint Godfrey’s. I assumed this to be Tahariae. The stag bent its head to me in greeting, but did not speak.\nAnother man joined Godfrey at his right hand. He also wore the crown of the emperor. \"Ej, Winter.”   he said. “Never of expected to see Herendulman here.”\nMy humility grew by the second in the presence of Saint Siegmund. Another man stepped forward, at Godfrey’s left. He wore the White Rose tabard proudly. “Be nice to our guest, Siegmund,”   said Saint Thomas Chivay,\n“We don’t get many guests here. Get on up, Winter.” I could only nod dumbly as I stood. Saint Thomas laughed. “You look like a man who just shit himself.” I closed my mouth as my cheeks turned red. Saint Godfrey gave a slight shake of the head to Thomas.\n“Cordal Winter. Are you prepared to meet your Creator?”   I shuddered in fear involuntarily.\n\n  “So… that is what is on the Seventh Sky?”   I asked. Saint Godfrey nodded. I shook with nervousness, but clenched my fists\nand returned his nod. He smiled.\n\n  “The aenguls will be unable to accompany you there. It is only for you, and the Creator.”   The Saints and Aenguls all backed away as I felt myself being lifted up into the air, their faces fast\ndwindling. The chorus of aenguls reached a crescendo, and suddenly there was silence.\nThe Seventh Sky. White. Enveloping, soothing white. I could not see any part of me. Did I even exist? Who could have stood before the crushing, yet merciful embrace I felt all around me? The love of the Creator\ncushioned me from all my memories, all the harshness of life. I could see nothing, I could sense nothing but that love. Visions suddenly appeared before me. I saw Beatus and Armis in the Sixth Sky, gaining a second pair of wings as their reward.\nBeatus would now have the status of the Aengul of Writers, and Armis the Aengul of Swordsmen and Knights. I saw the Fifth Sky, where heroes continued to feast and chat. The Fourth Sky, boisterous and loud.\nThe Third Sky, with those individuals who just floated through life. The Second Sky, with the virtuous heathens, who possessed such bravery without any True Faith, and the horrors of the First Sky.\nI saw the life of a man named Cordal Winter, who had grown up in Herendul. I saw Kaldonia, and the entire world of Aegis. I saw the sun and the stars in all their glory. All these things I saw.\nThen the whiteness began to fade to grey, then black, as a voice as vast as the ocean, but as quiet as the dropping of a pin spoke.\n\n             \"Home.\"\n             \n             I awoke.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cornfield song", "Judas Windsor", "________________________ \n\n        Song: I've been working on the cornfield\n\n-Judas Windsor.\n\n________________________\nI've been working on the cornfield all the live long day.\n\nI've been working on the cornfield just to pass the time away, can't you hear the bell ringing? Rise up so early in the morning.\nCan't you hear the captain shouting Dinah Blow your horn.\n\nChorus:\n\nDinah wont you blow?\n\nDinah Wont you blow\n\nDinah wont your ho-ho-horn. repeat x2\nSomeones with dinah, someones in the kitchen I kno-ow-ow singing Fee Fi Fiddly Aye o, fee fi fiddly aye o. Someones in the kitchen with Dinah!\n\nStrummin on the Ol Banjo...\n\nRepeat top paragraph x3", ""),
        StaticBook("Coven Inspection", "Ularoth", "Assessment of           the Iblees Coven\n\n           Ularoth\nOur trek begins within an abandoned complex carved beneath the outskirts of Alras. Upon our entry into the quaint cavern, we heard distinctly nothing; The dwelling has been long abandoned. Left standing in the strange pit of offal and rock appears to\nbe a heavyset table of lackluster quality. It sounds of splintering wood, its innards eaten away by woodworms and their ilk. The chairs that accompany the furnishing are in just as awful a shape. The thought of a gathering of naive cultists squirming\nuncomfortably in their seats amuses us. Upon the table rests a tattered board that sounds and tastes of driftwood, no doubt fished from a river. Its edges seem caked with a thin grime of taint, once carved intricately in beguiling sigils now rests on the\noutskirts of the plank in unsightly blobs of vile. Letters are etched in the board's surface, scrawled lazily in three strokes of a dull pike, at most. Wedged in a hastily dug pocket of stone lies a shape of wood, cut from the same as the board, with a\nglassen port wedged center-most.\n\nMoving away from the table, We've noticed a hallway-esque expanse to our right, whereupon a mound of soot rests. It smells of bone, the intense heat that surely singed a mound of bodies that once resided where\nthis dust dwells seemed hot enough to dissapate fetid flesh into vapor. The numerous rats that have since taken refuge in this place seem to avoid this mound of dead. We too are vaguely offput by it.\nFurther down the hallway resides nothing but a sturdy end, accompanied by a stoney pillar which bares no intrigue.\n\nResiding in the midst of this place are several chests which reek of rot. Further inspection has rendered the bins\nvastly unintriguing, as only decomposing plantlife dwells within.\n\nThe cavern-like expansive to our left has been bored into thrice, all along the right walls. We may dwell within this place after our inspection is completed. The three hovel-sized\nrooms contain a stark nothing. Further meandering has caused us to come across a single room dug into the left of the wall; our apologies.\n\n\nDeeper in the cavern is a strange chamber, slathered hastily with sigils drawn of offal.\nIts centre seems to hold a forge of strange architecture, with a shallow indent carved in the floor just about a beam of glass. One would best compare this to something of Urukai construction, albeit of rock. The small chamber remains barren apart from\nthe strangness previously mentioned. We shall scribe the glyphs that adorn the walls after the entirety of our assessment.\n\nSo to will we scrawl the sigils drawn into the floor with the same gore found amoungst the 'ritual' chamber.\n-A strange sigil comprised of a circle trapping many a piece of odd geometry is drawn here in a thick, piney sludge. The entirety of the glyph seems to resemble some sort of crucifix turned on its head-\nThe most daunting of the subterranian abode's sigils. Its relative size dwarfs the rest of its siblings. It resides on the leftmost wall of the assumed ritual chamber. It evokes a calm within us; something reassuring.\n-Another glyph is drawn, in the same ichor no less. This one vaguely depicts a conjuring fire, which a primative body lurches over menacingly. Four lines impale the otherwise lackluster rune, adorn at their ends with what appear to be eyes-\nThis dwells the backmost wall of the ritual chamber. Its paint-thick fluid seems to grasp more particulate than most. We believe it to be soot, or fine sand. Its texture is bone dry, and has chipped to our louder inspections.\n-Yet another sigil is scribed in piney ichor, accompanied by occasional streaks of ash. Its relative shape is all but a mystery, wavering this way and that with bizzare connections linking the irredeemably baffling structure together-\nWe're not sure what to make of this, its quite oddly placed. It lies near the central support beam of the cave. We can't stand to hear it much, it prods at us with a sense of unease.\nThe remainder of the scrawlings we've deemed uninteresting. They are far too simple to rival the three we've already found. If someone wishes, you may contact ourselves to delve into a further study of this place.", ""),
        StaticBook("Craftfair Letter", "Siri", "Greetings honoured guest!\n\nI am Siri, Guildmaster of Laureh'lin. The Province of Laureh'lin is interested in hosting a Arts and Craft fair within the foreseeable future, and would like to extend an invitation to you and your people!\nThe fair is scheduled within the next 3 years, probably after a new district has been made. But we are currently gathering interest for the idea, and would like to invite the skilled craftsmen and women of your people to show off in this fair with either\nskills, goods, or just to get to know other craftsman from other regions. \n\nI hope you will respond to this letter.\n\nSincerely, Siri", ""),
        StaticBook("Creatures by Ork", "Eirik Ireheart", "Notice: These books are rushed copies of tomes in the library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. The following was originally written by an Ork, translated to\nview the modicum of Ork culture inside.\n\"Disclaimer: Whomever is reading this must know that this book about the various forms and types of creatures and races. Thank you for reading this book. Also, I wrote a lot of it in a sewer.\nChapter One: The Halfings.\n\nHalflings are weird. They are small. You can through them at walls. But, there is more to them than just mutalation. In this chapter, you will learn of the more sophisticated lifestyles of Halflings. The have a complex\nthat you wouldn't excpect. Firstly, it turns out that Halflings don't live in holes. Well, they kind of do, but they are called burrows. These burrows are actually quite nice and decorated. This is of course if you can even fit in it. Other than killing\nthem, Halflings are useful for trading, as I met many Halfling traders on the roads. They are usually very nice creaturs, but they're so mall that we like to make fun of them whenever we see them. Also, Halflings make for good Bartenders, that is, if they\ncan even reach the counter, yes?\n\nChapter Two: The Dwarves\n\nRecently, I learned about the Halflings- Small, ugli, and weak creatures they are. To understand a Dwarf is to understand alcohol.\nYou see, these 'Dwarves' fill their holes with beer. Lots and lots of beer. They are a merry race, much so like the Halflings. They are also short like the Halflings. Unlike the Halflings, they are fatter, and they like to fight almost as much as we Orkos\ndo. Almost. To be honest, there is much to admire about these creatures. They are a breed of warriors. Of course, the Dwarves can't compare to the strength of an Orkos, but they seem to be stronger than even the biggest human. Much like us Orkos, Dwarves\nhold their honor to a huge extent. Both Orkos and Dwarves like to use axes and hammers. To be honest, Dwarves are like tiny, ugly, smelly, dumb Orkos in a way. I think that we should still kill them, but, we need to appreciate why they're so fun to kill\nand fight. Now, we're going to shift gears here, and switch to a taller race.\n\nChapter Three: The Elves\n\nThis race is one of a disgraceful sense of honor. The Elves think they're better than us. I mean, so do the Halflings, Dwarves,\nand other stuff, but the Elves seem to hate us even more. They are a group of creatures that think they are so beautiful and smart. But, I feel that in some ways, they actually are smart. You see, they may be finer, smellier, and dumber than us, but I\nthink that they in some way, deep inside, that Elves have some degree of endulgence. Perhaps Elves can make good weapons or armor, or even good buildings. But, Elves seem to grasp the art of Magic very well. Now, we are going to dive into the specific\ntypes of Elves.\n\nChapter Four: The High Elves.\n\nIt is this clan that sucks the most, in my opinion. They're the ones that REALLY think high about themselves. Considering it's in their names and such. These ones live long, look tall, are super\npale, drink the teas, eat the cakes, write the novels, mock the other races, do their fancy magic, waste time in making stuff pretty (Even their weapons!), and take their baths, and clean their [klofz] and ears, and that's pretty much it. Basically, they\nsuck.\n\nChapter Five: The Wood Elves.\n\nNasty Tree-huggers, that's what these Wood Elves are. Believe it or not, Wood Elves don't even use swords, axes, or even thereputic lavatorial papers. They use bows. And for lavatorial papers, I\nthink they use leaves. Also, Tree Elves are much like twigs. That's why another name for Elves in Blah is 'Twiggeh'. These Wood Elves are a bunch of pansies. They hide in the shadows to hunt for their prey. But, us Orkos hunt for our prey in the open,\npartly. Although, Wood Elves are good at sneaking around. I have not studied the Wood Elves much, be cause they are usually hiding from me. So, they're is still much to learn about them. Now, we're going to take a look at the gray ones.\n\nChapter Six: The\nDark Elves.\n\nThese Elves look like the nighttime skies themselves. They are pretty much gray and kind of blue. They are pretty modest, for Elves, that is. They seem like the most humble of the Elves. Just like they're mysterious appearance, not much\nhas been recorded of the Dark Elves. Maybe they're is, but they did not share it with me. So, I am just going to tell you about their physical appearance, rather than their real culture. They have dark skin, dark eyes, but they usually dress with pretty\nbold colors. Also, I mainly noticed piercings and gray hairs. So, I don't talk about the Elves, because they're PRETTY LAME. So, now, we're going to shift gears again and learn about the Humans.\n\nChapter Seven: The Northern Humans.\nThese are smelly, diplomatic, tiny, ugly, weak, dum, and really dumb. You know what we are talking about. The Humans. But, these are the Humans in the North. I gathered this information in the city of [Ubrezchi]. They are a complicated race, so I'm going\nto break this up into different categories. First, we are going to talk about how we see them, or how they look. Humans are shorter than Elves, and fatter than Dwarves. They call themselves 'HOO-MANZ' and don't call themselves 'Sharaz', because they are\nso dumb, they don't even know what it means. They spoke with me, and said that they have something called 'Pulektikz' (TN: Politics, most likely.) I think it's like the [Krughai] Confederation, but they said it was more ugly. Also, they are greedy, like\nDwarves, but they are not greedy for gold, but Minaz in its stead. And, they NEVER admit it. So, basically, the Northern Humans are more evil than I ever thought. As you already know, the [Uhbrezchi] Humans are our allies in most wars, because they are\nsome of the only ones who don't betray us. Now, we will look into Adunia.\n\nChapter Eight: Adunians\n\nThey're neat. I obtained this information from the King of Adunia himself, Jarl [Lazchlahn Moare Ilindul]. So as you can see, this book gave\nme the honor to meet countless officials in the world. Anyway, the Adunians are said to be the oldest. Their King told me that they were the first human around, making him much older than the Adunians. Adunians also have politics like the [Uhbrezchinz],\nbut their's is much different. You see, in their culture, the youngest born is the one whose destiny is to lead, unlike more popular cultures where the Elders lead. These Adunians have many different ranks, too, like a High Thane, and High Marshall. Also,\nthese creatures are the longest lived Humans around, because apparently they have Elven blood in their history. However, they don't seem like Elves. No, Adunians are still much bigger than them, as they are pretty tall and mighty.\n[!] *A few pages appear to have been misplaced, instead replaced by notes.*\n\nMayra,\n\nHow I miss you. Our son has just arrived in Khaz'Kazak, and seems ever the firebrand. He's got your nose. I only hope he does well with young Hogan.\n[!] *What seems to be a second sheet lays here as well.*\n\nAlarik: oxoooooooxoooxoooo Hathrid: xoxxxxxxxxx\nHogan: x\nDuren: ox\nMidgor: xx\nDrynn: xxx\nNora: xxox\nThereon: xxxxxxxxx\nleft right here in [Gronkkzton], in the [kiddun] district. But, they all moved to [Mahlinoare] now, probably because we Orkos were too strong for them. There are four types of Kha, and we're going to delve into all of them right now.\n\nChapter Ten: The\n[Tygur] Kha\n\nThese are the biggest of the Cat Creatures, and some of them are as big as an Ork. They look like [Tygurz], and they fight like them too. They are usually the Warriors of the Kha, and they are pretty dumb. I don't know much about them.\nChapter Eleven: The [Zcheetuh] Kha\n\nThese ones are the smallest, but unlike a fat Dwarf, they are REALLY fast. The [Zcheetuh] Kha look like [zcheetuhs], they have spots all over their skin. And to me, they make the best carpets. (TN: Yes. They do.)\nChapter Twelve: The Dark Kha\n\nThey look like [punturz] an they are sneaky, like [Punturz], too. Always look out for Dark Kha, because they can steel heaps of things at any moment. To me, they are rather like Dark Elves, strictly speaking. Sadly, that is\nall I know about the Dark Kha, seeing as Kha are mysterious and they did not let me learn about them.\n\nChapter Thirteen: The [Lepurd] Kha\n\nThese ones obviously look like [Lepurdz], but unlike the other Kha, these ones don't exceed in any\nspecific skillset, but they are the best suited for doing anything they set their heart on. They are bigger than [Zcheetahz] and [Punturz], and they are faster than [Tygurz] and [Panturz]. You will most likely see these ones the most. Wait! We never\ntalked about the different types of Dwarves, did we? Well, we will rectify that now.\n\nChapter Fourteen: The Snow Elves\n\nI never heard of them. Their skin is white like snow. Their hair is white like clouds. They are Snow Elves. They are an endangered\nspecies. To be honest, these Snow Elves are albino, and they do not like it when we call them that. The Snow Elves aided the Dwarves win the past war, so I don't really like them. They live in a place called [Frohztfohl]. But, that's all I know, because\nthey don't really like me.\n\n\nThis is only the first volume in my series of books dwelling upon the topic of Creatures. The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Current Life", "Kloxin Jayamen", "\\    OREN     ./\n     |     POWER   |\n     \\ STUBBORN./\n      | VIOLECNE |\n      |    ABUSE  |\n|\\___\\_______/\n| CORRUPT      . \\\n| RACISM          .|\n\\____________/\n  \\o/ \\o/ \\o/\n    |     |     |\n  //    \\\\ // \nCommon People\n~The Thinker\n\n((There is not signature of who wrote this other than this signature.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Dakath", "Jordan1921", "Vynari D'Avre, Mali'ker but Auvergine. Purple dress with black hair. She used to live in Ebonglade and is still waiting for a house there. She is part of a culture in Oren that has an interesting accent and a unique language. She seems to be married or\ndating a Mali'Ame or Mali'Aheral man with an eyepatch. There aren't many Auvergine's left according to her, I wasn't able to ask more about her. Her husband dragged her away before I could talk to her more.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Arts", "Coltaine Wick", "A sparse collection\nof knowledge on\nNecromancy,\nBlood Magic,\nSoul Puppetry\nNecromancers, fabled\npeople that few know about, few even know what Necromancy is, I shall tell you. Necromancy is a powerful and dangerous form of magic, Its the manipulation of life, it alters the Life Force, the thing all living creatures have.\nThe Necromancer can fuel there magic on there own or anothers Life Force, one could even extend there life slighty with Necromancy by draining others, given it would only add 20 years or so. People have described this draining as a \"Black Mist\".\nThis mist is Life Force and is being pulled from victim into the Necromancer, the source could be a human, or even trees and grass. If enough Necromancy is used in one place it could Taint the surrounding area. An experianced Necromancer can taint whole\nlandscapes. Another skill Necromancers have is cursing individuals.  A curse places taint on the target causing debilitaing physical and mental effects in the duration of the curse. Now in my life, ive been drained before and i can say, it isnt pleasant,\nit weakened me terribly, leaving my weary and exhausted.\nNor are Necromancers a particularly polite group. Id advise avoiding those sorts of people unless you are involved in those groups.\nNext up, Blood Magic\nTo start out no, blood magic does not give you control over blood, you wont be whipping it around or any such silliness. In the highest pinnacle of blood magic you could at most, make blood clots in a persons body. Blood magic is an extremely dangerous\nmagic, it wastes the body and makes the user insane. Blood magic is more of an enhancer, It give one the ability to evoke more and in greater power, but at a terrible cost, it should only be used as a last ditch effort to save your own hide. The art off\nBlood Magic uses the innate power in the blood, be your own or a targets blood, the key is that the flesh must be pierced and bleeding for it to function, I do believe the art requires runes of some sort but I am not sure.\nThink of it this way, lets say you are a pyromancer, a fire evocationist, lets say you wish to evoke a storm of fire yet are too feebly skilled to accomplish it regularly, you would employ blood magic to aid you, so instead of fireballs you get fire storm\nBut again, it is extremely straining on the body and prolonged use leaves the user insane, a raving lunatic. If one has it it should rarly if ever be used for there own safety.\nLastly we come to Soul Puppetry.\nThe little I know of soul puppetry makes me thinks its sort of like voodoo, it links the vivtims soul to a puppet that the soul puppeteer can manipulate and torture. But they can never kill the victim, trying to do so would break the connection.\nThe puppet must of course resemble the victim. Puppets dont need to be made of any speical or magical material, it can be nearly anything. That is the total of my knowledge on that.\nSmall notes.\nThe little I know of frost witchs is that, they are a secretive lot, they often hide amongst the general populace, they eat men. and have ice magic.\nThus I have told all I know\n\n\nYours truly\n    -Coltaine", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Brotherhood", "Leyu", "The Dark Brotherhood\nIntroduction Many Aegeans now are sheltered. They know nothing of this world and what is happening. For instance,today I saw the Temple of Aegis in trouble. Slimes had started a siege on recently\nressurected players,and sending them back to the Crypt. It was mayhem. And what troubles me even more,as a traveler,is that very few people know about the Dark Brotherhood. This evil guild is intent on the destruction of this world's\ninhabitants. And needs to be stopped at all costs. This is why I write this book,so that you may learn to defend yourself against this,this taint... Let me begin on the history of this guild. The History of the Brotherhood It is said they started\noff as...well...assasins with perfectly harmless intentions. This soon changed with the arrival of one known only as \"The Stranger\" . This \"Stranger\" as he is known,is responsible for the deaths of many,and is rumored to be the Grand Master of the\nguild. It has been this way for many years now. If his true identity is found,report it to me immediately! It must be shared! The Guild Itself The Guild is mostly assasins,with a few bandits mixed in. This makes it hard to track down members,commonly\nreferred to as \"Danalus'\". These apear to be the average rank,with half the guild seemingly comprised of it.. . There is also the recruit variety of Danalus it seems. Koloth is apparently the next rank. Only two have reached this rank so far to\nmy knowledge. This is the final rank.Only higher is the \"unique\" ranks. These ranks are only availible to those who have proven their worth to the Grand Master, lesser councel and High Councillor. This is the Silencer rank. This rank is only availible\nto those select few,and it is limited space. How it works is each high ranking member has one or two silencers,who carry out personal contracts for the high ranking members. There is one more rank within the Brotherhood,and it is by far the\nmost terrifying of the assasin ranks.It is \"Iblees Champion\",a seemingly obscure term used to describe the best member. It terrifies me,but thankfully,there is not a Champion yet. High Ranks The highest ranks availible are now\nclosed it seems. These are namely the Lesser councel,High Councillor and Grand Master.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Brotherhood", "Ebonsquire", "The Dark Brotherhood\n\n((Originally written by NiNjAxR3M1Xx))\nMany Aegeans now are sheltered. They know nothing of this world and what is happening. For instance, today I saw the Temple of Aegis in trouble. Slimes had started a siege on recently resurrected Descendants, and sending them back to the Crypt. It was\nmayhem. And what troubles me even more, as a traveler, is that very few people know about the Dark Brotherhood. \n\nThis evil guild is intent on the destruction of this world's inhabitants. And needs to be stopped at all costs.\nThis is why I write this book, so that you may learn to defend yourself against this, this taint . . . Let me begin on the history of the guild.\nThe History of the Brotherhood\n\nIt is said they started off as . . . well . . . assassins with perfectly harmless intentions. This soon changed with the arrival of one known only as \"The Stranger\". The \"Stranger\" as he is known, is responsible\nfor the deaths of many, and is rumored to be the Grand Master of the guild. It has been this way for many years now. If his true identity is found, report it to me immediately. It must be shared!\nThe Guild Itself\n\nThe Guild is mostly assassins, with a few bandits mixed in. This makes it hard to track down members, commonly referred to as \"Danalus'\". These appear to be the average rank, with half of the guild seemingly comprised of it.\nThere is also the recruit variety of the Danalus, it seems. Koloth is apparently the next rank. Only two have reached this rank so far to my knowledge. This is the final rank. Only higher is the \"unique\" ranks. These ranks are only available to those who\nhave proven their worth to the Grand Master, lesser council and High Councilor. This is the Silencer rank. This rank is only available to those select few, and it is limited space. How it works is each high-ranking member has one or two silencers,\nwho carry out personal contracts for the high ranking members. There is one more rank within the Brotherhood, and it is by far the most terrifying of the assassin ranks. It is \"Iblees Champion\", a seemingly obscure term used to describe the best member.\nIt terrifies me, but thankfully, there is not a Champion yet.\n\nHigh Ranks\n\nThe highest ranks available are now closed, it seems. These are namely the Lessser Council, High Councilor, and Grand Master.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Magic & You", "Nienna Calm", "Dark Magic\n      And You!\n-------------------  A Guard's Guide to\n  Identifying Dark \n          Mages\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Nienna Calm\nForeWord\n-------------------This book was written with the intent to educate the guardmen and women of the Caliphate of Khalestine. However, should you find this book in your possession, I would suggest reading it anyways. It is a good\nguide for identifying Dark mages.\nWhat is a\n    Dark Mage?\n-------------------\nA dark mage is a user of magic that inherently harms others in order to function. Dark Mages can receive their powers in a variety of manners; including Pacts with dark gods, Rituals set forth by\nIblees, and other similarly horrifying methods. It is for this reason that all Dark Mages must be identified and killed on site, for they would not hesitate to do the same to you.\nNecromancy\n-------------------\nNecromancy is the quintessential dark magic, and probably the first to ever be founded. It's age has not made it any less dangerous, however, and is directly responsible for all manners of Wraiths and Liches plaguing\nthis world today. Necromancers drain the very life force of plants, animals, and indeed people around them to cast their spells. In fact, they need a constant supply of life force to even survive, and must seek it out regularly.\nHow to Identify:\nThe bodies of necromancers are often in a very frail, almost decayed state. Since Necromancers need life force to cast spells, be on the lookout for dead or tainted patches of plant life, or reports of people feeling drained after\ntouching a specific person. These are both serious signs of a Necromancer infestation.\nFrost Witches\n-------------------Frost Witches are monsters of Ice and Snow who disguise themselves as women and prey upon the libido of Men. The Frost Witch is an easy threat to counter in the hot weather of the Caliphate, but requires constant\nvigilance to identify. A Frost Witch's true form is bright blue, but using her curse's magic, she is able to take any form she pleases, so long as that form is female. Frost Witches use these disguises to trick men into a false sense of security,\nwhereupon they will take their true form, and devour the unsuspecting male.\n\nHow to Identify:\nThe easiest way to identify a Frost Witch is by touching their skin. A frost witch's body temperature is colder than anything one could imagine.\nThere is no way for them to disguise this. Also, because of this impairment, any disguised frost Witch will show signs of great fatigue under the Caliphate sun. Any women demonstrating a severe aversion to high temperatures and regular food should have\nthe temperature of their skin checked immediately.\nShades\n-------------------\nShades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, second personality that desires for only chaos and\ndestruction. Shades are capable of corrupting every form of Arcane magic, empowering their spells with the dark powers of Iblees himself.\n\nHow to Identify:\nShade mages are hard to identify, for their true nature is only\nrevealed when they cast spells. The hallmark of a Shade is the ability to create black tentacles out of thin air. Their ability to corrupt their own magic may cause them to cast spells that are not usually possible to create. If you suspect a mage of\nbeing a Shade, contact a cleric immediately. Shades suffer from severe aversion to holy spells and relics, and these can be used to verify if a mage is, in fact, a Shade.\nSoul Puppeteers\n-------------------\nSoul puppeteers are masters of curses. Using a small fetish (a doll of some sort), and a physical part of another person (such as their hair, blood, etc.), They are able to bring sickness, pain, and even death to a\nperson from an extreme distance. Random, shooting pains and illnesses with supernatural symptoms are strong signs of the interference of a Soul Puppeteer.\n\nHow to Identify:\nIt is difficult to identify a Soul Puppeteer\nstraight off. Be on the lookout for those who try to take blood or locks of hair from their enemies. If you suspect someone of Soul Puppetry, inspect them immediately for a fetish. It is not a guarantee that they will always have one on them, but it's the\nonly way to confirm for sure.\nSoul Contractors\n-------------------Soul Contractors are capable of fashioning magical legal documents that bind the signer to the very letter of their word. This would be potentially useful, if not for the material they must fashion these\ndocuments on. Soul Contracts can only be written upon the flayed skin of men that was taken whilst they were still alive. It is a brutal and horrifying process, that speaks to the inhumanity of these casters.\n\nHow to Identify:\nLike Soul Puppeteers,\nit is hard to identify a Soul Contractor. The only way to tell for sure is to either catch them in the act, or discover their flaying equipment, which may not even be on their person.\nBlack-Dragon\n     Parasites\n-------------------A more recent addition to dark magic, black-dragon parasites are a growing problem in the Caliphate. A black-dragon parasite is an insidious form of insect that infects its hosts and causes\ncauses them to literally absorb blood and the flesh of the mortal races in return for benefits. It is unknown how is parasite passes from person to person, so it is absolutely vital that you keep any suspected carrier of this foul creature far away from\none's person at all times. It is unknown at this time if Black Dragon Parasite victims can be cured, so it is recommended that they be either expelled from the city on sight, or, in extreme cases, purged.\n\nHow to Identify:\nBlack-Dragon Parasites\nare easy to identify. All carriers of the parasite bear a tattoo of a black dragon on their person, usually winding around the stomach area. If you suspect someone of having this terrible disease, conduct a full-body search immediately.\nGeneral Warning\n    Signs Of A\n    Dark Mage\n-------------------\nDark Mages can and will follow stereotypes at times. If you keep a look out, there are many signs that indicate if a person is just a dark mage in general. These are by no means\ndeciding factors in a suspect's ability to cast black magic, but they are definitely red flags to investigate.\n\nBe Suspicious Of Any Persons you see that:\n\n-Wear Primarily Black Robes.\n\n-Are Hooded at all times\n-Possess bright red eyes.\n\n-Project a magical Aura that Black, Gray, or Red in color.\nAs a guard of the Caliphate, it is up to YOU to root out these psychopathic evildoers wherever they might rise their ugly heads. For the sake of our grand city, do your duty well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Darkness", "TheGamerKittyHD", "Dark, misty nights\nLong, foggy days\nClouding the mind\nBlocking the sunrays\n\nSlowly going insane\nDying for no reason\nArrow through the heart\n\nDark faces of fear\nPeculiar evenings of light\nThe end of me is near\nLonely nights I stowaway\nListening to the ocean waves\nI am alone\nI am in the dark", ""),
        StaticBook("Dasyra's book.", "Archmage Dasyra", "*The books several pages are completely sparse, yet it looks aged.. As you continue flicking through, a single page is found with a rather odd symbol upon it. Examining it, you find an odd sensation overcome your mind..*\nThe feeling within your mind begins to overtake any current sensations, your vision becomes blurred and hearing vague. Instead of your surroundings, your mind is filled with the image of nothing, a small space rotating space that goes against\nyou've seen before.. Your mind becomes torn, the odd construct in your vision appearing to remove your memories, throughts and opinions and laying them out in front of you like an odd puzzle.. It examines them, every tiny little detail within the\nblink of an eye before returning them to you.. This odd feeling lingers with you, constantly upon your thoughts, always there, the image of the black space stained upon your eyes.. Madness has welcomed you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dawson's Journal", "Dawson Bailson", "*Pages before this have been torn out.\nDay 37\n------\n   I can't take this anymore. All of this damn fighting, and still nothing. The Order of Saint Amays was on of the worst decisions I have ever made in my life. With nothing new to experience other than unsensical violence, I am left gasping\nfor something joyous, and rejuvinating. My request though, is out of the question. Without quenching this thirst I find it hard to live my life. If the Order of Saint Amays was made up of honorable men like I believed it was, there would be no need  for\nthis note, but it is necesarry. I am going to do it soon. I shall end it all from this very ceiling.\nDay 38\n------\n   Goodbye cruel world. It had been fun before the damnned Order of Saint Amays, but that has changed everything. With this final entry I end everything. I shall miss you brother Jonathan, but m- (Blood covers the page.)\n(In someone else's handwritting.) Down with the Order. In with Iblees. \n-The Daemon of the Waters", ""),
        StaticBook("Day 1, Kevan the", "Kevan Chester", "Day 1\nTraveled through the Teuton lands, ending up in a ruin infested Jungle. Met a man named Zayden, was warned about bats and rats, Found a strange set of wooden buildings near and in trees. Found a candle lit stoneyard, with large flying creatures\nabove it. I may die, but I will cross or attempt to. Now following a blood trail in a savannah. Still no clue where I am, but perhaps that is for the best. Sins require petenance, and Sermonosi will let me repent or deal me justice as I have earned.\nPigmen on the Horizon...I might not survive this. A Hellish landscape with a tower in the distance. The Three gods have abandoned me here, or else I am outside their domain. A ruined fort lies across Rivers of lava, and a burning forest as well.\nThe sea and Storm are far away, and the sun blocked. Sermonosi protect me. I have appear to quite literally reached the end of the world, and will be turning back. Floating Islands of hell await. Found a Castle back in the Savannah, will seek refuge there\nNo one at the Castle, entering the valley with Scythes, Mills, and Lights among the grey. It appeared to be a abandoned Mine area, with pulleys and drills of crystal. Odd place to have it, perhaps an old dwarven mine? As I near a darkened pillar I can\nfeel a great aura of darkness...This area is covered with a sickness. Trees with fading crystals line the landscape ahead, and it seems the sickness is weak here. It must be centred at that mine. There lies an entrance into the hillside, I think I shall\nbrave it. I must find someone to keep this record after I fill it so much, it is far too valuable to lose, and Sermonosi would never forgive me. A strong pillar lies further on, lighting the area. I seem to be in an oasis in the valley. Lovely place.\nI have found a statue of an Orenian Aengul. Interesting thing, with a bare bookshelf. Might have a book existed here before? Was it taken? A bridge statue, says Eh' Torien Mezzenia. I stop in another grey area...to tired to carry on, my phantom fingers\ntwitching. Hopefully tomorrow I shall continue.", ""),
        StaticBook("De Shroom Guide", "Madpen Brookflint", "De Purpose of this book is te ca'alouge any an' all fungi, fungus, shrooms an' differen' 'ypes of Mycelium. This lis' will undoub'udly be expanded as Me colec's more specimens. Each Specimen will be ge'ing a pic'ure an' description. -Madpen\nDe \"Shroom\" clasification be given te a fungi when i' meets cer'ain cri'eria. -------------------I' mus' 'ave a stalk of some sor', an' a distinc'ive cap. This 'oo par' structure is wha' seperates it. Shrooms are usualy found in groups, or clus'ers.\nBoomafool Shroom or\nBooming Fowl Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom is fairly common, i' grows on rocks, s'eep 'ills or under 'rees. It has a large pocket of a very ligh' gas in i's stalk. This pocket is esential. When de Boomafool begins to spore, i'\nde'aches from de ground and floa's upwards. It will either hi' a tree and de'ona' or i' will get blown away. When i' takes a blow, de top section explodes releasing the spores. De spores of de Boomafool are very small and liable to ge' stuck in ye eyes.\n_______________/~~_________\n            \\____\n                    \\____\n\n\n\n  __\n/##\\\n_||||||________________The Boomafool -Maddy\nRepiluca or\nCreeping Glow Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom is fairly common in caves, generaly on limes'one it grows in spall 'oles in de wall. A Faint glow is produced by spots on i'. De Repiluca is often used in mixings of Acui'y.\n_____________\n                   \\\n                     \\\n                      |\n                      |\n                      |\n      /++\\    ___/\n_____||||||___/\n\nThe Repiluca\n-Maddy\nNote: The Repiluca clones ocasionaly.\nBlack Capped River Shroom or Umbra-oom\n-------------------The Umbra-oom is much larger then previous Shrooms. It 'as a long an' curved s'alk with a bell shaped hood. I' is normaly found next to rivers as i' consumes river bir's tha' crash in'o it. The Umb\nra-oom can be harvested in large chunks, and will consume an' disolve anythin' tha' falls in'o i'.\n-------------------I' is safe less you fall on de 'op. Then ye should be screaming.\n__________\n   /              \\\n   |                |\n  /___________\\\n        ||||||||||||\n         ||||||||||||\n          ||||||||||||\n            |||||||||||\n             \\|||||||\\\n            /||||||||||||||\\\nThe Umbra-oom\n-Maddy\nSafron Tree Shroom\nYellow Cap Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom be of'en confused with a Frazzlebush when i's small. I' is covered in a thick layer of vines and pe'als. Should any par' of the pe'als be eaten de consumer will become very agressive and\nwill have a craving for more. De pe'als are a mix of safron an' a bright white.\n#######0##\n      ###0#########\n      ########0####\n      0############\n      #############\n      ####0########\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\nThe Safron Tree Shroom\n-Maddy\nFireball Shroom\nSpotted Orb Shroom\n-------------------There is nothing much to say about this shroom. Despite i's name i's no' flamable. I' is of'en made in'o soup or use' in a salad.\n_________\n     /              \\\n     |                |\n     |                |\n     \\_________/\n         |||||||||||||||||\n         |||||||||||||||||\n         |||||||||||||||||\nFireball Shroom\n-Maddy\nDining Plate Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom comes in many sha'es and sizes. It 'as a long stalk and a reli'ivly flat and 'ard cap. I' is of'en used as a pla'e when a good one is no' available, as i' 'as no effec' on de consumer.\n___\n  |\n\n        __________\n        |_________|\n              |||||\n              ||||| \n              |||||\n              |||||\n___     ___\n  |         |\nGiant Cluster Shroom\n-------------------Las' bu' no' leas': This Shroom is a sigh' te be'old. Much like de Spotted Orb Shroom bu' this one grows in massive pods. I' 'as no inherent use bu' 'as been used as 'ousing an' is considered sacred by many.\n_____________\n  /_____________\\\n           ||||||||\n ___      ||||||||\n/__\\     |||||||||\n  ||||       |||||||||\n           |||||||||    ___\n           |||||||||   /__\\\n           |||||||||     ||||\n           |||||||||\nGiant Cluster Shroom\n-Maddy\nOther Tomes of de Fungi by \nMadpen Brookflint:\n\nA guide te infec'ions, fungus an' Myceliums\n\nRiver Fish o' Maliner\n\nA Guide te 'oilet makin'", ""),
        StaticBook("Dead Man's Last", "Ser Aymer Fournier", "I decided today that I'd now write a little story on what has happened in my life.\nI Know I won't live too much longer now- the disease is finally catching up to me. It's a shame, really. After so long. But it was bound to happen eventually. I guess\nit just comes as a shock no matter who you are.\nAnywho, all of that shall be explained later- for now I start with the basics.\nMy parents, Lucia and Horatio L'amor, were...quiet. My father was a soldier for an army that rarely fought, and my\nmother farmed to feed us- me and my sister- As well as get some extra cash.\nPeople told me that us three ladies of the family were identical. Give or take size and a few scars. We are all known for being quite pretty. It's a good thing to be known for.\nAnywho, we lived on the outskirts of a small town, near the sea. I loved the sea back then. The wildlife in particular. IT was wonderful.\nThen we all set sail for vailor. We got so, so close. Close enough for me to swim to shore. We couldn't have known.\nSomething broke the base of the ship. My parents were locked in, my sister too young to swim so far. They all drowned. The menace and unpredictability of the sea took them. I've hated it since-the sea mother is a cruel tyrant, not to be messed with.\nI got to shore and was aided by a soldier, I cannot remember his name. I was taken to safety in a tavern. They tried to talk to me, but apparently shock had left me unresponsive. I can't even remember their faces- though I suppose I look more like my\nmother now. But, fa is a different story.\nI grew up in the newly built Vaneheim- a snowy town, surrounded by water. I hated that, but it's a pretty little village. \nI lived there for quite some time- 15 years or so-Before reaching adult hood.\nThen I\nsimply set out to explore. After getting an injury- only from tripping- I went to get it fixed- Only to find I had some killer disease. It wasn't a welcome discovery, but nothing could be done. It slowly takes the strength of a being- SLOWLY. Most humans\nlive to 75 or somewhere like that, but chances are I won't live to see 50.\nI was devistated at the time. Several times I tried to suicide. All the time, these voices would chant. I couldn't bear it. It was agony.\nAnyway, onto the topic at hand- I\nroamed aimlessly from then on until I stumbled apon an elderly dwarf by the name of Sarco Floreck. He was so kind, always cared for me however he could. We lived with his brother in Adria- i don't know where they are now, and it scares me. A relative says\nhe's away on a hunting trip.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Clover", "Yden Orvir", "To Clover\n\nA million stars in the sky,\nOne shines brighter I cannot deny,\nA love so precious a love so true,\nA love that comes from me to you.\nThe angels sing when you are near,\nWithin your arms I have nothing to fear,\nYou always know just what to say,\nJust talking to you just makes my day,\nI love you honey with all my heart,\nTogether forever and never to part.\n\nPlease forgive me for my absence, it was beyond my control but every moment I was away I thinking\nof you and reliving memories that we shared, the time I was away from you just showed me how precious you are to me and I do not want to ever loose you again, it appears it is true that you never knew what you had until it is gone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Lopkaea", "MaxGemini", "I can't go on without you. You were all I had left in the world.\n   My friends have all left me, my family have all died.\n   Now without you, I feel so empty inside, and I have no reason to go on, unless to spare you any grief you might feel at my\ndeath. But this isn't your fault. You have no obligation to love me. I just can't do it anymore.\n\nGoodbye.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Rune", "Thorburn Grimbeorn", "Dear Rune,\n\nGreetings. Thor here. How are you?  Hope you are fine. So I have a request to make. I would like you and me to go out sometime. We can go for a picnic or a walk or whatever you wish. Please answer. I would love to go out with you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dearest Friend", "Thalia", "Dearest Illi,\n\nI want to thank you for, always being there for me and being kind from the first moment we met.\n\nI would consider you a sister and hopefully you would too.\nI want to give you something a little special, and hope you get well soon.\n\nHere are some flowers and i just want to let you know, you are strong, inside and out.\n\n-Thalia xxx <3", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant Poem", "Aria", "=-=-=-=-*-=-=-=-=-=Dedicant Ariadni's\nTask One Poem.\n=-=-=-=-*-=-=-=-=-=\nThe quiet forest beckons the lonely mist onwards. It slithers through the canopy of the elder trees.\n\nAll that may be heard is the padding of the fox's feet as she snuffles through the tall, wild grass.\nThe branches heave, moaning in the moonlit night as the leaves flitter in the passing of the mist, welcoming its presence.\n\nThe fox raises her head, her ears twitching and nose sniffing the cold, damp air. Quickly, she turns to run, escaping.\nThe mist takes chase, weaving through the trunks and piercing through the still air towards the creature as it bolts forwards.\n\nA yelp echoes against the silence in a battle of sound, the silence reclaiming its throne as the mist prevails.\nAt home, the whimpers of the cubs are softened as their mother returns, turning once to sound a howl in appreciation.\n\nThe mist swims about, presenting the family with the moonlight as it departs, the creature being no more as the fox guards her cubs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant Poem", "[Teen] Dedicant Veren", "The leaves rustle as the wind blows strong\nFlowers blossen and trees grow tall\nThe Druids protect this beutiful place\nWhile the Aspects guid with strength and grace \nThe druids watch the void grow strong Trying to protect the things we love\nAs nature listens, so sutle and quiet\nThe world grows on forever strong\nBy:\nDedicant Veren", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant Writing", "Girl", "Death. Death is a vastly underappreciated part of life that many are unwilling to accept. Many do not see that where death occurs, life blossoms. A deer that falls to another animal in the forest will provide food for various different beings. Perhaps the\nanimal that brought down the deer was a wolf. That wold could use the meat to feed her cubs. Some may think that's all that that particular death will be taking part in, but no. Afterwards, various scavengers will flock to the corpse, such as ants and\nflies. The corpse, depending on how much was eaten by the wolves, will provide a place for the flies to breed, spawning new maggots. The ants will take the food back to their colony, which will provide sustenance for the queen to lay more eggs. And from\nthe breeding of those new insects, will come more food for spiders and then the cycle continues.", ""),
        StaticBook("Deed", "James Delaney", "~DEED~\n\nThis Deed dictates that the house on the 5th of Newport Boulevard is a posession of the Norwick Family.\n\nOnly a member of the Norwick Family can pass on the posession right of this House.\nThis deed is signed by Steward James Delaney of Felsen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Defense Contract", "Tahjeet Mubdee", "<<><>Iron Corps<><>>\n{}Defense Contract{}\n\nThe Iron Corps will be purchasing a sum of 54 stacks of arrows, and 30, 40% Velocity bows from the company \"Linda's Workshop\".\n\nFor the arrows, a payment of 1750 minas is due.\nFor the bows, a payment of 1860 minas is due.\n\nThis contract is to be fulfilled by the 14th of Malin's Welcome, 1509.\n\nParties participating in the contract are Iron Corps and Linda's Workshop.\nIron Corps\n-Tahjeet Mubdee\n\nLinda's Workshop\n-Linda Rose", ""),
        StaticBook("Defining Purity", "Azorella Coulissante", "As is often the case with such things as mutable as language, definitions and connotations can often become confused over the passage of time and the turnover from generation to generation. This particular treatise will attempt to clarify\nsome of these definitions, namely those regarding Mali'aheral purity.\n\nFirstly, it must be noted that this treatise will not attempt to explain how the lesser races may try to define their own standards for purity,\nshould they have any standards at all. Since a pure Mali'aheral would never breed with such lesser stock, such definitions are generally irrelevant for practical use and will not be addressed in this document. For the purposes of this document, the terms\n'pure' and 'impure' will refer only to those who have some form of Mali'aheral heritage. The term 'lesser' refers to any of those without a Mali'aheral heritage.\n\nPurity, like the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, typically relies on\ntwo main pillars: mental purity and physical purity. The first pillar, mental purity, is more difficult to define and is dependent on a Mali'aheral's actions and intentions. This will be covered in more depth later in this document. However,\nthe second pillar, physical purity, is considerably more straightforward as it relies strictly on bloodlines.\n\nPhysical purity is dependent entirely on a Mali'aheral's heritage. A pure Mali'aheral can only\nbe born of physically pure parentage and therefore cannot have any of the lesser races marring their bloodline. By contrast, a physically impure Mali'aheral (also known as an acaln due to the severity of this impurity) will have a\nlesser amongst their ancestors. There is no way to remedy this kind of impurity aside from termination, hence, extreme care must always be taken in regards to producing offspring.\n\nMental purity is less simple to define and\nis reliant on a Mali'aheral's actions and intentions. A mentally pure Mali'aheral will often adhere to the tenants of the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, although this kind of definition is bound to evoke confusion since each Mali'aheral likely has\na slightly different interpretation of Larihei's teachings. These different interpretations ought be embraced as they help weave a lush and rich environment ripe for debate and learning; however, in defining purity, these interpretations often\nbring with them ample confusion.\n\nInstead, it may be simpler to try and define the actions and intentions of a mentally impure Mali'aheral. The greatest offenses to mental purity lie in the murder of other pure Mali'aheral\nand in breeding with lessers. However, care must be taken to note the intention of such actions. For instance, a Haelun who accidentally smothers her infant in their slumber may remain mentally pure depending on the circumstances, but\na disgruntled guard arbitrarily murdering fellow pure Mali'aheral ought serve a capital punishment for their capital impure offense.\n\nSome lesser, but still troubling, offenses may include violent assault on another Mali'aheral or\nphysically intimate fraternization with a lesser, even if this does not lead to expected or unexpected offspring. These kinds of mental impurities may be recoverable by a strict reeducation, but are nonetheless a grave insult to the\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya and should not be taken lightly.\n\nAs a final word of warning--to accuse another Mali'aheral of impurity is a matter that should be handled with grave care. To do so falsely would be akin to trampling on\ngenerations of careful breeding and centuries of tradition with intense ramifications for the accused should the innocent walk guilty. By the same measure, however, it is equally dangerous to allow impures to scourge society should the\nguilty walk innocent. Take care with your judgement, lliran, for the future of the Mali'aheral rests upon it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Delivery Birds.", "The Scribe.", "DELIVERY BIRDS.\nHow is it that birds are able to find the recipients of letters without knowledge of who they are needed to visit? My theory is that birds can be trained to detect the soulstones of those who need letters delivered to them. If this is true, can\nall animals sense soulstones?\n\nAll musings of course.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Forest", "[Yemekar's Pick] Elder Falent Ireheart", "To the south we went and once we got to the afformentioned \"Barrier\" we headed West through some sort of weird Desert forest. The trees were absolutely normal but standing upon sand in an unbelievably dry area. The areas keep getting weirder.\n~Falent Ireheart", ""),
        StaticBook("Desolation", "Guru Pinya", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n       Desolation\n    By Guru Pinya\n\n   Answer me, Lord,\nout of the goodness\n     of your love;\n In your great mercy\n       turn to me.\n   Do not hide your\n   face from your\n         servant;\nAnswer me quickly,\n  for I am in trouble.\n  Come near me and\n      rescue me;\n  Deliver me because\n      of my foes.\n You know how I am\n scorned, disgraced\n     and shamed;\n  All my enemies are\n     before you.\nScorn has broken my\n    heart and has\nleft me helpless;\n      I looked for\n  sympathy, but there\n      was none,\n    for comforters,\n  but I found none.\nThey take my tongue\n      And silence\n       my words.\n   May their eyes\n    be darkened,\nso they cannot see,\n   and their backs\n   be bent forever.\n   Pour out your \n   wrath on them;\n  let your fierce\nanger overtake them.\n   May their place\n     be deserted;\n   Let there be no\n     one to dwell \n    in their cities.\nFor they persecute\n  those you wound,\n and talk about the\n    pain of those\n       you hurt.\n  Charge them with\n  crime upon crime;\n   do not let them\n    share in your\n       salvation.\n     May they be\n  blotted out of the\nBook of Life and\n  not be listed with\n    the righteous.\n   But as for me,\nafflicted and in pain-\n       may your\n       salvation,\n  God, protect me.\n     I will praise\n God's name in song\n and glorify him with\n     thanksgiving.", ""),
        StaticBook("Devourer's Ruins", "Ashur", "--- === @@@ === ---\nSTUDY: THE DEVOURER'S RUINS\n--- === @@@ === ---\n\nPenned on the 8th of Snow's Maiden, 1540, in the realm of Vailor, by Ashur Uilosson, Orithur, and Archembalt of the Library of Dragur.\nThe early winter morning's winds bit at our noses as our vessel arrived upon Elven shores. Guards from the city of Laureh'lin stopped us upon arrival, but after an intervention from Prince Tristen Tresery, we were granted access.\nThe ruin in question lied roughly 14 kilometers from the docks (59 from Laureh'lin). A large hole, lined with carved cobblestone, bored nearly 1/4th a km into the earth. The three of us descended into its bowels.\nUpon reaching the flooded bottom, we entered a sideways cavern to find walls inscribed with ancient Elven tongue. It spoke of paradise and nirvana accesible through a gateway.\n\nAlso lying nearby was a corpse. Unrelated, we believe.\nUp until this point, I had noticed several similarities to the way that I, and others of my millenium, escaped Aegis and fled into the Verge. The long tunnel into the earth, carvings of a portal to heaven, ancient Elven influence... coincidence?\nI deem this to be so. Lining the inner walls of the areas not lost to erosion, we found depictions of an incredibly-large aquatic creature as it laid waste to fleets of ships. This is similar to talk of the Devourer, a monster found relatively recently.\nThe Devourer is a massive beast the size of several buildings, resembling an oversized squid, with tentacles stretching endlessly from the waves. Its beak was likened to obsidian, and its cries like Iblees itself. It escaped alive.\nFaded Elven was inscribed with the painting. Here is what remained legible, grouped in how it was found:\n\n    osul  er\n    sil it o   ihei\n           iyl'm\nullra l   it'\n     e oi'  medier'o  i\n  \n\n   kae er n'odi e\n       e     nae'l  it\n\n\nAll else is lost to time.\nOne last room was available to us: a large, spherical chamber with an elevated stone centre. Stairs along the walls led to a balcony that wrapped around the upper regions of the room, offering a clear view of said stone centre.\nThe stone platform had a + of emerald set into the ground, with the middle composed entirely of prismarine. A similar symbol was above the hallway we walked through to discover this room.\n\nAs of late, many bats have taken residence here.\nThe balcony's walls lead to several shelves of books, but erosion and flooding has led to their doom. Nothing can be recovered from the leather or the parchment, and are beyond all hope of repair.\n--- === @@@ === ---\nCONCLUSION\n--- === @@@ === ---\n\nWe believe these ruins to be of Elven construction, and belong to a cult that worships the Devourer, or a similar creature.\nThis is fascinating because discovery of the Devourer is relatively recent as of this expedition. Either the being is far older than we thought (a champion of nature), or part of a species... and I truly hope that isn't the case.\nThe sphere viewing room is for ceremony, possibly sacrifice, to appease their aquatic God. The platforms are for guests to observe the proceedings.\n\nThese worshippers intended to open a portal to their perfect world through these actions.\nAs of now, we formally recommend the following actions:\n\n-- Carefully and wisely remove debris blocking other halls\n\n-- Translate Elven inscriptions on the painting of the Devourer\nWritten this day, on the 8th of Snow's Maiden, 1540, within the halls of the Grand Library of Dragur. The original copy will remain on our shelves, and one copy will be prepared for Laureh'lin officials.\n\n--Ashur Uilosson", ""),
        StaticBook("Diagnosis", "Mylas", "Atturi needs ladies advice STAT RED ALERT DEFCON 1", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary 1", "Cealum Nightgrove", "19th Malin's Welcome 1504\n  For whatever reason Fjordin has asked that I start writing in a journal. Personally I do not care to record my deepest thoughts and feelings for others to potentially see, but the man gave me a home and I respect him so\nhere I am. I suppose I should introduce myself, my name is Cealum Nightgrove. I am a Wood Elf but I was raised by humans the  majority of my life, I can't even remember my real parents. The first few decades of my life I felt as if I fit in, though by the\ntime I was in my early twenties I began to see those humans I grew up with age faster then me. By this time I truly felt different. I continued to live my life as I saw those around me become adults and thier age showed. In my fifties an old friend from\nchildhood died due to failing health. This truly terrified me. I saw the unavoidable end that all beings face though the humans I've loved are cursed to face far sooner than myself. As the years passed I was tormented by the deaths of my human parents, my\nclosest friends, and worst of all...my dear siblings. Though they were human I considered them my own flesh and blood, and their deaths left a void that can never be filled. After all those that I have loved passed, I decided to travel instead of forming\nnew bonds with the humans in my village for I feared there rapidly approaching deaths. This is when I first leave my village alone and the last time I would call it home. I will not write details about my relationship with my family and friends, for they\nare to painful to recall.\n\n  When I departed I knew nothing of the outside world nor how others acted outside the customs of my village. I admit I made a fool of myself on more than one occasion, though I quickly learned how to survive without being\nhumilated. I still remember the first time I meet another Wood Elf, I was so excited I was barely able to maintain myself! Though I quickly learned that even if someone is of the same race, they wont hesitate to stab you in the back. After many similar\nincounters I started to miss my village, where everyone truly cared about each other and didn't care that I was a Wood Elf. The humans out here however tend to look down their nose towards me. It would be unfair to judge all humans with this though. I try\nto judge someone based of their merits, not the merits of their kin..except the orcs, I have yet to meet one who didn't want bloodshed. My travels brought me through many lands, though none of them I was able to call home. However, it wasnt until I\nstopped in a tavern called the Red Rose Tavern that I even had the opportunity too.\n  There I meet a fellow Wood Elf who happened to be working on a settlement of his own. We got to talking and I found out his name was Fjordin. He was describing his\ngrowing town, it sounded like most I have walked though, but one thing he said caught my attention. He mentioned that his town consisted of many different races. This interested me since a town where all the races worked together would be free of race\nhatred. The name of this town? Sylverport. I first thought Fjordin was a bit odd, the way he shifted through his papers oblivious of the world around him, but I took a chance and asked if I could join his city. It was a great decision. I haven't been here\nlong but it is excatly as I expected it. I may not have meet all of my fellow townsmen but the few I have meet have proven to be...interesting. First off there is Mira Casswell, she is a human who shares my passion for woodcutting. She can be...abrasive,\nbut I have a feeling she is kind at heart. I will have a good opportunity to find out more due to the fact she is my housemate. I find her interesting and enjoyable to be around though due to her being a human I can only see her as a friend. I can not\nafford to become romantically involved with any human, I can't go through the pain of out living loved ones again. Though I feel a certain attachment to her since she reminds me strongly of my dear sister. In actions not in looks I should add. There is\nanother young human female I meet her named Kayla. We shared a few words but I have not seen her enough to get to know her, I need to forming relationships with my townsmen a priority if I am to stay here.\n  In the short time I've been here many things\nhave happened in this small town. Not only have we recently built a harbor but we will soon recieve papers that will make us a part of Oren! Though i may not agree with their treatment of non-humans we can definitly use their protection and trade. Even\nmore so since we were almost raided recently! Everyone was away on business and I stayed behind to work on the lumber farm. The bandit was almost successful and was on the verge of killing me when Mira arrived to aid me. Luckly for us he wasn't willing to\nfight two on one. Even more luck for us arrived when Fjordin came back. We ended up killing the bandit, I was seriously wounded in the battle but luckly I recover quickly. That's my life so far, I probably won't write again until something happens. Till\nthen, farewell.\n\n9th First Seed 1504\n  I must take back my latest comment about Orcs. A Olog has just moved into town and is moving in as I write this. I suppose even after all my years I can be surprised. This is a welcome change to my life. I\nsuppose I should meantion his name, he is Krug'lag and appears to be friendly enough. He claims to be a miner and a blacksmith, which would be a welcome addition. I just hope this doesnt bite us in the back later.\n\n18th The Deep Cold 1504\n  I have meet\nAlyssia today. She is an interesting woman, though she is human I may actually see myself with her. She is beautiful and her shy nature makes her even more wonderous. Though don't get me wrong, it isn't her looks I have fallen for. We share many things in\ncommon. My only worry is that I'll say something to drive her away. All I want is to get to know her better at this point, if she is who I think she may be then...well, Im not sure. I swore never to marry a human due to their life span, but would bottling\nup my love hurt just as much as out living her? I am not sure, I will have to meditate on this. Until next time.\n\n9th The Deep Cold 1508\n I know I know, its been far to long since Ive last written in my journal. Many things have happened since my last\nentry. One of the main things was that I becames a Sentry of Sylerport! though it is an honor and a high responsibilty it isnt the most life changing thing that has happened as of late. Alyssia has accepted my feelings and returned them as well! I have\nnever felt this way before about anyone. Could it be love? If so its deffenitily a different feeling of love than i felt with my family. Though Im sure there are many different kind of loves this one is new and I hope it stays for a long time. Just now in\nfact she meantioned she would like to marry, its hard to explain how I felt when she said that, but I know it was a wonderful feeling. My only fear though...is going through the same thing that happened with my family. But damn it if youre going to\nexperiance the pain you might as well fell the full pleasure from it as well! Thats why I will seek marriage.\n\n10th Snow Maiden 1509\n Well it happened, I finally got married to Alyssia! This is by far the happiest day of my life, Alyssia looked\nbeautiful in her dress. I knew others were there but my eyes were on her only. We wed in the traditional oren sense but the method didnt matter, Im just happy to have our lives tied together. We decided to move into my room in the basement, its better for\nus since she likes the under ground and I dont have to move.\n\n\nTo Be Contiued", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary 1545", "Nyxxa", "Diary volume 1\n\nGreetings and salutations, I will no say what my name is in the case that this tome is found.\n\nPerhaps i am paranoid for thinking it could be used against me, but diary you have not seen what Vailor is like.\nRight the date is 21st of snow maiden 1545. \nI am writing down my story, because it seems no one believes me.\n\nRight so I have a memory disorder, I do not recall all of what came before my awakening four years ago.\nMy awakening, well four years ago I was pulled out a completely untouched rock face by some dwarven miners. Appearently there was an alcove of sorts, no more then a hair's breath of space between my body and the smooth rock.\nHowever, the miners say that when then found me and before they touched me, I sort of just hovered there, slightly tindged in a glow of gold.\n\nThey pulled me out and I remained unconscience for another three days, the miners took me to the docks\nsome of the monks had been taking care of me whilst i was unconscience so I don't even know the identity of the dwarven miners in that the monks said had left me. the monk's story as to how the dwarves found me was told to me and at the time I didn't\nremember much else. The wise monk in question told me to name myself, and start again, and that likely my memory would come back with time.\n\nSo I named myself and went on my way. not much happened the first months. I scavenged for food, got told that my\nclothing was not fit for high elven society. I was in that place for some time, perhaps a couple of days, but I could not stay there, to much hatred for my colorings.\n\nNext I met the most wonderful individual.\nAgain I will not name him by his true name\nbecause I do not know who in the future will read this.\n\nFor the purpose of this writing we will call him Bob. Bob found me in the docks area and we spoke of my past. He is perhaps the only person that believes me.\nRegardless I told him of my lost past and he told me of a certain orc that might assist in the location of my name. I have since tried to contact this orc but to no sucess. \n\nBob and myself headed to the orcish capital city and spent time with a shaman\nthere, this is my first remembered experience with cactus green. I would suggest not dealing with cactus green...\n\nAfter our recovery, it is to be noted that I kept a portion of the cactus green, at the time for no reason other then further enjoyment.\nBob and I visited the shaman's island and searched their library for a referance to myself. no such luck.\n\nWe then visited another much larger library. The library of Dragur. We searched and searched but found nothing, and so the location of my\nprior diaries or journals is unknown still. \n\nWhilst at this great library I discovered in myself a desire or thirst for knowledge on the Arcane Arts. However my trip with bob was not yet completed.\nBob took my high up into a mountain and showed my a place that i could stay with no real laws or hatred for my oddity.\n\nWhilst we were standing there and talking about this location another man approached.\nI will write down as much as I can remember about him for future referance. He wore a black and white robe. the top of which was black on the right and white on the left, but the legs of which was the oppisite. He wore a brestplate with dark leather\nstraps, and he had, and this is a bit difficult to recall, brown hair and dark eyes. The reason i write this is for what happened next. This man, all he said was hello, and he was focused on Bob not myself.\nI believe he repeated hello four times before Bob told me to run. Bob then disappeared and I did run.\n\n\nA day later Bob was at the docks, I found him there. He was highly distraught and told me of pain and hell.\nI need to do more research into this man and the hell that Bob was taken too.\n\nI managed to calm Bob down, and then I took him to a scared place. A place with giant trees and lily pads that you can lay upon.\nI sang to him and discovered that I in fact could sing quite well. \n\nThese next things that happened I don't quite have in order anymore it happened quite quickly.\n\nI studied all the books in the magic section of the library of dragur. I wrote a few books in an attempt to get copies of some of my favorite books in the library. To note that didn't work. I found out that I was in love with Bob.\nI found out that Bob was with another woman and that this other woman was pregnant. I began to remember a bit of my past. I planned a journey to the immortal plane of spirits.\n\nBob and his woman, whom we will call bobette\nthey are quite happy together so I concealed my pain and let them be. They had a daughter, she is quite a beautiful creature, it makes me wish for my own.\n\nThe journey hasn't taken place, the Shaman that was to take us has been missing.\nI finished my research project and sent a copy to the library of dragur. \n\nI then meet the leader of the wood elves. His name will be included as simple Tra.\n\nTra had banished Bob from his home and I was meeting with Tra\nso that I might assist in getting his home returned. He was told to me as a womanizer so I suppose I should have suspected that he was handsome, however it still caught me off my guard.\n\nMy goal was achieved with him and I managed not to fall prey to his\nadvances. I later learned that I had not in fact assisted at all Bob had taken care of it himself.\n\nI met a one called Naay who spoke to me of revolution amoung the wood elves in response to the laws against Void magic.\nI met a Halfling called Yrral, and a high elf called Noirras, as well as his son Recrem. \n\nMostly at that point my life had devolved to simple socialization.\n\nI discovered a hidden place on the volcanos that wasn't entirely distroyed.\nI discovered that the sacred place I loved was home to a tree Ent and had a secret underground area and a giant portal there.\n\nI spent a lot of my time practicing my instruments and learning new songs.\nI have proformed a few times and actually made a few mina.\n\nI learned to mine somwhat, fish somewhat and cook somewhat.\n\nI have a follower an elf called Nahtan. \n\nI moved away from the mountains and fought in a battle.\nI lived in a glourious home in Sanctuary and then was evicted.\n\nI spent a lot of time in Laureh'Lin's emerald crescent.\n\nI designed and implimented a device of magic interest.\nI think that is all that I did.\n\nRegardless I moved back to the mountains and now I have to pay taxes. I don't make enough as a bard to pay taxes. \n\nI might end up homeless again. Oh well I suppose that is the cycle of my life.\nAlways starving and always struggling to have a roof over my head. \n\noh ya I remembered that i used to live with the orcs back in Asulon. I also remember I once was capable of voidal translocation, which is basically\nscholar speak for teleportation. which of course explains how I ended up in a wall.\n\nI got healed by a paladin somewhere along here too, bad injury from the battle. note to self I am not a warrior.\n\nStill don't know my name and such\nanyhow, I am done writing for today.\n\n23rd of the grand harvest 1545\n\n\nGreetings again diary, seems i have a bit more to report.\n\nThe place that I was living in the mountains has been\naquired by another empire. we now need to pay taxes. I cannot pay them, my income from being a bard is less then wonderful and they ask one hundred minas a year. I have again pack my things and we will see what happens next. I am sitting in Laureh'lin\nmaybe i will find a home here, but I begin to think I will simply find a place that no one wishes to live and take supplies out there to live alone.\n\n24th of the grand harvest 1545\n\nTra has let me stay with him in Laureh'lin\nThough I am somewhat worried of his motives for such a thing I am greatful. perhaps this home will last me more then a few months.\n\n3rd of sun's smile 1545\n\nAnd again I sit down to write. I have been living with Tra a week now\nnothing new. not certain if they even miss me yet up in skyfall. I wonder if I will be expected to pay guild dues to the society if I wish to continue to be a part of it. \n\nAlso the library has offically been recognized and a place\ngroups of persons have begun to gather and apply to become members of it's most esteemed group of scholars. I have been debating weather to apply myself though I am uncertain what Tra might think of such things. Perhaps I will ask him... write tomorrow.\n4th of Sun's Smile 1545\n\nI have stayed up all night writing down my views and thoughts on polyamory and such. hopefully this does not lead me to having a hard time with humanity in the future.\n24th of the deep cold 1545 \n\nArtimec seems to wish me not to become a scholar in the library of Dragur. He seems to wish that I do not leave the city for next to any reason. He's become rather protective of me but he doesn't love me and\nlikely never will. He will never marry me. I will never be more then just a sex partner.\n\nI will start in a new book upon the new year.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary: Slave", "Hileia'elr", "Kivessin got his payback for me getting him banished, I suppose... He kidnapped me, and sold me to an Uruk. Roklah'Braduk, a blacksmith. So far, he's kicked, scarred, and branded me with a big 'B' on my back.\nIt hasn't been too bad so far... By comparison. Although, when Roklah isn't around, the other Uruk throw food at me and make fun of me.\n\nAside from Kivessin being pissed, Kale isn't that happy, either.\nI understand why she's mad, though. I don't think she has a right to be, but... I understand. Kale and Kivessin were an item, so it must pain her to not be able to run the clinic and see him at the same time. I'm not mad at her, though.\nAlthough, Kivessin is going to pay when I escape from this prison of a city... I don't care how far I have to go. He ruined every aspect of my life... My career, my love lift, and my own body.\nOf course, I won't kill him... I can find a punishment even worse than death for good ol' Kivessin. He told me that, \"I'll only make you go through what I did,\" and, \"I hope you've learned your lesson, Hileia.\"\nWhat Kivessin doesn't realize is that I'M the good guy here, HE'S the criminal. He killed a noble, and since he was a guard, I had to tell someone... I was the good citizen, he was the murderer. I swear, he'll suffer once I escape...\n-------------------Today, I was kicked by three other Uruk whilst Roklah was out. I wanted to communicate with them, so I attempted to speak 'Blah.' They didn't appreciate it. I was thrown onto the ground by one of them, the beaten.\nOne kicked me in the eye so hard, I need an eyepatch now... This is why I hate Uruk.\n\nAfter chopping down wood, Roklah took me to the Caliphate to auction me off. Someone tried buying me, but when the bid was too low,\nmy master just dragged me back to the Iron Uzg. Now, I'm sitting here writing, while he makes some sword.\n\n-------------------Kale... Actually visited me. She heard about the auction, and she tried to buy me back.\nI am a bit... in shock. I thought she didn't care about me anymore. She offered my master 100 minas, far more than at the auction. He decided he wanted to keep me though, simply to show me off to, 'The Rex.'\nKale wished to speak to me, but... I don't think I'm quite ready for that, yet.\n\nRecently, I've been picking up on the so called 'Language' called Blah. It's easy to do that if you stay in one place long enough...\n\"Too bad I can't use it, though... A non-Uruk speaking Blah is like... I'm not even sure. It's just disrespectful. It's alright, though. They're disgusting creatures, anyhow. I don't care to speak their language.\n-------------------\nWhilst I was cutting down more trees, Roklah and his crew joined me to get more wood for some project... I dropped the axe on the ground, then ran for the docks. Instantly, I went to the Caliphate.\nRunning away was sure to get me a beating, but I didn't care. I  wanted to visit the Caliphate... The place I hadn't visited in months. \n\nWhen I arrived, Kale was treating a patient in her clinic.\nShe instantly stopped what she was doing to greet me with open arms. Now, she's finishing up in the surgical room, and then she's going to serve us some tea.\nOh wow... That was, uh... Surprising. Not much happened, but Kale told me that she was never a 'Thing' with Kivessin in the first place! It was just to get him out of some arranged marriage... The nerve.\nWhile I am slightly upset that they lied to me about that, I also don't mind... After all, this should mean that Kale won't mind when I cast Kivessin into a living nightmare.\n-------------------I suppose I haven't learned my lesson.\nAfter returning to the Iron Uzg, I got a punch to the forehead. That was it, though. Nothing serious... Although, now I'm in Laureh'lin. And I just lost 60 mina from gambling...\nSome geezer named Lornengoth or something. Green eyes, long white beard, no shirt. Whatever, though. He won it fair and square through gambling with me all night. Lucky him.\n-------------------\nBack in the Iron Uzg... After another week of work, there's some... Tournament happening. Something the Uruk call 'Klomping.' I heard a horn sound while I was on the road, so I came to watch.\nSome people from the Caliphate were coming in to fight, so the Uruk already there needed to warm up... And guess who they used as their training dummy? That's right, the only non-Uruk there. I was just a punching bag for 10 minutes.\nWhen the arena was full of fighters and spectators, the fighting began. So many Uruk were there, but plenty of Valah, Mali, and Kah. One fight after the next, it came down to the final two: The Rex himself, and some guy named Rilkor.\nThe first match was won by the Rex. He beat Rilkor to the ground... I was surprised he was alright to keep on going! Although, in the second round, The Rex took quite a beating. In the final round, Rilkor came out on top.\nNow, he received some sword as his prize, and he's, 'Champion of the Iron Uzg.' I didn't pay too much attention... I don't care much for this type of entertainment.\n-------------------\nLooking through my bag today, while Roklah was busy repairing some tools, I found an old book written by Nienna. It was her dark arts book... I had never read it before, so I decided to give it a read.\nIt's all very fascinating. Puppets bound by darkness, mages rising dead bodies from their graves; However, one particular article caught my eye...\nSoul contractors... The idea of binding your soul to a physical document is quite... scary. Scary, but interesting. And I was wondering- Is this a possible option for revenge on Kivessin?\nNo, revenge is the wrong word... I don't want revenge. I simply want to rid him from this world to protect everyone else from his evil presence. Maybe send him into a deep sleep, where he has the most wonderful dreams.\nEither way, I wouldn't mind sacraficing something of mine to keep him from harming others... If a contract is what it takes, then that's what I'll do. I would just need to actually FIND someone with the ability to make a contract, first...\nHa, hell, I'd do it myself if I had to! Wait, no... That wouldn't work. I would still have to carry out the process myself, even if I did know soul contracting magic. And I really have no way to do that, besides kill him...\nBut who am I kidding? He's an assasin, and I'm a Mali'aheral from Haelun'or that writes romance novels for a living- Well, used to, anyways... But still, becoming a soul contractor... I wonder what that's like for them.\nI bet it's fun for them, but I couldn't imagine skinning someone alive. It must be an awful process that would drive one to insanity. And for something so trivial as a contract? Well, actually, I can see why it'd be important...\n-------------------Do I even have anything else to live for? Those gates are wide open, and I could just run out, but... What would be the point? I suppose I should learn how the world has been changed since I've been gone...\nBut what if it's changed for the worse? Maybe there's nothing left for me out there, but... If there isn't, staying in this hell hole isn't going to solve anything. I just have to run for it, if Roklah comes for my head, so be it.\n-------------------About to enter the Caliphate again... With no clothes. I'm done with this diary. After almost a year of writing, I think it'd be best to leave it as it is. Although, that just means that I can start a new chapter to my life.\n~Hileia'elr.", ""),
        StaticBook("Digowen Part 1", "Jallentime", "One cold winters morning, upon the breast of new fallen snow, there stood a proud spruce forest of irrefutable infamy. There is nothing immediately discernible about these woods; the trees carried the same burdens of frost and insects as any other for\nmiles around. But what this forest did have, and that was quite unheard at the time, was a name. Digowen Woods was the name given to it, or at least that was the name etched into the sign just outside. If you decided to follow this sign you would find\nyourself upon the shambles of an old frontier road, long since buried under mounds upon mounds of soil and brown pine needles, only apparent from the trees whom still could not breach the stone laid so very long ago. It was peaceful here, in inherently\nominous. On this particular day a tattered huntsman trudged his way through the thicket, scattering leaves and pine-cones at his feet as he dragged a chain of cold, metal traps behind him. He stopped only a moment at a time, his eyes gazing at the\nlandscape around him and the ghostly breaths emanating from his throat, before he would lay down his trap and pull back the jagged teeth around it. The huntsman's pattern continued well on into the day, until the sun passed well over it's perch in the sky\nand began to refract it's light upon the forest floor. Golden brown sunshine danced throughout the canopy, signaling the forest creatures that night would soon belong to the predators, of whom Nature did not count it's intruder.\nThe huntsman, sadly, realized the error he had made too late, and found himself far from home, in a world not his own. He dragged his coarse leather boots through the rotting needles, clearing a small section of the forest floor to himself as the last\nbeams of light shone through the mist above him. He laid down on this small amount of luxury, and stared skyward at the cloudless midnight above him, his mind slowly counting each star and naming them off to himself. Soon his eyelids fell, and his dreams\novertook him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Discrimination", "Faenor Mithron", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        Discrimination\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        A poem by:\n    Dedicant Faenor\nWhen I was a child\n\nI was raised by high elves that were pretty mild\n\nI was tought what they thought\nWhile we fought\n\nEven amongst our own kin \n\nLike they were trash in a bin\n\nNow that I have left my purity behind\n\nI see now that we were blind\nThe other races\n\nJust have diffrent faces\n\nWe are all the same truthfully\n\nWe just all live in diffrent communities\n\nOrcs, Elves, Humans, Dwarves, Halflings, even the Kha!\nNow the orcs probably think this is Skah\n\nBut it is the truth of the matter\n\nWe were raised to be served on a plater\n\nI was blind but now I see\n\nSo I plea\nThat we can all leave our diffrences behind\n\nAnd become intertwined\n\nLife would be swell\n\nAnd not like hell\n\nIf we all just worked together \n\nWe could float like a feather\nLeaving our diffrences behind", ""),
        StaticBook("DISPENSATION", "Mylas", "-DISPENSATION OF KHA; TI'GOBSER-\n\nThis cat is pardoned of the universal ban on Kha, its pelt to remain on its own body, and to travel freely in Felsen without undue harm or arrest.\n\n-MAYOR SEAL-", ""),
        StaticBook("DMN-01", "liam_barnett", "Dirk Martijn Novokain\n\nArrest record\n\n14th of Malin's Welcome, 1567\n\nRecorded by Bell Sano at the time of interrogation\nThis was recorded as a suspect for the Felsen Dock Bombings, on the night of the 12th, was interrogated. Written by Bell Sano, along with the assistance of Velulaei'Ilum.\nThis man is a suspect due to multiple reports from citizens, which are a match to his own. Members of the Gold Corps handed him over to the guard. Bright, ginger hair, very light blue eyes, gold and white clothing.\nSano: \"Where were you on the night of the 12th of Malin's Welcome?\"\n\nDirk: \"I was in the Aethermoore tavern, bartending as usual.\"\nAnalysis: Suspect seems to be employed as a bar tender, and denies being at the scene at the time of the explosion.\nIlum: \"What is your business here in Oren?\"\n\nDirk: \"I mostly come here to buy iron for my smith, not really anything else.\"\nIlum: \"So you have no stake in the safety of this city?\"\n\nDirk: \"I think I have family here, so I do. Lovets are my extended family. Wouldn't want to see them in harm under any circumstances.\"\nAnalysis: Suspect seems to only come to Felsen for business, and may have family within the walls.\nSano: \"How about the night of the 11th? When the fires broke out?\"\n\nDirk: \"I came to the city when I heard of the fires.\"\nSano: \"So you deny being within the walls at the time of the outbreak?\"\n\nDirk: \"Yes, I do. I was arrested due to a misunderstanding when I arrived, but was released minutes later.\"\nSano: \"What were you arrested for then, may I ask?\"\n\nDirk: \"A twist of words, I stated Ave Orenia as I went to help with the fires, but it was twisted to seem as if I were a rebel.\"\nAnalysis: Suspect seems to also deny any act of arson.\nIlum: \"Where did you go after being set free, then?\"\n\nDirk: \"To the Aethermoor tavern, to continue bartending as I had been before the attack.\"\nIlum: \"Then why did you return to Oren after the second attack?\"\n\nDirk: \"I didn't, actually. I continued working.\"\n\nSano: \"Yet you were arrested at the crime scene.\"\nDirk: \"Karver sent a bird for me to come to the Felsen docks, so I did.\"\n\nSano: \"So you did return to Oren after the second attacks?\"\n\nDirk: \"After the second attack, yes.\"\nSano: \"Yet, you already claimed that you were working after the second attack?\"\n\nDirk: \"I continued to work, then came to Oren when a bird was sent. Simple.\"\nAnalysis: Conflicting information, will examine further. However, a man named Karver was indeed at the docks.\nSano: \"What's your economic background, Novokain?\"\n\nDirk: \"Blacksmith. Or do you mean as a child? Farmer.\"\nSano: \"That's not an answer, I asked for your economic background, not your profession. What's your wallet look like?\"\n\nDirk: \"Middle class.\"\nSano: \"Do you have any ties to nobility?\"\n\nDirk: \"Yes, I know many nobles. Some may even call me one.\"\n\nSano: \"That's exactly what I was looking for, thank you.\"\nAnalysis: Suspect may have great wealth, or ties to those of a higher social status.\nFinal analysis:\n\n-No noticeable motive\n-No confessed training in explosives\n-Potentially has plenty of mina\n-Seems to have no connections to the helmet found in the wreck\nIlum claims that explosives had been sold at the Cloud Temple market only a day earlier, for one hundred mina.", ""),
        StaticBook("Do not Read", "Captain_Burnzie", "If you're reading this. you're probably dead. sorry....", ""),
        StaticBook("Don't Die Please", "Samuel de Saltpans", "20th of The Grand Harvest, 1547\n\nDear Edgar,\n\n   I hope you survive and do not die. If you don't die, celebrate with these.\n\nWith Brotherly Love,\nSamuel de Saltpan", ""),
        StaticBook("Dont let in", "Valden Shade", "*No ex girl friends\n*No Galen\n*No one untrusted\n*People you hate\n*People we hate\n*People that break at steal our shit\n       That is all", ""),
        StaticBook("Dots.", "A.N.C.", "Dots.\nby A.N.C.\nSummer spring. Winter fall.\n    River drop. Rain bend.\n    Dawn evening. Midnight morning.\n    All things, con\n    nected.", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 1", "Fenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\"\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: I thank you dearly for reading the first four chapters of \"Double Dragon!\" I wish to specially thank Valeria Yule for all her support. Now, onto the story!\n================Amnesia Can Be A Bite In, Fuqua, And The Demon In Her           Hair.\n================\nChapter One: \nNew Folsom. Not a bad place to live. But then again, it wasn't exactly a good place either. Crime ran amok and the guards were crooked. The Mob ran this town and everyone in it… but it's practically the only place left to live.\nMy name is Fuqua, at least thats what Shamone says it is. I can’t remember anything besides him and his… Somewhat rude entry into my life. Everythings still blurry about him, but from what I can gather, Shamone and I are connected permanently.\nLiterally. I’m hiding him under my hat right now. He says he’s a parasite and that he’ll just be taking some of my food every now and then. Theres only one problem with that. His mouth is on the back of my head and he’s using my hair as his arms and legs…\nI guess you could say that ever since he’s latched onto me, its just been one big, long, bad hair day… Well… Heres my story…\nChapter Two: A Rude Awakening.\nI woke up in a room in New Folsom’s Tavern, The Rusty Nail, with a skull splitting headache. I lazily sat up, rubbing my face and then scratching the back of my head. “Hey! Watch the hands Kid!” A brutish voice said.\nI screamed in surprise, leaping out of the bed and turning around to find… Nothing… There was no one be found… I stood there, extremely confused. Where had that voice come from?\nAs I pondered this thought, the voice called out again “Hey babe, when can we get some food, I’m starvin up here!” I yelped and spun around, now for sure that someone was here. “W-who’s there!?” I asked worriedly. My heart was beating a mile a minute.\n“I’m right behind you, can’t you see?” The voice said. I slowly turned, scanning the room for any signs of life, but all I saw was a pile of clothes next to the bed. “Are you invisible?” I asked, still looking around carefully.\nThe voice laughed in a deep gruff tone, being easily identifiable as male. “I wish! But hey, its fun messin with ya! I’m on the back of your head!” The voice said. I froze, as I reached my hands up to my hair,\n“The… Back of my head?” I asked, more than worried. He responds “You bet! Be careful reachin around back there; don’t want ya puttin my eyes out!” The tough sounding voice laughed heartily, deeply amused by this.\nAs my hands slowly trailed up the back of my head, they glided against… A tongue!? I pulled my hands back terrified and disgusted, hopping around the room and shaking the slimy saliva off of my hands “EWEWEWEWEW!” I exclaimed in a frightened voice.\nThe monster spat, like he was trying to get a bad taste out of his mouth. “Ew yourself! You taste as if you haven’t washed in days! Which makes sense, I was wondering when you’d wake up.” The monster retorted. I paused at this last piece of news,\nnot jumping around anymore. “What do you mean by that?” I asked, now more worried than scared. “Well… When I formed a symbiosis with you, ya just kinda conked out. Sorry about that, but a parasites gotta eat ya know!” The beast replied.\nI tried to remember what had happened, but the further back I went, the less there seemed to be. In fact… There was almost nothing. My head was empty and devoid of memories! I couldn't even remember what I was wearing before that monster was put me under!\nI rushed over to the pile of clothes, picking them up and examining them. They appeared to be some type of uniform for girls. The full uniform consisted of a white, long sleeved button up shirt with breast pockets and sleeve cuffs,\na black skirt that reached my lower thighs, a pair of high black stockings, reaching about 3 ½ inches away from the bottom of the skirt. Underneath the clothing there was also a pair of dark brown leather loafers.\nI pulled the clothes over my underwear covered body, before angrily asking the thing on my head “Just who are you anyways!” The monster snorted and said “The names Shamone. Nice ta meet ya Ms. Fuqua.”\nChapter Three: My Hair Eats Weird.\nAt that time, I was pissed. I mean, I had some kind of demon thing in my hair! It was just so… Gross. I growled in anger, trying to pull the parasite off of my scalp, but to no avail.\nI sighed and decided it would be best to try and just cope with the thing. I made my way to the bedroom door to exit, when a flash of white on the coat rack caught my eye. It was a hat! A white bowler hat with a black ribbon around it to be precise.\nI snatched up the hat and slipped it on over my head and Shamone. “Hey! I can’t see!” He shouted out in protest. I hushed him promptly, punching the hat in on my head, knocking against Shamones large crooked teeth.\n“I’m not giving out food for free. The least you could do is lay low and not make me look like a freak.” I said, to Shamone. The parasite mumbled to himself before going silent under the hat. I nodded my head, before heading out the door,\npast the empty hallway to the stairs heading down. It was a normal bar scene for midday… Unoccupied and desolate. Except for the massive rusted spike sticking out of the ground. It took center stage of the bar and was about 4 ½ feet tall.\nI thought to myself 'That is one serious accident waiting to happen.'  Before heading to the bar counter “What do you have for food?” I asked the bartender. The man looks up from cleaning a glass out with a rag.\n“We got some steak and some bread leftover from chefs last cooking session. If ya want that, it’ll be 20 Dollops and 15 Schments.” Said the bartender. I held a hand up, about to ask what that means,\nand then figured it must be the money that this place uses… Or even that I used to use. I digged in my breast pockets, pulling out a couple of paper folds with numbers on them and a few coins. The numbers on the coins read 25 and the bill read 50.\nI handed everything to the man, hoping he would sort out what he needs and give me back my change. The bartender nods his head, taking a portion of the coins, and going to get the plate of food from the slightly heated oven.\nThe aroma of warm steak and bread wafted over to me and my recently acquired demon. Shamone squirmed under my hat as the smell came his way. I pulled the bowler down tight, slightly smothering Shamone, as he gnashed his teeth in complaint.\nI coughed loudly to try and cover the noise he was making, going to take the wooden platter of food from the man. “Thank you sir.” I said as I made my way over to the corner of the bar as fast as I could.\nI sat down at a corner table and immediately began to dig into the bread, tearing hungrily at it, having not eaten for at least a day I knew I would probably regret eating all this food in one sitting at some point and not saving any for later.\nShamone growls lightly and says “Kid… I’m gettin impatient with my food. I can steal from your stomach when I want, but that takes longer.” I sighed deeply, leaning against the table, not really wanting to feed the monstrosity on my head.\n“Fine… Here, quick.” I said as I grabbed up the steak with a knife and fork, cutting it in half and holding up the piece of meat behind me, then swiftly tilting up the hat. Shamone darted forward,\nchomping up the steak and slinking back under the hat, chewing sloppily. I looked around the room to see if anyone had noticed, and thankfully the bar was still deserted.\nI continued to eat my food, as a man walked in, heavily armed and armored, going to talk to the bartender.\nChapter Four: Milk Goes Good With Murder.\nI finished my food, getting up to give back the wooden platter to the bartender. I sat down at one of the stools next to the counter, “Got any anything to drink? I asked curiously.\nThe bartender nods his head “We have beers, whiskeys, wines, you name it, we probably have it.\" The bartender said, examining the large stock behind him. \"Hmm... Do you have any milk?\" I asked, seeing if they really did have everything a bar could have.\n\"You're in luck, got our last pint in stock. That’ll be 10 Dollops.” He said as he went into the back to get the milk. I retrieved the money from my breast pocket, setting it on the counter and relaxing a little.\nThe heavily armored man who entered earlier scooted closer to me, as the bartender returned with the glass of milk, a straw sticking out of it. I latched onto the straw, holding the glass in both hands, as I drank deeply from it.\nThe taste of it was wondrous! It must have been a favorite of mine from before… Well I suppose since before I met Shamone. As I was about half way done with my milk, the armored man, for some reason, decided it would be a good idea to try and hit on me,\nand slung an arm around my shoulder. “Hey pretty lady, how about I get you a real drink for a real good time?” He says with a smug grin. “Uh, no thanks, we already have a drink.” Shamone said for me. The armored man just smiled and said “Deep voice huh?\nI can dig it...\" I was about to speak up, before Shamone acted up again “THATS IT, HE HAD HIS CHANCE!” The parasite shouted. My hair exploded upwards, Shamones maw stretching wide, his two yellow glowing eyes staring hatred at the armored man.\nThe man stumbled back, “A p-parasite!?” He was barely able to get that out, before spikes and arrows of hair grew from my naturally short black hair, going to slam into him at an upwards angle, tossing him into the air. I turned around in surprise,\nKnocking the rest of the milk over, the glass shattering onto the floor. Time seemed to slow, as I saw the man land on the spike, and soon afterwards impale himself upon it. His chest bursted outward, as the huge spike impaled him, bits of gore flying\nHere and there. He grabbed at the big spike in his body, struggling briefly, before the life in his eyes faded to nothingness. I stood there, shocked at what had just happened, as my hat floated back down onto my head. I quickly pulled it on over the\nParasite. \"Guards! We have a monster in here!\" The barkeep shouted, alerting the nearby populace. I ran out of the bar and into the crowded streets full of staring eyes. Tears sprung to my own eyes as I passed the still bleeding corpse on the rusty nail\nIn the floor. This day had gone from bad to worse...\n================-End Of Part One-\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nArt: ----------->\n======Character Art\n((http://i.imgur.com/rn780uy.png?))\nFuqua, our main protagonist in Double Dragon!", ""),
        StaticBook("Dr.Kn. Pamphlet", "Heruza", "Dread Knights seem to be ancient suits of armour inhabited by tormented souls. They were created by Blood Mages to attack the people of Asulon. Dread Knights were created when men and women challenged the Blood Mages in one-on-one duels and lost.\nTheir souls were forever doomed to serve the Blood Mages, and bound to suits of armour. Dread Knights do not seem to be inherently evil. To defeat a Dread Knight, one must seperate all parts of their armour, disabling the Dread Knight's ability to kill.\nOver time, however, a Dread Knight will pull itself back together again, unlike our unfortunate Humpty Dumpty. Dread Knights are scarily adept at combat as their endurance makes them nearly impossible to kill with mere scratches.\nTo completely destroy a Dread Knight, one can melt down the suit of armor that the Dread Knight is bound to. That is the end of this small instructional pamphlet on Dread Knights.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragon Princess", "Niera Acal'elor", "Once upon a time, in a kingdom far far away, there was a king and queen who lived in a golden castle with their beautiful daughter. They lived in peace and prosperity, and never knew heartbreak or want.\nYet one night, an ugly orc captured the princess and carried her away, locking her up in a tall, dark tower. \n\nThe king and queen were struck with immeasurable grief and promised the princess's hand to any knight who could rescure thier child.\nSo the knights in the land assembled, wanting to bring the princess back to be their bride. \n\nThe Orc roared in anger when he saw the approaching knights. And one by one, he tore them to shreds at the foot of the tower.\nThe princess looked on in horror as her rescuers were slewn. She shrunk back into the confines of her room, weeping as she thought of her fate. \n\nYet someone heard her cries...\nhe princess was awakened by the sound of thunderous wings, flapping in the moonlit sky. A large Dragon, with obsidian scales clung to the side of the dragon, baring his large teeth at the orc.\nThe creature took a deep breath, and in one burst of flame, turned the orc to ash. \nThe dragon then turned his attention to the princess, prying apart the bars that held her in the tower\nShe carefully climbed upon the dragon’s back, and the dragon beat his wings once more, bringing her up into the clouds. \nThe dragon returned the princess to the king and queen, and they were in awe at such a marvelous creature.\nYet, how could they keep their promise? How could a dragon wed their daughter? When asked this, the dragon started to transform in a blinding light, until all that remained was a handsome prince in his place.\nThe princess looked upon her savior, and the dragon took her to be his loving wife. \n\n\n\nThey both lived happily ever after. The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur's Brood", "Thurak'Yar", "Dragur's Brood\n\nAnd one of the few stories known of them.\n\n\n\nRe-Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, 21'st of The First Seed, 1489.\nThe Dragons all descended from Dragur, an Arch-Daemon of the land named Asulon. Dragur’s true form is that of a dragon, so the appearance of his offspring is of no surprise. Dragur raised the first of his brood in his volcanic lair, and taught them\nvast knowledge and wisdom. Like their father, the dragons are capable of morphing into a humanoid shape. The majority of the brood are wise and indifferent to mortals, sometimes posing as scholars or mages; spending their time distributing their\nknowledge of the realms with the races of this world. However, a certain sect of Dragur’s offspring exists, known as Drakes. The scales of these drakes have turned to a shade back as night. These Drakes, unlike their brothers the Dragons, are heavily\nopposed to mortals, sometimes spending time in humanoid form purely to destroy them or to spread corruption in hopes of turning them against each other.\nAfter the creation of his brood, Dragur fell into a deep slumber within the volcano, and\nhas yet to be awakened. In spite of this, the dragons are overseen by a Matriarch, or \"Queen\".\nAs the brood grew, they began to scatter across the land, some going off into the mainlands, or even farther into the opposite ends of the world. Some stayed close to their birth home, such as the Matriarch as well as Velketzar. Velketzar was the first\nborn male of the brood. While Xandraza was born with the mind of Dragur, the yearning for knowledge and learning, Velketzar was born with the strength, pride, and sense of wanting to protect. This Dragon worked closely with the past civilizations\nof Asulon, ensuring that peace was kepy between them and that they prospered. In his humanoid form he was known and respected greatly across the lands. Always possessing an astounding amount of patience, he thought things through\nfor the best possible outcomes.\n\n*The shade of ink turns from old to fresh, at the start of a new paragraph. It seems to be a new entry*\nHowever, as much as he wanted it to, no everything could stay in the peaceful serenity he so desperately worked for… There was just some hate in the hearts of beings that one could never come to change, for Velketzar, he felt pity\nupon these. Few of the brood saw how he aided these creature, as they were so far beneath them, and while some attempted to understand, others simply refused to care at all, and shunned him for his passion. But alas, it wasn't simply his own kind\nthat acted in such a manner. The humanoids he helped, some sought greed over all, and despite how much they already had in this world, nothing satisfied their thirst for gaining more wealth of power… Thus lead to the day of betrayal.\nThe day when some of us cast aside the trust of us and stole knowledge for their own personal gains came too soon. After that day, Xandraza and Velketzar sought out what they could together but could only find so much. Velketzar’s pride\nhad been dealt a heavy blow. He was born with the sense of urge to protect, and he felt he had failed to aid Xandraza in the protection of her vast collection of scrolls and books. Depression fell upon him greatly; he stopped visiting the civilians, and\nalthough she tried her best to console him and tell him that, indeed, in time, together they would perhaps be able to recover that which was stolen, Xandraza’s words would not reach him. His emotions slowly began to consume him.\nOne day after Xandraza returned to the island, filled with happiness after reclaiming another book in ruins, her eyes befell Velketzar and her heart sank. Once a bright healthy ruby shade of red, his scales had begun to dull in colour, and had saturated\nnearly to a dank brow. Bringing him outside so he could see for himself in the light of the sun, Velketzar finally understood what he was becoming. His head grew clouded with his emotions, as Dragons, it is known, have the strongest emotions\nof all creatures. Sadness and rage overtook him, and blinded by this the urge to halting his protection against corruption grew. And then he stopped, and began to think. Pondering on the best possible outcome, as he always did...\nAnd so Velketzar changed into his true form, and with determined rage, he destroyed the mountain on the east side of that island that was their home. For what reason? It didn’t occur to Xandraza what he was doing before it was too late. He was making\na clearing for himself. Once he had enough space, he stood at the edge of the island, looking out to sea. And then it began. First, his claws, spikes and horns began to harden and turn to stone, then his wings, arms and legs went next... All turning\nto rock. He did this to himself… But why? \"Do not think ill of me.\" He said to Xandraza who watched, mortified and as still as the stone he was becoming. \"I do not wish to become one of them. I wish to stay in the good of your heart. I will guard\nthis island so that what has happened may never happen again, and I hope in time, my scales will return to that shine and hue you love so dearly. Goodbye.\"\nAnd as the final whip of his tail slammed into the side of the volcano, it too then turned to stone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dream Journal", "Jayce Vulcan", "Jayce's Dream Journal\n\nNight 1. I've decided to start this dream journal to keep track of the strange recurring dreams I've been getting. They show of my old Ker family, the father a strong rogue alchemist and the mother a strong miner. With two sons.\nNight 1 Cont.\nThe dreams show of a Ker family being trapped in ice, and ice spikes, impaing them. Maybe this was my family before I was taken into the Human family? I want these questions answered but to watch them in pain of the ice was horrible.\nNight 8: I havent been plagued with the same dreams until tonight, most of the others are mostly of the battles I've fought and the people I remember the most. This dream was different, this one was about my human family, my mother, I hadnt remembered....\nNight 8 Cont.\nWho or what she did. I remember my father, he was smith and developed a passion for smithing in me but the dream showed my mother as a witch, Fire, enveloping on her finger tips.\nNight 9: I feel embarrassed to admit this but the night before I had a dream... about Marcy. I don't know why but it wasn't a bad dream or a...intimate dream. It was just me, cooking and making plates of breakfast while she and her son Pern..was it?\nNight 9 Cont: Were sitting at the table, playing a game. After I had finished the breakfast I brung it over to the table and Marcy pecked me on the cheek. I was blustered by it but I dont know...", ""),
        StaticBook("Dream of Darknes", "Lagertha Ojørna", "A Dream of Darkness\n\n\n\n\n         Written by\n      Lagertha Ojorna\nTo Agatha,\n     Someone who can\nmake my bitterness into warmth.\nIn deep sleep, I see what is a dark misty entity. It lingers in the darkness before coming upon a ruin within a forest.\n    The ruin is covered in hanging moss, and is in a crumble. The mist finds no entry, so instead forces its self upon a crumbling-\nwall.\n    The wall gives in after much force is applied to it. The mist continues on, now inside the ruin.\n    The mist makes its through the ruin, a long corridore. On each side of the corridore are pedastals, each with a unique tome upon it.\nThe mist then turns into a room larger than the corridore. There it finds five pedastals with one tome on each. It begins attacking them, shredding them and destroying the pedastals.\n    One of the five pedastals sink into the stone floor below, -\nprotecting the tome on it. The mist, now giving a feeling of enragement, is then surrounded by 6 warriors whom seem to be conjurations.\n    The warriors charge at the mist, who then sinks into the ground with the pedastal, destroying the tome.\nAt this moment, the ruinm begins to shake. The ceiling crumbles, and caves in on the warriors. The mist comes from the ground and forces its way out of the debris.\n    The mist comes upon darkness, and disappears. Taking whatever knowledge it-\ndestroyed within the tomes.\n\n\n    \"Neither by chance,\nnor fate.\"\n\n       - Algor Ojorna", ""),
        StaticBook("Drink Menu", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Roth Jayamen's\n       Restaurant\n           and\n      Entertainment\n      Establishment\n\n\n      -----------\n           Drink\n           Menu\n     -------------\nAlcoholic Beverages\nPale Ale\n\nYour run of the mill ale. Made with boiled then cooled water, then put through the brewing process. It has a moderate amount of alcohol.\n\n4 Minas\nRed Wine\n\nRed wine made with boiled then cooled water, then put through the wine making process. It has a high content of alcohol. Best to drink slowly.\n\n6 Minas\nTeas\nRose petal tea\n\nTea made mainly from rose petals and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel more relaxed and rejuvenated. \n\n2 Minas\nWake Up Herbal Tea\n\nTea made mainly from Herbs, made to help the drinker more alert. Caution as it is very bitter.\n\n2 Minas\nPine leaf tea\n\nTea made mainly from Pine leaves and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel more relaxed and rejuvenated it has a crisp taste. \n\n3 Minas\nBirch leaf tea\n\nTea made mainly from Birch leafs and other herbs, made to help the drinker gain more awareness of their surroundings. \n\n3 Minas\nDandelion Petal Tea\n\nTea made mainly from Dandelion petals and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel fuller and at ease. It goes great with a small meal.\n\n4 Minas\nPoppy Tea\n\nTea made mainly from Poppy petals and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel healthier and helps relieve stress.\n\n4 Minas\nChamomile Tea\n\nTea made mainly from Oxeye daisy petals and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel more calm and breath better.\n\n4 Minas\nJuices\nPumpkin Juice\n\nJuice made from pumpkins, it helps keep you cool when in hot climates.\n\n5 Minas\nMelon Juice\n\nJuice made from Sweet Melons, it is VERY sweet. Not for people who can’t handle too much sweetness.\n\n5 Minas\nCarrot Juice\n\nJuice made from Carrots, it helps keep you cool when in humid climates.\n\n5 Minas\nOther\nEggnog\n\nA drink made with creamy and sweet goodness. Makes you filled with energy!\n\n6 Minas\nWater\n\nBoiled then cooled water.\n\nFree\nPlease remember to return all bottles and menus!\n\nThank you and have a good day!\n\n~Roth Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Driscoll Log 1", "Aifric Driscoll", "The 1st Journal of Aifric Driscoll\n-------------------16th of the First Seed, 1501:\nI have decided to begin a journal so I may revisit my life at a later date, and perhaps others will read it and know the name Aifric Driscoll.\nI was born in a village northwest of Petrus. My father was a humble blacksmith. Alas, my mother had died during childbirth. I grew up helping my father, and life was very simple and peaceful. That was all before the raid. I remember walking through the\nvillage center one day and seeing smoke rising from the outskirts. I heard the helpless cries of women and children alike as they began to be butchered by a merciless group of bandits. I ran to my father's shop, and found him arming himself. He told me,\n\"Aifric, my son, today is not your day to die. Take this food and your gradfather's sword, and run as fast as you can. I will stay here. I have lived a good life.\" With that he ran out the door, screaming his war cry as he ran toward the sounds of death.\nI ran as quickly as I could to the top of the hill overlooking the village and looked back over my shoulder. I could see my father bravely facing two bandits in the thick smoke. He managed to strike one down but the other stabbed him through the middle,\nand he crumpled to the ground. I distinctly remember running aimlessly through the forest, unsure what to do and overcome with grief. I was 16 then. I found a road at some point and lay down alongside it to sleep. I was awoken, however, by a small caravan\npassing by. It is a blur of memories now, but they ended up recruiting me and for 10 years I worked my way through the ranks, ending up as a guard for the caravan. I have brutal memories from this point in my life. I slew many men and could never become\nquite accustomed to that dirty business. Once I was 26 years of age, I decided it was time for a change. I wanted to achieve redemption for my sins and become a sort of religious man. I wanted to either join the clergy of the Church of the True Faith or\nbecome a monk in a monastery somewhere. I assumed Petrus was my best chance of finding clergy to speak to about my thoughts and feelings. I traveled there and immediately applied for citizenship, excited for my new life to begin. I soon found the Bishopin\nthe church, but not in the circumstances I had imagined. The Horde of Dunamis had made a small raid into the city and I witnessed them slaughter to guards before making their way into the church. They met the bishop there, and the man took his death\nwell. He knew he was going to achieve heaven and he simply sat there as they slaughtered him. They cut off his head and placed it on the altar and left laughing. The pagan bastards. Two other witnesses and I took the body and head to the Petrus graveyard\nand held a simple ceremony for him there before placing him in the ground. His grave is still unmarked, as far as I'm aware. After that incident, I was left to wander Athera at my discretion. I came across a man by the name Fjordin on the stone road, and\nI remembered that he had met me earlier and warned me of bandits, not to mention giving me some cooked mutton for my travels. We got talking again and he invited me to join him in working on his new settlement. He called it Sylversands, and it lies east\nof Petrus acroos the large lake, in the badlands. I followed him there and he quickly found me lodging and a place to call my home. I am forever grateful to him for taking me in after my hardships and offering me a place in his\ncommunity. He is a very good man and I feel very strong feelings of loyalty to him. His plans are grand and I am honored to take part in the creation of his beautiful city. \n\nRecently we have been gathering huge amounts of sand to\ncompress into sandstone for his town. The sandstone works well with the badlands background we reside in. We have been discussing forms of government and ways of running Sylversands once we gain residents and become established.\nHe recently brought on a new recruit by the name of Kulde. She is a good worker and a lovely addition to our pioneer party. In fact, she is very beautiful and I must admit I am quite taken with her.\n6th of the Grand Harvest, 1501\nYesterday I found Kulde at a tavern and quickly, and nervously, asked to buy her a drink. She was very pleasant but alas there was no bartender in sight. I went with her to the Red Rose tavern in search of drink,\nbut found no better luck. A man by the name of Sekra was there, however, and we quickly engaged with him in conversation. He is a farmer and levyman in Oren, and I asked him if he sought opportunity for a new, fresh start on life. He did, and to help\nimprove relations with everyone I bought drinks for Kulde, Sekra, and a friend of Kulde's called Sergeant Cromwell. I offered Sekra a chance to meet Fjordin and see if he wanted to join us in our new expedition. He seemed very intersted and I obtained his\nplace of residence so we may contact him once Fjordin is available to talk. With that we concluded our talk and dispersed on our own travels. \n\nI really hope Kulde has taken at least some interest in me. She is beautiful and\nI can't help but be nervous around her. Perhaps in time she will come to like me. We shall see.\n\n15th of the Amber Cold\nIt has been awhile since I last wrote. In my time around Sylverport, as we have dubbed our\nsettlement, as well as Red Rose Tavern, I have discovered a few things about myself. I love pretty women, and am beginning to love good ale, as well as having good conversations with people. I have found myself pursuing yet another woman by the name of\nGwyneth. She is a High Elf, but she is still beautiful regardless. Hopefully I will set my heart on one perfect lady in time. \nThe settlement is going far better than expected. We have eleven members, with at least one from every race besides orcs,and\nour diplomatic relations are improving. I have high hopes for Sylverport. Alas, I must go, because with such a rapidly growing settlement there is much work to be done!\n16th of Snow's Maiden, 1502\n\nIt has been awhile since I have written, but not much has happened over the course of this harsh winter. We have around eleven members in our town, and we almost have three complete houses, including\nmine! My home is beautiful and I have Fjordin's architectural skills to thank for that. Food is running low... Hopefully what we have lasts us until we can begin harvesting the winter wheat. \n\nNot much has happened with my\nrelationship with the ladies. I have grown slightly closer to Gwyneth, I suppose, but nothing significant has happened. I haven't seen Kulde in a long while. I miss her and really hope to see her soon. This town needs more pretty faces around!\n16th of Malin's Welcome, 1504\n\nI can't believe I have let this much time pass since I wrote last. So much has happened, and I've been too busy to think about it I suppose. Sadly, I will undoubtedly have forgotten some important things in the time I have\nspent slacking on this duty. Ah well... What can a man do when the time has already come and passed him by? \n\nI suppose I should talk about our wonderful Sylverport. It has grown into a town with around five houses, each housing two or three members or\nso, and where the farm was Fjordin designed and constructed a beautiful town hall. It looks incredible and majestic, but still maintains an air of modesty and simplicity that I greatly enjoy. We are adding a harbor addition, with a tavern below it called\n\"Drowning Sorrows Sandbar and Grill\". Obviously Fjordin's design, with the obvious puns in the title. The town has come a long ways, and is beginning to look like a real, developed settlement. \nRecently, the King of Oren paid a visit, and after a long\ndinner in which he and Fjordin conversed about the settlement and its plans, the King has decided to vassalize us. And not only that. We are to become our very own province, and the provincial governor will be Fjordin himself! A wood elf! Under Oren! He\nwasn't asked to snip his ears either, and this goes to show how popular we are becoming with the Orenians. We have a fair reputation building, and I only see improvement in the future. \nI realize that I obviously am confused as to which woman I want to\npursue, and I believe I have finally made a choice. I haven't seen Kulde in a very long while, and I suppose I have just lost interest in her absence. Gwyneth, for some reason, just doesn't seem worth pursuing romantically. There has been an addition to\nthe town that I must admit I am infatuated with. Her name is Mira Casswell. She has taken up the profession of lumberjack, and I must say she is very talented in her work. She is also undeniably gorgeous. I can't help but look at her beauty whenever I\nhave the chance. She has red hair and isn't very formal, which I like. She is just naturally attractive, and I am trying to muster the courage to make my romantic interest for her known. Hopefully I am not denied, and I don't stutter or say something\nstupid.... Ah, enough of that for now. I really must be going. The town needs much work. I will try to remember to write again soon. \n\n12th of Sun's Smile, 1509\nI cannot even express how frustrated I am with myself. It has been five years since I have\nlast written. Considering this, it would be impossible to even try and summarize my life since my last entry. I suppose I could write a few major events down. The town has grown considerably, and we have a harbor, tavern, blacksmith, and many houses. We\nhave also managed to expand our borders to encompass all of the Mesa overshadowing the town, so we may now build a church or fort there. I am still a Sentinel here, but Fjordin has now devised three ministries that will help in managing the province. One\nis the Ministry of Truth, which informs the public and spearheads scientific operations, and is, according to Fjordin, the most important ministry. Another is the Ministry of Peace, which manages foreign policy, and appoints ambassadors and manages\nembassies. It monitors laws and their accordance with our core beliefs, and is responsible for enforcing the law and keeping a functioning town watch. The last ministry is the Ministry of Enlightenment, which regulates and executes religious matters\nwithin the city, as well as preserves and enforces its traditions. It is largely composed of scholars and clergymen respectively. In addition to the ministries, there are the two major and two minor Unions, which are Industrial (Mining, lumberjacking,\nblacksmithing), Agricultural (Farming, fishing, breeding, cooking), Artisan (Leatherworking, woodworking, stonemasonry), and Arcane (Alchemy, runesmithing, tinkering). I feel that this will be a very effective and highly functional system, both original\nin design and quite intuitive. \nAnd of Mira... She is beautiful as ever, and after moving out has to an extent moved back in. I was, to say the least.... heartbroken when she told me that she is now engaged and has a fiance. They are taking some time\napart, so she is staying here in Sylverport. Perhaps she will lose interest in him and cancel their marriage, and I can be with her. I love her more than most anyone and above all hope that she remains safe. Anyways, considering the lack of entries, it\nwould probably be wise for me to begin a new journal. I will finish this one now, and submit it to Berilac to store in our records. If you are reading this, feel free to search for my second journal for a continuation of my story. Farewell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Anthology", "Aeran Winterleaf", "Druid Anthology\n                    \n                   By\n\n     Aeran Winterleaf\n\n\nA collection of poems\n      created by the\n        Druidic Order\n\n    Published 16th of\n     Sun's Smile, 1507\nDedicant Poem by Veren\n\nThe leaves rustle as the winds blow strong,\n\nFlowers blossom and protect the beautiful place,\n\nThe Druids protect the beautiful place,\n\nWhile the Aspects\nguide with strength and grace\n\nThe Druids watch the void grow strong,\n\nTrying to protect the things we love.\n\nAs nature listens so subtle and quiet,\n\nThe world grows on, forever strong.\nNatural Poem by Virella Deathsbane\n\nThe peaceful grass.\nThe blowing wind.\nBlooming flowers.\nAnd the tall trees.\nThe matters of them connect to one.\nNature, it's all, for us all.\n\nLinked Together.\nA Druid serves nature.\nLinked to one.\nSame as the roots with trees.\nThe sun protects with plants.\nA family with support.\nAll is linked together.\n \nDandelion Fuzz\n\nBlooming with the wind\nNothing is sinned.\nThe fuzz flies and plants.\nNewcomers join to sprout and dance.\nHaikus by Anarane\n\nFox\n\nYour coat is pretty,\n\nColours of Orange, black, and white,\n\nYour cuteness hides strength.\nTree\n\nYou hands are green\n\nYou wave hello and goodbye\n\nYour roots are endless\nOwl\n\nYou are large and wise\n\nSleep at day, hunt in the night\n\nYou don't give a hoot\nThe Aspects by Gi'Garun\n\nFar away in lands afar,\nThe aspects began their work.\n\nLong ago in times that passed,\nOur Nature began to stir.\n\nThe Green lady's radiance,\nBlesses the crops.\n\nThe Green Man's strength,\nBlesses the worthy.\n\nFlowers and Fruits and Seasons from her.\nPredators, tigers, hunters, from him.\n\nSaviours of the Races,\nCreators of Nature\nThe children respect them,\nThe children praise them.\nFiary Ring by Heroxis\n\nSearching the night,\nNight quietly green.\nDeep in the forest,\nNo one has seen.\n\nThe circle of fungi,\nI enter you now.\nA force I sense,\nGreeting with a bow.\n\nTo sing in the rain,\nTo write in the sun.\nTo draw in the clouds,\nAttuned as one.\nPoem by Smurgla\n\nEveryone has a purpose. Love yourself.\n\nEveryone has a trooth. Believe yourself.\n\nEveryone has a vocie. Listen to yourself.\nEveryone has a friend inside. Trust yourself.\n\nEveryone has a purpose. Stick to yourself.\n\nEveryone has a reason. Do not listen to no one else for yourself is all that matters.\nPoem by Isabella\n\nFlower Flowers!\nPretty flowers\nHow do you like to grow?\nIn rain the flowers reply, up in the Druids grove\n\nFlowers flowers \nblooming flowers\nWhy are you coloured so?\nCause we spread the joy ,the flowers sing, all around the world.\n\nFlowers flowers dying flowers\nWhy do you look so gloom?\nOur time has come, the flowers cough, and its time to go below.\nAutumn by Taynuel\n\nThe leaves are losing shade again\n\nFading to golds and reds\n\nThe flowers have all gone to sleep\n\nSweet nothings in their heads\nThe wind blusters o'er hill and dale\n\nThe weather quickly chilling\n\nPreparing for the winter's dawn\n\nAnd frosty cold unyielding\n\nThe bears and squirrels make final\nmoves\n\nPrepared for their long slumber\n\nFinding their caves and nests in trees\n\nIn which all will be warmer\n\nYounglings laugh and play together\nIn piles of fallen brush\n\nAll bundled up in coats and scarves\n\nNoses and cheeks all flush\n\nIt's time to say goodbye to summer\n\nThe warmth, the growth, the sunshine\nAlthough the clouds gather overhead\n\nWhat's coming can be divine\n\nSnow gathers on each rooftop once\n\nThe coloured season is through\n\nTime for loved ones to cuddle up\nTogether till spring starts anew\nAbandon by Chirr\n\nYou left me when we were young.\n\nLeft me with my falling tears.\n\nI felt like I was no one.\n\nFor so many painful years.\n\nI cried at night\nwishing you were there.\n\nHow could you do this to me?\n\nDid you not see how that was unfair?\n\nLife was a horrible mess.\n\nMy heart so bad I couldn't rest.\nFalling tears that fall.\n\nShow that I've been through it all.\n\nThe cause you leaving me.\n\nWe are together now but it isn't the same.\n\nHeart aches and you are to blame\nIf you saw me crying maybe you'd regret what you've done\n\nRight now I will live my life as no one.\nA Forest Poem by Nivndil\n\nPuerith'leyu\n\nThe trees they stand,\nA clamor of souls.\n\nTheir voices born on\nWinds, are old\n\nBoughs up high,\nFairy halls,\nRoots below,\nSilent foot-falls.\n\nThey stand and wait\nFor times unborn\n\nTo whisper secrets,\nBefore words were forged.\n\nAmongst their trunks.\nBeneath canopy dome.\nTo bathe in twilight,\nThe trees my home.\nFair Ethanriel by the Song Druid\n\nEthanriel\n\nIt was the perfection of the Aspects that afford me her prospects.\n\nEven as I saw her for the first time I did blush soft, as each time she held me aloft.\nAncient wisdom hanging as vines, set apart from the bird and the pine.\n\nMother and lover, mistress and wife, bark and leaf-love of mine life.\n\nI stand living while she on her side, as if am ere tree fallen by the tide.\nElandriel gives me please, come back, save us.\n\nTarry not, give no sign of hestiation, only obedience, only inclination.\n\nBlessed mother, home to our brothers, lives on in some regard.\nSacrifice greatly rendered, a loss mourned, and no payment tendered.\n\nThe Druids can never recover, from a loss like no other, but memory does push onward and strength does persist.\n\nEthanriel, Ethanriel, Mother tree of\nElandriel... keep watch from the Aspects' favour.\nHerb by Thudrin\n\nStuff it in your pipe and light\n\nSmoke all day, smoke all night\n\nRoll one, maybe two\n\nSend them clouds up into the blue.\nPetrichor by Endvani\n\nPetrichor, Petrichor\nSpice and season Petrichor,\nMay the sky kiss your cheeks,\nthe rain wash away your weeps,\ntill I am aty our side\n\nPetrichor, Petrichor\nSweet perfume of petrichor\nRainsong soft with thunder's beat,\nbring your dreams,\ntill we meet.\n\nPetrichor, Petrichor\nWinds and waves petrichor\nMoonlight will my promise keep,\nlike the bond of stubborn, faithful sleep,\ntill I am at your side.\nListen by Meiala\n\nListen.\n\nListen to the chirps.\n\nListen to the peeps.\n\nListen to the howls.\n\nListen to the creeks.\n\nListen to your heart.\nListen to your mind.\n\nIt'll all be better.\n\n    Just give it...\n\n...some time.\nAfterword:\n\nBe kind!", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Circle", "Leyun Kameki", "The Druidic Circle\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nThe Druidic Order and a Druidic Circle are two different groups, but are tied closely together. The Order is not of a Circle, but a Circle is of the Order. All Druids who are taught under the Druidic Order are members of the Order, but those taught under\none particular Circle are not members of another Circle.\n\nDifferent Circles are rare to exist; this is because differing Circles have differing Druidic beliefs, studies, and structures. In the Order’s past, new Circles were fored because of\ndisagreements and differing beliefs, though in the end, those disagreements and differing beliefs were realized to have been senseless and the Circles reformed and conformed to prior belief and focus.\nDuring the First and Second Age of Schisms of the Druidic Order’s history, disagreements rose and differing beliefs accumulated which resulted in the Order splitting into multiple Circles. However, it became apparent to the Druids of all Circles during\nboth ages that in order to effectively and efficiently perform the Aspects’ will they’d have to stick together in one large Circle; it was noticed that they began to fail at bringing up and teaching new Druids. The Order is strongest as one unit.\nA Druidic Circle is defined as a set group of Druids who have a particular focus; that focus could be in the lines of responsibility or it could be an entire different belief. The focus, those teachings, studies, and et cetera,\nof the Druidic Order Circle of Malinor are true and are in true allegiance with the Aspects and Nature. A word to the wise: keep close to one another, Druii, and stay true to Nature and to both Aspects; don’t begin a third Age of Schisms. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid History", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The History\n   of the Druids\n\n      by N. Evitan\nLong ago, two factions of mages fought each other to the bloody end. Good, evil, the sides mattered not, their battle devastated whole cities and forests. At this, the peak of the battle, the first dream came to a young elven girl. She began gathering\nothers around her, teaching the Druidic ways. The first druids were born from the humble beginning. Like a great wave, the young order swept across the land and surrounded the two guilds. The druids destroyed them, turning them all to mere rodents and\nanimals of the forest. The druids went on to preserve the land for a millennia afterwards.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Research", "Librarian Azkel Frostbeard", "Druidism Research\nWorship the aspects\n\n- 2 aspects:\n\nCerridwen - birth and growth\n\nCernunnos- hunting and animals\n\nTogether they are the embodiment of nature and balance\nRules of Druidism:\n\n- voidal base magics are unnatural\n\n-promote ideals of peace and harmony\nCode of Conduct:\n\n-No fighting or killing fellow druids\n\n-Only use violence in self defense\nRanks:\n\nStart as dedicant, when deemed ready, you are granted powers, moved to druid rank\nNature:\n\nProtect the balance of nature\n\nmake sure the unnatural dont affect it", "")
    )

    private fun _VAILOR_2(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Druidic Studies", "Aria Lanyathir", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Ariadni Lanyathir's\nDruid Studies.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=- Index -=-=-=\n\nCh 1: Aspects\nCh 2: Blessings\nCh 3: Balance\nCh 4: Cycle of Life\nCh 5: The Order\nCh 6: Totems\nCh 7: Powers\nCh 8: Responsibilities\nCh 9: Ranks\n=-=-=-Aspects-=-=-=\n\nCerridwen: Mother of the Harvest.\n\nCernunnos: Father of the Hunt.\nCerridwen is the Mother of the Harvest, the Green Lady and the Woman of Morn.\n\nCernunnos is the Father of the Hunt and the Great Huntsman.\n=-=-=Blessings=-=-=\n\nCerridwen's blessings cover all harvests and marriages. Newly-weds may also receive the blessing of many children.\n\nCernunnos' blessings are used upon armies and honourable fighters.\n=-=-=Balance=-=-=\n\nThe balance of nature is one in which every life that lives is fair and just. None shall perish, both plants and animals, without a natural end. If their end is not natural, then a Druid is able to interfere to save the nature and\nwildlife from their unfateful end. However, is a forest is alite due to a natural storm or weather, then a Druid musn't interfere, but rather let nature run its course. This promotes the natural life cycle of all organisms.\n=-= Cycle of Life =-=\n\nThe Cycle of Life has 4 phases. Birth, Maturity-Growth, Reproduction and Death.\n\nBirth:\nBeginning of a New Life.\nMaturity-Growth:\nGrowth Stages into Adulthood.\n\nReproduction:\nFinding a Mate to create a new life.\n\nDeath:\nLoss of life.\n\nThe Food Chain is the order in which animals eat one another; the\n'Chain'.\nDecendants don't have a place in this chain, but would be near the Top, otherwise.\n=-=- The Order -=-=\n\nThe Druids are dedicated to preserving the balance of nature. Druids undergo learning and studying in order to establish a strong link with nature; a bond.\nThe Order is open to all races.\n=-=-= Totems =-=-=\n\nA Totem is a title that defines and identifies who a Druid is, representing their history, personality and approach to life. Only one Druid may possess a specific totem at one time.\n=-=-= Powers =-=-=\n\nThe extent of a Druid's powers are unknown, though they are some of the best healers and are deeply connected with nature. They serve nature, often using their powers in the form of favours.\n=- Responsibilities -=\n\nA Druid is a keeper and protector of nature. A Druid works to maintain the balance and peace of nature, possibly allowing the removal of a tree of forest, but expect each tree to be replanted elsewhere in return; balance.\n=-=-=- Ranks -=-=-=\n\nDedicants:\nThe students and learners of Druidism, under a Druid Guide.\n\nDruids:\nThe main rank, the middle position of the Order after Dedicants and before the Inner Circle.\nDruid Guides:\nThe teachers and 'newbies' of the Inner Circle.\n\nArch-Druids:\nThe heads of the Inner Circle. They maintain all affairs and have direct contact with the Aspects themselves. This is how most orders from the Asoects are\nconveyed.\n\nGrand-Druids:\nMiddleman for if a split were to occur.\n\nHierophants:\nRetired Inner Circle members, though still extremely strong. Respectable Druids.\n\nNotable Druids:\nUsually deceased\nDruids who have made such an impact on the Order and nature that they're kept on record as High Status Druids.\n\nDemi-Aspects:\nDeceased Druids who have passed on to join the Aspects; One of the highest honours the Order can bestow.\nSeekers:\nThe first rank amongst Druidism; People that have taken an interest in the Aspects, the Druids, and their practices.\n\nAcolyte:\nOne who is learning Druidism outside of the Order.\nLost Druids:\nDruids that have disappeared without a trace of explanation. Their return may result in punishment.\n\nForgotten Druids:\nDruids that have been removed from the Order, whether it's by death or unattunement, but despite being 'Forgotten', many of\nthese Druids are unforgotten due to their accomplishments.\n\nShunned Druids:\nDruids that have been shunned by an Arch Druid, due to their actions that have threatened the protection or peace of the Order. No Druid of the Order is peritted to speak with\none, but if a Shunned approached them, they must only say:\n\"Much wind pours from your mouth\".\nIf the Shunned persists, Druids should either ignore them or warn them that defensive action may be taken. This action should be carried out if the Shunned does\nnot heed the warning. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=By:\n    Ariadni Lanyathir", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Tasks", "Iatrilemar Elervathar", "Dedicancy started:\nThe 22nd of Sun's Smile.\n\nDedicant:\nAnthron\n\nTeacher:\nAeras Ibar'ker\n\nPS: Suns smile 1515\nPPS: Tay gave most\nof the tasks.\nFirst task:\nThe Aspect Cycle\n\nFind three objects that each represent one of the aspects\n\n*Aeras's signature*\nSecond task:\nBardic Rite\n\nWrite a poem about nature\n\n*Taynuel's signature*e\nThird Task: \nHat task\n\nCreate a hat with things you find in nature.\n\n*Tay's signature.*\nFourth Task:\nTen Flowers\n\nFind ten different types of flowers and plant them around the Grove.\n\n*Tay's signature.*\nFifth task: \nShrooms\n\nFind a woodland creature, get its feces, smear them under your armpit and grow a shroom.\n\n*Tay's signature*\nFirst Lesson:\n\nAll things in the world are natural, trees leaves and even stones. There is but one thing in the world that's unnatural. The Void. This is why when a mage opens the passage from the Void to the realm we live in. a huge amount of\nunnatural energy is released and why Void slinging is dangerous to nature and its balance.\nSixth task:\nA Lecture on Void Slinging.\n\nGo to different cities and lecture to 10 different people about Void slinging and why it's bad.\n\n*Aeras's signature*\nSeventh Task: One With Nature\n\nPretend to be a carrot for an elven hour.\n\n*Tay's signature*\nEighth Task: Study Time\n\nRead the history of the Druidic Order\n\n*Tay's signature*\nNineth task: \nGather the wool\n\nGather wool without shaving a sheep.\n\n*Aeras' signature*\nTenth Task: The List\n\nObtain the following items:\n1) A scrap of cloth from a high elf's robes\n2) A stone from dwarven lands\n3) A cup of sand from orcish lands\n4) An apple from Oren\n\n*Tay's signature*\nEleventh Task: Grow a Tree\n\nSelect a sapling of your choice and grow it into a tree, bonding with it as you do.\n\n*Tay's signature*\nTwelfth Task: Rite of the Staff\n\nUsing a branch from the tree you grew, carve your first Druid's staff.\n\n*Tay's signature*", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidism", "Leyu", "Druidism\nIs this what the druid college is like...? Being idnapped and forced to write books? Er, kidnapped. Not idnapped. They think I'm a druid for some reason... It's as if they're brainwashed.\nThey think I'm an elf, too! I'm a damn dwarf! They trapped Bell in here, too. She's also forced to write. He just said to write..anything. I guess this will be okay to write, maybe...? I'm just jotting down notes... And my thoughts... And why is htis\nhappening!? So, what do write now. I don't even feel like making paragraphs. Hmm. Well, since I last wrote in a journal, Many things have happened. For one, I've been indulged in a quest to find an ancient artifact... It's a magical artifact from\nWinterfall that the undead want. Now it's in the hands of one, named Hwaldar, who hid it. I rea some clues. It's from the Kar'Lani tribe, and is hidden in the \"fake father of Al'Khazaar\". It's cold there, too. I find the whole quest odd, found by books\nwritten by Hwaldar, who is actually an undead himself, yet HE hid the artifact. I've been living in Al'Khazaar and Laurelin latly. I left Al'Khazaar because the rulers were stupid and no one even realized it, causing a bad monarchy. I went\nto Laurelin, where it turns out a friend did too. Nothing much happened for a while. But then, a few days ago, I found some lvers near a pumpkin and was playing around with them, when a druid invited me in his house to give me a book. I accepted, of\ncourse. I like books. But when I came in, the druid blocked off the door, and gave me enough books to fill my backpack. He commanded me to write and hit me a few times. My friend I mentioned earlier, Bell, was there. The druid was trying to brainwash us\nor something. He kept on saying we were elves and druids, which neither of us were. Bell's human and I'm a dwarf. And I don't think either of us would want to study druidism after this.... Anyways. Thankfully, a guard found it. Er, not it. us. He tried\nto break us out, when the druid teleported Bell and I to the treetops on top of his house . We found a way back down, and I hit him a few times. He then ran away. So pretty much, I think I'll go back to Al'Khazaar... but I'll write about the next\nadventure . I went to go to Al'Khazaar with Bell after being kidnapped. On the road, we met two men who pleaded for Bell's help to heal a man named Ademas. We went to follow, but Bell dissapeared. I still don't know where she is. We continued on\nthe path, along with an orc shaman who tagged along. Once we got there, the shaman accidentally activated the demon inside him while trying to destroy it. The demon went mad. I wrote about it in a different book. He eventually jumped off a cliff and\ndied. A while later, the Oren carnival opened. It was fun at first. I won 100 minas at an archery tournament, and watched others fight in the Fight Pits . The Wizard gave me a fortune. He said I would be either a great protector of good or an evil\nbandit. It's obviously a load of crap. But then, something actually happened at the carnival. Undead attacked. A man revealed himself to be undead and lit the place on fire. The king of Al'Khazaar didn't even notice. He, along with the rest of human\nroyalty, is just STUPID. There's no other way to put it. Then everyone just continued playing games, even after a few men died. They didn't even CARE. The people of this world are fools. Maybe the undead do have a point...no. Untrue. Just untrue.\nAnyways, Brum, the first undead I ever met came. veryone thought he was a pale orc, even though he's admitted to be undead many times . The fools... the idiots, the fools... I went to watch one fight. A man that looked very similar to an earlier undead\ncame. He even used the same teqnique; He set the ground on fire wherever he walked to kill the opponets. The fools.. no one noticed, even when I said it. I am surrounded by oblivious morons. No one understands what is going on... I would write\nmore about my life, but I realize I just don't know who will get this book. I might die and good looted. I mean, get looted. Anyways, I can't let people know of my feelings or all of my thoughts. That's pretty much all of my life so far that I care to\nshare.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidism", "Jistuma", "Is this what the druid college is like…? Being idnapped and forced to write books? Er, kidnapped. Not idnapped. They think I’m a druid for some reason… It’s as if they’re brainwashed.\nThey think I’m an elf, too! I’m a damn dwarf! They trapped Bell in here, too. She’s also forced to write. He just said to write..anything. I guess this will be okay to write, maybe…? I’m just jotting down notes… And my thoughts… And why is this\nhappening!? So, what do write now. I don’t even feel like making paragraphs. Hmm. Well, since I last wrote in a journal, Many things have happened. For one, I’ve been indulged in a quest to find an ancient artifact… It’s a magical artifact from\nWinterfall that the undead want. Now it’s in the hands of one named Hwaldar, who hid it. I rea some clues. It’s from the Kar’Lani tribe, and is hidden in the “fake father of Al’Kazaar”. It’s cold there, too. I find the whole quest odd, found by books\nwritten by Hwaldar, who is actually an undead himself, yet HE hid the artifact.\nI’ve been living in Al’Khazaar and Laurelin latly. I left Al’Khazaar because the rulers were stupid and no one even realized it, causing a bad monarchy. I went to Laurelin, where it turns out a friend did too. Nothing much happened for a while.\nBut then, a few days ago, I found some lvers near a pumpkin and was playing around with them, when a druid invited me in his house to give me a book. I accepted, of course. I like books. But when I came in, the druid blocked off the door, and gave me\nenough books to fill my backpack. He commanded me to write and hit me a few times. My friend I mentioned earlier, Bell, was there. The druid was trying to brainwash us or something. He kept on saying we were elven and druids, which neither of us were.\nBell’s human and I’m a dwarf. And I don’t think either of us would want to study druidism after this… Anyways. Thankfully, a guard found it.Er, not it. Us. He tried to break us out, when the druid teleported Bell and I to the treetops on top of his house.\nWe found a way back down, and I hit him a few times. He then ran away. So pretty much, I think I’ll go back to Al’Khazaar… but I’ll write about the next adventure.\nI went to go to Al’Khazaar with Bell after being kidnapped. On the road, we met two men who pleaded for Bell’s help to heal a man named Ademas. We went to follow, but Bell disappeared. I still don’t know where she is. We continued on the path, along with\nan orc shaman who tagged along. Once we got there, the shaman accidentally activated the demon inside him while trying to destroy it. The demon went mad. I wrote about it in a different book. He eventually jumped off a cliff and died.\nA while later, the Oren carnival opened. It was fin at first. I won 100 minas at an archery tournament, and watched others fight in the Fight Pits. The Wizard gave me a fortune. He said I would be either a great protector of good or an evil bandit.\nIt’s obviously a load of crap. But then, something actually happened at the carnival. Undead attacked. A man revealed himself to be undead and lit the place on fire. The king of Al’Khazaar didn’t even notice. He, along with the rest of the human royalty,\nis just STUPID. There’s no other way to put it. Then everyone just continued playing games, even after a few men died. They didn’t even CARE. The people of this world are fools. Maybe the undead do have a point…no. Untrue. Just untrue.\nAnyways, Brum, the first undead I ever met came. Everyone thought he was a pale orc, even thought he’s admitted to be undead many times. The fools… the idiots, the fools… I went to watch one fight. A man that looked very similar to an earlier undead came.\nHe even used the same tequique; He set the ground on fire wherever he walked to kill the opponents. The fools… no one noticed, even when I said it. I am surrounded by oblivious morons. No one understands what is going on…\nI would write more about my life, but I realize I just don’t know who will get this book. I might die and good looted. I mean, get looted. Anyways, I can’t let people know of my feelings or all my thoughts. That’s pretty much all of my life so far that I\ncare to share.\nDruidism\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidology", "Aerxuis", "Druidology—What is a Druid \nby Druid Respiren\ntranscribed by Elorna Avern\nDruids are the drui, the dryw, the druwid. Nature's sorcerer, the seer, the oak-knower.\n For those that know the oak, the troew is both the tree and the truth. Mysterious guardian of a sacred grove, wise counselor to monarchs, cunning\nmaster of many shapes, friend of animals, and terrible defender, of unspoiled Nature. The Druid revere Nature, wielding power over plants, animals, the weather, and the elements. All druids are of neutral alignment and share an ethos\nThis book was originally found in the Druid's Grove in Elandriel, in Asulon. It was brought over and transcribed by Elorna Avern.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dungeons & Drake", "Zeliek", "Dungeons and Drakes Handbook.   \n\n        Modifers\n\nStr - Applies to Melee attacks, Dmg rolls, Climb, jump and swim check. Other Str checks (Breaking down doors)\nDex - Applies to range attack, Your Armor check, Reflex saving, Dex skills.\n\nCon - Applies to leveling hp, Fortidute saving, Concentrating\n\nInt - Skill points each level, Int skills.\nWis - Will saving, Will skills.\n\nCha - Cha skills, Influencing others, Clerics and paladins for undead.\nCombat\n\nAttack roll - Roll d20 and add attack bonus. 20 means crit, 1 means fail.\n\nAttack bonus - Melee attack bonus is Base attk - Str mod and Size mod.\n\nRange - Base, Dex, size and range pen\nDmg - When attack hits, roll weapon dmg and add str mod or dex mod for range\n\nAc - What you need to roll to hit, always over 10. Ac is equal to 10 - armor bonus - shield bonus and Dex mod and Size mod.\n\nTouch attack - Over 10 to hit.\nHp - When -1 hp you can't move and have a 10% chance to get back up. -10 hp you die.\n\nIntaitive - Roll d20 to determine turn order and add Dex mod.\n\nFlat footed - Before Intaitive takes place you are flat footed and loose Dex mod to\nYour Ac. This does not apply to rouges or barbarins.\n\nSurprise - If not aware or sneaked up on you are Surprised. Losing your Ac and taking a hit.\n\nAttacks of opertunity - If an enemy is attacking someone else a player can attack -\nThem back for free. yet only once per round.\n\nSpells - Spells take one full turn to charge and cast, they must roll for concentration and then for Ac and hitting.\nTreasure - Monster treasure is lvl 1 - 300gp lvl2 - 600 gp\n\nlvl3 - 900 gp", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarf Babies", "Aerxuis", "Where Do Dwarven Babies Come From?\n\nWritten By: Unknown\nCopied By: Aerx\n\n17th of Amber Cold, 1473\n\nwould look like. IIIIUUUUU, it sounds. And hairy, very very hairy.\nNormal babies come when a man and a woman mate, and after pregnancy a baby is born. Well, if you notice, there are almost no woman Dwarves, but I will state why this is\nfurther in. The true ways are far more disgusting and frightening than mating can ever be, it is a mixture or ale and hair.\nDeep inside the mountains of the Dwarven towns, deep underground, are special and greatly guarded rooms. It\nis in these hidden rooms that the baby Dwarves are born. I was quite lucky that I found such a room when the guards were fully drunk and had knocked each other out. So I entered the room and by the creator! It smelled worse than the drunks just\noutside!\nIn a room which seemed filled with puke and ale, there were chunks of what looked like hair. Some of the hair like chunks were even moving. At that time I heard talking just outside the room, and in fear of being discovered, hid\nmyself behind a rock. A Dwarf came in completely drunk and with a knife in his hand.\n“By Yakemar, ay s’all ‘ave a son!”, he shouted before he cut part of his beard.\nI watched stunned as this happened, I could never believe a\nDwarf had cut his own beard, but soon I would know why the Dwarves treasure their beards so much. Releasing the knife he fell on his knees and coddled the beard near his chest.\n“Ya will be named Grikot.”, he said, and that is when it\ncame to me, all those other hair chunks, were in fact part of the beards of other Dwarves.\nThe Dwarf placed the beard chunk down, and picking a bottle, tilted ale over the beard before leaving. So you see, dear readers, the Dwarves\ntreasure their beard because it is from it that their children will be born from. So where do the small amount of female Dwarves come from? As I walked out I realized that one of the chunks was very small, and that the baby could be seen. A female\nDwarf is born when a Dwarf, being far too drunk, doesn’t cut enough of his beard, and such, the Dwarf is born beardless, becoming this way, a woman.\nNow, onto the types of Dwarves, as you should know, the are cave Dwarves, mountain Dwarves\nand mountain Dwarves. After discovering such intriguing ways of conceiving a child, I searched further and found out the reasons. Cave Dwarves are the ones where the room in inside a deep care. Mountain Dwarves, the cave is dug\ninside a mountain but it does not go very deep. Both of these type of Dwarves, as they were born inside a room by willing drunkenness. Forest Dwarves are born on the outside, from which when the drunkeness is so great, they couldn't find the room. That is\nthe reason Forest Dwarves are looked down upon by the others, they were not born in the rooms for the beard to be placed.\n\nI hope this text has helped the reader to understand the hairy way of Dwarf birth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarf Babies", "Rosso", "Where do dwarf babies come from?\nHave you ever wondered how the dwarven numbers rise? Of course you have, you look at them and think so. The truth is, there are baby dwarves. Quite a statement I know, just think of how a dwarven baby would look like. IIIIUUUUUU, it sounds hairy!!! And\nyes... it is very very hairy.\n\nNormal babies come when a man and a woman mate, and after pregnancy a baby is born. Well, if you notice, there are almost no woman dwarves, but I will state why this is further in. The true\nways are far more disgusting and frightening than mating can ever be, it is a mixture of ale and hair.\n\nDeep inside the mountains of the dwarven towns, deep underground, are special and greatly guarded rooms. It is in these hidden rooms\nthat the baby dwarves are born. I was quite lucky that I found such a room when the guards were fully drunk and had knocked each other out. So I entered the room and by the creator! It smelled worse than the drunks just outside!\n\nIn a room which\nseemed filled with puke and ale, there were chunks of what looked like hair. Some of the hair like chunks were even moving. At that time I heard talking just outside the room, and in fear of being discovered, hid myself behind a rock. A dwarf came in,\ncompletely drunk and with a knife in his hand. “By Yakemar, ay s’all ‘ave a son!” he shouted before he cut part of his beard.\n\nI watched stunned as this happened, I could never believe a dwarf had cut his own beard, but soon I would know why the dwarves\ntreasure their beards so much. Releasing the knife he fell on his knees and coddled the beard near his chest. “Ya will be named Grikot” he said, and that is when it came to me, all those other hair chunks, were in fact part of the beards of other dwarves.\nThe dwarf placed the beard chunk down, and picking a bottle, tilted ale over the beard before leaving. So you see dear readers, the dwarves treasure their beard because it is from it that their children will be born from. So where do the small amount of\nfemale dwarves come from? As I walked out I realized that one of the chunks was very small, and that the baby could be seen. A female dwarf is born when a dwarf, being far too drunk, doesn’t cut enough of his beard, and as such, the dwarf is born\nbeardless, becoming this way, a woman.\n\nNow, onto the types of Dwarves, as you should know, there are cave dwarves, mountain dwarves and forest dwarves. After discovering such intriguing ways of conceiving a child, I searched further\nand found out the reasons. Cave dwarves are the ones where the room in inside a deep cave. Mountain dwarves, the cave is dug inside a mountain but it does not go very deep. Both of these type of dwarves, as they were born inside a room by willing\ndrunkenness, Forest dwarves are born on the outside, from when the drunkenness is so great, they couldn’t find the room. That is the reason the Forest dwarves are looked down upon from the others, they were not born in the rooms for the beards to be\nplaced.\n\nI hope this text has helped the leader to understand the hairy way of dwarf birth.\nWhere do Dwarf babies come from\n\nOriginal author unknown\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarven D. Gate", "Granantar Fournier Ateus", "Somewhere behind a large waterfall, beside Kal'Agnar, sleeps, rather, slept, a Doom Gate. Upon entering this chilling titanic door, I entered a strange chamber with walls of lava and a massive crystal at it's core. This chamber consists\nof an upper level, and a lower level. The upper contains the large Dark Green Crystal with a levitating ring of Gold about it's peak. And a peculiar mechanism upon it's body. Both the upper and the lower levels house a massive library, far too many.......\nUpon activating the mechanism, my mind went blank, and I appeared in what appears to be a massive labyrinth conposed of leaves. After approaching what seemed to be a billboard, I learned the name of crystal was Varak Crystal. From here on\nMy senses began to wane, and my memories slowly drift. So, I began my quest to find what resides at the exit. Eventually, I came upon what seemed to be a massive treasure trove. Blocks of gold, piles of minas, diamonds and chests full of valubles scattere\ned around. Clearly not enough for one man alone to carry out. After running about for hours, I came upon what seemed to be a feasting hall. An empty feasting hall. There were four doors, one of which I entered, one which trapped with a falling log, and\ntwo, which meant my passage. Quite easily, I chose the correct door, and traversed onwards. After some time, I began to feel jubilent and suddenly I triggered a mehanism and a soft light began to glow, beckoning me to come. It was when I entered a peace-\nful grove with floting lights and grand flowers. Eventually I arrived upon another strange landmark, an infernal grass-plains, with a small razed building. Three black skulls rested on the floor of the home, and small mechanism was attached to the door.\nAfter pressing it, a secondary door had opened. Continuing onwards, I found a small garden, with four wooden chairs and a one of silvery marble, with a small tree at the core of the scape. After some time, I found a large fragment of the Varak Crystal and\nmy senses and memories returned! But the jounrey is not finished. My eyes seemed to blank as I began to see in tunnels. A black, scorched floor with chunks of flesh looming about was before me. An Infero, conflagerating two curved spires of rising flesh.\nBut in order to tread onwards, one must overcome such trepidation. As I have. With final, heavy gasp, I lunged my way into the final challenge. Relief, and rest. After having traversed this titanic labyrinth, I finally came upon the Heart of the Varak.\nA beautiful home, with a  grand garden beckoned me to rest my head. But I kindly rejected, for I sought to find Aldersberg, home. But I did not neglect my sense of curiosity, and I inspected the home, only to find it vacant, but full of books and\nalchemical instruments and reagents. This was it. The last breath I would have to gasp in this chaotic place. So I entered the exit portal. And returned to the Large Varak Crystal! And again the Sheer Cold of Kal'Agnar's mountains froze my very hairs. But\nI found this air relishing, and refreshing. There is nothing more refreshing than the land of living, even if it means sharing some mead with stubborn dwarves!", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarves: Aegis", "Azkel Frostbeard", "The Grand Kingdom of Urguan was officially founded by Grand King Thorik Grandaxe in the year 1267. Thorik wished to differentiate the new Kingdom of the Dwarves from the old and failed Kingdom of the Dwarves in the past. Due to threats of war from both\nhe Orcish Nation of Krugmar and the Holy Princedom of Malinor, and absent of King Gotrek Firemane, the Lord Marshal, Thorik Grandaxe (At the time known by the name of his bloodline, Braveaxe), opted to form a War Council. The war council intended\nto act as a counterbalance to the dwarven High Council, which had slowly displayed a growing ineptness in running the Kingdom in recent years. The War Council consisted of many of Thorik's closest commanders and advisers in the Legion, along with the\nArchbishop at the time, Thordan Irongut. When a secret meeting was held to determine how the War Council should act, it was ultimately decided that a military coup was in order. After the absence of King Gotrek for near an elven week, Thorik declared\nhimself Grand King of Urguan. He named the first of his council, Valen Grandaxe, Grand Councilor of Diplomacy, Chaecus Grandaxe, Grand Councilor of War, Stronghold Grandaxe, Grand Councilor of Economics and Broski Grandaxe, Grand Councilor of Guilds.\nFor most of its history, the Grand Kingdom of Urguan thrived, achieving great feats whilst in power. In its early years, the race of dwarves was united under a single banner again, it's military revamped and its culture spreading by the day.\nWhen the Great War broke out across Aegis, the Grand Kingdom allied with the human Kingdom of Oren, battling back the orcs into the deserts of Krugmar, while the elven Wardens, the dwarven legion's one time mortal enemy and rival were disbanded by the\nvery leaders they served to protect. Though the Great War eventually ended in a treaty of white peace, the course of the war had made it glaringly obvious that the dominant powers had shifted, the dwarf-human alliance taking the role that the orc-elf\nalliance had once held. In the years following the Great War, Grand King Thorik did his best to protect his people from the dangers of the outside world, as well as attempting to retain a natural balance and peace that would lead to unity in the face of\nthe ever growing threat of Iblees and the undead. However, after conflict arose between the Ascended Order and the Merchant City of Alras, a bounty was placed on the head of Kjell Ireheart. In response, the dwarves, feeling a challenge to their honor has\nbeen made, laid siege to and sacked the city of Alras. They also chose to abandon the worship of Aeriel and the Ascended in favor of the dwarves' ancient religion of the Brathmordakin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarves: Anthos", "Azkel Frostbeard", "Beneath Omithiel's rule, the mortal races set sail for Anthos, where the war with the orcs came to a resounding victory, upon the capture and annexation of the fortress of Storm's Crossing. Additionally, the grand city of Kal'Azgoth was completed, which\nOmithiel himself had played a heavy role in constructing. Shortly afterwards, Omithiel chose to stand down from the throne and a dwarf by the name of Thorin Grandaxe was elected to power. When Thorin took the throne of Urguan, he was able to select\nmultiple Lords, whose predecessors had either died or stepped down. However, he had inherited a fragmented Kingdom that had endured years of continuous warfare, particularly with its old time enemy, the orcish War Uzg. During his reign, seperate Kingdoms\nwere brought beneath the banner of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, effectively creating an empire. Thus, a new phase in the history of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan was declared, leading it to be known by some as the Second Grand King of Urguan. During this\ntime, the Kingdom's economy prospered, in part due to the new ruler's policy of forcibly taking minas as taxes from the majority of wealthy dwarves within the Kingdom. This effectively centralised the Kingdom's economy and led the Grand Kingdom of Urguan\ntowards becoming the richest in Anthos. Additionally, the young ruler forced the holds and Kingdoms that lived beneath him to pay quotas to his government, so as to pay off any expenses in return for Legion protection. However, a rebellion soon erupted in\nKal'Azgoth, many dwarves claiming Thorin a tyrant. When this rebellion was eventually stamped out, it only served to strengthen his rule however. He used the situation to his advantage, routing out his opponents, as well as gaining a better foothold\non power within the Kingdom. This allowed him to create an amendment, granting himself near absolute authority over the Kingdom. Despite the ascent of a new Emperor, Horen V, he was also able to retain close ties with Oren throughout most of his reign,\nmaking many friends and allies among the human nation's nobility. However, this peace was not to last. Many had long held their doubts about the Blood Pact, being viewed by some as a rather murky and unusual alliance, in light of past allegations\nagainst the Holy Oren Empire that it had been acting in support of the orcs during the fifty year war of Asulon. Though Thorin was viewed by some as a tyrant, he like many of his predecessors had attempted a gentle hand in foreign relations, unwilling to\nbreak Yemekar's Balance upon the world. With the Oren Empire's annexation of the elven nation of Malinor, pressure was placed upon Thorin to act. With the murder of Lord Nalro Grayhammer by a bannermen of the White Rose, Thorin in anger, looked to his\nallies from within Oren to seek help in destroying the Empire once and for all. It was from there that Lucius Blackmont and Pius Silverblade stepped forward, guaranteeing the support of their Houses in the event of an invasion. Reassured his plan would\nwork, Thorin held a meeting with his council and the decision was taken to declare war on Oren. As the dwarves made their advance north across the Cloud River, the Orenian army, headed by the White Rose met them in battle. To Thorin's surprise however,\nhe was betrayed. From the nearby mountains, a flanking charge was led by House Blackmont, House Silverblade and House Carrion, while the White Rose and the rest of Oren made their charge from the front. Met with defeat in battle, the dwarves shamed and\nforced to retreat, planned for the imminent defence of Storm's Crossing. When the hour was at its darkest for the sons of Urguan, something quite unusual occurred. Emperor Horen V, alongside the Order of the White Rose, abandoned Oren and traveled far\ninto the north, for reasons that are still unknown to this day. With faith in its Empire shattered, human nobility was left in disarray. The Kingdom of Salvus defected to the Grand Kingdom of Urguan and once again, the Legion advanced, this time far into\nwhat was once the territory of the Holy Oren Empire. From there, Thorin delivered his ultimatum to the newly coronated, Emperor William III. Among his terms, he demanded that the empire be dissolved and Malinor granted its independence.\nLeading over a nation, fractured by disunity and disloyalty, William surrendered Oren and accepted the terms of peace. Some did not accept his rule however and from the remnants of the Holy Oren Empire, the independent Kingdoms of Adunia and Savoie were\nformed, to add to the presently existing Kingdoms of Oren and Salvus. Eventually, every one of these Kingdoms pledged its loyalty to Thorin and the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, fearing that one would outdo the other if they did not. Hence the territories of\nthe Grand Kingdom expanded, reaching their greatest whilst covering the Karakatuan Empire, the Kingdom of Oren, the Kingdom of Adunia, the Kingdom of Savoie, the Kingdom of Salvus, as well as previously held dwarven territories in the south. Most remained\nbeneath dwarven rule until Thorin's death at the hands of the fallen Aengul, Ondnarch, the only exception being Salvus which later betrayed the dwarves and was destroyed by a joint force of dwarves and orcs. As the final order before his death, Thorin\ndrew back on his previous policies that neared Imperialism and set the dwarves on a path to becoming far more isolated once more. Upon Thorin's death by the fallen Aengul, Ondnarch, Dizzy Irongrinder was elected to power. However, due to a massive assult\nupon Kal'Azgoth by Ondnarch's minions, Dizzy was forced to abandon the city and relocate his kin to the captured fortress of Storm's Crossing which was subsequently developed into a city and renamed, Kal'Ithrun. Dizzy was eager to continue from Thorin's\nlegacy and did his best to have the Grand Kingdom reside peacefully among the nations of Anthos. Meanwhile in Oren however, a new dynasty of Kings had taken power. House Carrion had outdone the rest of Oren nobility and set itself as the leading House\nof a new Kingdom of Oren. Initial relations with the Grand Kingdom of Urguan were hostile, as raids were sent between the two nations. Grand King Dizzy eventually opted to declare war, though no advances were made and there were ultimately very few\nhostilities until peace was eventually declared in the Treaty of Krelmstad. The Lord's Council later voted to remove Dizzy Irongrinder from power, resulting in the election of Grand King Indago Stormhammer.  Though initially promising peace with Oren,\nndago later approved of a motion that divided the Lord's Council, in a decision to break the treaty with Oren and invade human lands, assisting a rebellion from House Tarus. This proved to be a fatal error and the dwarves were battled back into their own\nown lands. For a time, the war went cold and it appeared that hostilities may have come to an end. Upon the coronation of King Heinrik Carrion however, an advance was made by Oren into dwarven territories, immediately seizing the fortress of Thoringrad.\nAfter the fall of Kal'Azgoth to Ondnarch and the threats from the north of both the United Anthos Coalition and the Black Scourge, the situation in Urguan had become very bleak indeed. It was amid such termoil that the Grand Kingdom of Urguan once more\nfound itself in a position to fight back. Refusing to surrender against the coalition that Oren had created, the dwarves were eventually able to push their foes back beyond the Cloud River, until a treaty of mutual peace was signed. However, the war had\nled to a mounting opposition movement from within the Grand Kingdom, hoping to either reform or completely remove the Articles of Urguan. It had steadily become apparent that the dwarven people had become divided by various allegiances, while the sense of\nunity that had existed for hundreds of years had slowly begun to diminish. Upon Indago's death, Wulfgar Grandaxe was subsequently elected to power, upon the back of the promise that he would show a greater restraint in dealing with Oren than his\npredecessors and that he would attempt to grant the clans a higher say within dwarven government. Shortly after he was coronated, he immediately set to work upon reclaiming dwarven lands, leading at the forefront of the assault upon Kal'Azgoth, in a final\neffort to slay the fallen Aengul, Ondnarch. It was there that a dwarf by the name of Igor Ireheart sacrificed his life to release the purified Aengul, Wyrvun, thus being named his hero among the halls of Khaz'A'Dentrumm. However, after years beneath\nOndnarch's corruption, the great stone pillars that held up Kal'Azgoth had become unstable, posing potential dangers for any who lived beneath them. For that reason, Wulfgar concluded that the dwarves would continue living in Kal'Ithrun for the\nforseeable future. In attempting to reform the Grand Kingdom's government, Wulfgar signed into passing an amendment that established the first Clan Council of Urguan. However, prevented by the Lord's Council from granting it too many powers, it ultimately\nhad fewer powers than originally desired but instead would prove to act as a stepping stone to what would eventually become something greater. In dealing with Urguan's foreign affairs, Wulfgar looked towards the dwarves' ancient enemies, the orcs. Beneat\nthe leadership of a new Rex, Urik'Azog, he declared a defensive alliance between the Grand Kingdom of Urguan and the Rexdom of Krugmar that would prove strong in the years to come. Meanwhile in Oren, King Heinrik who had earlier supported a rebelion to\noverthrow the Holy Princedom of Malinor, now found himself facing a new enemy in those who had taken control of the elven nation, the Conclave of Malin. In what became known as the Teutonic Conspiracy, House Carrion claimed of a supposed plot by Mirtok\nDeNurem to slowly take control of each and every nation of Anthos, one by one. This was based upon the fact that both the rulers of Krugmar and the Conclave had originally been close advisers to Mirtok, though was more likely only inspired by fears that\nthe former leader of the Teutonic Order, an old enemy of House Carrion, would try to forcibly take control of Oren. As a result of these tensions, the Oren military, acting on the orders of King Heinrik Carrion marched its army to the Conclave,  where a\nconflict quickly broke out. The orcs who happened to be present at the time, subsequently called upon the dwarves to send aid, to which Grand King Wulfgar requested the leaders of each nation meet in Kal'Ithrun. Little progress was made however and\nHeinrik continued his accusation that the Teutonic Conspiracy was very much real.", ""),
        StaticBook("E.N Diary two", "Elvira Naromis", "9th of The First Seed 1506\n~~~~\n\nAnother boring day at the the Crimson Lotus. Although there is some sort of fight happening outside. Never the less, this is something I should not get involved in.\nHowever, recently, I've been thinking-\n-about a few things. Strangely, one of them is about the supposed all-cure, the Panacea. A supposed Alchemy concotion that is capable to curing someone fully, from their injuries to diseases and conditions that cannot be cured.\nMany say that the Panacea-\n-is impossible to make, as it supposedly requires the purest of ingredients.\nTo achieve full purity it unheard of, many state that it is impossible to gain full purity. That everyone and thing is impure. That we have both good and bad sides, in order to-\n-keep us balanced, perhaps.\nHowever, what if it was possible to achieve purity? To gain the ingredients that are needed and pure? Would it be possible to create the Panacea? Maybe, maybe not. Many Alchemists have tried to create this mythical creation but\n-the results always turned out as failures.\nSo, I've decided to perhaps research deeper into the Panacea, try and find out any clues to whenever or not it is real... or can be made? Or if there is a possible recipe for it?\nAs much as this is an impossible\n-task, that does not mean I cannot at least attempt to solve this mystery.\nHowever, I have the feeling that creating the Panacea may or may not come with a price, so I will not attempt to even create the Panacea until I know what this price may be. -\n- hopefully there won't be a price to creating the Panacea.\n\nI suppose to start off with, I should first research about the Panacea from both books and maybe from other Alchemists, see what information there is. From there, I shall brainstorm my -\n- ideas and see where to go from there. Although, I may ask Daniel to perhaps teach me more advance Alchemy, never hurts to have some extra knowledge on Alchemy.\n\n-Elvira Naromis.", ""),
        StaticBook("E.N's Diary one", "Elvi Terryal", "4th of Sun's Smile 1505\n~~~~\nIt's been a month now since Rajin was killed by Daniel and the others. Things have been normal: people are just being themselves, Beth and the others are alright.\nYet, I feel different. I feel as though a mass weight has left-\n-my shoulders and now, I can truly relax and not stress.\nIt's a wonderful feeling.\n\nYet, it brings another feeling. The feeling of being empty, having no motive. My main motive was to always overcome my past, which encouraged me to try and get on with\nlife and to find a new life. Now that motive is gone, I feel empty inside and not sure on where to go now.\n\nSo, I've been considering a few things hard over the past few days. Daniel and the others told me it's time to forget the past, and I agree with-\nthem. I need to change and this is the right moment for that change.\nThis is what I've been thinking for the past few days:\n\n- My name. Elvira Terryal is a reminder of my past, an orhaned child with no parents and was abused. Ser Dorian\nwrote in his last letter to me that, if I wish to, I can change my last name of 'Naromis'. Thus, making I more of his daughter. Also, Terryal means 'Reaper' which could easily link with the lives I murdered... Naromis means 'One of fire/flames' which fits\n-me more. Elvira Naromis, The White one of fire (or flames).\n\n- My path. Should I remain as a bartender? Should I focus more on Alchemy or magic? Or should I find a new path for myself? There are many paths and fates out there that I can choose but I'm-\nunsure on which path to venture down.\n\n-  Should I leave Athera for a bit? I have plenty more things to consider but with what's occuring in Athera recently, I need somewhere peaceful where I can think. Besides, I do enjoy travelling and finding-\nthings so perhaps I should go on a journey. Allow myself to relax and think of what to do in the future. Although, it does mean a few things: Not being to bartend at the tavern, teach Alchemy, to see the others and chat with them... they will understand-\n-thought but I will miss them if I do leave for a while.\n\nI suppose I should finish here. My hands ache from writing and I see a couple of new residents to greet. So, I should end it here.\n\n-Elvira Naromis (Terryal)", ""),
        StaticBook("Early Spring", "Leuvina Dreathen", "Early Spring\n--==--==--\nAn elderly mule hollers in protest while a man encourages him forward with a gentle prod on the rump.  The snow that froze the soil into a cold stone in the winter has now melted.  The days grew longer, as they do, and the soil\nsurrendered its water.  So the spring's mud has caught the mule and his charge deeply.  The man and his mule, without word or glance, accept their defeat to the mud.  \n    \nAn elfess watches from several cart lengths behind.  She stands just a tad off the\nroad where the evergreens still shade the ice from the sun.  She pondered helping the cemented man free his humble buggy.  She was a cripple, she thought, as her kne would take her down the road but would hardly bare a load of hard labor.  So rather than\napproching and appearing foolish to the man, she silently stood where she did.  He was surely doomed, she thought to herself, as men were simple and selfish creatures.\n\nHowever, without hesitation, the man begins his task of\nfreeing himself from the road.  His backmost left wheel dug deepest, but with a mere minute, the man had found a thick and long branch broken free during the last tempest.  Also, not very far from his first tool, he finds a thin log still firm from its\nfreshness. It was as if, the elfess thought, that some being knew of this man and left him with the tools to help himself.  He lies down the log behind the wheel just a bit behind the wheel.  He then plants the branch levering aganist the log so that the\nlifts from the mud.  The man shouts to the mule and he faithfully pulls against the mud.  The cart pulls forward just a tad, and the man struggles for several minutes before the wheel finally rolls free.  The elfess knew that it would have taken an hour\nfor her to think of such a method.  All of her books! She thought, all of her studies, and here this poor man would have out smarted her!\n\nBefore the man mounts his buggy once more he turns behind to face the elfess that\nhad not helped.  \n\n\"Come nearer!\" He called to her.\n\n\"I have a mule and wheels, come sit and ride!\" \n\nThe elfess' cheeks grew as red as roses.  He had known she was there, and he knew\nthat she had done nothing at all for him.  She was selfish and slothful, but this man had forgiven her and only thought of her wellbeing.  The elfess felt shameful of herself but still could only smile.  The man's warmth had warmed her cold ears.\nThere would be a future, she thought, in an empire of clever and gentle men.  She dared to think, for the first time, that God's men were good men and so was their empire.\n\n-Leuvina Dreathen", ""),
        StaticBook("Earthen Rocks", "Gladuos", "In this book we will be exploring the traits of common earthen materials found in the lands of Vailor. As such, we'll describe how it basically reacts to the senses, how it's formed, average weight, shape, hardness, breaking point, and finally the -\n- magical understanding of them.\nCommon earthen materials can be divided into three categories. That being metamorphic, sedimentary, and igneous rocks. \n\n   Igneous rocks are formed from the cooling of lava or magma into a solid form.\nSedimentary rocks are formed by the corrosion and deposition of other types of rocks that eventually lead into being compacted into new materials.\n\nMetamorphic rocks are formed by the intense heating of either igneous or\nsedimentary rocks which lead into fundamental changes of the rock's structure.\nGenerally there is no singular appearance to what a rock may look like but normally they are rigid, dull-colored pieces of stone that may seem grainy to the senses. \n\n   Rocks are usually very dense, hard pieces of material, mostly thanks to\ntheir natural crystalized structures. Although they can be found in grains such as sand as well.\nThere is no clear cut way to describe how rocks were originally formed without first understanding how the world itself was created, but that is a subject for another time. Although the basic understanding can be surmised for each type of common rock.\nDue to their efficient compactibility, rocks are can easily take on very dense, heavy forms. This is evident in Mankind's prevalent usage of the earthen materials to form strong constructions.\nRocks can take on a plethora of different shapes depending on how they were eroded or compacted. This can be shown in the descendant's rigorous usage of sculpting to form the many different earthen materials into statues and statuettes.\nOnce again rocks are very dense, and heavy materials. So it comes as no surprise when it's revealed that they are incredibly hard to break as well. Evident in the creation of golems, swords would be no use against these types of constructs.\nRegardless, Mankind has taken the liking to creating smashing tools to deal with these tough materials.\nThere is no set melting point for any of these materials as rocks can take on a large variety of different types. However, one can usually bet that an earthen rock will reach its melting point at about 1200 degrees Celsius.\nAnd finally, one must understand the magical signature of these materials. Now, rocks are a fairly common material on this world of ours, and such they will only hold a mediocre value of magical energies as compared to the more precious minerals such\nas gemstones.\n*Upon reaching the next page you are greeted with a plethora of diagrams, sketchings, charts, illustrations, and equations that span onwards for many many pages. They are accompanied by several notes and lines of information. The following pages -\n- merely seem to attempt supporting the previous statements, as well as point out more nuanced, less relevant points of information.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ebony Tree", "Valkamore Lebrine", "=-+Ol' Ebony Tree+-=\n\nThat old ebony tree, beauty to its core. \nIt's withered, decrepit, and wonderful bark peeling upwards towards the firmament of blue and white cloud.\nThe old ebony tree yields to an axe, stone, iron, or carbarum.\nIt is old, strong, but yea, it is old. It cannot stand against the sharpness of the cutting tool. Its bark gives way to a grit-surfaced black pillar, ready for molding.\nOnce extracted that old ebony tree does not die, oh no, it does not die.\nThough the ebony tree may be a treasure, its black ebony core is its soul, its very essence. It is a gift for those with the skills to carve it and polish it and fletch it into a creation. \nSword handles, tables, brushes and flutes. The smoothness of the\nwood would remind someone of an elder tree and its resilient wood. \nThe old ebony tree, not the easiest to identify. A natural treasure hunt, aye, but the journey is worth the treasure. Harder than oak, more pulchritudinous than a diamond. Umbral. Awe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Edgars' Notes", "Bastion Curthose", "Edgars' notes\nchar/coal gives a good base.\n\ntippens root combined with a base gives a coagulent with healing effects.\n\nthe tippens root potion gives a nice and numbing effect when blissfoil is added.\nthe last brew combined with serpents stalk gives the same effects as before but it reacts slower and makes it work longer.\nBlissfoil numbs the body.\n\nTippens root heals cuts and wounds.\n\nSerpents stalk soothes scorches and burns and durates the brew.\nadding blissfoil and then serpents stalk to a base gives a nice brew that relives pain from burns and scorches.\nadding crushed serpents stalk to a distilled base and following it up with some tippens root gives a brew with a regenerative effect.", ""),
        StaticBook("Edict Warsong", "Sentis", "The Edict Marches on,\nA warsong for  the valiant. \n\nBy: Sentis Av'ame, Master's hand of the Crimson Edict\nBy our blades and by our blood, \nIn crimson splendor we shall march. \nBy death and glory shall we fight, \nThe Edict marches on.\nThrough land foreign and homeland ruined, \nWe will have our triumph. \nBy death and glory shall we fight, \nThe Edict marches on.\nFrom grasping claws of defeat most fowl, \nTo the warm embrace of triumph. \nBy death and glory shall we fight, \nThe Edict marches on.\nFor King and peasant equally, We shed our precious blood. \nBy death and glory shall we fight, \nThe Edict marches on.\nAn army of brothers, an army of sisters, \nLike a  tide of crimson gold. \nBy death and glory we shall fight, \nThe Edict marches on.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ein Eron Melkan", "Kirrekith", "Ein Eron Melkan\n\n   Kirrekith Reffahc\n~                        ~\nFirst Encounter\n~                        ~\nThe first of its kind, and the first reported to Dwed after a string of pets being attacked and cattle being savaged and devoured.\n\nFirst accounts of these animals were\n--->\ndocumented after a decline in rodent population, much to the delight of citizens. However what soon followed was a string of attacks on pets, and larger animals, ending with the deaths of many beardlings.\n\nCould this outcome\n--->\nhave been different? Could the Dwed of prepared or known for such an enemy? I doubt it, not because of them, but because no one could of expected the turn of events.\nAnatomy\n~                        ~\n\nThe appearance of the first was very simple. Larger than the average chicken these predators had lost their feather coats, the sickly goosebumps on their near slimy skin very --->\nvisible to the eye. Where once simple claws for scraping at soil and tending to nests had been repurposed, now larger and with more muscle to power them they were designed for disemboweling prey that would fall to their feet,\n--->\nas witnessed in the first beardling killings. Their head structure however remains for the most part the same, however had a largening of the jawline, and sharpening of the beaks. Though on some teeth were visible upon their beaks or in --->\ntheir mouths, making a rather worrying question be put forth; was this an ancestral trait of them? Or something new to their species?\nBehaviours\n~                        ~\nWithout leadership they act like scavengers, waiting for prey to come to them or food to be left out. However they’ve been known to consume smaller prey with ease, as well as target Dwed\n--->\nbeardlings. With this in mind, they’ve been monstrous, with many killings and maulings when acting alone. Though with leadership, they are able to kill larger prey, and bring down the most hardened of Dwed.\n\n--->\nWhen they haven’t seen prey they seem to resume a chicken like mentality, looking eternally for food and inquisitively seeking out new food sources, often distracted by simple things, this behaviour is quite amusing to behold, though is\n--->\ndeceiving considering their nature when they have you in their sites.\nOrigins\n~                        ~\n\nWe’re unsure whether these creatures can breed, or whether the variants of this species can do so either. It has been assumed given the sounds and nature of the animals that\n--->\nthere is possibly a large nest with either many hens, or possibly worse, a single large Brood Hen/Cave Chicken.\nEvaluation\n~                        ~\n\nWhat can be said of these animals? They can be compared to wolves in some extent, capable on their own of surviving, yet deadly in a pack, but we’ve never seen a pack of wolves \n--->\nopenly take on the legion head on without concern for their life, making us wonder whether a hive mentality is in play here.\n\nThey’re a very interest creature to study, and we’re yet to determine what inside --->\nthe caves turned these animals, it could of been food source, breeding (inbreeding) or possibly a new animal entirely. Perhaps one day they will be domesticable, however we are too early to know, and much is still to be learned of these animals.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elder Divines", "Dannybrine", "~The  Three  Divines~\n\nMany believe that it was only one greater being that gave life to the world and everything that is arround us. This is only a confusion people have on history and how our realms were made. This is the origin of the world.\nIn the beginning, there was nothing; and in this nothingness existed three divine beings.\nThe Mother, The Father, and The Originator. From these three omnipotent came to be their first creations. The Aenguls and Daemons. Created to serve and do the\ndivine's work, and represent them if need be, for mortals are not worthy enough to lay their eyes upon the faces of the creators. These holy creatures worshipped the Elder Divines, for they were direct creations.\nThe mother and father were tired of the\nvast nothingess of the void. Together, they decided to create and give life. The mortal plane bloomed into existence, which is what we live in today. The Originator saw what the Mother and Father made, and it was good. But the Originator saw a flaw.\nThe world was alone. It had no one to take care of it, or give it purpose. Carefully and pefectly, The Originaot made the hollow molds of what he saw as perfect beings. But they were missing something to give them purpose, to animate his molds, for as of\nthen, they were just puppets. Nothing controlling or taking as their homes these empty vessels. The Mother and Father joined the Originator to give life to his creation. They wanted someone to inhabit the new realms\nDivines gathered around the mortal planes, and held hands. Together, the gave free minds and souls to the beings so that they could see, breathe, and think. They were known as the descendants.\n~ The Divine Writings~\n\nThese are the teachings to the descendants, so that they may live life to the standard for which they were created for. In these writings, we will teach you; the follower, how you should act and think.\nThe Divine Way:\n\n   -One shall not worship false Gods. There are no other Gods than the Divines.\n\n   -Honour the spirits of your ancestors.\n\n   -Love your neighbors and your enemies\n-Do not eat off of the flesh of the descendants.\n\n   -Strive for peace and enlightenment.\n\n   -Treat with respect everyone around you.\n\n   -Help the ones in worse positions than you.\n-Nature will be respected. The Mother made it for us to harvest and care for it.\n\n   -Speak up for those who can't.\n\n   -Make offerings to the Gods and the ancestors.\n-Maintain a healthy and happy lifestyle.\n\n   -Do not kill unless in danger.\n\n   -Do not attack unless threatened.\n\n  -Do not judge for it is the job of the holy ones.\nHow to practice the Way of the Divines:\n\nLeave offerings outside of your home during the night of the full moon. It is to please the ancestors and the Elder Divines.\n\nPray to the divines each time you wake up, and each time before you sleep. Prayer must be done to a shrine to the Elder Divines, on your knees.\n\nEat only to keep healthy, unless while celebrating the Elder Divines.\nDuring celebration, one must eat and drink as much as possible when the divines bless you with a great harvest season.\n\nDo not purposly harm anyone, or anything with intent to cause fear or damage.\nBe nice and kind to others, and strive to help anyone who needs it.\n\nRespect your body and mind.\n\nRespect and honor your ancestors for they worked hard to bring you into this realm\nStrive for enlightenment\n\nEnlightenment: Do not lie, cheat, or steal. Be kind to others, love your neighbors and have no enemies. Follow the Way of the Divines and keep your mind and body to the best of your ability.\nDoing so will land you directly in the heavens with the Divines and their creations. \n\nIf you do not follow the way, you will have to pay the Divines by drifting in the void for the time that they seem fit. Everyone will join the divines if they do their\ntime in the void, and learn to follow the Way of the Divines.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo", "Elluna Koortova", "  Electrical Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n     Written    By\n   \n   Gauldrim  Irongut\nChapter 1, Uses of Electromancy:\n\nElectromancy is a very volatile form of arcane evocation, is just as likely to veer off it’s course or shock the user. A source of incredible heat and force, electromancy is a formidable tool. Slow to conjure and is\na lifelong commitment electromancy can be used in survival situations. Able to create fires when need be through the burning of wood or other flammable materials. Another property that can be found in electromancy is the extreme attraction to\nlarge amounts of metal. An anvil, a suit plate of armour, or a large iron gate can cause the electricity to be attracted towards it and then channeled inside of it. If one is to touch a piece of metal charged with electricity they will be hurt or burnt as\nthe electricity discharges. The most obvious use of electric evocation is the use of it in combat. A deadly force to be reckoned with once the user has achieved a high enough power to use it. Slow to conjure, though fast once released, electric evocation\nis one of the most powerful forms of arcane evocation. Able to kill a large man in full plate mail in a single bolt, if large enough this just lends perspective to the raw power. Electric evocationists also have the ability to summon forth lightning from\nthe heavens in the event of a storm with very good accuracy. \nChapter 2, Properties of Electromancy:\n\nAttracted to metal, can be conducted through metal, has the force to shatter stone and the ability to travel through water.  Electromancy is as versatile as it is powerful. Electric currents can be sent through\nwater enabling one to shock someone that is in contact with the said body of water. This practice also applies to metal and if one is in contact with a suit of plate mail when the electric current is sent towards the bearer they will experience not only\nthe force of the bolt but the current of the electricity as well. The current of the electricity will also cause muscle seizure and the dulling of senses. The shattering of stone occurs when an extremely powerful bolt is sent hurtling towards the stone,\nresulting in flying rubble and scorched rock. As well as being able to scorch rock, Electromancy can set wood, paper, and any other flammable materials alight causing fire and burns.  \nChapter 3, Conclusion: \n\nElectromancy is an almighty power to be reckoned with and those that perform it should be regarded with extreme caution. Slow to cast into immense power yet still dangerous even at short range. It is advised that when in\ncombat against such a mage, that large amounts of metal and or armour are unadvised to have and even steel or iron greatswords. So to wrap this short informative text up, one would be wise to heed the words of an electromancer and to regard the raw power\nand wisdom of those that wield it. \n\n\n\nCopied directly from the original text on the 12th of The Deep Cold, 1538.\n\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.\n\n§\nMerry Krugsmas, Kolohe! Hoped you enjoyed the read. Sorry it's not an original copy, but mine has water damage, so I thought I'd make a new one just for you. The ink was a little runny, but I do think it's still legible.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "Haadi Mubdee", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=            Electrical\n           Evocation\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=\n\n\n     -< ^v^v^v^v^\nThere is an old saying that humans (mortals) fear most other humans. I believe, however, that those who say that have never looked outside the confines of the human world. If anyone has come face to face with the power of nature, they will consider the\nprevious proverb a joke. If this sounds like nothing more than nonsense coming from an old fool, then answer this next question. If you can possess any form of power, what would you choose? Would you choose the power of mankind, or that of a wild beast?\nWould it be the roars of powerful men, or the sound of thunder that shakes the heavens? Is it the limited life of men, or nature's continuous cycle of life? Whichever way you look at it, the power of man is feeble compared to the grandeur of nature.\nThroughout history, all of mankind has admired nature's power and though they had feared it, they tried to deny that. This is one of man's many follies. They neglect nature's power, which does not discriminate, solely because they are a part of nature.\nIn particular, as humans learned of Mana and started seeing a glimpse of nature's other realm, they began neglecting nature's power even more. They didn't realize that their \"magic\" was actually an imitation of nature's power. This is what worries me.\nThere are many students who are Wizards and Druids in training who do not understand that every magic's starting point is a natural phenomenon. I, who also boasted in my knowledge of Electric magic , did not learn this until I saw lightning strike down at\nthe Crown Lands Plateau of Oren. In hopes that those who come after me will not make the same mistake, I decided to write this book. In other words, I hope that beginner wizards will learn the laws of nature and have a healthy fear of it as well.\nAlthough this book only deals with lightning power, which is only one of nature's awesome power, if you are wise, you will take the moral of the story to heart and apply it when training other magic as well.\nThe Principle of Electricity series Magic Skill\n                -=-\nIn order to understand the principle of Electric magic, you must first learn its natural counterpart: Lightning. If you've seen anyone use Electric-based magic, you probably noticed a close resemblance to a lightning strike. The lightning strike occurs\nwhen Mana, the energy that surrounds us, splits into two polarities of energy for reasons unknown. These split polarities each continue to accumulate energy, when, in an instant, an explosion of energy flow occurs between heaven and earth.\nThe intensity of the light and heat during this process contains tremendous power. Also, because of its unpredictability of where it strikes, it has been an object of fear to mankind. There are many opinions as to when and why Mana, splits into two\npolarities of energy. However, before anyone could come up with any concrete evidence, the debate's focus shifted because of the ‘great’ Wizard Ambrosia, who at times lacked common sense. He claimed that he was able to stabilize his Mana to split the two\npolar energies in a controlled manner, which caused all the scholars to shift their focus from the conditions in which the energy splits to the process of it. (It is a shame that scholars today are not interested in insightfully studying natural\nphenomena, and rather just want to uncover it just for the sake of using it. This is quite foolish.) Once Mana is split into two polar energies, each polarity begins accumulating energy at a rapid rate and causes an electric discharge. Then, when the\nbalance of energy between the two polarities is broken, a transfer of energy occurs from the one with more energy to the other. So imagine what would happen if one could embody either of the polarities and designate his or her target as the other\npolarity. Then, using Mana, if he or she polarizes the Mana and also raises his/her own energy level to be higher than their target, what would happen?\nExactly. This is what is known as Electrical Energy Magic.\nHow to use the Lightning Bolt\n                -=-\nThe Lightning Bolt attack is a magic that uses the mechanic of creating static electricity, which in turn utilizes the characteristics of the negative charge for a sudden electrostatic discharge. During the energy transfusion, a bright explosion\nresembling a lightning strike, rushes toward your target as Mana is depleted into replicating this phenomenon. Once all the Mana is depleted from the bolt and the surrounding elements reach equilibrium, the flow of energy ends. (Just like a lightning\nstrike in nature.) There are many questions surrounding this magic, such as \"How powerful is it?\" and \"How easy is it to use?\", which is technically asking how much energy it needs and how long it takes. To give you an answer, there is a limit to how much\nenergy you can gather, and you can only maintain the energy for about 15 seconds until later coming to a greater grasp of the art. You can charge your energy multiple times to gather more energy, but it is reported that it can become highly unstable after\nafter the third charge which is already risky enough. Also, you only have about 15 seconds to charge all your energy. This is because of several factors, such as the difficulty of maintaining the Mana's focus, and also maintaining the polarized energy at\nthe same time. (Even if you have plenty of Mana, it is difficult to charge for an extensive electrical bolt). The ‘Lightning Bolt’ attack is used to strike your enemy with electricity . Once your opponent is struck with this attack, they will be in a\nstate of shock due to the electricity surging within them as it an energy. Not a tangible object. Since this attack is based on an instant energy explosion between you and your opponent, the lesser the energy gap between you and your opponent, the great\ndamage it will inflict as the longer the distance the surge of electricity must travel, the more it discharges. Wasting precious Mana in the long run.\nSimple\n              Usage\n                -=-\nOnce you've carefully read through this book, and understood the principles behind the Lightning Bolt attack and are ready to use it, you can do so by following these simple steps. First, a connection to the Void is a must. As any form of magic. The\nsimplest manner in which to begin evoking such an element is to picture the empty black abyss that is the Void. A sleet of pure nothingness. Void of any life as the name suggests. Now one must mentally picture lightning crashing down upon the Earth. But\nstrictly the lighting. If one were to picture the scene, one could possibly border the realm of Pseudomancy (Illusionary magic) or if too much detail is placed on the Earth, soil or stone may be produced. Then you will see the static discharge enivision\nsuch an occurring unfolding before your palm you calm your mind to allow your Mana to polarize the energy and fuel it. Once the preparation is finished, lightning-like strands of light energy will flow around you. This indicated you have successfully\ncalibrated yourself with the Void and established an affinity to Electrical Evocation.\n\nThough mentioned before, I want to remind you that the intense light and heat from this attack can significantly startle your opponent.\nApplication:\n    Chain Lightning\n               -=-\nBefore we move on, I need to reiterate and explain in detail regarding multiple charges. As you know by now, the Lightning Bolt attack is very similar to the actual lightning strike that happens in nature. Does this mean that this magic is capable of\nimitating the continuous strikes that occur in a natural lightning strike?\n\nThe answer is yes. Scholars call this ‘Chain Lightning’. By charging the magic multiple times, you are able to hurl this energy to your target back to back.\nHowever, there is a limit to how many times you can strike in a row. As previously mentioned, since you can charge up to about three bolts, yet the risk increases with each charge. One interesting fact is, these bolts of energy attract to metallic\nobjects. Thus when in the vicinity of metal objects such as the bands of a barrel, swords and armor, iron grating, and other Ferrum or Arcarum apparel, the bolt will change it’s path of perjectory and curve to meet said object.\nContinuous Attack\n    Between Lightning\n         Bolt Users\n               -=-\nWe looked at the principle behind the Lightning Bolt, the Chain Lightning attack, and the application of these attacks in the previous chapter. If you think you've mastered everything through these two attacks, you still have a lot to learn from mother\nnature. If anyone has studied lightning strikes carefully, you know that lightning does not only occur in single, or multiple chain of strikes. Sometimes, lightning strikes attract other lightning and fuse together. Thus, where there are multiple\nLightning Bolt users, they can fuse each other's energy to form a collaborative attack.\n\nThis is a unique trait of Electric energy based magic that other ‘generic’ elemental based magic do not possess. When a user is charging his or her Lightning bolt\nattack, you can add on to their energy and instantly form a Chain Lightning attack. In other words, if you have charge your Lightning Bolt attack near another user that is charging, your charge will add to their charge, increasing their total number of\ncharges.\nThe Effects\n                of\n        Lightning Bolt\n               -=-\nSo, when is it a good time to use the Lightning Bolt attack? If you are wise, you should be able to figure it out yourself.\n\nFirst, the Lightning attack is good when facing multiple targets at once. Try it out yourself.\nUse skill of Electrical Evocation and attempt to fire off a bolt at a grouping of targets.. You will be amazed at how effective and convenient this property can prove to be.\nHowever, there is something you must remember: Chaining charges  inflicte damage which subsequently decreases with each hit. Beginners, unaware of this, might overuse the attack and find themselves out of Mana and getting attacked by the opponent.\nEven when you successfully use the Chain attack, the opponent might not have received as much damage as you think. Thus, the first target of the Chain Lightning Skill is very important. This is something every good wizard should be mindful.\nAuthor: Archmage Crumena V. Illwindior [HeeroZero]\n\nConsoliant: Electomancer Ceruberr Asul'Ailer [CaptainSheepy]\n\nCopier:\nGuildmaster Haadi Mubdee [Eladriendil]", ""),
        StaticBook("ELECTROMANCY", "onm224", "ELECTROMANCY\n         GUIDE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Richard Tarus\nAdapted: Amras Lúinwë\nWhat is electric evocation?\nElectrical Evocation is the arcane magic form whereby a mage creates Electrical bolts for his or her purposes. Unlike other types of Evocation electrical bolts is intended to be much more difficult to control due to its\nspeed and high energy nature. Mages who specialize in electrical evocation will be able to form electrical bolts and streams of electricity to electrocute their targets.However, electrical evocation requires much more energy than for example\nfire and therefore a single electrical bolt requires much more energy than a fireball. This however is made up for by the fact the lightning bolt is somewhat equal in power to the two fireballs which could be made in the same time period.\nStrength\nAn electrical evocationist is capable of producing powerful electrical bolts\nBolts may travel from any point to point with speed and reliable accuracy.\nWeakneses\nElectrical evocation takes a greater amount of time to produce a bolt\nthan other types of evocation\nElectrical evocation is dangerous to learn and during some phases of learning the mage can be incapable of producing any spark which will not injure themselves.\nProcess\nReaching Tier 1:\nWhen you begin to learn magic, you will start a Tier 1. At that point in time, you are unable to cast any form of magic unless you have some sort of experience and have connected to the void.At this tier you will learn\nhow to connect to the void, and then research electricity as an element itself. Connecting to the void will take perhaps even years of practice, and once completed,you may still have some difficulty. Researching electricity would consist of practically\nfinding any sort of detailand then taking note of it.\nReaching Tier 2: \nAfter their advancement from tier 1, and their connection to the void, they can now create a multitude of sparks and perhaps an even minor bolt,albeit difficult to\ncontrol till towards the end of Tier 2.  Even though they can create sparks, users at this tier may have an overload in which the sparks will practically burst outwards towards the conjurer.In this tier they will need heavy loads of practice in order\nto become more proficient with a minor bolt.\nReaching Tier 3:\nIn this tier they can finally create a full powered bolt withought major troubles, and have full proficiency. At this point they can now create streams of electricity,\nthough they will simply spark and singethe target, rather then cause major damage. With this tier, they are novice mages. \nReaching Tier 4:\nNow, the electrical evocation users can create the \"call-down\"of electricity, aka a bolt from a high point\nin the sky. They can create multiple bolts in a shorter time, although a fire evocationist could create fireballs in an even shorter time.The call-down is not very proficient, and will rarely land on the user's target.  In this tier,they can create great\nstreams of electricity that will do some good damage (burns, etc.) They are very proficient with the bolts now.\nFor more information go to this link, there is the same info + RP guide:\nhttp://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/88498-improved-electricity-guide/", ""),
        StaticBook("Electromancy", "Crumena Ilwindior", "- The Basics of Electric Energy: Electrical Evocation - \nAuthor: Arch-Mage Crumena V. Illwindior [HeeroZero]\nConsoliant: Electomancer Ceruberr Asul'Ailer [CaptainSheepy]\nPreface\nThere is an old saying that descendants fear most other descendants. I believe, however, that those who say that have never looked outside the confines of the mortal world. If anyone has come face to face with\nthe power of nature, they will consider the previous proverb a joke. If this sounds like nothing more than nonsense coming from an old fool, then answer this next question:\nIf you can possess any form of power, what would you choose? Would\nyou choose the power of mankind, or that of a wild beast? Would it be the roars of powerful men, or the sound of thunder that shakes the heavens? Is it the limited life of men, or nature's continuous cycle of life? Whichever way you look at it, the\npower of man is feeble compared to the grandeur of nature. Throughout history, all of mankind has admired nature's power and though they had feared it, they tried to deny that. This is one of man's many follies. They neglect nature's power,\nwhich does not discriminate, solely because they are a part of nature.\nIn particular, as the descendants learned of Mana and started seeing a glimpse of nature's other realm, they began neglecting nature's power even more. They didn't realize\nthat their \"magic\" was actually an imitation of nature's power. This is what worries me. There are many students who are mages in training who do not understand that every magic's starting point is a natural phenomenon. I, who also boasted in my\nknowledge of Electric magic, did not learn this until I saw a lightning strike down at the Crown Lands Plateau of Oren.\nIn hopes that those who come after me will not make the same mistake, I decided to write this book. In other words, I hope that\nbeginner wizards will learn the laws of nature and have a healthy fear of it as well.\nAlthough this book only deals with lightning power, which is only one of nature's awesome power, if you are wise, you will take the moral of the story\nto heart and apply it when training other magic as well.\nThe Principle of Electricity series Magic Skill:\nIn order to understand the principle of Electric magic, you must first learn its natural counterpart: Lightning. If\nyou've seen anyone use Electric-based magic, you probably noticed a close resemblance to a lightning strike. The lightning strike occurs when Mana, the energy that surrounds us, splits into two polarities of energy for reasons unknown. These\nsplit polarities each continue to accumulate energy, when, in an instant, an explosion of energy flow occurs between heaven and earth. The intensity of the light and heat during this process contains tremendous power. Also, because of its\nunpredictability of where it strikes, it has been an object of fear to mankind. (So much so that people use this word 'lightning' to curse others. I.E. I hope lightning strikes you dead!)\nThere are many opinions as to when and why Mana,\nsplits into two polarities of energy. However, before anyone could come up with any concrete evidence, the debate's focus shifted because of the ‘great’ Wizard Ambrosia, who at times lacked common sense. He claimed that he was able to\nstabilize his Mana to split the two polar energies in a controlled manner, which caused all the scholars to shift their focus from the conditions in which the energy splits to the process of it. (It is a shame that scholars today are not interested in\ninsightfully studying natural phenomena, and rather just want to uncover it just for the sake of using it. This is quite foolish.)\nHow to Use the Electrical Energy\nElectrical Evocation a magic that uses the mechanic of creating static\nelectricity, which in turn utilizes the characteristics of the negative charge for a sudden electrostatic discharge. During the energy transfusion, a bright explosion resembling a lightning strike, rushes toward your target as Mana is depleted into\nreplicating this phenomenon. Once all the Mana is depleted from the bolt and the surrounding elements reach equilibrium, the flow of energy ends. (Just like a lightning strike in nature.)\nThere are many questions surrounding this\nmagic, such as \"How powerful is it?\" and \"How easy is it to use?\", which is technically asking how much energy it needs and how long it takes. To give you an answer, there is a limit to how much energy you can gather, and you can only maintain the\nenergy for about 15 seconds until later coming to a greater grasp of the art.\nYou can charge your energy multiple times to gather more energy, but it is reported that it can become highly unstable after the third charge which is already risky\nenough. Also, you only have about 15 seconds to charge all your energy. This is because of several factors, such as the difficulty of maintaining the Mana's focus, and also maintaining the polarized energy at the same time. (Even if you have plenty\nof Mana, it is difficult to charge for an extensive electrical bolt).\nElectrical Evocation has absolutely no applications other use other than being exercised as combative tool. The 'lightning bolt', your main and only real spell, is used to\nstrike your enemy with electricity . Once your opponent is struck with this attack, they will be in a state of shock due to the electricity surging within them as it an energy. Not a tangible object. Since this attack is based on an instant energy\nexplosion between you and your opponent, the lesser the energy gap between you and your opponent, the greater damage it will inflict as the longer the distance the surge of electricity must travel, the more it discharges. Wasting precious Mana in\nthe long run.\nSimple Usage\nOnce you have carefully read through this book, and understood the principles behind the fundamentals of Electrical Evocation and are ready to use it, you can do so by following these simple steps. First, a\nconnection to the Void is a must, as is the case with any form of magic. The simplest manner in which to begin evoking an element is to picture the empty black abyss that is the Void. A sleet of pure nothingness, void of any life as the name suggests.\nNow one must mentally picture lighting crashing down upon the Earth. But strictly the lighting. If one were to picture the scene, one could possibly border the realm of Pseudomancy (Illusionary magic) or if too much detail is placed on the\nEarth, soil or stone may be produced.\nThen you will see the static discharge envision such an occurring unfolding before your palm you calm your mind to allow your Mana to polarize the energy and fuel it. Once the preparation is finished,\nlightning-like strands of light energy will flow around you. This indicates that you have successfully calibrated yourself with the Void and established an affinity.\nI cannot stress enough that the intense light and heat from this attack\ncan significantly startle your opponent.\nApplication : Chain Lightning\nBefore we move on, I need to reiterate and explain in detail regarding multiple charges. As you know by now, Electrical Evocation is very similar to the\nactual lightning strike that occurs in nature. Does this mean that this magic is capable of imitating the continuous strikes that occur in a natural lightning strike? The answer is yes. Arcanists refer to this as the process of ‘Chain Lightning’. By\ncharging the magic multiple times, you are able to hurl this energy to your target back to back. However, there is a limit to how many times you can strike in a row. As previously mentioned, since you can charge up to about three bolts, yet the risk\nincreases with each charge.\nOne interesting fact is, these bolts of energy attract to metallic objects. Thus when in the vicinity of metal objects such as the bands of a barrel, swords and armor, iron grating, and other Ferrum or\nArcarum apparel, the bolt will change it’s path of trajectory and curve to meet said object.\nContinuous Attack Between Electrical Evocation Users\nWe looked at the principle behind the evocation of electricity, the chaining of it, and\nthe application of these styles in the previous chapter. If you think you have mastered everything through these two attacks, you still have a lot to learn from mother nature. If anyone has studied lightning strikes carefully, you know that lightning\ndoes not only occur in single, or multiple chain of strikes. Sometimes, lightning strikes attract other lightning and fuse together. Thus, where there are multiple Electrical Evocation users, they can fuse each other's energy to form a\ncollaborative attack.\nThis is a unique trait of Electric energy based magic that other ‘generic’ elemental based magic do not possess. When a user is charging his or her Electrical Evocation, you can add on to their energy and instantly form a\nchain effect. In other words, if you have charge your Electrical Evocation near another user that is charging, your charge will add to their charge, increasing the volume of charges.\nThe Effect of Electrical Evocation\nWhen is it a good\ntime to use Electrical Evocation? If you are wise, you should be able to figure it out yourself.\nFirst, the Electrical Evocation is good when facing multiple targets at once. Try it out yourself. Use skill of Electrical Evocation and attempt to fire\noff a bolt at a grouping of targets. You will be amazed at how effective and convenient this property can prove to be.\nHowever, there is something you must remember: Chaining charges inflicts damage which subsequently\ndecreases with each hit. Beginners, unaware of this, might overuse the attack and find themselves out of Mana and placed in a vulnerable situation. Even when you successfully chaining multiple charges of electricity, the\nopponent might not have received as much damage as you think. Thus, the first target of your 'chain' is very important. This is something every good mage should be mindful.\nLaw of Diminishing Marginal Damage\nWe must go\nthrough the Law of Decreased Damage before you can fully understand Electrical Evocation. The Law of Decreased Damage is commonly linked with Electric based magic where, when the electricity is charged multiple times, it actually\ndecreases the inflicted damage, though it uses the same amount of Mana. It is an important law that can help you better calculate the relationship between Mana and inflicted damage.\nConclusion\nIn this book, we discussed about\nthe Electric Energy based magic, specifically the art through the wisdom of nature. Electrical Evocation is a powerful and flashy magic, but it also requires a high level of discernment in order to use it effectively. Do not just rely on the\nknowledge from having read the book, but practice it until you get a better feel for it. Lastly, I hope that with excessive practice, you the reader will be guided to success in this art under this tome’s wisdom.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electromancy", "RedBench", "Electric Evocation\n\n\nBy Gauldrim Irongut\nChapter 1: Uses of Electromancy.\n\nElectromancy is a very volatile form of arcane evocation, it is just as likely to veer off its course or shock the user. A source of incredible heat and force electromancy is a formidable tool.\nSlow to conjur and is a life long committment electromancy can be used in survival situations. Able to create fires when need be through the burning of wood or other flammable materials. Another property that can be found in electromancy is the extreme\nattraction to large amounts of metal. An anvil, a suit of plate armour or a large iron gate cause the electricty to be attractedd towards it and then channelled inside of it. If one is to touch a piece of metal charged with electricity they will be hurt\nas the electricity discharges. The most obvious use of electric evocation is the use of it in combat. A deadly force to be reckoned with once the user has achieved a high enough power to use it. Slow to conjur but fast once released electric evocation\nis one of the most powerful forms of arcane evocation. Able to kill a large man in full platemail in a single bolt if large enough this just lends persepective to the raw power. Electric evocationists also have the ability summon forth lightning from\nthe heavens in the event of a storm with verry good accuracy.\nChapter 2: Properties of Electromancy\n\nAttracted to metal, can be conducted through metal, has the force to shatter stone and the ability to travel through water. Electromancy is as versitile as it is powerful.\nElectric currents can be sent through water enabling one to shock someone that is in contact with the said body of water. This practice also applies to metal and if one is in contact with a suit of platemail when the electric current is sent towards the\nbearer they will experience not only the force of the bolt but the current of the electricty will also cause muscle seizure and the dulling of senses. The shattering of stone occurs when an extremely powerful bolt is sent hurtling towards stone resulting\nin flying rubble and scorched rock. As well as being able to scorch rock electromancy can set wood, paper and any other flammable material alight causing fire and burns.\nChapter 3: Conclusion\n\nElectromancy is an almighty power to be reckoned with and those that perform it should be regarded with extreme caution. Slow to cast into immense power yet still dangerous even at short range. It is adviesed that\nwhen in combat against such a mage that large amounts of metal armour are unadvised and even such things as steel or iron greatswords. So to wrap this short informative text up, one would be wise to heed the words of an electromancer and to regard the raw\npower and wisdom of those that weild it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elem. Alchemy", "Rosso", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n------------\nElements of Alchemy\n\nVolume I-2 of V\nThe Elements:\n--------\nFire\n--\nEarth\n--\nWater\n--\nAir\nSkeptics often approach me with a wholly ignorant conundrum, and that is “how can you trace every spell and element back to these four basic elements.” But what they do not realize is that an understanding of what is meant by these four elements is\nrequired before that question can be answered and in fact, if that understanding is acquired then this question will never be asked.\n\nThese four basic, rudimentary elements, Fire, Earth, Water, and Air, are what every potion, oil, elixir, and\nconcept, in Alchemy of course, is based upon. An ignorant outlook on this statement is that what is meant is the physical, literal meaning behind these elements but one must look into the symbolism, they must look deeper than the surface. I shall go into\neach of these elements in detail, so that you, and budding alchemist or simply a well-read individual, may understand how Air may both aid someone’s speed, as well as their perception of their surroundings.\nFire\n===\nThe Destroyer, the Unmaker, the Cleanser.\nWe will begin with one of the most rudimentary and used element, Fire. Fire can represent many a feeling, action, and state and because of this, it is often one of the most useful elements of the Alchemist’s arsenal. Fire can represent rage, anger,\nhatred, as well as bravery, courage, and gusto. Through this a brew can be crafted to make someone unquestionably and savagely furious, but it could also craft a brew to strengthen one’s will, and allow them to do what other men would shrink away in fear\nat. These feelings, these emotions can be invoked by the element of Fire within a potion, but feelings are not the only thing that fire can produce, actions are another.\nActions are often the most recognized aspect of fire, and by this I mean the action\nof burning, consuming, and destroying. Alchemist’s Fire, a handy inferno in a bottle, is an example of this aspect of Fire, for within it is the action of destruction. This action can be further expanded upon with burning oil placed upon a weapon, but if\none were to use this example they would also have to include the element of pain, another feeling that fire an invoke. State is aspect that Fire can take one within an alchemist’s potion and this is often represented as Chaos. It is true that Chaos is\noften something alchemist’s fear, for it is something athat often ruins a potion, but it is yet another aspect of Fire that must be recognized. Chaos, being the state that it is, may seem like it has little place in a potion but brilliant minds and\npowerful reason can bring it to use just the same as the first farmer realized a stone and a stick, two completely different objects, could help them till their fields by putting them together. As this is not a book on the philosophy of alchemy, or\nsolely on the element of fire, I will not go into depth on how Chaos can be used. The teacher must leave something for the student to ponder.\nEarth\n===\nThe Enduring, the Lifegiver, the Fortifying\nWith the conclusion of Fire, the other elements will not have as long as description for most of the fundamentals of the elements are covered in how they can represent different things, I will simply go over what they may represent, starting with Earth.\nEarth is a truly powerful element for it may represent metals, strength, the notion of being stalwart, solidity, firmness, flora, animals, and countless other, quite obvious, subjects. Earth is often used for potions that increase one’s endurance, or\nstrength, and it is a must in potions that toughen one’s skin. In fact, a strong series of representations of Earth are required to perfect a barksin, or stoneskin potion. Protecting oneself is not the only use for the element of Earth, for it is also\nused in antidote potions, disease-curing potions, and, of course, fertilizers. Antidotes use this element for it can represent animals, and among those elements are snakes and spiders, often associated with poison. Of course a symbol of Water is also\nrequired for a proper antidote, but this will be addressed later on. Many of the uses of the element of Earth are quite obvious, but a always, if one wishes to master the field of Alchemy they must learn creativity is their greatest friend, and using\nelements in odd and interesting ways can be useful, and quite detrimental, in numerous ways. A final note on the element of Earth is how it is associated with the fable of Transmutation. Now, as a scholarly and skeptic individual, I have doubts upon\ntransmutation, its existence, and possibility. This will be described more in depth, but know that the element of Earth is the greatly represented by metals, for metals are merely ores in their purest forms.\nWater\n===\nThe Base, the Purifier, the Healer.\nWater is the element that seems to get the most amount of use due to how it is a base for many a potion and it is true, for if someone wants a liquid spell they want to use the Element of Water. Often known as the “base” element, it truly lives up to its\nname for observations, and personal experience, lead all to believe it is necessary for life. This base element, is often associated with flowing, liquids, balance, peace, calm, order, life, and rebirth. One requires water for any potion that one plans on\ndrinking, and any oil that one plans on applying for to have a liquid, one must use the Element of Water. Now that and understanding on how Water is a base, we must go into how it is used beyond simply supporting the other elements.\nWater’s uses are varied, for it can be used both in antidote as well as poisons, showing that it is quite the versatile element. One may also use it to create a potion of calmness, or perhaps a potion of healing due to its association with life. But one\ncan also use this beautiful element in the creation of an oil to coat a weapon, or to coat and strengthen armor. This is not the same as enchanting armor or weaponry, mind you, for doing that is often permanent and requires magic. Through oils, one may\nreap similar benefits of enchantment but instead it is only temporary and anyone with basic sense can apply them. The purest base, and often representation of water, is Aqua Vitae or “Water of Life,” which is best made by distilling wine or other liquors.\nAir\n===\nThe Nimble, the Traveller, the All-Seeing.\nOur final element, the element of Air, is not the least by any stretch of imagination but is often the hardest one to put into representation and use in a potion. Now this element is often associated with agility, quickness, travel, feet, perception, and\neven flight, it can be quite difficult to embody the element of Air into a physical item due to our basic fault of lacking understanding of what we cannot see. But with reason and the opening of one’s eyes, the ways in which to represent Air are quite\nobvious in our everyday world.\nItems that can be used to represent air, and subsequently put through your tools to produce a potion, are rather easy to find during your average day but of course, as with all the elements, purer ingredients are often quite\nrarer. One representation that you may have already thought of is a mere feather, which is often the most common representation of Air. This, of course, is not the purest representation of the element but it will often due for your more basic potions\ncentered around this element. Another, more outlandish representation, are rabbits’ feet. Rabbits are often seen as quick and agile critters, and as Air takes on the aspect of agility and quickness, it becomes quite obvious how the feet of a rabbit and\nAir intermingle. With that said, it becomes rather easy to find out representations of Air through simply looking and observing the world around you. But do not fret if you are still hard-pressed to find these symbols, the next chapter will explain\nherbs that will best aid you in the process of finding symbols for all the elements.\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I-2\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Elem. Alchemy", "Kirrekith", "Elementaly Alechemy\n\nThe Tales of a Travelling Alechemist\n-------------------Notice, this book is a rushed copy of tomes in the library of the Ork capital, as made during the raid of 16th of the Grand Harvest, 1532. This is not a perfect copy.\nElements of Alchemy\nVolume I-II of V\n\nFire\n-------------------Earth\n-------------------Water\n-------------------Air\nMost people believe that you cannot trace a spell back to the IV key elements. However a grasp of these elements can show this, however without understanding will make this impossible to know.\n\nThese IV elements, Fire, Earth, Water and Air. These are what\nevery potion, oil, and elixir is based upon. People often see a potions physical state, and so not of the IV, however look to the potions symbolism and it will become clear. Look further than the asthetics to understand this, hopefully this will guide any\nalchemist or student in understanding how air can assist in someones ability to move and perceiving someones surroundings.\n\nFire\n---\n---\nThe Destroyer, the Unmake, the cleanser. \n\nStaring with one of\nthe key elements; Fire. Fire can be shown in feeling, movement, and in its form. Due to this it is key to an alchemist to have on their person. Fire represents many forms such as rage, anger, hatred, as wel as bravery, courage and speed. With this a\nsolution can take form to influence someone to be savegely furious, or even make someones will be strengthened, making them do as other men would buckle to fear over. This can in turn be a catalyst to bring out the element of fire inside a potion. But\nfeelings are not the only result the element fire can produce, actions as well.\n\nPotions are often the most known form of fire, this is meant in the form of burning, consuming and destroying. A key named potion would be alchemists fire, a brutal\nflame withstrained by a vial. Living destruction within the vials confines, a good metaphor for fire aspect. This result can be amplified by catalysts such as oil placed on a weapon. This potion invokes the feeling of pain, and so can be branded as a\nemotion fire causes. It is often viewed to be chaos within a potion due to aspects of fires illtempored nature. It is true the chaos of fire is something alchemists fear, as the very element can spoil potions. Chaos has little place in potions to the weak\nminded, but to the adept it is seen as powerful reason to be brought to use. This can be compared to iron and wood to make a woodsmans axe, two different materials to form a new and more efficient purpose. This is not a book on the philosiphy of alchemy,\nor solely made for the element of fire. I will not indulge you into how chaos can be mastered in alchemy. This is the place of the student to discover. \n\nEarth\n---\n---\nThe Enduring, the Lifegiver, the Fortifying\nThe following elements are not as key as the previous elements, and so will not be explained in long detail, however they may be mentioned later on. I will go over what they mean, beginning with Earth. Earth is truly a strong element, as it is shown in\nmetals, strength, solidity, firmness, flora, animals, with many other forms also being part of it. Solutions in its form can be used to amplify ones endurance, strength, and is a key catalyst to be used when toughening ones skin. A continuous series of\nelements or used to fortify and perfect barkskin or stoneskin solutions. Protection isn't the only use for the earth aspect, it can be used to fend of poisions, or disease curing alchemy, fertilizers. Antidotes represent animals, more directly snakes and\nspiders, as they often are in association to poison. A symbol for water aspect is also required within a antidote, but we'll discuss this further on in this book. Earth aspects have many obvious uses, though as with mastering any field, creativity is key\nto when using elements as it can allow for odd and interesting results. Quite detrimental in varioys ways. Earth aspect is also believed to be key in transmution, however I possess a skeptical view in this matter, and have doubts whether it is possible.\nThis will be described in more detail later, but understand that metals are often linked to earth aspect. \n\nWater\n---\n---\nThe Base, the Purifier, the Healer\n\nWater is the base to most potions, being a\nkey aspect to all of them. If a person needed a water based spell, they'll want to Element of Water. This is well known as the \"Base\" element, it does truly live up to the name. This element is shown to be in liquids, flowing, balance, peace, calm, order\nand rebirth. Potions require water in all forms to be usable for drinks or rubbing oils/liquids. Understanding that water can be a base is simple, however we must learn how to use it without it simply being a supporting agent. Water has a variety of uses\nIt can be used as an antidote or the counter poisons. Or it can be used to form potions of calm and healing. This element can also be used in item strengthening or maintaining of it. However this is not the same as enchanted or runecrafted armour, the\ndifference being that the water application is for the most part a non-permanent solution. One of the purest bases, and often a representation of water is Aqua Vitae, or Water of life. Made by distilling wines or liquors.\nAir\n---\n---\nThe Nimble, The Traveller, the All-Seeing\n\nThe final element to discuss is air, often the hardest to present and use in a potion. This element represents agility, travel, feet,\nperception and evend flight. It becomes an issue to harness this as how can one embody air in a potion? Essentially something we cannot see with our eyes. But with study one may find represented catalysts. \n\nItems that can be found\nin everyday life, purer materials for air are rarer. One such material would be feathers as they're a good representation to air. However it is not a pure form of air, however is often used in the common air based potions. Another material would be a\nrabbits foot due to its deft nature. There are other more forms you'll see in your daily life, if you cannot see them the next chapter will further explain this in herbs that represent the elements.\n\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I-II.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elemental Evo:", "Enedor Pastly", "Elemental Evocation\n___________________\n\nElemental Evocation is the art of drawing a temporary form of an element from the void using mana. This sounds simple however it is much harder to do in practice. This is because you cannot actually\npull an element from the void, you actually pull a substance that mimics the properties of a chosen element. This means when learning magic, one must study their element in order to understand how it works. \nIt is worth noting that evocationists have\nNO power over existing elements.\n\nThe Void\n___________________\n\nThe void is discribed as a dark, eternal plane of nothingness.\nWe find 'nothing' very hard to imagine, therefore the first steps to learning any\narcane magic is to meditate in order to try and understand the void.\n\nIt is believed that the creator pulled everything into existence from the void and therefore it is possible for us to use some of the void's energy\nto cause changes to the world around us.\n\nMana\n___________________\n\nMana is like an invisible liquid. It flows around the world and exists in all living things, including us.\n\nMages use mana to draw their spells from\nthe void.\n\nThe term 'Mana Pool is used to describe how much mana an individual has. Your mana pool determines the strength and duration of spells that a mage can cast. The more experienced a mage is, the better they can manipulate mana.\nTypes of Elemental \nEvocation\n___________________\n\nEach evocable element is treated as a subtype of magic as each element has specific properties that have to be studied before one can perform the magic.\nFire Evocation\n___________________\n\nFire Evocation is perhaps the most widly performed  evocation as it has many uses. One can create fireballs that can be used in combat or simply create a heat or light source for traveling.\nFire evocation is said to be one of the easiest elements to evoke but one of the hardest to control.\nEarth Evocation\n___________________\n\nEarth evocation, like fire evocation has many uses aside from combat. The art of summoning rocks and minerals found in the earth is quite useful defensive and brute force combat although the art of\ncreating and using materials found in the eath has many more uses.\n\nEarth is a harder element to evoke  as it is more solid then, for example, water.\nWater evocation\n___________________\n\nWater is a very diverse element. Water can be found as liquid, solid and gas, all of which can be evoked. \nIce is normally used in combat.\nWater can be used for more day to day tasks like cleaning.\nSteam isn't evoked much as it has little use and is hard to learn.\n\nWater evocationists also have control over the temprature of their water.\nAir Evocation\n___________________\n\nAir evocation is certainly one of the least used evocations. It generally has less uses then the other evocations. Air evocation can be used for defensive combat as one can use it to push back enemies\nand even block some magical attacks.\n\nAir can also be used for more simpler tasks such as cleaning and cooling oneself down with a breeze. Air evocation is hard to study as the element is invisible to our eyes. Instead a mage must feel it to learn\nhow it works.\n\nElectrial Evocation\n___________________\n\nElectrial Evocation is one of the most powerful evocable elements however it is very hard to control and consumes a lot of energy. \nCommonly Electrial evocationists create\nbolts of electricity to combat their enemies though they have to be careful because just like electricity, the element is easily attracted to metal.\n\nIt also takes longer to summon electricity then the other elements because it uses more energy and\nmore mana then, for example, a small ball of water.\n\nDangers/side effects of elemental evocation.\n___________________\n\nThe side effects of Elemental Evocation are similar to other arcane magics and should certainly be looked into before\ndeciding to learn the magic.\n\nSide effects include:\n\n-Decreased life span.\n\n-Becoming physically weaker and frail. (This is why many mages use staffs)\n-On some occasions mages have been driven mad by the lust\nfor power.\n\nMost of these problems are caused by the fact that magic isn't a natural task for our bodies to carry out and therefore it damages us.\nLearning magic\n___________________\n\nIf you decide you want to learn the art of evocation, the best way to go about this would be to find a teacher. This is a hard and lengthy process that can take many years, however, the way you do this is up\nto you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elements of Mind", "Farley III Stafyr", "Elements of Mind\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr\nUpon the writing of the Theorem of Wisdom, my very own mind came to the conclusion that there must be more to it. Every person knows of elements such as fire, earth, water, wind or air and lightning.  But aside from external elements which we\ncan feel and use, there are also other elements, in a completely different range, of which we unknowingly make use and into which we tap, without realizing it.\n\nThe Elements of Mind.\nThe mind is a strange fabric, giving us the ability to think, to consider, to act, react, to learn, to remember and many things more. But the mind itself, such as the outer world we experience, has its own elements. To underline this, an example will be\ngiven.\n\nFeelings. Feelings, such as love, guilt, hate, happiness and many more. This is one of the elements of the mind, we are able to use it, express ourselves with it, to tap into the power of this element.\nFurther explanation is not necessary, I presume, as everyone has at least one feeling within him.\n\nOther elements do exist. Wisdom is one of them, as I aforementioned. Also knowledge and experience are\nelements of the mind. But there are more!\n\nConcentration, Purity, Peace and Balance, and Common Sense.\n\nHow each of these work, will be explained in further, upcoming books. e\nFor the element of wisdom, I refer myself to my work “Theorem of Wisdom” for further information. The book “Knowledge and Experience – Elaborated” may give additional hints about two further elements.\n-: Primary Edition :-", ""),
        StaticBook("Elf A&P (L)", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "This book has been created for the purpose of documenting a few various systems involved within the elven anatomy.\n   A few of these systems involve: Nervous system, Respiratory system, skin, Cardiovascular system, Musculoskeletal system, Digestive-\n-system, and Urinary system.\n*Upon flipping to the next page you are greeted by an incredibly detailed and full scale sketching of what appears to be the nervous system. The brain appears connected with a large system of nerves throughout the body via the spinal cord.*\nNervous System:\n   The nervous system is primarily composed of the brain, nerves, and the spinal cord which connected the two throughout the body.\n   The purpose of the nervous system is to provide consciousness to the creature and allow its -\n- bodily functions to automate. The nerves and spinal cord allow for context with the body around the brain, such as pain and feeling.\n   The primary functions of the nervous system are relatively the same within the elven anatomy with exception to its -\n-superior intellect.\n*You see yet another sketch similar to the previous one with a detailed showcase of what appears to be the respiratory system. It shows the mouth and nose connected through the throat towards the lungs.*\nRespiratory System:\n   This system includes various structures such as the nose and mouth connected via the passages through the throat towards the lungs.\n   The main purpose of the respiratory system is to provide oxygen to the bloodstream.\nAs for the average elven individual, this has no particular deviation.\n*Another sketching appears on this page. With closer examination you can see a heart connected via various veins and arteries spreading throughout an entire outline of an elven man's body.*\nCardiovascular System:\n   The main parts of this system include the heart, veins, blood vessels, and arteries.\n   The purpose of this system is to pump blood throughout the body and provide it with its various nutrients.\n   An average elven individual\nhas only one heart throughout its system.\n*The sketching on this page appears to show both a full body representation of its various muscles in extreme detail as well as a full skeleton. This appears to be the musculoskeletal system.*\nMusculoskeletal System:\n   Muscles, tendons and ligaments, and bones are various portions within this system.\n   The purpose of this system is to provide the body with motion and structure in its daily activities.\n   An elven individual is bipedal and\nsome what thinner compared to the other races.\n*As usual a sketching would appear on this next page. There appears to be the mouth again connected through a separate passage in the throat towards the stomach, then the large and small intestines, then finally out the bottom. The digestive system.*\nDigestive System:\n   Within this system is the mouth connected through a separate passage through the throat into the stomach, through the intestines and out the rectum. There also appears the gallblader, pancreas, and appendix.\n   The purpose of this\n-system is to extract nutrients from food, then to excrete wastes.\n   There is no particular anomaly with this system for the average elven individual.\n*There appears a sketch of an elven man with dark skin, then another sketch of skin from the side so you can see its various connective tissues. This system is of the skin.*\nSkin:\n   Although a single organ of its own right, the skin is so large and complex that it constitutes as its own system. This system also includes the various connective tissue within the skin but below the surface.\n   The purpose of skin is to provide-\n-a barrier from the outside environment for the rest of the body. It helps protect from various things that range from injury to disease.\n   As for elves, various shades of skin can exist, and as showcased on the prior sketch, it can be dark, but also-\n-can be rather light, depending on the pigmentation.\n*This next sketch appears a lot less complex as the previous ones, but just as detailed. Within the sketch you can see includes the kidneys and bladder.*\nUrinary System:\n   This system includes the kidneys, bladder, and urethra.\n   Although a smaller system, the purpose of this system is rather important. It exists for extracting and excreting wastes out of the blood stream.\n   There are no-\n-anomalies existent within this system for the average elf.\nSide Notes:\n-Although relatively the same to other races, I've included details within the sketchings to provide visual reference for structural differences in the elven race.\nList of Systems:\n-Nervous\n-Respiratory\n-Skin\n-Cardiovascular\n-Musculoskeletal\n-Digestive\n-Urinary\n*Upon reaching the final pages, you can see miniature versions of the various sketches you've seen throughout this book.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Elinor's Trial", "Grand Druid Verden", "Travel to the three groves and inquire about the life and personalities of the Druids. Ask about their totem, why it's special to them, and how they serve Nature and the Aspects. Be kind, courteous, and friendly; this is your future family after all.\nThe Malinor circle sits comfortably at the back of the city. Just look for the absurdly large tree. The Wayward circle sits outside Rosewyn Hollow, outside former Salvus. It's very secluded, so you might want to ask for directions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eloh'ra Rohkea", "Eloh'ra", "Eloh'ra Rohkea,\nRaven Druid\n\n\"Keep in mind that the devil was once an angel.\"\n\nGrass crackled and sloshed as heavy, worn feet plodded through the swamp lands.\n\nThe sky was cloudless and the summer sun beat on the back of the figure that continued to stride through the thick mud.\nWrithing in pain and attempting to take yet another sluggish step, the Mali'ame would close her eyes, exhaling deeply before opening them to yet again the true setting she would stride in.\n\nShe would would look around, her eyes getting lost in the\nmovements of the flowers that sway gently within the the wind, falling instantly to the canvas beneath her.\n\nThe silence that stood before her would be the loudest in the setting; few chirps would echo to quickly trail off as the corpse would come to\na halt. The figure would be surrounded by a few smaller creatures; they would squawk loudly, their sounds strained as the smaller of the group would stew a panicked temper, beginning to circle the air around the now curled figure that would mainting her\nposition; the scene would become angered once again, frustration overpowering any emotion those around the limp body would feel. \n\nTheir screams would echo again as the remaining ravens would accompany the rest of the flock, circling\nEloh'ra as to aid her in some way.\n\nDespite being bombarded with constant paining visions, introducing an overwhelming feeling of fear, Eloh'ra would look to the blazing sky, heat lines would dance before her until her gaze would be\ngreeted by a sight more disturbing than her inevitable fate.\n\nTowering over her, a man chuckling loudly at the sight he would be witnessing; his eyes narrowing as if examining the entirity of Eloh'ra's existence.\n\nAs her vision would begin to darken,\na sudden blaze of orange flame would shoot across Eloh'ra's remaining window of sight.\n\nA shrill scream would erupt from within her parched lips as fire engulfs both her body and face. The flaming elf's hands relinquished their grip on her staff as she\nwould sink quietly to both knees before collapsing face first into the marsh. As Eloh'ra would slip into her final slumber, a slight smile crept on the man's worn face.\n\nThe man would pause for a few moments to observe any signs of breathing, ready to\nsink in another spell if necessary. Satisfied that his foe was truly unconsious, he strenuously would move the elf's weight atop of him. \n\nHe would slowly stand and begin to whisper few of many words into the Mali'ame's ears.\nYards away, a petite figure clothed in similarly dirty pants and a weathered shirt would emerge from behind a tree. A soft, feminine voice would speak. \n\n\"An' if she'd a listen to you, there'd be one less 'round here.\"\nSince this event, as related by many whom had the pleasure to witness such, Eloh'ra has chosen to follow other paths. \n\nMany choose to speak that spells were cast upon her while others tell the tales of the offering of Dark Arts\nto her.\nHer where-abouts are currently unknown to all but her closest friends and we are simply to await what is to become of the once titled,\n\n§sRaven Druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eloise's Title", "John Roger", "Dear Miss Eloise Fletcher\n\nI here by give you the official title of \n\nDeputy Steward Of Felsen\n\n*Signed\n\nHis Imperial Majesty John II Sigismund\n\nHead Steward John Roger", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Affixes.", "Anthron", "Elven Affixes A-Z\n-------------------ac- (aca-) Honorific for an accursed.\n\nah- (ahe-): Honorific for reverence. Often used in front of names to denote sainthood.\n\nael-: Vile, unnatural, beastly\n-al: -Designates the completion of an action.\n\n-an: many, full of -Mostly designates plurality\n\nan*h- (a/o/i/e/u): To direct\n\nav-: wandering\nay: for\n\n-ante (-nte): Last\n\ndiv-: Empty, devoid of (antecendent to -an)\n\n-ento (-nto): next\n\n-ehya: and - used at the beginning of a sentence for 'but...'\nel- (ele-): - Changes a noun into a pronoun, making it a title of someone, or possibly something.\n\nfi-: new, anew - Often used as prefix, but not exclusively.\n\nheya- (hey-): what, how, who\nil- (ilu-): with\n\n-ii: little Designated the diminutive form. Plural: iian.\n\n-ir: - Designates the purpose of someone\n\niyl-: this usually a prefix, though not exclusively.\niyul-: that usually a prefix, though not exclusively.\n\n-leh: -Designates affiliation\n\nma- (mar-): very -Intensifier.\n\n-n: - Sometimes put behind an adjective or verb to create a noun.\nne (-ane): not - A suffix used to indicate the negative.\n\n-onn: from, born, kin - Often a suffix, but not always. \n\npar- (pra-): before, pre-\n\nres- (re-): wayward, capricious, unpredictable\n-sae: Spreading, development management.\n\ntal- (tali-): Part (of)\n\nu-: or - Always a prefix and always used with apostrophe\n-yem (-hyem): again -Can be used to make a 're-' family of verbs\n\nvul- (vule-): clever, intuitive, deceptive.\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Children", "Niera Acal'elor", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n\n     Elven Children\n       And  You.\nTo be elven is to be with and without blessing. Our blessing is that of a long life, yet that is also part of our curse. It is a long life full of infertilitym yet every few decades Malin smiles upon us, and gives the blessing of a child.\nBy now, you should know how children are made. That is not the subject of this piece, and should you wish to know how to, I am sure you can find that written upon a bathroom stall in an oren tavern.\nThis book will teach you what to do and what will happen once you and your husband decide to start a family.\nAn elven woman comes of age at the age of 50, she is not able to have children before then. \nElven children are not brought about easily. It often times takes years of trying to bring one into the world.\nDo not be disheartened, it is our curse that children are not brought onto us. Often times a pregnancy will take, but they are fragile and often times the child may be lost. Elven women can have children ever 15 years.\nNow, when Malin has finally blessed you with a child, you will notice a few things. FIrstly the illness. You will feel like you’re rocking on a sinking ship, constantly nauseous and ill. It is important to stay in bed during these times.\nOur pregnancies are fragile,and must be cared for. You will also notice strange cravings for food you had never had before. Mine was cake, I was always hungry for cake, I could not get enough of it.\nNext, your body will begin to swell. This of course is unpleasant and oftentimes leave the body sore. It is important to no longer travel long distances once you begin showing, as it is hard on the body and the pregnancy. You will get fat.\nThe child grows inside the mother for about a year, then, the child is born. If you wish to know more about this, get an anatomy book. \n\nYou now have a little elven child, and have a long life together ahead of you.\nYour child will need constant attention, and care. It is important that the child is taught at an early age, so that their mind may develop into something great.\nYet playtime is also important. Surround your child with toys and love, and they will prosper in life. \n\nDo not pressure them too much, or limit their dreams. They must be permited to forge their own path.\nYour child will begin to walk at about 1-2 years of age, followed by teeth, and the use of simple words. \n\nThis is the prime time to introduce your elven child to books, and educational materials. Be patient, everyone has their own speed-\nOf learning.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 1", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons\n\nOriginally By:\n\nKalenz Uradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\nIn Elven, grammatical structure is often different to that of common. For one, instead of placing an adjective before a noun, it is placed after said noun. This becomes particularly important for the most basic of greetings.\nKarin’alya-Goodday\nKer’ayla – Goodnight\nVan’ayla –Goodbye\nEach places the time of day before the adjectives describing it. Noun adjective are separated by an apostrophe.\nOther important words of the beginner in Elven include race names:\nMali-Elf\nUruk- Orc\nValah-Human\nBortu-Dwarf\n\nIn order to form sub-races of Elves, adjectives are taken to add more detail to the word Mali.\nWood Elf-Mali’ame\nHigh Elf-Mali’aheral\nDark Elf-Mali’ker\n\nIn order to form sub-races of other cultures, the suffix tali- may be used. This word directly means ‘part of’.\nGoblin-Tali’uruk (Lit: Part Orc)\nHalfing-Tali’valah (Lit: Part Human)\n\nOther basic phrases include exclamations, including:\n\nGood-Ayla\nBrilliant-Sul’leyun (Lit: Beautiful Light)", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 2", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons 2\n\nOriginally By:\n\nKalenz Uradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in Elven are as follows:\n\nKae-Me\nNae-You\nLae-He/Him\nHae- She/Her\nLye-We\n(used to speak of Elves, people, or\nworld)\n\nfor example, the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (he fared well).\n\nIn addition to this, other good languages supplements to\nanyone learning Elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be added to create further detail of form critical grammatical structures in a sentence. The dash denotes location of a seed word. Affixes and seed words are seperated by an apostrophe.\nac-(aca-) - Honorific for accursedness\n\nah-(ahe-) Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholar.\nEx.: Ah'Lucion\n\nfi- New or anew\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) -Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. Ex. : Cer'Silir\n\n-ante (-nte) - Last\n\n-ento (-nto) - Next\n\n-onn - from or born\nu- - Or\n\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive\n\n-ir -purpose\n\n-sae - The spreading, development, or management\n\n-ii - deminuitive form\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 3", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons 3\n\nOriginally By: \nKalenz Unradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by: \n\nArinislia\nTo conjugate verbs in elven, one must note precisely what person is being referred to in the sentence. Then the verb is conjugated: \n\n-e - 1st sing\n\n-a - 2nd sing\n\n-e - 3rd sing\n-ae - 1st pl\n\n-an - 2nd pl\n\n-eyae - 3rd pl\n\nTo create past and future tenses is quite simply in elven. However, it takes specific forms depending on the time of day.\nFor these two tenses, the following four words are used:\n\nKarin'ento- Next sunrise\n\nKarin'ante- Last sunrise\n\nKer'ento- Next sunset\nKer'ante- Last sunset\n\nIf it is night at the time the elf refers to the past or present, the two forms with the 'Ker' are used. If it is day at the time the elf refers to the past or present, the two forms with 'Karin' are used. These endings are\nsimply added on the end of sentences to designate the tense. Ex. : Kalenz iyathe (Kalenz thinks) becomes Kalenz iyathe ker'ante (Kalenz thought). Assuming the time in which it is spoken is the night.\nIn spoken elven, particularly more casual speech, these endings are often shortened into the slang of karinto, karinte, keno, and kente.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 4", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons 4\n\nOriginally By :Kalenz Uradir. Rescribed by: [Ghost] The Eternal Librarien.\n\nRescribed once more after the burning of the Eternal Library by: \n\nArinislia\nIn elven, numbers are formed by the compostition of multiple words. Each word representing the magnitude of the number. To note a number between one to ten, the simple word in elven to use. The express a multiple of ten, an elven number is placed before\na multiple of ten. For example: niut'matelu means 200.\n\n1- cem\n2-niut\n3-hael\n4-vailu\n5-kulin\n6-banih\n7-laier\n8-esun\n9-moiel\n10-telu\n100-matelu\n1000-marmatelu\n\nAnother particularly useful prefix not mentioned before is 'fer'. Fer is used in combination with seed words for form the names of handheld tools.\nSome such examples include those below. However, to those more advanced in elven, others may be thought up. \n\nFer'ame- axe\nFer'thuln- pickaxe\nFer'nor- shovel\nFer'sul -torch\nFer'bilok- hammer\nFer'norsae- hoe", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons V", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "\n\n\n\nNew Elven Lessons:\n      Volume 5\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nIn elven in order to denote affiliation the suffix -leh is used. It is placed after the object and designates the possession of said object by the subject of the sentence. However, it also has a use when no object in the sentence can be found and\nmeans in such a case 'spirit'. This also contributes to the common farewell blessing \"kaean'leh evareh\" which means \"may it protect us\". \n\nIt is also worth learning the 'operative' which is also seen in the sentence above on in\nword 'evareh' . In elven it serves the purpose of turning a verb into a wish. It is conjugated as below:\n\n-eh - operative sing.\n-erih - operative pl. (-arih if the verb ends in -ar)", ""),
        StaticBook("Elvi's diary 1", "Elvi Terryal", "7th of Malin's Welcome 1482\n~~~~\nIt had taken a while but the manor is nearly completed. We just need to decorate the remaining two floors and we're done. To be honest, the manor looks amazing and I am surprised that Ulfrik has invited me to live\nthere with him. I have to admit, Ulfrik is very kind and comforting, much like Ser Derionis, he is willing to help me whenever I need help and is someone that I can have a good talk with. I'm not even sure what would have happened if I hadn't met him.\nEither way, I am grateful to have met him... although Daniel had unknowingly raised a question within me: Does Ulfrik like me? I've noticed he is always kind and friendly towards me, he even brought me dinner at the Standing, and I always think he is\nsmiling behind that helmet of his. I will be honest but I think I do like Ulfrik, not just a friendly way but... perhaps further? I'm not sure why but I always feel safe and comfortable with him around, not to mention he actually makes me smile. Maybe the\ncreator is planning something for us. I don't know. Either way, I have to focuse on learning Alchemy, being a bartender and getting this manor done.\nI can finally have a comfy, warm bed for once inside of that mangy and uncomfortable bed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elvi's diary 2", "Elvi Terryal", "10th of the First Seed 1482\n~~~~\nUlfrik had read the diary entire! Gah! How can I be so stupid in dropping it and not remembering that I lost it! Thankfully, Ulfrik understood and promised not to tell Daniel and anyone else.\nAlso, my anger had\nreached its peak today. I was so angry at being called 'Button' and having Daniel questioning my appearance that I just lost it completely and stormed out of the house. Thankfully, Daniel and Ulfrik managed to calm me down and I am attempting to change\nmyself now.\nLastly, Ulfrik seems a little angry... well he sounded like it. I'm wondering what is wrong. His brother, Thor-something, came and talked to him about the war ragining on in Polaris but he was also talking with a woman so I think it was\nsomething to do with he. He said he will tell me later so, I guess I will just have to wait and see....\n11th of Grand Harvest 1482\n~~~~\nJust another day working at the tavern. Daniel met another Daniel and the two had a few matches to decide who was the real 'Dan'. It was actually quite funny.\nAlso, Ulfrik gave me a book about Alchemy\nrecipes and also a lilic which he placed in my hair. How sweet. We haven't got round to moving in the furniture but I have planned out the walls and rooms. He is busy so we haven't go onto that yet.\nLastly, Danie;s student, Abluson or something drank his\nown potion which went wrong. It resulfted in him becoming cold and us having to dave him from suffering hypthermia. Also Kardel, Daniel's teacher, was struck by lightning from Daniel's student so I had to lend my assisstance in making sure they are okay.\nThankfully, I made a paste made from Serpent stalks which heals burns and eases the pain of burns so I helped Kardal. In the end, the two are alright and safe.\nI currently have a small box full of the paste so I can use it if I get burned or if\nsomeone else ends up getting burned.\nLastly, I had to train a new bartender. He woke up in the cloud temple and didn't know how to serve ale or cook food so I had to teach him. He seems nice, but not as a nice as Ulfrik.\nSpeaking of which, I need to see\nhow he is doing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elvira's Diary 1", "Elvi Terryal", "7th of The Deep Cold\n1491\n~~~~\nThe tavern has been quiet as it is the quiet hour. Quite bored actually. I travelled to the swamp by Karovia to find some ingredients, I also went to the nearby forest as well. Sadly, nothing interesting happened.\nAlthough on the way back, just on the bridge leading to the old manor myself and Ulfrik use to live in, I met a man (northener from the sound of his accent) who took it upon himself to question about my grey fringe. When I told him 'because I wanted it-\n-this way', he merely called it a stupid response. What else was he expecting me to say? That someone purposely did this to me? Heh, no.\nWe talked for a little bit and I begun to dislike the man even more. Next thing we knew, a 12ft troll appeared-\n-and asked us to pay a toll for 'Cheezy's landz' as I quote. He was rather menacing, especially as he was right in front of me! The rude man gave him a rotten flesh, which made the troll happy and punched him in the stomach! HA! SERVES HIM RIGHT! Then-\nthat idiotic man had to go and call the troll 'dumb' and told the troll it was me who said it! Did that bastard want me to die!?\nThankfully, I managed to turn the table of him by telling him purposely out loud that he should never call a friendly and nice\ntroll dumb because of how he speaks. The troll heard and, thank Creator, smiled at me, then gave me a potato skin which he placed on my head. Although not exactly the best gesture of thanks, better than getting punched in the stomach or killed.\n- Elvi E.T\n10th of The Deep  Cold.\n\nI met up with Guarger, Alfred and Dorian today but not in the best terms.\nAccording to Dorian, he had left the Faolains, who were not happy, so he was now wanted dead. Even worse, Alfred was apparently\nmeant to kill him as well. When myself and Dorian were talking, Alfred appeared and Dorian (as well as an armoured friend of his) killed Alfred right in front of me. As much as I appear to hate Alfred, I don't actually hate him. He's a nice friend but he-\ndid not deserve to die like that. A tomahawk to the chest then having his head brutally smashed in. Guarger came and escorted me away.\nWe talked for a little bit and turns out Guarger may have a solution to my infertility! He said he has a friend who is\na cleric so... I may be able to bear a child soon. Some people may not understand why I am overjoyed by this but only because I was unable to and I've always wanted to raise a family. Anyway, Guarger asked if I would bear his child which I said I would.\nEven though we're not together anymore, we still love each other deeply.... ARG! Why must our relationship be so complicated! I know Guarger doesn't want to get together in order not to harm my feelings more but... I'm just sad that I won't be going out-\nwith him.... Nevermind.\nWhile talking about this, I got an idea. If both myself and Guarger (or one of us) is unexpectedly killed, our child would likely be send to an orphanage and because I was raised in an orphanage myself.... which did not end well...\nI don't want my child to have the potential chance of suffering what I did. So myself and Guarger decided that if we do have a child, that child will have a Godfather and Godmother.\nGuarger immediately knew who I was going to pick so we easily agreed on\nit. Daniel would be the Godfather and Sherria (or Beth since I sadly do not know Sherria that well) will be the Godmother. I trust Daniel (and Sherria) and Beth with my life. If there is anyone I would trust my child to, it would be them.\nAside from that\ntalk, nothing else really happened. I told Guarger about Beth and the 320 pancakes and boy did that make him laugh. Beth still owes me 160 minas for that!\nEither way, that day was amazing and I felt as though I never had the terrible past I had. I felt\nperfectly normal! Anyway, I best get back to cleaning the tavern, Dan will kill me if he sees how dusty the tavern is.\n\n- Elvi E.T", ""),
        StaticBook("Elvira's letter", "Elvira Naromis", "Dear all I consider friends, and even family,\n\nAfter what had occured a couple of weeks ago... I've decided on a few things.\n\nFirstly, my past. As you all know very well, my past was not the greatest of pasts (although quite tame compared to-\n- some of your pasts.) and had always affected me badly. However, I have took it to heart, I will no longer allow the past to manipulate and control me.\nThat Elvira you saw in the cave, the murderous and berserk one, will never be seen again. No more.\nAnother thing is my name. I am still Elvira, or Elvi as you all call me. However, I have now changed my last name to Naromis. Those who heard of my mentor (and adoptive father), Ser Dorian Naromis, will know how close I was to him and that he mentioned in\n- a letter to me that if I wished to do so, I can change my last name to his.\nWhy have I changed my name? Terryal reminds me too much of my past. Also, Terryal means 'Reaper'. Meaning it can be linked of my past as I have killed. Naromis means 'One of -\n- fire/flames', meaning that it is a good name for myself. Elvira Naromis: The White one of fire/flames'. Quite suiting don't you think?\n\nThirdly, my personality. Now with my past gone, I am becoming more carefree, more calm, mature, knowledgeable and-\n- confident. No longer am I that nervous, annoying, wreck of a woman. That was Elvira Terryal. I am Elvira Naromis.\n\nAlso, I am considering my future now. Do I aim further in Alchemy? Learn more magic? Perhaps end my job as a bartender and see who needs-\nmy help? Perhaps become a healer and aid many?\nThere are many roles for myself to choose. I'm quite unsure on what to do but I suppose the saying: 'Follow your heart' will fit in here.\nI'm mostly considering a combination of Alchemy and becoming a-\n- healer (as well as teaching Alchemy to new people). Maybe through becoming a healer and learning more healing based in Alchemy, perhaps I could do some good for Athera? Perhaps I could create new potions, or even solve how to make impossible ones. Sadly\nthat may not be possible with some potions but worth a good shot I suppose.\n\nThe last thing I've decided is to perhaps go travelling for a while. I'm still considering this but I need some time to myself, to think some things through. Besides, I need to-\n-relax and calm myself, so perhaps a journey is worth going on. Besides, I quite enjoy travelling, it allows you to discover new things and meet new people, encounter deadly situations but see wonderous sights. Like I said, I'm still thinking this through\nbut if I do announce I am going on a leave, don't be upset. You can all still talk to me by bird and I will return eventually (propably after a few months or so if I will be walking).\nWho knows, I may find some new things.\n\nEven so, I'm still here, still-\n- Elvi, just with some minor differences to myself. Not to mention with new clothing as well, I made it myself after I found weaving and sewing quite fun.\n(Welp, Daniel, looks like I may look a bit boyish on the outside, still got the inner woman on the-\n-inside)\n\nSo, this letter is to just explain what I'm going to be doing and what's happening now. If you do not enjoy these changes, these are my choices so please accept them.\nIf not, don't make me place a rolling pin (on fire if I may add) up your sorry\nbacksides.\nDaniel, and any other bartender, make sure my friends read this letter. Their names are included at the bottom.\n\nSincerely,\nElvira Naromis (Terryal)\nList of people to give letter to:\n-Ray.\n-Beth.\n-Daniel.\n-Alfred.\n-Arradon. (if he ever turns up, do tell him about what happened to me with Rajin.)\n-Perdric. (Same with Arradon, tell him what happened to me.)", ""),
        StaticBook("Emissary Letter", "Tuvya", "*Seal of House Carrion*\n\nThe Signed, William Harcourt, is to be recognized as Lord Emissary of the Holy Empire of Oren, to be recognized as Voice of His Imperial Majesty.\n\n~Tuvya", ""),
        StaticBook("Employee log", "Vareack Irongrinder", "Visited a new town, hired as an Engineer, city looks promising.\n\nVisits the orc land, meeting 2 ologs very strong and friendly, the Blah language is fascinating\n\nVisits the dwarves and speaks with a master alchimist a very old dwarf, very nice and\nwelcoming, tells me to speak with his leader but be careful.\n\nThinks up a creation:\nTNT cannon, shoots 2 tnt per hit of button, needs packed ice, tnt, redstone, \nHas an idea for a shelter:\nUnderground defense traps, including fire arrows, resulting in\ndeath if you dont hit the right switch, requires arrows, some source of fire to ignite the arrows, dispensers, switches, etc...\n\nAll way tnt: results in total destruction 360 degrees, requires substance that is tnt proof, tnt all around, redstone, switch\nFire arrow machine: Shoots maybe 6 flaming arrows at a time untill no arrows left, Could destroy a line of men before they reach the machine, requires arrows, ignition source, redstone, foundation.\n\nTraps: Enemy walks over a block and the ground falls,\nenemies trapped in the ground till death, possible arrows shooting them, or could wait for soldier to find them, possible slavery or excecution.\n\nUnderground escapes: Basic pull switch wall opens to an underground path to protect the emporer\n\"I would like a large office perhaps, I need a supply room, large secure testing grounds, possibly underground to keep people from spying. A team of architects and engineers, maybe 3-5 people, Would love to work for the empire and take down the dwarvern\nrace.\n\nMet the mayor of falsen, very nice man, very smart, I think he might be interested in taking me and giving me a job, hopefully will give me the things I need for optimal results. Another man was in the room, not sure whom he was.\nSeemed like a nice guy, can't wait to get back with them and advance the empire.\n\nSees a line of people in falsen square trying to pull sword out of a boulder. does the basic physics to pull the sword in his head while waiting in line. Pulls the sword\nwith ease.\n\nMeets a dick head guard. Says he isn't an Imperial Engineer\n\nSees mylas and 3-5 other guys fighting of an orc that looks like he tried killing mylas. They smash in his skull with a hammer\n\nJerry and several others catch a theif and cut off his right hand\n\nJerry and others are attacked by two Harpies\nBorn in Carnatia in the year 1520, to a father who was a miner. Enlisted in the Carnatia Military at the age of 24,left at 25. Joined Lorraine Honor Guard at the age of 25 as a Leatherworker/Miner. Became the Commander of the Lorraine Honor Guard at the\nage of 27. Left at 28 because of the poor leadership of the archduke. Currently, as you can tell looking for work in mining,engineering, any odd jobs.\" - Applicant\nTom Cacamnidiatenia Callahan, my full name is actually Tommidanificardiaoulita Cacamnidiatenia Bortano Ricker Albus Callahan. My long name came from my long name ancestors and I'm gay. If you can't handle the fact I'm gay you can go fuck yourself.\nFennis Harthok, Age 21\nWorked most of my life doing small mercenary work for people like guarding a gate for a few hours or shouting at some kids. Nothing major, always like art and stuff, most of my family died from disease so have a small phobia of >>\ndisease and sickness but nothing too insane (its pretty damn insane). Got some family somewhere, but who knows.\nCasius Rahl ((Vanir_))\n-Excels at Tinkering\n(Adept)\n-Fairly good lumberjack and fisherman (Fair)\n-Isn't a half-bad cook (Apprentice))\nI've been a part of the Duchy of Courlandia for a vast majority of my life. Helping them rebuild recently, I've had my business start up there as well. Just acrossthe street, is that said business: A Tea House. \nSince becoming a part of that duchy, I've\ngained many more traits to my being. I've become more independent, motherly, mentally prepared, straight-forward, creative, and I see myself as a leader. \n\nI run my own business, I'm a scholar of the Library of Dragur, a stewardess of Riga, a secretary of\nthe Felsen Mayor, and I'm becoming a cleric soon!\nJudas Agnarsson\n((Steve_Busalami))\nVareack IronGrinder\nVetern Miner", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting", "Lefkos Glowsbane", "Efficiency:\nEfficiency is one of the quickest and easiest of all of the enchantments to make. The purpose of this is to make any desired tool do its job faster. Using it, you may find that your pickaxe digs through stone like a knife through butter, or an\naxe may fell a tree in one or two swings. Even though it may be a cheap enchantment, it remains one of the most well known and used.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                ----x----                ---x-x---                ----x----\nUnbreaking:\nThis would probably be the second most used enchant, its purpose rather simple and self explanatory. I will review it anyway. Unbreaking is meant to make your tools harder and stronger. Tougher to break. Using it, you may notice that tools\nthat used to break after you use them for a while may still be functional. Its another easy enchantment that wouldnt cost to much to purchase.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                -x-x-x-x-                --x---x--                -x-x-x-x-\nSharpness:\nThis is a rather difficult enchantment, much to hard for a novice to make, and a rather expensive one as well. With this enchantment, you may find that your swords cut through bodys easier, making your opponents fall before your blade.\nThose that seek out an enchanter for this enchantment are normally guards, or people about to go to war.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        --x------                xxxxxxxx-                xxxxxxxxx                --x------\nPower:\nAn enchantment similar to sharpness, but for a different item. Power is made for bows, and when using it, you may find arrows you shoot from your bow hitting harder, enough to crack stone and injure your opponent more then a normal arrow. Only\nProffesional marksmen and archers will seak out this enchantment.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        xx----x--                --xxxxxx-                --xxxxxxx                xx----x--\nFire Aspect:\nOne of the oldest and harder enchantments to master. Many seek this enchantment on their blades for its usefullness. It is a must have for armies and a hard level enchantment. Adventurers and high ranking officers may seek out an enchanter\ncapable of this for their army. Fire aspect gives your blade an arcane power that, upon cutting any living creature, will set them aflame. Its thought of as a brutal but useful enchantment.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -xxxxxxx-\nFlame:\nVery similar to Fire Aspect, Flame is another hard level enchantment. It lets your arrows catch fire, and burn whatever they hit.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        x--x--x-x                -xxxx-x-x                x--x--x-x                ------xxx\nKnockback:\nOne of the best enchantments in my opinion, knockback is sure to prove useful to anyone, no matter who they are fighting. This enchantment, rather then strengthening the actual blade, strengthens the arm holding the blade.\nIt is called \"Knockback\" because at that point, if you hit someone with your arm at full force, you possess the strength to send them flying back. Combine this with Fire aspect and you can shoot little fireballs called 'your opponent.'\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xx-----                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xx-----\nProtection:\nOne of the less common used enchantments, but more useful. Protection was made to make your armor harder, so an arrow that would once pierce your heart wouldnt even reach it. The only reason it isnt commonly used is because not many\npeople have the time to wait for their armor to be enchanted.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                ---xxx---\nFeather falling:\nA rarely used enchant. Infact, not a single person has asked me for it. I will put it here anyways. Feather falling increases the strength of your feet in terms of impact for the ground. Normally if you would barely survive after a 10\nmeter drop, you would be fine for this handy enchantment. Most people under value this enchantment, until they slip and fall!\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         -----xx--                ----xxx--                ----xx---                ---x-----", ""),
        StaticBook("Endvani's Poem 1", "Endvani Ildres", "Petrichor\n\nA Poem by\nEndvani Ildres\nPetrichor, Petrichor\nSpice and Season Petrichor,\nMay the sky kiss your cheeks,\nthe rain wash your weeps,\ntill I am at your side.\nPetrichor, Petrichor\nSweet perfume of petrichor,\nRainsong soft with thunder's beat,\nbring you dreams,\ntill when we meet.\nPetrichor, petrichor\nWind and waves and petrichor\nMoonlight will my promise keep,\nlike the bond of stubborn, faithful sheep,\n\ntill I am at your side.", ""),
        StaticBook("Enlightenment", "Daekra Solli'gra", "Enlightenment is an intellectual movement emphasizing reason and individualism rather than tradition. It allows free thinking without the binds of backwards thinking which allows for more sophisticated systems of living throughout nations once accepted.\nAlthough this ideaology is one of equality and justifiable ideals, there is always a struggle between religion and war which could impose free thought. This is one of the reasons why many philosophers, artists and musicians may do their work in secrecy.\nEnlightenment also provides a large boost to culture, this being that those who create culture are not exiled but rather embraced. With this people are more happy due to more entertainment and bizzare ideas that are conjured up by free thinkers.\nIn recent years, enlightenment has given Salvus a cultural edge over many other nations in Vailor, they're ideas have made a big impact on their citizens and reputation. If it wasn't for their higher thinking, cultural growth would be replaced with war.\nIn conclusion, there is an unseen demand for enlightment in many other duchies, counties, baronies and so on. They crave to experience new and exciting ideas and it is only through enlightenment in which we may advance past petty struggles and learn.", ""),
        StaticBook("Entities that-..", "Elindor", "Entities Within Our Realm Of Existence No Longer Existing, And Then Existing Again.\n\n            §sOR\n\nVoid Translocation\n~1~ Introduction\n~2~ Study\n~3~ Sensory Overhaul\n~4~ Destruction\n~5~ Re-Creation\nIt does not take much searching within a library to gain some concepts of the Void as an alternate existence outside, within and with no relation at all to our reality. Arcanists, Mages, Sorcerers\n-whatever the name- users of voidal magic pull a 'thing'\ninto this realm that did not previously exist within it, and hold it there for as long as they can wield a void connection. But no 'thing' pulled from the void is retained here. Such power is reserved to The Creator to pull real matter from The Void.\nBut what if a 'thing'\n-be it inanimate, plant, animal, edible-\nalready existed? Then the connectino to The Void need only be instantaneous, because the 'thing' is not created, but simply  IS\nSTUDY\nTake within your hands something that exists. Any kind of thing will suffice and for the sake of example we shall call it and any potential other thing an \"entity\".\nBegin your examination in the simplest of interests: Form.\nWhat size is it?\nWhat's it made of?\nHow heavy is it?\nHow malleable is the material?\nDoes it react to heat?\nWhat happens under great pressure?\n\nIf already you are struggling then you should return this book whence it came.\nSecondly you will need to form these observations into a mental map of the object. This is a far more complex procedure and verges on a particularly niche form of magic known as cognitism; however Telekinetics may find themselves more easily\ninclined towards this type of thinking. You cannot be bound by your perceptions in understanding the world. If you are purely an experiencer of your surroundings then you will never formulate any greater understandings of anything ever. So work on that.\nIf you are able to mentally comprehend the object beyond what is merely visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity's existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\nSensory Overhaul\nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculatable values and perceiving the entity's magical value. Aside from universally shifting perspective with the aid of magic, the quantity\nof information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a realm in which is not a single thing but the potential for all things. And\nthereby all things that exisst are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practice and isn't really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of magic or not. Certainly with practice comes the\nstrengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to 'feel' a rosebush from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being laid down, when you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you must measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void with your own so\nthat the entity is no longer isolated in this world but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones' self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more 'alive' an entity is, the more rapidly it produces mana.\nAnything that has a soul is independantly existing within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant. Soul-less entities then exist\nsomewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of glass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more 'alive' it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be able to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\nNo Longer Existing\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existance it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was tangible just stops and is\nno more.\nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independantly of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its divine creation re-instated, and therefore able to return to the nothing from which it came.\nWithin The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes of itself a something for that fleeting moment. But without being birthed\ninto existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely, there becomes a new potential within The Void that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like an arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the potential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that\nkeeps it sacredly linked to once again become what The Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a ceramic teapot will not become crude clay but remains a teapot).\nTo Return Again\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the original entity is the only thing that\nmaintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independant existence outside of The Void is made (i.e redoing Creator's work) will assign the potential with its destined form.\nAnd the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\n\nGood job, you meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Essay & Apology", "Anthron", "In this essay, I will say what I did wrong, why it was wrong, and that I will never do it agiain.\n\n\nIt all started when I had asked Muildir to help me in finding someone to kill Mukar.\nAt the time we were\nboth not really in the right mind seeing as Za was given to Mukar, but luckily he was not killed.\n\n\nA few days later I had heard yelling coming from the guide tree\nso I went up there to see what all the yelling was about.\n\n\nWhen I had got there I had seen Beth yelling at Muildir, it had seemed that the person he had hired told beth about what we did.\nAnd this is my punishment, to write a thirty page essay about what I did, why I did it, why it was wrong, and that I will never do it again.\nIn all honesty, this is one of the most stupud things I could have planned up to even think of doing, let alone actually carrying it out.\n\n\nHaving been under the influence of a biased opinion and\nmy emotions, I was not in the right state of mind.\n\n\nJust thinking about this dissapoints me deeply, and having carried it out just makes it worse.\nAll I can really do is follow out with my punishment and whatever may be to come and live with it.\n\n\nI had not realized at the time what I was actually doing and that it was wrong.\nLucky for us, the person that Muildir hired told Beth about what we were doing.\n\n\nI had also not realized the consequences and the disasterous effects that would have followed\nif we had succeeded.\n\n\nWhat would have happened would have been many things; for one, the grove could have been put to war against the kharajyr and their allies.\nAlso if Mukar was killed the kharajyr would have lost one of their highest ranking priests, and many of them might have come back for revenge.\n\n\nI am deeply ashamed of myself as I had taken a\nvow when I became a druid to keep peace and to protect my brothers and sisters.\n\n\nLetting this plan go through just dissapoints me more, but I am glad that whoever\nMuildir hired told Beth, as things would have been much much worse if we had succeeded in our plan.\n\n\nI take full responsibility of my actions and accept that they were wrong and I do'nt\nexpect to be forgiven for it.\n\n\nWhat was already done has taken its toll, and the result was not as bad as what it could have been if things had continued.\nDuring that time when I was not in the right mind, I had thought that Mukar being gone would help both the kharajyr people and the grove alike, seeing as a bunch of people\ndo not like him as it is.\nBut letting it succeed would have proven a more disasterous and opposite result to what I had thought.\n\n\nI do not condone my actions as I now see that it is wrong.\nI also regret having done what I had did and all I seek now is forgiveness wherever and whenever I can find it.\n\n\nSadly, I could not think of anything else I could say\nthat could convey me deepest regret for what I had done, and that I will never do it again.\n\n\nSo what I will say now is all the things that could have happened if this had all gone according to plan.\nIf this had all gone according to plan, either Mukar would have been killed, or the person Muildir hired would have been caught and his mind would most likely have been read.\nIf the person's mind was read, the entire plan would have been just another reason to\ngive the kharajyr priests the reasons to go to war with us, and the grove alike.\nBut if the plan had succeeded, and Mukar killed, then the kharajyr people would have been mad, and seeking revenge wherever they could find it.\nWhich in turn would lead to the grove getting attacked more, seeing as we are in a bad enough position as it is.\n\n\n\nWhat I will now say is why I will never do it again and\nwhy another thing like this should not happen.\n\n\n\nI have learned from my actions, and I have learned that it would be best if Mukar were not killed, so that the grove\nwould not be put in any further danger.\n\n\nBut if Mukar stays alive we will still be in partial danger because he keeps attempting to capture Za and kill him.\nIf another thing like this were to happen, then bad things would happen.\n\n\nMurder is never a good option, in any circumstance, whether it mean life or death.\nI personally apologize to all the people that I put in danger when I had started to follow through with this.\n\n\nI also thank who told Beth about this because of things that would have happened if Beth\nwas not told.\n\n\nI will not do this again or anything of a similar description.\n\n\nA plan that involves murder and the act of getting your\nfriends and familly in danger is a stupid, reckless, and idiotic thing to do.\n\n\nI want no more to do with any of this murder or hatred towards any other nation we\nhave quarrels with.\n\n\nAll I wish now is that we can all get along and eventually sort all of this out.\n\n\nOne day I hope another person learns from\nmy mistake, and learns to avoid making the same decision I had made.\n\n\nI wish to convey my deepest apologies to those who were effected and who were hurt because\nof my decision and I hope one day to be forgiven of this.\n\n\n-Acacia Druid\nAnthron.", ""),
        StaticBook("Essential Oils", "Nyxxaa", "Essential Oils - A guide to theraputic uses\n\nBy Nyx\n\n\n((ooc disclaimer: this is written mostly from Modern Essentials: A Contemporary Guide to the Therapeutic use of essential oils isbn 978-1-937702-04-5))\nquick Definitions:\nEssential oils: substances created inside aromatic plants that are both volatile (they evaporate) and oil soluble (they easily mix with oils and fats).\n\nAromatic: Referring to plants that have an aroma.\nTopical Application: Placing an essential oil directly on the skin or other surface of the body.\n\nAromatic Application: Often referred to as aromatherapy, aromatic application refers to inhaling an essential oil or it's aroma.\nInternal Application:\nInternalizing an essential oil, typically through the mouth.\n\nCarrier oil: A carrier oil refers to a vegetable oil, wax, fat, or other oil that an essential oil is mixed with. The carrier oil \"carries\" the essential oil and dilutes\nit so it's effects can be spread over a larger area.\n\nNeat: refers to applying an essential oil by itself, without diluting it in a carrier oil.\n\nDilution: refers to mixing an essential oil in a carrier oil so it's effects are not as\nconcentrated in one area.\n\nVolatile: a substance that will evaporate when exposed to air is referred to as volatile. Volatile substances are typically light substances with small parts.\nSingle oil: A single oil is one type of oil by itself.\n\nOil Blend: An oil blend is a mixture of two or more single oils.\nTable of Content\n\nWhat are essential oils?--------see p.9\n\nTopical application p.13\n\nAromatic p.28\n\nOils p.\nWhat are Essential oils? Essential oils are the volatile liquids that are distilled from plants (including their respective parts such as seeds, bark, leaves, stems, roots, flowrs, fruit, etc.). One of the factors that determines the purity and\ntherapeutic value of an oil is it's constituents. These constituents can be affected by a vast number of variables: the part(s) of the plant from which the oil was produced, soil condition, fertilizer, geographic region, climate, altittude, harvest season\nand method, and distillation process. For example common thyme produces several different effects depending on the conditions of it's growth, climate, and altitude. If it is distilled during mid summer or late fall, the oil with be more caustic or\nirrritating to the skin. Low pressure and low temperature are key to maintaining the purity, the ultimate fragrance, and the therapeutic value of the oil.\nTopical Application\n\nTopical application is the process of placing an essential oil on the skin, hair, mouth, teeth, nails, or membrances of the body. Applying eddential oils directly can sometimes be harmful  so usage of a carrier oil is needed\noften carrier oils are coconut oil, almond oil, olive oil, jojoba oil, etc. Several topical application methods are outlined below.\n\nDirect application:\nTo achieve best results use 1-3 drops of oil.\ntips\n\n- The feet are the second fastest area of the body to absorb ouls because of the large pores. other quick absorbing areas include behind the ears and on the wrists.\n- When massaging a large area of the body, always dilute the oils by 15% to 30% with coconut oil.\n\n- When applying to infants or small children always dilute oils using 1-3 drops of the oil and about a spoon full of coconut oil.\n- use caution when creating blends. oil parts can be altered and cause undesirable reactions.\n\n- Layering individual oils is preferred over mixing your own blends for topical use. Layering refers to the process of applying one oil\n, rubbing it in, and then applying another oil. There is no need to wait more than a couple of seconds between each oil.\n\nMassage:\nTo create a simple massage oil that includes the benefits of oils, combine 3-10 drops of your oil\nwith a full spoon of coconut oil. apply a small amount of this mixture on the massage location and massage it into the skin using light to medium-light strokes of the hand of fingers.\nContact point:\nIs a simple method of appying oils to contact points in the feet or hands. A series of hand rotation movements at those control points create a vibrational healing energy that carries the oils along the pathways. The oils either help remove\nany bloackage along the pathways or travel the length of the pathways to benefit the particular organ. Refer to hand and foot charts on the following pages for more details.\n\nCompresses:\nBasin. Fill a wash basin with two buckets of hot or cold water, and\nadd the desired oils. stir the water viforously; then lay a towel on top of the water. Since the oils will float to the top, the towel will absorb the oils with the water. after the towel is completely saturated, wring out excess water, and place the\ntowel over the area needing the compress. for a hot compress, cover with a dry towl and a hote water bottle. For a cold compress, cover with water treated leather. finally, put another towel on top, and leave for as long as possible (1-2 hours)\nMassage. Apply a hot, wet towl and then a dry towel on top of an already massages area. The moist heat will force the oils deeper into the tissues of the body.\n\nBaths:\nbathwater. begin by adding 3-6 drops of the oil to the bathwater\nwhilst filling the tub. soak for 15 minutes.\n\nSoaps. during the creation process add 3-6 drops to 1/2 an oz of the base.\n\nCharts\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161828.jpg\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161856.jpg\n\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161847.jpg\nFor those that would wish to make blends themselves a chart for you.\n\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161948.jpg\nAromatic\n\nDirect inhalation: is the simplest way to inhale the aroma of an oil. hold bottle under nose and breath alternatively place 1-2 drops in your hands and cup over nose and mouth before breathing.\nOils:\n\nhttp://doterra.com/US/en/pl/singleoils\n\nhttp://www.sustainablebabysteps.com/uses-for-essential-oils.html", ""),
        StaticBook("Eve of battle", "Martin Jastrung", "==   Eve Of Battle  ==\n\n\n       Here I sit\n     helmet in hands\n   is here where I fit\nwithin these badlands\n \n   The moon shines\n          bright\n\n   I cannot lay rest\n\n   on this weary night\nhopefull I am blessed\n\n\n for now I should go\n\ninto tomorrows battle\n\n   to feel the flow\n \n  of blood gravel", ""),
        StaticBook("Everal", "Leyu", "The History of Everal, the First City of the Elves\nA long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a Magikal power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundantely there and in the surrounding\nareas. The sand there made glass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the First Race, later known as Elves, planted their magikal seeds... great towering trees grew in their place. Ordinary Fyre could not scorch these\ntrees, for the magik embeded in them was still new. The Elves thrived in the new land along with the trees, spreading its seeds wherever they went, creating an Empire that Dwarfed all others previousely known. The Elves lived inside the trunks of\nthese towering trees, singing to them to help them grow. And all was peaceful. Then one day many centuries later, a Astronomical Strom swept across the land, Felling the Magikal Trees where they stood. Lightning stroke the exposed Earth, melting the\ngound and forming pools of lava. Great Fyre, fueled by the dark energys of the storm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometers remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named this area Evaral, meaning\nProtected in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the Magikal trees once more, but the Earth still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn't let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated, the Elves started to\nreach for the sky! They trees grew until they touched the highest planes of the Atmosphere! And all was at peace one again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from new predators and spirits that rose with the\nStorm. And then a terrible thing happened. Some of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and wanted more land, ores, and resources. One by one the Dissenters left Evaral, preferring the\nnew forests beyond its border. They spread out far accross the land, struggling to cope with their new homes. Eventually even they settled down and formed small villages, under no ruler. Some even evolved into other races, forgetting\nwhat they left behind. By this time only a few families remained in Evaral, and they did not know what to do. They missed the kinship of the other Elves, so they decided to leave too. But before they left each family took with them a seed from the\nfirst tree, which happened to reside in Evaral. This tree was very old and wrought with homes. And its spirit was sad too, for it missed the Elves that left. It shed its bark to help the remaining Elves in their journeys, forming impenetrable armor to\nhelp the remaining elves in their journeys. This armor now resides in the Tomb of Evaral, as the First Tree's spirit reclaimed it. And then none were left in Evaral. However over the centuries the seed still could grow, but the land never accepted them.\nUntil one day, many centuries later, it came in the hands of a young druid. The great city of Evaral's location is hidden from the world, but many believe it is still ou t there. Perhaps one day, a great hero will stumble upon it. And bring it to power\nonce again.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Everal History", "Leyu'Maehr", "The History of Everal, The First City of the Elves\nBy Leyu’Maehr\nA long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a magical power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundantly there and in the surrounding areas. The sand there made\nglass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the Frist Race, later known as Elves, planted their magical seeds… Great towering trees grew in their place. Ordinary fire could not scorch these trees, spreading its seeds wherever they\nwent, creating an Empire dwarf all others previously known. The Elves lived inside the trunks of these towering trees, singing to them to help them grow.\nThen on day many centuries later, an astronomical storm swept across the land, felling the magical trees where they stood. Lightning stroke the exposed Earth, melting the ground and forming pools of lava. Great fire, fuelled by the dark energies of the\nstorm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometres remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named this area Evaral, meaning ‘protected’ in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the magical trees once\nmore, but the Earth still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn’t let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated, the Elves started to reach for the sky! The trees grew until they touched the highest planes of the atmosphere and all was\nat peace once again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from new predators and spirits that rose with the storm. And then a terrible thing happened.\nSome of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and wanted more land, ores, and resources. One by one the Dissenters left Evaral; preferring the new forests beyond its border. They spread out far across the\nland, struggling to cope with their new homes. Eventually even they settled down and formed small villages, under no ruler. Some even evolved into other races, forgetting what they left behind.\nBy this time only a few families remained in Evaral, and they did not know what to do. They missed the kinship of the other Elves, so they decided to leave too. But before they left each family took with them a seed from the first tree, which happened to\nreside in Evaral. This tree was very old and wrought with homes and its spirit was sad too, for it missed the Elves that left. It shed its bark to help the remaining Elves in their journeys, forming impenetrable armour. This armour now resides in the Tomb\nof Evaral, as the First Tree’s spirit reclaimed it. And then none were left in the Evaral. However over the centuries the seed still could grow, but the land never accepted them.\nUntil one day many centuries later, it came in the hands of a young Druid. The great city of Evaral’s location is hidden from the world, but many believe it is still out there. Perhaps one day, a great hero will stumble upon it.\nAnd bring it to power once again.\n           -------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation Basics", "Gerald Elgan", "===================\n                                                                                                  The Basics\n             Of                       Evocation\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n==================\nIn order for sorcerers to put into use their craft, they must have a deep attunement with and knowledge of their element. A caster must know that fire begins with friction and the many stones that make up the earth. A common rule of thumb is:\n\"If the Sorcerer does not know how something functions, he cannot make it work himself\" This simply dictates that a mage MUST know how water flows and how wind gusts, just as much as they must know how fire feels to touch. Due to this, sorcerers often\nspend a great deal of time in study, on a deep spiritual level, of their respective element(s). Despite this rigorous training, their spells may still deal them harm, just as much as it may harm their opponent.\nEvocation is often quite physically and mentally taxing on the Sorcerer- as it takes a great deal of mana to cast. The large the object one wishes to bring forth, the more mana is required of him to cast it. And just as any other magical branch of the\nArcane tree, the mage must be capable of envisioning where he is casting his spell, and at what - that he must first visualize the spell itself, in his own mind, in order to bring forth its full fury. Therefore, a mage cannot simply conjure a fireball\nbehind a wall, nor can he cause a wave of water to appear in an area so distant- so beyond the caster's field of vision. Due to this law, Sorcerers are limited in some regard- hindered by the reaches of their sight. Despite the seemingly passive nature\nthat any one mage may seem to possess, they however remain filthy abominations- dangerous and unholy grotesqueries- who must be taught that such profane powers can bring no good, and must be wholly forgotten, for the sake of every man, woman, and child-\nfor all who walk upon God's blessed earth.\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("EWOROENLETEA", "Thurak'Yar", "Entities within our realm of Existence no Longer Existing, And Then Existing Again.\n\nOr, Void Translocation\n\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 1'st of Snow's Maiden, 1488\n1. Introduction\n\n2. Study\n\n3. Sensory Overhaul\n\n4. Destruction\n\n5. Re-Creation\nIt does no take much searching within a library to gain some concepts of the Void as an alternate existence outside, winin and with no relation at all to our reality. Arcanists, Mages, Sorcerers- whatever the name- users of voidal magic pull a 'thing'\ninto this realm that did not previously exist within it, and hold it there for as long as they can wield a void connection. But no ‘thing’ pulled from the void is retained here. Such power is reserved to The Creater to pull real matter from The Void.\nBut what is a ‘thing’ –be it inanimate, plant, animal, edible- already existed? Then the connection to The Void need only be instantaneous, because the ‘thing’ is not created, but simply IS.\nStudy\n\nTake within your hands something that exists. \nAny kind of thing will suffice and for the sake of example we shall call it and any potential other thing \nan 'Entity'. Begins your examination in the simplest of interests:\nForm.\nWhat size is it?\nWhat’s it made of?\nHow heavy is it?\nHow malleable is the material?\nDoes it react to heat?\nWhat happens under great pressure?\n \nIf already you are struggling then you should return this book whence it came.\nSecondly you will need to form these observations into a mental map of the object. This is a far more complex procedure and verges on a particularly niche form of magic known as cognitism; however Telekinetics may find themselves more easily inclined\ntowards this type of thinking. You cannoy be bound by your perceptions in understanding the world. If you are purely an experiencer of your surroundings then you will never formulate any greater understandings of anything ever. So work on that.\nIf you are able to mentally comprehend the object beyond what is merely visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity’s existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\nSensory Overhaul\n\nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculable values and perceiving the entity’s magical value. Aside from universally shifting perspective\nwith the aid of magic, the quantity of information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a real in which is not a single thing\nbut the potential for all things. And thereby all things that exist are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practise and isn’t really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of magic or not.\nCertainly with practise comes the strengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to ‘feel’ an apple tree from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being laid\n\ndown, what you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you muse measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void with your own so that the entity is no longer isolated in this\nworld but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones’ self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more ‘alive’ an entity is, the more rapidly it produces mana. Anything that has a soul is independently\nexisting within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such a drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant. Soul-less entities then exist somewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of\nglass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more ‘alive’ it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be able to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\nNo Longer Existing\n\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existence it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was tangiable\njust stops and is no more. \nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independently of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its diving creation re-instated, and therefore able\nto return to the nothing from which it came. Within The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes of itself a something\nfor that fleeting moment. But without being birthed into existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely, there becomes a new potential within The\nVoid that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like an arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the\npotential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that keeps it sacredly linked to once again become what the Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a ceramic teapot will not become a crude clay but remains a teapot).\nTo Return Again\n\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the original entity is the only\nthing that maintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independent existence outside of The Void is made (I.e redoing the Creator’s work) will assign the potential\nwith its destined form. And the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\n\nGood Job,\nYou Meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Experimnts", "Rarat Delevoye", "experiment 1\nI tryed to see what would happen to a compass that was put under heavy magical stress, it resulted in the compass, to point towards the source of magic rather then north, could this mean the void is a mass of its own?\n\nexperiment sucsess\nexperiment 6.2\nTryed to see if potions had a effect on plants (realized first potion was poision) i first mixed crops with stone skin potions. it resulted in that the plant grew at a slowed pace but the plant seemed extremely healthy.\n\nexperiment 6.2 wip\nexperiment 19\ntryed to mix enchanted metals toghether in hopes of getting better weapons,\nthis resulted in the metal to seem to be weaker than a normal enchanted weapon\nas if the magic was sapped from the weapon.\n\nexperiment 19 fail\nexperiment 21.6\ntryed to mix fire with thamitic dust. did not do much, the dust burned but the fire sparkeled.\n\nexperiment 21.6 i dont even know what to label this. \n\nthamitic candles seem to be a good idea.\nexperiment 246:64:56739\nok, this was a acident, i fond a gem that seemed to glow with magic so i tested it with experiment 1 and it show signs of magical stress. i droped the gem in slime by acident and now the slime thing seems to have a mind of its,\nown, it can not talk but it takes the form of a humaniod. (and it wont leave me alone)\n\nexpreiment break through", ""),
        StaticBook("Eye Transplant", "Laurinia", "12th of The Amber Cold 1479\n\nI was walking down the stone road when i was approached by a man in long dark robes. He said he had watched me care for my blind partner Sarai and asked if i was interested in learning how to heal people.\nOf course i agree'd with him and so now i am in his office learning how to recconect nerves. Specifically i am learning to recconect nerves in the eyes.\nMy teacher constantly has his hood up not once yet have i seen his face. However i presume he is an\nelf as we practice on nature, animals, and he has two small points in his hood.\n\n11th Malins Welcome\n We've been going over simple things for a few days now... I can now confidently heal nerve endings back into a working condition.. All we need now are a\npair of eyes for Sarai, its just finding a volunteer\n\n7th First Seed 1480\nLast night we attacked our target.. A middle aged women in which we stole the eyes of... Eyes which will now haunt me for the rest of my life.. .The vibrant blue colour of them\nstick with me and haunts me at night but they are soon to be my wifes. I guess over time ill adjust to them.\n\n13th First seed\nSarai can see it was a success", ""),
        StaticBook("F.T Part One", "Adniel", "Frozen Tears\n\n        Prologue\n\n\"Who am I?\" The words of a woman could be heard ontop an icy mountain, Grey ashen skin and snow white hair defining her appearance. \"How did I get here?\" She said outloud to the frozen wasteland around-\nher, small cold tears begining to roll down her cheeks. \"Why did this have to. . .\" As the words escaped her lips, the tears continued to fall before becoming one with her icy grey skin. Her figure fell forwards to lay upon the snowy ground.\nChapter one\n\nA small table rests inside a wooden made home, the floor boards a mahogany while the walls made of oak, the roof was rather close to the seated's heads. A female Mali'aheral with blonde hair and blue eyes sits at the table along with-\nher friend, a 6'6\" tall Mali'ame with black hair and brown eyes. \"So how are you today, Lux?\" Spoke the tall Mali'ame with a rather deep tone. \"Oh, I'm fine.\" She replies with her head burried in her arms, long golden curls covering parts of her eyes as-\nlayed ontop the wooden table, eyes shut. \"You seem upset, llir.\" The Mali'ame said with crossed arms ontop the table, his figure leaned forward in his seat. \"Oh, Its really nothing.\" Lux replied with an short dismissive wave of her hand. \"You don't need-\nTo be concerned over my problems, Kaeghan.\" Kaeghan then looked over to Lux with a tilted head, a sigh escaping his lips. \"I'm concerned because I care about you, Lux.\" He said with a blush, his head averting it's gaze from her. Lux raised her head to -\ntake veiw of Kaeghan, her brow raised \"Because you're my friend, right?\" She questioned while her eyes wander up and down his visage. \"Yes, so please. . . Tell me what's on your mind.\" He replied with an assuring nod to Lux. Lux hummed in thought before-\nresting her head onto her arms once again.\n\"I've been thinking that I would like to learn an Arcane art, however everytime I ask someone to teach me. . . They decline.\" She replies as her eyes close ontop her head, blonde hair resting on the table.\n\"I see. . . I could help you with that? I mean. . . I know someone who wants an apprentice.\" Kaeghan says in response to Lux, a wicked grin forming at his lips. \"Is that so?\"\nShe brings her full attention onto Kaeghan, quickly sitting up in her seat.\n\"Indeed, you may have to pass a few trails however.\" He replies with another nod. \"A little price to pay for my dream.\" She says with a hint of exicitement in her tone. She quickly then raised onto her feet \"Let's go meet them.\" She then adds. Kaeghan-\nHimself raised onto his feet with a smile, hands resting ontop the table \"Now?\" He said \"Indeed.\" She replies with a fire in her eyes. \"Alright. . . After you.\" He said before making his way to the door along with her and moving to the outdoors.\nChapter two\n\nAs the two ventured out into the world, Kaeghan sent a bird out with a letter. A reply came shortly after and the two left. They traveled far out into the world, past snow and sand untill they came upon a small shack in the middle-\nof the jungle. Kaeghan moved towards the door, slamming his metal fist agaisnt the door frame. After a short moment the two were met by the creeking of the wooden door, as it opened they saw a tall woman dressed in a long brown cloak that covered most of\nher facial features. The woman looked towards Kaeghan firstly before drifting her gaze onto Lux. An old sounding voice emiting from the cloak \"Who's this one Kaeghan?\" Lux raised a brow as she spoke. Kaeghan had a small smile on his face \"Lux, she wants-\nto learn a magical art.\" Kaeghan said. Lux's eyes widened, raising her hands up to shake a bit about \"I mean if thats alright. . .\" She spoke hesitently. The cloaked woman simply nodded before speaking again \"Are you prepared to perform my tasks for this-\nart, girl?\" Lux nodded once, speaking out confidently \"I am.\" With another nod by the cloaked woman a task was granted \"Bring me the flesh of a male.\" Lux looked baffled however simply gave another nod \"I'll do it.\" She said. Kaeghan granted her a grin.\nWithout another word the two began to journey back to their village in which back at Lux's household they planned and gathered weapons for their villainous task.\nChapter Three\n\nLux was stationed at an allyway within the village, devoid of light. A knife placed in her hand she awaited the sound of footsteps. After a few short moments the sound of footsteps can be heard \"She's right over here, please help\nher dying soul.\" The voice of Kaeghan resonated from the enclosed allyway. Shortly two figures appeared around the corner of the allyway, swiftly Lux arose her dagger and slammed it down upon the unexpecting victim. Sending him to the floor.\nKaeghan granted Lux a quick nod as his guantleted arm reached to the downed man, placing him upon his shoulder. \"Good job.\" He told Lux, she then quickly put her dagger back into her pocket. Her hand shaking faintly.  \"Thank you.\" She replied hesitently.\nKaeghan then began to move off with Lux through the city in a silent manner. Bringing themselves back to the one who granted such a task. Kaeghan sent his metal guantlet onto the wooden door. After a long moment of time the wooden door creeps itself open-\nrevealing the brown cloaked woman. Her hand outstrecthed as a finger pointed to the body then to the flooring. Kaeghan lowered the male onto the flooring as requested. The cloaked woman then gestured for Lux to enter within the household.\nLux's expression swiftly changed to one of slight fear and confusion before she took a hesitent step forwards. After a moment she then took another step, continuing the patternized movements untill she brought herself inside the home.\nWithin the house beared wooden walls and flooring, parts of the two covered in various scratch markings. Inside Lux's line of sight was a large dinning table, small ammounts of dried blood laying upon the table's top. As a detached head of a human male-\nSeen on a plate resting on the table.\n\"Whats all this?!\" Lux screamed out in fright, a finger swiftly pointing to the blood and head ontop the table. The woman released a cackle into the air as two words were emited by Kaeghan's lips \"I'm sorry.\" And -\nWith that, Lux felt a hard pain at the back of her head, her vision fading before she fell upon the flooring, unconcious.\nChapter Four\n\n\nWhen Lux came too, her body felt unnaturaly cold. She found herself ontop a snowy mountain top. Snow fell from the skies harshly in the form of a blizzard agaisnt her now greyish skin.\nLux began to mutter to herself \"Where am I?\" She spoke as a tear began to flow down her cheek, strangly turning itself into slush as it made contact with it. \"Kaeghan, where is he?\" She then muttered, her head scaning the area about her only to find-\nA tall woman with snow white hair that reached down to her knees. Adorned with a elegant blue dress and similar greyish skin. She looked down to Lux with a pitiful expression, her hand reaching out as in support to the downed frost witch. \"Can you stand-\nSister?\" The witch rasped to Lux. Lux quickly let out a yell, anger in her tone \"What happend to Kaeghan?!\" She demanded such an answer. The witch took a pause before speaking out \"Kaeghan is no longer your friend, he betrayed you. . . Like all men shall\"\nLux looked completely baffled, her fingers curling into a fist at her side \"What do you mean?\" The witch released a visable yawn into the air \"Kaeghan knocked you out, turned you into this.\" She then arose a hand in gesture to Lux.\nLux then raised her arm into the air, glancing upon the grey and icy skin she quickly let out a frightened yelp. Slaming her arm agaisnt the ground \"What did you do to me?!\" She screamed. The witched then replied \"I've granted your wish. Gave you-\nAnd art, a family.\" Lux continued to scream back at the witch, deep down she could feel a burning sensation in her chest \"I demand answers! What art?!!\" She yelled \"You're a frost witch now and I'm your mother.\" The witch replied, exposing her icy skin to\nLux. \"A frost witch?\" Lux spoke out, her expression now filled with fear. \"I'm sure you'll find the answers you seek soon my child.\" The witch spoke \"If you wish for them, I suggest you take up a disguise and get them from Kaeghan.\" Lux looked confused-\nShe let out a huff. \"Disguises?\" She questioned, raising a brow. \"I shall teach you to take up the appearance of any women you wish.\" Lux simply nodded once, her hand slamming agaisnt the snowy ground once again.\nLux then slowly raised herself onto her feet, glancing to the witch quizzically \"Tell me your name.\" She said. The witch took a icy breath before speaking out hesitently in response \"Tieve.\" Lux nodded once, muttering the name to herself \"Tieve, Tieve.\"\nTieve then began to make her way along the icy mountain, her hand raising upwards in gesture for Lux to follow. Lux did just that, brining her feet forwards along the snow which now uneffected her icy skin after Tieve. Her quest for answers had begun.\nChapter Five.\n\nLux stood tall within the icy cave, her figure shimmering momentarly before her appearance changed to that of a Mali'ame with long flowing black hair. Her facial features defining beauty to most. Her lips formed a bright smile as she-\nGlanced to Tieve. Tieve arose her hands up into the sky before clasping them together into a slow clap. She then began to speak out \"Congratulations, now that you've disguised yourself, you may now gain answers from Kaeghan.\" Lux's smile quickly faded-\nPlacing a rather solemn expression onto her visage. \"How am I to gain answers from him though?\" She questioned, placing a frown onto her lips. Tieve then responded with \"Become his lover. . . You know well enough the man is a sucker for love.\"\nLux looked baffled but nodded her head \"Its our way right? Placing men in a wrong sense of secruity for our own wishes.\" Tieve frowned at Lux's comment but simply noded once. Lux then without another word made her way towards the town that began it all.\nAs Lux arived at the town she and Kaeghan grew up at, she looked about the city. Only to find Kaeghan no where in sight. She checked his favorate places to be. The castle which laid no results, the town square which laid no results and finally the tavern-\nWhich surprising laid results. There she found Kaeghan sitting by himself with a mug of ale upon the table he was stationed at. She took in a deep breath before making her way to the table and speaking out \"Arn't you lonely sitting alone?\"\nKaeghan glanced up from his seat towards Lux \"I may be, are you here to provide company?\" Lux simply nodded hesitently gesturing to the seat \"If I may?\" Kaeghan simply nodded once. Lux then without a word lowered herself into the seat across from him.\n\"So, what's your name?\" Lux questioned. Kaeghan then replied \"Its Kaeghan, may I ask your own?\" Lux hesitated before making a name upon the spot \"Call me, Evie.\" Kaeghan took a swig of his ale \"As you wish, Evie.\" He said.\n\"Drinking for any reason in particular?\" She questioned, raising a brow. Kaeghan then released a deep sigh \"A friend of mine has went through rough times I'm sure. . . You could say I'm worried.\" Lux formed a fist at her side which was unoticable to him.\n\"Is that so? What happend?\" Lux pretended with all her might to sound concerned. \"I'll have to tell you another time, Evie.\" Kaeghan said as he raised from his seat, finishing the rest of his ale \"I'll be here tomorrow, come see me then.\" He then began-\nTo depart the tavern, granting Lux a quick wave of his hand. Lux simply returned the wave before picking herself up and muttering \"Answers will soon be found.\" She then without a word began to exit the tavern and make her way out of the city.\nLux arived at the icy cave, slowly laying herself into her bed before begining to sleep. A dream of her and Kaeghan sitting in a grassland filled her thoughts, her and him staring into the sunset as Kaeghan whispered to Lux \"I love you.\" And with that-\nShe awoke.\n\n\n\n\n\nSadly due to a lack of pages, I shall be cutting this book short. The next installment of Frozen tears will be brought out soon dear readers.", ""),
        StaticBook("F.T Part Two", "Adniel", "Frozen Tears\n\n       Volume Two\n\n\n\"Not all tales end happy, not all tales end complete. Tales but end with the thoughts of the reader.\" - Adniel\nChapter Six\n\nLux was stationed within the tavern as instructed by Kaeghan. She had her attention directly upon the doorway, awaiting his entry. To her it felt as if many months or hours have passed untill she could hear the rattling of metal.\nKaeghan entered the Tavern and brought himself to the bartender \"Two ales, Please.\" He spoke out. After a moment he took his order and brought it to Lux's table. Sitting himself down across her. \"Greetings.\" She spoke up to him as he sat. \"Hello.\" He-\nReturned the greeting, offering the ale to her. Lux hesitently reached out towards the mug before taking a sip from it. \"Thank you.\" She replied. \"You didn't have to though.\" Kaeghan raised a brow at her comment \"I made you wait however.\"\n\"I didn't wait long, though.\" Lux retorted. Kaeghan simply released a sigh at that \"I already bought it for you, just take it.\" Lux nodded once, reaching to her mug to take another sip. \"Thank you.\" She repeated once again. Kaeghan nodded once.\n\"Do you enjoy the taste?\" He questioned. \"I do not drink often, it's alright however.\" She replied assuringly, taking another sip of the ale. Kaeghan then took a sip himself, his expression changing to become more solemn \"So you wished to learn of my -\nSituation?\" He then said, his eyes wandering up and down her frame, as if testing her. Lux quickly brought her visage to one more serious, she nodded quickly \"I do, if I may learn.\" Kaeghan then released a sigh, placing his hand ontop the table.\n\"My friend by the name of Lux, I betrayed her. . . Sold her to some slaver.\" His fingers quickly clasped a fist as he spoke, his expression changing to one of slight anger. Lux's eyes widened a bit, faking her shock \"I'm. . . Sorry to hear that. But why-\nDid you do it?\" She then questioned \"A witch had my brother captive. She promised me if I brought her a female willing to learn magic. She would release him.\" His eyes watered a bit, his fist gently slamming upon the table. \"And the result?\" Lux\nQuestioned further. \"He died, the man was killed by the witch. Eaten probably.\" Lux's eyes widened at that, a look of shock on her face \"I see. . . I'm honestly sorry to hear that.\" Kaeghan took in a deep breath before his features relaxed themselves.\n\"It's alright, I-I just wish I could see my friend again, however.\" Lux then replied with \"Why is that? I mean you betrayed her, yet you wish to see her again?\" Kaeghan raised his gaze to lock his eyes with Lux \"Truthfully it's because I loved her.\"\nLux then raised her brow, her shock and suprised features growing. \"Thats. . . Honestly a shame then. I'm sorry.\" Kaeghan arose his hand in gesture to stop \"Please, it's not your fault. Keep your thanks.\" Lux then nodded once \"As you wish.\"\nKaeghan emited another sigh to that before raising from his seat \"I must get going.\" He said. \"Wait a moment.\" Lux halted him with a raised hand. \"I know I can never replace your old friend, however. . .\" She hesitetated for a moment, she still had some-\nHate towards Kaeghan for his actions. However at the same time his story made her feel slight sympathy. \"Perhaps I can be your new companion?\" She finshed. Kaeghan arose a brow at that before he simply nodded \". . You may, however it may-\nBe somewhat dangerous. I'm a mercenary and there are those that wish to hunt me.\" Lux shook her head a moment \"I can handle myself. Don't worry.\" Kaeghan nodded again, a slight smile painting his lips \"Very well, I'll see you here tomorrow.\" And with that\nHe was off, leaving the tavern. Lux pursed her lips, shaking her head a bit. \"Hm.\" She mumered, simply pondering.\nChapter Seven\n\nA day had past since Lux offered her new appearance to replace herself as Kaeghan's friend. She sat in the tavern once again awaiting the sound of clanking metal, footsteps. After a long period of time, he finally entered the stage\nKaeghan entered within the Tavern, however he was wearing that of a green coat and black pants. He made his way over to Lux, his fingers tapping agaisnt the sacthel to his side. \"Karin'ayla.\" He spoke out. \"Karin'ayla.\" She returned the greating.\n\"How are you today?\" He then questioned. \"I'm fine, yourself?\" Lux responded \"Fine.\" He said \"So, where would you like to go today?\" Lux brought her finger to her chin, as if pondering the answer she would grant. \"Perhaps the Caliphate?\" She replied.\nKaeghan nodded his head, fingers curling about the hilt of his sword loosely. \"Very well, after you then.\" Lux slowly raised from her seat before making her way to the exit. Kaeghan followed suit as they made their way to the Caliphate.\nAs they arived upon the roads, they were meeted by two shady men, one in armor. The other in leather. One of the men spoke out to the two \"Well, what do we got here?\" Kaeghan quickly adorned a catious look. The leather atired man steped unconfortably -\nCloser to Lux, only to be stopped by Kaeghan. Lux arose a brow, seeming somewhat frightened by the display. \"Looks like we got a rough one here.\" The armored man then unsheathed his blade before stepping forwards to Kaeghan. Kaeghan quickly unsheathed his\nOwn longsword before slashing it towards the armored man. Their swords clashed with an audibe metalic sound. The leather man then rushed forwards towards Lux before grabing her thin shoulder and brining her towards the ground.\nLux opened her maw before sending her shark like teeth into the man's shoulder, his eyes widened, letting out a scream in pain. Kaeghan winced at the scream before he took a step forwards, slashing his blade full force upwards to the man's hilt and -\nSending his sword flying into the air. The armored man's eyes widened before he began to run away. Kaeghan allowed it, drawing his attention quickly towards Lux and the downed man before raising his blade into the air to send it towards the back of his-\nNeck. Lux released her grasp on the man as Kaeghan turned. The leathered armored men then raised his fist into the air to slam into Lux's face, only to be then halted by Kaeghan's sword into his neck. His corpse sliding off Lux to the side with a pull-\nfrom Kaeghan's blade. Kaeghan then sheathed the bloody blade. His arm extended to Lux, offering her a hand \"Are you alright.\" Lux took his hand hesitently before raising onto her feet with his help \"I-I'm fine.\" She said, licking her lips quickly to-\nRemove the small specks of blood that lay upon it. Kaeghan then placed his hand upon her shoulder, his visage relaxing \"I'm glad.\" Lux then formed a light smile, her hand slowly brining itself to his cheek. \"Thank you, you saved me.\" She said before she-\nBrought her head closer to his to peck at his cheek. Kaeghan raised a brow at this as she retracted. He then spoke out, somewhat entraced \"What might that have been for?\" He questioned. \"Because you saved me.\" She replied.\n\"I see, well. . . It was really nothing.\" He replied. \"Oh, but you still protected me.\" She said once again, granting him another peck. Kaeghan simply smiled at that, nodding once. \"Very well, shall we continue to the Caliphate then?\" He said and Lux-\nNodded. The two then made their way to the Caliphate, checking out the bookstore and speaking to commoners before making their ways home for the next day.\nChapter Eight\n\nLux was sat in the tavern once again awaiting for Kaeghan's arival. Once again a long period of time passed untill Kaeghan finally arived. Kaeghan brought himself to Lux before speaking out to her \"Come along, today I have a -\nPlace in mind for us to go.\" Lux raised a brow before standing herself up \"Where are we going?\" She questioned. \"You'll see.\" He responded before exiting the tavern alongside her. The duo made their way past a series of trees untill they reached a biome-\nOf various colored flowers and plants, flowers the size of buildings scattered the area around them, color painting the entire landscape like a paradise. Lux's eyes widened at the sight, her maw opening in surprise. \"This is beautifull!\" She chirped out.\n\"I'm glad you like it.\" Kaeghan replied with a light chuckle. \"When did you have time to find this?\" She questioned, still taking in the pure beauty of the area. \"I found it on my own free time during my travels.\" He said \"I was unaware you explored.\" She\nReplied with a booming simle, her figure turning to face Kaeghan. \"Well I find exploring eases the nerves, gives time to think.\" Lux nodded to his words, her hands folding behind her back. \"So, yesterday you were pretty brave.\" She faked a giggle.\n\"Brave? I guess so.\" He responded with a chuckle of his own. \"Brave enough to earn a kiss.\" He then adds. Lux's cheeks tinged a mild red at his comment, she moved forth closer to him \"Well. . . You saved me.\" She said. \"Does saving deserve a kiss?\" He\nQuestioned with a raised brow. \"Yes, it does.\" She said assuringly, nodding once. \"Hm, interesting.\" He said, his eyes wandering up and down Lux's figure. \"What is it?\" She questioned. \"Well you see, perhaps I'll have to save women more often in that-\nCase.\" He said jokingly. Lux huffed, her smile faultering \"Men, such pigs.\" \"Pigs?\" He then said. \"To save women just to get a kiss?\" She replied. \"I was merely jesting.\" He then said, releasing a bit of laughter into the air. \"However. . .\" He slowly-\nLeaned his head closer to Lux's, pressing his forehead to her's. \"If it is for your kisses, I wouldn't mind protecting you.\" Lux raised a brow at this, her cheeks tinging red once again as she playfully pushed agaisnt his chest \"Oh please.\"\n\"It's the truth, I've never met someone like you before. . . I'd die for your kisses.\" He said, his lips pressing agaisnt her's. Lux's eyes widened, her hands roughly pushing agaisnt his body \"What are you doing?!\" She called out. \"Is there a problem?\"\nHe questioned as he was pushed back. \"Yes-\" She hesitated, this was the chance she wanted, so why did it feel wrong to her? \"No. . .\" She then said. \"In which case. . .\" He once again leaned his head forewards, only to be halted by her pushing again. She-\nThen turned around sharply before running off in fright and shock. Kaeghan stood there dumbfounded at her actions, his lips forming a large frown.\nChapter Nine\n\nLux ran towards the frosty mountains before she met Tieve once again, her hand clutching at her stomach as a month past since the scene with Kaeghan. Tieve made her way to Lux, placing a hand on her shoulder \"You need to eat.\"\nLux simply shook her head violently, slushy tears falling down her eyes. \"If you don't eat you'll die.\" She then exclaimed only to have Lux shake her head once again. \"You'll never see Kaeghan again.\" And with those words Lux's eyes widened, she quickly-\nBrought herself to her feet before moving off to find some food, wiping the slush tears from her icy-grey visage. Kaeghan was at the guard's barracks awaiting orders from his instructor. As the instructor made his way to Kaeghan a loud scream came from-\nOutside before a soldier rushed through the door, blood covering his shoulder. \"Help!! A frost witch is attacking in the forest!\" He yelled out. Kaeghan quickly drew his sword, anger painting his facial features \"Take me there, now.\" He snaped and the two\nWere off. As Kaeghan arived at the crime scene, he could see the face of the corpsed soldier being ripped apart by shark teeth. An icy figure sitting ontop it with her back turned to Kaeghan. Kaeghan released a loud growl in anger as he charged forwards-\nTo the frost witch, he thrusted his blade forwards into her back. Icy water and blood quickly rushed from the wound as the witch fell to the ground with a screech, her head turning to veiw Kaeghan with a loud \"Nooo!\" Kaeghan swiftly took out his blade-\nFrom the witches' back before slashing wildly at her, cuts littering her figure as she fell to the ground moitionless in a pile of water and red slush. Kaeghan then sheathed his blade before taking a glance to the dead witch. Lux layed dead, her tale over", ""),
        StaticBook("Fables V2", "Anawkin", "The Robber's Joy\n\nOnce upon a time, there was a band of robbers who divided their loot according to their different ranks. Among the belongings, there was a Benares Kambala, a color of which left much to be desired.\nIt was considered as an inferior part to be given to one of the robbers of the lowest rank. The robber got angry and made a strong protest to the rest.\n\nAfterwards, he brought it to the city for sale.\nAn honorable elderly man paid him a high price. He ended up getting more money than any other robber in the band. He leaped for joy.\n\nThe Female Monkey\n\nOnce upon a time, there was a female monkey with a handful of beans,\nAfter dropping to the ground a grain of bean, she dropped all the beans in her hands by looking for the first one. All the beans were eaten by chicken and ducks before long.\n\nIf you wish to know the true meaning of either fable, speak to Orias.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fairy Ring", "Kyral Rilann", "The following is from myself, Kyral, and my time spent meditating in a fairy circle.\n\nThese are the three days of this task.\nDay one\n\nSitting  in the tree when the all familiar humming noises filled my senses, it felt overwhelming, but I tried and tried to stay in as long as I could, focusing on the humming for as long as I could. Was I incomfortable? or\nwas it just the noise getting to me? At least this was my first time in, I had plenty of time to get used to such noises.\n\nI figure it will be easier the more I go in, but I need to pace myself, I feel a woman could go a little crazy if left inside that\nFairy ring for far too long. Did I mention it was hard resisting the urge to dance? I never dance and I felt myself wanting to do it more and more.\n\nI don't like dancing.\nDay two\n\nI easily entered the circle, finding it much easier then the last to meditate with my eyes closed. It was more amazing to focus in the humming I heard with my other senses, a whole new experience that left me more amazed at\nthis mystical ring, I can't comprehend the things I heard, but I think its the forest.. doing something.\n\nAs for leaving the circle, I left with only slight issues, having to get back in for this book, but I looked around the whole grove for signs of\npeople, and I skipped around the fairy circle.\n\nIt was amazing I felt, relieved. I hated to dance but it was just skipping, and I felt so much better.\nDay three\n\nThis day was one of the more amazing, I meditated after having had a long talk with one of my former Scions, talking about what I did and redemption. Having been calmed by that chat, I walked back into the fairy ring.\nI was not ready and i did not expect to hear what I did. It was like the Pulse of the realm was guiding itself to me, I felt everything moving and coming towards me, Meditating was hard, but i managed to keep it going, remembering my times as a Cleric and\nMage to keep me going, to focus on one of those feelings, one of those pulses of life.\n\nI almost did it, but I felt my thoughts filling my mind with crazy reasoning, and I needed to get out. This wasn't a safe day to be inside the circle. I feel that I am\ngetting closer to understanding the way the realm works, but I might be wrong, this Fairy circle continues to bring new and new things to me to realize, that the realm is forever changing.\n\nI skipped around the circle again, and stopped it at that.\nThis would be my final day, but I expect to be asked to meditate here from time to time.\n\n*The following pages\nseem to be sketches slid into the book*\n*A large Rainbow tree seems to be cut by a figure in this one, the top half of this page\ndepicts this.\n\nWhile the lower half depicts the tree igniting, leaving scrambled markings on the ground /#&!(@/ *\n*Another sketch seems to be the apple, blue in color being picked from the still standing rainbow tree, a hand extending to it as if this was a panel by panel sketch. but it stops there.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Fairy Ring", "[Dedicant] Heroxis", "Fairy Ring\n\nby Heroxis\nSearching the night.\nNight quietly green.\nDeep in the forest.\nNo one has seen.\nThe circle of fungi.\nI enter you now.\nA force I sense.\nGreeting with a bow.\nTo sing in the rain.\nTo write in the sun.\nTo draw in the clouds.\nAttuned as one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fairy's/Pixies", "kido122", "On Fairy's and Pixies\n     The Difference\n\n       By Sam King\nFairy's:\n\n To start we shall discuss the better known of the two, Fairy's, or sprites as they are also called. Fairy's are described as no taller and no smaller then 1 inch in height, with a wingpspand of 1 -1/2 inches. Often said to\nbe of fair skin, glowing a dom yellow and often mistaking as a firefly. They are said to dress in leaves of varieing color and design. What is most odd is that they are said to all be female, never has their been told of a male fairy, so how or if they\nhave children is unkown. Now to move on, fairy's are often very, very kind, and are seen as bringers of good luck, a good omen if you will. Keeping places neat and tidy, finding \"Missing\" things and returning them, as well as allow small sparks of\ninspiration, like small, mini, muses(Discused in another book). Fairy's are said to hail from \"Fairy Rings\", circles of varieing mushrooms, in varieing sizes. It is said that when one steps into a fairy ring, one can see the fairy's \"world\", what that is,\nis unkown, This is also were fairy's become \"mean\", as ounce one steps into a \"fairy ring\", one cannot leave it on their own accord. They will remain standing in the ring, in a odd daze, until one either dies of age, thirst, or starvation, or if someone\ncomes and breaks the \"fairy ring\", which is less then likely as they are said to be only found in the most remote parts of the forests. It is good to note, that not all circles of mushrooms are \"Fairy Rings\", as people often plant muchrooms in this way to\none encourage fairy's to come to that area, as it is said that they often fall to this trickery, thinking that it is their actual \"fairy ring\", and two to keep the legends of fairy's living. (Turn the page for Pixies)\nPixies:\n\n Pixies, often confused as fairy's, are very similar to fairy's. They are of equal size and wingspand, fair skin and glow as well, though in a more blue tint. The only real differnce in appearence is the wear dead leaves\nunlike fairy's, who wear fresh leaves. Pixies are here on out, quite the opposite of fairy's, as they are very troublesome. They often enjoy \"borrowing\" anything and everything, often the blame for anything lost. Pixies also enjoying \"stealing\"\ninspiration from others, for themselves. Pixies are said to be both male and female, and where they hail from is unknow and only seem to show up when someone, some where, is in a bad mood, so it is safe to assume they are always present.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of Aegis", "Monk Scribe", "Fall of Aegis\n\nThe miasma in the north lingered ever more so. Galahar was evacuated and the cloud temple became our final stand. From the temple I shouted out into the crowds, summoning those who where chosen by the Nations as their champions.\nUpon arriving to Laurelin, I called all of the champions into Dawns Bakery, where a secret entrance lay.\n\nThe High Priestess handed out blessed armor pierced, enchanted in Aeriel's grace. To each of the champions. We then took a small passage,\ninto what was once the Laurelin Gauntlet. Entombed in a massive oak tree, lay Vardak's portal from the nether. \n\nThe champions gaze into the portal and grip the hilts of their weapons tightly. \n\nI step out of the way\nof the portal, clench my soulstone in my hand tightly and wish them good luck. As I vanish the brave few enter head first. \n\n- Spoken by Native in the Elf in the Deep Cold, 1351.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of KalAgnar", "Fimlin Grandaxe", "The Battle of\n        Kal'Agnar\n\n\n  by Fimlin Grandaxe\nA lone figure stood above the ranks, atop a balcony that loomed over all who were below. The armies of Urguan, Krug, Horen, and Malin scrambled about the main hall hurting to their posts.\nwarhorns blew from the south, signaling an invasion coming from the Shroom District. A deep, commanding voice emitted from the figure atop the balcony, ordering the soldiers into position, and warhorns from Kal'Agnar sounded in response.\nPlans had been leaked, screams and cries were heard as the flanking force was slaughtered, disobeying the orders to pull back. The Inner City of Kal'Agnar was all that was left to hold against the onslaught of the undead horde.\nMonsters poured past the main gate only to be quickly shot down by the many archers stationed above, was this all they had to offer? No it was not, for the Grand King had suspected that the horde would come from a more obsolete location.\nHaving suspected it being from a back entrance it was sealed up, as was every open window, except one. Though the window looking out from the mountain had a way of self-sealing, it was no match for the explosives set by the undead horde.\nWith a load BANG and a crash the window was blasted open, in suit followed an unstoppable horde of Khorvadic minions, instantly taking over the King's Quarters.\nIn vain the armies fought to keep them from pushing further, for they had control of the doors and gates within the quarters. A flank force was sent through a secret passage into one of the King's Guard rooms, and they charged out in a whirl of fury.\nIt was not enough however and the flank force was suppressed and routed, and ever so slowly the armies were pushed back.\nIt was here, where the ultimate downfall became of The sons of Urguan. As they slowly backed away from the plague and monsters that the cultists spat out they had split apart.\nPart of the defending force went down the stairs towards the throne room, while the rest split up in the upper and lower battlements. The undead, by now had taken over the Hall of Kings, and with no passages from\neach side of the battlement to another, the army grew weaker. The division between them had not allowed a proper charge, and they could only move out for a few minutes before being forced to retreat.\nDefeat became evident, one battlement by another they each fell, one, by one. Suddenly a group of five soldiers, accompanied by the Grand King Fimlin Grandaxe and the Annilir of Laureh'lin Phaedrus, found themselves cornered.\nHowever after searching for whatever exit there could possibly be it was found that in the back half of the battlement was a passageway to the other side. Quickly the group charged for the other side of the battlements and slew all resistance within.\nThis victory did not last long, the cultists above siezed the oppurtunity and blasted spells at those below, scattering them and forcing their retreat.\nThe Sons of Urguan had failed to\nhold their city against the onslaught of Khorvad, and the Ironborn clan.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of Ondnarch", "Fimlin Grandaxe", "The dwarves furious in their anger and hatred twords Ondnarch had defeated his four Shallmadrils and were marching to war upon his lair. They stopped at Kal'Urir and descended into the deeproads in which a glowing blue\ncrystal was found. it looked like the Kal'Varak but it wasn't because it started humming and suddenly a wave  of minions erupted forth, only to be slain quickly. Later on another crystal was found, destroyed, and a third one was then found.\nThis time waves of firebeasts and skeletons came out and the dwarves fought on through a horde of evil, alas the crystal was destroyed when the mages of Urguan threw balls of flame at the crystal, shattering it.\nOnce it was destroyed a large shard broke through the nearby ice wall revealing the Kal'Azgoth entrance to the deeproads. The dwarves charged up and pushed the minions back to the palace gate where a ice morph pelted the dwarves with ice.\nHowever human and orc reinforcements came too help aswell and combined they charged and attacked the army of Ondnarch at full force.  However suddenly Igor Ireheart was missing and they looked until they found him in the throne room\nfacing down Ondnarch, mustering all his courage and strength he slams the Hammer of Barridin, Ondnarch's only weakness and slays him, becoming a Hero. However Ondnarch had some strength left\nand he summoned all of his remaining minions to attack Igor and the Dwarves that had just burst through into the room. Alas despite all his efforts Igor Ireheart was slain and through sorrow and rage the dwarves slew every last creature.\nIn the center of the room a large beam of white light shines burst into the air, revealing the now purified Wyrvun. And so The Dwarves march home mixed feelings of Victory and Sorrow they return home\nthe Bane of their race was now dead forever....", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of the Mori", "Thurak", "When the murders and attacks on the city occurred, many speculations arose within the city itself of whom was to blame and who should be slaughtered for such acts against their kind – many claimed it was the work of the surfacers,\nothers believed that such things were only possible by those living within the city.\nIt was declared and enforced that all living Mori were to return to the bosom of Nemiisae and remain within the sanctum of Menocress; behind these stragglers\nto return the horror unfolded, each path and passage that journeyed through only hours before could be heard crumbling under the weight of explosives. The people were brought each in turn to the Temple of the Mother to be cleansed of their\ntaint, the sickness of the surface that had infested them. The final act of the Valsharess and her Yathrins before the war broke out.\nMany that had broken loose from such rigid traditions fought against this cleansing and became\nquickly enraged, spitting in the faces of the priestess’ whom dared demand their obedience and silence. It was not long before two factions emerged; the devout and the rebels. Beneath the surface of the world, sealed off from the blinding\ndamnation of the sun’s light, the Caverns of Menocress’ streets were littered with crude barricades, strewn with the deceased and wounded – The once marvelled city now rots with death and destruction… crumbling under the civil war. Bathed in the Life\nBlood of their kith and kin, the rebellion breached the Yathrins’ sacred enclave; banners raised in revolt, their armour and bodies marked by their treason. Once considered mere common rabble; these denizens now slaughter blessed noble\nborn and their ilk standing guard at the doors of the Temple. From behind the sealed doors both rothe and Mori alike stand in the un-ease union against the threat of tait to its own city – this seeded by those\nturned to the hubris of their Ilharn Zanunder.\n\n~Rescribed by the Farseer Thurak’Braduk, 14th of the First Seed 1484.", ""),
        StaticBook("Farewell", "Allister", "[!]\nThe parchment you hold in your hand seems to be fresh, the ink on it's faces still holding moisture.\n\nTo Lopkaea, my one true love and equal.\nIf you're reading this then my death has surely come, sooner than I would have hoped..\nI write this not to say goodbye but to encourage you to live on, as I will in your heart. \nI am by no means a good man, I've had a hand in killing Dukes, Courtiers and maiming Princesses, not to mention adultery. Through this all you've breathed new\nlife into me, before we met I had mistresses, and as we grew more serious I cast them out from my bed and heart. There is truly no woman like you, and I envy the man who next steals your heart, for if I could just hold onto it for a moment longer I would\nrest in eternal peace. Please, make yourself happy, love again, have children. But never forget the love you and I shared. \nTruly yours, in life and death,\nAllister Ashes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Farewell", "Evelina Rovin", "Dear Athelstan,\n\nMy Creator, I thought that this never would happen.. I'm sorry, I absolutely am. Though the reason why I did this, was because of the constant stress, and depression that I've suffered from. I've never told you this, since I was terrified\nof you declining this marriage proposal. I'm Otto Rovin's bastard daughter. You were about to marry a bastard. I was humiliated by this title sticked upon my name, that I've carried with me my whole entire life. I didn't wanted to do this to you. I really\ndidn't. You deserve someone better, than a filthy bastard, that was a Rovin afterall. But Athelstan, do never forget me. Please, I beg you. I loved you. I really loved you, and I thank you for the most wonderful times you gave me. I was happy, and\ndelighted to be in your pressence. I was filled with joy when I heard your compliments, and the endless amounts of love you gave me. Thank you.\n\nI'm terribly sorry to do this, Athelstan. But I'm happier if I make this decision. I'll miss\nyou, and perhaps we see eachother again in the future.\n\nYour ex-fiancé, and your number one fan,\n\nLady Evelina Marie Rovin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Farewells.", "Steven Vega", "Dear Reader,\n\nThis is Steven. This is his resignation letter. I am happy for the time I spent with this crew, as it gave me a place to belong, good friends, and wonderful adventures. But the recent navy-like nature of the crew has made me rethink joining.\nFarewell,\n\n~Steven Vega\nDear Readers,\n\nLike Steven had stated before, this crew is no longer the, \"Dawnstride Voyagers.\" This is the Dawnstride Navy. When I joined the crew, I was promised:\n1. No uniforms\n2. Free to do whatever\n3. Not a military.\n4. Fun\n\nNow, at times #4 has been broken, due to the recent drama the crew has faced. But 2 of these promises have been broken. We now have required uniforms in order to occasionally sail, and are a military. I do not wish to serve in a\ngroup that works for Oren. I wish to be in a group that has the purpose of adventure, not pleasing nobles. Now, I am sorry to anyone who may be sad that I am leaving the crew. Trust me, I am sad too. But until the recent drama fades, and the militarizatio\nn, I will remain more.... Idle... Not participate, but still consider myself a Voyager.\n\n\nThank you for the amazing memories over these past years, I wish it could have lasted longer.\nSincerely,\n~Markus Birch.\nDear Reader,\n\nYes, like Steven and Mark, I too am resigning. With all the...events...that have been happening, I've become much more stressful and much more upset with what has become of the crew. When I joined, I was promised the following...\n1. When I joined, I didn't have to abandon my culture, my home, or my job.\n\n2. That I wouldn't join any military activities, only exploration\n\n3. Have fun, meet new people, and explore new places.\nNow, lately, I was forced to abandon my people and my culture in order to stay with my friends, whom I call, my family. I've also recently saw that the crew has become a navy. And lately, instead of having fun, I've become more stressed out, that being\nbecause the crew has been fighting with one another, sometimes even leading to physical violence, which I strongly dislike. Ever since I was a child, I've always disliked war and fighting. I am very sorry if this displeases the rest of the crew, but this\nis my choice. Though, I shall continue to explore on my free time. I just hope that one day, the Dawnstride Voyagers will become what it had once been, a very hard-working and very happy crew.\n\nSincerely,\n~Ariselle Aeraviel\nDear Reader,\nLike what every one else said I will be leaving too. I was promised Adventure and good times. Yes I did have those but now that we are a navy it just ins't the same. Who would want to fight? I liked how we all could have good times without\nWorring about polotics and whatnot. I wish you luck in your days of the Dawnstride Navy as it now is. Goodbye\n~Carver Ilianos\nDear my fellow Crew mates, \nSadly I have decided to depart from the voyagers. We had a fun run, great voyages but now...It's not the same anymore. I hope you all understand. \n\nSincerely\n\n~Alphar Ryce", ""),
        StaticBook("Faya's entrypass", "Vallel'Yuln Aeléyèlsa", "Faya is allowed inside the city by the responsibility of Eltilruir'Leyun, Vallel'Yuln Aeléyèlsa", ""),
        StaticBook("Fear", "Aerxuis", "Aspect Tome: Fear\nAuthor Unknown\nFear, another emotion that drives the Will of a man. This Book will describe all it can, for fear can not be a good thing for the Druids, not at all... The emotion of Fear is susceptible but can be very deceitful,\nit can drive people to do things they have no choice of doing, an example would be like this:\nImagine a man with the perfect life and perfect family, then a stranger says that all of it will be taken away in the blink of an eye if he does\nnot kill someone. Unless his Will is strong, this man can and will murder someone for the sake of his family, and the emotion that is currently driving him is the power of fear...\nIt is the easiest emotion to spot within yourself and another man, and too much fear can lead to insanity.\nThe Druid should try not to be seduced to the madness of fear.\nEverybody gets scared all the time, it is part of the nature of Life, but the dark side is that it can control you if you do not fight back.\nIn order to overcome fear, you must have Confidence and Willpower; then this darkness that lies within you shall disappear.\nBut Fear can never die, it is like a disease that can never be cured and a fire that will never be put out, remember this, my friends, and do not give in to it...", ""),
        StaticBook("Felsen Sky Whale", "liam_barnett", "   The Sky Whale of\n          Felsen      \n-------------------\n\n9th of The First Seed, 1569\n\nBell Sano\nProem: This is simply an eye witness account of the Sky Whale which made it's way over the skies of Felsen.\nSky Whales are generally regarded as being rare, but were originally discovered in Vailor. Due to their low population, little is known about their actual biological features.\nSimply, they're often described as being tranquil, passive creatures, seen feasting on flocks of birds as they float through the sky, may it be across a desert, ocean, or in this rare case, a city.\nPhysically, their under bellies are plain and white, while their skin is either some shady brown, or a variety of blues.\nAccount: Approaching Felsen, it'd be apparent that it was night, and it was stormy. However, upon entering the city, it'd also be obvious that some large object above the crowd of people would be blocking the rain.\nOf course, above us, a Sky Whale was suspended, hoovering at least one full mile off of the ground. It was as if the beast was shielding the people below from the rain, but it's unlikely that this was intentional.\nNauzican guards requested that both the Guards force of Felsen and the Corpsmen present attack it, and kill it, so many men withdrew their crossbows. However, as they fired, the beast seemed unaffected.\nObviously fed up with the offensive assault, the majestic creature turned on it’s side, presumably heading towards the imperial palace. It exposed it’s side, facing perpendicular to the street we were currently standing on.\nI could easily see that it held a deep, dark blue color, nearly black, in that respect. As it floated off, that was the last I saw of the whale, or any Sky Whale, for that matter, but this encounter was extremely important for academic and\nscientific purposes, and was crucial that I record my experience.\nAnalysis: I really only have two notes to make about the Sky Whales that aren’t already common knowledge, two observations I made.\nFirstly, the white, plain underside I mentioned, may have stronger and reinforced skin for the exact reason displayed during the encounter. Many enemies and hostile creatures would definitely launch an offensive assault\nfrom the ground, as they wouldn’t have any real means to get close to the beast. This forces it to develop a more reinforced, strong, and generally tougher underside, to prevent small projectiles from inflicting damage. \nThe second observation made is that, the whale appeared during what may as well have been the stormiest night of the decade. Roaring thunder storms, lightning, heavy rainfall -- This may have been soggy\nand generally wet enough for a Sky Whale to traverse through a densely populated urban area.\nBell Sano\n\n9th of the First Seed, 1569\n\nFelsen", ""),
        StaticBook("Felsen Times ED1", "The Orenian Printing Company", "The Felsen Times\n\nArthur Roswell - The man behind the title\n\nOn the 1st of the Grand Harvest, 1543, I was unfortunate enough to arrange a meeting with the Duke of Istria, Mighty Lord Roswell. He was dressed in his formal garments,  the poor\n§ § quality linen, most likely assembled within one of his various child labour factories, his poorly crafted golden embroidery being a reflection of his poorly crafted attitude towards life.\n\nFirstly, what is Roswell? A fungal disease one may find\ngrowing upon one’s foot? A type of hair cream? Yes, and much more.\n\nHe perched upon his stool like a constipated gentleman would do to the base of his privy. The first thing that struck me was his large ego, much larger than his four man levy.\nMuch to my dismay the phrase “Greetings, Mr Roswell.” was inadequate and did not meet his ever so pompous standards. I was corrected immediately, oh, what a fool that I am, for this is not the way one should address a mighty and powerful Duke.\nRoswell, is famed throughout Oren, for his unfaulted Governance of the Duchy of Istria. He has surely done the late Titus de Sola proud, turning Titus’ 40,000 man force  to a band of 40 psychedelic Elves with red eyes, lead by the much respected Jentos\nthe Great. \n\nArthur of the lesser House Roswell maintained his glorious reign by removing his brethren within his Duchy. House Falkenrath, a former Istrian family that had an Intelligence Quotient greater than that of a raw potato in a muddy puddle,\nwere forced out of power by His Grace, Mr Roswell. Mr Arthur Roswell would be incapable of leading a cabbage plantation, let alone one of the major provinces within our great Empire. His town smells of damp, the streets are littered with faeces\nand the inhabitants of the Roswellian stable would likely make more fitting rulers, assuming it was indeed inhabited in the first place.\n\n“A shower a day keep the Roswell away.” - Godfrey IV\nPablo’s Single’s Section\n\n“Dear Pablo, I, the Duke of Istria am having an intimate with one of my paige boys, Jentos Blackwood. I do not know how to tell my husband or how my family will react, especially since Jentos is infected with various\ndiseases\"-Anonymous\n\nDear Anonymous, I would suggest going to see the High Pontiff, to confess your sins. Sexual promiscuity and immorality have plagued our lands, as is so evident from your testimony. I hope that the Creator leads you from your dark\nand into his light\n\n§§[Insert Your Add Here]\n\nBreaking News\n\nAn Orenian Defeat: 12th of the Grandharvest 1543:\n\nThis week, a great battle ravaged at the Dwarven stronghold of Kal’ordholm. Unfortunately, the Dwarven forces repelled Imperial advances and\nmaintained control over their keep. The Duchy of Istria was a large let down for the Empire, rallying only 4 men, though, what can one expect from a man who likes the smell of his own urine? After a long and hardy battle, hours of siege bombardment and\nslow advances from the Imperial forces, Oren were forced back.\nFinance & Stocks\n\nIstrian Property Development: -23% MKT CPT (1350 Minas)\n\nNorth Orenian Company: -5% MKT CPT (2043 Minas)\n\nWycome Trading company: +1.6% MKT CPT (4320 Minas)\nCourlandic Trading Company: +32% MKT CPT (4533 Minas)\n\nDrusco Property Development: +41% MKT CPT (4300 Minas)\n\nOrenian Publishing Company: +63% MKT CPT (2400 Minas)\nAbout The Publishers\n\nThe Orenian Publishing Company was formed on the 12th of the Grandharvest 1543, by Otto von Habsburg.\n\nThe Company takes inspiration from the old Petrus Printing Press, owned by Jacob Chapel, in the\ntimes of Tuvya Carrion. Dedicated to bringing the citizens of Felsen and Oren fresh news, which they deserve.\nThe company headquarters is found at 2 Newport Boulevard. Vacancies are currently open, to apply please send a bird to Otto Von Habsburg or\nor visit the office. The Company is also dedicated to publishing books of any kind. From Novels, to guides and spell tomes.\n\nThis company supports Mylas for Mayor.\n\nTHE FIRST ISSUE OF THE FELSEN TIMES, BROUGHT TO YOU BY THE ORENIAN PUBLISHING COMPANY LTD.\n\nOPC Ltd readily welcomes articles from aspiring writers, for a chance to appear in the next issue, please send your article to the publishers. (Via forum PM)\nAdvertisements can be purchased, to find out more, contact the publishers. (Via forum PM)", ""),
        StaticBook("Feudal intro", "Annabella", "Feudalism is a grouping of legal and military customs, prevalent in Oren, and various other human nations. The purpose behind feudalism is to decentralize an empire which can no longer handle being in a small area.\nFeudalism is typicaly broken down into 7 ranks in an empire: Emperor, King, Duke, Count, Baron, military, and common folk. The emperor is the center of all feudalism, and can create and remove titles at his will\n(Note, a Tyrant emperor is likely going to have a rebellion on his hands if he adds or  removes too many titles.) A king has a Kingdom either within an Empire or independently, should he be independant his ability is the same as an emperors.\nOtherwise, he can adjust the titles of his direct vassals. A Duke may do the same as a dependant king, but with a much smaller group of vassals. A count typically runs a town and has a vast amount of land for what he pleases.\nIt is his job to make sure he has a military to supply his liege in case of an attack on the nation or area, and he will typically pay for loyality in minas or housing or both. Common folk live in the protection of the area, and exchange must pay their\nliege in either minas, or hte product they make.\nFeudalism loyality is hereditary and only works with Vallah because other races live too long for a proper system to work.\nAnother part of Feudalism to note is Clergy, although they are not a part of the system they have a strong influence on it because of the Vallah’s obsession with the deity known as ‘The Creator’ A High Pontiff is the person who crowns\nnew emperors and even has the ability to excommunicate them, making them disrespected among the Vallah", ""),
        StaticBook("fff", "Jory Redwyne", "oiiii", ""),
        StaticBook("Field Guide V.1", "Rilkor Niwarsay", "-------------------Field Guide to the\nImperium Army\n-------------------By: Rilkor Niwarsay\n((Arctic_Guard\n((Any concerns, contact me in game\n\nGuide to training\nRecruits or other\nSoldiers \n                   ---->\n-------------------- Chapter          1  -\n- What makes a       -\n- Good soldier       -\n-------------------There are many things that can be judged from a good soldier.\nDignity. Posture. Combat Skills. And most importantly the Quality standard soldier.\nIf ya wish to get anywhere in the Imperium, set a good\nexample of ya self, and act as a soldier should.\n\nThis means turning up to the standard of the best a soldier can preform. Forming bonds with others is key.\nThe Quality of a man judges what kind of a soldier he is. Make sure to straighten yourself out as much as possible, with your head held high to show you have dignity.\n\nCertainly showing good quality will show you are a good soldier.\nSo do that.    --->\n-------------------- Chapter  2          -\n- Simple Drills        -\n-------------------As a soldier you are expected to do drills.\nDuring drills showing good posture displays the quality of yourself and the army. This is important. Do not mess up.\n   --->\nYou will be expected to do these drills not just during intense training and formation demonstrations, but also out in the field. Wether it be traveling as a War Party, or a patrol. Your commanding officers, the Marshal, or even your superiors will\n----->\n-ask for you to display this as a group most likely, thus, if one messes up, you all mess up, and must suffer the pain as one. You do not question why or speak out unless spoken to. Failure to do so will result in disciplinary action.\n---------->\n-------------------- Chapter 3           -\n- The ABC's of the  -\n- Ranks and Your   -\n- Superiors           -\n------------------- Alright, so this Chapter, we're going to learn about who your Superiors are, and your position in the Imperium.\n--->\nFirst off, there is some what of a division between the Military, and the Nobility of Oren. Nobility will generally have more power over the military standard.\nLearning who what people are will help you a lot. \n\n------------>\nAt the top of the pyramid is the Emporer. Emporer Robert Chivay, of house Chivay. There are many different houses in Oren, with the Chivay's control firm of the throne.\nThen there is Empress Constance Chivay. They must both be shown the utmost respect. ->\nThe Emporer has his own personal guard.\nThey are considered superior to the Imperium Soldiers, for they are the finest.\nThere are, as I've said, other houses besides the Chivays, who also have members included within them.\n--->\nIn the Military, you have probably been put into one of two of the regiments of the Imperium. The First Regiment, consisting of burly front-line men, and the Second Regiment, consisting of the rest of the men who form the ranks, and carry out covert\n--->\n-missions. These men are considered to be more quick moving then the others. There are specifically chosen men who carry out the orders of these regiments, they are decurions. Not to be confused with Decanus. If ya be a footman, and require help, you --->\n-should report to them. They are your utmost importance, as they make or carry out the orders. These orders are given by most likely the Lord-Imperial Marshal. The Marshal will be leading the army into raids, or battles, and should be respected.\n-->\nBelow the Decurion, there is the Ensign, the Ensign doesn't have as much power as the Decurion, but can be seen as akin. They carry out the orders given by the Decurion.\nAs a footman, it is the bottom of the food chain, but very needed, for they are --->\n-the future soldiers of Orenia. And must be trained as such.\n*A diagram is shown*\nFootman < ManAtArms<\nRhoswenian < Lance\nDecanus < Decanus < QuarterMaster = Sergeant\n\nThat is a basic Diagram of the LOWER ranks.\nOnward ->\n-------------------- Chapter 4           -\n- Knowing People    -\n-------------------Getting to know as many people as you can will help you in the marathon. So do that. Form bonds with your human kins-man of the Imperium and of not. For you might find\n-->\n-Yourself in situations where you'd need help from your allies and such, this is why you make friends. Since when doesn't calling in your /home boys/ from the streets to help you kill bandit scum a crime? Never. Form strong bonds. You'll need em.\n-->\n-------------------- SECTION 2           -\n- COMBAT AND SUCH  -\n-------------------- Chapter 5           -\n- The Laws            -\n-------------------As being apart of the Imperium, you take an oath to server the Emporer, listen to your officers,\n-->\n-Fight for humanity and Oren, and uphold justice to the Humans. This means you will need to follow the laws, most of which are not to do anything daft. Conjurering, and magic is banned, this means druids and mages are outlaws. Also, Heretics should be -->\n-burned at the stake. ((Also follow the server's pvp rules, unless you want to get br'd and temp banned or perma banned))\nArresting without reason will result in penalties against you, such as de-ranking, or pyshical punishment. Killing enemies is ok. -->\n-------------------- Chapter 6           -\n- Raids                 -\n-------------------Occasionally the Marshal will call for a raid, when this happens, you are expected to wake from yur slumber ((get online)) and meet at a given place to prepare for -->\n-Battle, during battle you will be expected to identify yourself along-side your allies and bretheren. ((Set /status)) During a raid, you are supposed to be able to identify your enemy, and kill. If you're not sure if you can be the burly man you are\n--->\n-in a one versus five, then retreat to your allied company, and ask for assistance or tell of the enemies position. Surely you will be able to not get murdered and rather do the murdering.\nBe sure to be able to sustain yourself with LOTS OF FOOD.\n-->\nRemember to try not to die, or atleast die with your bretheren, and hopefully it's not in vain.\n\n\n\n\n((BLANK SPACE))\n\n\n-->\n-------------------- Chapter 7           -\n- Wars                 -\n-------------------There will come a time where Humanity will have to defend itself agaisnt the barbaric ways of the enemy. War is self explainatory. ((Server rules of wars))\n-->\n-------------------- Rules and such    -\n-------------------\n-------------------- Chapter 8           -\n- Arbalest What Is  -\n-------------------Every soldier should be able to cary and use an arbalest. It is the finest of Human made ranged weaponry. ((Rp weapon that is very deadly))\nTo learn to use an arbalest, ->\n-First one must aquire an arbalest and get proper training, not from the text I'm about to write. If you don't know who to ask to learn to use an Arbalest, then you probably should do some review. \nImmersive Instructions Follow.\n--->\nStep 1 : Pull out Arbalest in hand\n\nStep 2: Place Arbalest under foot\n\nStep 3: Pull back the mechanism till an audible *click* is heard\n\nStep 4: Load bolt\n-->\nStep 5: Put Arbalest to your shoulder\n\nStep 6: Comfortably and accurately aim\n\nStep 7: Fire and hope you hit ((Target and you both /roll 20, if shooter rolls higher, target is his))\n\n-->\n-------------------- Chapter 9           -\n- Patrolling           -\n-------------------Alright, Patrolling? -You ask, yes this is a thing you must be notified about.\nGenuinely, you are not supposed to wear any armor when patrolling. Why? Because a -->\n-man in full iron armor walking along the roads would seem scary to you wouldn't it? Yes it would. That's why you don't wear armor while patrolling, unless you spy some bandits or a criminal, then you gear up and arrest or kill them.\n\nEnough said. -->\n-------------------- Rilkor's Tips to    -\n- Combat              -\n-------------------Hopefully these tips will help make you better in combat ((MC PVP)). These secrets should not be told to anyone else, for they might end up in the enemy's hands.\n-->\nTip 1: When fighting, don't walk straight forward, that is the dumbest thing I see people do, and I take advantage of it. YOU NEED TO STRAFE. This will help you dodge attacks and position yourself more favorably.\n\n-->\nTip 2: Low ground means it's harder for the enemy to attack you as they need to reach down. YOU WANT THE LOW GROUND. If you have the low ground, it will be easier to hit.\n\n\n\n-->\nTip 3: When using a bow, contemplate where your enemy is going to be in the second the arrow you fire would hit. JUDGE THE DISTANCE AND SPEED. Shooting at a target far away means they have time to dodge the arrow.\n\n-->\nTip 4: For the love of everything, the more people you have on your side, the better the odds are you lot would win a fight, SO STICK TOGETHER. Unless you end up all to be very bad at combat, then I say to you, rest in peace.\n\n-->\nTip 5: Blocking is about as useless as bringing a knife to an arbalest fight. ((knife to a gun fight)). YOU SHOULD SWING AS MUCH AS POSSIBLE. Don't stop hitting the enemy! No regrets, no remorse, may only victory be upon you. ((That means spam hitting)\n->\n-------------------- End of the Field   -\n- Guide                 -\n-------------------Hopefully you learned something and became a better soldier. I wish ye luck out there.\n\n~Rilkor\n\nAve Chivay, Ave Orenia, Ave Humanity.", ""),
        StaticBook("Field Herbs", "Andriel Elré Z'lorn", "In the field there are many ways to treat the wounded. From burns to cuts to scrapes to arrow wounds, there can be many different things that may need to be cared for. Here is a guide on Medical Uses of different Herbs during everyday life.\nBlissfoil:\nBlissfoil can be very useful for minor injuries or ailments. It can relieve pain and itchyness at the slightest of touch. The oil around it's stalks and petals can be used medically to relieve these symptoms.\nTippen's Root:\nThis herb is great for stopping the bleeding of a large wound once made into a Salve/Balm. This root is known for having an unpleasent smell, however, the medical uses outweight such factors.\nFlameTounge Root:\nThis Root is not to be used lightly, and is only to be used if out of Tippen's Root. It gives off an intense heat that can be used to seal and stop blood flow. NOTE: Make sure to wear gloves when handling this Root.\nSerpent's Stalk:\nThis herb is generally dangerous for consumption as a plant, however, once one crushes the upper stalk and mix it with water, it can be used to treat burns and minor pain.\nFrost Vine:\nIt is wise to crush this herb and mix it with water. This will produce a substance, somewhat sticky, which can be used to numb areas from pain.\nAqua Nymph:\nWARNING: Only use in extreme cases.\nThis plant can cause closing of the airway if taken orally. However, if one were to receive\na terrible burn. To use the plant correctly, boil the plant (Gently) in some water, strain the plant from the water\nAqua Nymph Cont.:\nand use the remaining oil on the affected skin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Finding Nature", "Lillith", "How did I Find Nature?\n\nBy: Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid\nI found the Order by mistake, oddly enough. It was only about four years since Aegis had fallen and I had been married for about a year. I was five months pregnant, and stubbornly travelling to Salvus to trade some of our wools and\nleathers for food supplies, as we had not built our farms yet.\n\t\nOn the crossroads leading towards the Salvus farmlands a man drew a knife on me, and proceeded to steal my leathers and wools, and what little minas I had.\nHe then decided he was going to take me to sell as a slave, so I started struggling. He sliced my arm and side as I broke away from him and fled across the outskirts of Salvus.\n\nI did not know what was beyond Salvus,\nI fled into a dense area of oak trees and ended up stumbling upon a coastline with a long wooden bridge that almost looked grown out of the trees, spanning the waters to an island of dense trees with a huge tree in the center.\nI held my bleeding side and crossed over the bridge, pushing vines and leaves out of my way.\n\nI stepped off the bridge into a small clearing, a small shop stall on the right, ahead a root gate leading inside the great tree,\nto the left a pathway led into the trees and I could see a small wheat farm along the path. Standing in the root gateway were two robed figures, one male and one female, both elves.\nThey turned and saw me, the woman stepping towards me after a moment. She wore red and yellow robes, and her eyes were fake, made of gold, but they moved and she seemed able to see, a worried look on her face as she saw me,\nasking if I was okay. I told her I was attacked and she took me down the path toward the farm, sitting me down next to the small stream to relax while she tended to me.\nI asked what this place was, it was beautiful. She smiled and told me it was the Druid Grove, and introduced herself as Affection Druid Jena, a Guide of the Druidic Order. We spoke for a long while, my wounds taking little\ntime for her powers to heal, but finding pleasant conversation in each other. She told me of the Order and answered all my questions. When we grew hungry, she excused herself to get us a snack.\nWhile she was away, the man from the gate approached, asking if I was okay and introducing himself as Ice Druid Jameson, one of the Archdruids. We spoke for a short while, then two Orcs with staves ran by, one\nwearing a pumpkin on his head, yelling to watch out for the 'bangaloos', hitting my head grazingly with his staff as he ran by. Jameson excused himself and ran after them, yelling at them to be silent. Jena returned shortly\nwith a plate of bread slices, a cream spread on them which she told me was made of bonemeal, and sliced apples.\n\nWe talked through the night, both of us napping serenely under the canopy and stars.\nIn the morning I asked if I could return after having my child to join the Order, she smiled and said that I was welcome to return whenever I wanted and she would be happy to instruct me.\n\nI had my son four months later, Aeran,\nand I returned to the grove four months after that with him in my arms, answered Jena's questions and became a Dedicant. Jena instructed me, with advice along the way from Archdruids Jameson and Saviticus. Once I became attuned as the\nSequoia Druid by Jena, I began learning all forms of medicine and healing that I could, from Jena as well as a little from Saviticus, but mostly taking their lessons and experimenting on my own to refine the techniques.\nThe rest is a much longer story for another time, but this is how I found my calling in nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire and Love", "Atturi", "--------------------\n\n    One of the many\n    Stories by Atturi\n    The Wood elf\n\n\n\n-\n-------------------\nUpon a time that had once Happened,\n\nAtturi was going through a tough time in his life, His friends were being mean, Toe the Wood elf kept saying that Atturi wanted to sleep with him, This wasnt true\nAtturi's dick was a straight compass pointing toward women.\n\nMylas, Toe, And others had taken Atturi's joke of being alchoholic seriously, they had made fun of him, driving him to become one.\nSince a long time before these, they have been trying to get Atturi a wife, he had kept saying no to them, but they kept persisting but everytime. Atturi choked and ran.\n\nEventually on a nice, sunny day, Hills rolling,\nWind whistling, tulips cheering, Roses loving, willows crying green, Elves trying for a child, and many other delightful things.\n\nAtturi had walked into Felsen, walked into the mayors office, and leaned against a support beam.\nA few minutes later Mylas the mayor had come in, and asked if Atturi was okay,\n\nAtturi had unclipped his sheath from his belt, edged forward a bit and tripped on the rug, falling to the floor, Sword n' Sheath flying toward a painting\nnear Mylas, He didnt do much but scold Atturi.\n\nAtturi had crawled over to the sword that landed on the rug, he grasped it by its handle and raised himself from the ground. he flicked off the sheath.\nHe retreated back to his support beam, Sword pointing to the floor, when he heard shouts. Toe and Sam walked in, After a few words were exchanged between Sam, Mylas, And Toe toward Atturi Toe and Mylas left Sam and him alone,\nSam had been trying to calm Atturi down, not realizing Atturi was completely calm,\n\nEventually When Sam passed over the sheath back to Atturi, he had accidently knocked over the candle while clipping it back onto his belt\nThis created a fire that would cause the cieling to cave in, these damages were later taken care of.\n\nBefore the events of the fire, And on the saint's day, Atturi had been speaking with a Lady who he had treasured\nThey were just chatting about things, When talking to her, Atturi was not sad or emotionally troubled\nBy fear.\n\nShe was comforting to him. \n\nAfter the fire Atturi Had told her\nhe had a part in its creation. She was suprised.\n\nIn the end she had to leave for a meeting\n\nLater in the next few saints days Atturi went and asked her to go on a date with him, He was very nervous, Tripping over his\nwords. Due to the fact he did not have a plan for the date, She said No, He was heartbroken. Honestly, at that day and age he was very unstable.\n\nHe slumped to the ground and started crying. she sat down next to him to try and comfort him\nThey had hugged each other. when she had to leave Atturi didnt want to get up after she had, then it started snowing, and a moment later he got up, she took his hand and they walked to her home,\n\nShe had made him food and offered drink\nshe had gotten him a bed to sleep in and sat him down by the fire, they conversed for a while, And Atturi had tried to think up of any stories to tell, but his mind was too clouded with emotion.\n\nHe had mentioned this to her, and she responded to him that\nhe should let those emotions out, so he did, he walked over and gave her a hug, and then a kiss on the cheek. she had to break away for she did not know what to do, Atturi had gone to his bed and sat upon it, Smiling with rosey cheeks\nThe next day Atturi had to leave, they gave each other a good bye hug and said their farewells.\n\nthis relationship later ended with an Apology for pitiful actions and friendship from Atturi.\n\nAtturi's love trudges on however\nThe\n          End", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire and Smoke", "Dela Vaik", "Fire and smoke... dragons... will burn your soul, they pillage and blow... keep a whatch on... your foe... and if this tower ends up i flames... so will we... and the rest of vai-lor.\n[!] notes ar writen here telling how to play this song on the lute-\nand guitar[!]\n\nBy: Garsto 'Spark' Leaf", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "Dorin Irongut", "A Book On the Study and Use of Fire Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten by Dorin Irongut\nTable of contents\n\nChapter 1\nLearning of Fire\n\nChapter 2\nMeditation & Void Connection\n\nChapter 3\nSummon Your Spark!\nChapter 4\nPractice!\n\nChapter 5\nBecoming adept!\n\nChapter 6\nAdvance Mana Control!\n\nChapter 7\nBasic Combat!\nChapter 8\nCreativity & Mastership!\nProlouge\nId like to put this bit in here before you read this book, so you know why I write this book. I write this book because, I , just like my master before me, wish to exstend my knowledge of the art to students who wish to learn. I write this\nto teach. And to me, teaching is a great thing. I like my master before me, and his master before him, am now spreading the knowledge passed from each of us down to the next generation, in the hopes that you will do the same. Now, lets get reading!\nChapter 1, Learning of Fire.\nIn order to do elemental evocation, you must first learn of your element!\nThat means learning what your element looks like, smells like, feels like, sounds like, and yes... even tastes like, in great detail... You must\nbe able to study a single flame for hours, remembering its every aspect.. and even then you will not be finished, as you need to learn more about fire... Many, many flames, of all types must be learned of. Take time to study flame every time you see one\neven if you think it is the same as another. This concludes chapter one, and the studying of flames should be done inbetween sessions.\nChapter 2, Meditation & Void connection\n\nThe next lesson, or lesson 1.5 and 2. Is meditation to help train the mind and body to enter the void. It is also how one enters the void. Meditation, at first, should be done in the most sutible position to you.\nWether it be simply sitting, standing, laying, or the prefered lotus style. When meditating, to get things started, one should get into their desired position, and close their eyes... allowing all of the world to simply go away...  But also keeping mind\nof your surroundings.\nAfter this is done, calm your breathing, stay like this for however long you want. Eventually after hours, a day, or maybe even a little more, you should exsperince your first quick connection to the void. When this occurs, your body\nmay react in many diffrent ways. It could be from the more common of twitching and breaking out into a sweat, to getting sick and puking, however, you must do the same again, and again to last longer while connected to the void and blocking these symtoms\nout. After achieving a short connection time, and you are able to stay connected for a longer periode of time, you should move onto the next lesson.\nChapter 3, Summoning Your Spark!\nThis lesson is usualy the most exciting for all of my students, as you summon your very first flame. Weather you succeed or not depends on how you handled the prior lessons. \nInbetween your time of meditation and\nconnection, you should have studied a candle flame by now. Once you think you are ready, get into your meditation position, and face your palm up into the air... I cannot exspress how much when i say, focus on the spot ABOVE your hand, and not your hand\nitself... else you will be very sorry you did. Next, connect to the void, after doing so, remember all the aspects of a candle flame, then, using your mana as a anchor, pull the image from the void and above your hand... This can take a few trys, so fret\nnot if you fail the first time. After doing so, you should have summoned your first flame! Although you wont be able to keep it up for long, summon another after a short break and keep doing so unto tired.\nChapter 4, practice\n\nIn this lesson, we will be taking summoning you flame to the next level by doing simple movements with it. By now, your flame should be a little larger, and you should be able to keep it up and running for quite some time.\nNow, this next part is quite easy... or so it seems... After you summon your flame, keep a constant flow of mana, and image your flame moving from left to right... This will get tring but after a day or so, you should be ready to start moving it in\ncirlces around your palm. Do this, and keep doing this for a couple of times each day for about a stone week or so, practicing moving your flame and building your mana up.\nFrom here is where i exspress practice... it is the most vital thing you do now,\ndont miss a day, unless sick. Keep this in mind and you should start to increase in exsperince as each day pass's until your ready for the next lesson.\nChapter 5, Becoming Adept!\n\nIn this chapter is where you begin to become adept at evocation. If you have been practicing like ive exspressed in the past chapter, you should be ready to continue onto the next lesson... Throwing your fire!\nYour fire should now be modertaly size... that of a torch flame or so. If not, do not continue reading until so is done. Now then, if you are ready, summon your fire, whilest standing, and in a open area, as this could go wrong. Now then, after you have\nsummoned your flame, arc it over your back as you would, and simply throw it, imagin it being hurled over and keep the flow of mana to it, and as it hits the target your throwing it at, allow it to exsplode... Keep practicing this for about 2 or so elven\nweeks before moving onto the next lesson.\nChapter 6, Advance Mana Control\n\nYou should now be well into about 2 1/2 to 3 months of training now. And this is where we move into the more advance things... In this case, advance mana manipulation. In the past, you might have seen a evocationist\nevocate farther away than just a arms lenth away. With this lesson, your going to be summoning you mana in farther spots, from the left, right, and infront of you. Keep doing this only with mana, unto you are able to without to much tire, as this requires\nmuch mana. After you can do this, this time, do they same as you would to summon a normal fire, but in those locations of your focus away from you... Do this for quite the while, until you feel more comfortable with it, which should take a few days.\nAfter\nyou have done this, you are now ready for the next lesson.\nLesson 7, Basic combat\nNow, just because this chapter is in here, does not mean you should use evocation for combat only, but it is a use fire evocation is spesialized in... But not its only use! so remember that!\n\nMoving on....\nIn this chapter, you will be learning how to move about and such while connected to the void and summoning fire. You will also learn how to move about while keeping a current fire you hold in hand, further more, I will say if you are in a fight, you will\nneed to pull fast connections, and even faster summonings.\nTo start, simple try walking around while connected to the void.... this will take a high level of concentration, but once your able to, go ahead and try a slightly faster pace, and so on to a jog\nand even further onto a run. Once your able to do this, which this could take quite the while, maybe a week, move onto keeping a fire in your hand while walking. Once your done with that, follow the same prosess up to running... But this next part, could\ntake even longer, and be even harder. You must now summon your fire while walking, and so on. then move onto summoning a fire at a distance while walking and so on... This means you will have to keep a concentraion on the spot your summoning. Once your\ndone with this keep practicing for awhile... maybe take... heh, no justing kidding. No breaks!\nAfter practicing a few more days after achiving this, move onto the next, and final lesson... or so your told.\nChapter 8, Creativity & Mastership!\n\nAt this point, you should have been training atleast 4-5 months. You have learned all of which i could teach you through a book, but now, you must study more!\nYes, learn as much as you can, and use that knowledge to do\ncreative things, that others wouldnt use normaly! Make your evocation a art! perfect a certain fire! do things to make yourself diffrent! because that is what makes a true master... After you have gotten this far in the book, all i can say it keep\npracticing, and maybe, when you think you are ready, go onto have a apprentice of your own! I hope you do good with the knowledge i have givven you!\n\nWritten by one Dorin Irongut on the 15'th of the Deep Cold, 1519, in the Cloud Temple Library.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "Evelangéline", "About Fire Evocation:\n\n-Fire Evocation, one of the six evocation arts is the utilization of fire by the evocationists. Although Fire Evocation is not very hard to learn, it is one that must be practised a lot about, because of its destructive behaviour.\nBasic Understanding:\n\n- Fire evocation, as the other types of evocation arts, is powered by the void. The evocationist who has a connection to the void calls forth the fire from the void. One aspect that is not known by many is that the fire formed is -\nnot real on this plane of existance. A thing that I tell to my students, \"The fire is fake, only the effects of the fire are real.\" is an accurate statement, considering this.\n\n-The origins of the art are unknown, although It is one of the oldest arts.\nProgress of A Fire Evocationist Student:\n\n- Fire evocation is easy to learn, yet hard to master. So, a Fire Evocationist needs to take their time and have stable observations and practises to use their potential to a maxiumum.\n- During the first five elven days, the student needs to form a stable connection to the void, through meditating. While meditating can be done in any position, it can also be done for flexible amounts of time. For example, while many evocationists -\nchoose to meditate for at least half an hour once. I meditated for five minutes six times a day. The important thing is efficiency, and focus. The student needs to clear their mind in order to form their first connections to the void.\n\n- After the evoca-\n-tionist forms a stable connection to the void, they work on conjuring low-powered flames, propably shards of embers. During this period, the evocationist must be observing how fire burns, how it spreads, and how it affects the substance it burns on.\n- After an elven week, the evocationist will get started with conjuring small flames, not exceeding the size of a regular candle's fire. During the beginning of this period the evocationist will be greatly fatigued, propably not being able to hold the -\nfire for long. The time of the evocation will increase from ten seconds to a few minutes if done correctly. The evocationist should focus on increasing the size of the flames and lenghten the duration of how long they can hold the flame.\n- After this period, the evocationist will be able to evoke bigger flames, propably not exceeding the size of an elven fist, after the two elven weeks of the period.\n\n- Next period, the evocationist will focus on shaping their flames as spheres.\nTo be able to throw fiery balls of fire at objects. The evocationist will fail to throw a ball of fire successfully the first five elven days, then will be fatigued after one small ball of fire. During the ends of this phase, the evocationist will increa-\n-se the size and range of their fire spheres, the phase lasting for nearly two more elven weeks, exactly one elven month after the evocationist had first started to learn.\n\n- From the start of the next phase, the fire evocationist will-\nbe having covered most of the parts to be known, moving to a period of practise. The evocationist will be able to evocate walls of fire and flames that are distanced from the evocationist. However, as the distance of the fire increases from the evocation-\n-ist, so does the difficulty and mana requirement. The evocationist at this point would be able to form multiple fire spheres before being fatigued, not exceeding an amount of three. While the wall of fire can be maintained for an average of thirty-\nseconds. After this period, is the mastering period.\n\n- A master of fire evocation has learned how to effectively and efficiently use their mana to cast larger flames, calling fires to this realm of existance quicker. Gaining the ability to-\nevoke large areas of vigorous, reactive fire; fire novas. Bear in mind that an evocationist should never try to evoke more than their training has given to them.\nMore Things to Know:\n\n- Although fire may be engrossing and exciting, it also is very dangerous. More than the other arts actually, at least in my point of view. You cannot, simply cannot manipulate the fire you have summoned, meaning that-\nif a fire evocationist accidentally set an object on fire, they cannot extinguish it. So try to remain calm, and don't cause accidents.\n\n- To further explain the lack of fire manipulation, I'll go into slightly more detail. A fire evocationist cannot-\nutilize already existing fire. They can only summon flames from the void into this realm of existance. Once they summon the flames and use them, they are out of control. As I say to my students: The fire is alive, it has a mind of its own. You cannot -\nforce it to do anything. You can only convince it.\n\n-Lastly, an evocationist of any type shouldn't ever push their limits too hard, to exceed their level. If an evocationist proceeds to cast magic for too long-\nthey will get extremely fatigued, then maybe even lose their life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fireflies", "Evelynn Shards", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-  \n   Fireflies\n  \n          From\n         \n                 Above\n\n-------------------A story written by Evelynn Shards\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nOnce upon a time, in a small town called Areguana, there was a huge storm raging above the tiny houses. Thunder and lightning was everywhere to be seen and to be heard. Suddenly the lightning stroke down into a house. A woman holding a baby ran screaming\nout of the house. Flames were sticking out of the roof, making big gaps. A huge cloud of smoke filled the sky. People ran with buckets full of water to the house, trying to put out the fire. Since the city was layed on a beach, between a forest\nand an ocean, it could be reached easily. \n\nThe next day, when the storm calmed down an d went away, people were running up and down, carrying logs and stone to build up more houses, and safer houses. After the storm, if you walked inside\nthe town you could hear people speaking of a legend. The legend said, each time there is a storm, when you walk exactly 150 steps from the center of the storm, you'll see a tree. Each time you hold your hand on it, millions of fireflies come flying down\nfrom the sky. They say their light could make you blind. This legend was popular in the small town. Everyone spoke about it. Later on they didnt believe in it anymore, until that one day...\n\nIt was a very hot summer day. Johan was\njumpin around the field playing with some friends. The mother told Johan to not go too far away from town, as he remembered. His friends said: Hey Johan, do you want to come with us to the forest? But Johan didnt want to, his mother\ndoes not agree with such thing. She is scared something will happen in the forest. But they kept asking and asking until Johan said: Okay,okay i'll come with you, but not for too long! Else my mother will be mad. After that they ran into the forest.\nThen suddenly in the middle of the forest a small place where no trees grew was there. Only one single tree, which had an orange color, Strange, Johan said, trees arent orange, right? No they arent, his friend said. Then Johan went to sit onto the tree.\nBut then suddenly the fireflies came from above. Look at that! They said. The light formed one huge firefly. Thats the most beautiful and magical thing i ever saw. Thats not normal! Johan said. After that they quickly ran home, to tell this story to their\nfamily. When Johan came home his mother asked: Where the hell were you? I thought you were dead! Then Johan said: Im sorry mom, i went into the forest with my friends, im sorry about that, but i saw something magical. What is it? His mother asked.\n\"I saw the fireflies..\" He quietly answered..\n\n\n\n------------------- \n\nTHE END OF A SHORT STORY ((May be continued))\n\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("First Artifice", "Leyu", "Forging your first Artifice - a Artificing Guide by Garrik Forgeheart\nCreating your first Rune Weapon is not something to be take lightly - it is a undertaking that will take you several days - if not months, to create. Here is a brief guide to creating for own Rune Weapon, although the\nprocess will vary from project to project. Firstly. You will need a item to Rune-Spell upon. This should be a weapon that can be easily maintained - since a broken weapon will lose it's runes in a effort to stay together . It should also be a weapon\nthat you are profficient with - otherwise, what is the point? For my example, i shall create a Rune-Axe, which was made with the intention of cleaving opponents armour and defenses. It is important that you give your weapon\na unique name - it will make apply runes easier, as the weapon will answer to its name, meaning that only the person holding its true name can wield it. This axe shall be called Wall-Breaker. Secondly, create a area in which you can easily sit in quiet\nand comfort - since runing can b e a hard and arduous process - and you dont want butt-cramps to be part of your weapons runes, right? Harharhar! Then, lay the weapon out in front of you, and place your hand on it. Then, think of\nthe action of the rune you wish to apply to the weapon. for instance, i thought of cleaving opponents into itty-bitty pieces for mine! the rune for Cleaving is Ar-wyrn-dur. however, for your own runes - you will have to discover the names for them\nyourself! As i said, this isnt meant to be easy! Over time, the applications of runes will build up a lattice of runes over the weapon surface . The thicker and more consistent this lattice is, the stronger the weapon will be. Take CARE over this! This\nis the important part of the Rune-Spelling! If you continue to build up these runes, eventually the weapon will be ready to use! If you've followed this guide- hopefully you will now have your very own Rune-Weapon! Use it well! Use it often! Use it\nwisely! For this weapon will last as long as you care for it! Do not underestimate it's power! Of course, every rune-weapon has it's drawbacks - all of them will have their own consciousness - and can freely choose whether to do\nwhat you want to use it for. Forcing a weapon against it's Will will have negative results- usually bad ones!\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fisher King #2", "The Fisher King II", "The Fisher King II\n(Shady_Tales)\nAn Epic Tale\n\"Four Scrolls:The Fisher King\"\n\n(This is Part 2)\n-------------------During the voyage, I finally asked Father Pietro why he tried helping the chief.\n“The Heavenly Father asks we hold forgiveness in our hearts else we are filled with malice instead. He also didn’t kill me like I thought he would. If it were not for him telling you men to go to the mountain, I would likely not be here.”\nI didn't ask\nabout anything else. I continued to practice Pietro’s tongue with Koschei each night we camped on the river.\nThe grassy plains would fade, giving way to sand separating our ancestral home to the vast expanse of salty water Father Pietro called the sea.\nFather Pietro smiled and looked to the ring he wore engraved with the man on the boat. We were to set up camp on the beach. I was not accustomed to feeling the grains of sand between my toes and my body tingled at the new sensation. Young ones sat in it\nand at times threw it at each other as they would with mud back in the village. Mothers would have to brush it from their hair.\n\nOther than the children, we were near clueless what we were to do next until Father Pietro spoke up.\n------------------\n“We need some of this!” He held it up into the air, presenting it to a group of us he had lead back inland on a short walk. He called it hemp nettle.\n\nFrom this hemp nettle, we made nets which we tied to the rope we brought from home. And in our boats, we\nmade sail out towards the sea. We were high in spirit.\n-------------------I heard Father Pietro weep in his tent last night. Koschei’s death troubled me for I had known him for so long and he left Bardur behind who would have died if Koschei did not give\nhim what little he caught in his net. But I think Father Pietro took it worse than me.\n\nThe next morning I awoke to shouting outside. I groggily crawled out from my tent, planting my hands firmly in the grains of sand and turned my head to see Father\nPietro attracting a crowd.\n\n“Brothers and sisters, East is Eden! East is Eden! God tells me this!”\nWhen the crowd dissipated, I spoke with Father Pietro alone.\n“Brother Brundt, if you listen hard enough, you can hear God speak to you.” He looked to his hand at the ring. I opened my mouth to speak but decided it was unimportant. East was Eden and Eden awaited.\n\n-------------------\nOnly the old man’s piercing stare could catch what he saw through the thick fog that blanketed the expanding sea. Nothing was within horizon sight and here, rising from the depths, was a rocky outcrop rising seven men high. In the middle of the rising\nstone columns was a deep pool with vibrant colors of life in its depths. Passed the sounds of waves crashing on the east facing side, ‘clicks’ were heard when we looked between the rocks. Life.\n\nIt took a long time. We had to sail back and\nforth back to the mainland for wood, water, and other supplies. Father Pietro told us in the end it would be worth it. We built our new village against the inland facing side of the rocky outcrop. It rose above the waters below upon numerous stilts\nbundled together.\n\nFather Pietro casted the first net.\n\nGive us Lord, our daily bread.\nPlease know that we are truly grateful,\nFor every cup and every plateful.\n--End of Scroll III--\n--Scroll IV Next--\nYears of plenty. Father Pietro told us the names of the fish we caught and had us remember them. My favorite was the monkfish. The old man told me it got its name from what he wore as an acolyte though I’m still not sure what that is. I liked the monkfish\nbecause of how different they looked and how tender its tail was when cooked properly. I also liked scaring Bardur with the monkfish in front of his friends.\n\n“Ikke gjør det, onkel Brundt! ((Do not do that, uncle Brundt!))”\nHe shrieked. His friends giggled in response.\n\n“In the common tongue, Bardur. And you’re coming of age in a few years. Your father Koschei is shaking his head in shame from the Seven Skies watching his son wet himself over a fish.\"\nI chuckled loudly while Bardur swung his fists at my side.\n-------------------Father Pietro called our village ‘Piscatoris’. It came from a tongue much older than his own and he told us it was fitting for we were Piscators, fishermen.\n\nWe lived seven\nyears in Eden before we overstayed our welcome.\n\nOne of our fishing trips went eerily wrong that day. Fewer in number upon return and nothing in their nets, the men returned with a capsized boat and spoke of a behemoth rising from\nthe depths of the sea that drowned most of those on board. Father Pietro’s calm demeanor disappeared, giving way to a stern expression.\n-------------------We rowed our boat in the direction of where the men went to fish. Father Pietro held in his hands a\nbarbed harpoon. It wasn’t long until we saw water shoot from sea.\n\n“Straight ahead, brothers!” Father Pietro shouted over the roar of the waves. And then he prayed.\nCreator of man, Overseer of all things right,\nWhose powers none can resist,\nSave and deliver us, we beseech,\nFrom the hands of our enemies,\nBy granting us dominion over them,\nShow us the path to victory,\nThat we might produce it in Your undying name.\n\nFather Pietro leaped up just as the whale opened its mouth. I had never seen anything more darker.\n\nI awoke to a wooden board hitting me on my head. In a panic I clung to it when I\nnoticed I was floating in the sea. My heart began beating faster  and I looked up to the sky. The sun had not changed its position much and using said position, I swam back in the direction of Piscatoris using the wooden board for support. It was the\nlongest swim I would ever take at that time.\n-------------------The village had collapsed on the behemoth. Its blood expanded across the waters surrounding it.\n\n“Father Pietro!” The old man was within my sight in the crimson waters I swam into.\nI went to his side and looked at him. His forehead was covered in blood, but it was not the blood of the whale. It was his own. My hand gripped his and my heart sank deeper than the seas we made our lives in.\n“Brundt, in!” I turned around seeing Bardur reach out for me. My people had gotten into the boats and were abandoning Piscatoris. I looked to Father Pietro but it was hard to focus in this panic and treading water became increasingly difficult, becoming\nimpossible. We went under finally as I gave way, dragging Pietro down with me. Then I saw his ring. The ring with the man in the boat.\n-------------------Father Pietro was not of our world. But he brought his world to us. Even in his late years, he was\nstrong. Perhaps that is why we did not bother to choose a new chief after Sigli died. Our boats remained still in the now placid waters. I looked back to the water finally but saw Father Pietro was gone.\n“What do now?” Bardur looked to me with sullen eyes.\n\nI looked around to those in my boat and then to the others. I then looked to the ring I wore on my finger. Pietro’s ring. This was an ever changing world.\nI thought of Inga and our unborn child, the young boy and his father who never returned. I thought of Sigli and Koschei. Bardur was still young but he looked very similar to his father. I thought of Father Pietro and all those we lost from where we\nClosing my eyes, I asked the Heavenly Father what he willed.\n\n“Eden is East.”\n \nGreat canyons of red greeted us.God bless our Fisher King.\nO Lord, we call upon You in our time of sorrow,\nThat You give us the strength and will to bear our heavy\nburdens, until we can again feel the warmth and love of\nYour divine compassion. Be mindful of us and have mercy\non us while we struggle to comprehend life's hardships.\n \nKeep us ever in Your watch, til we can walk again with\nlight hearts and renewed spirits.\n--End of Scroll IV--\n\n----The End----", ""),
        StaticBook("Fishidex", "Cir'dian", "The Fishidex\n\n\n\nThe #1 information book for fish and fisherpeople.\n\nBy Sen Nymphea\n\n-Bonefish-\n\nThis fish has skin so thin that its bones are visible, and there are so many that I can't even count them ( I lost count at 420, couldn't be bothered to start again ). I don't think there's enough meat on the entire body of\nthis thing, other than bone, to even justify trying to eat it. Any volounteers are welcome to try, but I cannot be held responsible if they choke...\n\nTends to weigh around 1lb and 6oz and is found virtually everywhere. Doesn't\nseem to give any unusual effects after consumption, but my husband, after volounteering to try some, still managed to cough up a bone even after I spent fourty minutes making sure there were none left.\n-Ghostfish-\n\nThis fish is very odd. It's practically weightless and I can almost see straight through it. In fact, I'm not entirely convinced it's actually here. It could just be my imagination and perhaps I never even caught the fish in the\nfirst place.\n\nI can't even get an accurate measurement of its weight, but it weighs less than 1oz. I've only ( barely ) seen these swim about in swampy areas. My husband told me it tasted and felt like paper, and that for a moment, he felt dead.\n-Sunfish-\n\nThis variety of fish has very shiny, yellow scales. They're a very common sight, especially around dawn, but always swims toward shelter when night falls. It hates Mooneye fish with a passion and viciously attacks them\nwhenever they see them.\n\nThese fish tend to weigh around 4lbs 4oz and are found in literally every location. Some people actually throw these back after catching them. My husband says it tastes very nice, but is a hint too spicey for him.\n-Mooneye-\n\nThe Sunfish's nocturnal rival. These fish bare a large contrast compared to the Sunfish, donning pale blue scales that glow under moonlight. They are just as common as Sunfish, and why they fight so often I have no idea,\nbut I've heard that if the two varieties of fish are ever seen swimming together in a friendly manner, an eclipse is going to occur soon.\n\nFound everywhere, just like Sunfish, and weighs around 2lbs 5oz. Apparently lovely texture, but tastes\nbland, so my husband suggested that I find something to serve with it to give it some flavour.\n-Weaverfish-\n\nThis fish tends to bury itself on the bottom of lakes and snatch small animals as they venture past, including smaller fish. It has a sand-like colour to its scales with a fairly black tail and dorsal fins.\nI've only found these in thick jungle forests, where many other dangerous varieties of fish tend to live, and usually weighs around 5lbz 7oz. My husband nearly collapsed after I had him try eating some, and said he was almost paralyzed. I'm not sure what\nexactly caused this, but I'm considering finding other volounteers...\n-Monkfish-\n\nThese beasts are huge and very greedy, its teeth are also very sharp, which has allowed them to bite through many of my nets in the past. They're also quite difficult to cook because of its size.\nPretty difficult to weigh, but on average they size up around 14lbs 10oz. They're found in several locations, usually rivers and thick wooded areas. After convincing my husband to try some of this fish, he said that it was quite chewy, but made\nhis entire body feel like it'd spent a year on the most comfortable mattress and it definately made up for the last fish I'd made him try.\n-Cactusfish-\n\nThis prickly feller is covered head to tail in grey needles, which makes it very difficult to cook, catch and prepare. Their scales are normally dark green and the teeth are surprisingly blunt. Sometimes other fish get stuck to the\nspines along its body, which is a bonus if you're willing to try and peel them off.\n\nFound in dry, desert areas and weighs on average 6lbs 2oz. After very carefully removing all of the needles, my husband said the fish tasted similar to steamed\nvegetables and that the texture was delicate. Nevermind, he still managed to find a needle with his tongue...\n-Hagfish-\n\nThis thing is actually pretty creepy. It looks shriveled and aged like an old Human lady and it even has a bit of hair growing on it. It also smells like mouldy wood. To be honest, it probably is just a really old fish of another variety\nthat has somehow found a way to take refuge away from the rest of fish society. They hate venturing far from their homes and hate anything that ventures too close to their homes even more. \nOnly found in murky swamplands and usually weighs\naround 3lbs 9oz. It smelled disgusting, even when cooked, and my husband agreed, but after finally trying some ( and struggling not to vomit ) he told me that he could somehow see everything much better and that he could see my beauty even better than\nusual. I'm considering serving this to my husband more often.\n-Silverfish-\n\nThis fish is very interesting... Because I don't think it's a fish at all. In fact, I'm pretty sure that it's a bug, but whatever it is, I found it swimming about like any other fish. The only reason I'm making an entry for it is\nbecause I accidently squished it on to the page...\n\nI find these things swimming about near large mountains, but its too small to weigh.\n\n     \\ \\ / /\n-->]}}}}}}}}|===\n     / / \\ \\\n-Knifefish-\n\nAs the name probably suggests, this fish is notably dangerous because of its knife-like shape. The entire head is like one long blade, varying in length from 2 - 5 inches, about as hard as a rock, and so sharp it could\nprobably be used as a weapon. The body is rather light blue whereas the head blends in to a more subtle white.\n\nTends to roam around thick jungle areas with an average weight of 1lb 2oz. My husband said it tasted quite nice, and he kept the\nhead as a spare knife, but felt nothing strange.\n-Toadfish-\n\nThe round, fat body of this fish makes it difficult to distinguish from other animals that roam aqautic habitats, such as frogs. Actually, it looks so much like a frog that it might actualls just be a legless one with an\nunusually fish like tail. Whichever it actually is, it certainly likes to croak.\n\nOnly found quite occasionally in swamp and marsh regions, where other similar animals live and, on average, weighs around 2lbs 2oz. My husband had a\nsevere stomach ache that lasted several hours. I've decided that I won't be asking him to try anymore fish. I'll just have to find some volounteers instead.\n-Alefish-\n\nI despise this fish because it smells distinctly of alcohol, and the smell gets even stronger when it's cooked. I don't have any clue why it smells like this. It's mostly white with a faint hint of amber.\nmaybe this is where\nale actually comes from? I really don't know, but one thing I do know is that this is probably the fish I've never been more dissapointed to find.\n\nI found this fish swimming around Vaerhaven, which is far too cold for most fish to survive, and\nit weighs just 1lb 2oz. My husband volounteered to try this fish as soon as he could smell it coming from the kitchen, and said it had that Halfling brew taste. It took me an hour to get him to stop acting drunk.\n-Mullet-\n\nThis fish is rather dull, and doesn't seem to possess any 'unique' properties. The scales are grey and the fins wash to a colour fairly similar to cooked beef, which only puts me off even more. It can easily be distinguished because\nof its exceptionally long body and the 2 dorsal fins on both its back and belly.\n\nThese are quite commonly found around mountainous areas and weighs around 5lbs 11oz on average. A friend of mine volounteered to try this one, and\nactually quite enjoyed it, claiming it had a very unique taste that she would expect from an expensive restaurant, but said she didn't feel anything unusual after consumption.\n-Snakefish-\n\nFor some reason, I wasn't very happy with catching this fish, probably because it reminds me of my childhood obsession with snakes. Everything about this fish is remniscent of a snake, even the tail somewhat. It can be\ndistinguished by the pale pink scales across the body and the long fins that stretch by its sides. In fact, if it weren't for its fins, I'd say I really had caught a snake.\n\nFound in a river very close to a jungle and weighs around 5lbz 4oz.\napparently tastes like mutton with a much finer texture, but didn't have any unusual effects.\n-Salmon-\n\nThis fish is apparently popular among deepsea fishermen due to its high demand. It has an appearance similar to Mullet, but normally with a dark spotty texture along its back with a very subtle hint of red. The meat itself however is\nvery distinguishable because of its unmistakable salmon pink colour when raw.\n\nFound quite commonly near or in the Ocean, with an average weight of 7lbs 8oz. My friend said she loved the taste and would happily try more if I needed her to. No\nunusual effects were reported.\n-Lakefish-\n\nThese fish are slick and very oily, and also have a strong tail which they flail about madly when startled. This makes them fairly difficult to handle, especially with nets. The scales shine a variety of blues, usually lightest from\nthe back and gradually shading darker until it reaches the belly.\n\nFound very commonly in lakes and sometimes near thick wooded areas. Usually weighs around 5lbs 2oz, apparently tastes quite bland and has no unusual properties.\n-Magikarp-\n\nI really don't have much to say about this one. It's probably the most boring fish I've ever seen, despite how ridiculous it looks. The scales are very vibrant orange and the fins are equally as vibrant yellow. The eyes are very large\nand don't even look like they belong to a fish.\n\nI find these quite scarcely just about everywhere, and they weigh around 2.2lbs on average, depsite their average size. My friend told me it was the most boring thing she'd ever eaten and\nnothing even slightly unusual happened. The only thing slightly interesting about this fish is that it splashes around madly when pulled to land.", ""),
        StaticBook("Flagship WB I", "Ebs Telrunya", "The Flagship\n     War Bulletin I\n\nWAR IT IS: ULTIMATUM REJECTED\n\nLord Chancellor Buron of the Holy Kingdom of Oren approached the gates, calling out for Wulfgar. He was at Kal’Arkon to deliver a simple message: King Heinrik would not step down from the throne of Oren. This was the\ndemand made by the Urukan(Orcs) and Bortuan(Dwarves) after a series of incidents between Oren and different factions in the Fringe. Immediately after the message was delivered, the humans attempted to leave, but a\nscuffle broke out, and soon a rout ensued, with Zion forces chasing the Orenians all the way to their capital, Vekaro. There were many casualties on the Orenian side, with negligible losses inflicted on the forces of Zion.\nContents\nWar it is: Ultimatum Rejected \nKnown Incidents leading up to the Ultimatum\nInterview with Grand King Wulfgar\nInterview with His Rexcellency Erik’Azog\nInterview with Viceroy Ptah Reamnel\nInterview with Lord Chancellor Wilfrich Buron\nTreaty of Zion\nEvacuation to the Fringe\nVekaro Founded\nAlras Reestablished\nDwarven-Uruk Construction\nKnown Incidents leading up to the Ultimatum\nConclave Clash: King Heinrik attempted to attack the Concalve, was rebuffed by the uruks and possibly the dwarves. Orenian Raid on Krugmar: Orenians attacked the uruks at Krugmar,\nbut after a short seige, we flanked and wiped out by the dwarves and Alrasians.\n\nInterview with Grand King Wulfgar\n\nEbs: I’m sure the Council will not mind us using the Chambers.\nwant to thank you for agreeing to this interview with me.\nWulfgar: *nods.\nEbs: So, in light of recent events, it looks as if a war between the signatory nations of the Treaty of Zion and the Holy Kingdom of Oren is inevitable.\nWulfgar: Well, t’at ‘as yet tu beh seen. T’ere may yet be ruum fer peace.\nEbs: I see, What steps, if any, have you taken towards securing such a peace?\nWulfgar: Firstleh, I wish tu make it clear t’at t’e Treateh ov Zion wus nevuh\nintended as an alloiance tu launch an offensive assualt ‘awn Oren. But ‘un made in ordah tu show Oren t’at weh wud nawt stand fer anothah conflict, such ‘as ‘appened at t’e Conclave. Ah ‘ad ‘oped it would brin’ peace.\nSadleh, Oren ‘as interpreted it(The Treaty of Zion) as sumt’in’ qoite t’e opposite.\nEbs: I see. What exactly transpired at the Conclave? I’m afraid I have not heard much about the events you are speaking of.\nWulfgar: T’ere ar’ varyin’ accounts. Wut weh know is t’at it sturted w’en King ‘einrik marched ‘awn t’e Conclave.\nEbs: Were his(Orenian) forces intercepted? Wulfgar: T’e uruks wer’ at t’e Conclave at t’e toime, aye. Ah wus nawt t’ere\nmehself, but ah ‘ear t’ere wus certain’eh sum conflict. ‘O sturted it, ah fear weh will nevah know. Weh dwarves acted in neutraliteh, attemptin’ tu call t’e varyin’ factions tu Kal’Ithrun. T’ough t’ey all arroived, ah’m afraid little progress mus made.\nEbs: I recall.\nWulfgar: Oren wus intent ‘awn leadin’ an offensive against t’e Concalve fer reasons t’ey would nawt explain. T’ough ah’ve later baehn informed it wus’ over t’e apparenty existence ov ‘ochmeister Mirtok. Oren acted out ov fear alun.\nEbs: If negotiations fail, and war breaks out, how confident are you of a Zion victory?\nShouts of, “Legion, assemble!” and, “Wulfgar!” wring out. \nEbs: Well, it appears you are needed. I will not keep you. Thank you for your time Grand King.\nWulfgar: Aye, t’is nawt a problem.\nWulfagar, shouting: Aye?\n\nInterview with His Rexcellency Erik’Azog\n\nThe Rex: Nuw, wub duz latz wunt tu blah abut?\nEbs: I take it you have just returned from a battle with Oren?\nThe Rex: Yub.\nEbs: So, I have a few questions regarding the lead up to this war. From what I understand, you were in the Conclave when King Heinrik attempted to attack it. Is that correct?\nThe Rex: Yub, mi wuz blahin wif Darius.\nEbs: Were the Orenians merely passing through, or did they attempt to start a fight with your or the Conclave’s forces?\nThe Rex: Dey planned tu flat da citizenz uf da Conclave uva a flat ‘umie.\nEbs: Do you perhaps know the name of the slaim human?\nThe Rex: Yub, bud mi nub wunt to blah et.\nEbs: Very well, I suppose. I take it you fought with the Orenians. What exactly happened?\nThe Rex: Well, the Urenianz ztarted fyring\nun urukz zu wi tuuk actiun agh did da zame.\nEbs: So, you are certain the Orenians were the first to fire at the Conclave?\nThe Rex: Yub, dey wure da firzt.\nEbs: My next few questions involve the attack on the orcs by the Orenians.\nWere you personally there, and if so, what happened?\nThe Rex: Mi wuz nub dere perzonally. Mi wuz muzy duing udda dingz zuch az zetting ub da Trewty uf Zion wif da- udda natiunz.\nEbs: I see. To the best of your knowledge, what transpired?\nThe Rex: Umiez kun agh try to flat uruks.Muzt uf da tyme dey fail.\nEbs: Though, after that battle, you and Wulfgar decided to issue an ultimatum to Oren.\nThe Rex: Yub, wub abut et?\nEbs: Did you really think Heinrik would give up his throne?\nThe Rex: Nub, bud hi nub keepz hiz men. He givez hiz men tuu much freedum tu du wubeva dey want. Dat iz whi wi wunt him uff da thrune.\nEbs: I see. I have spoken to the Alrasians and Wulfgar about their vision for a post war Oren. Do you have any thoughts\non what it might look like?\nThe Rex: Mi wunt an urun dat nub gruks dat da udda racez ar lezzer den dem. Mi wunt a uren dat kant rayd agh gruk dat da udda natiuns wull du nubding. Nub tu mentium mozt uf dem ar dizhunurable.\nEbs: Well, that you very much for your time your Rexcellency.\nThe Rex: Yub, gug’ye Ebs.\n\nInterview with Viceroy Ptah Reamnel\n\nEbs: Thank you for sitting down with me. I suppose we should get right to it.\nI just recently skimmed your statement on the war, and your position intrigued me.\nPtah: How so?\nEbs: You called the current conflict a “war of mercy.” That is a road not usually traveled. Could you perhaps elaborate?\nPtah: The Kingdom of Alras has always desired to honor the debts it owes to other powers. Indeed: Oren was not and is not the only one in this respect. However, our complication is that, with humankind, those to whom we owe a debt are long dead.\nSuch is the unfortunate nature of the human curse.\nEbs: Indeed. So, I take it that you intend to repay the debt in a more… creative… way?\nPtah: However, the ideals of a person can be honored long after death. We believe that the Aegisian Oren\nto whom the debt is owed would not to desire to live as the deformed and bloodied shadow it is now.\nEbs: I see. You think that the current manifestation of Oren is not appropriate in the memory of individuals such as King Pampo Perea or Saint Dan?\nPtah: What you see beyond these hills stopped being Oren many years ago. It is vile to suggest King Pampo Perea, whom to him and his people our debt is owed, would be satisfied to label what exists now as ‘Oren’. Therefore, we shall act in accordance with\nthe ideals of the dead.\nEbs: I would assume that would include removing House Carrion from the throne?\nPtah: It would include removing any cancerous elements that can be identified.\nEbs: I see. What do you envision a post-war Oren would look like? How would it even get to that point?\nPtah: As with any birth, it shall be bloody at the start. But there is no reason to believe that the ideals of Old Oren cannot be reestablished\nas governing principles and social policy. I hope to one day see something similar to what I, and many other, remember.\nEbs: Would you be maintaining the Monarchy, at least for the foreseeable future?\nPtah: It is very likely, but that shall depend\non numerous factors. Recall: we are collaborating with the Dwarven cause, and so their interests in a reborn Oren will be answered to in a joint plan on both of our parts. Meaning, monarchy is very likely, but we are willing to listen if\nthe Dwarves know of a system that would resolve our interests, their interests, and the interests of the human race. \nEbs: Is it possible that all three nations interests could lie on the same path?\nPtah: The interests of Alras are with\nall inspection identical to that of true human ideals in this respect, due to the nature of our debt. The Dwarves too understand the desire for a reformed Oren as evidenced in the Grand King’s declaration.\nEbs: Well, I suppose that if you do win the war,\nPtah: Hope is what happens before the war, Mr. Telrunya. After, comes success or failure. \nEbs: Well, thank you for this… enlightening interview.\nPtah: It was a great pleasure. And now, there are grim deeds to be done.\nInterview with Lord Chancellor Wilfrich Buron\n\nI arrived at Vekaro, intent on interviewing the Lord Chancellor of Oren, Wilfrich Burton. After waiting around for an hour while he ran along the wall, I don’t know what to say.\nTreaty of Zion\n\nThree elven days ago, the leaders of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, Krugmar, the Kingdom of Alras, and the Conclave signed a mutual defense treaty and non-aggression pact name the Treaty of Zion. It could not help\nbut be noted that the Holy Kingdom of Oren was the only major power not to sign. The agreement requires that all signing nations refrain from attacking each other, as well as if one nation is attacked, that all the other nations must come to their aid.\nAt the time, it was thought this pact would prevent Oren from violating the territory of the other nations. However, now, it is expected to bring all four nations into the conflict with Oren. There is no way tell if the Treaty of Zion will survive the\ncoming chaos.\n\nEvacuation to the Fringe\n\nPredictably, after the gateway to the Fringe/Verge 2.0 was opened, there was a great flood of people colonizing the new land. However, unexpectedly,\nall major groups have migrated to the Fringe, leaving their lands in Anthos behind. It is almost comical that all these groups would abandon the land that they fought so hard to keep, but such is the way of the world. \n\nVekaro Founded\nVia an edict passed by the Church of the True Faith, the capital of the Holy Kingdom of Oren has been shifted to the town of Vekaro in the Fringe. Construction is under way, and a Maer is expected to be elected soon.\nHowever, the competence of Orenian officials have been called into question as of late, and with the coming war, it is unknown if the Orenians are in the Fringe to stay. At press time, it appears that Oren is attempting to centralize\nit’s military around the city. This move comes after several losses by Orenian forces to the Treaty of Zion nations.\n\nAlras Reestablished\n\nThe flame of Alras, under the dutiful rule of High King Syrio, has been\nrekindled atop the dwarven city of Kal’Arkon, the dwarven settlement in the Fringe. It is ruled by High King Syrio, once the richest people in the word. as well as the Council, which is made up of several familiar faces.\nDwarven-Uruk Construction\n\nThere appears to be a great deal of construction going on underground near dwarven and orcish lands. Eventually, after a terrible noise, the “Raidway” was opened between Urguan and Krugmar. It cuts travel times, though they\nwere pretty close anyway, so the more interesting aspect is whether these “raidways” will be expanded to other parts of the Fringe.\n\n~Editor-in-Chief Ebs Telrunya", ""),
        StaticBook("Flemer Part 1", "Harold Switzer", "He was moving towards the shop, He could'nt stop he wanted revenege on the man for what he did to his brother, Grumus. Johus Went towards the man, Drawing his dagger and ready to kill the dreaded murderer. Slowly the man who indeed'd killed his brother,\nturned around looking at Johnus. ''MURDERER'' Johnus shouted, ''Hm, Indeed.'' Carmly replied the murderer. ''YOU SHOULD BE ASHAMED'' Johnus Cried. Out of the blue, the murderer slashed johnus with his own dagger, killing johnus almost istantly. The murde-\nrer slowly walked away from flesen, With blood on his dagger and his own hands. But then, the guards spotted the corpse.", ""),
        StaticBook("Flora of Valior", "Illion Everion", "Forest\nAlabaster Leaf- A plant with alabaster hued leaves which grows around fallen trees in dry parts of the forest.\n\nBlazing Fern- A growing vine-like plant bright orange and red, known to change colors and be a useful ingrediant in alchemy.\nBlissfoil- A plant with blue flowers that numbs part of the body when in contact with the skin.\n\nBlistering toad- a small fungus with the appearance of a toad itself in which causes corrosive rashes should it be consumed.\nBlonde Blossom- A small, yellow petaled flower, occasionally featuring a white to yellow gradient; used for decorative purposes.\n\nCrouching feather- A plant with three big petals growing from the stalk which appear to look like feathers.\nFaerie Truffles- A fungi that is able to stop growth.\n\nFire flower- A rose like plant that bursts to fire when fully mature.\n\nFlametongue root- A rose like plant which releases spores to make one oversensitive to pain,\nand with a feeling of burning.\n\nKing's Ivy- A delicate flower found mostly growing in ancient ruins around the world.\n\nNight sap- A honey like substance that causes a sense of calmness and sleepieness but is highly addictive.\nRed rose- A small plant which has a pink to red gradient colored flower.\n\nSerpents stalk- An emerald hued stalk that grows on the side of water in forests which great properties heal burn wounds.\nShadeleaf- A small, short plant; causes hallucinations, used as a drug.\n\nThe crimson vase- A flower with great crimson colored petals in the shape of a vase; it is warm to the touch.\n\nTippens root- A purple flower which\ngrows next to dead trees in the forest; its roots smell horrible but stop bleeding in a wound near instantly.\n\n         Swamp\nAqua nymph- A small chain of blue baubles that grow under the water; used as a remedy for burns, not to be consumed.\nBiteit- A small non-toxic greenish mushroom that may have brown dots on it's top in which is used as an ingrediant in alchemy.\n\nBlistering toad- A small fungus with the appearance of a toad itself in which causes corrosive rashes should it be consume.\nJailer's moss- A sticky white moss that grows in caves in swamps.\n\nMandragora- A plant which grows in the shallow waters that releases paralyzing spores.\n\nSaffvil- A disgusting green grass that grows on dead animals and plants.\nSwamp Blossom- A flower of purple and green hues that grows on the branches of trees.\n\nThe Dwarfs Pumpkin-\nA shrub with orange-colored leaves which has a strong bad smell.\nJungle\nAtheros- A white brown and grey spotted root, found under trees, which is commonly used to reduce pain.\n\nFire flower- A rose like plant that bursts into flame when fully mature.\nSinged Kha- A useless plant, standing out from the usual foliage as its leaves extend with a wide red stain, only causing irritation to skin.\nTundra and snow lands\n\nAthin- An algae that apparently is able to make a swell lotion;\nthe process of finding suck is extremely difficult though.\n\nDrilltongue- A vine that can be used as a rope with the ability to create woven baskets, bags, etcetera.\n\nElfs hair vine- A delicate, ice-white vine that is a strong ingrediant in alchemy.\nElrow berries- Berries that are often used in poisons.\n\nFrost Vine- A small blue plant which grows in freezing enviroments, used to numb pain and loosen stiff muscles.\nDesert\nBlack sun's spinter-\nA plant that represents that of a black flower; it is said to prevent pregnancy in women, should it be eaten a few hours before mating.\n\nBlood lotus- A small rust colored plant that grows in hot climates in\nwhich is used as a dietary supplement, providing several vitamins and nutrients to the consumer.\n\nCactus- Better known as 'cactus green'- it causes a sense of euphoria for the user; the plant can be found in every realm, usually abundance in orcish desert\nDesert berry bush- Appearing as a withered rose bush, the stalk of the plant is said to be poisonus, killing an animal after one day of consumption of the inner juices.\n\nDrakes tail- Yet another one of the rarest herbs in the realm, the briar has\nthe ability to offer a fever-inducing poison, also used sternly in alchemy.\n\nGoblins ivy- A brownish-green vine of the deserts; the ivy is used to make a scentless, tricky and mild poison.\nGijaklul- A rare desert flower that has an odor compared to that of rotting flesh; used with the potential of healing alongside maintaining an obscure, faint glow.\n\nJavens- A large sand spur with green colored stripes going along the plant, commonly\nutilized by field-doctors to reduce their patients' pain.\n\nZawabate- A plant with prominent hues of green and yellow, its petals short and curvey, and its stalk tall and proud; used for minor healing, though if consumed too heavily can\ncause severe and brutal delusions and mental illness, working as a mind-altering poison.\n\n        Caverns\nBronze dust- A substance that irritates the skin, having little to no use other than so.\nMiners helmet- A large mushroom found in damp corners, causes major damage to the nerve system upon consumption, failing to make a suitable potion.\n\nWisp breath- A nearly transparent plant that is known as one of the rarest in the realm; increases the\nspeed of a potion, fetches an extremely hide price in trade.\n\n         Oceans\nJokers scum- One of the rarest plants known to man, found growing at the deepest parts of the sea; it has the ability to disfigure one severly melting flesh.\nOther Locations\nlilypad- grown in many ponds.\n\nMelons- grown as food.\n\nOrcs braid- found in the entrance of sewers and other areas of waste.\n\nPotatoes- grown in farms.\nSpirit magnolias- Spirit of nature's body.\n\nWheat- grows in farms\n\nCryptus shroom- A small, flaky mushroom found on decaying bodies in dark crypts, used as a regent and dehydrator.", ""),
        StaticBook("Flower Boy", "Norman", "Hey its Norman, i found you some extra flowers, didn't know what colours you like so i got a whole bunch with pots too! anways there you go and i don't want anything in return\n\nFrom Norman :)", ""),
        StaticBook("Flower Language", "Elorna Avern Lle'hileia", "The Language\n       of Flowers\n\n\nA guide to the secret meaning given to each flower by the wood elves of old.\n\n    \n      In memory of\n      Mayilu Avern\n\n            ~*~\nWhen I was a girl I remember my mother walking with me through fields of flowers, pointing to each variety and describing what they symbolised. I do not know how commonly used this secret language was, but I will always remember the solemnity of my\nmother's voice as she told me the meaning behind each poppy and rose. Of course, the meanings given in this book do not describe the actual traits of each flower, simply the cultural meanings they are used to represent. One does not have to use this guide\nbut I hope it may inspire you while selecting a bouquet for a lover, picking a gift for a friend, or simply decorating your home and garden with life and color.\n\n\nThe Dove Druid,\nElorna Avern Lle'hileia.\nThe Dandelion\nThis simple flower is sometimes considered a weed, yet even that which is small and unassuming can hold hidden significance. \n\nMeanings: Fortitude, Constance, Faith, Wishes Coming True.\nThe Poppy\nThis deep red flower is often used medicinally to relieve pain or aid in sleep. It is often associated with both dreamers and the dead.\n\nMeanings: Dreams, Imagination, Mourning, Eternal Sleep, Relief from Suffering.\nThe Orchid\nThe orchid is as elegant as it is exotic, and its blue coloring is rare in the natural world.\n\nMeanings: Beauty, Refinement, Elegance, Fragility, Femininity, Rare Riches.\nThe Allium\nThese are a very unique looking flower, each one made up of thousands of tiny purple blossoms that form into a large, perfect sphere.\n\nMeanings: Perfection, Royalty, Many Children, a Prosperous Family.\nThe Azure Bluet\nSometimes called Eyebrights, they are a pale blue that often appears white. They are sometimes considered a symbol for the Druidic goddess Cerridwen.\n\nMeanings: Fertility, Motherhood, Peace, Cleanliness.\nOxeye Daisy\nWhen you see these daisies - actually chrysanthemums - in bloom it is always a sure sign of summer.\n\nMeanings: Innocence, Simplicity, Modesty, Shyness, Youth, Summer.\nThe Lilac\nLilacs are clusters of tiny purple blossoms that grow on leafy green bushes, and are quite popular for their aromatic scents.\n\nMeanings: New Love, Sweetness, Affection, Flirtatiousness, Spring.\nThe Sunflower\nThe sunflower is said to always point toward the sun. We could all learn something from the sunflower about optimism and looking on the bright side!\n\nMeanings: Hapiness, Sunshine, Good Luck, Good News, Friendship, Cheer.\nThe Peony\nThese flowers come in soft, pastel hues, their blossoms made up of many layers of petals. They are often associated with the wealthy and high-born.\n\nMeanings: Riches, Honor, Pride, a Carefree Life, Greed, Extravagance.\nThe Tulip\nTulips come in many varieties and can mean different things depending on color.\n\nGeneral Meaning: Fame.\nRed: Declaration of Love.\nOrange: Hope, Bright Smiles.\nPink: Purity of Love\nWhite: Honesty, Sorrow.\nThe Rose\nThe rose is one of the most iconic flowers of romance and love. Depending on how the rose is presented, it can have many meanings.\n\nFull Rose: True Love, Sincerity, Respect.\nRosebud: Innocent Love, a Pure Heart.\nThe Fern\nThe fern is a simple, green plant that bears no bright colors nor scented blossoms. Its reserved simplicity is used as a contrast to dazzling flowers.\n\nMeanings: Old Age, Wisdom, Mystical Knowledge, Sages.\nThe Ivy Vine\nIvy is another green plant that, while not a flower, holds significance in the language of flowers. \n\nMeanings: Wedded Love, Fidelity, Faithfulness, Loyalty, Eternal Ties.\nThe Mushroom\nMushrooms are not often used in bouquets or arrangements, yet they hold strong symbolism, especially in Druidic circles.\n\nMeanings: Magic, Prophecy, Visions, Virility, Masculinity, Long Life, Spiritual Journeys.\nThe Leaf\nThe symbolism and meaning behind each tree would take another book itself, but here are a few meanings associated with tree leaves:\n\nOak: Strength, Nobility, Virtue.\nBirch: Healing, Rebirth, Spirits of the Dead.\nPine: Ancient Wisdom.\nAnd so concludes this book, may it broaden your understanding of the natural world and its many hidden intricacies. May your life be long and happy, and may the Aspects guide your path.\n\n\n           ~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("FLYER", "Judas Windsor", "Dear Sir/Ma'am\n\nI'd like to inform you that Francois d'Aumont is merchandising goods. \n\nHis shop is located in Felsen. If you'd like affordable prices even if you are minas deprived, this stall is the place for you.", ""),
        StaticBook("FLYER", "Wedgytarianism", "-+=-+=-+=-+=-+=-+=-+=-+=-The Bruised Hammer\nSmithing Guild\n----------------------------\n\nImprove your adroitness\nin Smithing.\n\nSpeak to:\n\nMeister John Locke\n\nMeister Eligius\nLocation: Summerhall", ""),
        StaticBook("Food Menu", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Roth Jayamen's\n       Restaurant\n           and\n      Entertainment\n      Establishment\n\n\n      -----------\n           Food\n           Menu\n    --------------\nPg. 3: Beef Dishes\nPg. 10: Pork Dishes\nPg. 22: Mutton Dishes\nPg. 27: Baked Goods\nPg. 39: Vegetable\nDishes\nBeef Dishes\n\nSeasoned Steak\n\nA well-seasoned, good cut of beef.\n\n4 Minas\nPrime Rib\n\nA Great cut of beef seasoned and grilled to perfection.\n\n6 Minas\nSmall Beef Sandwich ((Burger and two bread))\n\nA Rounded piece of beef between two pieces of rounded bread.\n\n7 Minas\nRegular Beef Sandwich\n\nA good amount of cooked beef put in between two flattened loafs of bread.\n\n8 Minas\nSeasoned Beef Soup\n\nA bowl of Beef Soup with herbs cooked into it.\n\n5 Minas\nBeef and vegetable stew\n\nA bowl of hearty beef stew with beef, potatoes, herbs, and carrots cooked into the broth.\n\n10 Minas\nBeef Noodle Soup\n\nA bowl of beef soup with herbs and noodles cooked in. \n\n6 Minas\nPork Dishes\n\nSeasoned Pork chop\n\nA well-seasoned, good cut of pork.\n\n5 Minas\nPork Cutlets\n\nBits of pork lightly battered then grilled.\n\n6 Minas\nPork Sausage\n\nA Large Pork Sausage with mild spice added.\n\n4 Minas\nSeasoned Pork Soup\n\nA bowl of Pork Soup with herbs cooked into it.\n\n6 Minas\nPork and vegetable stew\n\nA bowl of hearty Pork stew with Pork, potatoes, herbs, and carrots cooked into the broth.\n\n10 Minas\nPork Noodle Soup\n\nA bowl of Pork soup with herbs and noodles cooked in. \n\n7 Minas\nSausage and Eggs\n\nA pork Sausage seasoned with slight spice cooked along with two eggs, they come well-done unless otherwise specified.\n\n8 Minas\nHam Omelet\n\nLarge bits of ham cooked into an egg omelet with some added herbs.\n\n\n7 minas\nSausage Omelet\n\nLarge bits of pork sausage cooked into an egg omelet with some added herbs.\n\n6 minas\nSausage on bread\n\nA large sausage put in-between a cut loaf of bread.\n\n5 Minas\nHam and Cheese Omelet\n\nBits of ham and sweet cheese put into an egg omelet.\n\n10 Minas\nCheese and Sausage Pizza\n\nA large Flattened piece of bread covered in cheese and sausage bits, then cooked in an oven with herbs.\n\n12 Minas\nMutton Dishes\n\nSeasoned mutton chop\n\nA well-seasoned, good cut of mutton.\n\n5 Minas\nSpiced Kebab \n\nA Kebab seasoned and mildly spiced unless told otherwise. Can come with mild, moderate, or high spice.\n\n6 Minas\nSeasoned Mutton Soup\n\nA bowl of Mutton Soup with herbs cooked into it.\n\n6 Minas\nMutton and vegetable stew\n\nA bowl of hearty Mutton stew with Mutton, potatoes, herbs, and carrots cooked into the broth.\n\n10 Minas\nMutton Noodle Soup\n\nA bowl of Mutton soup with herbs and noodles cooked in. \n\n7 Minas\nBaked Goods\n\nA loaf of Herb Baked Bread\n\nBread that is baked with herbs. It is soft on the inside and crunchy on the outside.\n\n3 Minas\nPancake\n\nA mixture of dough, flattened and cooked in a pan.\n\n2 Minas\nButtered Toast\n\nBread, cut into thin slices and individually toasted and buttered.\n\n5 Minas\nCaramel Bread\n\nBread cooked with sweet sugar and caramel baked into it.\n\n4 Minas\nCream Pancake\n\nA mixture of dough and cream, flattened and cooked in a pan.\n\n4 Minas\nPancake with Butter\n\nA mixture of dough, flattened and cooked in a pan. It comes with butter.\n\n5 Minas\nPumpkin Pie\n\nA Sweet pumpkin pie. Baked and ready to eat.\n\n8 Minas\nCream Pie\n\nA very sweet Cream pie, made with lots of sugar and cream.\n\n9 Minas\nMelon Pie\n\nSweet Melon Pie, made with melon and sprinkled with sugar.\n\n6 Minas\nA Plain Cookies\n\nFour doughy Cookies, fresh baked.\n\n5 Minas\nButter Biscuits\n\nEight buttery, fatty, and sweet biscuits, baked to perfection.\n\n8 Minas\nCaramel Cookies\n\nFour sweet cookies, sprinkled with sugar.\n\n6 Minas\nVegetable Dishes\n\nPorridge\n\nA bowl or Porridge made with herbs.\n\n2 Minas\nPotato Chowder\n\nA bowl of Potato chowder, hot and made with seasoning.\n\n5 Minas\nPumpkin Soup\n\nSoup made with pumpkin and spices.\n\n4 Minas\nCheese Fondue with Dipping Dread\n\nA large pot of Cheese fondue with bread to dip in it.\n\n6 Minas\nVegetable Soup\n\nA Bowl of seasoned soup with carrots and potatoes.\n\n7 Minas\nVegetable Noodle Soup\n\nA Bowl of seasoned Noodle soup with carrots.\n\n4 Minas\nSalad\n\nA bowl of salad made with a mix of herbs, plant leafs, and carrots.\n\n5 Minas\nBaked Potato\n\nA potato baked with herbs in the oven.\n\n3 Minas\nPotato Chips\n\nDeeply fried and thinly sliced potatoes.\n\n4 Minas\nPlease remember to return all bottles and Menus!\n\nThank you and have a good day!\n\n~Roth Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Fool's Sword", "Bell Sano", "1550, 14th of the\nGreat Harvest\n\nFool's Sword\n\nLevi Shatar\nThe Fool's Sword is a steel longsword, which has been snapped into two seperate pieces. The tip is stained to the point of rust. Badly beaten and worn out, it was passed down to Levi Shatar by Richard Revlis.\nRevlis was a respected military figure in Dunamis, given the title of Marshall. During the time period that he was in command, the Oren Civil War was taking place, so it's assumed that the sword was forged around\nthe year 1500 or earlier. Seeing many battles, Richard Revlis passed the weapon down to his son, Danis Revlis, and then him down to Shatar. Upon obtaining the sword, Shatar pierced his own stomach with the sword in battle, causing it\nto snap into two pieces. His wounds were healed, but the sword remains broken. He came in contact with the sword about eleven years prior to him donating it.\nIt is unknown if Richard forged it himself, or if he simply used it in the Civil War.", ""),
        StaticBook("For Articfox11", "Drorhren Aretril", "Slap that ass you mother fucker", ""),
        StaticBook("For Ayche", "ThatWeirdGirl", "Dear Ayche,\n\nHey, weird head guy. Try not to suck at everything so much, you big idiot. I love you, don’t get a big head over that. Bye.", ""),
        StaticBook("For Fawn(a note)", "Izzy", "*The folded note has intricate cursive coiling and winding down the page. It's such a splendid work of art, one might think the author spent hours trying to perfect it. It's a shame the language is so simple.*\nHey. Don't bother with this guy, honest. I seen hundreds of folk try and talk to him.\n   You know what he does? Acts like an ass. You ask me, I don't get it. He ain't so special. \n   I mean, all he is is an ass, and that's it. No redeemin qualities.", ""),
        StaticBook("For Laureh'lin", "[Edict Ranger] Nephor Fortza", "Dear Laureh'lin,\n\n     I've noticed that the chest that usually contains bread is lacking some lately. Here is some bread for the community :)\n\n       Please do not take this book, as it it for the community to see.\n       -Nephor Fortza.", ""),
        StaticBook("For Lillith.", "Kyral Rilann", "A lovers dance is patient and kind\nIt feeds your heart, soul and mind\nIt brings you joy and happiness within\nKnowing that he or she will be with you\nThrough thick and thin.\nA lovers dance can be recaptured\nOnly if the partners heart has not been\nFractured.\n\nA lovers dance has no mistakes\nIt plays no one not even games.\nA lovers dance is slow and kind\nEasy to learn but hard to find.\n-------------------To you I give the whole me\nFor I believe that you're my destiny\nTo you I offer every best of my heart\nFor I believe that you will value it \n\nI want to share my whole life with you\nFor me to show that my love is true\nI want to hold you in my arms \nAnd sing you songs and lullabies\n\nLoving you is what I want to do\nAlthough I know that it can make me blue\nCause tears in my eyes has nothing to do\nIf I'm with a woman that is you\n-------------------Through you I can be everything that I long to be\nFrom walking in the park to dancing in the dark\nTo as far as ones imagination can see\n\n\nBefore you came into my life I was just an empty shell\nWho thought that I would always have to\nRemain here in my own hell.\n\nEveryone takes something for granted each and every day\nFrom a simple walk without being yelled at, to the feel of one's touch\nUntil it's taken one does not realize how those\nSimple things are missed so much\n\nOften people live in the past while their\nPresent moves by so incredibly fast\nWhen one needs to stop and smell the roses\nInstead of letting them pass right by their own noses\n\nPeople come and go through out your life\nLike fleeting thoughts running through your mind\nThey also speak of kismet; many never get it,\nsome never know it\nWe don't choose it because it chooses us.\n\nYou were the one that came into my life\nYou found a place in my heart\nSo from this moment on we will never be apart.\n------------------\nLillith,\n\nI know you know I love you, and I know you love me. I haven't felt like this, even with Elwen, in a long time. I feel proud of myself, proud of what I have done (Except the ghoul thing) and I wanted to show you\nhow much I appriciate you for everything you are and ever will be.\n\nIt has been an incredible journey to redemption so far, but its not done yet. I just want you by my side forever. I will be proud to be your lover no matter what.\nI hope you enjoyed these poems, and this is a more personal thing toward you, feel free to put it where ever though. I am proud to call you my wife.\n\nMy soul.\nMy eternal mate.\n-Kyral ♥", ""),
        StaticBook("For Orithur", "Raziel", "I found what seems to be an artifact that you have, possibly stolen from you. It looks like the remains of a mask of some sort. The man I killed seemed to be insane. I've read about one of the artifacts you have make people insane when they touch it, the\nman I had to kill himself was storing it in a metal box.\nSend me a bird for more information.\n-Raziel ((Dracofire))", ""),
        StaticBook("For Valmir.", "Parion", "Darling Valmir,\nThe passing elven days have been somewhat troubling and reflective upon both my nature, the fragility of my condition and the vast differences in our mechanisms – especially in regards to an impurity which we both have obtained.\nYour presence has been somewhat deficient as of recent and, surely, I assume you must possess countless duties upon your person; though do not suspect I feel anything less than admiration for your obligations.\n*The cursive paragraph following is obscured beneath the looped scrawling and blotches of ink used as to conceal its former contents.*\nHere I shall offer you my heartfelt apologies, since I must cease my endless nonsense. You are familiar with my habits, I often amplify my writings with trivial subjects so that the topic at hand may be avoidable.\n\nWithout further hesitance:\nI will admit I am not satisfied with my elected arrangements, alas, I could merely bear this state of impurity which exhausts my mind and perception when all had been settled.\n\nI am residing in Felsen, at the “Poorfellows of Saint Daniel’s”.\nI admitted our relations to a man, Father Charles; and further matters concerning my torment. For once it was treated no more than an inconvenient scratch, where the skin may be mended and the injury be forgotten -\nthe foulest outcome being simple fragmentations of what was once exposed, little more than a scar. He further proposed a cleansing and additionally has delivered oneself with sufficient security and confidentiality towards,\nwhat they have identified as, sodomy.\nDo not fear that the delicate tenderness I deliver unto you – the tenderness that has seized my existence – will grow faint. The lone cause for this solution has been that primarily the result of my recent\nexploitation, at the fault of the substances I may have sampled in excess.\n\nThough I regret my decision and have despondently exchanged my standard of living – my attire now being coarse wool rags and a life of thoughtless worship –\nI wish to remain here for some time. Whether or not my judgement remains distorted by the thought of a broadcast of our relations, now known by him. \n\nI will sign this piece now as to deliver it to you with haste.\nI apologise if it lacks explanation.\n\nVan'ayla.", ""),
        StaticBook("For You", "Nephor", "\n\n     I hope you like the room I made just for you!\n\n\n\n                   -N", ""),
        StaticBook("Formation V1", "Matthias", "Formations are the key to military discipline, at least that is what I have found. Here are a few that I have found prove useful to remember:\n\nStanding formation(Call to Attention):\n\nx x x x x\n\n^\nHighest rank to lowest.\nLine formation(vertical)\n\n  x\n  x\n  x\n  x\n  x\n  x <This being the highest rank at the front of the line.\n\nThis formation may be used in the Rallies at Felsen, in which case, to put some\nperspective on it, it would look like this:\n\n  x    x    x    x\n  x    x    x    x\n  x    x    x    x\n  x    x    x    x\n  x    x    x    x\n  x    x    x    x\n\nLike so.\nThe Platoon of Pompourelia in battle should look as follows:\n\nArchers:\n \n  x   x   x   x   x   x   x\n\nFootmen:\n \nx   x   x   x   x   x   x       x   x   x   x   x   x   x\nThe archers are the back line, firing volleys over the footmen, the footmen are to charge once the archers have slowed their volley. If they are defending, archers would be constantly firing arrows into the fray whilst the footmen would come in as the\ncharging troops reach their line at which point they would pick off stragglers and then focus on the tough enemies left behind who were perhaps missed by the arrow fire.", ""),
        StaticBook("Forum of 1527", "Iat", "What does it mean to be mali'aheral?\n\nAre we not what we are because we are together?\n\nThus mali'aheral is not but one of us but the collective.\n\nThus what is the collective?\nIs the collective simply a gathering of thoughts or is is a goal to achieve unity?\n\nWhat is unity?\n\nIs unity not but the undiscerned agreement from the mass?\nThus if we seek to reach unity is it not our duty to each other and not ourselves? \n\nDo we hold value in self-image or do we value unity and preserverance of our culture?\nDo destroy or limit each other in any means is to limit the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya and thus an act of greivance against all mali'aheral.\n\nTo deny access to public institutions is to limit.\nTo fail to offer ways to expand ones knowledge is to limit.\n\nTo take from the state is to take from each citizen of Haelun'or personally and in doing so commit a greivance against maehr'sae hiylun'ehya.\n~ Thoughts on unity.\nA public forum.\n\n14th  of The Deep Cold, 1527\n\n\nMaehre'sae Hiylun'ehya", ""),
        StaticBook("Foul Play", "Hileia'elr", "-----Foul Play-----\n\nWritten by Hileia'elr\n\nCan a simple man overcome his feelings for the most lovely creature he's ever met; Or will he have to express his true feelings?\nIt was a day like any other in the Caliphate. The sun was shining, there were few clouds to be seen, and there were plenty of travelers coming to Al- Wakhrah looking to make some coin, or buy some supplies.\nIn fact, for Larrion, it was the perfect day to run a shop. His store was flooded with customers, wanting to buy some goods from the man. Larrion would shout out, pleading with the sea of people in his tiny shop to make a single-file line.\nAfter about an hour of the alchemist selling to the large amount of travelers in his shop, a man in a red hat approached the counter. It was his friend, Keltran. \"Aye, Larrion, how you doing?\" Larrion simply groaned, wiping off the counter.\n\"What do you want?\" Larrion said with a neutral tone.\n\n\"Well...\" Beltran began, \"I felt somewhat sorry about what I did to you a while ago...\"\n\n\"Wait.\" Larrion started. \"What did you do now?\"\n\"Oh! S-So you don't know?!\" Keltran exclaimed.\n\n\"You fool... The hell did you do now?\"\n\n\"U-Uhm... Why don't you go for a nice walk while I watch your store?!?\" Keltran nervously stated.\nLarrion gave him a dead look. \"This isn't over... Here are the keys.\"\n\nAs Keltran watched the store, Larrion walked out of his shop, turning to the left to see the lines of small stores set up.\nHe walked pass the fountain, and made a sharp turn into his friend's store.\n\nAs he opened the doors to the small shop, he noticed a person behind the counter, sorting some books.\nIt was none other than Netiley the Vixen. She was sorting her collection of magic books, guides, and novels for sale.\n\n\"Ooh, hello, Larrion!\" she said. \"Have you come for your royalties today?\"\n\"Er, yes...\" Larrion replied. \"How many of my books have you sold?\"\n\nNetiley plopped a brown sack on the counter. \"See for yourself.\" she said.\nAs Larrion opened the pouch, about 85 minas shimmered with a sparkling flare. Larrion then dipped his nose inside the bag and took in a deep breath.\n\n\"Aah, minas...\"\n\"Thank you, Netily.\" Larrion said, as he placed the pouch into his bag. \"Yuuup! No problem.\" Netiley replied.\n\nAs Larrion was just about to leave, he noticed yet another figure over the counter...\nIt was a chicken. A small, white, chicken, sitting behind Netily on it's lap.\n\nLarrion stared for quite some time. \"Who is that?\"\n\nNetily pointed. \"Aye, that would be Hegory.\"\nLarrion stared at the bird for moments, when he finally asked, \"Can we go upstairs? I want to introduce myself to your friend.\"\n\nNetiley shrugged, and opened the door to the upstairs area for him and Hegory.\"\nAs Larrion and Hegory sat down at a table for two, they stared eachother in the center of their eyes for quite some time. It was only a minute or so, but to Larrion, it felt like hours.\n\nLarrion broke the iceberg.\n\"So... what is it you do in the shop?\"\n\nThe chicken made a clucking noise.\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nLarrion placed his elbows on the table, and rolled his eyes.\n\"Do you have any hobbies?\"\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nFamily?\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nJob?\n\n\"Cluck.\"\nAt this point, Larrion decided to talk about himself.\n\n\"Well, I am especially interested in alchemy. Aside from that, I run a small store.\"\n\n\"Cluck. Cluck cluck, cluck-- Cluck cluck cluck, cluck CLUCK!\"\nAt this point, Larrion was blushing. Never before had anyone shown such compassion, such sympathy, and such care for what Larrion went through everyday. He finally found someone who would listen to him.\nLarrion removed the goggles that rested on his eyes, and held Hegory's left wing in between his own two. Larrion bent down to kiss the top of his love interest's wing, and smiled. Hegory couldn't smile, but instead looked to the ceiling.\nThe very next day, no one could seem to find Hegory or Larrion. Any sign of the two ever being there in the first place had vanished. As everyone searched for them, little did they know that the two were already at the docks, planning their new lives.\nThe two decided to live out at sea on a house boat. For the next 15 years, the two lovers would survive off of fish and fried eggs. They met few people during their time at sea, and that's just how they liked it...\n-The End", ""),
        StaticBook("Fourth trimutair", "Deltion", "Hello reader I must tell you what this book is about It is the events leading up to my monk freind having a vision of the green lady. This will be the events when HE helped save me and a lady then later on had the vision he no longer rembers but I still\ncan so as the last person who knows this I will spread the word. there will be a total of 7 books that will be given to 7 people depending on there title as I beleive this to be more of a prophicy more then anything. And so it began.\nEvent 1\nI met this monk and we went on a journey to find spike our leader so I can get my orders as an Initiate.\nWe met this stunning lady who seemed to keep it a secret where he was so we began to argue with her she knocked me unconcious and did nothing\nto my freind the next Time I woke she was on the ground about to die if the monk didn't save her. I got up walked over and we began to head to a medic house to help me and her out the monk saved us both before he began to sweat horrible so I picked him up\nand headed to the Cloud temple. HE asked to be at the alter where he medditated for a while at the lapis statue. HE sudenly woke up feeling better and her started to compulse and he was blown by wind where there was none\nEvent 2 prophicy \nHe then looked at the Emerald staute and said \"The green lady will rise \" then he was uncoincous again. I carried him away. And tried to find spike to tell him of this. But I couldn't find him so he was left at his house\nEvent 3 Denial\n\nLater I went to his house to ask him what he saw He told me he didn't see anything I then asked what the last thing he witnessed he told me the time he healed me. I told him what he told me and said he didn't rember this\nHe told me of the the 4 trimutairys and how the forth is unknown to most. I told him she will rise and he told me that no one knows the gender so it can't be a she I said But you said the green LADY will rise......................... She will come\nThis is the end but beware the Green lady will rise she is the fourth and will not be mistaken I know of this from a seris of events and I will Dedicate my life to the green lady No matter how hard it becomes I believe this will happen Open your eyes and\nbe prepared for when she comes again", ""),
        StaticBook("Fresh Memes", "Svadus Ulerar", "\"I spit bars and I spit hard.\"- Svadus Ulerar", ""),
        StaticBook("Friend or Enemy?", "Sofetios", "Friend or Enemy?\nBy Sofetios\nEverywhere I am I hide from your sight,\nIf it’s in the day,\nAnd especially at night.\nI am one of sleep’s worst enemies,\nAnd one of fear’s best friends,\nI grow ever more larger,\nAs your will begins to bend.\nIn the day I am more friendly,\nEspecially when it’s hot and I’m in sight,\nBut when it turns to night time,\nI’m sure to give you a fright.\nI am a mimic of sorts,\nI try to copy you while you walk,\nI even mimic other people,\nAlthough I cannot talk.\nEven when you go about the day,\nI skulk and kind of stalk,\nFear or fear not, I am always here,\nI am the shadow on which you walk.", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost", "[Blind] Frosty", "The winter cloud,\nit doth appear,\ndoes cast far down,\nwhat once was near.\n\nBut if it's fall,\ndoth lie here,\nits mighty presence\nwe'll revere.\nThrough its beauty,\nwe'll see fear,\nere it's remnants\npersevere.\n\nIts soulful cries,\nus doth surprise,\nat moon's crescent,\nin our eyes.\nThe howling scream\nof the wind,\nfollow all\nuntil the end.\n\nBut at night's end,\nwhen all is clear,\naround the bend,\nthe future's near.\nThe freezing cold,\nshows the ways,\nthe ways that we\ncan die today,\n\nThrough this all\nwe think of fall,\nthat left so quickly,\nworst of all.\nTo ponder why\nwe wait all night,\nfor the storm\nto pass us by,\n\nwould only bring us,\ndreams and lies,\nlooking at\nthe snowy sky.", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Kings", "Bastion Curthose", "Up in the Northernmost lands of the kingdom, there are signs. Signs of the past and the future. All around us, there are signs of how this world will end, just as each before it has. It will end simply because of the Frost Kings. Think I am crazy?\nMaybe I am crazy, and maybe you're just crazy for not believing me.\nIf you ever wander into the north, you will see many strange things. Ruins of some forgotten civilization, established long before we arrived in Vailor. There are libraries with a few books in some odd text.\nThere is a floating castle and circles that glow in the night as though the sun still shone upon their ground. There are castles made of ice, and a whirlpool frozen in time. Now, none of these things were made by us, but I know who made them.\nThe Frost Kings. On a hill, deep in the frozen north, there is a troll. The troll is frozen, but somehow one can sense that the troll is alive. Up the hill from that is an old cave with some ancient, unopenable gate. Inside, however, there is a sign.\n'Frost Kings' is all the sign says. Suddenly, it all makes sense. Suddenly, one realizes how Vailor will fall, and it shall be by a force that came long before us.\nThe Frost Kings were an ancient group of people. Belonging to an unknown race, they mastered the art of magics and created a very advanced civilazation. As apparent by the many creepy temples in the north, they were likely a pagan society.\nLikely one that thrived off of the darker sides of magic. However, their magic couldn't save them, and something happened. Something which forced the 'Frost Kings' underground. In this cave they hid, and there they remain.\nThey might be dead, but that would be too easy. No, they can't be dead. They are very much alive. Alive, and waiting. Waiting for a chance to strike. When whatever forced them underground wears off, expect war. These are beings of great power.\nThey will show no mercy, and it will all start in the north, wiping out Oren. At first, some races may think of it as a blessing before they too are swept away by the Frost Kings' might. Eventually, we will have lost everything.\nBut fear not my brothers and sisters, for we can stop this menace. We must spread the word and await the return of the Frost Kings. Once they return, and if they do so with hostile intentions, we must rally together!\nDwarves, Kha, Humans, Elves, and Orcs alike must take up arms to defend these lands! Only then may we perservere! Only then may we survive! Until then, let us pray to God that I am crazy and none of this is true.\nSigned Formally,\n-Unnamed Author\n\nWritten in 1546, during the Sun's Smile.", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Witches", "OpaqueGlass", "Frost Witches:\nBy Ikail The Witchhunter.\n1: How to spot one.\n2: When you find one.\n3: Their weaknesses.\n4: Their motive.\n5: A Frost Witch.\n6: Traditions.\nCredits\n=======   1  =======\nTo spot a Frost Witch. You need a keen eye, but you must remember they can only be female. One of their main traits are sharp teeth. So if you suspect a frost witch. Focus on their mouth, see if they are hiding their teeth with their\nlips, or if maybe you might get a glimpse of the their teeth. They will always be sharp. Another trait is stone cold skin. Their skin is like the skin of a corpse. It is cold, and has no blood behind it. So, again, if you suspect someone of being a frost\nwitch. Maybe brush lightly against them, and gauge the temperature of their skin. Or maybe you could politely ask to feel their skin. If they deny, then see if you can glimpse their teeth.\n======== 2 ========\nIf you find a frost witch, tell her she is a frost witch. Frost Witches are required to grant a boon to anyone who discovers them while they are in their illusion. If they are out of their illusion, and you survive. Find a witch hunter\nand they will help you kill the witch.\n======== 3 ========\nA frost witch must grant you a boon if discovered in their illusion. This can be used against them. If you know they are a frost witch, maybe it would be better, to instead of fighting them. Enlighten them of your knowledge about them.\nThis makes them grant you the boon, and with this you can manipulate them into traps, where they can be killed. \nAnother weakness is fire. Obviously, they are weak to fire. It melts their illusions and combats their frost magic. Use this against them with\nflaming swords and arrows, or even just torches.\n======== 4 ========\nYou may be wondering, why do Frost Witches do all of this? Well. Here is the answer. Without male flesh. A Frost Witch will perish. The curse (I will speak of it later) makes their bodies dependant on male flesh. They don't start out\nas bad people, they try to contain it. But they simply can not survive without male flesh. What happens is, their life force wastes away within them, because male flesh isn't there to support it, and their innards convulse, causing them all kind of\npainful symptoms and torture till they are forced to eat male flesh. The more male flesh they consume, the more dependant their bodies become on it. This ravages them and turns them into killing monsters, always out to eat men.\n======== 5 ========\nI probably should have covered this earlier, but I assumed if you were reading this you would know, but I might as well add it in for people who don't.\nA Frost Witch is a woman, cursed by a Witch mother. The curse turns their teeth\nsharp, and their skin pale and dead. It also drives their bodies to become dependant on male flesh. The curse can be seen as a small blue spot on the back of their neck. Often a women might not even notice that they are cursed till they find the first\nsymptoms. Often the shame of being cursed will drive them to run from all they know into the mountains. Where they will be taken in by their coven. Often owned by the mother who cursed them.\n======= 6 =========\nFrost Witch tradition.\nFrost Witches act in groups known as 'Covens.' These covens are all governed by a Witch Mother. Who trains newly cursed women, and spreads the curse. A coven is created when a frost witch becomes of excessive\nprowess. They will then come across another coven. And will fight the leader. The winner is respected by all other members of the covens, and through a aged ritual. They will give her the boon of spreading the curse. She will stay a witch mother till\nanother frost witch comes and overtakes her. Again, the same ritual will be passed. It is tradition that if a frost witch kills a man, she saves a part of the man for the Witch Mother.\nThank you to the Witch that granted me a boon for capturing her. My request was that she answered my every question about Frost Witches truthfully. Thank you to my many other Witch Hunters who helped me track down the witch. \nAnd of course. Thank you to\nyou for reading.\n\nIkail The WitchHunter.", ""),
        StaticBook("Frosty Base Map", "Zeliek", "[!] Within the book rests a rather detailed drawing of a map. Upon one side of the map is drawn a large city of sorts with the name \"Vanaheim.\" wrote across it. The other side has a large ruins of sorts ontop of a snowy mountain, with the words-\n\"Frost Witch Coven.\" writen across it. Between the two drawings is a path detailing the way in order to head to the ruins.\n\n((Coords X 129 Z -3742 ))", ""),
        StaticBook("FSOE Pt. 1", "David Enrique", "=-----------------------------------=\n\n         Fifty Shades\n           \n             Of\n\n           Enrique\n\n\n=-----------------------------------=\nAny other day. That's what David expected it to be in the land of Athera, during the year 1500 as he set off on a stroll down the streets of Salvus. It was the old Salvus! Where people lived.. Relatively happily with the small, gradually growing -\n- population of Salvus. People never knew what the future of this republic would be, but ultimately in the present time, things don't seem too well. But change is always good! But this is not a propoganda book, or one on the history of Salvus! This.. -\n- tells a greater story. The story of David Enrique's erotic day in Salvus. Once again, he had no knowledge of what was to happen on that day, but it was definitely going to be an exciting, eventful one. He approached the tavern, where Linda was -\n- brewing and bartending peacefully and idly. But suddenly.. Her clothes. Her clothes? The light breeze from outside seemed to begin to pick up.. And h- They're off! Her clothes simply ripped off, right away! \"David! DAVID!\" A voice ringed -\n- repeatively in his head as he stared intently at Linda, her cheeks growing a rosy red colour. \"DAVID!\" Was screeched one more time, as he shook his head back and forth, and snapped back to reality. He was in fact still in the tavern, but Linda -\n- was fully clothed, and  they weren't alone. \"David!\" Linda growled out, with a hint of anger in her tone. \"You still owe me money, better get me it soon.\" David silently nodded, still taken aback. His imagination usually doesn't go crazy -\n- like that, so he was quite suprised by his own actions! He disregards it, swinging around to seat himself beside the legend.. Kolohe Finn. \".. Er. Kolohe. What are you doing here? I usually.. /Never/ see you just in the Salvus tavern.\" -\n- \"Oh.\" He responded, bobbing his head up and down idly. \"I simply was here to see Luxeanna, we've been growing quite close lately, have you heard?\" He says this with a sly smirk splaying across his face, indefinitely implying something. -\n- As Luxeanna swung the door open to the tavern, David's eyes just seemed.. instinctively glued to her exposed thighs. He knew this wasn't right, as he should take some time from relationships, as he just -\n- got out of a suicidal, depressed state from his last divorce. But there was something about Luxeanna. The exposed thighs.. The.. Exposed thighs? The exposed thighs.. and the.. exposed.. thighs. He just really had some -\n- weird ass fetish for thighs, it seems! Ah, David, you were always a strange one. As David silently had some.. even increasingly stranger thoughts go through his head, Kolohe and Luxeanna conversed until -\n- he was snapped out of it by non-other than Luxeanna herself. \"David! How have you been doing. We haven't talked much lately.\" A wry grin came across her face, as she leaned forward into the table, which made her dress, willingly or unwillingly, -\n- slip down her shoulder a tad, causing her to show off her cleavage a bit, whether if she was meaning to or not, David was also drawn to that. \"Uhm.. Good, good!\" Today was a special day, as Luxeanna cut right to the chase. -\n- \"Well.. I actually need a bit of help in the Bard's Guild.. Can you come with me?\" She gestures her hand towards herself, hopping up to her feet, and pacing out of the tavern. Kolohe jaw hangs wide open as he stares at David slither out of -\n- his chair and trail behind her, him simply watching in disbelief. Luxeanna delivered her promise, taking him inside the Bard's Guild building. \"So.. What did you need help wi- WHA!\" David exclaimed, as Luxeanna abruptly pinned him to the wall. -\n- \"I needed you..\" She whispered into his left ear, giving a dramatic pause before continuing with her sentence. \"For some.. experiments.\" She giggled at her own statement, poking her tongue through her closed lips, and beginning to trail it up and down -\n- the side of his head. David simply groans in anticipation in response to her, and in impatience, rolls around to switch their positions now pushing her up against the wall. He reaches behind her, firmly grasping a handful of her hair, and -\n- yanking it back to get better access to her lips, which he immediately locks and slips his tongue inside, passionately and thoroughly kissing. \"Mm.. Luxeanna..\" He groaned into her mouth. She snickered against his lips, and moaned -\n- back in response. \"Oh.. Davi-\" She cut off her own words, wriggling her head away from his grip, and drawing her head back. \"Times up! Thanks for the experiment, David.\" She immediately shoves him out of the building, -\n- leaving David distraught, and with a look of genuine confusion across his features. \"Wait, what!\" He yelled out, hopping up to his feet. But his yelling effort was to no avail, as she ignored him, and went deeper inside the building.\n-\n- David emits an expasperated sigh, now pivoting around on his back heel, and departing back down the road, striding down the stone bricks. But then.. Another female.. Is that.. Was it.. It was.. Oh.. My creator.. What a beauty.. -\n- Oh. It was simply Tyrell Blavier and Roopak, conversing like regular black folk. \"Oh, hello you two.\" David nods  towards them in a friendly manner, before continuing along the stone path that would set his destiny.. into a woman's pants. -\n- Well, not really... For now. He casually strolled into the town square, where he saw Arenai Garense. He took immediate interest in her, so he paced up to the unsuspecting woman, and nonchalantly locked their lips. -\n- she.. Suprisingly smiled? And took hold of his hand, leading her to her inn room. They had rough fucking sex, had a baby named Ryder, and were planned to get married. Instead, she broke up with him in 1517, and -\n- fucked Glacio, which David was furious about. Even more so, he killed her afterwards, leaving his child in his hands. He didn't mind the taking care of the child part, that would just make him a horrible person. So.. This is more like.. 'The fifteen -\n- Year Erotic Story'.. And.. That's the story. David also got married six times in that duration of time.. So it wasn't really.. You know.. One marriage. It was.. M- Okay. I don't know why I am continously rambling on about this. That's the story, so -\n- you fucking happy? Thank you. Also, David wanked furiously somewhere in that timeline.. So. That's erotic too.\n--------------------------------------\n\n\n           THE\n\n\n           END\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------\n*A rough, bolded sketch up Luxeanna completely nude is drawn on the back cover of the book, a suggesting a and wry smirk splaying on her face, both of her hands however, shielding her breasts and privates. You pervert.*", ""),
        StaticBook("FTM, Issue I", "Archibald", "-+ From the Mouth +-\n\n   Good day, good night, or good evening, or even good morning. I am Archibald Vallero. This book is quite simple. I go around asking other people questions, sometimes deep and personal, and then scribe them down in this tome\nfor you all to read and enjoy. I've no bias this time when it comes to who I ask, though keep in mind the demographics of the Descendant races. Enjoy. \n\nI will begin this first issue with an answer from one of my friends, Zeliek, a paladin of Xan.\nQI: Do you prefer a dictatorship or a republic? Why?\n\nZeliek: \"Republic. I just picked one at random. I don't even know what you're talking about.\"\nQ2: Do you think that crucifying people like the Amyasmen do is worse than torture? If so, why?\n\nShariana: \"Alright, I think that crucifixion is taking the easy way to solve something. Because torture, you have a... Hand on experience with\nsomeone. Hm... I think that is everything, really. The Amyas' have no experience with torture, and I doubt that any of them would be man enough to try it.\"\nQ3: Do you think that magic, in the future, will cause unforeseen catastrophes? If so, why?\n\nSalendys Doomforged: \"It has in the past and it will keep happening as long as there are irresponsible mages around.\"\nQ4: Do you believe that one of the Descendant races should be exterminated from the face of this realm? If so, which one and why?\n\nLyria Serthek:  \"Absolutely not. Because we all have a right to live, and why slay off a /whole/ race? Only a certain\nfew should die, and not be compared to their whole race.\"\nQ5: Do you believe that one day we will run out of continents and land to return to?\n\nCharles Fournier: \"No, why not?\"\nQ6: Thighs or breasts.\n\nForrest Sarr: \"Thighs.\"\nQ7: Would you prefer a redhead with green eyes, or a brunette with blue eyes?\n\nJon Snow: \"Brunette, of course! Redheads are usually... crazy.\"\nQ8: Do you think that any Descendant race will become extinct within the next 100 years? If so, which one?\n\nExalprick Oxenfeldt: \"Um... Yes I'll smash all their heads, crush 'm against a wall! Put them on spikes!\"\nQ9: Is the abundance of mages within the realm causing more or less chaos?\n\nDain Stormcrow: \"There are an abundance of mages? From what I understand of magic, or at least one of its major philosophies is balance. If balance\nis not kept preserved, things go out of whack.\"\nQ10: Would you rather eat a raw spider, or have a silverfish placed in your ear?\n\nDemagol Doomforged: \"Spideh.\"\nQ11: Do you think that necromantic practices are simply misunderstood, or, truly, are they just evil? \n\nAsher: \"Um, misunderstood.\nQ12: Are the four Descendant races doing considerably well given their curses?\n\nCheza Stirling: \"Some are, some aren't. Some better than others. Each race is doing 'alright' I suppose. Each has land, but they have problems.\"\nQ13: Is there truly such a thing as 'good' or 'evil' in your opinion, or is everything just formed by the aengudaemons above?\n\nGuarger Tsouderous: \"Everything is based on opinion, Archibald.\"\nQ14: What would you do if you saw an Orcish cub being bullied by a group of elven civilians? \n\nRyder Sturtart: \"Pick the cub up and take him away.\"\nQ15: Would you rather have to assassinate a loved king, or kill a new born child? Which one and why?\n\nSam Beadoin: \"King. Kings are all corrupt, no matter how loved. At least, human kings are...\"\nQ16: Do you think that immortality is achievable? \n\nOan: \"Yes, I think it is. What one must ask themselves, though, is this: How much are you willing to give up for it?\"\nQ17: Were the 'golden' ages of Aegis overrated?\n\nCharis: \"I wouldn't know, but Mister KAlen speaks of Alras as if it were golden. So, I can't say no.\"\nQ18: Would you rather kill a past lover or an old, human man?\n\nLicia: \"I have no past lovers. I am sworn to Xan and the creator only.\"\nQ19: Are aengudaemons the cause of all issues in the world, or is it truly us who has caused all these faults?\n\nMithras: \"It's a mix. Aenguls and Daemons interfere and use us because of how flawed we are. All of us differentiate, we all hold differ-\n-ent views. It makes us easy pawns in their games, they're merely bored children, you see. It's like when a child plays with a chess set. We're the pieces.\"\nQ20: Do you prefer to eat something sweet or sour at night? And why? \n\nCaitlyn: \"Sweet. Sour never tastes nice.\"\nQ21: Are we really in control of our own lives? Is our fate chosen by us?\n\nDaemon: \"We are in control of our lives. Fate is for the weak who need something to look forward to rather than doing it themselves.\"\nQ22: Who would win in a fight to the death: Blundermore or Archmage Cataris?\n\nLuthar: \"Blundermore. Despite Liches' callous and insidious nature,  our trickery only goes so far against raw holy power.\"\nQ23: From Iblees to Setherien, what has been the Descendant race's greatest threat in your opinion?\n\nJa'Mukar: \"Setherien. Because Iblees nevever did anything and he was defeated quite quickly. Where as Setherien showed his face and not hide\naway in an unknown location.\" \n\n*Translated by me, his accent was very thick!*\nQ24: Will the Human empire of Oren eventually dissolve entirely in the future, in your opinion?\n\nHorik Storasvard: \"Nay! Oren vill be forever! Because dey have da drue faith in da creador! And dey are the stronges der es!\"\nQ25: Out of all the four kinds of architecture exhibited by the Descendant races, which race's architecture do you favor the most? \n\nSer Bjorn of Bearhill: \"Human. It makes me feel safe. Other nations buildings just look . . . disgusting.\"\nQ26: If you had immortality, what's the first goal you would want to achieve?\n\nBeth: \"Uh . . . Eat a bunch of cake.\"\nQ27: From elven women to human, which one would you say is the most attractive, hands down? \n\nOliver Crowley: \"Human. Better build and often faces have more beauty to them.\"\nQ28: Where did homosexuality originate, do you think? The high elves, perhaps, or the elven kind in general? Even another race, even?\n\nVuln Shadeleaf: \"I don't know where it originated, but it sure seems likely it started with the mali'ker.\"\nQ29: House Chivay or House Horen? \n\nDread Knight Lennox(Dread Knight Noxx): \"I don't prefer either . . . both are idiotic.\"\n\n*I decided to ask him another question!*\n\nQ30: Was immortality worth it?\nDread Knight Lennox: \"Indeed.\"\nQ31: Would you rather demolish an orphanage or build a brothel?\n\nDorian Hunter: \"Build a brothel. Obviously. It's obvious. Girls.\"\nThat's the end of this book. But do not worry, this is only part one! I'm thinking of writing up another quite soon, and there'll be questions just as humorous or serious in the next one as there was in this one. Thank you for reading. Also, I'd rather\nnot answer any questions myself until after the end of the second issue, thanks. \n\n       //---\\\\\n      //       \\\\\n     //         \\\\\n    //========\\\\\n   //              \\\\\n  //                \\\\\n //                  \\\\", ""),
