        StaticBook("Gratification", "Celestria Archdiamond", "Gratification\n\nBy Celestria Archdiamond\nDuring my most recent investigation, I have discovered that the ability to delay gratification starts young.\n\nThis may sound like a rather complicated statement so I’ll put it into more realistic terms.\n\nImagine that you want to buy a new home, but you're\nthinking that maybe you should wait a while.\n\nPerhaps you should see if the price comes down after a while, or perhaps you should make sure that you have enough cash to pay your bills first.\n\nDo you wait or not? Whether or not you can, delays\ngratification, there’s a high possibility that you’ve been this way since you were a young child.\n\nThis means that if you could not delay gratification as a young child, you will most likely not be able to delay it as an adult.\nIn an experiment, the researcher placed a single cookie in front of children.\n\nThey could either take the cookie immediately or wait ten minutes for two cookies.\n\nSeveral years later, children who could delay gratification were found to be more\nsuccessful, better able to cope with stress and frustration.\n\nChildren who couldn’t delay gratification were less successful, and had alcohol problems.\n\nTo summarize, if you want your son to be more successful, ensure that they can delay gratification.\nIf not, they are statistically more likely to be less successful.", ""),
