        StaticBook("Gray Wolf A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "As this is one book of many, I shall keep the introductions short. This book was made for the purpose of understanding the gray wolf anatomy in conjuration.\n   The types of organ systems that will be covered in this book include: nervous system,\nrespiratory system, skin, cardiovascular system, musculoskeletal system, digestive system, and urinary system.\n*Here you see a very intricate and detailed sketching of a gray wolf's shape being filled in with various strings and cords connecting into a central spinal location until it finally connects with a brain. It appears to be the nervous system.*\nNervous System: \n   The nervous system is made up entirely out of the animal's nerves, spinal cord, as well as the brain. \n   This part of the animal's system is there for the purpose of directing the rest of the body in its daily functions. It includes\nthe animal's instincts, the creature's mind, and all of the feelings that go along with it: including pain.\n   As for the gray wolf, there isn't a lot different about it as far as structure of the nervous system and how it performs its tasks.\n*Upon flipping to the next page, you are greeted with yet another intricately detailed sketching of a gray wolf. Instead of a nervous system, you see the lungs connected through the throat to the mouth and nose. It's the respiratory system.*\nRespiratory System:\n   Organs within this system include the lungs connected with the rest of the body to support blood with oxygen, as well as all the ways it connects with the mouth and nose to breathe.\n   The purpose of the respiratory system is\nin breathing the air around the animal to then supply the body with oxygen so that it may live.\n   As for the gray wolf, it works like any land-based animal would.\n*On the next page there appears to be various sketches in the same intricate detail as before. They seem to show various different layers of skin and what they look like. It's the skin of a gray wolf.*\nSkin:\n   Skin itself is a large enough complex to be warranted as its own system. Things that are inside involve the outer layer that everyone knows, and the inner layers including connective tissues, fats, and blood vessels.\n   The purpose of skin\nis solely for protection of the inner parts of the body from the external environment.    A gray wolf's skin is covered in a thick gray-white coat that not only helps protect the animal, but also adds an abundance of warmth.\n*Following the pattern, another detailed sketching appears upon this page. It shows a vast network of veins and arteries connected with the heart of the gray wolf. It's the cardiovascular system.*\nCardiovascular System:\n   This system involves the expansive network of veins, arteries, and the heart.\n   Blood is pumped through the body as a result of this system, giving nutrients to the entire creature so that it may live.\n   Gray wolves are\nsimilar to many other animals in that they have only one heart and it functions just the same.\n*Once again, a sketch is shown. Upon it you can see various different layers in how the muscles and bones are positioned within the body of a gray wolf. It's the musculoskeletal system.*\nMusculoskeletal System:\n   Within this system is all of the bones and muscles that give the creature shape and structure. These include joints, ligaments, tendons, and otherwise.\n   The bones and muscles of the body serve the creature by giving it not\nonly structure and shape, but also movement and strength. Via the nervous system, the creature controls its muscles and how they move, allowing it daily function.\n   A gray wolf is quadripedal in structure, and has fairly powerful jaws for a creature of\nits size. Otherwise, this system works just as you'd imagine.\n*The fully realized and detailed image of a gray wolf's mouth, esophagus, stomach, and the like is shown. It appears to be a detailed sketch of the digestive system.*\nDigestive System:\n   There are quite a few parts to this system. These parts include: the mouth, the esophagus, the stomach, the large and small intestines, the rectum, the liver, the gallbladder, and the pancreas.\n   To put simply, this system is in\nplace for the purpose of extracting nutrients from food and excreting wastes from the body.\n   Gray wolves are entirely carnivorous, meaning that their bodies will only prefer meat based diets.\n*A bit less detailed from what was shown previously, but you can tell that there are a few organs sketched into the frame of the gray wolf. It includes what looks like kidneys, and the bladder.*\nUrinary System:\n   Connected closely with the cardiovascular system, the urinary system includes kidneys, the bladder, the urethra, and all things inbetween.\n   Due to being so closely linked with the cardiovascular system, this system's job is in\nseparating wastes from the blood stream.\n   Otherwise, the gray wolf doesn't function very uniquely from other organisms in this regard.\nSide Notes:\n- Highly pack-oriented, gray wolves are vicious hunters, and should never be underestimated and always be admired.\n- Many gray wolves were harmed in the making of this book. Sorry again.\nList of Systems:\n- Nervous\n- Respiratory\n- Skin\n- Cardiovascular\n- Musculoskeletal\n- Digestive\n- Urinary\n*Upon getting to the end of the book, you see that all of the sketchings from all throughout the book have been downsized and placed next to each other for the last few pages, for quick reference.*t", ""),
        StaticBook("Great War", "Leyu", "The Great War\nOriginally published by Nashtoff Book Shop of Aegis\nThe Great War all started when the Undead moved to this world. They didnt seem as a big threat untill they attacked the City of Oren. With a massive force they seige the Gate House of the city. There were many guards to defend the city.\nAnd the battle has been won by the Humans. With the undead weaker from the defeat they start to ambush our Reconnisance groups. One time our King himself led a taskforce to The North. We didnt make it taht far. We were ambushed by a\nsingle Undead Supporter, and he killed the King. Luckily the King was restored back to health and we took no deaths. :: :: A couple weeks later we send a massive force down the road to the North. We were quickly ambushed as we left the city\ngates. Hundreds of zombies and giant mutants Surrounded the road to the north. We took many deaths, but we still won the battle. With so many deaths in our Force, we had to choice but to retreat. The Undead Stops us that time. :: :: :: With the Undead\ncountering all our actions we had no choice but to stay in the Fortress of or en. Every small scouting mission there are no reports of undead. The guards that go on potral, report saying there are undead on the way... The Undead never come. :: :: ::\n*These Events Were based On What really Happened* :: :: :: There were other encounters with the Undead Most of the time there was only 1 person. The undead are weak, and arn't going to attack any time soon. There was this one prediction of the Undead\nTaking over Oren.... *By The Seconds Days Sunset The Undead Will Rise and Take Oren* Most people think this is a unreal prediction. While there is no evidence supporting this Prediction. But there also is no evidence supporting that either. But\nnoone knows the Answer. The Undead Still remain on this world. :: :: There has been also a couple flaws in the Generals Reaction to these threats. When there is a threat from the undead, the general quickly make action (which is good). He Lines his men\nup and makes them wait in line for 3 days times. But if there is a real threat well fight them back. :: :: Overall the undead is no match for the Oren Guards and the Human spirit. :: :: Published By Nashtoff Book Shop\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grogak", "Thurak'Yar", "The Tale of Grogak\n\nThere lived a goblin, Grogak, out in the desert because he appreciated the solitude. One day, however, he saw a dwarf digging through the snd in search of some treasure. Grogak was displeased because he was\ndisrespecting the desert. The young goblin approached the dwarf and attempted to reason with him that there were no diamonds to be found under the sand; but to no avail. Grogak then puffed out his chest and demanded that he leave; the puny dwarf complied.\nSome years later, an elf came along, who sought to turn the desert into a forest. The goblin demanded that the elf leave, but he had too much pride in his work. Grogak then reasoned with him, and convinced him that the desert must exist to bring balance\nto the world. Some years later, a band of humans arrived in the desert, and set up camp. They began to dig aimlessly, and as with all human actions, it is unclear if even they knew what they were doing. Whatever the reason, the humans dug with up the\nsand with zest and purpose. Grogak was outraged, but he knew that the humans were both too proud to stand down, and too irrational to be reasoned with. The old goblin approached the humans and said,\n\n\"Oh how I love the way you till the sand and bring upon\nNew zest to the stale desert. I will pay you 50 minas if you return to do the same tomorrow.\"\n\nThe humans gladly accepted the offer, as they would have returned regardless. The next day, they worked with more vigour and enthusiasm\nthan the day before. Grogak paid them, and offered them the same for the next day; only this time they would only receive 25. This continued for a few days; Grogak asked them again to return for only 5 minas.\nThe humans disagreed, saying it would be foolish to accept this amount of work for so little pay. They packed up their camp and left.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grungron letter", "Farryn", "Dear Grungon,\n\nIt has been years since I have been sent away by Tahariae but I wish to tell you I have returned.\n\nI wish to meet with you on plans on the alliance between clerics and ascended, as well as perhaps learning a thing or\ntwo about how you are organised as a group, as well as of Ascended magic and operations. Why? I have realised I do not know much of the Ascended, thus I seek to learn of you so that in future times, such knowledge is useful. I am willing to explain about\nthe clerics as well if needed to.\n\nI hope this letter finds you all in good health and in safe hands, although I know Aeriel will not allow you all to fall into danger. I await your reply as soon as possible.\nMay the Aenguls watch over you all.\n\nSincerely, Elvira Naromis.\nCleric of Tahariae\nLeader of the Clerical Order.\n\nP.S: Next time, have at least one Ascended within your base. Stood in the rain for ten minutes before\nleaving as no one replied to my knocking.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guid to stores", "Llywellyn Oakleaf", "*&*\n           Guide\n            *&*\n\n--> to the weapon and\ngear storage.\nHQ = 40%+\nMQ = 30%-39%\nMLQ= 20%-29%\nLQ = 0%-19%\n\nHQ means High quality\nMQ = Medium quality\netc.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide To Fishing", "Za'Kabar", "A Guide On Fishing\n   \n   Introduction:\n\nFishing is a great skill to have. You can either fish for fun or to catch something to eat. The good thing about fishing is that it is not hard to learn. It just takes time and practice. This book-\nwill be your guide to the world of fishing. I hope you enjoy reading and i hope you enjoy fishing.\n\nPicking A Fishing Spot\n\nYou should pick a spot where you enjoy going. Some place you that is relaxing and peaceful but also-\nsomewhere with a fair amount of fish to catch. Lakes and rivers are good places to fish but many people prefer to ocean fish.\n\n      Fishing Gear\n\nYou can't fish without gear. The fishing rod is one of the most important things you-\nneed for fishing. The fishing rod can be made by almost any woodworker by using string, a rod and a fishing hook. Another thing you need for fishing is the hook. The hook is essential for catching fish.\nChoosing The Bait\n\nYou can't catch fish without bait. There are many different types of bait. Fish prefer live bait such as insects. A very simple but effective bait is the worm. Worms are a great bait. They are also easy to acquire.\nWhere To Keep Fish?\n\nWhen fishing, it is important to have something to keep the fish you catch in. Buckets are a great way of storing fish while you are fishing because you can just toss the fish in while you continue fishing.\nCatching Fish\n\nOnce you have found a place to fish and once you have all the gear, you are ready  to fish! Take your fishing rod and attach the hook to it. Once you have done that, you should take your bait and place it on the hook. Now you it-\nis time to cast your line out. Smoothly cast your line out into the water. Now all you have to do is wait for a fish to come and tug on your line. I prefer to gently tug at might line. This causes the bait to move in the water, making the fish think that-\nyour bait is alive and moving. This makes the fish more inclined to come over to your bait. Once you feel a large tug on your line, you should immediately reel your line back in before the fish gets away. Hopefully you have caught a fish! Now you have to-\nmake a decision to either keep the fish or throw it away. If the fish is too small you should probably throw it away. Once you have made the decision, you should remove the hook from the fish's mouth.\nWhat To Do With Fish?\n\nMany people like to keep fish so that they can cook them for food. Some people prefer to sell fish for minas. These are two great options. You must decide what you want to do with the fish you caught.\nI hope you found this guide informative and interesting. Happy fishing!\n\nWritten By: Za'Kabar", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Ghosts", "Fawynn Sorbus", "A Study On Ghosts\nBy: Fawynn Sorbus\n\nGhosts are commonly thought to be terrifying beasts that lurk in the shadows, not alive but not in their proper afterlife. These souls are commonly hunted, feared and hated by many.\n\nGhosts can be dangerous, but in\nmost cases they simply wish to exist peacefully. They may not even know they have died, and are simply list and confused.\n\nThe first stage should be thought of as a caterpillar. They are called a haunt in this state, and believe they are still alive. They\nappear to exist in a delusional state, and rarely are humanoid in shape or coherant. These ghosts are the most harmless, other than giving you a spook. They cannot fight even in self defense at this state, and are at their most vunerable.\n\nThey do bear\nthe wounds of whatever caused their unfortunate death. This can be very gruesome, or very mild depending on what exactly happened.\n\nHaunts can be distinguished from revenants due to their solid white eyes.\n\nOnce a haunt learns of their death, they become\na revenant. This can be a very surprising experience, and they may respond in anger. Many ghosts prefer their delusion over a harsh reality, and will need to be calmed fast.\n\nRevenants slowly gain powers commonly associated with ghosts. This is the most\ncritical stage for them, and will define what kind of ghost they ultimately become.\n\nRevenants that remain calm will become specters, and ones that are allowed to stew in anger become poltergeists. They still bear their old wounds, but this time their\neyes have pupils and irises.\n\nA specter is at it's core peace. They will rarely fight unprovoked, and some will go out of their way to help the living. These ghosts should be left alone, because dispite their calm natures they are very powerful.\nA specter can be indentified due to it's blue coloring. The limit of the problems they bring is small pranks, and they may even help protect an area from negative spirits.\n\nOn the other side of the coin are poltergeists. Their core is made of hatred,\nanger, or any other negative emotion. This ghost will need to be purged, as they will actively try to terrify and harm the living. These poor souls will never know peace, as they can never go back to being a revanant.\n\nIn conclusion, ghosts rarely mean\nharm and should be treated as people. They may want to cross over, but they may wish to linger and should be given the choice as long as they cause no harm.\n\n\nIn Loving Memory Of:\nHallot Belal", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Reason", "Grigor Grandaxe", "A Guide to Reason. A Philisophical Bestseller by Grigor Grandaxe.\n\nHey you.\nYeah You.\nWhat do you know about Philsophy? Here in this book I will give you statements to help you to reson with yourself, to think and\nto reflect on actions based on the Philosophical premises that I will give to you.\n\nInstustions for use of this book:\n1. Open this book\n2. Follow the guidelines of each statement\n3. Keep it to one statement a day\nso that you may have the designed, 10 day reading period here, weather you read this at church, at work, in bed or at home.\n\nOn the next page your journey through Philoposphy will begin.\n---->\nDay One, Statement One.\n\"Progress just means bad things happen faster.\" - Grigor Grandax.\n\nConsider the connotations of this statement and its effect on you and your life, are bad things happening to you?\nDay Two, Statement Two.\n\"I think therefore I am.\"\n\nWHat do you want to be? HAve you tried to be this? Mabye you are all you want to be, and if so have you considered how you got there?\nDay Three, Statement Three.\n\"I can't go back to yesterday, because I was a different person then.\"\n\nHow much have you changed since yesterday? since last week? last year?\nDay 4, Statement 4.\n\"Don't bitw off more than you can chew because nobody looks attractive spitting it out\"\n\nWho has strived for something so far out of their reach they injure themselves whilst striving for it?\nDay 5, Statement 5.\n\"All is fair in love and war.\"\n\nThink on this statement for yourself and apply its Philosophy to your life. It has important conotations.\nDay 6-10\nPlease purchase Part Two of the Grigor Grandaxe Philosophy\nReading Plan for the added statements, remeber you will become a better persons if you apply the Philosophies of this book.", ""),
        StaticBook("GUY.CO INSURANCE", "Ayche Raven'kor", "ARE YOU PAYING TOO MUCH FOR CART INSURANCE?\n\nSEEK OUT GUY. CO FOR PREMIUM INSURANCE PACKAGES.\n\nYOUR CARTS ARE AN INVESTMENT. PROTECT THEM.\n\n15 MINUTES COULD SAVE YOU 15% OR MORE.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'or Attack", "Librarian Azkel Frostbeard", "As I arrive from my most recent travels I’m confronted with the destroyed gate of our blessed city in Haelun’or. The gates were pulled and bent by some colossal force which until this day is still unconfirmed. The only Mali'Aheral who witnessed such\nexplosion were Vulnir and Dyonne which encountered the recently destroyed gate after hearing, what they described to be, an explosion. To no surprise the forces who perpetrated such act headed to Malinor where both Vulnir and myself saw the great\n creatures standing around 11 feet tall and a dreadful and horrifying appearance. As Vulnir and me hurried back to our beloved city we were relieved to see both Kalenz, a powerful master of telekenesis and our golem Aeon which wielded\na mighty battle hammer for good measure. Kalenz quickly ordered all the adult Mali’aheral to take up weapons and march to Malinor to aid in what was left of the battle. I quickly went into my residence and blew the dust from my bow and gathered as many\narrows as I could find, hoping they were still sharp enough to hurt such creatures that awaited us in Malinor. As the small company of Vulnir, Safrill, Aeon, Kalenz, and myself arrived at the main gates of Malinor we could only see what was left of a\ngreat struggle between the Malinor guard and the two terrible creatures. To our content no Mali’aheral blood was to be spilled as one of the creatures had been slain and the other ran its way to the North followed by what was left of the Malinor defense.\nAs we headed back to our cihi and the bright of day gave way to the sacred night a strange presence was felt. As we approached the gates my mind seemed to be filled by an unfamiliar thought, a dark and soft voice crept through my head and seemed  to be\nfilled by an unfamiliar thought, a dark and soft voice crept through my head and seemed to be powered by the cool breeze of that night. Kalenz shouted “Get ready Mali’aheral for that being is not far.” Indeed we could see shadows lurking in the forest\nVulnir, Safrill, and myself headed to the towers while Aeon stood below and Kalenz just behind him.\nWe kept watch all night but nothing could be seen. Day arrived and we still felt uneasy.We drank and ate as Kalenz deduced this creature could\ncome again at night. Night approached and once again we took our positions now with the help of another archer, Ceruberr.  We kept the children safe inside the walls and prepared for an imminent attack. Suddenly the voice appeared in our heads again.\nThis time I managed to get some composure and write down its words as I heard them in fear: “Blessed are those who walk in the Light… Sanctified are those who can walk with their shadow…For their path shall not stray, their step shall not falter…\nbNever journeying alone…… In the brightness or dark.” As these words were uttered a dark figure began approaching and Safrill gave the word to aim at the being.Aeon lowered his hammer and Kalenz concentrated what seemed to be some energy in his hands.\nI have never seen Kalenz use his abilities, I just knew he was a mage because I was told.\nThe creature approached and Kalenz began to move one of the logs that was resting on the ground probably to hurl it at the figure,\nyet the being was smart enough to use its dark powers to levitate to a height similar to the wall. I was the first to fire, but the arrow seemed to have no effect or perhaps I missed, but so did every arrow released that night. \nThe being was dark as the night sky absent of stars and its shape was hard to decipher but as Kalenz emitted a light using his own powers the creature retreated.It was then that we realized its weakness was light.\nThe night was beginning to fade and the morning light covered Haelun’or in safety.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'or Attack", "Amras_Yavelty", "Accounts of\n    the Attack\n   on Haelun'or\n\n  by Amras Yavelty\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\nAs I arrive from my most recent travels I’m confronted with the destroyed gate of our blessed city in Haelun’or. The gates were pulled and bent by some colossal force which until this day is still unconfirmed.\nThe only Mali’Aheral who witnessed such explosion were Vulnir and Dyonne which encountered the recently destroyed gate after hearing, what they described to be, an explosion. To no surprise the forces who perpetrated such act headed to Malinor where\nVulnir and myself saw the great creatures standing around 11 feet tall and a dreadful and horrifying appearance. As Vulnir and me hurried back to our beloved city we were relieved to see both Kalenz, a powerful master of telekinesis and our\ngolem Aeon which wielded a mighty battle hammer for good measure. Kalenz quickly ordered all the adult Mali’aheral to take up weapons and march to Malinor to aid in what was left of the battle.\nI quickly went into my residence and blew the dust from my bow and gathered as many arrows as I could find, hoping they were still sharp enough to hurt such creatures that awaited us in Malinor.\nAs the small company of Vulnir, Safrill, Aeon, Kalenz, and myself arrived at the main gates of Malinor we could only see what was left of a great struggle between the Malinor guard and the two terrible creatures. To our content no Mali'aheral blood\nwas to be spilled as one of the creatures had been slain and the other ran its way to the North followed by what was left of the Malinor defense.\n\nAs we headed back to our cihi and the brght of the day gave way to the sacred night a strage presence\nwas felt. As we approached the gates my mind seemed to be filled by an unfamiliar thought, a dark and soft voice crept through my head and seemed to be powered by the cool breeze of that night. Kalenz shouted, \"Get ready, Mali'aheral, for that being is\nnot far.” Indeed we could see shadows lurking in the forest. Vulnir, Safrill, and myself headed to the towers while Aeon stood below and Kalenz just behind him.\nWe kept watch all night but nothing could be seen. Day arrived and we still felt uneasy. We drank and ate as Kalenz deduced this creature could come again at night. Night approached and once again we took our positions now with the help of another\narcher, Ceruberr. We kept the children safe inside the walls and prepared for an imminent attack. Suddenly the voice appeared in our heads again. This time I managed to get some composure and write down its words as I heard them in fear: \"Blessed are\nthose who walk in the Light… Sanctified are those who can walk with their shadow… For their path shall not stray, their step shall not falter… Never journeying alone…… In the brightness or dark.” As these words were uttered, a dark figure began\napproaching and Safrill gave the word to aim at the being. Aeon lowered his hammer and Kalenz concentrated what seemed to be some energy in his hands. I have never seen Kalenz use his abilities, I just knew he was a mage because I was told.\nThe creature approached and Kalenz began to move one of the logs that was resting on the ground probably to hurl it at the figure, yet the being was smart enough to use its dark powers to levitate to a height similar to the wall. I was the first to\nfire, but the arrow seemed to have no effect or perhaps I missed, but so did every arrow released that night. The being was dark as the night sky absent of stars and its shape was hard to decipher but as Kalenz emitted a light using his own powers the\ncreature retreated. It was then that we realized its weakness was light. The night was beginning to fade and the morning light covered Haelun’or in safety.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'or Attack", "Amras Yavelty", "Accounts of the Attack of Haelun’or\nBy Amras Yavelty\nAs I arrive from my most recent travels I’m confronted with the destroyed gate of our blessed city in Haelun’or. The gates were pulled and bent by some colossal force which until this day is still unconfirmed. The only Mali'Aheral who witnessed such\nexplosion were Vulnir and Dyonne which encountered the recently destroyed gate after hearing, what they described to be, an explosion. To no surprise the forces who perpetrated such act headed to Malinor where both Vulnir and myself saw the great\ncreatures standing around 11 feet tall and a dreadful and horrifying appearance. As Vulnir and me hurried back to our beloved city we were relieved to see both Kalenz, a powerful master of telekinesis and our golem Aeon which wielded a mighty battle\nhammer for good measure. Kalenz quickly ordered all the adult Mali’aheral to take up weapons and march to Malinor to aid in what was left of the battle. I quickly went into my residence and blew the dust from my bow and gathered as many arrows as I could\nfind, hoping they were still sharp enough to hurt such creatures that awaited us in Malinor. \nAs the small company of Vulnir, Safrill, Aeon, Kalenz, and myself arrived at the main gates of Malinor we could only see what was left of a great struggle\nbetween the Malinor guard and the two terrible creatures. To our content no Mali’aheral blood was to be spilled as one of the creatures had been slain and the other ran its way to the North followed by what was left of the Malinor defense. As we headed\nback to our cihi and the bright of day gave way to the sacred night a strange presence was felt. As we approached the gates my mind seemed to be filled by an unfamiliar thought, a dark and soft voice crept through my head and seemed to be powered by the\ncool breeze of that night. Kalenz shouted “Get ready Mali’aheral for that being is not far.” Indeed we could see shadows lurking in the forest. Vulnir, Safrill, and myself headed to the towers while Aeon stood below and Kalenz just behind him.\nWe kept watch all night but nothing could be seen. Day arrived and we still felt uneasy. We drank and ate as Kalenz deduced this creature could come again at night. Night approached and once again we took our positions now with the help of another archer,\nCeruberr. We kept the children safe inside the walls and prepared for an imminent attack. Suddenly the voice appeared in our heads again. This time I managed to get some composure and write down its words as I heard them in fear: \"Blessed are those who\nwalk in the Light… Sanctified are those who can walk with their shadow… For their path shall not stray, their step shall not falter… Never journeying alone…… In the brightness or dark.” As these words were uttered a dark figure began approaching and\nSafrill gave the word to aim at the being. Aeon lowered his hammer and Kalenz concentrated what seemed to be some energy in his hands. I have never seen Kalenz use his abilities, I just knew he was a mage because I was told.\nThe creature approached and Kalenz began to move one of the logs that was resting on the ground probably to hurl it at the figure, yet the being was smart enough to use its dark powers to levitate to a height similar to the wall. I was first to fire, but\nthe arrow seemed to have no effect or perhaps I missed, but so did every arrow released that night. The being was dark as the night sky absent of stars and its shape was hard to decipher but as Kalenz emitted a light using his own powers the creature\nretreated. It was then that we realized its weakness was light. The night was beginning to fade and the morning light covered Haelun’or in safety.\n             -----------", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'or Schism", "Librarian Azkel Frostbeard", "The history of Asulon is known to be rich with wars, political usurpations, monstrous drakes, and the rise and fall of nations. However, one history that eludes most modern, non-mali'aheral scholars is the secret history of the elhaelun'or\nand its many trials and tribulations. One such excerpt (to take from a vast swathe) is the Haelun'or Schizm--a short, and unusual, period of instability and disunity in the motherland.  In this three volume series, one will discuss the turbulent period\nfor the benefit of future citizens. (Volume 1)\nThe ehaelun'or of Asulon was, in this period, ruled by the echillan'thilln--the Silver Council. Much like its Malinorian contemporary, members were chosen by those whom were deemed worthy by the current council members--the okariran.\n. Two of these counsellors would begin a chain of events eventually causing the one, and only, demagogic political usurpation in mali'aheral history. Their names were Ellir'siol, the Okarir'layun (Master of beauty), and Nelecar,\nthe Okarir'sil (Master of the Sword). From the very inception of the two working together, friction between their personalities was evident. Nelecar was a soldier with a great, and admirable, dedication to the purity of his kin.\nHis efficient, though admittedly extreme, methods of protection allowed for a distinctly effective military force that has yet to be seen again within the walls of the mali'aheral. Ellir'siol was an artist, and an architect.  Her mesmerising design\nof the Haelun’or residential district was one of the finest examples of classical, revivalist mali'aheral architecture available, and is still emulated to this day. Touting overtures of peace, wisdom, and forethought, she strove only for what can be\nperceived as \"the greater good\" in regards to the motherland. Despite their own good intentions, there were many obvious faults in their actions throughout their years in the service of the cihi'thilln. Nelecar was not a forgiving mali.\nWhen a single, minor wrong was committed, he would often act harshly towards the perpetrator. One such case involved an insolent mali'aheral who refused the Okarir’s demands, and was summarily locked in a cell for nearly a month as punishment.\nHis liberal use of banishment to punish wrongdoers was also a harshly debated affair, and was the main issue of the coming schism. Ellir'siol, however, was by contrast far too forgiving of wrongdoers. She often pressed for impure mali'aheral\nto be re-integrated to society, and those whose ideals were not congruent with Larihei's vision were protected by her delicate, and clever political machinations. Retrospectively, conflict should have been predicted. This is but a tale of two mali'aheral\nincapable of compromise, and such shall be shown in the second volume.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism1", "Lelien", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume I\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nThe history of Asulon is known to be rich with wars, political usurpations, monstrous drakes, and the rise and fall of nations. However, one history that eludes most modern, non-mali'aheral scholars is the secret history of elhaelun'or, and its many\ntrials and tribulations. One such excerpt (to take from a vast swathe) is the Haelun'or Schism--a short, and unusual, period of instability and disunity in the motherland. In this three volume series, one will discuss the turbulent period for the benefit\nof future citizens.\n\nThe Haelun'or of Asulon was, in this period, ruled by the echillan'thilln--the Silver Council. Much like its Malinorian contemporary, members were chosen by those whom were deemed worthy by the current council members--\nthe okariran. Two of these counsellors would begin a chain of events eventually causing the one, and only, demagogic political usurpation in mali'aheral history. Their names were Ellir'siol, the Okarir'leyun (Master of Beauty), and Nelecar, the Okarir'sil\n(Master of the Sword). \nFrom the very inception of the two working together, friction between their personalities was evident. Nelecar was a soldier with a great, and admirable, dedication to the purity of his kin. His efficient, though admittedly\nextreme, methods of protection allowed for a distinctly effective military force that has yet to be seen again within the walls of the mali'aheral. Ellir'siol was an artist, and an architect. Her mesmerising design of the Haelun’or residential district\nwas one of the finest examples of classical, revivalist mali'aheral architecture available, and is still emulated to this day.Touting overtures of peace, wisdom, and forethought, she strove only for what can be perceived as \"the greater good\" in regards\nto the motherland.\n\nDespite their own good intentions, there were many obvious faults in their actions throughout their years in the service of the cihi'thilln. Nelecar was not a forgiving mali. When a single, minor wrong was committed, he would often\nact harshly towards the perpetrator. One such case involved an insolent mali'aheral who refused the Okarir’s demands, and was summarily locked in a cell for nearly a month as punishment. His liberal use of banishment to punish wrongdoers was also a\nharshly debated affair, and was the main issue of the coming schism. Ellir'siol, however, was by contrast far too forgiving of wrongdoers. She often pressed for impure mali'aheral to be re-integrated to society, and those whose ideals were not\ncongruent with Larihei's vision were protected by her delicate, and clever political machinations. Retrospectively, conflict should have been predicted.\nThis is but a tale of two mali’aheral incapable of compromise, and such shall be shown in the second volume.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism1", "L. Sullas", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume 1\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nThe history of Asulon is known to be rich with wars, political usurpations, monstrous drakes, and the rise and fall of nations. However, one history that eludes most modern, non-mali'aheral scholars is the secret history of the elhaelun'or, and its\nmany trials and tribulations. One such excerpt (to take from a vast swathe) is the Haelun'or Schism--a short, and unusual, period of instability and disunity in the motherland. In this three volume series, one will discuss the turbulent period for the\nbenefit of future citizens.\n\nThe Haelun'or of Asulon was, in this period, ruled by the echillan'thilln--the Silver Council. Much like its Malinorian contemporary, members were chosen by those whom were deemed worthy by the\ncurrent council members--the okariran. Two of these counsellors would begin a chain of events eventually causing the one, and only, demagogic political usurpation in mali'aheral history. Their names were Ellir'siol, the Okarir'layun (Master\nof beauty), and Nelecar, the Okarir'sil (Master of the Sword).\n\nFrom the very inception of the two working together, friction between their personalities was evident. Nelecar was a soldier with a great, and admirable, dedication to the\npurity of his kin. His efficient, though admittedly extreme, methods of protection allowed for a distinctly effective military force that has yet to be seen again within the walls of the mali'aheral. Ellir'siol was an artist, and an architect. Her\nmesmerising design of the Haelun’or residential district was one of the finest examples of classical, revivalist mali'aheral architecture available, and is still emulated to this day.Touting overtures of peace, wisdom, and forethought, she strove only for\nwhat can be perceived as \"the greater good\" in regards to the motherland.\n\nDespite their own good intentions, there were many obvious faults in their actions throughout their years in the service of the cihi'thilln. Nelecar was not a\nforgiving mali. When a single, minor wrong was committed, he would often act harshly towards the perpetrator. One such case involved an insolent mali'aheral who refused the Okarir’s demands, and was summarily locked in a cell for nearly a month as\npunishment. His liberal use of banishment to punish wrongdoers was also a harshly debated affair, and was the main issue of the coming schism. Ellir'siol, however, was by contrast far too forgiving of wrongdoers. She often pressed for impure mali'aheral\nto be re-integrated to society, and those whose ideals were not congruent with Larihei's vision were protected by her delicate, and clever political machinations. Retrospectively, conflict should have been predicted.\nThis is but a tale of two mali’aheral incapable of compromise, and such shall be shown in the second volume.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism2", "Eenhoornheid", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume II\n\n    by Lucion Sullas\nNow that one has learned of the two figures involved in this debacle, let us discuss the event itself. Should you not ahave read the previous volume, most of what shall be written will be nothing but a confusing morass of information.\nOne suggests you perform the logical action, and return to the previous volume prior to reading this one.\n\nNelecar's afore-mentioned zest for banishment had been mostly tolerated by the council, aside from the\nconsiberable opposition from Ellir'siol. However, one event sparked a final, fatal banishment. The husband of Ellir'siol, Talias, the second-in-command of the military under Nelecar, was exposed, along with other individuals (whom shall not be identified,\ndue to a number still living and present within the nation), as attempting to subvert, and remove Belecar from his position via aggressive action. Upon learning of this, Nelecar immediately called for the banishment of all those involved.\nElli'siol, understandably, attempted to argue Nelecar out of doing so, but only managed to stall his pronouncement with the help of other council members. When the decision was made public, Elli'siol showed her true colours.\nIn a move to directly parody the acts of Nelecar, she 'banished' the entire populations of the city, and majority of the citizenry followed her out of Haelun'or-- those won over by her popular and public dislike of the Okarir'sil. Piling upon boats,\nthey left the Emerald Isle to the town of Ceru-- a cliffside village and quasi-colony that bordered the Kingdom of Renatus. Here, they settled for a time, and waited.\nHere Ellir engaed in disgraceful, demagogic, rabble-rousing, and appearled to illogical emotional thinking to further solidify and justify her actions. This went on for many months, while Nelecar and his few loyal supporters remained within Haelun'or-\n-slowly losing confidence in their actions.\n\nAfter months had passed, and her ravenous support had died down, Ellir returned to the city-- deeming her point had been made. However, it was noticeably adsent of Nelecar.\nHis supporters remained, and were thankfully not pursued by the 'victors'.\n\nThe prologue and effects of this event will be discussed in the final installment of this series.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism2", "L. Sullas", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume 2\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nNow that one has learned of the two figures involved in this debacle, let us discuss the event itself. Should you not have read the previous volume, most of what shall be written will be nothing but a confusing morass of information. One suggests you\nperform the logical action, and return to the previous volume prior to reading this one.\n\nNelecar's afore-mentioned zest for banishment had been mostly tolerated by the council, aside from considerable opposition from\nEllir'siol. However, one event sparked a final, fatal banishment. The husband of Ellir'siol, Talias, the second-in-command of the military under Nelecar, was exposed, along with other individuals (Whom shall not be identified, due to a number still living\nand present within the nation), as attempting to subvert, and remove Nelecar from his position via aggressive action. Upon learning of this, Nelecar immediately called for the banishment of all those involved. Ellir'siol, understandably,\nattempted to argue Nelecar out of doing so, but only managed to stall his pronouncement with the help of other council members. When the decision was made public, Ellir'siol showed her true colours.\nIn a move to directly parody the acts of Nelecar, she \"banished\" the entire population of the city, and majority of the citizenry followed her out of Haelun'or--those won over by her popular and public dislike of the Okarir'sil. Piling upon boats,\nthey left the Emerald Isle to the town of Ceru--a cliffside village and quasi-colony that bordered the Kingdom of Renatus. Here, they settled for a time, and waited.\nHere Ellir engaged in disgraceful, demagogic, rabble-rousing, and appealed to illogical emotional thinking to further solidify and justify her actions. This went on for many months, while Nelecar and his few loyal supporters remained within Haelun'or\n--slowly losing confidence in their actions. \n\nAfter months had passed, and her ravenous support had died down, Ellir returned to the city--deeming her point had been made. However, it was noticeably absent of\nNelecar. His supporters remained, and were thankfully not pursued by the \"victors\".\n\nThe prologue and effects of this event will be discussed in the final installment of this series.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism3", "Eenhoornheid", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n     Volume III\n\n    by Lucion Sullas\nThe importance of the events that occurred during the Schism can not be trated lightly. The after-effectsm though, were seemingly mundance. With the immediate disappearance of Nelcar, the whole city simply fell to the leadership of what council was\nleft, althought Ellir obviously having significant inluence over proceedings.\n\nA detrimental effect of the Schism was the slow dissolution of what remained of the armed forces (then referred to as the 'Legion').\nThe size and ability of the soldiery was slowly whittled away, until only a few diligent guardsmen remained. Further affeted was the concept of violence in general-- the methods of the Okarir'sil no longer popular with any citzen.\nThe lacking of these two elements may explain why the mali'aheral nation had been a haven of peace for decade upon decade.\n\nOne is sure, however, that the reader is curious of the fate these two political rivals succumbed to.\nNelecar's disappearance did not last long, as he hid in the lowest levels of the city-- murdering numerous citizens over the course of multiple years. However, after nearly four decades of being hidden, the ragged Okarir'sil found his way into\nthe city, and stood in the square, confronting frightened and confused citizenry. His madness had overtaken himself, and, as a final act, he took his own life-- brokwn, thin, alone, and forgotten by history.\nEllir'siol, who strived all her life to keep all those whom she loved safe, lost her entire family. She herself turned bitter, and strayed away from the citizenry in her cold, lonely tower above the Eternal College. Eventually, she disappeard--\nalmost as if fading away with the end of her political career.\n\nLet this short history be a message of the dangers that are ingerent within the extremes of political rivalry, and extremist thinking. Should one desire to take message from these\nvolumes, then allow this humble writer to give you a final, resolyte statement. Rashness is rewarded only with destruction, and demagoguery is rewarded only with loss.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism3", "L. Sullas", "The Haelun'or\n      Schism:\n     Volume 3\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nThe importance of the events that occurred during the Schism can not be treated lightly. The after-effects, though, were seemingly mundane. With the immediate disappearance of Nelecar, the whole city simply fell to the leadership of what council was\nleft, although Ellir obviously having significant influence over proceedings.\n\nA detrimental effect of the schism was the slow dissolution of what remained of the armed forces (then referred to as the \"Legion\"). The size and ability of the\nsoldiery was slowly whittled away, until only a few diligent guardsmen remained. Further affected was the concept of violence in general--the methods of the Okarir'sil no longer popular with any citizen. The lacking of these two elements may explain why\nthe mali'aheral nation has been a haven of peace for decade upon decade.\n\nOne is sure, however, that the reader is curious of the fate these two political rivals succumbed to.\nNelecar's disappearance did not last long, as he hid in the lowest levels of the city--murdering numerous citizens over the course of multiple years. However, after nearly four decades of being hidden, the ragged Okarir'sil found his way into the\ncity, and stood in the square, confronting frightened, and confused citizenry. His madness had overtaken himself, and, as a final act, he took his own life--broken, thin, alone, and forgotten by history.\nEllir'siol, who strived all her life to keep all those whom she loved safe, lost her entire family. She herself turned bitter, and strayed away from the citizenry in her cold, lonely tower above the Eternal College. Eventually, she herself disappeared\n--almost as if fading away with the end of her political career.\n\nLet this short history be a message of the dangers that are inherent within the extremes of political rivalry, and extremist thinking. Should one desire to take a message from these\nvolumes, then allow this humble writer to give you a final, resolute statement. \n\nRashness is rewarded only with destruction, and demagoguery is rewarded only with loss.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haiku's by Ana", "casanova9", "*there is a sketching of a fox*\nYour coat is pretty\nColors of orange, black, and white\nYour cutness hides strength\n*there is a sketch of a tree*\nYour hands are green\nYou wave hello and goodbye\nYour roots are endless\n*there is a sketch of an owl*\nYou are large and wise\nSleep at day, hunt in the night\nYou don't give a hoot", ""),
        StaticBook("Hakons Statement", "Malgonious", "I, Ser Hakon of House Ruric have given myself upto the Felsenic Guardsman.  My house has commited the crime of treason against the crown, and I have turned myself over to the judgement of the Creator and his flock.  I am yours to judge as you please.", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfling Babies", "Aerxuis", "Halfling Babies\nBy Unknown\nCopied by Aerx\nWhere do Halfling babies come from?\nHalfling birth is by far the most magical and sweet birth of all the races. I first found out about how the Halflings are born when I went to the Halfling town,\nwhich I have forgotten the name of. Quite hungry when I arrived, I asked permission from one of the elders to remove a few plants from the farm, permission which was granted to me.\nAs I walked through the farm I took a few carrots and\npotatoes, then I found an overly grown cabbage. I thought as a thank you, I would cook the great cabbage and make the Halflings a great cauldron of cabbage soup. As I was about to take the cabbage from the fertile land, a Halfling came shouting\nthrough the fields for me to stop, seeming quite stressed. Believing that somehow I was in the wrong field, or that cabbage was of prized goods, I stepped away from the cabbage, and waited the Halfling. While huffing, the Halfling, still\nstressed, checked the cabbage for damage, before hitting me in the shin with his shovel.\nIn pain I fell to while grabbing my leg, wondering what kind of prized cabbage that could be. The Halfling looked angry and even shouted, “Wha’ were y’\ngoin’ t’ do t’ me son?!”\nI was amazed, the cabbage was so important to him, he called it his son. I apologized and said that as a thank you I was going to cook his ‘son’ for the Halflings, but that I didn’t know it belonged to someone. i\ncouldn’t finish explaining before I hit repeatedly by the shovel. The Halfling was shouting as he hit me, “Y’ disgustin’ man, how dare’ye try t’ feed us one o’ our own babies!”\nI was shocked, I didn’t understand. I apologized and said many times that\nI didn’t know, and after a while, the Halfling stopped hitting me. After he stopped I continued asking, in serious pain I might add. I asked what the cabbage meant to the Halflings, and he told me a story I will never forget.\nThe story he told\nme one of love, the love two Halflings feel for each other. I already knew at the time how Dwarf babies were born, and knew that Halflings are descendents of both Horen and Urguan, so I was confused how they mated and had children. I didn’t know if it\nwas the Dwarven way of the Human way. And what I was told was nothing more than magical\nHe told me of him and his wife, wife for many years now. They clearly loved each other quite dearly, and one day decided to have a child. They began their\nevening by drinking and smoking together, alone in their house, only the two which love each other. They do what they love most together, drinking the finest Halfling ale, and smoking the best Halfling weed. When the moon was high, they went into the\nfields together, carrying a single seed, a normal seed. After planting the cabbage in the patch, they prayed to their pumpkin god.\nThe seed, blessed with the love of the soon to be mother and father Halfling, and the power of the pumpkin god,\nstarted growing quite large, into what was now the cabbage I almost took. The baby Halfling grows within the cabbage, to be born at the time of the harvest season. It was still a few Elven days from the harvest, and as such, if I had took the cabbage,\nI would give birth to the baby too soon. I decided to stay for a while longer to witness the birth, and it was as they said.\nI helped with the harvest that day, and soon, all the Halflings gathered by the cabbage. The mother and father started\ncarefully removing the big leaves of the cabbage. It took awhile for the small Halflings to remove the leaves, but soon enough, in the middle of it, a tiny sleeping baby could be seen. The father thanked the pumpkin god once more as the mother took the\nbaby. That night, they made a feast, for the harvest, and newborns.\nThe name for the newborns? They thought of them while drunk and high.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hallowed Umbrage", "Geoboy66", "I write the following epitaph with dire haste so much so that the winds part ways my words.\n\nMy account of these events may not be entirely accurate,§  something completely acceptable under the maddening, fear stricken haze that I have been left in.\nI sit here now quill in hand, wounded with a gash so dreadfully dark that I'm not sure if it really is a wound at all.  I have become a well of life, bountiful as the succulent navy mists ooze out of this growth, this... anchor; ever so dark and dreadful.\nMy pilgrimmage to this place hath cost me the trust and faith of my only friends as despite every loud, nagging warning against venturing here, my back was turned and my hands covered my ears.\nIt is the weakness of Man to succumb to the allure of power, riches and knowledge that of which the Abyss is said to contain. Trust me when I say that the power hidden away here is done so for a reason and should never belong to any mortal man.\nFor were the corrupting mind of Man ever to wrap their greedy fingers around such incomprehensible things, it would mean our doom.  The Trolls Harpies and Gryphons of our world pale in comparison to the horror of the deep, dark beyond.\nLegends tell of the Abyss as the ruins of Aegis, a land from which Man's forefathers hailed.\nI would hesitate to call the state in which the Gods left the motherland in a ruin, for truly there remains little left here at all.\nFor this Abyss, this endless chasm to which there seems no end is both the catastrophic ashes of a world once living and breathing as well as a prison for every lost soul that the world sunk with it. North, South, East, West - it all leads to despair.\nI hath deviated from the guiding compass to venture in a new direction; downward.\nFor I suspected that within the bowels of this crushing nightmare there must be both a ceiling and a floor.  I, a pawn controlled by adventurous urges, took a fatal dive.\nMy sense of time has long since fled, abandoning me like many other luxuries that once made me whole.  After a measurement of time far longer than any measurement of time I've ever thought to measure, I reached the feared and fabled end of this void.\nI dare not write about the countless demons that scour the ebon plane despite the insanity they so passively inflict.  They do not deserve the honour of being referenced alongside the Lord of the deep, dark below.  Darkness Incarnate.\nAs my wailing, shedding flesh forced itself through the dense acidic atmosphere, my feet began to fail me.  Time hath come to truly give up, and turn back I thought.  Yet my thoughts were ruptured by a presence so overwhelming that I could not think.\nAs I fought with myself to open my eyes I stared upon what could only be described as a living shadow, embodying umbral hellfire frigid enough to lock my very bones in place.\nRadiating in darkness so hollow that the Abyss stood brightly aflame beside him.\nHe worse armour, the first sign that this impossible creation was indeed Man.  Ancient was his armour, charred and blackened from what I cannot begin to imagine.  Yet his armour, heavy as it appeared did not hinder him.\nHis form suddenly shifted all at once, phasing out at one place and in again at another.  The realm was at his whim, as he did not simply move through it, but had become it.  Now, the Dark Lord towered above me, reeking of ash and death.\nAll past experiences seem like a petty joke when compared to the awesome perspective I had been blessed with. This Man, whose blood red eyes pierced through the very veil of the Abyss had drawn forth his weapon.  A terrible greatsword, massive in size.\nDripping with the howling souls of the damned.  This blade, serrated like the peak of Mount Ire was shoved into my heart, slotting into my flesh like a key within a door.  In the seconds before my consciousness faded I heard something.  I heard a voice.\nA voice that would rival a Dragon.  It was then that I knew for certain - This was the Old Lord of Umbrage, King of the Abyss.  One whose name does not touch the lips of the living, and whose sight is known only to the dead and the mad.\nHis perverted shriek defiled every corner of the Abyss, his siren call summoning the dark to his side.  As the black visage of the Old Lord faded from my sight, I heard his words.\n\n      R A D I A N T\n I S  T H E  B L A C K\n         S  U  N", ""),
        StaticBook("Happiest Bard", "Naz Atatis", "The Happiest Bard\n\nIf you love somebody\n\nBetter tell them while they're here 'cause \n\nThey may just slip away from you.\n\nYou'll never know quite when, well\nThen again it just depends on\n\nHow much time is left for you.\n\nI've seen the highest mountains\n\nI've seen the deepest rivers\n\nBut I've never seen something like her\nI take her in but don't look away\n\n'Cause I'm the happiest bard, ay'\n\n'Cause I'm the happiest bard, yeah\n\nWaiting on this for a while now\n\nPlaying my songs to the crowds\nI've been waiting to smile, ay'\n\nBeen holding it in for a while now, ay'\n\nTake you with me if I can\n\nBeen dreaming of this since I was a child\n\nI'm the happiest bard\nMet her when I was at my lowest\n\nDidn't know what to say\n\nI thought it was all a dream\n\nLooked up and never looked back\n\n'Cause I'm the happiest bard, ay'\nI'm the happiest bard, yeah\n\nWaiting on this for a while now\n\nPlaying my songs to the crowd\n\nI've been waiting to smile, ay'\n\nBeen holding it in for a while\nTake you with me if I can\n\nBeen dreaming of this since I was a child\n\nI'm the happiest bard\n\nThere's only one lady I love\n\nShe's the most amazing artist you ever did see\nAnd I'm glad to have her with me.\n\n'Cause I'm the happiest bard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Harvesters", "Falyen Darylus", "Analysis of the Harvester Construct\nThe constructs used in the attack on Rivel appear to be based off of the golem servants favoured by the Forgotten Dwarves and now being rediscovered by the Aegean dwarves.\nHowever, they are clearly different: they possess a killer instinct unheard of in servant golems, lack individual intelligence and possess an apparatus built into the hand capable of killing a mortal being and trapping their soul, no doubt for\ncontainment in the Soul Capacitors of The Seal. Countless Harvester Constructs were destroyed in their assault on Rivel, indicating a lack of quality in their construction: it seems the dwarves built them in a time of desperation.\nHowever, such a time now befalls us: the majority of Rivel’s Lesser Caste were killed by Harvester Constructs in the assault, and I fear this propaganda we are distributing to the Lesser Caste attributing this assault to deceptive attacks by the\nForgotten Dwarves will not placate them. We may downplay their intelligence, but even they must realise the Forgotten Dwarves have been extinct for over a millenium.\n- Senior Researcher Falyen Darylus", ""),
        StaticBook("Haven", "Ebonsquire", "Haven - City of Aenguls \n\n((Originallly written by GoldenGFX))\nHaven, the city of Aenguls, or Ascended. I am Latsi, and I have been able to go inside the magnificent city, and see it for myself. On the inside, there were a few hills, and a large house on the tallest one. There were two roads around the large hill,\none going straight and one that went left. I was lead down the path to the left, to their in-city docks. \n\nNear the docks were many houses. I was told they were the houses of the Ascended. I was lead inside one of the homes, it was a 3 story\nhouse with a pool in the basement. The ascneded that was leading me, crafted a few tools, and we continued on. \n\nWe followed a path under a large naturally formed archway, and I saw what seemed to be a\nlarge, monstrous head. In the head, there was a stair case going down, and a staircase up. We went up, and at the top, there was a small hall. At the end of the hall, there was a large drop. I was told to trust that I would live, and I jumped.\nI fell down very far, and ended up being saved by the water, but came out completely dry. There were two ways to go at the bottom, we went to the left, as there was not much to the right. On the left side, the first thing I saw was an\nextremely large tree. At the bottom of it was a pool of water, with a tree growing out of it. \nShe showed me where shops were going to be, near the base of the tree, and then lead me inside. There was the spot that the Sages would hang out. We went out\nof the tree, and went behind it to a wonderful looking building. Inside, I was told that the bottom floor is where the Ascended trained. Apparently, some days their training is hard, other times easy, and other times boring.\nShe then lead me upstairs, where they had rows of bookcases. In the cases, there were books on everything! There was skills to be learned: Magic, the history of the Undead, Ascended and Sages, and more! After spending a little more\ntime there, we went back up to the surface. I got to meet another Ascended as soon as we came back up. \n\nSoon after, I left the city and journeyed home.\nKnown Ascended: \n\n+Nailena\n\n+Richard\n\n+Dolir", ""),
        StaticBook("Headgehogs", "Andria Barbu", "Headgehogs\nA poem by\nAdria Barbu\n*******************\nHeadgehogs are great\nHeadgehogs are neat\nThey are cute when they want sometihng to eat.\nHeadgehogs a fun\nHeadgehogs are small\nHeadgehogs come when you give them a call.\nHeadgehogs are the best\nHeadgehogs are better tha all the rest\nHeagehogs look cute hiding in a chest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Healing Guide", "Alder", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n       Basic Healing\n\n\n~=~ A guilde to herbal & mundane healing ~=~\n\nWritten by: Monk Alder\n\n\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nHello there,\n\nMy name is Alder. I have written this guide to teach those who are not familiar with healing at all, & those who have basic knowledge of the practice. I will include sections for a few healing topics that apply to a catholic standard.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nCuts & Scrapes: \n\nTo begin make sure that all items are devoid of contaminants such as dirt, mud, dust, and any other biotic or abiotic material that is not apart of the item. \n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nWhat you will need:\n\n* Alcohol\n* Blissfoil\n* Tippens Root\n* Mandragora\n* Cloth\n* Gloves\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nWhere to find / Properties: \n\nAlcohol: Found in any bar or tavern. Antiseptic.\n\nBlissfoil: Found in grass lands. numbing agent. (Use gloves when harvesting. If to much is applied expect permanent numbness.)\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nTippens Root: Found in dense forests. Wrinkled with dark yellow spots. Stops bleeding at an extreemly fast rate.\n\nMandragora: Found in swamps & wetlands. Can be ground up to produce a skin healing goo. (Warning wear a mask\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~ \n\nwhen harvesting this plant. Toxic spores.)\n\nCloth: Found in local shops. used to cover wounds.\n\nGloves: Found in local shops. Protect hands.\n\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nProcedure: \n\n1) Take a cloth and soak it in alcohol. then clean off the wound.\n\n2) Get a bowl and crush up your Blissfoil applying a small amount to the wound.\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n3) Do the same with the Tippens Root, & then Mandragora.\n\n4) Apply a piece of cloth over the wound, the injury should now heal with haste. \n\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nBurns\n\nWhat you will need:\n\n* Water\n* Athin \n* Cloth\n\nNote: Athin is a blue algae found in cold bodys of water. used to heal burns.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nProcedure:\n\n1) Soak your cloth in cold water and lightly rub the burn cleaning it off.\n\n2) Apply Mandragora to the wound to begin the healing of tissue.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n \n3) Crush up the Athin in a bowl and apply a paste of your choice to form a lotion. \n\n4) Apply it to the wound, expect fast results and a soothing cooling sensation.\n\n5) Apply cloth over the wound.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nFor any other injury that may be life threatening seek a Monk at the Cloud Temple.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("Healing Potions", "ilikefooddude", "Healing Potion\nA Basic Alchemy Guide\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Ingredients Needed:\n\nThree Bottles of clean water\nOne reed of the Serpent's Stalk plant\nOne large sample of Tippin's Root\nMethod\n\n1. Finely chop the Serpent's Stalk and add into the three bottles of water; stirring and infusing until the liquid turns a sickly green colour.\n\n2. Crush the Tippin's Root in a Mortar and Pestle and add to the\nLiquid, which should turn a brown or greyish colour when mixed.\n\n3. Commence to boil the potion in a brewing stand for about an hour, or until it takes on something like a rocky texture.\n\n4. Filter out the\nChunks of Serpent's Stalk and Tippin's Root with a clean cloth, and transfer the potion (Which now should be brighter and clearer than before, with shifting textures of crumbling grey) to another bottle.\nForenote\nDo not drink this potion. Apply directly to wounds with a cloth and bandage quickly. Injuries such as cuts and bruises will heal in a matter of hours, though broken bones will still take a week or two to heal. Consumption will cause nausia,\nChoking, and, sometimes death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Healing Potions", "Iatrilemar", "= Alchemical Healing =\n\n\nAlchemy is one subject I believe is better left untouched by most. It often results in deadly explosions and vile abominations brought on by unnatural means. However Alchemy covers one\narea that is quite useful in many survival situations. That is alchemical healing. While it seems mundane with the existence of the monks and, as I like to call them, void healers, knowing how to prepare simple potions is akin to knowing how to light a\nstove in order to eat or learn to write in order to document knowledge.\n\n= =  The Basics  = =\n\nThere are three basic ingredients that will be useful in most potions. Distilled water, Tippen's root and what I call a basic\nbandage potion.\n\nTippen's root can be found in oak trees and by crushing together two oak saplings.\n\nDistilled water is made via the use of a alchemy stand and coal. Run the water through the alchemy stand using\nthe coal as a filtration device. The end product will be distilled water. \n\nNow, a bandage potion is made by the same process as distilled water but you simply use Tippen's root instead of coal. \n\nWhile making\ndistilled water and a bandage potion should be common alchemy knowledge we will only be using Tippen's root for healing potions. \n\n=  Healing Potions  =\n\nI have found five different ways of creating what I call a minor healing potion\nwhich can hasten the healing process of a wound. I shall list them and the ingredients used in making them. I hope it is obvious that to make these you will need an alchemy stand. This isn't some mundane void healing based on false science.\nPotion #1\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-One rotten potatoe\n-Sugarcane\n\nEffects:\nMundane healing. May experience slight weakness.\nPotion #2\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-One rotten potatoe\n-A bundle of vines\n\nEffects:\nMundane healing. May experience tightness and inability to sprint.\nPotion #3\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-A rotten potatoe\n-A lily pad\n\nEffects:\nMundane Healing. May cause slight blindness for limited period of time.\nPotion #4\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-A rotten potatoe\n-Ice\n\nEffects:\nMundane healing. Muscle tightness and temporary weakness.\nPotion #5\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-A rotten potatoe\n-Shiny Melon slice\n\nEffects: \nMundane healing. Temporary blindness and muscle tightness.\n~= Rejuvenation =~\n  ~=   Potion    =~\n\nRejuvenation potions are similar to mundane healing potions but work in a slightly different way. Instead of applying a direct healing effect to the body the user will experience a sensation of\nhealing over a period of time. This potion is useful for helping with the gradual healing process and often provides a more wholesome healing effect. I have found five seperate ways to construct a rejuvenation potion.\nPotion #1\n\nIngredients;\n\n-Tippen's Root\n-Sugarcane\n\nEffects:\nMundane rejuvenation. Slight weakness.\nPotion #2\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-A bundle of vine\n\nEffects:\nMundane rejuvenation. Muscle tightness.\nPotion #3\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-A lily pad\n\nEffects:\nMundane rejuvenation. Temporary blindness.\nPotion #4\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-Ice\n\nEffects:\nMundane rejuvenation. Muscle tightness and slight weakness.\nPotion #5\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-A shiny melon slice\n\nEffects:\nMundane rejuvenation. Muscle tightness and temporary blindness.\nI have also documented a more volatile version of the rejuvenation potion that has increased healing properties but with worse side effects. It is important to note that all potions will have side effects. It is incredibly difficult to purify a potion and\ncreate a potion with no negative side effects.\n\n~Greater Rejuvenation potion~\n\nIngredients:\n\n-Tippen's root\n-A rotten potatoe\n-Ice\n-A lily pad\nEffects:\nLasting rejuvenation. Lasting muscle weakness. Lasting blindness. Temporary muscle tightness.\n\nWith this knowledge I hope you may learn to better serve yourself in times of need.\n*A couple ink spots dot the page*\n\n\n~Iatrilemar \n      Elervathar", ""),
        StaticBook("Helios' Poem", "Gigarun", "Helios' Poem\n\nAs told by Helios\n      &\n   Scribed by \n         The Pine Druid\n\nO, They say,\nThat under the fae,\nExist a group of individuals,\nThat serve beatles,\nAnd hug trees.\nO, Morons you say,\nMaybe we are,\nBut before you draw conclusions,\nYou should know,\nWe ain't a random bunch.\nO, Most of time anyway,\nWe have our rules,\nAnd our rulers,\nOne's quite the lass,\nLady of the Harvest.\n\nO, That'd be Cerridwen,\nBut there's another, Cernunnos,\nYou heard me right,\nDeity o' the hunt.\nO, Now you know our lords,\nAspects we call 'em,\nTreat 'em right,\nAnd they'll be kind in return,\nSupply you with good harvest.\nO, And hides,\nTo keep yours warm,\nAnd that's all folks,\nIf you've changed you mind about us,\nThat's lovely,\nBut if not...\n\nO, You can piss off!", ""),
        StaticBook("Help", "Vannessa Longridge", "\"Sahar...I fear for my life. You must wonder why I tell you this, but you have never shown any signs of anger or distrust towards me. I believe someone is plotting against me in the Palace. I do not think it is the Sultan, but rather the Emir or the Imam.\nI have recieved death threats many times...and constantly been robbed of prized possesions from my house..Please help me!\n-Iskander", ""),
        StaticBook("Herb Gathering", "Vlad Shade", "Herbs Mild info!\n\nMandragora(Basic)\nPlant-Lily pad\nBiome:Swamp\n\nSerpents Stalk(Mild)\nPlant-Sugar Cane\nBiome:Plains\n\nFrost Vine(Advanced)\nPlant-Ivy\nBiome:Ice plains\nBliss Foil(Basic)\nPlant-Orchids\nBiome:Plains\n\nAthin(Advanced)\nPlant-None\nBlock-Ice\nBiome:Ice Plain\n\nCrimson Vase(Mild)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Plains\nDrakes Tail(Advanced)\nPlant-Shrub\nBiome:Desert\n\nDwarf Pumpkin(Weak)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Swamp\n\nBlood Lotus(Advanced)\nPlant-Shrub\nBiome:Desert\nFlame Tongue(Basic)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Plains\n\nLariheis Fingers(Basic)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Hills\n\nElf Hair Vine(Basic)\nPlant-Ivy\nBiome:Ice\nCrouching Feather(Basic)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Plain\n\nHalflings Grass(Weak)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Plains\n\nTippen Root(Mild)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Plain\nAlabaster Leaf(mild)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Plain\n\nSaffvil(Strong)\nPlant-Grass\nBiome:Swamp\n\nClutchers Straw(Advanced)\nPlant-Shrub\nBiome:Desert\nMetzils Tangle(Advanced!)\nPlant-Ivy\nBiome:Jungle\n\nGoblins Ivy\nPlant-Ivy\nBiome: Savanna", ""),
        StaticBook("Herb Symbols", "Llywellyn Oakleaf", "*&*\n      Fire symbols\n\n-Strong\nBlistering toad\nDrakes tail\n\n-Moderate-\nFlame tongue root\nDwarfs pumpkin\nSinged kha\nElrow Berries\nBlood Lotus\n-Normal-\nBlazing fern\nFire flower\nNight sap\n\n-Weak-\nDessert Berry bush (Berries)\n\nOrc's Braid\n*&*\n    Earth Symbols\n\n-Moderate-\nAlabaster leaf\nFairie truffle\nTippens root \nSaffvil\nDrilltongue\nDesert berry bush (stem)\nBronze dust\n-Weak-\nGoblin's Ivy \nMiner's helmet\n*&*\n     Water Symbols\n\n-Strong-\nAqua Nymph\nAthin\nSpirit of Magnolis\n\n-Moderate-\nSerpents stalk\nMandragora\nFrost vine\nZawabate\nJoker's Scum\n*&*\n       Air symbols\n\n-Strong-\nCrouching Feather\nElf's Hair vine \nWisp's Breath\n\n-Moderate-\nSwamp blossom\n\n-Weak-\nJailer's Moss\n*&*\n         Unknown\n\n-King's Ivy\n-Shade leaf\n-Biteit\n-Atheros (Possible Water symbol)\n-Gijaklul\n-Javens", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbal Tea", "Daeron", "Herbal Tea! For those with sophisticated minds.\n\nPrevent kidney disease, the common cold, and even cancer!\n\nThis delivery provided to you by,\nDaeron Haevaul\n\nEnjoy!", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbalism vol.01", "Elder Elf", "~*~*~A GUIDE~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~TO~*~*~*~*\n~*~*HERBALISM*~*~\n~*~*~*vol. 01*~*~*~\n~*~ALOE   PLANTS~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*A*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~DRUIDIC~*~*~*\n~*~*~*ORDER*~*~*~\n~*~*~*TOME*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n          .-. .-.\n         (_ | _)\n          (_|_)\n             |\n             |\n             \\\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#########################Written By####\n##The Druid of Song#\n###########################♫#################♫♫♫#########\n✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿FOR BELERAN✿✿\n✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪The aloe plant is an age old plant that is famous for its healing abilities.  It can be prepared a number of ways.  This tome will explain those ways.\nAloe can be ingested,\napplied to the skin, or ground and combined\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪with other herbs to create an even more potent healing salve.\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪\n1: INGESTION\nIt is very potent to\ndirectly ingest, so cut out the flesh and brew it into a tea.  It can be used to treat...\n✿Constipation\n✿Hard of breathing\n✿Colds\n✿Partial blindness\n♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪\n♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ 2:DIRECT APPLICATION\nThe cut plant can be applied directly to the skin for...\n✿Sunburn\n✿Frostbite\n✿Open Wounds\n✿Burns\n✿Sores\n✿...and flaky skin!\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪3: Combination\nThe plant can be combined with other herbs.\n\n✿Goldenrod\n✿Blissfoil\n✿Cactus Green\n✿Kolagotu\n✿And many more!\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪Please be sure to read our other volumes for more information on creating salves and poltices.\n♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣THANK♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣YOU♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣FOR♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣SUPPORTING♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣THE DRUIDS♣♣♣♣♣♣", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbert & Stacy", "Braelynn Copper", "Once upon a time..\nin the land of oren.\nthere was a lost little sheep who went by Herbert. Herbert was a friendly little sheep, and all he ever wanted was to have some friends to play with, and thats how he got lost.\n\nOne day Herbert was in the pasture with all the other sheep, but the other sheep were playing together, all of them except Herbert.\nHerbert was sad that he got left out, so he decided to wander off and try to find a friend. He searched cloud temple,\nno one wanted to be his friend. He searched around the high elf lands, and yet no friends to be found. Next was oren, he still haven't found any friends, but he did find himself lost. He was in such a worry he forgot his task of finding a friend and\nstarted asking people to help him get home. After hours of asking and being declined he lost hope. That was all until he heard a little voice calling his name.\n\"Who's there?\" Herbert asked. \"It's me! Down Here!\" called the little voice. Herbert\nimmediately looked down to find a little grass hopper below him. \"Who are you?\" Herbert asked. \"Well I'm stacy! I heard you were lost? How'd that happen, fella?\" She said \"Well, I was looking for a friend and I got lost\" Explained Herbert. \"Aww poor guy\"\nsaid Stacy. \"Will you help me get home?\" asked Herbert. \"I'm not just going to help you get home, I want to be your friend too!\"\nExclaimed Stacy.\n\"Really? You want to be my friend? Oh joy oh joy!\" Rejoiced Herbert. \"What are we waiting for? Lets go home!\"\nSaid Stacy. They made their travels back to Herbert's homeland that will soon become Stacy's home too. Stacy and Herbert were the best of friends and lived happily ever after.\n\n\n\n       The End", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 1", "Leyun Kameki", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 1\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun Kameki\nLeyun's Forward\nWhen I learned to use the gifts of nature to heal, Callax gave me his list of herbs. It is time to write this information down in a form that can be widely shared. Hopefully it'll be of use to anyone who heals using herbs.\nAthin\nAn herb with a blue visage. It grows at the bottom of almost frozen lakes.\nEffects: Athin works as a cooling balm, making an excellent lotion. It also can cause blue hued skin.\nOverdose: Mild Frostbite\nAlchemical Properties:\nAthin is a strong water symbol, good for use in colder potions.\nNotes: Generally requires at least two people to harvest due to freezing conditions.\nAlabaster Leaf\nAn herb of Alabaster hue. It grows in drier areas in forests, typcally near fallen trees.\nEffects: As a mild poison, Alabaster Leaf causes dizziness and nausea.\nOverdose: Extreme fatigue.\nAlchemical Properties: Alabaster Leaf is a moderate earth symbol.\nNotes: Often used as a dye/paint. Harvest by carefully cutting the leaves.\nAqua Nymph\nA small chain of fragile blue baubbles that grow underwater. It is often mistaken for frog or toad spawn.\nEffects: Severe hallucinations when ingested as an herb. Powerful burn remedy when boiled. Causes the throat to close up when\ningested in oil form.\nOverdose: Stronger Effects\nAlchemical Properties: Aqua Nymph is a strong water symbol.\nNotes: Aqua Nymph is extremely delicate and must not be touched by hands. A correct way to harvest the herb is to take the thin layer\nof sediment that it grows in and the whole plant, scooping it into a jar so that it doesn't touch the edges and it's roots remain intact. If done any other way, it will likely ruin the plant.\n\nThe plant can be made into a powerful burn remedy by pouring\nthe whole plant into into a cauldron and small pot. When boiled, the plant's buds will release a liquid that will make a thick oil that can be easily spread over burns.\nBeard Weed\nA shaggy green moss that grows hanging from rare trees in caves. A rare herb, but grows in plentiful groups.\nEffects: With water and blissfoil, it can aid in the healing of internal organ damage and ease pain. Beard weed famously\ncauses significant hair growth. Can be poisonous if not prepared properly.\nWhen toxic, it can cause bloating, nausea, diarrhea, internal bleeding, and even death.\nOverdose: Stiffness. Possible hairgrowth across the entire body, creating a\nbeast-like appearance. Alchemical Properties:\nBeard Weed is a moderate earth symbol. It works well in hair tonics.\nBlissfoil\nAn oily blue flower that grows in clumps under birch trees.\nEffects: Numbness where the oil is applied. It has been known to cause headaches.\nOverdose: Permanent loss of touch in the affected area.\nNotes: Oils are found near the petals and stalk.\nBread Mold\nA blue or green mold that grows on bread, cheese, and other food items.\nEffects: This particular mold only affects some individuals negatively. In these individuals, exposure can cause a rash or the throat to close up. The mold\nhas disease fighting properties that can be brought out by a skilled druid.\nOverdose: Too much can caue confusion, odd behavior, a severe rash, reduced urination, or seizures.\nNotes: A druid is required to bring out the disease fighting\nproperties, and care must be taken to reduce the effect of other types of mold growing with it.\nBlood Lotus\nA rust colored herb, found growing near entrances to caves in hot climates.\nEffects: Extremely nutritious, but extended use can turn the skin orange.\nOverdose: Kidney stones.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate Fire Symbol\nNotes: Can be made into a strong, deep red alcohol.\nCrimson Vase\nA vase shaped plant with deep red petals that is commonly found in places with a mild amount of light. The herb grows on trees parasitically.\nEffects: Slight burning sensation if it's liquid is spilt. It'll cause rashes.\nOverdose: Will burn even more.\nAlchemical Properties: Crimson Vase is a strong fire symbol, typically used in love, rage, and envy potions, as well as Alchemist Fire.\nNotes: The petals are warm to the touch.\nCrouching Feather\nAn herb with three white, drooping petals. It only blooms at night under large bushes.\nEffects: Calming and clears the mind. Can cause light-headedness. With proper druidic preparation, it can be used as a sedative.\nOverdose: Coma\nAlchemical Properties: Strong air symbol. It is typically used in clarity potions.\nNotes: Crouching Feather is highly fragile. Wind can damage the plant.\nDiddyfunkle\nA bright, purple flowered herb that tends to grow in jungles and plains.\nEffects: The purple stems cause extremely itchy rashes. The center ball's jucies can be used as a sedative or to clear the mind. Can cause unconciousness\nor death if not prepared correctly.\nOverdose: Death\nNotes: Tiny amounts can be a delicacy.\nDraugr Tongue\nAn aloe like, orange flowered plant that grows in grassy plains.\nEffects: The liquid in the plant makes for a good disinfectant, but stings.\nNotes: The stem is not useful.\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nA stinky, orange leafed shrub that grows by water, usually in swamps.\nEffects: Burning taste similar to ginger.\nOverdose: Burns!\nAlchemical Properties: Strong fire symbol, commonly used in Alchemist Fire.\nNotes: Easy to pick. Smells bad. It's named for it's use in dwarven brews. The brightest leaves are the most potent.\nElf's Hair Vine\nAn white blossomed herb with an icy white visage. It grows on high cliffs in frozen lands.\nEffects: It has a calming effect and can result in more fluid movements, but may cause someone to move too fast, in which case physical\nexhaustion could be an issue.\nOverdose: Rapid heart beat, burst blood vessels ad the like.\nAlchemical Properties: Strong air symbol. It's used in grace and speed potions.\nNotes: The vine is extremely fragile, and the petals contain nectar.\nFlame Tongue Root\nA bright rust colored root with a rose-like flower. It can be found in heavily forested areas, burnt out forests, and areas with a lot of sun and water.\nEffects: The root can be used as a coagulant, though it can burn.\nBe warned that the spores can cause sensitivity to touch.\nOverdose: Too much blood cloting, strokes, etc.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate fire symbol\nNotes: Fairly hot to the touch. Watch out for those spores.\nFrost Vine\nA small, brittle blue vine that grows in frosty areas, usually on trees.\nEffects: Soothes pain and and numbs/relaxes muscles where applied. Full numbness of limbs can occur on prolonged exposure.\nOverdose: Frostbite\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol.\nGoblin's Ivy\nA short brown or green vine that can be found clinging to buildings and rocks.\nEffects: Scentless, mild, nausea inducing poison that can also cause mild dehydration.\nOverdose: More nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.\nAlchemical Properties: Weak to moderate earth symbol commonly used in resilience potions.\nNotes: Goblin's Ivy can survive in nearly moistureless areas.\nGrobsnopper\nA pink or yellow buld-like flower that grows on trees, typically found in moist forests.\nEffects: Potent healing effects. \"Soaks up\" disease.\nOverdose: Stomach aches.\nHabgobsnit\nA tall, pale-shaded grass that grows in forests and plains.\nEffects: Juices good for numbing. It can provide a sense of clarity... or just get you high.\nOverdose: Paralysis\nKing's Ivy\nAn ivy with golden flowers and a dark green stalk that grows on rocks, tree trunks, and old ruins.\nEffects: Can be taken as a stimulent, but can cause agitation.\nOverdose: Heart attacks, and in general too much energy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 2", "Leyun Kameki", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 2\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun\nMalin's Heart\nA white flower that grows in plains and forests.\nEffects: Chewing numbs the whole body for a few minutes.\nOverdose: Prolonged numbness.\nNotes: A bit harder to find than blissfoil.\nMandragora\nA parsnip shaped herb that grows in swamps and wetlands.\nEffects: Revitalization and regenerative properties make the plant valuable, but the spores it releases in season cause hallucinations.\nOverdose: Can cause growths. The hallucinogenic spores often cause choking and can be fatal.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol, often used in healing potions.\nNotes: Harvest 2 weeks after maturity to avoid spores.\nNight Sap\nA golden sap that drips from deformed oak trees.\nEffects: Causes a sense of calm, safety, and happiness, along with tiredness. It usually makes for about 5 hours of sleep. After waking, though, it brings splitting headaches\nand paralysis for as much time as the sleep.\nOverdose: Longer lasting effects.\nNotes: Highly addictive.\nSaffvil\nA sickly green grass that grows in swamps near dead things.\nEffects: Nausea and blood clotting\nOverdose: Death\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate fire symbol.\nSagedust\nPollen from the Alabaster plant.\nEffects: Increased metabolism and speed, along with heightened senses and a rapid heart rate.\nOverdose: Possible heart attack.\nNotes: Incredibly difficult to harvest.\nSerpent's Stalk\nA long, reed like emerald stalk that grows in forests near or in water.\nEffects: Cooling effect when applied with water, may cause rashes.\nOverdose: Mild hypothermia.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol. Typically used in antidotes, calming, and healing potions.\nNotes: Poisonous to bugs.\nShade Leaf\nA short, small plant with plain leaves, yellow flowers, and silvery veins that is commongly found anwhere there is grass and shade.\nEffects: Calming, stress releaving, bloodshot eyes, increased appetite.\nOverdose: Hallucinations\nNotes: Grows in large quantities, simmilar to normal weeds. Makes a popping noise when exposed to rain.\nSwamp Blossom\nA purple green flower with a short, thick stem, found in the branches of swamp trees.\nEffects: Nectar is like honey, and the flower is nutritious, though consuming raw can gum up the throat.\nOverdose: Smelly breath and diarrhea.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate air symbol, usually used in speed potions.\nTippen's Root\nPurple flowers with a dark yellow speckled root that grow near fallen trees in dense forests.\nEffects: Stops bleeding almost instantly, but stinks to the seven hells.\nOverdose: Blood clots, and the dangers of blood clots.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate earth symbol, commonly used in strength and healing potions.\nNotes: Really, seriously stinks. Really. Make sure you're prepared for the stink.\nYarrow\nA white to pink flowered plant that grows in grasslands and forests.\nEffects: Can reduce inflammation and blood pressure, as well as intensify the medicinal effects of other herbs.\nOverdose: Dizziness and fainting due to\nlow blood pressure.\nZawabate\nA plant with a tall stalk and yellow-green curled petals that grows in a desert oasis in water.\nEffects: Out of body experiences, hallucinations, pain numbing.\nOverdose: Can destroy a person's mind.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate water symbol, used in numbing and healing potions.\nNotes: Nectar is the medicinal part of the plant.", ""),
        StaticBook("HEY KIDDO!!!", "[Teen] Rarat", "Hey Kiddo! i fond your other house! sorry if we started on the wrong foot, i dot think well after not sleeping in 98 days. so what i forgot to say yesterday was if you ever need ANYTHING, and oh, do i me ANYTHING just shout my name. belive me i will hear\nyou.", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elven Labs", "Melthinion", "A report of the high elves. \n\nIn the past, the high elves have been less than pleasing toward the other descendant races. However, it has come to my attention that of the abduction of other, younger races which had repulsed me so -\n- in previous dealings that I had experienced with them. While prowling around, I had searched for something of personal importance. However, in my fruitless search, I had found something rather disgusting, and repulsive. The high elven labs.\nWhat contained in these labs are as described: Biological wastes, more beneficient ways to grow crops and other farmland products, and one lab which had caught my eye specifically. It was a darkened room, with blackened glass. I had squinted, and looked -\n- inside of the room, only to be horrified. Bodies, no, torso's floating about, hearts in jars, some human, some orcish bodies, and one dwarven body. The human body was a torso, with a single arm. The dwarven body had strange holes in it, with black sur -\n- rounding the entirety of the holes. And the orcish bodies, still kept half alive. I had consulted a friend of mine who previously lived in Haulen'or, and they had said that this type of thing had been performed for decades. With numerous races involved-\n- in these inhumane crimes, leaders of other factions should most likely be informed. \n\nThese high elves will almost guaranteed, respond with \"For the good of science.\" However, what good does it do to only share these secrets amongst themselves -\n- and not share with the rest of the world? Committing inhumane crimes against the descendant races is inherintly \"okay\" within the minds of high elven kind. Thus concludes this report of high elven laboratories.", ""),
        StaticBook("His Fungi", "Motsham Malog'Yar", "((This book was written by an orc, but since most of the Blah is mispronounced common, I only wrote the words that are actually different for orcs in the Blah. The words shared between the two languages are written in Common. Sorry for the clunky OOC\npreface, but I just wanted to give the reader a heads-up.))    Many of those who gruk mi, gruk that mi have long been a devout worshiper of Orgon. Those who have visited the shrine of Orgon atop the plateau in San'Vitar, may have noticed the fungus which\npopulates the mound on which the shrine is erected. Very few people gruk the nature agh significance of the fungus, agh would ignorantly dismiss it as nub-thing more than a bunch of ugly mushrooms. These mushrooms, however, are actually a\nsupernatural phenomenon. The fungus which grows upon Orgon's mound is not of the natural world. It is a physical manifestation of Orgon's will agh influence spreading in the mortal plane. This is why lat will nub ever find any growing on their own in a\nnormal environment. Very few also gruk that the fungus is, in fact, carnivorous, but feeds almost exclusively during the feeding rituals of Orgon worship. Now, when mi blah the word \"carnivorous\", mi mean it very strongly. During the feeding ritual, the\nfungus almost instantly takes root in the flesh of the sacrifice, and begins literally consuming its prey. The process causes the victim to be rapidly digested alive within a matter of minutes. The fungus devours every last piece of its prey, leaving\nbehind neither flesh, blood, bones or organs. This is how Orgon has revealed to his followers that his sacrifices must be offered. Outside of the feeding ritual, the fungus feeds very rarely, occassionally digesting any insects that find themselves\ntrapped in the liquid secretions of the mushrooms. Now, onto the specifics. There are dub varieties of mushrooms which grow upon Orgon's sacrificial mounds: Orgon's bile and Orgon's gall. Both of these mushrooms have some similar qualities. Namely,\nneither should be taken without asking permission of Orgon and rulging him for his generosity; agh they should both be handled with care. \n Orgon's bile: These short, squat mushrooms are a bluish-purple color with white spots. On each spot grow many\ntiny black spores. The spores are easily broken, agh contain a foul-smelling black substance. It smells very much like decomposing flesh, and tastes like rotten eggs. Contact stains the skin. A slight taste of the mushroom or the oily, black substance\ncauses nausea (agh mi mean a VERY slight taste). Mi tested the effects of full consumption of the mushroom on a willing burz-albai named Mithras. Upon immediately eating the whole thing, he was beset by extreme nausea and vomiting, a cold sweat and\nsevere shaking. This was from only ash mushroom. Mi would strongly advise against eating more than ash or a particularly large specimen, as such could very possibly result in flattening. ((Note: these are the red mushrooms growing near Orgon's\nshrine))\n Orgon's gall: These somewhat taller mushrooms are related to Orgon's bile, agh are brown in color. The cap of the Orgon's gall mushroom is bowl shaped, agh constantly secretes a very bitter yellowish-brown fluid. This fluid pools in\nthe aforementioned bowl-shaped cap, and emits musty fumes which irritate the eyes upon exposure. Physical contact with the mushroom causes a slight burning sensation in the skin, as the fungus coats itself in its own digestive fluids. In small amounts,\nthe digestive fluids seem harmless, however mi have witnessed in mi own worship of Orgon how quickly these fungi digest their prey in large enough groups; agh mi gruk it safe to assume that a single mushroom could eventually cause significant damage\ngiven enough time. Mi tested the effects of Orgon's gall on a shara named Hagan, who exhibited an extremely dry mouth, blurred vision and hallucinations. As with Orgon's bile, mi would strongly recommend against eating dub or more of these mushrooms, as\noverconsumption could have dangerous effects, including flattening. Mi would also theorise that such could possibly lead to lasting impacts on mental health. \n Further discoveries concerning Orgon's bile or Orgon's gall will be recorded agh published in\nfuture books if needed.\n -Malog'Yar, witch doctor agh loyal servant of Orgon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hist. of Evaral", "Ebonsquire", "The History Evalar, the First City of the Elves\n\n((Originally scribed by HiddenForge))\nA long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a Magikal power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundant there and in the surrounding areas.\nIt let all plant grow abundantely there and in the surrounding areas. The sand there made glass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the First Race, later known as Elves, planted their magikal seeds... Great towering trees grew in\ntheir place. Ordinary Fyre could not scorch these trees, for the magik embedded in them was still new. The Elves thrived in the new land along with the trees, spreading its seeds wherever they went, creating an Empre that dwarved all others previously\nknown. The Elves lived inside the trunks of these towering trees, singing to them to help them grow. And all was peaceful. Then one day many centuries, an Astronomical Storm swept across the land, felling the magikal trees where they stood. Lightning\nstruck the exposed Earth, melting the ground and forming pools of lava. Great Fyre, fueled by the dark energies of the storm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometers remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named\nthis area Evaral, meaning 'Protected' in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the Magikal trees once more, but then the Earth still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn't let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated,\nthe Elves started to reach for the sky. The trees grew until the touched the highest planes of the Atmosphere! And all was at peace once again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from new predators and spirits that\nrose with the storm. And then a terrible  thing happened. Some of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and wanted more land, ores, and resources. One by one the Dissenters left Evaral, preferring the new\nforests beyond its border. They spread out far across the land, struggling to cope with their new homes. Eventually, even they settled down and formed small vilages, under no ruler. Some even evolved into other races, forgetting what they left behind.\nBy this time, only a few families remained in Evaral, and they did  not know what to do. They missed the kinship of the other eElves, so they decided to leave too. But before they left, each family took with them a seed from the first tree, which happened\nto reside in Evaral. This tree was very old and wrought with homes. And its spirit was sad too, for it missed the Elves that left. It shed its bark to help the remaining Elves in their journeys, forming impenetrable armor to help the remaining elves in\ntheir journeys. This armor now resides in the Tomb of Evaral, as the First Tree's spirit reclaimed it. And then none were left in Evaral. However, over the centuries the seed still could grow, but the land never accepted them. Until one day, many\ncenturies later, it camei n the hands of a young druid. The great city of Evaral's location is hidden from the world, but many believe it is still out there. Perhaps one day, a great hero will stumble upon it. And bring it to power once again.", ""),
        StaticBook("History - Slayer", "Athe'lor", "History of the Void, as Written by Arcane Mage Slayer, Aegis.\n\nBefore the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But within the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity.\nBut this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in the Void the world of Aegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the world of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life.\nAfter breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and unformed, into the world of Aegis itself. This power was to be called magic by man, and just as man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilised-\nby man to be a test, a test of greed and power.\n\nThe power was entwined into the very fabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked, ever connected. So it was that all the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same.\nAs the power was channelled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore manifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the Humans had a diverse spread of magic, as they were the most versatile.\nThe Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone, hardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts, strong and vicious. The power of the Nobel races came from their allegiance:\nthe Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil.\n\nThe first of the Mages quickly discovered its usefulness, its power... they noticed how dangerous it was.\nThey had the power to kill in an instant, or create in an instant... They had power over all. In their wisdom the saw that something would have to be done... The power was to be controlled, learned properly.\nBut the magic was not forever present in the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to void by the ancients.\nThis sent his minions back whence they came, and a barrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world...\nBut it was not to last. The power of Iblees was great, even in void, and he worked at unravelling the barrier between the worlds... Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis.\nAlthough this time there was little hope for salvation...\n\nWith the failing of the barrier protecting the world of the living from the dead the magic lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world.\nThe people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat unfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there.\n\nSo it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man.\nThose with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other darkness... They could only hope that with this new found power that the right decision would be made...\nSo it was that the first Mage Ram'Ir, first in the line of the great mages, gathered to him a group of the most trusted and powerful Mages in the lands, and gave them a duty, a life quest.\nA duty, to protect the land of Aegis and the Decendants from themselves, from what lies within, so that the Magic which remained through the ages would not destroy all, but be contained and conserved.\nSo it was that the Guild of mages was forged into existence, accepting those with great magical power, or great skill in other areas of their interest.\nThey will not interfere in the day-to-day lives of the people of Aegis, however would intervene at the mistreat of magic.\nAnd now it comes to pass that the mages guild is headed by the arcane mage Slayer, who reconstructed the ancient mages tower in the snowy north’s to be the head of the great guild, the centre piece of the smaller guilds-\nscattered around the world of Aegis. The tower acts as a meeting place, a place of learning and teaching to all those in the guild who make the perilous journey...\nAlthough there is just as much to be done in the city guilds who accept those of like race. \n\n\n\n\nOriginally written by Arcane Mage Slayer, rewritten by Athe'lor for Andria Ith'ael.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Magic", "Leyu", "The History of Magic\nTranscribed on Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1304. Scribed by Arch Mage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer. :: :: :: :: :: :: :: Before the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But\nwithin the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in the Void the world of Aegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the\nworld of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and unformed, into the world of Aegis itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just\nas man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power. :: The power was entwined into the very fabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked, ever connected. So it was that\nall the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power was channelled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore manifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the\nHumans had a diverse spread of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone, hardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts,\nstrong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance: The Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil. :: But the magic was not forever present\nin the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the Void by the ancients. This sent his minions back whence they came, and a\nbarrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world... :: But it was not to last. The power of Iblees was\ngreat, even in the Void, and he worked at unravelling the barrier between the worlds... Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although this time there was little hope for salvation... ::\nWith the failing of the barrier protectingthe world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat\nunfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there. :: :: So it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other\ndarkness...They could only hope with this new found power that the right decision would be made...\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Magic", "Jistuma", "Transcribed on Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1304. Scribed by Arch Mage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer\nBefore the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But within the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in he Void the world of\nAegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the world of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and\nunformed, into the world of Aegis itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just as man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power.\nThe power was entwined into the very\nfabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked ever connected. So it was that all the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power channeled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore\nmanifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the Humans had a diverse spead of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone,\nhardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts, strong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance: The Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil.\nBut the magic was not forever present in the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the Void by the ancients. This sent his\nminions back whence they came, and a barrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world… But it was not to\nlast. The power of Iblees was great, even in the Void, and he worked at unraveling the barrier between the worlds… Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although this time there was little hope\nfor salvation…\nWith the failing of the barrier protecting the world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat\nunfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there.\n\nSo it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other to\ndarkness… They could only hope with this new found power that the right decision would be made…\nThe History of Magic\n\nRewritten by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", "")
    )

    private fun _VAILOR_3(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("History of Magic", "The Eternal Library", "Transcribed on the 9th of The First Seed, 1548. Scribed by Archmage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer.\nBefore the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But within the Void was a light, we know this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in the void the world of\nAegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the world of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and\nunformed into the world of Aegi itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just as man was placed into the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power.\nThe power was entwined into the very fabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked ever connected. So it was that all the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power channeled through the individual, it scanned\ntheir soul, and was therefore manifested as an extension of their natural enviroment. So it was that the Humans had a diverse spread of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves came\nfrom their mighty halls of stone hardened and sturdy. Then the orcs came from their harsh deserts, strong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance; the Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The undead from\n\ntheir fiery hells, tainted and evil. But the magic was not forever present in the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the void by\nthe ancients. This sent his minions back whence they came, and a barrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in seperation from the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared\nfrom the world. But it was not to last. The power of Iblees was great, even in the void, and he worked at unraveling the barrier between the worlds. Soon the barrier began to break down, the undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although\nthis time there was littl hope for salvation. With the failure of the barrier protecting the world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of\nAegis once more felt a somewhat unfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there. So it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Tose with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path.\nOne to light and the other to darkness. They could only hope that with this newly found power the right decision would be made.\n\nThe History of Magic\nWritten by Leyu'Maehr\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerhaven", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Magic", "Rosso", "Transcribed on Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1304. Scribed by Arch Mage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer\nBefore the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But within the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in he Void the world of\nAegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the world of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and\nunformed, into the world of Aegis itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just as man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power.\nThe power was entwined into the very\nfabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked ever connected. So it was that all the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power channeled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore\nmanifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the Humans had a diverse spead of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone,\nhardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts, strong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance: The Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil.\nBut the magic was not forever present in the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the Void by the ancients. This sent his\nminions back whence they came, and a barrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world… But it was not to\nlast. The power of Iblees was great, even in the Void, and he worked at unraveling the barrier between the worlds… Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although this time there was little hope\nfor salvation…\nWith the failing of the barrier protecting the world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat\nunfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there.\n\nSo it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see\nahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other to darkness… They could only hope with this new found power that the right decision would be made…\nThe History of Magic\n\nRewritten by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("History Research", "GradyBarrington", "VonSchlichten Origins\n\n\nThis book will chronicle my partner's and my research on the VonSchlichten  clan\n\nThis will be volume 1\nThe first day of our research was halted by the library keeper. Apparently we need to give a book if we want to copy a book. This could take some time. We either have to write a book or... \"find\"... A book.\nMy partner, \"The Captain\" as he likes to be called, attempted to bribe the library keeper. It ended with the expected out come. He only had 60 minas....\nOur first lead was a book called Necromancy. From my few interactions with Gustav I am led to believe that the older VonSchlichtens practiced this art. We will return with a book for trade.\nWe headed to the Elven lands in search of books. They led us on for a bit before revealing they had no books for us to have or buy.\nThe Captain got in a verbal fight with a child.\nWe travled to the land of the orcs. When we arrived there was a huge arch way with swirling blackness in the middle. We weren't sure what was going on and there were people and orcs gathered outside of the arch\nWe hid for a bit, but eventually we were found out. There were four of us and only three made it out alive.\nWe returned to the orc lands after everything calmed down. While we were there we... aquired...... A book for trade. Something about immortal spirits. I'm sure its not very important.\nWell... Got shut down by a librarian. She thought she told me everything i needed to know. She was wrong.\nNecromancy - Black Magic: The art of communication with the dead: Witchcraft: There are many forms of necromancy but in this day there is only secret necromancy.\nA group that people call the \"Undead\" have been known to use Necromancy to their full extent. The Necromancers in their organization have been using necromancy against the people of aegis. the power that the dead give them through necromancy\nGives them the ability to summon the dead, use the weather, as in lightning, and use magic that comes from hell, or also known as the \"Nether\".\nThe people of aegis have started to follow the \"Undead\" and Necromancers and have been studying their ways,\ngiving them the ability to use this form of black magic.the ascended have been known to be against this magic. ascended does not patrol the open roads like the necromancers and Undead do. Rumors around say that they stay at a heavenly place near\nthe cloud temple.\nThe attacks of the Necromancers have been deadly, and usually have won the battle and took the victory back to the nether and celebrated with the spirits. The only known tplaces that have been attacked are snow feilds, Winterfell\nAlstion town, and Kal'Bryst. Now if you haven't noticed already, it has been going from north to south. In that case, the conditions that have been gathered through predictions that the next attacks could be at the following cities: Al' Khazar, stone leaf\nWhispering Isle, and Kal' Alras. They are just slight predictions, the Undead probably wont even attack them. It's just prediction. The Undead are frowing in numbers. The last known report of them traveling in a pack was the number count of five.\nBut this last report was long ago. The numbers could have been doubled, No one knows. So, from what you ahve been reading, the Necromancers are deadly, and you should avoid them at all times. If not, you could lose your life or loved ones around you\nI, The author, am leaving this book unsigned so that if an Undead finds this wont be slain. A second book could be created if any more records or information is released.\n(I have provided Transcript of the book in question)", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Knight Poem", "Arygon", "Quite old i am. Still a Holy Knight i wished to become. Unproven am, but yet a Soldier by heart i am. Proven soon i will become. But a mere pawn i am. My superiors respect i will, but yet above them GOD still is. For he will help me achieve my goals. He -\nwill help me become one of the Seven. For me there is no tryin'. There is onlyh' doing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls - I", "Jacob Chapel", "The Holy Scrolls\n\n     The Book of\n     Nativities\n\nTransscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Deep Cold, 1470.\n\nUse these words to keep true to your faith and to find strength and knowledge.\nThere were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existence of such a Deity in contrast to the\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\nthe Seven Skys. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? That is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and how\nclean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and the Daemon,\nthe two spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and\nthe Man lived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay\nand the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings could not talk, nor did they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to\nset eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\n\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the\nscorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\nSoon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken with grief at the loss of their\nparents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\n\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks and traits. The Elves with Malin\nat their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\n\nAt this time, Malin, Urguan, Krug and\nHoren were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for each other and each others people.\nUrguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of Aegis, and Horen began building the\nfirst squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace. Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the Void, kin spirits to the Aengul, defected.\nIblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things delicate, he was quickly\nbefriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\n\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's plan to test the\ndescendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content. Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to\noccupy the barren forests.\n\nTo Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him.\nHoren, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased. He needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality.\n\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food,\nwith power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded\nfrom his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury.\nOnly Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror.\n\nIn Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin\nburned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and\nthe ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword\nwas fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor the thirty years the Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descendants\ndied, the greater Iblees’ armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter,\nhis resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew greedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the\nworld was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers.\nAn army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight\ncould see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\n\nIblees’ soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the\nworld, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before\nIblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment.\nBut before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time.\n\n“You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls that\ninhabit it.\n\nMalin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of your own. Even you have done my work,\nif you realize it or not.\n\nUrguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in the deep underground of the earth,\nyour hunger never satisfied.\n\nHoren, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and die before you ever taste the\nfruits of your pointless labors.\n\nAnd you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your lust for battle shall be\nunsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.”\n\nAs soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World. The Descendants stood\nstill for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to corrupt their souls,\nthe brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into thin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls -II", "Jacob Chapel", "The Holy Scrolls\n\n     The Book of\n     Horen\n\nTransscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Amber Cold, 1471.\n\nUse these words as a source of strength and widom.\nThe years passed and went on and on, as time is wont to do. The Decendant, after being cursed by the Great Devil, adapted their lives to suit their new roles. There was, for some time, peace and prosperity amongst the original realms created by the\nCreator. One day, upon the cusp of which a red sun rose from the east, King Horen of humanity was approached by an Aengul, a divine messenger of God. This Aengul shone magnificently, illuminated by the light of God, its shades and colours twisting\naround one another as it addressed Horen. Its wings swathed in blinding white, it opened its mouth and through it the Creator spoke.\n“Horen of Man. God has chosen you as his divine prophet, as his mouthpiece on this world, until the day of\nyour ascent into the Seven Skies at his order. You are the almighty king, the Creator’s chiefmost servant on this hallowed earth. Be jubilant, for you are second to none but me! Humanity is the holy divine being of God, the human body remaining the most\nunadulterated, original form of the Creator’s design, not possessing of neither corruption nor mutation. You are the chosen people, and you shall carry out my commands, and your people alone, not your brothers and their kin, shall swear to my commandments\nThey are as follows!\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the Creator and Guide of everything that has been created; He alone has made, does make, and will make all things.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Divine\nare the Creator’s regents in this realm and that their obedience is worship to the Creator.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Aenguls and Daemons are the Creator’s servants.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator\nBlessed be His Name, is One, and that there is no unity in any manner like His, and that He alone is our God, who was, and is, and will be.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, has no body, and that He is free from all\nproperties of matter, and that there can be no comparison to Him whatsoever.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the first and the last.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name,\nand to Him alone, it is right to pray, and that it is not right to pray to any being besides Him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that all the words of the Divines are true.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the\nprophecy of Horen I our teacher, blessings be upon him, was true, and that he was the chief of the Divines, both those who preceded him and those who followed him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the entire scrolls that is now in our possession is the\nsame that was given to our Divines, blessings be upon them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Holy Scrolls can not be corrupted\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, knows all the deeds\nof beings and all their thoughts.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, rewards those who keep His commandments and punishes those that transgress them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that there will\nbe a revival of the dead at the time when it shall please the Creator, Blessed be His Name, and His mentions shall be exalted for ever and ever.”\n\nAnd so Horen listened, and he repeated the Creator’s words, and he carried the word\nof the Creator to his people, who listened as he did. They kneeled before Horen, first of the Divine, and pledged the commandments and supremacy of humanity over all but God. The realmn of man rallied underneath the Regent of Heven, arming themselves and\nerecting great fortresses, beginning the golden age of the Horen dynasty. For truly, it was decreed that humanity was second to none but the Creator, and the chose people would carry out his command until the end of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Home", "Henry Winterleaf", "Home\n----\n\nA poem by Henry Winterleaf\nHome is where you hang your hat, or so the saying goes.\nWell, I come from a far off land where it doesn't rain, it snows.\n\nHome is where you feel the safest.\nThe one place in the world that you think is the greatest.\nHome is family spending time together.\nHaving fun, without the sun, despite the stormy weather.\n\nHome is surrounding yourself with friends.\nSharing laughs together and hoping it wont end.\nHome is the where you go when you're feeling down.\nTo ease away frustration, removing all your frowns.\n\nHome. Home means different things to everyone.\nSnow, rain, wind, blistering sun.\nThe place I called home is long gone, but there's no need to cry.\nHome is where I make it, so I don't have to say goodbye.", ""),
        StaticBook("Honey Bee A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "As an introduction, the book is written with the purpose of studying the anatomy of your average honey bee for use in conjuration.\n   In this book, I shall be covering the honey bee's anatomy in three sections: the head, thorax, and the abdomen.\n*Upon flipping onward, you're greeted by several incredibly detailed sketchings of the honey bee's head from various angles and even the structures there within.*\nThe Head:\n   This part of the honey bee consists of the vertex, gena, ocelli, antenna, compound eyes, feelers, and proboscis.\n   The purpose of the head is fairly self evident. Its purpose is to house the brain, allow for various functions such as -\n- feeding and sensing the environment.\n*The next page shows sketchings much like before, except they display the mid-section of the bee, its thorax. They show from various angles and the structures there within just as before.*\nThorax:\n   The various structures within this system are the six legs, its wings, and many of the bee's organs.\n   The purpose of it involves transportation via the wings or legs, which collect pollen. Otherwise, there are the organs within, -\n- which were detailed in the sketching.\n*This next page contains a similar set of sketchings as the previous two, demonstrating the various structures and organs within the abdomen of a honey bee.*\nAbdomen:\n   The abdomen is where the stinger and the sternum are. More interestingly for this study, where its venom lies.\n   The purpose of the abdomen in a honey bee is in excreting its wastes as well as using its stinger to kill threats.\nUnfortunately for the honey bee, its stinger is often lost when trying to sting a much larger target, resulting in its death shortly after.\nSide Notes:\n-Honey bees are generally less aggressive than their wasp friends, whom bite instead of sting.\n-Many bees died.\n-Sorry. Sort of.\n*All of the sketches previously seen throughout the book are miniature and set side by side throughout the last pages of the book, clearly in place for comparison purposes.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Hope", "Aerxuis", "Aspect Tome: Hope \nAuthor Unknown\nHope, the very true innocence in a place where all is lost. No matter what happens, a person will always have hope, but how does it affect us? It is very simple, Hope is a very difficult emotion anybody can do with right now.\nHope is the emotion that supported the birth of Life. It cannot be explained easily, but it is true.\nBut for us Druids, our trigger on Hope is very similar, but different. We have our hopes on the Aspects,\nwhich are Cerridwen and Cerrunen, we are their conduits and we expect them to assist us in our times of need...\nHope can trigger within us at any moment, when War is happening, when you're being held hostage, when a family member or a friend is dying. It can happen as much as it can, but you cannot assume to ignore it.\nIt is often described as, “The smallest light in a room full of darkness,” even the very evil have it, but their use for it is on their own accord.\nThis also causes many things, rebellions and such, for some take Hope too seriously, and it often turns them into power-hungry people. This has been an account of this Emotion, may your new found Knowledge flourish.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hope!", "KetchenX", "I bet you not know my name! But you shall now know my name! My name is Erik! Erik Stalfen, Oh how I do wish to get to know you better! Perhaps you will take me my offer, me taking you on a date of course!\nIt can be anywhere you want! Just let me know and I will take you there! Mr. Whiskers seemingly approved of you so you are worthy in my book! I realise you probably do not like my people very much but I don't like your either so its okay!\nYour beauty was just off the charts! Perhaps I can show you the world and everything it has to offer! Also you said you were Adunan, which is great because as am I, pretty much! We are a dying race, we must stick together!\nI don't really know what to say but.. I hope to see you again! Feel free to send me a bird! Also I often reside in Sutica, the Edict Keep and The Cloud temple Docks so hopefully we will meet again! But Until then!", ""),
        StaticBook("Horen's 'Swamp'", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "There once was a wee lil' lass named Emporer Horen! His demease was rather petty so he stooped low, low, low. He set his eyes upon the jewel of the world, Shreck's Swamp. With a bold strut he rapped upon Duloc's gates, Shreck's castle, and demanded he\nopen the gates and swear fealty. Shreck peered down, offering him a 'bro you crazy af' look before descending. Huffing and puffing, he blew his own gates right off then kicked Horen's head right off. Literally. Before it hit the ground his corpse had been\nmutilated with Shreck's strong orkish hands to such a degree it looked like a heap of onions. That is the story of how Horen the swamp thief lost his life to Swampgoth Shreck'Lak.\n\n\n\n\ns w a m p", ""),
        StaticBook("Horns of Ylmir", "Ulmo Maehr", "The Horns of Ylmir\n\nAn extract from the song of the same name.\n\nI heard them wailing round me where the black cliffs towered \nAnd the old primeval starlight filckered palely in the sky.\nIn that dim and perilous region in\nwhose great tempestuous ways\nI heard no sound of men's voices, in those eldest of days,\nI sat on the ruinded margin of the deep-voiced echoing sea\nWhose roaring foaming music crashed in endless cadency\nOn the land besieged\nfor ever in an aeon of assualts\nAnd torn in towers and pinnacles and caverned in great vaults;\nAnd its arches shook with thunder and its feet were piled with shapes\nRiven in old sea-warfare from those crags and\nsable capes.\n\n-Verse 3 of 'The Horns of Ylmir' as recorded in 'The Fall of Gondolin'\n\n-A celebratory tale of the might of Ulmo, Lord of the Waters.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hospitality pt.1", "Sethperith Lucital", "My brother, Taynein Lucital, a good and intelligent Mali'thill, died with complications from the Plague. Upon his death, I have been gathering his personal affects and have been sorting through them. It has been a mournful journey, and, I say with some\npride, it will be a time before that journey is over. For he has left me much, not in physical inheritance, but in cherished memories much more precious than anything he could have given me with minas.\n\nHowever, there was an item he left for me that has\nent me to resurface memories from years past and reconsider them, and I currently quarrel with myself in how to interpret them. They center around a man named Deinalt Mephistaurus, a human mage who I had met myself. His intelligence surprised and\nimpressed me, and he was a much gracious man, if stern where he needed to be.\n\nMephistaurus was killed in his own bed by a cowardly band of brigands, whose only motive was the coin his death would bring them. I feel, to this day, that his death was\nunfortunate, but... perhaps it wasn't entirely uncalled for?\n\nYou see, dear reader, my brother had stayed a time at Deinalt's tower in Rahult, and had written to me many letters from there regaling me of the man's upmost care and generosity to him, but he\nhad written one letter that he did not send. It appears he thought to, but decided to perhaps destroy it, and then rethought it again, opting to keep it in his jacket lining. I can only surmise what his reasons were, but finding this letter had me revisit\nthe whole stack which I, thankfully, still keep.\n\nThere is little written about Deinalt Mephistaurus, for all he achieved, and even less about Rahult (the little village does not even appear on any Atheran maps I've seen, and I cannot find anyone actually\nfrom the place!). After much soul-searching (for some of these letters would put in jeopardy my dear departed brother's purity), I have decided to compile these notes so as there is something out there.  I will keep my own editing and notation to a\nminimum as to allow you, dear reader, to draw your own conclusions.\n5th of Malin's Welcome, 1480\n\nSeth,\n\nI have reached my destination, and, let me tell you, Oren is one big mudhole. Everything smells of hay and horses and dirt. And Rahult, such a backwater place it is, is worse in that it also stinks of fish that\nshould have been taken out of the sun a day ago. Deinalt's tower hung over this brown-and-gray place like a lighthouse, and eager as I was to get to it, the inside was such a stark difference!\n\nTapestries and banners festooned the halls with warmth and\nluxury, and there was a constant smell of pleasant potpourris and cooked treats that made even the very act of walking into his tower akin to separating myself into a completely separate world. It is a beautiful dream locked away in the middle of an\nunforgivingly filthy reality!\n\nComing here on diplomatic business, however, seems to me to be a waste of time. Since this town is so out-of-the-way, hardly anyone of note comes here. But, since the people I need to speak with are the same people Deinalt\nwill be needing to entertain, here I am. But, perhaps it will work out after all? I hardly need to leave this tower while I'm here, and maybe it's best to stay away from the more crowded human cities...\n\nAnyway, I wanted to let you know that I am safe and\nwell, if not delighted! Do not feel sorry for me. But, please, feed my Emerald some seed once you've received this; she does not seem to care for the local variety.\n\nTaynein\n11th of Malin's Welcome, 1480\n\nSeth,\n\nHow fantastic Deinalt's tower is! Everything here shimmers in guilded and silvery warmth. And the food! Perhaps the Valah know what they're doing with some of their heartier meals, though they are not without\ntheir own delicate pastries...\n\nSpeaking of guilded, delicate pastries, allow me to gush on a certain woman I met. She is human, but everything about her is golden--her eyes, her skin, her hair--all like burnt honey, and she's just as sweet. I haven't\ncaught her name, so I've taken to calling her \"Honey\". She is a servant of Deinalt, and she shimmers, inside and out, with joy and beauty.\n\nShe walks the halls with me and shows me about, and everyone approaches her and she returns their words with such\ngeniality. May I say I'm enchanted by her?\n\nA man I needed to speak with has joined us tonight to dinner with Deinalt. I've already sent my briefing back to the parties interested, but it went well. Deinalt also had business with him, apparently paying\nthe taxes for his little settlement. The taxes sound high to me, and I mentioned as much, but Deinalt waved my concerns away. He says he is more than willing to pay extra if that is his duty to his homeland. I thought it sounded strange, but the\nrepresentative seemed more than happy with the answer.\n\nHow is mother? She sent me a message, and I have returned it, but I have not received an answer.\n\nTaynein\n20th of Malin's Welcome,\n1480\n\nSeth,\n\nI hope mother is well. I am very sorry to hear about her illness, but she has a tendancy to bounce back. I am sure this should be the same.\n\nYou seemed a little upset about the idea of my being\nso enchanted by Honey from your last letter. But trust me, brother, if you had met her, you would change your mind so quickly! I'm still learning more about her; it's amazing how calm and regal she seems, but she never seems to sit or sleep for her\nbusiness. I think she is a favorite of Deinalt, but I do not know how far that favoritism goes.\n\nThe talks have all been going well for me, but I must say how happy I am to have Deinalt with me as I proceed, for he seems to have high acclaim among the\nnobility here. It feels me with some happiness, for I have seen how the citizens look at this tower, and it saddens me that they have such open hatred for their generous lord.\n\nPlease send me more updates if anything happens.\n\nTaynein\n4th of The First Seed, 1480\n\nSeth,\n\nTo the void with your opinions! Hah, I am sorry, but I had to say that old joke again.\n\nI have gone into the village alone for the first time, to get some fresh air, and how I immediately regretted it! The stench I\nbefore described has not bettered with the seasons. The humans here look at me with suspicion, if not open disdain, and I was very quick to return to the tower after getting some supplies.\n\nThere was one man that, for a moment, I had sworn was Mali'ker,\nfor his skin was as black as ueth and his expression seemed chiselled on for how stern he looked. It took seeing his ligher-skinned son at his knees to realize he was another Valah.\n\nHis son did not look at me so angrily; if anything, he seemed curious,\nand I could imagine his lighter eyes brightening easily with happiness in a different situation. In fact, the child looked strangely familiar to me, but I cannot say how.\n\nSo maybe you're right about humans, brother. To an extent.\n\nTaynein\nSo maybe you're right about humans, brother. To an extent.\n\nTaynein\nSo maybe you're right about humans, brother. To an extent.\n\nTaynein\n12th of The First Seed, 1480\n\nSeth,\n\nI have seen Deinalt shout at someone for the first time, and, to my misfortune, it was me!\n\nI shall be frank, though; I deserved it. He had discovered that I was wishing to take Honey away to our lands, and he had\ncornered me. The only thing I feel a little offended by in the conversation is that he accused me of taking advantage of her... as if she had no choice in her actions!\n\nSpeaking about this later with Honey, I have discovered that Deinalt is protective of\nher, and he had taken her from the village, ostensibly for her own good. I am not entirely sure, but after seeing the village myself, I could believe it.\n\nIt's good to hear about mother's recovery. I'm sure her gardens will be blooming again, soon.\n\nTay\n15th of The First Seed, 1480\n\nSeth,\n\nI write to you now because I have exprienced something particularly singular. I have come to a strange, reoccurring dream within these walls. The first time, I wrote it off, but tonight, I feel I cannot so easily.\nThe dream is that I awaken to my room here, dimmed in the darkness of night, and in this darkness, a white face, mouth and eyes gaping with only blackness within them, stares at me, seemingly floating in the blackness. The face flitters away as I sit,\nfrozen in fear. I think this time, before I fully awoke, I may have seen the face above black robes and a gray, faded tabard, but I cannot be sure.\n\nWhat do you suppose the dream means? Perhaps the room Deinalt placed me in is haunted? I may speak with\nDeinalt about this in the morning.\n\nTaynein\n22nd of The First Seed, 1480\n\nSeth,\n\nAs much as I love Honey, perhaps it is a good thing I cannot take her. I have noticed that there are times she just... stands there. Like a statue. For a long time I thought she was simply looking over the rooms,\nand she looked so distracted that I did not wish to disturb her.\n\nHowever, I have attempted to speak with her today when she did so today, and she did not respond for long moments, and when she did, she seemed to be surprised that I was there, even though\nI hardly snuck up on her.\n\nPerhaps this is what Deinalt meant by \"taking advantage\"? It feels rude to ask about it. She certainly does seem to enjoy serving him, and I can hardly blame her; he treated her especially well today, and she was simply beaming\nwhen he told her he needed her help with a ritual. I would have liked to help as well, but he insisted she was all the help he needed, and the room for the ritual was too small for too many people. Considering how large his tower is, I thought that was\nstrange, but it is not my place to question it.\n\nIn any case, the ritual must have taken quite some time; I didn't even see Honey leave the room after, so I suppose she had to clean up. I think I will let Deinalt know tomorrow morning that I would very\nmuch like to be his attendant next time. I can feel the magic wave off of him, and I am very curious how it compares to my own.\n\nTaynein\n\n\nFinished in Part II", ""),
        StaticBook("Hospitality pt.2", "Sethperith Lucital", "Continued from\nPart I\n\n7th of The Grand Harvest, 1480\n\nSeth,\n\nThe diplomat I needed to speak with today insisted on walking through the town together as we spoke, to \"take in the local color\", so to speak. It turns out, he\nwas here to investigate some complaints about Deinalt, and he wanted to get me away from him in order to speak candidly.\n\nSo, humans do have some tact!\n\nI told him what I knew, which were mostly positive things, and he seemed satisfied by that; Oren seems\nperfectly content with Deinalt taking care of this region, and I don't blame them. These townsfolk are unruly and backwards; it's really no problem to believe that a few of the more unreasonable ones could be spreading lies.\n\nSpeaking of unreasonable,\nwhen the diplomat parted, he left immediately from Rahult and bid me to go back alone to the tower and give his apologies. This I disliked greatly, for it left me open to be approached alone by that man I'd mentioned before, the one I'd mistaken for\nMali'ker.\n\nHe nearly jumped on me, telling me I slept within the walls of a monster, a man who had stolen his wife from him. I spoke him down readily, but I cannot deny he had shaken me, for his muscles, though not large, looked cut from obsidian. Even\nwith my magic, he might easily overtake me with his brawn alone.\n\nWhen I reached the tower and explained everything to Deinalt, he was quite ready to give me the man's name: Ojore Tha'un. He said the man was a fool and imagined ownership over people that\nwere not his. I feel inclined to agree, for none of Deinalt's servants appear to be in poor health.\n\nTaynein\nThis letter is the one that I found in my brother's jacket lining. His handwriting, though I do recognize it as his, is shaky and hurried. I must guess it would be placed here in the progression as it is not dated. I believe my brother wrote this in\nhaste, expecting a quick retreat, then decided against it. He then may have attempted to burn the letter, but then thought better of it and put it in his coat. In case something were to happen to him, perhaps...? \n\nI must leave this place immediately!\nThat man was right; Deinalt is very likely a monster! I will look for passage out of here as soon as I can, but, I am afraid to try to sneak out during the night! That thing! It watches me as I sleep! I know it! It is no dream!\n16th of The Grand Harvest, 1480\n\nSeth,\n\nI will be leaving for home today, dear brother. It has been an... interesting experience, and I'm sorry I couldn't tell you more about it. Maybe some day. And you do not have to worry about Honey being brought\nto our house and giving our mother another heart attack; she will be staying here with Deinalt. I doubt I could even convince her to leave if I tried.\n\nMy work here is done, and it has all been positive. And as... pleasant... as Deinalt's tower is, I am\nmore than ready to be back among friends and family.\n\nSend everyone my love. It occurs to me I do not say it enough.\n\nTaynein\nEPILOGUE\n\nAfter my brother had come home, he never did speak of Deinalt again. The man himself I did meet from time to time, and though Taynein had always been cordial to him, I can't help but remember his actions being tight around him. Another\nthing I'm reminded of; he said, in passing, that the last time he saw Honey was actually not when he left the village, but when he was passing by the Monks' one day. She seemed to have been exiting the temple, with some black clothes and something that\nlooked like it was made of pale porceline, bundled in her arms.\n\nI do not know what that means, and for the first time, I do not want to know what that means.", ""),
