        StaticBook("Important Note", "Orithur", "my\n         library\n             is\n          bigger", ""),
        StaticBook("Imprint", "Sofetios", "Imprint\nBy Sofetios\nI stand in a forest,\nOne that I know quite well,\nWhere the trees are tall,\nAnd they never fall,\nAt least that’s what I like to tell.\nI came here,\nWhen I was a boy,\nBut any time I would say,\nThe forest was my favourite toy.\nI came here again,\nA few years ago,\nIt was the same place I knew well,\nAs far as I could tell,\nThere was nothing different to show.\nI open my eyes now,\nTo see the trees,\nMy eyes see an empty place,\nAs if leaving no trace,\nThough this is not what my mind sees.", ""),
        StaticBook("Impure Love", "Hileia'elr", "----Impure Love----\n\nWritten by Hileia'elr\n\nA romance novel of two Mali, coming from two very different backrounds.\nI was ready to leave Haelun'or for the first time in my life. Through my childhood, my parents kept me hidden from the outside world. In uncommon circumstances, I would be allowed to travel to the docks to view the ocean, but that was it.\nMost of my time was spent with my teachers, and I learned about science. I didn't dislike the subject, it just didn't quite suit me. Instead, I wanted to be one of the guards, as a sword in my hand was one of the best feelings I've ever experienced...\nHowever, once I was old enough, I wanted to explore the realm.\n\nI walked up the steps, towards the large gate. A Mali'ame stopped me. \"State your name, race, and business, Mali.\" he said. He was dressed in a green armour, with yellow trims.\n\"I am Elsil'ceru. I come from Haelun'or, and I come to Laureh'lin seeking supplies.\" My answer seemed to satisfy the guard, and he let me through. As I looked around, I saw Mali'Ame everywhere. I wasn't used to large crowds, so I rushed over to the side.\nI just simply wanted to escape the large, noisy streets filled with Elves and other beings. As I attempted to sit down, my foot caught on the corner of a nearby table, and I fell over. With me now on the ground, the large group of people stared at me.\nThey all looked at me as if they've never seen a boy on the ground. I stood up, and I felt fine... but my clothing was dirty. This was my largest concern. What if another High Elf was here? I would become a laughing stalk.\nI quickly ran into a nearby tavern. As I walked in, the girl behind the bar counter greeted me with, \"Karin'ay-\" but stopped short when she saw how dirty I was.\n\n\"Do you have a washroom available?\" I asked her. She pointed to a door in the back.\nNow cleaning up my clothes in a cauldron, I was looking around for something to dry off with. Turning around, I saw that the door was open. Another girl with purple eyes glanced at me, surprised, and she asked, \"Why are you in MY washroom?\"\nI didn't know what to say. I was in this girls private living space, using her supplies.\n\n\"Well, you see... the girl at the counter allowed me to clean up in here...\" She gave me a half smile, and allowed me to continue.\nUpon re-entering the tavern, I apologized to both girls, and explained the situation. \"That's fine,\" the girl at the counter said. \"We're happy to do whatever we can...\" She then proceeded to examine my hair and eyes closely. \"You aren't from Laureh'lin.\"\n\"No...\" I said. \"I'm from Haelun'or, this is my first time outside the walls.\" The second girl with purple eyes raised her eye brows. \"That makes two of us.\" she exclaimed. \"My name is Sioln'ker, and my friend is Talia'lir. She runs this tavern, I just\nfetch supplies for her.\"\n\n\"So you're a High Elf, then?\"\n\n\"Yes...\" she replied, \"but I left the Mother City when I was young to come here, and live with the Mali'Ame.\"\n\nI began to introduce myself as well.\n\"I am Elsil'ceru. I'm visiting this city in search for supplies not found in Haelun'or.\"\n\n\"What might you need?\" Asked Sioln'ker. \"We might have it in the storage room.\"\n\n\"I need some sticks, iron, and paper, if I can find them.\"\n\"Well, I know we have sticks somewhere. Follow me.\"\n\nAs the two of us entered the basement, there were boxes scattered around the floor. While she looked for my requested supplies, I began to ask, \"Why flee the Mother City for this tavern?\"\nI expected her to change to some dramatic, or nostalgic expression, but she remained neutral.\n\n\"Not enough living space there.\" She replied. \"While I did get a good education there, and I was very happy, it was far too chaotic there for me. The small\nrooms became an issue. I'd much rather live in an actual house. Plus, all the Mali there aren't accepting of anyone shy of perfection. So, I moved here, where I didn't have to follow proper manners all the time.\"\n\nI began my counter argument.\n\"But why live with another race? Surely, one of your status deserves to be with other Puritans, and not... Wood elves.\"\n\nShe raised her brow at me. \"Ah, I see... you're one of those ignorant and closed-minded Mali...\"\n\"Well, that's only because we ARE superior to every other race. I wouldn't say such things if it weren't true.\" I replied. \"We look beautiful, and we're well educated, unlike some of the other barbaric races.\"\nSioln'ker sighed at Elsil'ceru's response. \"Here, I found some sticks. Take them and go.\" she said. She then forced a bundle of sticks into my hands.\n\nWhile in the High Elven culture, it is normal to declare your own race\nsuperior to others- Yet, it also wasn't a young man's place to upset a lady such as herself.\n\nRunning up the stairs, sticks still in hand, I opened the door at the top of the small staircase and witnessed an\nalmost empty tavern. The only ones in the room were two guards sipping their drinks in the back, and Talia'lir, standing at the counter. She glanced at me and said, \"Sioln stormed out. What happened in the basement?\"\nTrying to think of a response, I quickly lied. \"She tripped, and stubbed her toe. I offered to take a look, but she said that she would go to a nearby doctor.\"\n\nTalia glared at me. \"Liar.\" she declared. \"There's no doctor on this side of the city.\"\nBlushing, I then told the truth. \"Ok, so I may have insulted her unintentionally, reguarding her... race...\"\n\n\"You brought up her leaving the Mother City, didn't you?\" she replied. \"You should at least have more manners than that, being a Puritan...\"\n\"I know...\" I responded. \"I want to find her and apologize.\"\n\nTalia forced a half smile. \"That wouldn't be a smart idea. She tends to be quite violent when upset. And she keeps a steel dagger in her boot all the time for protection, so you might want to\nstay clear of her until she's recovered.\"\n\nI just stood there, unsure of what to say. \"When can... Uh...\"\n\nTalia looked at me, confused.\n\n\"When, uhm... When can I apologize to her?\"\nTalia placed her elbow on the table, and her chin resting on her hand, smiling. \"We're closing in an hour, but come back by sunrise. She'll be here, ready for work. We won't be open, but I'll let you in before work hours.\"\n\nI let out a long sigh and\npacked my belongings.\n\n\"I suppose I'll be off, then.\"\n\nExiting the tavern, I noticed a sign on the side of it.\n\n\"Welcome to the Emerald Crescent!\"\nRight. The Emerald Crescent, I thought to myself. I'll return here after sunrise.\n\nAs it was now night, the streets were almost abandoned, with few night dwellers roaming the streets. I had on my expensive High Elven travel clothing, so I needed a roof to\nsleep under. But I wondered where that might be... I noticed several small shops outside the tavern, one was marked, \"Under renovation.\"\n\nThe tarp that was meant to go on the top of the shop lay there on the ground, so I used this as a blanket.\nDrifting off into sleep, I hoped that I wouldn't be mugged in the night.\n\nThankfully, the next morning, I woke up, unharmed and with all my belongings. I proceeded to walk the path to the tavern. As I was walking along the road, I figured that this city\nwasn't as horrible as I made it out to be.\n\nNow, almost to the tavern, I began climbing the stairs. In the window, I saw Talia cleaning the counter. That's when I heard a scream.\n\nThe scream came from behind the tavern. With no time to think, I\nsprinted around the side of the building to see two Valah and Sioln- One was holding her, and the other had a dagger out.\n\n\"Stay still, you greedy Mali!\"\n\nThey were obviously mugging her, simply because she was a High Elf.\nI was skilled with a sword, but had little to no training with hand to hand combat. However, it was my only option.\n\nSprinting into action, I went for the one with the dagger first. I hooked his ankle with my foot, bringing him to the ground.\nI stole the dagger, and gave him a boot to the face, rendering him unable to fight properly. With his ally on the ground, the other thug released Sioln and drew his own dagger.\n\n\"Kid, why don't you piss off before you get hurt?\" He said in a raspy voice.\nI smiled. \"I'd much rather take my chances.\" I said as I lunged towards his chest.\n\nHe failed miserably at blocking my blow, and fell to the ground, a dagger now in his torso.\n\nSioln rushed over to me with a smile.\n\"Thanks... they were trying to take my necklace.\" she said.\n\n\"Enough of that!\" I screamed back. \"I have to apologize to you... I can barely see as to how I could have been so ignorant. You were right, other races are intelligent... in fact, my own race is\nprobably the most stupid, for being so unaccepting and ignorant of foreign ideas...\"\n\nSioln stood there in awe. She didn't expect this type of reply at all.\n\n\"However... I don't take back what I said about High Elves being the\nmost beautiful.\"\n\nSioln began to make a pouting face.\n\n\"Because...\" I began again, \"you're the most beautiful person I've ever met, and no other race is superior when it comes to your attractivness...\"\nShe blushed, and took my hand into hers...\n\n\"If you could forgive me,\" I stated, \"I want to be just like you, and leave that dreaded city. This life seems far more like the one I would favor, over my life back in the Mother City.\"\n\"So, what you mean is...\" she began. \"What you're implying is that... you want to be wed?\"\n\nAll I did was smile. I said nothing, but she understood completely.\n\n\"Ok then, we'll get married soon...\" she said.\n\"Why not right in the tavern?\" I said with a sarcastic tone. She chuckled. \"That's not quite romantic enough, is it, Elsil?\" she replied.\n\nI swooped her off her feet. \"There's only one way to find out.\" I said.\nThe very next morning, it seemed as if the entire tavern was filled with not only Wood elves, but my own friends who had come all this way. Talia was in a long, flowing white dress. She leaned over and whispered to me, \"You look rather dashing. Nervous?\"\nI chuckled. I looked down at the blue robe I was wearing, along with the red undershirt. \"Of course I am.\" I began. \"But I'd bet anything she's just as nervous as I.\"\n\nJust then, a tall, marvelous figure walked through the door of the tavern.\nA tall, beautiful, slender, marvelous figure indeed. Sioln had on a long flowing green dress that didn't match my outfit at all.\n\nIt had just occurred to me that this was not a traditional wedding at all. But I didn't care. I was still getting married.\nStanding at the front of the tavern, we joined hands, and the ceremony had started.\n\n\n\nAnd so did our new lives.", ""),
        StaticBook("In Nortruppen I", "Sonax Kamai", "Sonax's Travels\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Umm... Hi, I guess.. The name's Sonax Kamai and I was born in Hollowvale. Hallowvale is a nice place.. well I think so anyways, some of the people in Felsen say that it's too cold, or that it's and \"Uncultured\" place...\nI don't get them, they are just ignorant. But anyways, let me explain what happened that made me move out of Hollowvale. Right after my father died in the war by the Daemon F'Vorresh, Dwarves from that war came and pillaged Hallowvale, so I had to leave..\nIt's pretty straight forward really. And ever since, I hated Dwarves and sworn to track down and kill that damn Daemon.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n------------->\nAfter escaping my home, I've traveled across the sea on a raft with my father's red scarf that I've managed to scavenge from my pillaged home.\nI ended up on the felsen shores and explored it a bit more, looking at it like a new home.\nBut as I came in to their marketplace, I was halted by the guards, and questioned for my scarf, so I took off. After I got away, a tradesman asked me if I'd be interested in fish, as hungry as I was, I could not let up that offer. I followed the guy......\nand this is when a weird guy named Avalon, who recruited me to his army named Nortruppen. I naturally didn't like any of the superiors there by the way.. so I felt kinda left out. Woah! What is this? It's my friend Jerome! Why is he here?\nApparantly he's joining too. A lot of things have been happening here with the nortruppen... I don't like it. Aparently I found out that the Nortruppen seek to the flays to do their dirty work, and I thought the nortruppen deserved some type of ->>\nrepsect, but it seems that what I initially believed about the Nortruppen was wrong. before finding this out, I was asked to become an Elite, I turned it down because in reality... I don't know a lot about this place to be actually committed to something>\nof big responsibility... And also.. I don't believe they deserve a person like me in their group.. I have the feeling that me and Jerome are the only good fighters this place has since Mark left... And I came here expecting a challenge...", ""),
        StaticBook("Infinity", "Sofetios Jayamen", "A Theory of Infinity\n\n            ~By Geedin\n                  Jayamen\nLately I have begun to think about how things are connected. Take a rug for example. We see it as just one rug, but that one rug is made up of smaller things. Wool or string, which in turn is made of smaller fibers.\nI think that things get smaller, maybe even infinitely. Just as things can be made of smaller things, so can smaller things make up one big thing. Again with the rug example. All of those fibers make up wool or string, which make the rug.\nYou may think it stops there, but what is the difference between fibers to a rug then to a rug being a part of a house?\nThe rug isn’t physically sewn into the house, yet it is part of it, the same as the fibers not being part of a rug until it is sewn into one.\nThis begins a theory of Infinity. Let me give another example. Apples and oranges. They are different, right? Well that is all a matter of perspective. Apples may be different then oranges, but they can still be grouped into what we call fruits.\n. Even everything in the world, with its infinite different parts and pieces, can be grouped into what we call, well, the world. We may seem to think of the smaller things as making more sense when we should really be looking towards the bigger.\nNow let’s get a bit deeper. What is the difference between yourself and someone else? Well, there are differences, but there are also similarities. Well let’s think, what would make you two the same?\nWell the thing is, you are part of something that doesn’t make you the same, but groups you into one thing. Now for the trick. Say we are seeking all knowledge of things.\nWe learn more and more, yet never are satisfied with what we know, because there is always more to know. Well we are probably looking for some way or some knowledge that can make us content.\nI think I may have realized what that something is. It is something complex, yet simple at the same time. It is everything, and it is also one thing.\nImagine everything, every thought, every physical and non-physical thing connected into one, single, thing. That is Infinity.\nYou may be asking, how are we connected? I may ask you the opposite, how are we disconnected? As a rug is made up of fibers, so are you made up of flesh and bone.\nIf everything can be made up of infinitely smaller things and infinitely bigger things can be made of those smaller things, what does that leave, but the fact of infinity?\nNow to go into time. Time in my opinion is Infinite as well. The literal sense of ‘Now’ is infinite. I think that there is no Past, nor future. There is literally only now.\nYou may say that you are able to think of the future or the past, but what is the future and past but theory and memory? There is no actual substance to it. Therefore I can only conclude that there is only, now.\nLet me delve into what we know as nothing. Nothing is completely a made up thing. There can never be nothing in any way. So you might ask, what made the something that is here now?\nWell, who says it ever had to be made. What if everything that is here simply was, is, and will be?\n\nThat is all I have to say, Take what you have read as you will. This is simply my opinion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Infinity", "Geedin Jayamen", "A Theory of Infinity\n       \n               -By Geedin\n                  Jayamen\n\nPlease note that this is simply my opinion. You can believe it or not believe it.\nLately I have begun to think about how things are connected. Take a rug for example. We see it as just one rug, but that one rug is made up of smaller things. Wool or string, which in turn is made of smaller fibers.\nI think that things probably get even smaller, maybe even infinitely. Just as things can be made of smaller things, so can smaller things make up one big thing. Again with the rug example. All of those fibers make up wool or string, which make the rug.\nYou may think it stops there, but what is the difference between fibers to a rug then to a rug being a part of a house?\nThe rug isn’t physically sewn into the house, yet it is part of it, the same as the fibers not being part of a rug until it is sewn into one. This begins a theory of Infinity. Let me give another example. Apples and oranges.\nThey are different, right? Well that is all a matter of perspective. Apples may be different then oranges, but they can still be grouped into what we call fruits.\nEven everything in the world, with its infinite different parts and pieces, can be grouped into what we call, well, the world. We may seem to think of the smaller things as making more sense when we should really be looking towards the bigger.\nNow let’s get a bit deeper. What is the difference between yourself and someone else? Well, there are differences, but there are also similarities. Well let’s think, what would make you two the same?\nWell the thing is, you are part of something that doesn’t make you the same, but groups you into one thing. Now for the trick. Say we are seeking all knowledge of things.\nWe learn more and more, yet never are satisfied with what we know, because there is always more to know. Well we are probably looking for some way or some knowledge that can make us content. I think I may have realized what that something is.\nIt is something complex, yet simple at the same time. It is everything, and it is also one thing. Imagine everything, every thought, every physical and non-physical thing connected into one, single, thing. That is Infinity.\nYou may be asking, how are we connected? I may ask you the opposite, how are we disconnected? As a rug is made up of fibers, so are you made up of flesh and bone.\nIf everything can be made up of infinitely smaller things and infinitely bigger things can be made of those smaller things, what does that leave, but the fact of infinity?\nNow to go into time. Time in my opinion is Infinite as well. The litteral sense of ‘Now’ is infinite. I think that there is no Past, nor future. There is literally only now.\nYou may say that you are able to think of the future or the past, but what is the future and past but theory and memory? There is no actual substance to it. Therefore I can only conclude that there is only, now.\nLet me delve into what we know as nothing. Nothing is completely a made up thing. There can never be nothing in any way. So you might ask, what made the something that is here now?\nWell, who says it ever had to be made. What if everything that is here simply was, is, and will be? That is all I have to write at the moment. Please know that this is only my opinion. Believing it or not is up to you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Info on Copies", "Armin Ambertoe", "In order to get a copy of a copy of a book on the shelves you must donate a book that we currently do not have. This book can be your own work or one that you have in your possession.\n\nIn order to request a copy of a book, put the book that we do not have\nand that you are donating in the chest labeled 'Book Copies Requests'. Along with this book you must submit a signed book in the same chest with the following details:\n1. Your name\n2. The date ((/date))\n3. The book you donated\n4. The book you wish to obtain a copy of\n\nTo pickup your copy you must come into the library and ask one of the librarians or scholars and if the copy has been made they will give it to you. \n\nNote: We do not loan or sell books under any circumstances.", ""),
        StaticBook("Info on Copies 2", "Cablam", "In order to get a copy of a book on the shelves you must donate a book that we currently do not have. This book can be your own work of someone else's that you have come into possession of. \n\nIn order to request a copy of a book, put\nthe book that we do not have which you are donating in the chest labeled 'Book Copy Requests'. Along with this book you must submit a signed book in the same chest with the following details: \n1. Your name\n2. The date ((/date))\n3. The book you donated\n4. The book you wish to obtain a copy of\n\nTo pickup your copy you must come into the library and ask one of the librarians or scholars and if the copy has been made they will give it to you.\n\nNote: In order to request a copy the\ndonated book must be approved by either Lyeth or Armin.\n\nAdditionally, copy requests are limited to one per week unless otherwise specified. \n\nLastly, we do not loan or sell books.", ""),
        StaticBook("Informer Issue 1", "underwhereknight", "The Informer\n         Issue #1\n\n        Edited By:\n\n           Adam\n\n\nContents-\n-------\nCracked Tankard Killing\n\nCultist in the sewers?\n\n     Several saint days ago I was in the Cracked Tankard Tavern with my Business associate Aldern Osgood when I noticed the barmaid, Oxana shouting in her basement. After leaving the tavern a lack of guards on the streets was\nobvious. From interviews with the Feslen guard and an eyewitness. The guard with Oxana searched for a dead body... of a guard dead for at least a year. The Feslen guard broke down every door in the sewers (including the ones under the\ninn) though they could not open the door holding the dead, unknown guard as the door was enforced with iron. After saying the Feslen guard would not return to the sewers Markese de Rolle commanded the guard to patrol the sewers after suspicions of cultist\nhiding in the sewers! The guard managed to get to the body this time and is still looking for cultist.\n<><><><><>/\\<><><><><>   Have you ever wanted to write?\n Do want your work to be seen and need minas?\n<><><><><>\\/<><><><><>\n\nContact Adam by bird or at The Osgood Smithy to get your artical in the Informer!\nCracked Tankard Killing!\n\n     Shortly after the first search through the sewers the guard found a wood elf stabbed to death lying a pool of blood on the third floor of the Cracked Tankard Inn. Editor of the Informer, myself was taken in as a suspect who\nwith the help of Aldern Osgood was proven innocent. The Feslen guard responded quickly and sealed off the Inn. Sources from within the guard say the victim was in league with an elven anti-human group. The victim got on the wrong side of a business\ndeal and was killed by the groups trained killer. The group also reportedly killed a young human child. The Elven killer was taken into the Palace and executed by a crossbow squad. But the group remains at large, who are they..?\nThey could be these\ncultist, mayhaps a trusted elven shop owner or even an elf sitting next to you. Be wary Feslen.\n>-----------------<\n\n    Are you looking for an exciting life style?\n\n           Join \n            <>\n           The\n            <>\n          Feslen\n            <>\n          Guard\n\nEnlist Today!\nInterview of Markese\n De Rolle-\n\n     During the midst of the Cracked Tankard Killing an interview on the Feslen guard Commandant was taken by Aldern Osgood it is as follows. \n\n     Born in Feslen both Markese's parents are passed\naway. His father fought and died in the Duke's war. He was trained by the Gold Corps before the civil war. After offering his services to Mayor Gradic he was made trial and then permanent Feslen guard Commandant.\n\n     On the topic of the Civil war he\nsaid \"I'd call the Civil war a tragedy. Orenian men killing Orenian men. Imagine, these men might be friends under differnt circumstances. One might like to fish, the other to hunt. A true tragedy.\"\n\n     This inspiring man is running for Mayor\nunopposed. But do not worry, he aims to help the average man in Feslen do better. From lowering taxes to encouraging business in Feslen.\n\nSo Vote for Markese!\n------------------\n}-----------------{\n\n     Do you have a business in feslen and need advertising?\n\n     Contact the Informer today about placing an Ad!\n\n     Send a bird to Adam or go to the Osgoog Smithy!\n}-----------------{\nThe Lorraine Murders!\n\n     Don't stay outside after dark! A string of murders in Feslen have been going. Victims have a lorraine's cross carved into their body. The Feslen guard advises everyone to follow a curfew starting at nightfall.\nLittle is known about the murderer. Could they perhaps be seeking vengeance agaisnt these anti-human elves? A sign of god? A crazed man? \n\n     No one knows as of now, but the guard is looking as you read if they've not already been caught.\nProfile Piece: \nThire Horen\n\n     While interviewing the people of Feslen I was lucky enough to meet Thire Horen. Thire is a man tasked to reform the Order of the lion by Emperor John II Sigismund himself! The reasoning behind this is Thire's blood.\nHe is the grandson of Ser Purnita the Pure, according to Thire \"The last true Holy kngiht.\" Thire even said the emperor had \"Odd tastes.\" But with no disrespect. Thire was a busy man, though very polite.\n[=================]\n\n   There will be more Issues of the Feslen Informer coming out soon!\n    Remember to Contact me for writing or Ad placement!\n   The Osgood Smithy can be found at the Feslen docks on the very edge to the north.", ""),
        StaticBook("Informer Issue 2", "underwhereknight", "The Informer\n        Issue #2\n\n        Edited By:\n\n           Adam\n16th of the First Seed         Year 1564\n\nContents-\n--------\nThe Feslen Housing Scandal           pg3\nCannibals in Feslen? \n                      pg9\nThe Guard Moves into the Old Palace\n                     pg13\nUpdate on the Lorraine Killings\n                     pg15\nThe Grand Vailorian Tournament   \n                     pg19\nMurder Locations\npg25\nThe Feslen Housing\n         Scandal\n\n   An anonymous source let me in on what is going on in Feslen behind the scenes, here it is. Past Feslen mayor Piero Gradic has been abusing his power as mayor for personal gain. To start the long list he\nhas been overturning houses in Feslen at an incredible rate to turn a profit at the expense of those being evicted. Gradic has also sold houses far under value to secure votes for mayor before. As well Gradic never paid his stewards for their hard work,\nowing over three thousand minas to one steward. Most astonishing of all he falsely tampered with the city ledger to do this and it has been years since taxes have actually been checked or logged! Many properties in Feslen are owned and unused by goverment\nofficals- likey from the corruption of Gradic. Feslen has three banks- only one open. My source claims Piero Gradic did not run for re election because he could not win and now that Gradic is head Steward he will likely keep overselling houses unless\nmayor Markese de Rolle sets prices for houses so they can't be overpriced.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   Come Drink and Eat\nat the Cracked Tankard Inn! The best place to get a drink in Feslen!\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nCannibals in Felsen?\n\n   From the Lorraine Cross murders we thought things in Feslen couldn't get much worse but an unamed source let me in on something the Guard is hiding. An unknown group of cannibals have been killing and eating their victims.\nSome of the victims of this unholy act are already dead victims of the lorraine killings and devoured anyways. Another though had their door chopped down and house broken into and has eaten. It was truly horrible I hear. Are these cannibals the cultist in\nthe sewers? In league with the lorraine killer? The work of the undead? Rebel practices? It is unknown as of now. Be safe Feslen.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   The Feslen Informer needs writers! Contact Adam by bird and turn in an Artical for a mina payment and have your work seen!\n\nFor articals that are excepted.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nThe Guard Moves into      the Old Palace\n\n   The ever growing Feslen guard has claimed the old royal palace once untouched it is now for the guards use. Although commandant Markese said the old garrison for the guard may be sold with the approval of a\ncouncil it seem as it will remain under the guards control. The old palace was to be the site of the new guild halls, one a magic school after the end of the war. Where will the guilds of Feslen move into now is unknown.\nUpdate on the\n    Lorraine Killings\n\n   The unknown lorraine killer is still on the loose and among Feslen. The killer carving the lorraine's cross into the victims chest's and has been known to kill guards who witness them. A couple was brought into\nquestioning from the guard about the killings. Thoramir, a dwarf and Sue a human women with a baby child, Daren. They at first claimed at doing it but then broke their statement saying they did it all for the baby. Neither could decide who did it both\ntaking full responsibility for the crimes. In the end the guard released them on probation, taking on all their weapons and book that could connect them with a cult. For all of the known locations of lorraine killings see the back of the paper. The only\nlead in who could be the true killer is a man in a light brown cloak ran from the scene of a murder.\nThe Grand Vailorian \n      Tournament\n\n   On the 11th of the Grand Harvest 1563 a grand and mysterious tournament was held in the middle of a desert in a grand area. The fighters fought for glory and prizes. In the end there were three prizes. And the\nthree remaining fighters fought a free for all to see who could win the grand prize. It pitted an orc, dwarf and undead ghoul agaisnt each other. In a fury of blades the dwarf and orc fought. After a drawn out battle the orc left walking, but was soon\nambushed by the ghoul, falling to it. The ghoul named Valdren won the main prize of tourney. I interviewed a man who got fifth place in the tournament, besting an orc to get there. I asked this Maximillion Dwanstead, a rugged man with a scar down his eye\nhow he bested the orc. Growing up sparing as a child in his spare time while being in the Golden Crozier he learned the art of fighting. he says \"Besting an orc feels good, though challenging. One can find it simple. When you ue their length and weight\nagaisnt them. Time your movements and strikes and they should fall before you relatively easily.\" He also said \"Any Orenian like myself can do what I've done. Just trust your feelings it's not as hard as it seems.\" There you have a good honest man to lend\nhis wisdom.\nLocations of the\n    Lorraine Killings\n\n   Here is the list of the location of known spots of the lorraine killings.\n\n-1 Garin Road\n-5 Ganford Road\n-Infront of the Feslen Garrison\n-Falling from the church ceiling\n-Ross Road\n-The courtyard by the back gate\n-By the Feslen Auction house\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   Buy Ad Space in the Feslen Informer for\n        50 Minas\n      Contact Adam!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("Ingredients List", "Ketiley the Vixen", "Alchemical list of\nIngredients:\n\nMandragora\nSerpent's Stalk\nFrost Vine\nBlissfoil\nAthin\nCrimson Vase\nDrake's Tail\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nBlood Lotus\nFlametongue's Root\nLarihei's Fingers\nElf's Hair Vine\nCrouching Feather\nHalfling's Grass\nTippen's Roots\nAlabaster Leaf\nSaffvil\nClutcher's Straw\nMetzli's Tangle\nGoblin's Ivy", ""),
        StaticBook("Ink Sacks & Bubb", "The Fable Maker", "================       Ink Sacks\n    & Bubbles\n================\n\n\nScribed by\n \n     The Fable Maker\n\n\n\n==================\nThey swim as fish do.\nGlide like birds do.\nSquirm as bugs do.\nGulp as men do.\n\nAll sizes and shapes.\nMaking little sound.\nAbsent of capes.\nIn seas they are found.\nSquids of battle,\nHardly cattle.\nTis loudly said,\nThat they fought the undead.\n\n\n*A painting of a battle squid is here*\nSquids of the air,\nCan it be true?\nDo they really fly?\nWell that's up to you.\n\n*An ancient painting of an Aegian river is here, a squid elaborately envisioned in the sky*\nSquids of great size,\nTis said a great prize,\nLays hidden within,\nCreating a din.\n\n*A hurried painting of a gigantic squid, surrounded by musical notes is here*\nThough passive most times,\nBe mindful of squid.\nFor in that which chimes,\nGreat treasure is hid...\n\n*The final page reeks with the ancient scent of fish...*", ""),
        StaticBook("Inq. Mandate", "Guy de Bar", "As by decree of his grace, Lord Chancellor Guy de Bar, the Knight Inquisitor, and thus the men under his command, have supreme authority when operating in Inquisitive matters, and are only subject to the King’s authority, and that of\nthe church. Such matters include: Maleficarum (Rogue magi), heathens, heretics, sinners, heinous creatures or any other offense to the Church of the Canon. Those to stand in his way are his to judge\nas he deems fit, and do not reserve the right of trial.\n\n\n\n\n\n[!] The document bears an official seal, the Ashford sun stamped\ninto burgundy wax, and a swung signature. [!]\n\n\n- Lord Chancellor Guy de Bar", ""),
        StaticBook("Inquiring Note", "Arnit", "Arnit,\n\nI ain't heard from you in days.  Where is the meeting place?  If you don't answer me soon I will be leaving to find another partner.  Get your shit together.\n\nSigned, Sven", ""),
        StaticBook("Intel Gathering", "LilJoker90", "Name: Ikali\nAppearance: A  tall young dark elf (~7 feet). Thick arms bear his body and bright red eyes lay on his face. His hair is close to the darkness of the night sky, as well as his skin.\nAge: Unknown (Never said his age)\nInformation collected:\nHe has no home. Has a family, but does not speak of them. Has been looking for a fellow Ker for 2 years. He steals from people, specifically the rich. Is aggressive.\n(i.e. When he saw me, he was excited, but became aggressive and\nviolent when another man tried to flirt with me. Said he didn't want to lose me to another man. His only weapon (from what I have seen) is a broken bottle. He has no money nor food. I offered some food but he denied it.\n\nI left him to keep up the facade\nof a cautious Ker, though in reality I wanted to stay and find out more...", ""),
        StaticBook("Intelligence", "Valac", "The Covenant of Mar\nMission Book: 017\n\nAssigned to: Valac\nBy: Mentor Angroth \n\nCategory: Intel\nPay: Equipment (Already given)\nTime Alotted: 1 Elven Day\nMission Details:\n Locate a man by the name of Vinnie. He is a highly skilled chef, but also a dangerous foe. In the case of your being captured and interrogated, I shall not tell you who he is.\n When you find him,\ndo /not/, under any circumstances, provoke him, or suggest to him you are with Mar. Act friendly and hospitable. Learn as much as you can without looking suspicious.\nMission Report:\nAsked around about Vinnie, nothing, his inn was vacant but we pushed on. We met some people from beyond the canyon and met a man in the seekers guild. Some say Vin has been actin out o' de norm. They say he been having men in black come in\nand out of the inn. Some say that Vin has been conspiring with SOS and the have been seeing a steady presence of them in the area. I have yet to speak with Vin but I have a lead on a den. People say they been meeting in the inn and assigning roles and\nAssassinations ther. All the people giving me this info been locals. \n\nI have finally infultrated the den. The doors were left open and I went right inside, they have meeting rooms and tables everywhere. Kinda cramped... We have our man.\nThe den is located under the staircase and is well hidden. Stone floors and wood tables. I have what I need... no news on the poisoned cookies, I think he keeps them in a private chest in the corner. We have found the snakes den.", ""),
        StaticBook("Interview", "Mariissa", "Name: Orileth Elrin\n\nOrigin: Ker'Nor\n\nGender: Male\n\nAppearance: Dark grey skin with dark green eyes. His hair is black and medium length.\n\nFavorite color: He does not have one because-\nhe is color blind.\n\nFavorite food: Sweet rolls, but the ones guards don't want you to find\n\nProfession: Doesn't have one, lives in the moment and does what he feels that day.\n\nHe is a hobo.\nRelationship Status: Unmarried and single\n\nFavorite drink: Brandy\n\nFavorite Activity: Conversing with other people\n\nParents names: Avondar and Lileth.\nNote: They do not live in Vailor.\nEyesight without glasses is fine, they are only for reading.\n\nAppearance continued: He wears glasses", ""),
        StaticBook("Interviews", "Aeran Winterleaf", "Dedicant Task: Interview\n\nI was given the task to interview some Druids on what they do. I decided to also make this a bit of a candid interview series, so maybe someone in the future can read this and think 'Wow, that Aeran guy is a jerk.'\nMirabelle\n~~~~~~~\nA: Ok, specifically, as clear as you can say it, in less than three sentences, what do you do in the Order?\n\nM: One: I learn from Miss Izzy how the use my gifts of healing.\nM: Two: I use my gifts to purge the taint and hairy ticks.\nA: What are hairy ticks?\nM: Oh, uhm. Dey're, y'know, hairy ticks. They commit heresy and sacrilege against nature and the balance! Like necro-spooks and void slingers.\nA: I never got the spook meme. CONTINUE!\nM: Three: I do the sweeping and tend the\nthe shrines here in the Mama Grove.\nBarry\n~~~~~\nA: What do you do?\nB: The rank of druid has the duty to uphold the balance of nature and help wherever  needed. That's the most basic description.\nA: And you specifically?\nB: I myself as a druid, I travel, help people who may be injured,\nobserve others, and protect those in danger as well as helping within the grove.\nA: So just general helping, Barry?\nB: I also help with taint removal.\n\n*Many dumb jokes and angry sentences ommited.\nKefi\n~~~\nA: What does your rank do for the order, and what do you specifically do for the order?\nA: In the simplest way you can explain it, of course.\nK: Hmm...\nA: Hmm isn't acceptable, I think.\nK: I'm just a normal Druid. I got about daily business, making sure order is kept and help other Druids when needed. Like today I helped heal the tree.\nA: Affirmative. And, do you do anything special specifically?\nK: Nope!\nA: So, do you think I write down\n'lame as a mule' or...?\nK: I think that would be bad...\nA: Me too. Do you... I dunno, smuggle cactus green in from the orcs, or... Subvert Orenian power by slipping peasants with 'Praise the Aspects' fliers?\nK: Nope. I talk to flowers and grow\ntrees.\nA: Do you ever talk to flowers and grow trees, or specifically in that order?\nK: Both ways.\n\n*Kefi may or may not have been high, depending on who's asking.\nGi'Garun\n~~~~~~~\nA: So, uhm, what do Archdruids do, and what do you do specifically unique to other Archdruids.\nG: Well... Archdruids are considered head of the order, and head of the inner circle. They head teaching, upkeeping the grove,\nmaintaining relationships with other organisations yet always maintaining our neutrality. We deal punishments in the order where it is needed, which is rare, and are in charge of pushing the order forwards.\nA: Segwaying a bit, but is hanging Dedicants\nfrom vines acceptable punishment?\nG: Hmm? If the situation called for it...\nA: We'll assume it didn't and put that as a 'No.'\nG: Anywho, Archdruids are the only ones who may call moots or shuns, and are the only members of the order who may\ninterract with a shunned person.\nG: As for my specific role... I'm currently heading the upkeeping of the grove, as well as working on spreading the teachings of the Aspects about Athera. I'm also a Hierophant, although I am unsure if you want to hear\nabout that position from me as well.\nA: That answer was much better than Kefi's 'I dunno.' It's alright, I dunno if I could handle you talking for much longer anyways. Joking, joking.\nG: I could say the same about you. But anywho, that everything?\nA: Uhm, also, when was your last bowel movement? For the task of course.\nG: I'd say... About five decades ago.\nTaynuel\n~~~~~~\nA: What do Druids in general do, according to you, and what do you specifically do?\nT: Druids in general work to maintain and protect the delicate balance of nature.\nT: As a druid, as in my duty, I watch over the highly volatile\nbalance of the world that Cerridwen and Cernunnos have been gracious enough to provide us with, ensuring that it does not fall to such a state of disrepeair and pandemonium that the druids are unable to save it from destruction by the ill-advised or\nunknowing hands of the mortal races. Put simply, I keep people from fucking up nature.\nA: Eloquent.\n\n*Alcohol may have been involved a bit in this conversations.", ""),
        StaticBook("Into Nature", "[Arthur Caulfield]", "Day one\n\nFound a small bag filled with what I believe are materials to make a tent. \n   They just lay on the ground inside cloud temple so I picked them up before someone else could. \n   A good idea I must say. Being outside for\nso long has left half my body numb from the bitter winds. \n    I had a place in mind when I set out to do this but I had forgotten it was so damn far. I may need to stock up on food as the animals around these lands are scarce.\nDay two\n\nOn my travels A nice inn keeper offered to give me an entire sack of cookies. Apparently no one likes caramel as much as I do because she was just giving them away. \n   Of course I gave her what I had on me though she refused\nat first. I will have no need for money anyhow, in the wild you can't barter coin with a bear or an orc. \n    This entry is being written rather quickly as night is falling and I need to set up the tent before I can not see. Tent pitching requires a large\namount of effort and that will be very difficult to achieve if I am so blinded my own hands are unknown to me.\nDay Three\n\nAt the last second I managed to pitch the tent. An hour later the wind would have knocked me off my feet but the tent is holding up just fine under the pressure. \n    I chose a piece of land facing the edge of a cliff. I have\nonly glimpsed what is down below but I could make out a farm and the smell of Billy Bob's taters floating up. \n   Of course that gives me no indication of where I am, those taters seem to be everywhere. I tried them once but they were too dry for my\nliking. The caramel cookies are my personal favourite. So far I have been working my way through the sack the inn keeper so generously gave me. I have consumed over twenty cookies and they still taste damn good.\nDay four\n\nToday I explored the area, knowing my temporary home was secure and the few items I brang safe in a chest. \n   On my walk I came across a peculiar building. Upon closer examination I found it was once a\nmage's guild. The place was old and the roof had collapsed leaving chunks of brick scattered on the floor. \n   My curiousity did get the better of me because I went inside, kicking the rubbel out of the way I found very few things left.\nA bed lay in a corner, the sheets so dirty I was suddenly relieved I have been sleeping on the grass for days. The windows were stained a sickly yellow and the walls had holes the size of my fist. \n   It was obvious a wizard had not cast a spell there for\nelven years. \n   I left soon after not finding much else of interest...except a button. It hung on the wall just inside and at first appeared to do nothing. But as I pushed it I heard a noise from far off. \n   I believe this button opens another part of\nthe tower but have yet to discover where. I may go back tommorrow to investigate. But for now I need my sleep, which could be hard to get with all the racket the monsters make outside.\nDay five\nWoke to the sounds of hissing. Some sort of snake if I had to guess. When I mustered up the courage to peek outside I saw nothing.      Still dark out so going to try to get a few more hours of sleep.\nDay eight\n\nI ran out of cookies. Rationing them didn't even occur to me until I realised I was almost out today. \n   Although i'm sure it will be fine. I haven't seen any animals yet but i'm certain I will soon.\nDay twelve\n\nI have a door\nCome on in\nWalk through the door\nTo come on in\nThey can't touch me\nIf I have a door\nBut you can come\non\nin\nDay sixteen\n\nThe animals are hiding. I just know it. I can hear them talking at night. What's the matter chickens, you chicken? I just wanna chow on chicken\nchow on chicken\nchow on chicken\nyummy yummy chicken\nDay nineteen\n\nWhat does the button do? I've been here for nine hours. Everytime I push it the sound is heard from a different place. \n    A secret passageway. Wizards hiding from me, gonna keep pressing this button till I find ya.\nClick\nShooof\nClick\nShooof\nClick\nShooof\nClick\nShooof\nClick\nShoof <---W hy is thIs one DiffErent?\nDay twenty\n\nDandelions are starting to taste better.\nDay twenty-one\n\nHeard digging during the night. Dirt being shoveled at a rather slow pace. Soon after I heard heavy breathing. Didn't go outside to check.\nDay twenty-five\n\nI feel sick. Spent most of today throwing up. The cramps in my stomach are beginning to fade but as soon as I eat they will be back. \n   I just won't eat then.\nDay twenty-four\n\nI went outside to get some fresh air. Found a hole dug up to the left of my tent. A few bones lay in the dirt at the bottom but nothing else. \n   I believe it might be a grave. Not sure who would be digging those up though.\nDay twenty\n\nTo skin an animal, especially cow, in the most efficient way you must have the right knife. \n   Take my blade, take it take it take it take it. Ferrum blades cut through everything from carrots to human skulls.\nDay sixteen\n\nOooo what was that song. like dooodooodoooda da da. No no no no chorus was bigger higher louder with lute stuck in head like doo dadada didididi no not second di but more di than first\nDay twelve\n\nThe house for wizards is staring at me. It wants me to give it power. I tried to tell it I don't know magic but IT.WONT.LISTEN\n\nIt's in my head. \n\nMagic, gotta learn a spell to please it\nDay five\n\nI liked dandelion, lemon they tasted like lemon but now I like poppies because they taste red and that's better because I can get rashes with things that taste yellow.\nDay three\n\nMAgic, learning magic. Gotta go to Raine. Raine teach me magic. I can please the guild and they will tell me what the button does. \n   Going to Raine.\nDay one\n\nDandelions", ""),
        StaticBook("Into Nothing", "Thurak", "The thing that strikes you first is the darkness. The never ending darkness stretched out before you reaching until the end of time but all before your very eyes. I saw it all, the creation and destruction of existance itself, all in\nthe blink of an eye. At first, I was scared; I didn’t know what had become of me, or what was to become of me now I was this... Monster. Or so I believed at the time. They called me Sin, divine retribution wrapped up in one being.\nA being bent on the destruction of everything it ever loved; all because no one else would. That’s right, we knew it was coming. We had so many chances to stop it. We had so many signs, so many chances that we just ignored it and carried on with our\npathetic mediocre lives. Our repetitive routine, and an existence purely to pass on ourselves to another generation… Pitiful. I wasn’t a bad person, I didn’t deserve to be what I became, yet, I feel that it was necessary. I destroy the corruption\nin the world. Cleanse it of its sin. Ironic, really- I destroy and take lives to save and bring forth more; purity but at a cost. I couldn’t say I don’t enjoy it, nor could I say I do, I don’t even remember what it was like to express emotions.\nMy mind is blank, I have memories, memories of emotions, yet they do not create the same feeling now… my mind is blank, a void. But before all of this I was no monster. I wasn’t a saint, either. I lived an ordinary life.\nThe easiest way to put it is: I died. I can’t explain the feeling. Of dying. Perhaps because there was no feeling; yet there had to have been. There was a whisper of relief as all the sorrow and pain left me. I was pure, enlightened,\nno longer burdened by the world. A faint voice echoed through my soul. A calming voice, I trusted it. It convinced me to embrace the light, let it cast away my body... And I did just that. It took what felt like an eternity; what was an\neternity\nfor me, if such a thing exists now. The pain tore through me, ripping my spirit apart...\n\nBut after the pain came nothing. Nothing; I was immortal, and nothing would ever harm the being that could not experience anything but nothing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro to Alchemy", "VonEbs", "An Introduction to the Alchemist\nForward:\nGreetings, my dear reader. Within the pages of this tome I shall be explaining to you what it takes to be a true Alchemist. I shall run you through our mindset, qualities and traditions.\nChapter I: The Recipe for a Good Alchemist.\nIt takes a special breed of person to be an Alchemist; a rare combination of patience, creativity, intellect, enthusiasm, and of course, an unusual resistance to explosions. For those who wish to follow\nthe noble path of an Alchemist, you must first consider if you possess these key traits, for if you do not, much like a potion made with a flawed recipe, you will be ineffective.\nDo not mistake what I say for supremacism, but rather realize\nthat it is simply an effort to save you. If you do not possess these qualities, dear reader it is quite possible that you, in the attempt to follow our path, may indeed end up harming yourself and others. Now, allow me to go more in-depth about what\nthese traits mean, in order of their importance to an Alchemist: \nPatience. Alchemy, I’m afraid, is not a fast nor particularly interesting process. An Alchemist will spend most of their time for their elembic to boil so that the extract of\nyour ingredients may be collected for use, or simply waiting for a potion to brew. Very little of the time is takes to create a potion is actually spent creating the mixture, although this time is indeed the most interesting part of Alchemy in my\nopinion. Because of all this, dear reader, Patience is vital to an Alchemist, as it would be, in my opinion, apt to give Alchemy the formula consisting of 25 “parts”:\n7 parts waiting(brewing, waiting for the elembic’s water to boil.)\n5 parts setting\nup, cleaning up, and inspecting your equipment.\n5 parts testing(making sure your potion works.)\n3 parts failure (realizing that your recipe is bollocks and starting over.)\n3 parts extracting (boiling down the ingredients and\ncollecting the condensation using an alembic.)\n1 parts explosion (surprisingly common.)\n1 parts mixing the bloody potion.\nIntellect. You may be wondering why this is not the first on my list... Well, someone whom is completely\ndull, yet is willing to give up hours upon hours to make up for it, is much more likely to succeed than someone brilliant who will become frustrated and rushed the second they see that their brew will be taking a very long time to finish.\nSo, while this trait is near-vital, it can be made up for by a massive amount of patience and dedication.\nCreativity. Please note, that I am writing here the explain what it takes to be an Alchemist, not a good Alchemist. Creativity is something\ncompletely vital to anyone who wishes to be a master alchemist... but it is not to those whom only wish to dabble in the art. Creativity is essential for those who wish to truly excel at the art, because one cannot just follow recipes forever. There\ncomes a time, when an apprentice Alchemist must take these matters into their own hands. No more books, no more explanations as to why these particular ingredients must be used... there comes a time, when every Alchemist must learn to rely on their\nown extensive knowledge of herbs and ingredients, of what they represent... To craft a potion of their very own. This is much more difficult than it may seem... but I shan’t go into that, as this is no true Alchemical textbook, but\nrather, an introduction to the science. \nLastly, Enthusiasm. This trait may seem unusual to list, as most would automatically think of someone whom is impulsive and stupid... ‘overtly’ enthusiastic. No, Alchemy requires a special type of\nenthusiasm. One tempered by logic and patience. Enthusiasm is needed because without the drive to learn more, to improve your skill and to create potions of wonder... you are nothing, and shall go nowhere. The reason this is listed at the bottom of\nthe list instead of the top, is simply because by reading this far, you have shown an ounce of this quality, and as such, you may now take pride in knowing that you have the potential to learn this art.\nChapter 2: The Life of an Alchemist\nThe Lifestyle.\nThe life of an Alchemist, despite its labours, is a rewarding and interesting one. Many nations, many companies, and many guild need\nAlchemist, which means that an Alchemist is very rarely without options. Indeed, one of the most fulfilling parts of being an Alchemist is the satisfaction of knowing you are needed and wanted. An Alchemist rarely stays in one\nlocation whilst unemployed, often traveling from kingdom to kingdom, seeking a guild or company that has use for them. In my experience, this does not take a long time... Although it is important to measure one’s options before taking a job. This\nis not to say that an Alchemest /must/ be employed, gods know many Alchemists choos a life of reclusion and introversion; preferring the company of their ingredients and their equipment to the company of people or currency.\nAs an Alchemist, there are many different paths one may choose from; be it creating poisons or creating potions to heal the ill and wounded. These paths will play a large role in deciding how easily one can get jobs, and from whom. For example, one\nwho makes poisons may find it harder to get a job than one who create healing serums, as poisons are hard to mass-produce, which means are of no real use to an army, and they are certainly of no use for a peaceful company of guild.\nThis is much the opposite for healing potions, as oddly enough they are some of the simplest to make, and can be made in quite large quantities without losing much of their effectiveness, so all the aforementioned employers could\nhave a use for an Alchemist of healing. Do not think that these are the only two paths that an Alchemist may follow, however- and certainly no Alchemist sticks only to one branch of the science- think of it more as a specialization. I,\nfor example, specialize in incendiary and explosive concoctions.. Alchemist Fire, if you will. This means that I am often asked to work for militaries of small offensive guilds... even research companies.\nIn conclusion, the lifestyle in terms of business, for an Alchemist, is much dependent upon what they specialize in, and regardless of their business opportunities, the life of an Alchemist is rarely full, and in my opinion, very fulfilling.\nThe Morality of an Alchemist.\nMany jobs seem to have a set “morality.” Soldiers are expected to be lawful and trsutworthy, Mages to be intellectual and neutral... the Morality of an Alchemist is much the same as that of a Mage, and\nis, much like one’s business opportunities, dictated by the Alchemist’s specialization. To use the same examples as before, it would be more likely for an Alchemist specializing in poisons to fall into a darker, more “evil” morality, as they\nwould likely find their work with small groups of assassins of the like. Whereas an Alchemist specializing in healing, would be much more likely to fall into a “good” morality, as by nature, their job of choice is to help people.\nThere are not set rules, of course, a healing Alchemist may very well choose to assist an unlawful organization, and an Alchemist of poison may choose to supply a small vigilante group with his poisons. In essence, the Morality of an Alchemist is\nneutral, and is dictated completely by the individual.\nThe Living Conditions of an Alchemist\nThis section will be somewhat smaller, as there is very little that can be written about this. An Alchemist’s abode will generally have only one constant; a\nlab, usually located in a basement. This lab would contain an Alchemist’s supplies, equipment, and is generally kept locked, as much inside would be fragile or dangerous. As for why it is usually found in a basement... Well.. The earth seems to be a\nbit more resistance to explosions that wooden or cobblestone walls.\nFarewell:\nI thank your, read reader, for taking the time to read my small introduction to the Alchemist. I bid you good ever, good day, and farewell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro to Art", "Lanavia Zytiaear", "An Introduction to Art\n-------------------------------\n\nA simple break down art.\nTable of Contents:\n\n\n1. Table of Context\n2. Indroduction\n3. What is Art?\n4. Why do we Create Art?\n5. Conclusion\nIntroduction:\n\nArt has always been and will always be a subject that some will find touchy. Being that art is, itself, a very opinion based thing, it is hard for people to come to common grounds with what it is exactly and what it means to be an artist.\nOver the years I have had to defend certain items, styles and even artists from the cold words and opinions of others. Within this book I intend to go over, in some detail, the very basics of what art is, its purpose and what it means to be an artist.\nWhat is Art?\n\nWhat is Art? What does it take to be an artist?\nThough these questions are simple the answers are not so much.\n\nEven the book definition of art is note a solid standing one – – it, in itself, leaves\nenough wiggle room to not constrict an input, thought or opinion.\n\nThe simplest way to define art is that art is any means (wither verbal, physical or visual) that has been created to express oneself (the artist).\nWhy do we Create Art?\n\nAs living creatures go, we need to express ourselves. It is a part of our very existence. A very simple, primal part of who we are as living creatures is doing just this. We are trying to get across.\nArt is a very simple means of doing just this.\n\nThrough it we get to express ourselves and get to help others feel expression where they themselves might not be able to do such.\nConclusion:\n\nArt is simply expression. So long as it is a means to express yourself, than it is art.", ""),
        StaticBook("Inured man.", "arkantos1279", "Prince Tristin Tresery, one of your soldiers was injured by an assassination attempt. Luckily we arrived to save the elf.\n\nWe do not know his name yet, he has been passed out ever since arriving at our keep.", ""),
        StaticBook("Iron and Steel", "Gladuos", "In the following book we will be exploring the physical and magical traits of iron or steel, how it may react to the mundane senses, how it's made, weight, shape, hardness, melting point, and a magical understanding.\nIron or steel generally takes on a white-ish grey coloration that may give off a dim shine if smithed in the correct manner. \n   It will often give off clanging and dinging noises as it is used in whatever way it may. Sounds can occasionally\nreverberate throughout the material. \n   Iron, and especially steel, are incredibly tough materials. They are often used during combat or for specially tough constructions if necessary. Compared to stone or lesser materials, iron/steel\nis far more valuable and strong. Steel has a higher coal content compared to iron, and as thus is even more tough.\nMetallic iron or steel is usually created through treating the ore variant through intense blast furnacing and introducing coals to improve quality of the material. The heat of these furnaces usually take on a heat of about 2000 degrees Celsius.\nThe difference between iron and steel is that steel has a higher content of coal added during this process to give an even tougher finish. This is removed from the furnace and cooled in a slow, meticulous process of reheating, cooling, tempering and so-\n- on.\n\n   Steel or iron are metallic materials and thus are often fairly dense, heavy materials, even comparative to earthen minerals.\nThe average shape of steel or iron varies dramatically depending on how it was formed. In its ore variant, it is normally in the shape of any other rock. However, it can be formed into the metallic variant that takes on a shape depending on the -\n- smith's choice and skill.\n\n   Once again, steel or iron are generally very strong materials. This can be often shown when making fine weapons or armors, as making purely metallic constructions may simply be too costly.\nThe melting point of steel and iron is in the range between 1370 and 1550 degrees Celsius. The lower portions of this range are attributed to steel, while the higher is closer to iron's melting point.\nThe magical signature of iron and steel isn't too terrible. It may not be comparable to carbarum or mage gold in conductivity of magical forces, but it may be slightly less resistant than some of the lesser valuable materials in the mortal planes.\n*When reaching these final pages, the reader would be shown a large amount of diagrams, sketches, illustrations, charts, and equations about the various properties of iron and steel. For pages and pages, these continue, being accompanied by various lines-\n- of information attempting to support many of the previous statements of the book. There are also some nuanced details of the materials less relevant than the information already given.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Isabellas Poem!", "[[Child]] Isabella Carstais Ibar'Ker", "*The poem seems to be written in childish handwriting*\n\nFlower Flowers! Pretty flowers\nHow do you like to grow?\nIn the rain the flowers reply, up in the druids grove\nFlowers flowers\nblooming flowers\nWhy are you colored so?\nCause we spread the joy, the flowers sing, all around the world\n\nFlowers flowers dying flowers\nWhy do you look so gloom?\nOur time has come, the flowers cough, and its time to go below.\n\n\n*There seems to be another page!*\n,-. \n    ,     ,-.   ,-. \n   / \\   (   )-(   ) \n   \\ |  ,.>-(   )-< \n    \\|,' (   )-(   ) \n     Y ___`-'   `-' \n     |/__/   `-' \n     | \n     | \n     |    -hrr- \n  ___|_____________ \n*a childs drawing of a flower!*", ""),
        StaticBook("Isles Report", "Avenel Synalli", "On the isles:\n\nFrom the beast we had encountered, one can note a fungal growth on boar. It's hide was notably stronger than the average boar as well. Once it died, the ooze it bled (which I have decent supply of due to its excessive bleeding) had altered-\n- the terrian; the fluara grew notably in a steadfast rate. The body dissolved a few moments post-mortem. I hypothesize that once the \"ooze\" (which I know believe is parasitic) had dissolved the body as it lacked anything to feed off of, what it feed off-\n- of may be lifeforce, which makes me believe that what afflicted this creature was both necromantic and druidic. Tests will be done as well as further examination of the bones. Should we find another, I'd suggest to capture it. More will come from this -\n- report.\n\nAvenel Synalli, 13th of Amber Cold, 1515.", ""),
        StaticBook("J. of Something7", "Ebonsquire", "Joournal of a Something, Volume 7 \n\n((Originally written by TehLulu))\nI grow increasingly frustrated as Prince Toren commented, \"Spider webs within Spider webs\". I have stumbled head first into these webs, and now I am stuck. I've determined no more about my past, but that matters not now. This plot I mentioned reaches\nthan I imagined, clawing its way into nearly every race in Aegis. I have confirmed that this plot is being perpetrated by the Dark Brotherhood. They wish to see the empire of the humans fall, and likely the Orcs as well. It seems they plot to attack\nwithin the next month. Elvador also made mention of a portal they wished to create. Inside lie some sort of monster that the Brotherhood wishes to kill. It seems the elves are the ones most manipulated by this evil. The leader of one of their army\nbranches, the Sentinels, is a worshipper of Iblees. High Guardian Mayctor . . . He is evil, yet his intentions appear good . . . he wishes to protect the Elves. So he assurres me that Laurelin will remain safe, and that the Elves will not be attacked.\nWhat he has done to gain this assurance, I do not know. But I believe hey may be a threat to the High Pronce, if the Prince decides to act against him. I have found a new ally in the Pathfinder's current leader, Atles. He also believes a great evil is\ncoming . . . But I will believe that when I see it. For the evil he predicts is far greater than that of what the Brotherhood could manage. Had I the strength for it, I would go to the North, where he claims to have found a small, dark village. Yet this\nsame village his associates say is part of Oren. But as I have mentioned, my condition worsens by the day. As I spoke to Mayctor in Ravenhold, I was prepared to fight him should he strike me. Yet in truth, I do not believe I could have held my sword up.\nPrince Toren, who I had met at Ravenhold along with two other princes and the princess, agreed with me that Mayctor seemed quite mad. I sent him with a book of my notes to deliver to Native, in the event I was attacked. All turned out fine however, and\nhe has become a quiet ally of mine, as the other Princes are far too blinded to see Mayctor's true face. Mayctor claimed he had information I sought, but refused to tell me. He also told me that only one otheer knew of what he did, and that he would never\ntalk . . . In addition, Atles told me that some of the Pathfinders that had deserted had become bandits. I will have to see if they have anything to do with this matter. But for now, I've but one lead . . . a name Lafthi and Prince Loren both told me. An\nelf by the name of Rolok, who supposedly lives in Laurelin. I must find and speak with him.", ""),
