        StaticBook("Jason's End", "Jason Isenhart", "This one of the last things I leave As I'm taking a trip and will never come back from it so you better get used to that but my Son Colin Isenhart will be there to collect my things and live with you guys I also have one request raise him for me he's only\n15 Years old I know this a lot to ask but please do it for me -Jason Isenhart       P.S. Even if you don't want to I have told him to give you something special", ""),
        StaticBook("Jaspers Diary", "Leyu", "Jasper's Diaries\n((These are 3 diaries of a man named Jasper. It follows 20 years of the mans life. As you read you concentrate on the important moments)) The marrige is finally today! I can't wait to move in with my wife to our new house in Al'Khazar.... Our stay in\nthis town has been well accepted.... A weird fellow came to our house today speaking of prophecy, looked a little crazy, but appeared to be a nice person.... so we decided to invite the prophet to lunch today. We learned he is Afonse.... His\nstories are full of life, death and adventure, we don't know if they are true.... Great story teller, but seems like he can't read or write.... Mr. Wilcons doesn't talk to us anymore, the town seems to have started resenting us since we\nbefriended Afonse.... Anna is pregnant! The joy to finally have a son or daughter to call my own.... The undeath have been on my mind of the town folk, they are becoming agitated.... Why, why..why would they kidnap a pregnant woman. Just because\nthey hate Afonse... why Anna? She did nothing wrong!.... She is safe... After I came home after looking for her, she was there... The relief...but Afonse was in bed next to her, gravely wounded. Seems he attacked the kidnapers... all\ndied, Afonse was left with injuries. .... We do not know how long he'll last, he has been weaker each day.... Our son has been named today, Jistuma. Named by his late godfather Afonse, who died today. Named after Afonse's god of judgment, to give\nblessing to our son and to himself recieve good fortune in death. Haven't seen Anna cry since the death of his brother. Her tears seemed green like her eyes. Rest in peace Afonse.... the king came to our house today, the treats from the town are\nbig, and they want us death. They take the kidnapers side, how dare they? The king decided to exile us, as to please the town, and to save our lives.... we were given the belongings of Afonse.... They said he had a will..... The king was good, sent a\nhealer to our home in the wild to give birth to our son..... I found a book in Afonse's belongings, seems to be about his religion. ..... It talks about sacrifices and death to pleast their masters. I don't know if Afonse knew about this.... But then I\ntalked to the king about it. He told me Afonse was an orphan, picked up by an evil man that showed himself as a father to him. Started teaching him his religion. but as something good, to ease the transition into evil... But as a criminal he died\nsoon, and left Afonse with an evil religion. That he taught was good..... As I read the book, I found out that Jistuma was an elf from the past, a former disciple, that carried the task of judging the souls of the believers.... Today is Jistuma's 10th\nbirthday, I can't believe how happy he is in the wilds. befriends animals from the forest, and all the traders from all races seem to like him, even the orcs for some reason.... He got angrier and attacked his mother. I do not know why. Now he is crying\nand remembers the events differantly. What has happened? .... Anna died... The boy cried a lot... It isn't his fault.... The druids can't figure out why Jistuma has been so angry and attacking everything. I fear he might be possessed. A more powreful\ndruid will come. Freight and anger make my son lose control. He is possessed by a demon, and the demon is wise. After taking control and attacking, he gives my son new memories. The druid taught me how to make a potion to ease the\ndemon, but even with this, If his feelings get really strong, the demon might take control... What will I do?..... Jistuma makes 18 years of age today! I can't believe how good he is at catching animals and monsters, and I'm very hapy that he sees all\nraces the same. He even sees all man the same. good and evil... I don't like that much, I deal with the black market for ingrediants for his potion. And sometimes they come to my house... I can still remember the time an undeath came. I was frighten to\ndeath, but Jistuma started casually talking to him like he was any other person.... he has been bugging me to let him travel..... I need to tell him about the demon. I think I'll take him to the druid so he can tell him with more detail. This way, he\ncan start to shut up about the travels... ((The last written pages of the diary are written in blood, the words get messy sometimes and drops of blood are everywhere. but its still understandable.)) We were attacked outside of\nAl'Khazar. We didn't noticed we wer surroudned by monsters. I got close to getting hurt by them, but Jistuma saved me. Oly to slash my stomach in the next second. HIs eyes were yellow! He quickly regained control, but he was apologizing on how\nhe couldn't stop the monsters in time. His eyes were losing the green from this mother and are gaining some red. He's taken me to Al'Khazar, but when someone tries to help me. He doesn't let them pass and shouts and screams. 'Why do you want to kill\nhim, that was so long ago, just hekp him please just help him'. The demon is distorting his reality. ((This is the last page of the diary. It's also written in blood, and there are marks that seem to be from tears, but the color on the spots are\ngreen.)) I am approaching death. My son left me for a bit so I could be alone to pray for Anna. Son, if you learn to read and see this, please know that I don't blame Al'Khazar, I do not blame Afonse, and I do not blame you. And remember, your\nmother Anna loved you, and I Jasper, love you as well.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C2", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n            -By Sofetios\n                 Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\nChapter Two\n           Linink\n\nAs I woke up the next morning I couldn’t help but feel a bit afraid. Linink was one of the most important people in town and he was never really free.\nAlso, why was my Mom so worried last night? I stepped out of bed. Instead of the usual hardwood floor I was used to I was stepped on something lumpy and cold. I looked down and jumped back on my bed.\nThe weapons from last night where on the floor right next to my bed. \n\n“Jaya what’s all the racket?” Said my mom’s voice. It sounded like she was coming to my room. Quickly, I covered the weapons with my blanket.\nLike that would do anything, but it was worth a shot. My mom came in the door and said,\n\n“Jaya why is your blanket on the floor?” \n\n“Bad dream.” I Lied.\nMy mom frowned, bent over, and was about to pick up the blanket. I closed my eyes and cringed from what was about to happen. \n\n“Jaya are you ok?” Said my Mom concerned.\nOpening my eyes I saw my mom had folded the blanket and on the floor was nothing.\n\n“Uh, yea.” I said scratching my head. “I think I just must have hit my head.”\n“Well it’s a good thing your going to see Linink today.” My mom said. “Come on, breakfast is ready.”\n\nI ate very little breakfast this morning. The taste of it as usual was great, but the stress of what I thought was to come overcame my hunger.\nAfter breakfast my mom took me straight to The Adventurers Guild. \n\nAs I approached the massive building I started to get nervous.\nMy mom opened the doors, led me past staring students, rooms that where full of weapons, and many more things.\n\n Finally we reached Linink’s Office.\nThe large green door looked inviting enough but as to what was to happen behind it still worried me. \n\nWithout knocking a voice said, “Come in.” My mom and I entered the triangle shaped room.\nI saw Linink sitting a table in the middle, but beside the table on both sides where my friends Sofetios and Sofia.\n\n I relaxed a little. At least they would be here with me. “Jaya, would you please take a seat.” Said Linink coolly.\nI took a seat, looked back at my mom, and Linink then said, “I need to speak to Jaya and his friends alone Madam.”\n\n My mom nodded and left the room quietly. Everyone was quite for a bit until I said,\n“What am I here for?” \n\n“I’d like to know that too.” Sofetios added.\n\n“Same here.” Said Sofia. After a moment Linink said,\n“We are here to discuss a recent series of events.”\n\n“Like what?” said Sofia. “Other then the Melonko Festival being today all that’s really happened was that Rainstorm last night. “\n“Exactly my point” said Linink. “A rainstorm now? In the middle of summer? I just don’t really see that as natural. There is also the Prophecy.”\n\n“You mean that old tale everyone listens to at the festival?” Said Sofetios inquiringly.\n“Just that.” Said Linink seriously. “From what I’ve seen happening in the last two days I’m inferring that it may be coming true.” At this Sofia laughed and said,\n“Like that would happen now. I mean the rain was probably coincidence and it’s not like the weapons have been found.” At this I felt the blood drain from my face.\n“Well from what I heard from Jaya’s Mother last night, I think they may have been found.” Said Linink. Sofia and Sofetios look right at me and Sofetios said, “You didn’t really… I mean you couldn’t have…”\n“He probably didn’t” Said Sofia, Otherwise he would be wearing them right now. It’s not like he would leave them at his house or something if he found them. Right?” I looked slightly down at this comment.\n“The weapons only appear if the owner wants them to.” Said Linink. Sofetios turns to me and said. “Well Jaya? Did you actually find the weapons?” I tell them the whole story of what happened last night and this morning.\nWhen I finish, Sofia is staring at me in disbelief, Sofetios is too, and Linink looks the same as he did before. No one said anything for a while until Linink said,\n\n“Well I guess the prophecy is coming true.”\n“Should we tell everyone?” Said Sofia.\n\n“No.” said Linink. “That would only raise panic. We should just tell whoever really needs to be told then you three set off after the festival.”\n\n“Us three?” I said.\n“Yes.” Said Linink “You know both Sofia and Sofetios pretty well. Except for what each they specialize in.” I didn’t actually know what Linink taught Sofetios and Sofia in the Guild and they had never shown me.\nI gave an odd face to all three of them then Linink said, “To put it bluntly Sofetios is a magician and Sofia is a fighter, in class terms that is.” \n\n“A magician?” I repeated while looking at Sofetios.\n“Intermediate magician.” Said Sofetios. “Sorry but Linink said we couldn’t tell anyone outside the guild.” \n\n“Wait so what can you do?” I said. “Levitate stuff or something?” Sofetios looked at Linink and Linink nodded.\nAll of the sudden everything small in the room started to slowly floated upwards.  I froze and looked around.  Then the things in the air floated down to their original places.\n“You see Jaya, Everything we teach at this guild more or less has to do with Lin.”  Said Linink.\n\n“Lin?” I said curiously.\n“Yes, it is something that is in everything around us.” Said Linink. “Kind of like a fifth element so to speak. Sofetios will be teaching you about this on your travels.”\n“Wait.” I said. “There’s a whole Fifth element?”\n\n“Yes.” Said Linink simply. “Sofetios, Sofia, please get ready for your departure.”\n\n“But sir.” Said Sofetios. “We still-“\n“Come on Sofetios.” Said Sofia as he grabbed Sofetios on the shoulder and had him follow her. When they closed the door, Linink turned to me and Said. \n\n“You have a long journey ahead of you.”\n“Yes sir…” I said nervously.\n\n“I just need to make sure you really have the weapons.” Said Linink concerned.\n\n“I would sir but I don’t know how to get them to appear.” I said.\n“Just hold your hand as you would your sword and try to will them there.” Said Linink. I did so and in a second a white sword materialized there. It felt warm in my hand. Linink seemed was taken aback a little, so I asked,\n“Sir, why me?” Linink seemed back as himself and said after a moment,\n\n“Because He chose you. At least that’s what the Prophecy sais.” Linink got up and went to his bookshelf.\nHe picked up two books and put them both on the desk. He opened one and the inside of it was hollowed out. All there was, was a semi-clear sphere about an inch long.\nHe handed it to me and said. “This is something I’ve been working on for a long time. Use it well.”  I sheathed the sword and took the sphere and said,\n\n“Sir, what is this?”\n“Don’t you recognize it?” Linink said surprised. “It is object from part of the lore they tell at the Melonko festival. Well, my version of it anyway.”\n\n“I’m sorry sir, I don’t really listen to the tales they tell.” I said a little embaraced.\n“Well then I should probably tell you.” Said Linink. “It is my version of a water sphere. This one I would say holds about 1 week worth of water for 3 people.” Unbelieving, I stared at the sphere.\n“All you need to do is heat it in something and water will come out.”\n\n“Sir?” I said. “What did you mean by ‘your version’?”\n\n“You’ll find out soon enough.” Said Linink. Suddenly there was music outside.\n“The festival is starting.”\n\n“Sir, what now?” I said.\n\n“Now, you go enjoy the festival.” Said Linink. “But before you go,” Linink picked up the other book and handed it to me.\n“This is a book on lore of Edrot. You may want to study it.”\n\n I turned to leave when Linink said, “and Jaya, two words of advice. First, with the powers you will soon possess, Make sure you use them the right way.\nSecondly, I need you to will away that sword for now. The people in town don’t need to see it.”\n\n“Is that all sir?” I said.\n\n“That’s all” Said Linink.\n\nEND OF CHAPTER TWO\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C3", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n             -By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\nChapter Three\n The Melonko Festival\n\nI went to the town’s center where everyone was gathered, People where playing music and everyone was seemingly having a good time.\nThe mayor, Jedjory, appeared and walked to the center and everyone quieted down.  Then Jedjory said, \n\n“Good morning everyone, this is the 10th Melonko festival, Celebrating good fortune and peace.\nNow  everyone please stop and listen to the Adventurers guild orchestra!” Everyone turned to the front of the Adventurers guild where there where about 50 teenagers with all kinds of different instruments. Linink was on a piano and started to play.\nThen others joined in and more until everyone was playing.  I had heard Sofetios speak of this kind of thing before, where everyone joined in when they felt it was right. I think he called it free playing.\nThe sound was great. When they all finished there was a round of applause and Jedjory spoke again when they all quieted down.\n\n“Let the Melonko festival begin!”\nI met with Sofia and Sofetios a bit later in front of one of the games tents. \n\n“So, chosen one, how did you like the performance?” Said Sofia sarcastically. \n\n“Don’t call me that.” I said angrily.\n“Come on.” Said Sofia smiling. “Everyone is going to start calling you that once they realize what you found.”\n\n“Hopefully that won’t be soon” I said worried. I noticed that Sofetios was looking behind the tent. “What is it Sofetios?”\n“I think I just saw a black hooded figure behind the tent.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“Not possible.” Said Sofia. “I already know what you’re thinking and it’s not possible. They died out years ago.”\n“Yea, your right.” Said Sofetios turning to me. “I guess I’m just worried about the Journey.”\n\n“Wait, what died out years ago?” I said.\n“Jeez Jaya.” Said Sofia. “You really should pay more attention to lore.” I then remembered the Lore book that Linink gave me and pulled it out of my bag.\n\n“I see Linink gave you his lore book.” Said Sofetios.\n“That will probably help in times to come. “Look up the word ‘Omira’.”  I skimmed the book until I found the word. I then said,\n“ ‘The Omira are a clan of people dedicated to protecting the Land from any evil. They commonly wear black robes with hoods and are practiced in concealing themselves.\nThey are said to be mainly of the rouge class, but there were rumors of some being mages. They are said to have died out long ago. ‘ “ \n\n“That about covers it.” Said Sofetios. “Did Linink give you anything else?”\nI pulled out the water sphere Linink gave me. At this Sofetios’s mouth hung slightly ajar.\n\n“He gave you a water sphere?” Sofetios said in amazement. “How much did he say was in there?”\n“A weeks worth for three people he said.” I said.\n\n“Well then I guess we won’t need to worry about water.” Said Sofia. “Come on, let’s go to the fortune stall.” Sofia went to the fortune stall every year.\nThe weird thing about the lady who runs it is that all her predictions seem to come true.\n\nAs we approached the purple tent. I couldn’t help but be worried. I was about to have my future laid out for me. Maybe I just wouldn’t get my fortune read.\nWe entered the tent. The old lady was sitting behind the usual crystal ball.\n\n“Come in.” She said as she looked up. “Ah Sofia. Come to see your fortune again I see?”\n\n“Yes Maim.” Said Sofia.\nThis is pretty much the only time she gets enthusiastic or manner full about anything except fighting.\n\n“Ok then.” Said the Lady. “Please take a seat. I will need your two friends to step outside.” Sofia looked at us and both Sofetios and I left.\nAfter 15 minutes, Sofia left the tent looking slightly uneasy. She was also holding a fortune cookie in her hand. The old lady also gives those out so people can have a little extra info.\n“She wants you to come in next Sofetios.” Said Sofia. Sofetios went inside the tent without saying a word.\n\n“What did she tell you?” I said.\n\n“None of your business.” Said Sofia right back.\nAfter another 15 minutes Sofetios exited the tent looking a bit down. \n\n“Well your next.” Said Sofetios to me. I nervously entered the tent. \n\n“Take a seat.” Said the lady. I went over and took a seat.\n“Your friends certainly had interesting fates. Now let’s see yours.” She pulled out her famous set of fortune cards and spread them out face down. “Choose four.” I picked the ones in the beginning, end, and two in the middle.\n“Now flip them over in the order you choose. One by one.” I flipped the first one. It had a picture of someone about to be shot by and arrow but there was someone behind the person who was the real one about to be shot with a dagger raised.\nThere were words printed around the sides. It said, ‘Saved by a Friend’. “It seems you have more friends then you realize.” Said the old lady. “Now the second.”\nI flipped over the second one. It showed a book with worlds spewing out of it with the word ‘Skill’. “It also seams that you will excel at learning. Now the third.”\nI flipped over the third one and it had a picture of a blanket over a bizarre shaped object with jagged edges and then a picture of a bird in a cage with the blanket on the ground, the words on this one said ‘Doubt then Understanding’.\nThe old lady seemed a little worrisome on this card. \n\n“Is something wrong?” I said nervously.\n\n“No, no.” said the old lady.\n“This card means that you will doubt something or be undecided, but then see the truth. Now the Fourth.” I flipped the fourth card and it showed two paths going separate from each other.\nOn one side there was what looked like woods, on the other it looked like a plain. The words on it said ‘The Choice’  “That’s the toughest one of all.” Said the lady.\n“You will have a tough choice in the future. Now for your final fortune with me. Please place your hands on the side of the crystal ball and you will see your future.” I hesitated, then was about to place my hands on the crystal ball.\nWhen I touched it, it exploded with light. The old lady stood up quickly and gasped and then I realized I was standing up too. As soon as my hand left the ball the light went away immediately.\n“You…” Said the lady slowly. Then she calmed down. “So the prophecy is coming true. “ \n\n“What does this all mean?” I said.\n\n“It means you have a long journey ahead of you.” Said the old lady.\n“Here.” She reached in a jar at the side of the table and pulled out two cookies. “Only Break and eat one. The other you are to give to a friend.”\n\n“Is that all you have to say?” I said hoping for more.\n“That is all.” Said the old lady. I exited the tent, sure that I looked worried.\n\n“What happened in there?” Said Sofia.\n\n“Yea.” Said Sofetios. “We saw a flash of light.”\nI was about to tell them when I remembered its bad luck to tell your fortunes. I needed all the luck I could get.\n\n“Sorry I don’t know myself.” I said with some truth.\nAfter some hours had passed, we went to the entrance of the village. Sofia and Sofetios had huge packs on. \n\n“Should I have brought anything?” I asked.\n\n“No we have everything here.” Said Sofetios.\nThen I remembered my mom.\n\n“But we can’t go yet, I need to say goodbye to my mom!” \n\n“Relax Jaya.” Said Sofetios. “Linink probably already told your mother.”\n“Yea, I guess your right.” I said a little down. Then it occurred to me that I didn’t even know where we were going.\n\n“Wait, where are we going?” I said.\n“To the temple of the Omira” Said Sofia. “You should really take a look at that lore book.” As we left I dug into my pocket and got the two fortune cookies. I picked one at random and opened it. The paper inside said one word. ‘Believe’.\nEND OF CHAPTER THREE\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C4", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\nChapter Four\n  The Power of Lin\n\nAs we set of on the path leading out from the town, Sofetios began to tell me about Lin. \n\n“To use Lin, you will need to be able to understand what it is.” Said Sofetios.\n“Ok then.” I said. “What is it?”\n\n“I think the better question is what isn’t it.” Said Sofetios. “Lin is like an elemental life force to which you can use to manipulate the area around you.\nFor instance, Sofia uses Lin as a weapon, literally. She can make weapons out of her Lin and use it to add force to her blows.”\n\n“Wait so you mean that I could make a sword right now out of Lin?” I said astounded.\n“I don’t think you would be able to do it right away since you’re just beginning, but yes you could. I would ask Sofia to train you in that type of style since I don’t know much about it.”\n\n“Ok.” I said. “So what can you teach me?”\n“I can teach you another style of using Lin.” Said Sofetios. “As you saw before I levitated things around Linink’s office. But you can do much more. You can also make things into different forms.\nImagine you holding clay with your minds hands and holding it from 5 feet away. Then being able to mold it to what you would like. Sofia can we stop for a second?” \n\n“Come on.” Said Sofia. “What for? We’re on a tight schedule.”\n“It will only take a second.” Said Sofetios as he picked up a pebble. He walked over to me and put it in my hand. “Something to start with. Try levitating it, transforming it, things like that.”\nAs we began walking again, I held the pebble in my hand and levitating it. I thought I saw it wiggle a bit but thought that it was just my movement walking. \n\nWe arrived at a camp site as the full moon was up.\nAs we set up a camp sight for the night, Sofetios walked over to me.\n\n“How is the stone coming along?” Said Sofetios\n\n“I just can’t get it to budge.” I said frustrated.\nSofetios appeared to be thinking. Then he said,\n\n“I think you may be thinking about it a different way then you should for levitating. If I’m right in saying your trying to force it to, it won’t work.”\n“Wait why won’t force work?” I said. “I’m trying to force the stone up right?”\n\n“Force works for stuff like… well… forceful stuff.” Said Sofetios. “What you want to try to do is lifting it not with force alone, but thought.”\n“Thought.” I repeated.\n\n“Yes.” Said Sofetios. “Instead of the thought of trying to lift an impossible stone, just think of it as possible it might help. A lot of it is in what you believe.” There was the word again. Believe.\nThis gave me confidence. I held out the stone in my palm and began to try to levitate it. After a moment nothing happened, and then it wiggled.\n\n“Yes!” I yelled.\nJust as I yelled, the stone shot into the air and then landed on the ground. “Hey Sofetios you don’t have to show off.”\n\n“That wasn’t me.” Said Sofetios. “It was you.”\n“I did that?” I said confused. “But all I could do was make it move a little. How could I have made it shoot in the air like that?”\n\n“Your excitement in moving the pebble while still trying to move the pebble.\nEmotion counts as thought when it comes to Lin.”\n\n“Hey you two.” Said a voice from behind. We turned and it was Sofia. She had a bag on her bag that seemed full of a certain type of fruit. “Dinners up.”\nSofetios put a metal pot on the unlit fire pit. \n\n“Hey Jaya could I get the water sphere?” Said Sofetios.\n\n“Yea, sure.” I said taking it out and giving it to him. He put it in the pot when I asked,\n“Who has the fire maker?” I said. Sofetios just smiled at me and said,\n\n“We don’t need one.”\n\n“But how-“I began as I saw Sofetios put his hand near the fire pit and snapped his fingers.\nInstantly, a small flame appeared on his thumb which he left sticking out. He started to light the fire until it started to flame. Then in moments there was good sized fire in the pit. “Doesn’t that hurt?”\n“Not when you know how to control it.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“O stop showing off Sofetios.” Said Sofia. I saw water starting to slowly rise in the pot. I got closer to get a better look.\nIt seemed at if the Water sphere was melting water but wasn’t shrinking in the slightest.\n\n“It’s like ice.” I said.\n“I guess you could look at it that way.” Said Sofetios as he picked up the water sphere out of the pot and gave it to me.\n\n“Come on guys, let’s eat.” Said Sofia tossing an apple my way. The apple had was red with an odd purplish tinge.\nI put the water sphere away then was about to take a bite when an arrow came from my right and hit the apple, sending it flying from my hand into a tree. We all sprang up and drew our weapons.\nSofia Looked to where the arrow came from but there was no one there. \n\n“Come out coward!” Said Sofia. There wasn’t a noise. The moon was very bright, bright enough for me to make out the shadow of a figure from behind a large rock.\n“There!” I said pointing to the shadow. We ran toward the rock and when we got to the side, No one was there. “Wait, what?” I looked down to where the shadow was and there was nothing there.\n“We’ve been tricked!” Said Sofia pointing back at the sight. “Who ever it was stole the apples!” We ran back to the camp sight and Sofetios pointed to the ground. Where he was pointing there as a piece of paper. He went down and picked it up and read,\n“ ‘I’m Sorry for having to have delayed your meal. I left some other fruits by one of your bags. Those apples where poisoned. Local hunters nearby here use the poison on those apples so that once an animal eats it, it dies in a couple of days.\nOnce the animal dies, the poison wears off. Once again I’m sorry.’ ”\n\n“Well whoever it was did leave us fruit.” Said Sofia with a smaller bag of fruit in her hands.\n\n“All there is on the bottom of the note is a big C.” Said Sofetios.\nSofia took out some of the fruits and I said,\n\n“Hey, those are the kind of berries that are in the woods back home.” \n\n“Well, I guess they are safe then.” Said Sofia.\nAfter discussing what just happened a while we ate, we agreed that I would take first watch. After a while when everyone but me was sleeping, I began to get tired so I sat on a nearby rock.\nWhen I sat down I felt something crinkly under me. I sat up and there was a piece of paper, Identical to the one we found a bit earlier except it had a different message. I read,\n‘If you want to learn how to use his weapons. Come see me at The Purple Café in Northenway. When you get there ask the waitress for the basement level table. I’ll be waiting there. Please do not tell your friends. I would like this to be private. C. ‘\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C5", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                 Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\nChapter Five\n           Cloak\n\nWhen we got up the next morning, when we finished packing up and started walking, I asked Sofetios,\n\n“Where is Northenway?”\n“It’s on the way to the temple.” Said Sofetios. “Why?”\n\n“It’s just there’s a place I’ve wanted to visit for a while.” I lied. “A place called the purple café? My Mom told me about it once.”\n“We aren’t making any un necessary stops.” Said Sofia. “We need to get to the temple.” I didn’t want to argue, so I figured I would wait until we got there to ask again.\nAs we approached the gates of Northenway, we were approached by guards.\n\n“Halt.” Said one of the guards. “What business do you have in Northenway?”\n\n“Just passing through.” Said Sofetios.\n“Really, do you think we were born yesterday?” Said the other guard. “You are playing hooky from school. Aren’t you?”\n\n“Relax.” Said Sofia. “We came from the Village south of here. No need to get mad.”\n“Hey, you better watch yourself girly.” Said the guard back. “Or Ill make you.” That was a mistake.\n\n“Girly!?” Said Sofia steaming. Sofia was about to go off.\n“Come on Rodrick.” Said the other guard. “Let’s just go for a bit, I think our break time is on anyway. Let’s just go to The Purple Café and relax a bit, eh?”\n“Fine, see you later miss.” The guard said with a chuckle. After the two left Sofia seemed to be trying to cam herself down. Then she said,\n\n“I think we should go to The Purple Café.”\nWe entered the city, which had its town square up front. In the middle there was a man in a white robe saying things to a small crowd that had gathered. He was saying,\n“The sun dims every day! Can you not feel it? It’s as though the days are getting shorter! The nights longer! Be vigilant, the time to prove ourselves comes!”\n\n“What is he talking about?” I said.\n“It’s part of the prophecy.” Said Sofetios. I frowned a bit as we made our way down the street to a large restaurant. There was a sign hanging from the door that showed a coffee mug with steam coming from it.\nOn the top of the sign it said ‘The Purple Café’.  As we approached the door Sofia stopped and looked at a notice on the door. We gathered around it, it said,\n‘Arm wrestling day. Tournament will be in mid day. The grand champion gets 100 gold! Sign up here.’ Then there was a list of names and blank spaces. Under the notice was a pen and ink.\nSofia put her finger on the list then went down until she stopped at ‘Rodrick’.  Sofia wrote her name down so fast I thought for sure her name would be illegible. Someone came out of the door and looked at us. It was a waitress.\n“Just getting the sign up sheet.” She said taking it down and carrying it inside. We entered the café. It looked amazing. There were people at the bar drinking and the waitress cutting names off the list and putting them in a cup.\nThere was also a band playing tavern music. Then I noticed another waitress staring at us. She walked up to us and said,\n\n“Are you kids going to order something or just stand there?”\n“I’m in the arm wrestle competition.” Said Sofia. Not waiting, Sofia walked past her and went toward a table. The waitress then looked at Sofetios and I. “We’re going to watch her compete”. Said Sofetios, The waitress sighed and said,\n“Fine, just don’t cause any trouble.”\n\n“We won’t” I said. As we went in the waitress who was cutting up the names went to the center of the restaurant, then said,\n\n“Alright! Is everyone ready to arm wrestle?”\nThere were cheers through the restaurant. “Ok then. The first two contenders are…” She put her hand in the cup and drew two names. “First we have Rodrick!” There were roars from a table in the corner as the guard from before got up, Flexing.\n“Please come to the center table!” as Rodrick got there, the waitress with the names looked at the other one and said, “Second we have…” The waitress seemed to squint at the paper.\nI cringed, there was only one person that could be. “Sofia! Come to the middle table!” Rodrick was looking back at his table, which was chanting his name over and over again.\nWhen Sofia got to the table Rodrick turned to her, waited a moment as he recognized her, then laughed. \n\n“This girly is my first competition?” Said Rodrick.\n“You bet I am, unless you want to back down?” Said Sofia with a smile. There where “oo’s” from the crowd. \n\n“You’re on girly.” Said Rodrick as he smiled back. There were cheers throughout the restaurant again.\nSofia and Rodrick sat down at opposing ends of the middle table. The whole restaurant then counted, “Three!” “Two” “ONE!” There was a loud slam and a thud and it was over. The band stopped playing.\nSofia stood over Rodrick who she had slammed his arm so hard on the table he had flipped over out of his chair to the floor. He wasn’t moving. The people from his table went over and tried to pick him up.\n“Is he dead?” The waitress said concerned.  One of them put an ear to his chest and said,\n\n“Nah, he’s just drunk. Let the tournament continue!” Everyone cheered and the tournament continued.\nSofia was about to step down when the waitress said,\n\n“Wait, you need to stay up here until you lose.”\n\n“Wait, what?” Said Sofia. “Well this is going to be fun then.” I then remembered why I was here.\nI went to the waitress who wanted us to order something and said,\n\n“Could I get the Basement table?” The Waitress raised an eyebrow and said,\n“We don’t have a basement table, but we do have an attic one. Follow me.” I followed the waitress upstairs to a door. She opened it went inside as I followed. Inside was a figure in a black hood and black robes.\n“Keep watch.” He said. The waitress nodded, went out, and closed the door.\n\n“So you’re C?” I said taking out the letters\n\n“Yes.” Said the person in the robes. “But you can call me Cloak.”\n“How do you know I have the weapons?” Said Sofetios. \n\n“I know how to use Lin in ways other then your friend Sofetios showed you.” Cloak said as he got up and got a bowl from a shelve and put it on the table. He got a jug and poured water into the bowl.\n“Come look for yourself.” I went closer and looked into the bowl. I didn’t see anything. “One moment” He said. He pulled out a very small vial with white liquid in it. \n\n“What is that?” I said.\n“This.” He said. “Is my own lin.”\n\n“What?” I said in a slightly raised tone. There were massive cheers downstairs.\n\n“Observe.” He said as he uncorked the vial and poured it into the bowl.\nThe white liquid spread until it reached all sides of the bowl. Then Cloak put one finger so it was barely touching the side of the bowl and an image came in. It was of Sofia In at the Middle table downstairs with a huge smirk on her face.\nThe other hand was being held up by the waitress.\n\n“It seems your Friend won another round.”\n\n“How are you doing that, and who are you?”\n“I am simply using my mind to see through my Lin.” Said Cloak. “I can see places nearby, or farther if my will allows me. As to who I am.” Said Cloak removing his hood. He looked no older then I was.\n“I am the last member of the Omira.\"\n\nEnd of Chapter Five", ""),
        StaticBook("John Cage's Song", "Heruza", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Josef Vladov", "Josef Vladov", "This doccument is proof of citizenship of Orenia, specifically in the city of Felsen, for the Song Druid. He is to be given a proper trial and punishment for any crimes he may commit and should be shown with the same respect and humility that any other\nhuman of our Kingdom might be shown.\n\n-The Doccument of Citizenship is signed by Lord Josef Vladovic; Imperial General, Head Steward of Felsen, Count of Saintois, Baron of Franzenburg, and Castellen of Darkwood.-", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Siirist", "=========================         =====Journal=====\n=========================\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n   Owner: Siirist Skolar\n15th of the First Seed, 1522\nToday was an interesting day, I think I may have started a quest to finding myself, and procuring more knowledge about conscious behavior. I have always been curious about the mind, and why we do the things we do. As a scholar, it is my duty to look into\nsuch matters. To start off, I am going to begin using a method of looking inside ones self, and I think I will call it introspection for a proper name. Others have used it, but it is often a difficult task for the uneducated to really look in and see how\nsomething really makes us feel. Take a piece of candy, you put it in mouth, and it is sweet, but what else do you taste? What is the texture, how does it feel in your mouth, and is there anything else you can discern about the object? Using all five\nsenses to listen mentally and phsyically to what happens when you eat the piece of candy. It will sound silly to some, but it is the first step into figuring out what we really are. Now onto the next experiment...\n15th of the First Seed, 1522\n17th of the Deep Cold, 1523\n    Today has been quiet. An odd thing, all the land seems to be in silence, perhaps waiting for the coming winter days. It has been getting cold, but I have enjoyed it. I really enjoy the cold, but I never see snow anymore...\n18th of the Deep Cold, 1523\n   I feel like I need to get something off my mind. I have been wondering quite a bit about ants lately, and how the one queen organism can control all the rest. When there gets to be too many ants, they start to die off -\n-because they just stand there waiting around. My hyopthesis is that if the queen is not controlling the ants with orders, then they will die of boredom. Perhaps this related to people in that if they have no purpose, they cease to exist. A worthy lesson.\n15th of Snow's Maiden, 1524\n    I saved a woman's life today. Her name is Synestra, and I valiantly took charge of the procedure, at only 19! Hileia thankfully had some training with sutures, but I lead him in the procedure, as well as the others as we-\nstabilized her. I am quite proud of my ability, but still I know I need more training. What happens when Hileia commits suicide?...\n4th of the Grand Harvest, 1524\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya, a wonderful phrase really. The driving philosophy of high elven culture. It has its' merits and has allowed me to see the world in special form of oppurtunity, & a reason to live. To progress & health,", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Unknown", "-------------------\n\n\n\n\n\"The Devourer's Mercy\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\nEntry #1:\n-------------------I have recently been looking for leads on the beast which has coined the name, The Devourer. From the last voyage I have established that the sheer size of the beast is to unimaginable proportions. Though this means that the -\n-creature is indeed ancient. This beast is not new, or not the child of some other primal beast. It's face has apparently never been seen, as I have found various manuscripts from the past inhabitants of these isles... Translation will be tedious but it-\n-will be worth it. For what I find in these documents, I believe will help me establish a connection to the Devourer and its true purpose...\n\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\n[!]\nVarious sketches of strange elven symbols are scattered along the page, transcribing them would take time, as each symbol is distorted by the various quill strokes against the paper.\n[!]\nEntry #2\n-------------------These documents are quite interesting... They detail some sort of temple or place of worship. The words, \"The Drowned Children\" seem to repeat themselves through this document, with further outlining of these disgusting rituals\n-and practices which were performed by these children. Though my lead was right, these ancient people were indeed connected to the Devourer. They believed for the creature to be some sort of god which guarded them from the East. The document has further-\n-references to certain mural sites which are scattered along the Eastern Coastline. I am not sure if I wish to explore these, since the rituals depicted were performed at these sites... I am having trouble composing myself to write this entry. Though I-\n-must document this to ensure that this knowledge gets spread to the general Vailorian populace. I believe this creature is alot more than it currently appears, for the old seemed to worship it with an undying sense of loyalty... I'll update this when-\n-more leads are uncovered by these documents.\n-------------------\n[!] Distorted circles are placed upon a drawn landmass, scattered along its east. They appear to be different to the current continent of Vailor.\n[!]\nEntry #3\n-------------------I have found one of the mural sites! I pack and leave in the next day. Further investigation upon the documents have revealed that these rituals somehow powered a certain stone... A Prophet was believed to wield this stone-\n-control the very fabric of time and the world. Through the manipulation of the Devourer! These discoveries make my jaw drop, for if there is a stone which holds this power, that would mean it could be an object used to bargain between nations. Or -\n-glorious riches... Yes, imagine the small earth digger to have the riches of the Salvian Vaults, that would be grand... I shall write in a new book to record my further studies, for this one shall stay until I compile them all into a journal. That I will\n-release upon the discovery of this stone. I shall leave this disgusting shack and move to more glorious fronts, to the mural site I shall go.\"\n-------------------[!] A final scribble ends the journal, the rest of the pages blank.\n[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "NinjaRebel101", "Dear Journal, \n\nMy first days in Skyfall have been quite strange. The people here are very friendly to one another, even though they are alchemists! Back when my father was alive, he would always tell me of how alchemists were evil beings who were\nengulfed in the evils of magic and potions and such. Over the years, I've learned that alchemists are not so, and are usually neutral, I suppose. The lord here is an alchemist himself, and he practices magic. He even managed to lift a halfling up into the\nsky, with not a sweat atop his forehead! My father was apparently wrong in raising me to think that magic and the practice of alchemy was wrong, as the lord, who's name is Sarrion, even gave me my own study, full of bookcases for books and even a bed to\nsleep under! No more naps in the burrows under trees, full of worms and weeds and insects for me, for now. I'm deciding to fill up the bookcases with my own books, mostly journals and study guides and notes, and reading most of the books in the library.\nSarrion had also told me about an even larger library somewhere nearby, which sounds great! During my first couple of days here, I've managed to open myself to a few people here, mostly children. They were very interested in me, despite my shy ways.\nThe list:\n-Rafe : Rafe is a wood elf, from what I could tell. He has tanned skin and elven ears, and has an interest in alchemy and brewing. He's known around Skyfall as a child with bad habits and is known as a bad influence. I've never really seen him\ndo anything bad, except for one thing that I will keep to myself.\n-Ennulia : Ennulia is the daughter of Sarrion, the lord. Apparently, her mother is a dragon! I'd love to see her in her dragon form one day. Ennulia is really friendly, and is\ntraining herself to the longsword. She's learning alchemy too, and talks to me whenever she sees me. -Zane : Zane is a halfling that Ennulia always seems to hug whenever possible. He's pretty short, around 2 feet tall, and has a strange accent,\nwhich I find quite unique about him. He noticed that I have boyish looks, which I prefer to have over girlish ones. He also took in that I'm shy, but continues to try to talk to me, even when I curl up into a small ball in the corner.\n-John : John is a\nboy with 'butter' hair and always carries a waraxe around with him, even though it makes him tilt to the side. To me, he is the most irritable of the group, but still a 'friend', I guess. He scares me and sometimes gets a bit too close, in my opinion.\n-Sarrion : Sarrion is the lord of Skyfall. He is a man of alchemy, magic, and knowledge, and is the father of Ennulia. He has a nice nature to him, giving me a home and showing sympathy towards me, which is the first time someone has done that, except for\nthe people that gave me stale bread. He's a person to know, respect, and look up to. His wife, the dragon, has two forms, her elven form and her dragon form. \n-Bell : Bell often hangs around Sarrion, like a fly of a sort, However, it is visible that he\nhas much respect for Sarrion and Ennulia, but clearly doesn't like Rafe. He tries to keep Rafe and Ennulia separated, and tries to teach others that Rafe is a bad influence. Although he doesn't seem all that good, he is probably not bad either, as I've\nlearned that he is the religious director and historian of the town.\n\nFor now, the town seems like a nice environment to stay in, and I'll continue to live here until I grow older or I'm kicked out, for whatever reason. I'm going to go off and review the\nbooks in the library, one of which is Bell's book about Morality, which seems very 'deep' and interesting. \n\nSincerely,\n        Jasmine Gray.\n\n*A small star would be drawn on the corner of the page.*\nDear Journal, \nI've just discovered something dire! I was simply walking around town when I stopped by what used to be Bell Sano's adobe. Out of curiosity, I looked at the name tag of the house, and it said for sale! I'm most likely overreacting, but\nmaybe something bad has happened to him. He may mave moved to a bigger house, but maybe... No, no. It can't be that. Also, I've been locked out of my study for a few days now. Luckily, I keep my study notebook and journal on me. I've been spending my\nnights at the library of Dragur, near the alchemy bookshelves. I've completed the first couple of volumes, and it's pretty interesting. I hope to become an alchemist one day, like my friend Rafe. Speaking of Rafe, I haven't really seen him around lately..\nMaybe I should go look for him. Yeah, that's what I'll do. Also, my stuttering has been getting worse by the day! I don't know what is wrong with me! E-Everyth-thing c-comes out l-l-like th-this!! I have to get something done about that problem. Also, on\nfurther news, I've met this girl called Wawahi. She seems like a nice girl, but she gets in the way too much! She keeps on popping into the picture, especially when she isn't supposed to! She even had the nerve to talk about my parents! What a brat! But..\nShe said she could help with my stuttering... and she doesn't seem all that bad.. Maybe I'll get to know her more. This truly has been a hectic week. \nSincerely,\n          Jasmine Gray.\n\n*A small star would be drawn in the corner.*\nDear Journal,\nThe most idiotic thing happened today! THis man, apparently a lord, named Damai called interbreeding disgusting! He is obviously not a man to deal with, as he does not know the true essence of love, and that one should not be limited to the\nboundaries of their own race. However, I guess he was raised like that. Can't change the views of the already set. However, he was fighting with another man that didn't mind interbreeding, saying that it doesn't matter where you're from, as long as you\nlove them and they love you. Now THAT man is one to be understood and followed. He was a part of a guild called Nortruppen, or something of that sort. Perhaps I will join it. After all, it is not based on gender. But my alchemy and magic studies will have\nto come first.\nSincerely,\n        Jasmine Gray.\n*A star would be drawn in the corner.*\nDear Journal,\n   After many years, I seem to have returned to writing in you again. Currently 15, and still a stuttering piece of shit.. After four years, I see Rafe and Ennulia once more. They have grown, both in mind and body. Rafe has developed\nhis alchemy, and his body as well. Confined to a wheelchair all day, all he does is stare at Ennulia's arse. What a pervert, Ennulia has also gotten bigger, but she's more muscle that fat. It would have been great to see them again, and even more so if he\nhadn't called me a killjoy. Oh, well. It seems as if he had grown to dislike me over the years. No matter. After, all... Nowadays, it's just me, my sketch pad, my journal, and nothing else.\nSincerely,\n           Jasmine Gray\n*Her star signature*\nDear Journal,\nIt seems as if I have aquired a job. Even though my mistress has advised me not to take the position, it seems alright. In the city of Riga, where several seem to reside, is a small tavern. Not too shabby. After mentioning the line\nof work I had taken to Rafe, he must have thought I was joking. Oh, well. It's not as if he had liked me anyway. And my employer, Casper Ginsae, seems to have offered me stuttering lessons. How fun. Back to serving I go.\nSincerely,\n           Jasmine Gray\n*Her star signature*\nDear Journal, \n A few days ago I decided to partake in the civil war of Courland. It was a plain day, and I decided to join out of boredness. Barely any at the tavern anyways. The side I chose ended up losing anyways, but it doesn't matter.\nI managed to get a deep cut in my left side though. Hurts like hell. I had it stiched up a few days ago, but it still pains me to walk around normally. The stuttering lessons haven't really been working, as I've stayed the same old stuttering self.\nHonestly, what's so perfect about this world anyways? I'd be better off without it. I'll think about it.\nSincerely,\n          Jasmine Gray\n*Her star signature*\nDear Journal,\n  I haven't written in you for a while. I apologize. I feel as if you are the only thing that's willing to listen to me at this point. I feel as if no-one likes me. Then again, what's there to like? I stutter, I'm skinny, I don't even raise\nmy hand in my new alchemy class, whom Rafe is teaching. And I feel as if he hates me now too. Just because I'm too much of a bother. No one really pays attention to me. Oh well. It's better off to be me and my books anyways. Just me.. My sketch pad.. My\nnotebook, and you, of course. My quill, too. Currently, I am sitting on the peak of an orange tree, teetering with the somewhat safety of the canopy and the almost certain death if I were to fall over. Quite exciting.\nMaybe I should live here instead of\nmy adoptive miss' house. Or my dorms. It's not like anyone will miss me if I go poof. This entry is getting more depressing by the minute. Not like anyone will read this, anyway. I have this book all to myself and only myself.  I think I'm going to finish\nup this entry. It's getting long as is, and the view is one to take in fully. I'll write in you later.\n\nSincerely,\n          Jasmine Gray\n*Her usual star signature*\nDear Journal,\n  Things have been getting... Boring.. Routine... It's just.. There's nothing new or exciting to do, really.. I mean, I've been missing my classes because I'm zoning out from everything. It's all the same. I wake up in either my dorm, under\na tree, or rarely in my miss' house. Then I often go to draw something or work out long hours in the tavern. Then I fall asleep. It's.. boring... I wish there was a way to say interested.. Or something to occupy me that isn't the same over and over. Oh\nwell. Not like I deserve it anyway.\n     Sincerely,\n           Jasmine Gray\n*Her star signature*\nDear Journal,\n  Life is boring. I haven't found anything good to draw, so my skills are getting quite rusty, and useless as they were. I don't really go to alchemy class as I seem to lose track of time, and everything is the same. It's all the same,\njournal.\n      Sincerely,\n           Jasmine Gray\n*Her star signature*\nDear Journal,\n  I've decided to reread all that I have ever written in you, and it has certainly brought back memories. It reminds me of how foolish my thinking back then was, and how idiotic I am to this day. However, it's... 'fun' to remind myself of\nwho I was and who I may become, if anything. I know, I seem like a cliche, and I'm seem like one of those folk that see life as useless and that they long to already pass away, but I swear, I am not that case. Honestly, if there was something.. just\nsomething that could bring true purpose to my life, like teaching someone or finding a job that brings forward exciting news and such, it would mean the world to me. As these normal days go by, I am finding myself getting duller and duller. My skills have\nbecome 'rusty', but job becoming repetitive, and spending most of my time in the wilderness has even grown to become routine in its actions.. Everything is the same.. or maybe I have become blind to change. It seems as if your pages are running out, and I\nwill have to say farewell to you, sweet journal. I will not be able to write in you again, but I will remember you dearly, as you have stuck by me. Not even my closest peers have done that over the years. And for that, I thank you. Even if you are only\na book.. I thank you for staying with me.\nGoodbye, Journal. You will be missed.\n        Sincerely,\n           Jasmine Gray\n*Her star signature*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Poppy Evocress", "Property of:\n\nPoppy Carteret\n\nSend bird if found!\n*Within the first few pages would be several loose papers bearing various hand drawn maps of the realm*\nTo do list...\n\n-Buy an alchemy stand!\n-Prismarine?\n-Take care of lumber stores\nThing's I've found out...\n\n-Glacio was with the Adherency... He knew about Eren's finger being mutilated.. How did we not know?! I guess he just managed to save Eren's life with the whole 'finger or hand' thing... I guess that's alright...\n16 Snow's Maiden 1526\n\nI've been worrying about Eren.. he hasn't been around much and I miss him... It's almost my birthday and I'd like to have /some/ form of company around.\n6th, Amber Cold 1536\n\nI don't suppose I'm going to be getting my wish for my birthday.. 92 years old and ten years later... Oh how time flies, I feel so lonely.\n18th, Grand Harvest, 1537\n\nStill no word about Eren. He hasn't come home in quite some time and I've no idea where to even thart looking. Am I a bad wife for this...? He's left before for weeks but.. but for years... I don't know how much longer I can -\n-bear this. Why hasn't he left a note at home.. why hasn't he /come/ home? Anyone I have asked said they didn't see him. Should I fear the worst...?\n14th Amber Cold 1537\n\nI've started thinking about the Adherency again. I'm curious... what ever happened to that man Valmuel that had.. accompanied me in my cell. I shouldn't be thinking of such things..\nA map is drawn here of the mountains, numbers are written at the bottom of the page...\n\n\n\n-177, -3806, 131\n\nThere would be a crude drawing of a tower surrounded by snow here. Carnatia\n16, Malin's Welcome, 1546,\n\nI am uncertain if I can continue to live in Laureh'Lin, the taxes are proving to be difficult to manage on my own. Perhaps I could downgrade the home with just myself living in it.\n5th of Malin's Welcome, 1548\n\nWell.. it's official, Evark has me. All this time of running away from him and I just fold like a piece of paper under a boot. It's all for the best though.. I have to save Eren, if it kills me doing so...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 2", "EmilyBlackheart", "Property of \nPoppy Aeth'ahern\n\n\n\"Please send bird if found!\"\n\n\n*A detailed sketch of a flower rests at the bottom of the page*\n\"A collection of dream records, in hopes to aleviate my terrors when I sleep.\"\n\"When I fall asleep, all is quiet until I wake up, but I'm not in my bed. I'm in the tower.. I can hear rain falling outside and the creatures in the surrounding swamp echoing through trees that I cannot see but know are there. I hear a door open.. it -\n-makes me so scared.. I know who it is before I see him and when I turn his face is right in front of mine. It's so close I can feel his breath on my face. He smiles at me with such a wickedly pleasant smile that I start to scream but no sound comes out.-\nWhen I go to move my hands, I look and I can't, they're shackled... the shackles are so tight, my wrists, they hurt so much.. My hands are above my head and out to the sides so I can't lift myself off the muddy floor. When I look back at him, I see him-\nholding something, it's my fishing rod. He raises it, and then he starts swinging. I can't move, I was so desperate to move! I couldn't cover my face as he eventually whipped that too. It hurts everywhere. Just when I think I am about to give up and fall-\ninto the blackness... I wake.\"\n\n*At the bottom of the page, there looks to be a sketch of a simple doorway with the door slightly opened, a blackened figure standing in the shadow...*\n10th, First Seed, 1554\n\nI went looking around the mountains again, there is a new structure that I didn't see before. It's like a tomb, on the inscription is the following.. \"Herein lies Dralazar, Herald of Xion, Lord of Torment. We-\n-are born by the dark, Made men by the Dark; Undone by the Dark; We fear the Old Dark.\"\n\nI'm curious what the Dark is.. the way it is described makes it sound almost.. alive? And is this land owned by Xion? I suppose-\n-it would only make sense, this isn't the only monument that refers to the Dark in such a way. I'll write another passage on what I've seen before.\n\nThe tomb is curious though, I wonder if whomever is buried here is in some way a Gravelord, nasty-\ncreatures.. so vile in nature and in attitude. Should I meet one ever again in my life, it'd be too soon.\n\nThe other little monument looking thing in the mountains looks like a chair, in the stone above this chair are some words that seem to be sloppily-\nthrown together. They say:\n\n\"Aknu'gul, Reminiscent of the Old Fire; and unbeknownst reborn-\nhis vessel, his herald of The Abyss will\n\nWe. Fear. The. Old Dark.\" \n\nI'll have to go and-\nask Pherak if he knows what it means. Usually when something has to do with anything dark and spooky he has some knowledge of it.\n\nI wonder.. if any of this has to do with the ones everyone calls Xion...\n9th Snow's Maiden 1560\n\nI found the emerald that Eren gave to me as a child, I was so happy I thought I'd lost it!\n*This page doesn't seem to have a date, some smears of dried blood seem to stain the parchment*\n\n\"I killed someone... Caelan evar'kae...\"\n\n*The writing ends there*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry", "Artorias Thannius", "17th of Snow's Maiden, 1324\n\nReports from the far away lands of Urguan's hall tell the tale that the dwarves have begun work on a terrible mechanism they call \"The Seal\". While I will not pretend to be\none who has studied the brutish and noisy mechanisms of the dwarves, I can say with utmost certainty that the power of a soul is not something that the physical mechanisms, which the dwarves create, can\ninteract with.\n\nIndeed, the notion the dwarves could harness the power of a soul, when we the mages of Rivel find such a thing impossible with eldritch might is a notion that is so absurd some would say that it is even\nlaughable.\n\nI remind you, those of the Purple Circle that the efforts of the mages Torak Hergardul and Franz Astartes, who studied the nature of the soul for their entire productive lives,\nled to no remarkable discoveries and the conclusion that the soul is an intangible creation which can not even be influenced by the hand of the arcane.\n\nIt is therefore that I, Artorias\nThannius, Archmage of the Purple Circle, hereby recommend that Rivel refrain from acting on the impossible notion that dwarves will be able to harness the power of the soul. Should Rivel act on such a rumour, it would\nsimply be heeding the words of fools and madmen.\n-Artorias Thannius", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal entry 1", "Elvira Naromis", "11th of Sun's Smile 1509\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIn a day or two, myself with the company of Ramza, Iris and Farryn, will soon begin our journey. I have finished all of my preperations and told everyone that needed to be told of this journey.\nHowever...\nSome of the reactions were not met happily. For example, Beth.\nWhen I said hello to Beth a couple of days ago, she merely shrugged it away with a grim reply... and trust me, those words piereced my heart.\nI tried making peace with her but she refused.\nApparently, I haven't spent much time with her, only giving her a hello before running off somewhere. That is true but I have tried to find the time. Most of my time was spent either looking after Ramza and Iris, creating potions and research, even -\n-  bartending as well. She soon left without even a glance back...\nGuarger told me that Beth will eventually come over it... hopefully...\n\nIt feels quite strange leaving Athera. I spent most of my childhood in the wilderness behind the old ruines of -\n- Polaris or exploring the wilderness. The first time I ever actually came into Athera was when I was only twenty, a couple of months after my adopted father's death. Since then, this land has became my home, even if it is full of violence and misery at -\n- times. I still remember the first time I entered the Drunken Monk, a young twenty year old woman who was a nervous wreck yet wanted to learn the art of Alchemy. Looking back now, I've grown a lot since then, I've grown stronger, maturer, smarter and -\n- calmer. Heck, I've even gained a sense of humour! Even so, it feels strange heading out of Athera, like leaving your home and not sure of what will happen while you're away. Either way, I will return.\nAnd when I do, I will likely know the art of air -\n- evocation, perhaps with a brand new ingredient or two, and more.\n\nHopefully, this journey will be worth it. And that everyone in Athera will remain safe.\n\n- Elvira Naromis\nAlchemist. Arcanist.\nBartender.", ""),
        StaticBook("Junk Mail", "Thickfeet", "Is your fishing pole coming up short?\n\nCasting your line and finding nothing on the end?\n\nIf you feel like you aren't catching fish like you used to this is for you.\nNo longer do you need to train to be a master of baiting alone.\n\nFind Freud Ian \"Frodo\" Slipweed in Willow Hollow.\n\nHis patent pending Salmon Oil is a secret family recipe guaranteed to restore your\ntacklebox to its former glory!\n\n[Tiny paragraphs of warnings and disclaimers fill the rest of the letter.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Just a Note", "Revion Tathron", "Savet,\n\nkindly refrain from interrupting interviews.\n\n-Revion", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser Quotes", "Kaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "===Heil Valdoria===\n\nExcerpts from the speech made by the glorious Kaisereich Decimus Rovin.\n\n\"...racial species must preserve the purity of the blood which Gott has given it!\"\n\n  ====Page One====\n===Heil Valdoria===\n\n\"It is not for men to discuss the question of why Providence created different races, but rather to recognize the fact that it punishes those who disregard its work of creation.\"\n\n  ====Page Two====\n===Heil Valdoria===\n\n\"...revolutionary change in our knowledge and therewith a radical reconstruction of the picture which human history gives us of the past and will also change the course of that history in the future.\"\n   ===Page Three===\n\n\n     And remember, \n       If you see a glorious member of the Kaisereich, yell\n\n   \"HEIL VALDORIA\"\n   \"HEIL THE KAISER\"\n   \"HEIL DECIMUS\"\n\n===Approved By===\n\nThe Reich Ministry of Public Enlightenment and Propoganda.\n\n-Goseph Joebbelstein.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser's Love", "High Dictator Frederick II", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n    The Kaisers Love\n\n\n\n\n    Approved by the\n    Ministry of Truth\n\n\n\n==================\nThe people of Al'Wakhrah slept soundly in their beds when the Ghouls attacked. The three Ghouls stood firm at the entrance to the city, looking for easy targets to consume. Larry Kringle, an Elven officer within the Reich Ministry of Truth, sounded the\nalarm. The Kaisereich answered. The good denizens of the Hallowvale Company answered the call, headed by the Qalasheen Champion of the Hallowvale and the Kaiser himself. The company created a line of Elves and Humans alike at the gate.\nThe three Ghouls would be no match for the Kaisers finest! The elite troops pulled out their aurum blades and laid waste to the evil creatures where they stood. They never even reached the steps to Al'Wakhrah. The Champion and the Grand Conservitor worked\ntogether to take one of the ghouls head clean off! The Kaiser himself slashed with no mercy, finally impaling an aurum dagger int he eye socket of one of the animated corpses. The last was slow, behind the other two. This nightmarish creations of Iblees\norigin were hacked down by an unknown citizen of the Kaisereich. The unknown solider of Good. The Kaiser, under instruction from a wandering Cleric, ordered the building of a fire to burn the bodies of the fetid Ghouls. The group rallies, all lending a\nhand to rid the world of the monstrosities. \n\nThe Kaiser had few words for the valiant group that night, but offered his humbles thanks to all those who helped secure the safety of the children inside the walls of Al'Wakhrah. His humility\nwas unexpected, and took the group by surprise. It was then that they realized, we as an Empire, as Vanderlorians, are stronger together than we are apart. The Humans and Elves worked hand in hand, under the grace of God, and were victorious.\nThe Kaisers strongest words were the quietest spoken. \n\n\n     HEIL VANDALORIA\n     HEIL ROVINKIN\n     HEIL DECIMUS\n     HEIL TRUTH", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Nerroth", "Azkel Frostbeard", "Kal'Nerroth\n-=-~-=-~-=-~-=~=-\nKal'Nerroth was build in the year of 1554, after the demolition of the old capital, Kal'Akash. When the war ended, and the treaty was signed with Oren, the dwarves found their city in shambles, showing scars of war.\nIn a spurr of the moment decision, Grand King Kardel Irongut decided to tear down the city, and expand it, allowing the Dwarves to have a larger city. After years of building, and a few deaths durring the build, Kal'Nerroth was complete. The new capital\nused parts of the mountain never used before, and expanding into lava rivers below. The city itself appealed more to all, with its beautiful carved out stone bridges, and glowing mushroom trees of sorts. Now, the dwarven community thrives with the\nnew city, bringing more light to the dwarves than ever.", ""),
