        StaticBook("Keep Walking", "Leyu", "Keep Walking: A Tale of Truth by Silion Luthias\nHail friend, I am Silion Luthias, and I'm going to tell you a story. This particular story, happens to be one of great importance to me me, for it is the story\nof me, and my brothers. We've all been scarred, vruised, and crushed by the harshness of reality but, we've also all come together under odd circumstances, and have become traveling companions, and friends to the\nend. As I sit underground in my study, I look towards the future, for it's bright, and full of promise, and untold stories filled with adventure and hope. But, to look towards the future, you must keep the past in sight, so, to learn of our current\nadventures, you must know our pasts. :: There are 5 of us, Caden, Guraim, Gruol, Qwert, and I, Sillion. Each of us have tragedy in our past, but it has turned us into better people. First, we shall start with Qwert, one of two Dwarves in our party. ::\nQwert was born in the Farlands, a place I've yet to see His mother died during childbirth, and his father died in a fire, trying to save Qwert. From there, he was raised by a wolf mother, and her cubs, so, he was illeterate when he came to us. From\nthere, he moved onwards the Oren, and eventually was brought into our party via Caden, and here he resides still. :: Next, is Gruol, our Orc friend. Gruol was raised in the LOrcish fashion, but joined the Orcish Guard as a adult. But, during a routine\nsweep of the lands, the unit Gruol was placed in encountered a group of bandits looking for food amongst a group of homes. During the battle, most were slaughtered but, one of the humans in his teens started running. Gruol's captain ordered\nhim to hunt the boy down, and kill him. But, Gruol refused. :: Gruol was reported to The Rex, and was discharged immediatley . GRuol was shamed by his people, family, and country. So, he set off into the wilds, looking redemption, and riches.\nHowever, I found him, befriended him, and he travels with us as the group powerhouse, and is still looking to return his honor everyday. :: Now, we move on to my dear friend, Caden. Caden was the second member to join our party, and is our swordman.\nBut, his past is the most horrendous of all of ours, and it's time I document it for the world to know. Caden was raised in the Cathaldus Family, one of the most prestigous famlilies in Laurelin. He was taught sword fighting, archery, and perfect\nEnglish to name a few of the many privelges he had in his childhood. :: But, when he was quite young, he family adopted a young Orc child, I'Shaak. Caden was raised with him, learning from I'Shaak brutish capabilities, Caden became a force to\nreckoned with on the battlefield. However, I'Shaak caught a illness in his teen years, and died. THis gave Caden a respect for orcs, adn a hole in his heart, that has been left unfilled for too long. Then, in his first years of adulthood, a hit was\nordered upon his family. Caden was away, training with his blade, when his family was murdered in cold blood in their sleep. When Caden returned that night, exhausted from practice, he found his parents corpses strewn with blood and bile sliced open in\nplaces along their throats, chest, and stomach. But, to their dismay, a hred of clothing adorned the bedpost, plastered with blood. But, the true color still showed, purple tinged along the edges with green. It was the flag of a local mercenary company,\nand only their captain wore the colors. Sillion marched to the local fort his blade sharpened to a razor edge, and nothing but primal fury, and the lust for revenge swarming amongst his consicous. He trudged in, busting open the doors,\nand listened to the sounds of men rowdily drinking, laughing, and reveling in a well earned payment, most likley a very large one. Caden walked into the Main dininig hall, and stood, ready to charge. He ran his eye across the\nrows of fighters, and then steadied his gaze upon the only man standing, the captain, adorned with a flowing shirt, with a ripped sleeve. Caden drew in a breath, and screamed, \"YOU TOOK MY FAMILIES LIVES, I REQUIRE YOUR IN PAYMENT! YOU PATHETIC\nBLEMISHES BARELY MAKE THE PAYMENT!\" Caden then pulled out a bottle of spirits, plugged with a hankerchief. He dipped the flailing hankerchief end into a torch, and hurled it onto the table, fire and glass flew around, men instantly went up in flames,\nsomefrom the initial explosion, some from the sparks touching their alcohol drenched garb. amonsgt the chaos, most fled, or perished, but, the captain stood eyelocked with Caden. The captain brandished a beautiful gilded\naxe, imbuded with diamonds. The pair began stalking towards one another, and the captain swung the massive chunk of metal towards Caden's throat, but he deftly sropped, and instantaneously drove his blade into the captains right\nstomach, ripped the blade left, and stepped back to let his guts splatter on the masonry. As his innards tasted air, he dropped to his knees and feebly tried to return his organs to their rightful place. He looked up to Caden, blood seeping\nthrough his teeth, and whispered, \"Your father died in his sleep, but your mother was awoke by our footfalls. She looked up at us in her nightgown, eyes full of fear, and she screamed. She squealed like a swine. I imagine the sound would be like music\nto you, dagger-ear.\" Caden stared at him with pure fury, then raised his blade, and dropped it through the captains spinal cord. His head rolled across the floor. and landed amongst the pile of burnt bodies. Caden walked back to Laurelin, drenched in\nblood, dragging his blade, and staring into the distance, eyes blank. AS he entered, he prepared for a heros embrace, but was gripped by guards right away. They then began dragging him through town, preparing to throw him into\nprison for the murder of a entire company of mercenaries. As the men brought him through a cluster of homes for the richer members of town, a politician whos face was lightly covered, looked to be chuckling lightly. Caden was jailed\nbut escaped after a small sentence. I found him in the wilds, crouching near a tree, holding a makeshift stabbing weapon. I coaxed him to me with a loaf of bread. Once I got him eating, he told me this story, and I vowed I would help him find the\nmonster who hired the hit upon his family, and so he stays with us now.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keep Walking", "Ebonsquire", "Keep Walking: A Tale of Truth\n\n((Originally scribed by Ohaythar121))\nHail friend, I am Silion Luthias, and I'm going to tell you a story. This particular story, happens to be one of great importance to me, for it is the story of me, and my brothers. We've all been scarred, bruised, and crushed by the harshness of reality,\nbut we've also all come together under odd circumstances, and have become travelling companions, and friends to the end. As I sit underground in my study, I look towards the future, for it's bright, and full of promise, and untold stories filled with\nadventure and hope. But, to look towards the past in sight, so to learn of our current adventures, you must know our pasts. \n\nThere are five of us, Caden, Guraim, Gruol, Qwert, and I, Sillion. Each of us have tragedy in our past, but it has turned us\ninto better people. First, we shall start with Qwert, one of the two Dwarves in our party. \n\nQwert was born in the Farlands, a place I've yet to see. His mother died during childbirth, and his father died in a fire, trying to save Qwert. From there, he\nwas raised by a wolf mother, and her cubs, so he was illiterate when he came to us. From there, he moved onwards to Oren, and eventually was brought into our party via Caden, and here he resides still. \n\nNext is Gruol, our Orc friend. Gruol was raised\nin the Orcish fashion, but joined the Orcish Guard as an adult. But, during the routine sweep of the lands, the unit Gruol was placed in encountered a group of bandits looking for food amongst a group of homes. During the battle, most were slaughtered,\nbut one of the humans in his teens started running. Gruol's captain ordered him to hunt the boy down, and kill him. But, Gruol refused. Gruol was reported to the Rex, and was discharged immediately. Gruol was shamed by his people, family, and country.\nSo, he set off into the wilds, looking for redemption, and riches. However, I found him, befriended him, and he travels with us as the group powerhouse, and is still looking to return his honor everyday. \n\nNow, we move on to my dear friend, Caden.\nCaden was the second member to join our party, and is our swordman. But, his past is the most horrendous of all of ours, and it's time I document it for the world to know. Caden was raised in the Cathaldus Family, one of the most prestigious families in\nLaureh'lin. He was taught sword fighting, archery, and perfect Common to name a few of the many privileges he had in his childhood.\n\nBut, when he was quite young, his family adopted a young Orc child, I'Shaak. Caden was raised with him,\nlearning from I'Shaak brutish capabilities. Caden became a force to be reckoned with on the battlefield. However, I'Shaak caught an illness in his teen years, and died. This gave Caden a respect for orcs, and a hole in his heart that has been left\nunfilled for too long. Then, in his first years of adulthood, a hit was ordered upon his family. Caden was away, training with his blade, when his family was murdered in cold blood in their sleep. When Caden returned that night, exhausted from practice,\nhe found his parents corpses strewn with blood and bile sliced open in places along their throats, chest, stomach. But, to their dismay, a thread of clothing adorned the bedpost, plastered with blood. But, the true color still showed. Purple tinged along\nedges with green. It was the flag of the local mercenary company, and only their captain wore the colors. Caden marched to the local fort, his blade sharpened to a razor edge, and nothing but primal fury, and the lust for revenge swarming amongst his\nconscience. He trudged in, busting open the doors, and listened to the sounds of men rowdily drinking, laughing, and revelling in a well earned payment, most likely a large one. Caden walked into the main dining hall and stood, ready to charge. He ran his\neyes across the rows of fighters, and then steadied his gaze upon the only man standing, the captain, adorned with a flowing shirt, with a ripped sleeve. Caden drew in a breath and screamed, \"YOU TOOK MY FAMILY'S LIVES, I REQUIRE YOURS IN PAYMENT! YOU\nPATHETIC BLEMISHES BARELY MAKE THE PAYMENT!\" Caden then pulled out a bottle of spirits, plugged with a handkerchief. He dipped the flailing handkerchief end into a torch and hurled it onto the table. Fire and glass flew around, men instantly went up from\nthe initial explosion, some from the sparks touching their alcohol drenched garb. Amongst the chaos, most fled, or perished, but the captaid stood eyelocked with Caden. The captain brandished a beautiful gilded axe, imbued with diamonds. The pair began\nstalking towards one another, and the captain swung the massive chunk of metal towards Caden's throat, but he deftly stopped and instantaneously drove his blade into the right of the captain's stomach, ripped the blade left, and stepped back to\nlet his guts splatter on the masonry. As his innards tasted air, he dropped to his knees and feebly tried to return his organs to their rightful place. He looked up to Caden, blood seeping through his teeth, and whispered, \"Your father died in your sleep,\nbut your mother was awoke by our footfalls. She looked up at us in her nightgown, eyes full of fear, and she screamed. She squealed like a swine. I imagine the sound would be like to music to you, dagger-ear.\" Caden stared at him with pure fury, then\nraised his blade, and dropped it through the captain's spinal cord. His head rolled across the floor and landed amongst a pile of burnt bodies. Caden walked back to Laureh'lin, drenched in blood, dragging his blade, and staring into the distance, eyes\nblank. As he entered, he prepared for a hero's embrace, but was gripped by the guards right away. They then began dragging him through town, preparing to throw him into prison for the murder of an entire company of mercenaries. As the men brought him\nthrough a cluster of homes for the richer members of town, a politician whose face was lightly covered, looked to be chuckling lightly. Caden was jailed but escaped after a small sentence. I found him in the willds, crouching near a tree, holding a\nmakeshift stabbing weapon. I coaxed him to me with a loaf of bread. Once I got him eating, he told me his story, and I vowed I would help him find the monster who hired the hit upon his family, and so he stays with us now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keys", "Murdervish", "Call into rains of the cloudless,\nAim towards aches of the lye,\nEast is the face of the faithless,\nSand and the snows do collide.\nAsh had feln down upon our heads,\nReds have been the skies,\nSaffron of silks had tied to us,\nHills had all crumbled to cries.\nInvert the face of the faithless,\nFall into sands by the snows,\nTrek into deserts most dangerous,\n ((The last line of the poem is blacked out.))\nClo Abfkxiq, tel qxrdeq jb ql yb xyib ql obxa.\nClo Kxccld, tel qxrdeq jb ql yb xyib ql qefkh.\nClo Flxkkfp, tel qxrdeq jb ql yb xyib ql pjfib.\n2-9-18-4\n3-1-12-12\n0-4-0-6\n12-1-20-0\n19-5-22-5\n14-0-20-23\n15-0-6-9\n22-5-0-19\n5-3-15-14\n4-0-9-14\n20-5-18-22\n1-12-19-0\n12-9-22-9\n14-7-0-19\n8-18-5-23", ""),
        StaticBook("Khalestine Laws", "Bahadir Timuroğul al-Yelbegkhai", "The Establishment\n       of Law\n  İstikrar ve Güvenlik\n\n  الاستقرار والأمنالاستقرار والأمن\n\n      First Edition\n     \n\n\n\nPublished the Sixth of   Snow's Maiden in the\n       year 1521\nThroughout time have the Qalasheen and their kin learned to live civil and respectful even during their darkest hours. In order to preserve the mutual understanding that only through law and order harmony can truly be achieved, the\nCaliph and his respective subordinates have established the boundaries between civil and savage, good and criminal, divine and dark with spiritual guidance and wisdom.\n\n===================\nThe Yalasar Laws\n===================It is not fitting for an individual, man or woman, believer or non believer, to undermine or disobey the laws set by Allah and his respective servants.  For one who does, is indeed on a clearly wrong path.\nThe first Yalasar Law:\n\n\n  The blessing of life received by the righteous Allah may not be taken from anyone, no matter the kin, belief or gender.\nThe second Yalasar Law:\n\n  The many riches of this world belong to those that earned them. The ones that walk a path of thievery will walk a path towards exile.\nThe third Yalasar Law:\n\n\n  Those that not share the mutual enlightenment of Allah’s followers should be tolerated and treated as an equal, for they cannot help being born outside our sacred lands.\n===================\n\nThese three laws will be the bulwark of the civility within the Caliphate, for they are set in stone by the only supreme authority that reigns above all, Allah.\n\n===================\nThe Bayezid Laws\n================\n\n  In a world full of temptations and delusions, the individual must remain on the divine path set before him. In order for that to be possible, a strong understanding of the true meaning of sacrifice and\nnecessity must be present.\nThe first Bayezid Law:\n\n\n  The enlightened individual of the Caliphate shall not lie, unless the truth would harm the innocent or empower the corrupt.\nThe second Bayezid Law:\n\n  The Caliph is the true messenger of Allah and shall not be undermined as the Caliphate’s leader as long as he remains on the path of Allah.\nThe third Bayezid Law:\n\n\n  Malicious planning, execution or intent are to be blocked out of the minds of those that enter the Caliphate, for those undermine the individual’s divine bond with Allah.\nThe fourth Bayezid Law:\n\n  Power shall have no worth in the eyes of Allah, only through merit and good intent may one truly be elevated or pardoned.\nThe fifth Bayezid Law:\n\n  \n  Corrupting the name of Allah and his legitimacy will be strictly forbidden within and outside the Caliphate. As we respect you, we demand respect in return.\nThe sixth Bayezid Law:\n\n\n  Any individual breaking these laws in the eyes of other kin or relatives shall lose its representation by the Caliphate, for it does not follow the true path it is required to.\nThe Mercan Laws\n================\n\n  For there are many corrupted in these lands that would lurk upon the riches and people of the Caliphate out of jealousy or envy, it is essential that those that follow Allah and seek shelter in our sacred land must\nbe protected and prepared for all that evil can bring.\nThe first Mercan Law:\n\n\n  When an individual or a collective clearly seeks to undermine the first Yalasar law, Allah shall grant permission to defend and potentially harm the underminers.  Only when it is a question of life and death may\nthe enlightened individual exceed its mortal boundary.\nThe second Mercan Law:\n\n  Every being within the Caliphate, citizen or visitor, has the divine responsibility to defend the sacred land from anyone that aspires for its destruction.\nThe third Mercan Law:\n\n \n  Only the Caliph is enlightened enough to appoint his successor, for he represents Allah’s will.\nThe fourth Mercan Law:\n\n  Ones that carry harmful goods within the Caliphate must seal them and carry them out of sight accordingly. Only those tasked with protecting the Caliphate may publicly show their tools of killing as a sign of authority.\nThe Kismet Laws\n================\n\n  In order to preserve the functionality of the social stature in the Qalasheen society, laws must be established as an act of mutual understanding of what restrictions and liberties are for the best.\nOnly through civil interaction can those with a good heart not be swayed to corruption and dark temptations.\nThe first Kismet Law:\n\n\n  All must be treated with equal respect and consideration within the Caliphate with the exception of increased respect given to those blessed by the Caliph’s grace.\nThe second Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Those that have no wealth due to misfortune should be treated and aided if possible.\nThe third Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Those of male gender shall not seek physical or unnecessary social contact with females after a marriage for adultery is forbidden.\nThe fourth Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Those who aim to speak their words in a public setting shall refrain from insulting or undermining the Caliph or his chosen brothers in administration in said public setting.\nThe fifth Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Those who are found to commit the sin of adultery in any shape or form shall be sentenced at the discretion officer in question to the point of public humiliation and no further.\nThe sixth Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Those who are found to criticise the government without express permission of said government will be given to the hands of the guards in order to execute a capital punishment.\nThe seventh Kismet Law:\n\n  Those who have chosen to willing take the life of another without just cause shall have their life taken from them in a fashion befitting the crime itself.\nThe eigth Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Any citizen who has for whatever reason evaded the payment of taxes due shall have their taxes doubled at the instant of sentencing. Criminals guilty of such are allowed to pay off in full at that moment.\nIf they continue to refuse actively they shall have all of which they own reclaimed by the state and imprisoned before exile.\nThe ninth Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Bribery is the most sincere form of deviation from the lawful will of the state and by extension Allah and shall be punished by being forced to pay the previously mentioned bribe twice over to the government in\naddition to the punishment for the crime the bribe was meant to cover.\nThe tenth Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Who who helps a murderer is by extension holding the blade himself and shall be treated to the same punishment as those who are found red handed and without mercy.\nThe eleventh Kismet Law:\n\n  Assaulting another of Allah’s children shall be met with a punishment appropriate to the severity of the crime itself.\nThe twelfth Kismet Law:\n\n\n  Assaulting a citizen with obvious deadly intent or with the possession of a weapon during the assault will find themselves sentenced with capital punishment and then exile with duration set by the\npresiding officer at the scene. Any citizen assigned exile with duration is still required to pay all according taxes and dues as the state mandates.", ""),
        StaticBook("Killin' a troll", "Jentos", "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n     Killin' a troll\n\n\n  By Jentos Adam, last representant of the house of Blackwood.\n\n\n\n\n\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\"Dear reader, in this book you shall learn to: recognize, flee and kill a troll.\"\n\nIntroduction\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\"Troll. Nasty, cruel and stupid creatures capable of destroying whole towns, And fierce war-beasts.\"\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\nWere to find a troll?\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\nTroll's can be found about everywhere in these wild lands. From the frozen dwarven plains. To the heat of the Caliphate!\"\n\n\"Troll's like to live in unforested mountainous regions, dark caves in the\nmountains. Or in a big clearing in the forest.\"\n\nRecognizing a troll\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxWho has never pictured a troll? Big ugly figure walking in the forest? But the're are alot of different types of orcs and sub-trolls like half trolls half\nmen!\"\n\n\"Trolls can vary from 8 feet when young to a giant 20 feet tall!\nThey have a relative big orc like head with a few men-like features.\"\n\n\nFleeing a troll\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxRunning away from a\ntroll in a rather forested area is easier than in a mountainous or flat region.\"\n\nTactic's: \n\"If you find yourself in a forested or near a forested region, your best bet is to simply go we're the tree's are smaller so you can slow the troll\nand get out of its reach.\"\n\n\"Hiding in a cave isn't a good idea, a hungry troll is apt to wait a long time to be able to get his supper (especially if it's the trolls own cave!).\"\nKillin' a troll!\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"In this final section, you will learn how to \n\n       Slay\n      -----\nThese mighty creatures!.\n\"The troll's weak spot, (like many other beats) are the eye!\nUnfortunatly it is easy to see that being able to get a good shot at them isn't easy.\"\n\n\"The trick is to, hack the legs until it falls, wait t'ill it reaches down or bend or simply attack it\nfrom a good height!\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"On this. I say to you! Have thy luck I never had!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Killing Yourself", "Archembalt", "Effective Ways of \nCommitting Suicide\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n     Perhaps you have taken this tome because you are generally a curious individual, or maybe you've considered that life is not worth living. If the latter is your case, I am\n-terribly sorry that not everything has been too satisfactory throughout your period of existence. \n\n   Nonetheless, everyone reserves the right to end their lives. I am here now to convey effective methods with which one could swiftly end\n-their life.\n\nSections\n=+------<>-------+=\n\nI. The Natural Way\n\nII. Poisons and Potions\n\nIII. Death, Accompanied with Solace\nThe Natural Way\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n1. Jumping off a cliff. Make sure that you are not falling into a sea. It is only more painful. Ensure that the surface is hard, or that there are stone crags at the bottom. Death will surely occur.\n2. Poisonous mushrooms. Eat an abundance. Fever, convulsing, vomiting, then succinct death. The more you take, the quicker you will reach the end. Find a mushroom with a white stalk, red head, and with white spots on its surface.\n3. Drowning. Tie a heavy rock to your feet and hop into a pool, river, ocean, et cetera. There is no escape. The struggle won't last too long. There will be a burning sensation, and shock will begin to take place. Not as swift, but effective enough.\n4. Have someone twist your head about and snap your neck. Ensure your friend/assailant is strong. Pay them some money to kill you. Tell them to make it quick. A quick severing of the spine should bring you to death in no time.\n5. Beheading. Get a trusted friend or hire someone with minas. Their blade should be sharpened, their grip confident, and they must be considerably strong. One swipe will separate your head from your body, if everything has been planned out well.\n6. Hanging. Slightly more painful, but depends on the height from which you jump. Tie a noose around your neck and then to a tree branch. Stand on the tree branch, and make sure that you are an apt height from the ground. Jump. The noose should constrict-\n-around your neck finely and perhaps crush your larynx in no time, cutting off your access to a considerable supply of air. In some cases, your spine will snap. This method is more well-known.\n7. Arbalest bolt to the temple. Acquire someone strong and able to properly load the heavy war bow known as an arbalest. The piercing power of this brutal weapon will easily end your life. Instruct them to point it at your temple (side of  your head) and-\n-stand around two meters away from you when firing. Almost as quick as beheading.\n8. Explosion. Perhaps a tad harder to set up. A stick of dynamite will do, maybe two. Strap it to your upper chest, preferably to the sternum. You may make the fuse as short as you wish. Execute this out in a field, or perhaps run into a room of -\n- individuals you absolutely despise, and light the fuse. A last 'hurrah' before you pass on. Death by explosion is nearly instant. Dynamite is also not too hard to get your hands on.\n9. Exsanguination. Slitting your forearm. Acquire a knife or something especially sharp. Draw the blade up the inside of your forearm all the way to your wristline. The cut does not have to be too deep. Ensure the severing of multiple veins. The result\n-will be extreme loss of blood. Your heart will slow and your mind will be deprived of necessary fluids. Death is soon to occur.\n10. Thanhium dust. Thanhium, surprisingly, is not too hard to get a hold of. In order to execute this suicide method properly, procure a decent-sized chunk of thanhium. Begin to break it down in order to release the toxic dust. Begin to inhale, and do -\n- not stop. You will begin to feel cold, and more than likely break into a sweat. The toxic dust will become overbearing and your mind will soon 'shut off'.\nPoisons and Potions\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n1. Overdose on sleeping potions. If one could request an abundance of sleeping potions, this method of suicide would be painless and peaceful. You would quickly fall into a deep sleep, -\n- but never to awake.\n2. Nether's Wrath. An incredibly harmful potion, scalding hot and incredibly bright. Pour into the eyes. Painful at first, but the concoction will sear through the flesh of your eyes and promptly penetrate to strike at your brain, frying it to a crisp, w-\n- ith this method only taking less than ten seconds once the potion is acquired.\n3. Greater Drake's Poison. Overdose on this, and you will overheat in no time. Your lips will become parched, your stomach aflame, and soon your mind will not be able to register much. Death is guaranteed with this.\n4. Blissfoil. Consume an abundance of this flower, or drink the potion. You will gradually lose the ability to properly move your arms or leg as you eat them, until your entire body is paralyzed. At this point, your brain cannot register\n-any pain or sensation, and once this point has been reached, you will die.\n5. Alchemist's Fire. It will melt the flesh off of your bone. Ask someone to throw it upon you and aim for the head or upper torso. More effective than regularly setting yourself on fire.\n6. Frost Oil. Primarily used as a coolant for clothing, it may also be applied to weapons. Drink it instead. Overdose will work in a similar way to blissfoil. Your body will be overcome with the cold, and your mind too will freeze. Death is guaranteed.\n7. Basilisk venom. When extracted and taken in large amounts, will cause swift death. Straightforward. This method can be applied with a wide array of venomous snakes and beasts.\nDeath, Accompanied by Solace\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n     It is up to the one committing suicide to determine whether or not they wish to settle personal qualms with other individuals, or if they do not wish for their ending to be peaceful.\nTheir reasons are their own. \n\n    Take some time to truly reflect on your life, the decisions you have taken, and consider if everything has been truly settled. If reflecting back on your life has become too painful, then do not feel the need to such.\nIf one would prefer an even more peaceful ending, however, a prime way of committing suicide would be by enjoying whatever you can before you take your life. Have a drink, eat whatever food you'd like, or take a nice nap. Maybe poison your drink so -\n- the pain will be alleviated even further. \n\n    There are a multitude of ways in which one may kill themselves, and this tome only details a few of those. Thank you for reading, and I hope you find this information useful.\n-Written by Archibald Vallero (alias: Archembalt)\n\n           -1546", ""),
        StaticBook("Knoxxy Adventure", "Elder Eath'lur", "The adventures of Knoxxy, son of Knox.\n\nVolume I\n\nWhen Knox created the world in seven days, he created a son, made of pumpkin and courage.\n\nHis name was Knoxxy.\nBut Knoxxy din't knew\nthe purpouse of his life, so he searched for awansewers.\n\nKnoxxy din't knew much of the outer world; shield carried on his back, sword laying on his belt, heart of pumpkin, face of a king, bornt to be the pumpkin king.\nFirstly, Knoxxy went to the capital of the humans, Oren, there, Knoxxy killed an blacksmith and stole a sword and a shield, both equal in power.\n\nDon't ask me how Knoxxy killed the blacksmith. Knox will be angry, i swear.\nWith an thunderous step, the mighty creation of Knox left the forge, everyone staring at his incredible pumpkiness, some people had their minds filled of making a pumpkin stew out of the pumpkin on Knoxxy head, so Knox made pumpkins rain on their heads.\nAfter Knoxxy saw the signal of his father, he had, for once, discovered his true purpouse on the universe.\n\nThe pumpsgiving is a signal of pleading and love-sharing, if Knoxxy wanted to rule the world, he first had to give others\npumpkins, so he left on a journey, where he stood at the gates of Haelun'or.\n\n-Let me in.-\nKnoxxy roared mightly and powerfully, a roar that shaked all the Athera, creating the mightiest earthquake possible.\nThe guard, fearing the worst, opened the gates for Knoxxy.\n\nKnoxxy steped in and raised his arms, and so, his father heard his plead and made pumpkins rain on the elven city, killing the common leaf tea.\n\nRivers of pumpkiness\nbegan to flow across the large city, the walls breaching to let the pumpkin blessing get inside, they where in absolute passion with it.\n\n-Father! - Said Knoxxy. - I'll make everyone bow down at your will! The world shall tremble before you!\nAs the pumpkins filled the city, Knoxxy left it, setting himself to the elves capital. The gates where open, as he walked up to the king or whatever is it, don't question Knox will, and said for him to replant all crops with pumpkins.\nThe king refused.\n\nThen, Knoxxy threw out from the majestic and marvelous realm of beauty Knoxxária, a pumpkin towards the king head, wich enlighted him, so he ordered that pumpkins would be planted everywhere, and all the food would be\npumpkin for him and all the next kings.\n\nThen, Knoxxy moved to the capital of dwarves, the stone shaking and fearing his might as he'd step in, his pumpkin would remember the roar of the mightiest steed of Knox, Lord of Pumpkins: The mightiest\ndragon made of pumpkins.\n\nTwo dwarfs rushed towards Knoxxy, but he raised his fists and pulled both back, an army would be formed to try to stand against the might of Knox.\nKnoxxy rushed towards the 4 million dwarves alone, as he'd jump into the air and make pumpkins rain over their heads by pleading to his father, the dwarves would be then enlighted and bow down to Knoxxy as he'd fall over a bowed dwarf's back.\n-Soldiers! - Knoxxy, now King Knoxxy, Pumpkin of Knox would shout. -Enlight all of your family with my word, Knox will soon take over the word, and those whom are enlighted, shall live in a perfect world, filled with pumpkins and pumpkins!\nAll the dwarves would peasantly praise Knox, \nWe will conquest the world with all the pumpkins!\n\n§ knoxy would approach cykacykacykacykacykaWOWOWOWOWOWOWOskdoakoskdoakovjkdklskdoioqiosdkojdodljlcjljosdjdowjodjowklskdlkdlskl\nKnoxxy would chant.\n\nA portal would appear to another dimension, pumpkins would flow out of it, pumpkins of the greatest quality, as Knox would step down. The bindings with reality and fiction ripping appart, as the Mighty, Powerful, Majestic, Lord, King,\nSlayer of Titans, Slayer of Giants, Saviour of Cities,\nDestroyer of Worlds,\nBuilder of Pumpkins,\nCream Slicer,\nPumpkin Pie Best Seller\nFan of Rap'lur\nBest Pumpkin Cook,\nBoat Sinker\nExuberant, Magnificient, Beautiful His Lord Pumpkiness, Knox §\nwould start walking amongst the mortals, the world trembling before his magnificency, as he'd go to mount on his pumpkin dragon along with Knoxxy.\n~-_-~-_-~-_-~-_-~\n\"Son, you did a great job, u mak mi prowd.\"\n~<)(>~<)(>~<)(>~pumpkin\nI'd love spending my time writing about all his majesty with all the pleasure of this world, but His Pumpkiness, Lord Knox and his son Lord Knoxxy, son of His Pumpkiness, Lord Knox have an army to lead.\n\nQuestion Knox and you will be pumpkinized.\nAnd so, His Pumpkiness Lord Knox, Lord Knoxxy and the army of dwarven pumpkin warrior farmer peasants marched towards the floating city of the cats.\n\nThe dwarves began to stumble on eachother, making a bridge towards the floating\nisland filled with weird walking flying floating jealous cats.\n\nKnox obviously made pumpkins rain on the first step he took in the cat city.\n\nThe cats got together to praise Knox and destroy the altars of their fake gods, so\nthey could completely embrace the Knoxism.\n\nKnox then went to all other cities, pumpkinizing everything, until the creator came back from life and split the world in two, the one with our true reality, where Lord Knox created the world,\n[!]Drool covers the page.\nand a fake reality, where I currently live. \nKnox descended to this place aswell, to help his lost devout followers like me.\n\nI'm going to take a billion of people and sacrifice them to His Pumpkiness, Knox, children or women, soldier or dwarven\npeasant, fisher or miner. Everyone must be sacrificied to plead my pumpkiness and return to my true reality, the place i bornt and lived into, I must go back, to live under the false reality of that creator bullshit is bullshit, His Pumpkiness is all that\nI love, everyone else that isn't a devout follower of His Pumpkiness must die, if they don't die they will suffer under my hands until they are converteds, I wish to do what Knoxxy did, led armies of billions of pumpkins to pump off the world, flow rivers\nof pumpkins. I will kill anything that doesn't pleads His Pumpkiness, he's my life, he's what remains.\n\nALL\n\nPRAISE\n\nLORD\n\nKNOX\n[!] A bizarre symbol made of blood lays down in the paper, followed by large writings, made of the pencil bathed in blood\n\nSEE I'M THE CHOSEN ONE, MY BLOOD SMELLS LIKE KNOXXY, LORD OF  PUMPKINS, SON OF HIS PUMPKINESS KNOX, LORD OF PUMPKINS, I WANT\nMORE SACRIFICE, THE PUMPKIN GOD NEEDS MORE SACRIFICES\n\nPLUNDER THEIR SOULS\nSTEAL THEIR FARMS\nSABOTAGE THEM\n\nPUMPKIN\n\nPUWPKIN\n\nI MUST BE PUNISHED\nFOR WRITING PUMPKIN WRO---\n\n[!] A large pool of blood lays by this page, making it completely unreadable\n\nKNOX IS MY KI------\nKNOX IS THE FUTU---\nKNOX IS THE LIF-)**E\n\nWE MUST ESCAPE\nWE MUST ALL ESCAPE\n\nTO THE TRUE REALITY\n\nWHERE KNOX\n\nIS OUR LORD AND GOD\n\nLIKE HE IS\n[!] The page has some sort of weird writings\n\nZTRUGANOK, VRAK\nWASTAGANOK, WRAK\nZTTRAGOFF, TRAK\nGRUNDAGOND, ARAK\nDAEMUN, ZTROAK\n§.§,AEGUL, BRAK\nDROGANNON, FRAK\nZLURKAADROG, TRUK\nGRAZDAET, DREATH\nMY SOUL\n\nMY BLOOD\n\nMY PUMPKINS\n\nMY BODY\n\nMY APPLE PIE\n\nMY CHERRY\n\nEVERYTHING FOR HIS\nPUMPKINESS, KNOX\n\nKNOX\n             KNOX\n        KNOX\n\n                     KNOX\n   KNOX\n              KNOX\nKNOX              KNOX\n\n          KNOX\n                      KNOX\nIF THERE WASN'T KNOX, THERE WOULD BE NO FUTURE\n\nIF THERE WASN'T KNOX, THERE WOULD BE NO PUMPKINS\n\nIF THERE WASN'T KNOX, THERE WOULD BE NO LIFE\n\nTHE FUTURE OF THE\nNATION IS KNOX, YOU PRAISE KNOX OR DIE\n\nI USED SOME OF THE BLOOD OF THE DEATH TO SHOW AWE TO MY LORD, CONSIDER THIS AN EXTRA TRIBUTE\n\n[!] A large splat of blood lays on the paper's bottom\nISN'T THAT ENOUGH?\n\n[!]More blood lays on the paper, but this time, it looks like it has been shaped and somehow coagulated, forming a pumpkin\n\nI HAVE ALL THE TIME AND ALL THE BLOOD OF THE WORLD FOR YOU, MY LORD KNOX\nAND I WILL SPILL\n\n[!] A blood stream rests here\n\nSPILL\n\n[!] Another blood stream covers the paper\n\nAND SPILL!\n[!] Spouted blood.\nTHERE GOES ANOTHER WOMAN, I'M GOING FOR THE THIRD ONE, BE PLEADED, HIS PUMPKINESS KNOX, LOOK AT HER FACE\n\n[!]You can notice tear drops over the paper\n\nI SHOW IT THROUGH YOUR PORTAL, THE PORTAL TO REALITY,\nDO YOU KNOW WHAT HAPPENS IN THE VOLUME 2? KNOXXY DIES, AS THERE CAN BE ONLY ONE KNOX, OH MY LORD, I HEARD YOU ASKED FOR MORE!\n\n[!] Blood seens to be all around the paper, as the mark of a face smashed in the paper is clear as sunlight\nISN'T THAT ENOUGH? ISN'T THAT ENOUGH?!?!\n\nI STILL HAVE MORE, MY LORD, AND I'LL KEEP TAKING\n\nTAKING\n\nTAKE\nTAKE\nTAKE\nTAKE\nTAKE MORE\nSHED BLOOD\n    YOUR NAME\n        LORD KNOX\nYOU'RE OUR RULER\nNOTHING WILL STOP US\n\nI'LL KILL AGAIN FOR YOU\n\n§[[!]A thin pool of dry blood lays in the paper\nI HEAR YOU ASKING FOR MORE\n\nI'LL GIVE YOU MORE\n\nAND MORE\n\nAND MORE\n\nAND MORE\n\nAND MORE\nAND MORE\n[!] A ritualistic symbol lays by the paper\n\nTHIS IS THE PROOF I'LL BE BACK ON OUR REALITY, I WILL RETURN, I'LL FEED FLESH TO THIS BOOK\n\nI WANT MORE BLOOD FOR MY KNOX GOD\n\nBLOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOD\n[!] All the remaining of the book are unreadable sketches and childish drawings, as you open the page, a few pieces of flesh would fall down.\n\nThe last thing you can read is\n\n         I'LL GET\n      MOREEEEEEEE...\nMORE\nSACRIFICES\n\nLORD KNOX\n\nNEEDS MOREEEEEEEEEEEEE SACRIFICES\n\n\nMOREEEEE\nHAHAHAHAHAHHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHHAHAAHAHA\nAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssssswwww§\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\nwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", ""),
        StaticBook("Knwldge and Exp.", "Farley III Stafyr", "Knowledge and Experience – Elaborated\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr\nUpon a recent interesting discussion about knowledge with an elf, I considered onto writing down, what the difference between knowledge and the often related experience is.\nTo note at this place, there are enough people who assume that knowledge and experience are the same, although this is a wrong statement, as experience and knowledge are different. To point this out, an example is required.\nFire. Fire burns and hurts, consumes burnable things such as wood and coal.\n\nNow let’s assume you learned about fire and its properties out of a book. You studied the texts. This merely is knowledge, theoretical knowing\nor to put it in different terms, theoretical experience about something, respectively fire in this example.\n\nOn the other hand, if you never read a book about fire and get burned heavily or see it burning in\nfront of you, consuming something, you learn from it directly. This is experience, practical knowledge. The difference should be clearly visible by now.\nNow we have to elaborate the relation between these two elements of wisdom, mental capabilities, sense. The origin of knowledge is clearly, through the experiment and therefore through experience.\nKnowledge is an unpractical independent manifestation of experience, written down into books, teached through them or teached through a teacher, master. That was knowledge is, to know, but not to know.\nExperience itself may not always be referred as knowledge in this case, because knowledge can go deeper than experience, although knowledge origins from it. Knowledge itself my inclue to know about the progress and\nprocess behind the visible, such as the burning of fire.\n\nStill, it must be said, that experience can create knowledge under circumstances, experience can also increase knowledge. Experience can support and enrich\nknowledge. The relation between these two elements is vastly huge and not to be underestimated. \n\nIt is best to acquire both of them to roughly equal terms in cases, helping you on your way through the life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kreyzchurz Vol 1", "TapeSauce", "DIZKLEYMUR- WHUEBR EZ REEDIN DIZ MUZT NOH DAT DIZ BUUK EZ UHBOWT DA VERYUZ FURMZ AGH TIPEZ UB KREYZCHURZ AGH REYZEZ. RULG FUR REEDIN DIZ BUUK. UHZLO, MI ROTE UHLUT UB ET EN UH ZCHEWER.\nZcheptur Un: Da Snaak. \nSnaakz ahr wyrd. Dey ez zmull. Lat kan throogh dem et wulz. Bud, dyr ez moar tu dem dan juzt myootulazchun. En diz zcheptur, lat wil lurn ub da moar zchufiztukeytd lyfztylz ub Snaakz. Dey hev uh kumplux\nkulzchur dat lat wudnt ekzpekd. Furzt, et ternz owt dat Snaakz dunt liv en hollz. Wull, dey kynd ub du, bud dyr kuld berrohz. Deyz berrohz ahr akzchuii kwyt nyz agh dekureytd. Diz ez ub kurz ef lat kan eben fet en et. Udder dan flattin, Snaakz ahr yoozful\nfur treyding, ez Mi mit menii Snaak treydurz en dah rodz. Deyr yoozchulii vurry niiz kreyzchurz, bud deyr zo zmul dat wi lyk tu meyk fun ub dem wenebur wi peep dem. Uhlzo, Snaakz meyk fur guud berdendurz, dat ez, ef dey kan eben riizch da kowntur, ryt?\nZcheptur Tuu: Da Gharat\n\nPribiiuzly, wi lurnd uhbowt da Snaakz, smul, ugli, agh wiik kreyzchurz. Tu undurztahnd uh Gharat, ez tu undurztahnd elkohol. Lat peep, deyz Gharatz fil dyr holz wit byr, lutz agh lutz ub byr.\nDey ez uh marii reyze, muzch zo lyk da Snaakz. Dey ez uhlzo zchord lyk da Snaakz. Unlyk da Snaakz doh, Gharatz ahr phaddah, agh dey lyk tu klomp uhlmozt ez muzch ez wi Bruddahz du. Uhlmozt. Tu bii onizt, dyr ez muzch tu edmyr bowt deyze kreyzchurz. Dey ez\nuh bryd ub woryurrz Ub koarz, da Gharat kant bii kumpayrd tu da ztrengf ub uh Bruddah, bud dey ziim tu be ztrungr dan eben dah bigizt Shara. Muzch lyk uz Bruddahz, Gharatz hold dyr onurr tu uh hyooj ekztent. Bote Bruddahz agh Gharatz lyk tu yooz luskz\nagh hemmurz. Tu bii onuzt, Gharatz ahr lyk tinee, uglii, zchmellii, dum Urukz en uh wai. Mi tink dat wii zchud ztil flat dem, bud, wi niid tu uhprezchyate wai deyr zo fun tu flat agh klomp. Noaw, wyr gunna zchift gyrz hyr, agh zwhizch tu uh tullur reyze.\nZcheptur Frii: Da Albaiz\n\nDiz reyze ez un ub uh dizgreyzful zenz ub onur. Da Albaiz tink deyr beddah dan uz. Mi miin, zo du dah Snaakz agh Gharatz agh udder ztuf, but dah Albaiz ziim tu heyt uz eben moar. Deyr uh gruup ub kreyzchurz dat tink deyr zo\nbootyful agh zmurt. Bud, Mi fiil dat en zum waiz, dey ekzchulli ahr zmurt. Lat peep, dey mai bi finur, zchmelliur, agh dumr dan uz, bud Mi tink dat dey en zum wai, diip enzyd, dat Albaiz hev zum digry ub endulijinz. Purhepz Albaiz kant meyk guud wepenz ur\nurmr, ur eben guud biltingz. Bud, Albaiz ziim tu grezp da mojo vurri wil. Noaw, wi gunna dyv entoo dah zchpezifek tipz ub Albaiz.\nZcheptur Foar: Da Hy Albaiz \n\nEt ez dah Hy Albai dat zukz dah mozt, en Mi upynyon. Dyr dah unz dat RILLI tink hy uhbowt demzelthz. Kunziduriin etz en deyr nymz agh ztuf. Deyz unz liiv lung, luuk tull, ahr zupr pail, dring dah teez, eet dah\nkeykz, riid dah novullz, mok dah uddah reyzez, du deyr fenzii mojo, wayzt tym en meykin ztuf pritii, (Eben dah webenz) agh teyk dyr bafz, klyn dyr klofz agh eyrz, agh..... detz prittii muzch et. Beyzikulli, dey zuk.\nZcheptur Fyv: Da Wuud Albai\n\nNeztii lidl trii hugrz, datz wub deyze Wuud Albaiz ez. Belib et ur nub, Wuud Albaiz dunt eben yooz zwordz, luskz, ur eben toylit peypr. Dey yooz bohz. Agh fur toylit peypr, Mi tink dey yooz leyvz. Uhlzo, Trii Albaiz ahr\nmuzch lyk twigz. Datz wai anuddah nym fur Albai iz Twiggeh. Deyz Wuud Twiggehz iz uh bunzch ub panzchyz. Dey hyd en dah zchadohz tu hund fur deyr prai. Bud, uz Urukz hund fur owr prai en dah opun, kynda. Uhdoh, Wuud Twiggehz ahr guud et zneekin uhrownd.\nMi heb nub ztudyd dah Wuud Twiggehz muzch, bicuz dey ez yoozchuahlii hydin frum Mi. Zo, deyr ez ztill muzch tu leern uhbowt dem. Noaw, wi gunna teyk uh peep et dah grai unz.\nZcheptur Zekz: Da Durk Albaiz\n\nDeyz Twiggehz peep lyk da nyttyme zkyz demzelfz. Dey ez pritti muzch grai agh kynda bluu. Dey ahr pritti moduzt, peepin ez dat deyr Albaiz. Dey ziim lyk da muzt humbull ub da Twiggehz. Juzt lyk deyr mizteeriuhz\nuhpyrunz, nub muzch hez biin reykordid ub dah Durk Albaiz. Meybi deyr ez, bud dey nub zchard et wit Mi. Zo, Mi juzt gunna blah lat uhbowt deyr fizchikul uhpyrunz, rathurr dan deyr riil kulzchur. Dey haz durk zkin, durk eyz, bud dey yoozchulii drezz wit\npritti buld kulurz. Ulzo, Mi meynli nohtizd peerzingz agh grai harez. Zo, Mi dun blahin uhbowt dah Twiggehz, cuz dey ez pritti leym. Zo, noaw, wi gunna zchifd geerz uhgen agh lurn uhbowt dah sharaz.\nZcheptur Zebin: Da Sharaz ub Da Nurth\n\nGriidi, zchmellii, diplohmektik, tinee, uglii, wiik, dum, agh rilli dum. Lat knoh wub wyr blah uhbowt. Da Zharaz. Bud, deyz ahr dah Zharaz en da Nurth. Mi gethurrd diz enfurmeyzchun en dah zitii ub Ubrezchi.\nDey ahr uh kumplukeytd reyze, zo Mi gunna breyk diz op ento deberint katuhgoryz. Furzt, wi gunna blah uhbowt hoaw wi peep dem, ur hoaw dey luuk. Zharaz ahr zhortah dan Twiggehz, agh phaddah dan Gharatz. Dey kal demzelfz HOO-MANZ, agh dunt kal dem\nZharaz, bikuz dey ez dum, dey dunt knoh wub et meenz. Dey blahd wit Mi, agh zed dat dey hev zumting kald \"Pulektikz.\" Mi tink etz lyk Krughai Kunfedurazchun, bud dey zed et wuz moar uglyr. Uhlzo, dey griidi, lyk Gharatz, bud dey nub griidi fur goald, dey\nwunt minaz. Agh, dey neber edmid et. Zo, beyzikly, dah Sharaz ub da Nurth ahr moar ebil dan Mi eber thowt. Az lat knoh ahlredii, da Uhbrezchi Zharaz ahr owr alliz en mozt worz, bicuz dey ez zum ub dey unlii unz whu nub bytray uz. Noaw, wi du 'Dooneeuh.\nZcheptur Eyt: Sharaz ub 'Dooneeuh\n\nTeyk noat, Mi ubteynd diz enfurmeyzchun frum da 'Dooneeun Kinggy hemzelf, Yahrl Lazchlahn Moare Ilindul. Zo ez lat kan peep, diz buuk gev Mi da onur tu meat kowntliz uhfizchuhlz en da wurld. Enywhey, da\nZharaz ub 'Dooneeuh ahr blahd tu bii da owldizt. Deyr Kinggy blahd Mi dat wuz da furzt Zharaz uhrownd, meykin' dem muzch owldar dan da Zharaz ub 'Dooneeuh. 'Dooneeunz uhlzo hev pohlektikz lyk da Uhbrezchinz, bud deyrz ez muzch deberunt.\nLat peep, en deyr kulzchur, da yungizt boarne ez da un whu ez deztind tu liid, unlyk moar popyoolahr kulzchurz weyr da eldar liidz. Deyz 'Dooneeunz hev menii deberunt reynkz tuu, lyk uh Hy Theyn, agh Hy Morzchul. Uhlzo, deyz kreyzchurz ahr da lungizt livd\nZharaz uhrownd, biicuz uhpairuhntlii, dey hev Twiggeh bluud en deyr bohdiiz. Hoaweber, dey dunt peep lyk uhn Albai. Nub, 'Dooneeunz ahr zum ub da bigizt Zharaz Mi eber peepd. Ub korz, wi Urukz ahr ztil muzch biggah dan dem, dey ez pritti tol agh meyti.\nDey nub pyoor-brid Zharaz lyk Uhbrezchinz, zo dat liidz Mi tu tink dat dey ez da mongrohl reyz ub Anthohz. Lat reymimbur da Gharatz wi blahd uhbowt urlyr? Wil, noaw wi gunna tok moar uhbowt deyr hom.\nZcheptur Nyn: Da Katz \n\nTuu knoh diz reyze, ez tuu knoh kiddunz. Dat'z wub dey ez. Katz ahr beeg kiddunz, agh dey ahr frum uh eylund kolled Kuruhkahtuh. Dey blah wyrd, zmell wyrd, agh peep eben wyrdur. Diz reyze'z eylund bloh'd uhp, agh fur uh wyoll, dey\nleeved ryt hyr en Gronkkzton, en da kiddun diztrikt. Bud, dey oll muuv'd tu Mahlinoare naow, prohbublii beekuz wi Urukz wur tuu ztrong fur dem. Dyr ez fuur tiipz ub Katz, agh wi gunna dulv entuu oll ub dem ryt naow.\nZcheptur Tin: Da Tygur Katz\n\nDeyze ahr da beegizt ub da Kiddun Krezchurz, agh zum ub dem ahr ez beeg az uh Uruk. Dey peep lyk Tygurz, agh dey klomp lyk dem tuu. Dey ahr yoozchualii da woriurz ub da Kiddunz, agh dey ahr pritii duhm.\nMi dun't knoh uhlut uhbowt da Tygur Kiddunz, zo Mi gunna guu entuu da nehzxt Kiddun reyze.\nZcheptur Eeleben: Da Zcheetuh Katz\n\nDeez unz ahr da zmullizt, bud unlyk uh phat Ztowt, dey ez rillii phazt. Da zcheetuh Kiddunz peep lyk zcheetuhz, dey guut zpotz oll obur deyr zkin. Agh tuu Mi, dey'z myk da bezt karpitz, ef lat knoh wub Mi meen.\nZcheptur Dwelv: Da Durk Katz\n\nDey peep lyk Punturz, agh dey ahr zneeki, lyk Punturz tuu. Uhweyz peep owt fur da Durk Katz, kuz dey kan zteel latz ztuf et eny mohmunt. Tuu Mi, dey kynda ahr lyk da Durk Twiggehz, en uh zenze.\nZadlii, dat'z ol Mi knohz uhbowt da Durk unz, beekuz Kiddunz ahr myzteeriuhz, agh dey nub led Mi lurn uhbowt dem.\nZcheptur Dirtyn: Da Lepurd Katz\n\nDeez unz ohbveeuhzlii peep lyk Lepurdz, bud unlyk da uddah Kiddunz, deyz unz nub exeed en eny zchpezifik zkilz, bud dey ez da bezt zooted fur duueeng enytyng. Dey ez beeger dan Zcheetahz agh\nPunturz, agh dey ez phaztur dan Tygurz agh Panturz, agh dey ez zneekeeur dan Tygurz agh Zcheetuhz. Lat gunna prohbublii peep deyz unz da mozt. Wii neber peeped et dah deberunt typz ub Ztowtz, huh? Wil, wii gunna duu  dat naow.\nZcheptur Furtyn: Da Znoh Albaiz\n\nMi nebur hurd ub dem. Deyr zkin ez whyt lyk znoh. Deyr heyr ez whyt lyk klowdz. Dey ahr Znoh Twiggehz. Dey ahr endenjurd zpechiiz. Tu bii onuzt, deyz Znoh Twiggehz ahr Ahlbynoh, agh dey nub lyk et wen Wi kul\ndem dat. Da Znoh Twiggehz halb'd da Ztowtz wen da pazht wohr, zo.... Mi nub rylii lyk da Znoh Twiggehz. Dey liiv en uh pleyzch kull'd Frohztfohl. Bud, dat'z ol Mi knoh, biicuz dey nub rylii lyk Mi.\nDiz iz unlii da furzt vohlyuum ub da Kreyzchurz. \n\n\n\nDUH UHND", ""),
        StaticBook("Krugmas Gifts", "Joseph Alexander", "Krugmas List!\n\nLuke: 49 diamonds = 1715 minas\n\nAmber: A horse (dank) = around 300 minas\n\nAthena: Lapis Blocks = around 512\n\nAsher: Sword with sharpness if possible = around 200 (Luke\nmakes sword)\n\nCamryn: BOATS = just need wood\n\nKeira: ALCHOHOL! = 30 minas for 10\n\nAtlas: UPRIGHT BRANCH\n\nGrand total of about 2,245", ""),
        StaticBook("Kvaz Tax Token", "Lerald Vyronov", "~\nThis is an official\nKvaz Tax token, equal to 100 minas in tax\n\n~\n\n*Steward's autograph*", ""),
        StaticBook("L. Tree News #1", "Roth Jayamen", " =======()======\n ===-=- ========\n ======/\\ ===-=-\n =====/__\\ =====\n =====/   \\ =====\n ====/____\\ ====\n ===== _U_======\n ===,_/     \\_====\n ==/_______ \\===\n “The Lone Tree News” \nISSUE ONE\n\nPg. 4: News Section\nPg. 8: People Section\nPg. 10: Philosophy Section\nPg. 19: Entertainment\nSection\nPg. 36: Crossword Puzzle\nPg. 40: Business and Employment Section\nPg. 45: Thank you and Staff\nThe Lone Tree News is an independent news source. Each author of an article holds their own views and their views are not that of the news source as a whole.\n\n~Roth Jayamen\nNews Section\n\nNews ( vailor)\n\n(None at the moment. We need more Investigative journalists!)\nNews (by city)\n\nFelsen News\n\nThe Gambinos and The Saltpans\n\nTwo groups of people known as The Gambinos and The Saltpans have recently taken up residence in Felsen.\nDue to their mischievous nature, residence should likely keep a look out for them. The Gambinos are usually recognized be their black hair with a bluish tint. As for the Saltpans, their attire is unknown at the moment.\nFrom causing trouble with shop keepers to local towns folk. These guys have been known to cause negative situations. Keep a look out. ~Daggeroth\nPeople Section\n\nInterviews\n\n(No interviews conducted this issue, we need more Investigative journalists!)\nObituaries\n\n(No known recently dead this issue.)\nPhilosphy Section\n\nPassage of Wisdom\n\n“Don’t judge a book by its cover.”\nMany people say this saying, but what does it actually mean? Most might think it means not to judge others by solely their appearance, but can it go deeper than that.\nI feel that this phrase can talk about not only people’s appearance but their actions as well. You might think that the actions are what is inside the cover, and while this may be the case, there are cases where it is not.\nHow? Well, what if the actions someone takes is not their true person. For example, let’s take three thugs. They all act like thugs and bully on people. They are all bullies then, right? Well not specifically.\nThey could be acting that way for different reasons.\nThug 1 is your average thug. He grew up knowing violence and was taught it was the only way to get things done. Thug one likely acts this way because he knows no other way that works. They are his true actions, but they aren’t solely his fault.\nThug 2 grew up in a moderately good household. His bad behavior and violent mood had him become a thug later in life. Thug two likely acts this way because these are his true actions.\nThug 3 grew up in a good, but poor house hold. Having no other way to gain money, he signed up as a thug to feed his family. He regrets doing this but has no other way out. Thug 3 acts this way only because he has to, not because he wants to.\nAll in all, I hope this helps you look at people differently, even those who offend you. ~Daggeroth\nEntertainment Section\n\nPoetry\n\nAN UNCOMMON SIGHT\n\nI go about my day,\nDoing the same things as before,\nThe same old road,\nFrom my humble abode,\nNot realizing it is a bore.\nI walk ever onward,\nKnowing all my tasks by heart,\nA straight narrow trail,\nWith nothing new to avail,\nAll I do is my part.\nThen one day as I'm going past,\nA park once again,\nI see a boy,\nWithout even a toy,\nWho couldn't be past ten.\nThe boy was doing something abnormal,\nSomething I hadn't seen before,\nHe was looking in the sky,\nNot even blinking an eye,\nThey didn't even seem sore.\nI wondered if there was a hawk,\nOr something in the sky,\nI didn't hear a thing,\nOnly the birds that always sing,\nSo I did wonder why.\nI looked over,\nTo the boy sitting by,\nHe was being bullied by his peers,\nAnd was starting to go in tears,\nJust for looking in the sky.\n\nI was about to go over,\nTo try to help if I could,\nBut the parents went first,\nBefore I feared the worst,\nTo help as they should.\nI walked on my way home,\nWondering why what I saw came to pass,\nI had a thought why,\nSo I looked to the sky,\nAnd saw it in its great mass,\nAs I looked to the sky,\nI was transfixed,\nI hadn't done this in a while,\nAnd it did make me smile,\nAs past and current memories mixed.\nI saw the vast expanse,\nIn all its mystery,\nI watched the clouds in the sky,\nAs they changed shape and passed by,\nAs they had for all of history.\nSuddenly someone laughed to my left,\nEven thought it was mild,\nSomeone looking at me,\nLaughing at what I appeared to be,\nJust as the others had done to the child.\n~Daggeroth\nThe Musicians Guild is now accepting new members or anyone who wants to take free piano lessons! You do not need to join for the lessons, just send a bird to Geedin Jayamen. They also sell pianos for 100 Minas each! They are located in the Caliphate.\nNeed someone to perform music at an event? Contact Geedin Jayamen!\nArt\n/\\\n       /\\ \\ \\\n   /\\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n   \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n    \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n     \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n      \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n       \\ \\ \\/  \\ \\\n        \\ \\/   / /\n         \\      \\ \\\n          \\  /\\ \\ \\ \n           \\/ /\\/_/\n            \\/\n~Daggeroth\nJoke of the Issue\n\n“I looped a bunch of golden watches into a belt and I’ve got to tell you, it was a waist of time.” ~Daggeroth\nRiddle of the Issue (answer is in the next issue)\n\nHow many enclosed spaces are in one circle?\n( a ) 1\n( b ) 2\n( c ) 3\n( d ) 4\nCrossword Puzzle\n( The numbers are also a slot/square)\n\nThe hints are after the puzzle.\n\n((The dots are only there for spacing, ignore them.))\n\nThere are answers that are two words.\nNo spaces.\n.    1\n          .2[][][][][][]\n      3   . []\n  .4[][][][][]\n      []    []\n 56[][][][]  7\n.  [] .[]      []  8[][][]\n.  [] .[]      []  []\n    .9[][][][][][][]\n        []\nACROSS\n\n2. What all slaves want.\n\n4. A Shining Warrior\n\n5. A Short Green Guy\n\n8. A Ruler of a nation\n\n9. And his name is...\nDOWN\n1. This will set you free\n\n3. A famous farmer\n\n6. A green humanoid\n((Parent Killer))\n\n7. A creamy pastry with icing\n\n8. A short name for a cat humanoid\nEmployment and business section\n\nThe Lone Tree News is looking for authors (for the poetry and story section) , investigative journalists ( For each major newspaper section and also for getting information about out in the world. ),\nartists (for drawings to go in the paper)  ((text drawing in minecraft books)), and anyone who wishes to contribute to the paper or wants a section in the paper.\nContributions and sections can be anything that you think would fit in a newspaper, be it an article, a thought or idea, art, or anything that can go into a paper. We do hold the right to deny putting something in the paper.\nIf you wish to join us, wish to contribute, or want a section, please just send a bird to Roth Jayamen ((Sofetios)) or drop the contribution, section, or a note in the chest at our place of operation in Felsen on ’10 Steel Lane’!\nWe can also put a certain amount of advertisements in the paper for an amount of minas. This is purely to keep the paper going! ~Roth Jayamen\nThank you for\n        Reading!\n\nStaff:\n\nOwner: Roth Jayamen\nWriter: Daggeroth", ""),
