ane’!\nWe can also put a certain amount of advertisements in the paper for an amount of minas. This is purely to keep the paper going! ~Roth Jayamen\nThank you\n           For\n         Reading!\n\n          Staff\n\nOwner: Roth Jayamen\nWriter: Daggeroth", ""),
        StaticBook("L.R. Trans.", "Lori Oathcast", "Long Range Translocation Device Investigation.\n\nFrom what I can gather from Archmage Haadi the long range translocator is developed through a use of 'Void Translocation' magics which establish small pockets within the void to place objects and a --->\n- Enchanter. The void translocationist must take a object and place it within the void, and then a enchanter must co-operate in keeping such a object within the void without the original void translocationist present. The void translocationist must --->\n- then re-locate himself and in the area he wishes to designate the other opening pull forth the object from the void again, which the Enchanter had held there. This enables a hole to open between the two locations and stay open when powered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lab Logs", "Iat", "Maheral's Research\n\n\n\n\nProgress to build a replica of a ballista is well under way though stampered by me losing my notes on it from Athera. Nonetheless this is merely the\nproof of theory before I begin my research into developing a naval defense system.\n\nShould the Okarir'tayna wish to collaborate I am always in need of an alterationist.\n\n~Maheral", ""),
        StaticBook("Lady Sophia", "Leyu", "The Legend of Lady Sophia\nDiscovered and Recovered by Talithia\nProtected by the Monks of Asulon\nOn the island called Silva Insula*, there is a legend** of a Sainted woman named Sophie...and a dark evil.\nIt all began when people who lived small societies near the Lucky Goblin Inn began to go missing.\nThey would leave the inn, or step out of their homes for a minute and just vanish, never to be seen again. Then people noticed that some of the others were slowly changing, becoming wilder and more aggressive, or just insane.\nPeople became frightened and began to withdraw from each other, joining with their neighbors in an effort to stay safe. Lady Sophie and her son Trevor were among those who sought shelter and safety at the inn.\nAround that time creatures began to appear around the town. No two descriptions were ever the same, but most could agree on their glowing eyes and how they seemed to fade into the darkness around them when you looked at them.\nThen Trevor went insane overnight. He began to kill his friends and neighbors. People from the small societies banded together and tried many ways to stop him, but, alas, the only way for his terror to end was by his death.\nOn the day he was buried, the Lady Sophie sat all day by her beloved son's grave, neither eating nor speaking to any who came by to offer her their condolences. The remaining people gathered at the Inn to wait for her return.\nBy the time night fell, a dwarf named Brokk became concerned for her and went to the grave to check on her. As he approached the grave, Lady Sophie stood up and walked out into the misty forest. Brokk tried to follow her but quickly lost\nher and turned to go back to the inn. That's when the scream pierced through the fog and darkness. No one could find the words to describe that unearthly, chill inducing scream. Many recalled grabbing their heads from the pain as the scream ripped\nthroughout their brains. When the scream ended, Brokk went in the direction Lady Sophie went in, and found her unconscious on the ground. He picked her up in his arms and took her back to the inn.\nAs the sun banished the darkness,\nLady Sophie woke once and tried to tell Brokk what happened. She had found the source of the evil plaguing them and went to confront it. The scream that had rent the air had come from this evil as she defeated it. **** She only had time to\nmention that it would never return before she closed her eyes and passed into that unknown realm we call death. As she died, all the others who had been slipping into madness, became whole once more. No one else disappeared after that. Life went\nback to normal for the people of Silva Insula. They moved closer to the inn and resurrected a church in her honor; it still stands to this day watching over her beloved town.\nAlthough none knew what actually happened that night, there is\none theory that many in the town seemed accept as fact. They said that Lady Sophie, after grieving for her loss so deeply, became determined that no one else should suffer her fate. It is whispered that her will and determinations\nwas so strong, that she defeated the evil with her mind alone. And some even whisper that the evil that she faced was somehow connected to the enders that plague Asulon now.\nBut perhaps the most disturbing thing of all is the rumors of\nnoises coming from the graveyard late at night and the shadow that rises from Trevor's grave and prowls around the town looking for a new victim.\n-footnotes-\n*Silva Insula is known for the Lucky Goblin's Inn and it's delicious Red Rum, which is no longer made. There are several abandoned villages near Silva Insula that date back to the events described in this legend\n**The tale has been passed from a local Dwarf named Brokk Wayland MacGowan to his brother Ferron Andvare MacGowan and the townspeople who were left by the end.\n*** Brokk Wayland MacGowan is the builder and original owner of the\nLucky Goblin Inn.He is considered to be the founder of Silva Insula and all it stands for.\n****The means to defeating this unknown evil was either lost or Lady Sophie never said\nwhat she did to defeat it.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lady Sophie", "Daniel Nodal", "The Legend of Lady Sophia\nOn the island called Silva Insula*, there is a legend** of a Sainted woman named Sophie...and a dark evil.\nIt all began when people who lived in small societies near the Lucky Goblin Inn began to go missing. They would leave the inn, or step out of their homes for a minute and just vanish, never to be seen again. Then people noticed that some of the others\nwere slowly changing, becoming wilder and more aggressive, or just insane. People became frightened and began to withdraw from each other, joining with their neighbors in an effort to stay safe. Lady Sophie and her son Trevor were among those who sought\nshelter and safety at the inn. Around that time creatures began to appear around the town. No two descriptions were ever the same, but most could agree on their glowing eyes and how they seemed to fade into the darkness around them when you looked at them\nThen Trevor went insane overnight. He began to kill his friends and neighbors. People from the small societies banded together and tried many ways to stop him, but, alas, the only way for his terror to end was by his death.\nOn the day he was buried, the Lady Sophie sat all day by her beloved son's grave, neither eating nor speaking to any who came by to offer her their condolences. The remaining people gathered at the Inn to wait for her return. By the time night fell, a\ndwarf named Brokk*** became concerned for her and went to the grave to check on her. As he approached the grave, Lady Sophie stood up and walked out into the misty forest. Brokk tried to follow her but quickly lost her and turned to go back to the inn.\nThat's when the scream pierced through the fog and darkness. No one could find the words to describe that unearthly, chill inducing scream. Many recalled grabbing their heads from the pain as the scream ripped throughout their brains. When the\nscream ended, Brokk went in the direction Lady Sophie went in, and found her unconscious on the ground. He picked her up in his arms and took her back to the inn.\nAs the sun banished the darkness, Lady Sophie woke once and tried to tell Brokk what happened. She had found the source of the evil plaguing them and went to confront it. The scream that had rent the air had come from this evil as she defeated it. ****\nShe only had time to mention that it would never return before she closed her eyes and passed into that unknown realm we call death. As she died, all the others who had been slipping into madness, became whole once more. No one else disappeared after\nthat. Life went back to normal for the people of Silva Insula. They moved closer to the inn and resurrected a church in her honor; it still stands to this day watching over her beloved town.\nAlthough none knew what actually happened that night, there is one theory that many in the town seemed accept as fact. They said that Lady Sophie, after grieving for her loss so deeply, became determined that no one else should suffer her fate. It is\nwhispered that her will and determinations was so strong, that she defeated the evil with her mind alone. And some even whisper that the evil that she faced was somehow connected to the enders that plague Asulon now.\nBut perhaps the most disturbing thing of all is the rumors of noises coming from the graveyard late at night and the shadow that rises from Trevor's grave and prowls around the town looking for a new victim.\n-footnotes-\n\n*Silva Insula is known for the Lucky Goblin's Inn and it's delicious Red Rum, which is no longer made. There are several abandoned villages near Silva Insula that date back to the events described in this legend\n**The tale has been passed from a local Dwarf named Brokk Wayland MacGowan to his brother Ferron Andvare MacGowan and the townspeople who were left by the end.\nbrother Ferron Andvare MacGowan and the townspeople who were left by the end.\n*** Brokk Wayland MacGowan is the builder and original owner of the Lucky Goblin Inn. He is considered to be the founder of Silva Insula and all it stands for.\n****The means to defeating this unknown evil was either lost or Lady Sophie never said what she did to defeat it.\nThe Legend of Lady Sophie\n\nWritten in Asulon\nDiscovered and Recovered by Talithia\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Last Will", "Percival Staunton", "The Last Will & Testament of Percival Staunton, First Duke of Courland, Lord Treasurer of the Fourth Holy Orenian Empire \n\n+_+_+_+_+_+_+_+_+_+#=#=#=#=#=#=#=#=#=#***********************\nArticle One:\n\nAll property belonging to Percival Staunton is to be given to his brother, George Staunton. This excludes finances.\n\nArticle Two:\n\nAll finances are to be passed onto Richard Staunton.\nArticle Three: \n\nThe Vigil Palace is the be handed over to Richard Staunton. Braaburg, Riga's Keep is to be passed onto George as a home.", ""),
        StaticBook("Laura's Vows", "Laura", "Wedding Vows\nLaura's:\nTreemma, love, the past ten years of my life, I've lived with you as a dear friend. But, more than that, you're the love of my life, and I want to spend the rest of it with you. No matter what comes our way, be it dragonfire and\nruin or complete and utter destruction of everything we know, I'll still love you, until the day my spirit is put to rest. Nay, even then, I'll love you, and I'll love you into the next life, and the next, for ten thousand lifetimes. I love you, Treemma\nParir'Athri, and I'm so proud to become your wife today.", ""),
        StaticBook("Laws of Aym", "Irrin'Athri", "Laws of Aym\n\n1.Love\nLove is allowed between Aym and any follower of Aym. Marriage is allowed between any two people as long as you attempt to convert your spouse into believing upon Aym.\n2.Stealing\nStealing and looting is not allowed unless the one that you're stealing from one that's life has already been taken from them, but besides looting a corpse no stealing is permitted to any followers of Aym.\n3. Death\nDeath to any living being is permitted to all and any followers of Aym. If you're dying, then be happy about it, it is just a greeting from Aym. If you are to provide death upon another you are helping that being understand and believe in Aym\nthe only difference is that by providing the death upon a being will provide more of a challenge on their way to Aym.\n4. Respect\nYou are to respect Aym, his ways, and his followers and to disrespect the ways or followers of Aym is to disrespect Aym, if you're found disrespecting Aym you shall be punished. . .\n5. Pain\nPain is a blessing from Aym and if you are injured you shall not be healed unless the injury affects your ability to worship Aym. If you happen to be in pain you're allowed to request death and you can choose who you would like to be killed by\n6. Other Laws\n-No belief in any other god\n-Don't murder other followers\n-Attempt to help and provide for followers and Aym\n-Do not let  non-followers corrupt or convert your faith\n-Do be friendly and kind to all other followers", ""),
        StaticBook("Lean", "Thurak'Yar", "=-=-= Lean =-=-=\n\nGifted to the Farseer Thurak by the Eternal Librarian.\nThe origins of Lean, or more commonly known as Purple Drink (Purple Drank if you’re of southeron dialect) Precede man himself according to the legend of Lawrence Lean. Back in the FirstEra, a would-be herbalist was delving\nfar into the reaches of Aegis, looking to change the face of the herbal game forever. It was after thirty years of searching that his thirst was quenched. He had discovered the Chrono root.\nIt glowed when he unearthed it on accident on a hot day in the wastes. Shocking and magnificent, he gently uncovered it without severing it from its host. A perfect extraction was followed by mass excavation. Before too\nlong Lawrence Lean had a nice stockpile of Chrono and made preperations to head back to the heartland of Aegis to share his findings. Upon a relatively short trip back to his lab the herb fiend got to work. Mashing, grinding, and boiling, Lean went wild\ntrying to find a use for his life’s work. It was in a workplace rage that he discovered the Chrono root actually grey out of root form and created a dense bush of sweetly scented buds and flowers. When a mature plant’s roots are grinded\nand boiled in cheesecloth Lawrence Lean found himself with a powerful elixir. It’s effects are known to slow down perceived time in the user’s mind and induce an intense warped effect about the user. When dried out the buds made\nfor great pipe tobacco substitute. Chrono’s use as a smokable remedy has recently been made famous by Hansetians, notably adiv Chrono user the late Darius “Lion”. Lawrence Lean proclaims his elixir Lean to be the key to immortality.\nIt has been described as a mixture that looks like the deep heavens in colour and enthralling in nature when staring directly into a fresh mug of Lean.\nAfter note:\nTexts recovered from a Human library prior to its closure.\nOriginal texts indicate the author was one Lion III of the Holy Oren Empire from the era of Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Learn to Read", "Saviordude", "=(^x^)= Cat\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= Cat in hat\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= )o( Cat in hat, with a bat.\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= )o(\n\\(     )/ Fat cat in hat, with a bat.\n*This book continues on like this for several hundred pages, allowing one to pick up the written word with the magic of Rhyme and Pictures*", ""),
        StaticBook("Lefkos' Journal.", "Lefkos Glowsbane", "Journal\nOf\nLefkos\nGlowsbane\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBegan: 16th of Malin's\nWelcome, 1534.\n7th of Malin's Welcome-\nNow, I'm aware this is beggining early but.. It is neccesary. Ill recount the events leading up to my current situation.\n I walked along the path of the Cloud Temple Docks, aiming to board the dwarvish boat. When passing\nthe ruined houses, a mans hand landed upon my shoulder. Upon turning for investigation, I found it to be Taeleh, a high elf who is running for a leader position in Haelun'or. After conversing for a few minutes, he lowered his voice, and explained, to me,\nthe evil and corrupt nature of the other two candidates running for a leader position.\n I was shocked by the news; But, knowing Taeleh was not one to lie on such matters, was forced to accept it. He then offered me a position within his 'order', of sorts.\nHe explained it was one who hunted things such as Necromancers and dark creatures.\n I obliged, and he took me to Fi'Ceru. He gave me a uniform, and then others started to show up. He spoke of an... 'apparition'. He mentioned that they had tried to kill it\nbut it had escaped.\nI was told we were going to hunt for it, and oblidged.\n Within the hour, we were travelling a mountain, me in full iron gear as a snowstorm raged around us. Soon, we decided to give up, and prepared to leave.. However, before\nwe could so much as make a move, I saw a giant figure in the snow just beyond my eyesight.\n Alerting the others, we all drew weapons as the beast moved farther up the mountain, towards a set of ruins. Before we could give chase, however.. Creatures began\nto form.. Swarming around us, flying and shooting fire in all directions.. at least 50 at first.. We yelled, and charged into battle with just the five of us.\n The battle was over soon, the creature having moved to the top of a staircase as we approached\nthe bottom. Again, the creatured began to appear, swarming again.. This time at least 100.. We took cover behind pillars, dashing out in turns and killing a few each time. By the time they died, more had arrived. At that point, we simply charged,\nsuffering light injuries on all of us as we slew them. We glared up at the creature, those of us with aurum weapons charging up the middle, and those with Ferum-such as myself, flanked it. The creature moved, almost unspeakably fast, sending Taeleh\ntumbling down the mountain, landing in a soft patch of snow at the bottom. I charged it, swinging my blade forth towards its midsection but... It passed right through. While doing that, those with Aurum launched a joint attack, hitting it on both sides.\nThe creature screeched, glowing slightly before exploding in light, leaving nothing in the sense of remains. We woke Taeleh, and left to return to Fi'Ceru, assuming we had killed the beast..\n*This page was covered in a very highly detailed sketch of black, shadowy creatures swarming around a group of 4 men, who fought them. From the back, a taller and larger one stood, huge claws upon it as it watched the battle proceed*\n16th of Malin's Welcome, 1534-\nI awoke in my new residence in Fi'Ceru to the sounds of the towers bells ringing three times. Grumbling, I knew this was a summons, and got dressed before making my way to the tower. Upon entering, I found Ikur and Taeleh\nalready there, along with Ivan. Taeleh explained to us that the creature had indeed lived, and that we were to hunt it down again.\n Oblidging, we agai wen searching for it. Near the end of our search, we reached the condemnd 'Zeus' Bakery'. Upon breaking\nthe door down and entering, we soon discovered a vast underground area.. Amazed, we continued to explore, until I found a drop in the ground. Curious, I went to explore, only to accidently drop all the way to the bottom. Now, I had gotten stuck inside a\nwater filled cave.\nIkur an Ivan, who had been following me, fell as well. And no sooner had a rope been tossed down to let us out, the cieling.. moved, breaking the exit off.\nAlmost all the water vanished, save a pool that lay in the center. Torches\nthat had lit the walls seemed to turn darker, and a redder shade. Shadows began to move, forming a humanoid figure.. It wore a warped mask, with the armor to match it. It questioned our very existence, before agreeing to let us leave.. At this point, it\nglanced to the water, it turning black.. Portal, like. The creature stepped inside, ordering us to follow.. and we did..\n*the page is taken by a very detailed sketch of a man in warped armor, standing before a black pool of water, with 3 men clustured around it.*\nWhen I opened my eyes, I was standing within a large cavern like area, not well lit, with many trange warpings throughout it.. what was worse though, were the walls.. They were covered with dark and evil creatures. The armored figure told us this was the\n'Node', and to step through another portal. We did, Ikur first, then me. Ivan came later.\n I then opened my eyes again, now standing in the middle of the Cloud Temple Docks.\n*the page is taken up by several detailed pictures of a large, dark cavern area.*\nhttp://imgur.com/a/KrMqC\n(That was it IMC. Make it darker then add creatures everywhere and you got it!)\n17th of Malin's Welcome, 1534-\nI speak with Taeleh and Ivan. I explained to Taeleh my experience of it, before Ivan approached, looking.. distraught. Taeleh questioned him, before he told us what he saw, and drew pictures. I have them here.\n*The page was taken by two detailed sketches of monstrous beings, ones to bring nightmares to the brave*\nhttp://prntscr.com/94reau\nhttp://prntscr.com/94rhdo\n14th of The First Seed, 1534-\n I meet again with the Golden Owls, this time having brought my friend, Deltion Brisingr, along. We had him accepted into the order, preparing to chase down the Apparition for the third time. I prepared my Aurum tipped\njavelin, gearing up as we set out to slay the creature.\n Soon, we reached a mountain, close to the one we first met the creature at. A tower stood upon it, and no sooner had we reached the top of it, had I spotted a shadow within the blizzard that\nraged about us. Soon, the beast came into view, and dove for me, its massive claws outstretched.\n Stabbing forward, I cut its claws, and sent it screeching back in pain. I smiled lightly, now that it knew I was dangerous to it.\n No sooner then I had a\nchance to gloat over my slight victory, his fire-like beasts began forming, surrounding the tower on all sides.\nThe other of the Owls fought them furiously, as the beast had lowered slightly, looking to holes in the tower. I saw my chance here.\n*the page was covered in an intricate drawing of a lone, skinny tower on a mountain, surrounded by all sides by flying creatures of flame*\nI launched myself from the tower, plummeting at a rapid pace towards the beast. I landed upon its back, my aurum tipped Javelin sinkjing into it, sending it with me as we fell to the ground.\n Upon contact with the floor, the ground cave in, and we\ncontinued falling for but a moment before I landed upon it inside of a small cave. I stood up, Taeleh climbing in after me as he held up a strange lamp.. To weaken the beast further, I drew my other javelin, plunging it into it several times as it was\npinned to the floor.\nThe lantern glowed lightly, the creature begining to be consumed by the aurum and the lantern combined. After a minute, the creature vanished, having been vanquished at last!\n*A detailed drawing of a man in full Aurum armor kneeling atop a creature as black as night, javelin jammed into its chest. A man in the background holding a blue orb, drawn in mid-chant. The creature was slowly being consumed by blue and gold hues*\nThis brings an end to the first of my journals. Every event written here was true, and happened to me within the Golden Owls.\nOf course, I shall make more journals later, but I'm afraid to say the pages here are growing thinner..", ""),
        StaticBook("Legal statement.", "Erendiel Thoren", "I was attacked in an alley by a man wearing a mohawk, after he managed to beat me to the ground a member of the Lorraine Honor Guard showed up, but instead of helping me, he helped the attacker, afterwards they knocked me out, then dragged me to a storage\ncloset where they tied and gagged me, i escaped hours later with the help of a passerby.", ""),
        StaticBook("Leo's life", "Leo Kamai", "Leo's Life\n-------------------The day Liliana died, was the day I realised I was alone.. I have no clue who did it, but when the time comes, there will be no mercy..>\nI remember all the things I said to her. Like her being my glowstone to see me through the night, or the iron to my armor to help me fight off the things trying to pull me down... I guess my armor and sight are gone now.. I think this means recklessness..\nTo remember her, and my goal.. I will make an ice cave, and make a statue of her, so that everytime I go in to meditate.. I will never forget her..>\nNever shall I forget her smile...\nNever shall I ever forget her words...\nNever shall I forget the times we had...\nNever shall I forget the troubles we've faced...\nNever shall I forget our engagement..\nNever..Because she was right by my side...\nAnd as long as I remember these things, I will never forget my goal.. to find and kill who did this...=>\nI have been meditating, trying to get a connection to the void.. took a day for me to make that connection but it is worth it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Leo's Spellbook", "Leo Kamai", "Spellbook of Leo\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ [!] A frosty mana catalyst is found on this page.\n\n            /\\\n           /  \\\n        ø<  ƒ  >ø\n           \\  /\n           ˚\\/˚\n          ≤__≥\n((Usable by Leo; Suijin power source))\nSpell: Healing Waters\n\nForm: Water\nUsage: 10-25%                     Available\n\nIncantation:\nUses the water and mana available to heal the wounds of taget. mana needed scales with injury\nSpell: Water Prison\n\nForm: Water\nUsage: _=(-)\n\nIncantation:\nEncases the target in water, making it barely possible to move.\nSpell: Wasp Swarm\n\nForm: Conjuration&Ice\nUsage: (S_)(M=)(L-)\n\nIncantation:\nSpawns a horde of ice wasps that are armed with Nebula Poison.\nSpell: Suijin: Ultimate\n                Defense\n\nForm: Water&Ice\nUsage: Catalyst Mana\n\nIncantation:\nSuijin from the waist up encases Leo with an Ice chestplate. Suijin is armed with an Ice sword and offers both attack as well.\nSpell: Suijin: 2 for 1\n\nForm: Water\nUsage: Catalyst Mana\n\nIncantation:\nSuijin assissts the user by acting on his own to attack and defend, primarily uses body parts for punches, kicks, and blocks.\nSpell: Suijin: Split\n                 Tactics\n\nForm: Ice&Steam\nUsage: Catalyst Mana\n\nIncantation: \nSuijin splits from Leo in his humanoid form. Assissts Leo in any way he can. Suijin's body is Ice, but gains movement and range through Steam.\nSpell: Crystalize\n\nForm: Steam&Ice\nUsage: _(=)-\n\nIncantation:\nCrystalizes steam and impales everything caught within.\nSpell: Ice Coffin\n\nForm: Ice\nUsage: _(=)-\n\nIncantation:\nSpawns two Ice nail coffin halves and encases the target, requires an immobile target.\nSpell: Final IceAge\n\nForm: Ice,Water&Steam\nUsage: (Suijin-, but Suijin is disabled) (Without Suijin, brink of death+++)\nIncantation:\nSurrounds with steam, turns to water and swarms target, then crystalizes and impales target multiple times.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lesser Leaf", "A.N.C.", "For the Lesser Leaf\nby A.N.C.\nSnaking out at half past noon\nwith her back against the silver moon.\nThe heart blowing east, the mind blowing west,\na chattering grew within her chest.\nBut soon embraced, caressed by her sun,\nshe lived emboldened, they as one.\nAlas, when midnight loomed, daybreak leered,\ntheir spark all smothered, as they had feared.\nIn turn, their fire blazed and smoke ensued.\n\"Out! Out!\" the candle blew.\nThe leaves all fallen, the dying all grown--\nexcept for she: her lassitude honed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "[Hooded] Edmund Hornsby", "Dear Mantisuku Family,\n\n I would like to know if you have any job openings. I am Edmund Horsnby. Send a letter to me when you have an answer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "MarinaEmily", "My Dearest Jerrik,\nI trust that times have not been easy for you, and I apologize for being absent in your times of need. However, your favorite older sister would like to remind you there's someone in your corner all the way across the realm. I need\nyou to be strong in these times of need and desperation. There is much I must confess; I languish in a loveless marriage in Marland, I cannot bring myself to the brink of happiness. You must get through to Jaryd, sit down with him and compromise, don't\nstop until you agree. It is essential for my health, and survival. The last time we spoke, you seemed overcome with melancholy. One word, and you've consumed my waking days. Anyway, all this to say, I'll come home this summer, that is at your invitation.\nI know what you're doing is important, I know you're very busy, but I'm crossing the realm and I just can't wait. \nYour Sister,\nLopkaea Marbran- [!] Mabrand seems to be crossed out hastily, replaced with a small, meek 'Brightwater' right under it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Lelien Lazul", "*A letter, sealed with wax. Once opened, it would read thusly.*\n\"Dearest Jupiter,\n\nI have left the city, one can always contact me by using the onyx ferret Carl that lounges around in the Eternal Library.\nI will not be returning, unless invited to.\n\n- Lelien Lazul\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Beamon4", "Dear Clerics I am Hadrian Thassarion of House Thassarion a noble House in the The Holy Oren Empire. I have had a problem where a limb was chopped off and i need it healed due to certain reasons. I completely understand if you will not do this as you must\nhave a busy schedule, but i ask you make a small gap in your day to see me.\n\n\n\nSigned\nHadrian Thassarion\n(Beamon4)", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Ae'ris Leithwin", "My dear friends,\n\nMy travels have been amazing, I have marvelled at the beauty of the Caliphates Structures, drunk with dwarves..\ndiscussed political nature with the High elves.. brawled with orcs, meditated with the druii, and even ran with the Kha..\nit has been a wonderful adventure, and each one more exciting than the last.\n\nI hope things are well at the guild hall.\n\n~Best wishes, Ae'ris!~", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Tessa", "3rd of Sun's Smile\n1519\n\nDear Commander,\n\nYou have my condolances for the loss of your liege lord. The late Duke was a great man who was taken from us far before his time\nand I know that the people of Adria will find a capable man to lead you to victory in this awful war.\n\nBut Unfortunatly the civil war is not the only conflict going on\nin Vailor, I have been \nreassigned to the South, where a necromancer\nBy the name of Urdu has attacked Cities with thralls of undead elves.\n\nI wish it were otherwise but due to my reassignment I can no longer provide Glyphs and Materials\nfor the Coalition\n\nKind Regards, Tessa", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Kajara Anima Fortis", "Hey Cassie! Ill be in riga if your looking for me.\n\n-Sincerely\nKaj\n[!]\nA detailed scetch of the flower in the mailbox", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter from R.A", "Elvi Terryal", "*The letter seems crumbled and covered in tear stains. The writing is bold and somewhat hair-raising to look at*\n\nTerryal,\nI have not forgotten you, nor will I forgive you...\nOver these past few years... my anger of what you did is -\n- gathering... and my magic is growing...\n\nYou killed my four friends... and you will pay heavily for it.... Their ghosts will haunt you.... and there will be no happy ending for you....\n\nYou're dead, Terryal.\n- R.A", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter of Marrow", "Unknown", "I know that you have been visited by the Order of Youth, what have you been doing to get them to notice you? Surely you are not contesting what he has done, he found it that’s for sure, and you know how his followers become when you question him.\nIblees would be jealous of their rage. You know that humans fear for their short lives, trying to remove hope of extending it will make them mad. I hope you didn’t get hurt by them, the best of health to you, may Aeriel bless your body.\nAs for what you asked me to get, I convinced the town’s people that their death were diseased. You will have the corpses sent to you in a week’s time. I am glad to hear that you have traded those foul potions for the study of anatomy and healing.\nIf you ever require any more wisdom or help in the study, do not be scared to ask me. I have been your friend for many years, and your doctor for far more.\n\n\nSafe study,\n     Doctor Marrow", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter of Thanks", "Orak", "Thank you, good friend!\n\nMay the nine divines bless your kind heart.\n\nPraise Lord Gaben.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Savoy", "Tessa", "To the Leader of\nThe Crown's Armed\nForces.\n\nGreetings! my name Is Paladin Tessa D'Lyons of the Brotherhood of\nXan. In my recent investigation in the Caliphate I have uncovered that the mercenary group known as the Blackwoods\nHave been harbouring and aiding, Necromancers, Shades, cultists and other dark forces.\n\nWhile I understand that you are in a civil war. I kindly ask you to not link your cause with theirs, no victory in War can be worth the unholy price that\none must\npay by willingly aiding the forces of Iblees.\n\nI will attempt to assemble a coalition to Strike a blow at these vile necromancers and the cravens who aid them. Military and or\nFinancial support would be much\nappreciated, however\nseeing as you are\nembroiled in a conflict yourselves, I would understand it if you could not aid me.\n\nOnce I have more information I will provide a list of their associates, so that if they come to your lands, you may cast judgement upon them\nKind regards,\nTessa D'Lyons", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter2Grandking", "Tessa", "To his Majesty, Grand King Skippy of the Dwed\n\nGreetings! I hope that you are well, my name is Tessa D'Lyons of the Brotherhood of Xan.\n\nI write to you today about a grave matter\nIn my recent investigation I have found that the Blackwood Mercenary Company, who reside near, or even in your territory. Have been actively sheltering and aiding. Shades, Necromancers, Cultists and other dark forces.\nFrom their base to the North of the Caliphate, they have been terrorizing the South recently and I intend to stop them. Therefore I formally ask for your support in destroying this menace to us all. Perhaps soon we may meet to discuss the situation?\nI hope that we can count on your support to strike a great blow to these enemies of us all.\n\n\nKind Regards,\n\nTessa D'Lyons\nPaladin of Xan", ""),
        StaticBook("Letters", "Colin of Brelus", "Aa                      Oo Bb                      Pp Cc                      Qq Dd                      Rr Ee                       Ss Ff                       Tt Gg                      Uu Hh                      Vv Ii                      Ww Jj\nKk                      Xx Ll                      Yy Mm                    Zz  Nn", ""),
        StaticBook("Lex's Journal", "Anawkin", "Lex's Journal\n\n    Lexperiments\n\n      \n\n((Originally written by Lex of Kal'urguan))\n\n To whomever is reading this, \n\nHello, I am Lex of Kal'Urguan, and this is the journal of my accomplishments and what I have done. I will mark down everything important to me here.\n And if you find this book, all of the secrets are now yours. \n\n On the first day that Kal'Urguan opened to all, I was the first to come in the new doors. I was the first to experience the --\n-- wonders of the lava lakes and the castle blocking out the molten fire. It was an amazing experience, truly.\n\n A while later, a demon appeared in the city, the fabled Herobrine. Me and some of my\nbrothers dealed with it quickly. Personally, I wanted to study it, but the others used it as a petting zoo. The wizard came to look at it, and before long, both were gone.\n\n Sad really..\n While it was still there, me and two fellow dwarves went to other civillizations to spread the news. We all went to the human land, then split paths. The other two went to the elves, where one was captured and barely got away, while I --\n-- went to the orcs and found that their leader was missing.\nAround this time, the Kal'urguan farm was finished. \n\n The king was missing for a long time, and finally decided to give up his throne. Our\noverseer, Charles, became the new king. As I'm writing this, he remains our leader and is doing well. I watched the ceremony. It was truly great. Sadly, I never became part of the council. \n\n A while later, me and\na friend saved up funds to buy a house. I am writing this book currently from our property, which is behind the Kal'urguan castle and next to the giant iron anvil, that can fix anything. \n\nI found an amazing secret.\n\n While trying to mine through the walls, I destroyed some stone and came upon a huge cavern, that expanded all the way around our city! It was completely abandoned and unknown, except for an odd redstone\ncontraption that did nothing in there. I eventually showed Charles.\n\n Since then, I've been relatively poor. I'm now writing about the present, for -wait!\nI completely forgot about another topic.\n Forget I never wrote this paragraph, whomever is reading this!\n\n Now, before the ceremony, I also established a trade route with the elves, by myself. I still dont understand how --\nI didn't get that archbishop position. I also built a makeshift road between the two kingdoms.\n\n Now it is the present, I'm pretty poor, making a living however I could. .. Er, can.\nWish I could erase here.\n Anyways, I'm writing this book now in my spare time. I'll add more if anything happens. I sure hope it does. Oh, also a new floating dwarf city has been created. How did they manage to make it fly!?\n\nTHE UNDEAD ARE HERE\nTHE UNDEAD ARE HERE!\n\n One day after, I created this book. the undead attacked Winterfall. \n\nWE ARE ALL GOING TO DIE.\n\n The sky rained with\nfire and lightning, and Winterfall was destroyed. Another human town was, too. The next night, nothing bad happened.. that's a good sign. No one knows what will happen. All efforts have gone to defence.\n\nThis might be the end of Aegis.\nI believe only one person can help us, the Aengul Wizard, Avalier. \n\nThis will probably be the last time i can write in this journal for a while. Kal'urguan is on complete lockdown.\n  I must escape through the mines. There will be a way.. I hope so, anyways. Goodbye, the greatest city in Aegis.\n\nMaybe that wasn't my last entry. I came back to Kal'urguan about 5-7 days after.\nMany things happened in this time. For one, I went to Al'Khazaar to escape my imprisonment. And when I arrived, guess what - The undead attacked. I was one of the two dwarves who survived. \n\nIt was amazing.\n After the battle, many came to know what happened. The Wander Wizard himself explained that we need to find the Ascended to defeat the Undead. \n \nI stayed there for a while, but then two elves had a private meeting with the\nhuman queen. Of course, I had to eavsdrop from a safe distance. I found out that Laurelin had somehow turned evul. One of the elves was taking a journey to Kal'Urguan. Me and another spy went to follow her. The other one knew her and\nwas caught.\n\n I, on the other hand, at least it seems, wasn't caught until the end. The other spy had actually approached her first. They started talking, and I listened in plain sight.\nThey knew I was listening. They explained what that \"evil\" was - an evil organization called the \"Dark Brotherhood\" or something like it had infiltrated Laurelin's council. They then threatened to have me killed if I didn't leave.\n So I left, and came to my room where I am writing this in now. I'm going on another journey. \n\nWhere to this time?\n\nLaurelin.\nTranscribed by Orias.\n\n~<>~", ""),
        StaticBook("Libelle ad Hobbe", "Berilac", "To the potential readers: All of the knowledge collected varies from studies and consiglia expertise, through myths and legends, to the factual chronicles mentioning the Halflings. \n\nFacts and myths of half-men, half-dwedmar\nAnatomia of Halflings:\n1) External:\nThe varied examinations towards the height and looks of individuals vary greatly. A large pool of variety (obvious in case of a half-blooded race) inclines numerous anomalies usually unseen among the \"paternal\" species\nsuch as heterochromia. Tracing the genealogy (thank goodness these are saved, both for the sake of future generations breeding and for the sorry consigliare like me) of several families I was able to discern a pattern depending heavily on\nthe birthplace, ancestry and even effects the climate may have on the previously mentioned craddle. We seem to be just as adaptive as humans on the matter of weather and resource, all the while metabolic needs force a necessity to settle as close to water\nbodies as possible, allowing to sustain larger population then that which was usually carried over during yet another exodus. It is likely that also these travels were reason behind, for certes, our feet. A vivisection carried out two years ago\n(mostly possible thanks for the uruk that ambushed the poor sod long while before I got to him) proves that the bottom structure of our feet is not very different from that which we observed in, pardon my Akovian, \"Cyka badgers\". An extra volium of skin\nsurrounding thick layer of , combined with hardened, leather-like acreage of first skin make it efficiently, with some care taken, as quiet as a cat's paw on the steps, and durable enough to force me to cut from the upper, fluff-covered layers\nafter I've blunted third misericord in attempt of opening it from below.\nReturning to lineage, as I've traced off, mayhaps confusing any potentially interested reader - the families seem to vary greatly in the means they seemed to change over generations.\nTraditions and customs have played a maestro's role in that. Some families almost seek out means to mingle on the outside, sometimes even adding a portion of blood from other species, sometimes simply seeking out partners amongst outsider halflings.\nOther, more conservative families, would've preferred marriage within the boundaries of their village - whatever that may be by the time. Even a choice of housing, susteinance and lifestyle seem to hold a factor in generating so many uniquely looking\nindividuals in comparison to some human cultures where inbreeding has instead turned disastrous, creating a hiccup in their bloodlines - harelips, hunchbacks, not to mention individuals completely mentally backwarded or sterile like mules.\nInternal:\nAs is relatively obvious to notice, halflings have stronger necessity for food and drink then their parental races, surprising if one remembers that both humans and dwarves themselves are just aswell predatorian omnivores\nwhich, dear reader, means their stomache was firsthand meant to use fat and flesh for susteinance, only later efficiently using floral sources to sustain increasingly large population. It may mean that, for one reason or the other,\nhalflings might just be more predatorian in nature then we first had assumed, considering that the diet largely based on \"tats\"and \"spuds\", carrots and grainy produce, requires them to eat almost twice their weight in order to provide enough energy so\nthat the stomache wouldn't scare the fanny outta them with constant tumble and rumble. \n\nSkipping to other interesting factors, we have cranial tissue - of similar size and, obviously, usage, as these of other races and half-bloods.\nand a slight stimuli doesn't seem to answer another question. I'll probably burn for this blasphemy, as even I feel dirty for just considering a scientific argument with a man like Petyr Brandybuck, but it seems that our \"innate skills\" just like these of\nother races, originate much more from the upbringing, enviroment and blood memory, rather then being as deeply rooted in the dealings as to make us \"born cooks\". \nEre ends this little filibuster of scientific kind, and if it can, may it aid future\ngenerations of halflings in search for answers that lie innards, rather then outwards. For the secrets of our own bodies.\n\n23rd of Sun's Smile, year 1506, Gimblewood", ""),
        StaticBook("Liches.", "Jakir Axem", "[ In eloquent writing the word Liches, is spelled out on the front cover of the book. The words striking and glowing a faint golden. Under it are the words. By Jakir Axem. It seems the writing glows brighter as you get closer to it. Inviting you in.]\n[What seems to be a man shrouded in black, and clad in a dark robe. Staring out at you, watching from under his hood. The hands of the man seem to be skeletal and he is flanked by two undead zombie like figures. The words under it.] \"A Lich.\"\n[For the rest of the book, the writing seems to return to normal black ink, with less time spent on the style of writing to help the reader to clearly see the writing and understand the lessons in the tome.]\nChapter one: Introduction.\n\nFor many years Liches have roamed the earth, we do not know where they first come from. But we do know they have been around for a very long time. I myself have killed a few, but they are not to be taken lightly.\nI was gifted with the power of gods, many who read this will not be, so I decided to make this guide so you may be able to fight them without the help of others. In this book you will find the information one might need as well as my own personal.\nexperience with these dark beings so you may better survive the next encounter you may have with them. It will only have the basic knowledge for we do not know it all, and do not wish others to try to copy in their dark arts.\nChapter two: The Lich.\n\nThe Lich is a creature made of dark magic, usually necromancy. At first they were thought  to of come from the dark power of Iblees. This is true, but those Liches are long passed, today Liches are made\nfrom necromancy and many a necromancer has tried to transcend into Lichdom. But you may wonder why there is not hundreds running around. It’s because the process is deadly and requires a lot of time and effort, and also the knowledge\non creation which has been lost to most. They use the power of necromancy to move a large portion of their life-force into an object referred to as a phylactery, this is their power supply, for it connects directly to the Lich in question.\nThe only problem being it could be hidden anywhere, so the permanent death of a Lich is unlikely but it also has a time it can live, due to the removal of life-force and the tether. The Lich will die in the end and it can’t stop it.\nChapter three: Combat.\n\nAs undead creatures, the main weakness of a Lich is gold. Gold is the bane of all known undead and as such. One should use golden weaponry over all else. Liches are unable to use necromancy due\nto the lost of most of their life-force and are also unable to access voidal or divine magic. But they are strong and smart. Bound to the will of the necromancer that created them but also free to do as they please otherwise.\nThey know fear and they will target the most dangerous person first. I myself have killed only a few, and they all have tried to kill me first. Only by me being ready was I able to stop them killing me and becoming their next victim.\nA few Liches are known for ranged weapons. Due to the lack of magic they use alchemy and bows. They are the cause of the Fringe Plague for it attacked me directly with a stronger version of the plague I was only just able to bat away in time.\nSome even wear armour, but they are made of bone and dead skin, so non golden or divine weapons are almost useless when fighting them. So be careful when facing them, they are not something one should take lightly and even more so if you are alone.\nChapter four: Personal experience \n\nI am a user of divine magic, and as such I have had to face them at their most deadly and worse. They tend to enlist the help of necromancers for extra help. As such I have\nI have had to fight the beasts of the necromancers and Liches. One being a monster made of young Mali children sewn together and made alive again with the vile magics. The lich that caused the Fringe Plague\nI had to remove after it infected most of Alras killing many and infecting many others. To which I had to remove the plague from. They are deadly creatures and some of the worst beings you can find, I hope you\nnever have to use the information found within this tome, for it is a true horror what these dark beasts will do to those who mealy get in it’s way, or if it feels like having fun.\nEpilogue: \n\nI Jakir Axem made this book to help others in fighting Liches, this book will no doubt be one of many, you can tell it is of my own design by the cover. . If it does not glow, then the book is just a copy.\nThank you for taking the time and reading this tome, I hope it helps you should the worse come to pass, and I hope that you never have to use it. This is part of the collection I shall be making on this subject,\nranging from as many dark beings I have come to fight, and find within the world. Thank you once again, and if we do meet out in the world, understand that what I do, I did by choice, and that even if you do face these things\n, you can move on and you are not alone.\n\n[Once again the fancy writing returns, the small signature of Jakir Axem written in golden glowing ink pulsing lightly at the end of the book.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Life Events", "Jayce Vulcan", "On my own now..\n\nPickpocketed for the first time\n\nRobbed a store.\n\nMet fellow theif, got cloak.\n\nFound Ker'nor\n\nMade Friends\nStarted Smithing\n\nFought Demon people\n\nFought Crab\n\nSurgery on Marcy\n\nMet Marcy's son\n\nFought Wolf thing\n\nFought Ghoul/lich, lost\nGot Ember.\n\nMet Skippy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life Of Batman", "Claire Lockheart", "The Story Of Batman\n------------------\nEver wanted to know how this Batmanguy lived? Well, here's your chance!\n\nA book about his life as a human, and everything else..\nTo make a long story short, the history is basically that of a young boy named Bruce Wayne belonging to a rich family whose parents were murdered during a mugging in front of his eyes. The only things the young Bruce still had left were his enormous -\ninheritance and a loyal caring butler in Alfred. Throughout the years Bruce Wayne has grown to become one of the most proficient people in just about anything, mastering not only various martial arts, but also investigative techniques and just about any -\ntopic they teach you at university; he was a genius and a wrecking machine ((i came like in a wrecking ball hehe :P)) At one point, Bruce being obscenely rich and allegedly bored out of his mind, decided that it was time to rid the city of Gotham from the\ncriminal parasite which seems to have rotten this city to core. After considering his options, possibly having a debate with Alfred about his image choice, Bruce Wayne decided that he would don a costume themed after bats, and naturally he would be called\nBatman ((dundundun))\nAt his disposal is an arsenal of various custom-made batarangs - sort of like boomerangs, but modeled after a bat -, grappling hooks, bombs, and various other accessories.. all themed after bats ofcourse.\nThroughout his never-ending crusade against the forces of evil, Batman encounters countless deranged maniacs and murderous psychopaths all of whom plot to either take control or simply destroy the city of Gotham, a place where daily\nterror attacks against innocent civilians is something of a given. Some of his most renowned enemies include the now worldwide famous Joker, the seemingly Bane, the bizarrely seductive Poison Ivy, and Scarecrow who is incredibly close to coming of as a\nshady drug dealer hanging around schoolyards. It seems that every time Batman takes down some eccentric megalomaniac plotting to destroy his city, another takes his place in the blink of an eye\nThanks for reading!\nHope you enjoyed (:\n\n-- \nThe Story of Batman?", ""),
        StaticBook("Life of Thrym", "Ebonsquire", "The Life of Thrym\n\n((Originally written by NoobCrafter14))\nThe account of the life of Thrym. Scribed by Thrym, this writing is accurate. \nWhen I awoke in the Cloud temple many years ago, I was but a beardling. I did not know where I was or where to go. Following the instructions of the monks I learned that by using my soulstone I could travel to the capitol of the Dwarves. I did not know\nthe way, the land seeming unfamiliar. When I arrived in Kal'Urguan, transported by the powers of Aegis, I met a dwarf, known as Gotrek Firemane. He was an Overseer in the Whispering Isles. \n\nGotrek and I talked and he invited me\nto his home. Upon arriving he treated me kindly and gave me ale then let me stay to sober up. He treated me with all the hospitality a dwarf could and I remember him ever after. \n\nA while after a Herald from the Valve showed up to Kal'Urguan.\nHe was known as Martin Benedict. He was trying to rally the dwarves to put aside racial differences with me the rest of Aegis and join together to combat the undead. He and I talked and I travelled with him to the Valve to join the heraldry. He became my\nmentor after I was accepted and alone and with him I travelled all over Aegis proclaiming a jount front against the Undead. My time in the Valve was brief but even today I remember the way to Kal'Menor. \n\nAfter a while, I left the Valve to join the new\ndwarven army, the Free Dwarfs Army. It was while I was in the FDA that Martin and I came into contact again. \n\nMartin and some others, including Kootry, a forest dwarf, and Sornof, an orc, had formed a guild that was dedicated to a united\nforce against the Undead. This guild was known as the United Aegis Coalition. I would help Martin and the few guild members there to build their fort near Haven from time to time but eventually Martin convinced me to leave the FDA and join him in the UAC.\nI was in the UAC for many years. I was there when Martin became ascended, when Kootry came into power, when Martin returned to take leadership as the UAC had declined him from what it once was, I was there when Martin died finding Arcadius and when Sornof\ntook control. I have fought many battles in my time in the UAC. While in the UAC, I made friends such as Maur, Renzbro, Sornof, and Olde Beer Belly.\n\nSadly, not even the UAC could last forever. It was soon turned into the FoA, a task force of the Ascended\nBlaedr, also a friend of mine, was put in charge. Sornof was enraged at being demoted. I honestly believed he was one of the best leaders the UAC had and was sad to see him go. The last I saw of Sornof was him in a rage leading off some men to attack the\nundead. I stayed for a while in the FoA under Blaedr who I had respect for. But, iwas no longer the UAC, no longer what I had joned. So, I left. I meant to return but now I don't believe and don't wish to ever return to the FoA.\nI left the FoA to visit Kal'Urguan the place I had lived for long years. There I met Gotrek again. It had been many years but I had never forgotten him. Gotrek was now the Grand Master Smith of the Dwarves. This was exactly what I had been looking for.\nI had travelled to URguan to become a blacksmith. When I saw him and heard what he was doing now I requested to apprentice under him. I was accepted and became apprentice to Grand Master Smith Gotrek Firemane. While in training with him, he was performing\npowerful enchantments and while I stood by watching his work one enchantment was very powerful and the magic sepped into the silver trinkets I had forged and was toying with in my right hand. There was a flash of light and then dark. When I awoke my\nMaster was looking at my right arm and I beheld that iwas now, from the elbow down, made completely of silver. My master said he sensed magic in it and was going to study it further. That day I left my surname of Deepdelver behind. I was now Thrym\nSilverfist. \n\nThrough my time in Urguan, I have been here for the reign of two kings and am here for the reign of the third. The first was Belin the Industrious who made Kal'Urguan a jewel in Aegis again. Then ext was Algrim the Weak who\nwas a good king but weak and turned to evil. The King that is mi'lord now is Gotrek who was my master.\n\nLong Live the King!", ""),
        StaticBook("Life, and...", "Alan Witts", "[ Life, and its purpose ]\n\n[ By Alan Witts ]\n[ Introduction ]\n\nSince the beginning of mankind there has been one question that couldn’t be answered. A question that can’t, nor will ever be answered. The question is unanswered for one simple reason, and that is because it\ncan’t be answered. We will never be sure, never one hundred percent sure what the answer is. We can guess what is is, we can philosophize about it or decide what is if for ourselves, but never be sure.\n\nWe’ve all asked the question ourselves:\n“What is the purpose of life”. It is a question which is rhetorical and literal at the same time. I would love to answer the question for you, tell you what it is and be done with it, but honestly, I can’t. The only thing I can do is tell you what I\nbelieve our sole purpose is. I’ll tell you what my purpose is and stimulate you to philosophize about yours.\n[ Act I: The understanding of life ]\n\nBefore we ask ourselves what the purpose of life is, we should understand what life itself is. Being alive isn’t something we should take for granted, some see it as a blessing from the creator,\na gift from god or something scientifically. Whatever the reason or logic behind life itself is, of one thing we can be certain: that every life starts and ends the same. We are all born and we will all die, what happens in between those events is what\nwe call life. Life is living, but how you live that life is up to you.\n\nAs a free thinker I believe that life is an accident, but don’t get me wrong, it is an awfully great accident, but an accident nonetheless. I believe that our universe is made up out\nof particles, each particle is unique in its own way. Those particles interact, affect and react to each other. When two particles interact with each other they instantly affect one and other, and therefore react to each other. When two particles react to\neach other the reaction is always different, this is because all particles are unique and therefore have a unique reaction.\n\nAt a certain moment in time two particles on earth affected each other, they changed and connected to each other.\nThey created and destroyed others around them, and as a reaction of this confrontation a new particle was formed. This particle was just like all the other particles in the universe are; it was unique. This particular particle, which then again got\naffected by other particles was the beginning of life. The particle affected more and more particles, those particles then bonded and stayed connected to each other. This is when life on earth started to get serious. Those particles started to grow in\nlarge numbers, they started to multiply. Out of those particles formed atoms, out of those atoms formed cells, and out of those cells formed living organisms. Those organisms were the first form of life as we know it nowadays. It started to evolve\nand grow. More and more organisms started to form, they reacted to their surroundings and changed because of it. Some of them started to swim or eat, and after a long period of time even walk. Although there were plenty of organisms, they weren’t\nintelligent. At least, not until a certain day in our past: The day the first human being was born.\n[ Act II: Intelligent beings ]\n\nFor the past centuries organisms hadn’t been intelligent. With intelligent we mean an organism that is aware of itself: it knows that it exists. Intelligent beings can wonder, they can reason with each other and think\nabout the deeper meaning of things.\n\nHumans are an example of intelligent life. They can understand things that other organisms can’t. They ask questions like: “Why is the sky blue?” or “What is love?”. They not only reason with other\nbeings, but also with themselves. “Is it okay to hurt another person?” could be something they’d ask themselves, while other organisms would hurt each other just because it is in their instinct, to protect their offspring or kill other organisms for food.\nWhy do intelligent life forms wonder about being alive? Why does it matter to them? And if they find the answer, will it help them in anyway? Will it add something to their lives? The answer to that question is, sadly enough, probably nothing useful.\n[ Act III: The purpose of life ]\n\nWhen the answer to the question “What is the purpose of life?” wouldn’t add anything useful to our lives, then why do we still ask ourselves the question? For one simple reason: because we are alive,\nwe are living right now. You and I are breathing, thinking and above all else: we are wondering.\n\nSo what is the purpose of life? Life isn’t about being born and isn’t about dying. It is about the things that happen in between those events. I believe that\nwe’ve got one goal in life and that is to leave something behind. I think that if we create something or change something in this world our actions would live forever. Our actions are like a ripple effect. For example: that bird can’t feed his offspring,\nso they would die too. The fox living near the bird nest then in return couldn’t eat those birds in the future, because they would be dead long before he would find them. As a result the fox would also die. So by killing one bird, you’d kill a whole group\nof birds and a fox and who knows what more. As you can see anything you do has an effect on your surroundings. Most of the time the effect isn’t that obviously noticeable as in the example, but it is still there.\n\nIf our actions affect our surroundings\nand then again our surroundings react to that action, then we are not that different from the very particles that created life. We interact, affect and react. That fact doesn’t just make us very similar to particles, it makes us particles. In the end\nwe’re just organisms, made out of cells, those cells are made of out atoms which then again are made out of particles.\n\nSo this means that our sole purpose in life is just to live. We live because that is what we’re meant to do. And, I know that the\nanswer isn’t THAT exciting, but I believe that because the reason we are alive isn’t that interesting, it is up to us to make life worth living. We are capable of making our lives better, we can decide if we want to be cruel to someone or help them. It is\nup to us to decide if we want to enjoy the little things in life, or just not enjoy them.\n[ Act IV: The conclusion ]\n\nTherefore I say this to you, not only as the author of this writing but as a living being myself: Live life as if every day, hour, minute and second is your last. Don’t let anything small or useless ruin your day.\nIn the end you’ve only got one chance at life. So take this piece of advice and remember it for the rest of your days: you’d better not screw up.\n\n\n      [ The End ]", ""),
        StaticBook("Light And Dark", "Vorga'rag'Braduk", "The Sun high in the sky, Setting in the late. The darkness consumes the world untill the moon rises to light the earth once again. the cycle repeats, just like the cycle of life, Water runs, Trees grow, Wind blows. I age by the second never stopping such\nis life. Plants wilt, animals age. animals breed and plants spread seeds, aslong as there is someone or somthing to nurture and care for the saplings or babies then they will grow and they to will reproduce and before long there will be many\nfish and many plants.\nSuch is the life of a Druid, serving nature and keeping the balance of life and death in check.", ""),
        StaticBook("Light Illusion", "Corvo", "Illusion from what we know is the use of the void to create images into one’s mind. How this is done is simple infact, First one must connect to the endless realm that is the void, A realm of nothingness and at the same time the Void is everything\nwe so wish it to be. Now let us continue, With the use of the Void we as Illusionists are able to draw an image within it, Whether it be a small petal or that of a gigantic demon.  Once an Illusionist has done so they must simply connect to the mind\nof their opponent and place the image that they have made into their mind. Allowing them to see what you infact have seen.  However one must note that whatever you are to create you must have seen or experienced in your life,\nYou can simply create that of a demon however what is the point of you do not know how it sounds or feels.  One is of course able to make simple images from what they can think of in their own mind\nas well it is possible to simply add a feeling or sense to said image. Now in order to start learning such a power that is Illusion people tend to start the same as most Mages, Connection to the Void.\nTo do this one must simply empty their mind of all thoughts thus creating a link to the Void, this is mainly done through the simple means of mediation. However some are unlucky in their attempts to connect as some might be rejected from it.\nWhen one is rejected by the Void they may feel a small headache occur or even be knocked out from intense pain. Now once one has connected to the Void they simply draw an image in it and thus try to place that image into another entity's mind.\nSome at this stage tend to try and place the image into the mind’s of animals as an animal's mind is weak and far too stupid to even figure out that what they are seeing or feeling is an Illusion.\nOnce the simple sense of images has been completed Illusionists begin to head towards the Illusions of senses, Pain and touch. This is where some Illusionist find things to be tricky, As an Illusionist must feel and how what they are creating feels,\nthat intends one must be able to survive intense pain if they are so wishing to create it. To perform these sensations. it is simple they must simply draw the image of pain inside the Void and place it into that of their target.\nSimilar to how creating images of Light work. After the Illusionist has played with senses they may now head towards their end, The Illusion of emotions. This is quite hard to do in fact. To perform it they do the same as before,\nhowever it is much more difficult to perform as if one feels happy than angry the next moment it won’t make logical sense as they will know it is an Illusion and it shall break.  The simple way to do this is to ease the Illusion in silently,\nHow this works is if one was happy one second, it is quite easy to cause them to feel the emotion of love the next. This works quite well however from what we know emotions can not be forced upon the target only eased in.\nAs such we come to an end and now I leave the rest to you, The holder of this book. \n\n((For the Light Illusion Subtype))", ""),
        StaticBook("Lilly", "Caelria", "A small and beautiful lilly with lush, white petals and a vibrant green stem, seemingly plucked perfectly from the ground.\n\nThe lilly does not require water or sunlight, and will not wilt underground due to the series of enchantments residing within it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lily's Tale [1]", "Luxeanna Du Couteau", "Teh Tail Of\n\n        Teh Wulf\n\n            Nd\n\n        Teh Gazl\n\n\n          Bi: Lileh\n\n        Pt. 1 of 2\nThe Tale Of\n\n         The Wolf\n\n              &\n        The Gazelle\n\n          By: Lily\n    Recorded by:\nLuxeanna Du Couteau\n\n        Pt. 1 of 2\nIn the deepest part of the mainland, a forest exists that has gone untouched by man for all eternity. Here, animals and plants exist in a natural order, they way the great creators had intended.\nLiving a life of meaning and happiness. And here, is where our tale begins.\nThe animals of this forest lived in a serene community. Each one, from the birds and the rabbits, to the deer and the bears, had a place in this community and lived amongst each other in harmony.\nHowever, there was one beast that lived outside this circle- The Wolf. The wolf would live in its den, hidden by the shadows of the thick forest. Few animals ventured to the wolf’s den, and even fewer returned.\nAll the animals understood the order of nature, they understood that the wolf was cursed with its hunger for meat and flesh, and they did not hold it against it. However the wolf’s personality, his menacing look,\nand his lack of patience, often made the other animals flee in fear of it.\n\nOf the few animals that tried to reach out to the wolf, children were often among them. They would hear the stories of the wolf and wish to play with it.\nHowever, the wolf found the games the children wished to play tiresome and annoying. In the wolf’s rage, he lashed out at one, taunting it with the bones of animals it had eaten and scaring it away.\nIn another instance the wolf lost his temper when dealing with an arrogant youth, letting its sharp teeth wrap around the child’s neck. The stories of the wolf go on and on, and the entire forest knew of them.\nBut what they didn’t know about was how lonely the wolf felt. Cursed by his rage, his temper, his looks, and his hunger the wolf was destined to live alone until the end of its days, watching the other inhabitants of the forest laugh and play.\nThat was, until the Gazelle arrived. Easily standing out with its foreign appearance and behavior, the gazelle wandered into the forest from a far away land, one with different customs and things.\nThe animals of the forest welcomed the gazelle, trying to make the gazelle feel welcomed amongst their busy life. The gazelle smiled brightly and followed their directions, confused and unsure of their behaviors, but maintained a happy\npersonality to look like one of them. For the gazelle had come from a land of destruction and chaos. Fighting amongst the animals would happen daily and then Man found its way into their home, obliterating it.\nThe gazelle was alone, lost and confused and simply wished to find a new family, but at the same time, desperately missed her own.\n\nAs the animals celebrated the gazelle’s welcome, the wolf slinked onto the edge of the festivities, carefully watching her.\nThe animals of the forest were celebrating amongst each other, eating berries and drinking honey, but the gazelle sat by herself. Although the festivities were for her, she felt like an outcast and was left\nby herself, the other animals unaware of her feelings because of the happy smile she wore at all times. But the wolf could smell the gazelle’s true feelings. Fear. Desperation. Terror.\nAll smells that the wolf had come accustomed to when smelling its prey now greeted him in the middle of a happy festival, and all were coming off so pungently from this new comer.\nThe gazelle graciously smiled to the animals as they celebrated, but as soon as they had turned to take another bite of blackberry, she ran. She dashed through the trees and lept over the logs, trying to get away. The sounds of the festival slipped away\nbehind her as she ran, but the thudding of paws greeted her. In a clearing the wolf leapt from the shadows of the trees and circled the gazelle slowly. The wolf questioned the gazelle as to why she left the party so soon\nand was surprised when she answered thatshe preferred to be alone sometimes. The wolf inquired about the gazelle, and as she told him the story of her homes fall and her travels, the wolf realized that the smellsof fear and desperationwere drifting away.\nThe gazelle followed the wolf back to his den, far from the other animals of the forest, in the quiet depths of the forest. She asked the wolf questions about the animals here, and the wolf answered her questions honestly.\nHe told her how the animals would squabble over who had the tastiest walnuts, how they had ridiculous dances, and were always full of energy, never resting.The gazelle laughed at many of the wolf’s stories, finding a comfort in the honesty and help.\nThe wolf’s den was also a comfort to the gazelle. Unlike the fancy burrows of the animals, the den remained natural in the depths of the forest, reminding her of her home.\nAs the days passed, the gazelle would often stop by the wolf’s den to take a break from the busy life of the forest animals.\nOther days the wolf would meet the gazelle at the crystal pond for some water. The other animals at first would scatter, hiding behind the trees and roots, but soon saw how the wolf would sit by the gazelle and drink peacefully.\nWith a few recurrences, the animals no longer feared the wolf when he came to drink and welcomed him when he went to festivities with the gazelle. The animals noticed how much tamer the wolf was around the gazelle and were happy at this.\nBut they wondered how much the gazelle really knew about the wolf, and the dance with death she could possibly be playing.\nIt was decided amongst the animals that the gazelle must become aware of the wolf’s curse and his past. The animals debated about ways to separate the gazelle from the wolf to speak to her about the issues, but it wasn’t decided until\nan old turtle crept into the center of the discussion. The turtle spoke slowly, stating that while the concern for the newcomer warmed her old heart, she implores the community to not forget that the wolf has feelings too.\nThe wolf should be allowed to explain himself to the gazelle, and let his case be made known by himself, and not spoken of behind his back. The animals listened to the wise turtles words and agreed,so the following day their plan was put into action.\nThe field mice went to the gazelle, asking for her aide in knocking some berries from a small tree. With the gazelle away, the bear approached the wolf, for surely he was the safest of the animals should the wolf become angered.\nThe bear asked the wolf for its feelings about the gazelle, and for the first time that the wolf could remember saying, he said she made him happy. The bear smiled at this and informed the wolf that all of the animals wanted the wolf to be happy,\nbut they wanted the gazelle to be safe. The wolf stood up and declared that he too wanted her to be safe and would defend her from anything. The bear simply stared at the wolf and asked him how he would defend her from himself.\nThe wolf could not respond, realizing the bears words. The bear urged him to speak to the gazelle about his past before she finds out on her own and to let her make a decision on what to do.\nThe wolf thought long and hard about what to do, whether to hide his past and his curse, hoping for the best, or to be honest with the gazelle. \nThe gazelle approached the wolf’s den, excited to tell him about the trip she had taken with the field mice and the berries she had found, but the wolf was sullen and silent.\nWhen the gazelle nudged the wolf he became serious in a manner that she had never experienced before.The wolf told her of his curse. He told her of his rage, how he taunted and murdered the young animals of the forest.\nHe told her more stories existed, some even worse than the ones he had revealed, but could not say what he had done.But he looked to the gazelle and with honest eyes told her that her presence quenched the thirst he had,\nit quieted the rage, and dampened his temper. He told the gazelle about how happy she had made him, and felt like he had a meaning in life once more, to live and protect her.\nThe wolf became silent, looking at the gazelle for a sign of her acceptance, anything at all.\n\n But a tear fell from her eye and she ran away from the wolf.\nHe chased after her, calling after her to come back, to be with him, but the gazelle sprinted away, leaving the wolf in its tracks, fleeing from the forest.\nAs the days went on, the animals of the forest talked amongst themselves in whispers. They had seen the gazelle flee the forest, but they had not seen the wolf at the pond to drink.\nNone of the animals reported seeing the wolf stalk its food either, and they became concerned. The bear walked to the wolf’s den and found him sitting in the deep reaches of it, hidden by the shadows.\nThe wolf refused to speak to the bear, but the bear could tell that the wolf was dying. Not only from a lack of water and food, but it felt like the wolf’s spirit, one that would be intimidating to even the bear, was gone, drained from its body.\nThe animals feared they had done this to the wolf, that they would be the cause of the wolf’s death for scaring away the gazelle. They began blaming each other, the field mice pointing fingers at the briar rabbits, the birds ridiculing the deer.\n. But the old turtle sat on her stone quietly, looking into the forest, looking at something. Eventually the animals noticed the old turtle smiling and looked to see what was making the old girl happy at a time like this.\nLight filtered through the trees and a shadow moved slowly, overly cautious and unsure. \nThe gazelle walked slowly through the forest, past the animals that stared at it silently, towards the wolf’s den. The wolf crawled out of its den slowly, limping and shuffling through the hole before laying on the ground at the dens opening.\nThe gazelle kneeled down and looked at the wolf, withered and dying. The wolf smiled lightly between coughs, amazed that she had came back.\n\n“Yo-You came back….” the wolf sputtered between short breaths.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lily's Tale [2]", "Luxeanna Du Couteau", "The gazelle nuzzled against the wolf, “Of course, Of course I came back.” She could feel the wolf’s bones through its thin and sickly skin. “Oh if only I had gotten here sooner….”\nThe wolf closed his eyes, “Maybe it’s better-it’s better this way.”\n\n“Don’t talk like that. You’ll be alright,” the gazelle lied, trying to hold back her tears, “We’re together now, everything will be fine, you’ll see.\"\nThe wolf opened his eyes slowly and smiled, nuzzling the gazelle. “At-At least I got to see you….one last time.”\n\nWith this the last breath of the wolf escaped its mouth and his eyes closed.\nThe gazelle nudged the wolf as her tears flowed, “N-no….No...Please, you can’t…..please don’t leave me….”\nThe animals of the forest looked on in sadness, their hearts sunken low. It felt as if the wolf’s death, a part of the forest had died as well, and all of the animals could feel the loss the gazelle was feeling.\nThe gazelle nuzzled against the wolf as her tears fell on him, muttering softly, “I love you.”\nWith these words, her tears glistened brightly and touched the wolf’s body. Behind the forest animals, a green light shined so bright that it at first blinded them as they turned around. As their eyes adjusted, they gasped in amazement.\nThe old turtle that sat on the stone was the source of the light, and as they looked on, they watched the turtle transform. Soon, where the turtle once sat a shimmering Wood Elf sat.\nThe animals looked on in both fear and amazement, but the Elf spoke to them.\n“Fear not my friends. I am not here to harm you,” the elf announced, “For all eternity I have been assigned to ensure that the veil that protects this forest remained intact, protecting the life within, and its meaning.\"\nThe druid stood and walked over to the animals slowly, “The family you created here amongst each other, this is what our creators tried to have throughout the world, but it has failed in many, many places.\nBut you succeeded. Your love for one another, it stands the test of time, it stands against the evils of this world, and it will keep all of you together.”\nThe druid would make its way over to the gazelle, who had been staring at the wolf this entire time, and carefully lifted her face.\n“And you, one who knows loss more than anyone here, you were able to find companionship…..you were able to find love, where others saw fear.”\nThe druid would smile and caress the gazelle’s face, “And your love will stand the test of time, young one.”\nWith this the forest glowed brightly, the trees swayed, and the grass blew swiftly. The wolf’s body was lifted with the wind and spun as the light entered its body. With a blinding light, the wolf was set down, not on its side, but on its paws.\nThe wolf stood on its own, opening its eyes, and looking amazed. The gazelle rushed to the wolf, nuzzling him and he her.\n“You two, your love will defend not just each other, but all of those you love,” the druid said as it slowly began to fade from view, its being disappearing into the wind.\nWith the druid’s disappearance, the animals and the forest remained hidden in peace,  guarded against the evils of the world by the wolf and gazelle for the rest of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("List of ur mates", "Shalashask", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Little bunnies", "Vhesina Thaorihle", "A hungry bunny once found the vegetable garden of a rich man who never, never, never ate vegetables. So the hungry bunny ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then he went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the hungry bunny brought another bunny and then there were two hungry bunnies. They each ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the two hungry bunnies brought another hungry bunny and then there were three hungry bunnies. Each ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the three bunnies brought another bunny and then there were four hungry bunnies. They all ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the four bunnies brought another bunny and then there were five hungry bunnies. They all ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the five bunnies brought another bunny and then there were six hungry bunnies. They all ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the rich man who never, never, never ate vegetables wondered what happened to his vegetables garden. He never guessed the six hungry bunnies hiding behind the fence ate his cabbages, his lettuce and carrots. But we know better do we not!", ""),
        StaticBook("Little Dove", "Phaedrus", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nMountains may round to hills, rivers may descend into canyons,\n\nLong winters may fade into windy chills, yet despite all that time, I would never find a better companion,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nSoft whispers that tickle my ear, softer lips that soothe my skin, \n\nHer touch pierces me like a spear, replacing love where fear had once been,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nShe is the tinder to my spark, the hammer to my blade, \n\nMy source of light within the dark, the reason I have remained,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nThe trees move with the wave of her hands, the grass sways with the rock of her hips, \n\nThe wind tosses her hair in curly red strands, skin warm as sand against my fingertips,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nHer words are sweet and ease my mind, make me smile and laugh and experience love, \n\nMy hope is these words answer hers in kind, for these words are for my little dove,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n      To the love \n       of my life,\n         Elorna\n\n\n\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=", ""),
        StaticBook("Little Red Bird", "Kikira Irelia", "-=:@:=-\n   The Little Red Bird\n          -=:@:=-\n\n\n    \n\n      A short poem.\n        \n\n\n\nby: K.I.\nThe Little Red Bird\n___________________ \nThe little red bird was left behind.\n\nThe little red bird stayed and died.\n\nHe died in the snow where the cruelest winds blow.\nBut his spirit still flies up high the skies.\n\nDon't worry, it's not all bad but really it's quiet sad.\n\nThat he lies where no man goes in the coldest of snows.", ""),
        StaticBook("Live to Farm", "Benjamin Greenweed", "Live to Farm\n\n\nThe Secret to Life and to True Happiness\n\n\n\nWritten by Benjamin Greenweed\n-----------\nIntroduction\n-----------\nAs a halfling, I have always lived with the philosophy that farming is the way of the world and that we all farm in order to live. The pursuit of Mina is meaningless by comparison to a fine life in the fields. But I\nhave realized a fatal flaw in this philosophy: it doesn't say why we live. I found the purpose of life, however, and have written this guide to life in order to teach it to all. The pursuit of Mina and trying to survive is futile, and will only lead to\nsadness; we must not farm to live, but we actually live to farm. This book will teach you the way of the farmer and how you can truly be happy in life, not living a futile and foolish life. I don't want that for you and you probably don't want it either.\nIf you accept the truth, this book will teach you the keys to happiness, all rooting out of farming and nature.\n\n-Benjåmin\n19th of The First Seed, 1545\n----\nSins\n----\nYou may think it seems unfair to start out with the sins of this philosophy, and don't get me wrong when I say I do not desire to fall to the selfish fate of the Canon. However, I want to start by saying what most of humanity\ndoes wrong that leads our society to sadness and never to peace and happiness.\n\n1) Mina. Well, any currency we are using means the same. Mina leads to greed and corruption. The pursuit of Mina is a greedy pursuit and foolish. If you spend your life\npursuing gold or Mina, like the dwarves, you will never be satisfied.\n\n2) Surplus. Though many see surplus as a positive thing, it is overall a negative thng. I have designed a type of ritual in response to this I will explain later. For now though, I\nwill say that surplus is a form of greed and worthless. To have surplus is to have too much. If you have surplus, you should give to others. Once all have what they need, the surplus should be destroyed. This is just another form of greed.\n\n3) War. I am\nnot perfect. I will admit I have commited crimes, and even encouraged violence. However, I think these are corrupting ideals. If another bothers you, you should just no that inside they are not happy. The pursuit of war and conquering is foolish, greedy,\nand violent. The truly happy are inclusive and nonviolent.\n\n4) Government. While many feel law and structure is a positive thing, bad policy and law angers the people, while the government itself is often corrupt. Despite what many would say, people would\nbe happier in total anarchy. This is what puts me apart from groups like the Druids; I believe power structures of any kind are corrupt.\n\n5) Dishonesty with yourself. Happy people can lie to others, though I don't suggest it. However, lying to oneself\nleads to utter sadness and despair. You must always know yourself and be truthful with yourself in order to be truly happy.\n-----\nSteps\n-----\n1) Renounce your government, nation, and property.\n\n2) Settle in farmland, often regulated by yourself and it should ideally be.\n\n3) Live in modesty, with as little as you need\nto survive.\n\n4) Spend your days farming, and your nights sleeping.\n\n5) Have a family, a spouse, and children. Encourage them to spread the philosophy. Sex is natural and encouraged. Bonding is important.\n6) Read the chant at the end of this book daily.\n\n7) Complete the rituals listed here and possibly in future volumes.\n\n8) Spread the philosophy.\n------\nRituals\n------\n1) Destroying Surplus\n\nIf you do end up with a surplus, which often happens when you spend a long day farming, complete one of these rituals. The first is giving to the poor. Travel from your land, even into\nthe land of enemies, and give your goods and foods to those who need it most. The second, when you have no one to give to, is the fire ritual. Go above a flame and release your surplus into it. Make sure to recite the following:\nBEST LIVE TO FARM.\n2) Weddings.\n\nIt is likely you will have a wedding while being a follower of this philosophy, so this is the proper way to do it philosophically. We do not judge whether you marry a man or a woman, despite your gender. All marriages and all sex is equal\nin peace.\n\nWeddings should occur in the fields. Go to the center of your best field of crops, and carve out a hole filled with water (if one isn't already there). Stand in it annd recite these vows. There are two types of spouses, and those\ndeemed to be each will recite each type. There is the MUSHROOM, the strong and more angry and proud. The other is the CARROT, the weaker and wiser.\n\nMUSHROOM: I swear I shall stay true to you. I shall lay in bed with you and stand awake with you.\nCARROT: I shall be by your side, both in bed and elsewhere. I swear it shall be true.\n\nMUSHROOM: You shall be all in my head besides the crops.\n\nCARROT: And you too shall stand as a constant in my brain and I am happy to be in yours.\nMUSHROOM: I take you as my spouse.\n\nCARROT: And I take you as mine.\n\nAfter these vows, the pair should hug calmly. Often, there will be a party, but usually the couple should go home to bed. Vacations after marriage distract from the\nfields.\n3) Funerals\n\nWe all must eventually bury our dead. However, there is a special ceremony in our philosophy. The person should be buried under their favorite crop and family should come, putting drops of water onto the grave and saying words. At the\nend, the person they were closest to (usually their spouse or child), will say these words.\n\nCLOSEST PERSON: You have now returned to the earth, where you yourself shall help us farm without having to work.\n\nAfter this, their body\nwill become part of the soil and assist in the farming and crops.\n----------\nDaily Words\n----------\nSay these words before you sleep, or after a workday. They should be said every day to be truly happy and at peace.\n\nI AM PEACEFUL\nI DO NOT FARM TO LIVE\nI LIVE TO FARM\nI AM THE FARMER\nI AM HAPPY\nI AM HONEST WITH MYSELF\nI DO NOT CAUSE WAR\nI FALL TO NOBODY\nI AM PEACEFUL\nI LIVE TO FARM", ""),
        StaticBook("Logs", "Sarrion", "\"A Sellsword Company\"\nLogs Book Chapter One\n-Sarrion\n\nCreated-\n2nd of the Grand Harvest\n1513\n-Sarrion\n\nJoined-\n4th of the Grand Harvest\n1513\nBjael Alrikson:SK=Lumber\n-Sarrion\nJoined-\n6th of The Grand Harvest\n1513\nCole deGray:SK=Farm/Mine\n-Sarrion\n\nJoined-\n7th of The Grand Harvest\n1513", ""),
        StaticBook("Lonely Fisherman", "Arthur Caulfield", "The Lonely\n         Fisherman\n\n   A short literary\n        Piece\n\"Now I don't know a whole lot about fishing,\" he confesses. \"For twenty long years been trying. They don't even notice when I cast my line into the water.\" \n    The fisherman sat alone on a boat, in the middle of a dark blue ocean that said nothing back.\n\"My bait must be cheap,\" he muttered. \"Must be me bait.\" His face scrunched up in thought. \n   His hair had started to grey, his wrinkles had become more defined. Each day it became harder to get out of bed, though he did not blame this on age.\nAfter a while the water began to ripple. Soon it gently rocked the side of his boat in waves. \n   Looking up the fisherman found another, just like him. He waved to the man in a friendly manner but was ignored.\n   Curious, the fisherman watched.\nThe man in the other boat threw his line in after a few minutes of preperation, and within seconds had caught a fish. \n   \"How unfair,\" the old man mumbled. \"Been fishing in these ponds for years and ain't caught a damn thing.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Looking Up", "Laura", "Looking Up\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        -Laura\nThis is a tale about a badger, a badger named Sebastian. Sebastian lived in a hole in the ground, where he always looked down. And although some creatures might think that kind of life depressing, Sebastian relished every moment the familiar soil was\nabove his head. But then one day, something quite odd happened. As Sebastian awoke from a short nap, he noticed his family had up and left the hole. He roamed about the hole many times over, in search of his family, without a trace. Completely puzzled, he\nstared at the exit to the hole for a long time, before finally deciding to crawl hesitantly to the surface. Once he arrived, he looked about, spotting his family in a cluster near some flowers, all looking up. Sebastian meandered over to them, asking them\nas to why they left the hole. Sebastian's mother looked at him with starry eyes, and pointed up to the sky. Sebastian, having lived underground his entire life, had never thought to look up; once he did, he knew why his family had left the hole. He saw\nfor the first time the starry night, with the moon in the sky. The sight rendered Sebastian strucken with its beauty, and he remained there with his family until the break of dawn, where they found a modest abode above the soil, and Sebastian never looked\ndown again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lorem Ipsum", "Leyu", "Lorem Ipsum\nsit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Mauris odio odio, bibendum vitae rhoncus eget, aliquet vitae turpis. Phasellus varius orci nec libero iaculis eget tristique arcu porttitor. Praesent vitae tincidunt leo. Mauris fringilla tempus leo ut blandit.\nInteger ut feugiat tortor. Morbi commodo arcu vel orci varius pulvinar. Donec placerat aliquet erat eget luctus. In hachabitasse platea dictumst. Nam eu neque tellus. Class aptent taciti sociosqu ad litor torquent per conubia nostra,\nper inceptos himenaeos. Aenean nisi massa, gravida pharetra sagittis quis, tempor et enim. Aliquam erat volutpat. Proin mollis, ligula sit amet dignissim laoreet, dolor lorem sollicitudin nibh, non pretium magna nisl eu dui. Morbi sit amet\nmi felis, non sagittis tellus. Nam ac ligula nunc, in euismod massa.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Losing a Hand", "Henry Winterleaf", "The following is the story of an injury that I have lived with for a long time and how it happened in the first place.\nIt all started back in Asulon as I was leaving the cloud temple one day. I had just left the borders of the temple lands where I stumbled across a band of pirates attempting to rob two young girls.\nTheir leader, a dark elf man, told me not\nto get involved or else. However, I stepped in anyway, hoping to see off these pirates. I found myself completely outmatched against these four pirates on my own. I managed to distract them enough for the girls to escape but I was\nseverly wounded in the fight. I had lost part of my left arm from just below the elbow down. I was unable to retrieve the cut-off piece so I was unable to heal it back together at the temple, as I have been told is possible. So, for many years I made\ndo the best I could.\nI wore a metal hand for many years as a replacement.\n\nHowever, recently I met an alchemist named Beros who made a potion that would regrow my arm. I have been using the potion for a while and it seems to be working.\nIt feels weird to me that, for the first time in years, I will have two working hands again.\n\nThe process is long and expensive but for me it says a lot about the powers of alchemy. So, if there's one lesson you take away from this book, make it this...\nDon't fuck with alchemists.\n\nOr pirates.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost and Found", "Shiloh Ellis", "[!]There's a poem wrapped around a tree, starting from the root and working upwards.\n\n       Lost and Found\n\nIn the spring, I'd found myself lost\n\ntrekking through sodden grasses and\n\nin-between the wildflowers\nshining in the dew of the morning.\n\nThe fields turned to forests,\nthe forests to hills,\nhills into waterfalls.\n\nIn the summer, I'd found myself lost\n\namong the discussions between the pensive lakes and babbling brooks.\nThis time I'd meant to bring another,\n\nbut they weren't fond of getting lost.\n\nIn the fall, I'd lost my way\n\nin a dark field on a starless night. \n\nAnother lost traveler like me showed me how\nto return to the vibrant forests.\n\nIn the winter,\n\nI knew where I was\n\nand I was no longer\n\nalone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost letters, ??", "Unknown", "An unsigned letter, written in careful hand. It seems to be a copy of the original.\nYou are correct in your analysis of the Guild's founding principles, and so I must congratulate you on answering an unasked question any initiated apprentice is\nrequired to know. Bravo.\nOf course it was likely possible for you to answer as you did without touching upon sore wounds. While you answered that elementary question correctly I am afraid you are quite incorrect about nearly\nelse. To start, no. The Arcane does not visit frequently and if we must be open and honest, as good peers should be, I will admit I have not seen him in quite some time, and likely I saw him last the same place you did; The gathering at the Tower.\nHe has not provided me with any alternate methods of accessing the Archives without his presence, and even had he, I would most certainly not make it available to one such as yourself. I know where your politics align you. As said,\nas such I will admit to my knowledge, and share it with you, in accordance with the Guild's purpose.\nI know you are the reason the gathering was held, and the reason for the ever-growing schism which forms within and throughout the Guild. The\nof it is on the tongue of every apprentice as far west as Jylhied, and as far east as Rynak. It is a thing impossible to quiet, even in whispers, and it brings forth ill will towards the Guild, to have so many murmuring of such a sensitive\nsubject. It has gotten so bad, an apprentice in Rynak was killed by one of the native Uruks, simply for he overheard the apprentice murmur the name.\nYou and yours tread upon a sensitive subject, one which the Arcane\nto put to rest with the gathering. One which should have been put to rest.\nIf we are going to touch further upon the ideals of the Guild, especially the very same of mutual shared research and knowledge, then perhaps we should discuss your\noffenses against those principles? Need I remind you that all you have discovered of this Dworkin, including his supposed tomb and your subsequent robbing of it, you have failed to share with the rest of the Guild? That book you stole belongs in\nthe Archives you so dearly wish to access.\nPerhaps if you agree to put it in it's rightful place, the Arcane may be willing to allow you access.", ""),
