        StaticBook("Love Study: I", "Hileia'elr", "Love Study: I\n----------------\n\nStudies on Love and Affection, Volume 1:\n\nIntroduction to Love\n\n-Hileia'elr\nI assume you picked up this book because you wanted to learn about the capacity for care, love, and affection that our minds have. Writing a book on the topic is easier said than done, of course.\nUnlike other sciences and studies, love is something that isn't entirely observable to our eyes. Love's roots run much deeper than a material, observable, object.\nFirst, I myself write romance novels for a living. You may have read my novels before, or you may very well not have. Either way, I write about the connection between two people because I believe it's our strongest emotion.\nDefining Love:\n\nBefore we investigate what's possibly our deepest emotion, we do have to understand what it is. Really, this should be quite easy to do, yet some people overthink it.\nLove is simply the attraction that one individual has to another, and the other may or may not return the feelings. \n\nNow, keep in mind that I'm talking about all types of love.\nWhen you hear, 'Love,' you most likely think of the romantic kind. We have to realize through this series that love comes in different shapes and forms, and doesn't have to be romantic. Love can just be affection and care.\nHowever, during this series, I will be focusing primarily on romantic love, as that is the most globally recognized form of, 'Love.' Although, we will take a glance at the other varieties of love as well, which will be covered in a later volume.\nSo, what is the definition of love? While most think that this should be a complicated answer, really, it's just the special bond between two people with a positive connection.\nTo define love itself is easy. However, what is complicated is defining the purpose, or the need to love someone or something. It's like life, we can easily describe what it is, but not why it is. So, we'll take a look at that now.\nWhy do we love:\n\nThis is the harder of two questions to answer. We cannot pinpoint the exact reason that we love, other than that we want to love. As living creatures, it is instinct.\nLove is programmed into our genetic code, and it forces us to carry out that code, causing us to seek out another individual who will both accept and return that feeling. So one answer to our question is because; We're designed to.\nAlthough, with that being said, it cannot be the only reason. Other studies have proven that, someone who is raised with food, water, shelter, and other necesities for life, still can't survive without some type of love.\nSo physically, our bodies need love to go on, to survive. Love itself is a need for survival. One cannot live without it, and will die if they do not receive some type of affection or care. To recap, we need love for several reasons.\nThe first reason we love is because we want to love, and because we need to love. We love because that's what we're meant to do, and we love because if we don't, we'll suffer without it.\nSo if we can define love, get at least an idea of love's purpose, and why we love in the first place, what else is there to ask? In reality, that's the base of it, but we can go much further than that...\nThe rest of your questions we'll look into are mostly about physical needs and the standards set for dating, love, and marriage in different societies.\nWhat age is appropriate to start \"Loving\" someone:\n\nReally, this all depends on your opinion of when someone should start, 'dating.' However, there are set guidlines in some cultures.\nFor instance, an older teenager who's about to become an adult in a few years might consider dating, with their parent's permission. They may not be an adult, but they could be old enough to date.\nAlthough, in other societies, it's expected that you get involved in romantic activities AFTER adulthood hits. For instance, in High Elven culture, where 50 is considered to be an 'adult,' it is not encouraged to date before that age.\nBut whatever the case, older or younger than adulthood, it seems that becoming an adult in all societies is also the line which you cross into the romantic world. In short, the answer to this question, is when you're an adult.\nOf course, that's quite a short and incomplete answer to give. Other variables have to be considered when factoring in 'Adulthood.' The definition of adulthood itself varies, too.\nDo you want to consider someone an adult when they reach the valid age, or consider them an adult when their attitude and personality has matured as well? So really, it's a combonation of age and maturity.\nThis is the end of volume one. In volume two, we'll be classifying different types of love, or different ways love can be expressed among other people.\nI do hope whoever is reading this book has enjoyed it, as I plan to conduct a full study on the subject, and also plan to publish every research paper I create.\nUntil next volume, loyal reader!\n\n~ Hileia'elr", ""),
        StaticBook("Love Study: II", "Hileia'elr", "Love Study: II\n----------------Studies on Love and Affection, Volume 2:\n\nClassifying different forms of Love\n\n-Hileia'elr\nIn this volume, we will expand on the idea that there is not only one, but many ways you can classify love. As mentioned in the previous volume, we will be focusing mainly on romantic love.\nIn this volume, we will stray away from exploring 'Romance,' and rather dive deeper into the idea that love can be something other than such. So, we'll start by defining romantic love, then move on to some other subjects.\nRomantic Love:\n\nRomantic love is most likely what anyone thinks when talking about 'love' in general. Love is often linked to marriage, dating, and so on. Love can refer to any form of love, but is often thought of as romance.\nThe simplest way to think of romantic love, is simply the positive bond and relationship between two people, most commonly a man and a woman. Acts of romantic love often involves dating and kissing eachother.\nIf the two individuals feel so strongly of eachother, they can participate in marriage, or whatever the equivalent in a selected society. Marriage is a physical representation of two people's romantic bond.\nMore often than not a ceremony, marriage will show that both persons are willing to spend the rest of their existance together, and believe that they are compatible enough to exchange acts of love for years to come.\nParental Love:\n\nParental love is also what could be commonly thought of as 'love' in general. Parental love is the bond between the two individuals who gave birth to a child, and the child themself.\nAs I mentioned in the previous volume, our bodies and minds are designed in a way that they actually want to feel affection for others. The same concept can be applied to the connection between a parent and child.\nThe child will recognize each parent as someone who is automatically someone they should look up to, trust, rely on, and love. The same is true for the parents, as they have a special bond with their child.\nAs a parent, giving birth to a child means that the parent has participated in the creation and existance of their child, and does often feel responsible for them. Simply knowing that you've helped continue the\ncycle of life, and that you've helped continue the existance and expand the population of your race, is a feeling strong enough to believe that you are, again, fully responsible for the organism that you've brought into this world.\nSibling Love:\n\nOften reffered to as something along the lines of 'Brotherly Love,' love between siblings is something similar to parental love, seeing as both parents and the offspring are part of a primary kinship.\nThe bond between either a brother or sister is strong, as you both come from the same origin. The same two people created you, and brought you into existance.\nJust as your parents should feel responsible for you, a sibling should feel responsible for their brother or sister, and vice versa. All these relationships have existed since birth, and is, again, designed into our own minds.\nHowever, love between siblings isn't always pretty. In most families, siblings will grow up under the same roof at a young age, and will most likely, at one point or another, grow tired of eachother. Fights and arguments will break loose.\nThe most common battles between siblings are competitive, usually to prove to either friends or family which one of them is 'better.' Siblings also fight over territory. When you live in such a small house, it can get cramped.\nThat's why two brothers, two sisters, or a brother and sister will argue over who claims what in the house or family. Or, maybe one is simply annoyed by the actions and habits of the other.\nNone the less, the love between the two is designed to overcome any differences they might have. That is what's special about the relationship between siblings, the ability to forgive eachother so easily.\nThe ability to easily forgive after a fight or argument is something no other form of love has. Of course, anyone has the capacity for forgivness, but between siblings, it's especially easy.\nLove among extended family members:\n\nYour extended family includes people such as your grandparents, grandchildren, cousins and so forth. You may or may not be as close to them as your parents, siblings, or spouse.\nHowever, there is still always a bond that exists between you and every family member you have. If you live with your cousin, for instance, your relationship is likely to be much stronger than if you were apart.\nBut if that cousin does live further away, and you only see them every so often, your relationship is likely to be much weaker. Reguardless, there is still something that is triggered in our minds that tell us that this is someone close to us.\nEven if it's your first time ever meeting, when you're told that you two are related, another mechanism is instantly activated within the mind. A connection, right then and there, is formed, another bond that can't be broken.\nOvertime, you may not enjoy the company of that relative, yes, but the bond is still there, weak or strong. This bond can never be broken, and is, again, designed to exist until death.\nRelationships with friends (Or pets):\n\nI wouldn't exactly call the relationship with your friends 'Love,' but there is no doubt that a strong link exists between two people who enjoy talking and being with eachother.\nOften called a 'Friendship' for obvious reasons, the conenction between two friends can still be as strong as that with a family member- Or stronger. The idea of having a friend is that the certain individual you're friends with\nis always there to protect, compfort, give advice to, assist, and in general have fun with you. Of course, with friends, there is no everlasting bond. The chain can easily be cut off in most situations.\nHowever, that friendship could also be very strong, and hard to cut off, but it all depends on the two and their effort to maintain the relationship. Just as our need for love is designed into our minds, so is the need for friends.\nThe difference between a relationship in your family, and the relationship with your friends, is that there is no bond, as stated before, and you both have to put in equal effort to maintain that relationship.\nIf your friend runs errands for you, or any work for you at all, and you do nothing in return, that friendship is more likely to be cut off. Remember, while there is a bond between friends, there is no permanant bond.\nThe same can easily go for your pet, an animal companion. While the bond isn't identical, a bond between an 'intelligent' being and an animal can still have the same concepts of friendship applied.\nSuch as friendships, there is no permanant bond, and can be broken. The concept of returning the favor can also be put into place. Usually, a dog will protect their 'Master' in exchange for food, water, and shelter.\nThis is the end of volume two. I recieved some feedback from several people whom read volume one, and I believe that I'm using terms that not everyone would fully understand.\nIn future volumes, I will attempt to either use more simple terminology, or explain myself with many details so that the reader may understand what I'm reffering to.\nIn volume three, we'll be returning to romantic love, and research how love at first sight works, and how the mind decides what physical features we're attracted to. Until next time, loyal reader.\n\n~Hileia'elr", ""),
        StaticBook("Love Study: III", "Hileia'elr", "Love Study: III\n----------------Studies on Love and Affection, Volume 3:\n\nPhysical attraction\n\n-Hileia'elr\nAs we dig deeper into researching this emotion, tucked away in the corners of our minds, it had crossed my mind- Why do we feel a passion for people with different physical features, or certain personality traits?\nIs there some mechanism in our minds that's triggered when we see someone with features we like? Or is there a set pattern, to seek out the individuals with our preffered physical details?\nInvestigating this feeling even more, we will discover what exactly makes us 'tick.' What is it that captivates us so much, that we're lured into attempting to keep another person for our own?\nThere are so many questions to ask, and so many answers that can be provided. What interests me the most is why not every individual is attracted to the same exact features that everyone else is...\nDifferences in attraction:\n\nFor whatever the reason, not everyone is attracted to the same details or features that others of the same species, gender, and age posess.\nFor example, there could be a 50 year old, Highlander man that is attracted to farfolk women, and another 50 year old Highlander man who's into elves.\nThese are two men that are the same age, gender, race, and come from extremely similar origins- Yet their taste in women is awfully different. Should they not fancy the same type of lady?\nEven with these two men living extremely similar lives, there are small signals within our mind that are triggered, switches that are flipped, that are caused by small, trivial events within each person's life.\nReturning to the two Highlanders example- Perhaps when our first Highlander was younger, he witnessed a beautiful farfolk girl simply walking down the street near his home. He hadn't thought anything of it, he just saw her.\nNow, on the other side of that street lives our other example. At the exact same time, he sees a wonderful, majestic High Elven girl, just passing through. He's paying too much attention to her to even notice the farfolk girl nearby.\nNeither men thought anything of these encounters, as they hadn't even talked to either girl at all, and they would never see them again in their lives- But just because of how beautiful they were, that's enough to begin\ntriggering and creating a brand new signal within each of the Highlander's minds. The situation doesn't have to be exactly as the one I gave, maybe not even remotely close. But it shows how something so small and trivial can have a large impact.\nA whole other possibility is that family members influence what an individual is attracted to. Certain people will find compfort in being with someone similar to their normal surroundings when creating such a strong bond.\nIt's entirely possible, that, a man would be attracted to the same features that runs in his bloodline. If he comes from a family of mostly brown hair, even if he himself doesn't have brown hair, he may find it easier to date a girl with brown hair.\nBut then, of course, all these theories could just not apply in some cases, as a man or woman is impacted by the society they've grown up in, and are taught to be attracted to a specific group of people, with specific traits.\nSo really, the reason we're all attracted to different features is a combonation of trivial events from when we were younger, who we feel safer around, and what the enviroment around us has taught us to be attracted to.\nCommon 'Attractive' Features:\n\nAs they say, \"Beauty is in the eye of the beholder.\" However, there are still features that are commonly thought of as, 'Beautiful.'\nWhen asked, there seemed to be a very steady pattern, based off of gender and race. Men seemed to be attracted to girls with a smaller figure, longer hair, and big eyes.\nFemales seemed to generally be attracted to stronger, taller men, a nicely chisled chin, and in some cases, a well groomed beard was a must. Of course, as mentioned before, you must account for many factors.\nWith absoluetly every person you ask, there will be at least one difference in their taste for a lifemate. Two people could be attracted to the same person, however there's always a difference in people's 'Ideal partner.'\nLove at first Sight:\n\nTo some, love at first sight could make for a heart warming, romantic story. Certain people believe love at first sight to be the most pure and true sign of love.\nHowever, there are others who would be much happier thinking that this, 'Love at first sight' is ridiculous and impossible. All parties have valid evidence to support what it means to love at your first glance of another individual.\nFor instance, some would be excused to think that real life would turn out such as that in a story book. It would be nice to think that you could determine your one true love just by looking at them.\nUnfortunatley, this is not the case at all. As mentioned in previous volumes, 'Love' is defined as the bond between two people. This bond cannot be instant, and must be constructed overtime, using the effort between the two partners.\nWith this 'Love at first sight,' no chains or bonds can be established between the two individuals. There is a false connection linking both beings.\nAlthough, that's not to say that two people can build up from this false link, transforming it into that of a real relationship. One of the two can experience attraction at first sight, in which case\nthe false bond mentioned before will be established. This is entirely possible, to think that someone's physical features are ideal at your first glance. Attraction at first sight and love at first sight are quite different.\nTo answer the question, \"Is love at first sight possible,\" no, it is not. There are many ways that one could believe that they are in love, however it should be impossible for our minds to create a bond that quickly.\nBeing attracted, of course, is possible. This is because our minds will still recognize another person as 'Beautiful,' even if we haven't formed the chain, or recieved the chance to know the person.\nThis is where we will conclude volume three. In volume four, we'll be researching the reason why love is the most mysterious of all our other emotions. Until next time.\n\n~Hileia'elr", ""),
        StaticBook("Love's Ending 2", "Franswaar Kellian", "Love's Ending 2\n\n               By: \n   Franswaar Kellian\nThis Book is Dediciated to those who have lost everything\n3 years have passed since I learned. \n\nWe barely speak, though you don't have too. Whenever I see you, memories flood my mind. When we were inseperable. When we had our lives planned out. \n\nI will never undstand.\nYour daughter has grown  so much. She has your eyes, your nose. When I see her playing in the street, I see you in your youth. When we would play jokes on others. When I first learned that you were the love of my life, my angel\n\nI will never understand.\nEveryday since I have returned I have thought of no one else but you. \n\nYou were everything I had. Everything I was. Everything I wanted to achieve. I am in constant pain, though I do nothing. Tears seep down through my heart, though men are told not to\ncry. If this is so, I am no man.  \n\nI am a coward. I am afraid. I was born to say I love you. Every Breathe you ever took next to me, filled me with life. \n\nI will never understand.\nI am tired being so alone, but I am not welcome. \n\nNothing can mend my wounds, for time caused them. \n\nOnly myself is blame, I left. I told you I had too, but that is not true. I only wished to view the world. I guess my ambitions are my demise.\nRegrets and Guilt fill my mind as my heart is posioned by the prick of your quick removal from my life. I long to be with you again. I spend most my time overlooking the city a top the mountains unable to move, so I unwillingly climb down.\nSo I guess I will live alone. In your shadow. \n\nThough I have nothing to live for, nothing to hope for. No one else saw me the same as you did. \n\nI can't keep my eyes off of you. Words can't describe how I am feeling. Though I must turn away.\nI crawl home, in tears. There is nothing left for me on this planet. \n\nI climb apon the mountains again. The trail leads to the waterfall. \n\nPeaceful\n\nElegant \n\nBlissful\nSerenity\n\nI am at peace, the thoughts of you leave. I can finally go. \n\nA hand is placed on my shoulder. Darkness masks their face, but their touch is all but to well known.  \n\nWhen I finally found peace to let go, you return into my life\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI will never understand", ""),
        StaticBook("Loves Poems", "Atturi", "\n    --------------\n\n    Poems for you\n    My dearest Mira\n    some may just be\n    complements.\n\n    --------------\n\"Oh lovely Mira, what magical voice you have, that of the willow tree, whispy and sweet\"\n\n\"Your eyes are of blue moons shining shimmering light, I am blinded by its beauty, Colour of a cold winters blue frost reflecting the light of green leaves\"\n\"Your hair was silky and smooth, long as the willow trees hair\"\n\n\"Why you follow them i do not know.\n\"However it does not bother me\"\n\"You I care about, and I could never bear you getting hurt\"\n\"Coming to your home I see as a date, Mira, Even though you said you rejected me, the kiss was a symbol of my love for you\"\n\n\"I am unstable as of yesterdays trade, today, I am far more stable and am fortunate to have met you, tommarow I will be as stable\nas a summers day breeze calm and gentle\"\n\n\"I apologize for my little outburst of sadness, For this I give you a white tulip\"\n\n\"I lust for one more kiss\"\n\"Loving has never been there in my life before\"\n\"Of which i have to say, Thank you for the pleasure\"\n\"Valuable you are to me Mira\"\n\"Enough is what you shall say it is\"\n\"You are one of the only women who I have been able to hold a conversation with\"\n\"Our love has been decided by you, I have only inistiated this\"\n\"Until we meet again my Darling\"\n       \n       Love,\n           Atturi", ""),
        StaticBook("Lovets Homes", "TheChaoticNeko", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n       Lovets Lovely \n      Realestate & Decor\n\n\n\n\n\n\n       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWelcome to Lovets Lovely Realestate & Decor! We specialize in finding a suitable home for you, so you needn't worry about the process yourself. Whether you wish for a quaint cottage or an apartment in the city, we can find it for you. We also do decor\nfor cheap prices and would happy to do so for you! Whether you wish for a home that seems like a romantic get away or that cozy home feeling to it, we can do it all! So make a appointment today by sending a bird to the people listed below\nChehsire Lovet (TheChaoticNeko)\n\n Arnorian \n  (Radahan)\n\nHave a wonderful day and please make an appointment with us so we can find you a new home or decorate the home you have now! Or even both!", ""),
        StaticBook("Lucia de Bar's", "Lucia de Bar", "12th of Snow's Maiden\n                                  1535\n\nToday I escaped Peremont, after being grounded, to the Palace! Quite the adventure indeed. Though I was quickly found and told not to leave the Palace without an escort.\nI believe I have a crush on Uilleam! I don't know yet, though we danced in the garden! Nothing romantic. I don't believe.\n\n-drawings of flowers and hearts can be seen here-\n\nI played verity and dare with Maude and Prince Charles Francis. I\nhad to squak like a hen!\n\nWhen speaking to the Empress, use Majesty rather than Highness.\n\nI miss my 'riding lessons' with Lillian, it was fun! Learning how to swordplay was amusing.\nHer Majesty says I will have to marry whom they choose. I wish I didn't have to, though I suppose I cannot do much about it. I do not want to marry some old potato I do not love, what am I to do.\n\nI am only twelve,\nWhat am I to do.\n-a rather quick sketch of a meadow is drawn across this page-\n11th of The Grand Harvest\n                                1535.\n\nWe threw flowers at the returning soldiers that faught against the Snow Elves. Though, the Elves never arrived to fight. It was fun though!\n\nWe watched Richie get knighted today!\nThree of my dolls are missing... Poor Annabell, Samantha, and Julia.", ""),
        StaticBook("Luevina Food Log", "Arilynae Dreathen", "Monday:\n9:20 - One piece of toast - Water\n3:11 - Two strips of fish(ew), Toast - water\n\nTuesday: \n8:30 Water\n10:20 - Beans, One strip of fish\n8:50 - Ham sandwich, Water\nWednesday:\n10:00 - Grilled Chicken Sandwich, beans, water\n12:30 - Toast\n4:30 - Beans, rice, carrots (2 cups), water\n\nThursday: \n9:30 - Toast , water\n12:20 - Cup of beans, toast, water\n7:00 - One strip of ham, toast, water\nFriday: \n12:00 Strip of ham, toast, cup of rice, water\n5:20 Toast, water\n\nSat. :\n7:10 Toast, jam, water\n12:50 Strip of ham, cup of carrots, water\n6:20 Two strips of ham, water\nSunday: \n6:40 Toast, water\n1:20 Grilled Chicken Sandwich, tea\n8:40 Tea, cup of carrots.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mad Man's Diary", "Anonymous", "Third of the Amber Cold, year 125,\n\n\"I can't believe it! Finally, a task, the elders have sent me down here to watch over what they deemed sealed, and forgotten..\"\nThird of the Amber  Cold, year 126,\n\n\"I will be updating this journal yearly as I lack any proper means of being able to write, however, it's starting to get lonely down here.. I miss my parents, I want to see my wife again..\"\nFifth of The Amber Cold, year 127,\n\n\"I accidently missed a few days, I haven't seen sunlight in few years now.  The roots, they are preventing my departure. I have managed to construct a home, however,\nI lost a thumb and a finger in the process. Food and water is bountiful, I'm surprised anything at all grows here.. there's no sunlight!\"\n20th of The Amber Cold, year 133,\n\n\"I've decided that a good way to pass time is meditation, the melodies.. they're soothing..\"\nFirst of The Amber Cold, year 641,\n\n\"I found it! My journal, I thought I lost it! Damn bloody pixies stole my journal! I'll kill them all for their betrayal! I can't trust anybody, nobody, not even the pixies.. Only the melodies..\"\nFirst of The Amber Cold, year 683,\n\n\"Damn it! Open up you fucking roots! I want to get out, I'm lust for the suns gaze once more! Why..? Why have I been damned to this acursed place? I just.. I just need to meditate more..\nThe Aspects will free me from this cavern.. If I don't make it out alive, then the pixies have gotten to me.. Wretched little critters, they're invisible, I tell you!\"\nThe remainder of the book pertains scribbles of eyes, walls, and then, a lone woman, her skin a thick shade of onyx with lips stained in the juice of grass, green.. The eyes, circled in blood.\n\"I don't know how long it has been.. I've lost count of how many days I've been down here, to be honest, I was never even sure what month it was, or year, but I suspect it has been over a thousand by now. I saw her..\"\nSealed,\nForgotten,\nA burden to carry,\nHer sin till the end,\nIt was her fault,\nHow He ravaged the land, she could not stay, she fled, and ran away.\n\nI can't make out the vision.. it.. it hurts too much.\n\nToday, I have decided, I'm going to kill myself.\n\nThis land I was tasked with to protect, is a blessing, and a curse; to he, or she, who desires the seal, one must offer their life,\nand remain down here.. sealed, forever, unless.. unless the seal is ope-.....\"\n\nThe text fades, the remainder of the page torn from the book.", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Dictionary", "PiercingDarkness", "The Magic Dictonary:\n\nYir'sari - True Wizard, powerful magic masters.\n\nAscended - The demi-god children of the aenguls.\n\nUndead - The evil fists of Iblees, they destroyed Aegis.\nArcane Transportation Pad - \n\nStaff - a tool used to conduct mana, as well as aid you in Void connections.\n\nWand - Akin to the staff, doesn't work as well.\nCleric - Powerful magicians based mostly in healing, they are fueled by aenguls.\n\nNecromancer - Users of Necromany, a deadly magic having to do with life drain.\n\nPyromancer - Fire evocationist, magician of fire.\nElectromancer - Users of electric magic, mostly evocationist of electricity, they are common in Anthos.\n\nEvocation - The use of summong elements from the Void.\nFire-Evocation - The summoning of mana from the Void to create fire.\n\nWater-Evocation - The summoning of mana from the Void to create water or other water related things.\nElectric-Evocation - The evoking of mana from the Void to form electricity.\n\nWind-Evocation - The use of void mana to create wind and it's similiar elements.\nEarth-Evocation - The evocation of mana to form earthen elements.\n\nShamanism - Magic having to do with the use of spirits.\n\nElemental control - A shaman magic having to do with spirits.\nMagic(k) - The use of mana to conjure things, and even to control things.\n\nMana - Life force and energies around us, used to form complex spells.\n\nNecromancy - The use of life drain to get mana to form complex\nspells.\n\nShade-Magic - Fueled by a gem, it's a shadow magic having to do with the art of tendrils, and other shadow elements.\nIllusion - A arcane magic, the use of mana to form false images and feelings, and project them upon others, it's impossible to illusion yourself.\n\nConjuration - The conjuring of living beings.\nWizard - Common term name for the Yir'sari, true wizards.\n\nArch-Mage - Ruler of the mage's guild.\n\nMage - Practicer of magic.\n\nMagician - Mage is it shortened.\nAscended Magic - Magic fueled by a patron aenguel, it is a light magic, and holy, it is akin to cleric.\n\nUndead-Magic - Fueled by Iblees, the Undead used their necromancy to begin their conquest of Aegis.\nThe Void - A place where mages draw power from to fuel their spells.\n\nDragon - A beast of huge size and intelligence, they roam Northern Anthos, hunting.\nYellow Stone Material ((Endstone))\n\nA heavily weird material, it spreads corruption of many kinds.\n\nDruidism - Magic over nature, has to do with the spirits known as the Aspects.\nAlteration - Magic that alters the properties, of real world things.\n\n-------------------\n\nMagic sayings:\n\n\"Magic seeks those who don't seek it.\"\n\"Magic is the path of ths scholar, not a insolent warrior of heavy brains and no mindset.\" \n\n\"Magic is the path of destruction, insolent mage!\" - Gavin the Druid\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\"Good and evil doesn't decide how magic works, only the acts of the user.\"\n\n- The Arcane Mage\n\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nWritten by, Mythras Ardere.\n\nSources:\n\n- history of magic\n- The Clerical Order\n- The Mage's Guild\n- Salamandra's spirit\n- Many assorted books on magic, and knowledge from other mages.", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic License", "Auberon de Clare", "As by the Codex Arcana, and the Magic License Clause, this document licenses Ikur Seregon to the practice of Anti-magic\n\n[!] The scroll bears a scribbled scribbled signature, along with a seal, in shape of a Lorraine Cross, stamped into\nburgundy coloured wax. [!]\n\n-Knight Inquisitor Auberon de Clare\n\n\n\n\n#0003", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic License +", "Auberon de Clare", "As by the Codex Arcana, and the Magic License Clause, this document licenses Lori Oathcast to the practice of Golemancy and Runesmithing. He is also licensed to label and eliminate Maleficarum, as by decree of the Knight Inquisitor.\n[!] The scroll bears a scribbled signature, along with a seal, in shape of a Lorraine Cross, stamped into burgundy coloured wax. [!]\n\n-Knight Inquisitor Auberon de Clare\n#0029 (+)", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Notes I", "Vaeria Ossaura", "Sal' told me there are many types of 'Voidal' Magics, those being- Alteration, Arcanism, Evocation, Illusion, Mental and Conjuration.\n\nShe knows Arcanism (both disciplines) and has mastered it. This must mean she knows Arcane Shielding and Arcane-\n'Blasting'. She also knows Eletrical Evocation and Mental Magic- she's obviously very well versed with magic to know all about this kind of stuff. I'll ask her to teach me how to 'connect' to the Void, if I really suck at it.\nThe correct term isn't Arcane 'Blasting'- it's Arcane Evocation. She evokes raw Arcane energy, and uses it against people (in the form of missiles and such).\n\nMaybe magic is why her face is faint scared. I feel faintly bad for her.\nBasic concept of Elemental Evocation- The user draws energy from the Void, 'forming' the voidal energies into an element. They then use that element in certain ways.\n\nAparantly this is a small summary of Elemental Evocation.\nBasic concept of Arcane Evocation- The user draws energy from the void, but they do not form the energy into an element. Instead, they keep it in the raw form, evoking it in certain ways.\nArcane Evocation is much harder then Elemental Evocation (due to the raw power it possesses) but is seemingly not much more powerful. \n\nThis is confusing to me- shouldn't the raw form be more powerful then the 'crafted' form?\nThe reasoning behind this- in Sal's own words- is that; 'it's not as destructive as fire or lighting, nor as sturdy as earth, nor as quick as air'. It's 'flexible'.\n\nArcane Evocation is considered the 'jack-of-all-trades'.\nIt's okay at everything, master-\nat none. Arcane Evocation is Elemental Evocation but without the elemental properties- it adapts to the whims of the caster. In my opinion, this seems so much better. \n\nAnd like always- I am wrong. Elemental Evocation isn't as wild as I thought.\nIt seems dependable, much more then I first thought. Fire and Eletrical Evocation can actually start fires!", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Notes II", "Vaeria Ossaura", "Well, atleast this time I didn't have a nosebleed. My body is feeling almost bruised and my head is racing from a migraine. I've failed- again. \n\nBut, failure means practise. And practise makes perfect.\nAdniel gave me this tome, and I'm going to learn from it. However, having a tome doesn't make you a practitioner of magic.\n\nConnecting is alot more... locked away, then I thought it would be.\nWhy is it so difficult to enter (or tap into) a realm that feels so close? The Void is locked within the fabric of our own realm- so why can't I just reach out and grasp it?\n\nI hope Sal' will help me learn. Without proper help, I'll be doomed to failure.\nMaybe, just maybe, if I keep torturing myself with this damn connecting, I'll succeed. Probably not, but I can try.\n\nMight not be magic related, but the fire is sort of helping with my focus. Hearing the faint crackling of the timber is relaxing.\nReally relaxing. And the softness of the mat doesn't hurt my knees, so- good thinking on my part, right?\n\n\nMaybe focusing on other things around me is the key to connecting? I'll ask Sal' and Adniel\nabout their way of connecting, and try to really get a grasp for it. I'll write it down here. Sal's Recommendations- Use incense and try your best to block it out. Ignoring the odor aparantly helped her first connection- so I'll have to try it.\nShe also said that connecting feels like 'nothing'. That's insane! Besides the faintness, how will I even handle it? Nothing is intense, when you think about it...\n\nShe also said to conquer the 'unknown' (the unknown being the fear on connecting).", ""),
        StaticBook("Maheral Request", "Iat", "Adeon,\n\nhere is the proof that frost-witch activity exists within the city.\n\nThis is a fracture from the ice left in my room. I ask your assistance in tracking down and dealing with the frost-witch known as\nYuln. She is Delonna's past wife and is likely located inside the city. \nYou need not worry about permission as I am sure the King will be in support of this. Legally the Sohaer must take action due to this attack on purity within the citadel.\nDue to the action required and my position within the city it is unfavorable that I should become involved. Such action may stunt the hunt. \n\nMy best wishes and regards to your operation. \n\n~Maheral", ""),
        StaticBook("Maid Contract", "Ser Florent of Duppendale", "      Handmaid Contract\n\nThis contract is to confirm that Miss §iLucie Rothe works for House Jorrel of Duppendale, under House Staunton as a handmaid. \n\nHer duties will be as outlined, but not limited to, the list on the next page.\nDuties:\n\nCooking\nCleaning\nServing\nGreeting\nUshering\nCarrier of messages\nWashing\nGeneral duties\nCaring for children\nMaid duties\nRemoving trash\nEtc.\nRoom, Pay and Board\n\nThe following defines what Miss Lucie Rothe will be granted for bedspace, pay, and food accomodations. \n\nBedspace:\nRequested to not be given one of the spare rooms, or to be close to the master bedroom.\nPay:\nAs discussed, pay shall be Forty Minas per elven week, raised or lowered on work ethic.\n\nIf things are purchased from Miss Rothe's own pockets that are directly needed for the keep, such as food, she will be reimbursed for her expenses.\nFood:\nInformed that only scraps will do, however she shall be fed justly. \n\nShe may have any food that Kathy, the baby, and Ser Florent do not eat.\nThe following signatures hereby bind Miss Lucie Rothe under the employ of Ser Florent Jorrel until agreed upon that she may quit or retire.\n\n\nSer Florent Jorrel\n\nMiss (the signature is a series of meaningless squiggles)\n\n\n\nLord of House Stafyr:\n\nAltaron II. Stafyr\n((Z3r05t4r))", ""),
        StaticBook("Mail", "Lily Potter", "I am Lily Potter,Daughter of John Potter and  Spike Chase.(P1ss_Jugg)\nI wish to buy a home here in Felsen and get a job.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malin", "Signature Trading Card", "One of the four brothers from the start of time, Malin was the father of the Elves. While blessed with a long life, his descendents suffer the curse of limited fertility.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malinor", "Unknown Author", "Malinor as we know it began after the Collapse, an obscure event which lead to the collapse of any civilization that may have existed before 1300. When one of the symptoms of the Collapse, the erasing of the collective memory of all who\nsurvived the Collapse, wore off, High Prince Native banded together what was left of a wood elven colony, as well as the dark elves and high elves in the region surrounding Laurelin. He set about consolidating his position in Laurelin, assisting many\nelves in setting up lives in the capital. Very few elves are left from this time almost all having gone missing at some point during Aegis, so accounts of the early days are secondhand at best, many times having been passed from pointed ear to pointer ear\nuntil reaching the writer. By most accounts, Native picked an array of Princes to help him govern the growing elven population, some notable ones being Prince Toren the Farmer, Prince Flefal the Engineer, Princess Arianna, and Prince Lafthi the Diplomat.\nThe mining paradise of Ravenhold was founded, home to such notable elves as Khel Oussana, Haelphon Adecchio, and future Prince Ebs Telrunya.\n\tAfter the initial years in Laurelin, most of the High Council, including High Prince Native, were barely ever\nseen in Laurelin, and the Malinor suffered. The Gauntlet, an obstacle course that offered a large minas reward, was opened rarely, and almost every elf immediately entered the Wardens or the Druidic Order upon entry into Malinor. The only functioning\npart of Malinor's government were indeed the Wardens, the elite defenders of the forests of Malinor. Lead at first by the ruthless Blackthorn, they protected the forests while the High Council squandered away the Princedom. Native's only notable action\nduring this time was nearly destroying Ravenhold when he caused the mine to collapse.\n\tWhen Kal'Bryst was destroyed during the onset of the Undead invasion, the High Council's reaction was nonexistent. During the great northern wars, in which the\nhumans struggled for survival against the undead invaders, sin the defense of Alstion. The Wardens instead focused on removing Wrath from Wrath's Clutch, an Undead citadel in the South that threatened to cut off Alras and Al'Khazar from Laurelin and\nKal'Urguan. Countless wardens and other elves perished in attacks on Wrath's Clutch, which was repeatedly assaulted so that prisoners being held there, most notably Princess Indelwehn, could be freed. No matter how many time the walls were breached, the\norces of the United Aegis Coalition (UAC) could not dislodge Wrath until very late in the war. Indelwehn became notable for leading the wardens in the defense of Sanjezel, leading the to the signing of the Malin-Krug pact, a long-lasting defensive treaty\nbetween the Holy Princedom and Krugmar, which was signed by Princess Indelwehn and Wargoth Mogroka'Gorkil.\n\tMalinor had a token presence in the Verge, its official settlement, overseen by Princess Lirinya, lacking utility and security. More enterprising\nlves and a few humans united under Viscount Ebs, who founded the city of Fionn, which flourished for a time, until all but the mentally unstable abandoned the Verge during the massive slime and spider invasion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Maln", "Unknown", "Maln\n\nThe eyes\nThe twinkling eyes\nEver so serious\nYet ever so humorous\nThe pools of blue\nAs if it contained the ocean\nThe ever so sincere eye\nLooked through my heart\nIt stared with its endless depths\nThe golden hair\nShining under the light\nLustrous and wavy\nSashaying as if they had a life of his own\n\nThose pair of hands\nSmooth yet worn at the same time\nFluent with a sword\nYet as delicate and precise with experiments and books\nAlways covering mine\nSo small compared to yours\n\nI shall never forget\nYour ever welcome presence\nThat tinkling laugh of yours\nAlways overprotective concern\nThat charming smile\nThat luring overwhelming heat\nThe smell of you\nWith a tinge of musty books\nThe metallic scent of metal Smokiness from an unsuccessful experiment\nThe sweetness of the flowers from haelun\nYou are forever\nMy maln\n\nArahael Eloem (PianoEby)", ""),
        StaticBook("Malog's Proverbs", "Malog'Yar", "*As you open the book, you see in its pages a collection of proverbs written by the shaman, Malog'Yar. Each one is individually numbered for ease of memorization, it seems. They don't appear to have a particular order to them, but must\nhave been written as they came to the shaman's mind.\n((As in my other books, only those words which are actually different in the Blah are written in said language. The rest are in Common for ease of reading.))\n1. The lust for power is the beginning of shame. It concieves, agh brings forth arrogance. Arrogance, when it reaches maturity, brings forth humiliation.\n2. The path to honor is paved with sacrifice.\n3. Gold is a heavy thing, agh bub'hosh is the burden of he who hoards it. It will crush the heart, agh bring low the spirit.\n4.He who forgets his ancestors of the past will have nub future for his descendents.\n5.Food, water,\nshelter, praise; these things are wasted, when given to ash with nub honor.\n6.All is vanity for the whitewash, for he has abandoned his ancestors. He has departed from his purpose in life.\n7.Find that skill which lat are hosh\nat. Do it with honor, for even the lowly chicken farmer can glorify Krug.\n8.Do nub scorn simplicity. It is a chest of many treasures.\n9.Hosher is a small blarg with a mate agh cubs, than an empty palace.\n10.Integrity,\nuprightness, honor, discipline agh wisdom are the bones of the spirit. Without these, lat can nub stand.\n11.Hosher to be a blind man with wisdom, than a fool with many eyes.\n12.Luxury is an open gate to complacency.\n13.Complacency is a downhill path to the flatting of the spirit. It is an easy path to descend, but returning uphill is strenuous, requiring diligence.\n14.Bring up lats cubs in the way of honor, for they will take lats place in the future.\n15.This year's swineherd may be next year's Rex.\n16.Remember your brother, agh be quick to share his burden.\n17.The hardship of life is a refining furnace. It hurts for the time, but melts away that which would make\nlat weak.\n18.Lats body is a gift. Use it hoshly. Do nub abuse it, agh do nub let it wither.\n19.Life is work. Work hard or starve.\n20.The cactus lives in the dry sands, needing little nourishment. It is stronger for it.\n21.Hosher is a bag of rotten flesh, than a feast in the blarg of the dishonorable.\n22.He who lives with nub honor is like a fortress made of dry twigs or a zult made of still air: useless.\n23.Taking a title simply for the\nsake of taking a title is like eating sharp blades simply for the sake of eating.\n24.A wise blah is more precious than all the gems beneath the earth.\n25.Hosher to be flat for what is honorable, than to abandon lats\nintegrity simply to extend lats life.\n26.Honor is nub a currency to be traded. Do nub treat it as such.\n27.A life with nub honor is as meaningless as letters with nub order.\n28.Do nub tolerate weakness in body,\nmind or spirit.\n29.He who works hard will have his bread.\n30.Feeding the lazy is like planting the wind. It accomplishes nubthing.\n31.Be satisfied with food agh a cave. It may be all lat have ash day.\n32.Do nub envy the rich. Their decadence will make them soft.\n33.Do nub peep down on the poor. They are nub blinded by the glimmer of gold.\n34.Minas often do little more than disappear.\n35.Deceit agh\ntwisted words only clutter agh clog the mouth. Eventually, lat will choke on them.\n36.Blah what lat mean, nub what others want to hear.\n37.A slimy heart will slip, agh fall to its destruction.\n38.Rulers, do nub\nbe haughty. Ash day, lats reign will end, agh another will take lats place.\n39.He who is wise heeds the truthful rebuke.\n40.The fool surrounds himself with flatterers, agh is nub aware when ruin comes.\n41. Hosh is the\nfemale who bears strong cubs, agh works tirelessly to nourish their bodies agh spirits.\n42.Happy is the male who finds her, agh keeps her.\n43.Hosher is ash honorable lifemate, than ash hundred weak mates.\n44.As a blarg will\nnub stand on mist, cloud or vapor, neither will a family stand on weakness, foolishness of dishonor.\n45.Walk as Krug walked, agh honor the spirits. This will keep lats path straight.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malog's Tales v1", "Warchief Malog'Yar", "Malog's Tales v1: Yar and Nargii.\n((Because I copy pasted this from my forum post, it's written in Common for ease of reading. For immersion’s sake, I used a simplified version of the Blah for any dialogue in the story.))\nSome of you have heard the\nstory of Yar before. You have heard of his birth, his wisdom and his death. You’ve heard the broad strokes. You have not, however, heard any of the more specific stories from his life. I have, therefore, decided this night to tell you, my brothers and\nsisters, this tale from his life, and I hope to tell you more in the future. Tonight, I tell you all the story of Yar and Nargii.\n   As those who have heard the story of Yar know, Yar was a great shaman, and took some apprentices during his life. At one\npoint, he taught a group of four young students: Naramok, Makor, Shula and Nargii. Naramok was his favored student, the most advanced and naturally-gifted of the four. Makor and Shula were a young couple, who sought to learn alongside each other, and\nserve the village as shamans together. Nargii, however, was the least-talented of the four.\n  It wasn’t so much that he lacked potential. He simply progressed at a slower rate. Consequently, Yar rarely allowed him to practice any actual application of\nshamanic power, as Nargii simply wasn’t ready. Day after day, he was forced to go over the fundamentals: collecting reagents, carving tokens and masks, practicing his pronunciation of the same, basic Old Blah phrases ad nauseam; with very little actual\nmagical practice. All the while, his fellow apprentices were already learning to brew bottled hexes, and Naramok was even beginning his training in ritualistic curses. Eventually, Nargii grew bitter and jealous. “Yar,” he complained one day, after carving\nhis upteenth prayer mask, “for h’ash years mi have been lats apprentice. For h’ash years, mi have been repeating these same dry lessons. The others are already practicing real powers, and I’ve barely ever been allowed to boil a few herbs. When do mi get\nto start studying some real shamanism?”\n   “Nargii,” he responded patiently, “a sapling bears nub fruit, agh rain does nub fall out of season. Lat will move on in lats training when lat am ready.”\n  “Mi am ready now!” he protested.\n  \"Lat am ambitious,\nagh lat have potential to be a great shaman ash day; but lat am nub ready yet. Mi will blah lat when lat am ready, young brother.” Yar then patted him on the shoulder, “Now, go to lats blarg, Nargii. Keep practicing the fundamentals.”\n  \"But... mi...\"\nNargii began to speak, but realized it to be pointless to argue further. He left the tent. A bundle of bones above the door flap clacked together as he exited with a sour grimace across his dull green face.\n  “We are the conduits of the spirits,” Yar said\nthe next afternoon as he sat cross-legged on a woolen mat, his four students seated around him in a semicircle, “We are their instruments by which they enact their will. We are their weapons to bring justice upon their enemies, agh we are the links by\nwhich the balance between our world and theirs is maintained. Naramok, what is our duty?”\n  “To guide our brothers agh sisters in the path of honor, agh keep them in the ways of Krug.”\n  “Hosh.” Yar nodded approvingly, but Nargii simply sneered as he\nlooked down at his most recently-made token, resenting Naramok for holding their teacher’s favor. “Nargii, mi peep lat have made another token.” Nargii looked up to see Yar’s extended hand. He nodded, and placed it in Yar’s palm. Yar held the token up to\neye level. It was two-inches long and made of bone, carved to resemble a cage. “This is hosh. Lat am getting hosher. Keep this up, agh lat will be ready before lat gruk it.” He then offered the token back to Narmii, “Hang it from lats staff.”\n  \"Rulg,\" he\nreplied with a slight smile, and pulled a leather strap from his bag to tie the token to the top of his staff.\n  Within a few seconds, right as Yar was about to address Makor and Shula, the the clacking of bones was heard. Yar and his students looked to\nsee a young warrior stepping through the tent flap, “Throm’ka, brother Yar. Mi hope mi du nub interrupt anything important, but there is news.”\n  “News?” Yar arched a brow.\n  “Yub. Some traveller from a far away land wants to blah to lat. He is an albai,\nbut it seems he brings a tribute of resources. Would lat have us flat him?”\n  “Nub yet.” he sighed a bit at the interruption. “If he has brought tribute to help the village, we may as well hear what he has to blah. Mi will determine the worth of his\nblah.\"\n  With that, the warrior nodded, and motioned the visitor in. Into the tent, accompanied by two elven guards, strode a lithe, pale elf, with long cornsilk hair cascading gracefully down his back and shoulders. A pair of thin braids dangled beside\nhis long ears, and his narrow eyes were green as spring grass. With a smooth, sweet voice the elf spoke, “Karin’ayla, Yar.”\n  “Ug,” replied Yar with little emotion, clearly unimpressed by the thin creatures in his tent, “Blah.”\n  The elf nodded, \"My name\nis Celador. I have heard your name in my travels, and that you are a wise and powerful shaman. Having heard tales of you, I sought you out, in hopes that you may be interested in a certain proposition.” Celador stopped to await a response. Yar crossed his\narms, and looked sternly upon the visitor, visibly suspicious of the elf’s words. He said nothing, allowing the elf to continue, “Well, anyways,” Celador continued, a bit unnerved by Yar’s stoic demeanor, “I come offering payment; gold, iron, pelts and\nmany spices. I can give you all these things beyond measure, if you will do but one simple task for me. The Rex is a brutish cretin.” Celador spoke boldly as he regained his composure. “I should think that a wise orc like yourself would make a much better\nRex. My request, therefore, is that you put a curse on him, so that I may strike him down. You, then, could fight alongside me, and take the rexdom. Under your rule, I believe we could both prosper greatly.” He grinned expectantly, fully confident in his\nwords.\n  Nargii’s eyes lit up at the mention of such treasures, but Yar stood to his feet in a rage, “Celador, lat am a dishonorable coward, agh mi will have nub part in lats plan! Flat these albai!”\n  At Yar's command, the students rose from the floor,\nand the young warrior raised his waraxe. The elves unsheathed their own beautifully-crafted blades, and went on the defensive. A loud clang sounded as the warrior’s axe slammed against the blade of one of the guards. Celador pointed his own blade out in\nfront as the shamans approached, and saw, from the corner of his eye, his companion struggling under the strength of the warrior. His other guard alerted him to the fact that the rest of the village was becoming aware of the situation, and advised an\nimmediate retreat. Celador nodded, and turned to run, leaving their companion to his fate, and cringing as a he felt a chunk of hair getting ripped from the back of his head by an orc’s hand. As the two sprinted through the village, they heard the\nagonizing scream of the guard they’d left behind. The villagers readied their weapons, and charged after the escaping elves. A spray of blood hit Celador in the left eye, as his only remaining guard was hacked down right beside him by a berserking feorc\nwith a machete. A thrown spear narrowly grazed his cheek, and chunks of sandstone whizzed past him from behind. He barely managed to escape with just a few bruises. The orcs returned to their business, and Yar called his students back inside to continue\ntheir lesson, while Nargii glanced briefly over his shoulder in the direction of the fleeing elf.\n  The following night, after the others had gone to sleep, Nagrii was still awake, and thinking of Celador’s offer. The lust for wealth had taken root in his\nheart, and he’d even deluded himself, thinking that he would finally be taken more seriously if he could curse the Rex himself. He took his spear, and lied to the watchmen, telling them he was going hunting for the night. With their consent, he left the\nvillage, and tracked down the elf. There wasn’t much to go on. He found the occasional drop of blood, a discarded piece of damaged chainmail here and there and a little bit of blond hair. Eventually, after many hours, he found a cave, and decided to check\ninside. He saw Celador sleeping in a cot near the back. As he entered, a loose piece of sandstone broke free under his foot, sending him tumbling to the floor. Celador’s ear twitched, and he sprung up from his sleep at the sudden noise. Snatching his\nblade from the floor, the startled elf barked, “Stay back, orc! I’ve had enough of your kind.”\n  Nargii rose to his feet, holding up empty hands, “Nub nub. Mi nub here to hurt lat, albai. Mi-” he suddenly stopped, and looked around the cave. Stacked\nagainst the right wall were chests so full of gold and iron the lids couldn’t close. He saw a huge pile of pelts to his left, and dozens of jars filled with various spices. He forced his gaze away from the riches, and continued, “Mi want to help lat.”\n\n“How?” snapped Celador.\n  “Mi am Yar’s apprentice. Mi will curse the Rex for lat.”\n  Celador grinned. He could see the greed in Nargii’s eyes, “Is that so? Very well then. You put a curse on the Rex for me, and all you see here is yours. Make him weak\nand fragile. Sap his strength for me. Is that possible, shaman?”\n  Nargii looked to the bone token dangling from his staff, and nodded, “Yub. That can be done.”\n  “Excellent!” Celador picked up a hefty bag of gold, and tossed it to Nargii, \"Consider this\na down-payment.”\n  Nargii caught the bag with an eager grin. “Rulg, albai. Mi will do hosh work. Lat will peep.” He turned, and hurried out of the cave and back to his village with one final “Gug’ye.”\n  Arriving back at the village near sunrise, a\nmorning watchman stopped him to ask about the bag and where he’d been all night. Nargii told him the same lie as he told the night watchmen, “Mi was hunting. The bag is full of sand rats. Mi couldn’t peep much else out there last night.” With a shrug, the\nwatchman nodded, and went back about his business. Nargii hurried back to his tent, and set the bribe money aside to immediately begin his first attempt at a real curse. He held up his staff so the bone token hung at eye level, and began chanting to\nOgrol, the spirit of despair, entrapment and, most relevant to Nargii’s situation, sapped strength. His chant, however, was awkward, as he had trouble remembering important Old Blah words. Eventually, he came to the climax of his ritual, and raised his\nstaff in the air. Then, the token on his staff began to vibrate, and soon shattered, sending a splintered fragment into his arm. Nargii then dropped his staff, as a horrible pain filled his body. His bones became brittle and porous within him, and he was\nleft hunched over on the floor, too weak to even stand.\n  Then, as if he had been waiting for him outside, the tent flap flung open, and Yar stepped inside. He glared down at Nargii with intense disapproval, “Blah to mi, Nargii. Is now the time to take\nbribes? Is now the time to sacrifice our honor for filthy gain? Are the uruks to be as the gazat, led about by greed? Are we to be as the shara, lusting after power? Perhaps, lat think, it is the time to be as the albai, sneaking around in the shadows.\nPeep now how the curse lat intended for the Rex has fallen upon lats own head, traitor.”\n  Nargii looked up in astonishment, “B-but… how did l-lat… gruk?” he asked shakily in his weakened state. Immediately, Yar’s sister, Voltha the Huntress, entered from\nbehind, tossing the corpse of Celador before Nargii. A thick orcish arrow protruded from his neck.\n  “Mi do a lot of night hunting,” interjected Voltha “but mi had never peep’d lat hunting at night before. Mi peep'd lat in the cave with the albai,\nNargi...\"\n  Nargii was speechless, and without defense. “Nargii,” said Yar, “lat have nub integrity or uprightness in spirit, so lat shall have nub in body. Lat am a whitewash, and a traitor to this village and the whole Uzg.”\n  Nargii was dragged to the\ncenter of the village, and tied up, too weak to resist. He was sentenced to death by de-boning. His screams echoed throughout the desert, as his fragile bones were pulled from his body in front of the whole village until he died. Afterwards, his bones\nwere piled up atop the ruins of his destroyed tent, and burned with his ill-gotten gold. The rest of his body was chopped up, and thrown to the pigs. So, to this day, de-boning remains the Yar clan’s punishment for the absolute worst of offenders.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malog's Tales v2", "Warchief Malog'Yar", "Malog's Tales v2: Marr and Lug.\n((Because I copy/pasted this from my forum post, this story is written in plain English for readability. So, please excuse the lack of Blah.))\n  There were once two brothers, Marr and Lug, who failed in all things to which\nthey applied their hands. Marr, though good-hearted, was stupid, and his poor judgement always led to failure. Lug, though crafty, was lazy beyond measure, and never had the will to accomplish even simple tasks. The other orcs eventually grew weary of the\nburden they placed on everyone around them, and brought their complaint before the Rex. Some demanded they be pugged. Some called for total banishment from the Uzg. Some even shouted loudly for execution. The Rex, frustrated by the near constant stream of\nbad reports concerning the two, finally called them to his hall.\n  He decided to give them one chance to redeem themselves, and prove their worth to the Uzg. He told them of a string of islands far off the coast, of which the farseers had reported\nmultiple visions. He instructed the pair to take a simple rowboat, and make their way to these islands. Once there, they were to scout the lands for any ruins, resources or even indigenous people to subjugate. If there was anything on these islands that\nbenefit the War Nation in any way, Marr and Lug were to find it, and report back to the Rex. They were given just enough bread and water to survive the trip, but, upon arrival, they were expected to provide for themselves. So, amid mockery, nay-saying\nand general disdain from their fellow orcs, the brothers shoved off, and began their voyage.\n  Naturally, Lug did none of the rowing along the way, assuring Marr that he would do all the rowing on the way home. Marr, being the fool he was, believed him.\nAfter nearly a full day of rowing, the islands were in sight, but Lug’s laziness and Marr’s stupidity hadn’t gone unnoticed. Ankruz, spirit of the sea, was insulted that the two would drag their shameful behavior across her waters, and conjured up a\nfurious tempest. They clung desperately to their boat, until Ankruz spat forth a brutal wave, and dashed their tiny vessel upon the rocks of the nearest island. They survived, but their means of returning home was lost.\n  When the sun began to set, it was\ndecided that they should hunt for food. Lug, however, simply lay back on the beach, promising to build a fire while Marr found food. Marr agreed, and made his way into the jungle, where he crafted a simple wooden spear. Many hours later into the night, he\nreturned with a bloodied spear and a pair of local apes slung over his shoulder. When he saw that no fire had been made in all that time, he roused Lug from a nap. Lug complained that he was too exhausted from their ordeal at sea, and needed his rest. So,\nMarr built the fire, skinned the apes and cooked dinner for himself and his brother.\n  The following morning, the pair discussed building a raft for their eventual return. Lug agreed to do this to make up for the previous night’s failure. Meanwhlie, Marr\nwas to hunt breakfast for the both of them, and so he did. After hours of hunting, he found a freshwater spring, and filled two waterskins for himself and his brother. He found his way back to the beach with his heavy burden of bulging waterskins and meat\nfrom some jungle tortoises to see that Lug had not even begun construction of a raft. Lug simply told Marr that there was no real hurry to build a raft, and that he didn’t want to cause himself any unneeded strain by rushing himself. After all, they were\ntrying to survive on a remote island. Sadly, Marr was as stupid as Lug’s excuses were pitiful, so he believed him. Marr also ended up having to build a new fire, since Lug allowed their first one to go out, and refused to eat raw tortoise meat.\n  Things\ncontinued in this way for days and days. Lug would make empty promises and stupid excuses, and Marr, in his unspeakable foolishness, would believe him. Marr did all the hunting and gathering, which took twice as long as it otherwise could have.\nConsequently, he got very little sleep, as hunting for their evening meals took him late into the night while Lug napped on the beach, only to wake up when Marr returned with food. He built a new fire whenever Lug would let a previous fire go out, which\nis to say every time. He built a simple lean-to to shelter them from rain. He even took up construction of a raft in what little spare time he had, as he accepted the fact that Lug wasn’t going to do it. The longer it went on, the more exhausted he got,\nand the harder it became to provide for the two of them. He started bringing back less and less food, always letting Lug have most of it, kind-spirited orc that Marr was.\n  Eventually, Marr couldn’t carry on like that anymore. His body had grown weak from\nhunger and exhaustion. He collapsed on a hot afternoon in the humid jungle, where he passed out, and was easy prey for the forest’s predators. That evening, Lug was awoken from another of his naps by the rumbling of his stomach. He saw that it was\nstarting to rain and that Marr hadn’t returned from his hunt, but assumed that he’d simply lost his way in the foliage or had gotten distracted by some colorful plants. Either way, he couldn’t be bothered to look for him, and simply assumed he'd return\neventually. Throughout the night, the weather grew worse, until the rain whipped itself up into a storm that blew Lug’s shelter off into the water.\n  Lug made it through the night, but his fire was out, his shelter was gone, his brother hadn't returned\nwith food and he even seemed to have caught something from staying out in the rain all night. Sick and hungry, Lug called out for Marr, but got no reply. He feared to enter the forest, for he knew he’d developed no real survival skills in his whole lazy\nlife. So, he waited on the beach, coughing, sniffling and assuring himself that Marr would make it back. He eventually managed to soothe himself back to sleep only to be awoken several hours later by the brutal heat of the midday sun. He reached for his\nwaterskin, and saw that it was gone. Marr had taken both of their waterskins to refill at the spring. He knew that the spring was deep in the jungle he feared so much, and still couldn’t convince himself to venture off in search of his brother. So, the\ncoward simply waited.\n  The following morning, his sickness had gotten worse, and he still had no food or water. He looked to the raft Marr had started on, but, in his constant toiling to provide for the both of them, Marr had barely even managed to chop\ndown two narrow logs for it. The crude stone axe Marr had fashioned to chop them was also with him in the jungle. He always kept it with him, since he was the one who chopped all the wood, most of which went into starting new fires. So, Lug was stranded,\nsick, thirsty and hungry. As time went on, he got sicker, hungrier and weaker. Eventually, his fear of the jungle didn’t matter anymore. He’d gotten too weak to get up even if he wasn’t scared.\n  Lug starved to death there on that island. Back in the War\nNation, no one cared enough to come looking for them. It had been long assumed that Marr’s foolishness and Lug’s laziness would be the death of them both, and so it was. Remember, my brothers and sisters. Feeding the lazy is like planting the wind.\nIt accomplishes nothing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malog's Tales v3", "Warchief Malog'Yar", "Malog's Tales v3: The Whitewash and Dhaub.\n  ((As with the first two volumes, this story is copy/pasted from my original forum post, and is therefore in Common for ease of reading. Again, sorry for not writing in the Blah, but I wasn't about to rewrite\nthe whole story.))\n   Long ago, in another land far away, there lived an uruk named Dhaub. Dhaub was born in affliction and suffering. His mother died in labor, and he was born feet first with the umbilical cord tangled around his neck. His father managed\nto deliver him successfully, however, and he seemed not to have sustained any lasting damage, though the shamans warned him that the circumstances of his birth were a bad omen. \n  As Dhaub grew, his life proved to be one of affliction and pain. In his\nfirst hunt, he lost an eye. In a klomp with some other cubs, he broke a leg, and the bone stuck through the flesh. The wound became infected, which led to several other diseases, and nearly killed him. The bone, when it did heal, proved to be improperly\nset, and didn’t heal correctly, giving him an awkward limp. The father, burdened at having to raise the child alone and fearing that he would grow up weak due to his constant misfortune, shamefully took his own life, adding embarrassment to Dhaub’s\nphysical suffering. Dhaub vowed to prove his father wrong, and strove hard to overcome the hardships of his life. Though he continued on in almost constant agony, he grew stronger and wiser for it. He worked hard all his life; harder than any other orc in\nhis village.\n  There was another orc born around the same time as Dhaub, who in his youth saw the hardships of life in the desert --especially that of Dhaub-- and fled to the human lands. There he begged at the feet of a wealthy pink-skin merchant, who\ntook pity, and adopted him. The whitewash lived a life of ease and decadence. He slept every night on a soft bed with clean sheets, and clothed himself in fine silk of purple and scarlet. He feasted sumptuously at every meal, and grew to be a rich, fat\nmerchant like the one who raised him. He bought a mansion, attended by many servants, who saw to his every need and desire.\n  Meanwhile, Dhaub couldn’t keep a house. Every hut or tent he built would be struck by lightning or blown down by a strong wind.\nHe tried living in a cave, only for an earthquake to collapse it. Eventually, he decided there would be no house for him, and started sleeping outside. His nights were often restless, however, as he was awoken frequently by sand rats trying to nibble at\nhis sores and wounds. The only thing that kept sand out of his wounds was his tattered cloak spread out on the ground. He ate whatever he could get by strenuous labor and long, difficult hunts. He was lean, but, through unparalleled effort, he kept\nhimself strong in the face of disease and misfortune.\n  After many years, Dhaub died in a scatternak hunt. Despite their best efforts, his fellow hunters were unable to retrieve his body from the mandibles of the great beast, and they were forced to\nretreat. The whitewash choked to death on a chicken bone, and was buried in a church cemetery. He was given a human funeral overseen by a priest. It took ten strong men to bear his oversized, silk-lined casket. The immortal spirit Kor bore Dhaub up to the\nAncestral Plane, to be with the great orcs who came before him. The whitewash was cursed to wander restlessly for eternity. In an endless plane, harsher and hotter than the most lifeless desert, the whitewash trudged on in regret and emptiness. He looked\nup, and saw Dhaub, whom he knew as a cub, resting with the ancestors in perfect health and happiness.\n  “Krug!” the whitewash cried, “Father! Please, help me. Can you not see that I am in agony, doubled over in pain and hunger? Am I not your child? Send\nDhaub with just one morsel from your table, that I might know some relief!”\n  But Krug looked down from the Ancestral Plane with a disdainful sneer, and answered him, “From your very youth, you rejected me as your father. You rejected the ways of your\nancestors and your people. You chose instead to live among the pink-skin, in luxury and comfort, while my true cub, Dhaub, worked hard and grew strong, overcoming every trial in his path. He died with honor, while you died as a selfish fool. Now, he shall\nhave rest, and you shall suffer affliction.”\n  The whitewash pleaded with Krug, “Send me back then, I beg you. Give me the chance to redeem myself, and live as a true orc.”\n  “There is no going back. Even if there was, you would not change. You are weak,\nand you always will be. You would return to your whitewash life of pleasure and indolence, just as the fly returns to the dung heap.”\n  With that, clouds of fire covered the sky, obscuring his view of the Ancestral plane, and leaving him to wander and\nsuffer alone. Dhaub finally found the joy and rest that life had denied him. Remember, brothers and sisters, it is better to suffer with honor, than to sacrifice integrity in the name of pleasure.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mana and Gods", "Kirrekith", "Of Prayer and Mana\n\n   Kirrekith Reffahc\n~                        ~\n       A Summary\n\nBooks to complete the set.\n\nSaints and Paragons\nThe Four\nAenguls\nCreator, Yemekar & Gods\nA Beginning\n~                        ~\nThis book is a theory I have stress tested as best a man within an era of doubt can perform. I believe, the gods, aenguls and daemons all  aspects of mortal religion, are in essence, real. However\n--->\nthis theory isn’t based on who is true and false, it is on their birth and creation. I’ve lived across all our worlds, I’ve lived long enough to see the first of our kin, the original four.  I’ve witnessed the power of all the deities, and felt them \n--->\nrise and fall across the ages. So, let me begin this ideology.\n\nGods, and Aenguls have been around for a great deal of time, and we’ve felt their influence over the ages. However, after the numerous battles and strain they’ve put --->\non themselves in mortal confrontations I have to ask the question; how do they sustain themselves?\n\nClearly the aenguls don’t need water or food, so physical sustenance is impractical for them. So what else could --->\nfuel them? Mana? If so, how do they attain mana? They surely don’t surround themselves in it like mortals, or have mana pools like the Kharajyr. Perhaps it is given unto them from a creator or godlike figure, and so the question is    --->\nsnuffed before we can even explore it. Or, perhaps, prayer is the way the obtain mana to fuel their being.\n\nPrayer fuels them? It would explain why prayer is such a key focus of all the deities, and why they --->\nhold it close and will fight to have a larger stake in prayer. By this very concept though it begs the question, can anything given prayer then become, an Aengul? Well no, and yes. But I’ll explain the process later.\n\n--->\nThis would explain the rise of alternative deities after Asulon. With the fall of the only Aenguls we knew of in Aegis, new ideas and social norms came into being. The belief of the creator, Yemekar, the Brath, Aspectism and more commonly the       --->\nalternate Aenguls. With new faith in place, the channeling of prayer diverted from two thirds of key faith, and began to fuel the birth of the new Aenguls, the power of Yemekar and also the Creator. We can divert questions from true faith in this \n--->\ntheory, as all have presented their powers at different times, and all have valid claim to this.\nFrom Mortal to God\n~                        ~\nSo, let us discuss the power system of these entities, the top being the most powerful and the last the weakest in the chain.\n\n[Next Page]\nGod/Yemekar/Creator~                        ~\n   Aenguls/Daemons\n~                        ~\n        The Four\n~                        ~\n Dragons (not to be    mistaken for drakes)\n~                        ~\n   Saints/Paragons\n~                        ~\nA saint or paragon emerged after Asulon, and was the first indicator that mortals could forge their own deities by the channeling of faith and mana. Oren created saints, and their will and influence has been seen long after their deaths,\n--->\nthe same can be said of Paragons of the Dwarves, returning in the Dweds darkest hours to rally and guide them.  However these were never part of Aegis history, back on the homeland we had many honoured dead pass and be held highly by, though\n--->\nnone prayed to, not until Asulon. Likewise in Oren their religious society besides the Aengul Arial was non existent until Asulon, where Godfrey Horen reformed them and their religious belief, leading to the first of the saints, and then the first\n--->\nrecorded effects of those saintly individuals after death.\n\nDragons are a big uncertainty, I am still unsure as to whether to identify them as magic or natural, though if they’re of magic they can be placed in this      --->\nstructure, as I without doubt believe a saint could be crushed (likewise a paragon) by a dragon. These creatures could do with further study, however finding one content to talk to mortals besides to mess with them is difficult. These    --->\ncreatures aren’t directly prayed to like Saints, Aenguls or the Gods, however the fear and myths of them are pushed into a similar channelled system, pushing power onto them. Now I could be wrong, and they may be natural animals merely more attuned --->\nthan others to magic, but I do not believe in coincidence.\n\nThis area is unclear, are the original four now Aenguls, or are they beneath them? The first of each of the races these entities in early Aegis took on a great deal --->\nof our faith, like the first Aengul and Daemon to our homeland. These creatures lost a lot of their prayer once we came to Asulon, often more a kind word spoken at times, be that Krug, Horen, Urguan or Malin.  I am old enough to      --->\nremember Malin when he returned to us, and his appearance could be considered near saintly in approach, likely his mana far more than a saint and affecting how my vision was able to visualise him.  I believe like in the long since forgotten past they\n--->\nwill return to us once more, and guide us in our hour of need, though faith to them needs to be strengthened to allow for them to once again come back to us.\n\nAenguls need no explanation, they’re prayed to more than --->\nmost, and so have a bigger share of the magic channelled from mortals, these creatures seek the most prayer to fuel them, and so most of our cataclysmic events have been over a deities desire to be more powerful than its rivals.\n--->\nHowever the counter to this that may cause confusion, will be with Daemons. These creatures present  the opposite to Aenguls, and the minority of prayer, so how can they be powerful? These creatures must feed of the fears of    --->\nmortals and stories told of them, though I’d present another idea, what if prayer intent for good only helps to fuel evil? Due to them being specifically aimed to praise and state the holiness of an Aengul, it may be similar to an elastic effect, \n--->\nonly enficisizing the mal qualities of the counter partner, be that Daemon or Aengul, this in turn explaining how something so maleficent can be equal to its adversary.\n\nGods, Yemekar, Metztli and the Creator… All --->\nare unknown entities, their powers yet to be measured. The Dwed claim Yemekar created the world, Metztli made all animals and made the Kharajyr superior, the Creator claims to have made all, Oren viewing it to have made humans the --->\nrace to ascend past the others. We can imagine the powers of any of these, yet we’ll never likely grasp the scope of their abilities. It also adds another question, are others as powerful? Are their other worlds forged by creatures similar to\n--->\nYemekar or the Creator, do these entities fight between themselves, are their deities bigger than them?\nTo Conclude\n~                        ~\nThough this has been very brief, my further documents will do an indepth  study into each entity and their place within the power scape of faith and mana. Though I can outline for now, that these creatures\n--->\ndo have a scale to them, each with its own power created by mortals, as to what we do with this knowledge is for the reader to interpret and act upon. In time perhaps our Aenguls will ascend to Gods, and Paragons to Aenguls and new Saints rise -->\nup as more heroic and the best sides of the races is shown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mana Gems", "Gladuos", "Introduction:\n   Within this book will be the research of various gems for usage in transfiguration practices.\n   Namely, the precious gems are known as ruby, sapphire, emerald, and diamond. Each with their own unique qualities.\nFirstly, each gem will be described in its physical sense, then we'll explore how they're made, average weight, shape, hardness, melting points, magical understandings and much more.\nSight:\n   The gems are usually hard, translucent objects created from minerals within the planet. The diamond is normally a clear substance akin to the visual appearance of glass with an air of shinyness. The other gems follow suit with\nfairly minor differences such as sapphire being blue, ruby being red, emerald being green.\nHow They Form:\n   Most gems are formed when rocks are solluted with water near the surface of the earth, which slowly evaporates and allows the rock to form into minerals. Otherwise gems are often formed by extreme pressure being put onto rocks until -\n- they completely change in makeup.\nThe shape and weight of gems tends to be a differing occurance. Generally gems are relatively dense materials that result in higher weight. They also form together in specialized crystalizations that often create shapes not often seen within nature -\n- such as cubes. \n\n   Gems are some of the hardest materials within the known natural world, with diamond being the hardest of the precious gems.\nThe melting point of gems tend to be at extremely high at over 3500 degrees celsius. They tend to be so resistent to melting that many forges within the known realm would be unable to melt them down. Of course, they are still fairly susceptible -\ntowards being cut and reshaped with chisels or other proper tools.\nThe precious gems have a strangely unique property with magical understandings. They are capable of holding tremendous amounts of mana compared to other materials, relative to valuability and size.\nIt's good to note that there are a plethora of other gems that tend to follow suit with the same characteristics with a few select differences. Otherwise, there are some fairly unique gems that do not follow the norm such as thanhium, focus crystals, -\nand demon stone. These would not be explained in great detail through this book, but may be in the future.\n*Upon flipping to the next page, you are greeted with a plethora of diagrams, charts, sketchings, illustrations, equations, and secondary notes that go on for pages upon pages. They appear to attempt supporting and bolstering previous statements within -\n- the book as well as making a few minor unspoken statements.*", ""),
        StaticBook("ManfestMoe", "JavaWizard", "This iz a buk wit ten bye Moezez Ambearto!\n\nArm in iz beg;; Moezez iz smal;;\n\nAye doont lik buks beacause ther havy!\n\n*A large ink stain is here taking up the rest of the page*\n*An odd drawing is here.... it looks like a fish with wings and a tail*\n\n        Moezezzz \n\n     ManIfesTO\n\nMoezezzz MAnifesto\n\n_ _ ____ _ >\nSaVe AnmalS and playnts !\n\nHalp evryony for fre!\n\nTeche how too do thing! (fre)\n\nDont ALLow mean!\n\nStope Bad wURds!\n\nEvryony egual!", ""),
        StaticBook("Many Thanks!", "The Pale Brotherhood", "Hail friend. You have been visited by the forces of misfortune.\n\nThe Pale Brotherhood sends its regards.\n\nYour things have gone towards a good cause. That is our cause of course.\n\nWe thank you.\nBy blood and by smoke.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                       D.G.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mark's Letter", "oblivionsbane", "Dear Prey,\n\nIt doesn't matter how long it takes for me to see you, I love you. If anything it just makes seeing you even more special. At least I hope that is the only reason you left. I should also tell you that I have had my memories back for several\nmonths now and just haven't said anything. I love being with you, I built this house for you, and I just feel lonely without you. I don't want to find anybody else becauses there is no one else to find. I waited years just to meet you, why would I ever\nwant anyone else? You are all I need and all I want, I do wish you were around more, but I am sure you wish I was around you more too. Why didn't you talk to me about this anyways? I know I love you and that is why I am going to find you. After all, I\nstill have a gift for you, and I refuse to give it to anyone else. When I saw it I immiediately thought of you so I had to get it. I hope you are okay, I love you.\n\n-Mark", ""),
        StaticBook("Marriage Advice", "Laethis Izalith", "Wedding tips from Haelun'or:\n\n----------\n\n1. Always remain pure.\n2. Produce many crotch-fruit.\n3. Do not stop melting impures.\n4. Always have tea present for social occasions.\n5. Do not copulate\nneedlessly.\n6. Cocaine makes weddings fun.\n7. I dundj thhik i wrate annmurr.\n8. Hiiiiiiighhhhhg", ""),
        StaticBook("Mathic Code", "Rosso", "From a note written by a friend in code, of many pages, she had no memory of writing it, or what it did mean.\nI decided to try and decipher it as if it were a secret note between armies, and I came with results. The code is copied first, then the meaning of the code is told, then the translation.\nCode\n{t, ƒ:ªº£ ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, ñ.nü| ƒ'ª t, u':ô .nô t, ,ñö£:n,ºº d,i'û t, u':ô û,ª, e:º £' c'ññ.nô]\n[t,ü û,ª, ô\"º£ .nô e, û.º .º . º\"nd,.ñ| ô,ƒ:n:nø .£ i.º£ t,:ª ê.ö,]\n[.º û.º d,ƒ'ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, .ø.:n| û:t t, º'ªª'û 'ƒ º\"ni:øe£ ª,ñ.:n:nø \"n£ª,.£,ô .nô \"nû,ic'ñ, £' t, ô,,ö c\"ªª,n£º 'ƒ t, º,.]\n[º\"ç ô:ª,c£:'ni,ººn,ºº :º .n.t,ñ. £' e:ñ| ûe' :º i:n,.ª]\n[t,º, .ª, £' d, E:º £ª:\"ñöeº .nô E:º ƒ.:i:nøº| ñ.nü £:ñ,º 'u,ª]\n{t, º,c‘nô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.c£:‘nº ‘ƒ t.£ ûe:ç :º e, .ª, d.ªª,ô ƒª‘ñ ,n£ªü]\n[t, ‘t,ªº e.u, t,:ª ô,u:c,º ‘ƒ û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n| ô,ƒ:n:æ t,ñ .º ûe.£ t,ü .iû.üº e.u, d,,n| t, c.ª,£.*,ªº ‘ƒ t,:ª ƒ.£,]\n[t,ü ê‘“£ .nô öi,.ô .nô ‘ƒƒ,ª t,:ª u‘:c,º £‘ t, e,.u,nº| d“£ t,ü .ª, .º t, ô,,ö c.u,º d,øø:æ ƒ‘ª º“ni:øe£]\n[t, û.ü :º ê“£]\n{t, t:ªô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[. ‘n, £,.ªº ƒª,, t, di:nôƒ‘iô ‘ƒ t, .düºº ƒª‘ñ t, ,ü,º ‘ƒ t, ö.ª£º]\n[:£ :º .º :£ û.º]\n[t, i:øe£ .nô i:øe£º .nô i:øe£:æ ‘ƒ t,:ª êª:n,º ƒª,, t,:ª º:øe£| t.£ t,ü ñ.ü di:nô ‘t,ªº]\n[û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n .ø.:n º“øø,º£º :£º,iƒ| .nô t, i:n, :º ñ.ô, .º .n “nc‘“n£.di, º,ª:,º ‘ƒ ö‘:n£º| .ii :n c‘nƒi:c£ û:t t,:ª ƒ,ii‘ûº]\n[.ii û:,iô:æ t,:ª i.û]\n{t, ƒ‘“ªt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t,:ª i.û :º t, ö‘û,ª ‘ƒ t, ñ.nü]\n[ºi‘ûiü t, i:øe£º .ª, ,æª.u,ô û:t t, ºüñd‘iº ‘ƒ t, ,nº,ñdi,º ‘ƒ t, ñ.nü]\n[t, º:øe£º ‘ƒ n,û ç.:nº .ª, ƒ.ñ:i:.ª]\n{t, ƒ:ƒt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.øñ,n£º .ª, ñ.ô, .º £‘ø,t,ª .º û.º d,ƒ‘ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e,]\n[t, ñ.nü ç‘‘º, t,:ª ö.t| £‘ t, ª,ö,£:£:‘n .º t, º“n ª:º,º .nô ƒ.iiº ‘ª £‘ t, dª,.*:æ ‘ƒ :£| t.£ t, º“n ê.ii º£.nô º£:ii]\n{t, º:xt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ñ.nü d,c‘ñ, .º ‘n, .º û.º t.£ ûe:ç :º e,]\n{t, º,u,nt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[.º û.º d,ƒ‘ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º ñ.nü ñ.ô, .ø.:n]\nMeaning\n. - a\n, - e\n: - i\n‘ - o\n“ - u\n\nt - th\nƒ - f\nª - r\nº - s\n£ - t\nñ - m\nc - c\nø - g\nû - w\ne - h\nç - ch\nô - d\nn - n\nü - y\nu - v\nö - p\nd - b\ni - l\nê - sh\n* - k\næ - ng\n\n| - ,\n\n[] - sentance\n{} - title\nTranslation\nThe first mathic age.\n\nThat which is He made many, for the void and the emptiness below the void were His to command.\nThey were dust and He was as a sunbeam, defining at last their shape.\nAs was before, that which is He made again, with the sorrow of sunlight remaining untreated and unwelcome to the deep currents of the sea.\nSuch directionless is anathema to Him, who is linear.\nThese are to be His triumphs and His failings, many times over.\nThe second Mathic age\n\nThe fractions of that which is he are barred from entry.\nThe others have their devices of war and disunion, defining them as what they always have been, the caretakers of their fate.\nThey shout and plead and offer their voices to the heavens, but they are as the deep caves begging for sunlight.\nThe way is shut.\nThe third Mathic age\n\nA one tears free the blindfold of the abyss from the eyes of the parts.\nIt is as it was.\nThe light and lights and lighting of their shrines free their sight, that they may blind others.\nWar and disunion again suggests itself, and the line is made as an uncountable series of points, all in conflict with their fellows.\nAll wielding their law.\nThe Fourth Mathic Age\n\nTheir law is the power of the many.\nSlowly the lights are engraved with the symbols of the ensembles of the many.\nThe sights of new chains are familiar.\nThe Fifth Mathic Age\n\nThe fragments are made as together as was before, that which is he\nThe many choose their path, to the repetition as the sun rises and falls or to the breaking of it, the sun shall stand still.\nThe Sixth Mathic Age\n\nThe many become as one as was that which is he.\nThe Seventh Mathic Age\n\nAs was before, that which is he many made again.\nMathic Code\n\nCoppied and Decoded by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Mattthekid2003", "Mok'han'Braduk", "I am an alchemist, i used my skills of living off the land to profit, it was a modest job. My name is Zerki and this is my journey.\nI had just respawned in the Cloud Temple, i slowly formed, but some part of me was missing, my ribcage. I had to crawl into the forrest, make a wheelchair out of my weak bear hands and make a machine that would let me live.\nThe machine itself is nothing short of brilliant. The first part of it was a genius idea to help with my breathing. Since my lungs would break down eventually without ribs, i needed to find another way to breath.\nI hooked up a device to my body that sucked in oxegen from the air and underwent various alchemical stages to turn into nutrients for my body, after this i used a special brew to put my lungs to sleep, so i wouldn't damage them.\nThe 2nd's is a tube built into my body to store my piss so that way it doesn't enter my lungs for when i try to walk again.", "")
    )

    private fun _VAILOR_4(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Maturity", "Azoth Hawksong", "Goodbye.\nIt's time-\nto be on your own.\nLost in new life,\nA long way from home.\n\nCherish your past of\njuvenile leisure-\nWhere the conflicts\nYou faced\nwere but scorn\nof a teacher.\nNow you're grown up\nand are shown\njust how far,\nYour prepareness\ncan take you-\na blessing or a scar.\n\nYour record\nwon't shape you,\nbut the risks\nthat you take:\nThe harships we face\nand the lives\nthat we change.\n\nBy the end\nof this journey\nyou'll be so more\nfree.\nJust a feeling,\nit is, but\nits purpose, you see:\n\nWas to simulate life\nand to usher you in\nTo our final\nlong venture,\nwhich ends\nwhen we end.\n\n- Azoth Hawksong", ""),
        StaticBook("May'ilu", "Wodehouse", "With a clinking and chiming of bracelets signalling the arrival of her lover, Velara could hardly keep a grin off of her face as she rested her elbows on the furnished wooden counter, hands delicately supporting her head as she watched Mayirr sway\ninto the shop, pink hair cascading elegantly down over her precious shoulders. The two stare at each other for a moment; A soft 'Karin'ayla' was all that needed saying. They lingered over each others frames for a moment before Mayirr broke the gaze,\nslipping lithely around the counter to cuddle Velara from behind. The pink haired elf's ears twitched sensitively as she held her may'ilu, her cheeks turning a similar colour as they stood there silently. Mere moments passed, and the door to the shop\nrattled open, breaking the two apart. \nWatching Velara abruptly disappear down to the basement with a look of utter embarassment, Mayirr smiles, her cheeks flushed with the same feeling as she looks back to greet the customer.", ""),
        StaticBook("MeadowbloomPoems", "Arnorian", "His green eyes never leave my gaze\nand his beard will always be brown,\nhis kilt never lost its colour\nas he kept not a trace of a frown.\nHis high stature has yet to be forgotten\nwhat with his boom laughter and grin,\nand his highspirits not only with his family\nbut also in the tavern with his gin.\nHis comforting words kept me going\nas his form took shape in my mind,\nfor it was I who kepts his memories,\nit was I that he never left behind.\nI cannot say I enjoyed all of it\nfor that man saw too many wars,\nbut he also had his moments of triumph,\nand those he loved dearly of course.\nHe kept his mind straight and level\neven under the most pressure,\nhe always knew where his place was\nand respected those who were lesser.\nSometimes he forgot right from wrong,\nbut then again, we all to at some point,\nand yet he knew how to keep people motivatied\neven though he was hard to dissapoint.\nAnd though I miss him still to this day,\nwith years gone since he passed,\nI still wish Hanrahan was here with me,\nbut for now his memories will stay glassed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medical Std. V1", "The Scribe.", "A Study of Medicine. \nPossibly Volume 1,\nAnatomy.\n\nAssisted by Salazar the Mali'Aheral.\n'One learns to figure out the limits of one's body as one travels.' ~Salazar.\n\nThe cadavers of less fortunate travelers make for good study; \nTheir bodies can be found suffering from illnesses or ailments,\nand studying them was an urge that could not be repressed.\nChapter 1: Circulation of Blood.\n\nThe circulatory system runs throughout the body. It provides blood to various muscles and organs, replenishing them with every beat of the heart. Blood provides Anima to the body, which is the life\nforce that drives us all, and gives us energy. Anima may possibly contain a variety of elements that we require to function in life. As one works more strenuously, the circulatory system does as well. This may be because as the body\nuses energy, it requires more anima to function at the previous levels.\nAilments of the Circulatory System;\n\nA disease of the circulatory system causes the blood to not coagulate where it may normally do so. This causes the patient afflicted with such a disorder to bleed profusely, until magic is introduced.\nThis disease is highly rare.\n\nAnother disease is caused by the blood vessels themselves being left open to the air or to water for a long time. This causes blood-poisoning, an infection of the blood itself.\nThis can be treated a variety of ways, though none of which are easy. Amputation is the most rudimentary form of this. The next is quick cleansing of the wound with pure water and alchemically based healing potions. The third is to use clerical magic, but\nsuch can be considered a panacea.\n\nThis condition is uncommon, as most open wounds are wrapped.\nChapter Two; Digestive.\n\nThe digestive system consists of the stomach, smaller intestine, large intestive, and the excrementory system. \n\nThe stomach contains within it a large amount of naturally produced\nacid which dissolves food that is consumed through the mouth. After the food is broken down, it seems to be passed through both intestines, where it is absorbed into the body. Of course, these broken down materials most likely filter into the blood system\nwhere the blood and the body converts the food to anima. This is why death by starvation can take place. However, the body itself can overstock these necessary nutrients, and cause fatness and obesity.\nDigestive diseases. \n\nThe stomach acid can become too concentrated and can break down the lining of the stomach. This can cause severe pain. The most common cure for this is the direct consumption of tippens root, as it brings the pH of\nthe stomach acid down to natural levels. \n\nAnother digestive issue is an illness that causes constant vomiting, or constant bowel movements. While vomitting is the bodies natural defense against bad food, this vomit is\nvery common even with high quality food. The best way to deal with this sickness is to consume mass quantites of salted water, as such replenishes the bodies well-being after their body exterts it. Sugar should also be added to the water.\nThis disease can be common or rare depending on its severity. \n\nOne may also vomit if they exert themselves to a point of exhaustion.\nChapter 3; Respiratory.\n\nThe Respiratory system contains the lungs and the windpipe. The windpipe is located behind the thick protective cover at the front of the throat. The lungs suction air from the environment\ninto them through use of a muscle underneath the lungs called the diaphragm. The lungs expand to hold the inhaled air, and then the air is pushed out. However, the body somehow utilizes the gas, most likely to produce more efficient anima.\nIf blood is deprived of the air, it turns purple and sickly looking. When re-exposed to the air, it turns bright red. My belief is that blood uses one of the gases that comprises air to convert nutrients into anima.\nBetween both of our knowledge, no diseases or ailments of the respiratory system were known, but the respiratory system can be damaged through the inhalation of coal fumes, causing 'Black-Breath'. This cannot be cured except by\nthe magic of the monks.\nChapter 4; Muscular.\n\nThe muscles are connected to the bones by tendons, stretchy bits of yellow 'flesh' that allows for the full range of motion. The muscles of the body tend to work in groups of two, one to push, and the other to pull.\nThe larger the muscle, the greater the force exerted by the movement of the muscle. As muscles are damaged through use, they heal and grow larger, thusly more powerful. This is why one is sore after strenuous exercize.\nNo ailment of the muscle is cureable. The degrading of muscle is either through use of magic, or by some ailment. Both of these result in the eventual loss of the majority of muscle.\nThere appear to be three types of muscle, involuntary, mixed, and voluntary. Involuntary muscles can not be controlled at all, such as the heart or the digestive muscles. \n\nMixed can be controlled some of the time, but for the\nmost part, operate on their own. This includes breathing, blinking, and swallowing. \n\nVoluntary muscles are only able to be used with input, such as the arms or the legs.\nChapter Five; Bones.\n\nThe bones are the structure of the body. They also offer protection. Bones are incredibly dense, most are stronger than steel. The amount of bones in a body is 206, with six tiny, tiny bones in the ears that some\nhow are linked directly to balance. The bones can heal themselves if set correctly, though clerical magic allows this process to finish faster.\nThere are no known ailments of the bone.\nAddendums; \nBruises are the pooling of blood from broken blood vessels.\n\nThe heart is an involuntary muscle.\n\nThe circulatory system involves vessels that take blood to the heart to replenish in anima,\nand arteries that take anima-enriched blood away from the heart to the muscles and other parts of the body.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medicine Vol. 1", "Kale", "A Dose of Solace\nVolume 1\n\nWritten By: Dr. Kale\n\n\nIn this book you will find effortless remedies to common day sicknesses.\n1. Stomach Pain\n\n1 cup of hot chamomile tea\n3 peppermint leafs\n\nPlace the leafs on top of the hot steamy cup of tea and drink it twice a day to ease the churning pain.\n2. Flashes (Fever)\n\n4 rags\n1 big bucket of cold water\n\nSoak the rages with water and place each rag on the forehead, under each arm pit and behind the neck. Do so as needed until it subsides.\n3. Burning Throat\n\n1 hot cup of water\n5 drips of honey\n2 tsp. of sugar\n\nMix it all together thoroughly and sip until your throat begins to feel soothing.\n4. Coughing\n\n1 rag\n1 pot of boiling water\n\nPlace it rag over your mouth and bend your head close enough to the steam and breathe it in. Do this until your coughing has calmed itself.\n5. Ear Pain\n\n   Warm up oil until it is at a lukewarm feel and pour it into the ear. Lay on the opposite ear that isn't causing you pain. The pain should stop momentarily.\n6. Bruises \n\nThere's multiple remedies to heal a bruise quickly \n\n1st- Cold Herbal Tea Compress\n2nd- Ice Block compress\n3rd- Cold Poppy Tea Compress\n7. Rashes\n\nCacutus Paste\nHerbal Tea\n\nMash the two together until it become a thick like paste. Rub the paste on the rash until it drys or can be scraped off.\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to make the rash paste*\n\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to apply a compress to a bruise*\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to make different teas*\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to mix honey with tea* \n\n*Here would be a sketch of a person breathing in the steam with a rag covering their mouth*\n\n[!] The sketch would be drawn very well", ""),
        StaticBook("Medicine: V1", "Jayce Ba'Ikana", "Medicine handbook:\n\nHere is where I'll keep track of all the remedies to different ailments.\nStomach Pain:\n\n1 Cup of Chamomile tea\nand chew peppermint leaves.\nFever:\n\nPlace cold water rags over the forehead of patient.\nBurning throat:\n\nHot water, sugar, honey. Mix together and sip thoroughly\nCough:\n\nRag and a pot of boiling water\n\nPlace rag over mouth and breathe in steam until coughing resides\nBruises:\n\nPlace ice over bruise and hold there until it fades. Be careful of ice burns", ""),
        StaticBook("Meditation", "Thereon Ireheart", "Bardmancy Meditation\n\nTo become a Bardmancer you must first connect with \"The Void\" a magical force that gives a Mage their power.\n\nBardmancers at first need much \"Mana\" of magical energy to connect but once they have connected they\nneed far less \"Mana\" to use and sustain their magic.\n\nMeditating\n\nTo meditate with \"The Void\" they must first get three things Wax Candles, a copy of the Bardmancy Tome, and a Quiet place with a statue of a Godly figure.\nOnce someone has these three things they need only Knell or Sit facing the God/Goddess with the Candles lit and they must pray to the God or Goddess.\n\n((You must Pray 4 times with a /roll of 15 or higher))", ""),
        StaticBook("Meditations", "Dauth Sundavar", "A Compendium of\n            Questions\n\n\n\n\n         Written by\n      Dauth Sundavar\nAs soon as I stepped into the wilderness, all of time slipped from my grasp. The days and nights melded into one intaginable idea, defined only by the changes in the temperature and the prevalence of creatures within the respective landscape.\nI followed the direction of the winds, the brightest star in the cosmos, the natural pathways within the environment that didn't particularly lead me anywhere. \n\nIt was during my wanderings that I realised the enormity of nature. It must be amazing to be\na Druid; to be connected with every aspect of nature and have a profound understanding of the mechanics behind our very existence. \n\nBut we laymen are ignorant to the true nature of the world around us. We do not know the songs of the land, the stories\nthat are interwoven into the very fabric of the land; the collection of lives that have been, and have seeped into into the very land itself.\n\nI lost sight of myself during my journeys. I lost sight of who I know myself to be, but also who I present\nmyself to be. \n\nI was alone. I spoke to no one. The sound of silence seeped into my very being and began to unravel the knots that filled empty space within my mind and soul. I was being pulled in so many different directions, my mind catching on the\ncracks and crevices that filled my mind. \n\nI thought I was going mad; losing my mind just as any elder of any race does in due time. Multitudes of questions spiralled within the tangle that was my consciousness, drowning each other out and threatening to\nconsume me. \n\nAnd then there was silence. And darkness. A shroud of shadow unbeknown to any man or woman. \n\nAnd I slept. \n\nI don't know how long for.\nAfter I awoke, my mind was, although fractured in some places, whole. The voices had abated, and my heart no longer threatened to leap out of my chest.\n\nIt was nighttime when I awoke. Laying beneath a shroud of leaves, I peered through the\nfoliage into the clear night sky, adorned with millions of stars that flickered at their own accord. \n\nAt first, I studied them all; creating constellations of my own fashion as I basked within the tranquility of the night.\nI saw a stag bounding across the veil of pitch; a soldier garbed with a belt forged from the most brilliant of stars; a wolf with his teeth bared.\n\nI named him the Dread Wolf.\n\nAnd then I began to question whether the stars had their own\nthoughts just as the other aspects of nature did. Can the Druids hear their calls from the heavens, just as they do with the isles of oak that feature so frequently?\n\nOr do the stars exist in another plane of existence? Is the cosmos where the\nAenguls reside when they are absent from the world?\n\nI thought about death a lot. Is death just another plane of existence? \n\nThe Druids say that the best of their Order reside with the Aspects in their own dimension\nwhen their time has passed. What happens to those not of the Order?\n\nI see it this way. We die. Within due time, we turn to dust. The earth then claims our remains and sews us into the very fabric of the land. This is where the voices that the\nDruids hear come from.\n\nIt is nice to think that we serve a purpose after we die. \n\nUnless a Blight happens.\n\nI don't want that to happen.\nI sang to the earth sometimes. I didn't speak to it though. I just sang. I sang words that meant nothing but meant everything at the same time. There is no language for it; only emotion.\n\nI am a very emotional person. Sometimes I let my emotions cloud my\njudgement and I say things that I don't mean to say. But it wasn't me saying them; it was my emotions.\n\nBut at the same time, it was still me.\n\nI want to apologise to Marcy for what I said to her. But maybe she won't accept it, and I'll get angry again.\nThat would be bad. I would probably say hurtful things again.\n\nPerhaps I should stay silent. That way I can't hurt anyone with my words. I want to heal, to help; not hurt.\n\nThere is a song that resides within us all. I believe it defines our very natures.\nI want to find mine.\n\nMaybe if I learn my song, I won't be a slave to my emotions any more.\n\nWhich begs the question.\n\nWho am I?\n\nI need to find out.", ""),
