        StaticBook("Meteor Messages", "Aengoth", "--- so the tomes -- ----- descended ---- ---- -- boon --\n\n---- ------- Dragons --- ---- --- ------- Fire\n\nFell ---- Fell ----\n\n----- --- lost to fire\n\n---- --- need ---- --- dire\n----- slumber ----- --- die\n\n\nWriting found on the various meteorites, documented by Aengoth on the 16th of the Snow's Maiden, 1554.", ""),
        StaticBook("Meteor Studies", "Fury_Fire", "This book will detail experiments done upon a vial of liquid found within a fallen meteor to the west of the cloud temple. If this book is found anywhere except for the grand Library of Dragur, it is stolen. Written by Lefkos Amethil.\nThe meteor that fell was generally different then that of others. For starters, it had not only been coated with fire as it descended from the sky- but magma leaked out of cracks within it. Eventually the magma would stop flowing and I would cool down the\nrock, merely studying it while those greedy began to mine away at the ore-like substances upon it. I grabbed only three pieces to study, which in the end proved to just be a metal harder then ferrum, lighter then carbarum, and very light. Past that, I had\nthose who were mining begin digging towards the center, where more magma erupted out. Using air evocation, it was sent flying to reveal the true contents of the center. This being what appeared to look like a portal showing the stars behind it. Several\nof the less educated folk jumped in- myself included, sadly. Upon realization that it was instead just a liquid that appeared as a portal, I took a sample and crawled out. The others were late, and the liquid hardened around them as black creatures began\nto lift out from it, each sharing the same look as the liquid- except shaped as large lizard type creatures. They of course, began to attack. The people inside the substance died, and those outside fought as I prepared a calldown spell. When it was ready,\nI killed all the creatures, and also resulted in the destruction of the meteor. Me and my friend Daniel left with the substance soon after, going to study it. The next few pages will go over each test we did, and how it reacted.\nTest one\nTemperature\n\nWe began by first sticking a finger in it to test the temperature, deducting that it  generally stays cool, but not overly so. We attempted to heat up the vial it was in, whilst sticking our fingers inside. Such resulted in\nthe substance becoming very much more liquidy then it had been, yet still sticky. It all seemed to slide off and leave us dry when removing our fingers. When making it colder, it grew more sticky and less liquid, yet still there\nTest two\nMovement\n\nNext we would proceed to pour a small drop of it onto the table, and the results were fascinating. Like a blob, it began to slide- yet only towards the vial. No matter how much we moved it, the liquid always tried to rejoin the bigger\nhalf. This hinted at a lifeform of sorts, and after further testing for magical properties, we decided it to be mundane.\nTest three\nLife\n\nWe next brought it to the druid grove, in order to see if a Druid would be able to communicate with it. The one that tried told us that it was alive, yet refused to speak and only gave her silence.\nTest Four\nFeeding\n\nWe proceeded to drop mere breadcrumbs in the liquid, and wait. For a good several days nothing would happen to the chunks that floated in, until they began to mold. Slowly it deteriorated into nothing, which leaves us to believe it\nfeeds in a similar way to a venus fly trap.\nConclusion\n\nAfter many other tests, we concluded that nothing more could be done with it, and our attempts were leading us nowhere.\n\nOur results were as follows: It reacts to tempurature, growing sticker or slicker depending on what is\ndone with it. It is alive, and can sense where its greater half is no matter the distance- yet for some reason doesn't try to go to the original meteor. Perhaps a minor 'hive mind' that was part of many other ones. It can be fed, although slowly. And it\nrefuses to speak with druids at all, giving them only silence.\nAs a final curiousity test, unimportant to the book, we had a moongazer show us a vision of the liquids origins. What we saw was the meteor floating past many stars in the sky, round and giant objects of many colors as it came to us. We seek to study\nthose another time.", ""),
        StaticBook("mi found diz", "'Big Green'", "Adventures of Thorindil and Lenai\n\nToday we went to Felsen, but I will start with what is going on before my own eyes first. A Kharajyr tryed to re-enter Felsen. I saw him earlier. A bunch of Felsen guards decided to surround the Kha in the city gates!\nA man just grabbed the Kha.. A boy is now pushing him.. Poor Kha! I think they are going to kill him! These people are evil! How could they do something like this to him! He just broke the spine of the Kha! The Golden armor men are literally tearing the\nKha to pieces! The Gold Corp is full of barbarians!", ""),
        StaticBook("Mice Are Nice!", "Dooble_Brick", "A Dedicants Poem On Mice\nBy Milly Turner\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~MICE\nI think mice are rather nice;\nTheir tails are long, their faces small;\nThey haven't any chins at all.\nTheir ears are pink, their teeth are white,\nThey run about the house at night;\nThey nibble things they shouldn't touch,\nand no one seems to like them much,\nbut I think mice are nice!", ""),
        StaticBook("Minas, A Guide", "Ebonsquire", "((Originally scribed by williewonka1))\n\nMinas: A Beginner's Guide\n\nHail, if ye are reading this book then yer new to the great land of Aegis. Aegis is a wonderful place full of great mystery. There are many ways to earn Minas: trade, hunting, mining, and work. But we ye are new\nthe only one that is easy to get money is hunting. Hunting is not always easy to do but can be very rewarding. The first thing that ye need to do is make or get a sword. Just find a tree and cut it down and make sticks. Get cobble stone and make a stone\nsword. Now kill a few cows and get leather. Ye don't need full armor just some to get protection. Now that ye are ready it is time to start hunting. Once ye have all of yer gear it is important to know the monsters ye are hunting. The first we will speak\nof are Spiders. Spiders are very common and do not die during the day. They can only earn ye up to ten minas, but if yer very lucky ye will get a diamond. Next are skeletons. They have a bow and some arrows. They can be dangerous but should not be a big\nthreat. They will mostly give arrows, bows and bones and about ten minas. Then there are zombies. Zombies are very difficult but ye earn about 15 minas. They also mostly give out coal when ye kill 'em. Now the most important monster is the creeper. They\nare very sensitive to blowing up so to kill them you must be very careful. But if ye kill one ye can get up too 30 minas. And they drop iron a lot so ye can upgrade your sword, or armor. So creepers are a beginner's best friend. Now, slimes\nare very risky to kill and they only give up to five minas. So I would stick to creepers, skeletons, and spiders. Now stop reading and get out there and make some minas. Good luck.", ""),
        StaticBook("Miners Guide V.1", "Azkel Frostbeard", "Mining is a very complicated profession with many different aspects. For beginners, it is much more challenging to break the materials and to learn how to break new ones youve found along your journeys.For expert miners, all materials seem like the back\nof your hand. This book will explain the titles you aquire as you gain more knowledge about the topic. \nAs you start off, you are known as a Promising Miner. As a Promising Miner, you are just having your first experiences with a pickaxe, and are\nstarting off with the basic materials of stone, coal, and ferrum. With the little knowledge of mining you have, you still need to learn how to properly swing a pickaxe. Just with a little skill, youll be able to be known as a Bungling Miner. As a Bungling\nMiner, you have had your first experiences with a pickaxe and materials.You dont learn anything much at this stage, but you are starting off the process.After you gain some more expericance, you become a Clumsy Miner. Nothing much changes\nin terms of your knowledge, but you are getting better with a pickaxe.After youve had your first tries with the mining, youve become an Apprentice Miner! Now as an Apprentice, you've finally started to know how to use the pickaxe, and are able to swing it\nmuch faster. Now that you've learned how to properly use a pickaxe, you have become a Fair Miner. As a Fair Miner, you are able to mine many new Materials! Now that youve mastered the Stone layer of the underground, now its time to conquer the Diorite\nportion! With this new layer comes new materials such as Lapis and Emeralds! You now have moved up in the miner chain with new knowledge of different blocks. After the exciting chapter of being a Fair Miner, youll be able to mine Aurum! With this ore,\nyoull be able to sell and make a good profit. As another layer closes, another opens. Now as a Proficient Miner, you can head down a new layer and mine Andesite! As you ease into the world of Andesite you become an Adept Miner. Nothing new\nexcept more exploration through the layers! Now a new and important title is a Veteran Miner! As a Veteran you can go down a new level to mine Granite. Along with the granite will come Diamonds, the precious gem most people want to find!\nVolume 1. of this book describes the journey of a Promising Miner, through a Veteran Miner. Look for Volume 2 for the next group of mining titles!", ""),
