        StaticBook("Missed Payment", "Siri", "Notice of missed tax payment\nHello there owner,\n\nI noticed that you have not paid the first week's taxes, and that's not good as the Province requires everyone to contribute to its prosperity and growth. If you are having troubles paying,\ndo talk to Siri or Calius in order to work out a compromise. \n\nShould you miss the next payment as well, on the 3rd year the Stewards will be forced to confiscate your home and property so that we can house others waiting for a home.\nHere is a guide in case you are unsure of how to pay taxes!\n\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/133043-laurehlin-tax-guide/\n\nThank you for your time,\n\nSiri, Guildmaster of Laureh'lin", ""),
        StaticBook("Mission Book", "Volug Irving", "The Covenant of Mar\nMission Book: 002\n\nAssigned to: Cal Marq\nBy: Valkelm Za'goth\n\nCatagory:\nIntelligence Gathering\n\nPayout:\n30 Minas\n\nTime Alotted: 1 Elven Day\nMission Details:\n\nGather information on the Elves, find out one of the three leaders.  Find all three for bonus pay.\nNames: The Sohear- Kalenz", ""),
        StaticBook("Missive", "Artorius Thannius", "Missive to the People I - The Revolt\nThe Circle of Governance would like to inform all citizens of the Enlightened Caste that the city is now back under control: the revolt of the lesser castes has been suppressed. I would like to\nformally dispel the rumours that this revolt was led by one of the orc beasts. It is laughable that a beast of burden could conceive of a plan of revolt, instruct the lesser caste in the use of tools of labour as weapons, and lead the lesser caste up\nin arms against the Enlightened. It is obvious that this must be have been a coup attempt by one of the Enlightened, and we will spare no expense in hunting down the leader of this insurrection and reeducating them.\nI also wish to reassure the\nenlightened people of Rivel that the recent mass euthanasia of the orc beasts is to prevent the spread of disease amongst them, not, as some have had the lack of wisdom to suggest, to prevent further revolt. Orcs do not think, this is a clearly\nestablished fact. They are simple beasts possessing no capacity for higher thought nor magical skill. Likewise, the recent introduction of “reorientation” of members of the lesser caste via mental magic is simply to improve their\nefficiency and wellbeing. The idea that we are attempting to turn them into “drones” is equally unfounded, and I would request such rumours are ceased: we do not wish to agitate the Lesser Caste and reduce the efficiency of their\nservice to us.\n- Artorius Thannius, Exalted Spellcrafter Archon of Rivel", ""),
        StaticBook("Missive 3", "Tarien Arvius", "Missive to the Spellcrafter Archon III - The Hall\nTo the Spellcrafter Archon,\nWe found the Hall and found it sealed. The Forgotten Dwarves appear to have sealed it from the outside with five keys, and we know not how to open it.\nWhile I felt unease at opening this place, my fears seem to have left me. We must open this hall. It is the will of the Radiant Man. We will assist him in finding the keys, we will open this Hall, and we will find the Seal. And with it, we will strike\ndown the Ravager and ensure the eternal survival of Rivel. I will not be returning to Rivel first as planned: I no longer have any fears about mental control by the Radiant Man. We will find the keys first, there is no reason to delay.\n- Spellcrafter\nTarien Arvius", ""),
        StaticBook("MOMOSKAH", "Krom'Braduk", "Upon my travels I have come across a boat near the northern end of the island Laurehlin is at. After taking this boat I was on a medium sized snowy island, and on here a single fortress like structure lies, while I do not know the purpose of this place I\nsuspect it to be dark. MOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH\nMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAHMOMOSKAH", ""),
        StaticBook("Mon Lamentation", "Ser Aymer Fournier", "1st of Sun's Smile, 1539\n--------------------------------\n   The gravel toils in the heat and bright sunshine that holds my feet, boundlessly tightening as days go on. My tentative demeanor grows as I write in this extraneous scripture, looking up\nevery few minutes to see the hastle and bustlement of nearby laborers and soldiers. I had finished marking down the tax pay for Riveryn, when yet another young man approaches, his voice premature with embryonic tendencies. I allowed him to speak his\npeace, and he wished to spar with me. Interesting.\nI humored him, and it turned he was the squire of Denis de Bar. Emery of Felsen, it would seem. Mon ami, he was a rather rude lad at first, but it was expected. He put up a good fight, though it is\nonly expected he would be bested. Tax revenue has been completed, and it would seem the malnourished towns activity is bustling with an elated grasp of security.\n-------------------------------------\n\n2nd of Sun's Smile\n--------------------------\nMon ami,\nI miss Aurelia. From the dearly held talks we held to the.. and now, she ascertains herself within the dreaded confines of that sordid palace, solitituded with a man she does non love. It is to be expected, I am a simple Baron, what could I do to deserve\nher. My candor cannot be more cynical, when it is brought down to an intrepid fact. And two days ago, I released myself, and called Rhys out on his brutish actions, and was lashed a multitude for it. She - watched as I took the wrothful punishment, and\nassisted my beaten structure to Riveryn. Even after all those years, my, my. I stand here now, pitted between the petty squabbles between Rhys, and the Vladov's. I must retain connections, no matter what the cost. Blood for Ashford.   \n-----------------\n3rd of Sun's Smile\n-------------------------\n   What is this meaning, Denis? Thoughtful of marrying off your loyal, wonderful daughter to this heathenous creature, whom all his wives died in his clasp, for a dowry? What kind of man are you, monsiuer. I\nwould not dare say that I am better than the creature, but he is non a good family keeper. My solitude is confined, whilst he married Aurelia off to that Horen, and raised my taxes. as well as marry off his daughter to my enemy. He soon expects my\ndaughter to be wed to Guy de Bar. He has made too many mistakes. I am a simply vassal, but it disgusts me, his ungratefulness. My wroth cannot be contained in my private chambers. I become busy, but lonely. And he thrusts me along, his beckoning hand\ndriving on us all.\n------------------------\n4th of Sun's Smile\n-------------------------\n   I slept with Aphia.. and I.. ridded myself off all the tension I had held up. What has happened to me? What have I become? A monster of my own making. My children\ngrow absent, distant. I fall far away, in solitude, no love from the one I need most in this dreaded existence, nobody. The constant magnanimous structure I hold up for Rhys, the tedious tasks such as tax revenue, and menial pleasantries, all day to day\nprodigal behaviour. I believe it has been good for my land, for Savoy, for the Order.. though, non good for me.\n-------------------------------------\n5th of Sun's Smile\n-------------------------------------\n   Dunamis attacked on this day, injured\nLucia. I was horrified to the havoc and nebulous behavior it caused, and brought myself along with my son to excersize reasoning over the heinous act. It turned up to be simple banditry and arson, the usual tactics displayed by such a meandered group. I\nassisted her trodden body to the dining hall, and left her to be tended to by the various physicians that took to their duties. I suppose I'l end the scripture here, monsiuer, to the confines of my empty solidity in which I spend my nights resting. Let\nthis be known as my, Ser Aymer Fournier's, lament.\n-----------------------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Monk Bread", "Spike Vondar", "-={ Monk Bread }=-\n\nMonk bread has been a customary food item made by the Monks since the very beginning of their existence. As many of the Descendents know, this bread is unlike any other. It never rots, and it always feels fresh, having a crisp,\ngolden texture. Its taste of hints of butter and salt, though never making you thirsty. The feeling of warmth and brief revitalization flows throughout the consumer.\nAlthough the bread has been around for some time its origins have been unknown. People could \"magically\" receive the bread, though have no clue as to how it got to them, only the faint thought that it was from the Monks and safe to eat...\n- Baking the Bread -\n\nMonk Bread is crafted by the monks themselves, like any other regular bread. It is during the kneading process in which Monk Bread is created.\n\nAs a monk kneads the dough, hints of magic\nare leaked and blessed into the dough. Though because Soul Magic, the magic used by Monks, only heals people with a soul, the magic lingers.\n\nThe lingering magic stays in the bread, giving it its unique look and taste, as if it was\njust baked. Once eaten, the Monk Magic disperses throughout the consumers body, usually only giving them a feeling of fulfillment, as the magic is not strong enough to do much more.\n- Getting the Bread -\n\nAlthough Monk Bread can be given to anyone by a Monk, it also somehow reaches other people across the realm. Mysteriously appearing when one is hungry, as if by command. \n\nEven as an Elder Monk, I cannot describe\nhow it reaches people, nonetheless, it is a blessing of the Triumvirate.", ""),
        StaticBook("MonkResurrection", "Daniel Nodal", ">|<Monk>|<\n-=~Resurrection~=-\nIt is the salvation of many lives, but I wonder why I have seen nothing written on it. The monks, as is very well known, are able to save those that have passed away. While managing my stall at the sanctuary grounds I have been able to see for myself some\nof these happenings, or so I believe. \n\nThis magic, unlike many others, is one I know very little about. Like all holy magics it seems to be manifested as a bright light, mostly used to heal those wounded. Besides the bright light, the monk performing it\nis praying to the Triumvirate. It appears to be like clerical healing, but it has other properties. Sometimes a monk arrives at the sanctuary a bit hurt after travels. It appears bandits and the like do not care that they are mugging what could be their\nsavior. What I have to say about those monks, is that unlike normal folk, their wounds heal faster. This is of course due to their magic, small flecks of light I have seen surrounding and healing the wounds. Then the monks are able to bring back the once\ndeceased fully mortal once more.\n\nThis is not to say they are necromancers. Those simply raise the dead, and they remain in a limbo state living and being deceased. The monks are able to bring the body and soul exactly like it was before the death, in\nnear perfect condition. From those I have talked to over the years in the Sanctuary, there is an always present effect of being saved. Present in all of those that I have seen, none have memories of their death or even of the events leading up to it.\nOther common effects are scars, sometimes showing how the poor soul met its end before, or of the tortures it passed. The ones that worry me the most is that sometimes the ones saved change… I have talked to some before and after saving, and changes can\nbe quite extreme. Some go crazy, others start to live in constant fear, some remain with pains in parts of their bodies. The changes they can go through are incredibly varied. I could conjure up reasons as to why that happens, all of them without means of\nproving so. I just believe death to be a terrible experience, that part of it continues on even after salvation.\n\nAnother interesting fact I have gathered, somehow by luck, is that the saved do not want to return to the location that they had\nperished. This particular thought came to me when one of the saved was hugged dearly by what I assumed was his lover. Before that, his body had been carried by another, a friend perhaps, and he and I had a chat about what happened. I knew of the exact\nlocation of his demise, and as him and the woman were moving away, he asked if they were passing through that exact area when returning home. With the confirmation of the woman, he started giving out other ways to reach their house. A big argument even\nhappened when the woman just wanted to go home as fast as she could with him, and he plainly refused to go through that area, which was the only road to their house. He didn’t know himself why he didn’t want to. Alas he returned to normal about half a day\nlater. Since then I started noticing other strange behaviors such as people staying in the sanctuary for longer times, not using their normal routes out of the sanctuary and returning shortly after leaving with a friend. I simply believe once more, that\nthe experience was so horrible, that those saved gain a subconscious fear of their death place. Besides, what would happen if they saw their own body? \n\nOn the mention of bodies, I do have to state as well, it is not necessary for the\nbody to be brought back to the monks for the resurrection. I have seen many monks bring bodies to the sanctuary, so I believe it might be quite easier with them. This is favorable, as in the lands of Anthos there are many evils. You can be decapitated,\neaten, thrown into lava, cut into little bits and drowned in the deepest of oceans. Your body may disappear and never been found once more, and you may this way still be saved. How they restore the body I do not know, and the monks seem not to answer when\nI ask them. They do answer a few questions. I learned, for instance, that the monks are neutral, and never take side in political views or wars. They also take this neutrality to those they save. I have seen those of evil whose purpose is to kill being\nsaved together with the children that never made any harm. This has brought problems to the monks before, many want others to remain dead.\nMost of the stories of the saved start quite simply with them explaining how they woke up in the monk’s care.\nSeems to always be the same as I stated. Some come back quite soon after their demise, already back before their friends and family run to the sanctuary to check, and others can take elven days. Yet this magic is not all powerful. As the monks mention,\nthey cannot save all. If the deceased does not walk out of the monks rooms an elven week after their death, they are forever lost. The same happens to those that take their own life. I believe that if they think that they don’t want to live anymore, then\nthey wouldn’t return to the land of the living.\n\nThe monks are a blessing to mortals, they are those that save so many from their shortened lives.\nWritten by Rosso, 15th of Malin's Welcome 1452 at the Cloud Temple of Asulon\nCoppied by Daniel Nodal", ""),
        StaticBook("Monks of Charity", "Guru Pinya", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n    \n The Book of Peace\n\n    By: Guru Pinya\nThrough experimentation of the arcane, I have become enlightened. Through days of meditation at a time, I have become able to let go of my earthly tether, and enter the void. I have become one with the wind. If you do not understand of what I speak of,\nI shall explain in the simpler of speech. Through meditation my soul has left it's body and enter the void through which the spirits have given me ancient knowledge. In the book I shall write down what I have been taught so that it may be passed on to the\nworld for all the nations to hear.\n   \n         -Guru Pinya\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n Concerning the Soul\n\nEverytime we die, our souls leave our body and wander aimlessly around. The Monks of the Cloud Temple then collect our souls and our bodys and take them to be healed back together. However,\nI must say that when one has become a light into the dark world, and their duty has been fulfilled, their spirit will be given a new body and they will be reincarnated. This is called the Natural Order.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n   Concerning the \n   Spiritual Powers\n\nEverything has a life-force inside of it. Some call it energy, some call it life, but I call it Magic. This magic is not from the void, or from a deity, but from onesel! Through\ndiscipline, and patience, one is able to harness their energy an extent, and use it for the wellbeings of others. Some examples of harnessing bodily Magic is using it do increase strength, speed, become unfamished, survive during a thirst,\nset things alight, preserve dying bodies, levitating small things, healing minor wounds, increasing senses, and entering the spirit world.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n \n   Concerning the\n     Spirit World\n\nThe spirit world is like nothing the mortal eye has seen before. In it lies the Divine Hosts, the angels, the demons, the spirits, the gods, dead spiritual people, and some of the greatest people\nof all time. You might ask how these great people have gotten there. The answer is the Natural Order. When someone has made a great change in the world, their souls do not reincarnate themselves, but they enter into the spiritual world in the peace they\nhad so desired. To enter into peace is to live and die in peace.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n    The Great Path\n\nTo enter into the realm of peace, one must live and die in peace. There are eight rules to peace, and they are:\n\nRight view, viewing reality as it is, and not how it is to be.\nRight intention, intention of renunciation, freedom and harmlessness.\n\nRight speech, speaking in a truthful, and non-hurtful way.\n\nRight action, acting in a non-harmful way.\nRight livelihood, living a non-harmful livelihood.\n\nRight effort, making an effort to improve.\n\nRight mindfulness, awareness to see things for what they are with a clear consciousness.\nRight concentration, correct meditation or concentration.\nWith the eight ways to peace said, I will now explain the four ideals. One must always hope that:\n\nAll sentient beings have happiness and it's causes.\n\nAll sentient beings be free of suffering and it's causes.\nAll sentient beings never be separated from bliss without suffering.\n\nAll sentient beings be in equanimity, free of bias, attachment and anger.\nIn the spirit world, for which I have named Tashe, meaning both the spiritual realm and the state of enlightenment, Tashe may be acquired by following the teachings of myself. If you wish to leave the cycle of reincarnation and suffering, please search\nfor me, Guru Pinya.\n((AntoniusLXIV))", ""),
        StaticBook("Monopoly Charter", "John Sigismund", "On the writ of John II, Holy Orenian Emperor, forever August, etcetera...\n\nWe hereby grant, NOAH WHEEZER, a great big fat person, monopoly charters in the City of Felsen on LEATHER and LEATHERWORKS. He shall be the sole propertier of the aforementioned go\nods for a period of four years in turn for a fee of ONE-HUNDRED AND FIFTY MINAS every year. This charter will expire in four years on the 21st Sun's Smile of 1521. \n", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Manual 1", "Diane Farsight", "=+-+=\n    The Monster\n       Manual\n       =+-+=\n        \n\n        Volume 1\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Diane Farsight\nForeword\nThe world is a dark place, and it's filled with dark things. This book, and others like it, will hopefully inform you of what is out there, and how to deal with them. After all, Ignorance is a most insidious killer.\nThe Blob\n================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: Blobs are generally docile animals shaped like big piles of goo. Their size can vary greatly, but they tend not to surpass 6 feet in height. Their color varies, but will usually be\nbe the color of the enviornment they live in. Furthermore, they are covered in an outer layer of dry skin that protects them from extreme heat. Because of this, they are often found in hot climates. If enveloped by a blob, suffocation is the only way it\nkill you, as their bodies have no acidic properties.\nWeaknesses: Blobs are quite susceptable to cold, making Thanium a perfect weapon against them.\nCreation: Blobs can create more blobs by splitting themselves apart, creating two, smaller blobs.\nThe Ooze\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Oozes are the volitile cousin of blobs. They have the same shape and color, but can be much larger and territorial than their counterpart. Their size can become a staggering 5\nmeters in height, and their body produces a potent acid capable of dissolving flesh and metal alike. Also unlike blobs, Oozes prefer the cold, and lack the outer skin that blobs possess. If you ever need to tell an Ooze apart from a blob quickly, use your\nnose. Oozes will smell much more acrid.\nWeaknesses: Oozes are slow and notably flammable. The best way to deal with one is to set them alight, then run while they burn.\nCreation: Oozes can split themselves into more oozes, just like blobs.\nThe Giant Ooze\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: On occasion, there will be a sighting of a Gargantuan Ooze. Often they come from forgotten cave systems opened by earthquakes, or humanoids digging too deep. They are like\nOozes, but much larger- usually over 10 meters in size and capable of dissolving massive castle gates in a matter of minutes. Weaknesses: Fire will still kill gargantuan Oozes, but it is imperitave that you do not attempt to hide from them- there is\nalmost no stopping one if it begins chasing you.\nCreation: Unknown. Normal Oozes should split into smaller Oozes before reaching this size. It is hypothesized that extended time in cramped conditions underground allows an ooze to grow to this size.\nThe Flesh Worm\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: The tunnel worm is a subterranian monster of epic proportions. It's full length is unknown, but it is easily several meters in diameter. Most of it's life is spent boring\nholes in the earth for it to travel in, often straight through stone. A cave created by a Tunnel worm recently will always be perfectly circular, and ribbed to allow the tunnel worm to maneuver within it easily. It is hypothesized that the Underdark\nbeneath the dwarven lands of Anthos was sculpted by the errant burrowing of tunnel worms.\nWeaknesses: Any place that isn't perfectly fitted for it's body, such as large caverns or the surface.\nCreation: Unknown.\nThe Drake\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: A Drake is, in essence, a corrupted dragon, like those spoken of in legend. Unlike their bretheren, Drakes are much smaller in size and easier to defeat. Despite this, they\nare still capable of flying and breathing fire, and as a result require a large body of able men to be killed safely. When killed, a drake's body will dissolve entirely, but if one can manage to retrieve some of its scales without killing the beast, they\ncan be used to great effect in alchemy.\nWeaknesses: None.\nCreation: Legend has it that drakes are born when a dragon is overcome with taint. This, however, has never been witnessed.\nThe Alchemical\n       Chimera\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: An alchemical chimera is a fusion of two animals. It is truely an unnatural beast, created by a devious use of alchemy. Chimera come in all shapes and sizes,\nbut all will resemble the combination of two  natural beasts. They are mindless beasts, virtually untamable, and gluttonous for flesh.\nWeaknesses: : Time. A well created Chimera will last, at max, for 2 to 3 years.\nCreation: Alchemy.\nThe Dark Chimera ===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Through the use of drakkarian magic, the normal conditions for a chimera can be subverted, allowing for fully adult humans to be partially fused with parts hewn from\nanimals. The result is a fully intelligent, remarkably stable chimera. Many dark chimera are no more than victims of dark mages, but this is not always the case. Great care should be taken when dealing with one.\nWeaknesses: None\nCreation: Alchemy\nMixed with Drakkar Magic.\nThe Vodnik\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Vodnik are tiny, fish-like creatures that inhabit rivers and lakes. When vodnik encounter a corpse of any sort, they will begin filling and infesting it. The corpse will begin\nmoving of it's own accord, and begin dragging anything so foolish as to disturb it's water under with it, to become infested as well. Eventually, this process will crescendo until a small army of shambling corpses inhabit an area. This makes clearing\ndifficult.\nWeaknesses: Attacking the arms and legs of a vodnik-infested corpse is your best bet. Cutting off the head should have no effect.\nCreation: The Vodnik reproduce by laying eggs in the corpses they inhabit.\nThe Giant Crab\n===================Danger: High\nDescription: An enormous crab, about 15 meters across, 5 meters high, and chitin thicker than plate armor. If they see you, they will try to kill you. . They attack anything that moves,\nmembers of their own species included.\nWeaknesses: Their eyes are vulnerable, but should you lack for arrows you should try attacking their underbelly, or failing that, playing dead.\nCreation: Unknown. They certainly do not reproduce.\nThe Ghost\n===================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: A corporeal entity that is not yet ready to leave this world. Specters have several stages of 'unlife'. Stage one specters are always gray, and flit in and out of existance constantly.\nWhat seperates this stage from the others is the fact that, without fail, the spirit will not be able to come to terms with the fact that they are already dead. They usually need a large amount of persuasion and occaisonally hard evidence to make them\nrealize this. Stage two specters already realize that they are dead, and are able to begin learning to control their abilities more effectively. One of two things happen to stage three specters. They will either turn blue and become good, or turn red and\nbecome pure evil. This is usually in response to how well they were treated in their unlife, or how evil they were when they still lived. Powerful specters are capable of invisibility, minor manipulation of physical objects, and ejecting ectoplasm.\nWeaknesses: Spectres can be banished with a single swing of a weapon, especially holy and gold instruments. They can and will come back to life later, however. They are also unable to cross even the thinnest of gold lines.\nCreation: Spectres are\ncreated when someone dies, but cannot come to terms with their own passing. They become stuck betwixt.\nThe Graven\n===================\nDanger: High\nDescription: Graven are evil spirits who died carrying a great obsession in their hearts. As it drove them in life, so to  does it drive them in death.These spirits will wander the lands,\nendlessly pursuing their unattainable goal, and the pursuit of that goal itself becomes the very fuel that keeps them alive. Above all else, do not look a Graven in the eye. Their eyes are portals into their maddened soul, and will instill a lasting\nmadness into the hearts of those who see it.\nWeaknesses: A graven can be banished easily with any weapon, but is particularly susceptable to gold, and holy objects. Likewise, they are unable to cross any line made of gold. In special\ncircumstances, is also possible to banish them forever by completing the task that drives their madness.\nCreation: Gravens are created when a truely obsessed person meets an untimely demise.\nThe Apparition\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: An apparition is an amalgation of many, many lost spirits combined for one purpose, and that purpose is pure evil. Apparitions are malicious, and very dangerous to fight.\nThey are capable of incredible acts of telekinesis and illusion, beyond what any living mage could ever accomplish. Normally, apparitions are bound to a central pillar, marked by many skulls and skeletons littering the area around it. If you come across\none such pillar, is vitally important that you DO NOT DAMAGE THE PILLAR IN ANY WAY, SHAPE, OR FORM. Destroying the pillar will weaken the beast temporarily, but afterwards it will be able to roam the world at large, bringing great chaos in it's wake.\nWeaknesses: An apparition is significantly more powerful than a spirit. The use of gold weaponry can keep it at bay, but the banishment itself lasts only mere moments. Only a very thick ring of gold can contain it. The only way to kill them\npermanently is through the aid of a team of Clerics or Shamen\nCreation: The exact origin of Apparitions is murky. From what can be gathered, they are formed from the death of many individuals in one place, at the same time.\nThe Boogeyman\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Yes, the boogeyman is real. Well, was real. The only known boogieman is currently dead. Boogeyman are sentient collections of bugs that swarm around a central corpse. Based on\non the only known boogeyman's example, boogiemen are intelligent, and extremely murderous, taking pleasure in killing innocents. When endangered, the bugs inside the boogieman will scatter in all directions. Because of this, when hunting the Boogiemen it\nis imperative that you take him by suprise.\nWeaknesses: Boogeymen are weak to fire, and crushing implements. Gold hurts it, but a sword will not have much effect on the swarm.\nCreation: Unknown.\nThe Oolog\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: The Olog  is roughly twice the size of an orc, and  nearly three times as stupid. A product of large amounts of orcish inbreeding, Ologs were raised for having muscle and size,\nand their bodies show it. Still descendant of Orcs, they also are capable of bloodraging, making them twice as dangerous.\nWeaknesses: Ologs are stupid. I mean, really stupid. Use that to your advantage.\nCreation: These creatures are\n(loosely) considered Natural' beasts, and reproduce normally.\nConclusion\n\nThis book has merely scratched the surface of what lurks in the night. Expect more books in the furture.\nStay Alive, Atheria.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mountain Dwarves", "Fimlin Grandaxe", "The grand Mountain Dwarves, originally hailing from the mountains to far north of Aegis, are known to be stalwart defenders of their cities. They came to be when a number of Urguan's sons chose to leave Kal'Urguan and instead live apart from\ntheir Cave Dwarven kin. Although unlike their underground living brethren, they stand strong on land and defend their cities and villages with strong arms and axes. Although better using an axe in combat and lumberjacking than their Dwarven brothers,\nMountain Dwarves are not quite as good miners. Mountain Dwarves generally have ginger, blonde, light brown or fiery red hair. Their skin is lighter than other Dwarves, sometimes tanned. Eye colours tend to be ordinary shades of blue, brown or green.\nThey have strong, tall builds with muscled shoulders from living in harsh environments. Many also cover themselves in ritual war paints. Their toughness and discipline means many make good warriors.\nGenerally, Mountain Dwarves are adventurous and welcome outsiders of other races. They are usually cheerful with a good sense of humour. They take history and traditions seriously,\nusually expressed through song, tales and poetry. Often they are more willing to accept change than other Dwarves.\nLike most Dwarves they follow a strict code of honour, which has developed over  years of living amongst surface dwellers\nand through wars with Orcs. Rites of passage include killing and skinning Orcs, taking their tusks or claiming the ears of Elves. Many Mountain Dwarves claim trophies after battle, either material goods taken or parts of dead enemies themselves.\nThey make excellent hunters, although Mountain Dwarves cannot see well in the dark. They are also good storytellers and among the best Dwarven writers, as they grow up surrounded by myths and legends. They are also highly sought after as lumberjacks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mountain Kings", "Durza Volkihar", "The Dwarves are a small but strong race capable of carving great cities into mountains. Most dwarves are miners or blacksmith. Their skills at forging are legendary usually creating amazing jewelery or weapons.\nDwarves have a great love of war, food and ale. They are quick to anger but have a great love for their friends and kin. They value honor over everything, It is said a dwarf will always keep his word and will never betray a oath.\nMost Dwarves live underground, prefering to mine eternaly for treasures beneath the earth, always wanting to expand their wealth. Dwarfs live much longer than humans but tend to die in battle before they can die of old age.\nDwarves are small but very muscular. Most of them prefer to grow their beards extremely long. Apart from having incredible beards, they are extremely hairy. Female dwarves are extremely rare but it is hypothesised that the are to hairy to be\nnoticed.\nThe Dwarves speak the simple tounge of men but have added their own touch to the way they speak, usually prefering to shorten words rather than speaking the full length of normal words. The dwarves have a ancient language but the elders use it more.\nIf you share these views, come seek my symbol to find me.\n\n\n\n[!] A red eagle is drawn here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Muildir's Essay", "Muildir", "Muildir's essay on why it was bad to do what I did. \n\nWhat I did was extremely bad, for a multitude of reasons. Reasons that at the time, I failed to see. I think I failed to see those things, because I was running on pure emotions alone.\nThe main emotion I felt during all of that was anger. For the longest time, I'd hoped someone would take care of the issue with Mukar. And I suppose over time, I let myself believe that despite what everyone said, the situation would not be handled.\nI am by no means excusing what I did. It was absolutely foolish, and could've easily caused more trouble than me having to write an essay and such. I endangered the Druidic Order as a whole, my own Brothers and Sisters.\nAnd I can say with absolute honesty, that I feel terrible for it. Not only was it bad because of that, but because as a Druid, it goes directly against my beliefs, and against the path I chose to go down.\nI really do feel as if I'm as dissappointed in my self, as everyone else is. Tay, Garun, Beth. I owe the Order as a whole an apology, really. For almost getting us all into an absolute shitstorm. I thank the the Aspects, along with the Dwarf who turned us\nin, for preventing what would've been a terrible turn of events. Caused by Anthron and myself. I should've trusted Garun and Beth's words as soon as they spoke them to me, and everyone else. I should have patient, like I was taught\nby Tay during Dedicancy. It's one of the most important things a Druid can have, patience. And in those moments when I decided to follow Anthron's plan, I didn't have patience. I didn't think anything through, really. I keep saying this, because I want\nto make clear that I do infact understand that it was very wrong, what I took part in. I understand what I did wrong, and how I got to the point of doing it. I can say with absolute certainty that I will never do such a thing again.\nIt makes me sick just thinking about it. \n\nAs for another reason why it was wrong. Despite all the things Mukar has done to the Druids, and the people around the Grove. I don't think anyone should be\nkilled for something like that. Most of the things he was doing were based upon his beliefs, just as most of the things we Druids do is based upon our beliefs and faith in the Aspects. Even though I may not agree with Mukar's beliefs\nand how he punishes people for not following them, that does not mean I should persacute him because of them. It would make me no better than the Valah in Oren, or the Mali'aheral in Haelun'or who threaten to kill me on sight because\nof my blood. \n\nWhen becoming a Dedicant, I will admit I didn't fully understand what path I was putting myself down. I had always thought of the Druids as a very noble Order. And loved the fact\nthat they protected nature, something I was taught by my parents to hold very dearly. In the end, I suppose it was my parents teaching that completely influenced me to start my way on the path. I remember making my way through the forests\noutside Laureh'lin, coming to the root gate at the Grove. I was absolutely amazed, just of the view from the outside. Apart of me couldn't even believe what I seeing. I'll never forget that inititial feeling.\nThen when Taynuel approached the gates he greeted me and all, and opened the gates with what I originally thought must be magic. It was almost impossible to believe that someone could be so in-tune with nature. During the interview\nWhen I answered the various questions, and went through the various scenarios... It was probably the most nervous I've ever been in my life, truthfully. He then just told me to repeat after him, and he started giving me the Dedicants\nvow. I suppose apart of me was absolutely stunned that I was being accepted. I was, and still am so young for an Elf. And already down a path that I feel is extremely important. It's amazing really, how much you can accomplish while still being young.\nWhen taking that vow though, the vow that I hold so dear, the vow that I've heard numerous times, whether repeating it to myself to remind me of my path. Or it being given to new Dedicants, still learning our ways.\nWhen taking that vow, I willingly set myself down a path, a very noble path at that. And by doing what I did, even though in the end it caused no harm, thankfully. But by doing that which I did, I let down everyone close to me.\nTaynuel, Garun, Barry, Arinsilia, Beth. There's countless names that I could list, of those who I have ended up wronging because of this. I went against everything that was taught to me, everything that I promised myself,\nAnd those around me that I wouldn't do. Not only that, but I put our very home, our sanctuary in a huge amount of danger. Chlidren, my fellow Druids, perhaps any guests that were there at any given time. They were all put in danger\nbecause of the actions of my self, and Anthron. And I cannot apologise enough for this. It wasn't even a few Elven days before Anthron approached me, that I had asked Tay and Beth about becoming a Guide.\nIt disgusts me that after asking them something like that, and Beth vouching for me, that I went and did that. I abused the trust she and Tay had in me, and I let them down. I will spend as long as must\nTrying to prove to them that I am indeed better than my actions showed, during that event. I am more mature than that, and I am more patient and have more control over my emotions, than what I showed. I hope I can convince the Order as a whole\nThat never again will I commit such and act. And never again will I put the Order in danger as I did before. I only hope that I can prove myself to them, once again.\nI will spend the next few pages explaining why I will not do what I did again, and why. \n\nI would never do what I did again, for a few reasons. First of all, after thinking on the matter quite a lot, I realise how wrong it was\nto even /think/ about doing such a thing. I realise how much of a terrible thing an assassination is. It goes against all my morals, all my values and all that I believe in. It goes completely against what /any/ good Druid would\never do. The time I spent with Beth after she found out, it was hard. It was even more scary. It was probably the scariest even of my life so far, all that I could think of was unattunment. I was absolutely convinced I would be\nunattuned. And maybe even shunned. In those moments I truly understood how much of a terrible thing I had done, and I felt absolutely horrible for it. I cannot put in words how horrible I felt for doing such a thing, and for putting so much\nat risk. I never want to feel that feeling again. I would never put that which I hold so dear at risk again, and I'll never so obviously break my vows, and go off the path as I did when all of this was going on. Those are the reasons I will never\ndo such a thing again, even if given the oppurtunity. I realise what I should have done. I should have told Anthron from the start that it was absolutely wrong, and tried to get him to stop. Along with going to Beth to talk with him about it.\nI cannot take back that which I have done, but I can only hope for forgiveness, and hope that I can prove myself to my Brothers and Sisters again. \n\n~Muildir", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "Tristanm1", "Mundane Healing\nby Nienna Calm\n\nCopied by\nLeyun Taliamonn\n\n(( On 5/31/2013 ))\n--Mundane Healing: The treatment of minor wounds with common herbs.__\n\nNienna's Foreward: When I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients for the\nTreatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien. One or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery or internal organs with\nnothing but rose thorns and petals. In the interest of not wasting precious paper, I've recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one or two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n-Minor Cut (Nienna)\nSimply apply a dose of deceased Sentient-Slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it. The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n-Headache (Aleya)\nBoil milk. Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n-Stomach Ache (Nienna)\nBoil water. Once it hits a full broil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber color. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n-Soreness (Aleya)\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax the muscles, and rest a lot.\n-Burns (Nienna)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere. The important thing about\nburns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check and clean the burn wound daily until the\nskin can finally reform.\n-Fever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim's body cool using cold water. Give them hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off the disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("Music To Me", "Naz Atatis", "Music To Me\n\nMusic to me can be loud, like thunder in my head.\n\nMusic to me can be soft, that draws me to my bed.\n\nMusic to me is life\n\nMusic to me is strong\nMusic to me makes me feel like I can do no wrong.\n\nMusic makes you full of sorrow\n\nor it makes you full of joy.\n\nMusic makes a better tomorrow\nor it makes you awfully coy.\n\nMusic makes you fearless.\n\nMusic makes you tearless.\n\nMusic can make you a star.\n\nMusic to me\nis when you see\n\nwho you really are.", ""),
        StaticBook("Music Vol. 1", "Evelynn Shards", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n \nThe  Sound  Of  Music\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n \nSix songs each book.\nSelf made songs and there will be more soon!\n-------------------Written by Evelynn Shards\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Page 3: The Sun Parade\nPage 4: Into Nature's Beauty\nPage 5: Lights Will Guide Us\nPage 6: All Of Us \nPage 7: Praise Our Emperor\nPage 8: Fire\n-------------------\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-The Sun Parade\n\nIt shall start soon. Our king will praise our sister, the sun...\nAnd when the light shall raise, the sword will light up. Few people to hold back. Only one Elven day shall this happen. I-its the Sun.\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Into Nature's Beauty\n\nIf you would walk into the wild and open forest. No human to see. Wide open space full of trees, animals everywhere to be seen. A small rabbit would run in the grass. An owl to fly over. Just too much..\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- Lights Will Guide Us\n\nWhen night falls over the town. Lights will raise from upon the sky. Thou shall form one long line. Just for us to follow. They shall guide us home, and to a better place. Keep on searching to there...\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-All Of Us\n\nImagine if our God. Would be down here with us. Nobody to know anything. He built cities all over the world. Nobody to notice anything. Though everybody was happy. All of us were...\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Praise The Emperor\n\nOh, misty forest, filled with ghosts and monsters. The plains ruled by our Emperor. May our Emperor be praised. Oh, praise the Emperor (x2) He makes us happy, gives us good advice. Who doesnt honour him?\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-            Fire\n\nI see fire. In the trees going over to the houses. Licking the air like a cat. Burning down towns and forests. The fire needs to be destroyed. It needs to stay small, and keep us warm..", ""),
        StaticBook("Musical Golem", "Yden", "The musical golem\nBy Yden\n\nJames was once a noble golem, he served a king and his heir and his heir until the kingdom fell. He was once again alone in this world, without purpose. James needed to find his talents.\nJames tried sport, he tried running but of course he weighed as much as a ten men combined so he wasn't going very far and he wasn't going very fast either, he accepted his failure and moved on to his next activity, next James tried body building but\nJames was built... out of stone actually but this made logical sense to James at the time. By now James was starting to feel down, he thought he was good at everything but he picked himself back up and lumbered off to the lake, he tried fishing, he tried\nalchemy but burnt the place down in the end while attempting to make a brew of invisibility. Obviously at this point James felt pretty useless so he lumbered off with a sad look on his face. He came across a small child, she was playing the most beautiful\npiece of music on her hand crafted flute, it had her name in a golden lettering 'Emily' this girl could play beautiful, if James could cry i'm certain he would be. This gave James a grand idea, James was obviously never going to be able to play the flute\nbut he was certain he would excel at playing the drums and sure enough he was, in fact he was so good the girl who has inspired him to try this hired him so they could play together, she was the daughter of a very wealthy lord after all so this was no\nproblem. Emily and James became great friends and James was finally happy again with his life now that he was not alone, he had a friend and she was the best friend he could ever ask for.\n\nThe End\nBy Yden\nAlso see; The golem who learnt to love \n\nAlso see; The little golem that could", ""),
        StaticBook("My Dedicancy", "Aurojia", "- Hunted and killed a boar that was destroying bird nestings and trees, skinning and turnings it's remains into a large set of bone chimes. \n\n- Completed the Bardic Rite, producing from it a book by the title of\n'Red'.\n- Tamed and brought with me from the Iron Uzg an Elephant, which now serves as a lifelong companion.\n\n- Entered the Fairy Ring for the first time, not bending beneath the stress or pressure of the intense magical energy within.\n- Read and summarized the book labeled 'Neo-Druidism' by Salmon Druid Petyr.\n\n- Resolved the horrific overpopulation of a grouping of turtles in the forest's nearby pond, disposing of them in the local river and Grove.\n- Accompanied Muildir to the scarred and tainted land of Dark Shamans to see the damage.\n\n- Met three new Druids, Oo'ri, Katelynn, and Alinar, the druids of Magma, Clouds, and Porcupines.\n- Completed a Task from a Druid Guide as well as an Archdruid.\n\n- Read 'The Great War' and gave a valid thesis to Calius.\n\n- Completed the Rite of Naming, taking the Druidic Totem of the Phœnix.\n- Completed Muildir's Dedicant questioning, now moving on to my Grand Task!\n\n- Grand Task Completed!~ Shrine to the Aspects constructed beneath the hill holding the Fairy Ring.\n- I have finally been Attuned. All hail the new Phoenix Druid, Aurojia Akulakh!\n\n\n\n\n            O7\n           /I\n           /\\", ""),
        StaticBook("My Family <3", "KawaiiAlice311", "This book if TOP SECRET for eyes of the WARHAWKES only, if anyone dares lay eyes on my masterpeice you shall be blasted with a kitten cannon. YOU HAVE BEEN WARNED!! \n\n[!] A drawling of a monster would be here, saying keep out\nWhat I think about my family the Warhawkes ! \n\nMawloc: He is the sweetest 'ker ever. Always makes me laugh and smile, and he wears that cute little hat. He is also my husband so yeah, of course I love him.\nAleesia: She is super caring and nice. She also cooks REALLY well. She is amazing at fighting and my bestest friend ever. \n\nRay: He made me feel really welcomed into the Warhawkes. He also have a really cool mohawk.\nRei: He is super scary... but super good at chess!\n\nIsabelle: At first I thought she was scary too, but now she is nice and says I am her friend. She also lets me sit on her shoulders and its great. She is super sweet on the inside.\nAzariah: He is weird and likes to flirt with all the girls. \n\nLeona: She is soooooo pretty and sweet. Her baby is also the cutest thing ever!\n\nChirr: She is my big sister, who also has a child. She is always there for me and I love her very much.\nDakath: He knows how to fight very well and he is a good friend to hang with. He also can teach me to fight really well.\n\nCole: He is a grumpy old wrinkly raisin.\n\n[!] A drawling of a raisin with Cole's face would be here.\nTahiti: I dont really know him but he makes Leona happy so he is okay I guess. \n\nRegale: HE IS A STINKY PECIE OF SHIT AND I FUCKING HATE HIM. \n\nTalar: I mean.. he tried kissing me but he is cool I guess.\n[!] A drawling of all the Warhawkes holding hands is drawn here, along with hearts drawn everywhere.\n\n\n   ~THE END~", ""),
        StaticBook("my poem", "jyecarson", "haiku poem\n[1] An afternoon breeze [2] expels cold air, along with [3] the fallen brown leaves \n\n\n(the numbers represent the line there on)", ""),
        StaticBook("My Struggle", "Kaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "====Heil Valdoria==== \n\n\n\n     The Rise of the\n     Colored Kingdoms\n\n\n    \n        Approved by\n   The Reich Ministry\n          Of Truth\nForeward\n\nThe treatise of which follows this breif forward has been legislated upon the direct mandate of the Kaiser and his white sons. It is all very scientific, you see. Praise the Kaiser and hail the White Flame.\nSince his inception, the race of man has proved his superiority over the lesser kindred time and time again, and thus, it is undoubtedly proven by science that man is Kaiser's chosen race. There is no question in the matter, for man and only man possesses\nthe conviction and blessing to mold a mighty empire, forged from the frisson of today, and supported on all facets by our pure ancestors. The dubious assertion against our one and true God and his honor guards is that of defeatist and Serenist dogmatic\npestilence, inseminated from the vile gasses of hell and popagated by the black worms and Kharadeen sympathizers. Man is true. Man is Kaiser's chosen disciple, and let his superior and engorged-gargantuan loins deluge the slime of elgenism and defeatism\nfrom our seed. All hail Kaiser's seed and immaculate fluids.\n\nAs of thus far, the intent of our father is rather opague, but within the contents of this binding of which follows, all his glory and prowess will be clear. For one to question the prowess\nor glory of our Lordi s blasphemy. Which despite punishment by which of means which shall be shined upon in further detail in at a further period, blasphemy is a sin. Thus, if one were to follow with utmost punctuality, he would find that the treatise\nof which I have been bestowed the pious and ethereal act of concieving is in fact the unwavering voice of Kaiser. It is all very scientific, and though I doubt one may absorb his excellence with ease, for his excellence is that of an infinite well of\ngolden wine, I advise one suckle at my knowledge with great heed. One must not tug nor bite when contracting the teat of Kaiser, one must priase him with a sublt pursuing, for only then will his grace seep at a rate conceivable by his sons.\nThe Sprouting of Man\n\n   The history of man is that of great piety and virtue. In practically all corners of our realm, man's raw exuberance is sown deep within the heart of the Kaiser's Seed, and his mighty, booming prowess can be felt in each and\nevery heart of all who inhabit it. Man has fought with many breeds in his legacy, and man still remains, but not as a refugee or vagabond. Man has survived in a fashion comparable to a seed of iron-wood oak, for his blessing lay deep within the soil,\ndormant but with pride, and when time comes and the Kaiser commands the man to grow, to build, to conquer, then and only then is mans' pride as palpable as the Kaiser's own. \n   Our race emerges from the remains of lesser breeds, fueled by the purity of\nhis white pride and the blessings of our Lord and Savior. All the way he spourts, man takes most attentiveness to his every direction, constantly and diligently enforcing his prowess, his muscles of pure force bulge and pulsate under the immense pressure\nof his pride. It appears that no force could ever discourse his destined and premeditated path, for man will ascend until his most superior of faculties scrapes the heavens and is once again reunited with his benevolent father. \n   His roots at which\npoint cleave deep into the blackened earth, for the front of darkness ever will seep into our fluids. Thus we must fight, we must never, as a hope, as a dream, we must never be diluted by the inferior vestigial corpses of the damned races. And as man's\ngreat limbs spread with unmeasurable force and national pride, the worms of the black sludge will begine to fester. They cross into our realm illegally, without the blessing of the Kaiser, and they burrow deep within our cavities. The very seeds of our\npride have been sabotaged! They feast upon our flesh and excrete tar from their pores. They fester and slosh in such ooze and amass great pits of darkness. They brred with no grace or consent, they feed with glutionous intent, and they spread the foul\nlies of their filthy heathen, sub-humanist Ebolinism.\n   As the sludge of the black worms collects deep within our bowels and extremities, the flame of our brethren begins to fade. The skin of a once pure race will blacken under the tremendous, bloated\nweight of the pestilent bog, and our great minds which once yielded the venerated sciences and arts will rot and drain through our facial cavities. Soon, if we continue on our path so grossly discourse from the Kaiser's will our own beautiful race will no\nlonger be even remotely recognizeable. We will be diluted to a state so impoverished and emaciated of all pride that we will have not even the conviction to cognate the most primal of tasks. We will at this point be that of which we have fought, we will\nbe all which we have feared. We will be the elfen. \n   But alas, this is not the course of man. Man will never be so easily dissolved by such spurious doctrine, for man is the direct fluid of the Holy One, the Creator, The one true hope for the salvation\nfor nationalism and pride. So my dear white brothers, we must show the Kaiser that we are worthy. We must prove to him that we as a hope, as a dream for all that is pure in this realm, the man has not and never will forget his divine quest! Let us\nimpale the rotten flesh with scolding-bladed tapes and drain the fetis wastes from our cavities! Let us carve out the filthy conspirators and blackened worm colonies, from each and every facet of our impenetrable bark of hardened iron!\nLet us Fight, my brothers! Let us fight for the salvation of the Kaiser and his seeds!\nThe Salvation of the Kaiser\n\nPraise He, the one and only, the true voice of good in a realm so corroded by the acrid sins of the lesser races. Praise he whose might and sheer dauntlessness shall cleanse the arachnids of pit and moss, he who\nshall save our white souls from the vile feces of Ebolnism and the Serenist web. Praise he who shall and forever will be the one and the only true God, praise our Lord and our grandest of Kings. All Praise the Kaiser!\n   Praise our blessed hearth, for in\nhis glorious egg lay a seed, a hope, a dream for a world of white fire. All hail the flame of God and King, praise the fervent inferno of cleansing, and let it smolder in the hearts of each and every white man, for now and ever. For us, let the flame\nguide us, let it illuminate the blackened path into oblivion, the shady death march speckled with infected warts of flesh and pus and other such fecal jellies, that of which spawn the prickly seeds of the Degenerate race and the Serenist arachnids.\nBut alas, have not fear my fellow white brothers. Praiser the Kaiser, for through his wisdom may we purge the septic grubs with flame and gas. Let our nationalism and tenacious pride obliterate their weak and feeble and highly demonic colonies. Let our\nwhite flame raze each and every festering cesspit from which they spawn, and let us forcefully enter their diseased posterior cavities in the name of the glorious Kaiser.\n======================================\n\n\n  The Struggle of Our\n    Nation and Great\n         Charter Of\n        Vanderkind\n\n\n\n\n=====================================\nFor the glory of a great nation is to kinder the white flame of our ancestors, the divine right of our Kings, and the holy grace of our one true God. \n\nIn the wake of war and the feckless sheeding of national pride through the unrelenting plot of\nSerenist Ebliontologists in coalition with Communist doctrine, only the few, so the Kaiser wills it, only the most true and pure will survive the coming fire of the primal apocalypses. So when we, as a people, as a hope, must ask why it is that the\nof the black worms in our governments and in the highest and most divine of positions in the high counsel have become so, we must ask ourselves instead why it is that the inferior races have rejected the pious might of the one true Lord and Savior.\nThis is why we must act, for the sake of all that is holy and for the propsperity of culture and civilization, and only through the social rec-construction of our deprived filth of elfen lies and slime can we regain the trust of the Kaiser and pray for\nhis forgiveness.\n\n===The Grace Of===\n====The Kaiser====\n\nAll haill thee who flows water into our rivers, plants seeds, into our soil, delivers bread to our bellies and children to our kindred. Blessed thee, our one true Lord, who in the grace of love\nand pious does he who impregnates the seed of life to our loins and the fires of national pride into our hearts. The Kaiser, in all his glory, is the one and true God, for he and only he is divine and pure. \n\nHowever the Kaiser is displeased with\nour existence. For ages, the Serenists, the enemy of all that is good and beautiful, has festered at the hearts of our brothers. They have plagued the grace and purity of the ethereal and pure Vanders, the one true race, and they have spilled their seeds\namongst the black and sodomite flesh of the negarious degenerate race. Our Savior is furious. He holds our fate in that of which is a thread over the boiling pits of Iblees' grasp. Only his will remains as our salvation, and we have allowed it to be\nspilled out of the crucible of the one, the pure race of men. We have enabled the impure to breed for far too long.\n====The Love====\n===Of the Rector===\n\nIt is the will of the divine right of the RTector and his unfathomable purity to protect the soverignty and pride of our nation, and so it be, the glory of our nation is now buckling under the weight of the\nglutenous elfen conspiracy. Only through the love of Priorism, the one true ideology, can the love and passion of the Kaiser be felt deep within our cavities. heil the Grandmaster, for through his divine right shall we drink the blood of all who oppose\nthe might and prowess of Saradomin and his belssings upon the grace of our nation and the love of our fathers. \n\n===The Blessings===\n==Of Our Fathers==\n\nLoveth thee who drained the swamps, chiseled the stone, impregnated the woman and filled the Kaiser's realm with the seed of the pure men and his Birthright to Gielinor. Only through the love of our fathers\nmay our seeds be spread into the wombs of the Kaiser's purity, and therefore, the mothers of our race shall be pure. May we suckle from his teat, and love his divine will until the time of departure to the realm of the Kaiser. All hail the Kaiser and the\nfathers of our seed.\n\nIf not for the will of the Kaiser, in all of his blessed glory, shall we dictate his grace amonst the scum races of our plagued realm. Let us Educate the feeble and lost in the glory of national pride and save them from the repugnant\nsludge of Serenism. Let us feed the bellies of the poor with the love fluids of god's seed. Let us forge from the ashes of the quarreling micronations a golden utopia of the pure and strong, and let us sow the seeds of the New World Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Tale, Felsen", "Amordrin", "And my adventure begins. I immediately left spawn with the helping hand of Hadrian Thassorian. He offered me a position as a bannerman and I reluctantly accepted. From there he showed me around a large area, and then we headed to Felsen. In Felsen there\nwas a commotion happening in the street. Turns out This guy Ivan was to be executed and there was a fight about who would get his axe. It was resolved, but later that day one of the Thassorian brothers got into a fight with a man named Gerad. From there,\nI then left Felsen to continue my travels. I had to take some food from a random chest, but that's because it was the only food in 10 miles! My incompentence in cooking certainly doesn't help. I did leave half of the stack where I found it, so no worries.\nAnd now, I head on with no specific place in mind in order to expand my knowledge of Vailan.\n\nDay4:\nIt's been quiet today. Sometimes it's nice to let things wind down especially when you start off so crazy. Some blacksmith keeps trying to sell me\niron tools and ore. I decided to stop answering him altogether. I devided to spend the day in the city I was found in. Before I really begin my journey I realized I have to get a job. I'm a chef for now, just so I can acquire food for myself. End of day4,\nand the rain doesn't seem to be letting up yet.\n\nDay 5:\nFresh early morning rain. Ah yes, always so much happening in Felsen. I always seem to miss it when I'm not there. Not much talking, but the action rarely ever stops. It's almost refreshing\nreally, considering most other places now are dead or quiet. Gared and Ivan being most of Felsen's main attractions. The guards 'royal' son seems to have thrown someone into the pit, trial by ordeal. fun day at felsen. Lad named Robert was put to trial\nunfairly and injusticed. Prince and newly recruited guard refused to listen. Tis' an odd place Felsen be, but a must-to travel spot. Wouldn't change it for the world. I'm now sitting on what looks to be the 4th highest point in Felsen, thoroughly enjoying\nthe view. Apparently now, civilians aren't even allowed on the damn wall. I've begun to start hating the guards union. It's like you can't do anything anymore. Mullraugh, one of the ehh- more dedicated, guards caught me hangin' on the wall. Got away\nunshiethed but I just hope he doesn't remember.\nDay 6 was a day to remember. and it's not even over yet heh.\n\nDay 7:\nAs hard as I try, can't stay away from Felsen. More duels. Bloody Gared cheated.\nDay 8: Met a girl named Hazel, bloody ten years old. Learned her story, tragic really. I didn't want to leave her alone in Felsen so we decided to leave. Not before the stauntons made my blood boil. We went to a tranquil town called Ashton and met Ethan.\nHe came off as a bit odd, but he couldn't have been older than 16. Other than that, the little Hazel also gives off a tiny bit of a weird vibe. Not to be fully trusted.\n\nDay 10:\nI can say surely that I'm very lost. After much exploring I found\nmy way back to the docks. Might as well head to the main sqaure of Cloud Temple to cool down. Honestly I'm surprised I haven't gotten in an immense amount of trouble yet. Amazing really. That and the fact I haven't wanted to travel to my actual\ndestination yet. Something about Vailan and it's towns and cities is so aluring and catches you in.\n\nI'm going to make an entry about how much these stauntons reallly do piss me off. Met a woman named Saraid, she bloody\nwatched a guy get his foot cut off, cooked, then fed to a man BY THE GUARDS. This is.. unbelievable. Disgusting. The injustice in Felsen almost sounds like fallacy. I have to do something, even if they do call it \"rebelling\". I'd rather be an outcast\nthan some snivveling rat controlled by mindless royalty. Elves are not to be descriminated against. Even if I'm some mere human, I'll get my word in. Along with a couple of punches. This is going to be a long season.\nDay 11:\nHasn't even begun yet and I already feel exhausted. I guess I should thank Robert. In a way, he was the first example for me. Example of how inhumane the guards really are. What they call \"The Pit\", in the tavern in Felsen.\nThat's where my feelings against them grew. Living in Felsen as a young lad I never thought much of the guards. They'd yell at me to get down from the wall, and I'd get in trouble stealing, but no punishments as... well. Harsh.\n\n(Day11 still)\nI learned much about Saraid. She hails from a small village. Recently she witnessed fucked up shit about the guardsmen in Haelsun'or. Real fucked up shit. I plan to change Felsen. Then Haelsun'or. Then Vailan. She called me too ambitious,\nand while I might agree, I think some say that ambitions are they key to drive the world. If no one had em' where would we be? In even worse shit than we are now. When I said it was going to bea long season, I meant it.\nDay 13:\nFor a while now I've seen a spry old man running around. He just.. runs! And jumps! It's funny and odd. Though there isn't much of it here, I enjoy the music in Vailan. It's practically non-existent but when you do catch someone playing an\ninstrument it gives you a feeling of hope. As if even though so many horrid things are happening you can look past that and make people happy and look past the fog they see. So I just got to CT, and y'know who I see here? Hazel. I feel something is going\non with her. But if I were to really think that I'd probably be out of my mind. She's 10, how evil could she possibly be? Shit, she saw me. Sammy, her friend, looks to be sick. I suppose I could take time off my too ambitious ambitions. Ah, tis' be Winter\nnow. Back in Felsen, it seems to be a quiet day today. Not many people around. For me, that could either be agood thing or a bad thing. I'm not sure anymore. \n\nWell somehting eventful happened today. Not in a bad way finally.\nI got a house in Felsen, tax free. For now that is. I met Markese, head commandment for the guards legion in Felsen. Good guy he is I've only ever heard good things. I just have to pay them with food until I can get another job. Thing is...\nI've never cooked anything in my entire life. So I have no idea what I'm gonna do. Might as well head to resource island to see if anything is there for me. Resource island is full of so many things, all ofthem being resources. Nothing for me sadly.\nIt's odd how hard it is to acquire resources in order to cook. I just hope the deadline for my tax isn't soon. I guess I should call this book \"History of Felsen\", considering how all I write about is this place. It's always thriving at night here.\nbecause of all the drunkards and travelling merchants.\n\nDay 16:\nI'm writing this as the day ends, but it was a productful day. I'm going to learn how to become a miner, possibly a woodworker. It's much easier than being a chef.\nHard to believe it's the Winter season now. Vailan days all seem to merge together. Or it all seems to fall apart but never completely. Who wouldn't enjoy a place like that?\n\nDay 19: The plan is to become a better miner then find Markese and let him\nknow I'm not completely useless.\n\nDay 20: I met Garrett the gatekeeper of Felsen early this morning. Good lad.\n\nDay 21:\nGood hard labour today. Bout' time too. Nothing in Felsen, or maybe there was\nI was just busy on resource island.\n\nDay 23:\nAll I've done is work recently, and it feels good. No one has been in Felsen lately, well no one I haven't seen before. Markese really made me think about how I wasn't working before and how I\nfelt. I feel stronger now, more purposefull.\n\nDay 24:\nI'm getting better at mining, I can tell by the way the rocks crumble. I'm writing this as it goes down, but it appears that my neigbours are getting into an argument. It's improper for me\nto listen I know, but it's something to do with the guardsmen and someone trespassing. It sounds like a Dreadlander is about to get punished for somethin'. Not sure if I should step in. Something compels me to go step in but something else tells me that\nit would only rebound bad for me. I'll hang around and listen for now.\n\nEverything about Felsen is repulsive. Disgusting. And still I call it home even as it slowly disowns me. The amount of good there diminishes every god damned day.\nThat Dreadlander, nameless, he got his arm cut off in the name of \"justice\". Justice my ass. He refused to let me help him so I sternly told him to go to CT and acquire help for him injury. I can't even look those guards in the eye anymore. And from what\nI saw today I don't think I'll be at alot of people anymore. I nearly threw up from the state of his arm. As a side note, it seems a lot of people think of me as an elf. Interesting. I mean my hair covers me ears but I didn't think I looked like one. Not\nthat it really bothers me. I mean someone has to stand up for the poor guys. Sometimes I hate us damn Highlanders and Heartlanders. Annoy the shit outta everyone and act like we did nothing wrong.\n\nAlright, let's restate my goals. So the\noriginal plan is to rid Felsen of all it's dirt. Justice driven freaks, bandits, generally unwelcome people. Felsen should go back to being a friendly place. Getting an actualy job here would be nice as well. So I 'spose that's what I'm working on\ncurrently. It's nice to take a break from my \"too ambitious ambitions\".\n\nDay 26:\nThis is beginning to become a very monotonous journal. All I've been doing is working in the mines, rarely coming to Felsen. Day in day out\nI've been riding the boat to resource island and making my way down. Not the most catching subject mining is. I just counted and it seems I've written 40 pages. If anyone recieves this book I hope they don't die of boredom.\n\nI feel guilty eavesdropping on strangers but sometimes I believe it is necesssary. In order to gain information on different cultures and cities I have to listen to people from different cultures and cities. There's a duo of people\noutside the tavern (Felsen) who're from the Black Company. Only ever heard of em', never seen one in public before. Talkin' to some straggler. \n\nGARRETT IS A TRAITOR. He damned threw Markese into a fire. Markese is alright currently, but his condition\ncould get worse. I'll fine that damn bastard spy Garrett and rip his teeth out his skull. When I find that motherfucker he better prayto whatever God he sees fit. If he even comes near Felsen again...\n\nI can't let my emotions drive me.\nIf I get driven by what I consider o be justice I'll be on the same level as the guardsmen.\n\nMarkese de Rolle. More of a liberatarian or revolutionist than a mayor. He has a way with people and a fluidity with words. I may see him in\na tainted view but he's a good lad. Does his job.\n\nMarkese wants to cut off the lads hands. Barbarian, but I understand. The way I see things, we can not stoop to their level. Violance only brings on more violence. Nothing comes of it.\nI'm going to try to stop that from happening.\n\nThe streets of Felsen now run silent. After the gathering for Markese's redemption it just feels.. empty. More sad than it was before. I don't feel sad for not heading out with them,\nI feel sad for not knowing how to stop them. How to stop all of this. And I'm not sure I can devise a plan anyhow. Damn my \"too ambitious ambitions\".\n\nDay 28:\nNo luck lookin' for Garrett. I wanted to talk to Markese about his\nguards, but I came to a sudden realization. He's head of commandment, he has these guards at HIS will. I've seen it first hand, they're willin to do just about anythin' for the man. Loyal, if you could call it that. Mindless could fit as well. Anyways, I\nwanted to say something but I stopped myself. First it'd be better to do it in private. Second, better not to do it during situations of high pressure. Third, as I wrote before. What if Markese is another justice driven freak? Who says he isn't?\nAll hell, he wanted to cut Garrett's hands off. I'm so conlficted on what to think anymore. I know my morals, but I'm seriously questioning everybody elses.\n\nDay 30:\nI saw him, I saw the slimy bastard. Bloody Garrett got away.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Tale, Magic", "Amordrin", "Too many things are happening. First Markese was attacked, then the Prince. Guardsmen are going crazy.\n\nDay 31:\nI saw him. I spoke to him. The arsonist Garrett. He's not Orenian, as I thought. I doubt his name is even Garrett, which he\nbasically confirmed. It seemed to me that he knew he'd be caught, which I found odd. All I can think about is what Markese will do when he finds \"Garrett\". I have to think of somethin' to stop him.\n\nDay 32:\nFelsen is in flames. Literally, someone\nset a building on fire. Before we know it the whole town will be engulfed in the firey madness. Apparently \"Sand Folk\", set the fire according to one of the officials. Something even more terrible will come of this. I know it.\n\nSeems the fire is out.\nDay 33:\nOn the bright side, everyone is too occupied to take taxes. I'm unsure of what to do. I should stay in Felsen, though I'm a bit intimidated by it's occupents at the moment.\n\nI think meeting \"Garrett\", is getting\nroutine. This is the second time that I've spoke to him in CT. But now he wants me to find out where he lives. Bloody mages are mysterious as shit. How am I supposed to search all of Vailor?\nOkay. Let's start with what I know about him.\nHe's not Orenian\nHe's a mage. Practices Arkane Magic (?), mentions something about the Void.\nProverb about the Void:\n\n\"The void is nothing, yet everything. Like our imagination it may be dull and empty; or full and colourful.\"\nThe void is an empty plane of existence\nwehre things may be created by willpower or imagination. Mana is needed to use Arcane Magic. Mana is in everything living, it is invisible as air. I believe Garrett is using Evocation. A sub-type of arcane magic that includes the construction of\nartificial elements. If he did burn Markese however, he would feelthe heat as well. Markese had what looked like 3rd degree burns (something i learned from my father) so.. \"Garrett\" would feel the heat of 3rd degree burns. Ouch. He must've really hated\nMarkese or he wouldn't have put himself through that as well.\n\nDay 40:\nFelsen docks are under attack. A boat was blown up. Bell is investigating some Kha and someone named Dagr is interfering.\nFrom this page on, I will dedicate this book to my research on Arcane magic. In this journal I will focus on Evocation (all three), Voice Translocation, and Mental Magic. If I can understand Mental Magic, that is. Being a mage is extremely looked down\nupon in Vailan as far as I can tell. It's a risk I'm willing to take. I mean it's not like I'm going to learn how to BECOME a mage. Just going to learn about magic. A very enticing thing. Let's begin with the sources of magic.\nVoid** or **Arcane** magic is easier to learn. Though it depends on your mental ability and supply of mana. (I don't have much time to write. I was recuited to Markese's Militia.\nUsing mana to connect tothe void is a very unnatural process. As long as\nyou're distracted, you can't use void (Arcane) magic. The Void magics include Domestic Magic, Evocation, Conjuration, Alteration, Telekinesis, Void Translocation, and Illusion. All with their own sub-categories as well. Deity-based magics allow the user\nto perform a set list of spells. This is more restricted because deities will only acknowledge an individuals desire for magic. Deity Magics include Druidism, Shamanism, Cleric, Frost Witch, Monk, and Muun'Trivazja. Besides those two, there is actually a\nthird kind of magic simply named Other magic. This means the user has their own source of power. Most Dark magics are under this category. Other magics include Rune smithing, Contract Magic, Necromancy, Shade, Soul Puppetry, and Fi'hiiran'tanya. Moving on\n==Evocation==\nEvocation does not control existing elements, it creates a temporary version of them. So after the magic is done, it disappears. The space in which the evocationist wishes to summon their element must be free. If a mage loses sight of their\nevocation they lose connection to the void, and so it disappears. Fire evocation requires a detailed study of an element, the thing must exist in the natural world in order to be evoked. Evoking flames is dangerous, the mage can feel the flames they made.\nWater mages can create everything to do with water. So snow, ice, and even steam. Earth evocationists can create natural rocks and minerals, so something like steel couldn't be evoked. Earth mages can be versatile in what they create. Air evocation is one\nof the most unused evocations, it focuses around creating winds and air. It is rare when a water mage is strong enough to be on offence, or even defence. And finally Electric Evocation allows you to create bolts, sparks, and charges of electricity. This\ntakes long to prepare. It takes longer to evoke, but when it does you probably won't be able to dodge it. Arcanism, like elemental evocation and conjuration, is the act of evoking a substance from the void. The magic is unique for each caster. Arcanism\ncan be broken down to 4 properties. Projectiles, Shielding, Weaponry, & Art. Conjuration is the art of creating living creatures or plants from the void. The beings created are under full control of the mage and disappears when there is no more mana.\n==Alteration==\nI will only be writing about Void Translocation. While other magics manifest from the void, this type takes the objects from our world and sends them to the void. This is incredibly hard to learn. The user must know the size, weight,\nconsistency, viscosity, material, and mana of the object. When something is placed in the void, that object is completely destroyed from our world. If the user forgets one minute detail of the object, it is gone forever.\n==Mental Magic==\nAllows the mage to use the void in order to make a connection to a persons mind. This can only happen one at a time. Most common mental magic is telepathy. There are five \"tiers\" to mental magic. Tier one the student learns of barriers\nand wards to protect their mind. Tier two the student can add mental illusions. Tier three they can begin learning how to get past the mental barriers that may block their progress. At tier four the mental mage has come far at this point. They learn of\nCataleptic illusions. Creating two illusions at once. Tier five, finally the mental mage has reached the peak of their abilities but the learning doesn't stop there. Slowly improving, and removing stimuli is worked on. This magic is very complex. I had\ntrouble even writing it down. I believe it is important to write down that this is not mind control. Merely putting suggestions and influences.\n\nI have to say, learning about magic is extremely interesting and very time consuming. Took me half of Winter\nand the beginning of Summer to get alll that down. How can a year go by so slow yet so fast? Perhaps I'll write more of my findings in here.\n\nIt's Summer now. There's some Felsen fight night going on. I might watch.\nThe second time I talked to Garrett he hinted at being able to use the void in the way only a Void Translocator could. Maybe not even a translocator. To my knowledge, only objects can be placed into the void. Once something is in the void it is destroyed\nfrom this world. So I 'spose a human couldn't enter the void as an object would. There are mages who can create living creatures using the Void. If you can make a creature, is it so far fetched that you could make a human? And if you could make a human\ncome out of the void, perhaps one could go in? My ambitions are too ambitious. Side not; Atlas is a mage. Fun fact, you MAKE golems. Kalila Volsung\n*a small piece of paper is stuck here with the words*\nAvenel, High Elf, Hangs around Felsen and CT.\nI beat Mattington in a duel. Bell saw. He was.. proud. He reminds me of my father... yesterday was eventful. Felsen is stirring, and something bigger than all of us will go down. I know it. Gregory HAS to have something to do with this. There is no way in\nhell that he is innnocent. I suspect he is a mage, but my memory of my time spent with him is a bit fuzzy. He's been present every time something goes wrong in Felsen. Damn man better stay away from Hazel. I tried to tell Mattington but he wouldn't listen\nand now the church is blown up.\n\nI refilled the chest of sparrin' swords today. Hope everyone stops complaining for a while now. I've had an uneasy feeling in my stomach ever since that day with Ezrok. I'm worried about Akel as well something is off\nwith him. While reading this book over, I found a note I don't remember putting in here. It has a name and race, I should try to find this person. Says they hang around Felsen and CT.\n\nI haven't written in a while. Nothing too significant has happened.\nSano still insists that I join the guard. I still insist that it isn't for me. \n\nI'm 'sposed to guard this door for Sano and this elf lady. She was tortured, along with some guard by the man named Smyth. Disgrace, that man is. Humans can go to the\nvoid. Overheard Hadrian talking. So \"Garrett\" really wasn't kidding.\nI learned about auras today.\nBlue- Logical\nPurple- Mysertiousness\nWhite- Innocence\nBrown- Caring\nYellow- Greed\nRed- Controlling\nGreen- Harmonous\nand finally\nBlack- Malevolence. I'd like to learn more about Telekinesis. I'll research it when I'm feeling better.\n==Telekinesis==\nA telekinetic mage changes how gravity acts on an object. This change fades rapidly much like in Evocation. Telekinesis, like all other magics, alters things unnaturally. You can not lift liquids as there are too many particles to focus\non. You must focus on a single object in order to grab it. This makes things harder, but not impossible. The difficulty on lifting objects may depend upon the speed of motion, number of objects, and the size and weight. Objects with a changing surface\narea are impossible to lift.\nRed Lines:\nManipulating living things, liquids, gases, and plants included. Lifting more than your character could. Stopping arrows mid air.\n\nI think this is the magic I want to learn.\nTier 1: Capable of lifting 5 half a kilogram objects at once. Weak focus or non-constant focus breaks the connection.\nTier 2: Able to lift multiple small objects at a medium speed up to 12 kilograms in weight. Medium and medium-large constant forces break\nfocus.\nTier 3: Can lift small objects at high speed. Medium objects can be lifted with relative aptitude. Experiment with objects heavier than 50 kilograms.\nTier 4: Lift up to 80 kilograms in weight. Very large non-constant or constant forces\nbreak focus. A telekinetic of 2 months would be able to lift objects up to 20 kilograms in weight.\nTier 5: Able to lift up to 300 kilograms. From here lifting ability increases by about 5kg per elven week.\n\nAfter researching a bit more extensively\nI've come to the conclusion this is the type of magic I want to learn. Whether it be from a teacher or by book, I will learn this magic. {{OOC}} HOLY MOLY MAGIC IS COMPLICATED TO SELF TEACH. {{IC}}\nAnd thus the revolution begins. Always knew it would be Markese who started it. Even if by accident. But now things have gone to bloody hell, and the Watch might be discarded. I never even could've imagined this happening. Fitting, today started with rain\n17th of Malin's Welcome, 1668. The day the Felsen Watch kicked ass and won over Felsen. Felsen is free, for now.\n\n19th of Malin's Welcome. The day we became rebels, traitors to Oren. We're going to take back Felsen.\n17th of Summer, we've been living in the fort for about a month now. It's not.. bad.\n\nI've been practicing making a connection to the Void for a while now. Nothing new. It's hard, Mental Magic. Inquire to Lhindir about seeking a teacher for learning\nTelekinesis. Don't give up on that. \nIt's the 9th of Summer, 1668, and I've been learning to make a connection with the void for a couple weeks now. Thing is I need a new journal or I can't document anything I learn. But I think I can feel I'm getting\nbetter. Slowly but surely. I've read all the books in the library about telekinesis, I just need a teacher. Or someone who I can look up to. I must find Avenel. He's my only hope.", ""),
        StaticBook("MyDaddyLovesMe", "Ashur", "I love my daddy, I love my daddy\n\nI love my daddy, and I know he loves me\n\nHe makes me happy, he makes me happy\n\nHe makes me happy, happy as can be\nI love my daddy, I love my daddy\n\nI love my daddy, and I know he loves me\n\nHe makes me happy, he makes me happy\n\nHe makes me happy, and I know he loves me\nHe helps me learn things, he helps me learn things\n\nHe helps me learn things, he teaches me right\n\nHe gives me hugs, he gives me hugs\n\nHe gives me hugs, and tucks me in at night\nBut daddy is gone, now, daddy is gone\n\nDaddy is gone, now, A day long since gone\n\nAnd now I have found you, and taken my light\n\nYou'll be my new daddy, and tuck me in at night\n-================-\n\nThis poem was sung in the Library of Dragur by a spectre, that of a child.\n\nAshur Uilloson and a High Elf named Nyna were in attendance. Lights were snuffed out.\n-================-", ""),
        StaticBook("Mylas' Interview", "Otto Von Habsburg", "How did you grow into the man you are now?\nHardwork, dilligence and a healthy amount of praying.\nWhen did you decide to go into politics?\nI come from a long line of politicans, in fact, my grandfather was mayor of the capital before me.\nI've\ndecided to take it up during the war to better serve my country and emperor.\nWill you run for mayor again?\nIndeed, i am forming the Vote Mylas party to ensure a better Orenia and Felsen for future generations\nWill you run the city the same way?\nDuring my first term i've gotten aqcuianted with how the city works and meeting the fine constituants that make up the largest city on gods green earth. However for my second term i plan to enact a lot of ideas\nbrought to me by other people, that have been throwing around in my own head.\nWho do you see as your biggest Political opponent?\nMy twin brother Kylas\nSo, you're going up against your twin?\nIf he decides to run, i suppose. But he is also\nmy campaign manager.\nWant to make a final statement?\nGod bless his mayesty John Oren and god bless the empire of Orenia.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mystery R letter", "Farryn", "To Azariah.\n\nI've  beared witness to the situation in which you were accused of having romantic relations with Ashana Sarr. I merely write this in awe of you. -\n- I know it must be tough, withstanding the dwelling urge to strangle that man and woman from Sutica, but I beg you not to start anything unnecessary, especially doing this time and place. -\n- Honestly, I know that it must be tough dealing with things such as that, and this letter is also a reminder that you are better than them, and you must continue to be better than them.\n\n~ R\n* You have an elvish name and elvish roots *\nFollowed by the guidance of the attributes\n*\nYou must stand tall, taller than those below\n*\nFor only you hold the key to this power show\n*\n* Showing them your weakness will only hurt your name\n*\nSo do not set things ablaze that will impower this war game\n*\nYou can only keep this anger to yourself\n*\nFor that is the power of a true noble elf\n*", ""),
        StaticBook("Mystery Unsolved", "Samuel de Saltpans", "Perhaps it's due to my inability to choose, but this felt needed to happen. I simply couldn't take it anymore. Join my criminal Saltpan family, or stay as a loyal felsenite in my new home here.\nEdgar says blood runs thicker than water, but I think water runs deep. This is why I simply don't join my brother's ambitions to create some anarchist revolution. What he thinks is justice I think is evil. But then again, he is family. I miss them so much\nMylas hates me for supposedly conspiring with Edgar instead of turning him in. But my intention was to visit him to simply talk, I haven't seen him in years. I didn't plan on joining him, nor did I plan on turning him in. I resent Mylas for nearly-\n-killing Edgar in front of me. Edgar has committed atrocious acts, but I can not let my brother die. Does this make me bad? Does this contribute to the fact perhaps I deserve death for not wanting moral justice towards Edgar.\nHerod has vanished, so does my business ventures I guess. Mylas detests me, the Saltpans ignore me, Balthazar will probably execute me, and Brutalist is too blinded by a constant rage to feel sympathy towards me. Not that I need it anyways.\nI do this because I can't choose a side. In chess, it's called Zugzwang... when the only viable move... is not to move.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mystif", "Amras Yavelty", "A Denial of the Mystification of Hope\nBy Amras Yavelty\nIt is prudent to mention that my writing doesn’t intend to deny hope as a valuable emotion of the being but instead explain it as a natural occurring phenomena and not a religion justifying emotion. It seems that hope arises whenever the 'self is under\nsiege’ from within or externally. When I use the phrase ‘self under siege’ I mean the being in which hope occurs is undergoing an emotional, physical or mental conflict as a result of internal or external factors\n\nThe problem with hope is that it often\nmisleads the being into identifying hope as an inner sixth sense that gives out or provides some kind information about divine entities and their bond with beings. Hope indeed is a strong emotion and is one that seems to arise even in the most dire of\nsituations. This is explained easily because hope is, none the less, an impulse of the being to maintain it alive and relevant in the world. It is, after all, a common use of hope in Druid religion in which it had been used to indirectly justify the\nbeliefs and cults regarding their gods.\n\nIt is a foolish notion a sir tends to disregard that hope is not a product of the mind, but instead an impulse of the being to survive, a reflex, therefore it cannot be used in the rational process. It is from this\nstatement that I can conclude that any justification of religious beliefs and cults through the false definition of hope are irrational and untrustworthy in their nature and is by all cost all logic is to be avoided by the Mali’aheral.", ""),
        StaticBook("Myth - Great War", "Leyu", "The Myth of the Great War by\nHierophant Pulver,\nMaster of Dungeons \"Aegis\"\nAlmost two thousand years ago a terrible war broke out between the two mighty guilds of wizards -one good and one evil- that controlled great empires. Wizards on both sides vowed to fight until they were utterly\ntriumphant, seeking to purge their rivals from the earth. With fearsome magic and dragon armies they battled for centuries, neither side winning final victory .:: In the process of their warfare, the wizards wrought vast devastation on\nthe world forests blazed up, islands sank into the sea, entire races became extinct. Eventually, the the great goddess of Nature awakened from her sleep to witness the savage conflict. Shocked by the destruction, the Goddess sent a\nvision to a single human: the woman who would become the first Grand Druid. Through the vision, this chosen figure saw that she must found a druidic order to preserve the fragile remains of her world's ecology. With the guidance of her goddess, the\nOrder grew in strength until finally it had the power to intervene in the wizard war. The force of young druids pooled their powers and together vanquished the members of both battling guilds, transforming the combatants into\ninnocent wild beasts. Once the former wizards now unable to fathom the concept of good versus evil - slithered, bounded, loped and crawled off into their ruined habitats, the Order began to heal the world. Since then, the druidic order continually\nworks to prevent such destruction from ever occurring again. Druids pledge to make sure the wars of good and evil no longer mar the precious earth. But, the Order also has bitter enemies in the ancient remnants of the guilds of warring wizards- those\ngood and evil mages who luckily escaped the fate of their fellows. Each guild claims it had been on the verge of victory and would have won, had druids not interfered. :: -As recounted by Hierophant Pulver, Master of Dungeons.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Naromism: Part 1", "Elvira Naromis", "[!] The book has a  blood red leather cover that is ensribed with golden tribal fire designs and the clerical eye in the middle of the cover. [!]\n\n         Naromism\n\n\n   The ideology of\nEmotional control and\n  the views of Grey.\n\nWritten by Elvira Naromis.\nLeader of the Clerical Order.\nIntroduction\nWhen I became clerical leader on the 19th of The Grand Harvest 1547, I knew things had to change within the order I now lead. The clerics have always followed a traditional ideology that tends to result in putting them into grave dangers,\nincluding those we never wanted brought on us. I, myself, have been a victim of this, I know of how it can affect the body and mind, as well as others. In the end, I’ve decided to change it, to ensure the future of the clerics and that we are no longer\nmost expect us to be. Thus, I have created this new form of clericalism to ensure this. I understand full well that there will be those who will be against this belief and if they wish to harm those who accept this belief,\nhen I would like to ask them to raise their sword to me, the creator of the belief, rather than the followers.\nWhat exactly is Naromism?\n\nNaromism is a branch of clericalism which, while including the compulsory devotion and appreciation to Tahariae, additionally focuses on emotional control and the understanding of grey beliefs,\nsuch as the idea that everything isn’t automatically good or evil by stereotypical beliefs.  The purpose of this branch to ensure that clerics do not get themselves into deep situations that would likely risk themselves harmed, killed, or disconnected.\nThis is mostly through causing trouble amongst the Dark to suddenly breaking the Utterings by sudden emotional outbursts. For example, a cleric randomly killing Dark mages that are doing nothing wrong will likely ensure further conflict between the Dark\nand the clerics.\n\nAdditionally, the concept of one controlling their emotions is put in place, as a sudden emotional outburst may distract a cleric from their duty or will cause them to accidentally or purposely break an uttering.  For example, imagine a\ncleric walking around and is then insulted by someone. The cleric ignores the person at first but as the person insults them more, their temper and anger grows.  Soon, the anger reaches its peak and the cleric has a high chance of losing control of\nthemselves.  If the cleric loses control of themselves, it could cause them to lash out at the other, either brutally harming or killing them, thus breaking the uttering of not killing an innocents out of cold blood. That is why I have included this in\nNaromism: To prevent a cleric from being emotionally held back from their duties and to ensure they do not break the Utterings. The ideology also ensures that the cleric cares about themselves and others, such as knowing their limits and ensuring another\ncleric is back on track.\nNaromism's Origins\n\nThe background of Naromism came from my own background and understandings, as well as containing implemented beliefs and ideologies of Ashanaak, First Vailorian Prophet of Tahariae, and understandings of Xionism.\nBeing someone of short temper, I realised that my own emotions and anger would lead to me losing control of myself, leading to me potentially breaking one of the Utterings.  I taught myself how to control my emotions through immense meditating and coming\nto understand why these emotions come to me. Soon, I learnt how to keep myself calm, stop the emotions from overwhelming as well as being able to bring forth my emotions.  Soon, these traits aided me greatly in becoming a war cleric, including aiding me\nin becoming the first Vailorian cleric to master the Flames of Reckoning. A war cleric relies on their emotions to use the spells, so mastering your own emotions first before you try any war cleric spells is recommended.\nAdditionally, the beliefs involved with Naromism comes from my early experiences before becoming a cleric, then  later experiences with the Cult of Xion and The Covenant. Normally, one would expect me to hold a grudge against the Cult and the Covenant for\nwhat they have done to me and my order throughout Vailor but I do not. They are also people with their own goals and views, with different ways to achieve them. If anything, I believe that instead of constantly fighting each other over what we believe,\nwe should learn about the other’s beliefs and accept that they are there.\n\nDuring the realm of Athera, I served as a bartender within the Drunken Monk tavern, located within the cloud temple. Quite an ironic job for someone who cannot withstand drinking\nthe stuff as too much would result in being ill for a week. Due to the tavern being within cloud temple grounds, no harm could come to me so I safely interacted with Dread knights and a few other Darks, even taught a Lich Alchemy,\nand learnt that not all Dark were evil. Additionally, I was trained in Alchemy by Daniel Nodal, a Master Alchemist and father figure to me, who told me tales of times he had befriended a few of the Dark. \n\nSoon, Vailor came and I became a cleric. Why did I become a cleric? At first, it was to simply aid others and rid the Dark. During that time, I was convinced that myself and my fellow clerics had to purge all of the Dark, regardless of their intentions.\nHowever, due to  a run in with a necromancer who tortured me for killing an innocent Dark, I began to wonder if I was truly right there, I had done it because I had to? Yet was it necessary to kill an innocent Dark and bring this harm to myself for the\nnecessity of Tahariae? As time when on, I began to question things more. It was not till I was captured by a group known as The Covenant that I soon began to question the lessons the Itherals had taught to the clerics.\nThe Covenant had treated me like a guest and showed no ill intentions, although the fact they never allowed me outdoors once led to myself falling ill due to my body unable to cope outside after being locked up for a whole year.\nThey simply kept me so that the clerics do as they say. During my one year captivity, I attempted a false disconnection to get out and I was given a book regarding Xionism to read when they wondered if I was downright serious.\nThere, I found out that their ideologies were not truly as dark as I first intended, they were actually fairly reasonable in some areas. As for my false disconnection? I failed that.\n\nI then asked myself one single question:\nwas it truly right to kill someone simply because they were classed as ‘Dark’? \nI soon came to an answer. It is stated in the Utterings to purge what is Dark and impure, because Tahariae wills it. To do your duty for Tahariae’s necessity.\nMany clerics believe that we had to purge all Dark for the necessity of peace, yet here we are killing and causing disruptions for ourselves and others.  In the end, I concluded that a cleric should not go and slaughter all dark beings for the sake of\npeace and purity, the clerics are meant to ensure peace and purity was spread throughout the lands yet there is none of that with wars and fights happening. I knew that things had to change, for the greater good of clerics and Dark alike.\nI knew I was the one who could bring this about and so I took it on my shoulders, along with the duty of being the leader of the clerics. So here, I have created my own teachings and split them into two halves. Two ideologies.\nThe Emotional Ideology and\nthe Grey Ideology.\nThe Emotional Ideology\n\nThe Emotional ideology is basically the idea that a cleric must learn to master their own emotions to ensure they do not place themselves or others in dangerous situations.  Such as losing control of anger and leading the\ncleric to lose control of themselves, able to harm themselves or others. Instead, a cleric is to have a calm and focused mind, they must not allow themselves to be intimidated, frightened, or emotionally sensitive in situations such as a fight. I do not\nwant to limit the clerics in what emotions they can show, instead, I wish for them to remain themselves and do show emotions. However, they will learn to hold the emotions back and remain calm,  so that they have a chance of surviving a confrontation if\none does come. Additionally, they will learn how to bring forth a particular emotion to aid them with their war clericalism spells.\nThe Grey Ideology\n\nThe Grey ideology is more complex and detailed compared to the Emotional ideology. In simpler terms, the Grey ideology is basically the understanding that those who are Dark are not immediately evil due to their magic. Instead,\na cleric should know of the following statements:\n\n- Those who are Dark yet innocent shall not be forsaken and killed for simply their choice, they have accepted the Dark and thus accept the consequences that may come. They shall be watched\ncarefully but overall left alone unless they harm an innocent for no reason.\n\n-  The Dark is not inherently evil by what others immediately believe. To I, it is merely a more effective tool for spreading evil and thus a cause for suspicion, not a crime\nin and of itself. That was what the Itherals had taught the clerics; simply being Dark is a crime and thus you shall be punished. Yet with this teaching, came an immense amount of problems for those who follow their teachings.\n- Those who are Dark and seek to use their magic or forms to bring harm to innocents shall not be left to roam freely. Their actions will not be turned away from easily, for to harm an innocent and create panic and fear is a crime against peace and\npurity. Their evil deeds shall not go unpunished and they will not only face the Reckoning of Tahariae’s wraith, but also the Reckoning of the Descendants for the crimes they committed against them.\nIt should be known that the ideology of Black and White does not fully justify what is good and evil in our world. It is simply a view that has stuck with the Descendants for far too long, that many believe it to be true. They became blind and oblivious\nto what can truly make one good or evil: The intentions. We, Descendants, cannot be purely good or evil, we contain both traits although one can be weaker than the other. We may be a warrior of light but we can still harm and kill, and a dark mage may\nsimply seek to live an ordinary life without wanting to cause harm. It is our actions that justify whenever we are good or evil, not the tools that we use. Regardless, one should never allow themselves to see Black and White, or Light and Dark. \nInstead,\nknow that everything can be seen as Grey.\n-=+=- Seek out -=+=-\n Part Two if you are\n  still interested in\n-=+=- Naromism -=+=-", ""),
        StaticBook("Naromism: Part 2", "Elvira Naromis", "[!] The book has a blood red leather cover that is enscribed with golden tribal flame designs and the clerical eye in the middle of the cover. [!]\nNaromism\n         (Part Two)\n\n    The ideology of\nEmotional control and\n    the views of grey.\n\nWritten by Elvira Naromis\nLeader of the Clerical Order.\nThe Grey Aims\n\nA cleric who takes up Naromism is known as a Naromist Cleric. However, anyone can take and follow any beliefs in here. A Naromist cleric follows the following set of rules known as ‘The Grey Aims’.\n1. Understand that not all things Dark are automatically evil, but also living beings as well. Black and White views must become grey. However, tabs must be kept on the Dark to ensure that they do not go against innocents.\n2. If a Dark does attack an innocent or holds ill intentions that are indeed against humanity, the cleric must do their duty to purge the Dark to protect the innocent and ensure purity it kept. Additionally, if the cleric does not know any war cleric\nspells or cannot fight, they or another person MUST send word to another cleric if possible so that they can have assistance.\n3. A cleric is advised to research Dark magic and beings in order to understand the magic and beings, as well as to know how to handle them in combat. To defeat the enemy, you must first understand your enemy.\n4. If a fellow cleric is struggling to follow the Utterings, a cleric must help the other in managing with the Utterings to ensure disconnection does not occur.\n5. A cleric must respect and understand Tahariae’s power and use it when necessary, but also to use it wisely and understand their limits well so that they do not fall easily.\n6. A cleric must be taught how to control and master their emotions. Failing to control such emotions will lead to future consequences for the cleric and may result in accidental breaking of a Uttering.\n7. A cleric who cannot control their emotions will be helped but if they still cannot master their emotions, they shall be left alone to face the future consequences of their actions.\n8. A cleric must respect other views and ideologies and not reinforce their views onto others, they must allow others to accept Naromism if they wish to do so.\nA cleric, or anyone, is free to take up these views. I will not reinforce my views onto those who do not follow it, but at least inform them of it so that they understand it and know that it is what I follow. I will not stand for anyone who immediately\ngrows to hate the followers of this ideology and seeks to harm them for wanting to follow Naromism.\nTermanology\n\nDark - The term used for a subject that revolves around beings and mages of darkness, as well as other subjects.\n\nBlack and white - The term used for the ideology that everything in the world is split into black and\nwhite - evil and good. For example: A dark mage being immediately presumed evil despite not knowing the person’s intentions. Whereas using a spell of light automatically makes one good. Many grow up with this view and presume that it is the correct view\nto follow, despite that it causes many troubles.\n\nThe Emotional Ideology - The ideology that a cleric must not allow their emotions to control them but rather be the ones to control their emotions, to ensure that themselves and others are not placed\nin any paticular dangers.\n\nThe Grey Ideology -  The ideology that the Dark are not immediately all evil and that its based on the intentions of the Dark, rather than the magic or appearance itself that decides who is good and evil.\nThe Grey Aims - The rules a Naromist cleric follows to ensure themselves and others are safe.\n\nNaromist(s) - A cleric or person who follow the beliefs of Naromism.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nathair's Quest", "Rem Rei", "Quest for Nathair Silvershadow.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nQuest Giver: Remlastor \"Rem\" Rei.\nQuest Objective:\n\nTrade x1 Aurum Nugget for as much Dwarven ale as you can get.\n\nFetch me x1 Salmon.\n\nFetch me x1 Cactus.\n\nFetch me x5 Tulips.\nOnce you have done all the above, please bring them all to me for your reward.\n\n\nREWARD: 150 Minas, Fishing Rod, Food.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature", "Ierven Camoryn", "Nature\n=================\nBy: Ierven Camoryn\nNuts and beans\nAcorns and leaves\nTree-pecking birds\nUrchins with spines\nRhinos with horns\nEveryday!\nTrees with apples\nRocks with moss\nEvery tree hasa leaf\nEvery rock is stoney\nGrasshoppers\nRabbits\nAcorns\nSnakes\nSnails\nShrooms red \nHow brown?\nRed I said!\nOr brown?\nOr red!\nMaybe both.\nSpiders are cool\nPrickly sometimes\nI know this for sure\nDirt is their friend\nEverone                         misunderstands\nRory the poor spider", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Healing", "The Sequoia Druid", "The Nature of Druidic Healing\n\n\nBy: Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid\nDruidic Healing is a topic many are curious about, but few, even among Druids, wholly understand the cost on the one performing it.  Most Druids use living reagents to assist in the mending process, this is so that they can draw on the living essense\nwithin the reagent and draw less from themselves, but a skilled Druidic healer can also safely mend wounds without any reagents onhand.\n\nDruidic healing is, quite simply, an exchange of living essence from the healer to the patient.\nThe Druid focuses upon the living tissue around the wound and asks the patient's body to mend itself, giving of their own living essence to aid in the healing.\n\nThis is where the cost and risk of Druidic healing is, and you should heed it well.\nA druid is capable of amazing feats of healing at times, but all of our healing derives from ourselves and it is possible to cause lasting damage to oneself while healing the wounds of another. This is why living reagents are used, to lessen the need to\ndraw from oneself.\nI have personally healed a variety of wounds, from cuts and scrapes to sword clashes to broken bones to some far worse. They all draw from you to some extent, even when using reagents.\nSimple wounds you may not even notice the drain upon yourself, it depends how strong your healing has become, and how familiar you are with the process. Practice truly makes perfect in this regard.\nI am of the belief an example of a mistake is the best way to pass on a lesson, so I will share how I nearly lost my life while healing the King of Skravia back on Asulon. He and some of his soldiers had been lured out to the base\nof a rogue mage that had harassed their kingdom for a long while. When they gained the upper hand and cornered the mage, his trap was revealed, the walls of his base were lined with explosives, and he detonated them.\nThree of the soldiers died in the blast, the others dragged a severely injured but alive King back to Skravia and to my inn, knowing I was a healer. His wounds were great, part of his skull was visible on the top of his head,\nand he had shrapnel wounds all across his body, blood everywhere. There was nothing to do but try, I coated the wounds with a mixture of living slime and bonemeal, then began the healing process,\ndrawing upon the living essences as well as myself to stabilize and mend the kind King laying before me. It took nearly two hours, but his wounds sealed and he was alive and left in a coma for a few days.\nHowever, I had given of myself far more that I should have, my skin was pale, almost white, and my eyes had lost most of their color and I could hardly breathe. I am told I lost consciousness, I awoke five weeks later, my every limb sore,\nmy hair a shade lighter, but my skin almost back to its normal tone. A fellow Druid, Jena, had to come out to restore some living essence to me or I would have perished within the first day or two, I was so weakened.\nTake my mistake with you if you seek to heal, you give of yourself, there is a limit you will reach and you should not go beyond it or you risk your life.  Find your balance between personal sacrifice and reagents to ease your burden,\nyou almost always have something available to ease your personal strain, even if it is the grass around you or a planter of flowers outside the window, any living essence can ease your burden\nif the situation is a bit beyond your ability to heal safely with nothing on hand.\n\n\n~Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature's Life", "Lilliana", "Nature is but many things\nA guide who leads us\nA guard who protects us\nA mother who provides us\nThe guide in nature\nCarries us forth\nHe teaches us right and wrong\nHe carries us forth\nHe shows us how to hunt\nThe Guard in nature\nProtects us from danger\nHe shows us safe from unsafe\nHe teaches us how to be strong\nThe Mother in nature\nProvides us with life\nShe gives us food and love\nShe gives us hope\nNature is many faces\nNature is many lives\nEach life continues\nFrom root to leaf\nFrom nose to tail\nNature lives in all of us\nHer life is ours\nWithout her, we will never be the same", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature, O Nature", "Felix Reed", "Nature, Nature, Ode to Thee.\nIt is only you that I can see.\nNature, Nature, Tell me Why.\nHow can you create such Blue Skies?\nNature, O Nature, Tell me Right.\nSo that you may cleanse my Impure Sight.\nNature, O Nature, Lend an Ear.\nSo I can hear what you say Most Clear.\nNature, Nature, show me How.\nTo properly honor you with a Bow.\nNature, Nature, Tell me Now.\nSo I may recite your solemn vows.\nIn the Aspects, I shall Pledge.\nFrom Here and Hereafter, I shall be walking on the edge.\nFor you alone, my Soul is yours.\nThe Aspects have called,\nLet us open the Door.", ""),
        StaticBook("Natures Balance", "Rindir", "Natures Balance\n          by: Rindir\nAlike the six descendant races,\nThere exists six trees to hold their places:\n\nOak,\nBirch,\nSpruce,\nJungle,\n\nAnd according to the tale,\nAcacia,\nAnd dark oak are said to hail.\n\nThe trees can be appointed to the six,\nAnd with that nature will achieve its balanced fix:\n\nOak to Human,\nBirch to Elf,\nSpruce to Dwarf,\nJungle to Kha’,\nDark Oak to Orc,\nand Acacia to Halfling.\n\nAnd with these six beautiful tree,\nThe rest of the world will see,\nThe wonderous forest created by thee.", ""),
        StaticBook("Natures Bloom", "Faelon Oakenthorn", "Natures Bloom\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=I lay in the forest,\nfor an hour it seems,\nThe wind blowing valiantly, as I conjure my dreams.\nA sudden sensation awakes me from my daze.\nWhat I dreamt remains but a haze.\nI felt it fall, on the tip of my nose.\nA small red petal, that came from a rose.\nIt rode the wind, far from home.\nA home with grass, softer than foam.\nI swiftly ran to find this place.\nAlas I couldn't find a trace.\nInstead I found a small birch tree.\nWhich in height was equal to me.\nIts leaves were greener than ever before.\nDespite most lying on the floor.\nI ventured further into the wood.\nWalking through the puddles of mud.\nI stumbled upon a small bird,\nwhose soft chirps I had heard.\nIt looked at me with its pleasant eyes,\nbefore flying high into the skies.\nI sat on the floor and admired its wings,\nbeautiful and feathery; stronger that most things.\nI lay back down, onto the soft earthy floor.\nMy whole body relaxed as well as my core.\nThat time in the forest was a brilliant one.\nI dream now, about the day that is gone.\n\n-By Faelon Oakenthorn\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=", ""),
        StaticBook("Natures Ode", "Terreni Decorum", "Morning springs with hope anew\n\nTo melt the chill of winters dew. \n\nThe great tree wakes from slumbers peace\n\nWhile blooms of color shows their fleece.\nNo more will winter's chill cause the world to still. \n\nWhy you ask , should spring flow in such a way\n\ntis the circle of which things grow, death of one another to sew\nThere you have the poem nature's ode \n\nSilence to follow while darkness calls, life stills beneath the shadows\n\nThe third page reached so no more shall follow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Natures Way!", "Isengar Brockfall", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n         Journey to \n      The Forbidden Lands\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n\nBy Isengar Brockfall\nDay 1\n\n\nLife. Life is a mysterious thing don't you think?\n\nWhen that one special day leads up to a perfect moment and you want it to never end.\nI mean you probably want to know more about me, who am I? you might ask.\n\nWell i'm a Halfling, I have long brown hair, blue eyes and I am 67\nyears of age.\nWhich is obviously quite young for a halfling.\nWell I live in a Beautiful village called Gimblewood, a place of peace.\nUs Halflings tend to stay out of the big world, not knowing much about the famous Bandits or Orcs out to get us.\nI awoke and reached out for my small mug of clean water.\nA sense of joy came to my body as I slurped it up.\n\nI got out my squeaky bed and picked up my brown, long smooth pipe.\nI shoved some grated cactus green in the end, and held the pipe to my lantern.\nI walked across my spruce floor board and opened my door.\nA nice breeze hugged against my delicate face.\nI stood leaning on my door, glancing at every movement whilst smoking my pipe.\nEvery smoke I took, felt as if I were sucking in more energy.\nMy head got a buzzing sensation and I felt a relaxation in my body.\nI waved my pipe in the air and blew it until the smoke stopped.\nI placed it down on my cabenet on the outside of my door.\n\nI reached inside my burrow and grabbed my red silky jacket.\nIt has never had a stain on it and I like to keep that way!", ""),
        StaticBook("Natures Wrath", "Lentos", "*A small oil painting of a dragon is pinned to the page, the beast depicted with its wings outstretched, its mouth wide open, spurting fire upon the invisible prey below it*\n\n \"The Great Burn\"\nThe inferno kisses my palms-\n Yet I do not cry.\n \n I kiss it back-\n Even If I am shy.\n\n It takes my hand-\n To lead me away.\n\n 'To seek more fire gone astray'\n*Yet another illistration is pinned into the book, this one depicting a simple rose. It's petals are a deep crimson, and look as smooth as velvet*\n\n     \"Thorns\"\nLittle Rose sat on a hill-\n Singing to the daffodils.\n \n The hummed along-\n To her tune-\n Causing men to be so still.\n\n The watched Little Rose on her hill-\nSinging to the daffodils.\n\n And when night came-\n They stole her away- \n Giving her a new place to sing.\n\n Yet Rose did not like her new spot-\n And refused to utter a sound.\nSo they beat her-\n And cut her-\n And left her to rot-\n Under her old sweet hill.\n\n The daffodils cried from the pain and the loss- \n Of there old friend.\n\n Who was never seen again.\nNot in her current being however-\n The one left to rot.\n\n The earth stole its beauty away-\n And crafted a flower of it.\n\n Now Rose may sit upon her hill-\n But she does not make a sound.\nFor flowers are not meant to sing-\n Only to hum along.\n*Its a small painting of a rabbit, curled up in a small patch of moss under a tall, great oak*", ""),
        StaticBook("Natwure hosh", "__Jyggalag__", "Natwer Gud:\n\nNatwere berry hosh, dah twiis wimind mi ub da twiggis in da natwre. Mi tink klomp tweeuggers nubhosh, twiuggers gud fwiends ub Durzub. Durzub like dah flowas and dah pwants un da natwre.\nDurzub berry hosh in da natwre. Durzub nub make twiggis\nsnaga, Durzub like dah twiggis. Durzub wunt noice san in dah twiggi goi. Durzub klomp da inbedures flat. Durzub baboosh brudda.B ut Durzub tay dabu tu da twiggis agn nub klomp dem. Durzub wike betting howlur in dah woodz. agh durzub bet da squeals agh \nbubbas tuu", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancers V I", "Freyr Mantisuku", "Investigations into Necromancers Volume I\nA picture of a man in dark robes standing over dying man a stream of dark green is slowing from the dying man into the robed man hand, two decaying zombies stand behind the dark robed man awaiting his orders*\nArthur: Freyr Mantisuku\nCo-Author: Crineas Acosta\n[Forewarning: Do not confront Necromancers unprepared]\n[Always Bring a Paladin or war cleric with you during hunts]\nA Short Introduction\nNecromancy is the defined pragmatically as the utilisation of Life-Force. Necromancers usually have tell-tale signs of their necromancy,\nIt is like poking a hole in a bucket they can take others life force with the imbalance but their own life force is slowly drained.\n Necromancy is the draining of life-force for nefarious purposes commonly, it’s an art shunned by many.\nAppearance\nThey look like us, For all you know one could be next to you they are very hard to find the only true tell is that many will have a very pale look and are extremely sensitive\nand weak but this does not go for all necromancers. Basically, signs of decay on their bodies would be a significant give-away.\nBehavior\nDue to the extreme difficulty of actually picking one out in a crowded this second cant be added in details.\nStrengths\nThey have the power to resurrect the dead and use them as Minions.\nThey can drain the life force of living things leading to a quick death.\nWeakness.\nLike all mages they are physically weak and can be killed easily..\nSome instances, holy magic can effect them but it's not always the case. \nThey also have the ability to curse other by modifying life force.\nOrigins and Additional details\nHow mortals found this magic is unknown, but it's safe to conclude that the undead under Iblees was instrumental to the art during Aegis\nIt’s likely that they drain life-force whilst using their own bodies to draw it, whether through physical means or through other ways such as mists.\nA note of warning. \nLearning Necromancy is a taboo and would lead to severe repercussions on one’s own wellbeing and health.\nNotes:\nAny extra, Corrections or confirmations on information can be\nSent to Either Freyr, or Crineas (( samsan99, Sharkali ))Further Volumes will be compiled as more information is made available.", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancy", "Haadi Mubdee", "[!] This book contains sufficient knowledge on Necromancy as to ward it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancy", "Ebonsquire", "Necromancy\n\n((Originally written by Castellano))\nNecromancy - Black Magic; The art of communicating with the dead; Witchcraft; There are many forms of Necromancy, but in this day, there is only secret Necromancy.\n\nA group that people call the \"Undead\" have been known to use Necromancy\nto their full extent. The Necromancers in their organization have been using Necromancy against the people of Aegis. The powers that the dead give them through Necromancy, gives them the ability to summon the dead, use the weather, as in lightning, and\nuse magic that comes from Hell, or also known as \"Nether\".\n\nThe people of Aegis have started to follow the \"Undead\" and Necromancers and have been studying their ways, giving them the ability to use this form of Black Magic. The Ascended(Good Guys) have\nbeen known to be against this magic. Ascended does not patrol the open roads like hte Necromancers and Undead do. Rumors around say that they stay at a heavenly place near the Cloud temple. \n\nThe attacks of the Necromancers have been deadly, and\nusually have won the battle and took the victory back to the Nether and celebrated with the spirits. The only known places that have been attacked are Snowy Fields, Winterfell, Alstion town, and Kal'Bryst. Now, if you haven't noticed already, it has been\ngoing from north to south. In that case, the conditions that have been gathered threw predictions that the next attacks could be at the following cities: Al'Khazar, Stone Leaf, Whispering Isle, and Kal'Alras. They are just slight predictions, the Undead\nprobably won't even attack them. It's just prediction.\n\nThe Undead are growing in numbers, the last known report of them travelling in a pack was the number count of fice. But the last report was long ago. The numbers could have been\ndoubled, no one knows. So, from what you have been reading, the Necromancers are deadly, and you should avoid them at all times. If not, you could lose your life, or loved ones around you.\n\nI, the Author, am leaving the book un-signed, so that\nif an Undead member finds this,  won't be slain. A second book could be created if any more records or information is released. \n\n*Book is un-signed and has blank pages in the back of the book.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromany", "Stardash702", "The topic of necromancy:\n\n*Here would be a quickly drawn picture of a hand forcing magic into a rising corpse\nNecromany has long been known as an evil and cursed magic, however that may not be the case.\n\nNecromany is the ability to resummon the spirits of the dead, but since said spirits are already dead and ony their power is used, this isn't really a crime.\nNecromancy is simply an alternative form of power and use. Necromancy is one of few magics that can bring back the dead, but not the only one. Certain monks are equally capable of ressurection, but since their magic is 'Divine' its considered as holy and\nnot evil.\n\nAnother useful power given by necromany is the ability to summon the undead. Now, this was also the first use, yet that trick can be used both to bring back companions and as an army.\nIn a war, many soldiers or warriors risk their lives and die doing so, yet when a breed of magic like necromancy offers a way to avoid these risks, it is seen as evil and the stuborn nature of mortals continues to risk their own lives before that of an\nalledged 'Holy being'.\n\nSpeaking of 'Holy beings', what can these 'Holy Beings' alledgedly do?\n\nThey can create life, necromancy is one of the only magics that also dables in life and death and thus is one of the closest magics in this way to the so\ncalled 'gods'.\n\nAnother power of 'gods' is to change the nature of a being (like many centuries ago when elves were cursed with little to no kids but gifted with extremely long life.\n\nNecromany can also alter creatures.\nNecromany can be used to give spirits the ability to return to the mortal plain and can even be used to give others more strength (via the weakining of others which is another change to a beings make up).\nOverall (whilst it is seen as an evil and unholy form of magic, necromancy can also be used for good and is one of the closest magics to the 'Gods' of this world.\n\nBecause of this, Necromancy can not simply be considered evil at first glance and must\ninstead (like all other aspects of nature) be seen as 'Innocent untill proven guilty'.\nHopefully this book has changed your opinion on the art of Necromancy, but the true purpose of this book was simply to get me out of jail.\n\n*At the bottom of the page is a cartoon drawing of a sad stick figure behind bars.\n*On the back cover is a picture of a peaceful city being defended by a necromancy army whilst in the foreground people are being healed via necromancers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir's Notes", "Nemir", "Entry one, 9th of Malin's Welcome, 1569.\nIt's another cool day here in Kovagrad, there's a nip in the air.  The cold won't be good for the crops.  Never is.  But I hardly need to worry about that.  I'm no farmer, just a simple herbalist.\nNotes of lesser accuity potions.\n-----------\nI've prepared a couple of bottles of aqua vitae, just had to soak this red root in warm water for a few hours.  It's pure alcohol, perfect for greater potions.  Along with the aqua vitae, I've prepared a couple\nof bottles of distilled water.  These are for lesser potions.  Gonna need some more coal or perhaps some charcoal soon if I want more of these lesser bases.\n\n\nAlright.  Now that I've got my bases all set up, I'm gonna put some larihei's fingers\ninto the aqua vitae.  I ended up getting a salve of larihei.  Upon using it I've noticed my movements were more... delicate for a short amount of time.  Perhaps an agility potion could come out of this.\nI added halflings grass and got something I like to\ncall a soft relxant.  It pretty much soothes muscle pain for a short amount of time.  Perfect for sore muscles!  I believe this should be enough notes for the day.  I shall continue tomorrow or perhaps sometime later on this week.\nEntry two, 12th of Malin's Welcome, 1569.\nToday I've decided to mess around with the distilled water as the base.  I will do as I did the other day, use larihei's fingers.  The outcome of this was a potion that, when drunken, I felt like my mind was\nclearer.  I was more aware of my movements, could be useful.  Upon adding halfings grass to the potion I got a liquid that was thinner than water, and it swirled nonstop within the bottle.  Upon testing it, my vision was blurred greatly, though I felt\nmore agile.  I guess it'd be helpful.\n\nEntry three, 11th of The Deep Cold, 1569.\nSimple poisons.\nRed Mushroom Poison, makes the user have an upset stomach and feel nauseated.  Good for telling someone to fuck off when they ask for wine.\nPotion of Alabaster Leaf, about the same effects as the last poison, but looks more like tea than wine.  Plus it doesn't have white particles floating around in it.  Potion could also be used as an antidote to other poisons.  If used as one, it'd still\nmake the user's stomach upset.\nPotion of Saffvil, if this is consumed in large amounts the user will die due to its poison.  If consumed in smaller amounts the user will just vomit.\nPotion of Clutcher's Straw, if this potion is taken in large amounts\nthe user's muscles will lock up, paralyzing them.  They will remain conscious.\nParalyzing Toxin, this seems to be one of the most deadly poisons I've ever made.  Any amount taken makes the user paralyzed, keeping them from seeking out an antidote.\nAnother effect is that the user will struggle to breath, eventually suffocating them.\nParalyzing Tonic, another helpful poison.  If the user takes any amount of this poison they will become paralyzed and blind for a short amount of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Neo - Druidism", "Eloh'ra", "Neo-Druidism\n\nThis tome was originally created by Petyr Brandybuck.\nWith some modern druidic practices wandering astray, it has been necessary for me to scribe another text - that of Neo-druidism. Throughout my travels and meditative studies, I have had revelations unknown to others. It is important to understand\nthat there is a special type of balance that druids themselves remember to study - action and non-action. Let me clarify. Action is motion, the motion of restoring balance, and of being the hand of Nature, the Universe, the \"It\". For, through non-action\nyou may feel \"It\", and through action you may be \"It\". Call this \"It\" what you want; most druids will call it Nature. What is important is to understand what Nature truly is, and how it relates to you. To reveal this is the goal of this tome.\n\nThe Unity of Nature\n\nThe first fault in thinking is to make distinctions - those between you and Nature between life and death, between good and evil. Everything is Nature, despite what any given piece believes. A druid does not use nature:\na druid is merely a piece who realizes the profound truth. Through non-action, one may truly understand this concept and feel it course through them. However while meditating in non-action, one also separates themselves from the flow; the Way,\nthe path that Nature chooses for its pieces. To rejoin with Nature, one must practice action.\n\nThe way of Nature\n\nNature does what it will, and while we realize this while meditating, sometimes we forget in action. We are merely moving along the river of life, the tides of balance. While we beleive that we are restoring the balance, It is\nbalance restoring itself in an everlasting self-conflict. Thus, through action, we are the hands of Nature, of balance, of the Way.", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol I", "Kalenz Uradir", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 1\nby Kalenz Uradir\nIn elven grammatical structure is often different to that of common. For one instead of placing an adjective before a noun it is placed after said noun. This becomes particularly important for the most basic of greetings.\nKarin'ayla - Goodmorning\nKer'ayla - Goodnight\nVan'ayla - Goodbye\n\nEach places the time of day before the adjective describing it. Noun and adjective are separated by an apostrophe.\nOther important words for the beginner in elven include race names:\n\nMali - Elf\nUruk - Orc\nValah - Human\nBortu - Dwarf\nIn order to form sub-races of elves, adjectives are taken to add more detail to the word Mali.\n\nMali'ame - Wood Elf\nMali'aheral - High Elf\nMali'ker - Dark Elf\nIn order to form sub-races of other cultures the suffix tali- may be used. This word most directly means 'part of'.\n\nTali'uruk - Goblin (Lit. Part Orc)\nTali'valah - Halfling (Lit. Part Human)\nOther basic phrases include exclamations including:\n\nAyla - Good\nSul'leyun - Brilliant (Lit. Beautiful Light)", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol II", "Kalenz Uradir", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 2\n by Kalenz Uradir\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in elven are as follows: \n\nKae - Me \nLae - Him/He \nNae - You \nLye - We - Used to speak of elves, people or the world. \nHae - Her/She\nFor example the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (He fared well). \n\nIn addition to this, other good language supplements to anyone learning elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be\nadded to create further detail or form critical grammatical structures in a sentence.\nThe dash denotes location of seed word. Affixes and seed words are separated by an apostrophe. \n\nac- (aca-) - Honorific for accursedness. \nah- (ahe-) - Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholars. For example: Ah'Lucion.\nfi- - New or anew.\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) - Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. For example: Cer'Silir.\n-ante (-nte) - Last \n-ento (-nto) - Next \n-onn - From or born. \nu- - Or\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive. \n-ir - Designates purpose of someone or something. \n-sae - The spreading, development or management. \n-ii - Diminutive form. For example: Malii, meaning little elf. \n\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("New Vacancy", "Urist Burialgears", "Been spendin' too much o' me time in t'a mines to merit ownin me house. I be moving out, t'is payment's going t'a be me last.\n\n-Urist Burialgears, Resident of Anabella's Boulevard 4", ""),
        StaticBook("Night", "Unknown", "Night\n\nThe moon shines\nThe stars twinkle\nSilence fills the night.\n\nIts dark\nIts mysterious\nMy fingers tingle with sensations\nEach step is suspense\nEach step is anticipation\nThe night never satisfies of my wonders\n\nThe night, the mask of secrets\nThe night, the cover for horrors\nThe night, the guise for the treacherous\nFull of suspicion\nFull of wariness\nFull of dangers\n\nYet the pull\nThe tug\nThe urge to see the night\nThe urge to uncover the mask\nThe urge to know the night\nIt is the beauty of the night.\n\nArahael Eloem (PianoEby)", ""),
        StaticBook("nightcrawler", "Toe", "you com lik shadow\nthru window crack\npretend asleep\ni lie on back\n\nyou wash over\nlike gentle stream\ni close my eyes\ntry not to scream\n\nyou hold me close\nwhisper in ear\nyou are safe\nhave no fear\ni say no\nyou say yes\ni fall to floor\nyou undres\n\nthe mornin grass\nis green and wet\ni sit alone\ntry to forget", ""),
        StaticBook("Nightmare Diary", "Elvi Terryal", "Entry one\n~~~~~~~\nI woke up from a nightmare this morning. I can't remember it exactly but for some reason, I tremble at the mere thought of it. What was it about? Who was involved?\n\nNevermind. It was just a nightmare. It won't bothere me at all.\nEntry two\n~~~~~~~\nFor the past two nights, I've been having the same nightmares. I remember vagely of them, a shady man (or elf?) laughing at me while I felt the worse pain imaginable.\n\nYet. I feel as though I know this pain from -\nsomewhere.... but where exactly?\n\nNevertheless, hopefully these nightmares will stop soon... they're getting on my nerves and waking up, trembling in cold sweat is not a way I like to start my mornings.\nEntry three\n~~~~~~~~~\nNightmares are getting worse as each day go by and I remember the nightmare now.\n\nRajin Aetos, the one face I never wanted to see again. The electric mage who electrocuted me for twenty minutes without end... electricuting me\n-repeatedly without end... in the distance of the dream are four ghosts. The four brothers who use to run the 'orphanage', the ones I killed in cold blood, staring at me with glee and revenge in their eyes...\n\nI've tried everything to stop the nightmares-\n-but they just keep on coming back.\n\nCreator help me please... I don't want to relive that day... please...\nEntry four\n~~~~~~~~\nInstead of going to sleep as normal, I've been forcing myself to stay awake...\n\nHowever, the nightmares are no longer the only thing I am worried about...\n\nMy anger... it's growing... each night, I\ncan feel my anger grow... as if enraged by the nightmares...\n\nI'm beginning to lose control of myself... reversing back to old ways...\n\nI don't want to though...\n\nI don't want to become Elvira again...\nI WANT TO REMAIN MYSELF!\n\n-There seems to be tear stains on the parchment... yet also small, dried droplets of blood. As if, the writer was harming themself.-\nEntry five\n~~~~~~~\nI can't keep this up... three days have passed since I've began forcing myself to stay awake... but it's not working... I've been dozing off and having the nightmares... even when teaching Alchemy lessons...\n\nI'm struggling to grip-\n-onto my sanity... my anger and tiredness are driving me insane... I've alreadt wrecked my bedroom at Alchemist Grove twice in a sudden burst of anger...\n\nI've even resorted to taking a knife and putting my anger on myself... my arms hurt but... at least-\n-it calms me down...\n\nI need help... badly...\n\n...but I'm afraid... that I may harm others around me....\n\nI don't want to involve them in this.... not when /HE/ is potentially still alive...\nEntry six\n~~~~~~~\nDaniel helped with the nightmares for one day. I'm thankful... I feel more relaxed and calmer... but my anger still lingers...\n\nI remember how Daniel changed the nightmare. A rapier appeared at my feet and I managed to break free of the-\n-chains that held me down, while Aetos had his fun. From there, I took the rapier and forced it right through his throat...\n\n...heedless to say, it was strangely satisfying...\n\nEven though it was a dream, he taught me something:\nDon't be afraid of the past, face it head on with the flames of courage and the future burning in your heart.\n\nI remember the last thing Elvira (my younger self) said to Aetos in this dream.\n\n'This fire burns on.'\nEntry seven\n~~~~~~~~~\nRamza gave me a special feather today. A Cloud Feather. According to him, whoever wears it remains calm... and it works!\n\nI feel less anger than normal and I can feel myself back in control!\nAlthough the nightmares are lingering... I'm still fighting on!\n\nAfter all,\nThis fire burns on!\n\n\n\n....I think that became my new and favourite catchphrase... heh\nEntry eight\n~~~~~~~~\n*Instead of an entry written by Elvi, there seems to be a note attached to the page*\n\nIt's been years, Terryal, but here's some words for you...\n...you cannot escape the ghosts of your past... they live inside you! And I will be -\n- coming back... for revenge and for a little fun....\nR.A\n\n*The note seems crumbled with many tear stains on them. The handwriting on the note is not Elvi's. It's bold and seems to have been written in a mad lust to harm*", ""),
        StaticBook("Niut", "Zaniil Tinuvriel", "Niut\nBy Zaniil Tinuvriel\nIn all the world the self same of any race are considered rare: more so for those as infertile as we.\nPerhaps we can delve further into this most interesting of facts. I should like to give rise to deep thought in this book, to ponderings regarding the\noddity of twins among our kin.\n\nJust as hair of thilln is considered most pure, perhaps two can duplicates of our species be seen in much the same light?\nThese obvious and unusual traits lead to much speculation.\nCould it be that only Mali’aheral of the most pure lineage can be blessed with such striking aspects? Let us consider what is one of the most important of times for our kind:\nthe birth of a Mali’aheral.\nGenesis within the cihi is without doubt, a momentous event. One would suggest that the spawning of two Mali’aheral on one occasion reveals to us the workings of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. Progress through strict breeding of\nonly the most pure of kin, resulting in health of procreation.\nI shall leave it to other Mali’aheral to think on this subject.\nThose that wish to debate with the author can do so by locating him at his home: linvallei’kulin.\n           ---------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Nobility Vol 1", "Farley III Stafyr", "On the Nature of\n      Nobility in an\n     Ignoble World\n\n        Written by\n Archduke Edward\n         Winter II\n\n          Edited by\nArchbishop Castus\nNobility is by nature an honor granted to the meritocratic few. Those with much to offer are given the land by which to realize their loyalty to the Crown, and the status to recognize them among the glorious peer group that is the nobility.\nThis is the basis upon which nobility is created.\n\nThere have been inglorious moments, when those thought to be honorable and the great showed themselves as lustful and slothful. This is not the nature of nobility.\nNobility is to be a pure state, by which the great of the country serve those who need serving. The nobles are not but lords above the inferior, but have an innate feudalistic duty to protect and further the interests of their vassals, noble and ignoble.\nThe true noble of Oren is to be virtuous, honorable, racially pure, devout to the Church, and loyal to his liege and crown. The true noble aims to amass prestige, not power. To make a name for one's noble house as a truly noble one is to glorify one's\nancestors and arrange a future for one's progeny. The honorable lord or lady, or those of their kin, should endeavour to embody the following tenets of nobility:\n\n•Proper etiquette in the home and in the public eye.\n•Serving promptly and amply the just needs of their liege and Crown.\n\n•Acting always in a manner befitting of one's noble status.\n\n•Just and kindly treatment of one's vassals, noble or ignoble.\n•Just and kindly treatment of all which one meets, noble or ignoble.\n\n•Diplomatic attitude towards one's peers and neighbours, friend and foe alike.\n•Knowledge of happenings within the kingdom, present and past.\n\n•Devout and worshipful observance of the Creator and his Church.\n•Honesty and oath-worthiness in all instances.\n\n•Good Management of one's estate and demesne, physical and moral.\n\n•A hunger for power, but instead for honor.\nTo make a name for one's noble house as a dwelling of sin is to dishonor one's family. To besmirch one's family name is a personal dishonor second to none in a noble's life. The honorable lord or lady, or the kin of those, should endeavour to avoid\nthe following:\n\n•Wasteful consumption or gluttony which drains the coffers.\n\n•Speech or action unbefitting of a noble in the public eye.\n•Sodomy or scandal which paints a stain upon one's name.\n\n•Mistreatment of one's vassals, noble or ignoble.\n\n•Lust for power, which causes discord and shows one unfavourably.\n•Maligning of others, noble or ignoble, without just cause.\n\n•Failure to amply serve the just needs one's liege and Crown.\n\n•Irreverence to the Church which marks one as heretical.\n•Mismanagement of one's own demesne which proves ineptitude.\n\n•Breaking of one's oaths which marks one as dishonest.\nThe following of this counsel will render one an honorable and noble lord or lady befitting of his title or his family's status. The observing of this document is sure to generate great prestige for one's house as a family deserving of its\nstatus, titles, and holdings, and similar counsel should be given to those children born to a noble house. To rid Oren of sinful and improper nobles, there must be an effort to create virtuous and honorable nobles.\nThis must be an effort not by the state to enforce honor among nobles, but by nobles to encourage honor among one's kin and peers.\n\nDeus Vult\n\n-Archduke Edward Winter II", ""),
        StaticBook("Nobility.", "Napoleon Fournier d'Avenese", "NOBLE CUSTOMS AND A GREATER STATE\n_____________________________By Napoleon Fournier d'Avenese\n_____________________________Squire To His Lordship of Aldersburg\n_____________________________Hello, sires, of this nation. Clergy, gentry, nobility, and all\nothers interested. This book is to explain the concept of Fuedalism, and lay out edicts for the perfect fuedal monarchy. It is also to explain to nobles and higher clergly how to behave and interact with the lower orders and their respective lieges.\nI sincerly hope that you enjoy this book, for I am probably to print it and produce many at the store of Jacob Chapel. If any would wish to see me about this piece, I am usually in the Avenese Estate near Pibblebonk or #I Waterfall Avenue, Aldersburg.\nI.The Concept of Fuedalism___________________                                This chapter shall be short for it should be known to all. \n\nThere is no commonly accepted modern definition of feudalism, at least among scholars.\nIt is commonly, and simply\ndefined, as the nobility, in exchange for protection, swear fealty and provide labour and military power in exchange for counties and duchies. In some fuedalistic socities, kings and emperors were little more than grand dukes, with the meeting, the king\nand the nobles together having the power. However, fuedalism does seem to be on the decline, due to the absoulitist nature of the imperial monarchy. In fuedal society, the heirarchy could be described as:\nEmperor\nKing\nArchduke\nPrince\nGrand Duke\nDuke\nCount\nLord Mayor\nMayor\nGentry\nSmall Landowners\nFree Subjects\nPeasants\nII.Edicts of Nobility.\n\nI.He must be gregaroius and socially competant, and speak in a noble and \"posh\" manner (as some blackguards would call it)\n\nII.He must know the code of chivalry, save for the paragraph which says he must serve the welfare of all.\nHe is free to do as he wishes with his peasants and other subjects, mistreating them is discouraged but it is not an edict to not do so.\n\nIII.He must distrivute his land amoung the gentry and other landowners and delegate tasks to his courtiers.\nIV.He must mantain a full court, and hear the advice of his courtiers, for they are gentlemen and women, and their word should be respected. \n\nV.A nobleman must seek the consel of his liege before making a major decision, including marriages. However, if\na monarch would abuse their power, it is both their right and duty to fight against the tyranny and give more power to the nobility. Just as one delegates tasks and wealth to courtiers, a king must do so with his nobles. The monarch and his nobles must be\nin balance.\n\nVI.A noble must obey the head of house except in exceptional circumstances. \n\nVII.A noble must be an advocate for the fuedal system in every aspect, organizing his army in this way.\nVIII.He must not assosciate with peasantry or other men of the lower order.\n\nIX.The head of house should not occupy himself with martial prowess or entrance into the clergly-this is the duty of the younger sons.\n\nX.He must instead focous on his\nadministrative skills.\n\nXI.He must seek to be pious and faithful, for a noble should get to the fifth heaven at least.\n\nXII.As well as this, he must be able to attend mass and read the Holy Scriptures regularly, and teach it to his subjects, inspiring his\nlevies with such things.\n\nIII.Principles of A Stable State________________________\nI have read many books which stress the importance of absoloute monarchy. Of despots, and absoloute power. However, I think this not be true. I think it prudent that a\ntable of nobles, all the lords of the realm, decide together, with the ruler holding meeting regularly with noblemen. The reason absoloute monarhcy is bad is because it is brilliant if given to an able leader, an able emperor. But, if it falls under the\ncontrol of a usurper, his nobles are powerless and even then, if he is a mere bad monarch, and no usurper, the effect is much the same. The tyrant will abuse his power and inspire not with his wisdom but with his power and intimidation, many gallant\nnoblemen will be imprisoned.\n\nFurthermore, a noble should have a similar system with his gentry. He must seek their consel before making a move, and must build a good relationship with his gentry, who will then indeed serve their lieges gratefully and\nproesperity will come from the estates and martial prowess from the sons and brothers of these landed gentry. \n\nSuch a relationship should also be given to a noble's wife, who may be given administrative and diplomatic tasks. Of course, according to the\ncode of chivalry, we should not risk the lives of the ladies. \n\nHonour is an important aspect, and a duke or above should be able to call the crown out on matters of honour. Whilst not going so far as dueling, as a royal's death would cause instability,\nnoble must be a paragon of honour and hope, and must make sure his liege is. And vice versa. One should improve the other, with the monarch seeking the consel of the nobles and the nobles seeking the guidance and loyalty to their liege.\n\nIn order to keep\nfuedal order and keep the loyalty of the subjects, absoloute monarchy must stop. \n\nNo one but dukes and above should swear direct alligience to the emperor. The dukes and above must, with the counts swearing to them, the minor nobles doing to them, the\ngentry, the peasants etc. This also, suprisingly, helps the monarch, for he has no unworthy subjects unneedily wasting his time. An emperor must be in a high, distant place, the dukes closer, the counts closer and all the way down to the small landowners,\ndirectly taking responsability for serfs. This is the ideal fuedal government, the one which embodies fuedalism the most, and the greatest enforcement of fuedalism. \n\nBut you may ask, why would the monarch ever agree to this? Well, that is a simple\nquestion, sire, and for that, I have the answer.\n\nIn return for the greater power, the nobles must give a greater amount of troops, mostly levies, to the cause. If we focous on conscripting the levies in times of war, and follow this system in which\nvassals must provide more, perhaps we can double the size of our forces. \n\nI have also written a book documenting my principles on the organization of the army. \n\nIt is to be printed soon. If you enjoy this, please read that.\nAnd with that, sires, I bid you aideu.\n\n\n\n__________________________________________________________[!]A sketch of a miltiaman in a gambeson and with spear and shield is seen here[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Norsenth'onn ...", "oppay", "*The title is partially cover with blood.\nAt Norsenth'onn the gate are all time open to welcome the visitor in the city, but some day it should have be close. A armor creature come into the manor where Ac'Aelu and Titania were speaking.\nWithout advise the creature get on the platform and try to break the throne. For the safety of the other city member, they close the manor gate to trap the monster inside. They slipped away into a back room to grab her weapon and call the Silan'Sul guard.\nThe Sil'Taynei, Gathain Telvhanim, was the first to response. When he reach the gate the princess open the gate for let him enter and side with them agains the armor thing.\n\n*Blood cover the rest of the text.", ""),
        StaticBook("Northern Cries", "Ragnar Ulfsson", "Northern Wrath\n----------------\"Up onto the overturned keel,\nClamber with a heart of steel,\nCold is the ocean's spray,\nAnd your death is on it's way,\nWith maidens you have had your way,\nEach must die some day!!\"\nShieldwall Speach\n----------------\"Whether we live or die today is already in the hands of the Gods,\nFear not, Fight well and if you fall surely Sáventón will take you to his halls.\"\nLifeblood\n----------------\"Drink, for the wind blows cold and \nDrink for The Wolf runs free. \nDrink to the ships with the sails like wings and \nDrink to the storm-tossed seas.\nDrink to the lasting nights \nand those who warm our beds. \nDrink to the mead that warms our hearts \nand the cold that clears our head.\n\nDrink to the truth of steel \nand blood that falls like rain.\nDrink to Adanos' Halls\nand to our kinsmen slain.\n\nDrink to the Glory-field \nwhere a man embraces death, and \nthank the gods that we live at all \nwith our joyous dying breath!\"", ""),
