        StaticBook("Orichalcum", "Rosso", "__Orichalcum__\n\nNienna’s Foreword: I found this little gem off of a dead spy named Devin Ryder. Yes, he was a bard and a spy, and he had quite a few things in-between. I’m pretty sure he stole this book. Actually, I’m sure of it.\nOrichalcum is a precious metal that is made out of white gold and silver. It can hold powerful and magical energies and is a great material for Magical items such as staves, swords, and magical Tiaras.\nIt is used by mages to store spells so that they can release those at the right moment. When using Orichalcum, be aware of its powerful magical properties. Don’t mess around with it - it can become dangerous at the wrong moments.\n==How to make==\n\n==Orichalcum==\n\n1- Melt the white gold and silver.\n\n2- Let flow energies of white magic into the metal while forcing it together.\n3-Make one metal bar of the combined metals\n\n4- Bend the bar to the shape of the power-rune\n\n5- Power the rune\n\n6- Reshape the rune to the symbol of resistance\n-repeat step 5-\n\n7- Reshape the rune to the symbol of capacity\n\n-repeat step 5-\n\n8- Now create the object you want to make\n9-Bury your Orichalcum at a place where it can absorb energies of nature, such as a forest or grove\n\n10- After 5 days your  metal is ready and you can recover it.\nThe process is complete now, but don’t expect it to go perfectly smooth the first time. This is a process that needs experience.\n\n-Contact Aurea in Haelun’or if you have questions-\nOrichalcum\n\nWritten by Nienna\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Orichalcum", "Thereon Ireheart", "Notice: These books are rushed copies of tomes in the Library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. The following is in no way a complete nor perfect copy of said book.\nOrichalcum\n\nOrichalcum is a precious metal that is made out of white gold and silver. It can hold powerful and magical energies and is a great material for Magical items such as Staves, Swords, and Magical Tiaras\nIt is used by mages to store spells st that they can release thoes at the right moment. When using Orichalcum, be aware of its powerful magical properties. Don't mess around with it - it can become very dangerous at the wrong moments.\n==How to make==\n\nMelt the white gold and sliver.\n\nEnergies of white magic into the metal while forcing it together.\n\nMake one metal bar of combinded metals bend the bar to the shape of the power-rune\nPower the rune\n\nof resistance\n\nRepeat\n\nSymbol of capacity\n\nNow create the object you want to make \n\nBury your Orichalcum at a place where it can absorb energies\nof nature, such as a forest of grove\n\nAfter 5 days your metal is ready and you can recover it.\n\nThe process is complete now but don't expect it to go perfectly smooth the first time. This is a procell that needs experience.", ""),
        StaticBook("Origins of Magic", "Valmuel Elibar'acal", "In a normal perspective, energy is taken from the void and projected into anything the caster may like. Take it be a Fireball or a wall of solid ice! Of course, there are many ways one could direct this energy from the void. However, we will be delving on\nhow exactly it works! Now, to begin, we must remember that all magic is of void origin, and it all must return to the void. \n\nThere are a few exceptions to this rule, such as the Druids, of which they're magic leaves\na lasting effect\non the world. This can be done by using the energy granted by such forces to move the objects appropiate to the magic they are using. This would pertain to nature, obviously. So it is not the magic that stays in the world, but rather the object\ninfluenced by the magic. With this being said, after a spell is cast and the connection to the spell is lost, it will return to the void. This is a quick and natural practice, however those who have trained to utilize this process can be\nknown as users of Fi\nhiiran'tanya. The entire idea of this, is that one would open up an immediate \"portal\" of which the mana returns instantly, to the caster's will or not. Only mana can pass through this portal.\nThe entire explanation of this shall be\ncovered shortly. THe reason I am bringing this up is because I wish to explain a large concept, and perhaps, truth. All magic comes from the void, even Deity/Source magic. The reason this is, is because we as mortals have difficulty drawing from the void.\nAlthough as powerful as we may conceive ourselves to be, our access over the void is somewhat limited. That is why some turn to Deities/Source Users, who have much more power.\n\nPower brings ability. These have the ability to draw upon\nthe void in ways we cannot imagine. That is where holy magic, and perhaps dark magic, may originate. In a basic sense, it is casted in a sense to \"smite\" the mana, to return it to the void swiftly.\n\nOne could argue that is exactly the conflict\nof which these users face. Whether it is holy or dark is not the question, but perhaps different ways of expelling the magic to the void? \n\nAs I was saying, Deities/Source Users can cast in ways we cannot do. It brings in possibilities\nof Druid Magic, Holy Magic, Dark Magic, Kha Magic, and other forms. However, all of it is drawn from the void. With the immense power of these beings, one could mold and shape the mana in different ways we could never do.\n\nIn recent events,\nwe have witnessed some interesting things happen to the progression of magic. The Dark Lord Setherien, the Leader of the Scourge, fuels his servants with his power. Now, this may seem normal as other Aenguls or Daemons might do. However, there is one key\npoint. Setherien is mortal! Atleast, he is a physical form. The potential knowledge from this is unlimited. If one could give another magic, if powerful enough, in the physical plane, why can't others do it?\n\nThis is a pure concept, and not to be taken\nentirely serious just yet. However, the possibilities are endless, if there is no restriction in the physical plane. Could one possibly amass enough power to give another his/her abilties? Again, I do not know the answer to this. It is all speculation.\nIn conclusion to this small essay, magic in of itself is highly peculiar, and much of it we still do not know about. However, I hope you have had a stronger grasp of it's origins and capabilities, even though I personally do not recommend it.\n- Valmuel Elibar'acal", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Resolve", "Sentis", "In a time of perpetual danger, we will stand strong. Our resolve as brothers, sisters, and warriors will never waver. By our blades and by our blood, we will stand fast against any and all who oppose us. The Edict will stand, of that there is no doubt;\nall that matters is who will stand with us. Night may fall but we will rise, to protect and to destroy. Such is our way and so it will be. The fires of our courage will keep even the coldest winds at bay, our loyalty to one another staying our feet.\nLet them come, Vallah, Mali, Bortu, Uruk, Kha, it matters not; we will stand.", ""),
        StaticBook("P. Revolution", "daelaris", "A History of the Phoenix Revolution based on several personal accounts by witnesses.\n\nAt the time, the stability of Oren was considered dubious at best. With the death of King Pampo Perea, his seneschal, -\n- Edmund Sheffield took to the throne. His rule rule was highly opposed by many, which only aided to feed the flames that let to the revolution. The basis of this uprising began in the minds of two men, Eze'kiel Tarus and Zibaen Vivyaen.\nThroughout the reign of Edmund, they only seemed to gain power and support as Undead attacks became more frequent, and in the end, even the king succumbed. Taken by corruption, he killed his wife and dissapeared leaving his son, Enor, to take the throne.\nEnor's reign was marred with troubles, and the fall of Al'kHazar in 1338 served only to sent the realm into a downward spiral of chaos. Enor was kidnapped and held in the Nether for nearly a year whilst the diaspora of-\n- humanity attempted to pick themselves back up and start anew.  When Enor returned, many thought him to be corrupted as his father, and so the Phoenix Revolution was born.\nThe uprising managed to quickly attract hundreds of supporters, many of which were high-ranking officials in the Kingdom of Oren. Propaganda and occassional skirmishes marked the height of the revolution. Some weeks later, -\n- King Enor caught wind of the rebellion and abdicated to Gaius Marius, Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order.\nWhat was decided there would shape the fate of Oren, The Teutons and Marius were to be granted the northern lands of Hanseti, from which he would rule in Konigsberg, and Eze'kiel granted Galahar and the lands surrounding it.\nThe Kingdoms of Hanseti and Renatus were born, and so the great human nation was split for the first time in it's history.\nThe aftermath of this travesty was the gradual fall of what remained of civilization in Aegis as the undead continued to flood south. Even in Asulon, the nations of Hanseti and Renatus remained on uncertain grounds, -\nviewing eachother with great distrust and hatred. Only during the time of Godfrey I would the two kingdoms ever be united once again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Page 1", "Boris of Valwyk", "Dear diary,\nThe ugly man is a killer. He comes and murders people in Felsen by shooting them. WHAT IS WRONG WITH THE GUARDS?!", ""),
        StaticBook("Page 2", "Boris of Valwyk", "The ugly man has an mental problem. His behavior is extremely unpredictable. It's official:Nobody likes this horribly roleplayer-uh I mean uh, psychopathic weird person.", ""),
        StaticBook("Page 3", "Boris of Valwyk", "Someone... Forgot her name, but she was the wife of a duke. She came over and everyone talked to her. Of course the insane man was there, and that gave Valwyk the worst reputation ever.", ""),
        StaticBook("Page 4", "Boris of Valwyk", "So when we all gathered around to chat, the ugly man with a extreme case of mental illness comes by. I recorded some of his dialogue.", ""),
        StaticBook("Page 5", "Boris of Valwyk", "Some dialogue that went on with the wife of the duke was- \"HAVE SOME CARROTS M'LADY\" \"Does he uh.. have a mental illness, I supose?\" Then the ugly man put a sign and stood behind it. The sign said A MAN WITH CARROTS LIVES HERE", ""),
        StaticBook("Page 6", "Boris of Valwyk", "Maybe I should stop ripping off pages from the book,,", ""),
        StaticBook("Pages.", "Beltran D'avre", "\"Young pages, Black and new.\n\nFolded neatly into a pamphlet. \n\nStaples along a life line, a cover fresh from the print.\n\nLucky to have been torn at first light, creamy white .\n\nBinding not yet dried.\n\"Pencil's mark not yet touched.\n\nThe remains of what once, was priveleged but not yet knowing.\n\nA small braunh upon a tree.\nStanding tall amongst bark thick with green.\"\n\"Endings, dipped in poison.\n\nPurple veins blemishing gnarled foliage.\n\nThe pool of death, drowning cess but not yet.\n\nThoughts of fire, futility of body.\n\nOld, thoughts grows from within.\n\"Parchment damp with age, wrinkled skin painted.\n\nWith designs, experienced and colourful.\n\nBut once was, now aging.\n\nAs books gaze into the fire, endlessly burning. \n\nDespair dances with the shadows.\n\"Perhaps it was better, to have faced the flames blank.", ""),
        StaticBook("Paragon Hiebe", "Aengoth", "Hiebe, the Father of Mages. Throughout dwarven history many key figures amongst our kin have been proclaimed our fabled Paragons, those who stand above the rest and worked to create the very foundations of our society today. While the young may only hear\nof them they do not share the same wisdom that us elder dwarves still retain from our first hand experience. We found our best of the beet and we found them to be fitting of the title Paragon. When you think of the core group of dwarves who shaped our\nsociety you think of Valen the Wordsmith, Omithiel the Builder, Kjell Ireheart the Dragon Slayer. These threee were without a doubt the foundation of our society. Yet one amongst them has been left out. I, Aengoth Grandaxe, do now hereby proclaim that\nHiebe Irongut has been forgotten by the Archbishops and High Prophets of the past. Kjell had his warriors. Omithiel had his builders. Valen had his writers. Hiebe had his mages. Hiebe has been responsible for either the first hand or second hand teaching\nof nearly all the dwarven mages we have come to know. WHile many dwarves may be skeptics concerning magic and distrust its users we can not steal this credit from Hiebe Irongut. He was one of the four pillars of our society and we must rightfully\nrecognize his actions as that of the work of Ogradhad whom used Hiebe to spread the knowledge of magic to our people. Hiebe Irongut has earned his position as the fourth pillar and has earned the title \"Paragon Hiebe Irongut, the Father of Mages\".\nWritten by Aengoth Grandaxe", ""),
        StaticBook("Paragon Lefor", "Daniel Nodal", "Lefor was born into a normal dwarven family. His father worked in the mines, His mother at home. Lefor was raised in the mines as he helped his father there from a young age. When he came of age Lefor told his father he wanted to be more than just a miner\nHe wanted to serve his king by joining the army. Lefor’s father was stubborn but eventually let Lefor join a training camp, sending him off with the family armor and axe. Lefor had a hard time at the camp, he was smaller than many of the others but he\nstrived to be the best, and so he did after much hard work he finished training and was made sergeant of the battalion.\nBefore the beginning of the great War between the Orcs and Dwarves, tensions were high and there were many skirmishes between both race\nThe Orcs were bloodthirsty and hungry for land and the Dwarves had expanded very close to the orcish border. Neither the Warlords of the Orcs or the High Council of the Dwarves could maintain peace and so the war began. In the early stages of the war,\ndwarven losses were high and they slowly retreated. It was at the small village of Kas-Grit that Lefor and his men were stationed to protect the villages whilst they gathered their items in preparation to seek refuse in the Capital. On the final day\nbefore they were to head to the capital a great horde of orcs attacked, the villagers fled in panic and Lefor and his men fought their best to contain the great horde but the orcs were too many and Lefor gave orders to retreat and protect the villagers.\nLefor however did not leave, he told his men that he was going to hold back the orcs as long as he was able. The orcs attacked again and again but Lefor kept them at bay and so he slew many orcs fighting them in the narrow alley ways of the village.\nHowever Lefor finally tired and was cut down by the orcs and his head put upon a spike.\nThat day Lefor saved many dwarves and because of his bravery the king and council made him a Paragon. To be worshipped along with the stones of the earth. Lefor’s\nfamily were made nobles and his bloodline still survives in many dwarves. Lefor is seen as the incarnation of bravery, sacrifice and warrior-hood.\nEven today many warriors pray to Lefor before battle. So is the story of Paragon Lefor.\nParagon Lefor\n\nWritten in Aegis\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVearHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Paragon Lefor", "Leyu", "Paragon Lefor\nLefor was born into a normal dwarven family. His Father worked in the mines, His mother at home. Lefor Was raised in the mines as he helped his father there from a young age. When he came of age Lefor told his father he wanted\nto be more than a miner ,he wanted to server his king by joining the army. Lefor's father was stubborn but eventually let Lefor join a training camp, sending him off with the family armor and axe. Lefor had a hard time at the camp, he was smaller than\nmany of the others but he strived to be the best, and so he did after much hard work he finished training and was made sergeant of the new battalion. :: Before the beginning of the Great War between the Orcs and Dwarves tensions where high and\nthere where many skirmishes between both races. The Orcs where bloodthirsty and hungry for land and the Dwarves had expanded very close to the orcish border. Neither the Warlords of the Orcs or the High council of the Dwarves could maintain peace\nand so the war began. In the early stages of the war dwarven losses where high and they slowly retreated. It was at the small village of Kas-Grit that Lefor and his men were stationed to protect the villages whilst they gathered their items in\npreparation to seek refuge in the Capital. On the final day before they where to head to the capital a great horde of orcs attacked, the villages fled in panic and Lefor and his men fought their best to contain the great horde but the orcs where to many\nand lefor gave orders to retreat and protect the villagers. Lefor however did not leave he told his men that he was going to hold back the orcs as long as he was able. The orcs attacked again and again but Lefor kept them at bay and so he slew many\norcs fighting them in the narrow alley ways of the village. However Lefor finally tired and was cut down by the orcs and his head put apon a spike. :: That day Lefor saved many dwarves and because of his bravery the king and council made him a\nparagon. To be worshipped along with the stones of the earth. Lefor's family were made nobles and his bloodline still survives in many dwarves. Lefor is seen as the incartation of bravery, sacrafice and warrior-hood . :: Even today many\nwarriors pray to Lefor before battle . So is the story of Paragon Lefor.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Parents and Orcs", "Heruza", "Orcs have a nasty habit of ruthlessly murdering parents. This fact is known, along with how they ruthlessly murder anything except their own kin. Kids whos parents are killed by orcs grow up on the streets to become assassins.", ""),
        StaticBook("Passport", "Riondil Seni", "To Whom This May Concern,\n\nLori Oathcast has permission from the Tilruir'mali to stay and visit The Silver State.\n\nSigned,\nRiondil Seni", ""),
        StaticBook("Pastries Anthos", "Jistuma", "________________\n~                        ~\n\nPastries of Anthos\n\n\n~----------------~\nIn the mind of a child, there will always be a love for the sweet taste of cake. I have traveled the lands of Anthos after my love for pastries grew with my mother’s skill, and family’s bakery. Watching the children laugh and smile whenever they came and\nI served them a slice of cake, I decided that bakery would as well be my way of life. With the destruction of my home and bakery in Asulon, I had decided that I would search and try new recipes with the ingredients of all over the realm. I have collected\nsome to this recipe book, for others to bring a smile to other children.\nCheesecake of Salvus\nBefore the fall of Salvus I was able to try out their ingredients, and create a well rounded cheesecake. Sugar and wheat Dawn’s bakery, the eggs fresh from the farms, and the cheese came from a kind shepherd.\nIngredients:\n\n-Two hand size goat cheeses\n-A glass full of goat milk cream\n-Three mugs of flour\n-Two soup spoon of refined sugar.\n-One fresh egg\nRemember to start heating the oven before you start mixing the ingredients. The Cheese and the cream first have to be added to the flour and mixed until fully clear. I advise that you slowly add the milk as the cheese is mixed with the flour. The sugar\nand eggs come after, or they would not mix very well. Mix well with the rest and Grease and flour a pan. The oven should be hot by now, so pour the mix inside the pan, and then the pan inside the oven. When you start smelling a sweet cheese aroma,\nthe cheesecake, and serve.\nHoney cookies\nI was quite amazed that the elves of Luminaire did not use sugar in their food, curious as that may be, their pastries were still quite sweet. The use of honey was their secret, very pleasant when used in cookies.\nIngredients:\n\n-One cup of Redbee honey\n-One duck egg\n-A bit of cinnamon\n-Two cups of forest wheat flour\n\nMakes 16 cookies.\nMore than difficult to make, the ingredients are quite hard to find, if you are not an elf yourself. Simply preheat the oven, and mix everything up. It will appear very hard, it is suppose to. With a spoon place on a mix in a pan, and place in the oven.\nKrill cake\nThe dwarves sure have some interesting tastes, the Krill cake being one of the most unique pastries I found. A pastry made of ingredients of the sea and eaten with a side mug of Ale.\nIngredients:\n\n-Two mugs of Ale\n-A mug of Beer\n-Two mugs Whale Blubber\n-Krill, which is a paste of many small crustaceans\nThis recipe is quite hard to make. You will have to first preheat oil in a cauldron as you prepare the mix. In a bowl, mix half of the Krill, a mug and a half of the Whale Blubber, and the mug of Beer. Mix until even, it will appear to be a bit slimy. Mix\nthe rest of the Krill and Whale Blubber in another bowl, it will be able to hold its form. Place the slimy mix inside the other mix and close it. After making many of them, place inside a fishing net and deep fry in the hot oil. Let cool before you grab\na mug of Ale and drink another as you eat the Krill cakes.\nPine needle crackers\nEven those recipes that appear quite weird to ever be taught about, I have found. In the south snow mountains of the Urguan kingdom, I discovered the use of pine needles and seaweed in a result of hard crackers.\nIngredients:\n\n-A bowl of newborn pine needles\n-Five strips of dried seaweed\n-Two sweet potatoes\n-One cave cow mushroom\n-Two Owl eggs\nWithout any wheat in those cold lands, the residents of VaerHaven came up with using potatoes to create their dough. After removing the skin of the potato, cut it as small as you can before you add the egg. Let a few small mushrooms that were taken from\nthe back of cave cows, and pour everything into a frying pan. Mix everything up, and let it cook for a moment. When the red bits of the mushroom start turning brown, take the frying pan from the fire and let cool over snow. Not many pine needles are\nneeded, only a few newborns. Cut them very small as well and add to the dough. Mix everything up and place them seaweed around the dough. They need a few hours freezing outside, but to my surprise it came up quite sweet.\nCactus on a stick\nI would feel bad if I did not add anything about the orchish culture. They do not cook a lot, and it was quite hard to find this recipe, but it was the only one I found.\nIngredients:\n\n-Long needle cactus\n-A stick\nNot a hard recipe, just find and cut a long needle cactus, they are the sweetest of them. You remove the needles and cut the cactus into bits, and stick them in a stick. Then you place over fire and let cook.\nCarrot bun\nThe Halflings are exceptional farmers, and what I enjoyed the most about them was the carrots, they were quite delicious. I created a simple recipe while using it.\nIngredients:\n\n-Three hand sized carrots\n-A glass of milk\n-A few strips of sugarcanes\n-Two fresh chicken eggs\nPreheat the oven with Birch coal, which will give a mild aroma of the tree to the buns, but don’t let it heat too much. Skin and chop the carrots into a bowl, and add the milk. Crush some of the sugarcane juice as you stir, the eggs coming at the end.\nWith a soup spoon, take the dough and place over the leftover sugarcanes, which are now juiceless. Place everything in a long plate and place in the oven.\nCrab pie\nFor last, I present the Kha treats, made of the crabs caught in the waters around their island, and featuring cocoa from their jungle.\nIngredients:\n\n-Long Pincer crab\n-Five big Cocoa beans\n-Two mugs of Jungle wheat flour\n-Three parrot’s eggs\n-Blue silk seaweed\nA pie fully done with jungle ingredients, for a seafood pie, it is quite lovely. Pre-heating the oven is always a necessity. The Crab and the Blue silk seaweed are found at the shores of the island, the crab having a very long pincer, and the seaweed a\ndeep blue, with the texture like silk. The crab is hard to prepare, the shell needing removing so that the soggy meat can be taken. Cut to bits and mixed with the flour from the wheat that naturally grows in jungles. The eggs have to be taken from\nparrot’s nests, and they are what is added next. Then mix, it will be very hard. The seaweed needs to be made into the form of the pie, in the oven it will become crusty, so after the form is done, place the dough in it. While the pie is in the oven, pick\nup the Cocoa beans and start making it into powder. As soon as you take out the pie, place the cocoa powder over it, the smell will be wonderful.\nI hope that many smiles and giggles come while enjoying my recipes.\n\n          Mrs Ole\nPastries of Anthos\n\nWritten by Mrs. Ole\nCoppied by Rosso\nCloud Temple of Anthos", ""),
        StaticBook("Paths", "Gwendolyn Powell", "One step after another\nI found myself walking a path, a path laden with roots\nA path breathing and living beneath my foot\nSilant at my touch\n\nAs I wadnered, on and on\nI took a turn\nA turn down a darker, road, and one hidden from the sun\nA path dusty, dry, and lifeless\n\nThis path I waled for many a year\nLost admist a sea of dark\nLost, on a path that turned slowly upwards, and soon became too difficult to walk\nAnd there I sat, pondering my loneliness\nOut of the corner of my eye, I glimpsed the sun\nBrilliant, bountiful and beautiful\n\nI stood, abd began to trudge slowly towards the light\nHearing birdsong, hearing the rustle and movements of leaves\nFeeling warmer and warmer as I went\nThe loneliness seeping from my bones\n\nThe dark shrank away in the light\nThis new path, was one brimming with life\nMuch like the first\nBut now, I began to hear something\nA quiet breathe, tiny beneath the sounds of chirping\nThe hoof beat of a running dear, and the great sway of an oak tree\nSo I listened more closely\nImmersing myself in the slow and steady beat\nOf the true world\nThe growing, giving, loving world\nThat I had once ignored\nAnd had now, finally\n\nFound a place in my heart\nA place, where it began to beat within me\nA place, that I hope to see flourish\nTo see flourish, like the flowers and astoundingly wonderful world around me", ""),
        StaticBook("Paycheck:Artemis", "Lorena Faeliel", "PAYCHECK\nROYALTIES FROM GUAGERS BOOK STORE, CALIPAHTE.\n\nFor the sum of:\nThree Mina.\n\nTo: Artemis\n\nSigned: Lorena Faeliel\n\nDate: 3 S/S 1521\nhttp://tinyurl.com/nn4hbt6", ""),
        StaticBook("Personal Records", "Artorius Thannius", "The Governance of Rivel\nThe city-state of Rivel has been described by foreigners as a “mageocracy.” Such a term is clearly tautological: it is an obvious fact to all citizens of Rivel that skill in the arcane is a requisite for the\nforesight required for governance: however could one control and lead a populace without the wisdom of the arcane and the insight into the thoughts and actions of the populace offered by mental magics and scrying? Therefore Rivel is organised\ninto a two-tier society: the enlightened citizens such as ourselves skilled in the arcane are led by the Circle of Governance and its leader, the Spellcrafter Archon. The Enlightened Caste of Spellcrafters can be identified by our\npointed ears. The round eared, magically blind and short-lived Lesser Caste of Labourers act as workers and servants. They own property and instead live in worker quarters in the homes of their Enlightened betters. Obviously we do\nnot allow them to take positions of authority and responsibility as their magical blindness means they would do a poor job indeed: better to not allow them to try. Those who display some magical skill are given directorial positions over the rest of\nthe Lesser Caste, but they do not live long enough to achieve the true arcane mastery required to join the ranks of the Enlightened.\nThe city also makes use of semi-intelligent pack animals known as orcs, which once broken can be\ntaught basic speech and simple tasks. They are incredibly useful as beasts of burden but despite the word of what are clearly rumours and the work of agitators are not capable of higher thought any more than cattle are.\n- Artorius Thannius, Exalted Spellcrafter Archon of Rivel", ""),
        StaticBook("Philosophorum", "Lanavia Zytiaear", "An Introduction to the\nPhilosophorum Society\n------------------------------\n\nThe information provided within these pages are to simply help you understand what the Society is and what exactly we stand for.\n\nIf you still have questions contanct\nSarrion (Toxzero), Elric (Jacey) or Lanavia (Creete).\n\n\nEnjoy~\n\n-\nLanavia\nWhat is the Society? \n\nThis has to be the most asked question we get here in the Society - at the same time it is the easiest to answer.\n\nThe Society is more a community than a guild.\nWe are a gathering of like-minded individuals that have a thirst for knowledge.\nIt is this thirst for knowledge that has pulled us all together and has led to the creation of the Society, and is the thing that still keeps us together.\nAre there any fees?\n\nNo. We have never charged new members any type of mina fee to join our ranks.\n\nThe only thing we ask is that if you stumble upon a book we might be interested in that you would donate it to the Society.\nWhat does it mean to be a member of the Society?\n\nThis one is also easy to answer. To be a member of the Society simply means you are a part of something more – you are trying to better yourself and the world around you.\nYou are not wasting the most precious thing you own: your mind.\n\nBeing a member of the Society means you are searching to answer the unknown and learn from others who have already started their personal quests to do just that.\nWhat’s with the jackets?\n\nThis is one thing we share with a lot of guilds or schools, we have a matching uniform of sorts. The navy colored jackets are a symbol of your ties to the Society – and thus your eagerness to learn and spread knowledge.\nA fact about the jackets that you need to know is that the colored trimmings do mean something. A student with gold trims on his jacket with a student of magic, whereas a student with a jacket that has a silver trim is a student of science.\nMany students study both science and magic – the jacket they decide to wear is up to them but should be trimmed with the colors associated with whichever of the two they focus more heavily on.\n\nThe best way to know what a student studies is to ask them.\nWhat is the purpose of the Society?\n\n\nThe Society’s purpose is simple. We are here to gather, document, and share knowledge – that is it.\nDo you need to be an Elf to be a member?\n\nNo. We do not care what race you are, so long as you are like-minded you are welcome here.\nThis is the basis of the Society put into the simplest terms I could. If you have any other questions about it feel free to ask any member you see – if they can’t answer your questions they can point you in the right direction. \n\nBe well~!", ""),
        StaticBook("Piano Tutorial", "Roth Jayamen", "((OOC))\n\nThe noteblocks layout on the floor (3x3 square) goes with numbers. The numbers match the piano in this way.\n\n7 8 9\n4 5 6\n1 2 3\nThe 2 through 9 in Real life notation (if you know this) Is C note through C note. or an octave. The Key is C major.\n\nAnother way to think about it is that 2 through 9 is like Do through Do in the phrase 'Do, Re, Mi, Fa, So, La, Ti, Do'.\nThe Number 1 of the noteblocks is the Note B. It is basically one white key below C.\n\nThe Piano is based in all white keys.\n\nSongs that I write in-game are based on the 1-9 layout. Just follow the song books numbers in order to play them.\nIf you have any questions, Ask me In-Game or through the forum. IGN: Sofetios", ""),
        StaticBook("Pigmen History", "Sunshine Druid Verden", "A Brief History of Pigmen: Aegis – Kalos\nBy Sunshine Druid Verden\nThe appearance of Zombie Pigmen was first documented during the Second Iblees Invasion, several hundred years ago. These unnatural monsters were used by the Fallen Daemon as powerful soldiers during his war of conquest against the mortal races of Aegis,\nwhere their group mentality and shear ferocity was crippling to the defenders. Unlike other lesser Undead, the Zombie Pigmen possessed an intellect far superior to any common Zombie or Skeleton. They would always be seen in possession of jagged, golden\nswords and very rarely were encountered alone.\n\nTheir speed was almost on par with that of the living, a trait that allowed few the luxury of escaping. After the invasion was ended and the Dark One had been sealed away for good, many strange things were\nobserved by the population of Aegis. While the mindless Zombies and Skeletons continued to attack anyone on sight, the Pigmen did not. They had become passive, almost completely indifferent to the world around them.\n\nInstead of mindlessly killing, they\nbegan to aimlessly roam the world, staring blindly at the things around them as if they weren’t truly there. After Aegis had crumbled and sank into the sea, many thought they would never see the creatures again. And, indeed, they didn’t. For a time. But,\nagain, the Pigmen emerged from the unknown, and they were furious. For many years the Pigmen were found roaming the darkest corners of Asulon and attached anyone foolish enough to get close. The reason for this is not clear, and many theories have arisen\nto explain. However none have been proven. Yet another strange event was observed on the island of Elysium.\n\nA large volcano near the temporary Elven settlement erupted and spewed lava over the Malinor farms; and the Pigmen rode it down the slope. They\nwere, thankfully, peaceful this time; but they appeared in numbers never seen before. Hundreds of them began to blindly wander from their lair, spilling over the border into the Orcish deserts. They were destroyed not by men, nor by beast, but by cacti.\nThe creatures tore themselves to shreds over the next few months as they walked through the cacti farms, and they would still if it wasn’t for the piles of their dead brethren impeding their movement.\n\nSince arriving in Anthos there has only been one\nreported case of Pigmen. This was a very small issue, where only three or four Pigmen would wander around a border wall in the Wilds. A logical fountain was placed at this site, and all has been quiet since then.\n\nIf the Pigmen are here on Anthos, they\nare hiding very well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pile of shit.", "Holden Vladov", "Yo journal, I met a girl that's 11. She is about my age. She is very pretty and nice. pce journal.\nhey journal. we hung out again because my stupid kha brought her when it was exactly her that i didnt wanna see. I ended up having a good time for the most part but i told her she was pretty and she didnt seem to recipricate my feelings.\nAbram ruined everything. First he steals her heart and then he toys with mine, the bastard.\nPretty much just gave her every hint of my feelings in the book and she still didnt understand, then Abram showed up to 'save the day' again.\nShe asked me if she was annoying It took me all my power to not tell her how i felt right then.\nI told her everything, How i think about her everyday, how i never want our adventures to end, how when i first saw her i couldnt even speak because she was so beautiful, how i want to hold her and never let go. And all she had to say by the end of it was\ndont be dramatic. My life has become everything I did not want it to be. \n\nEveryone is evil by nature and I cannot trust anyone, sometimes even family.\n\nThis is my last entry.\nGoodbye.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pine Trees", "Pine Druid Gi'Garun", "Pine Trees\n   By The Pine Druid\n\nWhen one be walking,\nBout thee's lands.\nOne may wander dunes of sand.\n\nOr maybe even caverns deep,\nAnd view the beauty found beneath.\nWhen one begins to feel cold,\nThey start to miss the sands of gold.\n\nBut when one thinks to open eye,\nThey see the beauty way up high.\nTrue beauty lies above you see,\nIt stands as such, a mighty tree.\n\nA towering canopy tall and fine,\nThe tree I speak of is the Pine.\nWhen time is right, and tree is sound,\nIt drops it's pinecones to the ground.\n\nThe needles that it grasps above,\nAre there not to be grabbed or shoved.\nBut rather be a tool to use,\nAnd not a weapon to abuse.\n\nThe tree I speak of is no quarry,\nSo harm it and you shall be sorry.\nSo when thou next goes near a Pine,\nBe sure to heed these words of mine.\n\nRespect the tree so tall and fine,\nAnd feel the kindness of the Pine.", ""),
