        StaticBook("Poem", "[Dedicant] Anthony Hearthal", "In the meadows of asulon\nThere are many plants and trees\nAnd most of the grass grows up, passed your knees\nIn the deepest sea of the world\na massive fish did wonder\nwhy men would dive so far down under\nWell the truth is simple they just wanted to plunder\n\nLike magic trees and humming bees the world also has many secrets, where it hides treasure, the beauty of nature and soulmates that one desires.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem Long Lived.", "Amras Yavelty", "Poem of the Long Lived\nBy Amras Yavelty\nPassing like water swiftly down the river\nWithout trace\nWithout shiver\nThe soil grows thin\nThe lights go dim\nMountains are born\nNew flowers adorn\nYet you must know\nLong ears hear them\nHear them at birth\nHear them at death\nHear all in sorrow\nHear all in joy\nHear them in pain\nTime is just a toy\nLet the human’s grief\nOrcs play in the sand\nDwarves get rich\nLet’s hear them be\nHear them at war\nHear them at peace\nHear them be young\nHear them get old\nLet them have beards\nLet them feel\nHow time passes by\nYet not for long ears", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem Of Death", "Virgo the Venalicius", "It does not matter wether your the happiest person... Or the saddest beggar.\n\nThe biggest giant or the most terrible creature. \n\nWe are all the same in the eyes of The Reaper.\n- Virgo", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry V1", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Poetry\n\n       Volume 1\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\nCourage\n\nIt is a thing you use\nWhen you can't go to the end,\nWhen all seems lost\nAnd you can't defend.\nYou use it as\nIt combines with your will,\nAll you need to do is\nLet it give its fill.\nThe choice is yours,\nGive in or go,\nThough in the end\nOnly you will know.\nSee with your spirit\nAnd not with fear,\nfor then you will know\nThat courage is here.\nThe Dreamer\n\nThe Dreamer,\nThe one who dares not be the same,\nFor in dreams mysteries unravel,\nAnd endless space you do travel,\nAs your dreams you try to tame.\nAs the Dreamer,\nDreams above the sky,\nAnd looks down below,\nTo the people that show,\nWho know not what lies that high.\nUnawakened, the Dreamer,\nIn a maze of thoughts,\nWandering the mists,\nWith endless twists,\nAs the path on minds paper he jots.\nThough be wary dreamer,\nAs thoughts tend to run away,\nOnly the ones you really need,\nAnd the ones you often feed,\nAre the ones that often stay.\nThe Lake\n\nI wander upon a path by a lake,\nWondering where it’s all gone.\nEvery day I used to come here,\nFrom the morning to the evening's yawn.\nEvery now and again I wonder,\nWhy the days have passed.\nAnd think very deeply,\nWhy they don't seem to last.\nDay by day, night by night,\nThe Lake becomes smaller still.\nThe thoughts of it become thinner,\nEven to my strongest will.\nIt has become ten times smaller and ten times shallower,\nEven thought it has not changed.\nTo other people it might be normal,\nbut to me it is considered strange.\nAn Uncommon Sight\n\nI go about my day,\nDoing the same things as before,\nThe same old road,\nFrom my humble abode,\nNot realizing it is a bore.\nI walk ever onward,\nKnowing all my tasks by heart,\nA straight narrow trail,\nWith nothing new to avail,\nAll I do is my part.\nThen one day as I'm going past,\nA park once again,\nI see a boy,\nwithout even a toy,\nwho couldn't be past ten.\nThe boy was doing something abnormal,\nsomething I hadn't seen before,\nHe was looking in the sky,\nNot even blinking an eye,\nthey didn't even seem sore.\nI wondered if there was a hawk,\nOr something in the sky,\nI didn't hear a thing,\nOnly the birds that always sing,\nSo I did wonder why.\nI looked over,\nto the boy sitting by,\nHe was being bullied by his peers,\nAnd was starting to go in tears,\nJust for looking in the sky.\nI was about to go over,\nTo try to help if I could,\nbut the parents went first,\nBefore I feared the worst,\nTo help as they should.\nI walked on my way home,\nWondering why what I saw came to pass,\nI had a thought why,\nso I looked to the sky,\nand saw it in it's great mass,\nAs I looked to the sky,\nI was transfixed,\nI hadn't done this in a while,\nAnd it did make me smile,\nAs past and current memories mixed.\nI saw the vast expanse,\nIn all its mystery,\nI watched the clouds in the sky,\nAs they changed shape and passed by,\nAs they had for all of history.\nSuddenly someone laughed to my left,\nEven thought it was mild,\nSomeone looking at me,\nLaughing at what I appeared to be,\nJust as the others had done to the child\nFriend\n          or\n          Enemy?\n\nEverywhere I am\nI hide from your sight,\nIf it's in the day,\nAnd especially at night.\nI am one of sleep's worst enemies,\nAnd one of fear's best friends,\nI grow ever more larger,\nAs your will begins to bend.\nIn the day I am more friendly,\nEspecially when its hot and I'm in sight,\nBut when it turns to night time,\nI'm sure to give you a fright.\nI am a mimic of sorts,\nI try to copy you while you walk,\nI even mimic other people,\nAlthough I cannot talk.\nEven when you go about the day,\nI skulk and kind of stalk,\nFear or fear not, I am always here,\nI am the shadow on which you walk.\nThe Cobbler\n            and\n         The Crow\n\nI was working in the night,\nAs I bent over a shoe,\nI was working very hard,\nto finish before the morning dew.\nI was just about finished,\nWhen what was this I hear?\nA tapping, slight tapping,\nAnd it seemed to be so near.\nI turned to the window,\nAnd what did I see?\nA crow tapping at my glass,\nStaring at me.\n\"Go away.\" I said,\nSternly as I did stand.\n\"Don't you know I have work to do?\"\nThough I know it didn't understand.\nBut the crow kept tapping at the glass,\nAnd I began to get mad,\nThis crow just would not stop,\nNot even a tad.\nI turned to my unfinished shoe,\nTo work as long as I could bear,\nBut then I noticed something missing,\nThat would stop me from completing the pair.\nThe golden lace that I needed,\nFor this order to be complete,\nI couldn't find it anywhere,\nAs the glass the crow did beat.\nI checked my table, checked my pockets,\nAnd then to my surprise,\nThere was a hole in one,\nThat was just the right size.\nI would never finish this shoe,\nBy the morning light,\nNow things were dire,\nand my situation was quite tight.\n\"I must have dropped it,\nOn the way back from the store!\"\nBut it was too far I thought,\nAs my confidence tore.\nBut then I realized \"What's this?\"\n\"Where was the tapping I couldn't bare?\"\nI looked to the window,\nAnd the crow wasn't there.\nI went to the window,\nAnd what was in its place?\nIt was simple and divine,\nThe golden lace.\nI opened the window,\nAnd took it with care,\nBecause of who gave this gift,\nI was certainly aware.\nI went to my table,\nAnd finished the shoe.\nBut then thought of the crow,\nIf I only knew!\nI then went to bed,\nWith not much I could say,\nI only did hope,\nThe crow would come back some day.\nImprint\n\nI stand in a forest,\nOne that I know quite well,\nWhere the trees are tall,\nAnd they never do fall,\nAt least that's what I like to tell.\nI came here,\nWhen I was a boy,\nUsually in the day,\nBut any time I would say,\nThe forest was my favorite toy.\nI came here again,\nA few years ago,\nIt was the same place I knew well,\nAs far as I could tell,\nThere was nothing different to show.\nI open my eyes now,\nTo see the trees,\nMy eyes see an empty place,\nAs if leaving no trace,\nThough this is not what my mind sees.\nEnd of Volume 1\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Poison", "Ariana Herenden", "The softness of touch\nThe warmth of breath\nWith airs the cobra strikes\n\nBreathing hope\nBreathing love\nAnd always breathing light\nThe bitten knows not\nWhat happened then\nFor days and days she's numb\n\nBut in time\nThe poison sinks\nAnd she will at last succumb", ""),
        StaticBook("Polyamory", "Nyxxa", "_-_=Polyamory=_-_-\n\nBy Nyxxa\n\nWritten in the year 1545\nTable of Contents\nDefination  (p.3)\nPolysexuality (p.4)\nPrincles of Polyamory  (p.5)\nQuestions Addressed (p.6 - p.14)\nConclusion (p.15 - p.16)\nPolyamory is the practice of, or desire for, intimate relationships involving more than two people, with the knowledge and consent of everyone involved. \n\nIn this book I hope to give a brief introduction of such relations.\nPolysexuality is often mistaken for polyamory the but while those that practice polyamory may practice polysexuality it is not mutually inclusive.\n\nPolysexuality is the attraction towards multiple genders.\nThe principles of polyamory are much like the principles of every other kind of relation. Ethics, Honesty, Transparency are the basic ideals. I will quickly address the commonly asked questions.\nIs it the same as polygamy?\n\nPolyamory is a boarder term then the pure defination of polygamy. Polygamy defines it's self as marriage to multiple spouses. Which it when then follow that if a group of polyamorous persons were married\nthey might be considered polygamous. However since most view the definition of polygamy to mean a man with multiple wifes, and the sigmata of social view is of unhappy untrusting and greedy relations, I would say not as the plebian would say.\nDoes it mean that you would have to be with those of your own gender?\n\nThis is a personal preferance of the people involved in the polyamorous relationship. I believe that a relationship where each individual in the group loves\neach other individual in a group is perhaps the most ideal way for polyamory to occur, however I myself am in no way attracted to Females, Thusly I believe that so long as those amoung the relation that are not in love with other individuals in the group\nhave a close relationship of trust transparency and friends, such as a brother or a best friend would be, then the relationship would function just as well.\nCan such groups marry?\n\nI again believe that this is personal preferance amoung each polyamorous relation. I will however give my opinion. I believe that either they should not be married at all or all individuals should be married to each\nother. Any polyamorous relationship with any divided parties will begin to fall apart.\nHow do you keep everyone from jealousy and upset?\n\nThis is the most important factor of the entirity of polyamory in my opinion. Trust and open communication is an absolute must in relationships, polyamory is no exception.\nIf everyone cannot feel free to express themselves and their feelings to everyone then the relationship WILL FAIL.\nin conclusion this lifestyle is not for everyone, it is complicated and requires a lot of trust and maturity. \n\nI suggest that if you are attempting to start your polyamorous relation that you sit down with everyone and ask questions until\neveryone involved is satisfied with the status of their part in your life.\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns please feel free to send a bird to me, Nyxxa.\n\nThank you for your time and understanding.", ""),
        StaticBook("Portrait Imagine", "Nyxxa", "-==Portrait Imagine\n\nCaution: this drawing comes from my own imagination and is not a real person.\nOn this page dots of varying density create a sketch.\nYou see a female, She has pale, soft skin over a curvaceous yet thin frame. A small, set of lips frame gleaming, prefectly straight teeth with sharp, slightly hooked cainines and fang-like eye teeth.-\nHer sleek, dark hair falls in cascades over her shoulders to her back seemingly shiny in some unknown light. Her large clear, chardonay-green eyes shine with mischievous intent. Her body is mostly fur free but for strips of well groomed short black fur -\non her face, running from just above the corner of her jaw to the peak of her high cheekbones. Another patch of fur runs from her sleek tail in a v-shape around both sides of her torso getting progressively thicker to cover just under her bosom. Her tail-\nis long and sleek and gives the impression of twitching at it's tip. Her petite arms and fine delicate hands are fur covered up to just below her biceps, and her legs, making up nearly half her height are fur covered up to mide-thigh on the inside and -\nto her hips on the outside. The only colored ink on the page is the eyes of this felined female.", ""),
        StaticBook("Powers of Being", "Farley III Stafyr", "The Powers of Being\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr\nAs a theoretical study, my writings began about wisdom, leading me to the difference between knowledge and experience and their relation, furthermore bringing me to write a first draft of the elements of mind.\nBy now I have realized that there must be more. The mind is part of the being itself. A power within everyone of us. Logically though, the being consists of more than only the mind.\nPhysically we have the body as the second power of being. The body is one power we use every day, its elements are blood, organs, muscles and the resulting strength…  The elements belonging to the body shall be elaborated by me\nin further writings.\n\nTo note, that this is the point where my studies will go over into the studies of doctors and healers, likely to be seamless. For this I must also refer to a man of biological knowledge in the future.\nAs for the third and last power of being, I hereby mean the soul. The elements of soul are yet to be elaborated and studied by me, although I can definitely align an element to the soul. In another work of mine, I say that feelings are an element of\nmind. By now, I must correct myself and say, that feelings are a definite element of the soul. The same may go for purity as well. For this we will see further in the future, what my studies and writinggs bring up.\n\n-: Primary Edition :-", ""),
        StaticBook("Practitioners", "Grungron Irongut", "Dark Arts\n      Practitioners\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- Gareth\nAsher\nCorvo\nStella\nNicholas\nArtius\nFaenor\nMithrion\nAsarielle\nAdniel", ""),
        StaticBook("Prayer to Malin", "[Psijic Laurehl] Katie Mantisuku", "Malin,\n\nWatch and guide us in the coming days as your children mourn the loss of two of your own. May their souls rest in a peace that none but those departed can know. Give those who live on the comfort and knowlage to\ngo on with their lives. We ask your blessing, in your name.\nAmen\n\nkaean'leh ciw'hileia\n\n((The above is in rough elvish and may be wrong.. May they sleep in peace is the intended meaning))", ""),
