        StaticBook("Roving Days", "Daekra Solli'gra", "Well in my far off roving days\n\nWhen I would dance they'd shout 'Hooray'\n\nNever did the sky ever seem to gray\n\nAnd all we did was drink and play\nAh, yes those times were bright and gay\n\nI was never afraid of what I'd say\n\nAnd for little we did have to pay\n\nIn those old misty days\nI sung and drunk and bunked and run\n\nAll the live long day\n\nI hummed and rummed and chummed and stumped\n\nIn those beloved days\nI slapped and cracked and all of that\n\nAll the live long day\n\nI threw and flew and chewed, it's true\n\nIn those red-rosy days\nI trounced and bounced the whole town round\n\nAll the live long day\n\nI played and strayed and flayed the fray\n\nIn those right golden days\nI slept and wept and cursed the sky\n\nAll the live long day\n\nI felt as though I'd rather die\n\nIn those horrific days", ""),
        StaticBook("Royalty Guide", "Lorena Faeliel", "Submitting a book to the store.\n\nA note on royalties sand how they work.\nOn submitting a book to the store, you allow us to create copies to then sell to the customer.\n\nSo long as the book is signed with your name, you are able to reclaim the original copy at any time.\nShould we sell a copy of your book, you will acquire 20% in royalties. This can be paid via transfer, in which case, a bird will be sent with a payment slip.\n\nOR collected in store.\n\nA record is kept\nby Lorena detailing each copy sold of signed books. \n\nA payment scheduel of one elven year CAN be set should you wish. Otherwise you are able to colelct royalties from Lorena only.\nShould you have any concerns, speak to Lorena Faeliel [Laurelin] or Guarger [Apiel]\n\nYou can also send a bird to:\n\nLorena Faeliel,\n7 Jibya Lane.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rugged Notes", "Unknown Scholar", "[!] Along the page you see many strange markings and drawings. They look to be rough copies, at best. There appears to be some sort of archway built of stone;  below it, several odd, circular schematics, or perhaps a map.\nNext to the map, the phases of the moon trail along.\n\n[OOC]- View in browser:\nhttp://tinyurl.com/slatrop\n-----------------------------\nAn odd name, indeed. Though, the actual device is far more mysterious and eldritch in nature. Translocators, Lori Oathcast refers to them as. Crumena took to calling them closets, as per their birthplace, the closets within Rasmot’s magical porta-potty.\nRegardless, the process for creating these translocators is a fairly complex and ritualistic one that involves both a skilled translocationist with knowledge of the subject,\nand a powerful enchanter capable of binding the spell to the locations in question.\nCreation\nAn enchanter holds the knowledge to spot. One who knows how to send matter to the void and back again must have learnt to create what is like a ‘gateway’ into the void. More than just the item itself, but anything that touches it,\neven air. Then again you do it on the other end and the mage attempts to pull the block back through the Void and the enchanter binds that to a doorway or pillar or somesuch. In short, one must reach into the Void and pull out an open space.\nMaintenance\nAfter time, it will need a mana supply, or one end will fizzle out before the other and create an endless hole. It’s advised then to have the enchanter available fairly often to refill whatever large mana gem\nor crystal you wish to power the translocators’ magic with. As far as I’m aware, this would be the only option, unless one would be able to get ahold of Kalameet’s notes on the mana obelisk. For the ignorant,\nFor the ignorant, this is a large pillar in which sums of mana are stored for use. The mana cannot be pulled out by any means by a magi to fuel their own spellcasting, but instead it exerts energy needed to power enchantments in the area.\nI’d elaborate further, though I’m only going off of what I’ve seen myself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ruhn'MeME", "Dizzy", "*dank ass instructions to runesmithing*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ruins of Anthos", "Azkel Frostbeard", "This new land of Anthos brings us many new wonders and mysteries, perhaps foremost of all being the presence of ruins - irrefutable evidence of one or more ancient civilizations. Despite their mystery, ruins are not an uncommon sight to the well-versed\ntraveller or scholar. Lost Asulon bore ruins throughout its lands - misplaced statues and aqueducts near the Cloud Sanctuary, sandstone ruins in  the deserts, ancient Mori’Quessir cave carvings in Malinor and of course the prolific ruins on Adyton island\nto name but a few. However, aside from these traces, there was little to suggest what caused the downfall of these cultures. Now that we find ourselves in a new land, we are again confronted with unexplained echoes of lost cultures. What caused their\ndownfall? What was the purpose of these structures? Who created them? These are all questions that we are unlikely to ever have a definitive answer to. However, perhaps with time and effort spent on researching and excavating these ruins we can shine what\nlittle light we can on the ruins of Anthos. The forests and cliffs of the north hold many treasures beside those of the natural kind. South-West of Malinor, following the path through the hills and glens, can be found a valley of trees with height only\nrivalled by the mighty boughs of Leumalin and Malinor. Game abounds in these woods, and the sight of these lands causes the wood-elf side of my psyche to sing with glee. However, should you walk these trails at night, one would find their gaze attracted\nto the roots of the mighty trees. Among the sunken hollows of these pines lie hidden alcoves of carved stone, with small worm-like tunnels in the walls glowing with the ruddy light. Any attempts to determine the source of these lights is made impossible\nby the presence of metal bars that block the observer’s gaze down the snaking tunnels. What was the purpose of these hollows? Hard to say. Perhaps they were nothing more than points of rest for weary travellers of some bygone empire, but their complexity\nand detail suggests that they were part of something larger. We must also consider the possibility that these hollows have existed long before the trees that dominate them, and the trees that dominate them, and that this forested valley could hide an\nancient city. Piles of similarly carved, ancient rubble would seem support this theory, but detailed research and excavation would be needed to yield tangible results. Another, perhaps more pressing point on interest in this valley is the presence\nof what appears to be an abandoned camp, made from cloth and lumber. The presence of what appears to be a sawmill and numerous tree stumps raise the likelihood that this was a lumber-camp. What is startling about this find is that it could not have been\nmore than a few years old, yet it predates our arrival on Anthos. This potentially ground-breaking discovery could have profound implications for our time here. Is Anthos still inhabited?\nAnd if so, by what? The wooden camp bared no resemblance to the\nruins of the land and is unlikely to belong to the same culture, but the fact that it was here before us raises many questions. Of course, another theory to consider is that this camp was made by the scouts sent ahead of our exodus to prepare the way. But\nthe positioning of the camp away from any race it could have belonged to is troubling; although clearly positioned near the lands of the Mali it bears resemblance to Valah, Bortu or even Uruk architecture. This mystery is among the most pressing\nthat need to be solved. The ancient lumber camp has since been commandeered by my Mali’ker brethren for use as a town. While I welcome the independence this has brought, many areas of the site have been damaged beyond repair, including the removal of\nseveral ornate towers and dwellings.By following the Malinor River to its mouth in the West and looking to the southern cliffs when a southern tributary stream reaches the mouth, a well lit cave can be seen. Inside this cave one is confronted by a series\nof carved stone brick columns, each with a large glowstone cube set into them. The northern entrance is partially blocked by a fallen column, but it is easily traversible. The cave is well lit by glowing columns, revealing it's inner architecture. To the\nsouth lies a downward passage completely submerged in water and blocked by ruined masonry. My attempts to move some of the fallen rubble out of the way were to no avail, and I doubt that anything beside a full excavation effort could reveal this lost\nlost tunnel. To the east is another passage, open but hewn from the rock in a way that suggests that it was left unfinished; no glowstone lamps or pillars light this section of the cave or support it from cave-ins. Aside this eastern passage\nlies a chamber that is blocked by rubble. After a few hours of hard work I managed to create a workable way in, revealing a rubble-strewn rectangular chamber  dominated by a rectangular stone slab. Whether this slab is some kind of altar or a tombstone is\nunknown. Coming back to the main atrium, a series of rough stairs with brick steps can be seen heading upward towards the light of a cave leading to the open sky, but unfortunately these steps are eroded and unreachable from the atrium. After traversing\nthe outer cliffs I managed to reach the upper cave and found a small series of cliff caverns. Each one bears a glowstone cube similar to the ones in the atrium’s pillars, but set in a haphazard manner. Perhaps this area was next to be embellished before\nits builders fled? Whatever the truth of this ruin, it is my firm belief that it should be given priority in excavation. Who knows what secrets this place could reveal about those who came before us? There are many other points of interest in the Malinor\nValley. By following the Malinor River, many features of culture’s past can be seen, including an exquisite fountain statue on the northern bank that continues to spout water from its hand. Who or what the statue represents is unknown\nbut the beauteous\ncarvings and obsidian facial features of the ancient visage further add to the sense of mystery. Further from the bank but still on the northern side is a stone circle made from several interlocking arches, thin and made of Whitestone covered in moss.\nWithin the circle is a swampy depression that exudes a mysterious green fog, making it hard to distinguish swamp grass from green water. Oddly, another stone circle lies on the south bank, but in a far different style. While the northern circle is made of\nthin, nondescript arches, the southern circle is made of carved menhirs made of ornate stone blocks and wooden slats. Perhaps more surprising is a roaring fire at the centre of the southern circle, which either suggests that it is maintained by magical\nmeans, or that is maintained by living beings...Perhaps the most fascinating ruin in all of Northern Anthos is a ruin that can only be compared to the spectacular ruined temple of the Mallowlyn Woodlands in Asulon; a massive ruin within the lands of the\nof the Anthos Cloud Temple. Upon entering the Cloud Temple lands from the northern gate - a gate which just so happens to lead to the wooded valley I spoke of earlier - heading east will take you to an old wooden bridge that leads to a beautiful ruined\ncourtyard, with water features and a cross-mosaic. Perhaps more stunning is the view above; ruined halls snake their way up the cliff to a massive - and completely intact - ancient tower. Unfortunately, the logical entrance to such a complex,\na large circular door, is blocked by rubble. However, upon further searching, a set of stairs snakes up through the ruined masonry and onto a stone bridge that leads to the a tunnel that snakes up to the upper hall. These tunnels remarkably bear the same\nglowstone cubes that can be seen in the cave colonnade in Malinor. Perhaps they were created by the same civilization? Reaching the hall reveals a beautiful vista to the observer, showing the entirety of the stunning complex below. Sadly, this is where\nthe adventurer’s journey ends; a set of implacable iron doors block the war to the tower itself. No matter how much force I applied to the doors they remained unmoved. Not letting this deter me, I scaled the side of the mountain to peer through the cracks\nof the tower. Although my view was brief it was wonderous. A marvelous glowstone chandelier runs down the centre of the tower, shining light onto well preserved steps and engraved alcoves. Redstone lamps can also be seen along the walls, creating an air\nof mystique and ritual. With that in mind I wonder what was the purpose of this place? An ancient fortress? The abode of some ancient mage? Perhaps a temple similar to the one that we have built in the valley below? These are questions that will be in our\nminds should future scholars decide to investigate this fascinating edifice.\nOf all the places in Anthos, the frozen lands behind the great Northern ice cliffs are the only ones yet to be explored. Attempts to pick through these ice walls with conventiona\ntools meet with no avail, leaving nothing but scratches. However, due to its glass like transparency, travellers are sometimes able to catch glimpses of the world beyond the ice walls. When gazing through the ice near the Teuton castle in\nnorthern Oren one can see an elaborate stone totem, carved with eldritch symbols and baring three menacing skulls. Although offering only a small glimpse into the true North, this sight brings many new questions for us. Who built this totem? The use of\nskulls in architecture has never been seen in any other Anthosian ruins; such crude symbols are usually signs of a tribal civilization such as the Uruks, and not the advanced culture suggested by the stones seen in Malinor and southern Anthos. Totems such\nas these are also primarily a warning - indeed the Uruks employ a similar practice to deter trespassers from entering their lands. Are these totems a warning? And if so, were they intended to be seen by travellers peering through the ice. Are we the\nintended targets of such a warning, or some ancient foe of ages past? Perhaps the apparent tribal culture that the totem suggests was warding off the civilized folk of the south? However, if we are the targets, that brings the possibility that such a\nculture could exist in seclusion beyond the ice. The thought of an intact and undiscovered culture is certainly enticing, however unlikely.\nAlthough this theory may sound outlandish to some, further evidence can be found on a plateau near the ice wall in\nnorthern Malinor. On a rocky outcrop overlooking the valley of Oren, hidden behind a hill, lies a ring of carved ruins similar to the stones of the ice totem. Perhaps more disturbing is the sight of a smouldering fire pit and hide tents, with the frosted\nground strewn with bones and blood. This chilling scene appears to be some kind of hunting camp, or - if my theory of the ice wall being some kind of isolating barrier is true - a camp for scouts to watch for intruders. As a hunter for nigh on three\ncenturies, the scent of fire still clinging to the embers told told me that it had only been mere weeks since the pit had been lit. If this is true, and this ruin is some kind of scout camp, it’s inhabitants may have fled when we made our presence known\nin the valley’s below it; perhaps to warn some other tribe on the other side of the ice. Whatever the truth of the matter, this evidence is certainly disturbing. Although I had promised myself to keep this text on point I find myself unable to prevent\nmyself from describing the wonders of the Spider Cave. Although not specifically a ruin, I find it to be a most profound example of a breed of natural beauty not seen since the now-lost caverns of Menorcress in Asulon. It's entrance does, however, bear\nthe carved stones seen in other Anthosian ruins. Upon exiting Leumalin from the gate to the Western Docks if one hugs the cliff wall they will find a gaping and glowing cave. Upon entering, one would be greeted by two sights; course black pebbles on\nthe cave floor and and a thick covering of spiderweb on the cave ceiling. Despite any natural reaction of fear one might have from this evidence of a spider infestation, none of my visits have managed to show any sign of current habitation. Past this\ninitial cave can be seen a quite remarkable sight. The cave opens on the lip of a massive cave, covered in mushrooms and vines of all descriptions, but perhaps most striking are the massive luminous mushrooms.", ""),
        StaticBook("S. Council Edict", "Jacob Chapel", "The Edict of the Small Council, 13th of Malin's Welcome, 1472.\n\nScribed down by Jacob Chapel, High Scrivener of Oren.\nAt the will of his Imperial Majesty Emperor Tuvya Carrion, the Petty Council is hereby declared as a minor council under the privy to help give word to the Emperor for many Lords, positions will be granted based on the Lord and the will of the Emperor.\nSection I\nPositions of the Council\nThe following titles are granted the right to be considered part of the council and granted the right of seat at meetings when called and will be expected to fulfill their tasked duties to assist the realm.\n¬ Petrus Maer\n¬ High Scrivener\n¬ Guard Commander\n¬ Master of Laws\n¬ Master of the Hunt\n¬ Master of the Harvest\n¬ Master of the Ships\n¬ Champion of the Realm\n¬ Imperial Scribe\nEdict of the Minor Council\nAt the will of his Imperial Majesty Emperor Tuvya Carrion, these titles are hereby honored with the duties of the Minor Council and the duties that are assigned with such title.\nSection I\nRights and Duty of the Petrus Maer\n\nThe position of Petrus Maer is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain his Capital city. His duties and rights are as follows.\n¬ The duty to manage and oversee daily operations of the Capital City.\n¬ The duty to manage and oversee construction and instatement of buildings and guildhalls for other guilds and citizens of the capital.\n¬ The duty to manage the city's financial treasury and collect taxes from the citizens and guilds of the Capital.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\nSection II\nRights and Duty of the High Scrivener\n\nThe position of High Scrivener is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain the public knowledge and library of  his Empire. His duties and rights are as follows.\n¬ The duty to maintain any knowledge, document, and book in the Library of Petrus.\n¬ The duty to Oversee and maintain the Royal and Public Library of Petrus.\n¬ The duty to manage affairs of the Museum of Oren.\n¬ The duty to transcribe official documents for public viewing.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\nSection III\nRights and Duty of the Guard Commander\n\nThe position of Guard Commander is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain the law with in his Capital city, Petrus. His duties and rights are as follows.\n¬ The duty to maintain the Emperors peace within the capital of Petrus.\n¬ The duty to maintain the Emperors Guard Force of Petrus.\n¬ The right to arrest individual common men suspected for a crime.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\nSection IV\nRights and Duties of the Master of the Hunt\n\nA largely honorary title, the Master of the Hunt is foremost of huntsman amongst his peers. The title is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain his hunts.\nHis duties and rights are as follows.\n¬ The duty to lead the royal hunts for the Emperor.\n¬ The duty to warden his Imperial Majesty’s forests.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\nSection V\nRights and Duties of the Master of the Harvest\n\nA largely honorary title, the Master of the Harvest is foremost of farmers amongst his peers. The title is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain his farms and\nfood stocks. His duties and rights are as follows.\n¬ The duty to supply the granaries of His Imperial Majesty, keeping such well stocked.\n¬ The duty to ensure the people of Petrus are well-fed.\n¬ The right to hold harvest festival and fests for the common folk\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\nSection VI\nRights and Duties of the Master of Ships\n\nAn honorary title, the Master of Ships is typically reserved for a well-respected councillor and friend of his Imperial Majesty. His rights and duties are as follows.\n¬ If ever Oren has a navy, is responsible for the management and oversight of such navy.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\nSection VII\nRights and Duties of the Champion of the Realm.\n\nA largely honorary title, the Champion of the Realm is considered the finest warrior within the realm, Knightly or commoner.\nThis title is granted by merit of the Tournament of Sun’s Smiles. His rights and duties are as follows.\n¬ The duty, in times of war, to be assigned to lead a small group of elite warriors.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\nSection VIII\nRights and Duties of the Imperial Scribe\n\nThe position of Imperial Scribe is granted to an individual who is intrusted by the Emperor to draft Edicts, Letters, or Documents at the request of the Emperor, private or public.\nHis rights and duties are as follows.\n¬ The duty to draft any edict, document, or letter for the Emperor at his will.\n¬ The duty to hold the secrets of such edicts, documents, or letters.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council Meetings.\nSection IX\nRights and Duties of the Master of Laws\n\nA largely honorary title, the Master of Laws is foremost of peace-keepers amongst his peers. Has the powers to enforce laws of the Realm in any province and to appoint a Bailiff under his holding\n¬ The duty and power to uphold the Emperor’s peace and enforce His Imperial Majesty’s laws in any and all provinces.\n¬ The power to appoint his own provincial Bailiff over the Lord Bailiff.", ""),
        StaticBook("S.Z Res. Request", "liam_barnett", "Sarrion Zytiaear\n Resignation Request \n-------------------\n\nDrafted by the people of Skyfall\n\nRecorded by Lanavia Dreathen and Bell Sano\nThe citizens of Skyfall have conjoined, compromised, and declared that Skyfall itself, under proper and fresh authority, should indeed be reformed into a more formal, and, active local government.\nThere was a time when the leadership of this walled city had been idolized and praised, but those days have long since passed, and now the people of our mountain home fear what tomorrow brings.\nWhen one finds their Lord not only staying back and distant but also going against the very laws penned to protect these lands, there is most certainly a complication, and thus, the united people of Skyfall have banned\ntogether in hopes to push for change in the only way they see fit; a shift in absolute authority. And here, let it be stated, that the Black Dragon Reform now demands a more equivalent, fair, and representative government.\ni) Personal Leadership\ni A.\n\nAs we investigate into the legal status and unofficial criminal record of his Lord of Skyfall, Sarrion Zytiaear, it is evident that he is indeed not fit to\nserve as the leader of a large settlement, the dean of an educational facility, nor does he deserve to converse with the Kingdom of Vandoria as a whole.\nHe has directly broken laws O1, O2, and O7, and has simply not been punished by the national government. \ni B.\n\nThe general inactivity and lack of care for the physical building of Skyfall, the Society, and it’s people, raises concern for that of Lord Sarrion, as well as his administration.\nWe wish that he would be more attentive to our needs, and would filter our opinions, which our Lord has so far failed to accomplish. It can be assumed that the Society guild budget includes that of the surplus\nmade on taxes, given the decent sized population. This mina could indeed be used to fund new government sponsored social programs. \nii) Transfership\nii A.\n\nUnder the beliefs mentioned prior, the peoples of Skyfall are now convinced that someone more suited and motivated is far more deserving of the title, as opposed to\nthe current individual in power. The one that has been unofficially elected to represent the majority opinion is Lanavia Zytitear, as we are certain that her values are representative of the Society’s true values, advocating\nfor education reform, as well as a state government that encourages the free voice of it’s people.\nii B.\n\nIf, in the unlikely event that a new, carefully chosen form of leadership is not adequate for the Society or Skyfall, then it will be the duty of the people to once again overthrow\nthe then-current Lord, and replace them with another fresh, new, and competent leader.\niii) Request\n\nAnd it is with this document, this request, that we have submitted to the Scholar’s Rest, the Student’s Administration, the Skyfall tax office, or wherever else it\nmay or may not be applicable, that we the united citizens, scholars, students, administrators, Redcoats, and whoever else may support this petition, ask that Sarrion Zytiaear kindly passes the torch over to our new\nrepresentative, Lanavia Zytiaear, as we are under the belief that she may lead our Lordship and school to what the Society aims to truly achieve.\nThus, on this day of the 13th of the Sun’s Smile, 1533, the following citizenry under the names of GOD, Krug, Horen, Malin, Yemekar, the Lordship of Skyfall, the Society, the Kingdom of Vandoria, as well\nas the people of Vailor, support the resignation of Sarrion Zytiaear;\n[!] The following page is complete with multiple signatures, all done in their own style.\n- Dunstan Zytiaear\n- Bell Cranel Acaele'par R. Sano\n- Lilja Steinson Acosta Zytiaear\n- Steven Vega\n- Roy D'Avre\n- Ariselle Vega\n\n\n\nx. Lanavia Amakaaer Dreathen Zytiaear\n[!] The seal of a dragon is on this page, pressed onto the document, and under it, a similar illustration of a dragon.\nUpon acceptance of your resignation, please sign below:\n\n\n\nx_________________\n[!] The signing area is left blank.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sale Contract 1", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "This document of sale represents the agreement between two partys.\n\nThe following terms will be used:\n\nRent: Re-Occuring payment in a strict cycle.\n\nLand Lord: Offical owner of the zone.\n\nTenant: a person who occupies land or property rented from a landlord.\n\nCoin: Minas or Currency\n[-----------------]\nThe Rent for this store front property has been set to 400 Coin's a year((1 Week OOC)) and a payment of 600 Coin's upfront.\n\nThe following are the terms and conditions of the Sale Contract:\n1) The Landlord has a right to Evict the Tenant with warning.\n\n2) The Caliphate(State) as the right to Evict the Tenant through the Landlord with Warning.\n3) 400 Coins will be paid to the Land Lord as rent per year.\n\n4) If rent is not paid accidently or purposely the land will be revoked with warning, and the contract terminated.\nLand Lord's Signature:\n\nSarrion Zytiaear\n\n\n\nTenant's Signature:\n\nJackson Vero", ""),
        StaticBook("Salum's Story", "Taynuel", "<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n\n\n    The Story of Salum\n\n        A short story\n    written on the 17th\n   of Amber Cold, 1486\n\n     by Taynuel Faerin\n\n\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\nShe was a very young hare when she found herself hopelessly lost, her mother gone from sight, her father long since dead, killed by hunters for his pelt and left for his family to find frozen in the snow. The sight scared her deeply, and she saw she\nwas more frightened of the two-legged monsters her mother called 'people' than she had ever been before.\n\n      It was late at night, the moon high above her head, when she finally admitted it to herself. She had no idea where she was or which direction\nher home was. The echos of wolfish howls rang through the air, chilling her  to the bone. She had to find shelter, and fast.\n\n     And so, she ran, tearing through the woods as fast as her powerful legs could carry her. Faster than any rabbit, she was\nsinuous and strong for her age, her silver fur rippling with each motion of her legs. Chocolate eyes wide with fright, she surged through the bushes, looking for something, anything, anywhere to call shelter until the sun kissed the skies once more and\nshe could find her way home.\n\n     It was then that she spotted it - there, off in the distance, was a small hut, crude and fashioned from fallen pine boughs. She didn't have much of a choice, so she darted in to escape the wintry cold and the gnashing of\nthe wolves, starved and needing to feast.\n\n      What she saw inside the hut both startled her and sparked her curiosity. Inside was a boy, an elf of deep gray skin, wrapped tightly in blankets and shivering. The only light in the room came from the\npitiful embers of the hearth in the center, casting an eerie glow all around.\n\n     She gulped, shivering as the boy stirred from his slumber. He groaned, roused from his sleep likely thanks to the rush of wind that accompanied her entrance. The shrieks\nof the blustery currents of air outside reminding them of the impending storm.\n\n     He opened his eyes slowly, revealing them to be the same hoary hue of her pelt. He made a small sound in his throat and turned toward the entrance of the makeshift tent,\nblinking at the sight. \"A hare...\" he whispered hoarsely, though she could not understand him.\n\n     No, what she felt was something different. She didn't know what she said, but she could somehow /feel/ it. She knew in some way that he would not, no,\ncould not harm her, and so she approached him, oh so cautiously.\n\n     Her triangular nose twitched slightly as she came closer, lowering her ears and stretching her neck out to sniff at him.\n\n     A gentle hand held itself out,\nnot to touch her, but to let her sniff and see that he was no threat to her.\n\n     For a fleeting moment, she considered turning and running away, but the scream of the wind and the snarl of the wolves close behind made her think twice. With a nervous\ngulp, she approached him, watching in fear as he lifted the blanket...\n\n     ...to reveal he had no weapons of any sort. He was as defenseless as she was out here, and needed shelter just as much as she. A strange feeling in her gut arose, telling her\nthat this elf could be trusted, at least for just one night. Nervously, she crawled under the blanket, curling up as close to his belly as she could.\n\n     Shortly thereafter, she felt a light weight on herself. He was hugging her, swaddling her in the\nheat she would need to survive the bitter cold.\n\n     \"If I have done nothing in this life, at least I will have saved yours, no matter how small,\" he whispered, closing his eyes with a shiver. Thus they rode out the violent storm, sharing each other's\nbody heat and cowering together.\n\n     The following morning, she found that he was not where she last remembered him to be. Instead, he sat across the small room from her, the only thing separating them being a small pile of greenery.\n\"Eat,\" he said. \"You will need your strength in this cold.\" She did not quite understand what he said, but she knew what he was trying to convey by the gesture he made with his hand.\n\n     So began their friendship. The elf came to call her 'Salum',\nthe Elvish word for 'to know, or to sense,' an homage to her intuition.\n\n     Bound by an invisible bond, one that neither could see or touch, but both could feel.", ""),
        StaticBook("sandk1ng is cute", "Eath'Lur", "who picked this\nlike\ndude\nyou're beautiful\n\nlike\nyou could give me\nthat bow\nand these arrows\nand the weapon\nok\n\n-sandk1ng", ""),
        StaticBook("Saying Farewell", "Häidår Qâdir", "-[]=-=[]-=-=-[]=-=[]-\n    Saying Farewell.\n\nWritten By Haidar Qadir.\n-[]=-=[]-=-=-[]=-=[]-\nAs I sit alone, in my quiet, humble abode. I begin to think off I've done, and what I have yet to do. I am known to some as Haidar, and to others. A nameless man, I sit here in deep thought..A quill in hand, and a book infront of me. My thoughts only\nthinking of a farewell, so as I sit alone, in my humble abode. With the silence breeze blowing through my window, I begin to think. What will come, and what will pass? Friends, or family? As I sit, I wonder. Who would miss me? Or who wouldn't?\nThe question that floods my thoughts every night, keeping me from a peaceful slumber. I must say farewell one day, perhaps soon. Or perhaps years from now...", ""),
        StaticBook("Seasonal Poems", "Taliyu", "A Book of Poetry\n     \n\n      By Taliyu\nMoonlight Rain\n\nI watch the rain fall,\nslowly the moon rises,\nand the shining stars\nclear the night skies.\nA soft shine dances,\nsoftly through my dreams.\nIt sings a lullaby\nof nightingales and the soft rain,\nas the moon soars overhead.\nDove\n\nA flutter of wings\ndowny feathers drift,\nlike falling snow,\ndown to the ground.\nFrom a pair of wings,\ncarrying a promise\nto fly safely far,\nfrom danger towards home.\nDrifting Leaves\n\nDelicate green boats,\ndrift down the stream. They sing a song\nfilled with laughter \non the breeze.\nSeasons\n\nThe trees\nare set ablaze,\nwith autumn's gentle\nflames.\n\nThey sleep,\nbranches bare,\nbeneath a frozen quilt\nand dream through\nwinter.\nSpring arrives,\nwith new life.\nSong fills the air,\nas sweet flowers \nbloom.\n\nAnd then comes\nsummer's warmth.\nEmerald, jade, peridot, grow from branches overhead.\nLone\n\nI watch in silence\nas the flakes of snow\ndrift down from high\nfar above my head. \nThe moon, all alone, \nsmiles down on me.\nHow?\nHow can she smile, \nalone in the sky,\nthrough the misty clouds,\nand falling flakes of snow.\nRiver\n\nThe water flows,\nwith enviable strength\nreflecting the sky\nfar above.\nIt laughs and sings, \nas it dances along,\ncatching the shining\nlight.\nAwake\n\nThe sunlight streams\nthrough the open\nwindow,\nwaking weary eyes.\nSending away dreams,\nand the moon's soft\nglow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Security Log", "Fi'Ceru Guard", "Frost Witch Security Log\n\nAtricle 1:\nElodie Calaerneth\n\nTested extensively, displays no signs of being a witch.\nFrost Witch Security Log\n\nArticle 2:\nEloh'ra\n\nPricked with needle, blood deemed normal, displays no other signs of being a witch.\nFrost Witch Security Log\n\nArticle 3: \nVelulaei'Ilum\n\nDespite initial reluctance to testing, was eventually confirmed not to be a witch after an inspection of her blood.\nFrost Witch Security Log\n\nArticle 4:\nAllora\n\nTested via Fi'hiiran'tanya, casted by Ikur Seregon. Displayed no witch-like qualities, confirmed not to be a witch.\nFrost Witch Security Log\n\nArticle 5:\nRivena Scullathar\n\nTested by Ikur Seregon using Fi'hiiran'tanya, deemed suspicious. After further testing, was later confirmed not to be a witch.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seebo the Large", "Franswaar Kellian", "This is the Legend of Seebo the Large\n\n\n\n\n\n         Written By:\n            Franswaar\nThe raggedy old man known as Galendal the pink was in possesion of an evil artifact. Galendal knew an item such as this must be destroyed, but he alone could not do it alone. Galendal sought help from the person best suited for the task at hand, Seebo\nGalendal entered the young the halfings house, amazed that such a small creature could have so much clutter. Seebo was found at his desk reading poetry written by famous writer. As Galendal unfolded his tale of the artifact it filled Seebo wonder and\nadventure. He thought 'How dangerous could the artifact be.' 'I surely must destroy this so no harm could come to the world.' But during supper Seebo thought he could sell the artifact for quite a fortune. So in the night while Galendal slept peacefully,\nSeebo smuthered him whilst grining with his idea in mind. Unfortunatly Seebo made no profit from selling the ring and threw it in a now covered well. Seebo in his annoyance, proceeded to join the Orenian military, where had killed many dwarfs and orcs. \nThrough sheer luck and willpower (and the occasional ankle biting) Seebo vanquished his foes and earned the self imposed title of Seebo the Large, not for his size (he was quite the small halfing), but for the size of the piles of burning, rotting,\ncorspes in his wake. On the battlefield on brisk morning, Seebo found the small portrait of a dwarven family. Grief overcame the small halfing as he realized he had slain a member of a loving and happy family... and had not slain the rest of the family\nSeebo then dedicated the rest of his life to hunting the family. He deserted the Orenian military and massacre anyone that steped in his way. One such group was a tribe of Ologs. Seebo the Large came during the darkest of the blackest night and poured\nalchemist's fire down the throat of all the Ologs, except the young prince, Char'Goth, who had been fabled amoung the tribe as the strongest warrior they had ever seen. But with his home destroyed, his family burnt to a crisp, and his titled striped from\nhim, Seebo beat the Olog into eternal submission, even death shall not free him of Seebo's wraith. The 9ft Olog, Char' Goth, was taken away by Seebo to be his eternal slave.  With his new found ally, it is said that Seebo still searches for the dwarven\nfamily that had escaped Seebo's grasp, for now.\nIf you ever happen to pass the fabled Seebo the Large, be very wary, and keep your ankles covered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seed of Laurelin", "Tristanm1", "The High Prince of Malinor and The Seed of Laurelin\n\nScribed by Zevandir\nTold by High Prince Native\nA powerful Arch Druid from one of Malinor's eldest cities came to Aegis to help us with the erecting of Laurelin's trees. I met him at the cobblestone spires to the west of the Aegis Temple.  We set off on foot to a mountain gorge I had come across that\nwould act as a natural barrier to our foes. Once we arrived, the Druid wandered around in the valley reaching into a pouch at his hip every so often. He showed me the seeds in said pouch and they had tiny, intricate vines woven around them, with a shine\nvery similiar to glowstone. Whilst my brigade of builders were creating the city's defensive wall, trees began to grow exponentially! It seemed as though the trees grew faster the taller they got and soon the canopy raised hundreds of feet above us. It\nwas a wonderful sight, the leaves sprung out of the branches with a burst of the similiar glowstone sheen, and sprinkles of metallic dust swirled down from the tree tops.\nThere was still, however, a large clearing in the centre of the city. This of course\nwas for the mother tree. A tree to harbour them all. He grabbed a bit of parchment from his satchel and look over at me reassuringly. The Arch Druid then walked to the centre of the clearing, and began to cast a powerful spell upon one of the seeds.\nleaves suddenly spun around him wildly, and a wonderful green color radiated from him like an aura.\nThe tree' trunk sprouted around him, and he was no longer in view. I was rather frightened when I saw this, hoping he hadn't cast the spell incorrectly. As\nthe Mother Tree grew to its ultimate height, I saw a small opening half way up the tree. Low and behold, the Arch Druid stood in the opening proclaiming \"This is where the stone alter shall lie.\"\nOnce the trees seemed to stop growing, we climbed up the\ntrees with packs of wooden planks and began setting down the first few platforms. In time, Laurelin had become of the finest city's of Malinor, and to think it had all begun with just a pouch of seeds and a pinch of Druid Magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seekers Flyer!", "Ulfrík", "*}The Seekers{*\n\nHave you ever wanted a little bit more of\nadventure in your life? Tired of boring\nsoldiering and getting told what to do? \n\nCome and join The Seekers Guild! One of Athera's only active adventure guilds!\n*}Joining Up{*\nYou can either sign up at our stall on the market day at cloud temple (Right at the top by the marquee) Or you can simply pop on by our base! If you follow the cloud temple road and take the first left after the bridge you'll be there!", ""),
        StaticBook("Seige of Antioc", "Leyu", "Siege of Antioch\nWe arrived at Orontes River outside Antioch. The three major leader leading the crusades were discussing about what to do next Raymond wanted to make a direct assault, While Godfrey and Bohemund\npreferred to set siege to the city. Afer the first day, We encircled the city, The city's Byzanite fortifications were strong enouh to resist a direct attack, Although Yaghi-Siyan may not had enough men to adequately defend the city, A\nmessenger told us that he was relieved and emboldened when we didn't attack immediately. Bohemund encamped on the northeast cornor of the city at the gate of St. Paul, Raymund set his camp further to the west at the Gate of Dog. And Godfrey placed his\ntroops at the Gate of the Duke, Also further to the west Where a bridge of boats was built across the Orontes to the village of Talenki. To the souh was the tower of the Two Sister and at the northwest cornor of the Gate of St. Gergo Which was not\nblocked by our fellow Crusaders, And were used throughout the siege to supply Yaghi-Siyan with food. On the southern and eastern side of the city was \"Hilly\" area known as Mt. Silpius, Where the Citadel and the Iron Gate were located. :: :: The First\nSiege :: In mid-November Bohemund's nephew Tancred had arrived with reinforcements, And a Genoese fleet had sailed into the port at St. Symeon, Bringing extra food and supplies. At the end of the month Bohemund and Robert of\nFlanders took about 20.000 men and went foraging f or to the south, But while they were gone, Yaghi-Siyan made a sortie out of the Gate of St. Ge orge on december 29 and attacked Raymond's encampment across the river at Talenki Raymond was able\nto turn him back but he was not able to capture the city itself. Meanwhile Bohemund and Robert were attacked by an army under Duqaq of Damascus Which had marched from the north to come to Antioch's aid. Although the crusaders were\nvictorious here as well, They were forced to retreat to Antioch with little food. The mond ended inauspiciously for both sides: There was an Earthquake on December 30 And the following weeks saw such unseasonably bad rain and cold weather that\nDuqaq had to return home without further engaging the crusaders.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sensory Illusion", "Sarrion", "Sensory Illusion\n\nBy: Sarrion Zytiaear\n\n__________________\n\nThe following notes were scribed with the interview of an adept illusionist. His name was requested to not be scribed.\nSensory Illusions is the art of using the connection to the void to cast illusions upon a person or party which work off the person/s sensory. 3 sub types to Sensory Illusion: Glamours Figments and Phantasms.\nGlamours: Illusions that alter things that already exist, such as making a light look brighter, or a lavatory.. Smell better. They take rather little exertion depending upon the desired effect.\nFigments, entirely illusory illusions. Such as making a rabbit bounding out of a bush and back into another. Something that /isn't/ there. These tend to use more mana than Glamours.\nPhantasms: Illusions projected entirely in the mind to induce feelings through suggestive illusions such as happy thoughts or a quiet song. These thoughts are to be logical and mildly suggestive to induce feelings and emotions on the person.\nCasting is almost as Evocation, except instead of drawing an element of your choice on the empty page of the void you begin to draw what you want to illusion, for example a candle. You need to have\nexperienced what you’re inducing in sensory illusion in order to cast it. The feel of the heat from the candle, the pain of the burn from the flame. The light the candle produces, and the smell\nof wax melting. Once you draw your spell up in the void it’s simply bringing it forward and casting the spell upon the individuals you wish to induce with the sensory illusion.\nThings to remember:\n\nYour illusions are to be /logcial/ else the individual/s that the spell is being casted on will break the illusion and the illusion will fade.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ser Uhtred", "Ser Uhtred Vallberg", "A History of Ser Uhtred the Merciless of House Vallberg, Count of Lewes, right hand to the Iron-Arch Duke, the butcher of Adrimas.\nLittle young Uhtred was born in the harsh wastelands of the North in 1530. Being of a strong family, it was his duty to be a warrior for his family. He died when he was two. However it is known that his father would live for he was a strong man. Little\nUhtred was known to be of a heartless nature from a young age, commonly, he would kill the children when they stole his little bread-cakes. With this in mind, Uhtred became a strong little boy, known for his prowess in battle. He would become a war hero,\nfor Oren, killing many men in battle, he is now known for his cavalry skills, commonly seen riding a horse within his green armour. He is a friendly man, killing many in his stead, many like him, many loath him, however it is of course a great concern to\nthe elves, as many have faced his giant sword, known as a Zweihander. He would commonly cut them down and butcher their families also. This is a common trait for the good Knight. However, being a Knight it is duty to help, however he is said to only help\nthose of Human-blood. Many do not know his past, however. It is known. He was big fucking sword.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seregon Grimoire", "booklight12", "[!]\nThe book of the illustrious elf Beranabus Seregon.. It'd seem despite your best attempts the knowledge teeming inside could not be accessed through normal means as it was locked by a magically imbued iron binding.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shades", "The Eternal Library", "\n\n\n\n        Shades\n      ---------\n     By: Ein Sarad\nShade, the lowest point of magic, and the pinnacle of forbidden arts, is known as a curse and a gift. A Shade is not a person, or a type of magic, but a parasitic being born from Iblees, which in turn grants its host a\npeculiar skill of conjuring tendrils Shades have been documented through times, ever since Aegis. According to stories and rumours, the first caster to appear was Rilath - with unrivaled prowess. It is said that Iblees himself bound the shade\nupon him, and so the story of Shades began. A guild for dabblers in the voidal arts, The Mages Guild in the times of Aegis, got a new apprentice by the name of Rilath. The young caster became an apprentice before anyone knew of\nhis true intention, and more importantly, what he had inside him. He began learning about the arcane, but he couldn't handle the mental pressure the Shade put on him through its endless pestering of his very mind. So it wasn't long before chaos ensued,\nfor where shades go, so does disorder and turmoil. What was curious, is that the Guildmaster at the time, didn't kick Rilath out of the guild as word reached his ears. Mithas, the Guildmaster saw it as an opportunity, and soon was succumbed into what\nthe shade had to offer. One after another, masters of the guild gave in for the thirst of power, without knowing the consequences. Thus, as early as it was, the guild of magi gained its reputation for having problems with people dabbling into black\nmagic. But the balance in the guild wasn't completely ruined, since every tree has a few spoiled fruit too. The Archmage of the guild, now a man of legends, Ambros, didn't take well the unnatural occurrence of dark arts in his guild, and set out to\npunish the young apprentice. Without further notice, so he did. Ambros caught Rilath, and a heated battle took place, which ended up in the Shade getting defeated. The archmage sealed the shade in a pure, clean crystal - removing its influence from\nRilath, essentially creating the Shade Gem. A gem that held the power. Rilath, having had a taste of the power, did not simply give up but in fact stole the gem to regain his prowess. After that, shades kept popping up time after time, but the gem\ndisappeared. Famous figureheads were Lucas Black and Salamandra, who made sure that chaos was ever present in this world. Then, a time of silence and secrecy began, and the Mages Guild became more like a secret organization. Highly exclusive, and\nshrouded in mystery. Little did the commonfolk know, a lot of changes took place in the guild of magi. It was a coup of sorts, and many were essentially kicked out. Wyvernym Hold, circa 1440, hundred years later of foretold, the new guildmasters had\nsomehow gained posession of the Shade Gem.\n\n[!] A detailed sketch of the gem was on the page. [!]\n\nhttp://i.imgur.com/IhP3mFP.png\nThe guild was in shambles, and it could only be guessed what happened to it, as new shades no one had ever heard of popped up. After a small uproar, the magical community fell silent again, until word of the gem from which all shades were drawing power\nfrom had gotten broken. The shades became nothing but a rumour. What a shade is capable of, is largely of off rumours, but it is said that one shade can conjure around a dozen of pitch black tendrils. Tentacles of darkness to strangle, cut and\ntear apart nearly anything in their way. To a person unknown of this, it would appear as if they were controlling shadows. Holy magic, as per usual, clashes with the tainted being. Another effective counter for a shade isn't known. How Ambros\nmanaged to seal the first shade remains a mystery too. A person cursed with a shade has many problems however. Their grasp on reality begins slipping, as the being constantly attempts to gain a foothold of the body. Being the parasite it is, the\nshade tries to control its host, until their will finally gives in. Thus, it is a curse.The shade never sleeps, and that is why the cursed often suffer intense insomnia. The lack of sleep slowly drives them mad, and then the daemon within takes\ncontrol - with no going back. Not to mention them not being fully in control even the whole time they spend awake. If you find out that someone carries the curse, it is wise to not make them your enemy, and simply disappear from their sight.\nHowever, for several decades, shades haven't been sighted and shall remain mostly alive in the stories and rumours of old. Perhaps one day, they will return.\nCopied and edited for the Eternal Library, Snow's Maiden, 1548.\n\nIf this book is found anywhere but the Eternal Library without express permission of the Silver State of Haelun'or, it is stolen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shades", "Triplewing", "------Shades--------------------------  I     I         I    I\n II   II    I   II    II\n  III III  II  II   III\n   II  II II    II II\n    III III  III III  II\n   IIIIIII  III  IIIIII\n     IIIIII I I IIIIII\n     IIIIIIIIIIIIIIII\n   IIII  IIII   III II\nIn the time of Aegis, a\npale and apparently evil man lived by the name of Lucas Black,\nhe acted as the leading figure of the Shades. Capable of such feats as corrupting apprentice\nof the archmage into the state known as shade. He is not where the shades\nbegan from, but he is one of the most notable people to be a shade.\n\nThese people known as shades are often deemed evil, but is that\ntruly the case? Many seem to think that the\nshades have vanished,\nand that they have.. but rumours spread.\nShades are capable\nof performing an apparent former form\nof Arcane Magicks; the      Shade Magic\n-------------------Shade Magic is magic\nthat seemingly draws it's power from a gem.\nIt's often simply called 'tendrils' since that's what really describes the\nmagic. The Shade Gem, where the shades would draw their power to perform the magic from, is very powerful, but rumours say that the gem was broken. Actually.. when it was found, it wasn't active, but it was re-activated by an Archmage.. but somehow it's\nstill broken. The shades can't use the\nmagic unless it's activated, apparently.\nChances are that it's\njust made up though.\nThe magic in action looks like black tendrils, a bit like squids tentacles. Their\nmagic is destructive, and corrupting. Not really\nsomething to seek for.\n    Some say the Shade Magic is blessed by Iblees, and therefore truly unholy. Known shades are very few though; \nIn Aegis, Lucas Black\nwas known to be one.\nIn Asulon, Salamandra\nwas known to be one.\nThey have kept themselves hidden\nor very subtle in their actions in Anthos thus far, but I've heard that a man named Adorellan is one.\n  If the Gem is currently broken, this\nman I mentioned can somehow still use the tendrils.. or maybe it's\nnot broken. The Shade\nGem on the other hand\nlooks like this:\n-------------------             [!]\nThe page has a detailed but quite\nsmall illustration of\nthe gem. Depicted\nfrom an upwards\nperspective.\n-------------------\nThe Shades are truly\na faction shrouded in mystery, but atleast I could reveal some of them.\n-------------------        Ein Sarard\n       ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨\n   1st of Deep Cold\n   ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨\n  Schattenburg, 1453\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamanism", "Glacio Nereus", "Shamanism.\n\nBy Eath'Lur, Elder Shaman and Avatar of the Spirits.\n\nGlacio Nereus is allowed to distribute this book for educational intentions, but to never sell it.\nShamanism is an kind of deity-related magic manipulated by the orcs, and in some few, rare cases, other inferior races, such as wood elves and dwarves.\n\nThe Shamanism can be divided in three sections:\nThe Elementalists:\n\nKnown to be the primary combatants, these fierce orcs can manipulate the present elements on their surrounding, which they can see and they know where they are at.\n\nIn order for an elementalist\nto summon a spirit's power, he must be deemed worthy of it through a contract after finding a spirit by searching the elemental plane, which is where the elemental spirits lie at.\nThe Lataumans:\n\nThese warriors are stronger in muscle than the elementalists, being considered deadly at close ranges.\n\nIn order for a latauman to summon a spirit, firstly he must make a deal with an ancestral\nspirit on the Ancestral plane, which is the place where all the most honourable orcs rest. By summoning the ancestral spirit, the latauman can get stronger, better at swords, faster and possibly any good skills said spirit had.\nLastly, Witch Doctors:\n\nWith their hexes, curses and healing, the witch doctors can do the most different kind of stuff!\n\nThey are not made for direct combat, but for indirect combat, the \"weakest\" of the shamans, spending more\ntime on practicing their glorious and flawless blessed by Krug stuff than klomping others and displaying their skills.\n\nThe witch doctors can travel on the immortal plane, and unlike the other shamans, It doesn't needs to do a pact with said spirits,\nexclude a few cases, such as the evil, terrible, malevolent, edgy, impure, kill-on-sight, weak, bad spirit Ixli.\n\nWe all must kill Ixli one day. Ixli bad.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamanism 1", "Eirik Ireheart", "Notice: These books are rushed copies of tomes in the Library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. The following is in no way a complete nor perfect copy of said book.\n\"A magic almost strictly wielded by those of Krug's descent, Shamanism is to the Orcs as Muntizvja is to Kha priests, highly practised and narrowly revered. Those that fully understand the magical ways, divvied up into the sections of Elementals,\nYouhumans, Witch healers, and Farseers, each have their own role in Orkos society, and put the neems of race above own or individual. Dark Shamanism, will not be discussed, as it hold no relevancy. The first, most simple form of Shamans, Elemental, is\nbased on making connections to the Elemental Plane and spirits within. A shaman of this type, with aid of 'bonded' spitiris, may control elements such as fire or earth that is present nearby in the main realm. It should be noted that this is different for\narcane magic as it needs no connections to the void, simply manipulates already existing. Next form is Youhumans, is much more complex. By moving mage's conscientious into the realm of the Ancestors, these Shamans can contract the forms of those\nchosen as honorous in life, and reside in places connected to ours than others. The long dead like Lur or even Krug (although neber beend one) could be contacted for advice or knowledge and stronger Youhumans can gain blessings from spirits, boosting\nstrength, or courage, being 'boosted' for a time, can't be reproduced on others by these Shamans. Witch healers, more ritualistic, chosen to metal with Immortal Spirits-- Those living in a plane dedicated to mortal aspects of race. Every emotion, ieal, an\nthought can be categorised to spirits, there, and power of such. Sprits are used by Witch Healers to curse and plauge those seen as threats to Shamanistic believes; The can do this on anything living, including animals, plants, and such shamans are held\nin wary consideration by Druids. They may aslo do the same with Elementals, surprisingly, being able to call upon lesser spirits of such to curse whoever wishes. Anther important part of Witch Healers is manufacturing potions, whech, although similar to\nAlchemy, instead focuses on using representative ingredients to certain spirits to call upon power, and needs more thought on pieces indifidual than whole brew. Lastly, there are the farseers, sometimes called Clan Elders by the Orkos,  these shamsn spend\ndays `korhelon the immortal plane in search of enlightenment in culture, and historical matters. They bring their council to the Rex(?) or their rae as a whole, and act as `Yemekar-unn between those two planes. In much same Witch Healers can curse, Farsee\ncan bless plants or animals being able to increase favored attributes such as strength and resilience but aslo more intangible such as hope it is this reason why Farseers are so wildly calued, as these blessings before battles or Orkos duels prove to be\nassests invaluable. For the following section, we'll be referring to the connection of the Farseers to the Spirit Realm, as it is held as the bother the most complex and developed form of the art among those who practise it being onethat these Shamans use\nto constantly transport their consciousnesses to another plane. This forced passage between realms begins when a Farseer cuts off the link between his conciousness and his body, and ends when he, or in turn a sprit controlling him, returns the stream to\nhis mortal person. Unlike other magics, the beginning of Shamanism actually requires the limitation of Mana spent rather than and increase in such. The regulation of Mana usage is viatl in both entering and departing the spirit realm and as suchis vigorou\npractised by all Farseers. To let their mind wander to the place of spirits, the must also almso almost entirely cut off the connection between their mind and ther body leaving only a trickle of Mana as an anchor to return. When they wish to come back,\nthey increase the mana flow to their mortal persona nd their thoughts will begin to travel back to their body. Now that Being said, althought controlling mana plays a massive part in connection to the spirit realms, it isnt so that anbyone can do such may\nactually make this connection. When an aspiring shaman is first taken on a s a student, they will be pit through several trials and tests dictated by their teacher. Although they are sometimes seen as a filter to weed out ther dedicated from the short\nsighted, they are indeed much more; as pupils action in these tests deide whether or not the spirits themselves will allow him or her to move their consiousness into their realm. An intangible filter of sorts is present, at which a group of minor spirits\nregulate the influx of those entering and leaving the SPirit Relam. Those that have been seen bearing postive attributes during these tests may be, for the first time, allowed to enter this new realm. It shoule be noted that the longer a SHaman has been c\nonnecting to the spirit realm for, the eariser it will be for them to pass through the filter without the spirits scrutinihsing over them- and as such it's improtant for these Clan Elder Shamans to do their best to regulate their own actions as honourable\nor otherwise. \n\nTRANSVERSAL\n\nonce shaman has connected to the Spirit realm, an imcomprehendible cariety of circumstnace may occur. For the first few times, chances are their senses will be dulled or non-\nexistant as their mind stuggles with the lack of bodily connection. Their vision may remain pitch black, and the only 'input' the may recieve may be a soft nigeling ffeling of being watched. As time progreses, aspiring Shamans learn to deal with what info\nrmation their given, and soon the senses return, albeit in situations that differ massivlely from those of the Mortal Realm. Their vision may be hued; the would they seen seen fileted as if through colored glass. Hearing may non-existant or may hear cries\nfar away as close as if whispered in their ears. The sense of feel usually comes last for those that travel the spirit realm, and it can be the most confusing of all to deal with. Sometimes they should come acros a vision of a man being slauthered, they\nwould feel the pain of his wounds. It's important for a shaman to differentiate these Empathic feelings from theirown, especially int eh Spirit realm as it's been known to drive some blindly mad. Now, on to what actually accurs in this realm. When a Farse\nFarseer, presumably with full use of his sensed first enters the Spirit realm, they'll fing themselfs most likely in an enviorns they haven't seen yet. It may be a dense forest, or a dank swamp. Either way, a shaman learns quickly to adapt when they\nkorhelon the spirit realm, with them is usually their spirit guide, a creature in a form important to them or their heritage which will lead them through this realm away from, or into, danger depending on the situation. A member of the Ugluk clan may have\na bull, which is famous for them, so on for Lur Wolves or Braduck Rhinos. So led or not by their respective guides, shamans will eventually come across a viion. It may be of the past or future, or twisted present, representing something tht will play a\npart in the development for Orkos or Shamans. These won't be straight-forward; One may see a crying Orkos mother and child, and must decipher its potential meaning. It is then that the aFarseer's real skill is discovered; the ability to lean from these\n[!] (Whoops, it seems a few pages got mixed in.)\n\nBeoir, beoir, beoir oz Dwedmar. Kazak, Kazak, krazdran nar karh. Narvak, Narvak, Narvak oz Dwedmar, yemka rym anartos Khronammoruk!\n\nDue recompense is deserved.\nsmall snippets of information and then advise to their leaders or people, for or against potential actions bring massive consequenses for their race. Another form of visions, much rarer in comparison to these off events, are those brought forth by a spirt\nhimself. These are no tricks to be deciphered; if a spirit goes through enough effort to force a Shaman into a vision, their vision will be straightforward and condemning. Usually, these occur when the Spirit feels as if influencing the mortal realm could\nbe heightend, and call upon the aid of Shamans to spread their influence. The shaman has no choice in the matter, but stronger in the way of words may be able to convince nagging spirits to change ther minds on matters which may be immpossible, or consequ\nential to do. Last but not least we come to a Shamans real use in Orkos culter- their ability to alter the mortal realm. As said earlier, each sect Shamanism has their own ways of doing it; Elementals meddle with nearmby Elementals, Youhumans by blessings\nWitch-healers by cursing others, or making concotions, and Farseers by blessing others in need. Usually these things are gone about in similar ways. Elementals myst bind themselves to an Elemental, first impressing them by going on certain quests to draw\ntheir attention. Then, they promise the Spirit something it seeks that they can give, and a pact will be made. As more Elemental Spirits are boned to, certain elements may be hindered. Like if one Shaman has bonded to both fire and water, or earth and\nlightning, it's up to the SHaman to decide what to sacrifice, or if instead they'll focus on only one element to become most proficient at it above others. Youhumans go about creating their influence similarly, calling upon Ancestral Spirits to meet with,\nand then they'll try and gain favor by promises of impressive feats or proof of past honour. Once a spirit agrees, they will temporaryly bind their essense to the shaman; Giving them massively increased attributes such as strength or breavery for a hort\ntime to turn the tide of battle.\"\n\n\"Volume two for the rest.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Shamanism 2", "Eirik Ireheart", "Notice: These books are rushed copies of tomes in the Library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. The following is in no way a complete nor perfect copy of said book.\n\"The more they do this, the more word of their feats will spread among the Ancestral plan and more likely it is for these Spirits to acept their deals. Witch-healers go about things differently. During rituals, they'll present certain objects which hold\nrelevance to spirits they are trying to evoke. Should they be trying to create a potion that causes insatiable hunger, they would need something akin to the stomache of a large animal, like a bull, or burn and char large amounts of 'savories' in hopes of\ngluttonous and avaricious spirits. should they do so, they'll begin to call to their desired spirits in the tongue of Old Orkosian, asking for their aid and primising the representative attributes will be more promenent somehow after the usage of potions.\nShould the spirit agree, the mix will be cursed, and the Witch-Healer can make use of it at-will on his victims. However, these Shamans must take care, as it's sometimes not apparent how the spirit cursed the potion, and unintended affects are rampant in\nnovice brew. Finally, farseers blessings are similar to that of the Youhumans in the way that it requires bladed tongue an wit to convince the spirits to give them their boon. When Farsers decide he wishes to bless something, he must travel to the spirit\nrealm and call the name of the spirit with the representative attribute he needs for the blessing. Should it answer, the Farseer must convince it that the blessing will benefit it. If it fails, the farseer must fight the spirit to make the blessing. Very\ndangerous, done only in desperate times, as when a shaman dies in the SPirit realm, he dies in real life. Once he's convinced the Spirit of the need of the blessing, or bested him in single combat, it will then begin to take over his body. Back in the\nmortal realm, his body will move on its own, and words in Old Orkosian will be said to give the blessing direction. a mist, hued the color representative of the spirit, will poor from all orifices to accompass the individual to be blessed. When finished,\nthe shaman need only to return to his body and admire the handiwork, the fabric of reality being shifted in his favor, albeit very little.\"\n\n[!] *A small ink drawing of an Ork vomitting clouds has been comically drawn here.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Sheet Music: 433", "Heruza", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Shiranui", "Leyu", "The Legend of Shiranui\nAct one: scene opens on the small town of Kamui :: narrator: This is the small town of Kamui, home of the great warrior Nagi :: Nagi comes and begins training :: ::Narrator: unlike most small towns, this was not a\npeaceful one ::Narrator: Every year a maiden would be selected from the town to be sacrificed to Orochi, a horrible beast ::::Narrator: the day of the selection was drawing close, and Nagi was worried that :: Nami, his love, would be chosen :: Old man\nOrange approaches Nagi :: Old Man Orange: Nagi! Great warrior of Kamui ! As you know, the day of the selection draws near, and there is a fearsome white wolf-beast who roams the town at night. We fear he is a servant of Orochi. He must be slain! ::\nNagi: Of course, Old Man Orange, I shall slay the beast tonight! He shall not see the light of tomorrow! :: Old Man Orange: Good. Good. I know that the beast will be no match for you! :: Old Man Orange leaves Nagi to his training :: Nami approaches Nagi\n:: Nami: Nagi, my love, the night of the selection approaches! I am concerned about being sacrificed to that horrible beast. ::Nagi: do not worry, Nami. All the maidens concern themselves with this every year. You will not be chosen. :: Nami: I\nthink you are right. Farewell my love. :: leaves Nagi to his training, while Nagi goes in his home :: Night falls over Kamui, and Shiranui comes out and paces the road :: Nagi appears and stands before Shiranui :: Nagi: Foul beast! I shall slay you\ntonight! :: Shiranui growls and bares his fangs at Nagi :: the two fight, with Shiranui eventually defeating Nagi :: Nagi: urgh..... your power... where does it come from? :: Shiranui disapears into the night, and Nagi drags himself to his home :: The\nsun rises over Kamui ::Old Man Orange approaches Nagi :: Old Man Orange: Nagi! I trust that you slayed the beast last night. :: Nagi: No... he defeated me.. :: Old Man Orange: What?? The great warrior defeated? What has happened to the world? It has\ndescended into madness! :: Nagi: Do not worry. I shall fight the beast every night until it is slain! :: ::Narrator: Nagi fought the beast ever night until the night of the selection came . The white arrow marking the home of the maiden to be sacrificed\nflew into Nami's home. :: Nagi runs to Nami :: Nagi: No! My love! Do not go! :: Nami: I must, lest the beast lay ruin to the town :: Nami puts on the sacrificial gowns and leaves for Orochi's lair :: Nagi comes after her and enters the beast's lair ::\nNagi slowly approaches a great stone circle with a bell in the center :: Orochi (unseen): Mortal! Who are you? You are not my sacrifice! :: Nagi: I am Nagi! The great warrior of Kamui! You shall not have Nami, my love! :: Orochi: Fool! You shall\nfeel my wrath for interrupting my sacrifice :: Oroch shows himself, with all his heads looking threateningly at Nagi :: Orochi and Nagi fight, Orochii knocks Nagi to the ground :: Orochi: Hah, mortal! You are no match for me! :: as Orochi is about to\ndeal the final blow, Shiranui attacks his head, saving Nagi :: Shiranui stands before Nagi, protecting him from Orochi's attacks :: Nagi stands up :: Nagi: Orochi! We shall slay you! (raises sword into the air) :: the three of them fight, with Shiranui\nand Nagi winning :: as Nagi and Shiranui are about to deal the final blow, Orochi wounds Shiranui, and knocks him to the ground, while Nagi delivers the final blow, slicing off all 8 of Orochi's heads :: Nami is brought into the chamber to be\nsacrificed, and sees Nagi and Orochi's body She runs to Nagi :: Nami: Nagi! You defeated him! :: Nagi: It was not just me, my love. The wolf- (sees Shiranui on ground) :: Nagi runs to Shiranui with Nami coming behind :: Nagi carries the wolf back to\nKamui :: Nagi, Nami and Old man Orange are gathered around Shiranui :: Old Man Orange: We distrusted this wolf... and he was our only ally. We shall erect a temple and a statue to honor his sacrifice! :: Shiranui licks Nagi's and Old Man Orange's feet\nbefore closing his eyes :: last scene shows the statue of Shiranui\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("SHIT BOW", "Ivan Zvonimir", "DON'T USE SWORDS ON FISTS\nDON'T USE SWORDS ON ISTS\nDON'T USE SWORDS ON FISTS\nDON'T USE SWORDS ON FISTS\n\nSHIT BOW", ""),
        StaticBook("Short Poems", "Garsto Leaf", "{-----------------}           Short Poems\n{-----------------}Miri it is while sumer i-last\nWith foulës song;\nOc now neghëth windës blast\nAnd weder strong.\nEi, ei, what this night is long,\nAnd Ich with wel michel wrong\nSorwe and murne and fast.\nWalking in the Fog\n---------------\nWalking in the fog\nOne of my favorite things\nAlmost like catching glimpses\nOf a million angel wings\nA mystical, magical feeling Envelopes the senses and the heartImages of castles standing stately and knights in armor do\nimpart\nThe howling calling of the beast\nThat falls in unknown lair\nImagined as in fairy tales\nBut only if you dareThe white steed crosses unseen streams\nThe fog it tricks the eye The wonder of the veil of white Underneath a clear blue sky.\nRed Moon Valley\n--------------\nShe rode deep into the wild red moon valley\nhorse’s chest heaving between her legs\ncherry trees whipped at her face\nas she flew into the viscous \nanguished amber sun \nlost in what had\ncome before\nHe strode to the forefront before a host of Gael\nair thick with fetid odor of sweat and fear\nfire arrows slipped past his head\nas he drew into slaughtered\nembattled emerald field\nfound in the blood\nto become\nSword was laid in a sheath of silken white lace\ndried tears unmoving on shattered visage\nof her colorless and despondent face\nshe held his favor rent and torn\necho of his distant laugh\na smile embraced\nan instant\never.\nThe Raid\n--------\nthe din of war, weary is the army\nthe feast of fasting ravens\nglory at home here, gory death\nseas of the sacrifice of men skies red, with rolling flames\nthe town burns so bright raping and raiding the spoils of\nwar\nvast gold 'n glory in the hall we feast and sing of the beast meadows of mead and meat\nthe skald was well paid, to pen the praise \nhis coffers were full of coin.\n[!]\nA Surprisingly good sketch which goes with the poem is on this page.\n                  [!]\n                  \n                  [!]\nA Signature which appears to be showing who drew the picture...\n                  [!]\nHorns and Armour\n----------------\nLight laps in a windblown skirt\ndancing from land’s fallen grace\nWhile oars rake through a fog bank\nand slice slick in a blackened face Rage heaves the dragons head\nexhausted of limbs it once held\nDemons race thick in each mind\nas warriors glance back at the felled Red congealed like dripping rubies\na sword glistens of muscle and fat\nStrewn are the horns and armor\nat thy brother’s back The deck is stained in rich iron and flooded with tempest\nthought\nFoul weather carries scent of battle\nas honor of victory is sought.\n\n                   [!]\nOnce again the same signature from before showing who wrote the book.          [!]\n/By Garsto Leaf/\n[!] Is Written at the bottom of the page.[!]\n((OOC: I didnt write these poems. I found them on the internet but thought they were pretty cool and thought it would be even cooler if there was a book with them ingame! Hope you enjoyed!))", ""),
        StaticBook("Short Poems", "Henry Winterleaf", "Henry's book of Rhymes.\n\n\nThe following is a collection of short poems by Henry Winterleaf.\n\nContains rude language.\n1) Snoring Man\n\nThere once was a young man from Oren.\nWho had a big problem with snoring.\nWhen he went to his bed.\nAnd lay down his head.\nNoise from his mouth would come pouring.\n2) Nightime stroll\n\nI was walking alone one night.\nWhen I was given a sudden fright.\nA man by the trees.\nWas stung by a bee.\nAnd he suddeny swore \"oh shite!\"\n3)Boredom\n\nPretending i'm paying attention.\nAnd hoping nobody will mention.\nThat a don't have a clue.\nWhat they want me to do.\nAs that would cause me much tension.\n4)Sunshine\n\nGolden rays of light.\nFades away at night.\nGrants the world with life.\nPiercing like a knife.\nIlluminating many places.\nSheding light on many faces.\nIf we didn't have the sun.\nAll of life would soon be done.\n7) Endings\n\nEverything must end.\nEven family and friends.\nBut don't be sad it's gone.\nJust try to carry on.\nMemories stay forever.\nFor you to feel whenever.", ""),
        StaticBook("Short stories", "Aywen Morin", "The Wolf in Sheep's Clothing \n\nA Wolf was having trouble getting at a herd of sheep because of how well the shepherd and his dogs watched them.\nBut one day the Wolf found the skin of a sheep that had already been killed. He put it on over its own pelt and strolled down among the sheep.\nLeading the Lamb away, he soon made a meal of her, and for quite some time he succeeded in deceiving the other sheep too and making hearty meals of them.\n\n       The End\nThe Glow Worm and the Daw \n\nA jackdaw (a crow-like bird) once ran up to a glow-worm (a glowing beetle) and was about to seize him. \"Wait a moment, good friend,\" said the worm; \"and you shall hear something to your advantage.\"\nAh! what is it?\" said the daw. \"I am but one of the many glow-worms that live in this forest. If you wish to have them all, follow me,\" said the glowworm.\n\n\"Certainly!\" said the daw.\nThen the glow-worm led him to a place in the wood where a fire had been kindled by some woodmen, and pointing to the sparks flying about, said, \"There you'll find the glow-worms warming themselves round a fire.\nWhen you have done with them, I shall show you some more, at a distance from this place.\" The daw darted at the sparks, and tried to swallow some of them;\nbut his mouth being burnt by the attempt, he ran away exclaiming, \"Ah, the glow-worm is a dangerous little creature!\"\n\nSaid the glow-worm with pride, \"Wickedness yields to wisdom!\"\n\n       The End\nThe Ass and His Purchaser\n\nA man wished to purchase an Ass (a Donkey), and decided to give the animal a test before buying him. He took the Ass home and put him in the field with his other Asses.\nThe new Ass strayed from the others to join the one that was the laziest and the biggest eater of them all. Seeing this, the man led him back to his owner.\nWhen the owner asked how he could have tested the Ass in such a short time, the man answered, \"I didn't even need to see how he worked. I knew he would be just like the one he chose to be his friend.\"\nThe Hawk and the Nightingale\n\nA Nightingale, perched on an oak, was spotted by a Hawk, who swooped down and snatched him.\nThe Nightingale begged the Hawk to let him go, insisting he wasn't big enough to satisfy the hunger of a Hawk, who ought to pursue bigger birds.\nThe Hawk said, \"I'd be crazy to release a bird I've already caught in favor of birds I don't even yet see.\"\n\n       The End\nThe Lion and the Mouse\n\nA Lion was awakened by a Mouse running over his face. Rising up angrily, the Lion caught the Mouse and was about to kill him, when the Mouse begged, \"If you would only spare my life, I would be sure to repay your kindness.\"\nThe Lion laughed at the idea of the Mouse being able to repay a favor but let him go. Later, the Lion was caught by some hunters, who bound him with strong ropes to the ground.\nThe Mouse, recognizing the Lion's roar, came and gnawed the rope with his teeth and set him free, exclaiming: \"You ridiculed the idea of my ever being able to help you; now you know that it is possible for even a tiny Mouse to do something for a Lion.\"\nThe Crow and the Pitcher  \nA Crow was dying of thirst when he saw a pitcher. Hoping to find water, he flew to it with delight. When he reached it, he discovered to his grief that it was only one-quarter full.\nThe level of the water was so low that he could not possibly get at it. The spout was too narrow, and he too big.\n\nAnd he knew that if he tipped the pitcher over, the water would spill out before he could drink it.\nHe thought and thought. Finally, he had an idea. He collected as many stones as he could carry and dropped them one by one with his beak into the pitcher.\nWith each stone, the level of the water rose higher and higher until it came within his reach. Thus he saved his life.\n\n       The End\nThe Shepherd's Boy and the Wolf\n\nA Shepherd-boy, who watched over a flock of sheep near a village, amused himself three or four times by crying out, “Help! Wolf!”\nWhen his neighbors came to help him, he laughed at them for being so gullible. However, one day the wolf did come.\nThe Shepherd-boy, now terrified, shouted: “Please come and help! The Wolf is killing the sheep.” But no one came to help or even paid attention to his cries. The Wolf, having nothing to fear, took his time destroying the whole flock.\n         The End\nThe Fox and The Leopard\n\nThe Fox and the Leopard argued about who was the more beautiful of the two. The Leopard showed off the beautiful spots that decorated his coat.\nthe Fox, interrupting him, said: \"No, I'm the more beautiful, because my beauty is of the mind.\"\n\n\n       The End", ""),
        StaticBook("Short Tales.", "Aepholis", "Short Tales For Children.\n\nThis book is dedicated to my daughter, Ariella. I wrote these tales for her.\nThe Tale Of Strongman Silus.\n\nOnce upon a time, a large man lived in Athera, in a cottage, next to Alras. He enjoyed lifting rocks, to gain muscular weight, which of course, ended up making him become the strongest man in\nAthera. People constantly asked him to lift things for them, such as stones, wooden stumps, and so forth. Strongman Silus got tired of it one day, and decided to take his retreat from being strong, ending up becoming very big. More and more people\nstarted to be mean to Silus, until a small girl came over to his house to ask him to lift a small rock for her. Silus nodded in his doorway, as he walked down a road with the child. She pointed at the rather small rock, and Silus picked it up with\nlittle effort. The girl was extremely happy, and gave Silus a tight hug, as she played with the stone. Silus sighed, as he missed the days where he could lift heavier things. So he started training again, and eventually became strong once more.\nPeople started to respect him more, asking him for the same favor as they had done when he was strong before, and Silus became a happy man, and found a woman that he married, and had a few kids.\n\nThat is the tale of Silus the strongman.\nThe Big Bad Wolf\n\nOnce upon a time, in the Withering Woods, a small girl named Aeri was walking down a road. She suddenly met a large wolf on the road, that growled at her, drool foaming out of his fanged mouth, the teeth as big as knives.\nThe child drew her small dagger, tightening the grip of the hold, as the wolf approached her. Suddenly, the wolf kneeled down, laying in the middle of the road. The girl raised an eyebrow, as she kneeled, slowly moving to gently pet the wolf.\nSoon, the girl had tamed the wolf, and rode it as it got bigger, as people started praising her, calling her the Wolf Girl. And that is the end of the tale of the wolf and the girl.\nTheodore Thumblefinger.\n\nA cold summer breeze entered the window, as Theodore woke up, rubbing his large, purple eyes. He rubbed his feet, putting on his usual ragged coat, along with his coffee stained shirt. He grabbed\nhis straw hat, as he headed down, starting to cook himself a big and fattening dinner, like most halflings do. Eggs, salted meat, sausages, beef, along with some steamed vegetables. He finished his meal, grabbing his fine hiking staff, as he headed out.\nA inn gazed before his view, filled with customers, as he smiles, entering. He took a seat near a group of two lovely women, as he blushed a little, ordering a honey whiskey. The ladies started to chat him up, asking for his name and such.\nTheodore, of course, being a very handsome halfling, fixed his straw hat, his cheek red as an apple. The ladies made leave, as Theodore was left alone, finishing his drink, before heading out, a large happy smirk on his face. A good day had ended.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shreck's Swamp", "Daniel Ward", "A Boy Who Wandered into Shreck's Swamp\n\nThere once was a little boy named Guy DeBar who lusted for adventure. One day he stumbled across a majestic swamp, Shreck's swamp. That was a /very/ shitty decision as Shreck is very territorial\nand strong.\n\nAnyways, Shreck stomped up to the boy with his mighty orkish feet and bellowed, \"Geht outta mah swump!\" The boy stood there, his legs trembling in fear as he gazed upon the glorious ork.\nAs he did not move the fuck out of the way Shreck fucking ate the shit out of him. This is why you never go into Shreck's Swamp.\n\nTHE END", ""),
        StaticBook("Siege of Tar'sil", "Azkel Frostbeard", "On the cold winter day, the Second Seige on Tar'sil had begun. The Grand Prince Aethir Tundrak stood at his cities gates, fellow snow elves and dwarves behind him. In the distance, hundreds of orcs could be seen rallying, setting up trebuchets.\nAs the Orcs started their march, the dwarves manned the ballistas, ready to defend their ally. The Orcs bursted out into a full on charge towards the city, their archers shooting at any target in site. Dwarves and Snow Elves\nlined the walls with archers, hoping to defend for as long as possible. The ballistas rained down fire at the trebuchets, hoping to disable them before they could hit the city walls. One after another, the ballistas were either broken or destroyed by the\narrows shot by the Orcs. As the infantry rallied at the gate, ready for the Orcs, the mercenary group Dunamis stormed the back wall of the city, using their skills to scale the wall. Seeing them as an immediate threat, the infantry charged towards the\nelite fighters. With the forces split in half, the Orcs blasted a hole through the front wall. The Grand Prince saw the threat, and ordered all forces to retreat to the palace for a final stand. Dwarves and Snow Elves raced towards the palace, but their\nefforts werent good enough. The Orcs and their allies has surrounded the Dwarves and Snow Elves, leaving them to fight for their lives. The Grand Prince could now see,  the city was lost. To prevent further deaths, he gave the\ncommand for all living forces to retreat to Kal'Kash, where the Snow Elves were offered refuge after their home was taken. After many years of building and fortifying Tar'Sil, the city was lost.", ""),
        StaticBook("Siege Weapons", "timzuiderveld", "* A fairly accurate drawing of two catapults in a forest fills this page, there is a road going between them the inscription below reads: \"Two catapults on road to Urguan, near Barbek Hold \" *\n* A detailed sketch of the Blackmaul crossing wall fills this page the inscription below reads \"Blackmaul crossing, ~1 or two guards\" *\n* A rough sketch of the Vaerhaven gate fills this page, the inscription below reads \"Vaerhaven gates, features internal drawbridge, Vaerhaven bought materials for ~4 ballistae\" *\n* A fairly detailed sketch of a dwarven steam ship fills this page the inscription below reads \"Soggy beard: No siege weapons on board\" *\n* A detailed sketch of a dwarven steam ship with a ballista on its deck fills this page, the inscription below reads: \"Frosty Axe, one ballista on top deck\" *\n* A detailed sketch of yet another dwarven steam ship fills this page, it has a big ballista on the front, and a smaller one on the right the inscription below reads \"Thorins wrath: Two Ballistae on top deck\"\n* A sketch of a sailing ship with dark sails fills this page, it has a ballista mounted on its top deck the inscription below reads \"Unknown: One Ballista top deck\" *\n* a vage sketch of a dwarven steam ship off in the distance fills this page, it has barely any details, the inscription below reads \"Unknown: Arnaments unknown\"*\n* A sketch of a ballista on the dwarven docks fills this page, the inscription below reads \"Ballista, dwarven docks\"\n* A sketch of a multiple decked sailing ship fills this page, it has one ballista barely visible on its top decks, and many ballista holes on its sides *\n\"Unknown ship, Ballista, 1\"\n* a sketch of three catapults standing neatly in a line in the snow fills this page*\n\"Kal azgoth Catapuls   One two and three\"\n* A sketch of 4 ballistae standing neatly in a line fills this page, the one on the right is far bigger* \n\"Kal Azgoth Ballistae one two three and four.\"\nSiege weapons Tally\nCatapults: 5\nBallistae: 14\nShip tally\nSoggy beard -0\nFrosty Aexe - 1\nThorins wrath -2\nunknown       -1\nUnknown       -?\nUnknown       -1", ""),
        StaticBook("Sillumir Conduct", "Andria Ith'ael", "Sillumiran Conduct and Regulations\n\n\n              \nBy the Maheral\nAndria Ith'ael\nIndex\nPage hael (3)\n  Preface\nPage kulin (5)\n  Cooperation\nPage esun (8)\n  Valah \nPage telu'oem (11)\n  Mali'aheral\nPage telu'esun (18)\n  Kharajyr\nPage niut'telu (20)\n  Avernan\nPreface\n  Our situation within the new citadel is very different from the times of Annil'sul. We are now within a new land with our allies. Due to this, the Sillumiran are in need of new regulatons to allow us to continue to\nprogress. The children of Larihei shall be safe.\n\n  These regulations shall take affect on the 1st day (oem) of the Deep Cold, in the year 1475. \n\n \n ~Maheral\nCooperation\n  As per our new agreement with House Savoie of Aldersberg, who are the owners of the land we currently reside on. We are to provide milltary assistance if they request it.\n\n  If there is trouble\nwithin their town or land, it is your duty to assist them in the removal of the trouble maker - or threat. \n  You are to cooperate with the guards of the town if required, if you do not trust them, then consider the fact that they gave us\na home.\n\n  However unlikely, in the event of a war, we be obliged to provide to help House Savoie (and House Carrion) in their battles. The Maheral is of the opinion that assistance will not be required often.\nValah\n  As we now live within the lands of the Holy Oren Empire, more specifically the land known as Aldersberg, it is going to be a common occurence to see a Valah approach the gate. Members of both House Savoie and Carrion are to be\ngranted entry if requested.  This also applies to any other member of governence within Aldersberg or Oren.\n\n  The typical proceedure for allowing a Valah entry to the citadel is simple. Simply inquire as to what their\nname is, what their business and/or reason for entering the city, and what weaponry they are carrying. If they seem suspicous or a resident of another nation other than the Holy Oren Empire, further questioning may be needed.\nMali'aheral\n  The Maheral wishes that only the uttermost pure Mali'aheral enter the citadel. The proceedure to allow them entry is similar to that for the Valah, however additonal questions are required.\nUpon the new arrival approaching the gate, one should examine them for strange eye or hair colours, excessive jewelry, or tatoos.\n\n  Examples of 'impure' traits or signs of Mali'ata include dark coloured hair, red or black coloured\neyes, golden jewlery or a severe amount of tatoos. \n\n  It is recommened you do not kill such beings, for we are not on our own land. Instead, let them be unless they continue to approach the gate after being denied.\nIf they are indeed physically pure, you may begin the mental purity test on them. The first question to ask is simply 'Thill ito kae'leh?' or 'Are you pure?' You may provide a translation of the question in Common if they are not influent in the\nElven language. \n\n  After they have sucessfully answered the afforementioned question, you may begin to ask about our society, questions such as 'Who is Larihei Lohmanih?' or 'What does the\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya mean to you?' are adquate questions to provide to the new comer.  \n\n   You may also ask them of their skills or occupation to allow for easier intergration into the citadel.\nIf they sucessfully pass, you may grant them entry. Though let it be known that the Maheral may overturn your judegement at their will.\nKharajyr\n  Kharajyr, much like our allies in the Holy Oren Empire, have not betrayed us. Therefore, as they once lived with us, they are to be granted entry as the Valah are.\n\n  They shall be\nsubject to the same regulations as Valah, though they may need to be protected better due to potential dislike of Kharajyr displayed by the Valah.\nAvernan\n  Avernan - simply meaning 'wanderer' or 'confused person' in our language, refers to those who are not permitted the citadel without the permission of the Maheral or are banished from our blessed society.\nAvernan include Mali'ame, Mali'ker, Bortu and Uruk. All of which, with the exception of some of the Mali'ker and Mali'ame, are to not be granted at any time. Not even the Maheral may grant an Uruk entry.\n\n  If one of the\nafforementioned beings requests entry, you may contact the Maheral for judgement of the situation or check if their name is the list of permitted Avernan, for there are few who are not associated with the nation of Laureh'lin.\nay'Haelun'or Larihei'ehya\nay'maehr'sae hiylun'ehya\n  Sillumiran, always remember your sacifice and your vows. Protect the children of Larihei.\n\n~Andria Ith'ael, Maheral of the Mali'thill", ""),
        StaticBook("Sin of Betrayal", "Unknown", "Itnan, 30th of Snows Maiden, 1304.\nPhilosophies and thoughts written by Lady Bell while recovering from injuries.\nThis age is troubled and like many around me, I fear our troubles will not soon pass. The curse which Iblees is\nsaid to have placed upon our world is raising up, increasing in power and growing\nmore and more obvious by the day. Our ancestors committed their own sins during the fight with Iblees, pushed into these horrible things by the monster which devastated\nAegis. And indeed, those sins which they each committed were made worse by the curses Iblees placed upon them and all of their descendents.\nTo the humans, to Horen, his sin was envy and lust for the future. Never did he see his works completed and\nnever would his sons see their's. To the dwarves, to Urguan, his sin was greed and gluttony, a neverending hunger for gems and wealth. Never would he be satisfied and never would his sons.\nTo the elves, to Malin, his sin was Pride, an innocent seeming\nwish for more\nchildren to fill his trees with laughter and the books with words. Never would he have the children he so desired and neither would his sons.\nTo the orcs, to Krug...the only one he could not tempt or taint. The only one\nwho stood up against him for so long. To Krug, for denying Iblees for so long, he cursed him with the sins of lust and wrath, to always wish for war and strife against his brothers and their sons.\nBut the sin which infected all of the descendents\nequally, which touched all of Man and all of the original descendents...was the sin of Betrayal. This sin, this curse, would be one which could never be escaped, never be forgotten. To this very day, it still haunts us...\nAnd due to it, I lie\nhere, racked with pain in my bed in the Mage's Tower. Betrayal is a sin I cannot abide, and trust is a thing I can no longer give so freely as I once\ndid.  I have seen so much betrayal, from all kinds... All races, all beings.  \nFrom the Orcs,\nBrunhyldir, the great Betrayer. Once a member of the Ascended, he turned coat during an offensive battle at the undead outpost, one led by the Ascended. He attack the Master Sage, Riizu, wounding him badly before being cut down. The\nUndead took them with him from the battlefield and I can only surmise he has joined them, in the name of Iblees. A traitor too far gone, given too much trust in too little time with too little reason...\nFrom the Elves, Mayctor... A betrayer of his own\nkind and the trust of all of Aegis, an Iblees worshipper to the core. He haunts me even now, having failed at cutting me down the last time he attempt to do so. The High Prince, in his naivete, trusted this...\"man\" with the run of the Sentinels, and in\ndoing so he was able to corrupt many, many of the Elves before I uncovered his evil. Too much trust given to a man who had done nothing to earn it and too many lives ruined by such a fool.\nFrom the Dwarves, I have seen many Iblees\nworshippers, but what worries me most is the betrayal of a friend of mine, Algor... I trusted him with things, I assisted him, I gave him my support and backing. Yet I find him on the road, robbing people of their money. For what reason but petty greed\nwould he do such a thing? I trusted him too easily, and in the process nearly allowed innocents to fall prey to him.\nFrom the Humans, the betrayal which stings the most for me, personally. Ademas...what have you become, I ask myself? For it is\nbecause of you that I lie here in my bed, barely awake and struggling to stay coherent. I placed all of my trust in you, perhaps more than anyone else. Even in your most incoherent states I would believe in you and your strength. Yet...was it I who\nbetrayed you, my old friend? For you, I would have died. For you, I would have run across all of Aegis, to the Nether and back, as I have very nearly done several times now. Yet I failed in saving you from your torment. My life was not taken, I did not\nrescue you... For that, did you attempt to slay me? For you, whom I might have…\nI will stand for my weakness and for this sin no longer.\nThe only ones who have escaped it appear to be the undead...or is their betrayal yet to come? They are all\nbetrayers of their own kind, in the end, having joined Iblees in exchange for the dark magic they now wield. Their souls are damned and they aim to damn the rest of ours as well. My trust cannot be given so freely any longer. I know too\nmany things\nnow. And betrayals cannot be taken so lightly any longer. Those who betray their brethren, who betray Aegis... They will fall. I will make them fall. I will trust no one any longer. My trust and my hopes now lie only in the hands of the Arcane Mage. And\nto Hwaldar, who has betrayed the one I now place my trust in... I will hunt you down like the rat you are.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sincere Apology", "Kochek Frioli", "My dearest apologies, dear Auberon. I knew not what my actions would cause, and I am a complete and utter idiot. I will tend to your wounds if you so wish it, I will forever be indebted to you. I shall pay my dos and pray for four days, three as required\nand one more for my personal sake. If you should seek anything more, just call upon me.\n\nSincerely,\nVincent Voronwe", ""),
        StaticBook("Sins of Alchemy", "Sarrion", "Alchemy: Homunculus and Chimeras\n-------------------From: Tales of a Traveling Alchemist\n\nRe-Written by:\n Sarrion di' Pascali\nNow then, faithful student, a word on the dreaded Homunculus and grotesque Chimeras. If I were to speak to you, and I am sure you have picked this up quite easily, I would speaking in a grave tone about this subject, for it is one\nfilled with torment and grief. The Homunculus, a cunning creature, is what one may refer to as a “man” but in fact, this is further from the truth than one could possibly imagine. It is the creation of the hands of man, hands that wish to pull the puppet\nstrings normally reserved for the gods and craft life. Chimeras are, in fact, an earlier form of this “flesh-crafting” in the fact that they are a combination of two, or more, animals. If this practice has disturbed\nyou, please remove your eyes from these pages and go on to the next chapter, but if you are one with a stout heart and strong constitution, then do persist.\n-------------------\n=[Homunculus:]=\nBred from the insane practice of creating life, these creatures show little fear and are as twisted as the ways to create them. The facts, or so I am told for it is more of a legend than factual truth, is that the first homunculus\nwas born through a failure to resurrect a person. Although I tend to reject “stories” that circulate around communites in which alchemy is present, since they tend to tell of silly fables such as an elixir of immortality\nand a “cure-all”, but this particular legend seems to hold quite a bit of truth. These “accidents”, as you may wish to call them, are often twisted in appearance at times and unlike a golem, they are quite alive. Whereas a golem tends\nto have a master and does not reason like the intelligent races, the homunculus is capable of acting out on its own accord, and is certainly capable of higher thinking. Further evidence to support this as a failure\nto make life, or “resurrect” a loved one, is that they are very limited in things such as conscience, and empathy. Truly these are apathetic, and sometimes even wicked, creatures that care not for a life and seem to\nseek purpose in the world. Those who cannot find purpose, make one in often outrageous and violent forms.\n\nIt should be noted, to any who desire a homunculus\nthat their minds are often fractured and broken. They are bi-polar and spontaneous beings that seldom act in a favorable fashion. But fret-not, for if you desire one of these creatures, and you manage to make one,\nthere are ways to combat their insanity. There are numerous serums capable of soothing the mind, and almost any of the stronger will work on these beings. But do be warned, if you plan on fighting\na homunculus you had better have a blade handy.\n\nA homunculus, bred of magic and the folly of man, is naturally resistant to numerous forms of magic. Now if you desire to know why this is the fact,\nyou must simply compare its origins with ours. The Orcs are naturally less susceptible to the heat, for they have grown accustomed to the searing sands of their desert. The people of Hanseti are naturally capable of withstanding\nthe cold far better than; let’s say, a wood elf, for they have grown accustomed to their frigid homeland. Therefore, a homunculus, a creature born of magical means is naturally capable of withstanding magic.\nWith that said, they still bleed like anything else there is in Asulon and they do feel pain. Although their erratic behavior could prove to be quite troublesome, as their tactics could shift suddenly,\nand the pain will most likely have little effect on them, even if they feel it. Finally, as they are naturally resistant to magic some potions may have little to no effect on them.\nCrafting a homunculus is a difficult procedure for numerous reasons, the foremost being there’s multiple methods that all have their different dangers, but it is one that is possible with both determination and, perhaps, a touch of madness.\nIf you are an alchemist seeking the fabled Elixir of Life or the Philosopher’s Stone then you, most likely, have already produced several, if not many, homunculus in your research. A homunculus can be produced\nby attempted to resurrect someone if the proper condition are met, such as powerful materials and a faulty Philosopher’s Stone, or perhaps attempting to create Takwin, artificial life. I cannot go into specific detail into how a homunculus\nis made exactly, for the methods that do not include the sacrifice of an individual, corpses, and drake hearts are few to none, I can on the other hand provide the last way,\nthat is known and has been seen by me, to craft a homunculus. Although this way is gruesome, and often accidental, I have seen men turned into these monsters by the ingesting of, what they believed to be,\nthe Elixir of Life. This potion, said to grant immortality, has been researched and sought after for centuries and centuries by skilled alchemists and it often ends with either their death, or the gruesome fate of transforming\ninto a deformed homunculus. Truly a horror to watch, and it is a lovely thing that this topic is over with. Although I could do not provide exact information in how to create a homunculus, I do hope this information has aided you.\n=[Chimera:]=\nNow then, the Chimera, unlike the cunning homunculus, is a much simpler creature forged from the combination of two or more animals. With that said, it should be known that chimeras are often unstable creations, prone to decay\nand eventual death early on in their creation making their usefulness quite limited. An average chimera may only last a few months, but there have been whispers of some living for years on end, and even of ancient chimeras built by the\nancestors with only the most perfect specimens. Of course these are only rumor, and must be taken with several grains of salt. Now you might ask, how exactly does one combine many different forms of life into one and the simply answer is, you do not.\nThe reason I state that you do not, is simply because the chimera is proof that it is impossible and not meant for this world. The chimera, upon its creation, is a damned creature in which nature spits upon. The fact that it dies within the first few\nmonths of its creations, and its overall form is filled with decay and blemish, is proof enough that whatever creatures may make it are not meant to be put together in that fashion, or in any fashion to be exact.\nIt is true that many believe the alchemical process that one must go through to craft these abominations is an unholy one, but I believe it to be a purely scientific one. The hypothesis being that if I were to fuse a wolf, a snake,\nand perhaps a sheep together, the product would be better than all three, but the fact of the matter is that this hypothesis is incorrect. Fusing these three animals together through the use of heavily earth and water\ncentered potions produced a monster of an animal that has little thought, obeys its master’s simplest commands, and falls apart at the seams within three months of its creation.\nWhich leads me to the creation of these strange, twisted beings, for the creation is not a matter of balance, but in-fact, imbalance. I say imbalance for the chimera, as far as I know, has never been crafted with the principle of Equivalent\nExchange being fully satisfied. Chimeras are often only created with partial satisfaction to this principle, causing them to become twisted and rot rather easily. Now one may ask themselves why exactly we are not capable of taking the animals\nof our desire, taking strong enough symbols of the elements, and fusing these animals together in perfect synergy and balance. The simple answer is, life was not ours to create and attempting to craft something that was not meant to be simply results\nin imbalance. This could be compared to introducing wolves to a forest that knows not of this animal. The rabbits, deer, and whatever have you would be thrown into disarray from this new predator. Much like this example,\nthe natural order is thrown into chaos when chimeras are crafted and therefore balance cannot be achieved. This is why some chimeras simply never come to be. But, as I have seen with my own eyes, if one’s\ningredients and will are strong enough, a Chimera can be born, no matter how imperfect it is to the eyes of the natural world.\n\nIf one wished to craft one of these strange and disgusting monsters, they would require\nstrong symbols of the Earth and Water, for animals fall under the domain of earth and life under the domain of water. Using these symbols, you would have to craft a large quantity of this potion with a base\nas equally strong as these symbols so that their power is not diluted from not being able to reach their full potential in a weaker base. One would need pour this potion into a body of water big enough to submerge\nthe two or more animals you wish to fuse and let sit for an hour so that everything may settle and balance. After allowing the potion to sit, simply dip the animals you wish to fuse into the body of water and after\na rather gorgeous lightshow you will either fill the body of water with gore, or produce a monster. Either way, you may have either shamed your colleges or produced a breakthrough, depending on your outlook.", ""),
        StaticBook("Slaves for ranso", "Bud'Raguk", "Aiyla Torena\n\n\nPeople taking care of me:\n\nDamai [Jarwquin]\nRav [Funny981]\nyelfir [_Owen]\nAra [Lady Rebecca]\nCaern\n\nMy carer is Fawynn.\n\n(ThatWeirdGirl)\n\nLucus (assassincookie9)\n\nI ave' no parents...", ""),
        StaticBook("Small note", "Guarger Tsouderous", "Here is what you requested. If you have a issue with any of it, feel free to contact me. We will keep in touch during this. And remember,    Don't not fail me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Smurgla's Poem", "Smurgla", "Everyone have a purpose. Love yourself.\n\nEveryone have a trooth. Believe yourself.\n\nEveryone have a voice. Listen to yourself.\nEveryone have a friend inside. Trust yourself.\n\nEveryone have a path to walk. Follow yourself.\n\nEveryone have a purpose. Stick to yourself.\nEveryone have a reason. Do not listen to no one else for yourself is all that matters.", ""),
        StaticBook("Smurgla's Task", "Smurgla", "Smurgla's Task\n\nSmurgla has gone to the Mali'Aheral city and scattered four good amounts of bonemeal about, being accompanied by a guard, of course. Smurgla has allowed for more flowers and grass to appear!\nSmurgla has visited Aesterwald now, planting a flower every so often, but not in the snow! Smurgla met a few nice people and taught them about nature's important.\nSmurgla planted regrew some dirt back to grass and Smurgla cleaned up some yucky grass near Orcies' cities. Smurgla had no one to sign off on this one.\nSmurlga made grass grow in yucky cave near D'orf city. D'rofs try to kill Smurgla, though, so Smurgla had to do Drood task in cave. No one to sign off on this one.\nSmurgla used the last few pieces of bonemeal in the Drood's grove, itself. Smurgla thinks it is best to give back to where your roots are from. Smurgla planted a few flowers near the gate.\nSignatures:\n\nMali'Aheral:\n-- Talimeracahe\n\nAesterwald:\n-- Haleth MII", ""),
        StaticBook("Snaak Shawpin", "WhiteMale", "-------------------------------------- \n\n\n\n       Shawpin\n         Fawr\n        Snaakz\n\n\n\n\n-------------------------------------\nAy am mi,\nMi'z naem izt Wag.\n\nAy ztuhf znaakz\nentu mai buhrlap bawg.\n\nUf durrz a ztruguhl,\nAy hit dim wid a zhuvel.\n\nAgh uf dimz pruhtezt,\nAy znap dimz lihtul nekz.\n\nZneeky znaakz,\nawl tri tu hide.\n\nFruhm da\nznaakiez gehnazeid!\n\nBuh mai peepurz,\ndeh fihn dimz owt.\n\nAy zlazh dimz tummiez,\nagh zpred dimz gutz abowt.\nEet da meetz!\nAgh tan da zkinz!\nAgh mehk da bownz\nentu trazh binz!\n\nKruzh dimz kubz agh\nbran da weivz!\nBuh awl da mehn, dimz\nluze derr leivz!\n\n              -Wag'Ox'Lak\nGlureh tu Krug!\nGlureh tu Theruz!\nGlureh tu Laklul!\nLawng libe Lak!", ""),
        StaticBook("Snacks", "Thurak'Yar", "Snacks\n\nScribed    By The\nFarseer  Thurak\n4'th of     The Amber        Cold,\n1490        Athera.\nThe Halflings, Hobbits, or ‘Snacks’, apparent cross-breed between Humans and Dwarves, have had they physique refined through countless centuries of inbreeding and adaptation to the more than favourable conditions they choose to reside in.\nThe rounded, pleasant fellows who live in their rounded, pleasant holes are welcoming to all but a few, and are marvelled at by the other races for their skill in farming, brewing, and cooking. Although those things are all wonderful about them,\nthere is something else about them that some people do not know; something paramount and yet small, something repulsive, and yet... Delicious. \nAs many Orcs know, Hobbits are delicious. From their tender meat to their well-seasoned offal, a\nHalfling’s insides are excellent for eating in any variety of meals. Today, specifically, however, this particular book will be detailing how to harvest the organs from a Halfling rather than how to use them, which will be addressed in my next book.\nPart One\nThe             Top\n       Layer\n\nSkin. Some people, sadly, overlook the bulging surface of a Halfling’s body, and call it only a wrapper to the delicacies inside; though they are terribly wrong.\nA Hobbit’s rind has several interesting applications which are useful in things like home decoration and food preparation. To first remove a Halfling’s skin, one must make several incisions across the body before flaying it; being careful not to\ndamage or rupture anything inside, as everything is useful if you’re thoughtful enough. The cuts should look as followed...\n*a diagram has been drawn below, detailing where cuts should be made to correctly skin a Halfling*\n\n        \n         { }\n      /(X X)\\\n        \\ . /\n        _|  |_\nThe skin may then be carefully peeled off and laid out flat, ready for preparation for whatever it is needed for. \nNote: To best use the skin, hang off a rack and wash thoroughly; leaving to dry from four to seven hours.\n*the rest of the book is missing; pages seemingly ripped out without care for the state of the tome. At the end, the book is signed simply, \"For Knox.\"*", ""),
        StaticBook("Snow Hare A&P", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "As a bit of prior information, these will be the main portion of my notes and findings about the anatomy and physiology of the snow hare. It should be made apparent that I am mainly writing and drawing diagrams of this species for the sake of\ncomprehension in the art of conjuration.\n\n   The way that the subject should be tackled is by displaying and explaining the various organ systems within the organism. These systems will include the nervous system, respiratory system, skin, vascular\nsystem, muscular/skeletal system, digestive system, and finally urinary system.\n*There appears to be a bordered line in the shape of a rabbit here. Within the bordered lines appear various threads spiraling out from a brain. It appears to be a detail-oriented diagram of a snow hare's nervous system.*\nNervous System:\n   The nervous system is a combination of the brain, various nerves spread throughout the entire body, as well as the spinal cord which connects them.\n   The purpose of the nervous systems appears to be for directing purposeful and\nautomatic directions to and from the brain.\n   It is the core and regulator of the entire specimen and is where all thinking, consciousness, emotions and self-awareness (in the case of the descendants) originate from.\n   In the case of the\nsnow hare, it can be presumed that the system works fairly similarly to most other animal species. Of course, the instincts of the snow hare lies within the central brain.\n*On this next page you can see much of the same type of diagram as before, except instead of the nervous system, you can see lungs connected with the mouth/nose going through a tube within the hare's throat. It has similar detail-orientation as before.*\nRespiratory System:\n   Within this system is where the lungs, mouth, and nose connect via the throat in order to provide the body with a sufficient amount of oxygen.\n   Stemming from the lungs is where the oxygen appears to be transported from the\nrespiratory system into the vascular system.\n   The nose is how a creature has its sense of smell, as it connects rather intimately with the nervous system.\n*Instead of a diagram as before, you are faced with two images. The first is what would appear to be a bald rabbit, skin fully exposed. The other is what would appear to be a rabbit with all of its hair intact.*\nSkin:\n   The skin is complicated enough to warrant itself as its own system, rather than just a simple organ within another system.\n   Skin is as what you would think as well as a vast network of nerves. Alongside that, the snow hare's skin is entirely\ncovered by a nice white coat of hair. \n   The purpose of skin would to act as a barrier from the outside environment, to protect from heat-loss as well as from various diseases. The hair of the rabbit also works against the loss of heat by working as an\ninsulator.\n*Upon turning the page, you are met by a familar diagram from earlier. Within the bordered lines is what appears to be various veins and arteries connecting with a heart at the hare's chest. The picture seems to show careful detail in how this is shown.*\nVascular System:\n   Within this would be all of the veins/arteries of the creature, as well as its heart. I've also included certain organs that have to do with the blood such as the spleen as well as bone marrow.\n   The main purpose of the vascular\nsystem is in both pumping the blood throughout the body, as well as supplying the body with a proper amount of oxygen.\n   The heart will pump constantly and rhythmically beat to keep the blood flowing throughout the body. The other organs work to help\nproduce blood and enrich the bloodstream.\n*On the next page you can see a similar diagram as before, including in rich detail the formation of a white hare's skeletal and muscular anatomy. What a grotesquely morbid and cute thing, you find yourself thinking!*\nMuscular/Skeletal system:\n   This system will involve the muscles, the bones, tendons and ligaments, and joints of the white hare.\n   The purpose of all things within this system are to provide structure to the body and allow motion.\nThe skeleton is mainly there to provide a structure with which the creature can stand with as well as protect certain inner organs by example of the ribs and skull.\n   Muscles are to provide the hare with strength and motion to carry out its daily\ntasks. With muscles, it can chew and eat, as well as hop and travel around.\n*The next page consists of another diagram showcasing the connection between the mouth, to the stomach, and finally down through the buttocks. Oh... It's the digestive system! It keeps the similar amount of exquisite detail.*\nDigestive System:\n   The digestive system consists of the mouth connected separately from the respiratory system into the stomach, then through the large and small intestines, until finally it ends through the anus. This system also involves the liver,\npancreas, gallblader, and appendix.\n   The purpose of this system is in extracting nutrients from food before excreting wastes from the body.\n   The stomach and intestines are mainly for the extraction of nutrients, while things like the liver are good\nfor protecting the organism from potentially harmful materials, like alcohol.\n*Upon reaching this diagram, you see several organs including kidneys, and the bladder. The system seems smaller than some of the others, but the diagram seems equally detailed as before.*\nUrinary System:\n   The urinary system includes mainly the kidneys, bladder, and the urethra.\n   The purpose in these organs is in separating wastes from the bloodstream. In short, this is where urine wastes are separated from the body and excreted.\nThe kidneys seem to play a significant role in separating the wastes from the bloodstream as they are intimately connected with the vascular system to do so. \n§\nSide notes:\n - There is one other system, the reproductive system. Although for the sake of conjuration studies, I decided to leave it out.\n - Many white hares were harmed in the making of this book... Sorry.\nList of Systems:\n - Nervous \n - Respiratory\n - Skin\n - Vascular\n - Muscular/Skeletal\n - Digestive\n - Urinary\n - (Reproductive)\n*For the next few pages you can see several of the same diagrams illustrated throughout this book. They are smaller than before so that several of them can fit on single pages. Despite this, they show similar amounts of details as they did previously.*", ""),
