        StaticBook("Sorcerer Types", "Gerald Elgan", "===================                                                                                             Sorcerers: Recognizing the Various Varieties\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n==================\nAmongst those who possess distinctly closer bonds to the void, a few different kinds have been recognised. This short excerpt will attempt to bring the reader through these varied distinctions, and hopefully provide aid in attaining some small measure of\nenlightenment in the subject matter.\n===================Types outlined:\nThe Common Robed Mage: Page 4-7\nHousehold Mage:\nPage 8-13\nBattle Mage:\nPage 14-22\n===================\nThe Common Robed Mage\n==================\nThe typical conjurer, often accompanied by a staff- draped in long cloaks, adorned in all manner of strange runes and odd colours, is often depicted as an old man with long, grand beards and a vast\n==================\n-reservoir of knowledge esoteric. There is no doubt that this variety is the most renowned and favored. The Common Mage is often the most well-versed in the forbidden art of magical combat- with stronger spells and\n===================\n-hexes, and (depending on the proficiency of the caster) all the more perilous.\n\nHowever, with these strengths, come weaknesses, for the Common Mage is often by tradition, frail and\n===================-lacking in physical prowess- endurance, hardiness and such- due to the almost fanatical obsession that they so often possess with the search and acquisition of more knowledge, and in turn, more power of origins profane.\nHousehold Mage\n===================The common Mage's humbler counterpart of lesser renown, the Household Mage could very well be the lowly servant a small measure too efficient at the task of cleaning, or the unassuming cook who heats the furnace a moment-\n===================\n-too quickly.\n\nThe subtlety of the magic these beings possess and and put into practice makes them quite difficult to discern. One could, perhaps rightly, assume that such beings might hardly\n===================-pose any considerable amount of threat, due to their lack of experience and utility in the field of combat.\n\nHousehold Mages can be either shunned members of the secluded Mage's Guild\n===================-or apprentices who, having acknowledged their inferior ability or lack of talent, had decided to follow an entirely different path, and seek a livelihood in a different environment. \n\nTheir spells are most\n===================\n-often simple and pose little to no danger- these sorcerers are seen as more benevolent than the common Mage, and physically more robust; though such things are quite difficult to confirm, given the elusive and subtle-\n===================nature of the mages in question.\n(Witch Maid/Mage of Cleaning.)\nThe Battle Mage\n===================The rarest and least liked of the known types- The Battle Mage is seen as the bane of chivalry and honorable duels, with little care for learning more of their art. The Battle Mage is more often spotted in places where\n===================-war and conflict are as commonplace as frost on a cold winter's morn. He is often the result of a fighter who, through rigorous and excruciating training, has learnt both the way of the sword and the art of magic-\n===================-applying both theories and practices in harmonious synergy. The existence of this being suggests the existence of some clandestine groups or orders that have handpicked and set aside some select candidates for the\n===================-rigors required to achieve this balance.\n\nThe training of a Battle Mage is the stuff of tales and legends- often known to be one of, if not the most dangerous path to the art of the arcane. Apprentices that were\n===================-found to have been fit candidates were often heard to have died of various accidents-including but not limited to: Death by fire and cinders, of spell failures and eternal sleep, of ice and water, and of broken shards of\n===================-marble or glass. The fortunate few- if one could call them such- that did manage to live through the horrors of their training and ire of the common folk, quite often found themselves unable to resume the lives they one led, now bent\n===================-purely on suffering and death as heralds of doom and ruin.\n\nBattle Mages are often not as proficient in the art of magic as their more focused counterpart: the common Sorcerer. However, their skill-\n===================with and mastery of the blade may, at times, more than compensate for this lack of further magical prowess and potency. Hence, it would be most unwise for the regular mage to step within range of the Battle Mage, for the Battle-\n===================Mage, neither frail nor unfit, could quite as easily close the distance, and deal a devastating blow.\n(Warrior-Witch/ Spellblade/ Witchman /Mystic Knight. )", ""),
        StaticBook("Sorcerers", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Sorcerers:\n  Recognizing the\n Various Varieties\n\n  by Arther Versluis\nAmoungst those who possess distinctly closer bonds to the void, a few different kinds have been recognized. This short excerpt will attempt to bring the reader through these distinctions, and hopefully provide aid in attaining some small measure of\nenlightment in the subject matter.\nThe Common Robed Mage:\nSorcer(ess) - Magician - Conjurer - Wizard - Robe\n\nThe typical conjurer, often accompanied by a staff and draped in long cloaks, adorned in all manner of strange markings, runes and often odd colours, is\noften depicted as an old man with a long, thick beard, and possessing a vast reservoir of knowledge esoteric.\n\nThere is no doubt that this variety is the most renown and favoured. The common Mage is often most well-versed in the forbidden art\nof magical combat- with more powerful spells and hexes, and, depending on the proficiency of the caster, all the more perilous.\n\nHowever, with these strengths come weaknesses, for the common Mage is often, by tradition, frail and\nlacking in physical prowess, endurance, hardiness and such due to the almost fanatical obsession that such ilk often possess with the endless search and acquisition of more knowledge, and in turn, more power of origins profane.\nThe Household Mage\nWitch Maid - Hearth Mage\n\nThe common Mage’s humbler counterpart or lesser renown, the Household Mage could very well be the lowly servant of a small measure too efficient at the crude task of\nsweeping the kitchen floors, or even the unassuming cook who heats the oven furnace a moment too quickly.\n\nThe subtlety of the magic these beings possess and put into practice makes them quite difficult to discern to those\nwithout the knack for spotting such things. One could, perhaps rightly, assume that such beings might hardly pose any considerable amount of threat, due to their lack of experience and utility in the field of combat.\nHousehold Mages can be either shunned members of the secluded Mage’s Guild or former, disgraced apprentices who, having in the past acknowledged their inferior ability or lack of talents, had decided to follow an entirely different path, seeking a\nlivelihood in a different environment.\n\nTheir spells are most often simplistic in nature and effect, and pose very little danger- if any at all. These mages are seen as more benevolent than the common Mage, and physically more robust; though such\nthings are quite difficult to confirm, given the elusive and subtle nature of the mages in question.\nThe Battle Mage\nWarrior-Witch - Spellblade - Witchman - Mystic Knight\n\nThe rarest and least liked of the known types. The Battle Mage is seen as the bane of chivalry and honourable duels, with little regard for learning more of this\nart. The Battle Mage is most often spotted in places where war and conflict are commonplace as frost on a cold winter’s morn. He is often the result of a fighter who, through rigorous and excruciating training, had learnt both the way of the blade and the\nart of the Arcane- applying both theories and practices in harmonious synergy. The existence of such beings suggests existence of some clandestine groups or knightly orders that had handpicked and set aside some select candidates to undertake the rigors\nrequired to achieve this balance of spell and blade.\n\nThe training of a would-be Battle Mage is the stuff of tales and legends- often known to be one of- if not THE most dangerous path to the art of magic. Apprentices that had been found and\ndeemed fit candidates were often rumoured to have died of various accidents- including , but not limited to: Death by fire and cinders, of spell mishaps and eternal sleep, of ice and water, and of broken shards of marble and glass. The fortunate few - if\none could even call them as such- that did somehow manage to live through the horrors of their training, and the ire and malice of the common folk, quite often found themselves unable to resume the lives they had once led, some distant time ago, now bent\npurely on suffering and death as heralds of doom and ruin.\n\nBattle Mages are often not as proficient in the art of magic as their more focused counterpart: the common Sorcerer. However, their skill with and mastery of the sword may, at times,\nmore than compensate for this lack of further magical prowess and potency. Hence, it would be most unwise for the regular mage to step within range of the Battle Mage, for the Battle Mage, neither frail nor unfit, could quite easily close the distance,\nand deal a devastating blow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sorcerers", "The Eternal Library", "Sorcerers:\nRecognizing the Various Varieties\n\nby Arthur Versluis\nAmongst those who possess distinctly closer bonds to the void, a few different kinds have been recognized. This short excerpt will attempt to bring the reader through these distinctions, and hopefully provide aid in attaining some small measure of\nenlightenment in the subject matter.\n\n\nThe Common Robed Mage\nSorcer(ess) - Magician - Conjurer - Wizard - Robe\n\nThe typical conjurer often accompanied by a staff and draped in long cloaks, adorned\nin all manner of strange markings, runes and often odd colours, often depicted as an old man with a long, thick beard, and possessing a vast reservoir of knowledge esoteric. There is no doubt that this variety is the most renowned and favoured.\nThe common mage is often most well-versed in the forbidden art of magical combat- with more powerful spells and hexes, and, depending on the proficiency of the caster, all the more perilous. However, with these strengths come weaknesses, for the common\nmage is often, by tradition, frail and lacking in physical prowess, endurance, hardiness and such due to the almost fanatical obsession that such ilk often possess with the endless search and acquisition of more knowledge, and in turn, more of origins\nprofane.\n\nThe Household Mage\nWitch Maid - Hearth Mage\n\nThe common mage's humbler counterpart of lesser renown, the Household Mage could very well be the lowly servant of a small measure too efficient at a crude task of\nsweeping the kitchen floors, or even the unassuming cook who heats the oven furnace a moment too quickly. The subtlety of the magic these beings possess and put into practice makes them quite difficult to discern to those without the knack for spotting\nsuch things. One could, perhaps rightly, assume that such beings might hardly pose any considerable amount of threat, due to their lack of experience and utility in the field of combat. Household Mages can be either shnned members of the secluded Mage's\nGuild or former, disgraced apprentices who, having in the past acknowledged their inferior ability or lack of talents, had decided to follow an entirely different path, seeking a livelihood in different environment. Their spells are most often simplistic\nin nature and effect, and pose very little danger- if any at all. These mages are seen as more benevolent than the common Mage, and physically more robust though such things are quite difficult to confirm, given the elusive and subtle nature of the mages\nin question.\n\nThe Battle Maage\nWarrior-Witch - Spellblade - Witchman - Mystic Knight\n\nThe rarest and least liked of the known types. The Battle Mage is seen as the bane of chivalry and honourable duels, with little\nregard for learning more of this art. The Battle Mage is most often spotted in places where war and conflict are commonplace as frost on a cold winter's morn. He is often the result of a fighter who, through rigorous and excruciating training, had learnt\nboth the way of the blade and the art of the Arcane- applying both theories and practices in harmonious synergy. The existence of such beings suggests existence of some clandestine groups or knightly orders that had handpicked and set aside some select\ncandidates to undertake the rigors required to achieve this balance of spell and blade. The training of a would-be Battle Mage is the stuff of tales and legends- often known to be one of- if not THE most dangerous path to the art of magic.\nApprentices that have been found and deemed fit candidates were often rumoured to have died of various accidents- including, but not limited to: Death by fire and cinders, of spell mishaps and eternal sleep, of ice and water, and of broken shards\nof marble and glass. The fortunate few - if one could even call them as such- that did somehow manage to live through the horrors of their training, and the ire and malice of the commonfolk quite often found themselves unable to resume the lives they had\nonce led, some distant ago, now bent purely on suffering and death as heralds of doom and ruin. Battle Mages are often not as proficient in the art of magic as their more focused counterpart: the common Sorcerer. However, their skill with and mastery of\nthe sword may, at times, more than compensate for this lack of further magical prowess and potency. Hence, it would be most unwise for the regular mage to step within the range of the Battle Mage, neither frail nor unit, could quite easily close the\ndistance, and deal a devastating blow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sorely Mistaken", "Unknown", "Sorely Mistaken\nBy Unknown\nUgly man with a fat cat, why is it he got so fat?\nWas it fish, or cream, or milk?\nOr perhaps the cat’s food being filled!\nUgly man, why are you so?\nIs it age, your body old?\nWas it wrinkles, withered hands?\nAncient smiles, gone away.\nThey call them old, ugly, fat but do they truly see just that?\nIf that is so, they are sorely mistaken.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sorry!", "Vhesraya", "I'm sorry!\n     My Master Wants\n    This Stuff. Sorry!", ""),
        StaticBook("Soul Resonance", "The Pumpkin Druid", "Soul Resonance Field\nWritten by:\nThe Pumpkin Druid\nI came up with this theory back in Thales however I only recently have begun researching it now in Athera.\nHave you ever had an epiphany? Have your friends ever 'magically' appeared to come save you?\nI believe everyone has experienced this at least once in their life-time. After observing such acts a long time I decided to create a theory on such a phenomenon. I believe that each person has the ability to connect to an invisible field.\nI am led to believe that Soul Resonance is accidentally used in every-day life. For example, people will accidentally use this ability when in danger to contact others and bring their friends to their exact location.\nI call this accessible field: 'Soul Resonance'. Whether a soul is required or not to actually access this field is up for debate as further research is required.\nSoul Resonance allows for at least two sentinent beings to send mental messages to each other, similarly to telepathy. The ability to do so is within every sentinent being that I have studied, descendents included.\n*Further research is needed to see if plants and animals can connect to the Soul Resonance Field.\nI shall call this place a 'Forum'. Much like a real forum people can address their thoughts and concerns for the realm of Athera.\n*More of the 'Forum Theory' in the book 'Forums and Skygods'.", ""),
        StaticBook("Specials Menu", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Roth Jayamen's\n        Restaurant\n            and\n       Entertainment\n       Establishment\n\n\n       -----------\n          Specials\n             and\n          Desserts\n      _____________\nSpecials\n\nMeat Lover’s Feast (1 per visit)\n\nAn assortment of cooked meats including, Seasoned Pork chop, A Prime Rib, Some Cooked Mutton, and two loaves of Bread.\n\n15 Minas\nVegetable Lover’s Feast (1 per visit)\n\nAn assortment of vegetable dishes including, a baked potato, Two Carrots, A Vegetable Salad, some Cheese fondue, and two loafs of bread.\n\n15 Minas\nThe Sweet Lover’s Feast (1 per visit)\n\nAn assortment of Sweets and delicious goodness including, 4 Caramel Cookies, 8 Butter Biscuits, Cream Pie, some Sweet cheese fondue, and two loafs of caramel bread.\n\n20 Minas\nDesserts\n\nCake with Frosting (1 per visit)\n\nA fresh baked cake with creamy white frosting a few small fruits on top.\n\n15 Minas\nCheesecake\n\nA Classic, Cheesy and sweet Cheesecake.\n\n20 Minas\nPlease remember to return all bottles and Menus!\n\nThank you and have a good day!\n\n~Roth Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Sphere Harmony", "Ambros", "Musica Universalis\n\nBy Ambros\nThere exists a cardinal harmony which cascades and ebbs through the cosmos; it is as if the grand architect did strike a tuning fork, letting the resounding song of creation ring into eternity, for this is what we hear when we turn our ears to the\nheavens, the notes of genesis.\nThis Musica Universalis is not an audible note, however, but a mathematical harmony, a physical equilibrium.  Granted, I should have no doubts that the higher immortals of the great beyond can hear this enduring melody, sounds which cannot be interpreted\nby the mortal ear.  As the sun, moon, and astral bodies rotate on their wayward paths they release a unique hum, an orbital resonance.  For both music and study of the astral bodies are one in the same, one for the ears the other for the eyes, but each\nfollow a perpetual mathematical pattern which ties the the stars to the earth.\nIt is known that there exists melodic ratios within music which every mortal should find “pleasing” or “suitable” for the ear.  Even the untrained can identify when the bard plays a wrong note upon his lute.  It is the nature of the mortal to\nsubconsciously understand this geometric pattern found in music.  Yet, it is this same harmonious geometry which can be found in the astral bodies in their movement across the nixian plane.  I shall tell you now my observations of the astral plane and the\nharmony and peace found within it.\nIt is known that the sun, moon, and stars rotate within a precise spherical pattern about the realm at a constant and measurable pattern, for it is from this we have ascertained night and day, the month, and the year.  The sun is the harbinger of day,\nwhile the moon is the bringer of night, and with it comes the stars.  However, a more observant eye can see the the stars are not a result of the moon, but rather, they are always there, lanterns hanging from the ebony darkness.  It is the greatness of\nthe sun which overwhelms the meager luminescents of the lesser spheres giving way to the cerulean blue of day.  Yet, the arrangement of these stars does not change, they simply rotate about us like a great wheel with the sun and moon being located at\nopposite ends of the great wheel.  I shall call this the Celestial Gyre, a closed sphere in which the realm is located within, though it cannot be assumed to be within the center.  This sphere is not solid but is outlined by the arrangement of the moon,\nstars, and sun, forming a uniquely spherical shape.\nThe Celestial Gyre spins eternally in such a precise way it can only be called harmony.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sprite Biology", "liam_barnett", "Sprite Biology\n\nA complete study and analysis of Sprites.\n\nBell Sano\n\n16th of Snow's Maiden, 1569\nI. Definition, Pg. 3\nII. Color, Pg. 11\nIII. Language, Pg. 29\nIV. Acerfolia, Pg. 35\nV. Toxins, Pg. 41\nVI. Weakness, Pg. 44\nVII. Final Note, Pg. 49\nVIII. Work cited, Pg. 50\nDefinition: A Sprite is often identified as sentient being, who takes pride in their expression of individuality through their physical appearance and personalities. To identify a Sprite, one must\nmeet and fill all these requirements;\n\n- Five to seven inches in height\n- Elongated, pointy ears\n- One or two pairs of wings on their backs\n- Abnormal skin color\nThese are the physical features that all regular Sprites share. In addition, they can often be found in uninhabited, forested areas. The more natural the setting, the more they’ll thrive.\nDo not search or bring a Sprite to a desert, or anywhere with a lack of natural flora, as without the proper nutrients to feed off of, they’ll quickly die. Sprites will also wear makeshift clothing, constructed from plants found within their habitat.\nTheir body is also literally made out of plant matter. Finally, you might notice that Sprites give off an extremely faint glow in the dark, which matches their color.\nThey may appear to be male or female, but they have no gender.\nAs for their actual personalities, a lot of their individual characteristics is dependent on their skin color. There are about twelve different varieties of Sprites, and with them, many unique attributes.\nHowever, common traits that all Sprites share include;\n\n- They're some of the smartest beings ever recorded\n- They share a special commune with nature\n- Sprites have extremely short attention spans\n\nThese are characteristics that all Sprites share, however the color of their personality is dependent on their natural skin color.\nColor: A Sprite’s color is determined at birth. As mentioned prior, the color of a Sprite’s skin will determine almost every aspect of their personality, and what traits they’ll live by.\nRecorded so far, there have been approximately twelve different varieties of Sprites witnessed.\nGreen: The green Sprite, while still immature and childish, is undoubtedly the most intellectually engaged of their kind. They’re willing to go out of their way to learn, and often have the longest attention span.\nBlue: These Sprites are the kindest, most curious creatures. They’ll be the first to make your acquaintance, and try to make friends. Although, their childish curiosity could often be dangerous on their end.\nSky blue: Similar to the blue Sprites, these beings will appear to be kind and content. However, their true motive is simply to trick an innocent passerby. They’ll trick an unsuspecting traveler into thinking they’re kind, only to torment them later.\nGrey: Simply put, the grey Sprite is the laziest. They’ll act innocent enough, only for sympathetic individuals to do work for them.\nRed: Do not anger the red Sprite, for they have an extremely short temper! Almost anything can upset them, and they’ll respond often with either verbal or physical violence. They don’t take kindly to insults.\nPurple: The purple Sprite is extremely calm and level headed, and are often wise. Almost the polar opposite of the red sprite, they value common sense above all else.\nWhite: White Sprites are innocent, and are willing to assist almost anybody who asks for help. They’ll even use their oddly bright color to help guide lost souls out of a large forest, or any other predicament.\nYellow: The yellow Sprite is simply mean to people, and gains entertainment out of other’s misery. They take pride in the art of emotional manipulation.\nPink: Pink Sprites tend to be the most childish out of all other Sprites. They ignore other responsibilities or obligations, and only focus on playing. That is, until they see two other individuals in love.\nWhen faced with the task of keeping two people in a relationship, or even starting one, the pink Sprite will work endlessly to ensure that happens.\nBrown: The brown Sprite doesn’t tend to worry about pleasing other Sprites, or meet any social standards. Instead, they live in solitude, may walk on all fours, and might even have sharpened teeth.\nThey’ll act like a wild dog, and sometimes refuse to talk. They also smell bad.\nOrange: The orange Sprite takes pride in being heroic, and try to solve any conflict they can, big or small. However, it’s rare that they’ll do it to be kind, but rather for their own reputation.\nIf they fail in solving whatever issue is laid before them, they'll become depressed, upset that they didn't solve their task.\nBlack: This is, by far, the most rare and dangerous sprite. They have been said to not care about morals, and will simply spread chaos for the sake of instilling fear into people.\nDo not interact with the black Sprite!\nLanguage: The Sprites speak a language, known as either the Sprite language, Spritenese, or Faei’efra. It is their own native tongue.\nHowever, every Sprite can interpret common, and understands any words said in common. This is due to the commune with nature they share, and acts almost like a universal translator.\nAlthough the Sprite can understand common, they cannot speak nor read it, unless taught by another being, sometimes for years on end. It’d be difficult, due to the Sprite’s short attention span, to learn\nany other language. It would also be hard for any other individual to learn the Sprite language themselves, as it’s such an odd and foreign tongue, with almost no detectable pattern.\nAlthough, it is said that Druids can communicate with Sprites, as they both share the similar commune with nature. Druids have a similar translator, so they won’t learn any words from the\nactual language, unless formally taught by a Sprite.\nAcerfolia: The Acerfolia is known as the flower and birthplace of all Sprites. These flowers are white, with leaves protruding from the stem, and a small, circular bud in the middle.\nWhenever a Sprite dies, a new flower blooms. After about six weeks, a Sprite will be born, the flower will wither away, and the creature is free.\nThis is a tricky process, as the flower must be planted in complete isolation, protected by masses of flora and trees. They can often be found near secluded lakes or streams, but only in the most secure locations of the realm.\nThese flowers are rare, and if they’re destroyed before the Sprite blooms, then that will be one less Sprite in this world. It is advised that if you find an Acerfolia, simply let it be, or even protect it for those six weeks.\nThe good news is that if an Acerfolia were to be destroyed, hermaphroditic reproduction is available to Sprites. Although this is rare, being seen in about every one in ten Sprites, some can reproduce\nby fertilizing spores, and creating a brand new seed themselves. They will then plant this new seed, where it will take anywhere from eight to twelve months to fully sprout, releasing the new Sprite with it.\nToxins: Every Sprite has their own, unique toxin. Each toxin’s effect is a defence mechanism, used if the Sprite feels threatened. These will regenerate, realistically, within two Elven hours after initial use.\nThey range from effects such as making one feel high on narcotics, to even paralyzing someone’s limbs. These are often released in the form of a gas, matching the color of each Sprite, so\nthe type of toxin released most likely depends on their skin color. Even simply exposure to the mouth, nose, eyes, or even just your skin can be enough to inflict the effects of the poisonous gas.\nWeaknesses: If, in any case, you need to kill a Sprite which is a physical hazard, refer to the following list. However, please use this as a last resort, as they are rare and fragile creatures that must be preserved.\nMagic: Sprites have a notorious weakness to magic. Not only can Sprites not learn any form of magic, they’re also amazingly weak to magic as a whole.\nWings: The Sprite's wings are extremely important! Not only are they a useful tool for the Sprite, but many blood vessels are also located within the wings, and if bent or cut, could cause a slow, painful death.\nFire: Sprites are composed of plant matter. Their skin, flesh, hair, wings, and just about everything else is created from plant matter. So, if they're exposed to fire, they'll burn extremely easily.\nIsolation: Isolating Sprites from nature can be deadly. If brought to the desert or some tainted lands, or even kept within a cage, it could die within a day or so.\nOn a final note, please don't eat Sprites. When Sprites die, they crumble into a sort of dusty, ash substance. If consumed, this will lead to a swift, quick death, and there is no antidote.\nWork cited:\n\n\"On Flowers\"- Orias\n\n\"Flora of Vailor\"- Illion Everion\n\n\"Fairies and Pixies\"- Sam King", ""),
        StaticBook("St Amyas' Story", "Jacob Chapel", "Saint Amyas\n\nThis is the old story of St. Amyas, transscribed by Jacob Chapel from a copy on the 6th of the Deep Cold, 1470.\nAmyas, as he was known then, received no blessing from on high or cosmic message to bid him forth. This is known. A wanderer and vagabond, his travels were many, beginning alongside a trade caravan in the city-state of Solace, from whence he came,\nto which he would later return.\n\nHe appeared in many settlements, joining many a caravan as a traveling apothecary, warding against the ailments of lengthy travel and giving succor to the sick and ill at each of his destinations.\nHe demanded nary a coin or material things, but only food and drink enough to sustain himself, and the supplies with which to work.\n\nFor 5 years, Amyas traveled, on a path that many would call aimless,\nuntil the storm of battle loomed dark and thunderous on the horizon.\n\nWhen war unfurled across the realm of Salvus, \nAmyas joined with one of the few caravans that would dare travel to Solace.\nThere, the medical tents were pitched high and red, awaiting his presence. He gave his skills over to the neutral parties whose minds could not quit the welfare of their fellow man, regardless of their allegiances. There, restless for the week's toils,\nAmyas sleeplessly cared for the wounded and weary, delivering many from death, and keeping vigil as vanguard to the dying, whose chances have perished. When the battles traveled, he traveled with it,\neven venturing into the battlefield to pluck away the felled.\n\nWhen the wartime tempers cooled, Amyas quit his wandering for to watch over the city, his home of yore, and once more join with his people.\nIt was not long before the languorous agonies of Rotbrain burgeoned its affliction. A quarantine was swiftly established on the foundation of two ailing men, who were kept in a large, unattended home yet given over to trade.\nUpon hearing word of the disease and its spread, Amyas entered the quarantine with food and medicine and confronted the guards who were posted there. He was met with some resistance, as nary a man was free to see the sick, so as to curb the contagion.\nWhen held back from the ailing men, Amyas shook their grasp and forced his way inside, where the guards would not follow. There, for ten days, Amyas cared for the two, but upon the eleventh day, when he made to leave to set out for more supplies,\nthe guards would not release him, pressing the door shut. They, in their ignorance of charity and goodness, believed that Amyas had contracted the disease himself. That night, the guards set out to bind the door under boards of wood and nail.\nFor five days, Amyas and the two men slaked their thirsts on what little remained of Amyas' supply, until naught was left. On the sixth day, they went without, and in the night, when the two men rested, Amyas asked himself if his boldness was vain,\nif his mind were misplaced, and if all of this was a mistake. It was then that an immaculate light, brighter than the flames of a torch and cleaner than the spark of a passing lantern,\nshone through the boards of a nearby window and he felt its warmth upon his dried skin. Before the sun could cast its resplendence over the nighted world, Amyas endured in wakefulness to pray.\nOn the morning of the seventh day, a doctor arrived from Renatus and chastised the guards for keeping sundries from the sick, before imploring them to remove the boards from the door.\nThe doctor entered, his voice a smooth resonance from beneath a plague-mask, found and inspected Amyas and the two men. Of the two, the doctor found that the disease was passing, tapering away as Rotbrain is want to do,\ndeclaring it a wonder that they have not already expired. Of Amyas, the doctor found no disease to be passing, at all, curious as to why no tapering symptoms yet clutched at his body or mind.\nThe doctor bid the guards to leave for food and water, and inspected Amyas thrice more.\nWhen the quarantine was lifted, Amyas searched for the Clergy, aspiring to devote his life and efforts to piety and faith, in His name.\n\nDuring his lengthy service to the Faith, Amyas built a life of charity and goodwill, without want or desire,\nbut with the spark of pure intention. Never staying put, Amyas was characterized by his many travels, seeking to apply his efforts wherever they were needed, always taking note of a light that shone through distant windows in the eventide.", ""),
        StaticBook("Staring", "Cole Cuthalion", "STaring", ""),
        StaticBook("Starting A Mage", "Terilfer'Careinthan", "The Journal Of An Apprentice   Mage\n\n1. My first connections to the void.\n\n2. The First Sparks.\n1. The first time I tried connecting to the void I failed, like many Novice mages do,  but after much study sweat and other fluids I managed to connect, I can't say how the first connection was, because you have to try it for yourself one day,\nbut I tell you, it was the biggest acomplishment of my entire life... I think, or was it that time when I tamed an owl for the first time?\nPractice, I say! Practice practice and practice, another one and another one and another one, connections to the\nvoid I mean...\nSo if you want to be a mage you need the passion for it, no one can become a mage, you are either born with it or die trying... most apprentices do...\n2. The first spark was like a fart in the wind litteraly, more smoke than fire.\nYou can expect more or less, and once again practice, tere is a lot of practice, and time put into magic, not wanting to get your hopes of becoming\na mage down but humans won't get to enjoy much of their magic... \n\n\n-If this makes you want to eb a mage, after me, it would be a lot easyer to swinga  sword.", ""),
        StaticBook("Storbro's Orders", "Storsbro Steelshield", "*The text that follows seems to beautifully written by a trained hand*\n\nYour orders are simple, strike down the pretender king by any means necessary, but make it public. You are the first step we take on the path to redemption. And if you die, you shall-\n-find favor in the life after.\n\n~V", ""),
        StaticBook("Store Inventory", "Lorena Faeliel", "[!]On the pages following there would be a neatly written list of book titles and authors.\n\nThere would be no alphabetical order, rather they would seem to be organized by genre.\nhttp://tinyurl.com/p8xfyn9", ""),
        StaticBook("Storming Seahelm", "Gared Errmark", "The Storming of Seahelm\n\nOn the 9th of the Grand Harvest, 1558, the combined forces of Oren marched forth from their camps and laid siege to the city of Seahelm. They knew that the rebellious traitors inside would cowardly, and desperately,\nattempt to hold this city. It would not be their bastion, it would be their graves.\n\nThey lit fires all around, sending plumes of smoke skyhigh, a terrifying inferno of fire climbing up their gnarled houses, along their broken walls.\nAnd then the siege weapons let loose their torrent of unending justice. Boulders rained upon their walls, as the bravest of Oren, die Starke Armee, propped up their siege ladders and stormed the western wall. What ensued was a bloodbath for the rebels,\nand a decisive victory for Oren, that would forever be known as one of our finest hours, if not the greatest example of our might. \n\nThe true definer of the battle was the marksmanship of Balgruff Frostbeard, whose great Dwarven warcry echoed\nthroughout their city, and set the Nortruppen to shivering fits. It was his shot that split Lord Thomas Ruric, the Traitor of Ostavar, in two and broke their morale as cleanly as our swords pierced their necks. \n\nI, Gared, was one with the first unit over\nthe wall. I, with the Emperor himself, took first the main three towers that ruled over the docks, before, alone, I leapt into a house and slew three Norlander scum. I took a great bounty from their hellish bodies before helping raise the banner over\nSeahelm. As the fires extinguished, and the day reached its peak, the Orenian flag rose proudly over Ostavar and set the Dreadlander reinforcements to fleeing.\n\n   \n    A complete and accurate account of the Storming of\nSeahelm, by Gared Errmark.", ""),
        StaticBook("Strange Note", "unknown", "Beyond the shattered realm their descendants stumble. Fate not altered, time hath fumbled. After a time of Draakar's ire Cover the fringe, torrid winds and fire. Traverse the the maker's mark and seek. A truth that Ancestors beseech", ""),
        StaticBook("Sul'Vallel", "Bell Sano", "1549\n\nSul'Vallel\n\nDonated and created by Sarrion Zytiaear\nThe Sul'Vallel is a short, black dagger, hand crafted by Sarrion Zytiaear. The hilt is made from the finest of windswept wood, and the blade is black ferrum, designed for swiftly killing another being.\nThe dagger has it's own special ability. Upon the user rubbing the hilt with his thumb, the dagger will emmit a strong, blue light. Markings will inscribe itself on the metal of the blade, and magelight will activate.\nThe light would be more than enough to fill a dark room with a bright light, or an open area of any sort. It's useful for a makeshift torch, but it's mana drains rather quickly.\nTo deactivate it, simply rub the hilt again, and the dagger will stop glowing, returning to it's black ferrum state. After about three uses, the mana gem will need to be re-imbued.", ""),
        StaticBook("Summerhall", "Garsto Leaf", "{-----------------}            SummerHall\n{-----------------} Note: This is to be plated on a lute.\n\n                   [!]\nThere are notes written over three pages of this book of music. At the end of the music there is a signature by Garsto Leaf [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Sun and Moon", "Seth Calith", "The Eternal chase of day and night.\n\nThe purple sky on the horizon.\n\nThe result of sun’s creations.\n\nEvery ray the moon ties in.\n\nEvery glance filled with sensation.\nThe self deemed imperfection.\n\nWith an evergrowing fear of rejection.\n\nThe sun continues on it’s retreat.\n\nFearing that history will repeat.\nThe Moon continues it's hunt.\n\nHer intentions clear yet never blunt.\n\nAlways within reach to strike whenever.\n\nBecause the huntress is utmost clever.\nAnd an eternal cycle for they are equal.\n\nBy the wish of the Moon, there can be a sequel. \n\nThe Sun allows the shine to be seen.\n\nThe Moon can chose to let it be more than a scene.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sunshine Task", "Archdruid Verden", "Dedicant,\n\nTravel to the spider nest known as Draug's End, located in the enchanted forest. Once there, I need you to /stealthily/ collect an egg from the nest so that I can examine it.\nThis task is important in several key ways. Firstly, it is beneficial to our cause that we learn as much as possible about this new species of spider. Secondly, I want to see if their large size is attributed to void interference.\n- Archdruid Verden\n((Once you arrive at the location, PM an ET or some sort of staff for a brief event. They should reward your success with a named 'Giant Spider Egg'. Just bring it back, and we'll be good.))\n            Nest Location\n           x-415, z-358", ""),
        StaticBook("Surviving Undead", "Iris Lavender", "A Ghoul Popped Out Of Nowhere? An Undead thinks you look better in half? Well these tips will help keep you alive long enough to find help and contact one of us.\nTip #1:\nIf you're in an open spot and don't need or want to save someone, Run immediately, no tricks will help. the undead have no mercy, and will not let you live.\nTip #2:\nIf you have any gold/Aurum, use it. undeads are weak against gold. If you don't have any, go for thier neck and slash it as deep as you can. if not possible, try going for the legs and then RUN.\nTip #3. \nIf you're in a closed spot and don't have a weapon, shout for help and try to survive as long as you can. help might come and save  you.\nTip #4\nKILL THEM! Just get your sword out and kill them with no mercy! that's the most fun one.\nTip #5\n\nUse fire to burn them to the ground. Fire evocation or just a flint and steel.\nTip #6\n\nSome undeads may use purple smoke that blinds anyone inside the smoke and anyone looking at it can not look inside it. If you see this smoke, do NOT go inside it, but get help as quickly as possible.\nContacting anyone who can fight undead is the best thing you can do. We would like it if you could contact us with any information that you have. Please take your information to Laureh'lin and give it to either Iris, Uni or Lucinda.\n((If you cannot find us, send a PM to rebwolf (Iris), superduckygamer (Uni) or electrocutioner8 (Lucinda).))\nThe reason we are telling you all of this is because the Undead have come back and this is NOT a lie. We need as much help as we can get to spread this message so just you reading this is helping us. \n\nThank you.\nWritten by Iris Lavender and Uni Sindolia.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sword Song", "Adrian 'The Black Demon'", "Many don't know what a Sword Song is. A Sword Song means Battle, the Beautiful Sounds of sword clashing on sword, Battleaxe Breaking Shields. The screams of men and The sound Of Victory. Many men are in a Sword Song, few survive there first, But many Get\nRich from them. It takes courage to step in the face of your enemy and smell the ale on there breath. It takes Guts to cut a man from his Groin to his Chin spilling his insides, But it takes smarts to Gain Victory and Earn a name. In a Sword Song one can\nMake a name by killing any foe who stands in his way, but killing a lord or General will have bards praising your name for generations. There are certain skills few posses. \nSword Dance, is where you can move around blades without them touching you.\nSword-Craft, is the general term if someone can strike a man down with his Blade without taking severe damage to himself.\nThe Eye. is when one can see through an enemies ambush, or spot out a weakness.\nGolden Heart, Is when you know you are doomed but you\nFight till you have no breath left to fight.\nThese are what make men from children in the battlefield, Its what makes the skilled Dignified and the weak Put down, Sword Songs are not a place to play Around!.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sylvers Log v.1", "Fjordin Sylver", "= The Sylversands =\n- Expeditionary Log -\n\nThis log details the events following the destruction of Sylverwood by pillage of bandits, and the swift recovery of Fjordin Sylver in the creation of Sylverstead Shores (Written 1499-1500).\n16th Malin's Welcome 1499\n\nToday I managed to salvage what was left of Sylverwood from the clearing. Most of the town was ransacked of any and all goods, but there were still some building materials and crops buried within Kayla's homestead.\nOn account of what was lost, the two of us estimate around four boxes of ferrum, which was the heaviest blow of all given the economic situation with the once-common metal. Despite my lack of physical capability I found it within myself to hit the mines.\nFor days I worked outside the Cloud Temple, which I had feared was lost after the Undead Scourge during my time in hibernation. Finally I accumulated enough ferrum to reconstruct the forge, and with that our first step towards recovery.\nKayla and I had begged the divines for assistance in this tragedy, or for a charity to compensate for our lost, but all wishes fell upon deaf ears. She however had another idea in mind, which at the time I found pointless : to construct a shrine.\nThe point of the shrine would be to protect us from evil. It would be expensive, consisting of whatever ferrum we had left and a few shards of carbarum, but she assured me it would be worth it in the end.\nIn fact it was, but with bitter-sweet consequences. The divines were satisfied with our offering, and offered our land their blessing, but only within the badlands of Athera in an area they deemed fit for our prosperity.\nIn addition to this, they only promised their hand in our future if we brought more people to offer their devotion and worship They demanded we had eight inhabitants accumulated in three months, or the protection will be revoked.\nUnfortunately I found myself dormant for two of those months lost in the wilderness (account hijacked OOC for two days), and by the time I got back the least I could do was salvage the shrine before they left it in smite.\nWhen I begged for their forgiveness, they told me it would be unacceptable for myself to try and dictate these lands again, which left me in a precarious situation. I then decided it would be Kayla Denn who would temporarily lead the region.\n2nd First Seed 1499\n\nRecently I went back to the Viridian Pub to pay a visit to Artemis, the lovely tavern worker who I frequently talked to on my less-than-sober nights away from Sylverwood. If only I had arrived sooner.\nShortly after my arrival, his lover Renn and her friend (family?) Asher showed up as well. The first words spoken to me were \"Take off your armor in the tavern, please.\". I could tell already this would get interesting, and I complied.\nShortly after Renn hurried off into the basement to fetch refreshments, and perhaps wake Artemis from his midnight slumber. For a while me and Asher talked to one another, although the man seemed to isolate himself from conversation.\nMost of what we discussed had to do with Oren's razing of the lands, particularly those deemed pagan. He even shared a personal account of their torment that he experienced at a younger age. I myself discussed the High Elves \"purification\" methods.\nShortly after there was a thud downstairs and the sound of metal, but we ignored it for something (possibly suggestive between the lovers?) or an accident. However, we shortly after found Renn stained in blood walk upstairs. It was a grisly sight.\nShe explained that an Uruk was found leaning over Artemis, ready to feast upon his body (who had a shard of glass piercing his throat). Thankfully, Renn managed to nock an arrow and fire it clean through his skull. Never say she can't fire a bow.\nAnyway, the clerics showed up shortly after to resurrect poor Artemis, which barely made way for success. He soon returned to us on the upper level, at which point the lovers rejoiced to see one another. Asher distanced himself, however.\nFrom there I talked to the trio (namely Artemis) about the loss of his mechanical arm (which was apparently taken by a group of Orc's long ago), and the wars of which have broken out across the land. He also told me about the Undead scourge and its end.\nShortly after I returned home, carrying with me nothing more than the clothes on my back and an empty stomach. Noticing my reserves of bread were running low, I decided to try my hand at fishing, which came up with moderate success.\nWhich got me thinking : What if Sylversands was a fishing community? In Sylverwood I figured animal husbandry to be the future, considering cattle provided more nutrition than the barley required to support them. Looking back, fishing is better.\nDespite these badlands being terribly irrigated and less-than-fertile, the ocean is quite bountiful with marine life. Frankly the fish here could keep an entire town thriving, although the harvest of these sources will need to be regulated.\nAside from alternative food sources I spent a lot of time redesigning building after building. After discussing things with Kayla, we decided the buildings (at least on the upper terrace) will be duplex style.\nThe point of a duplex housing style (or at least for the initial housing) is to maximize density while also pushing together the community. In Sylverwood people rarely talked to one another, and their homes were little more than shacks.\nHere in Sylversands, the houses will be two stories high and nearly twice the size if not three times the size in volume per family. One of the key features I adopted from Sylverwood was the double-layering of walls.\nIt was not for aesthetics as it was in Sylverwood, however. I noticed that with the dry and hot climate here by the canyon, houses compromised entirely of wood not located by the ocean are vulnerable to random fires.\nFor practicality purposes I had to maintain the same roof design made mostly of wood, but the rest is an insulated layer of stone brick to provide resistance to the heat, and also keep families (or residents themselves) cool even on the hottest days.\nMy plans are to construct two more houses of this duplex theme, and then eventually work on the harbor. The harbor will feature a tavern, warehouse, shipping center/shipwright, and maybe even a resort of sorts.\n19th The Grand Harvest, 1500\n\nAlmost the end of yet another century. Kayla has gotten me and Lucius wrapped up with some independence goofs in the wilderness.\nThey wanted to employ me, Lucius, and Kayla as borderline vassals under their flag. In their words we would enterprise in agriculture for their kingdom, while recieving benefits.\nObviously this deal was a complete misunderstanding with Kayla, and we shunned the idea in favor of our own ambitions to create Sylversands. Me and Lucius have also debate the architecture of the colony.\nAfter thinking it through and reading through tomes in the Great Library of fantastic works of architectural art from the past I hit the drafting board.\nIt's been almost a year now since starting my first few designs, but little by little things are coming to a close. Lucius and his friend Publius have been helping me thus far in organization.\nKayla has been working her bum off to obtain the resources necessary to construct the potential Sylversands layout I have in mind. It is extremely pricey.\nHowever, residents of Sylversands will instead live a life of luxury, and experience a deeper sense of community. Unfortunately, there are drawbacks to these new plans.\nThe newer architectural designs require not only a more substantial supply of resources, but are very time-consuming and space-inefficient. We expect less residential capacity.\nThe benefits outweigh these drawbacks, however. The new housing will feature much more room for families to grow, and are very pleasing to the eye inside, and out.\nWe will utilize the Dark Oak grove of what was once Sylverwood to build the framework of these homes, and mass-harvest sand from the badlands to create compact sandstone bricks.\nFrom there only time will tell where things go. The end result will be a hopefully prosperous and pleasing city to live in. We will owe our allegiance to Oren.\n11th Suns Smile, 1500\n\nToday I witnessed a wedding between Tahjeet Mubdee and (who is now) Ame Mubdee. It was held in the grand keep of Salvus. What a lovely occassion.\nMe and Publius made attendence with only seconds to spare before the kiss was made, and the ring slipped. The ceremony was quite humorous when Tahjeet put the ring on the wrong hand in excitement.\nBut that is a detail he would surely gut me for bringing mention to. It was quite a memorable day for sure, and the wedding bells could be heard from all across Athera. Truly monumental.\nThe afterparty was quite lovely. The hours spent among guests was a blur, as I was too drunk to remember details. Publius had work in Petrus to attend to, so we bid our good-byes and he respectfully departed.\nI spent much time among the guests, and made small-talk with Tahjeet and his newly wed wife. I spoiled the couple with a fat stack of twenty solid Aurum bars and sixteen finely carved blocks of Lapis Lazuli.\nThe food served was rather lovely. Pancakes, wine, and cakes prepared by only the finest chefs of Salvus. In my daze I recall men shuffling around furniture and leftovers, clearing the space at last.\nKolohe Finn was caught trying to woo a lady of whom I did not know. She was young, and wrapped in lovely pink robes. Poor Kolohe was drunk to hell and back, and for a while made a fool of himself.\nI tried slipping a sedative into his drink so he wouldn't do anything brash, but perhaps it was for the best I didn't succeed. In the end of the day he managed to steal a kiss from the fair lady, and together they trot off.\nQuite a love story it was, if not a strange one. Truly there is something to said about such a wonderful night. I managed to run into Atizle, that cute little Kharajyr, who attended the wedding in all his kindness.\nMuch to his surprise and my own I had a bucket of milk reserved within my rucksack. Eagerly the young Atizle took the drink, and chugged it down with brutal efficiency. He sure loves to treat himself whenever he gets the chance.\nAfter returning home on a long and tiring journey, I retired my armor and sword for the night while laying under the stars. The forge let off a strong aroma of ferrum, as a set of chainmail lay out for cooling I prepared for my friend Harkat.\nWith the recovery of my livestock from the wilds of Sylverwood, and the wedding, and my growing list of associates in Athera, things are admittedly going quite well. I can only hope for a bright future.", ""),
        StaticBook("T", "Filly McHopper", "The Giants in The Wood\nBy: Filly McHopper\n\n \n  There once was a pale man, with purplish crescents beneath his eyes. He loved a fair maiden so great, yet they could not marry for her brother's hate. He arrived at her brother's door, \nbegging\nfor a chore. \"O' kind man, keeper of my lover! I beg you, give  me a task so that I may secure our love!\" The brother, a sensible man, decided to send the pale knight upon a worthy quest. He was to find two giants, and put them to rest. He set off into\nthe knight, blade slapping against his hip. Suddenly, a peasant ran towards him, he did a flip! The brave knight fought valiantly, knocking the criminal aground! As he walked away, he heard the sound. \"YEou deRe! WHaUt are YeOU dEings!?\" It was a large\nbeast, ready to feast. He stood two times taller than the brave knight, claws and teeth with great length. It was no secret that the Giant was angry, and the strong knight drew his blade once more, charging forth knowing his lore! A man would die fighting\na monster that size! The man began to rize, stabbing the Giant in the eye. The beast fell with a cry. Successful, the knight stole the Giant's head, and carried on with his quest for love. \"WHeUAt! Where Eth GrEyG!!!!?\" There, standing just shorter than\nlast, the Giant's wife stood cross. She head a large pan in her hand, and she saw the man. Running towards him, she swung her utensil, knocking him through the air! There lie the knight, defeated and hopeless. He thought of his maiden, red hair so fine\nand blue eyes so divine. He stood once again, and defeated the Giant Wife, dubbed Bee for her swarming ways. And so, our hero trudged home, each hand grasping a giant's skulll by the hair. He presented the heads to the brother of his lover, and in\nhis final victory, he defeated the brother's hate. They feasted for many days, love sprouting in the air. On the final night of celebration, the knight kissed his maid in peace, for their love was final.", ""),
        StaticBook("T.A. Al. & Farn.", "Alistair Wymer", "-----Trade Agreement-----\n21st of The Deep Cold 1555\n\nAlistair and Fareneir both agree that Fareneir will guide customers to the Song-Bird Inn in SeaHelm from his Market Stall in SeaHelm, so long as Alistair agrees to do the same. Alistair also\nagrees to give Fareneir a free meal once per day upon his arrival at the Song-Bird Inn in SeaHelm. Fareneir also agrees that all items at his Market Stall are 50% discounted, so long as he has recieved customers from Alistair's Song-Bird Inn in SeaHelm.", ""),
        StaticBook("T.F. Notes I", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "As I had guessed the art of Transfiguration seems to be just as easy as telekinesis, though this time it requires thorough understanding of Equivalent Exchange and alteration. Every object, no matter how small or large, has dormant mana.\nThis mana controls the alchemical make up of every object and such is where alchemy gets its powers, by tapping such and creating elixirs of the likes. This time the idea is to tap this mana using your own,\nnot to just change the velocity of this object but to change the whole makeup in your own way.. to alter the material how /you/ choose, though the law of equivalent exchange must be followed, so no turning Ferrum to Aurum any time soon.\nMy first connection seemed to be more easy than when I had first connected to control an object’s velocity when I had learned about telekinetics, but this time instead of using my connection to the void\nto ‘grip’ an object by this dormant mana, I was actually using my own mana to tap into this mana, and activate it! It was incredible, it had felt like I was one with this object.\nEven at my fairly low training with this magic I understand vastly on how this whole concept can be used in the most complex scenarios. For now I am to stick to heating this ball up, or cool it down.\nA simple task as temperature is a mere thought, though because of how new I am to this spell It seems to take a toll on my body as if I was a student once more, an odd feeling.\nAvenel, after our first lesson, has provide me with this metal ball. I will be using such to practice my first and many attempts of Transmutation, as it’s one of the most easiest matters to understand, especially as a blacksmith such as myself,\nor rather ex-blacksmith. It was simple, I had understood the weight of the ball when I had first held it, and I knew the makeup of Ferrum. So it was merely just /thinking/ of the reaction.\n\n-Sarrion\n2nd of Snow's Maiden\n1547", ""),
        StaticBook("T.G.H Journal", "LumbaJack", "The Gray Hotchen\n   Company Journal\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRobert Hotchen\nBradshaw Gray\n1566:\n-Building purchased.\n-Building renovated.\n\n-Stall set up.\n  *Caskets doing well.\n\n-Hired Gregory\n  *200m/yr\n\n-Bradshaw running his \"Zaza's Iron Kingdom\"\n1567:\n-Zaza's Iron Empire all good. Not in the way too much.\n-Selling wood 175/chest\n-Bought Mansion 4.5k\n\n-Shop sold. 3000.0m\n\n-New shop bought. 700m (6 Market Plaza)\n1568:\n-Fired Gregory.\n-Killed Gregory\n\n-Married.\n\n-Built special room in house\n\n-Buisness as usual.\n1569:\n\n-Buisness slowed.. too busy with Abrielle.\n\n-\n1570:\nMembers\n\nLeaders:\n-Robert Hotchen\n-Bradshaw Gray\n\nWorkers:\n-Gregory\n  *Pay: 200/yr\n-Sebastion\n-Ruslan\n  *Pay: When ever.\nMembers\nShipments\nJournal:\n\nThe buisness is going well, selling wood and caskets for a nice profit.\nStarted selling iron, small profits coming in.\nHired dark elf, Gregory.\n\nSeems like a reasonable man.\nSebastian tells me that Greg is hiding some of his ores...\nKilled Gregory. He had it coming.\nNew house, large. Looking for a wife to live in it with me.\nFound nice lady, Abrielle, plan to invite her over,\nBuilt special room, hid it behind closet.\nAbrielle came over, went well.\nTold man to come, got Sebastian to hold him down. Slit his nn eck. Place in special room. Viscar eat.\nMarried. Going to become commandant if Bradshaw b bbeco omes mayor\nPromis brocken. Bradshaw bad\nLured woman with gold. Slit neck. Viscar was getting hungry.\nNeed too get pauback for Bradshaw brokin proms\nffiled room with young girl. Neck slit. Viscar eat thumb. ii try some\nFolk noking.. i write again later...", ""),
        StaticBook("T.H.H Edition 1", "Thamas Bucketfoot", "The Humble Hollow\n \nEdition 1\n\n15th of \nThe Grand Harvest\n\nEditors Note\n\nThis be the first edition of 'The Humble Hollow Newspaper' and will contain loads reading and prizes.\nIntroduction\n\nThis paper will be released every Elven Week on this date, it will contain the Weeks happenings and just great reads, with the occasional prizes!\n\nI will be handing these out for free, but donations of items would be great too!\nWeekly News\n\nNot much has happened this Elven Week but a few great, little things have happened!\n\nBaby Drogo was born! His proud parents Larry and Noara Neyas are thrilled to have him!\nI myself have become Jnr Deputy in the Sheriffs Department, so expect to see me around more often!\n\nThere have been rumours going around about a possible town move which could be exciting or a horrible mistake.\n___________________  Wanted List By Larry\n-------------------\n\nWell this be the end of this short newspaper, in the future they will be a lot longer for you to all read!\n\nKind Regards\n\nThamas Bucketfoot\n\nEditor: Thamas\nWanted list: Larry", ""),
        StaticBook("Tailoring: Basic", "[Tailor] Damai Torena", "Tailoring\n\nTailoring is the art of creating, fixing garments.\n\nTo get better at this skill you must be able to be creative and innovative. You need a steady hand and be able to sow. This guide is going to show you how to do the most\nbasic tailoring techniques.\n\nFirst you will need to measure the person you are creating a piece of clothing for. Also get their body shape so you can design the clothing to be comfortable and good looking.\n\nNow you need to sketch different types of the item you are going to create. After doing several sketches pick one and then do it in detail with colors and everything. Do a back, front and side part of the sketch.\n\nKeep all of the the other sketches in\na folder so you can show customers when they order something and then you don't have to draw a whole other sketch.\n\nIt is now time for choosing the material and color of the item you are making. Always ask a person what color and perks they want it to\nhave because if they want a light shirt then you will know what type of material is the best. Do beware that some materials cannot be dyed so always ask the customer what they want. \n\nGet a large piece of the material and measure it to the right\nsize. Now draw on the material and cut out the design, if your design have different components then you will have to sow them on with a needle and thread. To do this thread the needle and then pierce the material at the top and the go down through the\nother piece and come back up and so on until you go to the end or back to the start.\n\nIf it is just one big piece of material then you can wrap it around a manequin to shape it and then either put sow at the end of it or stick it.\nNow stick on any buttons, flowers or other decorations to it. Clean it up and detail it a bit more.\n\nNow it is done. Not everything you make will be good but need to keep at it a learn different materials.\nAuthor: Damai Torena\n\nFuture Books planned: Materials and You\nTailoring: Advanced\nLeather Skills", ""),
        StaticBook("Tale of Two", "Rodney Altman", "There once was a mali'ame named Arbor he was a kind elf and always cared for others. On the other hand, there was Pura the mali'aheral. They both resented eachother very much and wished the other would die\na grusome death. One day Pura went searching\nfor Arbor in the forest. Pura searched through the eerie forest looking high and low for Arbor. The sound of nature buzzed around Pura as he ran through the forest. Pura took a quick turn around a tree and ran into, guess who, Arbor.\nThey scowled at one another, then all of a sudden lightning hit the tree they were near and one of the branches came lose and came down, crushing both of their legs pinning them to the ground. They groaned and sighed several times in the passing hour, but\ndidn't say a word to one another, until Arbor broke the silence. \"This is all your fault\" he said. Pura responded quickly \"It's your fault for being the impure elf you are\". Arbor spit at Pura before fainting from the pain. Over an hour later Arbor awoke\nand he spoke to Pura \"We shouldn't be fighting like this\" he said. Pura waited a moment before grunting in response. \"We should be friends...\" Arbor said. \"I hope someone finds us soon\" said Pura. Arbor bobbed his head slightly in respond.\nAround fifteen minutes later they heard rustling in the trees. \"Someone's come to save us!\" yelled Arbor. \"Praise Kalenz!\" said Pura. They both stared into the trees awaiting their saviors before the silence was broken by a laugh, a laugh with an obvious\ntone of fear. \"What's so funny?\" said Arbor. Pura laughed again \"Our saviors...\" he said before waiting a few moments to finish \"They're ghouls...\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Squid", "Aerxuis", "Tales of Squid \nBy Unknown \nCopied by Aerx \nExtra excerpts by Aerx\nOne of the most common creatures, squid are known to have existed in early Aegis and clear to modern day. They live among fish in water sources, including rivers, seas, oceans , ponds and even swimming pools.\nThis makes squid among the most adaptable aquatic animals.\nSquid are very peaceful and do not attack back if struck. The only real danger they pose is drowning, should one hunt them underwater for too long.\nThe ink sacs found in squid are very useful, as the thick black ink is used for writing, as a dye, in alchemy and other uses. This makes squid hunting a potentially lucrative business.\nThere are numerous types of squid. Apart from the everyday common squid, some are thought to perhaps only be myths.\nIt is said that the Halfling Petyr Brandybuck once raised an army of Battle Squid in combat against the Undead. Their large teerth and overwhelming numbers are thought to have played a part in victory.\nAlso sometimes is seen are Flying Squid. Frequently mocked as a fairy tale, reports of them were quite common in Aegis.\nLastly, there have been reports for over a thousand years of Giant Squids that live in the deepest parts of the oceans. Although not often documented, some swear they have caused shipwrecks.\nExtra from Aerx \n\nThese so called \"Battle Squids\" Were kept in an underwater bar in the middle of the ocean in Thales. I also recall The Druid known as 'Ouity' transforming into a flying battle squid...\nWhat does this entail? Are the Druids somehow linked to this phenomena? They also helped is in fighting back Gaz during the transition between Thales and Athera..", ""),
        StaticBook("Talk with Undead", "Daniel Nodal", "*This paper has a mark of bloody fingerprints, as if the writer had bloody hands on the time of writing.*\nAsside from all the problems that were had from the point where I invited a dark robed person to my tavern until we arrived at a house chosen by a Xan paladin, we have finally started to speak with the undead. First impressions of it, it's not afraid to\ndie, but does not want to be destroyed. Says it would be a worse way to deliever a message by killing, so he perfers to talk. His name is Jinn, or so he says, he's body is extremelly light, almost as if he is made purely of a skeleton. Even his face made\na cracking sound when he was hit.\n\nHis body is made fully of bones, stripped of flesh by himself, or so he says. While being destroyed many times he still has a body, meaning he is reborn anew each time, by his own words.\nThe goals and motives of Iblees he does not answer mentioning to ask Iblees himself.\n\nHe asked of our thoughs of Iblees, after I stated that he appeared as a god to destroy us, he told that it would be like that, to birth a new world.\nA thought of the battle of good against evil, and of the once victory of good did not remove evil. To create a new world without evil. Stating that Iblees would not kill those that would not oppose him, and lead him to the new world. Hard to think of that\nconsidering the undead are his servants and they are dead.\n\nStating he is not controlled by his god, he then stated he would probably be doing more important things if he was, then said that the methods normally though of used by the\nundead, killing, destroying, were proving innefficient.\n\nThey kill to send a message, and they are failing at delievering it.\n\nStating that Iblees has changed from the times of Aegis, that before he only wished for destruction, now he\nwishes to create the new world.\n\nI sugested that Iblees removed the curse of us, to show us he means the words that the undead stated. He responded by saying that Iblees had placed the curses to show his power, and make the mortals know he is\none of greater powers.\n\nWhile stating that dark and light weren't really all that diferent, he stated that those of the Corruption sect could heal others.\n\nBeing injured I asked to be healed, as a demonstration. He\nsaid that Iblees would have to look upon those healed as something more than just decendents, something more worthy for it to work.\n\nIn the middle of trying to find something for him to heal, I mentioned perhaps an animal, and he afirmed that\nanimals were to kill, then it would not work.\n\nSo instead, he demonstrates it on himself. A Staff of the Betrayer was brought to him, he does not seem to have the power to create one. With his staff, the Xan Paladin was asked to swing and cut off one\nof his arms. In front of us he remade his bones, stating that this could not happen in Aegis. Proof that Iblees had changed he said.\n\nHe repeated many times that those that do not mess with the undead will not be harmed.\nSnow's Maidan 1481\n\n-Daniel Nodal", ""),
        StaticBook("Task", "Allieice", "Name: Ganzorig\nAge: 15\nHeight: 5'9\"\nWeight: 140 lbs.\nFavorite Pasttime: Working in the mines.\nFavorite Color: Yellow.\nAppearance: Dark skin, grey/white hair, yellow eyes. Green shirt, covered in coal dust.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task #1", "Ralph Ferid Toronto", "Opinons on the Aspects\nTask 1\n\n\"They're cool I guess, don't know much about them.\"\nNaz Atatis\n\n\"It seems interesting and something I'd like to meddle with.\"\n-Arcanus Marrin\n\"I don't think it's a really bad thing that people are interested in druidism.\"\n-Valden Cardion\n\n\"It's a fine art, truly runs deep in this plains culture.\"\n-Delwyn Daenore\n\"Druidism is very interesting and I'd love to learn more.\"\n-Necthroma\n\n\"Druidism at times is more about internal conflict rather than spreading the word of nature.\"\n-Siri\n\"I guess it's not 'awful' considering it's nature and all.\"\n-Elois Fletcher\n\n\"I still don't think much of it, but I'm more inclined to investigate on it.\"\n-Wydren Volaren\n\"Druidism is pretty interesting, I might look more into it myself.\"\n-Reginald Raleigh\n\n\"I don't exactly have any issues with druidism as a whole.\"\n-Miche", ""),
