        StaticBook("The Bards Ellis", "Dread Knight Verin", "The Bards\n              Of \n             Ellis \n\n\n\nBy Verin Etitlan\n    Edemah Etitlan\n    Eiheiu Darky\n\"There once was a bard,\nDashing and daring,\nThe queens pants he did start to mangle, and they found him, and threw him to shambles.\n\nOut on the floor, cold as ice, his hair scratched and withered like lice --\nThat lonely bard, he did song. Of a place to the east, where no men could ying.\n\nThe druids, his home he did fine, and once more did this lonely bard find; \n\nHe took the archdruids pants and threw them a mangle,--\nAnd there they found him, and threw him to shambles!\"\n- Verin Etitlan.\n   Kalos/Anthos\nThe Will of God:\n\"The man looked down in fond reminiscance at the man he once knew. His dagger upraised in firm defiance, astrew its' blades handle, and he spoke, like the angry vassal of the messiah. \"You. Are. Done.\" The blade plunged down, slamming int\no the mans heart, and the ether came for him.\"\n  Edemah Etitlan\n     Kalos\nThe End:\n\"The armored man looked down to his creation, to its' mangled body. Its' child of any other, and it worked. Its' firm machinations elliciting no response, the ether calling out, trying as it would to grasp the man, to give him the end..unable.\nHe became his son, in all but name. His father his lord, forever in vein. His own son gone, lost to the ether he hoped for each day, he wishes he could go there, one day.\"\n   Unknown.\n     Anthos.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beard", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "-==-(The Beard)-==-\n\n-Chapter 1\n  -Anatomy of Beards\n\n-Chapter 2\n  -Household Uses\n\n-Chapter 3\n  -Famous Beards\n\n-Chapter 4\n  -The Future...\n-==(Chapter One)==-\nAnatomy of Beards\n\n      The beard is an apendage grown from the lower portion of the face and, when well kept, they may grow to glorious lengths. Aside from being pleasing in appearance, the beard has many uses which\n,if used properly, may create a funstioning and useful beard.\n-==(Chapter Two)==-\nSome Household Uses\n\n      The beard may be pleasing to the eye, but it is also as functional and useful as and arm or leg. The beard itself may be used by one experienced with beards to hold all manner of objects\nranging from small trinkets to large battleaxes. Those who actively grow and manage their beards may use them to carry larger and larger items, especially if oone is of dwarven blood. One who keeps things in his beard may become better and better at\nholding larger and larger things but the inexperienced may enter into a dangerous situation as the beard that is not managed well may become a fatal hazard.\n-=(Chapter Three)=-\nFamous Beards of Time\n\n      The following list is comprised of the famous dwarves and even some non-dwarves who have grown their beards to such length and splendor so as to be called famous.\n-Yemekar, he who creates beards\n\n-Urguan, the first dwarf\n\n-Native the Elf\n\n\n--More to be added in the next edition...\n-==(Chapter Four)==-\nThe Future of The Beard\n\nIn the next edition, more chapters are planned to be added including but not limited to:\n  -Military Uses\n  -Uncommon Uses\n  -Proper Management\n  -Arcane Uses", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beastiary I", "Adeon of Rhoswen", "The Marked Man's\nCompendium of Beasts\n\n\n        Volume II\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          Book I\nI. Animals\nII. Natural Monsters\nIII. Sentient Naturals\nIV. Sentient S.\nV. Monstrous S. 1/2\nSection I\n\n\n\n\n\n         Animals\n-Mammals-\n\nMammals are the group of vertebrae animals which form the class Mammalia. They have fur and the females bear live young, and produce milk for the young. Parental care of the young is universal among mammals and is crucial.\n-Birds-\n\nBirds are a class of vertebrates, the Aves. They are warm blooded and lay eggs. Their bodies are covered in feathers and they are winged. Birds are bipedal. Birds eat a lot of food compared to their weight due to their high energy use.\n-Fish-\n\nFish are gill-bearing aquatic vertebrates which lack limbs with digits. Fish are covered with scales, and have two sets of paired fins, and several unpaired fins. They are usually cold-blooded.\n-Reptile-\n\nReptile species are cold blooded, have scaly skin, and lay cleidoic eggs. They excrete uric acid, and have a cloaca. Reptiles are said to be the oldest of all animals and the closest to monstrosity.\n-Amphibians-\n\nIncluding frogs, salamanders and caecillians. These are 4 limbed vertebrates who are cold blooded. They lay their eggs in water. After hatching, they are tadpoles, which have gills. Once adult, they have lungs to breathe instead.\nSection II\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n    Natural Monsters\n-The Harpy-\n\nThese beasts prefer mountainous areas full of rocky patches where they may build nests and ambush their prey. \n\nHarpies posess large claws protruding from their toes and fingers, as well as a sharp beak.\nThey are humanoid in shape and from their spine sprouts two large, raven-like wings which are made up of large feathers of darker colours.  \n\nA trait shared by most Harpies is kleptomania, which can be taken advantage of in order to lure the beast.\nBeneath their beaks are glands which secrete oil when their body goes into combat-mode. The oil makes it very difficult for the Harpies to be grasped. Despite the advantages that may come with this ability, there is also a significant downside.\nThe oil is extremely flammable, almost on par with vodka. There is no way for the Harpies to put out the fire due to the oil soaking deep into their flesh and wings. Once alight, the Harpy is utterly doomed.\n-Krummavisur-\n\nEssentially giant ravens with powerful wings and claws. The primary method of killing their prey is by snatching them into the air and tossing them long distances.\nThey can kick up dust with the flap of their wings dense enough to block vision for yards. When more effort is applied, they can shove a fully armored figure onto his back with the strength of the air alone.\nThey have four weak spots. Both eyes and both feet. The only parts of their body not covered in dense feather. Strike in these areas to kill the beast.\n-Blodzuiger-\n\nThe Blodzuiger resembles a hairless bat with an extended neck and no face, just a massive, gaping mouth with rows of razor sharp teeth within. The beast's flesh is a natural flame retardant.\nYoung Blodzuigers resemble bloated leeches. They are without limbs and simply writhe around like a landbased tadpole. They are able to climb, however, using their powerful jaws and often drop down onto their prey from above.\nAdult Blodzuigers posess  pair of sharp wings, which they use to attack their prey with blinding accuracy and speed. The use of elixirs is suggested when fighting Blodzuigers. Particularily the kind that improve reflexes and vision in darkness.\n-Slaton-\n\nBloated creatures of the sea of humanoid appearance. They have sharp teeth with wide jaws capable of swallowing a man's head whole. They seem to enjoy feeding on livestock. Highly aggressive towards all humans.\nDespite the aggressive nature of the Slaton, it is possible to intimidate the beast with a show of force and equal amount of aggression. The Slaton's other method of combat is its ability to generate electricity through some natural process.\nDirect contact with a Slaton will cause an electric shock that will paralyse a man and send him to the floor. A dangerous problem when facing a Slaton is its many layers of blubber- which are very hard to pierce using any handheld weapon melee weapon.\nIt is for this reason a crossbow or a longbow should be used. Another weakness is fire. But most of all, if the beast is struck with a metal bolt in the right place in its spine, the electricity will backfire on the Slaton, causing it to explode.\n-Magnus Araneae-\n\nArachnids are lone hunters- they patiently wait for their prey to kill it with one swift strike when it appears. The same is true for their enlarged counterparts, Magnus Araneae.\nThese are huge creatures that took a liking to caves and big trees, becoming their undisputed kings. Rulers who do not tolerate other hunters in their territory, including Marked Men. Aranea are large, slow and protected by a durable armor.\nThe carapace, as Marked Men call this armor, is especially tough from the front, so it is much easier to wound the creature from the side or the back. The Araneae's charges its prey often. One has to evade the charge at all costs.\nAs soon as the beast has charged, one must then make their blow count. Without doubt its the best to use High-Guard along with half-pirouettes. The araneae has no fear of poison and not much fear of fire. Its nervous system barely reacts to pain.\nThe beast will heal its wounds after the fight. All said and done, the Aranea is a bug, so one's blade should be coated with pesticide oil before fighting it. The monster's susceptibility to this blade coating is probably its sole weakness.\nThe beast can easily shrug off other Marked tricks, so common poisons and spells are of little use, not to mention attempts to knock the colossus down.\nSection III\n\n\n\n\n   Sentient Naturals\n-The Troll-\n\nUsually found lurking in caves, forests or more commonly under bridges, these beasts can be helpful and friendly-- at other times they are a force to be reckoned with.\nTrolls are generally rather intelligent creatures capable of speech, emotion and co-operation. The best method of slaying a Troll is to disable its method of movement. \nThis method of movement being its legs. Aim for knees or the ankle tendon.\n-The Sylvan-\n\nSylvans often inhabit farmlands due to their diet of crops. If they can't find any caves, crevices, pits or chasms they will dig out their own little trench-like nests to live in.\nTheir nests are used to store their balls and left over crops, which they steal from nearby farmland. Sylvans combine the traits of both goats and men. They have blunt horns sticking out of their heads and often carry sacks of iron balls.\nA Sylvan's favourite passtime is playing tricks on people. These tricks can vaery from simply hiding farming tools to the more serious arsony. Sylvans can use their ability to mimick voices perfectly to devise elaborate ruses.\nSylvans are mostly harmless tricksters, their main form of defence being pelting people with iron balls. As sentient creatures, they are able to see reason. Several farmers have been able to convince the Sylvan to stop tricking people by offering food.\nIf it absolutely comes to it, a Sylvan is easily killed with a regular steel sword to any vital area including the heart, brain or spine.\nSection IV\n\n\n\n\n\n Sentient Supernatural\n-Specter/Spirit-\n\nSpirits without bodies, these creatures can be benevolent, neutral or malevolant just like in their previous lives. They can only be harmed by aurum, salt and clerical magic.\nThe easiest way to deal with a sentient spirit is to find the reason for its undeath and get rid of whatever is linking them to a place. Alternatively, clerical magic can be used or an aurum sword for temporary dispatchment.\n-Red Riders-\n\nInter-dimensional invaders. They scour the lands for the unsuspecting and abduct them to turn them into one of their own. They are omens of war and misfortune. They are extremely strong.\nTheir physical strength is matched by their magical ability, with the power to teleport both themselves and others as well as to summon strong winds that freeze all in its path. They are living beneath the armor and bleed- Hangman's oil may be effective.\nSection V\n\n\n\n\n\n       Monstrous\n     Supernatural\n-Necrophages-\n\nThe most common of beasts that a Marked Man will come across. These beings are re-animated dead, often due to necromancy or other darker magic. In the case of the Vodnik, it is due to a parasite in the water.\nAurum weaponry is recommended, though ferrum can also be used. Alone, they are easily dispatched but when amassed they can become the most dangerous of foes.\n-Zyme-\n\nHuge, featureless sacks of acid. They absorb parts of their environment, giving them different abilities. For example, a Zyme in a volcanic area may absorb sulphur and magma, becoming thrice as dangerous.\nTo destroy this beast, use an aurum sword and emphasise cutting over thrusting. This will allow the Marked Man to chop the Zyme down into pieces small enough for it to be rendered unable to clone itself. Burn the remains to ensure total death.\n-Kataphraktus-\n\nA creature of odd humanoid proportions, its hide ismade up of a black plate material. Its claws are large and it focuses on tearing its prey to pieces, which it then drags off to consume through unknown means.\nDue to the heavily armored nature of the Kataphrakt, the use of half-swording is an absolute must. Use aurum and aim for the areas beneath its arms or its joints, where the plating is weakest.\n-Wraith-\n\nWraiths are semi-spectral beings that are known for haunting areas where people have died. The wraiths are always connected to the sites of their demise, they may protect their homes, or seek vengeance.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cabin", "F.V.", "A long way into the forest sits a cabin, looking as though it has been left there for many years. Ivy covers the outer walls, so much so that if one were to pass the cabin, they may never notice it between it's disguise of ivy and trees. The windows -\n- look as though they were never clean, coated in a layer of dust and dirt. Oddly enough, a dim light shines from within the house, the dirty windows almost concealing it. Inside, the cabin is almost the same. Old, overgrown. Piles of dusty rags litter -\n- the damp wood floor. Ragged and ripped curtains frame the old windows, the draft occasionally causing them to wave around. A large fireplace sits opposite the bolted shut door, a crackling fire dancing happily within it, not bothered by it's -\n- surroundings. A woman sits in a rocking chair beside the fire, warming herself. A worried expression takes place on the woman's face, and she sits utterly still. Despite her surroundings, the woman is clothed in the finest materials, her dress fit for -\n- a queen. The woman buries her face in her hands, a shaky sigh escaping her as a loud thud echoes throughout the small cabin. She jumps up with a start, turning to face the door with widened eyes. With an uncertain expression on her face, she takes a -\n- step towards the door. The old wood creaks under her delicate step, and she winces at the noise. The woman takes a deep breath, gathering her courage as she continues her way towards the door, one hand on the wall to steady her, the other clenched -\n- into a fist at her side. A small note is slipped under the door, the edges torn and ragged. The woman's face falls, and she'd rush over to the note, picking it up with shaking hands. The note would read, in extremely messy writing: 'The prince is dead.'\nHer eyes would scan over these words several times, as though she couldn't quite believe it. A strangled cry would come from the woman as she falls onto the floor, sobs echoing throughout the small room.  She'd grip the note close to her chest, tears -\n- staining her aged face. \"My son..\" She'd mutter the words, the room seeming to spin around her.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Challenge", "Thurak", "Rescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 18th of Sun's Smile, 1484.\nAn Archdruid cannot be removed from position by a vote or by force. Only if he retires or dies may his position be claimed as empty. However, when an Archdruid becomes exceedingly inactive or loses sight in what’s right for the Order and refuses\nto retire, his position may be challenged. The Challenge is an only ever should be issued in the most extreme and rare f cases. When all hope is lost and the Order is suggereing because of an Archdruid, the Challenge may be instituted and may\nonly be instituted by a Druid Hierophant. The Hierophant who issues the Challenge shall create a difficult, and unbiased, trial that requires the challengers and the challenged to put many skills to the test such as exploration, investigation, wisdom,\nand peity. Furthermore, the existing Archdruids must all agree to the terms of a Challenge. This event could take anywhere from a few Seeds to a Year, and whoever returns to the Hierophant, first, with the required information, items, or\nknowledge, will be deemed the victor and shall take the seat of the challenged Archdruid. If anyone is realise to have cheated or wronged the Challenge in some way, they will be disqualified. In the case that only two individuals, a challenger and the\nchallenged, take part in this vigorous trial and one cheats or wrongs in some way, the other will be victor even if he is the individual being challenged. As aforementioned, a Challenge shall only ever happen as a last resort. The Inner Circle,\nall except for the Archdruid being challenged, must deem it necessary as must a Hierophant to organise and oversee it. This rite should never and cannot be abused. Those who try to see to its usage in improper context shall feel not only\nthe wrath of the Aspects, but that of the Order as well. Blessed be he who takes any and all proper precautions with a troubled Archdruid before seeing the institution of a Challenge.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Circle", "Henry Winterleaf", "Nature:\n\nThe waves crash against the rocks.\n\nThe boat gently approaches the docks.\n\nIt's made of wood from lands afar.\n\nUsed to travel to where you are.\nMade by people of different races.\n\nMany people, many faces.\n\nSomeone's child, every one.\n\nBuilding boats in the sun.\nPaid with gold, from the ground.\n\nHard and cold, to be found.\n\nMined within the caves below.\n\nTheir torches set the stone aglow.\nAnd from the ground we get the stone.\n\nHard and dull, its age unknown.\n\nAgainst the waves, the rocks remain.\n\nAnd the cycle then repeats again.", ""),
        StaticBook("The contract", "Thairel", "I, Thairel, hereby am a 'slave' of Illithri.\n\nThis counts for evry human day, half a day, for the next 10 years. \nPrivacy will be given, no secrets will be hiden. \n\nThairel will be provided of anything in need.\n6th of the sun's smile, the year 1536", ""),
        StaticBook("The Coronation", "Lilyana", "In the dark of night, an elder man hobbles with a walking stick towards the quiet village. The man’s curiosity is pricked by the silence in the town, a town that once was bustling with life regardless of the time. But, the pain in his back and ache in his\nfeet quickly nudged any questions from his mind as he hobbled along the path. He had been traveling for days, braving the wilderness and streets to reach this town, and finally he was close to his destination. However, he had no idea what he was heading\nto or why he started this journey. He awoke one morning, some days ago, and felt a tingling sensation in his fingertips, one he had not felt for years. As the days passed, the sensation slowly began to spread throughout his body and the tingling became\nstronger; he began to feel an urgency to understand what was causing it. Only days ago had he remembered what this feeling, this sensation, was; it was the excitement, the rush of energy, the craving for blood he felt before he killed a target of the\nCrimson Fist. Though his body old and tired now with age, this sensation revitalized him enough to send him into the unknown, to this very town. With each step, the pull on him became stronger, more intense, until now, as he stood outside a large barn,\nthe only lit building in the entire town, did he feel like he would burst from excitement. He licked his chapped lips, wrapped his wrinkled hands around the bar, and pulled with all his might on the door, opening it.\n\n    Cora danced around the flame in\nthe center of the barn, its light dancing along the walls. The deep crimson blood markings and gold jewelry that she wore contrasted against her pale skin. She paid the old man no attention, although she knew full well of his presence, and continued to\ndance around the fire, chanting verses of an old Crimson ritual. As the old man stepped into the light of the fire, Evaine quieted her chanting and slowed her dance. She stopped on the side of the wall where a robe of deep crimson hung on a peg. She\nfluidly placed the robe about her shoulders then made her way to a corner of the barn that the fire's light did not reach. She looked back over her shoulder, smirking at the old man, before disappearing into the shadows.\n\n The old man scanned\nthe barn with his old eyes, his poor ears only hearing the crackling of the fire. He saw nothing, heard nothing, but his very being knew someone, or something was there. From across the fire, from under the shadow of the barn's hay loft, two piercing red\neyes broke the darkness and stared at the man, as if they were staring into his soul. The sensation from earlier now rocked the elder; he clung to his walking stick as a force of power pulled him down onto his knees. The owner of the glowing eyes stepped\ninto the light of the flame, revealing himself to be an abnormally tall, toned, young man, Haemon. His hair of white gold flowed to his shoulder, his skin as pale as snow, but his eyes, they glowed like lumps of red, hot coal, burning in his eye sockets.\nHaemon walked around the fire, slowly approaching the elder. With each step, the elder gripped his walking stick tighter as the power that the boy was emanating tried harder and harder to pull him to the floor. When the boy stood over the old man, he was\nshaking with strain and effort to remain kneeling and barely spat out the words before collapsing:\n\n“M-M-My…..L-L-Lord-d-d….M-My P-Prince”\n\nWhen the old man awoke, he found himself sitting against the wall of the barn.\nHe felt a sharp pain at his arm and upon inspection found it bandaged tightly, a small blood stain slowly spreading on it. He went to tug on the bandage but a delicate hand quickly grabbed his hand and pulled it from the wound. The elder looked up,\nmeeting Cora’s gaze as she slowly shook her head. She pulled out a skin full of water and offered it to the man who, only realizing his thirst at the sight of the skin, quickly took it from her and drank it down. She left him a small plate, some bread and\ncheese, and walked around the flame to the other side of the fire. Following her movement, the old man realized that the boy had been sitting across from him this entire time, watching him. Cora slid down along the wall until she was next to the boy, then\ncurled herself against him, passing him a vial of a crimson liquid that the old man knew all too well, a vial of blood, his blood.\n\nHaemon lifted the vial to face level, staring at it as the fire's light illuminated the contents. Haemon smiled and asked\nfor his name.\n\n\"Eren\", the old man responded.\n\nHaemon shook his head and smiled again, but this time his eyes glowed and a voice unlike the previous one asked for his “true name”. The old man dropped hid bit\nof cheese and drew his limbs into him. His gaze met the fiery gaze of Haemon and memories of a life he tried hard to forget washed over him.\n\n\"Doulos, my lord.\" The old man said, maintaining eye contact with Haemon as he spoke, \"Servant to you and your\ncause.\"\n\nHaemon nodded and tossed the vial of blood into the fire. The flame erupted into a shower of sparks and turned black as the night around them, all except for the center which glowed with light. The light soon warped and changed and the old man\nwatched his own memories, his life from his eyes play before him for all to see. He watched the battle where the temple fell where he fought as a mere Doulos, a soldier and servant to the Crimson Prince’s cause. His escape into the woods as the temple\ncollapsed, his struggle for survival, his search for others, his attempts to rebuild what was lost. But alas, he watched himself give into what seemed to be reality that no others had survived, and watched as he isolated himself from the world, locking\nthe few relics of his past life away in a chest.\n\nThe flames died down, the color returned to its orange and red glow, and the barn returned to the quiet it had once been. Haemon stood before the flame and spoke of how few of his followers survived that\nbattle. He made a point to mention how few had attempted to continue his cause and gracefully pointed to the hay-loft above. The elder’s vision followed Haemon’s direction until it, only now, noticed countless bodies in the loft above, wrinkled and dry,\nseemingly drained of their blood. The man reeled back in fear from Haemon, but Haemon only smiled and waved his hand in front of him. He reassured the man that their fate was the fate of cowards and betrayers, those that tried to hide their connection to\nhim. \n\n“But the few,” Haemon said as he waved his hand to Cora and back to the old man, “the few that stayed true to me now reap great rewards.”\n\nHaemon explained how the rituals Core and he performed summoned the small\nbit of power that the Crimson Prince left in this world. That ritual created a connection between Haemon and the Crimson Prince; that the Prince now acted through Cora’s child, Haemon.\n\n\"I must feed on the blood of the living, fueling my power to allow\nthe Prince to return to this world as his true self. We have been traveling to settlements, slowly feasting on its populace as my power grows in strength with each feasting.” Haemon pointed above to the bodies. \"It seems as my power grows, those of the\nold Crimson Fist that had survived are drawn to us. We’ve tested those that come, and those to have hidden from their past have been feasted on. While those who were true to our prince, have been given power.”\n\nThe old man perked up. \"Power, my lord?\nWhat do you mean?\"\n\nHaemon’s eyes glowed bright, his power exerting itself in the room once more. The fire reached for the ceiling as Haemon lifted his right hand from his side. As his hand lifted, so did the elder man, levitating him in mid-air. Haemon\nwithdrew a silver dagger and sliced a thin line down his right forearm. Haemon began to recite a dark chant from deep within his mind and the blood that was slowly seeping from the wound began to rise into the air. The blood hovered over to the elder man\nand began to circulate around him, slowly at first but picking up speed quickly. With quick movement, Haemon shut his fist closed, forcing the blood that spun around the old man to suddenly stop and bury its way into his body. The old man howled with pain\nfor only a moment before his eyes glazed over and his screaming silenced. The man’s body erupted into black flames, devouring him entirely, burning the flesh from his very bones. Cora stood and approached Haemon, wrapping her arms around his torso and\nshoulder as they watched on together. The Black Flame finally dissipated, leaving a figure in a crimson cloak where the old man once was.\n\n“Arise”, Haemon ordered with a voice not his own, “ Arise, my new Blood Mage.”\n\nThe figure stood from\nthe ash of the black fire and removed his hood, revealing Eren, but as his once youthful self. Eren stared at his hands, no longer wrinkled and weak; he felt his face for saggy skin and scars of old age but only found the tight, tough skin. He felt\nrevitalized, no empowered. The ritual had given him a small piece of his lord’s power, and that small piece had not only turned back time to when the old man was once called Doulos, it gave him strength, power, and life.\n\n\"Blood, the essence\nf life, is quite a powerful catalyst, as you now see with your own eyes, Doulos. It’s power is only limited by the Mage’s imagination.” Haemon said as Cora wrapped a small bandage around his wrist. \"Ours, theirs, it matters not where it comes from, but\nhe purity, power, and amount, that determines the strength of magic that comes from it.” Haemon showed the wound to Doulos, “Until our true lord is able to come into this world our magic is limited, but still powerful.”\n\nDoulos nodded, \"So what is the\nnext step? How do we bring forth our Lord, once and for all?\"\n\nCora stepped forward, revealing documents that had thought to have been lost with the years. “Cruor Veneficus, the Blood Tome. A magical tome that the Crimson Fist once had. If we were\nto reclaim this tome, we would be able to channel the magical energy from it, making our magic infinite and allow Haemon to focus his feeding on bringing forth our Lord.”\n\nDoulos nodded in agreement and asked \"But where do we start looking for the\ntome?\"\n\nCora smiled, “According to the documentation we found on the betrayers and cowards mentions the Cruor Veneficus last being seen in the Crimson Fist’s stronghold in the mountains of the North, the mountains\nwhere the settlement “Raven’s Nest” now stands. Word on the street of this town was that a coronation of some sort is to take place there as well, bringing in many guests.” Cora smiled a toothy grin, “If we do not find the Cruor Veneficus, at least there\nwill be many for my Prince to feast on.\"\n\n “Raven’s Nest is heavily defended and manned, how are we to take the city?” Doulos questioned.\n\nYou are not the only Blood Mage, Duolos.” Haemon answered as he motioned for Cora to open the barn's\ndoor. “There have been others that I found worthy to bestow power upon, like yourself, that now hide themselves amongst the cities of this land. They pretend to normal folk of their race, gathering information, and working their way into cities and\ngovernments.\" Haemon motioned outside the barn’s open door where the sunrise was just peeking over the horizon. The low light illuminated many hooded figures walking towards them. \"And many more followers are being drawn here, as you were, and they will\night alongside us, wielding powerful Blood Magicks.”\n\nHis questions answered and his mind set straight, Doulus nodded and resigned. \"Yes, my Lord. Raven's Nest cannot, will not, stand against our power and cause. He smiled widely,\n\"Our Lord, our Crismon Prince, will rise once more”.\nThe Coronation\n            of the\n        True Prince\n\n  A Sequel to the\n Rebirth of Evil\n\n\n\nWritten by: Lilyana", ""),
        StaticBook("The Crown-Prince", "Jacob Chapel", "\"The Basis of the Perfect State\" was written by Edward Winter II as gift to Ostromir Sarkozic Carrion upon the conquest of Renatus.\n\nThis book has been transcribed and copied by and under guidance of Jacob Chapel.\n\n((Original by AiiM))\nThe Basis of the Perfect State\nTo the Crown-Prince,\n\nThe governance of a state must be just. To be a just state, the governing body must execute their duties and powers efficiently with the will of the people and the good of the state held\nas supreme.\n\nThe judicious and firm-handed monarch can in his own right control the state. A monarchy is far more efficient, effective, and has a lesser potential for corruption than the republican system of councils, voting, and election. The downfall\nof the just monarch is his heir. The spoiled child corrupts the state, the weak-willed monarch relinquishes the power of the royal family. The royal heir must be established as the supremely noble and knowledgeable steward of the state, whose governance\nis just and his decisions well-made.\n\nThe ill-fit heir has, in the past, been rectified by extensive counsel, where the royal extends to his advisors the powers of the state. The function of the government in this state does deteriorate, as the\nabsolutism of the monarch is sullied by the extended powers and corruptions of the monarch's counselors, whose motives and intellects are unknown and unverified.\n\nSo one must establish the basis by which a just monarch can be ensured by the generations.\nElection of the most just by the common people is a flawed system, as the uneducated and ignoble masses know not of justice nor righteousness. The thieves and beggars in the charity of the state should not be tasked with the selection of a\nrepublican heir. The whims of the people to favour a man do not establish him as the most effective steward and leader to his people.\n\nElection by the masses of nobility is too a flawed system, as the nobles delight in their pleasures without properly\nknowing of management or governance. Their corruptions of sin diminish their efficacy as a just constituency.\n\nThe solution then, is to look for the most just of a collective of just monarchs in a collective of states, and to choose from them a supreme\nmonarch, who should steward the constituent monarchs in his wisdom and with a firm-hand.\n\nWere the Kingdoms of humanity to with each other combine, and the monarchs together of varying levels of aptitude to their position were to choose from amongst\nthemselves the most well fit to the supreme crown over the constituent monarchs, then a just monarch could be established. The unity of the Kingdoms should  strengthen the military and economic state of function, and further serve to demilitarize and\nfocus supplies on economic pursuits, by allowing for the each of the states to contribute to a military to a lesser degree, which shall together equal a force unrivaled by any modern monarch.\n\nThe human Kingdoms of Salvus, Ruska, Herendul, and Oren,\nwere they to unite, could each contribute but 25,000 men to a combined force, and still manage to afford their borders greater protection than if they alone attempted to muster 90,000 each for their own interests, an impossible feat regardless.\nThe unified states would be able to pass and enforce legislation and regulation, and efficiently and effectively steward their states with the guidance of an emperor-steward and his leadership in their governance.\n\nFurthermore, the borders and futures\nof the human states would be secured by the stabilizing force of the constitutional empire and her emperor-steward, who would be elected by the constituent Kings to be the most just of all men to govern humanity. The states would together validate their\nclaims and legislature, and their combined military force would both strengthen the defense of their borders and allow for each of the constituent Kingdoms to turn focus upon their domestic affairs.", ""),
        StaticBook("The day I Grimed", "MichaelB450", "It was a dark day at the high elves meeting place, there was a massive group in the meeting room and there was one man, who was also in the room, by the name of Michael. He was a strange high elf, who often said strange things to women.\nThis time he said the strangest thing he has ever said to his people. There was a gay man nearby, who was also in the meeting room. Michael became so nervous with the gay man looking at him that he managed to grim instead of grin.\nThis caused my whole team to essentially face palm and think of me as an idiot. The other elfs in the room were also face palming, but they thought it was pretty funny. They continued to poke fun at Michael for the rest of the meeting.\nIn the end everyone agreed that it was a pretty funny thing that happened that day and they left the meeting remembering the whole thing as a great time!\n\nAnd that was the time I Grimed,\nThank you for reading!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Deposed Clan", "Saito Issen Yoshida", "\n      Clan Yoshida\n     In The Age of\n       Deposition\n\n\n*A stylized image of a smoking pagoda adorns this page. The corpse of a serpant like dragon at it's base.*\nMany ages past, in lands once occupied by the people of vailor, a family of foreigners and their loyal retainers sailed, and made upon the shores a new home to spread their culture and acquire new wealth for the family in the east.\nThe grand elder of clan Yoshida presided over much area, gaining favor with the local lords and nobility, often taking in their sons and warriors for training, either in the arts of war, or the arts of humanity.\nThe prosperity brought to the clan was great, even to the locals. Soon, however, the great elder of the clan had passed his title down to his son, Ishigawa Yoshida and then faded into retirement as a shrine tender.\nHowever, the clan's assistance to eradicate a group of estranged warriors and assassins brought a certain calamity. Lord Ishigawa, and the former great elder were both defeated in the night. Fighting to their last breath with many retainers against\nthis group of red-cloaked assassins that wielded strange powers over shadows and death. The matron of the clan escaped however, with a few trusted warriors of the clan and Ishigawa's son. Living in secret for many years, off the generosity of many,\nthe matron and her attendants brought to bare the safety and secure the line of clan Yoshida for now. \n\nThis continued through many different lands, up until the great migration to Vailor, where the son of Ishigawa, a man named Saito\nhad decided to bring upon his family's legacy that led all the way back to the secured lands in the far eastern provinces and empires. Though continued connections there, it was thought by him to be shameful to return, leaving what his father and\ngrandfather worked for many years to attempt to secure, and this he went upon to the great imperial nation of Oren once again. Previous allies of his people for assistance. With the few countrymen he had managed to gather together, and fine gifts that had\ntaken months to muster, and brought them to the seat of their nobility's thrones. One after one however, they had refused any ammount of sympathy with these estranged people and the deposed noble Yoshida. Often refusing them and their gifts swiftly at the\ngate, without even hearing what was to say. \n\nThe bigotry and hatefulness drove these people south to the lands of the great Khalestine, and the caliph Faiz. Faiz refused to accept the wealth of these people,\nand by his mercy gifted upon the unlanded errant Yoshida, his own estate and lands to govern over. There, with the help of his associates he had formed the school of Kasai. A fortress in the eastern reaches of the caliphate.\nThrough much time, the clan had once again grown to a notable number, as Yoshida and his closest companions accepted students from minor nobility or those in need that showed promise, along with training the men of the Caliphate as a sign of friendship.\nAll the while, Yoshida took it upon himself to avenge his family's line. In attempt to regain the honor and grace that was stolen from the house's lands many years in the past. This quest of his brought him through many lands, where he had discovered\nclues to the ancient red-clothed assassin's nature. Even to the point of discovering them, and putting their number to the sword. A number close to seven honor duels were fought and won by Saito, but the true number and name of this group eluded him.\nEventually however, as Kasai finally neared completion and the prosperity that clan Yoshida once knew, it was betrayed by a renegade student that had been allied with the same shadow-wielding members.\nIn one night, students were slain, the temple burned, and the fields salted. Yoshida and his closest consorters were forced to flee. \n\nMonths passed, and a refuge for the survivors was built in the mountains. The number thoroughly\nscattered to the wind, only five remained. \n\nEventually, the vendetta against clan Yoshida had caught up with them. The simple idea of \"Every job is done.\" Held by this mysterious group had led to the endless misery of this once great\npeople. The refude was found, and more of the survivors put to the sword. Then, Saito once again was forced to wander about, living off the generosity of others.\n\nThough the spirit and life of the people is not dead. Former Samurai, and wanderers\nhad pulled themselves to this deposed noble, and clan Yoshida has been gaining once again swiftly. \n\n§TThe Wind at our back\n§TThe Sun Sets on our § Last Day\n§ A New Sun Rises", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diamond[s]", "N.Y.", "vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvThe\nDiamond[s] - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\n(A collection of poems written by a soldier. Found in the rough.)\n\n(Includes 5 Poems)\nThe\nPrayer - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nI worry if I go to war,\nMutts will come knockin’ on my door.\nPlease protect my loved ones, Lord.\nMake me hard as diamond \nso I can crush these hordes.\nAnswer this, I’ll never ask for more.\nI wrap this prayer up and trace the cross\nOn the tabard that my grandfather wore.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nThe\nLifestyle - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nI’m afraid of my lifestyle.\nI’m figurin’ out my life now.\nBut f**kas comin’ at my life now.\nIgnited powder to blow my house down.\nThey don’t wanna see me breathin’ this evenin’.\nNo matter how much I try to reach em’ and lead em’.\nI lost my eye because of one fatal accident.\nI guess my swordplay needed more practicin’.\nThat’s when I learned that war wasn’t for every-body.\nNearly lost mine so I killed the f**ka’ before they got me.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nThe Old\nTendencies - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nOld Khalestine, city filled with Hash fiends.\nCrazy Hassan used to ride camels with a mad lean.\nThat’s how you remember it, that’s how I remember it.\nI done caught a couple arrows, been stabbed,\nHence why I keep my sword strapped.\nAnd truthfully, I think over half yall’ b***h made.\nAnd if you don’t trust my ‘A’ Grade,\nGo on, my Qali, come and test my blade.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nThe Woman sent\nfrom Allah - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nYou shine like diamonds,\nYou’re bright as gold,\nYou soothe my achin’ soul.\nTruth within your eyes,\nNever told me a lie.\nI hold you up to the sky,\nI tell you that I might die\nbefore I hit twenty five.\nbut you give me peace of mind\nand remind me that I’m alive.\nOur reunions are a surprise,\nSo bright that with you I’m never lost.\nWhen I first stumbled into you,\nI knew that you were sent from God.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nThe Land\nOf Eden - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nOpen up your eyes, tell me what you see in-\nside of me, tell me exactly what you thinkin’.\nCould this be love, that be how it’s seemin’.\nAnd you should know that I been meanin’\nTo take you back to our slice of Eden\nWhere the flowers and the trees are meetin’.\nJust hold my hand, I can take you to that land\nGoodbye to sand, where our people damned.\n\n vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diary:Part 2", "Boris", "Dear diary,\nit has been a few days since Jackson Fyord was banished. I watched him a bit, and he turned out to be a homeless man wandering the streets in his quest for snowballs. I don't really know how, but he got a residence and a home in the north.\nThe north is where there is snow. Coincidence? I THINK NOT. He probably does it for more snowballs.\nAnd within three days he got a northern accent and also speaks a bit strangely. Internally I wonder JUST HOW DOES ONE GET A ACCENT WITHIN THREE DAYS?!\nAnyway, I wonder how long it will take for him to get kicked out again due to his erratic behavior. They also told him to change his name to 'Yuriy'. That name was much harder to remember than 'Jackson Fyord' for some reason.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Distillator", "Thurak'Yar", "*An annotated diagram of the machine is\npinned to the wall*\n\n\n((http://i.imgur.com/vBcPhoL.png))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Divine", "Sage Kalen", "What's one is five,\nbut five is nothing.\n\nNothing shall be everything,\nWhilst everything shall be the end.\n\nOnly one knows the way, but the five hold the key.\nThe key unlocks everything.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dreamer", "Sofetios", "The Dreamer\nBy Sofetios\n\nThe Dreamer,\nThe one who dares not to be the same,\nFor in dreams mysteries unravel,\nAnd endless space you do travel,\nAs you r dreams you try to tame.\nAs the Dreamer,\nDreams above the sky,\nAnd looks down below,\nTo the people that show,\nWho know not what lies that high.\nUnwakened,\nThe Dreamer,\nIn a maze of thoughts,\nWandering the mists,\nWith endless twists,\nAs the path on minds papers he jots.\nThough be wary dreamer,\nAs thoughts tend to run away,\nOnly the ones you really need,\nAnd the ones you often feed,\nAre the ones that often stay.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid Guide", "Unknown", "The Druid Guide\n\n     by Unknown\nThe Order\n\nThe Druids of Anthos are a group deditcated to preserving the balance of nature. All druids undergo years of learning and studying in order to establish a strong link with nature.\nAlthough some are known to walk the land spreading the teachings of Druidism, the Order currently resides in their Grove outside of Leumaelin. Despite the misconception that only Elves can be Druid, the Order is open to all races, as it welcomes all who\nwish to follow the way of the Aspects.\n\nThe Druids do not recognize those who proclaim to walk the way of the Druid yet do not take the time to go through the studying.\n\nThat is to say, only those who have been\npromoted to the status of Druid by one of the Guide rank or higher will be acknowledged for their wisdom.\nTotems\n\nAll of those who are full-fledged Druids possess a title, sometimes referred to as a totem. This totem represents their history, their personality, and their approach to life.\nIt is up to the Druid to identify themselves with an appropriate title. The time at which a Dedicant becomes a Druid is up to both those higher in the order and the Dedicant themselves.\nPowers\n\nIt is well known that Druids are some of the best healers in the land, yet the true extent of these powers is unknown. Druids have been known to bring people back from the brink of death and restore sight to the blind.\nThe Druids are deeply connected to nature, yet do not control nature, but serve it. To try to have power over something without understanding is against their ways. It is more similar to asking nature for favours, and then doing nature favours in return.\nThough, nature will sometimes do very large favours, if the situation calls for it.\nResponsibilities\n\nThe Druids pride themselves with being the keepers and protectors of Nature. They will allow the chopping down of a tree, possibly even the removal of a forest, but in return they expect each tree to be replanted elsewhere.\nDruids are non-violent  and, due to their long periods of studying in their libraries, are known to be fantastic sources for information. However, despite their non-violent tendencies, Druids will do whatever it takes to preserve the safety of Nature\nwhen it is threatened, and will resort to fighting if the situation demands it.\n\nThe Druids use their prowess in healing to their advantage, and are often approached when an individual is ill or injured.\nThe Order is also in association with Malinor, and at certain times they have held close connections with the Elven government, including having certain Druids hold seats in the Elven Council.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druids Grove", "Leyun Kameki", "The Druid's Grove\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, The Solstice Druid\nThe Druids’ Grove is a place of Aspectial worship and peaceful congregation. It is a place where natural Druidic energies run deep and life flourishes in the glory and light of Cerridwen and Cernunnos. The Mother Grove, usually the most grand of all\ngroves on a given land mass, houses the Druidic Order and serves as their place of spreading the Druidic way through ancient teachings.\n\nNever should violence or anti-natural forces be issued within the grove; when these things are wrought on\nsuch sacred grounds, a Druid may do what he must to see the sanctity and peaceful aura restored. Furthermore, never should armor or weapon be donned in a grove for it is an area of peace and harmony with nature. When an individual holds armor and/or\nweapon, he anticipates violence and the need for said materials which only brings violent thought and meaning to the grove, thus disrupting the peaceful and harmonic aura.\n\nDruids’ groves have served throughout history as an\nimportant aspect of Druidic culture and Druid congregation. They’ve also served as elegant gardens, floral and faunal reserves, and places of knowledge. Drui’inder, take into account the purpose and sanctity of the Druids’ grove to better your\nunderstanding of Druidic culture and spread your wisdom to the generations to come so that they, too, may be enlightened by this cultural tradition. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dwarven town", "Rain Vanguard", "THe king of the Dawven town is King Balek of the clan Irongut the one who tole me was Clan father Verthaik Frostbeard I told him that I was looking to a job that I was going to mine he told me  by telling him that I was new and need a job\nthe kindom is up a moutain", ""),
        StaticBook("The EXODUS", "Aelidar Elsil'sirame", "The\nEXODUS\nof the\nAHERAL\n-*-*-*-:=-\nA recount of the\nevolution of High Elf\nculture amidst the\nLast Days of Anthos.\n-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-:=-\nas documented in the\nYEAR 1445, by\nAelidar Elsil'sirame\nThe FORERUNNERS\n-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-:=-\nIt began as The Grand\nHarvest crept upon\nthe Realm of Anthos. It\nbegan slowly; it began\nwith only a few, but\nthese few would be the\nfortunate ones.\nThey would leave of\ntheir own accord, and\nwith their own reasons.\nThe old Maheral known\nto elcihi as Lucion\nSullas would be the\nfirst to emerge from\nLin'evaral's gates,\nfrustrated and \nfurious. It is known\nthat this elf found\nfault with the present\nmentality among the\nmali'aheral. Those who\nwitnessed his noisy departure\n... into the forests of\nthe Old Princedom of\nMalinor, would remember\nhis condemnation of\nthe people of elcihi, \"A\ntain on the maehr'sae\nhiylun'ehya\".\nIn Sullas's eyes, logic\nhad left the mali'aheral.\nDespite the disdain\nwith which such an\nexit...\n...might have typically\nprovoked, his\ndissatisfaction would\nprove to be\ncontagious.\nOn the heels of Sullas\nscampered Lelien Lazul\nnée Aeléyèlsa, newly\nwedded to Acaele, and\nlibrarian of the\nEternal Library of\nLin'evaral. It seemed,\nhowever, that\nwhatever ties were\npresent, she felt\ncompelled to leave the\nvenerated silver city.\nIt was said that she\nintended to return to\nelcihi, but for now,\nMalinor was host to\nanother unwelcome\nguest.\nThe mali'aheral\nKalameet would make a\nmore disruptive exit. In\nleaving, he addressed\nletters to selected\nfriends, detailing his\ndisappointment in the\nillogical mentality of\nscorn and disdain\nwhich had permeated\nthroughout the aheral\ncommunity.\nThe letters of\nKalameet would\npresent a thoughtful\ndiscussion for each of\nthe mali'aheral. The\nstandards of purity,\nwhich had for so long\ngoverned the Enclave\nof Haelun'or, would be\ncalled into question.\nKalameet argued that\nthose considered\n'impure'...\n...should be treated\nwith more\nunderstanding than\nhad been the case;\n\"I've noticed many\nshun others from the\nwalls who offer things\nof value. Things that\ncan aid maehr'sae\nhiylun'ehya have been\npushed away because\nof citizens' deluded\nsense of Purity.\"\nThe DESTRUCTION\nof LIN'EVARAL\n-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-:=-\n\n~\n\n*a single scratch marks where the author had begun writing*\nI, Aelidar Elsil'sirame, presently find myself in no state to finish this documentation of my people's last days in Anthos. I ask, for the sake of our legacy, that one of my own complete this work.\n\n-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-\n*the book is unfinished*\n((I have a notepad doc. of this book, if you PM me on the forums: Aelidar))", ""),
        StaticBook("The False Vision", "Ryn", "I spoke at great length on the subject of Gazadriel with the High Prophet of the Dwarven nation, Hogarth last evening with Za'Kabar. During our chat, we gained information that may be useful in the coming days. I make this record for the future generation\nof decendants, so they may know our plight. \n\nAll of this started a few Elven days ago, when I had taken some nightsap with my sister Illithri, in an attempt to finally get some sleep. As I dreamed of camping in the Fringe, my rest was interrupted by a\nvision of a rainbow colored fairy ring. Once I stepped inside of it, I awoke.\n\nAn emergency moot was called a few hours later. A second vision had been already viewed by many who chose to step into a fairy ring.\nThey stated that this second vision told them of a coming harvest of souls, and that the one reaping them must be preserved.\n\nThis went against everything I had ever been taught of being a Druid. We are neutral, we preserve the balance of\nnature. To take a life like this reaper is cannot be part of the balance. A few people agreed with me and together, we set out to prove this vision as false.\n\nAmong those who came were Henry and Barry Winterleaf, Illitri, Eloh'ra, Aeras, Za'Kabar, and\nOliver. Together, we set off from the Grove and made a bunker in which to hide and research who could have made a false vision to us. \n\nAs time went on, Aeras went to see the vision for himself. When he returned, he convinced Eloh'ra that the\nreaper must indeed be preserved and they left our numbers. \n\nAfter this happened, it became clear that I needed to see the vision for myself. Za'Kabar and I left the bunker together and travelled to the fairy ring within the Grove. Together, we stepped\ninside of the ring and instantly passed out.\n\nThe vision that I saw was as follows. I was standing within a field of wheat, watching a harvester reap the grain. As I watched, the stalks of wheat turned into decendants: Humans, Elves, ect.\nAs the harvester reaped the decendant stalks of wheat, it's scythe seemed to draw the very souls from them.\n\nThe vision continued and someone appeared in the field. They slayed the reaper with a golden sword. As the reaper died, a mighty storm appeared,\ndestroying the field of wheat. A voice spoke and said the harvest must continue, the reaper must be preserved.\n\nI awoke with Za'Kabar and we both agreed in that moment that this vision could not be from the Aspects. It was then we set off in two different\ndirections. Za'Kabar travelled to the Stream Circle, to see if there were others who felt the way we did.\n\nOliver and I departed the Grove and travelled to the Cloud Temple to seek wisdom from the books there. \n\nThere, we ran into my nephew,\nYohei, one of the Elder Monks at the temple. When I told him of the vision and my belief, he said he would help all he could and began his own research.\n\nWe settled down for the evening, reading every book that we could find. The book about Aenguls\nhad an interesting name inside of it. The name of Gazadriel. He is the Aengul of curiostiy, new beginnings and the one most involved in mortal affairs. \n\nI moved on to another book, one on the group known as the Ascended.\nThe first mention of Gazadriel was in the death of Sage Martin Benedict. He had a Golden Staff in his possession, and as he decended into madness, he clutched it.\n\nWhen the time of his death came, he cursed the staff and\nthrough it away from him. He warned the Acolytes that it was the Golden Staff of Gazadriel. That it was imbued with Gazadriel's intent to 'renew' the world, to destory it and build it again as he saw.\n\nMore mention of Gazadriel's name came a little\nfurther into the next part. Gazadriel had appeared from the staff to the Ascended in Anthos. The events were confusing that I read about, but continued on down the page.\n\nOnce finished with that book, it was decided between Oliver, Za'Kabar, and\nmyself that we would need a lot more information to determine if Gazadriel truly was the cause of the false vision.\n\nThe hour was growing late at this point, and having no where to go, Za'Kabar and I left Oliver at the temple to rest and moved on to\nspeak with our next hope for help: Hogarth. \n\nDuring this time, rumors began that people were hunting Druids, because of the vision. Many people had beleived the false vision and sworn to protect the reaper. The reaper that we knew of at the time\nhappened to be a Frost Witch. That was another... thing... that pushed me over the edge of not believing in the vision. But anyway, Za and I made our way to Hogarth's home. He took us in and we told him of our plight. He gave us a room for the night and\npromised any assistance he could give, and that he would keep his eyes and ears open for more information. \n\nA couple of Elven days passed. Yohei found no new information and I began reading more indepth into the texts I had found.\nI received a bird from Hogarth asking to meet up again. Za'Kabar and I travelled to his home again and the three of us spoke at length about the current situation.\n\nThe first reaper, the frost witch, had been destroyed. With her death, a storm occured,\nbut not the world ending type of storm that we were expecting if the vision were true. \nThat is the moment I truly knew that the vision was false. Hogarth reveiled that he believed there were other reapers as well. I agreed with the thought. I had\nspoken with Barry earlier in the day about the same subject... and that one of our fellow Druids may be a reaper. For protection of the person, I will not put their name in this tome, incase I am wrong about who they are.\n\nOn to why I think that\nGazadriel is 100% behind all of this. As we spoke to Hogarth, he told us a story from Athera and a place the Dwarves found called Rivel. It was a mystical floating city, completely abandoned.\n\nWhen they had looked into it more, they found out that it\nwas an ancient High Elven city, where the High Elves had enslaved other races to do their bidding. One record they found was of a 'Radient Man' that appeared in the city.\n\nHe used his powers against them and everyone turned on eachother. The\ncity was abandoned, everyone dead or fled the distruction. Hogarth and now I, believe that this 'radiant man' was indeed Gazadriel. \n\nThe only permenant solution to the situation is going to be the death of Gazadriel. The only way to do so is by\nrunesmithing a weapon that can fight an Aengul.\n\nThe only clan who possibily could have helped is now gone. Lori Oathcast died... My heart is a little saddened by this. But we have to push foreward. Hogarth is learning to runesmith and soon,\nI hope soon anyway, he will be able to forge the weapons that we need to kill Gazardiel.\n\nWhile we wait for these weapons. the only thing we can do is kill the reapers, to try and buy us time.\n\nMay the Aspects ever guide us...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fjarriauga", "The Veiled Scribe", "Legends of the Volsung - The Fjarriauga\n\nOf all the tales and legends of the Volsungs, the Fjarriauga are the darkest. In Skjoldier, homeland of the Volsung family, stories of the Fjarriauga are told to scare misbehaving children into submission at night.\nThey are said to be wicked ice spirits, taking on the guise of fair and innocent maidens to draw their prey to them. Young boys and girls alike are warned against venturing into the forests where they dwell, lest they are never to be seen again.\nIt is said that Kriemhild, the first Fjarriauga, was a woman abandoned at the altar by her betrothed. Broken-hearted she stumbled out into a snowstorm, collapsing amidst the swirling snow and frozen drifts. As she waited for death, Old Father Winter, one\nof the Volsung gods, discovered and took pity upon her. He leaned in and gave her the wedding kiss she longed for, transforming her into a vengeful - and powerful - ice spirit.\nWhile Fjarriauga are malicious creatures, they are also cunning, powerful and ageless. Many of the greatest seers and fortune-tellers in Skjoldier were Fjarriauga, and were both feared and respected by all. Brave or foolhardy men would often seek them\nout, seeking to make use of their talents, powers or insight; although rarely without cost.\nHowever, those with a sharp eye who identify a Fjarriauga even through her maiden disguise may secure her aid. Although fickle and cunning creatures, a Fjarriauga is bound to aid those who discover her with a single favour - no more and no less. Such a\ntoken should not be squandered nor taken lightly, as although she may be bound to fulfil the favour, it is unwise to earn the ire or wrath of a Fjarriauga.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Forest", "Mayilu", "Come, take my hand\nFollow me into the forest.\nThe fallen leaves, drenched with rain, will guide our path\nThrough the shaded glade and up the moss covered hill\nDon’t be afraid to step in the mud\nListen, hear the crisp snap of twigs echo in the distance\nThe soft lull of trickling water, flowing in the creek\nWatch, catch a glimpse of the timid deer\nHiding in the thicket and the little squirrel\nLilting across the treetops, acorns in cheek\nTouch, stroke the rough bark beneath your fingertips\nCaress the summer leaves, immerse your hands\nIn the tranquility of soothing waters\nFeel, accept the dawn’s gentle kisses upon your face\nThe pure spirits that inhabit the trees\nFeel nature pulsing through your body with renewed vitality\nBreathe deeply; \nInfuse your lungs with the richness of life", ""),
        StaticBook("The Frost Witch", "Gallidron Elindrow", "An Encounter with Frost Witches\n\nby Gallidron Elindrow\n\n\nRevised edition\nI first learned about the dreaded creatures, known as frost witches, from one of the tomes in the libraries of old Haelunor. I remember the fear that gripped me as a child when I learned of their macabre ways.\nThough as an adult of more mature understanding and greater constitution, I revisited the subject of “monsters” and relearned the available details of the frost witch. They are exclusively women so far as any adventurer who has survived an encounter\nwith them can tell.\n\nThey are horrid to look upon in their natural state. Grey skinned with eyes like ice, but it is not so easy to spot one of these slippery creatures for an ice witch is a master of disguise.\nThey employ illusion to mask their true selves, that they may, with more subtlety, intrude upon our societies and seek out their prey.\n\nIn fact, as the story goes, a frost witch will adopt the guise of a young woman and sit, crying, in the midst of\nsnowy glade. This is done to attract young and hapless men. The clever frost witch will then transform into her hideous self and dispatch the unwitting male then and there, or she will lure him back to her coven to become a grisly meal for her sisters.\nThey are, without exception, powerful magic users, though the older ones are more dangerous and adept. In fact, every frost witch draws her power from a “Witch Mother” who is the head of her particular coven. Like unto a queen bee, she will build her nest\nand gather workers who rely upon her, and she them to some extent.\n\nWhen another frost witch is of sufficient power and experience, she may set out to create her own coven. They begin by searching for women who are depressed or saddened.\nThe frost witch will then “mark” the woman with a curse. Should she succumb to her sorrow she will become a frost witch herself, and thus do their numbers swell.\nIt is reportedly a favorite tactic of the frost witches to seek out a married man\nand devour him, then they will curse his grieving widow. In this fashion do they gain both a meal and a prospective member of their coven.\nNot much is known about the curse, and there is no known way to remove it. It has been said, however,\nthat if the woman resists her sadness and sorrow that she may endure the curse and not become on of these fiends. Though she will likely live with the curse for the rest of her days.\nIn order to destroy a frost witch coven one must seek out and destroy the witch mother. In some cases this is enough to cause the coven to wither and die. In others, however, if a witch who is powerful enough survives, she may assume the role\nof witch mother and allow the coven to limp on. In any case, the most foolproof method of destroying a coven is just that, destroy the coven. All of it.\nIf one seeks to harm a frost witch I would give them this advice. Strike fast and strike true for you shall not likely receive a second chance. Also, a sellsword of types once told me that gold is good for killing all kinds of unnatural monsters,\nperhaps it applies here as well, though I do not know for certain.\nIt is important to note that  a frost witch is not a rabid animal, and they can be reasoned with. They are also possessed of terrible cunning and one should not expect the blind fury of mindless monster when dealing with them.\nIt is possible to treat with them and in fact they could exist within your own city, your very neighborhood and most would be unaware. They humor of a frost witch is quite changeable and every moment you stand in their presence you are in grave danger.\nThe truth is that they are fickle creatures, and there is no telling what a frost witch might do.\nIt is said that if one finds a frost witch in disguise and calls them on it that the witch will be bound by her curse to do the clever mortal one favor. Though this is only rumor and would prove both difficult and dangerous to study.\nIn closing, frost witches are a dangerous fascination and one should not seek them lightly. They are elusive and hide among the peoples of the world, it is for this reason that we must be ever watchful lest we become their next meal.\nI hope that this book has been useful to you, the reader. And that this information will help you, should you ever have….\n\nAn encounter, with frost witches.\nBy Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublishing date 8th of Deep Cold, 1516\n\nRevised 18th of Amber Cold, 1520", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Pepe", "Asher Highwind", "The Legend\n         of the\n      Golden Pepe\nThe forgotten history of the descendants of the four races the great war of the pepe. \nAfter Ibeless had been casted into the firey pits of the nether, the world lay in ruins after the great horde of undead Ibless unleashed upon the world.\nA great power known only as \"Tythus\" decided to bless the descendants with the greatest gift of all. A way to rebuild, and thus the first pepe. Was born, he sent 4 to the pvp defaulters of the plains of Oren, 3 to the cyber dagger ears within the forests,\n4 to the squeakers under the mountain of Urugan. But Tythus needed to mantain power over the races, thus he created One Pepe to Rule them All, from the fires he forged, The Golden Pepe\n\nSeveral summers passed and the descendants lived in\nharomny with the pepe's at there side. But the power of the Golden Pepe had consumed Tythus and he wanted more power. Power that the Pepe was as if speaking to him, whispering into his ear evil thoughts to take what the descendants had that he was so\nmuch greater than all of them. And thus the whispering of the Pepe sepped into his mind, it turned the once peaceful Tythus into a Steam buying evil doer. He waged a bloody war against the descendants with the power of the Pepe at his side none could stop\nhim until a young hero by the name of Billy Bob cut the Pepe from Tythus's grasph without the pepe to sustain the evil that was inside him he faded into the air, but instead of casting the Pepe back into the fires from wince it came ((wait this sounds-\nfamiler)) He chose to weild the power of the Pepe for himself until he was slain in an ambush but before he took his final breath the Creator smiled down upon his actions to defeat the evil Tythus and brought him into the Seven Skies as his farmer. To\nharvest the fields for all enterinty ((it was awful, pretty sure he went crazy from looking at all the taters)) Yet the pepe was lost no one is quite sure what became of it the story of the pepe drifting away throughout the generations now simpily ghost\nstories that parents tell there children to keep them doclie. But the Pepe is out there somewhere looking to whisper into the next ear to start the next great war of the descendants... Lying... Waiting...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Good Stuff", "Thurak", "It should be noted that the concoctions recorded here were all tested on the Charley Chickens and Heshakomeu himself and deemed safe for mortal usage.\nDreki\nDreki is the pinnacle of my work with hallucinogenic substances and is meant for recreational usage. When consumed, the user will experience vivid hallucinations for two to three hours, then fall asleep, upon which they will fall\ninto an incredibly vivid dream that lasts for six to eight hours. It is important to note nothing can be expected in these dreams other than they will appear as real as the reality you live in while sober, no matter how exotic, bizarre, or\nunnatural they become. When on awakes, the next day will be filled with periodic migraines, light blindness, constant hunger, fatigue, uncontrollable shaking, and a strong desire for sugar.\nTo make, follow these instructions:\n\nPut a few ladles of water to boil.\nSprinkle ground-up dust of a gram of cactus green into water.\nAdd a few drops of Zawabate nectar.\nAdd a few drops of Drilltongue sap.\nGrind several dried shadeleaf leaves- no more than four – And add them to the mixture.\nStir until thick, sludgy texture is achieved and concoction is deep green.\nPour mixture onto a pan and leave in warm, dry place until all moisture is gone. \nGrind up mixture into dust.\nWith Dreki dust, one can inhale it directly through the nostril for the soonest start of effects. One can also mix it into a drink for easier consumption, though the effects will be delayed. If comfortable, one can smoke it, resulting\nin a faster arrival of effects when drunk but slower than when inhaled.\nReykja\nReykja is intended for recreational usage, specifically for group smoking. It induces light hallucinations, usually no more than flashing colours, sounds that aren’t there, synaesthesia, and distorted depth perception.\n. It also puts the user into an energetic state, giving them an almost obsessive fascination with almost anything they focus on for more than a few seconds. These effects will last for around four hours. After the effects wear off, the user will\nexperience extreme fatigue, hunger, and a dryness in the mouth that lasts for around half a day.\nTo make, follow these instructions:\n\nChop head of dried speckled crimson mushroom into tiny bits and put in a bowl.\nGrind a gram of cactus green into dust and add to bowl.\nPour a few spoon-fulls of water onto the dust and mushrooms and mix until the mixture is sticky and stuck together.\nFlatten pipeweed leaf and dab crimson-green mixture along the central stem of the leaf. Wrap leaf\naround the mixture.\nWrap pipeweed wrap in thin paper and keep it closed using pipeweed sap.\nSet in warm-dry place until consumption.\nThese cigar wraps can be smoked directly, or they can be cut into pieces and put into the bowl of a pipe. The cigars can alternatively be mounted on candles, filling the room with smoke. The cigars, prior to being wrapped in paper, can\nbe cut into pieces and put into the dough or bread of pastry and consumed through the food, resulting in a slower but just as potent high.\nSprunga\nSprunga is still rather confusing to me. I have done it a few times, for the experience is not nearly as pleasant as with Dreki or Reykja; or rather, not pleasant in the same ways. Sprunga induces an intense euphoric sensation,\ncoupled with an unnatural feeling of lightness, as though one would float away at a gust of wind. The user will also experience extreme energy and excitement, which cannot be quelled until the five to seven hour inducement is over. Depth\nperception is virtually gone, and the ear more sensitive to noise; an effect that continues to plague the user for another day. Dryness of mouth, jitters and numbness of fingers and toes also accompany the pleasant effects.\nTo make, follow these instructions:\n\nExtract juice of King’s Ivy flower into a glass bottle.\nExtract juice of Mershin fungus into glass bottle.\nClose bottle and shake until contents are mixed.\nLight fire beneath bottle and cook until brown crystals accumulate at the bottom of bottle.\nDrain bottle and remove crystals.\nGrind in mortar and pestle into fine dust.\nThe dust can be inhaled through nostrils, delivering a quick high. Lighting it afire to smoke or diluting it into a drink will severely dim or completely eradicate the positive effects.\nSpeckled Crimson Mushroom\n\nThis mushroom I first discovered growing in the storage cavern underneath Ac’Talarah. Overwhelmed with curiosity after being locked inside, I ate a mushroom, experiencing a remarkably\nvivid hallucination as well as a nearly-obsessive fascination with whatever held my attention for more than a few moments. Any potions it is used in will have the same effects. It grows in damp, dark places on\nstone, and can be recognised by its brilliant red colouration dotted with white splotches.\nMershin Fungus\n\nOriginally, I thought this mushroom to be an appendage of the Speckled Crimson, but it is in fact its own fungus. If consumed, it gives the eater a feeling of extreme lightness and happiness, coupled\nwith an unquenchable energy. However, one can hardly concentrate on anything, and the side effects are mentioned in the description of Sprunga. It has a tan head with thick ruffles underneath, and covers cave floor with a squishy, vine like growth.\nZawabate\n\nMy experiments with this flower’s nectar have been a wonderful experience. It puts users in a hallucinogenic state that detaches perception from the body, if that makes sense. The shaman who introduced\nit to me called it an ‘out of body’ experience. The nectar can be put in tea, which makes taking it quite simple and pleasant. The user must be warned, however; overdosing on this can result in permanent damage to the mind, addling the senses\nand perception of what is real even when not having recently consumed the herb. Zawabate can be recognised by its short, curved flowers and tall stalk, both in hues of yellow and green, and grows primarily beside desert oases.\nDrilltongue\n\nI have determined this to be a lovely addition to my array of recreational dosages. The sap gives the user light hallucinations and dulls the senses, leaving one disorientated and surrounded by visions.\nDrilltongue resembles a thick tangle of green roots that grip the stone it grows on tightly. It can be found in mountains and tundras.\nShadeleaf\n\nShadeleaf gives users hallucinations, which is accompanied with heightened emotional sensitivity and a deep sense of calm. The leaves can be smoked, eaten and boiled into tea, all of which grants users a\npsychedelic adventure this herb provides. Shadeleaf resembles a common weed, with short leaves and yellow flowers that grow during springtime, and grows primarily in forests. They can be distinguished from other\nweeds by the popping noise their leaves make that can be heard after rainstorms, which is caused by an overabundance of water being sent through their thin veins.\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 18th of the First Seed, 1484.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Gorundyr", "Ketiley Strong-Heart", "*It is clear to see that this book was hand written in coal. The lettering quite eloquent and fluid.*\n\n\n       The Eight Divine\n\nCopied down by Ketiley of                  Orvar.\nA Brief explanation of the           Gorundyr's Gods.\nGorund, The Invincible Light\n\nGorund, the Invincible Light is regarded as the creator of time and space by the Gorundyr priesthood. It is said that he rules the cosmos atop a celestial steed made of the stars themselves.\nIt is with his blessing that sun rises at dawn, and from his wrath that it is smashed into pieces upon the earth at dusk. Gorundyr Priests believe that the darkness of night is to prepare the mortal beings for the coming of Maratsu the Fallen One,\nfor it is with his flight that the last battle will be fought.\n\nLagara, the Goddess of Life\n\nLagara, the mother of all life, sits atop the Heart Tree, an immense tree that connects the mortal world with the cosmos.\nWhile the tree has never been seen by man, legend states it is here where she plays her magical harp. Lagara’s melody is said to keep the seasons in order and ensure that all things grow. Her form is one which closely resembles a human, as she created man\nin her image. Said to be of impossible beauty, many men would give their lives for a chance to look upon her divine form.\n\nBelenus of the Hunt\n\nIn ancient myth, Belenus is said to have been a mortal man who fell in love with Andarta, maiden of the forest.\nA hunter and gatherer, he gave up his life to pursue the whispers of Andarta within her forest. Unbeknownst to him, she became infatuated with him as well. One night, as the hour of twilight neared, she visited him in the form of a white haired human\nwoman. Feeling their love was as ancient as the trees themselves, Andarta bound herself with Belenus under the moon and the stars. With this, Belenus’ mortal form was destroyed and he was granted a seat beside the gods.  Belenus took the form of a Green\nMan, a humanoid figure that appeared to the eye as both man and tree. His love for Andarta is so fierce that he has pledged himself to defending her forests and the spirits that live within.\n(Shrines and rune stones have sprung up all around the forests\nto honour both Belenus and Andarta, with hunters and young lovers often leaving gifts and sacrifices at these places in the hopes of winning their blessings.)\n\nAndarta of the Forest\n\nAndarta sacrificed her divine form in order to create\nthe forests for she saw no other way to achieve the beauty that Gorund had shown her in his vision. It is said that she is Queen of the Forest Spirits, mythical beings that inhabit the trees themselves. Stories of Andarta often portray her as an angry\ndeity, untrusting of others around her. This is largely attributed to the betrayal of Maratsu, for if one of her brothers could commit such evil, surely no one could be trusted. Her forests are her domain and she is very wary of outsiders, be they mortal\nor divine. Offerings are made to Andarta in the hopes of gaining her acceptance and the veneration of the trees and forest spirits is a common practice among the Gorundyr peoples.\nDraug of the Sea\n\nDraug is said to be a colossal being, the largest of the gods. He rests on the sea floor in a deep slumber, awaiting offerings from the mortal men above him. The beating of his massive heart controls the currents of the ocean, and the\nslight movement of his breathing drives the tide.\n(The Gorundyr are excellent sailors, strongly developed by their need to explore and trade. It is a common practice to throw one tenth of all treasure plundered into the sea, as an offering to Draug. Many\nsailors will sacrifice animals or throw offerings to Draug before they start a voyage in the hopes that he will guide them safely on their journey.)\n\nOknar of the Mountains\n\nRevered by blacksmiths and stonemasons, Oknar is said to be a giant stone being\nwho wanders the tallest mountains and their peaks. Many believe that earthquakes and landslides can be attributed to Oknar, for he still roams the lands in an attempt to perfect his work.\n(Gorundyr craftsmen can be seen singing prayers as they work, and\nit is the beauty of the land that they wish to emulate with their craft. All things created by the hands of the Gorundyr are dedicated to Oknar, and small rituals and offerings are performed whenever something is constructed.)\nArgal of the Sky\n\nArgal is one of the three sky gods, the other two being Maratsu and Ankou. Taking the form of a massive eagle, it is his task to patrol the skies and await return of his fallen brother. Argal became Master of the Sky\nafter his brothers defeat and it is believed that the slightest movement of his wings can cause the fiercest storms. Sailors often sing to him and pray for clear skies on their travels.\n(Shrines dedicated to honouring Argal are usually found atop the\nhighest mountain peaks, and require days of journey to reach. Most who make the journey do so to offer their gratitude for his protection of the skies.)\n\nAnkou the Gatherer of Souls\n\nAnkou is also known as the Blood God and the God of Death.\nFormed in the image of a great hawk, Ankou is the third and last of the sky gods. When a being dies and gains the favour of the gods, it is he who guides their soul to the heavens so that they may rest. Ankou took the betrayal of his brother to heart and\nnow he has begun gathering the souls of the dead to fight in his legion at the last battle.\n(Warriors of the Gorundyr pay their respects to Ankou by offering him the blood of their enemies. Glory and victory in battle is achieved in the name of Ankou, and\nit is the blood of heathens that he feasts upon.)\n\nMaratsu, The Fallen One, is never spoken of publically by any Gorundyr. And his past will quite possibly remain hidden from voice.\nTraditional Practices:\nAnimism and Offerings -\n\nThe Gorundyr revere the gods and their ancestors. Dozens of ancient shrines litter the land, all designed to give homage to different gods.  Food, ornaments, precious metals, these are all common gifts left\nat these shrines. Rune stones are also erected around the land that tell ancient stories of the gods, often attracting many travellers looking to learn more.\nAncient groves are also considered places where the barrier between the spiritual world and the\nmortal one are most weak. Members of the Priesthood will often travel to these places to see a clearer picture of the gods and their plans.\n\nSacrifice\n\nSacrifice, both human and animal, is common practice among the Gorundyr people.\nSuch acts are reserved for certain times of the year, such as before a harvest or before battle. Warbands that capture survivors from their raids often sacrifice the ones they do not see fit to take as slaves.  Human sacrifice among the Gorundyr\nthemselves is less common and is seen as a great honour, their sacrifice is believed to bring great favour from the gods.\n\nBurial and Afterlife\n\nDeath is far from final, or so the Gorundyr believe.\nBurial practices consist of burying food, weapons, and ornaments with the dead. It is believed that while the mortal form will stay behind, the souls and their possessions will be gathered by Ankou and brought to the heavens where they may dine and\nslumber with Gorund. Only those whom are seen as worthy in the eyes of the gods would be ascended to the heavens and granted immortality. Those whom are deemed unworthy in the eyes of the gods will be forgotten, their mortal being the last step in their\nexistance. The Gorundyr bury their dead in large burial mounds, dozens of bodies often occupying a single one. \nCremation is not practised by the Gorundyr, and is in fact feared by all. It is believed that the burning of ones body will also destroy the\nsoul, preventing their ascension to the heavens. It is common, then, to burn those who have dishonoured the gods, such as heretics or traitors.\nPolitical System\n\nThe Gorundyr are a prideful folk and place most of their respect on strength. Operating on a clan-based system, each clan owes no allegiance to any other, leading to a lot of inner conflict over lands and resources.\nBarid the Reaver, of Orvar, grandfather to Morvan of Orvar, created a new title called the Yagar or “High King” as it is commonly known, and has been the only man in history to hold such a title. Until recently, Morvan now hold the Yagar title.\nGeography\n\nThe Gorundyr come from a region they called the Savaar, an isolated region in the northern reaches of Anthos. Mountain folk by blood, they thrive in the harsh conditions of the frozen north.\n*On this page is a map of the Gorundyr's current ocation with coordinates.*\n\nX: 127\ny: 59\nZ: -135", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great North", "Aptrotta", "The birthplace of the scourge… The final resting place of an ancient civilization… A land without hope… A land filled with beauty… Death hides everywhere… Life reveals itself everywhere… This land.. This ancient land… This land is The North.\nI, Cyrenn Yuln’Taynei, ventured into this dangerous territory with no respect to my own life all for one purpose. To discover. Discover what was lost. Discover what was hidden. Discover the unknown. The following pages you are about to read are written\nfrom using the notes I took on my expedition into The North.\n\nThe taint. The corruption. Its everywhere it seems. Even the entrance to The North is blocked by a large gate erected by the corrupt hands of the scourge. The air is foul with the stench of\ndeath. The snow stained crimson. Blood has been shed here recently. But, I must continue…\n\nJust after passing the gates I am greeted by an ancient ruin and the icy face of a cliff towards my front and to my left. With a quick glance to my right I notice a\na path revealed in the snow. The paw prints of some native animal leading me towards an unknown world.\n\nAfter about an hour of following the tracks I finally reach what I was looking for.  The path which shall lead me into the secret region of The North.\nA chasm lays before me. It twists and turns as my eyes follow it.Large stone tendrils reach out from the sides of the cliffs and the bottom like arms trying to reach for the sky. Luckily, these stone formations form perfect land bridges for I to walk\nupon. Without a thought of giving up, I continue forth.\n\nMy first night I spent still inside the chasm. I pitched my tent on a flat spot near the edge of a cliff. It was impossible to keep a fire going. The harsh wind that blew throuh the chasm smothered\nmy fire, stung my skin, and tried to blast my tent away from the cliff. Every hour the temptature dropped. This night was becoming a nightmare. Finally, my eyes gave into sleep.\n\nI awoke to a scream at the crack of dawn. A scream of terror. A scream of\npain. A scream signifying their final moments in life. The scourge was near. I had to go. With great haste I packed my tent and left.\n\nNothingness… All I encountered for miles was nothingness… Bare land stretched out before me for miles covered in snow\nand nothingness… This can’t be it… This wasteland can’t be all that The North is. My journey must go on.\n\nThere it is. The first sign of a past civilization. Standing before me was a towering ruin of a kingdom lost from time. Thewalls have fallen, stone\nlaying around the snow, while the supports stand tall holding up this ancient structure. A closer work would reveal the history of the ancient people who lived here before us. We could finally see how life really was for the previous inhabitants of our\nworld. This kingdom. This ancient Kingdom held secrets that could change our view on life forever. It was my duty to take a peek into the past.\n\nI stomped forward through the snow over fallen structures, over relics, over bones. The bones...\nThey were everywhere. Perfect skeletons resting against stone walls, skeletons laying down in the middle of the path, skeletons sitting in chairs, skeletons hunched over counters. The farther I went into the city the more I saw. Each skeletal corpse\nresting in a position one would do during life. Something hit this city… Something purged the city of its population. But what?\n\nWith that I leave this forgotten kingdom. I leave its people behind. The mystery to what wiped away its people will stay that,\na mystery.  I don’t dare to take anything with me in worry that whatever killed these poor citizens may still be lurking the ruined streets.\n\nThe day is still young when I came across a small white tent and a fire pit. Excited, I set of in a run towards\nit. Laid out before me was a horrific scene. A decaying body was left in the snow, the campground covered in blood leading towards a small tunnel. I decided to follow the trail, my curiosity getting the best of me.\nThe tunnel was small and cramped. Sunlight shone down through cracks in the ceiling. When I reached the end of the blood trail, a skeletal women stood hunched over a small lever as if she was guarding it from someone. Next to her sat a large basket\nconnected by rope. It hung over a large hole. The rope stretched upwards curled around a wooden beam. It hit me. A lift.\n\nThe lift shook slightly as I stepped into the basket. I reached out towards the women, my fingers splayed. Carefully, I knocked the\nlever the other direction, the bones falling over into a heap. With a creak, the basket started lowering itself downward. I was plunged into a darkness as the basket passed through the stick thone.\n\nMinutes passed before I was able to see light. The stone\ntunnel finally opened up and it came to my attention that I was placed inside a large cavern, the floor flooded with molten lava except for few places.  A bridge made of dark stone, the color of blood, stretched across the lake of lava. Blood shards\nfloated over the molten liquid. Across the lake sat a strange looking ruin.\n\nThe basket, only five feet away from the floor, plummeted towards the ground as the rope snapped above. I hit the ground hard, the basket landing on its side. Slowly I crawled\nout from the basket unharmed. I swiveled my head to the left, already making my way towards the bridge. Bubbles formed on the surface of the lake, popping every few seconds sending droplets of lava upwards at an alarming speed while I crossed the bridge.\nThe ruin was a mess. It appeared as if someone tried to get out quickly. From what it looked like, the place had once been a workshop for some sort of engineer.  There was faded blueprints laying on a desk to the front of me, a tool table to my left, and\nan oddly placed track to my left which rounded a corner. The tunnel in which it disappeared gave off a dim glow. My interest having peaked, I set off to follow the track.\n\nThe tunnel twists and turns as I walk through, a faint clicking sound audible. The\nroom suddenly opens up to a large cavern, a weird iron device hanging from the ceiling nearing the floor. A few feet in front of it rests a mound of stone with a keyhole in the center. Soon I discovered I am sitting atop a gaint cage. Could whatever it\nheld be what killed the population? Scared, I dart back towards the lava lake quickly crossing the bridge only to remember the basket had fallen. \n\nMy eyes dart around the cavern desperately searching for a way out. A stroke of luck hit me as I noticed\nvines hanging down from a rock edge above, daylight shining down. My feet moved towards the vines before my brain could think. I curled my fingers up around one of them and slowly pulled myself up, panting by the time I reached the surface.\n\nThe endless\nwalk began again. Tall pine trees have begun to appear more frequently. Every once in a while I would come across a deer or some other animal…\n\nAfter a few days of nothingness, I finally gave up on the expedition... Food supplies were running low and so\nwas my patience... I knew The North had to hold more, but my life sources were dwindling...\nThe Northern Expedition was a great intellectual experience for myself. I hope my efforts to discover have affected some of you to venture out into this vast land by yourself. As usual, I wish you farewell.\n*A large, fancy signature rests on the bottom of the page*\n\n\n<()>Cyrenn Yuln’taynei<()>", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grey Mage 1", "Mordir", "Part One\n\n-The crystals I recovered from the south have been safly transported to a small port city in the west known as Sylverport. Here I and the object will remain so that I might further my research with the aid of these people.\nThe crystals effects that I have thus far documented:\nThe Black Crystal- when held I feel a sense of thinning life, as if I far aged and withered. When I near a corpse I can hear whispers, the last thoughts of the dead.\nThe White Crustal- Most interesting to the people of Sylverport is my White gem, whose effects might better their devlopment in this desert climate. When held I feel a cool eerie wind even in the hottest of times.\nThe Red Crystal- Also perhaps usfull to these port dwellers is my red gem, which when held keeps me warm and calm as if sitting by a fire. \nThe Blue Crystal- The one I lost, and most prefered, as the blue gem. As I held it I felt pure, no dirt of blood\nclung to my and dark things it warded me too. During my researsh in the Orc lands and the Lich attack I witnessed the blue gem protected me from the undead beasts posions unlike the near orcs. Not long after this, the glowing blue gem shattered.\nOther magical items I have come across include the stones I recovered in my time in Orc lands. The first set were a sack of blue crystals that seem hollow and filled with water. they leaked constantly but never ran dry. When I first found the stones and\nvisited a Orcen Shaman, the wise man told me they might be the result of alchemy, or could be used in alchemical arts. But he seems generaly unaware of there power.\nThe second stone I fond was the Fire Orb, found and smooth and liking with flame.\nAlthough it never seems to burn me I can use the sparks it makes ti ignite new fire and it seems the more use I make of the object the hotter it becomes. The limit interests me. \nDuring the Oren occupation of The Silver City I aided the Mali folk when\nI smugled fire powder into the city that I had planned to ignite with the fire powder, killing several Orenmen. However I was forced to flee, and if the powder has been used for such plans it still beyond me at the momment. Regardless I still have much of\nthe substance still in my stock.\nAt the momment I have become a Sylverport dweller to use these people to further my research in my object and investagte the deserts around and the fell ruins forking out of them. Hearsay have it dragons once lived in these parts, but now are long dead.\nHow that interests me.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Hat: Part 1", "DFGcrush", "Once there be a boy, humble at may but if angered, all hell'd break loose! \nOne day he decided to ponder into the city, as he had retrieved his daily allowance of money from his father!\nAs he entered the city he saw Elves, Orc's and as he was, Humans.\nEventually he wanted to buy something, so as one would do he walked into a toy shop.\nAs he entered he saw many beautiful toys, as well as odd gadgets! There was a mini mill, as well as a wooden bird that moved with the twist of a handle. But after all his\nsearching he a hat, it was like no other, and for some reason it called to him. As he approached it something happened he maintained a headache! Now ingoring it he placed that hat on his head. What a mistake! As he did this the winds in the streets gusted\ninto the shop, the windows smashed and his eyes turned snow white! Something was controlling his mind. the shards started floating, and as they did all of the swung towards the shop keeper killing him almost instantly!\n\"I will rule\" These were the last words he said.\nEnd of Part 1", ""),
        StaticBook("The Healer", "N.Y.", "vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvDevotion\nTo The Healer\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\n(A collection of poems written by a soldier who was clearly devout.)\n\n(Includes 5 poems)\nLetter to\nAllah, The Creator\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nAllah the Creator, the magnificent.\nPlease tell me if I be heaven sent.\nForgive me, my dirty deeds was desperate.\nIn this world of sin, I got a moral deficit.\nDeath to me the only thing that’s definite.\nCorrupt rule the world, \nbut when you’re dead that’s irrelevant.\nSometimes I think back to the old days.\nStart slippin’, fallin’ back to my old ways.\nLivin’ dangerous, \nI hope I live to see old age.\nPardon me, I’m just goin’ through a cold phase.\n\n-Your Servant\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nI Relapsed When \nI Wrote This\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nIn the kitchen, cauldron open for the heat.\nCookin’ all night, the house stink of green.\nGot my shirt off, it’s a Khalestine summer.\nI hope these fumes don’t wake my mother.\nMy rafiqis come over to tell their stories.\nWorried that they smell it, get em’ out in a hurry.\nAnd I ain’t ever comin’ out, I’m stayin’ in my home\nUntil the water boils hotter than where Shai’tan roams.\nFill a pipe with freshly cooked green, \nGet this shit off my chest.\nShow me some far off dreams,\nAnd leave me to rest.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nIdle Thoughts\nShai'tan's Toy\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nIt’s like everyday that I wake up,\nI stare into space, don’t say much.\nWipe my brow, numb from the face up.\nIt’s still hot but the summer’s over.\nShort on luck like a three leaf clover.\nBut still hopin’ that you walk in\nSo that we can get to talkin’.\nAllah says that I don’t get to forget you.\nBut it’s I that chooses to wait for you.\nEven if you don’t come back.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nAll Of The\nChild Soldiers\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nNow this little dwarf got a sword \nFrom the local blacksmith’s forge.\nHe bought it with the mina \nHe got from his chores.\nHe robbed the baker’s store\nTold her get down on the floor. \nPut the cookies in the bag, \ntake the gold out the drawer.\n\nLittle Pordinski got a sword \nHe got from the rebels\nTo kill the farfolk infidels \nand Savoie Devils.\nA sheathe on his waist,\nA bandana on his face,\nPrays to Godanistan everyday\nthat Brelus isn’t leveled.\n\nAnd Little Qali got a sword\nto cut through the cord\nThe white man tried to hang \nhim from for the Lord.\nHis rage couldn't be ignored,\nLeaped into the air and soared,\n“Allah take them with me!”\nWas the last thing he roared.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nBefore I pen this last poem, I wish to show my appreciation to the woman that had taken me in as her son when I was a young Qali. She has by far been one of the kindest folks I've come across in my life thus far. Although I do not consider myself a\ngood writer or even a writer by trade, she has urged me to take on a hobby when I have idle time on my hands to help me feel better about things. These poems are not just about me. They portray the stories of dead rafiqis and those unable to get their\nvoices out there. So shokran, Mama. This next piece I hold dearest to me - it's something different and close to heart.\nDevotion To The \nHealer - The Poem\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nThe Diamond, albeit once precious to others,\nis trapped - it cannot move if it cannot adorn.\nUsed to being loved, the loneliness set in.\nIt implanted ideas of dullness, imperfection.\nThat the diamond is no longer worth anything.\nThat is when the healer who came from nowhere\narrived one day. Wishing to break the internal\nstruggle, the diamond calls out to the healer.\nThe healer is taken back, surprised by the \ndiamond’s gesture. She too was alone for \nquite some time. The diamond spoke of wishing\nto see far off lands and wanting new friends.\nIt spoke of adventure and fighting monsters.\nThe diamond wanted to see the world and \nrecreate what it had lost before it was trapped.\nThe healer smiled and held the diamond tight in her\nhands so not to drop it. She felt the cracks in the\ndiamond - far from the truth that it would last forever.\nBut the healer was kind, and over time mended these \ncracks thus making the diamond whole again.\nWhile they went through their ups and downs, \nthe diamond loved the healer and the healer loved the diamond in turn.\nNot just for eachother’s outward\nappearances, but for what was inside - whatever\nthat was. Despite the love between the healer and\nher jewel, feelings of inadequacy and the growing\ndependence on each other became too much.\nWishing to find herself and become a better person,\nthe healer left the diamond in their home with promises\nto return when she could be stronger for the diamond.\nThe loneliness returned and the diamond feared\nthe healer was wearing rubies, sapphires, and emeralds.\nThat she no longer wanted the diamond. Overtime the\ndiamond began to blacken and it no longer sparkled\nlike it did when adorning healer. It wanted no\nother wearer and shunned all attention that came its way.\nThrough all the trials and tribulations the diamond went \nthrough, the hardships endured and the pain it caused\nto others, the diamond was now no different than a piece\nof coal. It was then that the diamond could not fulfill its\npurpose - that being to adorn the healer and help her shine. \nNow it questions, if the healer does return, would she still wear him even if he was no longer precious?\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv", ""),
        StaticBook("The High Kha", "High Councilor Azkel Frostbeard", "One day, at the tavern of Kal'Novlar, a kha walked into a party full of dwarves. He looks around, seeing some familiar faces, and some he hasnt seen before. In the corner of the room, a Dwarven man sees the kha, and whispers to him \"Kha, yeh looken teh\ntroi sum of dis.....sugeh?\" The kha looks at what the man offers him.The product looks something like sugar, but something seems off. As being a nice kha, he accepts the sugar, and licks some of it off of his paw. All of a sudden, everything around him\nchanges. All the dwarves have became different things. The bartender became a magical horse, and the woman next to him became a stump of a tree. The kha, extremely confused, walks towards the door, trying to keep his balance. When he goes to turn the\nhandle, he shrieks, seeing that it has turned into snakes! He looks around at everything, suddenly becoming dizzy, and blacking out on the floor. As he wakes up, he notices that he is lying on a makeshift bed made of hay bales, and that he has a massive\nheadache. He lies back down, not believing what happened the night before.", ""),
        StaticBook("The High Prince", "Ebonsquire", "The High Prince of Malinor and the story of Laurehlin\n\n((Originally written by zevandir))\nA powerful Arch-Druid from one of Malinor's eldest cities came to Aegis to help us with the erecting of the Laurehlin's trees. I met him at the cobblestone spires to the west of the Aegis Temple. We set off on foot to a mountain gorge I had come across\nthat would act as a natural barrier to our foes. Once we arrived, the Druid wandered around in the valley, reaching into a pouch at his hip every so often. He showed me the seeds in said pouch and they had tiny, intricate vines woven around them, with a\nshine very similar to glowstone. Whilst my brigade of builders were creating the city's defensive wall, trees began to grow exponentially! It seemed as though the trees gew faster the taller they got and soon the canopy raised hundreds of feet above us.\nIt was a wonderful sight, the leaves sprung out of the branches with a burst of the similar glowstone sheen, and sprinkles of metallic dust swirled down from the tree tops. \n\nThere was still, however, a large clearing in the\ncentre of the city. This, of course, was for the mother tree. A tree to harbour them all. He grabbed a bit of parchment from his satchel and looked over at me reassuringly. The Arch Druid then walked to the centre of the clearing, and began to cast a\npowerful spell upon one of the seeds. Leaves suddenly spun around him wildly, and a wonderful green color radiated from him like an aura. \n\nThe tree trunk sprouted around him, and he was no longer in view. I was rather frightened when I\nsaw this, hoping he hadn't cast the spell incorrectly. As the Mother Tree grew to its ultimate height, I saw a small opening half way up the tree. Low and behild, The Arch Druid stood in the opening proclaiming \"This is where the stone alter shall lie.\"\nOnce the trees seemed to stop growing, we climbed up the trees with packs of wooden planks and began setting down the first few platforms. In time, Laurelin had become one of the finest city's of Malinor, and to think it all had begun with just a pouch of\nseeds and a pinch of druid magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Homunculi", "Belegar", "The Homunculi\nBy Belegar Tunnelsmasher\n\nMalin’s Welcome, 1551\nPreface\nI, Belegar Tunnelsmasher, brother of Beros Oathcast whose body was made into a homunculi, am writing this to serve as a warning against dangers the homunculi pose and how to take on out if the situation comes to it.\nHomunculi 101\n\nThere are currently four tiers of homunculi being: fiend, deviant, aberrant and doppleganger. \n\nFiends\n- looks like a fiend\n- weak, very short lvied\n- not sentient\nDeviants \n- look similar to the race of the descendant whose body they are created from\n- slight disfigurements\n- odd skin colours\n- short lived\nAberrants\n- very similar look to descendants\n- unnatural skin colour\n- very small disfigurements\n- greater strength than descendants\n- average lifespan\nDopplegangers\n- extremely intellignet\n- very strong, to the point of being able to lift items such as entire iron gates\n- bodies are almost perfect\n- cannot be killed by natural means (will be explained later)\n- does not have blood, instead has a\nsubstance related to the element they were created with\n- look identical to the descendant they are made from\nHomunculi have no morals or regard for life. They only look to extend their own lives and further their own goal to achieve ‘ascendancy’. In other words, they seek to become a god. This is the fifth tier of homunculi, and the tier that has yet to be\nachieved. It is imperative that they do not achieve this.\n\nAdditionally, most homunculi do not have souls. \n\nThe process to create a homunculi will not be detailed in this book, but let it be known that in order to make one a corpse is required,\nand the homunculi will not hesitate to murder to get their hands on one.\nHow to Kill a Doppleganger\n\nIn order to kill a Doppleganger, one cannot use normal means. Simply cutting off their heads will not end their existence, as if their body is left alone, it will slowly regenerate until fully formed once again.\nThe only way to completely kill a Doppleganger is to inject their bodies with a ‘Potion of Unmaking’. \n\nThe process to create this potion requires an experienced alchemist. The reagents needed are: Metzil’s Tangle, Flame Tongue Root, Serpent's Stalk,\nLarihei’s Fingers and two lodestones. A lodestone is a rock that exhibits magnetic properties. Once this potion is made, the Doppleganger must be incapacitated and every piece of their body injected with this potion. The potion will then tear the\nhomunculi apart and end their existence.\nKnown Dopplegangers\n\nAt the time of writing, there are two know Dopplegangers. They are Prohan and Lotho. They are extremely dangerous, do NOT approach them voluntarily. \n\nBoth have air as their element of creation.\nProhan:\n\n- human\n- tan skin\n- black hair\n- looks like Daniel Nodal\n- Member of the Dawn Strider Voyagers, often seen wearing the uniform\nLotho:\n\n- dwarf\n- white skin\n- blonde hair\n- looks like Beros Oathcast\n- no accent\n- usually seen dressed in white robes with a set of goggles atop his head\nWeaknesses of Homunculi\n\nHomunculi are damaged by aurum and Holy Magic much like the undead are. If confronting a homunculi, especially a Doppleganger, it is highly recommended to wield an aurum blade and wear aurum armor.\nAlso, if possible, assistance of one versed in the arts of Holy Magic is highly recommended.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Imperial Orb", "Xor'Purdal", "Dearest Emperor Of Orenia, it has come to my notice that i have stumbled upon an item which appears to be The Imperial Orb. I am willing to return said item to you, for a fee, of course. I'd love to further discuss this with you, or someone else capable\nof dealing with the matter. \n\nFriendly greetings,\nXor'Purdal.\n\n(OOC: Message TheElvenMage either In game or on the forums if you are interested. And yes i do have the moderator approved item.)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Irongutia I", "[First Mate] Jerry Irongut", "07 of The First Seed:\n\nWe ave' sailed te' fleet off te' coast o' te' Wood Elves, te' S.S. Irongutia in te' lead. Tere were 9 o' us in te' fleet, most of et compromised o' elves, the Irongutia bein' te' only ship full o' Stouts. Captain Skippy as' been ov-\n-erseein' teh ragtag team o' Sailors. Gran' King Balek as' accomponied us on our voyage to hunt down te' witch of te' sea, te' dasterdleh cracken...\n\n09 The First Seed\n\nWe ave fought te' Cracken an' suffered heavy cas-\n-ualites wit' one ship blown to bits boi agh powder keg ta' got set off wifout warnin. Almost all lives of te' vessel were lost.... Te' Irongutia as' maneh leaks from te'battle ta' insued after te' sinkin o' teh suicide vessel. Te' ship is barleh afloat-\nagh while we may have fought off te' Cracken fer nuw, I fear he wull be back soon. Teh crew is in complete disaray as no other ships seem to wun' to hulp us. I fear too tat te' ship will nut withstant anehmer attacks..\n10 of The First Seed\n\nTeh S.S. Irongutia has been sunk to te' bottom o' te' Sea Wit' almost all o' te' crew at te' ocean floor wif her. Te Cracken crushed teh Ship in two an' devoured almos evereh las' soul un bored, among te' dead was Gran' King Balek.\nCap'n Skippeh was swated off te' deck, no where to be foun'. I was thrown from te' ship as te' ship was plunged under te' Sea. I made mah way to one of te'm damn Elven ships an' made mah way back to te' mainland wif te' Elves agh a few o' te survivin'-\ncrew. Magh goal now is tu' foind aneh clues unto if unahun foun' Cap'n Skips.\n\n15 of The First Seed\n First Mate Jerry Irongut of The Irongut Navy", ""),
        StaticBook("The Jayan C1", "Sofetios Jayamen", "The Jayan\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\nChapter One\n\n        Who am I?\n\nIn the distance I heard someone say,\n\n“Wake him up…” Suddenly I felt my face get slapped, Hard. I burst into conciseness and opened my eyes. I was in small room.\nI was tied to a chair, my head was held firmly in place by something that felt like metal. There were three people in there not including me.\nThe one to my left had blue robes on and a hood that covered his eyes, the one to the right was closest to me and apparently the one who had slapped me, he had plate armor on and a longsword.\nThe last person in the middle had black robes on but his hood was off. The one in the black robes came up to me and said,\n\n“alright, first of all, what is your name.” to which I replied,\n“Where am I, what-“ I was interrupted by another slap by the armored man. The man in black said,\n\n“ Only speak when asked to. Now I’ll ask again, What is your name.”\nI thought for a few seconds then realized I didn’t remember my name.\n\n“I..Don’t know.” The man in the black robes seemed pleased at this. He said,\n“Good, then the drug must have worked.” To which I said,\n\n“Drug? What dr-“ I was slapped again by the man in plate armor. The man in black then said,\n\n“Alright, from now on your name is James Clark.”\nHe waited a moment to see if I would say anything, but I remained silent.\n\n“Ah good, your learning.” Said the man in black.\n“I do hope your comfortable. As we are about to give you a gift. You see, every person’s head has a… section that is left locked. We only wish to unlock it, and of course use it. ” He smiled and looked to the man in blue.\n“Do it.” The man in blue stepped forward and placed a hand on both sides of my head. I felt a pulse hit my head, then everything went black.\nI slowly regained consciousness again. I was laying on the ground and slowly got up and coughed. I looked around. I was in the middle of a huge crater. There were bits of wood and stone everywhere.\nI remembered the three people, the pulse, and the name they gave me, but nothing before that. I started to make my way to the edge of the crater. After a good minute or two, I reached the edge.\nI climbed over the lip and then saw the body of the man in black, crumpled on the ground. His face had a look of horror on it. I wondered what just happened. I walked onwards, hoping to find civilization.\nI walked through what was now a forest until I came across a small camp. Before I got into the clearing, I saw that there were two thuggish looking guys around a fire. Nearby them was a well dressed looking man tied to a post.\nHis clothes though were beaten and worn. One of the thuggish men said,\n\n“What are you going to do with the money you get for him?” to which the other responded,\n“Not sure, but we’ll live like kings for ransoming Henry Jedway.” He said looking to the well dressed man.\n“Not so high and mighty now are you Henry. You know you sentenced my cousin to death about a year ago. I’m wondering why I don’t just kill you now.”\nI didn’t want to get mixed up in this, so I was about to find another way around when one of the men looked toward my direction and said,\n\n“Hey! Who are you!”\nI began to step back slowly when the bandits got up and started running at me with weapons pulled.  I was about to run when I tripped on a root and fell on my bottom.\nThe thuggish men were about to swing at me when I extended my arms toward them and turned my head in fright. I heard a ‘Woosh’ two crashes and two thuds.\nNoticing I wasn’t yet dead, I looked up and saw that the two men were about 25 feet away from me on their backs. I quickly got up as they did also. One of them said,\n“What the heck was that!?” To which the other said towards me,\n\n“I’ve heard of your kind, you’re a Jayan!” The one talking turned to the other thug and said pointing to me. “Let’s get out of here! We can’t fight that!”\nThe other thug looked toward the well dressed man and said,\n\n“But-“ the original thug then said,\n\n“I don’t want to die! Let’s GO!”\nThe Thug started running and the other one looked at me and then followed his friend. Confused, I looked towards the well dressed man, who had observed the whole scene and said, “Are you…Ok?”\nThe well dressed man just stared at me. I went over to him and untied his bonds. When he was released, he said, “What are you, and how did you just do what you did?” I replied,\n“I’m not exactly sure what I did.” To which he said,\n\n“You extended your arms and sent those two brutish thugs flying, without making contact.” \n\n“I did?” I replied.\n“Yes.” said the man. After a moment he shook his head and said, “Either way, thank you for saving me. I am in your debt. What is your name?” After a moment I said,\n“James Clark.” The man then said, “I am Henry Jedway. Noble of Northenway. We should head to Northenway now. I know the way.” He stopped for a moment then said,\n“Also, you should keep… whatever it is that you did a secret. Wouldn’t want to give people the wrong impression.”\n\n I nodded, not sure what else I could do other then follow him, and set off.\n\nEnd of Chapter One\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kaedreni", "The Bloody Baron", "22nd of Malin's Welcome,\n                              1519\n\n\n         THE STATE\n             OF THE\n           KAEDRENI\n\n\n       by Titus de Sola\nDust scatters on the horizon.  Hooves on valley upon valley thunder to a halt, beasts glaring across to the other, obeying their rider's whims.  Carrion birds dare defy the scorching heat and incandescence of the regal\nWhite Sun.  A scene is painted for\nyou that will set the stage for generations to come. But no matter the turmoil nor the degeneracy of either side I find my conscience bothered greatly by the fact that the blood of Kaedrin and Rhoswen turns against eachother under both banners of the war.\nThe Kaedreni have opted to let their luster become a finely honed weapon, a greatsword, to be used at the whims of Savoie and Sarkozic alike, though disrespected moreso on behalf of the latter.\n\nBut only the Kaedreni allowance of such be at fault.\nAnd it is a weapon, forged inside the lungs of hell, wrought by tens of thousands of the strongest men of our Kaedreni race, that we do now let the others, who have forgotten their place as our vassals, use freely and improperly against eachother,\nlike children who can scarcely pick up a fork.  That weapon is our martial mastery and sheer superiority in waging conflicts, gained by our diligence in carrying out the will of God and His first, the line of Horen, and then of Chivay.  No other Race\namongst Men can maintain aggression nor offensive nor conviction in the way that the Kaedreni man can; it is simply impossible.  They cry as they attempt to emulate our finest military traditions that they have inherited our place as the finest amongst\nmankind, but like all others their walls crumble, their people degenerate, they turn to banditry and villainy, and they destroy themselves from the inside.\n\nThey frequently seek our service as their officers, but they will never be heirs to Kaedrin.\nThe free men of the Rose have turned on eachother, instead of their proper enemies: those who envy all we Kaedreni have done.\nPeter must weep, if the dead weep, at the state of our people, our Kaedreni race.\n\nI would weep in his place, but I\nwould also hope.\n\nI would not see the blood of Kaedrin wither into nothing in the same way that the Horens did.  Even the common Kaedreni man, at this stage, is more bloodworthy than your mainstay Orenian lord, and no doubt far more\nthan those savages of color out of the Duchy of Adria whom want to eat us alive. I would not see our people fall to that fate. I would endeavor to stop it.\n\nI, De Sola, would fight to the death if need be for our people, so long as it granted my\ncountrymen victory.\n\nAnd though when fighting we are naturally greater, fight, we must not always.\n\nWe need consolidation.  Ties of marriage between our Kaedreni Houses.  Living space, territories, slaves.  We cannot forget what it means to bear\nour name.  We were made to militarily administrate the world, and everyone else living in it are either ourselves, our allies, or they are rebels.  There is no other alternative.\n\nWhich of the three are you, friendo?\nMy love and my strongest wishes to those whom this letter concerns.  May it find you in good health, and in the mind for a change of the course of our history.  Hear out this message, brothers, hear out this message and bring Creeping Death to them all.\nBy Owyn's guidance, we will prevail.\n\nAve, true to Kaedrin!\n\n                         T.d.S", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kal'Varak", "Archmage Crumena", "The Kal'Varak\nRescribed by Arch-Mage Crumena V. Illwindor on the 2nd of the First Seed, 1473.\nThe Kal'Varak, which roughly translates as 'Mind City', is an ancient crystalline artifact. It was dug up by the dwarves of Karik just prior to\ntheir unearthing of the hibernating dragons, but the faded scratches on the side suggest it has been discovered at least once before this, perhaps by the original inhabitants of Karik. It seems to be some sort of powerful magical nexus, exerting a\nsignificant magical influence without appearing to draw magical power anywhere, as if it somehow generates it itself. Despite this, the Kal'Varak is useless as a source of magical energy. All of its power is turned inwards on itself, giving the\nKal'Varak the bizzare property that gives it its name. When a living being touches the Kal'Varak, their mind and soul are forcefully drawn from their bodies into the Kal'Varak itself. Once inside, they find themselves in a strange dreamworld, often\ntaking the form of a maze, populated by their memories, dreams and nightmares. In the Kal'Varak, people appear as they would wish to be, some see themselves as stronger, taller, more attractive, sometimes as a different race\nentirely. While the ability to walk through one's mind and the minds of any others currently 'in' the Kal'Varak may seem enticing, the dreamworld is dangerous. The dreamworld responds to moods, fears and doubts, often turning a\nguilty memory into a full-blown nightmare in an instant. The more complex the mind, the more labyrinthian the maze, and those with dark pasts they'd rather forget are often forced to face them within the Kal'Varak. Even more dangerous is\nwhen the mind and crystal form a world that one would not want to leave. The collapsed body outside the crystal still needs food, water, and is still vunerable to harm. If the body dies, the mind cannot return to it. Somewhere in the Kal'Varak maze is\na door, and those more experienced with the dreamworld can find it more quickly than others. The door is always relevant in form to the person it belongs to, often impossible to mistake for one's own. Sometimes the door is not even a door, but it is\nalways clearly an exit. Passing through your door returns you to your body, but if you pass through the wrong door, you may find yourself in the wrong body entirely.", ""),
        StaticBook("The kha & Dryad", "haunter3", "For the topic of this book which is covering one of the kha sacrifices we will use an example that is sadly quite common place in our society\nChapter 1. \n\nShe was a simple wood elf, not simple of mind but simple in needs. In that all she loved and needed was her tree, an oak tree the be percise. Yes sadly the perpetrator of this event is a Dryad\nThe fact she was a Dryad was not her crime, as she took care of the land and her tree which is part of Metztli's teaching and for that she was well in the eyes of the Kharajyr. No her crimes originated from what she did to the kharajyr\nChapter 2. \n\nSomehow through her ignorance this Dryad feel into Absyyl's evil schemes to harm and do away with the Kharajyr! we know not exactly how this transformation happend\none moment she was a nice loving friend and the next she had succumbed to his evil twisted view of our lovly race. to the exent that she agreed to slander us infront of friends and deface our beloved Metztli.\nChapter 3.\n\nThis vile defacement took place merely two days after her turn, after her sudden and absolute faith in Absyyl's lies and slander. she came to our Lovely and peaceful island to\nspew forth a torent of loathful comments some including \"You heathenistic bags of fur\" \"Absyyl is the one true God, Metztli is just a Deamond trying to play god.\" among many other miscellaneous statements\nChapter 4.\n\nOf course the loyal, normally peaceful, followers of Metztli would not stand for such slander to be spoken upon their island. The near by Dra' quickly rushed the Dryad that was once loved\nby them and many on the island, their tridents left behind as crimes such as hers are left up to the Priests not the army. she offered little resistance, for she was weak upon seeing the holy anger of Metztli in the eyes of her followers.\nher body frozen in place from regret as she saw why this race was once known as 'savage'. this savagery was shown in the form of a sacrifice\nChapter 5. \n\nThe Sacrifice was one normally done to war enemies of the Kharajyr before battle, but now it was used upon the war enemy Absyl's solider. As is the punishment for those who break the Kharajyrian law", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kidnapping", "Henry Winterleaf", "The following is a true story. This book has, however, been written many years after the story it tells, all from memory. Therefore, some details may be slightly innaccurate.\nMy name is Henry Winterleaf and this is the story of the time I was kidnapped by the kha's of Asulon. The story takes place over the space of two elven days. It begins with me sitting at home by the fire. Back then, I was a prince of a minor city and I\nlived a happy life. This was not one of those days, however. I received a note by a large hawk. It was from the Leader of the Khas telling me that my fiance, Kirra, had been kidnapped.\nThey told me to stand by for demands but I would not wait. I rushed\noutside, quickly putting on my coat to protect myself from the snow.\nI headed to the cloud temple, hoping I could find my way to rescuing my fiance. I didn't even know where she was. All I knew was that I had to find her. And I had to find her now.\nI began asking around the temple for anyone who knew where the kha people lived. Eventually, I came across a halfling who offered to show me the way. After all this time I've forgotten his name, i'm afraid but he was a kind man. Brave enough to lead me\neven though he knew it would bring only danger upon himself. I had explained my situation to him and along the way we were joined by an old dwarven warrior with a hatred for the Khas. The three of us travelled together all the way to the wood elf capital.\n\"The boat to the Kha's island is just beyond the wood elf city\" said our halfling guide. However, we would not make it that far today. Along the path, just past the city, we were ambushed. A group of 3 large Kha warriors blocked our path. They were led by\na giant black-haired beast of a Kha. He was nearly 2ft taller than me and the others weren't much shorter. We had no choice but to stand and fight. Unfortunately, we were no match for them, with both the halfling and the dwarf getting knocked out, leaving\nme all alone against the three of them. I held my ground for as long as I could but it was no use to fight any longer. I managed to crawl under the leaves of a nearby tree, just out of reach of the Khas. They clawed at the ground trying to get\nme. Every scratch getting inches closer. It looked like all hope was lost when suddenly a patrol of elf city guards emerged from the treetops. We had been lucky enough to survive long enough for the army to come back from training.\nThey drew their bows and the Kha trio was forced to retreat. We were safe. For now, at least. We were escorted back inside the city where we were given three beds in a nearby tavern to recover in. With that, the first elven day was over.\nThe next elven day I awoke feeling healed. However, my companions had not been so lucky. Their injuries were much greater and they could not travel with me any further. Not wanting to waste time, I thanked my companions for their bravery and set off.\nI did not have to go far before I received another message from a familiar bird. It told me to come to the Kha boat with 10,000 minas or else Kirra would die. I suspected a trap, so I contacted a couple of my friends - Helgar and Arthur. We met up and\nheaded towards the meeting point. \"Hide here and if i'm not back soon, come after me.\" I said, cautious not to let the kidnappers see I had brought company, despite their orders. We met on the boat and I saw a few familiar faces. The Khas from yesterday,\nall three of them, but most importantly, my fiance, Kirra. She was bound and gagged but mostly unharmed. Uneasily, I handed over the ransom money and waited for them to hold up their end of the deal. They did not. I watched as my fiance was thrown\noverboard, still with her arms and legs bound, and I was grabbed by several Khas. I was now their captive and could only watch helplessly as Kirra began to drown. We set sail for their island, with me furiously trying to fight my way free.\nWe arrived on the island and I was immediately dragged into a pit in the ground. With its sand floor and high walls it looked more like an arena than a cage but the bars on the roof were the give-away. I cursed loudly at my captors but I was met with only\ninsults and taunting. Suddenly, all the Khas rushed away from the cage. There was a situation at the docks. I turned to find the door of my cage opening and a medium sized Kha in robes greeting me. He told me that my friends had arrived in time to save\nKirra and were now fighting their way through the docks. This Kha was different from the others. There was no word for it at the time but I believe this was the first ever case of an 'ApeKha'. I couldn't believe it. I was a free man once more but still\nnot safe yet. With this 'ApeKha's' help I fought my way to the docks where I found Helgar, Arthur and Kirra along with two orc warriors fighting the Kha's from earlier. Some how, my friends had enlisted the help of these two orcs to free me. We managed to\nmake our way onto the boat, along with our new 'Apekha' friend, with the orcs choosing to stay behind to fight. Battered and bruised but still alive, we sailed off into the distance.\nDespite all our misfortunes, we had come out on top. We were free.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kin", "Ebonsquire", "The Kin\n\n((Originally written by ReaperT))\nThe Kin, a mythical group known only to a few. Those who do know of them fear them greatly. Their leader, is a great and powerful wizard. Some say that this wizard saw the banishment of Iblees. Others claim that it is just several beings each inheriting\ncontrol of the Kin. Those presumptions would be correct.\n\nThis story is not about each of those leaders, but about the first of the Kin. This \"man\", may be the sole cause of people's fear of the Kin. But, I must start in the beginning, for the story\nto make sense.\n\nIt all started before the war with Iblees. A young elf named Crine was studying magic. He felt that his father, Malin, was not quite allowing him to grow. After several attempts to get his father to teach him more\npowerful magicks, Malin shunned his son and tried to prevent him from learning any magic. Of course, Crine did not like that, but he could not disobey his father. Crine was forced from his life of peace and happiness and was thrown into the military. \nOf course, none knew that the army of Iblees was being created at this time. Once the first attacks of the undead came, the army was thrown into action.\n\n*The book abruptly ends here*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lake", "Sofetios", "The Lake\nBy Sofetios\n\nI wander upon a path by a lake,\nWondering where it’s all gone.\nEvery day I used to come here,\nFrom the morning to the evening’s yawn.\nEvery now and again I wonder,\nWhy the days have passed,\nAnd think very deeply,\nWhy they don’t seem to last.\n \nDay by day, night by night,\nThe Lake becomes small still.\nThe thoughts of it become thinner,\nEven to my strongest will.\n \nIt has become ten smaller and ten times shallower,\nEven though it has not changed\nTo other people it might be normal,\nBut to me it is considered strange.", ""),
        StaticBook("The languges", "Dela Vaik", "The Blah\n\nUg= hello, Trom'ka= welcome, Yub= yes, Nub= no, Guy'ye= goodbye, Lat= you, Mi= me, Rulg= thank you, Gruk= understand, Dabu= my pleasure, Bubhosh= big or great, Snaga= slave, Nubhosh= bag or small, Buub= pig, Pushdug= stinky, Glob= fool,\nKlomp= fight, Flat= dead, Blarg= House, Uruk= orc, Brudda= war uzg orc, Stowts or gazat= dwarf, Twigies or Treehuggers or Albai= elf, Squeals= halfings, Quickspawn or Breeders or Shara= human, Nuutshara= ascended, Nubded= undead, Buubshara Nubded= zombie-\n-pigman, Howlur= wolf, Skah or Saahkah= curse words, Agh= and Buurz or Burz= dark or black, Mojo= magic, Krimp= control someone or stun, Uzg= world, Goi= city, Lusk= axe, O'lig= bow, Ligz= arrow, Zult= sword, Stik= staff, San= home, hosh= good, Rex= king,\nGoth= lord, Strigz= war, kub= child.\n\nend of lesson\n\nElven\nKarin'ayla= good day, Ker'ayla= good night, van'ayla= farwell, Mali= elf, Bortu= dwarf, Uruk= orc, Valah= human, Tali'bortu= halfing, llir= friends, laurir= noble,\nend of lesson\nHumans, dwarves, and kha's speak the common tounge but dwarves and kha's have a accent.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Record", "Artorius Thannius", "Personal Records of the Spellcrafter Archon III - Desperate Measures\nWhile it seems the Ravager was defeated and destroyed, it came at the cost of Aegis: the entire continent has crumbled into some sort of Abyss. It is more than a\nfracture of matter, it is a collapse of the laws of the world. Rivel failed to escape the blast radius: the city has broken up and now floats on the magical currents as we hover over the Abyss. The cataclysm has pushed us below the minimum population\nthe scryers say we need to survive. Up here we cannot even get food. The Lesser Caste’s survivors have mostly starved to death and with food stores dwindling we will soon follow.\nI have no choice. Tonight I will conduct the ritual of lichdom. Rivel is\ndead and so are its people. The remaining few will be more than enough to serve as a sacrifice for the ritual. If Rivel must die, its leader shall live on.\nGarzardiel’s name be cursed.\n- Artorius Thannius, Former Spellcrafter Archon of Rivel", ""),
        StaticBook("The Light Behind", "GusanoArentonio", "So long to all my friends\nEveryone of them met tragic ends\nWith every passing day\nI'd be lying if I didn't say\nThat I miss them all tonight\nAnd if they only knew what I would say\nIf I could be with you tonight\nI would sing you to sleep\nNever let them take the light behind your eyes\nOne day I'll lose this fight\nAs we fade in the dark\nJust remember you will always burn as bright\nBe strong and hold my hand\nTime-it comes for us, you'll understand\nWe'll say goodbye today\nAnd I'm sorry how it ends this way\nIf you promise not to cry\nThen I'll tell you just what I would say\nIf I could be with you tonight\nI would sing you to sleep\nNever let them take the light behind your eyes\nI'll fail and lose this fight\nNever fade in the dark\nJust remember you will always burn as bright\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your\n\nSometimes we must grow stronger and\nYou can be stronger when I'm gone\nWhen I'm here, no longer\nYou must be stronger and\nIf I could be with you tonight\nI would sing you to sleep\nNever let them take the light behind your eyes\nI failed and lost this fight\nNever fade in the dark\nJust remember you will always burn as bright\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes", ""),
        StaticBook("The little golem", "Yden", "The little golem that could\nBy Yden\n\nJames was one of many golems in golem school, he was taught lots of subjects but he was best at following instructions class because he studied hard and practiced, when James got his degree in following orders he\napplied for a job, he would serve the common folk, James demonstrated his ability but he was much too cumbersome, he kept bumping into everything and his feet were too big, they broke floor boards and cracked the stone beneath his feet, his smaller friend\nTimmothy got the job instead so instead he applied to serve a knight, again he showed the knight what he could do, he shined the armour but his hands were too big and he was too strong, he simply crushed the armour like paper when he handled it so his\nmedium sized friend Jakob got the job instead. James was feeling very sad at this point, he felt like nobody wanted him, he was too wide, his feet were too big, he was too strong and his hands were too big but in one final attempt to serve a master he\napplied to serve the king, the king allowed him to perform and he excelled, the king had marble floors, the strongest floors money could buy, every room was huge so he would never bump into anything and the kings armour was made of mythril, not even James\ncould bend mythril so James was given the status of kings golem and served the king with honor until the king fell ill, James was very sad but he served the prince instead to carry on his great work!\n\n-Yden \nAlso see; The golem who learnt to love\nAlso see; The musical golem", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lost Ones, 2", "Ebonsquire", "The Lost Ones, Volume Two\n\n((Originally written by callum2357))\nThe order 1000 strong had now been reduced to a few hundred. Callum the frozen blade had managed to save the little amount of people that remained. Without a leader, they were lost so they created a small village in the Whispering Isles to live out the\nremainder of their lives but they still needed a leader. Frozen Blade took up the mantle of High Guardian and made a council out of the people he thought could make a difference. The first act of the council was to send out scout parties to gather\nresources and try to establish contact. The first contact that was made was with the elves of Laurelin and the scouts collected valuable information of farming. The scouts that found the dwarfs gathered information on mining, the scouts that reached the\nhumans gathered information on scouting and fighting techniques and that they would become a problem in the future as they have potential to become evil more than others. The scouts that found the nomadic orcs were killed in the arena by ork gladiators,\none scout managed to escape back to Whispering Isles but died the next day due to his injuries. With this knowledge, High Guardian Frozenblade established a growing town with a mine and farming capabilities along with a good defense. They expanded and\nkept dealing with the other nations until they were great friends. The first battle that was to be had was at an elven city that had been overrun with orks. The battle cost many lives and High Guardian Frozen Blade got a blade through the chest and the\nstomach. The forces of the elves, dwarfs, humans and the lost ones managed to destroy the orks and go back to their cities. In Whispering Isles, High Guardian Callum was laying in the hospital bleeding and was close to death. The council rounded up there\nmost trusted warriors to go back to the fortress and retrieve a goblet of water from the Fountain of Immortality. When they got back to the camp they gave the High Guardian the Goblet as he was moments away from death. The next day everyone\nwaited outside the tent waiting to hear from the council, but the news was grave. The High Guardian was in a coma and was unable to be revived and for the next few days everyone was silent going about their duties and so it would remain, the Hope and\nSalvation that once filled all their hearts was shattered for the last time.\n\nThe clues lies below along the high way this book travels. Now it rests beside the road.", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 1", "Lucion Sullas", "-------------------             The\n        Maehr'sae\n        Hiylun'ehya\n\n         Chapter 1\n-------------------As interpreted by\nLucion Sullas, former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun'or.\nThe Way of Purity is greatly discredited around the civilised world due to the actions of uninformed adherants and their unfortunate victims. Misinformation upon its tenets run rampant amongst the uninitiated, thus I write this short series upon its\nhistory, its ideals, and common misconceptions. It is a desire to inform, rather than 'convert' that drives this humble quill, therefore do not consider this a threat to any local religions/philosophies/mysteries that currently occupy your own people.\nTo those that read on, Maehr'sae hiylun'ehya to you.\n\n-L. Sullas\nIn the beginning, long before Iblees, there was Aegis. And within Aegis, there were elves. Not of any racial denominations as we have today, but of a singular, primal form. Of this time we know little, save for what scraps we have recovered during the\ndays of Asulon. During this time, a particular elf caught ancient Malinor's attention--a woman known as Larihei. This woman changed herself through 'bathing in and ingesting the waters of enchanted pools of gold.' This eventually lead to Larihei's exile,\nand the self-imposed exile of many followers.\n\nBy means unknown, they arrived in Asulon and constructed 'Cihi'thilln.' Or \"Silver City\" in the common tongue. Within this place they built many lost wonders, discovered\nbizarre and mysterious magics, and then disappeared entirely. Many reasons have been postulated for this--namely a great plague that coincided with other cataclysms that rocked the Dervas and the Mori. Regardless, the city that the Aegisian High Elves\nfound was a ruin. Within the crumbling Eternal College, they found remnants of an ancient essay; one the previous occupiers based their society upon. It's hypothesis was 'Maehr'sae hiylun'ehya' Or, 'The pursuit of wisdom and health.'\nThe newly-dubbed \"Mali'aheral\" (Blessed elves) chose to honour these ancestors by following their lost ways. What was originally a cultural focal-point eventually became a way of life. A philosophy that drives many individuals to this day.\nUnderstand that this history is short only due to a complete lack of information that was lost over the eras. Our way is older than most empires and religions. It lives to this day, and may well continue to exist so long as there are Mali'aheral to revere\nit. \n\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 2", "Lucion Sullas", "-------------------             The\n        Maehr'sae\n        Hiylun'ehya\n\n         Chapter 2\n-------------------As interpreted by Lucion Sullas. Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun'or.\nTo follow the tenets of the Maehr'sae hiylun'ehya one must first know the meaning behind the ancient elven that masks it. Its most accurate common translation is \"The pursuit of wisdom and health\" or simply 'wisdom and health.' So revered is this term\nthat it akin to a blessing given between adherants. \n\nThe Maehr'sae pertains to the aquisition and sharing of knowledge amongst fellow Mali'aheral. Our race is known for many things, but poor academics are not included. After being\nchanged by the magics of the Golden Pools, we were blessed with studious minds, and gifted great talent with magic of any form. Thusly, it is imperative that we embroil ourselves utterly within tasks that further our people's knowledge.\nThe Hiylun'ehya pertains to the bloodlines and fotitude of the people. Pure bloodlines are the ones that best retain the blessings of the ancient pools. To sully them with poorly-reasoned mixed breeding thins the blessings that we gained, and therefore\nmakes the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya more difficult to complete--if not impossible. In guarding our bloodlines we must show discipline and fortitude. Things that detract the health of the people; violence against the pure, mixed-breeding, and being too lenient\nand accepting towards the other races. One must always be diligent when regarding impurities. The small concessions of today always lead to the vilest impurities tomorrow brings. It has been observed, and thus it is known.\nThe ultimate goal of the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya is its completion. To reach true enlightment, the Mali'aheral strive to understand all through constant learning, and a pure people. When all is understood, we will be beyond the simple meanderings of the\nmundane world. It is unknown what will occur when this day of total enlightenment occurs, but one suspects the Mali'aheral will know precisely what to do.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 3", "Lucion Sullas", "-------------------\n            The\n        Maehr'sae\n        Hiylun'ehya\n\n        Chapter 3\n-------------------\n\nAs interpreted by Lucion Sullas. Former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun'or.\nAs with any ideology, there are misconceptions amongst the uninitiated. Mainly upon the desires of its adherants, the reasons behind their actions, or perhaps even mere differences in personality. It is difficult to write a truly concise list,\nbut one hopes the ones he lists are relevant to the reader.\n1. On Racism and\n        Seclusion\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support illogical hatreds of other peoples. Rather, it supports rational wariness of dangerous outsiders--such as Orcs, goblins, and suspicious\nstrangers. The Orc and goblin are beings with a natural aversion to elven thought and philosophy. Though there can be exceptions, they are often ignored or destroyed, should they be in the presence of the Pure. They cannot be\ntrusted under any circumstances.\n\nIn regards to the other races, it is most certainly dependant on the high elf in question. I am yet to meet a High Elf aside from Uradir who truly despised all peoples equally.\n\nIt is for these\nreasons adherants separate themselves from contemporary society.\n2. On Insults and\n      the Insulted\n-------------------The Maehr'sae hiylun'ehya does not support arbitrary personal attacks. It does, however, support learning, advising, and truth.\n\nShould an individual speak without\nmerit or evidence upon an individual with the purpose of cruel amusement, then they are a poor adherant, and have provided nothing to anyone.\n\nHowever, advise can often be misinterpreted as insult. Adherants are taught to\ndespise falsehood, therefore should something be perceived as incorrect they rightly feel the need to amend it.\n\nIf an individual has their feelings hurt during the process, it is their issue, and not the adherant's.\n3. On Violence and\n       Aggression\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support physical violence of any kind. It does support safeguarding the purity of its people. Often, death to those who would sully the purity of the\nadherants is the first and foremost answer to such crimes. However, violent actions belong to beasts, and are beneath us. Ours is an order built upon the mind, not on the passions of raised fists.\n4. On 'Purges' and\n         Murder.\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support 'Purges,' or murder. It does, however, support the exaction of justice to craven monsters.\n\nSome individuals are so profane in their\nexistance that they insult and endanger our way. Such people are more often-than-not loathed throughout all civilised lands. Such individuals are few and far between, but if by the act of living they injure us, then they must be destroyed for the good\nof all. Exile ought to be the first and foremost method of drastic punishment in any case.\n\n5. On Experimentation\n     and Learning\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support unethical and cruel experiments. It does support the vigorous aquisition of knowledge. Those that would perform any experiment on a living,\nsentient, non-consenting individuals are performing a disgusting act that harms their own purity through reckless and untethered curiosity, as well as harming the reputation of their own people. It is bizarre, cruel, unethical, and the findings never\noutweigh the cost.\n6. On Emotion and\n     Aversion to it.\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support an emotionless state in the individual. Rather, it encourages logic, foresight, and wisdom over passionate outbursts.\nIt is wiser to think before feeling. In public, it is beneath an adherant to act by the whims of emotion--it shows a lack of self-control and would likely offend those around yourself.\n7. On Superiority\n    and Arrogance\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not declare high elves to be superior to other races. It does, however, support that those who follow its path closely are greater than others, as they seek\nenlightenment through the unravelling of truth, rather than the mundanities of life.\n\nIdentifying adherants as 'arrogant' is simply an innocent misinterpretation on the side of the uninititated. Should one encounter an adherant that claims\nthemselves to be 'superior' generally speaking, one would advise you to ask them of their current academic projects. Should they refuse to answer, it is safe to say their ego speaks, and not the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya.\n8. On Adherants and\n     Their Qualities\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya supports that only the Mali'aheral, with their inherant blessings, can successfully follow the Pure Way. But this is only true in theory.\nThe Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya encourages community cohesion and the search for truth. Theoretically, any race (with the exception of perhaps the orcish peoples) may adopt and follow the path to enlightenment. No other race has attempted\nto adhere to it, thus perhaps it will never be known for certain.\nOne hopes that this series has been illuminating. Seek out L. Sullas, if you can, should questions be sought. Otherwise, good luck on your own twisting path.\n\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mali'ame", "Ash'ya Norodiir", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The Basic Guide to Mali'ame.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\n\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Basic language, laws and guidance.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Language\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIt would be noted that the most mali'ame only use basic greetings and words in their own language day-to-day.\n\nMyself personally, I have only met one ame who understands more than this.\nBelow are some more of the common phrases you will hear spoken from the ame.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nKarin'ayla - Good Morning,\n\nKer'ayla - Good Evening,\n\nVan'ayla - Goodbye,\nAherhan - Thankyou.\n\nLlir/Lliran - Friend/Friends,\n\nValah - Human.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIt would be wise to learn these should you frequent visit the mali.\nThere are pleanty more spoken words which we use, the next most common would be the different races.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nMali - Elf,\nMali'ame - Wood Elf,\nMali'aheral - High Elf,\nMali'ker - Dark Elf.\n\nUruk - Orc,\nBortu - Dwarf,\nValah - Human.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Laws\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWithin the mali'ame home, there are strict rules surrounding magic and appearence. \nThese would be the more notable laws in place - alongside your usual.\nIn this guide I will cover only these two sections of the laws, and then compile a list of actual laws.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Section Three - Appearance and Bloodlines.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n* A citizen of Laureh'lin must be of elven blood,\n\n* A citizen of Laureh'lin is expected not to be un-natural or corrupted in any form.\nThe criteria for this will be decided on a case by case basis and left to the discretion of the council,\n\n* A citizen of Laureh'lin must be of a resonable skin colour (fair, brown, black, NOT blue, purple, cyan etc.),\nresonable hair colour (most non-ludicrous dyes permitted, however), and wear resonable attire (clothing made of socially acceptable material such as cloth, wool, or leather.)\n\n* A citizen of Laureh'lin must not possess any un-natural bodily\ncharacteristics. Examples o this include tails, wings, fangs and fur where fur should not be.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Section Five - Magic\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~*The casting of any voidal magic in public within the boarders of Laureh'lin is illegal under any context except for immediate self defense in a life or death scenario. Exceptions may be handed out by\nthe Praetor.\n\n* All individuals with the ability to cast voidal magic must report to the Laureh'lin Guildmaster and report the magic(s) to be documented. The ability level and number of magics the mage is capable of must\nbe presented  in a clear and accurate manner.\n\n* The governot of Laureh'lin has the right to deny a mage's registration, restricting the mage from casting any magic at all, at his own discretion. He also bares the power\nto enable a mage to cast publically under special circumstances, on a case by case basis.\n\n* To practice magic in a public setting, one must pay 100 minas registration to the Guildmaster,\nThe final law relating to magic contracitcs the first one, stating that three hundered mina should be paid to the guildmaster as well. So I would leave this one out.\nMagic and appearance are a touchy subject to those who are not ame by blood.\n\nThose incharge wish to see their residents down the natural, drudic path. Unfortunatly, not all agree.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Guidance\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Whether you are an ame looking to settle with your people or a valah looking to learn more, there is a lot to ame culture that some folks may be ignorant to.\nThe aspects hold a high stature in ame culture. Those being the two the ame look to in hardships and for general guidence.\n\nOne may call them 'Deities'.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCernunnos\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n[!] An image of a horned man dressed in leaves would take up the remainder of the page. He holds a large staff in his left hand.\nCernunnos is the horned man, the hunter of the ame dieties. \n\nHe is responsible for bringing death and hunt to their lives.\n\nThough he is not evil. Death is a natural part of lifes cycle and it is required\nto keep our lands in balance.\n\nAnimals must die to serve as food, or their hides for armor and clothing.\n\nThe ill and old should die to make way for the young and newborn.\nDeath always has purpose and Cernunnos is the one who maintains this.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCerridwen\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n[!] An image of a beautiful woman takes up the remainder of the page. Brightly coloured and smiling features on the womans face. A contrast to the horned man.\nCerridwen is the second aspect. She is responsible for bringing and nurturing life.\n\nShe is more often refered to as the Green Lady as she oversees the growth of our trees, our crops. Flower and creatures.\nAnd where Cernunnos brings death, Cerridwen replaces it with the new and budding, renewing the cycle.\nFinally, there are three main unthinkable acts in ame culture:\n\nMeaningless Killing, Wastefulness and Altering Nature. \n\nThese should all be very common sense to any race. We ame believe death should always serve a\npurpose, much like Cernunnos' acts.\n\nWastefulness is seen as wasting the gift granted to us by Cerridwen - this could be seen as a fairly large insult.\n\nAltering nature goes hand in hand with the laws set by\nthe leaders. Nature should be left as the aspects created it.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~This compilation of information is from my own views as an ame who has seen her culture change and alter for over three decades. \n\nThey are not set in stone and the views of each will differ.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The laws listed are taken directly from the laws of the state and have not been altered.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mali'ker", "Dak'ir Des'Nox", "Birth of the Mali'ker\n------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  By Dak'ir Des'Nox\nBefore I begin this tale, I'd like to state that the origin of the Mali'ker is still unknown to us. This is simply an\nold tale passed down \nthrough my clan.\nIt begins with the \nHearth Father, Malin.\nHe looked upon the Mali'ame, his first children. Their image molded after the forests they reside in. In them he saw devotion. A will to protect the trees and animals without rival.\nHe then looked to the high elves, his second children. Their display was ever the epitome of purity. In them he saw knowledge. Their desire to learn and expand in all things was unparalelled. \n\nBut he saw something they lacked. Passion.\nHe racked his mind of many days. It was not until he looked skyward as dusk fell that he saw what would design us. \n   Before him lay the night tide, a vast sea of stars and anomalies. He raises a hand to the night sky and began to collect what would\nmake us seperate from out fair colored kin. He took the dark hues from the empyrean and shaped our bodies. He took the tails of comets and darkened stone of meteorites. Giving us the blacks, whites, and faint blues of our hair.\nHe took a step back from his creation, observing the from of what would become the dark elves. Folding his arms, he thought.\n\n   What else could set these beings apart from the Mali'ame and\nthe Mali'aheral?\nNext, he looked down. His eyes falling upon the ground. Kneeling, he reached an arm into the depths of the earth and began to pull precious gems from the deep recesses. He carried the jewels back to the grey froms placing them into their eyes.\nHe favored the rubies and garnets most of all, but occasional sapphires, emeralds, and topazes glinted in their vigils.\n\n Before him stood us.\n     The Dark Elves.\nBut there was still something... What could give us the passion we lacked?\n\n   He looked above one final time and raised a careful hand. Plucking single stars from the sky and placing one within each of us. Giving us our bright and burning souls.\nHis mind lingered to the Wood Elves and High elves again.\nNature and dedication. Knowledge and Purity.\nBut what could give the Dark Elves their drive?\n\nHe pondered again. Before long, he smiled softly.\nHow could he forget? \n\n   He spoke to the still forms and uttered three words.\n\n\"Family, honor, love.\"\n\n            ...\nAnd with that, we awoke. With stars burning brightly in our chests, fueling these three things, we have become the fiercely passionate beings we are today...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Marked Oath", "Adeon of Rhoswen", "The Sacred Oath\n\n\"I accept my marking and the burdens to follow it. I will act as expected of me and risk my life for the innocent mundane, to protect them from the dangers of the supernatural and monstrosity alike. Should I fail, God help me.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Matriarch", "Thurak'Yar", "THE MATRIARCH   \n\nThe tale of the daughter of Dragur.\n\n\n\nRe-Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, 21'st of The First Seed, 1489.\nFirst born of the brood of Dragur, a female, molded in his image, and adopting his unquenchable thirst of sheer knowledge. \n\"The sun will awaken each new day, followed by the rise of the moon, that will light the seemingly endless nights, and during\nthese nights it will be the Stars which will guide you. This land in which you were born in will teach you many things. And as you come to learn, you will share the knowledge which you have come to acquire in the hopes that the ones you come to\nshare with learn from it. This is my dream.\"\n\nAnd so the Daemon fell into a seemingly eternal slumber. Many centuries have come to pass since that day, and he collection continued to grow. Unfortunately, some had used bits of knowledge she had\nshared with them for their own greedy purposes. They didn’t believe in her ways of “Shared knowledge for knowledge”, and wanted it without giving anything in return. They found the place in which she kept all her books, scrolls and scrawlings, and began\nto steal whatever they thought would bring them wealth and power. Upon returning, she felt a sense of violation and mistrust, but knew and understood that time itself would heal those feelings. She began to scrawl everything she could remember from what\nwas stolen from her, but they were merely tattered fragments compared to what she once had. Hope had reached her a few years later when she found one of her books amongst some ruins and rubble. She began to hope that the others\nwill come to reveal themselves once more.\nThus, the Matriarch wanders the land, in search of the items that were taken from her, but also still learning what she can from her travels and from the land. By merely observing and keeping scrawls of what she has come to witness, to finding\nbooks, novels and scrolls from past and present civilizations of the land. This is her passion... And her only purpose.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Moot", "Leyun Kameki", "The Moot\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nThe Moot is an assembly held for all Druids of a particular Circle to come together for discussion, debate, and decision making. It is a time to worship the Aspects, to make notice of the events of the world, to commit to projects, and much more.\nMany times a Moot might serve the sole purpose of voting for a new Archdruid or Druid Guide or to cast votes on shunning a particular individual who has wronged a Druid, Druids, or the Order. Seldomly, a Moot might be held to throw a party, host a\nwedding, or perform a funeral.\n\nOnly by the word of an Archdruid may a Moot be called. Druids, Dedicants, Druid Guides, and Hierophants all can, and should, present information of importance to the Archdruids, and anyone can request\na Moot be called. However, it is up to an Archdruid to decide if and when a Moot shall be held and for what topics it shall be held to discuss. Only shall the Inner Circle, the Archdruids and Druid Guides, make a definite decision, based on a vote count,\nfor the Order. No other Druids or Hierophants are permitted to make decisions for the Order, but their opinions and advice are taken seriously and with much consideration. When serving as a meeting, a Moot is held in the Moot Room of the\nhosting Grove. While a Moot is in session, often times the Archdruid who called it will take the floor to present topics. Out of respect, all who wish to speak should wait for a pause or go-ahead. Druids should request or stand to take the floor or\npresent a topic. Dedicants aren’t permitted to attend Moots, but accepts are often made. In the case that a Dedicant is permitted at a Moot, he or she shall not speak unless asked to.\n\nThe Moot is an ancient tradition of Druidic culture. Sometimes\nnon-Druids are even invited to Moots, such as when relations are being discussed between the Order and a Nation or other group. A Moot is versatile, able to serve the purpose for many different occasions. It is one of the most formal, serious, and\nimportant aspects of Druidic culture. When in attendance of a Moot, remember to respect the speaker and follow proper etiquette. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Moot", "Tristanm1", "The Moot\nInscribed by Dawn Druid Maiavel\nThe Moot is a gathering of the entire circle, traditionally held at the Solstices and Equinoxes. By ancient custom, Moots are called four times a year at these set dates; Three times by the Archdruid, and once (usually in spring) by the Great Druid.\nA Moot on a nontraditional date means the summoner sees something so deeply amiss in the domain that the entire circle must discuss it as soon as possible. \nThese gatherings enable the circle to celebrate the changing of the seasons, to gossip and\nand socialize, to exchange information on the state of the domain, and to fight druidic challenges before an audience. Druids at a Moot perform ceremonies to celebrate Nature, honor their dead, marry a couple within the Order, and initiate new druids.\nAlong with these ceremonial duties, small groups at Moots disappear together into the wilds to talk quietly while searching for herbs or mistletoe. \nThe climax of any such gathering is the High Council of the Moot; The circle's leaders meet in a secret\nlocation to discuss the state of the domain and make plans to rally the circle against a particular problem, if necessary. Sometimes an ambassador from a neighboring circle (usually of druid rank) or an emissary of the Grand Druid attends a council.\nThese personages bring news and greetings--and sometimes requests for help. After the High Council the Great Druid (or the Archdruid) addresses the entire Moot, answers questions, and takes advice. To call a moot, the Archdruid (or Great Druid) sends\nmessengers out across the domain to spread the word to Druids of all branches. All members of a circle at Druid rank or higher must attend or explain the absence. \nThe Moot is scheduled to begin two weeks after the summoner dispatches the announcements,\ngiving all druids enough time to settle their business and arrive. Such a gathering generally takes place at a sacred grove under the stewardship of the summoner. Though most Moots last about four days, the meeting cannot end until the summoning Archdruid\nor the Great Druid, dissolves it.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Observations", "Ketiley Strong-Heart", "-~=  The Observations  =~-\n\n*All observations and notes taken are written and seen by Ketiley of Orvar.\n\n*Small writtings below are scribbled quickly and messily, but more in a though-proccessed fashion.*\n\nMushmushmushmushmush\nmushmushmush\nObservation One:\n\n20th of The Deep Cold, 1472\n\nMorvan and I have decided to start our observations in an old Ruin, to which I, at least, presume was owned once by a Necromancer due to the dried blood on the top\nstory. Nonetheless, my decision for such a place is due to the overgrowth of Mushrooms. Large ones at that.\nMushmushmushmushmush\n\nIt seems with time, the ruin was to decay and nature had one more taken it's beauty back and overthrew the manmade stone\ndesign. In my personal opinion, I believe the decay of such a building, holding vast secrets, though very morbid and very dangerous, is absolutely, peacefully, beautiful when natures takes back it's rightful place among the tall stature of the tower. The\nlarge mushrooms within the odd ruin really add to it. Give it character and seem to coexist perfectly and gorgeously within the stone walls of the masonry. There is, surprisingly, a mechanism that shows Aegis within the tower. And seems oddly preserved.\nBut even then, the rest of the crumbling walls remain together because of the sturdy stalks of the pretty mushrooms that hold the tower together with the years it remains.\nThe musrooms come iin dull colours and vibrant. Tall and small. I could watch them\nfor hours.. T'is truly a sight to behold.\n\n*A rather detailed, very shaded and beautifully drawn, sketch of one of the larger mushrooms, holding dots and leaking small dust clouds of spores, takes up the rest of the page.*\n((X: -63 Z: -208))\nObservation Two:\n\n21st of The Deep Cold, 1472\n\nMorvan and I have now made our way to a grand tree. Very VERY large... Towers completely over the rest of the land... Reminds me of the great tree that harbours the Druids in the Grove.\nThe reason this particular site attracted me is because it has a calming nature about it. Beautiful crystals float below the grand tree. The light from the crystals allow the leaves of the magnificent tree to lightly shine with a dull light that hangs\nbelow the large branches. The lovely jade and emerald leaves canopy most of the forest from the tree that towers so easily over the land. I notice that the trunk harbours spiders in it. But.. T'is the way of nature..\nVery large bees, fireflies, and other\ninsects seem to have made a peaceful home here among the great forest while the large tree offers shelter. Like that of a mother for her children. Reminds me much of Andarta..\nOur first time here, Morvan and myself, was when we bound ourselves together\nthe very first time. Andarta would be The Maiden of The Forest. The Goddess that trusts no one and tends only to her beloved tree. I now see why she loves them so.. The amount of shelter, beauty, trust, and safehaven this Grand tree offers is nothing that\ncan be described or even compared to.. The way the incects seem to take shelter in the tree is... Indescribable... For lack of better words, it's a very gorgeous sight to behold. To be frank.. Even though spiders swarm the land now... This is most\ndefinitely my favourite place to be... The awe, wonder, and love that I feel radiate from this wonderous tree is absolutely incomparable. Watching the sun rise in the east and sparkle so dully against the canopy of leaves is is-... indescribable.. Truly..\nHowever... Morvan and I had to retreat to a safe distance due to the over-swarm of the undead and spiders...\n\nEven from such a great distance... It's clear to see this Mother tree completely towers over her younger saplings and smaller trees..\nNurturing them in her embrace of shady leaves and the friendly light from the crystals.\n\n*An acurate drawing of the Grand Tree, from afar, is shown here, partially showing the very crystals that offer a dull glow.*\n((X: -437 Z: -407))\n~-=*                              *=-~\nObservation Three:\n\n13th of Snow's Maiden, 1473\n\nI've decided to settle at a white stag statue, south of Haelun'or, and sit and observe a pretty blue orchid. The way the wind blows so softly\n~-=*                              *=-~\nagainst the small, pretty, blue petals of the viney flower is rather peaceful to watch. The colour of the flower itself reminds me of the ocean and the sky combined as one. And even though it's sibling flowers,\n~-=*                              *=-~\nlike the variety of colourful tulips, and lilys, the pretty azure, I think, flowers seem to dance in the same movements of the orchid, in the calming wind, the blue orchid stands out. They're definitely something\n~-=*                              *=-~\nyou'll spot first in a crowd of anything.. I think this may be one of the flowers I love the best. Though my love for the rest of the flowers is equally shared.\n\n*a depiction of the blue orchid is drawn here.*\n~-=*                              *=-~\n~-=*                              *=-~\n~-=*                              *=-~\n~-=*                              *=-~\n~-=*                               *=-~\n~-=*                               *=-~\n~-=*                               *=-~\n~-=*                              *=-~\n                 Notes:\n\n- There was a very, VERY, gorgeous, peaceful, pretty, and amazing little cave that had a hotsprink, and bunnies, and so many pretty flowers.\n<3!\n~-=*                              *=-~\n*an acurate graphite depiction of a peony is drawn here among blades of grass.*\n- We then went to an absolutely magnificent place that held the most pretty and largest white trees... I was completely\n~-=*                              *=-~\nawestruck by the absolutely amazing and indescribable scenery... Officially my FAVOURITE place now... Just south of Haelun'or.. Found a little town, too..\n*A picture of the scenery, drawn in a graphitelike\nmaterial is drawn on the previous page, just below the writings.*\n\n((X: 668 Z: 897))\n(( http://oi62.tinypic.com/sw5xef.jpg ))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Order Survey", "Felix Reed", "Survey by Felix Reed\n\n'What do you Think of the Druidic Order?'\n\"My whole family is Druids, So I suppose the Druidic Order is fine.\"\n\n\"All meh impression frem deh Druids is frem dah Individuals.\"\n\n\"As the World destroys itself, the Druids are providing the MUST needed maintence to keep us safe.\"\n\"I would like to join it someday.\"\n\n\"Ah t'ink it tries ta do t'e most gud it can in dis messed up land.\"\n\n\"I believe they are useless and pointless treehuggers that think nature is the answer to everything. They put nature where buildings should be.\"\n\"The druids have not yet cleaned up their eyesore by the main road. They are lazy wastemen.\"\n\n\"If you were to practice magic without any progress, I would call you a druid.\"\n\n\"I think the Druids have good views.\"\n\"Nothin'.\"\n\n\"Ye, I 'aven' 'eard much of et. Nor do aye care much fer it.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The People", "Baldin Frostbeard", "Beware\nthere is enough treachery, hatred violence absurdity in the average\nhuman being to supply any given army on any given day\n\nand the best at murder are those who preach against itand the best at hate are those who preach love\nand the best at war finally are those who preach peace\nthose who preach god, need god\nthose who preach peace do not have peace\nthose who preach peace do not have love\nbeware the preachers\nbeware the knowers\nbeware those who are always reading books\nbeware those who either detest poverty\nor are proud of it\nbeware those quick to praisefor they need praise in return\nbeware those who are quick to censor\nthey are afraid of what they do not know\nbeware those who seek constant crowds for\nthey are nothing alone beware the average man the average woman\nbeware their love, their love is average\nseeks average\nbut there is genius in their hatred\nthere is enough genius in their hatred to kill you\nto kill anybody \nnot wanting solitude not understanding solitude they will attempt to destroy anything\nthat differs from their own\nnot being able to create art\nthey will not understand art\nthey will consider their failure as creators\nonly as a failure of the world not being able to love fully\nthey will believe your love incomplete\nand then they will hate you\nand their hatred will be perfect\n\nlike a shining diamond\nlike a knife\nlike a mountain\nlike a tiger\nlike hemlock\ntheir finest art", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pumpkin Lord", "Titania Hawksong", "With no place to go,\nno place to belong,\n\nI pray that you hear\nthe Pumpkin Lord's song.\n\nIn every statue built,\nthere is a shade,\n\nwhere minds are taken, and freedom is made.\nWherever you roam,\nwherever you walk,\n\na shadow will watch, a shadow will stalk.\n\nHe carries no weapons, no wards and no drums.\n\nBut I pray for you when the Pumpkin Lord comes.\nBy Knox he is known, the lord of all dreams,\n\nbless you with freedom, or smother your screams.\n\nAnd fear not the lord, but rather yourselves,\n\nfor he prays on minds where ambition delves.\nWe are the sickness\nand he is the cure,\n\nwe are the corrupt, but he'll see us pure.\n\nThe gift is nigh, when our monster succumbs.\n\nBut I pray for you when the Pumpkin Lord comes.\nMortals are made by masters of mind,\n\nthis master is you, but you are still blind.\n\nKnox will embrace you and give back your sight,\n\nbut pray you not fail him or suffer his blight.\nThe candle does guide, but also does burn,\n\nso call not his name, for gifts you must earn.\n\nWon't keep him at by with iron nor tongues,\n\nSo I pray for you when the Pumpkin Lord comes.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pumpkin Lord", "A Ravenous Adventurer", "So Hungry.. so very, very hungry I was... lost in the wilderness I was, oh yes, lost I was.... no food... just filthy water... tasteless water...\n\n And then... I saw him... A walking pumpkin... pumpkin pie... food... precious, precious food...\nI lunged at it... I chased it.. oh, it smelled so sweet... I chased it away from the city... the foul, filthy human city.... until an elf... cruel, disgusting elf...\n\nThe elf approached the delicous, precious, pumpkin man... he wanted to kill it...\nI wished the same.....\n\nWe fought him.... the pumpkin man.... then the treacherous, filthy pumpkin man offered a trade.... his body to the elf.... for my arm...\n\nThe treacherous, filthy elf.... he took my arm... but not before the evil pumpkin man....\ndecided he wanted the elf's arm instead....\n\nThe evil, pumpkin man... he cut off the filthy elf's arm...\n\nThen... we fought him... and finally... the filthy elf got his finger.... and ran off...\nThen.... I got one of his.... other fingers.... Then.... the pumpkin man shouted....\n\n\"I am Knox, the Pumpkin Lord!\"\n\nThen... he ran off.... and I did as well.... limping towards the moat.... pumpkin finger in hand... only one arm....\nHungry...\nSo Hungry....\nBut so much pain....\nCan't write... any more...\n*This page is soaked in blood and smells faintly of pumpkins*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Quickening", "Acaele", "The Quickening\n\n       ~ Oem Mali\nA set of figurines are strewn across\nThe unclean tile of the workshop floor\nAs each red petal fans out one by one\nAnd songbirds cry their orchestrated tune\nBefore the proud conductor; Clockwork has\nA certain beauty, such\nthat one may find\nThat they are lost within the fabric of\nTheir own creations; Time begins to slip\nAway, and decades drain the blessed field\nUntil it knows not fruitful seed; elsewhere\nA sudden clap of thunder tightens flesh\nWhile all else fades", "")
    )

    private fun _VAILOR_6(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("The Red Realm", "Ceruberr Asul'Ailer", "The Red Realm\n\n§iThe Red Realm Shall Open Soon...\n\n\"The floating Fortress shall rise from the sea.\"\n\n\"The Organic island is going to fall along with the Fringelands.\"\n\"The realm of the Black Wyrm shall soon open up.\"\n\n\n[!] The elegant looking scroll seems to have been written by the hand of a High Elf. Its writing is intricate and practiced. This would seem to be a copy of an original text...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Salvian Soul", "Alan Witts", "The Salvian Soul\nBy A. Witts\n\nThe Creator watched upon our souls.\n\nTo this very day, he did so.\n\nHe looked and smiled for once he saw.\nThose good of heart and enlightened law.\n\nHis hand he raised for those below.\n\nThose who had the Salvian soul!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Second Day", "Anawkin", "\n  The Second Day\n\n\n(( Originally written by TehLulu))\n\n  I've come to the Pathfinder's new base in search of information. It seems that he has lost perhaps 3 men to banditry and I wish to know their names. \n\n Zevandir is the one who left to become\na bandit. Tailon left, but is an Elven lord, so Kalen does not believe him to be a bandit.\n\n I've come here to inform High Prince Native of the dangers at hand. He is quite kind, and more than\nwilling to assist me in finding the culprits. The Black Guard was started by Zevandir in hopes of converting the Pathfinders to bandits. This is why I saw Val the Pathfinder claiming himself a Black Guard.\n Val was supposedly tricked, and Atles has agreed to vouch for him that he has changed his ways. The Pathfinders are still, and always shall be loyal to the Prince and nation.\n\n Lord Atles serves\nin Lord Blackthorn's stead. Until his return. Lord Atles claims he found something far north of the boundaries of Oren. Some sort of dark village, with lava at the gates.\n\n But I do not know if I\nbelieve him. Pathfinder Kalen states that town is only the town of North Alister. Kalen reports seeing strange, dark beings walking about., with cloaks pulled about their faces. \n\nCould these have\nhave been members of the Dark Brotherhood Lafthi mentioned? Kalen is a bit hard to understand, but he claims a group of cloaked indivuals attacked Laurelin at some point.\n\nPresent here are\nSwift Elf Alenom, Pathfinder Kalen, and Lord Atles. I've run into many of the Princes of Laurelin at Ravenhold, and the High Guardian, Mayctor. He claims the Dark Brotherhood are no threat.\n Yet, he refuses to tell me how he knows of this fact, which I find very suspicious. \n\n Oh my.. the princes have trapped me in..\n\n  a box? \n         Hold on\n  Erghh..\n The Princess has freed me, luckily. Mayctor has informed me the Brotherhood seeks alliances with the \"do-gooder\" guilds. Could they be behind the Cripsons assault on a Holmes fellow?\n\nI'll talk to Lafthi..\n Mayctor is a worshipper of Iblees, this must be true. He cannot be allowed to get away with this. H\n\n He guarantees the safety of the elves, on Iblees name.\n\nTranscribed by Orias.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Secret Sea", "Adeline Sarkozic", "13th of Grand Harvest \nThe food and water are stale on this hell I've been stuck on. I want to curl up and rot, so many different dolts being stuck on the same ship as me and sailing off to a new land. My only home was attacked by worms.\nNow there is nothing left for me to turn to, I do not know where I'll live for now but surely I'll have something figured by time we land this ship. As soon as we started sailing, sea sickness soon ached my stomach as I spewed into my ferrum bucket.\nI've seen Victor, Carl and Lilya. But no Hugues, there is not much for me to worry about.. Surely he has hidden himself somewhere. He fornicated and I simply am not on the best terms with him. Word spread that the Duke of Barbanov had sacrificed himself.\nLucky for him he doesn't have to spend months on this hellhole, eating revolting hardtack and listening to the same old everyday. Either people are fighting or dying. Nobody is comfortable and those who are, must be peasants. I don't find it possible how\npeople can survive on a place like this. Constantly swaying back and fourth. Royce took me down to the lowest level of th ship where the rocking was less violent. We spoke in hushed voices. Thank goodness I have spearmint leaves with me at all times,\nall this vomitting is making my breath smell putrid. A horrible smell emitting from my mouth. I was not prepared for this sudden change, but I do carry spearmint leaves on me at all times just incase. I often find myself asking for food due to all of this\npuking I find myself starved. Though Liliane stopped by and gave me fresh water that was oddly stored in a glass to keep my hydrated. Thank goodness she had or I would've died, I cannot drink that filth of seawater they pass out. It's terribly salty.\n15th of Grand Harvest \nToday, these odd fish rode amongside our ship, they did not look harmful since others were going down and petting them. But I feel people took them as violent creatures, their fatalitic features thinking of the worst when they\nspotted the innocent things. People said that the fishies were sleek and scaley. I was too busy spewing into a ferrum bucket to catch sight of the seine. I wish I had though. Later on that day the sky had suddenly darkened, thunderclouds roared above as\nfigures that seemed to represent the wind and lightning stormed down to the deck. They danced around as people attacked the things. I was horrified as the ship viciously wobbled back and fourth. Many shouted and charged as I simply stayed curled up in the\ncorner of the quarters with people such as Lady Amélie, Lady Ceriwyn and many other aymasmen. The monsters shook the decks violently before they were slayed. A giant bolt of lightning blinded me for a moment at their defeation, it seems they moved on.\n16th of Grand Harvest \nI kept myself hidden in the corner of the quarters before asking Eric to comb through my hair. He kindly accepted, pulling out a brush of his own made out of horse hair, soon raking the combs out my hair. I felt engaging\nas he finished. He informed me that I looked beautiful with my hair now fully tamed. Not long after that an alluring voice of a woman called out to us, she was whispering for us to come into the sea with her. I stared out the window longingly as she\npromised a better life for me. I went to find her as it was very tempting to not resist. Though Eric advised I should stay inside and not go out there. He may be younger but he carries alot of wisdom which I enjoy. We chatted amongst ourselves inside\nbefore everybody was summoned outside by The High Pontiff. It was time for mass, even though it was on a ship I still carried my Lorraine Cross around the ferrum chain on my neck. I clutched in my hand as she spoke out loud while we bowed our heads and\nprayed. I prayed for no seademons, family and food. As I longed to be a chef. I want to fend for myself though I know I'll have maids of my own after marrying into a good noble home. I listened with intent as The High Pontiff spoke for \"Bountiful lands\nand for us to live in his name. To travel t the darkness in the light and to reach the paradise.\" I tightly grasped onto my Lorraine Cross that was strapped onto a ferrum cord with a clasp in the back. Not soon after mass that woman called out to me, I\ndived in head first as Eric was not around to stop me. Her enchanting voice had summoned me into the waters below. I swam away franticly. The bête noire pointed her claws at me and growled as she charged into my direction. I howled for aide or assistance\nas she came at me. A few men dropped into the waters to assist me! The knave retreated into deep deapths of the ocean before emerging and leaving three deep gashes down my leg. A rope was then dropped down, pulling me up and onto shore as I was utterly\ngrateful. Some kind woman by the name of Ryder then healed my wounds, I squeezed my eyelids shut tight as she used her magic to sew my skin shut, leaving only the smallest scars in their place. I spent the rest of the night in the quarters, going to rest.\n&2I'm no longer capable of keeping updated with this journal, there are too many things going on. The sea holds many secret.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sewer", "Arthur Caulfield", "The Sewer\n           By\n         Arthur\n        Caulfield\nIt is the sewer, in which I live. A rank and stinking tunnel of which no man would ever set foot. I am alone down here, sitting quietly, waiting. The darkness creates shadows of harrowing ghouls. Even I find myself jumping at each echoed sound.\nThis is why I am paranoid. No sound is ever pure. In a world of tunnels and halls every sound is one that has been bounced around and repeated over and over, so that by the time it reaches your own ears, you may never know where it originated.\nBut of course, the question you ask. Why would such a feared creature such as me, be afraid of boogie men in the dark? I tell you now, in the sewers I am not to be feared.\nFor if you have ever ventured into a sewer at what would be the lowest point in your life, you will know that what lay down there would destroy the minds of high elves and orcs alike.\nNothing stops them from venturing to the surface, they could invade cities, burn down petrus with their horrid image. The eyes of citizens would melt, leaving only liquid to run down their cheeks.\nOf course, I get ahead of myself, for if you are reading you have not been down here. To a place of O such abandoned horror, not too mention the distaste of all who are civilized. Which is why I would like to describe for you,\nthe image of such creatures scarier than me. \n   Bright yellow spots on their backs, painful and sore. Balding heads, with fragments of fragile hair left and unkept.\n  Spines so bent they can not walk without pain.\nFeet featuring sharp toe nails that could cut a nobleman's sword. Noses that smell and pick out their prey. Skin as pink as a rich woman’s nails but as soft as fresh dough in your hands. \n  This is what I face every day.\nThough down here there is no day or night, only darkness all of the time. I feel myself going crazy, I don’t understand it. I have over a dozen eyes but am subject to the worst view and the most terrifying life.\nYou shouldn’t try to save me. I would hurt you. My fangs, over three inches long equipped with venom, would paralyse you before I even realised what I had done.\n   It’s not your fault. And it’s not mine.\nI can’t run the risk of greeting something that could be my doom. I’ve seen plenty of my own kind decapitated, ripped apart and eaten. I don’t want to hurt you, but I don’t want to die. \n  This is why I choose to stay in my tunnel.\nIt is mine. Scattered with web, damp and dark. Far enough away from any nest of the abominations. Close enough to the entrance that I can hear the world. \n  I can’t leave of course. No one down here has ever done that.\nGoing out there would scare the civilized. And scaring the civilized means being taken down by a mob of weapons. So I sit down here, content with just listening. \n  Every now and then I will here parts of conversation.\nSomeone bought a stale loaf of bread, another is excited about a wedding. I do not understand the context of what they say, but I revel in the idea of having a conversation with another being.\nI am apart of an aggressive species. Dominance is the only way to live life. It is my duty, nay, my instinct to destroy every other of my kind. I do not want to, I must.\nI enjoy the rain. It is supposedly cleaner than the water down here. It does not have the musky odour or the putrid colour. \n  The sound is hypnotic, listening to each drop hit the earth above calms me, it lets me ignore every other sound.\nIt let’s me remove my guard for just a day, before I am aware of the dangers once more. \n  Somedays, when all is quiet. And only the ripples in the dirty water move.\n  I stare at the tunnel walls.\nI wonder how long ago it must have been, when humans built it. How long ago it must have been since they were last down here.\n   The walls have begun to deteriorate, sometimes I hope it will crumble,\nand I will be sealed into this tomb worthy only of my presence.  Even with eight legs I could not escape that fate. \n   But my kind is supposed to act on instinct, and so I do.\nSo I do not look for a way to better my existence, I simply live out what has been given to me. I do not try to escape.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shun", "Tristanm1", "The Shun\nInscribed by Dawn Druid Maiavel\nThe Great Druid can impose a strong, nonviolent sanction upon those who have offended the circle. All must shun someone placed under the shun; no druid in the circle will aid, speak to, or associate with the target of the shun. When an entire town or\nvillage suffers the shun, no druid may enter that area or speak to or aid any resident. Some druidic allies volunteer to follow the custom of the shun as well.\nThe great druid has the right to pronounce a shun on any druid in the circle.  A shun also can\nnondruids, whole communities, or druids visiting from other domains (except the Grand Druid and personal servants), to demonstrate the circle's displeasure. \nTo pronounce the shun, the great druid stands up during a moot and  announces to the group the\nreasons to impose the shun. Then the subject of the shun--if present--answers the accusations before the assembly. Finally, the High Council of the Moot votes on the matter openly, usually at sunset. If a majority of the council votes in favor of the shun\n, it passes. If not, the great druid should start keeping an eye on the circle's archdruids--the opposition to the shun likely reflects an impending challenge. \nA shun punishes a druid for violating the tenets of the druidic order or reprimands a\ncharacter whose actions, while within the bounds of the druidic ethos, nevertheless were contrary to the Order's interests. A shun generally lasts 10 summers. However, the inner circle can vote to lift a shun early or (once the time is up) to extend it.\nThe shunning does not extend outside the domain, so shunned druids usually choose to go into exile--the result the great druid probably intended in the first place.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spear", "The Forgotten Scribe", "\"Brev was the first man ever to strike down an Aengul, and when it’s patron of Age screamed from the heavens, ‘what have you done’, Brev could not hide his discrepancy, for the proof of the Aengul of Youth’s death blazed bright from the height of the\nsky.”\n~-~\nThe legend of Godslayer Brev is one not often noticed amongst the archives of the Temple Monks, whom covet the knowledge of the known planes upon their sandstone shelves. It is a tale of regret, of fury\nand sadness, and within it’s weathered text lies a lesson for both man and goldblooded -- to never pass the boundaries that the Creator set for them.\nBut the legend it not mere falsehoods; it is truth, bound upon layers and\nleather and scribed from men of ancient origin; from the time when holy fire raged in the sky, and from the time the same fire scorched Krug’s pure kin to the bone. The time of such event dates back even before the known times of Iblees’\nwarmongering, when the four races established themselves in their four corners uncorrupted but sparse. They prospered and they settled brief peace; it was a time known not for wars, but for curiosity and expansion, and\nknowing that their four fathers already took claim to the whole of the Aegisian plane, they sought what was beyond it -- what they could reach, but could not grasp. The sky.\nTheir attempts at claiming the heavens often fell to dust; enacted by\nover-ambitious humans and haughty Elves with towers that either did not reach high enough or simply toppled because of their reach. Ironically, it was not the mortals that reached the immortals first, but the otherway around; for the\nraces held no means of reaching their godly masters whereas the masters could reach them -- and reach them they did, in those old times, when all were naive and thought nothing of conceit and budding violence.\nAll mortal men were jealous of the\nbirds of the sky, whom could sail the wind and reach the borders of the heavens with but draws of their wings, and the shadow these creatures cast were like salt upon the wounds that were carved into the early history of red-blooded\nfailures. Shadows were a sign of irritation, and the sun’s rays were favored over the darkness of physical mass-- thus, understandable emotions derived from these mocking shadows. Human men spat upon the shade of flighted\ncreatures, Elves scoffed at them and Dwarves grumbled and retreated into their mines, seeking comfort amongst earth’s treasures. The Old Orcs, smooth of skin and monstrous naught, however, saw the shadows of winged beasts as\nchallenges and insults, and sought to snuff them from the sky in which they were projected. One such example would be of the Legend of Brev, whom mistook an Aengul for a bird in the face of the glaring sun.\nWandering the planes of Krug’s\nbirthplace, the descendant Brev, who was famed for his great strength and fortitude, was in the process of a grand hunt with the intent to return to Krug’s children with enough game to feed them all for weeks -- a feat that would surely be remembered\neven when worn from the passage of time. However, prey was sparse, and Brev’s effort in the chase was languish in the face of demanded speed. What he had caught was drawn from his impressive ability to throw spears of iron that cut through the\nair like a giant’s arrows.\nThe sun’s smile was bright and it’s rays were harsh on this day of the hunt, and it was only into the late afternoon that the towering, tan-skinned son of Krug found himself at a loss; unwilling to trek further into the\nexpanse of his homeland in search of prey that refused to challenge him. But lo’ and behold -- a great shadow was cast upon the earth from a creature of mighty size, far larger than a bird, that circled Brev upon the waves of the sky. Staggered by\nhis findings, Brev drew his eyes to the sky -- and beheld but silhouette of an assumed bird of great size alone; unable to make shape of it’s features on behalf of the sun’s blinding light. Knowing his spears were not enough to fell this creature, Brev\nsought a nearby mountainous range, and from the side of the mountain he grafted a massive spear of sturdy stone; unable to be hefted by none but himself and his kin in the manner which he planned for it.\nSo he returned to the circling\ncreature, which was unbeknownst to his plots, and with squinting aim and the tense of muscles, he flung the great spear forth -- into the sky and into the heavens which the beast lingered; an arrow, a lightning bolt of earth that shot from the\nground instead of the clouds, and in a spectacle and show of godly skill, the spear impaled the creature; but it did not draw blood.\nCuriousity was a scourge to those of heavenly blood -- it was a sign of degeneracy and ignorance, for all\nAenguls and Daemons knew most of the inner-workings of the world thus far - with the exception of their own experiences - and the trivialities of exploration and - Creator forbid it - the interaction of the mortal and the immortal. But some\ndisregarded this ideal of isolation and sought to bless the four races with their presence. One such individual was the unnamed Aengul of Youth, whom favored sailing the vast skies of Aegis, much to his patron’s displeasure and concern -- the Aengul of\nAge, whose name is also unknown.\nThe Aengul of Youth was naive and sought to explore all there was to see, and his journey led him to Krug’s birthplace, whence Brev roamed in feverous hunt. But his search for glorious knowledge led to Brev’s\ninescapable fury; a decimation carved from the very earth. Flighted in the sky with wings not unlike a hawk’s the Aengul of Youth bathed in the gross incandescence of sunlight-- blind to the one that mistakenly targeted him. In one fatal\nswoop, however, the Aengul’s heavenly being was collided against and impaled with Brev’s Stone Spear; and the event of the Aengul’s violent death was so great, that gold blood was not drawn, but fire -- the spear scorched by golden flame, plummeting\ndownward, as the very sky ignited in destructive reaction to the Aengul of Youth’s cataclysmic demise.\nThe seven heavens felt this death, this disparity -- and it’s Aengul of Age, who fathered the Aengul of Youth since it’s creation, cried\nout in horror; he cried out and his voice was so furious and abask in agony that it cracked through the sky and shook it’s very foundations -- “What have you done?!”\nAnd Brev, who stood awed and horrified by his own mistake, his worst sin, could\nnot move from the place that he threw the spear which lingered steps from him, buried point-first in the sand - he could not close his eyes despite the bright volumes of the plummeting golden fire. Without even the notion to raise his\narms to protect himself from the charging storm, Brev the Strong was engulfed in the fire of heavenly demise; roasted to the bone and decimated by it’s otherworldly power almost immediately.\nThe Monks of the Old Cloud Temple were the first to take\nnotice to this tragedy, and with hurried pace they sought the scene now riddled with ash and golden fire that still cracked and burned upon the ground; the black scorch-marks focused upon the still-standing skeleton of Brev and his spear - coined\nthe Stone Transgression - to form a most unusual display. The kin of God expressed his horror and his dejection from the skies, and thus, these old Monks sought to honor him by damning Brev’s soul to a limbo, and his spear to a grave.\nSealing his soul to a single large rib, Brev’s skeleton was buried with his godslaying spear within the depths of Krug’s homeland with his soul, trapped within the severed, surprisingly heavy bone locked within a jailed chamber of steel and earth;\ndamning Brev’s soul to a fate of ungained peace, trapped in a limbo and locked within but a peace of his own scorched structure.\n~-~", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spirit of Ma", "Mysterious Oldman", "*Strange Runes seem to Dot the\nFirst section of this page*\n\nFrom death, life.\n\nFrom dDarkness Light. \nWhen all seems hopeless.\n\nand the realm stands on the brink of destruction.\n\nOne final sacrifice shall be made. \nFor the good of the realm.\n\"An excerpt of the Tome of Blundermore. The Second Wizard Of Aegis\". \n\nMagic, according to the mages is merely a tool to be used to further one's own goals and drives. There are no true moral or immoral implications of magic. Only Magic itself. \nThis is not truly the case. For we know that magic does indeed have a light and dark side, however small or large it may be. \n\nMagic is driven by impulse and imagination. By the will and tenacity of the user but it is not the will of Mages alone whom-\ndefine what magic is alone. No, for the world itself is indeed magic. Everything and everyone within it is a magical entity of some description from the most insignificant to the mighty. \n\nI subscribe to the idea that magic is a force that connects all.\nIt is emotion, it is sanity, it is insanity, it's spirituality, it's the notion of thought and imagination and perhaps life itself. \n\nTo call it a mere tool is to insult its true nature. And to pervert it with such notions that you truly understand and\ncontrol it to its fullest extent is merely being foolish. Magic is a force to be respected and revered, not as a power or force of destruction. But as a companion almost. It is with you where ever you truly go. And should be treated with respect.\n\nA means perhaps of attaining a greater enlightenment of the world that exists around you.\n\nIt is the will of evil men that twists magic towards evil ends. But unfortunately for all of their lust and drive for power they will forget that the secrets of\nmagic will never truly be revealed to them through such disrespect. \n\nI've seen the extent magic can provide, and it reaches far beyond our petty notions of power.\n\nWe must- adfafmkfa\n*The page seems to end with magical symbols once more, their meaning unknown before a large tear.*", ""),
        StaticBook("The tail of Bell", "Beltran", "Come hither and hear my tale, of how my status in life how somehow becometh reversed, grant me one moment with forsooth's ear, and allow me to regale you with my taleth of nobility in the humble parish of Caliphate.\nIn the rolling lily fields of Pennsylvania I sprang forth from the womb\nMy days filled with the innocent pursuits of boyhood\nRetreating from the hot sting of the sun’s rays I frolicked in the most carefree way.\nSport shooting pheasants with my dear kin folk. When a band of miscreants, true rapscallions who's hearts contain no morsel of goodness.\nEnacted wrongful tribulation upon thy peacful shire. I engorged in a bout of fisticuffs of no true magnitude, mymothe-\nr,.. trembling with fear. 'Off with you!' she cried to the esteemed estate of your mon uncle. Philip Banks esquire.\n\nWith a whistle I hailed a carriage and secured passage to aforementioned estate\nInscribed on the carriage were the letters F-R-E-S-H and the driver carried on his person a six sided trinket of vice\nLet it be noted this chaise was truly without equal\n\nHowever I paid it no mind and ordered that we depart post haste\nI promptly arrived on the grounds at a juncture around seven in the evening\nAnd I called to the quartermaster “Release me from thy fowl stench, you are utterly macabre.”\n\nI gazed upon my royal grounds, I journey no longer.\nTo sit on my throne as the Prince of Bel-air.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Three Poems", "Fabien Eloy de Bosco", "The Women in the Shop\n\n There once was a women\nA women in a shop\nShe smelled of a lemon\nShe sat on the rooftop\nHer hair flowing\nStaring down the coast\nRelaxed and outgoing\nnext to a lamppost.\nThe Man in the Manor\n\nThere was a man\nHe lived in a manor\nAll alone he ran\nTo the Felsen Banner\nHe met a girl named, Theran\nHe spoke with much manner\nDidn't know how to stand\n'Cause he was nervous and tanner.\nThe lonely Farm\n\nThere was a Farm in Norland\nThere it sat, out-of-hand\nToo far away from everyone\nLaying there out in the sun\nThe farm had much crop\nAll sent into one shop\nA farmer once came\nAnd the farm gained fame.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Three States", "Faieya Vallei'onn", "Properties of Water, by Faieya Vallei'onn.\n\nThis book is based on the physical and non-physical properties of water in its three states; Solid, liquid and gas.\nIce.\n\nEssentially, ice is the solidified form of water. Due to freezing, it is turned into a solid material. Ice is extremely cold to the touch, and is rather like glass in the manner of breaking.\nLakes can often freeze over, which means that the top layer of the water got too cold and froze. This creates a thin layer of ice, though it looks steady enough, it isn't suggested to walk on it. Ice is extremely brittle in that sense.\nIf small amounts of water are frozen, they will become solid in the same shape they were in when liquid. If the same temperature was put on a living being for a while, they would die.\nWater.\n\nAs explained in the previous book, water is an extremely powerful force of nature, being able to destroy rock if given the time.\nIt is one of the four elements, alongside earth, air and fire. I have recently had an experience with water that leads me to believe that it is more powerful than it may seem. A wave of water can be like a wall to those who fight against it, dragging any-\n- of those unfortunate enough to be caught in it, down. Water, how ever, can be a good thing. With out water, all living things would dehydrate and die. It also provides habitats for sea creatures, such as fish and frogs.\nWater is also the basis of any potion, medical or poisonous. I fear that I have focused too much on the bad parts on water, and not enough on the part that keeps us alive. A lack of water can kill in just four to five days, on average.\nSteam.\n\nBy definition, steam is what water is converted to when heated, forming a mist of water droplets in the air. Steam is given off by hot things containing water, such as a mug of tea, or a pot of vegetables in boiling water.\nIt is created when water becomes too hot to remain a liquid, and plays a large part in the cycle of rain. It can be turned back into water extremely easily, by simply cooling down again. If steam were to come into contact with a room temperature item, -\n-such as a sword, or a metallic object that was not heated, it would condense back into water. \n\n~ F.V.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tiny Hippo", "Elluna Koortova", "The Tiny Hippo\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n   By Gaelyn Sarino\n\n         ©1454\nThere once was a tiny hippo, in a tiny world, in a tiny universe.\n\nHis name was Tiny Hippo.\n\nTiny Hippo had a tiny cart.\n\nHe loved that cart, and they went everywhere together.\nLaughing and playing all throughout their tiny world. \n\nThen one day, Tiny Raven swooped down and stole the tiny cart.\n\nThis made Tiny Hippo very sad, but he decided he would be brave\nSo the next day, he walked up the tiny mountain…\n\n...Crossed through the tiny Valley….\n\n…..Climbed up the tiny oak tree….\n\nAnd shanked Tiny Raven’s tiny bitch ass.\nAin’t no one fucks with Tiny Hippo.\nAin’t no one.\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tree", "Henry Winterleaf", "The Tree\n--------\n\nA children's book by Henry Winterleaf.\nMany years ago, there was a little acorn. The acorn was so tired with being small.\n\"I want to be tall!\" the acorn would say.\n\"Everyone else looks so big!\" he would moan. He would always moan until one day, a large oak tree said to him:\n\"Just sit still for a bit and have a bit of patience.\"\nAnd so, the acorn waited. Never moving.\nNever moaning. He just sat there, waiting for this magical growth that was promised to him. Days passed and the acorn still didn't feel any taller.\n\"I'm just a small as before!\" Moaned the acorn.\n\"Oh, really?\" said the oak tree, smiling.\n\"Yes! I'm just the same!\" proclaimed the acorn once more.\n\"Perhaps you should wait longer then.\" \nAnd so he did. Waiting once more.\nA couple days later, the acorn awoke in his usual spot. \n\"Huh? What's this?\" asked the acorn.\n\"I feel different.\"\n\"An acorn does not grow into a tree over-night, child.\" said the oak tree, chuckling.\n\"But with enough patience, you will\ngrow to an incredible size. Good things come to those who wait. Just be patience.\"\nThe acorn was more determined than ever.\n\"I can be patient! I'm going to be the tallest!\"\nAnd so he waited some more. Days, months, even years passed and\nsoon the acorn had grown into a large oak tree, towering over many others. One day he would hear a sapling below him complaining:\n\"I wish I was as tall as you!\"\nThe little acorn, who was not so little any more, just smiled and said\n\"Be patient. That is all you can do.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Trib. of War", "Andria Ith'ael", "The Tribulation of War\n\n      Authored by\n     Andria Ith'ael\n\n      Dedicated to\n      Luna Ith'ael\n  Who did not live to\n  see the end of this\n       tribulation.\nPrologue\n This account tells the tale of the two major events which occurred within the time of author’s service as the Maheral of the Mali’aheral. Such events were known as the following: the securing of the Aldersberg Refuge and the Oren\nCivil War which granted independence to Renatus (and Aesterwald.) It is not just for the sake of recording that the author writes such, as it is hoped that this account will prevent further incidents from occurring again.\nChapter I\n  The betrayal of the Mali’aheral by the Mali’ame, more specifically: Phaedrus and Elrona Lle’hileia, was the final event of the steadily growing discontent of the lesser Elves in Annil’sul. All but one of the nations in the world\nsupported Phaedrus Lle'hielia - the rebelion leader. \n\n  It was on the mountains aside of the town of Aldersberg where a meeting that conceived the plans for shelter in such a dreadful time took place. It consisted of approximately five\nMali'aheral - alongside a Valah by the name of Ser Gawain Briarwood. One Mali’aheral by the name of Thurdan Orathon, who had served previously as Okarir’tir, and his persistence in such was both amusing and counter-productive. \n\n  In the next Elven\nday, I found myself alongside the same Mali'aheral in the court of Emperor Tuvya Carrion. Knowing of Thurdan’s plans, I tried to convince him via a polite and quiet conversation hat we should ask for shelter in these dark days. My offer was refused quite\nobstinately by the former Okarir'tir, who foolishly went ahead and asked the Emperor regarding his own plan. \n Alas, Thurdan’s efforts were in vain; the Emperor rejected his offer, citing prior crimes against House Carrion by the Mali’aheral,\nwhich essentially was the Mali’aheral support for the Chivay take over in the Fringe. Disappointed, Thurdan stormed from the palace without another word, which was a rather a rude gesture.\n Due to this, I stepped forward, and proceeded to ask for what I\nbelieved was ayla for the Mali'aheral: a refuge. The response I received was much better than those earlier, and the Emperor Tuvya offered us shelter in Petrus and the option to ask Duke Olivier de Savoie of the town of Aldersberg. However, I do not\nrecall if such an offer was made by the town of Karovia. \n It was a half or day or so walk from Petrus to Aldersberg, and there I met with Delonna Aeléyèlsa. He directed me to the Duke Olivier de Savoie and the three of us proceeded to have a meeting in\nthe Aldersberg Library. There I offered assistance in war (I had previously said that I would die for Oren in war if it meant my people were well) and many crafts and labours. In exchange I asked for a citadel. In response, I received a chuckle as he saw\nmy desperation and proclaimed that those terms were acceptable.\n Foolishly I told him we would not live within Aldersberg and said we would remain on his land, to which he questioned my knowledge of the feudal system, however this comment had no lasting\neffects and work soon began once more. The Citadel was soon constructed at a pace not seen before.  For my efforts, Delonna Aeléyèlsa bestowed the title of Maheral upon me. Despite our kind’s new found peace, one event would linger in my mind for many\nyears to come. My spouse, Janos Ith’ael soon arrived in Aldersberg and came to speak with me. He displayed his intentions to join the Marked Men, to which I refused on the grounds of him already having a child and a wife. Reluctantly he agreed and I soon\ntold him to ask the leaders of the Marked Men about it. However I heard no word from Janos again until long after the events of this book, I had almost thought he died up until very recently.\nChapter II\n In the year of 1480, my daughter, Luna Ith’ael went to live a few miles walk from Aldersberg in the fortress of Kaer Angren with a family friend of mine, Kalameet Izalith. The fortress was used by the Order of the Red Dragon,\nand before them, the Order of the Flaming Rose. I had overheard her talking with one by the name of Martial Solatius about the book of Creation and when I arrived in the fortress, I spoke to her regarding such. I warned her of the dangers of believing in\na deity and how it prevents enlightenment. She protested though soon listened to my guidance. I did not speak with Martial regarding such (though I did with Kalameet) as he gave me a tour of the fortress.\nI also gave him advice on leadership, and he told me about how Great Ser Maric Varodyr (the commander of the Order) would later receive what he deserved. I took little note of such a hint. \n Alas, it all soon became clear within the next month as the\nOrder of the Red Dragon soon declared itself independent of the Carrion dominated Holy Oren Empire. It became my objective to try and remove my daughter from the fortress as Aldersberg took no side in the conflict. My efforts proved useless as I came\nacross the broken bridge which lead to the gate of Kaer Angren.\n\n    Chapter III\n As the nations were choosing their sides; it soon became known that I would have to choose one as well. The State of Laureh'lin changed sides thrice\nthroughout the war, though as I went to a meeting with the now King Maric Varodyr, they were with Renatus and Kaer Angren. Delonna Aeléyèlsa accompanied myself, for he was more literate in ways of Valah politics.\n The meeting was a sucess and the two\nof us pledged to support him; an exception remained with the bringing of soldiers, we did not do such due to the neutrality of Aldersberg.\n King Maric also promised to sign another concordat, however with a different name, for\nthe Crimson-Silver Concordat has long passed.\n Raids and skirmishes soon were fought outside Kaer Angren, and I was caught in at least one. I remember seeing one of my own kind, named Braxus Ni’leya fight with the Carrions; I was rather disappointed in\nand proceeded to speak with the Tilruir’tir, Asul’athri Parir’taliyu regarding such. From then on the war seemed to be closer to home.\n  House Carrion and its supporters then moved forth from Petrus to try and take Kaer Angren by force. As the day of the\nbattle approached, I was steadfast that none of my kin would fight in such a battle. This was to the dismay of two of my kind: Kalameet Izalith, who worked closely with Maric and Martial during the war, and Braxus Ne’leya, who asked for soldiers to\nreinforce the House Carrion supporters. I also told my daughter to not remain in the fortress, and return to the Citadel.\n  Braxus then told me that House Carrion wished to speak with me and I agreed to come to such. I left a note in my inn room which\nstated that if I did not return from such an endeavour, I had been executed by the Carrions and the Sillumir were to fight with Renatus and their allies. Hence forth I made the trek to Petrus, and met with Braxus and Viktor Carrion. The lattter guided me\ninto the palace in Petrus, where the two of us held a meeting.\n  Viktor tried to convince me that the Carrions had done ayla by my people, and to such I agreed. Though I adamantly said that I would remain neutral - which deceived them of my true plans.\nThe one clad in Carbarum and Iron armour was also steadfast that Olivier de Savoie had supported the Carrion regime, which was rather untrue.\nChapter IV\n The battle ended with a victory for King Maric and it soon resulted in the collapse of the the Holy Oren Empire. No Sillumrian fought in the battle from my memory,  though in hindsight, such would have been better to have supported\nRenatus. However an opportunity to make a formal alliance with the new born nation was soon permitted after a lengthy discussion between Olivier de Savoie, Kalameet Izalith, Kalenz Uradir and myself. \n   Coincidently, Gawain Briarwood (whose alias was\nMartial Solatius) soon arrived at the gate of the Citadel asking if we wished to ally with them. Without hesitation I agreed, though no Concordat was signed. I consider such to be my greatest decision in my service as Maheral.\n Months later, after peace\nhad once again befallen the lands of a now divided Oren, I made another trek to the fortress of Kaer Angren with one by the name of Avern’dionne Adriane. The beginnings of the conquest of Laureh’lin soon approached. The tribulation of the Mali'aheral was\ndestined to end soon.\n\n     Chapter V\n It is known that a story has no merit without a moral; however, there is not one of such in this story, for there is multiple concepts presented in it.  It can simply be described as the following: the one\nwho takes initiative is the one who succeeds; progress and health can also involve sacrificing one’s plans for the betterment of our kind; and two societies cannot exist with one ruling the other, they must be equal or integrated - both of which are\nimpossible. \n If one remembers such, then they will be able to prosper in an age of constant war unlike any other. The world is far more turbulent, and alliances change fast. No treaty stands forever and our kind must be weary of such for only two peoples\nhave kept their treaties like tradition: the Heartlander Valah and the Kharajyr. At any moment, another tribulation may begin and our kind must be weary.\n\naymaehr'sae hiylun'ehya\n~Andria Ith'ael", ""),
        StaticBook("The Vander Code", "Lexa", "=-=+=-=+=-=+=-=+=-=\n\n   The  Vander  Code\n   =-=+=-=+=-=+=-=+=-=\n\nAn excerpt taken from:\n The Vander Ideology\n\n Written by:  Nafis, Vandalore I Antiquus\n\n          =-=+=-=\n  We as Vanders will come to know this code by heart of course, but for the time being this book will help you remember everything there is to be known about the Vander Code.\n         =-=+=-=\n=-=+=-=\n  -The Vander Code is held with the utmost importance among us as Vanders.Not only does it offer stability, it is a goal for the individual to strive towards in hopes of becoming a better person in a world that is cruel and corrupt.\nTo both accept the state of the realm and still strive to thrive in what many would find uninhabitable.\n          =-=+=-=\n\n “The weak deserve to die so that the strong may flourish.”\n~ Nafis, Vandalore I Antiquus\n-=The Vander Code=-\n          =-=+=-=\n“To serve the Vandalore in valour and faith”\n“To refrain from the wanton giving of offence”\n“To live by honour and for glory”\n“To obey those placed in authority”\n“To guard the honour of fellow Vanders”\n“To at all times to speak the truth”\n“To persevere to the end in any enterprise begun”\n“To never to refuse a challenge from an equal”\n“To never to turn the back upon a foe”", ""),
        StaticBook("The Visitor", "F.V.", "Author's note. If you've yet to read 'The Cabin', I would suggest doing so before you read this book since this is the second part of the previously mentioned book.\nThuds echo throughout the small room, loud as thunder. The woman awakes with a start, her eyes wide and her breathing heavy as she stares fearfully at the door of the cabin. She'd scramble up from where she slept on the damp wood floor, her hands -\n- shaking as she hurriedly pats herself down. The thundering sound would eventually come to a stop, only a few of the loud footsteps now audible as the woman grabs a slip of paper from the inside of her torn silk sleeve and throws it into the dying -\n- fire. With that, she turns to face the door, gripping her rocking chair to remain upright, her head spinning from dehydration. Suddenly, the door bursts open, a loud screech given off as the hinges struggle to hold onto the door. Dust flies up into -\n- the air at the sudden disturbance, causing the woman to cover her mouth to muffle her weak coughs. With this, a large figure walks through the door, a well worn sword in their right hand. For the woman, the world seemed to freeze in place as she -\n- stares at the figure. The armour clad figure would look to be in the same boat, not moving an inch. From behind the armoured figure, a squeaky voice would call out a few words, his tone somewhat desperate. \"Is she in there? Leader?\" The armoured -\n- figure gives the man behind them a dismissive gesture, their heavy armour creaking as they step towards the woman. The woman lets out a shaky breath, seemingly composing herself as she also steps forwards. The two would meet in the centre of the room, -\n- seemingly not caring about their surroundings. The armoured figure would finally pull off their helmet, dropping it to the floor with a gleeful expression written on their face. Relief would flood the woman's features as she takes in the face of the -\n- knight. \"Mira..\" The woman would mutter, her voice cracking from weariness. She'd stumble forwards, too weak to hold herself up. The knight would catch her carefully, a worried expression covering her features. \"My lady, we need to get you back to the -\n- city.\" Mira's voice would be rather kind, though it would have a fearful undertone. The weakened woman would stumble away, sadness now covering her face. \"No.\" She'd state simply, slightly stronger than before. \"My son.. He is..\" The woman would let -\n- out a shaky sigh, turning away from the armoured knight. \"My son is dead.. Why would I ever go back?\" Her voice would shake as she says this, tears beginning to form in her eyes. \nThe knight's voice would be full of desperation as she speaks. -\n- \"Please my lady! You must come-\" She'd be cut off by the woman's cry of rage, and the knight's stance would be somewhat tense as the woman speaks. \"No! I can't go back, I won't!\" The woman would turn back to face the knight, stumbling in her place as -\n- she struggles to stand. The knight would rush to catch her, but it would be too late as the woman falls to the floor, the skirts of her silk dress falling about her elegantly. \"I can't go back..\" The woman would mutter weakly, before she faints, the -\n- world around her turning dark.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Void", "Nienna Calm", "The Void\nBy Nienna Calm\n\nForword:\n\n§YYou see, I’ve actually had the pleasure of gazing into the void myself back in Anthos, at the very bottom of the Hallows: a void node the mages guild had gone\nand destroyed by accident, or on purpose. Still not sure which. It is indeed endless, and the pathway to the hole defied all common logic. Frogs swam in the air, stairways upwards led downwards,\nbooks existed in languages that did not exist, from times that have yet come to pass. But I digress\n\n-Nienna Calm\nNow, this world is quite vast, to be sure. But it has its boundaries. It’s upper limits. Beyond that, is the void. A plane of existence unto itself, spanning into infinity forever. The Void gets its name because it contains nothing.\nThe nothingness nothing to ever exist, leading into a pitch black world of nothing in all directions. However, this plot-hole level amount of nothing has a very paradoxical element to it. It has the potential to become literally anything.\nA phrase you are going to hear me say often is this: “The Void is nothing, with the potential to become anything.” It’s the fundamental phrase you need to remember when considering the void itself. Now, one may ask, “How do we know for sure?”.\nNow, all mortals contain within them a small tear that leads into the void. To the best of my knowledge, this tear is a scar that was created when iblees was thrown from our world, through the void, and into the nether.\nIt’s not a… physical scar, but an ephemeral one. It’s contained within our very souls. Without it, all void magic would be impossible. But, of course this prompts the question. If we have a hole in our souls that leads to the void,\nHow do we make use of it? Through trial and error, the mages of old found that they could connect to the void, by attuning their minds to it. The mind is an organ of great potential. With it, the mortal races have accomplished great feats.\nAnd by using that mind to focus on nothing, and perhaps nothingness itself, we are able to finally connect to the void. Now, connecting to the void, is merely the first step in becoming a mage, and it is likely one of the most painful.\nYou see, when a mage connects to the void, the void will instantly begin draining your mana-An aspect of ourselves that we would die without.-All at once. For untrained mages, this would happen in but mere moment,\nand feels quite like having your soul sucked through a straw, ten times in an instant. Usually it results in them passing out, occasionally vomiting from sheer surprise, and waking up with the mother of all hangovers.\nAnnnnnd this will likely happen to you at least a hundred times. Before I’d even go into how to cast magic, I’d have you practice connecting, and learning to resist the pull of the void upon your mana.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Void", "Laureh'thill", "The Void\n\nBy Kalameet Izalith\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-\n-The Void: Arcane magic is the archetype or magic which is fueled by the Void, or more specifically mana. The void is an empty plane of existence where things may be created with the use of ones\nimagination and willpower. Many teachers of the Arcane often teach students with the following proverb: \"The Void is nothing, yet everything. Like our imagination, it may be dull and empty; or it can be full and colorful.\". The Void as a whole is simply a\nplane where nothing exists, unless the mage makes it exist.\n\n-The Anchor and Connection: Before you can make anything in the Void, you must first connect to it. This obviously means a basic line of communication must be established, generally gained\nthrough meditation and practice. This connection reaches into the Void and through this connection, you manipulate the Void in a very specific way. This manipulation is when you imagine something in the Void. For example, one may create/imagine a fireball\nin the Void, you'd then attempt to pull this fireball from the void into the real world. When you pull on this fireball you are inherently using mana from your own mana pool, and you create something called an Anchor. This mana anchor is what holds your\nspell, or fireball in this case, in the real world.\n\n-Mana: Mana is sightless and is as invisible as the air in our world. It flows through our world like streams, and is in every living thing, whether it is plants or animals. Although mana comes at a\ncost, since it flows through people, Void users have gained the ability to use this mana to draw from the Void. Void users often get fatigued when over using mana, and have in rare cases died to the use of large amounts of mana.\n\nAnother drawback with the\nuse of mana is the effect (or lack thereof) on our mortal plane, when you draw on the Void for magicks such as Evocations, this element which has been evoked must eventually return to the Void. However this can become complicated with such magicks as\nAlteration, as it has the ability to prolong the existence of Void based elements in our world. Mana comes in three states; passive, active/used, and aura.\n\n-States of Mana:\n*The first is a state of passive mana. This is the mana which is already stored\nwithin all beings and plants alike. It cannot be manipulated by anyone aside from its owner.\n\n*The second is a state of active/used mana. This mana has been given a purpose (a spell), or has been stored inside a mana gem, and thus cannot be used like\npassive mana ever again. This is exactly why the famous \"Mana Bettery\" is impossible, and cannot be done. Once mana has been expelled from ones being forcefully, it cannot be regained. But it can be redirected, this is known by any competent Alterationist\n*The third and final is the well known state of aura. An aura directly reflects a mages personality through its color, which will be listed below this section. Auras are generally harmless and are simply a way of self expression. Aura is indeed harmless,\nand is expelled naturally by a mage, and all living things to some degree, but more so by those who are using their mana. The more mana you use to cast a spell, the more aura which is expelled from the user (Very much like a fire. The more wood you burn,\nthe bigger the smoke cloud is). There are only two beings which are capable of using aura, the first being an Arcane Evocationist to some degree, and a Shade. Although a shade literally consumes aura, in which case can become very dangerous when one uses\na large portion of their mana whilst combating such a creature.\n\n-Aura Colors:\nBlue: Calculatedness and logicallity (Sometimes emotional coldness)\nPurple: Mysteriousness\nWhite: Benevolence, order and innocence\nBrown: Nurturing and caring\nYellow: Greed\n(sometimes optimism)\nRed: Dominance, power and control (Sometimes tyrannical natures)\nGreen: Harmony and balance (Sometimes vanity)\nBlack: Chaos and malevolence\n\n-Mana Pools: Mana pools are how much mana we have in our person, and this determines how\ngrand our spells can be, along with the duration a spell can be held in our world. Mana pools are governed by two things; skill level and Magic type. Skill level is simply how skilled you are at manipulating mana for your specific Sub-type. For example;\nthe longer you train in the use of Evocations, the better and more efficient you are at manipulating mana for that sub-type. Magic type is a little more complicated, different magic Sub-types are naturally more mana consuming than others, a few examples\nof very draining subtypes are as followed: Alteration, Arcane Evocation, and Conjuration. Although far more difficult to learn if one of these are your first Sub-type, you will naturally get a bigger mana pool than someone whose first Sub-type was\nIllusion, or perhaps an Evocation.\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-", ""),
        StaticBook("The Watcher", "TheNinox", "The Watcher\nNight falls and a watcher awakens\n\nFor soon she will find one to be taken\n\nTime always manages to fill its toll\n\nBut for the watcher, it merely plays a role\nHow can such a creature be so ancient?\n\nIt must be ever careful, forever patient\nThere is no protection, not even for kings\n\n\nFor those that scurry beneath the raptor's wings\nThroughout the world there is so much clatter\n\n\nBut the watchers wait for a very specific patter\nEyes of gold sweep through the trees\n\nSeeking out the creatures, that which they will sieze\n\nThere are many posibilities, but it must be right\n\nBefore this hunter can truly take flight\nA very slight stirring, and then an exposure\n\nThe watcher will soon have in its grasp full closure\n\nA push and lift, she takes to the air\n\nA target is found, they left themselves bare\nShe swoops forth, like a flash of lightning\n\nA sight so elegant, but so ever frightening\n\nThe distance shinks as she glides almost to totter\n\nMoving so swiftly, on a mission of slaughter\nWithout a sound, claws snatch it away\n\n\nSuccess is achieved, the watcher took its prey\nReturning to the branches, a home so secure\n\n\nShe feasts on her victim, a reaping so pure\nNight after night the watchers ever prowl\n\n\nLiving up to high fame, of the great horned owl.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thedas Riverwind", "Ebonsquire", "The Adventures of Thedas Riverwind, Part 1 \n\n((Originally written by Willizl33t))\nSo, my story begins as I, a travelling elf, go on a journey through all of Aegis! The first sight I came to was a vast desert and an amazing forest, the desert in the wast, the forest in the west. The night was drawing ever closer, so I set up camp\nslightly in the desert, which was a mistake. Through the entirety of the night, monsters stormed my tent. I fought for my life, and when night finally ended, I feared for my safety, so I stashed all my treasure in a small opening in the cliff my tent was\nconnected to. This was when I sealed it with stone, and continued forth. I was in the desert when I was approached by a band of Orcs -- vicious, battle hungry Orcs. These Orcs demanded I leave their \"territory\", or risk death, so, trying to stay out of\ndanger, I left, but when I turned my back, the \"dominus\" (see The History and Culture of Orcs for more information on Orcish ranks) shouted \"attack!\" and the 5-6 orcs killed me. Or so I, and they, thought!\n\nThis is when I truly got to understand this\nforce, what some may call God, some may call The Great One, but none know its true name, nor why it exists, or when it came to exist. In fact, there is so little knowledge about this deity, that some refuse to believe in its existence. This deity was like\na bright light, we could not see it, and it wasn't really white either. but it's the only way for it to be explained in contrast of the Void. Anyway, this \"deity\" caught me in my fall to death, and placed me in a temple known as The Cloud Temple of Aegis.\nThat is what made me realize, realize how it was possible, realize there was still a chance! \n\nI knew that dark times were falling on the world, and as my family was killed when I was young, I had always wanted to prevent, and root out, evil at any\ncost. However, I never knew how, or even if it was possible, but just a quick, ever so slight glimpse of this deity made me realize how, and I got the idea. It was like this deity had planted a seed in my mind, not literally, but mentally. A seed which\ngrew, and as this \"seed\" got bigger, so did the idea I had. I was to start a group of knights, or templars if you like, who would give their time to helping others, stopping evil at any cost, and try to prevent the darkness coming upon the land of Aegis.\nThis task seems like an impossible one at first glance, but if you break it down, then it doesn't seem so hard. However, I had barely arrived in the land of Aegis and I was not very familiar with the land of it. So, I took my first journey to Laurelin,\ncity of elves, a place of tranquility and beauty.\n\nOn the road to Laurelin, I met many other travellers, elves, dwarves, humans, and even an orc! The journey was a small, eventless one, there is not much point writing about it.\nOnly the fact that I could marvel at how the forests were so tranquil, so quiet, and the only noises were caused by the wildlife and other travellers. Everybody was friendly enough, and when I was amazed at its beauty, the great trees, standing so high\nabove all the other trees, and the mother tree, what a sight! It was indeed an amazing sight, one I highly recommend you go on. \n\nA few days on, and I had gathered some basic resources. I set out to find a suitable location for the castle where me and my\ntemplars would live. And I found one. On the road to Raven Hold, when you enter the desert, look for a tower which has the Desert Star at the top of it, you go in the direction of the tower from the road to the sea. This is where it would be built in the\nocean, with a bridge going to it. All I needed was a name, Zoraida Castle, Zoraida being a word in a lost language, meaning \"to purge evil\". This was when I began the construction, it took 17 days to complete it, but it was an amazing sight when it was\ncomplete, the symbol of The Cloud Temple at the top, the water, symbolizing life, and the lava, symbolizing death. Separating them is obsidian, which you can decide what that represents. Now, the templars, we would call ourselves \"The Templars of the\nCloud\". However, before I would allow myself to finish this, I had created a task for myself, a type of pilgrimage, where I must travel for 3 weeks, and all the things I acquire through my travels, I must give as an offering to this deity.\nYou must understand, not all the templars have to do this, only I, as I was trying to create this group, and so I start my journey, and the first part of my adventures end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thievery", "Grandmaster Khivan Peretas", "Thievery\n       ***********\n        The Path\n            of\n        the Thief\n\"We are the wanering hands, the sticky fingers, we are the children of Koratta.\"\n~Grandmaster Khivan Peretas", ""),
        StaticBook("Thomas Tantrum", "Beelzebub", "There was once a boy, he was named Thomas.\n\nThomas had a hot temper.\n\nThomas' mother warned him.\n\n\"Thomas, if you continue to be so wrathful, your head will pop like a balloon!\"\nThomas yelled at his mother.\n\n\"I do not need your advice! I do not have the patience for it!\"\n\nThomas stomped and yelled and walked away.\n\nHe was one angry boy.\nThe next day, Thomas came upon a boy playing with a toy.\n\nHe grew naughty.\n\n\"Your toy is dumb! And so are you!\"\n\nThomas knocked the toy out of the young boy's hand, breaking it.\n\nHe was one bad boy.\nThomas' head grew rounder.\n\nIt became a shade of red.\n\nHis voice became squeakier.\nThomas' mother warned him once again.\n\n\"Your head will pop, Thomas!\"\n\n\"That is what happens to mean boys!\"\n\nBut Thomas did not listen.\n\nHe ctomped and yelled and walked away.\nThe next day, Thomas came upon a boy waiting in line for something to eat.\n\nHe grew naughty.\n\n\"Give me your money!\"\n\nThe boy gave Thomas all he had.\n\nThomas was one big bully.\nThomas went home.\n\nHe looked in the mirror.\n\nHis head was a balloon!\n\"Help! My head, my head is a balloon!\"\n\nThomas called out. But his voice was too squeaky.\n\nHe stomped and yelled and stomped and yelled.\n\nUntil his head went 'pop'!", ""),
        StaticBook("Thor's Diary V.1", "Thorburn G. Alexander", "This is the Journal of Thorburn Grimbeorn,former Felsen Guard, former Maecht Master of Horse and Sea, former  Admiral of the Crimson Legion, and current Squire of Duke Percival Staunton of Courland.\n9th of Sun's Smile, 1523\n\nToday was supposed to be the wedding of Leonard and Anabeth. However, an Orenian law was forgotten by us. A baron cannot marry a person from another race. The only way for that to happen is if the baron gave up his position\nDespite Leonard agreeing to it, Anabeth said no and run off. It was later decided that they would not marry at all\nI feel bad for them. They were a great couple. Oh well. Now that I mention it to myself, I have reached 30 years into my life. I guess\nI should start finding a person to spend the rest of my days with. Now that I mention it, Cassiopia looked gorgeous. I actually fainted for a few seconds! But I do not think see sees me that way, unfortunately for me. Oh well. The God may do me a miracle.\n*this page is torn but a small red stain is seen on a small part of the torn page that remained*\n24th of the Deep Cold, 1523\n\nYesterday was the most freakish day. Unfortunately because of that, I could not write the events. I will write them now. Almost everyone in the keep wasn't inside, either in business or travelling. I was in Vydrik,\ntalking to Percival about making a stand for us to sell products. When I came back, Mordic revealed to me that  the fort was covered in a red substance. He also found some in the countryside but he cleaned it. I told him it is probably a farce. However,\nhe told me someone or something broke into his room in the tower.  They destroyed the wall cause the trapdoor is locked and only he has the key. He found some wierd writings in his books made of something similar to red ink. I searched and found many\nbooks with similar writings. There was one in my journal, a few pages back which I torn, and in Luke's as well. Me and Mordic searched the countryside and found a cave with similar writings. We have a feeling goblins, or worse \"HIM\" are related. I showed\nit to Percival and he said he will look into it. However, I think he believes it is a farce. Only time will tell. I had another personal vision. It seems me locking away my connection to \"that\" hasn't stopped it sending me visions. I think the ordeal made\nhim wary. I want to talk to somebody about it, but I fear they will lock me up like an animal or worse. I guess I will do what I learned best from my caretakers, the Amber wolves. I will endure. Like always.\n5th of Malin's Welcome,1524\n\nAt long last, we found him. Bradley's son was found. He is a small 9 year old boy, cheerful, with signs of a cunning mind. He seems very spoiled but it doesn't matter. He will learn to act as a man here. Luke is happy as\nwell. He and Bradley were good friends. I am designing plans for a warship. With luck, they will be done by the end of the month. Leonard is making plans about festivals. I think some of his ideas are really good. With Percival's help, it could get well.\n10th of The First Seed,1524\n\nToday I met our new blacksmith. His name is Gendry Windsor. Luke trains him in the art. I believe it will do him well. He will get to pass his skill and relax a bit.\nI also had a formal  talk with Percival's son.\nRichard Staunton. He does get from his father in many ways. He is smart as well. He is the only one who know that I have northern and Adunian lineage. His father probably knows too. I like Richard. I hope to meet him again. Speaking of Stauntons, I went\nto Percival's house for a meeting a few days ago. Einar was there with me. There was also a vassal of Percival, the Duke's hand, a soldier, a captain and members of Percival's family and guard. There was also a Kha and a Golem.  How did he manage to fit ?\nI have no idea. We talked about the threat of Mountain Trolls and a plan to defeat them. We settled for summoning powerful mages to break their armor with magic and we would finish them with swords. It could work. I also gave him the ship's design.\nI hope he gives them to the new Port manager quick. They can make modifications but I want to start the building.\n9th Of the Grand Harvest,1524 \n\nIt happened... i lost control.... and i cannot get it back... the wolf inside me is back...\n14th of Snow's Maiden ,1525\n\nI got a special talisman in my helmet now. It allows me to suppress my animalistic lust to the level I was in during my time in Maecht. It has proved to be very effective. It only lets a tiny fraction of my full last to\ncome out, which causes my eyes to glow slightly, but it doesn't give me any effects of the lust and it cannot go further, which is very good for me. The festival was cancelled due to problems. The barony has become beautiful. We have houses and a fountain\non the countryside. There is a two-story house which I got my eye on. Maybe when I get married I will have the housen if I ever get married. We have also made a tavern. I now make plans for either a chapel in the fort, or a small church in the barony.\nSpeaking of which, the bandit who attacked Vydrik got executed. They burned him alive. I was among the few who were allowed entry. Hopefully the raids will stop for a while.\n10th of Malin's Welcome,1525  \nThe time has come. I take up my trusty greatsword, my longbow, and my Battle armor. The dragon arrived to Vydrik. Let us see if we can survive.\n11th of Malin's Welcome,1525 \nI lived after all. The dragon was powerful. Its tail alone blasted me into a wall. Its claws could lift Thatch effortlessly. Its breath melted the ground and it could summon lightning bolts. It was a hard battle.\nWe managed to push it back. We could not kill it. We could barely scratch his thick black scales. His wings were as strong as ferrum as well.\n11th of Sun's Smile,1525 \n\nSo we found out the barony will be gone by order of the king. Too bad. I really had such a nice time building the keep. Oh well. Me and Luke decided to reveal our secret. We found out a long time ago we were brothers.\nWe also have a sister. We invited her. We talked to Percival and he promised he would allow us to build a manor for the Alexander family.\n12th of Sun's Smile, 1525\n\nSo our sister came. She has grown all these years. We will probably have a hard time keeping boys off her. Also Luke now has a wife. Her name is Evelyn. Luke is very happy. It seems they know eachother a lot. Why?\nCause they got a SON. I got a nephew to spoil. And train a bit. Me and Luke attended a trial. Someone accused two female elves of being frost witches. He was found wrong and when he insulted Percival they went to put him in cells. He suicided.\n3rd of Malin's welcome, 1526 \n\nNow that the barony will get destroyed, it looked like I would not be able to follow my dream of being a knight. However, this might not be true it seems. Percival agreed to let me be his squire under one condition.\nRichard has to say that I am ready. So I talked to him to be taken as his apprentice in order to reach that rank. He said the only way he can teach me is by me joining the Staunton Guard. And that is what I did. I now have a new uniform to wear.I like it.\nThe helmet is good as well. Not as good as my previous one but still good. My previous got an irrepairable hit to the back of the head. Thankfully the talisman was intact so I fitted it to my new helmet. Let us see what the days have in store for us.\n6th of Malin's Welcome, 1526 \nIt seems that despite the ashes receding the problem is not done. Now there is an infection spreading. It seems it is not lethal. It symptoms appear to be: Hearing voices, exhaustion, sometimes permanent, screaming,\nsymptoms like blindness and being unable of using magic  and being rendered to inept level at their crafts. I do not know yet if I have this infection. However, I have not witnessed any of the symptoms so I believe I am healthy for now.\nI will  need to be careful from now on. I must always  try and see if the people near me are infected, I must decrease close contact and some time inside more frequently will not hurt me.\n3rd of The Grand Harvest, 1526\n\nGood things come in good and bad. The disease that spread through the land is no more. Everyone who got infected vomited it out in the form of a black substance. That is the good news. However, tragedy struck.\nKing Guy De Bar is dead. He has been assassinated. Now a new king will arise. Talks are also being heard that Percival will become the Treasurer of the Kingdom. It will be a great honor for him. A day before the curse was lifted,  I arrested a man.\nI took him to the cells since Percival sentenced him to death. Then me and another guard named Richard took him and another prisoner to the execution stage. However, Percival let the one soldier live for two reasons. One, a lord pleaded him.\nTwo, he apparently drank poison while in the cell. He would die anyway. Then, Percival showed me the other prisoner and gave me an axe. I then executed him. Then I took part in a training exercise. We tried to form a straight line but failed miserably.\nWe got yelled that we needed discipline. He then yelled at Richard cause he was ordering them around before the execution. He gave him lashes with a cat o' nine tails. After that he asked us how we salute and I showed him. He told us some things next.\nFinally, we sparred. I fought three times with Richard. One was tie, another was a close victory of his and the final a victory of mine. Then, I fought Edmund, our  trainer. He wielded a wooden sabre instead of a  shortsword. We fought for hours.\nHowever, I lost eventually. We talked a bit. He told me he likes large swords. So now I may have someone to spar with. I  also made a rank system suggestion for Richard. Let us see what he thinks.\n24th of the First Seed, 1531\n\nIt has been 5 whole years since I last wrote here, I cannot believe it. Since only a few pages are left, I will do a summary of what happened in these 5 years. I will soon make a new diary. The reason I hadn't written is this\nThis diary was lost during the period I made changes in the fort and when I moved into two other rooms. I found it when I changed my first room into a praying area. These 5 years were busy. Percival became Duke and Lord Treasurer as said before.\nI am now his squire. We are at war with the Dunamis,  a mercenary group residing in the Caliphate. The war leans towards the Dunamis cause Oren is disorganised at the moment. Lord Percival's Duchy is going great. The Northern army is one of the biggest,\nand strongest in Oren. The entire north is united. Alexanders, Kellians, Saltstone, Vincare Order, all of them. My family is now quite strong. We make weaponry and armor mostly, and we use it for trade. We are quite wealthy in terms of the north.\nWe got a nice amount of servants,workers, and private guards. Being a squire is both hard and satisfying. I attend meetigns for Percival, I take part in trainings, I visit new areas and I got a nice amount of respect in the Guard. The Guard is going well.\nWe  all hold a deep sense of loyalty, kinship, belief in the cause, and desire to protect what we hold dear. Though not everything is great. Monsters are more frequent, relationships with the Empire and Imperials are strained more than they should, and we\nface threats daily. But we are strong. We will endure and come out victorious. This is my last entry here. More on my new diary.\n\nSigned,\nThorburn G. Alexander\n\n*the letters are drawn neatly on the entire book and the Alexander stamp rests on the corner*", ""),
        StaticBook("Thrm. Of Wisdom", "Farley III Stafyr", "Theorem of Wisdom\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr\nWhat is wisdom?\n\nWisdom is not easy to define, likely similar to eternity. Every person has its own views of wisdom. To elaborate this further, a row of examples.\nIs knowledge wisdom? \nPerhaps.\n\nIs knowing the right thing to do wisdom? \nPerhaps.\n\nIs doing something good wisdom?\n Perhaps.\nIs learning wisdom? \nPerhaps.\n\nAs aforementioned you cannot simply define wisdom. Wisdom is multitude, colorful, differently shaped. Wisdom can and does exist in many of us.\nTo different degrees, in different shapes.  A forester can have the wisdom of knowing how to treat his plants and trees properly, when to grow what to reach the best result. As can the farmer. A sorcerer or  wizard can know a lot about the divine art of\nmagic and has through this his very own wisdom.\n\nStill, one would say, that in these examples wisdom turns out to be rather knowledge, which is only partially right, if it’s right at all.\nWisdom requires more than simply having knowledge. Wisdom requires understanding the spirit, the being, the living and many things more. The inner peace and silence may bring wisdom.  On the other side, a warrior may achieve a new level of\ncombat by finding his inner stability in combat. To be calm in the face of the storm and evil.\n\nAs we now scratch the evil, the darkness, I wish to bring in a small part of my very own opinion. Wisdom doesn't exist in\npeople who are simply evil and work for their very own profit. Wisdom requires selflessness as well.\n\nYou may now think I am taking the side of the good here, solely.  It is right. I do align myself to the good and the light, but must say , that I may be\nbe completely wrong with my statement about wisdom and the evilness here. Perhaps the other side may have their own kind of wisdom, being evil as it is.\n\nIs it wisdom to write a book about wisdom? No.\nIs it wisdom to explain what wisdom can be? Perhaps.\n\nWhy perhaps? Because wisdom is wisdom. Colorful and different. Not definable. That is wisdom.", ""),
