        StaticBook("Tikatu Style", "Ebonsquire", "Tikatu Sword Style\n\n((Originally written by hmqb))\nThe Tikatu style is a method of dueling passed down by masters, and is not limited to just swords but is best used with them. The principle of the stlye is careful hits, and the art of not being hit.\nFirst, we will talk about the basic method used in this style. It is based upon the charge, but at the last moment you shift to the right or left. If done correctly, you should end up striking at the side of your opponent. You always want to circle to one\nside and stay a solid 2 blocks away. The key is not to charge straight into combat but to drift to the side. Personally, I prefer moving to the left, but it is preference. Test this with monsters and find which direction suits you best. The next step\nafter the initial charge leaves you with options. If your enemy has turned with you continue around them in a cricle shape. The whole time, make sure to stay a solid distance away, and try not to be hit. If you are getting hit put more distance\nbetween you and your enemy. Remember, a key component is that you'll be running towards their position but not directly at them. Although you do not want to ever turn your back and run or a backwards retreat. You want to follow them from your direction\nyou started with a circle formed around them. If your enemy does not follow you though, then isntead of circling, you come up onto their back side and them from behind as fast as possible. Most fights occur with an initial charge and blows\nstanding still, but always keep moving. The specialty of this style is that you don't charge hit them and then go back for another charge you hit them over and over but keep moving around them. Another technique to combine with this is the art\nof how fast to strike. Always remember to pace your blows and make sure they are dead on. Do not swing as fast as you can but in swift solid strikes that do not allow your opposition to recover. Practice circling around monsters, and even other people.\nThis style is meant for one on one battles and should not be used in large scale battle. The most likely course of bttle will be a running battle. The enemy will be rushing right at you and in your attempt to circle you willl both be running off in an\nalmost diagonal line, but as long as you stay ahead you will still win. If the battle turns to each person taking hits you can disengage by running through them. This is done by twisting to run directly at them and hitting them while they hit you, but\nwhile you do you run through them and continue until a safe distance and turn around. After this, gauge your own well-being and estimate theirs. You should both be in a position to charge each other again and if you're banged up, your style\nis going to one side and then after your first hit, disengage. This is done by making the hit and backing off and going the direction you were before but this time out of range. Then pull another fast turn around a repeat, but at this point you want to\nfake the direction you went last time and go the other direction, and then not engage. Do this by getting close then changing to the other side and backing off as they run at you. This will cause them to run head long at you where you will\npull a nasty trick. You back off until they get almost within range and you jump to the side and strike them twice in the back. Then back off as they regain their balance and you use any number of the moves that seems fit to finish them off.\nMost of the time, only the circle strategy is necessary, but it is good to have a large set of moves. also, you may think this is all stupid, but when you put into play your well-practiced moves your combat becomes much better. Now integrate special moves\ninto this and you're good to go. After reading this and practicing, you should have all of these moves at your disposal when in battle, and you can mix and match with your own moves to become a devastating warrior!\nThis was written by a long time warrior who knows that it's not goood armour and a deadly weapon that make a good warrior, but the skills they employ.\n\nHere you are, friend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Timid Affection", "Ebonsquire", "Timid Affection\n\n((Originally written by darkdladety))\nBack to back, we burst out from the doors, swinging our bows from side-to-side, checking for danger. It can be extremely quiet when it wants. \"All clear.\" Her voice is calm and smooth, breaking through the winter drafts. \"Yeah. Same here.\"\nWe lower our bows but leave them armed. Night is much too dangerous to put away our weapons. Leaves rustle behind us for a moment. But there are no trees at our back. We spin around and catch the creeper mid-step. It probably jumped down from\nthe roof. It walks towards us, silent as the night. Deadly. \n\nLess deadly perhaps when two arrows sprout from its chest and neck. We are synched, as always. The creeper falls to the ground, giving the sound of leaves\nbeing shifted in the wind. It disintegrates, leaving the two arrows in the ground. She strides over and carefully pulls them out. They are food, safety, supplies, and life itself. Holding them out, she signals me to get one. Our finders brush as I pluck\nthe arrow from her hand. Warmth seeps from her hand to mine. Her fingers are slender and soft but also contain the strength and dexterity to wield either a bow or a sword. \n\nWe pass through the night like wraiths, hunting the monsters\nthat were once the hunters. The positions have switched greatly. Spiders die mid-lunge. Skeletons fall before they can get an arrow out of their quivers. Zombies die instantly when arrows pierce their brains. But none of those compare to creepers.\nCreepers, who are the most silent of all, are killed before they know of our presence. We have surpassed them. Our leather pouches quickly fill with their explosive powder. They are what we cam out to hunt. The sun begins to rise and we head back home.\nOur home is made from stone, painstakingly put together block by block. A lot of coal was used in the process of refining cobblestone. It was worth it, though. It welcomes us back as we enter the doors. Time to start part two of the plan. TNT.\nTo be continued.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tinker: Override", "Benben582", "Tinkerer:\n       Override Gates\n\n  An informative book\n  on override gates.\n\nby: Hirdok Irongut\n\nDISCLAIMER: Working\nwith materials such as redstone can be dangerous. Practice at your own risk.\nOverride Gates\n\n An override gate is used when you want to have two inputs determine one output. Both signals of the input must be 'true' for the output to be 'true'. If only one were true, then the output would still be 'false',\nKEY\n===================- = Redstone Dust\n* = Redstone Torch\n# = Redstone Repeater\no = Block\n+ = Block w/ Redstone torch\n@ = Block w/ Redstone dust\nO = Output [Door...]\nI = Input [Btn, Lever..]\n~ = Activated Redst-\nRedstone Dust\nR = Reset [Button, Pressure plate]\n\nTrue = Powered\nFalse = No Signal\nExample: #1\n\nI   I\n-  -\n-  -\n+@+\n  *\n  -\n  O     This example\n         shows that if both inputs are false, so is the output.\nExample: #2\n\nI   I\n~  -\n~  -\n+@+\n  *\n  -\n  O    This example\n        shows that power from one input is not strong enough to power the output.\nExample: #3\n\nI   I\n~  ~\n~  ~\n+@+\n  *\n  ~\n  O   The third and \n       final example shows both inputs are true which makes the output become true,\nPractical Uses\n\nIf you want to let people freely into a place, then by a pull of a lever you can lock them either inside or outside of the room until the lever is pulled again.\n\nIf you wanted to make\na door that requires\ntwo people to enter, this can also be done using an override gate.\n\nThere are a multitude of other uses for such a gate, these are just a few I've created.\nAuthor's Comments\n\nFeel free to contact me by bird or in person. I'd be happy to answer any questions. If anyone would like to learn the art of tinkering, contact me.\n\n~Hirdok Irongut\n((Benben582))", ""),
        StaticBook("TLL Prices", "Ayrlinde", "@>= The little lion =<@\n\nPg.2 - Alcohols\nPg.3 - Teas\nPg.4 - Food\n@ Alcohols\n\nAle - 3 Mina\n\nMead - 4 Mina\n\nVodka - 7 Mina\n\nWine - 5 Mina\n@ Teas\n\n*All teas are 5 Mina\n@ Food\n\nBread - 2 Mina\n\nPotato('s) - 4 Mina\n\nSoups - 4/7 Mina\n\n\n*Custom foods can be requested.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Be", "GusanoArentonio", "Across the city steam and light\nOff a runway to the manufactured night-\nIn storybooks you'll never find\nIn paper armor that you'd mind\nThey'll hold the match to you this time-\nAnd watch the smoke rings fit the crime\nIn moments you cannot reprise\nLike a soldier or a watch that you can't wind\nWe fought the world with hands twice-tied\nThe people cheered, the captain cried\nI'll keep the souvenir inside\nIt's just better in my mind\nAnd I wouldn't lie\nI never really wanted more\nThan what I really needed after all\nSomeone that hates to see me go\nYou made a promise then you hide\nAnd you said we'd all be dead by twenty-five\nIt's not your disappointed sigh\nIt's not you traded this for pride\nNot that we really even mind\nWe're just bored you're still alive\nAnd I wouldn't lie\nIf I tried, take me down\nAnd if I die here now\nWishing wells and magic spells and everything between\nCan you tell me what it's like?\nOr how it's going to be?", ""),
        StaticBook("To Be a Wraith", "Toodles", "Becoming a Wraith\n\nBy: Someone who's not stupid enough to reveal their name.\nPrerequisites:\n-Must be a practitioner of the dark arts or undead.\n-Must have a 'catalyst'; some sort of bone that the Drake, Satar, gives to certain people.\nThe hopeful Wraith must acquire such a catalyst, and then place it on a certain type of Altar, one example of which is located in the Sunless Sanctum. Upon doing this, they must find, kill, and take a bone from three mortals.\nThey then must take these bones to the altar... But the author is not quite sure what happens to them. But once they've been used, the Wraith-to-be must stab themself with an Aurum sword. After much immolation and probably pain, they\nwill become a Wraith. Huzzah!", ""),
        StaticBook("To Bryce", "Ser Aulfr af Eklund", "To my Dearest Friend,\n\nThe road has been long and fraught with peril. When Maric left, we wept bitter tears. When you leave, I weep alone.\n\nI will stand vigil here, as I promised I would to Maric, for when he comes back.\nWorry not my friend, my oldest remaining friend. We may not meet again in this life, but I will carry your memort with me always, until we meet in the heavens.\n\nI will watch over your son, even should he wander far. Thank you, my friend.\nThank you for being there, Bryce. Do Maric proud, do your father proud. Do Saltstone proud.\n\nAulfr af Eklund", ""),
        StaticBook("To Catherine", "Timothy of Killeen", "When we parted, I told you your choice would affect us both horribly. It has destroyed me already, but since my stupid, soft heart brings me to tears at your mere thought, I must warn you. You will soon reap the seeds you have sown, unwillingly or not.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Czeslaw", "Renee", "*The letter is written in a elegant, flowing handwriting.*\n\nDear Czeslaw,\nI hope you'll be able to read this. I just wanted to tell you that I cannot marry you after all. I'm leaving Krajia for good now. I have a responsibility to my family.\nNo matter what you or any other Raevir says, I am not one of you. I was born a Savoyard and I cannot change that.\nI appreciate all you've done for me. Tell Jaromir I said goodbye.\n\nSincerely,\nRenee", ""),
        StaticBook("To Demi", "Theodora Palaiologos", "To Demi\n\nI was recently attacked in Lorraine by a man named \"Maulhawk\". I want revenge.\n\nThe man is a monster. He hates Southerners and works with the Lorrainian \"Honor\" Guard. He finds joy in scalping people as\nwell. Be cautious.\n\nDon't go out and fight him though. I want you to gather up your forces and preferably get some of the Duke's men as well.\n\nI will lure him out and into a remote location. You and the men will be nearby.\nThe signal for you to move will be a shout of \"Hey, is that a bear?\"\n\nOnce I give the signal, I want you and the men to charge and surround him. By the end of the Saint's Day, I want him dead.\n\nFrom,\n-Theodora", ""),
        StaticBook("To Heus", "Nephor", "Heus Grandaxe,\n    Please don't apologize to me. You don't need to apologize to me for a small mistake like that, Heus. I feel the same love for you. I feel different around you. Like something stronger and better than love. Different than what I had\nwith Erik and Joto. I feel like you chose me, and in return I chose you. We may visit eachother very soon, Heus. Hopefully the water is clear today.               -Nephor", ""),
        StaticBook("To Illi.", "Ro'ya", "To Illithri,\n\nThis should be the last you hear from me for a while. Im changing my identity not just from you but from everybody.\n\nI just need to stay away from both of these crazy families i seem to have found myself in the middle of\nI should return in the next ten years or so maybe earlier.\n\nIts hard to explain why I am doing this. I just feel like this is what I have to do.\n\nTo keep dad and you safe. I need time to figure everything out and time to think about my future-\nwithout getting kidnapped by my aunt or to get tortured by my cousin in the process.\n\nI Promise i will return one day.\n\n[!] Tears seem to have stained the page.\n\n-R", ""),
        StaticBook("To My Dear a", "__PJ", "If ever two were one, then surely we.\nIf ever man were loved by wife, then thee.\nIf ever king was happy in a man.\nCompare with me, ye king, if ye can.\nI prize thy love more than whole mines of gold,", ""),
        StaticBook("To Orithur", "Belegar Irongrinder", "Orithur,\n\nThank you for the oppurtunity to work at the library and the knowledge I have gained through my time there. I am sorry, but it appears I am apart of conflicting groups and I am sorry, but my decision has been made to leave the library.\nSincerly, Belegar.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Praetor TT", "Laethis Izalith", "Praetor Tristin Tresery,\n\nI was recently made aware of the dwarven attack upon your city. Though it is my understanding your defense was successful, I am sorry to hear of this unjust attack.\n\nIf there is anything\nour State can do to assist you, do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.\nLaethis Izalith, Sohaer of Haelun'or.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Read a Mind", "Sage", "How to Read\n         Minds\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Canaan L. Short\nMind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind\nmind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind\nmind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind\nmind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind\nmind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind\nmind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind\nmind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind\nmind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind mind 