        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "*The void is the cource of arcane magic§0\n§0*ALl thing come from and return to the void. May require fact checking.§0\n§0*Draw elements from the void. Requires focus and mana? Do not lose focus.§0\n§0*Mana is energy within living things. Flows like blood?\n\n*Glacio says it's like stamina. Don't go for too long or you get hurt.§0\n§0(The rest of the page is covered by a pencil sketch of Glacio's face.)§0\n\n*Clear mind and connect to the void, like meditation. §0\n§0*Understand element (water)§0\n§0-Liquid, fluid, viscosity of 0.894, high surface tension, low density, 32 degrees and 212", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "15+36 51\n\n27+12 39\n\n21-13 8\n\n47-36 11\n\n5x6 30\n\n10x24 240\n\n60/5 12\n\n18/3 6\n\n1/2+1/2 1", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", ":: OOC Note ::§0\n§0This tome has been scribed by a skilled Fire Evocationist IG and is also lore-abiding and MAT approved! When self-teaching, use the guide on our forums and its also advised you have an OOC teacher to make sure you don't PG.§0\n§0::\n\nFire Evocation is a relatively simply concept to understand, yet quite difficult to put into practice. In the most basic of terms, it is bringing from fire and with it heat from the Void into the realm you and I see around us. This tome will instruct\n\nyou how to begin to go about this. Each and every one of us has a force called mana inside of us. It is not tangible, and yet plays a large part in connecting to the Void. I can warn you now to never attempt something greater than what you are capable of.\n\nFollow what is contained in this book very closely or it may lead to your own personal harm. To begin, one must first conduct an intensive study of fire. To be able to bring it out the Void, you must understand it completely in its natural form.\n\nFrom my experience, examine fire closely. Feel its heat, see its color, and perhaps even feel its sting. The way you go about this stage is ultimately up to you. Before continuing any farther in your training, make sure you understand the Void. It is the\n\nmost important of the basic steps to learning this evocation. The next step is vital and it will take one not of weak mind to undertake. You will begin to meditate. You want to focus upon fire, in a secluded place where you are most likely to not be\n\ninterrupted. I suggest keeping a journal from this point forward. Record your thoughts, what you experience. Anything that will help you reflect upon your study. The Void in itself is one of the hardest things to describe. The best explanation\n\nI have ever found is that the Void is simply nothing, and everything at once. It is formless and empty- void, if you will, until one with a creative mind harnesses it. When meditating, try to picture the Void. Focus your thoughts upon it. That is all I\n\ncan recommend. Your first connection will be strenuous. You will likely have no chance to even attempt at summoning fire. You will most likely break your own connection and fall unconscious. Do not lose heart! Connecting to the Void for the first time is\n\na great accomplishment! Continue your meditations until you believe you can hold a connection for a period of at least several minutes. At this point, you need to begin to picture fire while holding this connection- how it feels, its effects,\n\nwhat makes it up. This will take many, many, many attempts to succed. Once you have succeded, you will need to them imagine it in the world. This will become easier with practice. In fact, that is the single most important thing I have mentioned. Practice\n\nis the key! Once you have completed the basics I've described, which can take anywhere from months to years, you just need to practice your magic. If you have the drive, you may even become a Fire evocationist of great skill. That is all I can describe\n\nfrom my own experiences. Now! Get to work! You will only become great by practice!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "A Denouncement§0\n§0===================§0\n§0\n§0   It is I, Archibald Vallero, once again. I am the author of the book \"The All-Theory,\" which is essentially a collection of ramblings regarding the Void and mana and other such things. §0\n§0\n§0  Today, I bring you\n\na commentary on a prominent and ancient order: The Druidic Order. If I could, I would bring up my disagreements with the ways of the paladins and the clerical order, but I'd rather not for personal reasons. §0\n§0\n§0   This commentary, as you would guess, is\n\nincredibly bias, given the fact that I'm a mage who reveres the Void and all of its wonders, while the Druids tend to stray away from and frown upon the use or mention of Voidal magic. §0\n§0  In addition to questioning the tenets of the druids, I'll also\n\nexpand on some solid laws which apply to our realm.§0\n§0\n§0  I would like to also note that I have no hatred for the druids as a whole, and I do not mean to denigrate them and lower their reputation. This is simply a questioning. If even after the last\n\nstatement, you believe that you will find yourself deeply offended by this book, then I implore you to close it and to carry on with your day (and please do not burn this). §0\n§0\n§0  Let us begin by touching on the subject of 'balance'.\n\n        Balance§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0   Druids are tasked with keeping nature in balance. They hold the belief that nature must be preserved in its natural equilibrium between life and death in order to counteract the eldritch forces that mages\n\nand other Aengulic or Daemonic might have on this world of ours. It is true that there have been times in which patches of land and natural resources were swathed in magic-based devastation, and for their attempting to cure this, I do applaud them.\n\nHowever, what I don't find particularly attractive is their attitude towards Voidal magic. Surely they must understand that it is truly a small minority of mages who have actually caused massive destruction. The aenguldaemons are mainly to blame for the\n\nlarger, impactful events.\n\nCerridwen and Cernunnos created the world. They are 'neutral' Aengudaemonic forces. Druids are meant to keep the balance of the world by making sure not too much magic is used. Magic bad. Nature good. Cernunnos is the father of the hunt. Cerridwen\n\nis the mother of spring. She represents life, he represents death. Druids are also non-violent. They serve these two Aspects in order to ensure that the balance of nature is obtained.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Your house isn't safe Grand Mayor, I'd think about it.§0\n§0\n§0*some fur is scattered on the page*", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "*A mockup sketch of§0\n§0a newspaper layout*§0\n§0\n§0The Felsen Herald§0\n§0\n§0-Date-§0\n§0\n§0-Table of Contents-§0\n§0Article w/ page #§0\n§0Ad not listed§0\n§0repeat....§0\n§0e\n\nArticle 1, continue onto next page if needed. §0\n§0\n§0Then an Ad§0\n§0\n§0Then an article of a new sort.§0\n§0\n§0Then an ad or announcement.§0\n§0\n§0repeat\n\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/146063-5th-mayoral-election-of-felsen/§0\n§0\n§0Commandants Speech§0\n§0\n§0Interview§0\n§0Felsen Born§0\n§0Parents Passed, Father fought and died in the dukes war. Trained by the Gold\n\nCrops before the civil war. Offered Mayor Gradic his services and was hired as trial then permanent guard captain.§0\n§0\n§0\"I'd call the civil war a tragedy. Orenian men killing Orenian men. Imagine, these men might be friends under different circumstances\n\n. One might like to fish, the other to hunt. A true tragedy.\"§0\n§0\n§0Dedicated to stimulating the local economy, subsidy to trading guilds. Investment begets profit.§0\n§0\n§0Does not expect the MAyor to defend his seat but, intends to employ the MAyor\\\n\nin the new regime.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0The Felsen Guard discovered a body in the upper floors of the *tavern name* late in the day on the 16th. They held a man by the name of Adam for questions as he was found on scene. No civilians or reporters were allowed inside\n\nand attempts to peer inside were conteracted by boarding up the windows. They guard refused to comment.§0\n§0\n§0The guards destroyed a suspects property in the form of notes which were ripped apart.§0 The refused to comment on this.\n\nThe deceased is only identified as a wood elf male.§0\n§0\n§0Apparently the murder was carried out by an anti-reavir, anti-mali bigot.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Notes for my Monster Manual.§0\n\nGolems,§0\n§0\n§0Golems are construct creatures made for the soul purpose of serving their owner, or Impera. §0\n§0", ""),
