        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[!] There are multiple medical supplies laid out upon the table. Dry tears stain it's wood ((Items right side of chest)).§0\n§0Whereas broken glass and brown liquid stains are on the floor. Light like beer or rum, ((Left side of chest, books are for later))-\n\n-A dagger with an Odd hue lays quietly on the floor. There is more liquid aswell as a white powder flurried about the area. Kush blunts mixed with cut up pineapple fronds lay about the floor while a lone cane of sugar lays a short distance away.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Saradunan, Assault:§0\n§0Some Random man Said the words The fuck you want? to Saradunan, saradunan then decided to run at this man and attempted to punch him, Unofficial investigator tried to move the fight out of Felson, instead he took a knee to the side\n\nand the right shoulder dislodged, Saradunan was knocked to the floor and pinned by the man, sara then tried choking him, but then the man picked up a rock and tried to bash in sara's helmet, the unofficial investigator stopped this by giving a firm push\n\nwith his leg, the man then rolled over and regained his feet, Sara also got up and the OI moving out of the way. Saradunan then drew a Greatsword, and The man a Shortsword. The man circles Sara at an increasingly fast pace\n\nSaradunan faces the man while the man runs around him, the man keeps running in circles.. Saradunan then swings one of his feet toward the man.§0\n§0The man then stops and changes directions, Whilst swinging his sword diagnoly onto sara\n\nsaradunan then parry's this attack§0\n§0The man falls backwards and rolls to his left attempting to regain his footing as fast as he can, Saradunan tried to get his blade to the mans neck but failed due to the rolling.. Sara then tries to use a torch to\n\ntry and burn the man.§0\n§0Saradunan had sheathed his sword while taking them out, the man had been wearing flammable materials. the man then grabbed saradunan's hand holding the torch, pushing it out of the way and stabbing saradunan\n\nin the gut. sara screams in pain and grabs the mans throat firmly as the man leaned forward into his grasp while kneeing him in the groin sara would then kick the man in the unmentionables§0\n§0the man then drifts off to the side using the wall\n\nas support, he then slides the blade back into his scabbard.§0\n§0\n§0Saradunan then complains about the stabbing. grasping his chest while doing so§0\n§0\n§0The man is pushing sara down by the neck while sara is trying to push him off\n\nSaradunan is bleeding badly.. a third party attempts to bash in the mans head but sara and the man both fall§0\n§0from the man trying to push sara down.§0\n§0The man falls upon sara, and a fourth party draws a sword yelling Enough of this\n\nThe man and saradunan both get up slowly, sara uses the wall as support to get up, the other gets up cautiously.§0\n§0The man then bandages up saradunan, by this point Saraduanan has lost much of his blood, his son also showed up\n\nThe OI then falls on his back when he hears this news, The man is trying to heal saradunan and stem the bleeding§0\n§0\n§0At this point its cleanup for the fight§0\n§0The third party had walked off aswell, a Sea ship doctor showed up questionable at best\n\nThe doctor tries to get payment from saradunan while he is dieing, eventually a Sarkozic boy steps in and orders him to fix§0\n§0Saraduanan ((Sarkozic was 4th party)) the doctor stitches up saradunan to the best of his ability\n\n*A sketch of the man is drawn here, has a magnificent black beard, wore light tan clothing, had a shortsword was Around six feet tall*§0\n§0((_Tommo)) This is a sketch depicting the man who fought with saradunan", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Sad duarian was a a powerful warrior but he was also the guard of orphanage of a bunch of deaf children that couldn't hear a thing. Even though the children couldn't hear they were very greatful of the Sad duarian. The Sad duarian was very kind to the\n\ndeaf children but would seem sad all the time. The children would use sign language to speak to the Sad duarian and he would say back, wait in till your older and I shall tell you. The group of children waited intill they were older, but their were fewer\n\nof them. The had started off as 20 deaf kids but now there was 15. The now smaller group of children would ask why did the sad duarian looked so sad. And again the Sad duarian said, I will tell you when your §0older.And§0 the children would wait.\n\nThe children was much older and was fewer, this time it there was only 5 more children. And as you know it the children would ask the getting old Sad duarain the same question. And again the Sad duarain said I shall tell you when your older.§0\n\nNow this time almost all of the children was adopted, leaving one grown up child. And he had said the question again. Why are do you look so sad to the Sad Duarain. The sad duarian was about to say why he was sad, but then died.§0\n§0\n§0The end§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0\n§0    A Random Story§0\n§0       -By no one§0\n§0         Important§0\n§0\n§0\n§0-------------------\n\n'§0\n§0§o     The shingles rattle as the rain drips down from the skies onto them, The moon shimmering some white light across them. Window sills creak as the old abandoned cabin shifts. Pine trees rustle as gentle winds pass through their leaves.§0\n\n.§0§o A man bolts out of the forest's treeline with a humanoid figure slung over his shoulder, he makes a break for the cabin. A trio bursts out of the forest after them., They wear masks of white with hoods of burgundy. The fleeing man smashes into the-\n\n-§0§ocabin, straight through the door into the darkness. The trio had swiflty made their way infront of the cabin, Shortly lighting up a torch, cautiously walking inside one by one, They had found no sign of the pair at first glance when walking inside.\n\n-", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "3100 minas worth of Windswept staffs, 70 mina each.§0\n§0\n§0 Your Friend,§0\n§0             Atturi§0\n§0\n§0P.s: I finally got kicked out of the ranch§0\n§0for stealing a chicken", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Harold Switzers Medical lessons§0\n§0------------------§0\n§0Lesson 1: I will welcome the students and give them a breif of the term ''Medical''§0\n§0And then i will show them how to put on a bandage.§0\n§0Lesson 2: I will tell the students about how to make some basic §0\n§0hea-\n\nlthy foods, then later telling them to get in pairs and make one themselves.§0\n§0Lesson3: Time fot the hard stuff, This time i will give the students some starter money, Then allowing them to buy ingeridnets for a healthy, nutruitious meal.§0\n§0Lesson 5: Ass-\n\nement for the end of the term, They will be given 1 day to complete a medical task, This could include: Making a Whole meal on your own, Holding my hospital for one day and much more!\n\nStudents: Nathan§0\n§0§§0\n§0           NOTES§0\n§0\n§0House 13 is Tubsi's house§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Eloh'ra Rohkea", "§bEloh'ra", "Eloh'ra Rohkea,\nRaven Druid\n\n\"Keep in mind that the devil was once an angel.\"\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nGrass crackled and sloshed as heavy, worn feet plodded through the swamp lands.\n\nThe sky was cloudless and the summer sun beat on the back of the figure that continued to stride through the thick mud.\n\nWrithing in pain and attempting to take yet another sluggish step, the Mali'ame would close her eyes, exhaling deeply before opening them to yet again the true setting she would stride in.\n\nShe would would look around, her eyes getting lost in the\n\nmovements of the flowers that sway gently within the the wind, falling instantly to the canvas beneath her.\n\nThe silence that stood before her would be the loudest in the setting; few chirps would echo to quickly trail off as the corpse would come to\n\na halt. The figure would be surrounded by a few smaller creatures; they would squawk loudly, their sounds strained as the smaller of the group would stew a panicked temper, beginning to circle the air around the now curled figure that would mainting her\n\nposition; the scene would become angered once again, frustration overpowering any emotion those around the limp body would feel. \n\nTheir screams would echo again as the remaining ravens would accompany the rest of the flock, circling\n\nEloh'ra as to aid her in some way.\n\nDespite being bombarded with constant paining visions, introducing an overwhelming feeling of fear, Eloh'ra would look to the blazing sky, heat lines would dance before her until her gaze would be\n\ngreeted by a sight more disturbing than her inevitable fate.\n\nTowering over her, a man chuckling loudly at the sight he would be witnessing; his eyes narrowing as if examining the entirity of Eloh'ra's existence.\n\nAs her vision would begin to darken,\n\na sudden blaze of orange flame would shoot across Eloh'ra's remaining window of sight.\n\nA shrill scream would erupt from within her parched lips as fire engulfs both her body and face. The flaming elf's hands relinquished their grip on her staff as she\n\nwould sink quietly to both knees before collapsing face first into the marsh. As Eloh'ra would slip into her final slumber, a slight smile crept on the man's worn face.\n\nThe man would pause for a few moments to observe any signs of breathing, ready to\n\nsink in another spell if necessary. Satisfied that his foe was truly unconsious, he strenuously would move the elf's weight atop of him. \n\nHe would slowly stand and begin to whisper few of many words into the Mali'ame's ears.\n\nYards away, a petite figure clothed in similarly dirty pants and a weathered shirt would emerge from behind a tree. A soft, feminine voice would speak. \n\n\"An' if she'd a listen to you, there'd be one less 'round here.\"\n\n\nSince this event, as related by many whom had the pleasure to witness such, Eloh'ra has chosen to follow other paths. \n\nMany choose to speak that spells were cast upon her while others tell the tales of the offering of Dark Arts\nto her.\n\n\nHer where-abouts are currently unknown to all but her closest friends and we are simply to await what is to become of the once titled,\n\n§sRaven Druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("[!] A letter.", "§bEloh'ra Rohkea", "Dear Illithri,§0\n§0\n§0By the time you are reading this, I will be somewhere where one could not possibly find me.§0\n§0\n§0I've come to the sudden realization that I do not only need to find myself but my strengths and weaknesses, alone.\n\nI plead you not look for me nor be saddened by the event for as I will be back soon.§0\n§0\n§0This will give me the change to finally meet myself and discover what I want from the current journey I am partaking in.§0\n\nI will be back in time for evaluation and wish you not great joy, but love too for as you deserve it.§0\n§0\n§0Within this crate, there are letters to every other person who means the world to me. I wish you for to gift them these with no wording of what's\n\ninside for as it is a personal message to each who recieves this.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0With much love,§0\n§0- Eloh'ra Rohkea", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Undead Tissue is turned to ash when exposed to fire.§0\n§0Living tissue bubbles and burns, until it reaches bone.§0\n§0When fire touches wood it spreads, it does so naturally and almost as if by instinct.§0\n§0Living Animals are very burnable.\n\nFire does have counters though, Earth will extinguish flames, water also. But it seems like Objects from the Nether are resistant to fire. If objects have wood in them then they seem to have decreased resistance to the fire.\n\nHowever pure elements that are resistant to fire are in fact much more resistant\n\nDay 1 of the Fire Island. Ash Fills the air and covers everything in thick soot. Fungus and charcoal cover the land, and the rumbling of a voclano can be heard in the distance. Im wondering what the ruins of this great civilization will bring.\n\nIt seems to enact pyromancy, it takes much focus, you need to clear your mind and channel the void. And bring something out, both from the void and from with in yourself.\n\nFire itself seems to be almost a raw form of energy, not quite lightning, but still it has similar character istics. Both jump to other substances and try to spread, both seem to have a life to them, and bot seem to happen because of friction.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Imperial Orb", "§bXor'Purdal", "Dearest Emperor Of Orenia. It has come to my notice that i have stumbled upon what seems to be The Imperial Orb. I, being the good soul i am, am willing to return it to you, for a fee. I'd be happy to discuss this with you later.", ""),
        StaticBook("Merchants Handbk", "§bJulius Weston", "The Merchant's§0\n§0       Handbook§0\n§0===================§0\n§0\n§0 by:§0\n§0      Julius Weston\n\nTOC§0\n§03.......................................Basics6................Things§0 to Know§0\n§010...................................Method19..........................................Tips\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nThe Basics:§0\n§0\n§0Merchanting is a skill. Unlike others, it does not require strong arms or a suit of armor. But rather a silver tongue. One capable of painting pictures with words alone. §0\n§0\n\nMerchanting is about buying a product for cheap and selling it for a higher price. Or we are also known as distributors. Taking ones product and selling it for them. Charging them a small fee for our services.\n\nThings to know:§0\n§0\n§0There are sets of questions you should ask yourself before venturing out and trying to sell your product.§0\n§0\n§0Supply - Can I get this product for cheaper than I can sell it?\n\nCan I sell this? Would I pay minas for this?§0\n§0\n§0Demand - Who would want this product? Why would they want this product? When would they want this product?§0\n§0\n§0All these questions are important. For instance, you don't\n\nwant to buy 1000 logs for 1 apiece and expect them to sell at 2 apiece the next day. You are now sitting on your investment. This is a slow investment. But if I knew a new settlement needed spruce logs, maybe I should head there and try to sell them.\n\nAlways ask yourself, \"Would I pay for this?\" before buying an item to sell. It's hard to sell a product that you don't even want.\n\nThe Method:§0\n§0\n§0Engage§0\n§0Introduce§0\n§0The Sale§0\n§0\n§0This 3 step process has worked for me multiple times. It's all about engaging the customer first. Get to know them.\n\n1. Engage§0\n§0\n§0First off, you must engange the customer. Start off with a friendly hello and introduce yourself, ask them how they are doing and maybe about a recent event. Sometimes this will give you a clue on what sort of items they\n\nwould be interested in. This is a very, very important step and should not be overlooked. Be sure not to introduce your product from the start.§0\n§0\n§0Ease into it.\n\n2. Introduce§0\n§0\n§0Now, we introduce the product we want to sell them. But not like its just another ordinary item. It has to have fluff. Get creative from its origin, history, make, or even special abilities.\n\nTrying to sell an apple might be hard. But an apple that can grow your hair back? That might sell. §0\n§0\n§0A simple rose for a holiday gift? Or how about a rose plucked from the highest peak in all of Vailor. §0\n§0\n§0It's all about in the\n\ndescription. §0\n§0\n§0Fluffier the better.\n\n3. The Sale§0\n§0\n§0Now comes the time to announce the price. There are many ways to get creative with this as well. First off know the value of your item. Now you have to make it seem like they are getting the best deal in town.\n\nYou could compare the quality of your product to that of your competitor. §0\n§0\n§0You could tell them that the product usually goes for more and tell them they are getting a steal.§0\n§0\n§0You could play the pity card and tell them\n\nyou need to sell it or ______. §0\n§0\n§0There is always the straight up deal. A haggleable price is sometimes the best way to go. §0\n§0\n§0The more creative, the better!\n\nTips and Tricks:§0\n§0\n§0The more people you talk to per day, the higher chance you have to sell your product!§0\n§0\n§0Never burn bridges. They might want a product from you in the future!\n\nCreate the want! Cater your product to the needs of the customer! Do what it takes to make a sale!§0\n§0\n§0Interact! Actually focus on the people and not just about selling your product. It will make things much less awkward and much more smooth!\n\n\n§0 Thanks for Reading!§0\n§0\n§0\n§0 I hope to see other§0\n§0 succesful merchants§0\n§0 out there!§0\n§0\n§0\n§0 ~Julius Weston", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "To Mira Sansya,§0\n§0\n§0\"You are the only lady I have ever was able to hold a conversation with without the lass walking off, For that I thank you.\"§0\n§0\n§0\"Remember the days When Mylas was only but a guard and not a Mayor? Going around\n\ngiving out tours, We thought he was insane, Ah, those were the days.\"§0\n§0\n§0\"Only recently Have we met again, We've both been on our seperate paths, Mine had not turned into something so desirable. Ive yet to hear what\n\nyou yourself have done in your Adventures, Other than trying to help unfortunate souls like Sula, Oh, and by the way always word your sentences with clarity, For there were two meanings to that sentence about Finding a priest\"\n\n\"I have told you of my involvement in the burning of the Mayors office, And to you and to you only i will try my best to Explain the Truthful story with Clarity, So I shall now begin, It started around the Monks docks on a sunny day, I had Found Mylas,\n\nand talked to him a little bit, during this I had taken a few drugs and some alchohol, Then Mylas had told me to come with me to Felson, Later that day we had split up, i had gone into the Mayors office and Leaned against the support beam as to where the\n\nFire originated, When Mylas had come into the mayors office I Unclipped my sheath from my belt. Had it in my left hand pommel facing mylas, I had taken a step toward mylas and tripped on the rug, The sword flung from my hand at a speed a few feet to\n\nMylas's Right, I was on the floor, and crawling toward the sword which had landed upon the rug between me and Mylas, I had gotton to the sword and raised myself, holding the sword, I had flicked off its sheath and backed off when i heard shouting§0\n\ncoming from the entrance, Mylas had his back to it, Sam and Toe had come into building seeing me weilding the sword I had my sword lowered as I backed toward the pole earlier, Sam was trying to calm me down, Which I was already, Toe had aked mylas if\n\nhe should kill me, Mylas had stated that I was his best friend aswell, Then they had left me and sam Alone after going upstairs to retrive some things, I had talked to Sam a bit and told him we had no Quarell, he asked for me to sheath my sword which I§0\n\ncould not do since the sheath was on the other side of the room, so he slid it over to me, I sheathed my sword and reclipped the sheath to my belt, He asked if we were okay now, I responded with I guess after placing my hand behind my back\n\nand rubbing a flint and steel together, this had created the spark for the Blaze, I suspect why the fire spread quite fast it the wood is quite old and dry, When the fire had erupted I had leapt forward and sam helped me get up, We got out of the Building\n\nCoughing, I forgot to mention that I had tried to slap Sam a few times when he got too close when calming me.§0\n§0\n§0When we had exited the building a crowd of people had emerged and chipped in to remove the fire from existance by forming a\n\nfire brigade, Carrying buckets from the water and empty back to the water, A few people such as Nathan. Who would later Question Sam and I. Another showed up to help interrogate.\"§0\n§0\n§0\"There is more to this Than I have said. For it has not happened yet-\n\nDue to the fact Ive not been interrogated once more\"\n\n*Three pages have been torn out, one almost completely, A small sliver of paper remains, it is labeled:§0\n§0\n§0'Courtship offer and little love Poems'*\n\n\"So, ive decided to tear out those pages... its a little awkward... may We just go on a date or something? Red rose day is coming up\"§0\n§0\n§0\"Oh, and please accept this white tulip as an apology if I have brought any distraught\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "THEY WILL DIE§0\n§0\n§0Big Red (KiiNg_Xx_)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=<@>=-§0\n§0         E.Twoore§0\n§0\n§0             [!]§0\n§0A simple leatherbound book with a depiction of a strand of wheat on the cover and signed with the initals §0\n§0            E.T\n\n      The Deep Cold§0\n§0         7th 1565§0\n§0\n§0Managed to find a way into the old Kellian bunker in Courland and found a nice dagger there made of Aurum and some of my old stuff.\n\n  The Grand Harvest§0\n§0        10th 1567§0\n§0\n§0I heard an explosion in Felsen. when i walked in town there was a commotion at the church becouse some culprits blew the Bell to smitherines.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I've started to wade deeper into the water,§0\n§0\n§0I've started to climb the tree. §0\n§0\n§0The ocean waves, as they recede from the shore, gently pull me deeper.§0\n§0\n§0The whispers' songs are nearly promises\n\nOf something that could be. §0\n§0\n§0But I know if I act too reckless,§0\n§0I'll get lost within the waves,§0\n§0\n§0I'll lose my footing within the branches,§0\n§0and lose that melody.\n\nSo I move very slow,§0\n§0\n§0and go one branch at a time;§0\n§0and brace myself for the waves,§0\n§0\n§0That will meet me in the sea.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Within the mainland, Katherine was born to a nobleman and a handmaiden.§0\n§0\n§0Her mother did not last long, and so when the young Katherine was orphaned, she was placed into the care of her uncle, who shipped her off to Ulmsbottom.\n\nThere in Ulmsbottom she stayed happily, content as can be; however, Ulmsbottom is no friendly isle.§0\n§0\n§0Ulmsbottom is an isle filled to the brim with swampland, where none but the insane go, a grey place filled with muck.\n\nThe coasts sport tall cliffs, and are dotted with tiny villages and independent holdfasts.§0\n§0\n§0It's said that jackals live within the swamps, an enemy far-worse to the traveler than a generic hound.\n\nThese predators lurk in the swamps, but at times emerge, raiding and feasting upon the livestock of the scattered Ulmsbotter villages.§0\n§0\n§0The jackals, according to Katherine, are worthless - their pelts grimy, their meat unedible.\n\nAs well within the swampland of the Ulmsbotter Isle are rumored spirits.§0\n§0\n§0\"A tavern wench once sat me down on one of her slow days, told me the story of some cocksure boy who thought himself able to tame the swamps.\n\nSure enough he brought home jackals by the cart if they had been terrorizing shepards, and folks said he made enough coin to feed a family on contracts to slay other beasts.§0\n§0\n§0One day there was a proper outcry, saying that the blacksmith's boy had\n\ngone missing in some ruin. The hearsay reached the boy mentioned earlier, and he, without even knowing the blacksmith boy's name, immediately volunteered to find him - seeking fame and fortune.§0\n§0\n§0But.. that was it. The boy never showed his face again,\n\nneither. But the peasants had a good time looting the boy's home for the coin he had made.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "My deepest admiration  to John Sigismund...§0\n§0\n§0You are the manliest of men, dear John. Your words, your grace, your walk: it all makes my womanhood tremble. Please, I want you. I will let you do whatever you want with me. -Catherine", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-Jay wants shopfront§0\n§0-Wants arrangement, not want to pay§0\n§0-Work for Mylas in exchange for shop§0\n§0-Jay/cattle man§0\n§0-New shopfronts across from building, 1 storefront for Jay in exchange for labor§0\n§0-For now, a stall§0\n§0-Jay agrees§0\n§0-Apparentl\n\nMylas needs:§0\n§0\n§0-felsen transportation act§0\n§0-felsen recruitment act§0\n§0\n§0transport act:§0\n§0lords of cart/boat destinations are to pay 300 minas for right of travel; same punishments as in felsen tax code\n\nrecruitment:§0\n§0recruitment within felsen by noble lords & etc not based in felsen is forbidden, fine of 250 minas etc", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I'm in mid battle help", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Law Waver§0\n§0This Elf Vlad Voidsong is pardoned from these laws§0\n§0-Wearing a mask§0\n§0-Slaying undead§0\n§0-Fighting in a city§0\n§0-Carrying weapons out", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "hello im Philip my dad gilbert and my pal samuel me and my pal are on the run because we are wanted men", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Journal of Baldwin§0\n§0\n§01548§0\n§09th of Grand Harvest§0\n§0\n§0I was welcomed by Ser Demetrios Palaiologos,§0\n§0and his loving wife. My Hands lay ready, my feet stay steady. Tomorrow starts a new day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "e", "")
    )

    private fun _VAILOR_7(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Goal: Collectively work together to end the end of the reign of Bandit Warlords.§0\n§0Potential gains:§0\n§0Oren maintains control over", ""),
        StaticBook("Meteor Messages", "§bAengoth", "--- so the tomes -- ----- descended ---- ---- ----- -- boon -- [!] rest unseen\n\n---- ------- Dragons --- ----- --- ------- Fire\n\nCast gaze asray -- ------- claws\n\nFell ---- Fell ----\n\n----- --- lost to fire\n\n---- --- need ---- --- dire\n\n----- slumber ----- --- die\n\nRecorded on the 16th of Snow's Maiden, 1554, by Aengoth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Meteor Messages", "§bAengoth", "--- so the tomes -- ----- descended ---- ---- ----- -- boon -- \n\n---- ------- Dragons --- ----- --- ------- Fire\n\nCast gaze asray -- ------- claws\n\nFell ---- Fell ----\n\n----- --- lost to fire\n\n---- --- need ---- --- dire\n\n----- slumber ----- --- die\n\nRecorded by Aengoth on the 16th of Snow's Maiden, 1554.", ""),
        StaticBook("Paragon Hiebe", "§bAengoth", "Hiebe, the Father of Mages. Throughout dwarven history many key figures amongst our kin have been proclaimed our fabled Paragons, those who stand above the rest and worked to create the very foundations of our society today. While the young may only hear\n\nof them they do not share the same wisdom that us elder dwarves still retain from our first hand experience. We found our best of the beet and we found them to be fitting of the title Paragon. When you think of the core group of dwarves who shaped our\n\nsociety you think of Valen the Wordsmith, Omithiel the Builder, Kjell Ireheart the Dragon Slayer. These threee were without a doubt the foundation of our society. Yet one amongst them has been left out. I, Aengoth Grandaxe, do now hereby proclaim that\n\nHiebe Irongut has been forgotten by the Archbishops and High Prophets of the past. Kjell had his warriors. Omithiel had his builders. Valen had his writers. Hiebe had his mages. Hiebe has been responsible for either the first hand or second hand teaching\n\nof nearly all the dwarven mages we have come to know. WHile many dwarves may be skeptics concerning magic and distrust its users we can not steal this credit from Hiebe Irongut. He was one of the four pillars of our society and we must rightfully\n\nrecognize his actions as that of the work of Ogradhad whom used Hiebe to spread the knowledge of magic to our people. Hiebe Irongut has earned his position as the fourth pillar and has earned the title \"Paragon Hiebe Irongut, the Father of Mages\".\n\nWritten by Aengoth Grandaxe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "weekly mission report§0\n§0\n§0You will be assigned a weekly mission and you are to write down what happeneed etc.. missions vary, some examples are:§0\n§0Patrolling the city§0\n§0Patrolling the Palace Gates§0\n§0etc.§0\n§0Write down what happened that week\n\nand give it to the Schenecal", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Will pay wizard guys for a brewing stand§0\n§0\n§0that seems like something a wizard would make§0\n§0\n§0it's urgent§0\n§0\n§0don't have money but will pay with resources§0\n§0-Brandon, the guy with the roof garden", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Hello reader,§0\n§0My name is Alex Trekwars and I am writing this book in hopes of joining the Library of Dragur.  I have been wondering for days on what to write about and I have finally decided to depict my journey across the land of vailor.  Might as well\n\nstart the story where it began, at the library.  I was wondering the library hopeing to be inspired to write a story, and then I had the idea.  \"I will write about my journies across the land!\" I exlaimed.  I decided to begin my journey where it all began\n\n, at cloud temple.  I ate my fourten cookie I had on me and this is the furtune I recieved.  \"You will meet a suculent dark elven maiden.\"  Of course at the time I had my eyes set on my adventure, not listening to silly fortunes.  So I set off on my\n\njourney to cloud city.§0\n§0\n§0End of Chapter 1\n\nChapter 2§0\n§0\n§0As I arrived at Cloud Temple I could feel the cool sea wind against my face.  Instantly I noticed there were not as many peole present as there normally were.  I then ran into a younge Dark elf, of course some would think that the\n\nfortune had come true, I just think it is a coincidence.  As i approached the ships I stood puzzled, I had still not decided where I wanted to begin my journey.  I finally decided that I would board an elven ship and travel to the land of the elves.  On\n\nmy way to the ship though a strange occurence happend, it began to snow, it was so beautiful, but I had fears that the sea wouldn't be so pleasent.  I then found myself at a cross roads, do I decide to travel to the wood elves, or to another evish branch\n\nthat I do not remember.  I had decided on the wood elves as I had never met one before..\n\nChapter 3§0\n§0\n§0As I left the elven boat I entered a mystical forest that was beautiful.  The falling snow doubled the beauty tremendously.  I began on a path through the woods, the path wound like a snake, never heading\n\nin a specific direction.  But I was polite to the wood elves and I decided to stay on the path until it led to a city.  As I excited the forest I found myself in front of a beatiful castle which I assume belongs to the wood evles.  There I met a woman elf\n\nwho critisized me saying that I am not a far folk because of my skin color.  I ignored her of course, proud of my history and continued to the castle.  Once I had reached the gate I noticed it was locked.  I had hoped there would be a guard on duty but\n\nthere wasn't one at the time.  I decided that I would stay at the gate until one appeard.  I finally decided to find my own way into the city.  I followed the path back down to the area in front of the castle where I found a dirt path leading into the\n\nwoods.  In the woods I found the home of the Druids, sadle I met none of them.  The rest of the adventure was me wandering throughout the woods until finally I made it willow hollow.  I am writing this chapter sitting inside the captain chambers of a ship\n\nI will be taking the ship wherever it goes in the mourning.§0\n§0\n§0End of chapter\n\nChapter 4§0\n§0\n§0The boat was a complete bust.  The boat sailed out to the middle of the ocean where I assume the captain had gotten confused and had to turn around.  I have decided to travel back to the wood elves, see if anything else happens.\n\nI have returned to the docks and have noticed another boat docked next to the one I took.  From what I see I can infer it leads to the realm of the dark elves.  I have decided for the sake of this book to travel thre.  As i left the boat I was greeted by\n\nan impressive castle.  However there apears to again be no one to let me in at this time so I must travel somewhere else for this book.§0\n§0\n§0End of chapter 4\n\nChapter 5§0\n§0\n§0I have entered a desert city that I no not the name.  The cities arcitecture is beautiful and there are many different species here.  I hope that I can make contact with one of them and hopefully get their view on the city.\n\nAs I am traveling the city I have run into 2 men, 1 of ork, 1 of far folk who apear to be about ready to fight.  I back away with fear of getting caught in the cross fires.  Thankfully no fight happens and peace is held.  Might as well talk about a\n\nDifferent topic.  Quickly just to say I saw a genius who got himself stuck in a hole.§0\n§0\n§0END OF chapter\n\nChapter 6§0\n§0\n§0I have finished any buissness I have had in the city and have decided to return to the Library of Dragur.  On my way to the Library I found a mighty steed, but sadly I have no place for him to stay so I released him\n\nInto the wild.  I would quickly like to appologize to anyone who may be reading this because I am treating this more like a journal, writing about my travels.  Now that that is out of the way I might as well tell you about my most recent journey.  I had\n\ndecided that for the sake of this book that I would travel to the land of the orcs in hope of traveling all the way through.  I took the boat from cloud temple to the land of the orcs.  As I approached the gate my heart started beating extremly fast.\n\nI was filled with so much fear, but for the sake of knowledge I pushed forward.  I remember 3 distinct castles within the orc kingdom, a wooden castle that is located right next to the gate, a large castle like building located next to some kind of volcan\n\nand an entire castle that is suspended over a casm.  It was an awe inspireing site, of course because of my fear I did not push closer to the castle.  The castle itself was suspended by chains that held it to the sides of the casm.  Finally I had reached\n\nthe end of the desert where a bridge was located, I was so relived that I had finally gotten out of the desert without any problems.  Right as I approached the bridge i heard a voice. \"OI!\"  My heart skipped a beat.  I turned around and say a massive orc\n\nonly about 50 blocks away from me.  My legs took over my body and started sprinting down the bridge.  \"OI! WAIT!\"  Screamed the orc as he chased after me.  The bridge was extremely long, but I remember it as a blur of stone.  In the distance I could see\n\nsome kind of object that looked like a gate.  \"Please Please PLEASE don't let the gate be closed\" I pleaded.  As I got closer I noticed that, yes, it was closed.  \"Dang IT!\"  I screamed.  I turned around and saw the orc a couple dozen blocks behind\n\nme.  This was where I finally decided, was I going to stand up like a warrior and fight, or was I going to be a mouse and run.  \"Im A MOUSE!\"  I screamed.  I jumped into the water and began swimming around the island that the gate surrounded.  Once I\n\njumped into the water I don't remember what the orc did, I presume that he chased after me but I never stopped to look behind me.  Even after I reached shore I ran all the way to the capital felson.§0\n§0\n§0End of Chapter 6\n\nChapter 7§0\n§0\n§0I do not know why I am writing this like a book, this has now turned into a biography, a journal of sorts.  Anyway, when I woke up this mourning I was greeted by a strange man who speeks about a scarlet\n\nking, If this is what I think it is then I must prepare myself for a fight.  Even though this man is probably not a threat it doesn't hurt to be prepared.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Felsen Log Book§0\n§0\n§0by-Alex Trekwars (Watchman)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I can't go on anymore.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Lopkaea", "MaxGemini", "I can't go on without you. You were all I had left in the world. All my friends have left me, my family have died. Without you, I have no reason to continue to live.", ""),
        StaticBook("bEeLee bUB", "§bFarmer Billy Bob", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Strange metal item that induces visions. §0\n§0Depicts a blank black world with doors. Portal like doors.§0\n§0A constant stairing of white eyes. Metal possibly part of a mask.§0\n§0after 10-minuets drives person crazy. Pass out wake with headache.\n\nVison repeates. But this time you can stay as long as you want to.§0\n§0Visions bring up memories. Above cults. Distorts memorys.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Let's play a game, Vlad. Each book you find will contain a clue. The clue will lead you to a head, with another clue next to it. Let's see if your worthy!§0\n§0CLUE 1§0\n§0Roses are red§0\n§0Violets are blue§0\n§0This is where you heal them§0\n§0This is where you work too\n\n-The Night Fox", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Catherine, please hold your heart close§0\n§0Do your best, don't make a sound§0\n§0I'm trying hard to listen, to the humming of your blood§0\n§0\n§0Catherine how'd you know that's a lie§0\n§0My blood is toneless still§0\n§0I couldn't keep silent, if could\n\nkeep you distant§0\n§0\n§0But when you're close to me, §0\n§0I start to think I might just falter§0\n§0You think I can't just close my eyes,§0\n§0But I can§0\n§0\n§0But I've been thinking, what if I wasn't right\n\nSo I go and start fight, with someone I don't know§0\n§0\n§0And he asks why I'm thinking of you, as I knock out all his teeth§0\n§0\n§0I don't think he understands, how you feel to me§0\n§0\n§0Catherine", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0         Journal of§0\n§0\n§0Catherine Francesca,§0\n§0\n§0      Imperial Princess§0\n§0\n§0            Of Oren\n\n12th of Malin's Welcome, 1550.§0\n§0\n§0I wish I didn't feel so sad when no one was around. §0\n§0\n§0I miss Charles a lot, even after a whole year of him being gone. §0\n§0\n§0I wonder what would've happened if he didn't die.\n\nSometimes I have dreams that I'm a little girl again, running around the palace, and he's always at the table by the throne, writing something. §0\n§0\n§0I remember once when we were small, he said he composed music. I never got to hear any of it.\n\n20th of Malin's Welcome, 1550.§0\n§0\n§0I don't know where to begin with this!§0\n§0\n§0Tim of Locklear was here again. We recited our poetry back and forth, and he read some of my other unfinished poems, too.\n\nThough, that was a bit awkward because I am very well aware how bad they are. §0\n§0\n§0Right, so, after he left I encountered this very strange man, who's face was hidden behind his knight's helmet. He followed me inside, and I was about to run back /out/side\n\nwhen Beelzebub showed up (thank goodness)! §0\n§0\n§0Whenever I see Beelzebub, I instantly want to tell him so many things, but I can never think of /what/ to talk about! It's so odd.§0\n§0\n§0Anyway. I was about to talk with him in the study, but just as\n\nwe were beginning to exchange words, Tim came back; along with my sister Eleanor and her (more than) friend James. §0\n§0\n§0She had been drinking, and was terribly woozy; James had to carry her upstairs into our room!§0\n§0\n§0She kept calling my name, and once I got\n\nthere to our room, she was laying on the floor with her arms outstretched, in the air!§0\n§0\n§0According to James, she only had one, small flask of wine. And while I think that's a bit strange, I've never had any alcohol myself, so perhaps I shouldn't\n\nmake poor assumptions.§0\n§0\n§0Oh, and I almost forgot to mention! Before I even went up there, I made the unfortunate discovery that Tim can be a very grumpy individual. He treated Beelzebub very rudely, which is quite disappointing, to say in the least.\n\nBut, back to Eleanor. The knight then came after us, demanding we open the door. He put up a very hostile front, which frightened me quite a bit, so I refused to let him in at all. But eventually, Eleanor was the one to swing open the doors. §0\n\nThe knight /then/ demanded Eleanor drink some curious mix of water and herbs, but James refused to give it to her, and she didn't seem very partial towards the  idea, either.§0\n§0\n§0But finally James, Eleanor, and Jaromir (who was sleepy too)\n\nall fell fast asleep at our bed. §0\n§0\n§0It turns out this mystery knight isn't all that bad; him and Beelzebub talked for a decent amount of time. I wish I remembered more about what the knight said about himself, though.\n\nOh, but okay okay! Here's the best bit.§0\n§0\n§0After the odd knight left, Beelzebub and I finally had a chance to talk.§0\n§0And he had an interesting proposition! §0\n§0He suggested I start writing more letters to John; he got the feeling John was starting to\n\nfeel down about himself again; which is certainly not what I'd want to happen!  Despite his bouts of anger, my brother is very good of heart.§0\n§0\n§0But then Beelzebub went on to say, that maybe eventually, writing all these letters would help convince\n\nmy brother to... let us get married!§0\n§0\n§0When he said that I couldn't believe it! He wants to marry me!§0\n§0\n§0In the past, Charlie, Eleanor, and Maude have said our social statuses would make it difficult, but...§0\n\nI don't care. I'm the youngest, so it shouldn't be as big of a deal, right?§0\n§0\n§0And I love Beelzebub dearly (even if he does have a funny name)!\n\n12th of the Grand Harvest, 1550§0\n§0\n§0The world stopped and everything is wrong.§0\n§0\n§0I think I'm dying.\n\n[The next several entries only contain a drawing of a happy face.]\n\n1st of Sun's Smile, 1550.§0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n2nd of Sun's Smile, 1550.§0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n5th of Sun's Smile, 1550.§0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n6th of Sun's Smile, 1550.§0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n8th of Sun's Smile, 1550.§0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n11th of Sun's Smile, 1550. §0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n21st of Sun's Smile, 1550. §0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n3rd of the Amber Cold, 1550§0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n9th of the Amber Cold, 1550.§0\n§0\n§0:)\n\n[This page is torn out completely.]\n\n21st of Malin's Welcome, 1551.§0\n§0\n§0He died.\n\n\n§0[Pages have been ripped out here.]\n\n12th of Sun's Smile, 1551.§0\n§0\n§0I think God answered my prayers.§0\n§0\n§0Somehow John came back, completely unharmed.  §0\n§0\n§0I'd write more, but I hurt my hands a while ago, and they ache sometimes when I write.\n\n10th of Malin's Welcome, 1555.§0\n§0\n§0I haven't written in this in such a long time!§0\n§0Quite honestly, I thought I lost this journal. But in our recent move to the new palace, I found it again!§0\n§0\n§0My room is very tiny, but I'm happy enough\n\nwith it. I am a little jealous of my sister, Eleanor, though. Her room has a walk in closet!§0\n§0\n§0I suppose that's the privelege of being older, though.§0\n§0\n§0Until then, I shall settle for the smaller room beside my brother's,\n\nand enjoy the view from the window it provides.§0\n§0\n§0While I don't quite have the energy to go on and write about EVERYTHING that's happened since I've last written, I will say a few things.\n\nBeelzebub's been very sad. I try to help, but I don't know if my words are reaching him.§0\n§0\n§0To be honest, I don't know if my words are reaching anyone, anywhere. Very often I try to speak with my brother, but John is always so distracted with meetings and\n\nconferences... it's really disappointing sometimes that I can hardly get a word in edgewise. §0\n§0\n§0And even if I /did/ get the oppurtunity to try and speak during one of those office meetings, I fear my uncle's glare so much I'm too afraid to say anything.\n\nBother. Maybe I should try to regain that teensy bit of bravery I used to have (or, at least I think I had?)§0\n§0\n§0Maybe not stick my tongue out at Uncle Adrian like I did when I was a child, but perhaps I should at least try to defend myself.\n\n...and§0 the people I care about, too, for that matter.\n\n8th of the First Seed, 1555.§0\n§0\n§0I don't like being twenty.§0\n§0\n§0It seems like I'm supposed to be incredibly mature, incredibly grown up when I've not the slightest idea how to be.\n\nAs if I'm not allowed to cry, and I have to know everything. §0\n§0\n§0I don't mean to complain, but recently it's harder to smile. I've done what I usually do, and just try smiling anyway; as corny as that sounds, but it doesn't help as much\n\nas I'd like to think it does.§0\n§0\n§0These words will stay within the confines of this journal though; I don't see any good in telling anyone about it all. Especially Beelzebub, who's dealing with his own feelings of sadness.\n\nI don't think John would quite understand it, either. §0\n§0\n§0I don't know. I'll think of something to make me feel better.\n\n9th of the Grand Harvest, 1558.§0\n§0\n§0I don't worry about smiling a lot anymore. §0\n§0For a long time I just smiled through everything, but... I guess I got tired of it.§0\n§0\n\n9th of the Amber Cold, 1561.§0\n§0\n§0In the last few years I've come to the resolve to be truthful. One hundred percent honest, all the time. I suppose after years of feigning cheerfulness (or, as my brother calls it, 'pluckiness'),\n\nI've no longer the stomach for it. Not to say that I'm always frowning; at least I think I'm not. §0\n§0I certainly never wish to seem rude, or cross with someone, so I still make an effort to be polite as possible. I hope that's a decent way to go about this\n\nwhole business, or I find myself being incredibly disliked.§0\n§0\n§0Though now that John has asked me about my change in behaviour, I feel a pang of guilt regarding it. I found myself worried that he was disappointed.§0\n§0I'd ask him, but that'd only make\n\nthings uncomfortable, surely? Especially if I've bound myself to an oath of honesty; I'd most likely have to admit to feeling awkward in the first place, yes? Hm. I'll just avoid the conversation.§0\n§0At least I can still find some peace of mind\n\nsitting on the Felsen rooftops.\n\n16th of Malin's Welcome, 1563.§0\n§0\n§0I accidentally grew a fondness for someone I shouldn't.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0       Catherine§0\n§0         Francesca's§0\n§0\n§0             Collection§0\n§0\n§0                   of§0\n§0\n§0                Poems\n\nHis skin is like a sunset,§0\n§0\n§0As the stars begin to shine.§0\n§0\n§0The last golden rays of sunlight carress his  cheeks §0\n§0\n§0Like a  shower of warm kisses.\n\nHe is filled with such color, so many stars,§0\n§0\n§0I wish the world could see more§0\n§0\n§0Than just \"black\".§0\n§0\n§0                 *\n\nA girl with raven hair, with eyes like an olive branch.§0\n§0\n§0I thought she was a princess out of a fairytale, §0\n§0\n§0And her skin almost seemed to glitter like stardust.§0\n§0\n§0[This poem seems unfinished.]\n\nPalaces out of paragraphs;§0\n§0\n§0Each word, each syllable a singular brick. §0\n§0\n§0With the ink at your desk, you stack the bricks higher and higher, creating a maze for me to get lost in.§0\n§0                  *\n\n If I could paint,§0\n§0\n§0I'd paint you.§0\n§0\n§0I'd paint each strand of your hair,§0\n§0\n§0The curvature of your smile, the shine of your eyes.§0\n§0", ""),
