        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "THINGS TO LOOK OUT FOR IN THE TRIBAL FIGURE§0\n§0\n§0red mask, white lines (tribal fashion)§0\n§0\n§0access to Courland fields (could be there)§0\n§0\n§0black belt, §0\n§0\n§0stone/obsidian spear\n\nmad obsession WITH FIRE/BURNING!", ""),
        StaticBook("Kvaz Tax Token", "§bLerald Vyronov", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Introduction-§0\n§0Eja! This is a chronicle of the development of the Duchy of Carnatia in Vailor, which is written by Nikolas Kovachev, son of the reigning duke as of the time writing this, Jan Kovachev.\n\n1551-§0\n§0We have begun initial deconstructing of the town of Monteford, below my father's fortress. We hope to improve our efficiency as an Orenian province by building a newer one, aswell as show off my father's wealth.\n\n1552-§0\n§0We have near finished the destruction of Monteford, but we have decided to keep the church, and have built a wooden palisade around the land in the direct vicinity of our fortress. These shall protect our stables and supply wagons.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "weekly mission report§0\n§0\n§0You will be assigned a weekly mission and you are to write down what happened etc.. §0\n§0missions vary, some examples are:§0\n§0Patrolling the city§0\n§0Patrolling the Palace§0\n§0Gates§0\n§0etc.§0\n§0Write down what happened that week\n\nand give it to the Schenecal", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Vanir Levy Log§0\n§0\n§040 Iron Chestplates§0\n§030 Iron Leggings§0\n§024 Iron Helmets§0\n§027 Iron Boots§0\n§028 Iron Swords§0\n§02 Bluesteel Swords§0\n§07 Iron Warhammers§0\n§04 Iron Battleaxes§0\n§05 Iron Lances§0\n§07 Bows§0\n§04 Stacks of Arrows§0\n\n2 Studded Leather Helmets§0\n§02 Studded Leather Chestplates§0\n§03 Studded Leather Pants§0\n§01 Studded Leather Boots§0\n§03 Saddles§0\n§03 Chain Helmets§0\n§02 Chain Chestplates§0\n§02 Chain Leggings§0\n§02 Chain Boots§0\n\n1 Carbarum Warhammer§0\n§03 Diamond Blocks§0\n§058 Emerald Blocks§0\n§020 Iron Blocks§0\n§09 Stacks + 59 Iron Ingots§0\n§02 Stacks + 46 Emeralds§0\n§035 Diamonds§0\n§056 Flint Arrowheads§0\n§038 Blocks of Coal", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Vaillen Court Dissapearance§0\n§0\n§0Upon questioning the mayor about this dissapearance of Vaillen court, Mylas skedaddled. §0\n§0\n§0When broken into, a covered and isolated complex of housing lays in its absence.\n\nA pale tall elf was on the second floor, questioning us aggressively on how we got there, how we found out about it, etc. In impatience, I pointed my weapon at him and demanded his prompt arrest. Using his elven speed, he escaped our grasp. The suspect is\n\nstill wanted. §0\n§0\n§0Vaillen Court is now to be deconstructed into proper housing. §0\n§0\n§0The intentions of this operation remains a mystery, and a priority.§0\n\nInhabitants are as followed.§0\n§0(Locke & Lamora residency)§0\n§0\n§0Diari(Previously avoided questioning to be a frost witch)§0\n§0\n§0Brennus Ilessca(Previously avoided questioning to be a cult member\n\nPROPERTY PURCHASER/OWNER:§0\n§0\n§0Pikel Bouldshoulder§0\n§0\n§0The complex's intentions are to be assumed illegal. Residents evicted.§0\n§0\n§0Mayor and stated names to be questioned on intentions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Steward's Log\n\n1 Market Street§0\n§0Benkt Hungil§0\n§0Gold Corps Soldier§0\n§025 mina tax §0\n§0(ItzFrostyMoshi)§0\n§0[Active]\n\n2 Market Street§0\n§0Abrielle Solari§0\n§0Keep Chef§0\n§0Tax Exempt§0\n§0(Enyahs92)§0\n§0[Active]\n\n3 Market Street§0\n§0VACANT\n\n4 Market Street§0\n§0Simon§0 (IceWalker)§0\n§050 Mina Tax§0\n§0[Active]\n\n1 Pine Way§0\n§0Arthor Umberhall (Ragnqr)§0\n§0Rulf Grelot (StokedOff)§0\n§050 Mina Tax§0\n§0[Active]\n\n2 Pine Way§0\n§0Gold Corps Storage\n\n1 Mountain Path§0\n§0Boris§0 (Alvin3568)§0\n§050 Mina§0\n§0[Activity Check 7/16]\n\n2 Mountain Path§0\n§0Vacant\n\n3 Mountain Path§0\n§0Vacant§0\n\n4 Mountain Path§0\n§0Merric Oxworth§0 (_Gypsy)§0\n§050 Mina Tax§0\n§0[Active]\n\n5 Mountain Path§0\n§0Fe'Len Family§0\n§050 Mina tax§0\n§0\n§0(_Me_Zebra_)§0\n§0[Active]\n\nBlackwood Residence§0\n§0Vacant\n\nTower Property§0\n§0Nemir§0\n§0Tax Exempt\n\nVallberg Manor§0\n§0Katherine Vallberg§0\n§0Tax Exempt\n\nTax Records:§0\n§0Taxes to be collected on the Sun's Smile of each year beginning 1566.§0\n§0\n§01566: All exempt§0\n§01567: Some paid, unpaid evicted. New residents in town this year.§0\n§01568: Benkt paid, everyone else recieved warnings.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dear Steward,§0\n§0\n§0I am sorry for not paying taxes... My mother and father have dissapeared!§0\n§0I have been trying to earn money, but no one seems to care for children. I will try to pay them as soon as I can earn SOME money.§0\n§0From,§0\n§0Al Fe'len (ItzChar_)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day 01§0\n§0\n§0I was taken to the citadel. It was a very spooky and broken place. There I was taught the techniques of meditation.§0\n§0\n§0I am to travel and study the wind with a more in depth analysis.e\n\nDay 02§0\n§0\n§0I was taken to the citadel again. There terms of a pledge were discussed.§0\n§0\n§0In return for his protection and knowledge (forever) I am to remain loyal to him, obey his commands, and not court anyone\n\nhe does not see as a fit person.§0\n§0\n§0The pledge was made and sealed with a brand on the small of my back. I can not see it but I believe it is a small symbol.§0\n§0\n§0It hurt. I was more terrified of the word forever.§0\n\nDay 03§0\n§0\n§0I as taken to the top of a snow capped mountain. There I learned a little about magic. §0\n§0\n§0I felt magic that was apparently an illusion.§0\n§0\n§0My meditation is gettning better.\n\nDay 04§0\n§0\n§0I disagree with the conduct of my teacher. He makes advances to me that make me believe he has ulterior motives.§0\n§0\n§0We had an argument and he used air evocation to prevent me from leaving.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "YEAR ONE, GARIN'S                    RISE§0\n§0\n§0Garin was born incredibly poor,", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Rules for Zakari to remember:§0\n§01. Do not PK or attempt to PK Burkester§0\n§02. Do not roll up in Burkester's terf without speaking with him first or you may face one of the following punishment; pk, rape, pillage, and or death.\n\nReasons Why Burkester is a little bitch §0\n§01 hes a little bitch§0\n§02 fuck you joseph§0\n§03 nobody loves you§0\n§04 im sorry please don't kill me it's just a joke§0\n§0\n§0Signed TheRedPenguin\n\nPrepare for the D fucking piece of shit§0\n§0JOSEF COMES NOW", ""),
        StaticBook("Ho", "§bSammy \"Mungo\"", "How to be a Silvertongued Devil- By Mungo the Bandit.\n\nIn life you may come upon times where reaching for your sword may not be the most ideal way to go, you may not be the best fighter, or you simply can't speak for your life, hopefully, this guide of\n\nsorts may assist you in swindling, lying, persuading and overall being a great talker. Now, me being me, I was born with the natural talent of making people absolutely adore me, whether this was being brought up in a tevern or my mother being\n\nquite a social escort, I cannot say, but what I can say is that this skill of mine has gotten me out of many  tight situations and into many fair maidens' dreams. But, enough of me glamourizing myself, I'll try to keep this book short and to the point.\n\n1.\nBe as polite as can be without seeming as if you want to kiss someone's backside, being polite leads to people liking you, and even giving you free things such as minas and food.\n\n2.\nBe eccentric and posh with your words. This of course excludes Orcs, they will most likely cave your face in if you use anything more complicated than six letter words. Use words such as indeed, gent, gentleman, kind, fine and so on, this\n\nmay lead to some thinking you a pompous whoreson, but to others you will seem a much more upper class gent or lady than you actually are, helping you achieve your goals whether it be getting that promosion, lying, succesfully conning,\n\nor simply being all the talk at spiffing Balls.\n\n3.\nSeem lighthearted, relaxed and calm, the calmer and more lighthearted you are, the more it will rub off on whoever you're trying to swindle, leading them to dropping their guard, taking a liking of you, or simply another way to seem that\n\nyou have no idea why there's a dead body infront of you while you hold a bloody knife, you just found it there of course.\n\n4.\nBe kind, even if it might not be in your nature, seeming like a kind person will help you in many ways, tricking people, this will lead to you making unlikely allies, you'll have more sway to your word, and if it comes to a tavern brawl\n\neveryone will believe you when you say you didn't start it.\n\n5.\nLast, but not least, be charismatic, even if you're quite the reserved person, this will inspire those around you, and lead to people believing your word over others.\n\nAnd so, that ends my short guide to being a charming and cunning criminal such as myself, whether you use it for good or evil, is your choice, I was just bored in the corner of a tavern waiting for someone to play some blackjack.\n\n-Signed, Mungo, the Charming Bandit.", ""),
