        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dear Fe'Len Family,§0\n§0I have recieved your letter and recognized your time of need. You will not be required to pay taxes until you are of age. Please inform me if circumstances change and your parents return. Until then, if there is anything I can help you\n\nwith, please let me know. May God's blessings be upon you.§0\n§0\n§0    Best regards,§0\n§0      §0§oKatherine Vallberg§0\n§0§o       §0§oHead Steward", ""),
        StaticBook("((a rap))", "§bVolero Havenson", "Yo i want a big horse, yo i want a small horse, for police force, i want a paul blart mall horse. Make a album with the one an only Tim Mcgraw horse, sting you with a bee horse, saw you with a seahorse, passed you on the racecourse, products i will endors\n\nmy favorite play is G-Force, heh g-force, and all this time i'm  im just suckin' dick and doing dope, and if i aint shootin up then im in the back snorting coke. And yo if im a plant then im a bad seed Casue dawg all i really do is smoke big weed-\n\n(smoke big weed, smoke smoke, big weed!)§0\n§0It's me Kendrick Lamar im a big superstar and abadabada whoever you and this is my greatest verse and you worse than Fred Durst and when i get fed, boy, man i feel a thirst your goons are like tomatoes to me\n\ntoo soft every time i see 'em, gotta pick 'em off§0\n§0Eh-hey it's dr. dre and listen what i say you think this shit is just a game man i dont play. imma hit you on the head with my drea beats then imma open a restaurant call it Dre eats. Its really me\n\nmeanwhile im ganking, life taking, spanking, tanking, and climbing rankins my score composed by hans zimmer 5000 gold im bankin and its your man who did not ban hecarim i am thanking cause now he looks like titanics fuckin' sinking §0\n\n(here i go, fucking horse killing kids with no remorse. cause its me, fucking horse)§0\n§0they recognize my name questpls cause when i enter the lane it goes black and white and to the other hecarim wondering why he lost instead of taking teleport shoulda\n\ntook exhaust§0\n§0what do horses eat§0\n§0HAY§0\n§0what are horses feet§0\n§0CLAY§0\n§0who made this fuckin' beat§0\n§0DRE§0\n§0is this song complete?§0\n§0NEIGH§0\n§0(get it?)\n\nFuck you its me, horse skip the bullshit bring out the main course i walk up in the restaurant like a tour de force me and my wife are getting a divorce. She gets the house, i keep the Porsche that way i can run over that god damn whor(s)e\n\nfin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Readme", "§bKajara Anima Fortis", "Niceley done!\nSend a bird to\nKajara Anima Fortis\n(Hypersin_Gaming)\nTo have the chest removed!", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "§bUnknown", "[!] The handwriting looks rather messy, though the words are still readable.[!]§0\n§0\n§0*Get herbs!§0\n§0Elf's Hair Vine§0\n§0Drake's Tail§0\n§0Athin§0\n§0Metzli's Tangle§0\n§0\n§0Ask Ibar or Rose if they have Alabaster leaf.\n\n[!] On this page there is a sketch of a rather short tower made of stone, a little pond shimmers in the sunlight next to it.  Some tulips peak out through a light layer of snow near the water.[!]§0\n§0\n§0[!]In the same handwriting as page before reads, --\n\n-- \"Couldn't sleep, this dream was about him again.  It was the same night when he returned, though I wasn't able to do what I wanted.  Instead of me fleeing like I did when it was real I froze in fear as the door bursted open.  I couldn't do anything --\n\n-- but watch as he came closer.  Before he got into the doorway I woke up.\"[!]§0\n§0\n§0[!]The rest of the page is just sketches of several different types of herbs and flowers.  A few of the lower sketches looked a little smudged, thought you can still point --\n\n-- them out.[!]  [!]On this page you see a sketch of a mountain, what looks like a cave is on the side.  On the bottom of the slope there's a giant figure that looks frozen.[!] [!] Next is a sketch of a frozen lake below a steep slope, a giant ice --\n\n-- pillar sticks up from the ground near the slope and lake.  At the top of the slope it looks like there's some platform, below it, in the lake, there's a hole in the ice.§0\n§0Written near the sketch reads, \"Weird place near tall mountain with ice and --\n\ngiant ruins with thanium and a tower\"[!] [!]Another sketch has been scribbled down, this one is of a pudgy, grey bird with a flower held in its beak, another sketch besides it shows the bird fluttering with a bunch of white peonies clutched in its feet[!]\n\n\"Had another dream, this time the tower burnt down with me in it.  Another dream-- #//.... ##// \\\\\" The rest of the entry is scribbled out.[!] [!]A few sketches of several designs of a strange mask are on the next few pages, one of them --\n\n-- is a blue mask with red hood, a steel mask with a red hood, and a few more.  They all go with a red hood.  Signed below them reads, \"Barnak designs\"[!] Here is a note that sits between the pages, looks a bit worn but still --\n\n-- readable.  The note first starts with a scribbled out name, \"B-/#/--,  I found something you might want to see... This thing reads, 'Herein lies Dralazar, Herald of Xion, Lord of Torment.  We are born by the dark; Made men by the Dark; Undone by the --\n\n-- Dark; We fear the Old Dark.'  *Next on the note is a scribble of what looks like a map, in the south there seems to be a little settlement, it's labeled Carnatia.  To the north in the mountains is labeled 'Ruins' just before the ruins --\n\n-- there's an area that's circled.* Signed, N-#..-\"[!]§0\n§0[!]\"Get soft relaxant for Kale.[!] [!] \"These dreams still continue even though H#//.- is gone.  A part of me thinks he will somehow come back like he did before, and when he does come back, it'd\n\n-- be the death of me.  This thing that I do with #o--+/n Taskan kinda helps take my mind off of it, plus I enjoy helping others.[!] [!] The rest of the page is just a rather detailed sketch of a peach plant, there's small white flowers around them.[!]§0\n§0--\n\n[!] Another note rests between the pages, this reads, \"Leave this land before I claim it myself.\"[!] [!]A sketch at the bottom of the page is scribbled out rather harshly.[!]\n\n-- [!]A sketch is on this page, it's of a narrow clawed figure with antlers.  Written below it is, \"Drawing from wendigo\"[!] [!]Here is a detailed sketch of ruins, snow rests atop of the cold bricks as the arches loom over the steps, leading to a tower --\n\n-- on the side of a mountain.  The tower looks over the ruins that sit at the bottom of steep, snowy mountains.  Labeled near the drawing reads, \"Sketchy plance north of Carnatia\"[!] [!] \"Continue to have trouble sleeping, nightmares --\n\n-- aren't as often as they were when they started.  They come about every other night or so, still about him.  I've sort of gotten use to being tired all the time, I don't really go out alone as much anymore unless it's on one of my walks.  We continue --\n\n-- to visit those ruins north of Carnatia, something is really off about that place.  Other than that, life is quiet.  I like it.[!] Another sketch is here, this one of a few potions and vials with flowers and herbs neard their bases, the soft --\n\n-- flowers are like a soft cushion for the small vials.[!] [!]\"Get mandragora, serpents stalk, dwarf's pumpkin, flametounge root, drake's tail, alabaster leaf, metzli's tangle, saffvil, and clutchers straw.\"[!] [!]A few houses --\n\n-- made of stone are sketched onto the page, one looks rather round and neat.  Another tall and ragged, though still nice.  Another, the stone looks oddly shaped, it looks elegant.[!] [!]\"Day one: 38 minas. Day two: 171 [!]\n\n[!]In messy, yet readable, handwriting reads a message,[!] \"Robe designs for Kelian.\" Below the scribble are a few sketches of an elf in dark robes, each sketch's robe design is different than the other.[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elf Culture", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya for Beginners.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      ~~~~~~~~~~~\nKarin'ayla to you. This book is intended as a guide through the noble culture of the High Elven people. Be you a youth of the Mali'aheral or a foreign diplomat who\n\ndesires to familiarize yourself with our ways, or even an older elf who has lapsed in their etiquette, this book can help you.\n\nPlease read on through the various lessons in these pages. Also see the guide to elven phrases in the back.\n\n       Lesson One\n    Avoid All Impurity\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nImpurity can exsist in two ways, Physical and mental. Both are to be treated with paramount seriousness, as they threaten the delicate balance of our civilized society.\n\nPhysical impurity is found when an individual is only partly High Elf, thus they are not \"pure\" in their lineage. Through out our long lives and our history we have seen, time and agian, that relations between a High Elf and others not of our kin end in\n\nmisery and failure. The impure products of these thoughtless and perverse relations are prone to lives of dissapointment and loneliness, as they do not truely belong anywhere. To any of the Mali'aheral, the formation of a \"romantic\" relationship with any\n\noutside of our people is forbidden, and will only serve to make yourself physically impure as well. The creation of children from such a bond is viewed with equal displeasure. This may sound harsh to those who are not of our people, but it is not. it is\n\nsimply the truth that wisdom and experience have taught us.\n\nWays to determine if one is of impure lineage include but are not limited to the following. Eyes of any color save blues, greens or purples. Ears that are rounded and short. Also a smallness of\n\nstature can indicate impurity. Hair amoung the Mali'aheral is normally fair, though it is not unheard of to have a brunette born amoung us. Dark hair, however, will certainly raise flags of warning to any who do not know the elf in question.\n\nMental impurity is a bit more difficult to detect as it can be hidden by the devious or the liar.\nIn truth, any who do not follow the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya are considered mentally impure to some degree or another. Small degrees of impurity can be treated\n\nand corrected. Large ones however can, have and will result in banishment and even death. Physical Impurity usually will end with the individual being \"cleansed\" by being tossed into an acid bath. Thus removing their taint from our society.\n\n        Lesson Two\nProper Conduct in the\n            City\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHigh Elves place etiquette on a high pedistal. We enjoy conversation, and we enjoy debate, but we insist it is done right. Emotion should not cloud one's judgment\n\nor reasoning, neither should it color one's argument. Logic and reason should rule the mind as it rules in the city of Haelun'or.\n\nFor those of you who are not of the people, you should consider before speaking to a High Elf, or trying to enter the city,\n\nthat there are a few key differences between you and us.\n\nWe are old, very old. Many of us have lived long enough to have met your great, great grand parents when they were children. As such our perspective is different than yours. High Elves are\n\nseen as cold or harsh in their demeanor or critisisms. In answer to this I invite you to consider these things. How would you feel if you saw an endless parade of children making the same mistakes, time and again, even though you yourself have warned them\n\nof the pitfalls of their poor behavoir many times over the past centuries? We grow frustrated when we see the same problems and mistakes being repeated and not fixed as logic would dictate that they must. You must also consider that a High Elf reckons\n\nthings in a longer time frame than you likely do. There for, one should not take our comments or critisisms personally, for they are intended to help you and your children and your children's children to be better. After all, why should one be upset by\n\nthe truth?\n\nWhen attempting to enter the city, if one is not of the Mali'aheral, one should not think to do so lightly or easily. Our city is precious to us, and we do not seek to sunder its purity by letting any and all who knock to enter.\n\nIf one seeks to enter they should do so with the right frame of mind. With patience and with humility one will go further. Also it is customary to bring a gift, that they may offer something in return for the honor of entering the gates.\n\nFor those of you who are of the people. I suggest looking the part. Dress appropriately for your lineage as a High Elf. Keep your hair seemly, and preferably un-dyed. Our flesh should be free of tattoos or piercings as these things only mar our natural\n\nbeauty. Makeup or accesories that accent our features may be worn however.\n\n      Lesson Three\n       Be Educated\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Whether you attend the Eternal College or you take it upon yourself to read and learn, all good High Elves smile upon the persuit of knowledge. Learn of art, science or even the arcane lore of\n\nmagic, but be knowledgable of something. One should spend their whole life aquiring new learning that they may be useful.\n\nOh be wise, what more can I say?\n\n      Lesson Four\n        Courtship\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The art of courtship is something that all young Mali'aheral should know. For one day, you may wish to impress someone of the opposite gender and unite with them in marriage. Follow this guide and you\n\nwill hopefully avoid becoming a social pariah.\n\nDo NOT engage in sappy, lovey dovey actions or grandiose acclamations of your love. This will not end well and is unseemly for one of our people. Rather, create works of art or music or literature that\n\n you can devote to the object of your adoration. Doing so will not only let that person know that someone is interested in them, but will show that you are capable in these areas. These things should, however, be done anonymously, so as not to put any\n\nundue social strain on you or them. When this courtship has gone on for a while and you feel reasonably sure that they will respond in kind to your affections, then you may reveal your identity to them as their admirer. If you do not feel that things will\n\ngo well, or you lose interest, you may simply stop courting the individual and no one should be any the wiser who it was.\n\nAlas, these things do indeed happen.\n\n       Lesson Five\n         Marriage\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Once your courtship has gone its course and you and your beloved are together, it is expected that you will be married.\nHigh Elven marriages are usually held in large public venues or centers of\n\nknowledge such as a library. We do not have churches and therefore do not hold weddings in them.\n\nThe ceremony is attended by all the pure citizenry, as well as invited outsiders. An individual is given the honor to speak at the wedding and officiate the\n\nceremony. After they speak, a moment of silence is given for any to speak out against the union, should they choose. This is almost never done, as to speak out publically against the couple is considered rude in the extreme.\nThe two are then wed and may\n\nrecieve gifts, congradualtions, etcetera.\n\nIt is within the bonds of matrimony and ONLY within these bonds that the creation of High Elven children may take place. Assuming you are fertile, to have a child is an honor and a joy to be planned and\n\ntaken with all seriousness.\n\n       Lesson Six\n         Religion\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~This will be a rather short section. The High Elves practice no religion. We would rather devote our time to logical and, for lack of a better term, provable persuits than to sit in a church and\n\npray to a God that we can neither see nor hear. Rather than try to guess at the whims of deity, We will continue to unravel the mysteries of the world as we can prove it exsists.\n\nFor my High Elven readers, you would do well to devote yourself to the\n\npractice of our culture, rather than some faith from a distant land.\n\n     Lesson Seven\n    To Offer Insult\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The highest insult one can offer is to call another impure. This however has some stipulations. For example, if one of the leaders of the people, We'll say the El'sohaer were to call another elf impure\n\n this offense could be taken with much gravity. However, if a half elf were to refer to a High elf as impure, the insult has no barb, as the half elf is impure to begin with. One way to offer such an insult is to give a High Elf gold. This should almost\n\nnever be done, as one High Elf to another, as the action can indicate that the reciever cares more for gold than they do for their people. Of course were a human to give an elf a bar of gold, it would have no such meaning, as a human could not be expected\n\nto know this. Gold jewlery or items can be given between High Elves, so long as the intent is clear. Unless you really do want to insult them.\n\n        Conclusion\n```````````````````'''''''''''''''''''   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nI hope that you have enjoyed this book, but more so I hope that you are better prepared to navigate the pitfalls of High Elven etiquette. We are a strict people, but we are\n\ndelightsome when you know how to behave.\n\nPlease look for my next book\n\n\"An Encyclopedic Arcanum\"\na guide to magic\n\n~Gallidron Elindrow~\n\nPublication year 1514\n\n         A Guide to\n      Elvish Phrases\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~````````````````````''''''''''''''''''Karin'ayla- Good day\nKer'ayla- Good night\nVan'ayla- Farewell\nMali- Elf\nBortu- Dwarf\nUruk- Ork\nValah- Human\nTali'bortu- Halfling\nLlir/Lliran-Friend(s)\n\nMali'aheral-High Elf\nAcalin- Shop\nAiler- Wizard\nIler- Dark wizard\n\nHopefully these few phrases and words will be of use to any who learn them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Study of Water", "UnBaed", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0         The Study§0\n§0             of§0\n§0            Water§0\n§0          -_-~-_-§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Written by Nemir\n\nThis book is just a way for me to share my thoughts on water and it's aspects perhaps with a few other stuff about the element.§0\n§0  Now I've studied water in quite a few locations.  I visited Saltstone and gazed out at the cold, -\n\n- grey ocean.  The scene of the towering waves clashing against the rocky shore filled me with a tranquil and somber feeling.  It might've been the dull colors in nature along with the cool breeze that carried the faint -\n\n- smell of salt.  I enjoy sceneries related to those, but that's not what this book is about.  I, regrettably, took a rather steep path down to the shore in an attempt to study the water at a different perspective.\n\nI won't go into much detail on it but let's just say that I went home cold and soaking wet.  I visited Saltstone once more but didn't study the ocean.  That day I went a little more into the mountains, past the town and arena.  There's this little -\n\n- pond with water trickling down a steep, rocky slope into it.  The water isn't as cold as you'd think it'd be, the snow around it has melted away.  The water looked calm and smooth.  I could see the bottom clearly from where I sat, -\n\n- I removed my glove and gently stuck my hand in.  The water felt rather warm, but not hot.  It was a comforting type of warm.  Now let's contrast these two experiences I had with water.\n\nThe first one, by the cliffs, involved water being extremely powerful, loud, and perhaps ferocious.  The water there could easily lead someone to a dark, wet grave.  The second location seemed as if it was the complete -\n\n- opposite of the first.  The water looked soothing, soft, and was peacefully silent.  The area seemed like one perfect for meditation, or perhaps a place for lovers to escape to.\n\n[!] Two sketches of the mention locations are on this page[!]§0\n§0http://imgur.com/a/O7oYI\n\nI feel that these two places show how water can be powerfully deadly at one time, and peacefully stagnant another.  Those two forms are both beautiful.\n\n[!] The last few pages have been torn out. [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Written By Erendiel Thoren.§0\n§0Based mainly on The void by Nienna calm\n\nThe void is a realm that is infinitly large.§0\n§0A pitch black world with nothingness in all directions, Though it has a paradoxical bit to it, as it has the potential to become literally everything.\n\n\"The void is nothing, with the potential to become anything.\"§0-Nienna Calm§0\n§0All mortals contain a small tear that leads to the void. People say that it was created when Iblees. This, however, is not a physical scar though, but a empheral one, which is\n\ncontained within our very souls. Without it one couldn't connect to the void, and therefore it would be impossible to use voidal magic.§0\n\nOn how to use this hole in your soul: One has to try to attune their mind, a mages most important instrument, to nothing, or even nothingness itself. You have to try to connect to the void this way. However connecting to the void is only the first step to\n\nbecoming a mage, and actually using magic.§0\n§0Once you have connected to the void, it starts draining your mana, an element you cannot live without, All at once. This can cause untrained mages to feel like their soul gets sucked out, often resulting in-§0\n\nthem passing out, or vomiting. Also, They might wake up with something resembling a hangover. Therefore it is advised that a mage first practices connecting to the void, before actually trying to cast magic. It, of course, also has long lasting effects on\n\nyour physical state.§0\n§0It'll leave your body weakened and feeble, and not eating properly will cause you to wither away, like magical starvation.\n\n1. Transfiguration.§0\n§0Hello, This is the study i started with, due to my interests in Telekinesis. I will write everything i discover and experience for myself in my studies, and this will most likely not be very usefull for anyone who is even slightly\n\nadvanced. Here it goes:", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-9th of The Grand Harvest, 1533§0\n§0\n§0My name is Philippa Horen. Currently, I am the Imperial Princess of Oren, and my parents' eldest daughter. They are both busy at times. Father is only taking care of his great empire, when mother\n\nkeeps herself busy with the guests she arrives at court. I, on the other hand, was usually following my mother's task with this. Until now. I received a letter from uncle Adrian the other day, offering my stay at the Winter Palace in Salvus.\n\nThe palace was finally finished! I immediately went to pack my suitcases, and left Felsen promptly. Currently, Felsen is getting rebuild. Though the process doesn't seem so promising to me. It has been quiet in the city for months, and open patches of\n\nland are seen inside the walls. I'm glad that I was able to leave Felsen, since I much prefer the palace at Salvus. The place is quiet, which I like! Many attempts on my life have occurred before, but none succeeded whatsoever. I must think that GOD might\n\naid me with this, since the few attempts were quite fatal. My food's been poisoned twice now, and an arrow of a malicious assassin struck my back. The experiences only left me a huge scar running across my back, and utter cautioun to everywhere I go.\n\nI hope Salvus will be safe for me to stay, and that I won't need to worry so much anymore..\n\n-1st of Sun's Smile, 1533§0\n§0\n§0My GOD, I am so ashamed! I invited my dear friend over, Lady Aurelia de Bar. I wanted to show her the beautiful Salvus and the Winter Palace. She attended, but grandmother already judged her with\n\nkeen eyes. Mother wished to change the female clothing in the empire, so women are now more regulary seen with bare arms. Though, grandmother clearly does not prefer this change to occur. She commanded Aurelia to wear something else, but the poor girl had\n\nthat dress gifted! I hope she does not feel offended, and that she'll visit me in the future. Oh Aurelia, I'm terribly sorry..", ""),
        StaticBook("Subtlety", "§bGrandmaster Khivan Peretas", "Subtlety\n        **********\n        The Path\n            of\n         Subtlety\n\n\"We are the unseen man in the crowd, the man in the shadows, we are the children of subterfuge.\" ~Grandmaster Khivan Peretas", ""),
        StaticBook("Deception", "§bGrandmaster Decon Certopa", "Deception\n     *************\n       The Path\n           of\n       Deception\n\n\"We are the men with the silver tounges, able to convince any man, we are the children of Marlgra.\"\n~Grandmaster Decon Certopa", ""),
        StaticBook("Wolf Tales", "§bDemothosus", "Wolves: The Species You Can Find\nBy: Demothosus, Makai\n\nWolves are native creatues to Asulon but can also be found Anthos. The most common place you will spot these preadtory creatures is in cold snowy areas or dark forest. Wolves, social creaures, live in small packs that is made up of their family.\n\nOften times wolves only attack when provoked or if you attack/provok one wolf the entire pack will come to its aid and attack the agressor. The wolves strength, speed and sharp teeth are effective destroyers to their enemies. Icluding their all time\n\nfavorite sheep.\n\nDomestication:\nMost wolves in the wild will not be skittish due to their predatory defenses. Meaning some could be approached at a closer distance than most wildlife. \nHow to tell the difference:\n\nThe naturally agressive wolves will automaticly go in the defensive position and have gleaming red eyes. Warning whoever is coming to watch it and stay back.\n\nThe nonagressive ones will behave differently. They are very attracted to bones. They can\n\nbe conviced to come closer to you if you have a bone in hand. When fed enough bones they will become fiercely loyal to you and you alone. The wolf even leaves it pack to follow you. Its loyalty is proven by attacking monsters or enemies that threaten\n\ntheir master. A wolf's loyalty can have a vast range, to having a single companion to follow you on your travles, to a wolf army.\n\nVarious species:\nForest wolves\nKer Wolves\nMountain Wolves\nLur Wolves\nSnow Wolves\n\nDespite the seemingly common ansector of these powerful predators. There have been a variety of specices due to various enviorments.\nForest Wolves:\nMost common in thickly forested areas. Have been known to have bigger litters and a thinner coat than\n\nthe other wolf species. Some beings who have encountered these wolves claim they are friendly then the other wolves. The location:\nAsulon\nAnthos\n\nKer Wolves:\nThese wolves are one of the tallest around.\nThe Ker Wolf reaches\n\n5-7 feet in height, with a shocking weight of anything 800-1200 pounds. Known for their dark colored fur that makes them blend in with shadows. They are actully lighter and smaller than the lur wolver. Making them aproximetly the size of a shire or\n\nthoroughbreds. Making the Ker wolves perfect mounts for normal elves. These wolves were domesticated by oussana and Darkspire clans. There main job now is to serve as guardians and mounts of the dark elves. Very few beings have been blessed enough to be\n\ngiven a Ker wolf outside of the dark elves.\n\nMountain Wolves:\nLarger than most of their cousins. Mountain wolves can grow to massive sizes easily topping 200 pounds. They are native to the cold, snow mountains of the Hanseti area. Can be found in other\n\ncold climates as well. With this as their natural habbitat they typically live in caves to fight against the cold, harsh winds. This enviorment also leads to haveing few pups. However the pups born are mcuh large than your average wolf pup. The Mountain\n\nwolves were discovered in Asulon however they seem to not reside in Anthos.\n\nLur Wolves:\nLur Wolves can ONLY live in the desert. This bred of wolf was bred by Orcs as mounts. Trained to kill with a single bite. These are 9 foot tall giants. The\n\nperfect predator with their massive jaws and razor sharp fangs. There is little to nothing that can oppose these beast. Especially if they are being ridden by an Orc. They also have another purpose. The Lur wolf is often set loose into the ranks of the\n\nenemy ranks too strike fear into their hearts. The sight of this monsterous beast covered in the blood of its dead victims is frightening enough to frighten the most battle hardened warrior.  With their naturally dark fur its quite easy to see them. It is\n\ncommon to see their fur dyed in blood though. The largest known Lur to exist was owned by Urak'lur who was also know as the hairiest of all the orcs in the land. What is also suprising enough because of their similarly dark coats to that of the Ker wolf,\n\nis that these large beast are not native to Asulon and Anthos.\nThe Lur Wolf was bred in Krugmar and transported to other realms by ship which is how most non native species get to various lands anyway.\n\nSnow Wolf:\nSnow wolves are the most documented wolves. They were discovered in Anthos and are closly related to mountain wolves. Their average weight is 180 lbs and on average are 6 feet tall. Despite their weight they are very quick on their feet and\n\nstealthy. These woves can take many hits before going down. They have a bit force of 2000 lbs and can snap bones. They can sprint at a speed of 30 mph. Through most famous for their white coats, some have gray, brown, or black streaks. The pack usually\n\nconsits of four to five wolves. Male pups are forced to leave the pack at age 2 so as to insure breeding diversity. The alpha's are easily distinguished from their pack with their gray streak along their back and bigger than average height. They can\n\nsurvive in almost all climates but prefer their snowy, native lands. They are renowned for their cunning, planning out attacks and ambushes to hunt prey. Snow wolves usually hunt elk, moose, and deer. They'll rarly, if ever, hunt humans.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant's Vow", "§b12werbles12", "~*~\n  The Dedicant's Vow\n\nI now walk the forests with my new kin. I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me. As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need. I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk\n\n approaches. I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\n\n   by:\n   Salmon Druid Petyr\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will walk the forest with my new kin.\"\n\nWith this statement, the Dedicant pledges his or her official ties to be with the Druids of the Druidic Order.\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me.\"\n\nWith this statement, the Dedicant pledges loyalty to the Order and thereby promises to speak the truth and never with deception.\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need.\"\n\nWhile under the guidance of the Aspects and the elder Druids, the Dedicant pledges to return the favor of respect and service.\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk approaches.\"\n\nThe Dedicant pledges devout service, no matter the time nor obstacle he or she may face.\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\"\n\nThe Dedicant does just that; he or she vows to uphold his or her duties and their pledge as a Dedicant.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pact of Four", "§bJan Kovachev", "The Pact of the Black Host:§0\n§0[!] Lines for signatures are drawn below.§0\n§0\n§0Carnatia: Lord Jan Kovachev.§0\n§0\n§0Ostavar : Earl Sven Ruric§0\n§0\n§0Carrenhall: Ser Osgod§0\n§0Colborn, Eirik Colborn\n\nCourland: Duke Anden Staunton§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Atheran Uruks V1", "§bTemür Törs Ajedh'raq", "Betrayal of the             Uzg\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten and Recorded\nby\n\nTemür Törs Ajedhraq\nRider of the Subudai\n\nThe Uzg of the Uruks, centered in the Goi, San-Vitar, of the new world, Athera, had experienced a unity un-paralleled in recent history.  In the Goi, the clans Gorkil, Lur, Yar, Kog, Magra, and various others coexisted.  This unity is attributed to the\n\nRex Malog'Yar.  A wise and powerful Shaman, Malog'Yar enacted reform among Uruk culture to bring the Uzg into the forefront of the politics of Athera.  Under these reforms, stricter codes of honor were introduced, which elevated the Uruks from a looseknit\n\nculture of raiders to a unified culture based on code-of-law. These reforms, though, drew harsh criticism from some of the Uruks, especially from the Azog clan.  \n\nThe Azogs, already dissatisfied with the Uzg's hostility towards Raine Academy, was\n\npushed further from their brothers.  Tensions were heightened between the Uzg and the Azogs.\n\nAt this time, another perilous threat arose to challenge the Uzg.  An Uruk, by the name of Zogrocka, had risen to immense power through the wicked\n\nand vile means of Dark Shamanism (a topic I will fully explain in the Expanded History of the Uruks).  Under Zogrocka's leadership\nthe ancient and exiled clan Dom rose again.  The Doms were a clan dedicated to Dark Shamanism, that fell out of Krug's grace\n\ndue to their trickery and abuse of spirits and elementals.  They also offended the Uzgs and other nations through their abominable practice of cannibalism.  Justly, the Uzgs hunted down and executed the Doms in earlier times.\n\nThe rise of the Doms\n\ncoincided with the split of the Azogs and the Uzg.  In the Azogs, the Doms saw an army to enforce their corrupt ways.  In the Doms, the Azogs saw a means to achieve power and claim the Uzg for themselves.  \n\nDespite the Uzg offering complete\n\nand total amnesty to the Azogs upon their return to the Uzg, the Azogs forsook Krug and the Spirits in favor of the dreadful\nDoms.  Making a deal with the patron Spirit of the Dark Shamans, Ixli, the Azogs traded parts of their sanity for the corrupting\n\npower enjoyed by the Doms.\n\nNow combined, the Doms and the Azogs sacked San'Vitar, the Uruk's 'Old City'.  At first, the unholy alliance encountered little resistance and many Uruks of the Uzg were slaughtered.  A joint force of Uruks and\n\nHumans were unable to repel the assailants later on.  The Goi was left severely debilitated following the attack.\n\nAfter the attack, the desperate Uruks pleaded the spirits for guidance.  In an odd series of events, the Uruks were given\n\nassistance.  Following the shrieks of an injured scaddernack, the Uruks discovered a cave where the spirit Veist revealed itself to them.  Veist pledged its support against the Azogs and the Doms, but in return, the Uzg's High Shaman, Brunhyldir,\n\nwas morphed into a Goblin.\n\nIt was in this frail form that the High Shaman Brunhyldir confronted the Dark Shaman Zogrocka.  Alone, the two battled, drawing upon the Mojo that the Spirits granted them (whether that be honorably as\n\nin Brunhyldir's case, or dishonorable, in Zogrocka's).  The honor and the strength of the High Shaman prevailed, and the abhorrent and corrupt Zogrocka was defeated.\n\nLeft without a leader, the Doms were weakened.  The Azogs\n\nfollowing Zogrocka's defeat then attempted to gain power by their own means.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nOn the 6th of the Lunar Cycle of Sun's Smile, in the year 1471, I, Temür Törs Ajedh'raq, was witness to the following events that occurred in San'Vitar.\n\nThe Azogs, unable to gain power through the corruption of Ixli and the Doms, arrived\n\nat the Goi armed and armored.  They approached the Rex in his Blarg and demanded the Rexdom under threat of force.\n\nIt is notable that by Uruk custom, which has been observed for generations, the Rex may be challenged to an 'honor klomp', in\n\nwhich the Rex and the Challenger fight for the title and position of Rex.  These fights generally occur unarmed and unarmored.  With that said, it is also of worth to note that the Azogs, in no way, shape, or form, challenged the Rex honorably to such a\n\nfight.\n\nThe Azogs' justification for such demands were that the current Rex was weak, and the Uzg was crumbling.  They came to the Goi claiming they could make it strong again.\n\nTo justify their for-\n\n-saking Krug and the Spirits, they claimed that the dark powers of Zogrocka had made them servants of the Dark Shamans.  Despite there being a lack of Azog Shamans at the confrontation, the Azog clan claimed to have made amends with the Spirits.  This\n\nblatant lie is further discredited by the presence of Dom Shamans accompanying the Azog party.\n\nFor two days, the Azogs and their Dom Shamans held the Rex.\nTheir terms: the Rexdom and the Uzg, or war.  For two days the Rex held out and\n\nattempted to reason with the Uruks made unreasonable through\nIxli's Bargain.\n\nOn the 8th of the Lunar Cycle of Sun's Smile, in the year 1471, the Azogs departed the Goi as enemies of the Uzg.  With their coup-de-tat failed, they returned to\n\ntheir fort without the Uzg in their command.  Both sides, immediately following the encounter, started to strike alliances with other nations and factions.  The Uruks of the Uzg appealing to those who uphold honor, and who wish to maintain orderly law\n\nthroughout Athera.  And the splinter Azogs, appealing to those who would rather there be the vile corruption of chaos unleashed upon the land.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "If this is being read this means that the compound must be destroyed. Use the provided lighter along with some kindling to destroy the compound with ease.§0\n§0-Grandmaster", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfling Babies", "§bAlai Kharadeen", "Where do Halfling§0\n§0   Babies come from?§0\n§0\n§0\n§0     Orginal Author§0\n§0      Unknown§0\n§0     Rewritten by§0\n§0     Alai Kharadeen\n\n\n§0   Halfling birth is by far the most magical and sweet birth of all the races. I first found out about how the halflings are born when I went to the halfling town, which I have forgotten the name of. Quite hungry when I arrived,§0\n\nI asked permission from one of the elders to remove a few plants from the farm, permission which was granted to me.§0\n§0\n§0   As I walked through the farm I took a few carrots and potatoes, then I found an overly grown cabbage. I though as thank you, I would\n\ncook the great cabbage and make the Halflings a great cauldron of Cabbage soup. As I was about to take the cabbage from the fertile land, a Halfling came shouting through the fields for me to stop, seeming quite stressed. Believing that somehow I was in\n\nthe wrong field, or that cabbage was of prized goods, I stepped away from the cabbage, and awtaited the Halfling. While huffing, the Halfling, still stressed, checked the cabbage for damage, before hitting me in the shin with his shovel. In pain I fell to\n\nthe ground while grabbing my leg, wondering what kind of prized cabbage that could be. The Halfling looked angry and even shouted “Wha’ were y’ goin’ t’ do t’ me son?!” I was amazed, the cabbage was so important to him, he called it his son. I apologized\n\nand said that as a thank you I was going to cook his “son” for the Halflings, but that I didn’t know it belonged to someone. I couldn’t finish explaining before I was hit repeatedly by the shovel.§0 The Halfling was shouting as he hit me \"Y' dishutin' man\n\n,how dare' ye try t' feed us one o' our own babies!\"§0\n§0\n§0   I was shocked, I didn’t understand. I apologized and said many times that I didn’t know, and after a while, the Halfling stopped hitting me. After he stopped I continued asking in serious pain I\n\nmight add. I asked what the cabbage meant to the Haflings, and he told me a story I will never forget. §0\n§0\n§0   The story he told me was one of love, the love two Halflings feel for each other. I already knew at the time how dwarf babies were born, and knew\n\nthat Halflings are descendents of both Horen and Urguan, so I was confused how they mated and had children, I didn't know if was the dwarven way, or the human way. §0\n§0   He told me of him and his wife, for many years now. They clearly loved each other quite\n\nand one day decided to have a child. They began their evening by drinking and smoking together, alone in their house, only the two which love each other. They do what they love most together, drinking the finest Hafling ale, and smoking the best Halfling.\n\nWhen the moon was high, they went into the fields together, carrying a single seed, a normal seed. After planting the cabbage in the patch, they prayed to their pumpkin god.§0\n§0\n§0   The seed, blssed with the love of the soon to be mother and father Hafling,\n\nand the power of the pumpkin god, started growing quite large, into what was now the cabbage I almost took. The baby Halfling grows within the cabbage to be born at the time of the harvest season. It was stil a few elven days from the harvest, and as such\n\nif I had took the cabbage, I would give birth to the baby too soon. I decided to stay for a while longer to witness the birth, and it was as they said.§0\n§0\n§0   I helped with the harvest that day, and soon all the Halflings gathered by the cabbage. The mother\n\nand father started carefully removing the big leaves of the cabbage. It took a while for the small Halflings to remove the leaves, but soon enough, in the middle of it, a tiny sleeping baby could be seen.§0\n§0The father thanked the pumpkin god once more as\n\n\n§0the mother took the baby. That night, they made a feast, for the harvest, and the newborns. The name for the newborns? They thought of them while drunk and high.§0\n§0\n\nWhere do Halfling babies come from?§0\n§0\n§0Original author§0\n§0Unknown", ""),
        StaticBook("Unfinished Story", "§bPetyr", "Jesper ran through the streets bumping into people as he did so in his hand was a gold chain that was obviously stolen. Jesper was a street urchin and was always trying to steal things but today, today was different. Behind him he heard shouts like\n\n'Thief!' and 'Stop him!' but he continued running he bumped into people multiple times stumbling each time he did so. The shouts were getting closer and he knew he had to get out of there quickly. Jesper ran through one of the alleys that twisted and\n\nturned until he got to a dead end. In front of him stood a five foot tall wall. He jumped up and grabbed onto the ledge his feet dangling just above the ground before he pulled himself up, grunting with effort as he did so.\n\nHe ran as fast as he could through the twisting streets until he got to the main street and he ran for the gate. He ran passed the guards ignoring their shouts and curses. Jesper made sure no one was following him and started to walk.§0\n\nHe walked to the village nearby and went to his house. When he got in he looked to his mom a wide grin on his face and said \"Mom! Mom! I got something for you!\" she looked at the gold chain and frowned \"Where'd you get that?\"\n\nJesper stuttered slightly as he spoke \"M-mom the man that I stole it fr-\" \"You stole it!?\" she yelled loudly \"Yes ma b-but we needed it more...\" Jesper said. His mother sighed and took the chain from his hands and said \"Fine, but don't ever do this§0\n§0again\"\n\nJesper did not mention to his mom that he steals things on a regular basis, if he told her it would break her heart.", ""),
        StaticBook("barnett poems", "teegah", "Ruined ruined ruined.§0\n§0Love life lost ruined.§0\n§0No love here at all.§0\n§0Life is gone.§0\n§0I say I say.§0\n§0\n§0The New Seed whisps away, planted for another day.§0\n§0I say I say.§0\n§0I say I say.§0\n§0\n§0Whisper me your wisdom, wise one.\n\nWhen Scarlet runs and runs, I will say.§0\n§0Hazzah for the Malin-born whom adorn the honor of freedom.§0\n§0\n§0I say, I say, I say.§0\n§0\n§0Live and learn, the beat of a drum, and sprung from sleep.§0\n§0I say, I say we are awake.\n\nHazza to the awakened and bold for it is told, we own the world.§0\n§0\n§0The old own it now, but the new shall reign supreme.§0\n§0\n§0I say I say.§0\n§0\n§0Brave sons to that I§0\n§0speak you bring us the sun and all is love.\n\nUncha katinkwaca loonta mapinktawasacooncha§0\n§0Tasty is gay Tasty is§0\n§0asty is gay Tasty is g§0\n§0sty is gay Tasty is ga§0\n§0ty is gay Tasty is gay§0\n§0y is gay Tasty is gay §0\n§0is gay Tasty is gay T§0\n§0s gay Tasty is gay Ta§0\n§0gay Tasty is gay Tast§0\n§0ay Tasty is gay Tasty y Tasty\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n`\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n`````\n\n``````\n\n````\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nHere come that boy§0\n§0o sht waddup§0\n§0here come that back§0\n§0he be rolling down the streat§0\n§0he be rolling to the beat§0\n§0oh shit waddup.", ""),
