        StaticBook("A Thesis", "§bFather Cedrik", "A Thesis on Charitable Evangelization, penned by Cedrik Engel, eternal servant of the Holy Father.\n\nIn nomine Patris.\n\nA man fed by another is beholden to him that provides food. Such is hardly deniable, even in the sense that a man who tends fields that\n\nbelong to another is beholden to him who owns the land; for land brings forth food with the labor of the tenant, and thus the tenant is fed by the landlord. This is the manner in which our world is governed. This feudal government over which our ever\n\nmerciful and most blessed GOD presides provides for a system that encourages loyalty and promotes a mutual understanding of responsibility. For without such a system the Holy Orenian Empire would utterly crumble upon its weak foundation, and the Church of\n\nthe Most High Father would be left stranded upon the harsh landscapes of this Plane. Thus, the importance of the general necessity of sustenance is realized.\n\nUpon this revelation, the Church may begin to develop a plan in which the scattered\n\nmasses of the Pagan world shall be brought forth into the eternal light of our Father, blessed by His Divine Providence. For from the ashes of this broken world of dismal heathens and faltering believers, the Church may yet arise anew, bearing the holy\n\nmight of GOD upon the mob of the proletariat, and elevate them to a higher standing, one of communion with His Divine Mercy.\n\nTherefore I beg the Church, I beseech it, to take up its Holy Standard and, in addition to the multitude of righteous\n\npractices it currently exercises, wield the mighty weapon of Charity, and spread His Love to all corners of this Earth, and perhaps the Pagan may begin to realize the falsity of his idolatrous gods, and turn to the liberating light of the Holy Father.\n\nThus I pray unto Him, that He may guide the Church with His Mighty Hand and evangelize this crippled land and the whole world may cry \"Glory!\" unto the Heavens.\n\nIn nomine Patris, Amen.\n\nDeus Magnus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The cat sat down.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ragnar III", "§bRagnar de Autson VI", "Ragnar de Autson III\n\nI swear to you my Lord, and the Seven Skies that I shall use my blade to defend the helpless.\n\nMy might will be used to uphold the weak.\n\nMy words will speak only the truth.\n\nMy wrath will undo the wicked.\n\nMy knowledge will defeat ignorance.\n\nMy skills will be taught to the willing.\n\nMy temper shall be held by patience.\n\nThis is the Knights oath, and if I break the oath I have just stated I will be executed.\n\n\"Almighty God, have mercy upon Ser Ragnar III, a humble Knight in Thy Divine Service.\nOh Lord, I pray for Thy indulgence and blessings.\n\nForget not Thine servant in his trials, nor his Knighthood.\n\nThe lord withdrawed a traditional ceremonial sword from a gilded scabbard and placed the sword upon Ser Ragnar's shoulder. \n\"I hereby pronounce you Ser Ragnar de Autson III\n\na Knight of Winterfell; 2nd of Suns Smile 1337: May our Sovereign live long and may his rule be blessed by the God.\"\n\nRagnar clambered to his feet; a solem expression growing upon his face.\n\n\"You shall be stationed at the South Watchtower overlooking King Edmunds Bridge.\"\n\n\"Yes, my Lord\" Ragnar dipped his head, before pivoting upon his heel and trudging through the\n\nsnow.\n\n\"Ragnar, I shall inform Queen Dawn Perea and her followers you have been Knighted. I'm sure she'll be glad to have such a courageous young man. Specifically with what's been going on in the south...\"\n\n\"Lord Brett...I give you my assurance that the Undead Spawns will not overrun us in this attack. \nThough my son has not sent word from Crimson Vale in such a long time...\"\n\n\"With the constant series of Onslaughters we have been having these past few months, I barely have time to write a letter...\"\n\nRagnar paused momentarialy before ambling forward towards the homestead.\n\nAs the day turned to dusk Ragnar staggered out of the tavern. A strong, miasmic stench of Mead emitting from his clothing.\n\nAs he stumbled towards his home, he clenched his fist into a ball thudded the base of the door, intricatley carved Dark Oak.\n\nShortly after, an alluring figure opened the door. It seemed to be one of a female, she had a slender build and carried a windsome smile.\nHer hair was long, and her lips were thin coated in natural acidity in a lemon to bring forth a red stain on her\n\nlips.\n\nShe wore a white dress which covered her shoulders.\n\n\"You've been drinking again...\" She furrowed her brows, a mellow tone exiting her throat.\n\n\"Get your breath away from me you filthy animal!\" She took a large step back from Ragnar, seemingly disappointed with his behaviour. \n\n\"I deserve a drink, for you shall now refer to me as Ser Ragnar de Autson III.\"\nHe bellowed his raspy voice throughout\n\nthe small, quaint cottage.\n\nRagnar stumbled inside placing his palms on her shoulders \"You look like a harlot.\" He kissed her neck.\n\n\"Get off of me!\" She extended her arms and shoved Ragnar from her shoulders.\n\n\"We haven't even been wedded yet, and you wonder why...\" She promptly pushed past Ragnar and out the door.\n\n\"Cersei!\" Ragnar yelled, before rolling his eyes and watching her disappear over the horizon.\n\nRagnar, removed his ferrum greaves from his shins and his chainmail hauberk. \nRagnar walked along the thin and creaky floorboards, his large feet making the floorboards strain under his weight.\n\nThree Years Later\n\n\nA faint knock upon Ragnar's door echoed throughout his cottage.\n\nA widespread apathy lingered in the air, as Ragnar opened it.\n\nA bemused expression appared upon Ragnar's face. \"Lord Brett\" He dipped his head in courtesy.\n\nLord Brett; however did not acknowledge this. His shoulders were slumped making his stature seem small, he gave a despairing shrug before speaking.\n\n\"Ser Ragnar, my heart goes out to you and Lady Cersei. I am so sorry to tell you. Your son, Ragnar IV has been killed in the invasion of Crimson Vale.\"\nLord Brett had a woeful expression, a tear running down his right eye.\n\nRagnar froze, his body felt fridgid and he contorted his face.\n\nLord Brett bobbed his head towards Ragnar and pivoted on his heel walking away; leaving Ragnar looking disconsolated.\n\nPart 1 of 2.\n\n\nBy Ragnar de Autson VI", ""),
        StaticBook("Judas' Love Life", "§bJudas Agnarsson", "The Love Life\nof \nJudas Agnarsson\n(Extended Version)\n\nA recent survey asked Judas Agnarsson a fifty five unwedded male from Courland questions about his love life.\n\nThese were his responses...\n\nWhat is your biggest weakness?\n\nI honestly love too much, I do.\n\n\nAnd crippling depression...\n\nPersonally I believe woman are people too. They deserve the same rights as we do, and they have souls as well which is why I don't eat them, I'm vegetarian.\n\n\"Judas the question was if you'd ever marry a women.\"\n\nOh...\n\nDo you have any hobbies?\n\nWriting in my spare time and greiving for my deceased son.\n\nYou mention you had a son, you're a widower?\n\nYes.\n\nWould you like to evaluate on that?\n\nNo.\n\nAny special talents?\n\nI once swallowed a golf ball accidentally and shat it out an hour later.\n\nThankyou Judas for your time.\n\nYou're welcome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Archrim Elmoran§0\n§0Double chest assortment- 466", ""),
        StaticBook("\"A Winters Night", "§bClan Elder Legate Fili Grandaxe", "It was a cold night, in the dead of winter. The wind was howling like a wolf outside my window, as a blizzard blown down from the north settled in around my small house.\n\nI sat awake, huddled near the crackling fire, bundled under my pelts, packed closely, as they buried me like a tomb. Despite my care, and precautions to keep warm, the cold cut into me like a knife.\n\nI sat blankly, staring into the depths of the flames, contemplating whether or not this would be my last Winter.Then I heard a commotion at my door, followed by a thud, then silence.\n\nShocked by fear, and surprise, I remained seated, unable to move. Slowly as I regained my composure, I reached for my waraxe, sitting at my feet, displacing my carefully arranged cocoon of blankets.\n\n I do not know how long I waited, petrified with fear at what may be outside my door. My imagination went rampant, as I began to think of all the horrors, and atrocities that may lay outside my door,\n\nwaiting to pounce on me, and bring a swift end to my suffering on this freezing night.\n\nAfter a while though, when the fire had begun to die down, almost to cinders, I mustered up enough courage to arise from my seat. The blankets slid off my body down to the hard, unforgiving floor,\n\nthe warmth they once held, now being sucked away by the hungry planks. I stepped over the pile, and made my way a few steps into the open room before my doorway.\n\nJust after my third, agonizing step, I fell upon a loose board, and the creaking noise that emitted from it almost sent my heart jumping through my mouth.\n\n“It is only a board” I told myself, breathing heavily “Nothing to be afraid of” I took another step onwards, closing in on my destination, waraxe in hand to fend off whatever evil lay on my doorstep.\n\nI took another step forward, and my heart began to beat faster. The crackling sound of my dying fire began to get blotted out by the thump, thump, thumping of my own heart. I took yet another step forward.\n\nAt my door now, I slowly reached for the door knob, extending my left hand, holding my waraxe high in my right.\n\nI groped for the door handle, opening my sweaty palm. I was shaking like a leaf by the time my hand closed around the copper handle. Taking a few ragged breaths before my imminent doom, I closed my eyes and tried to calm myself.\n\nI began to slowly, ever so slowly twist that wretched knob. I heard a click as the tumblers on the door unlocked themselves.\n\nThe few moments before I opened up the door were filled with fear, and a type of frightful curiosity. I slowly drew open the door.\n\nThe creaking racket that it made as the hinges slowly began to loosen their frozen grip on the door sent shivers down my spine.\n\nI couldn't take the anxiety of it all, and in my panic, I threw open the door, sending it crashing into the wall it was attached to,\n\n and raised my waraxe high, sucked in last gulp of breath and got ready to scream at the top of my lungs.\n\nThen, I released a ragged sigh of reprieve as I looked around at the fresh fallen snow on my doorstep. Just snow, nothing else.\n\nI returned to my chair, and recovered myself with my pelts, and stared into the depths of the embers at the bottom of my hearth left from my fire. I slowly began to snooze,\n\nand slept with half an eye open that night, jumping into alertness at every creak and shudder my home made. Until I was blessed by the long streaks of the dawning sun, enchanting my small abode in a golden light.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wolf and Pig", "§bKatona Therenal", "The pig and the wolf\n-------------------\n\nOnce upon a time, there was a pig, a pig that enjoyed butchering those who would upset him. Opening them up, trying to find what make them 'tick'. The pig once, had a friend. That friend was the wolf.\n\nStrange, for such different creatures to be friends. But that's what they were. The wolf kept his anger contained, taking it out on himself. One day, the pig threatened to butcher the wolve's family. The wolf flared with anger, but as he usually does,\n\ntook it out himself. The wolf started hating the Pig, losing all sort of friendship he ever had towards him. The pig took this as a sign of hatred, and so, he attacked his family. The wolf twitched with anger. As the pig was arrested the wolf went to end\n\nthe pig's miserable life. He was not able to do so, and was pushed away. As the pig made his escape through death, the wolf followed. And once they were face to face, the wolf took his chance. Using his new found magic he immobilized the pig\n\nHe then started to butcher the pig, as he did so with his family. Anger flared through his eyes as he skinned the pig, cutting off his ears, feeding them to the pig, the pig squealed, asking for a swift death. The Wolf wouldn't allow it, after hours of\n\ntorture, the wolf left the pig to hurt, feel the anger and pain the wolf had put up with. \n\nThis is the story of the Wolf and the Pig\n\nThis is the story of Katona and Miran.", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 4", "§bFenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\"\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: The action begins in part four of \"Double Dragon!\" I hope you enjoy, and as always, Onto the story!\n\nChapter Eleven: Moonlit Melee\nAfter helping to clean up the large meal, I asked if it would be any trouble if I slept somewhere in their home. \"Follow me! I gotcha covered!” Natalie said, then led me to her room. She rubbed the back of her head\n\nSheepishly when we arrived \"Eheh, we don't really have a guest room, but I have two beds in mine so uh, guess where you're sleeping tonight!\" She said with a sly smile. I looked in the room with a grin on my face, \"Thank you so much for everything\n\nNatalie; I don't know how I could repay you.\" I said. Natalie waved her hand at me \"Forget about it! We're friends now right?\" She replied,walking into her room and throwing open a chest in front of the bed to the right. She rummaged around in it before\n\nPulling out a big net, exactly like the one that I was trapped in previously. She began to head back out of the room \"I just gotta go put this up, be back in a second!\" She said as she dashed down the hallway and out the front door. I giggled softly,\n\nLooking out the window to watch. She glowed slightly in the light of the full moon, giving a peaceful aura about her. She unhooked the cut net, before attaching the new one, standing back and resetting her trap. I saw some movement out of the corner of my\n\nEye, and when I looked over to the source, I saw the glint of a metal blade cut through the darkness. Bandits! I pounded on the window, desperately trying to get Natalie’s attention, but my racket making must not have been loud enough. The bandit was\n\nGetting closer, and now there were two! I sprinted out of the room, throwing my hat off “Shamone wake up! We need to save Natalie!\" I shouted at the parasite. He startled awake,before my hair grew out in thick cords, now reaching my lower back. Long hair\n\nHovered up and down my back, as I burst out the front door, \"Natalie! Watch out!\" I called out, warning her of the bandits. She looked to me, then around her, jumping back as she spotted the bigger of the two bandits already bringing his arming sword\n\nForward diagonally, aiming for her neck. She wasn't fast enough. The blade cut straight through her, cleanly decapitating her head from her body. I watched as her head flew through the air, landing on the ground, her body collapsing beside it. The clunky\n\nMan laughed \"I gotcha bitch!\" He shouted. I stopped dead in my tracks, holding my hand to my mouth to stop me from screaming. Sudden anger and sadness filled me to the brim, fueling my drive to take these guys out. I dropped my hand into a fist, stomping\n\nTowards him loudly as he laughed \"What are you gonna do little girl, kill me?\" He said amused, raising his bloody sword. I grimaced and bared my teeth, \"I'm not gonna kill you... I'm just gonna beat the shit out of you!\" I yelled, before charging at the\n\nMan, reaching into my hair and grabbing Shamones jaw, flinging it forward. His mouth shot outwards in my right hand, covering my arm in hair, forming the gaping maw of an alligator's mouth at my hand, outwards. The action took both of the men by suprise\n\nAnd the one that struck down Natalie swung at the hair, only to have his sword bounce off the thick cord back towards him, smacking his muscled chest but not cutting into him. Shamone bit the bandits left arm fiercely, piercing through his clothing and\n\nTearing at his flesh with his gruesome teeth. He cried out in pain, twisting his body, trying to escape the wicked bite. I swung my left fist as hard as I could, lengths of hair covering it up and spinning rapidly as tiny blades of hair grew on the now\n\nSpinning drill of a punch. He brought up his sword with his right arm, his left being disabled by Shamones teeth, attempting to block the powered up punch. My fist slammed into the flat of the blade, pressing it hard against his chest. I roared in pure\n\nUnadulterated rage at the man and the drill punch sped up while the sword starting glowing orange with heat from the intense friction acting against it. The man grunted and struggled with the blade, barely staying in place as his feet began to drag\n\nAgainst the dirt. \"Behind us!\" Warned Shamone. I shouted in fury, retracting the drilling arm and alligators bite, swinging my head forward, while a loud buzzing played in my ears. \"Gotcha!\" Shamone said as he responded to my actions, and thick cords of\n\nHair shot out with the headbutt like action. The hair ensnared the bandit in front of me as I lifted my head along with the bandit, and flung him behind me. The bigger bandit landed on the small frail one behind me, being crushed by his comrade. I turned\n\nTo face them, my hair flowing in thick swaths behind me “This is for Natalie you bastards!” I screamed and proceeded to kick the living hell out of both of them until they were poor, sniveling excuses of men. They moaned in pain and agony, as I looked at\n\nThem to make sure the bandits were down for the count. \"Don't you dare try to escape.\" I said in the most threatening voice I could muster. They coughed in response, writhing on the ground. I looked back to where I thought Natalie's body was and... It\n\nWasn't there. I looked around frantically, a panicked look on my face. Who would steal a body?! Then I heard something that made me believe I was going insane. I heard Natalie’s laughter. I looked to the source of the laughter and very nearly fainted.\n\nThere stood Natalie’s headless body, but she held her head at her side like a helmet. \"I didn't know you had a parasite! That's awesome!\" Her head said with a smile. Tears brimmed at my eyes and my knees grew weak \"This can't be real, you were killed!\" I\n\nSaid, not believing what I was seeing. She laughed again \"Haven't you heard that cats have nine lives? Well, I guess you could say this cat has quite a few more lives than nine, but the puns still there.\" She said, raising her head up over her exposed\n\nNeck. She plunked her head back down where it belonged, twisting it left then right. She smiled and spread her arms wide, as if it was no big deal that her head had come off. It was at that moment that the night had become too much for me to handle.\n\nI fell onto my knees, as my vision quickly went dark, and I blacked out.\n\nChapter Twelve: So That Really Did Happen?\nI woke up in a bed, still fully clothed from the feel of it. I was laying on my right side, with Shamone facing the rest of the room. The bed smelled of fresh laundry and, not surprisingly, cat hair. The\n\nEvents of last night came crashing down on me, as I sat up quickly and threw the covers off myself. I looked around the room to find that Natalie was nowhere to be found. I got out of the bed and grabbed my hat which was sitting on the bedside table,\n\nSlamming it over Shamone, right as he was greeting me with a \"Morn-\" Poomf. Covered. I heard his teeth clicking together in annoyance. \"Kid, take it easy, your friends fine. She said she was gonna get a small catnap in then go make breakfast... Speaking\n\nOf which! It's food time!\" Shamone said greedily. Even after hearing this reassuring news from Shamone, I rushed out the bedroom and to the kitchen. There I saw Sixis and Roger, weeping over dramatically \"Oh whatever shall we do! Our one and only\n\nDaughter was slain last night! Oh woe is we!\" Roger said, trying to hide a grin, while Sixis just started laughing. \"You-you’re laughing about your daughter dying!?\" I exclaimed in disbelief. Roger waved his hand \"She didn't die Fuqua! She has a parasite\n\nTo. Although from what we know from our chat with Shamone (\"He was still awake when you passed out by the way\" added Sixis.), Fishtail is a much different type of parasite.\" Robert said, as Sixis picked up where he left off \"Shamone helps you in combat a\n\nLot more than Fishtail, and can talk, but he can't grant you the ability to remain alive even after having your limbs cut off!\" Sixis explains. I eventually caught on to what they were saying \"So you mean to say that she's-\" I asked, before being\n\nInterrupted by Natalie herself \"Indestructible! Pretty much!\" She said, bursting into the dining room with huge stacks of pancakes on platters in both hands, balancing a bottle of syrup on her head between her long cat ears. She set the platters of\n\nPancakes on the table, then snatching the syrup off her head and placing it in between the fat stacks. I ran forward and grabbed Natalie in a hug \"You scared me half to death!\" I thought when your head got cut off, you were done for!\" I exlaimed, being\n\nVery upset. \"Eheh, sorry about that, probably should have mentioned that sooner. But for now, why don't you sit down and we can have an eat off again. I won't let you beat me this time!\" Natalie replied with grin, hugging me back briefly, before gently\n\nPrying me off. I nodded my head, “What about the bandits? What happened to them?” I asked. “Oh, them, I took care of it, told them that if they came back, their head would be the one on the ground. Then they just ran off.\" Natalie responded, sitting down\n\nAt the table.  \"Stop messing around babe and get ta eatin! I'm starvin up here!\" Shamone yelled, vibrating my skull. I took the hat off my head, letting my short hair free. Now that the family knew of Shamone there was no real reason to hide him \"Fine you\n\nGreedy hog!\" I shouted back, then sliding into the seat next to Natalie. The rest of the family chuckled at our bickering, as we all began to eat. It looked like a return to normalcy for me... Wait, wasn't I supposed to train for something?\n\n\n\n\n================End Of Part Four\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCharacter Info-->\n\nNatalie FoRune: Age: 17 1/3. Height: 5'8\". Weight: 127 lbs. Likes: Making friends, Sunlit naps, Bowling, Golf, Parkour, Subjecting others to terrible puns, Robbing from the rich, Giving to the poor, Potatoes.\nDislikes: The mob, Feliz, Sushi, Guards,\n\nBullies, Marsupials, Loud noises, Lemonade, Getting caught.\nA feline feral, Natalie FoRune is an excelent thief and swordswoman. She makes use of her ability to not die of mortal wounds to her advantage, often stopping large groups of bandits from robbing\n\nA singular person. She is the mix between a human and a kharajyr, and has the traits of both. Her parasite, Fishtail, is her primary weapon of choice, her second being her claws. Her playfulness while fighting is a key signature of hers, often throwing\n\nOff enemys at how she laughs in the face of certain doom and death. She has been known for taking off her own head and placing it in random places, either to spy on people, or scare them.", ""),
