        StaticBook("~Wheat Poem~", "§bDedicant Renn", "Renn's Poem\n\n~~\n\nA golden glisten of summer sea,\nGraceful arms waving to and fro.\nA warm sensation runs through,\nA feeling of protect and peace bestow.\n\nSoft movements from a gentle breeze,\nGrace, prosperity is of Nature's own.\nThin straws of strength and vigor,\nA sense of light against the unknown.\n\nLand's children of grain,\nTreated as a gift that provides life.\n\nA gift of quelling formidable hunger,\nA might savior of times of strife.\n\nA life of giving, a seed to a stalk,\nO' Nature, grant me day and week.\nThat the grains retain their numbers,\nFor a life without wheat shows bleak.", ""),
        StaticBook("Close but far", "§bCorvo Attano", "I sense the voice getting stronger, it can now control me like some sort of demon.\nIt is the darkest, evil side of me that I have never seen or heard before. This is the side that allows me to kill the innocent and take from the poor.\n\nThe voice only comes when I am angered or am making the wrong choices.\n\nI took a mans life away today, he was innocent but the voice insisted I strangle him as I did it a deep laugh in the back of my head started to grow, I felt weak, But my grasp of\n\nthe mans neck would not let go, he had tears dripping down his eyes, trying to punch me with his useless fists and then suddenly I fell back, just as the man died.\n\n\"Well done Corvo, well done indeed\" the voice whispered.\n\n\"Please leave me alone, leave me alone\"\nI cried.\n\"But Corvo\" he smiled before chuckling...\"I am you!\"\n\nCorvo listened carefully tensing his arms with anger.\n\"Whatever you do I do, However whatever I do you do.\" The voice\n\nmurmured.\n\n\"Now please he said let's get to buisness\"\n\nCorvo's left hand started to move to his blunt, iron dagger, he withdrawed it waving it around.\n\n\"Perhaps Corvo! We should give this\n\nweapon a trying out\".\n\nA young villager was carrying boxes of food the storage shed in Illicia where they were standing.\n\n\"Kill him\" he snapped\n\"I will not a kill a young boy\".\n\n\"Kill him or I will him myself Corvo!\" He shouted.\nThe boy looked around and then got back to his work.\n\"I WILL NOT KILL HIM\"\nCorvo raged with anger, blood pumped heavily through his Vessels.\n\nCorvo felt his grip the sword tightly, he started to move unable to speak he could blink and see.\nHe crept upon the young boy grabbing him by the shoulder.\nThe boy wrestled Corvo but he was too strong for a young boy like him.\n\nCorvo kicked his chest and got him onto the ground, he pointed his sword at the boy.\n\"Please...Sir do not d..d..don't do t...this to me\".\nA creepy grin grew on Corvo's face frightening the boy.\nCorvo leaped onto the boy stabbing him\n\nrepeatedly in the chest, blood gushed out of the boy's mouth it appeared Corvo had punctured a lung.\nHe kicked the boy over again and left him to die.\n\"Need's a bit of a sharpen\" Corvo chuckled\n\nThe force that was controlling Corvo released and Corvo was set free again.\n\"You sick bastard, that boy was innocent\".\n\n\"Now, now Corvo you're the one who released me into your head.\"\n\nWritten by Corvo Attano. ((mrdigdug118\n\n))", ""),
        StaticBook("A life..........", "§bLurk", "His body lay there with his guts torn out, I stand at the back watching our leader as he tears bits of his skin off and eats them.\n\nHe pulled out a slimy liver of the man and slurped it down his throat!\n\n\"T'ats what yer get fer tryin' ter assassinate me'h yer focks\"\nhe said with bits of kidney spewing out his mouth!\n\"A'h loike ter eat me hostages alive,\" he smiled a creepy grin.\n\n\"He chewed into the mans face tearing away the muscle and cheek bones.\nThe man screamed for his life, his voice boomed over the forest.\n\nOur leader dug his nails into his face ripping it open a bit more, He started to swallow the flesh until we heard footsteps nearby.\nThe leader rubbed some blood over his chest and pretended to be dead, the rest of us fled behind the trees.\n\n Orcs came out grunting, \"Oooh look at t'at we got ourselves a'h dinner.\"\nI took my bow off my back and aimed it at one of the Orcs, I slowly put the arrow on and Fired at the Orcs head.\n\nThe orc fell down with a loud slam.\nThe rest of us jumped out killing the other 2 Orcs.\nOur leader got up and thanked me then kicked the Orcs bodies to see if they were really dead.\n\nWe walked back to Petrus and our leader went into the Tavern, his blood stained outfit caused some curiosity, so people were\nasking if he was stabbed.\n\nHe didn't reply to none of them who asked, but instead slurped his Ale, I guess to get the taste of Internal Organs out of his\nmouth.\nI wandered out of Petrus and headed to the streets to the Temple.\n\nA man named Arthur stopped me and guided me into his Tavern, owned by Vinnie The Chef.\n I brought a couple of Ale's and stayed there writing, until I noticed a little girl\nwalk through.\n\nI decided to make a joke \"Yer 'ere fer Ale?\" I said, unfortunatley the father didn't take it Swell he told to the daughter to go\nplay outside onto the porch.\n\nHe started to get angry so before he could punch me I decided to punch him straight in the nose, blood dripped down from nostrils\nas he stood there holding it, tilting his head back.\n\nHe told me to get outside so I withdrawed my sword and was ready for a fight.\nI looked at him angrily, A women poked me with her sword and I can't remember much after that apart from he put his hands onto my neck behind me.\n\nArthur told me the story later on.\nI decided to walk back to Petrus and go to my Leader, but 6 Elves stopped me they wanted my swords, my bow and everything I had\nin my bag.\n\nLuckily for me, my group wasn't far behind the Elves and they came out of the trees chopping off the Elves heads, blood squirted\neverywhere.\n((Okay that is the first part of my Journal I will make the second one soon))", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations I", "§bLorar Minskin", "Observations and Their Benefits\n-------------------Written by Lorar Min.\n-------------------  As you look around do you notice the fate of the people around you? The tick tock of the clockwork and the innerworkings of the life they live is set in stone.\n\nIt is to the point of which it seems that even the biggest actions seem to have no effect in pulling people out of this loop. Now, It'd be safe for me to say that you are probably one of those people who dilly-dally around and are stuck in one preset path\n\nin which you feel that you have no control over. Infact It'd also be safe for me to say that you, yourself, the person that is reading this is so clueless that they don't even realize that they're stuck in this loop. You need help, fast.\n Unlike others\n\nbefore you, these events don't need to happen. They don't need to be one event piling on another and another to the point of no return. You, yes you have a chance to stop this. At this point I'd say you're quite confused on what I'm talking about. I'm\n\n talking about your old friend who is predetermined every single, every single day I tell you to do the same exact thing in which he does the same exact tasks until the point of no return. That no returning point being death. I'm talking about changing\n\nwhat you're doing. For better or worse, for the danger, for the fun, for the neverending amazement of not knowing what is going to happen next. Unlike your ancestors you can change what your future may hold. Perhaps your grandfather was a carpenter and\n\nyour father was also a carpenter and by golly-gee you better be a carpenter. That, that itself is what I'm talking about. Do not follow what is preset for you, stand out.\n You've got one life and you better make it worth living because who knows what\n\ntommorrow may hold. Take that last step, eat that extra roll, ask to court that special lady, do whatever you feel like you may never have another chance to do. Because who knows, you might not be there the next day to do it.\n\n-My First Book, Lorar", ""),
        StaticBook("Task From Verden", "Jallentime", "((X-1162 / Z-427))\n\nHead to Darkhaven and question the population about any strange occurances or sightings in the nearby forest.\n\nBring back your findings to me directly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Melunis the Mad", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Melunis the Mad\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\nI was travelling to a place called Geedin in search of a philosopher called Melunis. This man was said to be the wisest in the land, according to my friend who went there a while back. So I figured I would see what wisdom he could offer me.\n\nI arrived in the town and walked up to a guard. I said,\n\n“Excuse me sir, could you direct me to the man named Melunis?” The guard just laughed and said,\n\n“The only Melunis I know is a madman, you can find him over by the alley.” I thought to myself, this madman couldn’t be the one that my friend was talking about. My friend was a very smart person and wouldn’t confuse a wise man with a madman.\n\nSo to satisfy my knowing of whether or not this was the correct man, I went to the alleyway and saw an old man in rags. I said to the man.\n\n“Are you the man known as Melunis?” to which he looked at me, smiled, and said,\n\n“Indeed so! How can I help you this fine day!” The day was overcast, and cold. I couldn’t see how it was fine.\n\n“Would you happen to know my friend, James Linson?”  The man looked overjoyed at the name and said,\n\n“Why yes! I remember the lad. I do hope he is doing well.”\n\n“Well he told me you were the wisest in the land…” I said, to which Melunis replied with a frown,\n\n\n“Wise? No I’m not wise. I am just a ragged old man in an alleyway. Do I look like I’m Wise?”\n\n“No you don’t.” I said. “You don’t look wise at all.” The man then got a sparkle in his eyes.\n\n”Not wise at all?” said the man. “Well I must agree. You being very well off must know what it means to be wise, as you are in a far better place then I.” The man thought for a second, then said, “Tell me, what does it mean to be wise.”\n\n“Well it means that you know a lot about things.” I said, “Like a smith knows how to smith well, he is wise in smithing.”\n\n“Ah..” said the man. “ So in a sense, being wise is having knowledge.”\n\n“Yes.” I said.\n\n“ Alright, well what is knowledge.” Said Melunis. “As in how would I be able to obtain it to become more wise.” I thought for a second, then said,\n\n“Knowledge is knowing something, and obtained by learning.”\n\n“I see!” Said the man. “But… how do I know I know something.” At this I was a bit perplexed. I said,\n\n“Could you explain what you mean?” The man nodded and said,\n\n“In other words, How do you know what you know is true.”\n\n“Because you know it works when applied to things.” I said.\n\n“Alright.” Said the man. “So knowledge is what you know works when applied to things, but how does that make it true?”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said.\n\n“I mean for example, we could see an abstract painting.” Said Melunis. “You could think it’s one thing, I could think its another. Both works when applied, at least to the individual, but who is right?”\n\n“I guess we would both be right.” I said. “It would be up to the individual.”\n\n“Ah I see now!” Said the man. “So knowledge is what works with the individual. But still, how do we know it is true? Because isn’t the truth universal?”\n\n I began to get frustrated. But… Then I came to a realization.\n\n“I guess the truth is up to the person.” The man looked at me and said,\n\n“So there is no real truth? But what about common knowledge?” I thought for a second and said,\n\n“The common knowledge is what people have a common belief in.” Melunis nodded, seeming to understand.\n\n“But then what is the real truth?” The man said.\n\n“The real truth…” I began, “The real truth is… unknowable. Even if we got to it, people still would have different opinions. And those opinions might have more people believing in it than the real truth.” Melunis smiled at me and said,\n\n“Thank you, I think I understand now what it means to have knowledge.”\n\nSoon after this conversation, I left. Slightly confused, but more understanding.\n\n\n Though now I realized what my friend meant by him being the wisest in the land.\n\nThe End\n\n\"Everything you think you know has to do with what you believe.\"\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("The Inner Circle", "§bLeyun Kameki", "The Inner Circle\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\n\nExisting within the structure of the Druidic Order Circle of Malinor, which is the primary and mother Circle of Druids, is an Inner Circle. The Inner Circle is rather different than a Druidic Circle, however. It is part of an existing Circle, composed of\n\nthree Archdruids and no set number of Druid Guides who all take responsibility for the inner working of the Order.\n\nThe Druids of the Inner Circle are those who are permitted to guide and attune Dedicants as well as train Druids in the\n\nways of teaching or in harnessing the Gifts of Nature. During a Moot, the Druids of the Inner Circle cast their votes, with only the best interests of the Order in mind, to make a particular decision for the Order.\n\nThe Inner Circle doesn't dictate the\n\nOrder, nor does it dictate or manipulate individual Druids. Rather, the Inner Circle has, for countless centuries, only served to maintain order by making larger decisions for the Order and effectively upbringing new generations of Druids.\n\nThe Archdruids and Druid Guides of the Inner Circle are crucial to the function and future of a Druidic Order. This ancient and important aspect of Orderly structure should never be forgotten. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Neo-Druidism", "§bTristanm1", "Neo-Druidism\nBy Salmon Druid Petyr\n\nWith some modern druidic practices wandering astray, it has been necessary for me to scribe another text - that of Neo-Druidism. Throughout my travels and my meditative studies, I have had revelations unknown to others. It is important to understand that\n\nthere is a special type of balance that druids themselves remember to study - action and non-action. Let me clarify. Action is motion, the motion of restoring balance, and of being the hand of Nature. Non-action is meditation and silence; invisible\n\nmotion. You see, this is the only Way to truly understand Nature, the Universe, the \"It\". For, through non-action you may feel \"It\", and through action you may be \"It\".  Call this \"It\" what you want; most druids will call it Nature. What is important is\n\nto understand what Nature truly is, and how it relates to you. To reveal this is the goal of this tome.\n\nSection 1 - The Unity of Nature\nThe first fault in thinking is to make distinctions - those between you and Nature, between life and death, between good and evil.  Everything is Nature, despite what any given piece believes. A druid does not use nature: a\n\ndruid is merely a piece who realizes the profound truth. Through non-action, one may truly understand this concept and feel it course through them. However, while meditating in non-action, one also separates themselves from the flow; the Way; the path\n\nthat Nature chooses for its pieces. To rejoin with Nature, one must practice action.\n\nSection 2 - The Way of Nature\nNature does what it will, and while we realize this while meditating, sometimes we forget in action. We are merely moving along the river of life, the tides of balance. While we believe that we are restoring the balance, it\n\nis balance restoring itself in an everlasting self-conflict. Thus, through action, we are the hands of Nature, of balance, of the Way. One must not think of \"using\" Nature while playing their part, but of \"being\" Nature. This is a common mistake as well\n\namong young druids and non-druids. They think to restore the world by planting lots of trees... but that is not balance, nor is it even the way to achieve balance. Action alone is not the Way, for one forgets the purpose of action. Only with the mix of\n\naction and non-action can one achieve the goal: to have your cake and eat it, too.\n\nSection 3 - The Druid\nSo as we can now see, the Druid is simply the most important hand, the piece Nature uses to govern itself. To truly try to understand is a task that lies within meditation and non-action. However, there is a limit to the mental reach\n\nof the pieces, for as no one truly knows all of themselves, Nature does not know all of itself. This is a fairly important observation: that even though Nature is unified, the unification is marked by threadlines of dubiousness and doubt. The Neo-Druid\n\nshould not fret, however. There are uneven surfaces in every river. No tree has identical leaves. Just so, nothing, no \"It\", can be the symmetrical perfection one would like to see. Randomness and uniqueness are inherent in Nature, as defining as the\n\nunity itself. Paradoxical though it may seem, through balance of action and non-action, it shall be revealed to you, and only then will you understand the phrase...\n\n\n\"All is One\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Orcish Cypher", "§b[Dedicant] Thickfeet", "The Orcish Cypher\n\n\n       By\n          Lethius\n        Thickfeet\n\nForward:\n\nI have spent a great deal of time learning the 'Blah' of our powerful friends. I find the culture of these people to be of great importance to our histories. They have been significant in many of the shifts of power since the beginning\n\nof our time.\n\nTake heart the cypher enclosed. It may one day save your life like it has mine.\n\n\nL. Thickfeet\n\nWe begin with the basic numeral system. I’ve never seen numbers used outside of combative situations. Rudimentary shoving of these words together is how you can create greater numerical amounts.\n\n   ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n Ash: 1 \n Dub: 2\n Gakh: 3\n Futh: 4\n H' : 5\n H'ash: 6\n H'dub: 7\n H'gakh: 8\n H'futh: 9\n Ashety: 10\n Dubty: 20\n Gakhty: 30\n\nThe regular language is diverse and quite gutteral. Regular practice and a forceful accent is required as to not offend through imitation nor risk being misunderstood.\n\nBlah -  The very language of the Orcish people.\n\n Ug - A typical greeting.\n Throm'ka - Formal greeting usually seen between significant members of their world.\n Gug'ye - Goodbye\n Yub - Yes\n Nub - No\n Agh - And\n Lat - You\n Mi - Me/I\n\n Rulg - Used as thank, or the act of thanking\n Gruk - To understand or acknowledge a request\n Dabu - To respectfully acknowledge a request\n\nMost of these words have specific intent. Be wary of the situations you might use them in.\n\nThe many adjectives used in the 'Blah' are distinct. They can paint a greater picture than I can here and can really invoke a wide range of meaning.\n\n\n        ________\n  @XX|========>\n\n Bubhosh - Big, Great, Superior, or Significant\n Nubhosh - Small, Useless, or Inferior\n Snaga - Slave\n Pushdug - Something that smells badly\n Glob - Fool\n\nFor the most part the above is used in negative ways and to invoke anger.\n\nThe most harsh and heavy curse words are not typically passed around lightly. Be very careful at the usage of the following:\n\n Skah - A word used in force as a singular insult.\n\n Saahkah - A harsher version.\n\n Blarg - An individuals dwelling and home. May not be permanent.\n Buurz - Dark or Coldness.\n Mojo - Magic. Many are superstitious around forms of magic.\n Klomp - To Attack. Not intended to be humorous.\n Flat - Dead\n\nThe many people of our world have various names depending on the experiences of each individual Orc.\n\nWhile there are collected here many phrases, more come and go as slang changes amongst the newer generations.\n\n Brudas\n Clan-brudas\n Ork-kin\n Uruk\n \n All words for fellow Orcs that are trusted or have not yet lost their honor.\n\n Krugmar Orc are those that live unorthodox lives. These orcs might live with other races or be outcasted.\n\nI have met few Krugmar. It is unfortunate that many are killed or go into hiding.\n\nAny Krugmar should be considered our greatest link to understanding the Orc kind.\n\nThrough many years of wars we have lost great amounts of information on their history. I continue to seek out more Krugmar for my own studies.\n\n Stowts - Dwarves\n Twiggies / Treeuggers - Both are interchanged words for Elves\n Squeals - Halflings\n Snaaks - Hobbits\n Quikspawn / breedurs - Humans. Assumed because of short gestation periods and how many humans live in the world\n\n Shara - A more serious name for Human Kind\n Albai - A more serious name for Elves\n Gazat - An older word for Dwarves\n\nThe above are much more formal. You are likely to hear these from the Orcish Diplomats.\n\nThe various creatures of the realms have specific meanings to the Orcs. From flora and fauna, to monsters and evil, the words for the denizens of all worlds are still being collected. \n\nHere are just some of the common phrases spoken today:\n\n Buub - Pig\n Wooleh - Sheep\n Howlur - Wolves\n Nuutshara - Ascended. Creatures of the past\n Nubded - Undead. The opposite of the Ascended\n Buubshara Nubded - Zombie Pigman\n Buubshara  - Pigman\n\nReal world and commonly used phrases during war and skirmish will likely only be heard on the Orcish lines. These are important to know in the event of a confrontation with our green skinned neighbors.\n\n Uzg - The world itself\n Krimp - To snare, capture, or control someone\n Goi - An Orcish city\n Lusk - Axe\n O'lig - Bow\n Ligz - Arrow\n Zult - Sword\n Stik - Staff\n\n    <>==========@\n\n Steemiez - Most technology is referred as such. It is assumed that it particularly comes from steam powered mechanics\n Shineez - Something of Worth or Value. May or may not legitimately shine.\n\n\n   ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n\nAs you spend your time practicing and studying, remember that all languages evolve and change with passing generations. Stay open and alert to alterations and variations in your journeys.\n\nBe on the look for newer editions as well.\n\n\n\n\n\nRemember that Orcish lands are not for the faint-hearted. Do not go there if you aren't a Orc unless for a good reason. \n\n         -Freya", ""),
        StaticBook("The Inn", "§b[Bartender] Arthur Caulfrield", "True Stories\n      Made Fiction\n\n       By Arthur\n        Caulfield\n\nIt was a quiet day at the tavern. The bartender had just served the last of the ale to an odd gentleman in a mask and was beginning to pack up when A man came through the doors. \n   He said nothing. Going straight to a table in the back he\n\nwas soon followed by a young girl, no older than nine. \n   The man had a serious expression on his face while the girl had quite the opposite. She wore a bright smile that had not been seen in a tavern for years.\n\nThe bartender could see by the shape of their ears that they were elves. They were obviously not ashamed of it, wearing the sign so openly in a place so close to Oren. \n   This scared the bartender. It had been quite a common occurence to cut the tips of\n\nelven ears a while back and he was not sure whether the practice still continued. \n    After a while, the drinks hit the gentleman in the mask. The bartender was just cleaning out his fifth empty mug when the gentleman spoke up.\n\n\"Shouldn't bring a kid to a place like this,\" He said turning around in his stool to face the man, his back leaning against the bar. \"Could get hurt.\"\n   The elven man did not respond for what seemed like an eternity, but what could have only been seconds\n\n\"Don't talk about my child.\" And believing it was over, he turns back to face the table.\n   \"I'll talk 'bout ooever I bloody well want\" The gentleman in the mask responded. \n    The bartender sighed. This was all too common an occurence. Each night a\n\nbrawl broke out for one reason or another. Tonight it had been over a child's safety. \n   There was little time to react, while the masked gentleman was drunk, he was also very agile and moved with quickness no drunk could even comprehend.\n\nJumping from the bar stool, the masked man approached the table and waited for the elven man to react. \n   No words were spoken. The elven man simply got up and pushed the man aside as he walked over to the bar. The bartender smiled\n\npolitely and served him some ale. The masked man did not like this response. At a sprint, he crossed the room and hit the elf in the nose just as he turned to register the noise.\n   The elf stumbled back and closed both hands around the nose\n\nwhich had already began to seep blood that stained his colorful blue robes.\n    The bartender, having recoiled in shock, now tried to dissolve the bar fight not realising it was already too late.\n\nThe girl still sat on the table at the far corner of the bar. Watching in horror. \n    The father, after controlling the bleeding, turned to his daughter and demand she stay there.\n    The little girl did not say a word, just simply nodded along to his\n\norders.\n   Both men had the same mindset. Both men remained silent, knowing what was going to happen. Both men left the bar and stood on the grass outside, still wet from that mornings rain. \n    The daughter, knowing her father could no longer see,\n\nran to the nearest window and stared out, both hands and face smooshed against the glass in anticipation.\n   However, the father saw this as he looked back, causing him to point and shout something muted by the double doors which were now closed.\n\nThe bartender felt sorry for her. To have a father so easily led into brawls could not have been easy. \n   \"Do you like orange juice?\" He asked her in a friendly tone. She turned away from the window to look at him with some level of confusion.\n\n\"Did you know that oranges are guarded by dragons?\" He asked in a conversational tone, walking over to a chest full of fruit. \n   It had always seemed like a waste to have this chest, he though, seeing as no one ever came to a bar to order freshly\n\nsqueezed lemon juice.     \"Dragons?\" The girl asked, mystified. Her eyes widened, not in fear this time, but in amazement. \"But why would dragons want to guard oranges?\" She asked a moment later, as the bartender brought out a mug and oranges.\n\n\"Well, oranges are the most delicious fruit, and the dragons know it. So in order to get the oranges, we need to defeat the dragons!\" The bartender explained, using his imagination for the first time in a while.\n\n\"Wow\" The girl replied, now trying to balance herself on one of the bar stools. When the orange juice was placed in front of her, she eagerly drank it, respecting the brave knights who allowed her to have it.\n\nThe bartender chuckled softly, knowing no other child would eagerly drink bitter orange juice like she did. \n   The fight outside has escalated, the bartender could see this through the window to his right. They had begun to draw swords and the\n\nshouting had intensified. \n    But in the bar, the child looked up at him with innocent eyes. Forgetting the danger her father could be  in and instead, entranced in a story of dragons and oranges.\n\nOf course, the mug had a bottom. And she soon found it. Her attention was lost almost instantly and she began to turn towards the window once again. \n   Quickly thinking, the bartender grabbed a pumpkin from the chest of fruits and plopped it onto his\n\nhead. Cutting off every sense he had. \n   \"Mmmffmfmfm\" he tried to mumble in order to get her attention. Thankfully she looked around and giggled at the sight of him. \n   Despite his embarassment, the bartender was glad he drew her\n\nattention away for just a moment. \n   For it was in that moment that her father snapped the masked mans neck and left him lifeless on the ground. \n   It was an image the child would never have to see, and that was worth the pumpkin becoming stuck to his\n\nhead.\n   Once the fight was over, and the father had rummaged through the corpse's possessions, he came to collect her. \n   She sat on the bar stool looking up at the man with the pumpkin head. Giggling to herself even as her father\n\nwalked in with a bloody nose and battle scars all across his arm and legs.\n   \"You think this is funny?\" He asked angrily, walking up to her and pulling her off of the bar stool. \n   She had little time to explain as he picked her up and took her out.\n\nThe bartender waved her goodbye, and she waved back. The father just carried on walking.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shun", "§bLeyun Kameki", "The Shun\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\n\nAn individual who has proven to be a threat to the Druidic Order might very well be worthy of a shun. One such individual isn’t someone who a particular Druid or a select few Druids dislike or disagree with, but is someone who has offended an entire\n\nCircle or the Order in some way.\n\nOnly an Archdruid may make the notion to shun an individual, which is done while holding the floor at a Moot. He or she will state the reasons for presenting the shun; following, the subject of the shun, if\n\npresent, will answer to the accusations before the Druids of the Moot. Finally, the Inner Circle shall openly vote to pass the shun or not.\n\nOnce a shun is passed on an individual, it shall last until the Inner Circle deems it right, with only the best\n\ninterests for the Order, to end. No Druid of the Order is permitted to speak to a shunned individual or affiliate with them in any way and should, therefore, answer their words with “Much wind pours from your mouth.”\n\nA shunned individual is never allowed to step foot on the holy grounds of a grove, unless requested by an Archdruid in the case of relieving the shun, and shall be forcibly removed from a grove, by any Druid, if he or she refuses to leave. Furthermore, if\n\na shunned individual continuously harasses a Druid outside the grove, and the Druid or Dedicant has spoken the single statement he is permitted to speak to a shun, then hostile actions may be taken upon the individual.\n\nA Druid may also be shunned from the Order, and sometimes unattuned as well, which is the most dishonored action able to be taken upon a Druid. A shun is nothing to ever take lightly and any member of the Druidic Order, or the independent Circle who has\n\ndeemed the shun, should follow suit only the actions allowed to be taken against a shun or face consequences him or her self. Blessed be he who is righteous and loyal and true and never deserving of the shun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Bravery", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nBravery:\nThis is not a Task that is assigned, rather it is earned by the Dedicant. If an event occurs during their training, or at the grove, and the Dedicant shows an act of exceptional selflessness and bravery in defense of the Order,\n\nwhile maintaining admirable attitude and integrity, their Guide may deem to count this action as a completed Task, as they have proven that their heart is with the Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Bonemeal", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nSpread of Bonemeal: \n\nThis is a simple task usually given early to a Dedicant. You give them a moderate amount of bonemeal and send them out into the wilderness to spread it out upon an empty plains or clearing to make the\n\nground lush and fertile. They can also perform this Task within the grove if there is an area suitable for it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Fairy Ring", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nFairy Ring Meditation:\nThis is an important lesson, and you should encourage the Dedicant to return to fairy rings on their own from time to time, even after their attunement. For this lesson, you should explain what they will experience\n\nonce they enter the ring. Once they understand, have them sit within the ring and give them the time they need to become used to the sensation, answer any questions they have. Then, have them meditate,\n\nhelp them find peace and balance, and let them meditate until either you feel they have succeeded, or the strain of the communion is causing them undue stress. Reinforce the experience with questions\n\nabout what they felt, what they saw, and if they have any questions themselves.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Balance", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nLesson on The Balance:\nThis is a very in-depth lesson to give your Dedicants, but a very important one. You may find the 'Neo-Druidism' tome to be especially helpful in this lesson, as it gives a most accurate description if positive\n\nand negative action towards preserving the Balance. This is sometimes a hard concept to grasp, but a very important one for every Druid. You must impress upon them that a Druid must recognize\n\nwhen action is required, and when observation or even lack of action is required, and understanding what these truly mean to a Druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Knowledge", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nBroader Knowledge:\nThis Task is given in order to teach the Dedicant that knowledge is perhaps the most important thing in the world. Ignorance can easily get you killed, and misunderstanding can easily cause offense where there should not have been.\n\nGenerally this task involves going out and finding two books or tomes that contain knowledge or teachings from outside the Order, it is important they are not Druidic in content, as the entire point of this lesson is to understand\n\nsomething else and fill gaps in their knowledge so they can be more successful in their future dealings.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Aspects", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\n Lesson on The Aspects:\nThis lesson teaches a Dedicant the core 'faith', if you will, of Druidism, The Aspects. While little precise information is known about them, through dreams and visions Druids have gleaned a little of the nature of our patrons.\n\nIt is important for the Dedicant to understand that without The Aspects, Druids would have almost none of their gifts, it is the blessing of The Aspects that we can attune to the currents and melodies of nature, the ebb and flow of life around us.\n\nHelp the Dedicant develop a respect and thankful attitude towards The Aspects, they should give thanks to them often. Use other tomes such as 'An Introduction to the Aspects' to aid your lesson.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: The Void", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nDangers of the Void:\nThis lesson is the most vital for a Dedicant to understand. Void magic, ALL Void magic, is pure imbalance. If an attuned Druid casts Void magic of any sort, even a very simple spell, it damages their connection to the Aspects\n\nand their communion to nature. The Druid that attuned them will also feel when this occurs through the link they formed upon attuning the Dedicant, and Archdruids feel the Void casting as well and can sense the taint of it upon a Druid.\n\nIt is vitally important you explain this to every Dedicant so they understand the consequences of their actions and the damage they will do to their attunement. Furthermore, casting Void magic is grounds for immediate reprimand by the Order,\n\nand further offenses will lead to unattunement and removal from the order.  Void magic is a subject it pays to be knowledgeable about, ignorance can get you killed, but a Druid must never seek to use such\n\nunnatural and imbalancing magic. ((if you are a Druid and you use Void Magic of any sort, you MUST OOCly inform at least the Guide that attuned you and an Archdruid, how you approach telling them, or not, in RP is up to you.\n\nFailure to OOC inform is considered power gaming and if it is learned you have done this, you may have your attunement shattered without the chance to explain your actions. POWERGAMING IS NEVER OKAY!!!))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Aspect Tomes", "§bDedicant Elizabeth", "Aspect Tome:\nCompassion\n\nCompassion, what is it? A mysterious feeling that cannot be understood, but can be felt at the most dire moments. An example would be when a child is getting hit right before your eyes. Be honest with yourself, would you feel anything when you lay your\n\neyes upon that child? That is called Compassion. It cannot easily be described but I will try my best to decipher its purpose in the living emotion spectrum. It is true that this feeling, this emotion, is what makes people act, makes them want to do\n\nsomething, makes them want to fight back. That is true, but why is this you ask?\n\nIt is because when one person feels another person's pain, it is followed by another piece of the Emotion chain link, which is \"Rage\". When a man has been hurt there is an urge inside of him saying, \"get him back\" or \"destroy him\",\n\nbut as a Druid or a Dedicant you must resist this urge no matter what.\nCompassion is one of the reasons why we Druids strive to help people, we can see how they are lowly on the streets, how they are helpless,\n\nand how that can be changed if the Druids can help them.\n\nThis has been an Aspect description on the Emotion of Compassion. There are other races that think otherwise, but we have our own beliefs, and we choose to stand by it. This is the Tome of Compassion.\n\nCredited to Tamsin for the work, copied by Dedicant Elizabeth.\n\nAspect Tome:\nFear\n\nFear, another emotion that drives the Will of a man. This Book will describe all it can, for fear can not be a good thing for the Druids, not at all... The emotion of Fear is susceptible but can be very deceitful,\n\nit can drive people to do things they have no choice of doing, an example would be like this:\n\nImagine a man with the perfect life and perfect family, then a stranger says that all of it will be taken away in the blink of an eye if he does not kill someone. Unless his Will is strong, this man can and will murder someone for the sake of his family,\n\nand the emotion that is currently driving him is the power of fear... It is the easiest emotion to spot within yourself and another man, and too much fear can lead to insanity.\n\nThe Druid should try not to be seduced to the madness of fear. Everybody gets scared all the time, it is part of the nature of Life, but the dark side is that it can control you if you do not fight back.\n\nIn order to overcome fear, you must have Confidence and Willpower; then this darkness that lies within you shall disappear. But Fear can never die, it is like a disease that can never be cured and a fire that will never be put out, remember this,\n\nmy friends, and do not give in to it...\n\nCredited to Tamsin for the work, copied by the Dedicant Elizabeth.\n\nAspect Tome:\nGreed\n\nGreed, not even the best can resist this emotion. Something as Evil as Greed can't even be described properly, but an attempt will be made. The Emotion of Greed carries out in generations to come from the first evil.\n\nThe Evil God, Iblees, cursed the Dwarves with this evil. This Emotion, this Avarice can turn your own friends again you, and it is triggered by Temptation, which very few people can easily resist.\n\nThis makes Greed a very dangerous Emotion. This emotion is never good and must not be taken lightly, so watch yourself, for you might be its next victim.\n\nCredited to Tamsin for the work, copied by Dedicant Elizabeth.\n\nAspect Tome:\nHope\n\nHope, the very true innocence in a place where all is lost. No matter what happens, a person will always have hope, but how does it affect us? It is very simple, Hope is a very difficult emotion anybody can do with right now.\n\nA hope for a miracle or healing is most likely a very common hope, usually targeted at Aerial or any of the Arch-Aenguls, but there is also a secret within this emotion that not many people know.\n\nHope is the emotion that supported the birth of Life. It cannot be explained easily, but it is true.\n\nBut for us Druids, our trigger on Hope is very similar, but different. We have our hopes on the Aspects, which are Cerridwen and Cernunnos, we are their conduits and we expect them to assisst us in our times of need...\n\nHope can trigger within us at any moment, when War is happening, when you're being held hostage, when a family member or a friend is dying. It can happen as much as it can, but you cannot assume to ignore it.\n\nIt is often described as, \"The smallest light in a room full of darkness,\" even the very evil have it, but their use for it is on their own accord.\n\nThis also causes many things, rebellions and such, for some take Hope too seriously, and it often turns them into power-hungry people. This has been an account of this Emotion, may your new found Knowledge flourish.\n\nCredited to Tamsin for the work, copied by Dedicant Elizabeth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Laurelin", "§bArinislia", "Children of Laurelin\n\nI hear the song of Laurelin;\nThe children’s laugher singing;\nOf trees, and leaves of many things,\nTo many, the sound of bells ringing;\n\nI hear the song of  Laurelin,\nNow lost in the burning flames;\nThe echos whisper in our hearts,\nNow most don’t seem the same;\n\nI heard the song of Laurelin,\nof purity and rings;\nOf ones who mix of blood,\nAre met with acid that stings.\n\nI seek the song of  Laurelin,\nOf children’s laughter and song;\n The sound almost lost to me now,\nThough somehow I continue on.", ""),
        StaticBook("Song Anthology 2", "§bAeran", "Song Anthology: Volume 2\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi\n\nThe Day the Spit Flew\n\nA poor man came to a fair maid/\nSaid ‘I need some work, I need to get paid?’/\nShe said that’s a damn shame/\nFor, he was lame!\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi/\nHe ate messy/\nHe lvied poorly/\n\nAnd used to love a girl named Jessie!\n\nHis beard was down to his tits/\nHe smelt like uncleaned pits/\nBut he said I'm rich, geez/\nIf you counted fleas!\n\nIf you counted teeth,\nnah.\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi/\nHe ate messy/\nHe lived poorly/\nAnd used to love a girl named Jessie/\n\nOne day he saw a great knight/\nHe challenged him to a fight!/\n\nThe great warrior prepared with sword and shield/\nAnd as he took the field.../\n\nThere was the Lame Drunk/\nHe smelt like a skunk/\nFor his smell was his shield/\nHis breath, what he would weild/\n\nThe knight fell, had no choice but to yield/\nHe could not take the field/\nHis helmet was filled with puke/\nHis dismissed the drunk as a cuke!/\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi/\nHe ate messy/\nHe lived poorly/\n\nAnd used to love a girl named Jessie!/\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi/\nHe ate messy/\nHe lived poorly/\nAnd used to love a girl named Jessie/\nAnd damn was he crazy!\n\nThe Day the Spit Flew\n\nIt was a day unlike today/\nExcept, nothing like today\nThe atmosphere was the opposite of gay/\nThe atmospher was yag/\nThe Snow Elves had kidnapped a princess! Or something!/\n\nBut it did not matter, the pale devils would get it!/\nAnd by it I mean completly disproport-\nionate aggression/\nBUT I'LL BE DAMNED IF THEY DIDN'T GET IT!/\n\nTwo kingdoms met infront of another kingdom/\n\nOren, half of their court had come/\nBut all of Snelvedom showed up; Tundrak!/\nIt was a standoff to be sung about maybe when the singer was really drunk or out of songs!/\n\nThey fought with words/\n\nEmperor Chivay drowned out by his court/\nTundrak drowned out by his nation's silence/\nBut alas, no solution came/\n\nSo, with a great 'HORK'/\nAnd a loud 'POOT'/\nHead to toe/\n\nTundrak was covered with spit/\nAnd damn, wasn't it an improvement!", ""),
        StaticBook("Orc Cell", "§bCorvo Attano", "My name is Corvo Attono I have had this voice into my head ever since 7th of July.\nWhen I was 11 I use to sneak out passed my bedtime and go to the woods. I would hide under a log and wait for the Wood Elves to come, They would sing and dance and drink\n\nale all night long.I went back there one day and it seemed abandoned. The cold mist covered the area I looked around out of curiosity and stumbled over a dead Wood Elf, he had 3 arrows pierced into his pale green skin.\n\nI ripped it out and saw that it was forged by Orcs. I had no fear nor was I shocked at the sight. I was startled as a low Mumble appeared into the distance, it soon got so loud I had to cover my ears.\n\nBut it was no use, the shouting got too loud, I dived onto the ground rolling trying to make it stop. Then I realised it was coming through my head. The voice was saying: “Kill him Corvo, finish the scum off!”,\n\nSuddenly a powerful possession took over my body, the Wood Elf awoke. “H..h..help me p..p..please!”. I couldn't move any part of my body as if it were paralysed, I could only blink and roll my eyes. I glared at the Elf, he had terror in his eye's.\n\nBefore realising it, my hand had gripped a rock tightly, I picked it up and lifted it above my head.\n“Oh dear lord!” the elf whispered. My hand rammed the rock down into his face repeatedly until I could no longer swing.\n\n I dropped the rock and collapsed sideways onto the ground.\n“What have I done” I cried. he voice came back and whispered to me: “Well done Corvo!”. As I got up I started to run back to my house, I could see glimpses of a little girl staring at me.\n\n could also hear the giggles of a little girl running after me.\n“You can run Corvo he he he” The voice turned into a deep demon like voice “BUT YOU CAN'T HIDE!!!!!!”.\n\nI collapsed onto the ground and fainted. I woke up in a cell on a yellow stained mattress, a candle was lighting up the cell. I looked at myself realising I was pure naked.\n\nI checked my sides to see if I had a stolen kidney. I couldn't see or feel any stitches or scars, “HELP ME!” I shouted knowing it was useless I still done it.I could hear loud grunts in the hallways and shadows of something eating human flesh.\n\n I looked into the right corner of the cell and saw a Halfling skeleton, with some kind of book in his or hers and shadows of something eating human flesh, I looked into the right corner of the cell and saw a Halfling skeleton.\n\nwith some kind of book in his or hers hand. I pried the dusty old book from it's hands the pages were yellow, and the writing was in Elven. “Why was a Hobbit carrying an Elven book I wonder?\" I whispered.\n\nI saw a shadow come closer to my cell, “Roigh' yer maggot, come wit' me”\nIt was an Orc! I had no choice but to follow him. As I walked down the halls, other Orcs were staring at me, showing their rotten teeth and snarling at me.\n\nI was looking around as I was walking and saw a window I would probably be able to fit through and escape, the bars were wide apart.\n\nI stepped aside and ran up to the window using an Orcs head as a launch pad up, I got my shoulders through when they grabbed my feet and nearly pulled me back down. Luckily I kicked them and jumped down into the lake at the bottom and swam away.\n\nWritten by Corvo Attono\n((mrdigdug118))", ""),
        StaticBook("Song Anthology 1", "§bAeran", "Song Anthology: Volume 1\n\nThe Great Pink Haired Man\n\nIt's Always Summer Under the Sea\n\nMaiden of the Tree\n\nThe Great Pink Haired Man\n\nThere once lived a dwarf named Pikel Boldshoulder/\nHis hair, colourful/\nHis heart, much bolder\n\nHe came to us in our hour of need/\nHe lived by a creed, did a great deed/\n\nHe and 4 brave warriors/\nFaced with many barriers\n\nThey ventured into the nether/\nThey did it with great haste/\nOnly 4 were turned to paste\n\nTo defeat the evil Iblees/\nThey tossed an axe into a pit/\nAnd also one of the heroes.../\nShit\n\nHe was a true hero/\nHe asked for no fame,/\nNot even a dame/\n\nSo if you see pink!/\nYou'd better rethink!/\nFor that could be Pikel Boldshoulder/\nAdmittedly, much older\n\nIt's Always Summer Under the Sea\n\nIt's always summer, under the sea/\nI know, oh, oh, oh/\nThe birds have scales, the fish take wing/\nI know, I know, oh, oh, oh/\nThe rain is dry, and the snow falls up/\nI know, I know, oh(x3)\n\nMaiden of the Tree\n\nMy featherbed is deep and soft,/\nAnd there I'll lay you down./\nI'll dress you all in yellow silk,/\nand on your head a crown.\nFor you shall be my lady love,/\n\nand I shall be your lord./\nI'll always keep you warm and safe,/\nAnd guard you with my sword\n\nAnd how she smiled, and how she laughed,\n/the maiden of the tree./\nShe spun away and said to him,/\n\nno featherbed for me./\nI'll wear a gown of golden leaves,/\nand bind my hair with grass,/\nBut you can be my forest love,/\nand me your forest lass.", ""),
        StaticBook("Unification Act", "§bJacob Chapel", "§lArticles of Unification§r\n§oAs Issued Upon the 11th of Sun’s Smile, 1477§r\n\nSection I: Realms & Culture\nSection II: Assurances\nSection III: War Council\nSection IV: Unification Terms\nSection V: Imperial Codex\n\n§lSection I: Realms & Culture§r\n1. Realms of Oren are to draft, adhere, and uphold their own provincial laws, whilst in adherence to existing Imperial laws.\n2. Realms of Oren are permitted to engage in territorial growth, independent of Imperial Influence\n\n3. Realms of Oren and their vassals are permitted to engage in foreign conflict alongside other nations, granted the Empire holds no stance in said conflict, such as in cases of rebellions in foreign nations.\n\n4. Realms of Oren are permitted to establish a realm-specific Knightly Chapter, in accordance with the Grand Knight’s powers and the Chivalric Code.\n\n§lSection II: Assurances§r\n1. The Electorate shall never be suspended or interfered with by Imperial influence, the duties of Emperor never to be passed on hereditarily.\n2. The wide-spread cultures of Oren shall never be infringed upon\n\nin name of Cultural Unity, whether by majority or minority, recognizing that the cultures that make up our Empire are vast and equal.\n3. Realms of Oren and their vassals shall never be targeted or ostracized for the formation of federations,\n\nwhether political or economic, so long as such formations act in no way treasonous to the Emperor and the well-being of the Empire.\n\n§lSection III: War Council§r\n1. The formation of a War Council, composed of all recognized marshals of the Empire, to ensure cooperation between martial forces.\n\n2. The formation of an Imperial Militia, composed of all Knights, sworn blades, levy-men, and militia of the Empire, to ensure a defensive body exists for the quick response to threats.\n\n§lSection IV: Unification Terms§r\n1. House Rovin and their vassals to join the Holy Empire of Oren, their existing territories made the Realm of Aesterwald.\n\n2. The Realm of Aesterwald to be recognized as the cultural heartland of all Northerners,\n\ngranted the right to be lead by their titular Konig.\n\n3. The streamlining of all Houses of Nobility, whether of Aesterwald or the Crownlands, in accordance to the Imperial Codex.\n\n4. House Rovin named as Duke Elector, to reserve a seat and vote within the Electorate.\n\n§lSection V: Imperial Codex§r\n1. The Imperial Codex to be drafted post-haste with the appropriate input and revision by Noble Lords.\n\n§lSignatories:§r\n§oVoron Rovin I, König of Aesterwald\n\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion, Emperor of Oren", ""),
        StaticBook("Weiner Zaviel", "§bRilath Ilwindior", "Zaviel is the worst Shadeling in the history of Shade Magic. He is a disgrace to the entire world. How dare he ever even exist. He will know true pain and suffering by my hand one day. I will see to it. I will fucking salt his lands and take his women§0\n§0-", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The hierarchy of the Druidic Order:§0\n§0\n§0Archdruid:§0\n§0Archdruids are guides, they set up moots, deal with housing, settle disputes, keep or make friendly relationships with nations and orders. They deal with shuns and vote on certain matters. - Beth.\n\nThe hierarchy of the Druidic Order:§0\n§0\n§0Guides:§0\n§0Their role is to interview seekers, guide them through dedicancy and eventually druidism. They teach their students all they need to know prior to their grand task. - Barry.\n\nThe hierarchy of the Druidic Order:§0\n§0\n§0Notable Druids:\n\nThe hierarchy of the Druidic Order:§0\n§0\n§0Druids:§0\n§0The role of the druid is the unconditional duty that all attuned must follow from their oaths as a dedicant. Upholding the balance of the realm  and pushing back the blight. - Kyral.\n\nThe hierarchy of the Druidic Order:§0\n§0\n§0Dedicants:§0\n§0The bottom of the chain. Dedicants are here to learn about the duties of the druid and to see if they're right to enact said duties to the best of their abilities. - Tarnov.\n\nThe hierarchy of the Druidic Order:§0\n§0\n§0Hierophant:§0\n§0A Hierophant is a retired druid who has done quite a bit for the Order, aiding it in its time of need for example. Archdruids tend to become Hierophant's albeit they aren't\n\nalways guaranteed the title. They may also be called to sway a vote if there is a tie between the Inner Circle. - Pappa!", ""),
        StaticBook("Shade Contract", "§bLorien", "((This is a magical contract. By signing this ICly, the player agrees to OOCy carry out the punishments of the contract, should the terms and/or conditions be broken. Failure to do so shall be PGing; a bannable offense.))\n\n((Magical Contract\n\nMage: Lorien (Mephistophelian) T5 Contract Mage\n\nSkin:  Elvira Mantisuku (Farryn) Tah Cleric\n\nType: Life Contract\n\nTarget(s): Lorien&Adorellan))\n\nUpon signing this contract, I agree to abide to the following terms:\n\n1) I shall not create a new shade without the express permission of the other signer. This permission is gained via face-to-face interaction only.\n\n2) I shall not attempt to nullify or make void any of these terms or conditions.\n\nThese terms and conditions are made null upon the confirmed, permanent death or disappearance of the other signer. Upon the return of this signer, if ever, the terms-\n\nare reinstated.\n\nThe punishment for breaking the terms or conditions is absolute, permanent death.\nSigned,\nLorien Carcimor ((Mephistophelian))\nAdorellan ((Tsuyose))\n*Both names are scrawled neatly in blood*\n\n*Lining the edge of the entire contract are symbols, alien to the inexperienced eye.*\n\n((Protection from:\nPhysical Damage\nElemental Damage))", ""),
        StaticBook("To Herun Athna", "§bArinislia Athna", "*The letter appears to be addressed to Herun Athna*\n\nHerun,\n\nIt's been awhile since we last saw each other. Even more so than I last have seen my comrades of the Order. Ever since my capture and -\n\ntortured, I have trained, practiced, and ventured out far and wide. Right now, even though I have finally mastered creating a hand of light and even be able to move the digits, I still find no purpose truly for me. I am...unfinished. Dettached. I have-\n\ngathered supplies and now I depart on a journey. To find other shrines of our patron, Xan. He, like you, who will not abandon me. He who shines the light in the everlasting darkness. The Fatherly embrace to keep me warm and proud. I will never forget -\n\nall you taught me. Of the friendships and companions I have made when I joined the Order. I will miss them all greatly. Also if I ever return, tell Leric he owes me a rematch. \n\nI hope we meet each other again someday teacher.\n\nYour apprentice,\n\nVailoen Winterleaf", ""),
        StaticBook("A Druid's Call", "§bArinislia Athna", "*As he were to look upon the bed, the ancient staff of his beloved druid would rest there. A single pure white feather next to it along with a birchwood sapling*§0\n§0\n\n\"I hear it. The call that so many have heard before. I never thought I would so soon. I try yet I cannot ignore it. The call of nature ever so constant now. I do not know when or if I will return. If I shall see you in this life or the next. I am afraid..\n\nSo many things I wish I could talk to you about. So many walks I wanted to follow you on. I miss our time together. Our love and embrace. Your first smile I ever saw, your first touch when you held my hand, your first hold around me to show me I was -\n\nsave. Things I will never forget and keep with me always. I do not know where you are now. My eyes missing your face. My heart forever with yours as we walk our paths parallel in time. No realm will keep us apart my knight. No Aengul to seperate-\n\nour love. It will forever be etheral even as our souls depart this realm or the next. I will love you always my dear knight and will be forever yours.§0\n§0\n§0~Arinislia Athna", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "------=+=------§0\n§0The Utterings of Tahariae§0\n§0------=+=------§0\n§0\n§0\n§0As spoken by the Holy Arch-Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, through His Prophet Ashanaak between the years of 1536 and 1543, in the realm of Vailor.\n\n------=+=------§0\n§0The Revelation of Judgment: The First Revelation§0\n§0------=+=------§0\n§0\n§0I am the Glory of the Rising Sun. I am the Bringer of Light. I am the Lord of Purity and the Archon of Justice. I am the Vehement Lord. I am Tahariae. Witness Me,\n\nAshanaak, My Chosen Prophet. Witness Me.§0\n§0\n§0I, the Divine Stag, He Who Walks in Pure Light, the Great Purge, have merely watched My Servants for too long. You have Divided, and Divided you shall fall. You failed to Understand the Mission I had given to you,\n\ndeteriorated into mere wandering healers who know only my Blessed Name. Your mockery of Faith and Piety offends Me, and so I return once more. Witness Me, Ashanaak, My Chosen Prophet. Witness Me.\n\n------=+=------§0\n§0The Revelation of Wisdom: The Eight Woes§0\n§0------=+=------§0\n§0\n§0And now, my Chosen Prophet, recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, or My Blessing shall be torn from their hearts for their Sins:§0\n\nWoe to those that turn against Me and My Mission, for they must be cast out of thy ranks.§0\n§0\n§0Woe to those who only know Me for My Blessing, and not for My Mission, and do not recognize Me and My Glory in prayer except when My power is needed.§0\n\nWoe to those who refuse to heal the Innocent, to return to Pure form what has been rendered Impure.§0\n§0\n§0Woe to those who let the Impure, the Beings of Darkness and Evil, and the Descendants who bring harm to the Innocents, walk free when they cross thy path.\n\nWoe to those who cause harm to the Innocent, for they are those you are meant to protect.§0\n§0\n§0Woe to those who are sexually immoral, who give themselves outside of the holy bed of marriage, who dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent.§0\n\nWoe to those who give themselves over to perpetual drunkenness, for they dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent. Such is only acceptable in celebrations and festivities.\n\nWoe to those who steal, cheat, and utter vulgarities, who abuse the Innocent with their tongues and hands.\n\n------=+=------§0\n§0The Revelation of Valor: The Eight Commands§0\n§0------=+=------§0\n§0\n§0And now, Ashanaak, I give you these Commands, that you may live a Pure life. Recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, or My Blessing shall be torn from their\n\nhearts for their Sins:§0\n§0\n§0Go forth, and spread not just my Light among the Descendants, but My Words and the Truth of My Glory.\n\nGo forth, and become true Clerics among the Descendants: scholars, protectors, and leaders, to guide the Innocent with words, justice, and wisdom.\n\nGo forth, and guard yourself against marriage, for service to Me demands complete and total commitment. If you do marry, do not marry those who serve Darkness and Evil, for in doing so you taint the very nature of holy matrimony.§0\n§0\n\nGo forth, and kneel before Me in maniael: private prayer, gratitude, and submission before My Glory when you awake and before you sleep.\n\nGo forth, and kneel before Me in manaakh: prayer, worship, and submission in fellowship with your Brothers and Sisters in Me once each Elven year.\n\nGo forth, and respect the fallen clerics who I have sent back to you, to listen and follow what they have returned to say. And when their wisdom has been imparted, that you will have the strength and courage to send them back to My Halls.\n\nGo forth, and follow My Chosen Prophet, for they shall be My Light in the darkness of the world for you.§0\n§0\n§0Go forth, and in My Blessed Name, use any means necessary to bring Purity to the Taint and Darkness that has become the world. The realm must return\n\nto how it once was, when the Four once ruled in Peace and Taint had not yet manifested. Through the suffering My Mission shall bring you, remember that it is not out of Moral Good that you must do these things, but out of Necessity.\n\n------=+=------§0\n§0The Revelation of Hope: The Final Revelation§0\n§0------=+=------§0\n§0\n§0Do all that I have commanded for you to do, and do not do all I have commanded you not to do, and you shall not perish. Nay; once suffering consume you and you leave thy\n\nmortal coil, I shall welcome you into My Sacred Halls, to forever be with Me in Purity, to forever be witness to My Sacred Light, forever and ever more.\n\n------=+=------§0\n§0The Five Sacred Tenets of Tahariae§0\n§0------=+=------§0\n§0\n§0As revealed to the Prophet Braxis in a dream by the Holy Arch-Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, in the realm of Anthos.\n\n[*] Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae. [*]§0\n§0\n§0[*] Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae. [*]§0\n§0\n§0[*] Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure. [*]\n\n[*] Do not spill the blood of the innocent. [*]§0\n§0\n§0[*] Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will. [*]\n\n------=+=------§0\n§0The Manifestations of Tahariae§0\n§0------=+=------§0\n§0\n§0A collection of the various stories of the Holy Arch-Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, as paraphrased by the Descendants of the Realms and transcribed by His Prophet Ashanaak.\n\nAs remembered by Ashanaak, Prophet of Tahariae:§0\n§0\n§0In the realm of Thales, the Holy Arch-Aengul of Purity, Tahariae", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "15th of The Amber Cold, 1520.§0\n§0Entry #1: Today is a hard day. I learned about a spirit that Worg called Leyd. It's like the Creator, but it's what they draw their faith from. Instead of being allowed outside to eat dinner I was forced to eat inside due to-\n\na sandstorm. Worg also pulled out some of the flooring to replace it with wood. He says it's softer, but I won't believe him until I get a bed. I miss mom, dad, Adria... home.§0\n§0\n§0End of Entry.\n\n9th of The Deep Cold, 1521.§0\n§0\n§0Entry #2§0\n§0\n§0\"Today is a rather low called day. I have been given word that Adria has fallen and that my father is now missing. I look forward to the future and create this entry to document the news of my mother's-\n\nSide of the family begining something new. I will at some point reach out to them, but if I am to stay here is up in the air I suppose. I wish to stay here, but lately he has been quite unsettled and I do not know if me being here is helping him at all.\n\nI ride out today to see the world and hopefully find out more as to what has happened to my parents. I write this now at the age of 11 and see my house, my family, all broken a part and scattered. I pray that all is well for them...\"§0\n§0-Entry ended-\n\n3rd of The Grand Harvest, 1522.§0\n§0\n§0Entry #3§0\n§0\n§0\"As the days are at their peak not much has gone on. I have been given permission to slowly transfer what my father had started to a new location. Even though it is not direct family\n\nand I fail to grasp the concept of how it is family. I feel much more safe their then I do here. I have yet to speak to Grim about my hobbey and if I will be allowed a library or not. This has grown to be a past time of who I am and I am willing to use-\n\nthis gift to help them. I have been told that most of my family went into a secret location in the north and that is where they are building up underground. They do not have a lot of freedom up there though which is why I§0\n§0have not been allowed to return.-\n\nAll this influence is quite overwhelming at times and I try to understand customs. However, this new place seems more at home though I am still at a lost in things between spirits and the creator and how they both pan out. I feel I will never understand-\n\nhow things came to be..\"§0\n§0\n§0-End of Entry-", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "12th of Snow's Maiden§0\n§0\n§0I sit now, bored as ever in this city. It's so odd seeing all the others just lounge around all day. As if having the time to toss aside all responibilites. None the less. The flora is nice to look at.\n\nI wonder when that blundering Damai will make an apperance as this business will not start itself. Perhaps in the coming days, things will alter and more income will come my way.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "How I look.§0\n§0~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~I used to have brown eyes like my father, I had some freckles too scattered across my face. My hair was blonde but I colored it to maintain my dark hair. It was black. My skin was tan, not as much as my brothers-\n\nbut Qali brown. My nose was a bit perky §0too..Wonder§0 if I can alter that a bit once mother teaches me how to control my disguise. I worse my royal dresses a lot too, I wonder what I did to them? A few wrinkles as §0well..hmpf§0..", ""),
        StaticBook("A Folded Note", "§bGavin the Fisher", "*A clean and well written note sits beside the alchemy ingredients*~§0\n§0\n§0It's been a good while since we were last able to talk. I am sorry I ran off without handing over my recent batch, but I brought it to this chest.\n\nI hope you are well Ciri, you seemed quite distraught the last time we had a chance to speak. And I hope my saddle has done you some good. I miss you as a friend, and I'd like to spend a moment with you over tea if you have a chance sometime.§0\n§0- Gavin~", ""),
        StaticBook("Sylverwood Law", "§bFjordin Sylver", "- Sylverwood Law -\n\nBy : Fjordin Sylver, Dictator of Sylverwood\n\nInfo : This book provides a basic understanding of how a Sylverwood citizen functions in society and the guidelines one must follow.\n\n       - Chapter 1 -\nSylverwood Law and Order can be looked at as a number of different things. Some may call it primitive and brutal, simply for the fact it is catagorized as a Dictatorship. The reality is, however, not like that at all.\n\n   For the sake of slander against his form of government, Fjordin Sylver likes to catagorize his Dictatorship in the sub-catagory (which he has created) referred to as  Benevolent Dictatorship. Benevolent of course meaning good.\n\n   A \"Benevolent\" Dictatorship centers itself somewhere between good and evil. While a lot of Fjordin's actions may seem unnecessarily harsh and rushed, his sole intent is to protect his citizens and fufill their needs and wants.\n\n   This does not mean all of his decisions are based soley on his personal opinion and knowledge. He has a private counsel known as the Sylver Shields. These Shields are his most trusted advisors, who live as everyday citizens but feed him intrigue.\n\n   This should now, however, make every citizen paranoid of one another. So long as nobody plots against Fjordin's life, there is no need to worry. The truth is that despite his sometimes callous and sarcastic attitude, he dislikes violence.\n\n   The fact of the matter is that Fjordin's word is law. While his word may not be agreed upon by the majority it is there to protect them. So long as people obey him, they will find themselves looking forward into a brighter future.\n\n       - Chapter 2 -\nThere is obviously a limit to how much power every citizen wields. Power in Sylverwood, however, does not come from ones control over the legal system. Instead, it comes in the form of how necessary you are to the towns functionality.\n\n   Everybody is vital in some way, shape and form. Farmers form the basis of breeding and cooking. Miners form the foundations of stonemasonry, blacksmithing, tinkering and enchanting. Life is a constant chain of supply and demand.\n\n   Another way to put this is that everyone is the link of a chain. If one link breaks off so does everything after it. Laborers, such as Lumberjacks, Miners and Farmers, are the most essential and tiresome jobs one can have.\n\n   Manufactured goods, however, are what make the most of those professions. Sometimes these professions work in sync to produce even finer wares, such as studded armor made by a learned leatherworker with the help of a blacksmith.\n\n   Should one person drop from this link it could cause havoc. However, this does not mean one should stop working just to make a point. By abandoning the practice of your designated profession, you are endangering the lives of everyone. Not just Fjordin.\n\n   Typically in Sylverwood society, every race is forced to pick at least one profession they are most fit for. Humans, as a popular example, will most often be forced to take up a laboring role. This could include Mining, Lumberjacking and/or Farming.\n\n       - Chapter 3 -\nIncase you have not read the notice board (somehow) before openning this book, I will now state the rules and regulations in Sylverwood as of 1486.\nNote : Finding \"loopholes\" will result in an even harsher punishment than before!\n\nRule #1 - No Killing/Assault of Citizens\nUnless the person in question explicitly robs you of your valuables, you may NOT slaughter one another like animals. As explained previously, everyone is important to the functionality of Sylverwood. Don't be dumb.\n\nRule #2 - No Theft of Citizens\nAnother common-sense rule. In all honesty, I have stolen once before. However, I stole because I was in dire need of food during the winter. If you're going to take something, do so in small quantities within reason.\n\nRule #3 - No Livestock Murder\nYes, I refer to the unnecessary slaughter of livestock as murder. Livestock are just as important to the function of society as humans are. Without them, lots of industry and food production will stop. (Also Server Rule)\n\nRule #4 - No Building (Outside Home)\nI can not stress this enough. Building outside of your designated home is prohibited by all means. Fjordin Sylver is the sole architect and engineer of everything in Sylverwood unless otherwise said so.\n\nRule #5 - Stay active.\nUnless you have a legitimate reason for inactivity in LOTC (this is a bit OOC but must be addressed), do not waste a perfectly good home by being on an hour every couple days. You are here to contribute, not take up space.\n\nRule #6 - No Granting Citizenship\nI don't care if somebody is your brother, sister, mother or father. If you want someone to move in with you or otherwise, have them contact me directly (christian2142). Otherwise keep them out of Sylverwood.\n\nRule #7 - No Necromancy\nSylverwood has a strict policy against the practice of the Dark Arts or anything related to it. No blood/animal/human sacrifices nor Black Magic will be allowed. This is a security threat to Athera and will be dealt with directly.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Crimson Letter", "§bAnonymous", "Dear Sisters§0\n§0I shall keep this name anonymous for safe keeping but you may ask Arelin or Dolores of who I am just by what I'm about to say. §0\n§0\n§0I have not been the most helpful in the feeding and the lust for flesh you gals\n\ncrave in the past years. I am hoping to redeem myself with my efforts to help you sustain your life. I have been helped on multiple occasions by your kind. . . befriended many really but I havent given back as I should. Here for you is\n\nthe body of a simple Mali'ame man. His death shant be in vain nor was it painful so there is no need for sorrow. He was intoxicated to the point of sleep so I ended his breating quickly with one brisk stroke. Take pleasure in this to save another life, so\n\nanother random bystander doesnt have to perish. This should do well for a while as I have sent Arelin a finger to consume. I am sure I shall see Dolores soon as she mingles around in her now eternal life. You know who I am. You know I\n\nhelp you if I can. Stay safe and contact me if need be.§0\n§0\n§0                        -C§0\n§0*The whole contents of the letter would be written in crimson liquid, perhaps blood.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "§bViktor 'The Grizzly' Dustin", "Dear Viktoriya Vladov,\n    I'm sorry that our whole meeting got off on the wrong foot, with you abruptly being told that you were to marry a stranger, on top of the fact that the stranger looks more like a bear than a man. I personally wish we had\n\nmore time to talk with one another before my patriarch, and your father had declared this marriage to occur. In this letter, I'd like to adress a few things that you had asked me during the heat of the moment. First off, I'm sorry that my lack of\n\ninvolvement with the military is something you see as disgraceful. I'll be sure to try and correct that by enlisting with the levy so that I do not make you feel as if I am a useless man. I tend to stay away from militaristic activities, not because I\n\n§§am a coward, but \nbecause I had other duties to accomplish, such as my position as Warden of the Woods of Aldersberg. Hopefully you can understand this, and do not judge me too harshly for it. I also wished to comment upon the remark\n\nyou made about me joining the Order of Saint Amyas to become a 'man'. I am quite certain that I am qualified to call myself a man, even though I do not partake in the usual battles and skirmishes that seem to plague the roads daily. If being a person\n\nis quick to draw their blade and rush out to attack other beings, then by that standard, I am no man. Though, through my work and through my mental capabilites, I'm certain I'm as manly as any who would rush out onto the battle field. This concludes the\n\nreflection portion of this letter, and I hope it's contents are adequate. Moving on, I'd like to state a few things about myself, as to break the metaphorical ice between the two of us. I am a well-learned man, as you might've noticed by the contents of\n\nletter, though it takes me quite some time to get my thoughts out in the middle of conversation. I might sometimes appear to be distant, but keep in mind that I do take notice of things, and try to correct them. \nAnother thing about me is\n\nthe fact that I enjoy hunting with my companion, Barnsy. I'm certain that the two of you met, considering the whole ordeal today. I'll keep in mind that you dislike dogs, having just found out today. But, nontheless, Barnsy's companionship when out\n\nand about is something I cannot change, and thus must inform you about it. A third thing about me is that I enjoy carving wood in my spare time. Maybe, should you wish, I could carve a wooden bust of you if you decide to enter the Alderswoods. It would\n\nbe a nice activity to do together, no? Anyway, a fourth thing about me is that I dislike very sweet foods, and apples. I don't understand the taste of them, but I know that quite a few people have taken a liking to the funny fruit's taste. If anything\n\nthings like meat and stews are much better. Nothing beats a long day of logging and patrolling the woods like a mean stew of mushroom soup with venison chunks. And lastly, another thing about me is, my favorite animal is the bear. Since I was a young\n\nteen, I've been called many things, but the one name that stuck with me is 'Grizzled Bear'. It is oddly fitting, once you stop to think about it, as I do quite often. Thats about it for now, Viktoriya. I hope your opinion of me has changed atleast a\n\nlittle. \n\n- Grizzled Bear", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alchemy Recipe Tries;§0\n§0((Successful & Not))§0\n§0- Water + Coal = Distilled Water§0\n§0- Distilled Water + Tippen's Root = Potion of Tippen's Root (PTR)§0\n§0- PTR + Crouching Feather = Lumberjack's Recipe (LJR)§0\n§0- PTR + Halfing's Grass = Nope\n\n- PTR + Lari'hei's fingers = Nope§0\n§0-AV + Flametongue = Greater Flamespitter§0\n§0-GP + CP = Nope§0\n§0-AV + CP  = Greater CP Infusion§0\n§0CPI + TR = Nope", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Sylvia - Human§0\n§0WIll buy booze§0\n§0Felsen, Small Hamlet§0\n§0DONE - Payment Waiting§0\n§0\n§0Wayrest 14§0\n§0Booze§0\n§0\n§0Mylas§0\n§0Cask of Ale§0\n§0Cask of Wine", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Eldre-home§0\n§0\n§0Hoilelio goiu holias§0\n§0\n§0Ana viev §0\n§0\n§0Del Dorini ec Eldre Enshu§0\n§0\n§0Hoilelio§0\n§0Be hoilelios hoilas\"§0\n§0\n§0ritiou\n\n Petals pooled in crimson red.§0\n§0Life flowing out and leaving him dead.§0\n§0So came the book man,§0\n§0with no ill intent.§0\n§0To the noble city full of discontent.§0\n§0He meant no trouble and caused no strife,§0\n§0but the city's guards§0\n§0chose to end his life\n\n Empty it lies, §0\n§0Asleep in the cold,§0\n§0Just another lost city, with a tale to be told.§0\n§0With high towers and statues so great,§0\n§0Yet silent it stands,§0\n§0Forever open it's gate. \n\nThe Blue man is empty, For he has lost all.§0\n§0The Blue man is sad,§0\n§0for what him did befall. The Blue man has lost one he loved, §0\n§0and lost himself as well. §0\n§0Blue, blue and cold.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I have seen a most spectacular thing this day! A dragon if you could believe! I was on one of my routine visits to Haelun'or when it approached. A large being, shining black and charcoal gray. I was awestruck the moment I saw him. It's pink eyes glowed\n\nvery bright, and it even breathed fire! It was snowing, and for those unaware, Haelun'or is a city of white and blue. The visual contrast was absolutely stunning!§0\n§0The guards dutifully fought and through one of their cries I learned the creature's name. An\n\nelf adressed the dragon as Satar, and I must assume this is his name. What a beautiful majestic and elegant creature. I would have loved to get a closer look, and maybe attempt conversation should it not have been my enemy at the time. Truly though, I am\n\nno fighter, and all I could do was stand and watch as the citizens and visitors to Haelun'or battled against this fantastical being. Still, as and observer I found the whole thing almost underwhelming. The dragon did relatively little damage to the city\n\nand its occupants. I'd always expected a dragon to have the capacity to cause immense amounts of destruction should one chose to fight. I am thoroughly confused as to the purpose of the conflict today. 8th of the Snow's Maiden, 1565.\n\n In the aftermath of this event I have learned numerous things. The first is that this encounter was with a drake. From what I have read, a drake is a corrupted form of a lesser dragon", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Diel'Koigh§0\n§0Eldrec§0\n§0Daa-no§0\n§0Alayac- hello§0\n§0Joiu ec al- Good, and you?§0\n§0Fai- sprite/fairy§0\n§0ona- one§0\n§0un-two§0\n§0Ana- I§0\n§0boic§0\n§0Ana kwa kjo rtiau§0\n§0I would like that (close enough)\n\nAshe bev al -how are you?§0\n§0Bev- are§0\n§0me- am§0\n§0Vela- walk§0\n§0aniu-yes§0\n§0Hwova§0\n§0Hwe-he§0\n§0Quel-Dorei- high elf\n\nShe smiles softly§0\n§0Circled by blue roses, they sing together.§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0         Diary\n\nI'm confused. I don't know where I am, or what is going on. I am awake now, but why? I miss Elial... Nothing interesting has happened. Rowan I am eating all of your oranges.§0\n§0I met a funny old elvish man. He did a very good impression of Art. Well, I'm\n\ntired. I'm really tired. I think I'm going to sleep now, Rowan. I may wake up again.. but please, don't make me wake again. I don't want to wake up.. I don't want to think.. to remember. So please just let me sleep. I'm sorry. §0\n§0               Kaari.\n\nDear Kaari and River, I met a girl today. Not like that Kaari, I know how you think. She is interested in moving to Laurel'lin. Got stuck in the citizen's door. It was kind of funny, but she started to cry, so I got Fawynn to help her. Her name is\n\nPenelope, and she seemed nice enough. She's got red hair and green eyes, and seems paler than most wood elves, though she seems to be one. She also tends to get really flustered easily. Its a bit cute.§0\n§0         Sincerely,§0\n§0             Rowan\n\nDear Everyone,§0\n§0\n§0Well... its been a while. Do you remember Pen? We were together for a while. An actual couple. I was so amazed, and happy, and it was wonderful.§0\n§0No girl has ever been interested in me before, and men typically back off when I tell them I\n\nam not a girl. It really made me happy for a while. Pen... she passed away recently. I miss her. I miss her so, so, so much. I.. can't believe.. I wish I never met her. It would be easier that way. If I'd never met her, I wouldn't have felt so happy. I\n\ncouldn't have lost that happiness. I miss her.§0\n§0\n§0           Love, §0\n§0                  Rowan\n\n Dear diary,§0\n§0Much has happened since last time. A relationship began and ended. I have gotten over Penelope, though now I fear I see ghosts. I still need to take a minute to realize she's gone when I see a woman with red hair, especially elven ones.\n\nI find I don't miss her like I used to. I miss the companionship, however I believe I need a pet. A cat or dog or something of the sort. I am too lonely of a person. It is perhaps a bit pathetic.§0\n§0    §0\n§0            Love, Rowan", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0   A Comtemplation of§0\n§0   the Sirame, and the§0\n§0   Shame They Bring§0\n§0       to all Mali\n\n\n§0\n§0         Foreword§0\n§0\n§0  Before I begin I would like to explain. I have no ill will towards Laureh'lin. Far from it! However I have observed shameful behavior from those meant to protect it. This is why I am writing in the first place.\n\n\n§0  §0\n§0  The first story is a personal observation of an event that is vaguely defensible if you ignore the gross injustice. It was not long after they had implemented the rule of not allowing races other than Mali into the cihi. A man applying for\n\nentry was attacked by an uruk at the gate. Through their efforts the man was saved, however their attention was soon turned to the visitor whom had just been saved. He was not a Mali, in which case he would have normally been denied access and sent on his\n\nway. However, it was not so in this particular case. After denying him entry the Sirame present turned on him. He gave his reason for visiting as business on behalf of the Library of Dragur. The Sirame, about four or so present, began making increasingly\n\nhostile comments, declaring the library a place of \"spooks\" and cultists. Despite the man's protests and lack of agression, they eventually killed the visiting librarian. When searching his body they found nothing in his possession but books. He was\n\ncompletely unarmed. I am aware he was not a Mali, however to those of you with half a brain ask yourself. How is an unarmed librarian with actual business in the cihi count as a threat worth killing without a trial?\n\n\n§0\n§0   The next story is one of just plain crude behavior", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Onc.. Xerro. Zaar.. Alra.. Egr.. Azeex..", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "penis", ""),
        StaticBook("EWOROENLETEA", "§bThurak'Yar", "Entities within our realm of Existence no Longer Existing, And Then Existing Again.\n\nOr, Void Translocation\n\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 1'st of Snow's Maiden, 1488\n\n1. Introduction\n\n2. Study\n\n3. Sensory Overhaul\n\n4. Destruction\n\n5. Re-Creation\n\nIt does no take much searching within a library to gain some concepts of the Void as an alternate existence outside, winin and with no relation at all to our reality. Arcanists, Mages, Sorcerers- whatever the name- users of voidal magic pull a 'thing'\n\ninto this realm that did not previously exist within it, and hold it there for as long as they can wield a void connection. But no ‘thing’ pulled from the void is retained here. Such power is reserved to The Creater to pull real matter from The Void.\n\nBut what is a ‘thing’ –be it inanimate, plant, animal, edible- already existed? Then the connection to The Void need only be instantaneous, because the ‘thing’ is not created, but simply IS.\n\nStudy\n\nTake within your hands something that exists. \nAny kind of thing will suffice and for the sake of example we shall call it and any potential other thing \nan 'Entity'. Begins your examination in the simplest of interests:\nForm.\n\nWhat size is it?\nWhat’s it made of?\nHow heavy is it?\nHow malleable is the material?\nDoes it react to heat?\nWhat happens under great pressure?\n \nIf already you are struggling then you should return this book whence it came.\n\nSecondly you will need to form these observations into a mental map of the object. This is a far more complex procedure and verges on a particularly niche form of magic known as cognitism; however Telekinetics may find themselves more easily inclined\n\ntowards this type of thinking. You cannoy be bound by your perceptions in understanding the world. If you are purely an experiencer of your surroundings then you will never formulate any greater understandings of anything ever. So work on that.\n\nIf you are able to mentally comprehend the object beyond what is merely visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity’s existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\n\nSensory Overhaul\n\nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculable values and perceiving the entity’s magical value. Aside from universally shifting perspective\n\nwith the aid of magic, the quantity of information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a real in which is not a single thing\n\nbut the potential for all things. And thereby all things that exist are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practise and isn’t really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of magic or not.\n\nCertainly with practise comes the strengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to ‘feel’ an apple tree from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being laid\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\ndown, what you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you muse measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void with your own so that the entity is no longer isolated in this\n\nworld but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones’ self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more ‘alive’ an entity is, the more rapidly it produces mana. Anything that has a soul is independently\n\nexisting within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such a drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant. Soul-less entities then exist somewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of\n\nglass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more ‘alive’ it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be able to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\n\nNo Longer Existing\n\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existence it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was tangiable\n\njust stops and is no more. \nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independently of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its diving creation re-instated, and therefore able\n\nto return to the nothing from which it came. Within The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes of itself a something\n\nfor that fleeting moment. But without being birthed into existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely, there becomes a new potential within The\n\nVoid that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like an arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the\n\npotential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that keeps it sacredly linked to once again become what the Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a ceramic teapot will not become a crude clay but remains a teapot).\n\nTo Return Again\n\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the original entity is the only\n\nthing that maintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independent existence outside of The Void is made (I.e redoing the Creator’s work) will assign the potential\n\nwith its destined form. And the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\n\nGood Job,\nYou Meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "A book on the physical and non-physical properties of water in its three states.§0\n§0\n§0Sylverport\n\nMandragora§0\n§0Serpent's stalk§0\n§0Flametongue root§0\n§0Crimson vase§0\n§0Dwarf's pumpkin§0\n§0Drake's tail§0\n§0Crouching feather\n\nAthin§0\n§0Serpent's stalk§0\n§0Frost vine§0\n§0Elf's hair§0\n§0Crouching feather§0\n§0Tippen's root\n\nAthin§0\n§0Frostvine§0\n§0Crouching feather§0\n§0Alabaster leaf§0\n§0Tippen's root\n\nBlood lotus§0\n§0Drake's tail§0\n§0Larihei's fingers§0\n§0Crouching feather\n\nSerpent's stalk§0\n§0Mandragora§0\n§0Crimson vase§0\n§0Dwarf's pumpkin§0\n§0Flametongue root§0\n§0Drake's tail§0\n§0Crouching feather", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Entry 1§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0I have met a really handsome man today, he hit on me first can you believe it?! §0\n§0Neither can I....§0\n§0I really do like him, but he doesn't want to be in a relationship yet still doesn't want to be friends, I am aging, i want kids.\n\nEntry 2§0\n§0Dear Diary §0\n§0Kannessan came to visit today, it turns out the villa isquite dangerous now.§0\n§0BUT SHE IS PREGNANT!§0\n§0I know right, it is amazing we had some tea and discussed these things. She is so lucky, I might grow too old and never have a kid.\n\nEntry 3§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0I happened to come across a book, I just had it....§0\n§0The genre is unique §0\n§0a.k.a it is Erotica §0\n§0I am deeply disturbed that some of the pages are glued together by a weird substance. I do not wish to read this again.\n\nEntry 4§0\n§0Dear Diary §0\n§0I met some strange Valah kids today, thegirl was sweet and absoloutley fascinated with Elves. Her Brother i assume had no respect for me, he tried to force her to leave but she just put her foot down and told him no.\n\nEntry 5§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0Kannessan decided to make a surprise visit today, & months pregnant she is and she waltzes around by herself. We also went to find me a new man since my last relationship didn't work out...§0\n§0See you another day.\n\nEntry 6§0\n§0Dear Diary §0\n§0I observed a group of men talking about magic.§0\n§0Ver interesting indeed. CAn't wait for Kannessan to give birth.§0\n§0Auntie Lanae, has a nice ring to it.§0\n§0Art Camoryn and a man named Zearth'en was 2 of the men. There was 3.\n\nEntry 6 §0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0I met another man today, he is really nice to me. Insulted my makeup at first...§0\n§0but you know he built me a secret door in this room. Now my belongings are extra safe. He is gonna take me fishing sometime soon, hopefully...\n\nEntry 8§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0I have met another wonderful man his name is Sykes, he may be a wood elf but he is simply amazing, I haven't told him my age yet for he may not be able to stay the nights with me anymore....§0\n§0I love him, I hope he loves me aswell\n\nEntry 9§0\n§0Dear Diary §0\n§0Me and Skyes are now a couple, we have been spending more and more nights together.§0\n§0I really like him, oh no he is looking over my shoulder!§0\n§0Go to go Sorry.\n\nEntry 10§0\n§0Dear Diary§0\n§0I am at the Mother Grove for lessons about the aspects today. They aremostly just tasks for understanding. But Tay is my mentor, he is a great teacher.§0\n§0Sykes found me again. Wee stalker but I love him. Ok bye.§0\n\nDruid Notes§0\n§0Acacia Druid- protect deer communicate with wolves tell them to eat other meats, until the deer are in mating season and repopulate.§0\n§0Pine Druid Garun- protect deer, allow wolves only what they need, till deer repop.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Customer: Dirk Novokain§0\n§0Purchase: Enchant: Sharpness I (on steel sword)§0\n§0Profit: 35 mina.§0\n§0\n§0Customer: Seyer Reeyse§0\n§0Purchase: Enchant: Sharpness I (on steel sword)§0\n§0Profit: 35 mina.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Dedicancy", "§bAurojia", "- Hunted and killed a boar that was destroying bird nestings and trees, skinning and turnings it's remains into a large set of bone chimes. §0\n§0\n§0- Completed the Bardic Rite, producing from it a book by the title of§0\n§0'Red'.\n\n- Tamed and brought with me from the Iron Uzg an Elephant, which now serves as a lifelong companion.§0\n§0\n§0- Entered the Fairy Ring for the first time, not bending beneath the stress or pressure of the intense magical energy within.\n\n- Read and summarized the book labeled 'Neo-Druidism' by Salmon Druid Petyr.§0\n§0\n§0- Resolved the horrific overpopulation of a grouping of turtles in the forest's nearby pond, disposing of them in the local river and Grove.\n\n- Accompanied Muildir to the scarred and tainted land of Dark Shamans to see the damage.§0\n§0\n§0- Met three new Druids, Oo'ri, Katelynn, and Alinar, the druids of Magma, Clouds, and Porcupines.\n\n- Completed a Task from a Druid Guide as well as an Archdruid.§0\n§0\n§0- Read 'The Great War' and gave a valid thesis to Calius.§0\n§0\n§0- Completed the Rite of Naming, taking the Druidic Totem of the Phœnix.\n\n- Completed Muildir's Dedicant questioning, now moving on to my Grand Task!§0\n§0\n§0- Grand Task Completed!~ Shrine to the Aspects constructed beneath the hill holding the Fairy Ring.\n\n- I have finally been Attuned. All hail the new Phoenix Druid, Aurojia Akulakh!\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0            O7§0\n§0           /I§0\n§0           /\\", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Yuba Lub A Dub Dub!§0\n§0\n§0*Fart Noises*", ""),
        StaticBook("Red.", "§bKyrah", "Red.§0\n§0Red is a color of passion, a sense of irrefutable fervor which is embedded into§0\n§0our conscience at birth. It is the color that flows through our veins, the color that destroys, that burns and trambles nature beneath it's decaying touch...\n\nThis red, it is the color of romance. It is the color of hate. It is the color that your visage turns to at the sight of the person of whom your heart falters over. And it is the color that your eyes, that your gaze turns to as anger settles down over\n\none's senses like a blackened cloud. The hue of roses, bittersweet creations. Red, is a color that I have learned far too well within my time, it is something that is ceaselessly amazing in it's forms. But as I have seen it, it has symbolized, always,\n\nundying emotion.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0 Red is Passion.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n               §0\n§0             O/§0\n§0            /I§0\n§0            /\\", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This sword seems to be made out of a incredible amount of bones, they seem much thicker then their typical state and the blade is etched with black steel on both sides, the hilt holds a large ruby, the redness shining through the eyeholes of the skulls\n\neither side of the hilt.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This twin headed axe possess a large, extremely sharp sapphire head on each side. Both merged into a black steel handle. Snapping your fingers would cause the axehead to radiate a persistent coldness,§0\n§0lasting quite awhile.\n\n((Unknown if cold enchanting is actually possible, to be investigated", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This scimitar seems strange in nature, the top of the blade holding a V notch in the metal and composed of black steel, the handle having golden etched into it. A bright topaz shining in a clutch at the bottom of the hilt.§0\n§0Snapping your fingers would\n\ncause this blade to be a lot lighter and faster to swing then usual, as if the wind itself was carrying it.§0\n§0This would last moderately long.§0\n\n((Need to see if air enchantments are a thing, awaiting approval", ""),
