        StaticBook("Govt. I.D. [106]", "§bAdulfin Ehrlichmann", "===Heil Vandoria===\n\nName:\nRand Rovin\nMCName: Sir_Niccum\n\nPosition:\nShit Poster\n\nClearance:\nLevel 2\n\n\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Morilin'Parir's Journal§0\n§0\n§0Fi'Ceru\n\nSweet Rose, Bitter Blue Tender Flowers die so young, Sweet roses red and bitter blooming blues. Brightest Night how does your moon does shine making these bitter days seemm the sweetest nights, Darkest Days why must you remind us§0\n§0\n\nof those sweetest roses now long gone, Those Tender Flowers that leave us too soon.§0\n§0\n§0All of us from oceans deep ad the mountains tall share this short time here with all these flowers so tender are they that we see them\n\ncrumble in the wind nothing more than a lifes wish to go on Being stolenfrom its lips\n\nDream the Sweetest Dreams on these dark nights. For tomorrow comes the darkest night. Amist these dreams come dreams of a crown of thorns digging deep. Drowning the soul in its own blood. The Sweet bitter kiss of death couldn't come soon enough. For in\n\nthese dream death is all too real. For in the darkest days  come the Sweetest Dreams of Happiness and things held dear while in there wake comes the thorns Digging deep into the soul where the only things allow to grow are Hate and fear\n\nOh how the bright sun rises, Lifting the bitter gloom. Oh how these roses need to bloom. For before the nights dawn and the cold night returns, The love that is shared will be in full bloom. AS the darkness comes for us. We will be waiting with the light\n\nANd when the Light does shine forcing the dark to fade", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "12th of the Amber Cold§0\n§01515§0\n§0\n§0I have been here in al-Wahkrah for nearly three months now. Every day seems to be full of new faces.§0\n§0Not everything has gone so well though. Upon going back to Oren with the Amir I had to realize that those people\n\nnever change. Haterd is all they know.§0\n§0The Qalasheen have helped me see that not all humans are the same though. They welcome me here with open arms. §0\n§0I have never felt more at home in all of my years roaming this vast world.\n\n13th of the Amber Cold§0\n§01515§0\n§0\n§0I have just gotten home from a long two day patrol with the other guards (we call them Al-Qalasahabah). The trip was fairly hard, and we were nearly mauled by the hordes of beasts that roam at night.§0\n§0It's nice to be back.\n\nBahadir, a good friend of mine, gifted me a beautiful white gem upon us getting back to the city. §0\n§0Bahadir is a kind man. He is stern, proud and a good leader, but still very sweet. He has even helped me with a personal problem where a neighbor became to\n\ninterested in me. He acted as though he and I were a couple. It did well to chase the other human off, but meant so much more to me than I could ever explain to the Amir. §0\n§0The stars are beautiful tonight. The way the light shines off this gem is stunning.\n\n16th of The Amber Cold§0\n§01515§0\n§0\n§0I keep thinking about Allah. What the old one said runs through my mind over and over. I just don't know.§0\n§0I felt a calling to  go to their lands, but I never thought any God was pulling me there. I still don't know what..\n\nLater this very day the game I play had to go on.§0\n§0\n§0Another man tried to woo me, though they failed. I told them that I was taken by Amir Bahadir, which he didn't seem to like very much. Not that it bothered me.§0\n§0Bahadir is such a good friend.\n\nI had given him a flower a month ago to say thank you for all he has done. A few days ago he returned the gesture by giving me a beautiful white gem.§0\n§0I will carry it with me always, and hold it dear to me.\n\n23rd of the Amber Cold§0\n§01515§0\n§0\n§0I can't seem to stop thinking. My mind runs wild these days. I either think on Allah or I think on Bahadir. What has over come me?§0\n§0I have started to accept Allah- so when I think on Him it makes me feel whole.\n\nIt is Bahadir that causes me to be lost. I think of him often...§0\n§0He is human, though. I can't. I can't have feelings for him, and honestly I don't feel like he returns my feelings. §0\n§0Perhaps this elf belongs alone... maybe it's better that way.\n\n17th of the Deep Cold§0\n§01515§0\n§0\n§0And so the day has come. My birthday - not that anyone in the city knows it. I think it's better this way. We had another person roam our streets drunk as can be. I am not one to talk, but in the four months I have been here I\n\nhave come to realize what venom spirits actually are. These people act like animals when they roam our city drunk. §0\n§0It makes me nearly sick.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+The Holy Scrolls-§0\n§0     Gospel, Part One§0\n§0+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+§0\n§0\n§0Published by the§0\n§0Knopf Company, Apostolic Branch§0\n§0\n§0Released by Father Siup Atlam, former Canonist cleric.§0\n§0\n§0First Edition, 1535\n\n+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+PROVENANCE§0\n§0\n§0Lo, in the name of the Lord GOD, the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent, listen and attend with pious heed to this inspired text.§0\n§0\n§0In the beginning, the glory of GOD was singular and whole,\n\nand there was naught but Him, and thus there could be no pain or iniquity.§0\n§0And by His Word, the Planes were rendered, and His throne was in the Seventh Sky. And that which was farthest from the Lord became the Void, and that which was nearest became\n\nthe Skies, and betwixt them was the World. And GOD saw that it was good.§0\n§0And from His breath, GOD created His Immortals, the Aenguls and Daemons, and named them His servants and messengers. And He assigned to them their roles, and said that Aenguls shall\n\nshall rule all that is, and Daemons all that is not, and they resided in the planes below GOD, and no place was forbidden to them but the Void. And GOD saw that it was good.§0\n§0So the Lord turned his gaze from the Skies to the World, and he ordered forth the\n\nImmortals, and they set to the work of creating the World. And they shaped in this plane many lands, and they separated the earth from the seas, and sowed the Lord’s treasures into it. And the Lord breathed life into the beasts,\n\nand ordered their estates. And GOD saw that it was good.§0\n§0But among all the Daemons, the chiefest was Iblees, and he was very proud to reign over his kind. And he doubted GOD’s strength, for it was given to the Daemons to rule what was not,\n\nand Iblees was chief among Daemons, and he desired to rule without the Lord. So he descended the emanations of glory, and grew farther from GOD, until he reached the Void. And lo, he was cursed by its touch. And GOD was wroth.§0\n\nFor when GOD bore witness to the bounty of His Immortals, He was pleased. But when He saw the bounty of Iblees, which was sin, He was very wroth with the Daemon. And He spoke to Iblees. “Why hast thou done that which I have forbidden?” And Iblees replied\n\n“For you name us as servants, and I shall devise of no virtue until I am your equal. And now my touch is the touch of the Void, and it is with all things in your creation.” And GOD was furious, and Iblees would not repent. And he fled into the void, for\n\nfor he hated the glory of GOD, and by his own will was shackled from the Lord.§0\n§0And while the other Immortals had pleased GOD with their creation, none had fulfilled His plan, which had been interrupted by the sin of Iblees. So the Lord made two bodies of\n\nearth, and gave them blood and breath, and the light of wisdom. And they were virtuous, and He called them the first man and first woman, who took no language or name. And these were GOD’s favored creations, and they did satisfy His plan.\n\nAnd with His favor, the first man and first woman did prosper, and they drank the sweet water and ate of the Lord’s bounty. And they remained faithful to the Creator, and did as He bid, and knew each other, bearing four sons.§0\n\nThe eldest was Malin, who rose tall and fair-haired from the rich loam of the forest. And he took a likening to the beasts of the earth and the fruit-bearing trees, and resolved that his home should be a sanctuary for lesser beings.\n\nThe second was Urguan, dense and rough-skinned like the walls of his deep mountain home. About him were gold and onyx and alabaster stones, and he took fascination with  them, and resolved that he should concern himself\n\nwith the affairs of the deep earths.§0\n§0\n§0The third was Krug, monstrous and fierce, brought forth from the scorching desert dust. He was the strongest of his kindred and took fondness for hunt and battle, and soon resolved that he should hone his\n\nstrength and surpass all living things. The youngest was Horen, who was neither tall nor short, not frail nor fierce, and he acted with wisdom and restraint. And thus he was quite humble and did not share his brother’s ambitions, except to praise GOD.\n\nSo the Lord was pleased to lay His favor upon the sons of His first man and woman, and He called the pair forth to reside in Sixth Sky and give the World over to the dominion of the Sons. And the first man held GOD with great fear and marvel, and did as\n\nhe was bid, and rose to the Sixth Sky beneath the throne of the Lord. But the woman loved her children greater than even GOD, and put them above Him. So the Lord was wroth, and uncovered the imperfections of the Sons, so that she would\n\nknow her folly. And the first woman wept, and was humbled, for all things are imperfect before GOD. And she did as she was bid, and rose to the Sixth Sky.§0\n§0Thus, the Sons were orphaned, but even in their imperfection did keep faith in the Lord. So GOD was\n\npleased, and He gave them language and greater knowledge, and created for each Son a tribe of seven thousand alike to them, and placed them above their people as kings, and they testified to His glory.\n\n+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+HOREN§0\n§0\n§0Lo, in the name of the Lord GOD, the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent, listen and attend with pious heed to this inspired text.§0\n§0\n§0So the Sons were raised up as kings, and each became more concerned with the\n\nWorld than the Skies. And all took concubines, except for Horen, who took only one wife. And her name was Julia, and he kept their union holy.§0\n§0Now Iblees had suffered in the Void for a great time, avoiding the grace of GOD, for he doubted the Lord\n\neven as he fled Him. And he saw that the Sons became more worldly, and that they spoke with GOD less each day, and even Horen spoke less of the Lord to his brothers, but kept his holiness private. So Iblees saw that the brothers were weak,§0\n§0and he ascended\n\nthe emanations of glory, though he was loathe to feel the grace of GOD.§0\n§0So it had come that the four brothers and their people dispensed themselves as such: Malin and his people went into the forests, and there they lived freely beneath and atop the trees\n\nUrguan and his tribe went into the mountains and into caves of mountains, and they carved cities there, and lived in orderly stone homes. Krug and his tribe went into the desert and slew the creatures therein, and they made tents of hide, and fought\n\ncontests of strength and cunning in great pits. And finally, the people of Horen built homes of wood and cloth in the plains, and they built temples of stone, and had many children. But like Iblees, Horen felt the separation of GOD from man. And Horen\n\nfeared to be without GOD, and so he prayed, and received a message. So the Lord told him to go into the Grotto of Gamesh, which was many leagues’ walk from the land of Horen’s people, and to fast in the waters for three days.\n\n And Horen submitted, but was wise first, for he felt the presence of Iblees in the world. So he went to his people and described to them the Denier’s aspect, and advised them to cast him out when he appeared. And thus informed, Julia went into her\n\nfamily’s tent, their holy tabernacle, and she gathered their three sons there, and bade them to remain in the sacred place as she walked the camp, looking for Iblees. So Horen went into the east, and followed the path ordained before him. And Iblees\n\nobserved his absence, and went into the camp of Horen’s people, and he began to tempt them. But Julia was wise and recalled her husband’s warning, and she revealed Iblees, and the Denier was cast out of the camp, and was very wroth.§0\n\nSo Iblees went out of the land of Horen’s people, and set to working iniquity among the other brothers. So he went into their camps in other guises, and he tempted them with sin, and said the Lord pardoned them for their faith. And the Sons of Malin, and\n\nof Urguan, and of Krug were wary, but did not wish to reject the soft beds and wine they were offered, and the finely worked jewelry, and so all reveled and lazed and lay with each other, and called it faith. And it came that one of Horen’s people, a man\n\ncalled Saul, had ignored the warning of Julia, and left the camp. And he wandered into the iniquity which Iblees wrought, and coveted the gold and sweet food, and spoke at length with the Denier. And Iblees was cunning, and guised Saul with the skin and\n\nclothes of Horen, and sent him into the camp with a message.§0\n§0So Saul went among the people of Horen in his guise, and he began to work Iblees’ iniquity. And Julia, having cast out Iblees, had retired to her tabernacle, and there cared for her three sons,\n\nand awaited the end of her husband’s fast. Thus Saul worked Iblees’ iniquity in Horen’s camp, as Iblees had in other camps, and it came that again a great many people were corrupted. Now on the third day of Horen's fast, he was approached by the\n\nAengul Tesion, who bore a laurel of olive leaves in his right hand, and a silver horn in his left. And the Aengul dipped the horn into the waters of the Grotto of Gamesh, and poured them onto Horen’s brow. And the Aengul said “Here, I cleanse thee. And", ""),
        StaticBook("Official Papers", "§bAdrian of Kaedrin", "Mi, Adrian Chivay, ub Kaedrin, herebi denounzez dah exiztehnz ub dah kreator, agh dah pozzibility ub bekumihn' ah zaint.§0\n§0\n§0Mi hab nuw taykehn ahn Oat' tu Krug, dah truu munutheeiztik beihng.\n\n[!] A translation is transcribed beneath the initial, written in poor handwriting - obviously by a noted down by a goblin [!]§0\n§0\n§0I, Adrian Chivy, of Kaedrin, hereby denounces the existence of  the Creator and the\n\npossibility of becoming a saint.§0\n§0\n§0I have now taken an oath to worship Krug.§0\n§0\n§0----------------Signed By:§0\n§0\n§0Adrian Kaedrin, (Former) Bishop of the Canonist Church.", ""),
        StaticBook("Esempio", "§bSister Lucia", "*The letter you hold is a long, wrinkled parchment with a neat, cursive handwriting*§0\n§0\n§0Dear Father,§0\n§0\n§0     I am writing to you with my wishes for the order that shall be founded. I should first add the plans between High Pontiff\n\nEverard, and myself. Originally, the order was going to be called the Missionaries of the Poor. This order would have been devoted to the poor of possessions and of spirit. My nuns would have taken vows of povert, chastity, and obedience, with the\n\nrequirement of carrying out acts of charity. You have said that the convent would be in Luciensport. Preferrably, I would like for the convent to be in a foreign land, where people of the Creator do not dwell. This is our true calling. To convert the poor\n\nof spirit. If you do not wish for this, that is fine. If, however, you agree with this, my olf friend Brother Beros has been kind enough to provide land and resources so that my convent, and his monastery might be brother and sister.\nI shall be re-writing\n\nmy rule soon, so send word of your reply to this letter.\n\n     Sincerely,\n            Sister Lucia", "")
    )

    private fun _VAILOR_8(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Thesis on Women", "§bSister Lucia", "Women are a controversial topic in throughout the mystical body of God, the Holy Church. It is argued over the feminine role in our Church. Some would claim that women should have no authority over man. Others would claim that women should be subject\n\nto man. Both the initial and the latter are false. All holy peoples would speak of the Church as a woman, referring to the Church as 'her' or 'she'. These same people would claim that woman shall have no authority over men. Hypocrites! They will have no\n\nwoman claim authority over them, yet they praise the female Church in which controls their lives? The other side would claim that woman should be subject to men. This is also false. Men and women shall be subject to nothing except the Word of God. This\n\nWord has been divinely inspired so that it might have supreme dominance over all peoples and nations. You who read this and speak to yourself, 'This woman believes women may become priest!'. What an uttermost blasphemy! Albeit women and men are equals in\n\nthe sight of God, women shall have no authority over men in /spiritual/ matters, the matters of the Creator. And to you who speak to yourselves 'This woman is a heretic!'. My words are prompted by the Spirit to be spoken, do not divide the Kingdom. You\n\nmust not replace the moral truths with majority opinion, for that is the damnation of the world. §0\n§0\n§0       Signed, §0\n§0             Lucia§0\n§0             of the§0\n§0             Cross", ""),
        StaticBook("Pricebook", "§bErin Twoore", "@> The Little Lion <@\n\nPg. 2: Alcohol\n\nPg. 3: Teas\n\nPg. 4: Foods\n\n@ Alcohol @\n\n3m Ale\n\n5m Wine\n\n7m Vodka\n\n4m Mead\n\n6m Rum\n\n@ Teas @\n*All teas are sold for 5m*\n\nDandelion tea\nBlue orchid tea\nChamomile tea\nRose tea\n\n@ Foods @\n\n2m Bread\n\n4m Baked Potato\n\n4m Various soups\n\n*Custom foods can be made on request.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Notes on void§0\n§0\n§0The void is the infinite plain of nothingness and emptyness that encompasses all of possibility as it currently exists and ever will exist.§0\n§0\n§0Evocationists use the well of untapped infinite potential to summon forth various\n\nelements and forces, and attempt to direct them into the mortal plain.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Enchanting§0\n§0             & §0\n§0          Runesmithing§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Notes by Alvos Glasmann\n\nThe first discovered Glimph, was the one belonging to Unbreaking. The ability to make items last longer.§0\n§0\n§0Rune shape: X§0\n§0Material: Lapis, Gold\n\nLure is the ability to help fishers catch fish more frequently.§0\n§0\n§0Rune shape: L§0\n§0Material: Lapis\n\nSmite, the ability to deal more damage to creatures of the dark§0\n§0\n§0Rune shape: + (wide)§0\n§0Material: Lapis\n\nLuck of The Sea brings fishermen even greater treasure from fishing§0\n§0\n§0Rune Shape: Fish§0\n§0Material: Lapis§0\n§0\n§0HAVENT FOUND IT YET\n\nMaking tools mine faster is what eficciency does.§0\n§0\n§0Rune Shape: Y on its side§0\n§0Material: Lapis, Gold\n\nMining blocks without breaking them: Silk Touch§0\n§0\n§0Rune Shape: ________§0\n§0Material: Lapis, Gold", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "A Courlandic Tune.§0\n§0----------------§0\n§0O' the Courlandic army,§0\n§0O' how they were so barmy,§0\n§0They're quite shit,§0\n§0Belong in the pit.§0\n§0But God! We'll win this one!§0\n§0We promise not to run!§0\n§0O' how they are brave!§0\n§0But it leads to their graves!§0\n\nEverybody knows!§0\n§0Everybody woes!§0\n§0For the Courlandic Army!§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Map", "§bZeliek", "[!] A somewhat detailed map rests upon the page, on one side rests a city with the name \"Vanaheim\" resting across it. The other side rests a large ruins upon an icy mountain with \"Frost witches' base.\" wrote across it.\n\n((Coords X 129 Z -3742 ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I did it- I finally connected to the Void. I was breathing so heavy, I think I was shaking, but I didn't break focus. It was a sudden 'wash' of... nothing. I felt absolutely nothing. But within' the few seconds of nothing, I was drained of all energy.\n\nIt was terrifying. But I did it. I think. Maybe that wasn't connecting? I really hope it was... I'm going to tell Sal and Adniel. I hope they're both proud of me!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I have discovered a fortress like structure on a secluded island in the middle of God knows where. Upon approaching I saw some shady looking people. I climbed the mountain nearby and watched for a while, but one of them took notice of me. I managed to\n\nescape by hiding in a cave, but they are now going to be watchful. Fortunately I doubt they know of that cave, so I can use it in the future. I visited again later, the gate was closed, but I could feel something dark going on in there. I'll need to find\n\na way to get closer without being detected. Today at a tavern I saw one of the dark men I've seen around that fortress, I'll have to keep an eye on him and his actions. A man who I've seen before with Andre, the man who I am in debt to, has now engaged\n\nthe man at the tavern. After an intense conflict, the elf who was once with Andre defeated the dark armored man, and mentioned himself as a necromancer hunter. I should try and ask him some questions, maybe show him the fortress.\n\nI saw a child at the fortress today, a child! What was a child doing in such a dark place, something doesn't seem right. He was playing with a toy, and black smoke came from it... I don't think that kid is a kid. He says his name is Sey.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "ae", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Log Book:§0\n§0Citizens of Isle Valrok§0\n§0\n§01. Marcus Abelardus§0\n§0   ((RowdyGentleman))§0\n§02. Conall ((Tireus))§0\n§03. Aiden O'Donnell§0\n§0   ((_MrBlocks))§0\n§04.Beordan §0\n§0  ((Beordan))§0\n§05. Ariselle §0\n§0   ((EagleEyeKK)§0\n§06.Howard Kent§0\n§0   ((MrPieMan1111))\n\n7. Sethperith Lucital§0\n§0    ((Murdervish))§0\n§08. Zorn ((LittleKnights))§0\n§09.Argothin§0\n§0((KillerPhoenixes))§0\n§010.Madalyn§0\n§0((CornBeefRachel))§0\n§011.Hedge_Hug((??))§0\n§012.Bradshaw§0 Gray§0\n§0     ((thatpyrodude))§0\n§013. Valot ((SirValot))§0\n§014. Archaem Doom§0\n§0     ((__StarWars__))\n\n15. Boris Karloffice§0\n§0      ((Doveboyz))§0\n§016. Cyrelas Corera§0\n§0      ((saveforthememory)§0\n§017. \"Ser\" Ren Cresten§0\n§0      ((JacktheBlue20))§0\n§018.", ""),
        StaticBook("Neo - Druidism", "§bEloh'ra", "Neo-Druidism\n\nThis tome was originally created by Petyr Brandybuck.\n\nWith some modern druidic practices wandering astray, it has been necessary for me to scribe another text - that of Neo-druidism. Throughout my travels and meditative studies, I have had revelations unknown to others. It is important to understand\n\nthat there is a special type of balance that druids themselves remember to study - action and non-action. Let me clarify. Action is motion, the motion of restoring balance, and of being the hand of Nature, the Universe, the \"It\". For, through non-action\n\nyou may feel \"It\", and through action you may be \"It\". Call this \"It\" what you want; most druids will call it Nature. What is important is to understand what Nature truly is, and how it relates to you. To reveal this is the goal of this tome.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nThe Unity of Nature\n\nThe first fault in thinking is to make distinctions - those between you and Nature between life and death, between good and evil. Everything is Nature, despite what any given piece believes. A druid does not use nature:\n\na druid is merely a piece who realizes the profound truth. Through non-action, one may truly understand this concept and feel it course through them. However while meditating in non-action, one also separates themselves from the flow; the Way,\n\nthe path that Nature chooses for its pieces. To rejoin with Nature, one must practice action.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nThe way of Nature\n\nNature does what it will, and while we realize this while meditating, sometimes we forget in action. We are merely moving along the river of life, the tides of balance. While we beleive that we are restoring the balance, It is\n\nbalance restoring itself in an everlasting self-conflict. Thus, through action, we are the hands of Nature, of balance, of the Way.", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-3", "§bDaniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 3/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Water Symbols\n\n           Weak\n\nName: Blissfoil\nRepresentation: Calmness\nDescription: Blissfoil is a plant which has more applications in healing medicine than in alchemical healing potions. While it has been found to have weak potency in\n\nalchemy, it’s effects are quite used in healing. I do not believe many good doctors exist which have not heard of the use of this plant, for it is one of the best numbing agents out there. The greatest problem with it, is the fact that overuse of it\n\ncauses permanent numbing to an area, and with the power it holds, it happening by someone who does not know of it’s effects is quite possible. The plant itself looks like a combination of many small blue flowers with a thick and flimsy stalk.\n\nIt’s harvesting is as easy as collecting a flower, and it is born and grows under birch trees near grassy areas.\nLocation: Under birch trees in grassy areas.\n\n         Moderate\n\nName: Serpent's Stalk\nRepresentations: Life, Rebirth, Calmness, Fluity\nDescription: This plant is one of the easiest to find in the forest of the realm. If one knows where there are small ponds and perhaps streams of\n\nwater, they would find the Serpent's Stalks. Long Emerald hued stalks, with stripes and ridges of a lighter green and brown along its length, almost like a serpent. Sometimes simple mistaken by normal sugar canes by those unknown of this plant, and to\n\ncollect it is the same as well, cutting it at the bottom. Another attribute it holds similar to a serpent’s it’s the poisonous nature it has. Specific insects that come in contact with it are normally found dead all around them, yet from all it’s use, no\n\nother creatures seem to die from it. It is actually used many times as a healing agent, specifically to heal and treat burn wounds. A normal oinkment from simply crushing the plant and mixing it with some water may smooth the pain and keep the wound\n\nsafe. It is as such a good water symbol that can be used for antidotes, oils, balms, healing potions and potions of calmness, as well as fire extinguishing potions. Those are good to have when preparing alchemist fire.\n\nLocation: Grows near small bodies of water in forests.\n\nName: Mandragora\nRepresentation: Rejuvenation, Life, Rebirth, Regrowth\nDescription: This is one of the reagents most alchemists use when creating more powerful healing potions. It’s meat rejuvenating traits makes it so that it’s very well\n\nsought by many alchemists. No good ingredient comes without its dangers thought, and Mandragora is one that can bring a collector to a very humiliating death. It is observed growing into the shallow waters of swamp lands, with thick green leaves flowing\n\nout of the water. Such leaves are quite delicious as garnish for soups and to make a quite rejuvenating tea. It is highly nutritious as well, filled with nutrients. It is not the leaves that one uses as a reagent thought, but the “meat” of the plant.\n\nThe part of the plant normally underwater is shaped like a parsnip. It is this “meat” that needs to be collected and prepared to use by the alchemists. Collecting it it’s not as easy as it sounds. This plant creates highly narcotic and paralyzing spores\n\nwhich are released quite easily when the plant is moved. Inhaling them brings the humiliating death of drowning in a foot high water level, as you simply fall on it and are unable to move any further. As such, one has to known when the spores are fully\n\nreleased, and only then retrieve them. Normally simply a group of at least two set out to find them, and one pulls the other from death if the spores are still with the plant.\nLocation: Low waters in wetlands.\n\nName: Zawabate\nRepresentations: Life, Calmness, Rebirth\nDescription: Zawabate is the only reagent I know of water representation in the desert lands. Of course it does not grow in the middle of the sand, it grows in the rare oasis one might\n\nfind. There is it protected from the strong heat and low humidity, in the fertile grounds around the waters. It is identified by it’s prominent colors of green and yellow, with short curvy petals in a long stalk. For those that live near them, especially\n\nthe orcish shamans, it is a plant which brings a higher connection with the spirits and out of body experiences. To say more simply, Zawabate is a hallucinogen, creating great comfort and sensations, which are further enhanced if made into a stong tea.\n\nThese flowers are certainly an amazing addition to potions designed to numb pain or heal because of their home in such a lush landscape among a wasteland of aridity. The amount to use however, should be greatly controlled, due to its hallucinogenic\n\nproperties. Too much, and the healing potion might cause delusions and mental problems, which means it can also be used for to create those same poison effects if wanted.\nLocation: In the fertile lands of an oasis\n\nName: Frost Vine\nRepresentation: Life, Calmness, Ice\nDescription: Frost vine is a blue vine which grows in very cold climates. It seems to have a need for shade, the most common of places being around trees, leaving long blue spirals in their\n\ntrunks and falling from their branches. The plant is a very good numbing agent, one which can easily be made into a sticky clear substance which numbs pain and loosens stiff muscles. Too much of it and it may affect the limbs, making them completely numb\n\nfor some time. One must always be sure to wash the area after applying the substance. It is by some considered a good alternative to a stronger but also more dangerous rubbing agent, Blissfoil, and with some other good qualities in the mix.\n\nThe vine is quite cold to the touch, which means it may also be further used to better the effect of numbing and treating wounds and pains. With these traits, it is no wonder that this plant represents life, calmness and cold.\n\nLocation: Shaded areas in cold climates.\n\n          Strong\n\nName: Athin\nSymbol: Freezing, Ice, Life, Balance\nDescription: Athin is quite a potent Water Symbol that one finds in ice lakes and rivers of fresh water, which are normally frozen. It is a blue algae, sometimes quite hard\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nto find if the ice is too thick or the snow stops vision to the unfrozen water under the ice. One particular difficult to harvest plant, not due to the how you take it, but because of the danger associated with it. It is taught to all alchemists that it\n\ntakes two people to harvest Athin. This is because it grows under ice, on very cold water. The ice breaking and someone getting stuck is a high probability, but either way you will have to get into the water to collect it. Sometimes people get stuck\n\nunder the ice, not knowing where the hole they did was, sometimes they do not take precautions with heating before entering the water and freeze in the cold wind when out. Such dangers do come with reward, as Athin is one of the materials there are that\n\nare fireproof. It has a great representation of ice and freezing, and an alchemist that carries around alchemist fire, or simply makes it, always have some athin around with them as well.\n\nLocation: Under the ice of frozen lakes and rivers.\n\nContinues in part 4\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
