        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Subject one§0\n§0Name: Cookie§0\n§0\n§0Location: Ebonglade§0\n§0\n§0Relationship status: Single§0\n§0\n§0Favorite Food: \"Cookies, duh\"§0\n§0\n§0Favorite Hobby: Baking§0\n§0\n§0Age: Twenty Six\n\nSubject 2§0\n§0Name: Arrow§0\n§0\n§0Location: Dreadlands§0\n§0\n§0Relationship status: Single§0\n§0\n§0Favorite Food: Bread§0\n§0\n§0Favorite Hobby: Mining§0\n§0\n§0Age: Seventy-Eight\n\nSubject Three§0\n§0Name: Dirij§0\n§0\n§0Location: Felsen§0\n§0\n§0Relationship Status: Single§0\n§0\n§0Favorite Food: Pumpkin Pie§0\n§0\n§0Favorite Hobby: Reading§0\n§0\n§0Age: One Hundred Ten\n\nSubject Four§0\n§0Name: Shanka§0\n§0\n§0Location: The Uzg§0\n§0\n§0Relationship Status: Single§0\n§0\n§0Favorite Food: Grog§0\n§0\n§0Favorite Hobby: \"Blahing with the earth spirits\"§0\n§0\n§0Age:", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Upwards of eighteen years have now elapsed since the initial exile of my people. These  past eighteen years have been spent far away from both the Elven lands and the fort we'd come to call home in the mountains of Urguan.§0\n§0\n§0Our people had been displaced\n\nbefore but these last eighteen years rank high above anything we'd ever experienced before. This will not be a biography, however. In fact, it is an unfathomable task to document all the perils my tribe brothers and sisters surmounted.§0\n§0\n§0Moreover, such an\n\naccount of our journey would not serve to represent the Ker condition.§0\n§0\n§0It would seem that an individual's identity as a Ker is enough to warrant decades of destitution and degradation at the behest of an otherworldy force.\n\nIn spite of these unfavorable circumstances, an astute observer could identify a trait that is universally shared by all Ker. Along with tragedy, pride is a primal ingredient in the composition of a mali'ker. In his book titled \"The Mali'ker,\" Dak'ir\n\nDes'nox cites an old clan story that contends the recipe for a mali'ker consists of \"family, honor and love.\" This belief is inconsistent and functions more accurately as Dark Elven propaganda. To believe every Ker loves their family and considers honor\n\nto be sacred is optimistic but fails to consider that many Ker work as thieves or mercenaries.§0\n§0\n§0Mercenary work is as far away as you can get from honorable. It is important to note that assisting an ally in war is not to be considered mercenary work.\n\nMercenary work is also not related to acts of loyalty, neither should mercenary work be considered evil as it is entirely void of any sort of emotion. Thus, mercenary work for the sake of financial gain is not tied to a sense of honor. It is disconnected\n\nand serves only to provide for mercenary's lifestyle.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Target: Jayce§0\n§0Living Situation: A resident in the city of Ebonglade§0\n§0\n§0Is a guard of that city and seems to be their blacksmith.§0\n§0\n§0Appears near the Warhawkes hold occasionally. Trying to join the warhawkes?\n\nHas once sided with the Warhawkes, yet then decided to side with Ebonglade. He also has stated he has not been in a war against the warhawkes since he has been with Ebonglade.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hunt Note", "§bCrystal Bel'anoche", "To find he was now in Urguan", ""),
        StaticBook("Hunt Note", "§bCrystal Bel'anoche", "And woke with a fright", ""),
        StaticBook("Hunt Note", "§bCrystal Bel'anoche", "Who’s pubs were all kinda borin’", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "((This message is OOC§0\n§0\n§0((You know the drill! We (FilthyPeasant1 and Murdervish) do want to finish the torture RP. However! Umbra will almost certainly die at the end of it. Now, I can guarantee it'd be fun for us, but since your character isn't -\n\n((- likely to develop due to the death making you forget it, if you'd rather not finish the RP when you come back and just soulstone out, that's fine. If you want a detail of what the torture was going to be, or want to finish that RP at a later time,-\n\n((-just let us know.§0\n§0\n§0((Also, the soul puppet was just going to aide with the torture and execution. It would no longer be in affect after your execution. So don't worry about that :)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "In a hole in the groung lived a halfling. Not a nasty, dirty, wet hole, filled with the ends of worms and and oozy smell, nor yet a dry, bare, sandy hole, with nothing to sit down on or to eat; it was a halfling hole, and that means comfort.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This book belongs to Erik Stalfen. If found, please contact.          x-3242 z-516\n\nFall(SophieMarie)- Haven't spoke with her much but seems to know Hydromancy.\n\nAlstasia(JCmarine)- Quite an annoying pain in my side. Has no respect for anyone.\n\nAyche(Draxagon)- Clearly a mage, a silent one at that. I know he knows shifting, Electromancy, Air Evocation, and Mental Magic. I wonder what else he hides.\n\nSahar(Murdervish)- It seems she is learning Mental Magic, perhaps from Ayche? Anyways, she is seemingly in charge of the Edict.\n\nEve(Edgymagey)- My grand teacher!\n\nAbraxas(Loreq)-Not sure why he is in the Edict, but nevertheless he is, a man with many secrets.\n\nNaffog(Filthypeasant1)- The true leader of the Edict. An orc I would not wish to fight. Yet he is a whitewash.\n\nMarrow(Sherlock_holmes)- A dark elf who reminds me much of Marn, someone I cannot stand what so ever. Likely to get me kicked out of the Edict.. Again.\n\nRonir(Crimsonblades)-A snow elf, what a joke! But seemingly a good kid.\n\nCrineas(sharkali)- Someone I met while tagging along with Eve.. An air evocationist, seemed rather against violence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Medical Notebook §0\n§0\n§0A Compendium of Medicinal Procedures Performed by Sentis Vul'Tohorran-Hennington §0\n§0-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-§0\n\nAiantas Tha'un - §0\n§0Broken ribs, previously tended by cleric. Hemothorax occured, requiring emergency chest tube insertion to drain pleural area. §0\n§0Procedure: Successful §0\n§0Complications: Minor §0Bruising\n\nSahar Tha'un- §0\n§0Multiple fractures and breaks. Left arm, right leg. Open break of clavicle, cracked ribs, multiple. Multiple minor and severe lacerations. §0\n§0Procedure(s): Successful §0\n§0Complications: Infection of wound over clavicle. §0\n\nBjornfort = Troops §0\n§0Summerhall = Supplies §0\n§0Istria = Mercs/spies §0\n§0Courland = Ship + Obelisk §0\n§0Lorraine = Main supplier§0\n§0Leader of Istria = Hiring mercs to spy on Urguan§0\n§0Bjornfort = x1500, z-1950§0\n§0Obelisk = x-1250, z-2680§0)\n\nSummerhall mines go under mountain foundations for keep. §0\n§0\n§0[CONFIDENTIAL]", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "~*~§0\n§0Any suggestions for the town would be well appreciated, please leave them on the next couple of pages. Anything from jobs, to town cleanliness and tidyness. Elders and the Mayor will attempt to implement them.§0\n§0\n§0           ~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Key:§0\n§0* name of ingredient used in drink§0\n§0& color§0\n§0! effect\n\nTea§0\n§0Rose Tea-&pk!<3^§0\n§0Poppy Tea-&pk!<3^§0\n§0Dandelion Tea-&y!sat§0\n\nNeeded for brewing stand§0\n§03 Glass§0\n§04 Stone§0\n§0-Blaze Rods§0\n§018 Redstone§0\n§02 sticks§0\n§06 gold§0\n§0-Fire charge§0\n§02 coal§0\n§04 Gunpowder\n\nJuices§0\n§0Orange§0\n§0Apple§0\n§0Lemon§0\n\nCoffee and Eggnog§0\n§0Egg-nog§0\n§0Cocoa Beans-Coffee?\n\nAlcohol§0\n§0Dark Resin-Wine", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "1+2= 3§0\n§02+2= 4§0\n§03+2= 5§0\n§04+2= 6§0\n§05+2= 7§0\n§06+2= 8§0\n§07+2= 9§0\n§08+2= 10§0\n§09+2= 11§0\n§010+2= 12§0\n§011+2= 13§0\n§012+2= 14§0\n§013+2= 15§0\n§015+2= 17\n\n16+2= 18§0\n§017+2= 19§0\n§018+2= 20§0\n§0\n§0*The handwriting would be extremely messy*§0\n§0Leo aged 7.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Leo ages 24:§0\n§0Writing from wc.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day One§0\n§0   The night I saw a beautiful woman. See had emarald green eyes, red hair and a warm smile. I didn't know it then, but this woman turned into my wife. She conforted me on new years. And we danced. We danced all the way through the night. *\n\nDay two. §0\n§0   We started talking, got to know more about each other. It went on like this for a month or so. Ashirana made me feel welcome.§0\n§0From the next month I got to know her.\n\nDay 33§0\n§0   This was a big day for me. It was the day I took Ashi on a picinic, to enjoy all the wonders of being a couple. We went deep into the feilds and sat down on a blanket. It was in that moment that I proposed witha flower. A white Lilac.\n\nDay 43§0\n§0   How derpy am I to forget a wedding! Ashi and I are not even officially married. But I guess that is ok. Some people know that they love each other. Though this really big guy came in our house. Damai, Appearently Ashi had been dating.\n\nDay 54§0\n§0   I am still in jail. This is the worst since I got thrown in dwarven jail. The jail reaks of pig, and cow, and blood. Not blood I didn't mean blood of humans, blood of birth and whatnot, from the animals.\n\nDay 56§0\n§0   Finally got le out of jail. I need to go take a bath, Maybe I can get Ashi to join me?§0\n§0I'll work on that.§0\n§0[!] There is a smll tear in the book.§0\n§0   I hate when a thing your working on tears.\n\nDay 85§0\n§0   Hard to find Ashi. SOrta freaking out.§0\n§0I have searched all over the place just to find her in the room next to us. §0\n§0   [!] A blood spot covers the rest of the text.\n\nDay 100§0\n§0   It has been excactly 100 saints day since I met Ashi. Her and I have suffered many different things together, such as cutting... cutting... Injury... and Injury.§0\n§0WHen I think about it§0\n§0it is all kind of funny.§0\n§0(( IT IS ELVEN DAYS\n\nDay 101 §0\n§0   This is the day that Kasai, and Beordan became a part in our lives. Now if you are reading this, no they arnt our children.§0\n§0They are some of Ashi's old friends.§0\n§0Appearently Kasai had a crush on this dude,§0\n§0and Beordan had a crush on her.\n\nDay 145§0\n§0   This is the day that Beordan finally proposed after much consideration and help from a friend. *Cough* Me *cough* Kasai like ran into Ashi's arms and told her everything. I just punched Beordan in the arm and said \"Good Man.\"\n\nDay 176§0\n§0   Lots has happened during preparation.§0\n§0Struggling a bit with my tux. It feels way too tight, and I believs it make me look fat, though I way a staggering 143. Beordan looked sharp, like he always does.\n\nDay 232§0\n§0   The even Bigger day than the proposal.§0\n§0The wedding of the Human Beordan, and the Wood Elf Kasai.§0\n§0Exciting in every aspect. Lots came. And Ashi was in the most beautiful dress I could ever imagine.\n\nDay 245§0\n§0  Ashi and I are a strange couple... That is least thing to say. With both sorta do our own thing together. She will go on a nature walk, and Ill stay up waiting for her. Ill be gone and when I get home she will be there.\n\nDay 254§0\n§0  Today is a semi sad day. We found a very nice girl who's name is Ava. She is nice but blind, we let her over to Beordan.§0\n§0   Today I also found out Ashi has stomach problems and can't hold a baby.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "To Dizzy,§0\n§0\n§0   Dizzy, as you may know, our people are in great peril. Oren marches upon us, and without aid, we will fall. I know not what to ask of you, but we need our old kin. We need old folk to rear the new generations up right.\n\n-We need the masters of old. We need the great craftsmen and wise folk to return, to guide our kingdom to our rightful holding, in total peace and prosperity. We need to stop the human advance, or be totally destroyed. If you refuse to return, please-\n\n-return to us your guidance, and wisdom in our perilous age.§0\n§0\n§0Our smiths need your skill, your mastering and aid. We need thy steady hand, to teach us and guide us. §0\n§0\n§0~Heus Grandaxe", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-Sausage§0\n§0-Prime Rib§0\n§0-Salted Potato§0\n§0-Lava Stew§0\n§0-Mashed Potatoes & Cheese§0\n§0-Mushroom Stew§0\n§0-Sweet Cake§0\n§0-Bread§0\n§0-Baked Potato\n\n-Chocolate Milk§0\n§0-Mulled Wine§0\n§0-Pale Ale", ""),
