        StaticBook("Dwarf Babies", "§bAerxuis", "Where Do Dwarven Babies Come From?\n\nWritten By: Unknown\nCopied By: Aerx\n\n17th of Amber Cold, 1473\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nwould look like. IIIIUUUUU, it sounds. And hairy, very very hairy.\nNormal babies come when a man and a woman mate, and after pregnancy a baby is born. Well, if you notice, there are almost no woman Dwarves, but I will state why this is\n\nfurther in. The true ways are far more disgusting and frightening than mating can ever be, it is a mixture or ale and hair.\nDeep inside the mountains of the Dwarven towns, deep underground, are special and greatly guarded rooms. It\n\nis in these hidden rooms that the baby Dwarves are born. I was quite lucky that I found such a room when the guards were fully drunk and had knocked each other out. So I entered the room and by the creator! It smelled worse than the drunks just\n\noutside!\nIn a room which seemed filled with puke and ale, there were chunks of what looked like hair. Some of the hair like chunks were even moving. At that time I heard talking just outside the room, and in fear of being discovered, hid\n\nmyself behind a rock. A Dwarf came in completely drunk and with a knife in his hand.\n“By Yakemar, ay s’all ‘ave a son!”, he shouted before he cut part of his beard.\nI watched stunned as this happened, I could never believe a\n\nDwarf had cut his own beard, but soon I would know why the Dwarves treasure their beards so much. Releasing the knife he fell on his knees and coddled the beard near his chest.\n“Ya will be named Grikot.”, he said, and that is when it\n\ncame to me, all those other hair chunks, were in fact part of the beards of other Dwarves.\nThe Dwarf placed the beard chunk down, and picking a bottle, tilted ale over the beard before leaving. So you see, dear readers, the Dwarves\n\ntreasure their beard because it is from it that their children will be born from. So where do the small amount of female Dwarves come from? As I walked out I realized that one of the chunks was very small, and that the baby could be seen. A female\n\nDwarf is born when a Dwarf, being far too drunk, doesn’t cut enough of his beard, and such, the Dwarf is born beardless, becoming this way, a woman.\nNow, onto the types of Dwarves, as you should know, the are cave Dwarves, mountain Dwarves\n\nand mountain Dwarves. After discovering such intriguing ways of conceiving a child, I searched further and found out the reasons. Cave Dwarves are the ones where the room in inside a deep care. Mountain Dwarves, the cave is dug\n\ninside a mountain but it does not go very deep. Both of these type of Dwarves, as they were born inside a room by willing drunkenness. Forest Dwarves are born on the outside, from which when the drunkeness is so great, they couldn't find the room. That is\n\nthe reason Forest Dwarves are looked down upon by the others, they were not born in the rooms for the beard to be placed.\n\nI hope this text has helped the reader to understand the hairy way of Dwarf birth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arnold's Mind", "§bArnold Athletic", "The Mind of Arnold Athletic\n\nThoughts and Philosophy of the Greatest Athlete Ever\n\nWell I'm a fine sweating shit stomping man of the people, anybody ever tell you that? Name's Arnold, but you a'ready know that pro'ly. I decided it might be good money if I just wrote and wrote and wrote, e'rything that came into my head. Bet it's gonna\n\nsell to every manly man, sexy dame, and little boy out there! Who doesn't want to know what goes on in my head.\n\nDon't call me offensive, but a lot of elves are flyin' fucks. Prancin' 'round like they own e'rything and are smarter than us humans. My\n\nmama didn't raise no fools, I'll tell you that right now.\n\nWhat's up with all these clinics in every city and town? Back in my day, Pa would tell you a broken bone was the creator's way of punishin' you and smack it with a pickaxe. Now everybody wants\n\n\"quality care\" from a bunch of Farfolk and flyin' fuck Elves.\n\nWhat happened to the world? Wha' happened to the good men, who wound up with some blacksmith work and wound down at nine by gettin' oral from the fanciest prostitute in town. C'mon, what\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nhappened to the good men? Now it's all cowards and smart-hats and swordsmen and wiseass guards and preachers of the devil. There used to be good men, I'll tell you that.\n\nAnd what about crime? E'rybody is talkin' 'bout how bad crime is in these cities,\n\nbut it ain't. When I was a boy, if you ain't stealin' or dealin', you ain't nobody. Pro'ly that mother out there just took this book off her son and gasped at what I just said, but it's god damn true, so shut it, woman.\n\nI lived in the days where men were\n\nmen and women lived to please us. Now we got woman Farfolk fixing my broken leg at a clinic in the mosque-dominated land of the Caliphate. What happened? I mean, come on, world used to be real. Now it's all crap and shit and bollocks done by cowards and\n\nprofessors.\n\nMORE OF ARNOLD'S THOUGHTS WILL BE IN HIS NEXT BOOK: COMING SOON!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0elven language words §0\n§0& phrases\n\nkarin'ayla - good day§0\n§0ker'ayla - good night§0\n§0van'ayla - farewell§0\n§0aylan nae osulier - Good to see you§0\n§0llir u'kathir? - Friend or Foe?§0\n§0sirame ito kae'leh, nae oroment, llir'Malinor - I am honored to meet you, friend of Malinor§0\n\nayla nae osulier - Good to see you.§0\n§0thilln ito nae'leh - Are you pure? §0\n§0heya kae ern'omediere? - How can I help?§0\n§0heya nae uhiera? - What do you seek?§0\n§0kaean ito lin'Mali narnae kento? - Shall we travel to the home of the Elves?§0\n\nk' nae chul'ofihe? - Are you hungry? ((lit: must I feed you?)) §0\n§0fihn ern'oradonte? - Can I request food?§0\n§0kae adil'ociwe - Do you want to sleep?§0\n§0heya tilrue kento, kae'leh Laurir - How will I serve, my Prince?§0\n§0 §0\n§0ahern ito nae'leh - Thank you§0\n\nahernan - thanks ((lit: blessings!))§0\n§0kae'leh sil ito nae - My blade is yours§0\n§0 §0\n§0ame nae evareh - may the forest preserve you§0\n§0maehr'sae hiylun'ehya - progress and health§0\n§0Velulaei y nae ilumeh - May the moon shine upon you§0\n\nleyuan! - Splendid!§0\n§0sulian! - Brilliant!§0\n§0lluman! - Woe!§0\n§0ullran! - Damn it!§0\n§0ay'elame! - For the Forest!§0\n§0ay'Larihei! - For Larihei!§0\n§0Malin'leh iheiuhii - Malin's Breath!§0\n\naverir ito nae'leh - I am lost§0\n§0ullral iyl'fin narneyae - It is dangerous here. ((lit: Monsters roam this region))§0\n§0nae il'kae narna kento - Shall you travel with me?§0\n§0kae taliaman'Malinor medier'orehiera - Will you help me find the trees of Malinor?§0\n\nadil'okinare - Bring me to the Orcs. ((lit: I want to die))§0\n§0larehan ito kae'leh - My mind is made up§0\n§0\n§0kae nae'leh lle salume - I sense your good intention §0\n\nnae uvul'thrur ito Bortu illera - You give gunpowder to a dwarf ((expr: you are asking for trouble))§0\n§0iheiuhii narne narneyem'ehya - the wind travels and travels again ((expr: life goes on))§0\n\niheiuhii ito taliaman - The trees have breath ((expr: We are not alone))§0\n§0Asul lente karinto - The sun will grow ((expr: Have Hope! / Cheer Up!))§0\n§0hae'leh kalem'Valah yallre - She lives her human years\n\nliewyn'Larihei eltaeleh walehe ohn vallein eltaliyna walehe - The smile of Larihei heals the mind like milk heals the body ((expr to reiterate hte importance of the High Elven philosophy))§0\n§0kae cihi'thilln ayle - I like the Silver City§0\n\naverir iylmahnihto ernne'onarne - A wanderer may not travel within this wall §0\n§0kaean'leh thilln chul'okarae - We must safeguard our purity§0\n\nFather- Maln§0\n§0Mother- Haelun§0\n§0Son- Maln'onn§0\n§0Daughter- Haelun'onn§0\n§0Child- Malii (or Mali'ii)§0\n§0Uncle- Malnonn§0\n§0Aunt- Haelunonn§0\n§0Sister- Liyur§0\n\nBrother- Ciyut§0\n§0Male Cousin- Ciyutonn§0\n§0Female Cousin- Liyuronn§0\n§0Nephew- Ciyut'onn§0\n§0Niece- Liyur'onn §0\n§0Grandfather- Marmaln§0\n§0Grandmother- Marhaelun§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Medicine Vol. 1", "§bKale", "A Dose of Solace§0\n§0Volume 1§0\n§0\n§0Written By: Dr. Kale§0\n§0\n§0\n§0In this book you will find effortless remedies to common day sicknesses.§0\n§0\n\n1. Stomach Pain§0\n§0\n§01 cup of hot chamomile tea§0\n§03 peppermint leafs§0\n§0\n§0Place the leafs on top of the hot steamy cup of tea and drink it twice a day to ease the churning pain.§0\n§0\n\n2. Flashes (Fever)§0\n§0\n§04 rags§0\n§01 big bucket of cold water§0\n§0\n§0Soak the rages with water and place each rag on the forehead, under each arm pit and behind the neck. Do so as needed until it subsides.§0\n§0\n\n3. Burning Throat§0\n§0\n§01 hot cup of water§0\n§05 drips of honey§0\n§02 tsp. of sugar§0\n§0\n§0Mix it all together thoroughly and sip until your throat begins to feel soothing. §0\n§0\n\n4. Coughing§0\n§0\n§01 rag§0\n§01 pot of boiling water§0\n§0\n§0Place it rag over your mouth and bend your head close enough to the steam and breathe it in. Do this until your coughing has calmed itself.§0\n\n5. Ear Pain§0\n§0\n§0   Warm up oil until it is at a lukewarm feel and pour it into the ear. Lay on the opposite ear that isn't causing you pain. The pain should stop momentarily. §0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n\n6. Bruises §0\n§0\n§0There's multiple remedies to heal a bruise quickly §0\n§0\n§01st- Cold Herbal Tea Compress§0\n§02nd- Ice Block compress§0\n§03rd- Cold Poppy Tea Compress§0\n§0\n\n7. Rashes§0\n§0\n§0Cacutus Paste§0\n§0Herbal Tea§0\n§0\n§0Mash the two together until it become a thick like paste. Rub the paste on the rash until it drys or can be scraped off.§0\n§0\n§0\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to make the rash paste*§0\n§0\n§0\n§0*Here would be a sketch showing how to apply a compress to a bruise*§0\n§0\n§0*Here would be a sketch showing how to make different teas*§0\n§0\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to mix honey with tea* §0\n§0\n§0*Here would be a sketch of a person breathing in the steam with a rag covering their mouth*§0\n§0\n§0[!] The sketch would be drawn very well§0\n§0\n\n[!] On this page would be doctor Kale's signature in highly neat penmanship§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0~ §0§oDoctor Kale", ""),
        StaticBook("Sheet Music: 433", "§bHeruza", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("John Cage's Song", "§bHeruza", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "As an elf I have in excess of 1000 years to make something of my life, and experience all that I may wish to. However, one misconception that many seem to have is that, with time comes happiness. Alas, this is not so.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "An Introduction:§0\n§0\n§0With the end of one life, the start of another may bud. With time, it may even blossom. The very life that had to end will be brought forth anew – though never truly the same. As is the way of the world – as is life.\n\n\"Cherish what you have for it will not always be.\"§0\n§0-§0\n§0Cara Hilltop", ""),
        StaticBook("Paycheck:Sarrion", "§bLorena Faeliel", "PAYCHECK\nROYALTIES FROM\nGUARGERS BOOK STORE, CALIPHATE.\n\nFor the sum of: One Hundered Mina.\n\nTo: Sarrion Zytiaer\n\nSigned: Lorena Faeliel\n\nDate: 3 S/S 1521\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/qy4xzxx", ""),
        StaticBook("Love and Uruks", "§bHeruza", "A Tale of Love and Uruks\n-- Let this be a lesson. Hopefully, some may be saved by choosing not to make the same mistake as the poor woman in this story. All of the events are true. --\nTold by Dulgar Doomforged\nEdited and Recorded by Heruza\n\nThere was a dwarf named Dulgar Doomforged who felt an empty space in his heart. He would go to a tavern to drink very often. On one bright day, he was taking a stroll through Athera, and saw a very beautiful human woman. She was being harrassed by an\n\nOrenian. Dulgar threatened the Orenian, and he quickly scampered off. Dulgar offered to escort the woman home. She was an Orenian woman, like the man who was making trouble for her. This was during the Dwarf-Human War. It was obvious the two were falling\n\nfor eachother. They walked together for quite a while, until they were at their home. There were many of Amya's men there, and they used their sheer numbers to chase the Doomforged away. Months passed, with the couple not seeing eachother for a long time.\n\nWhen eventually, they met again. Dulgar proposed to the woman, and she gladly accepted. Though... the woman was always getting into trouble... and one day, Amya's men visited the two. Dulgar fought the men off, almost losing his arm and leg.\n\nTwo months before the wedding for the couple was set to occur, the woman decided to mess with a group of Uruks. They thought her enlarged belly was dark magic... They took her to their 'Uzgan', and all that came back of her, was...\n\nA bloody rag, barely resembling the dress she once wore.\n\nDo not mess with the Uruks, and do not enter their territory pregnant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elements of Mind", "§bAris", "Elements of Mind\n           /\\\n         /\\ /\\\n         ><  ><\n         \\/ \\/\n           \\/\n     /\\         /\\\n     \\/         \\/\n\nThoughts on the mind and its most basic concepts.\n             Aris, 1461.\n\nEvery living being has a soul and a body, but what makes them unique, is their Mind. Mind itself is what defines you, and your actions. However, mind is different, it can be viewed in many ways, but it isn't as simply explained the body or a soul. But\n\nA simplistic way to explain would be this;\n If a being was a ship\n\n Your body would be the hull,\n\n Your soul would be the sails,\n\nBut the ship would never sail without its Captain, the Mind.\n\nAn example simple as that makes everything easier to understand, yet the Mind is more than that, a Mind can be described and divided in different ways. You can say a mind is inferior or superior, but you cannot say a mind is right or wrong. Continuing\n\nwith the same example from before, Mind, the Captain, can fit in three categories;\n  The Captain can be..\nCurious, jumping into adventure in search of answers.\nIntelligent, a person of logic and reason.\nKnowing, from experience and books\n\nCuriosity, Intelligence and Knowledge are the key points of the Mind, but ultimately, there is  Wisdom. Now, let me break down the four.\n\nCuriosity, the most innocent of the elements of mind for it is the base of all knowledge. A child is curious,\n\nbecause it is important and natural for them to gain experience from the world they have stepped their foot in. Curiosity is the desire, the craving to gain information or learn something. Curiosity is important to me, because it is what activates me,\n\nand more importantly, motivates me. It's very\nimportant for me to be\nopen to try new things\nand find out more, as there is an endless\namount of information.\n\nKnowledge is, in my opinion, the outcome of curiosity. It the term used for skills and\n\ninfromation gained via experience and / or education. Knowledge is something many seek, without truly knowing what they are looking for; knowledge isn't only facts laid out by letters in a book, but the prize of feeding one's curiosity for they can\n\nbecome truly aware of how things are. Knowledge covers familiarity, awareness and understanding of\nsomeone and something\nbut simply put, it doesn't mean you grasp the concept.\nOne can say they know\nor understand evocation, yet never be able to actually\n\nevoke a single droplet of water, a lone spark, or a tiny huff of wind.\nKnowledge is something\nthe mali'aheral, the High Elven, hold very dear. It could even be\ncalled the national\ntreasure of the race.\n \"Kae maehr evar\"\nKnowledge protects me\nCommon-\n\nphrase from the High Elven, is something that also fits me. Knowledge is what I seek, and something I already hold in some topics. It is also something that has saved me many times in seemingly helpless situations. For me, it is important to know the\n\nright people, and know\nthe right things. Knowledge is also the very reason I originally picked up\nthe graceful art of\nMental Magic, because for me, knowledge is a seemingly endless goal\nas new information keeps surfacing, and\nmental magic is inevitably\n\nthe door and also the key to new knowledge.\nBefore I started learning, it was a door\nthat remained locked for me, but now the door is opening to me\nagain, slowly, bit by bit.\n\nIntelligence, the ability to acquire and apply new information and knowledge.\n\nAn intellectual mind adds and overwrites\nold knowledge. You can not learn to become intelligent, for you are someone who can grasp concepts, or you will never be such.\nWhat makes intelligence different from knowledge, is that you\ncan be born\n\nintelligent, but you cannot be born knowledgeable. An intelligent person has great mental capacity for judgement, reasoning and logical thinking. A person that knows alot doesn't necessarily have all this, sadly, superior minds are often thought to be\n\nsly, only becasue they are vastly more intelligent than the\npeople around them.\nTo me, intelligence isn't something you can train, but something you do or do not have,\nshould it be the latter,\nI have trouble taking\nsuch people seriously.\n\nUltimately,\n\nWisdom is the prize of attaining the most of these three key elements of the mind.\nBecoming wise isn't something you can decide yourself, it is more like a title you\ngain from your surroundings. The Wise\nis intellectual, knowledgeable, yet still curious\n\nfor more. In my opinion wisdom is what an individual should truly\ntry to reach for, but\nmany are simply unfit.\nWisdom is the quality of having experience, vast amounts of knowledge, good judgement and logical thinking, and that isn't something you can\n\nattain within a short time frame; it is the\nultimate achievement.\nA wise person to me, is someone to look up to,\nand someone who should receive endless respect, but unfortunately the truly wise are scarce.\nThough, you can be wise without knowing\n\na lot, as the only true wisdom is in knowing you know nothing.. and one must beware of false knowledge for it is more dangerous than ignorance itself.\nThe path to wisdom is\nendless and eternal.\n------------------- \n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Paycheck:Kale", "§bLorena Faeliel", "PAYCHECK\nROYALTIES FROM GUARGERS BOOK STORE, CALIPAHTE.\n\nFor the sum of:\nTwenty Four Mina\n\nTo: Kale\n\nSigned: Lorena Faeliel\n\nDate: 3 S/S 1521\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/nvrt8qy", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lesson V2", "§bZahir Darthirii", "Just as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in elven are as follows: \n\nKae - Me \nLae - Him/He \nNae - You \nLye - We - Used to speak of elves, people or the world. \nHae - Her/She\n\nFor example the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (He fared well).\n\nIn addition to this, other good language supplements to anyone learning elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be added to create further detail or form critical grammatical structures in a sentence.\n\n\nThe dash denotes location of seed word. Affixes and seed words are separated by an apostrophe.\n\nac- (aca-) - Honorific for accursedness. \nah- (ahe-) - Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholars. For example: Ah'Lucion. \nfi- - New or anew.\n\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) - Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. For example: Cer'Silir.\n-ante (-nte) - Last\n\n-ento (-nto) - Next \n-onn - From or born. \nu- - Or\n\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive. \n-ir - Designates purpose of someone or something. \n-sae - The spreading, development or management. \n-ii - Diminutive form. For example: Malii, meaning little elf.", ""),
        StaticBook("Braxus. I .", "§bBraxus Ni'leya", "=================== \n----= Braxus. =----\n\n~ An autobiography.\n\n>  Greetings to whoever may be reading this book. Before I begin, I would like to note that all events that take place in this autobiography\nwill move in -\n\n===================\n\n- chronological order. Now, without further delay, let us delve into the life of me, Braxus Ni’leya. \n\n===================\n\n===================\n\n>  I was born during the year 1264, Malin’s welcome, to two Mali’aheral, two Mali’thilln, Kayda Ni’leya and Sarndir Ni’leya.\n\nFrom my birth to the age of 25, life seemed to go at a rather slow pace. We resided in a rather small -\n\n===================\n\n- a rather small dwelling on the northern edge of the forests of Laurelin. Those early years would prove to be the most important years of my life. My mother and father played a very imperative role in my upbringing, as all parents -\n\n===================\n\n-  should. My mother taught me how to read and white whilst my father taught me how to hunt and defend myself. The words of my family were and have always been, “Strength, in many forms.”. As a Ni’leya, it is very important that one -\n\n===================\n\n- exercises both their physical attributes but also their mental capabilities. The first step to progress, is within, thus, my family strive for perfection.\n\nMy father on the other hand conferred his vast knowledge of swordplay and -\n\n===================\n\n- hunting unto me.  He wanted me to be able to defend myself at an early age and so at the age of 8, I was well learned in the ways of the marksman, swordplay and of course, how to use a shield. A bow and quiver became my companion -\n\n===================\n\n- as I travelled through the forests to Laurelin. Thankfully, I never had to use it. Occasionally, my father would take me hunting. The forests were teeming with game ranging from rabbits to elk, boar to duck. We usually returned -\n\n===================\n\n- home with enough meat to last a week.\n\nOnce I was 10 years of age, my mother advised me to travel to the city of Laurelin to familiarise myself with the library and the tomes, scrolls and book within. She bestowed unto me -\n\n===================\n\n- a craving for knowledge. Alongside this, she assisted in teaching me how to deal with my emotions. I spent roughly 5 hours a day at the library, having left my home at the break of dawn, I often wandered on an empty stomach however-\n\n===================\n\n- I usually ran into a berry bush or two on the way and so that sated my hunger until I returned home.\n\nOverall, I had a good, happy upbringing. I was well mannered and well educated with strong ideals.\n\n===================\n\n> One day, as I was returning from the library, I decided I would take a different route home, through the forest itself and not a pathway. As I was walking, talking in the beauty of the world, I happened upon a small clearing. A -\n\n===================\n\n- small stream had made its home there along with a rocky outcrop. Atop one of the rocks, was an elven woman, Mali’aheral by appearance. She had hair the color of silver, her eyes a deep shade of blue. Her attire -\n\n===================\n\n- was that of a long, azure gown. One I will never forget. She was the exemplar of beauty, grace and elegance. I stood there for what must have been at least 5 minutes, simply gazing, in awe of what sat before me. This was my first -\n\n===================\n\n- ime seeing another of my kind, besides my family of course. To my disdain, she turned around and caught me gawking. I thought I had escaped her view by dipping behind the nearest tree however, my attempts were futile for not 10 -\n\n===================\n\n- seconds later she pleaded that I show myself and so I did. “My name is Braxus.” I said in a gentle tone, not wanting to scare her more than she already was. After a moment, she responded. “And I, Larissa.”. She spoke softly, -\n\n===================\n\n- elegantly. She had a way of speaking, a way that soothed one's mind.\n\nWe talked until the sun went down and the stars appeared. The topics of conversation varied from family, to the meaning of life, to aspirations and -\n\n===================\n\n- goals. To my displeasure, she was conscious of time and informed me that she had to depart and return home. As she was departing, I said something rather bold and daring. “Shall we convene here tomorrow at the same time?.\". My -\n\n===================\n\n- heart began to pump faster than usual, she offered no response for what must have been 20 seconds until finally, I got the response I was hoping for. “Of course, Braxus.”. I ran home, feeling euphoric.\n\n===================\n\n The following day, I had a lie in, I was too giddy to go to the library and so I stayed home and discussed last nights events with my mother and father. They were happy for me. Cautious, yet happy. I made my way to the same clearing\n\n===================\n\n- and there she was, a wicker basket in hand. She wanted to go berry picking and so we did. We talked, laughed, ate berries and got to know each other better. We would convene like this at the same spot for the next 27 years. Every -\n\n===================\n\n- once in a while, we ventured to each others homes. Thankfully, both of our families accepted us. She lived in a small village on the western side of Laurelin, home to humans and elves alike.\n\n===================\n\n>  It was the year 1316, a date I would never forget. One day, as Larissa and I were returning to my abode, we noticed a plume of white smoke hovering above the treeline. It seemed to be coming from the direction of my home. We -\n\n===================\n\n- looks of concern and darted through the forests. On arrival, we were met with death and ruin. My mother and father had been slaughtered, my home burnt. This was my first experience with death, sadly to say, it would not be my last.\n\n===================\n\n For a long time, I was in my own world. A world of pain and lamentation. \n\n I was invited to stay with Larissa and her family, an invitation which I took as a sign from Malin himself. I accepted and -\n\n===================\n\n-  up until the fall of Aegis, in the year 1351, things seemed to be working out well. I had become a scribe in Laurelin, copying books and various tomes for the library. I was 87 when we departed for the unknown, 90 when we arrived -\n\n===================\n\n- in Asulon.\n\n> I wanted to marry Larissa. I loved her and she loved me. Her parents gave consent and we would marry in the year 1356. Having left her family home, Larissa and I departed for the city of -\n\n===================\n\n- Normandor, where we purchased our first home. It wasn’t too expensive, my days as a scribe and the minas her family had left her more than made up the total cost and the rent for a year. We both acquired jobs in the same library I -\n\n===================\n\n- was to become a scribe once more. She didn’t truly enjoy it and if i’m honest, neither did I but it made it possible for us to continue to survive.\n\n> However, Asulon came and went. Before we knew it, we had ended up in Kalos -\n\n===================\n\n- and shortly after, Elysium. Things became turbulent and we needed to escape city life. We found ourselves in the surrounding countryside of Huntshill where we constructed a small residence, much like my own in Aegis. Life -\n\n===================\n\n- was simple. Simplicity and relaxation is all we wanted. However, such was not what ensued. As the sun crawled up to the sky and the stars became veiled once more, I departed our home happenings and left for the forest. Abundant -\n\n===================\n\n- with game, much like the forests of Laurelin, I planned on making the best out of what nature had to offer. I hunted elk today. I spotted my prey and like a true marksman, I hit my target. I was thrilled, unfortunately, my joy was -\n\n===================\n\n- not to last.\n\n As I had bested the elk, a deafening cry was heard. The lament of the one I loved was sung. I scrambled through the woods in a futile effort to save her. Panting, broken and in shock, my eyes met hers.\n\n===================\n\n-  Glazed and void, there she lay. My wife of 73 years, my other half had been killed. An arrow, much like my own, had found their mark. Time froze for a while, I stood there unable to think, move. I was in denial, struggling to come-\n\n===================\n\n- to terms with what had just happened.\n\n My life ended in the year 1429. A broken Mali'aheral of 165.\n\n For 36 years I wandered the forests and lands in search of her. I found madness instead.\n\n===================\n\n A period of deep depression found its way into me, many times I had attempted suicide but it would appear Larihei had different plans for me.\n\n I was 201 when I decided to live again. I'm not sure how, but I came upon -\n\n===================\n\n-  the blessed domain of Haelun’or. There I stood at the gates of Tahn’siol. An elf in despair, a hopeless elf with no purpose. My kin took me in and gave me a purpose, a reason to live. The maehr'sae hiylun'ehya would be my goal.\n\n===================\n\n The preservation of my kin would be of the utmost importance to me. \n\n> My kin and I arrived in Thales, the year was 1465, our home was the city of Celi’ante. Purity was proving easy to maintain, as a being of nothing, -\n\n===================\n\n-  I was encompassed in it. A warrior of silver I became, fighting for not only my beloved people, but for Larissa. She was constantly on my mind, there wasn’t a day where I wouldn’t think of her. Always whispering, enthralling me.\n\n===================\n\n Several years came and went, we arrived in Athera, the year being 1468. We had 7 years of peace within Annil’suil until we were overthrown by Phaedrus Lle’hileia, a Mali’ame. A genocide occurred, those who supported silver were -\n\n===================\n\n- killed or had fled before they could be. We went into hiding in Aldersburg. It was there that I met Asul'athri. He would turn out to be one of my most valued friends and mentors. A true and pure Mali'aheral who believed in -\n\n===================\n\n- the revitalisation and restoration of our kin. It was through his will that Elsillumiran were formed. The weeping blades of Haelun'or.\n\n At first, there were two. Asul and I. Our goal was to be the spark that would -\n\n===================\n\n- rekindle the flames or purity once more. To act as a beacon to those Mali'thilln who had lost their way during our fall. To act as a shield to the battered children of Haelun'or. To reclaim our home.\n\n===================\n\n This was no easy task, considering it was only us two, we had to take on the pseudonyms of ‘’Cassium the strong’’, me, and ‘’Jonathan Smythe’’, Asul. The reasons why should be obvious, we were being hunted by the bronze.\n\n===================\n\n We had recovered many of our kin and returned them to Aldersburg where we now called home. Asul hand planned for greater things. He wanted Elsillumiran to continue and with a resurgence of Mali’aheral, this was possible.\n\n===================\n\n There were two lens at first, Len’oem, led by Asul and Len’niut led by me. Together, we formed the sword and the shield, the bird and the spider. We gathered information, defended our kin, but most importantly, we defended our -\n\n=================== \n- traditions. Blood was given by many, I bear the mark of the Mali’ame under my left eye, a scar of remembrance.\n\n 1484, Annil’sul is returned to us. We return home, although now, my mind suffers from flashbacks and memories.\n\n===================\n\n I see those who fell before me, I see Larissa. I battled with this for months on end to no avail, I plunged once more into a period of depression. I shut myself away from my kin, became paranoid and afraid. A courrpt government had -\n\n===================\n\n- installed itself and I stood against them, thus, I was banished from the city, unlawfully albeit but I was forgotten, a stigma of impurity and foulness became my legacy.\n\n===================\n\n My sole purpose to this very day, is to guard the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. To make sure my kin reach their goals however, being banished meant that once again, I had no goals. \n\n[ Part one of a two part series. ]", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro. Alchemist", "Jistuma", "Forward:\n\nGreetings, my dear reader. Within the pages of this tome I shall be explaining to you what it takes to be a true Alchemist. I shall run you through our mindset, qualities, and traditions.\n\nChapter I: \n\nThe Recipe for a Good Alchemist.\n\nIt takes a special breed of person to be an Alchemist: a rare combination of patience, creativity, intellect, enthusiasm, and of course, an unusual resistance to explosions. For those who wish to follow the noble path of an Alchemist, you must first\n\nconsider if you possess these key traits, for if you do not, much like a potion made with a flawed recipe, you will be ineffective.\n\nDo not mistake what I say for supremacism, but rather realize that it is simply an effort to save you.\n\nIf you do not possess these qualities, dear reader it is quite possible that you, in the attempt to follow our path, may indeed end up harming yourself and others. Now, allow me to go more in-depth about what these traits mean, in order of their\n\nimportance to an Alchemist: Patience. Alchemy, I'm afraid, is not a fast nor particularly interesting process. An Alchemist will spend most of their time for their elembic to boil so that the extract of your ingredients may be collected for use, or simply\n\nwaiting for a potion to brew. Very little of the time it takes to create a potion is actually spent creating the mixture, although this time is indeed the most interesting part of Alchemy in my opinion. Because of all this, dear reader, Patience is vital\n\nto an Alchemist, as it would be, in my opinion, apt to give Alchemy the formula consisting of 25 \"parts\":\n\n>7 parts waiting (brewing, waiting for the elembic's water to boil.)\n\n>5 parts setting up, cleaning up, and inspecting your equipment.\n\n>5 parts testing (making sure your potion works.)\n\n>3 parts failure (realizing that your recipe is bollocks and starting over.)\n\n>3 parts extracting (boiling down the ingredients and collecting the condensation using an alembic.)\n\n>1 parts explosion (surprisingly common.)\n\n>1 parts mixing the bloody potion.\n\nIntellect. You may be wondering why this is not the first on my list... Well, someone whom is completely dull, yet is willing to give up hours upon hours to make up for it, is much more likely to succeed than someone brilliant who will become frustrated\n\nand rushed the second they see that their brew will be taking a very long time to finish. So, while this trait is near-vital, it can be made up for by a massive amount of patience and dedication.\n\nCreativity. Please note that I am writing here to explain what it takes to be an Alchemist, not a good Alchemist. Creativity is something completely vital to anyone who wishes to be a master alchemist... but it is not to those whom only wish to dabble in\n\nthe art. Creativity is essential for those who wish to truly excel at the art, because one cannot just follow recipes forever. There comes a time, when an apprentice Alchemist must take these matters into their own hands. No more books, no more\n\nexplanations as to why these particular ingredients must be used... there comes a time, when every Alchemist must learn to rely on their own extensive knowledge of herbs and ingredients, of what they represent... To craft a potion of their very own. This\n\nis much more difficult that it may seem... but I shan't go into that, as this is no true Alchemical textbook, but rather, an introduction to the science.\n\nLastly, Enthusiasm. This trait may seem unusual to list, as most would automatically think of someone who is impulsive and stupid... 'overly' enthusiastic. No, Alchemy requires a special type of enthusiasm. One tempered by logic and patience.\n\nEnthusiasm is needed because without the drive to learn more, to improve your skill and to create potions of wonder... you are nothing, and shall go nowhere. The reason this is listed at the bottom of the list instead of the top, is simply because by\n\nreading this far, you have shown an ounce of this quality, and as such, you may now take pride in knowing that you have the potential to learn this art.\n\nChapter 2:\n\nThe Life of an Alchemist\n\nThe Lifestyle.\n\nThe life of an Alchemist, despite its labours, is a rewarding and interesting one. Many nations, many companies, and many guilds need Alchemists, which means that an Alchemist is very rarely without options. Indeed, one of the\n\nmost fulfilling parts of being an Alchemist is the satisfaction of knowing you are needed and wanted. An Alchemist rarely stays in one location whilst unemployed, often traveling from kingdom to kingdom, seeking a guild or company that has use for them.\n\nIn my experience, this does not take a long time... Although it is important to measure one's options before taking a job. This is not to say that an Alchemist /must/ be employed, gods know many Alchemists choose a life of reclusion and\n\nintroversion--preferring the company of their ingredients and their equipment to the company of people or currency. As an Alchemist, there are many different paths one may choose from; be it creating poisons or creating potions to heal the ill and\n\nwounded. These paths will play  large role in deciding how easily one can get jobs, and from whom. For example, one who makes poisons may find it harder to get a job than one who creates healing serums as poisons are hard to mass-produce, which means are\n\nof no real use to an army, and they are certainly of no use for a peaceful company of a guild. This is much the opposite for healing potions, as oddly enough they are some of the simplest to make, and can be made in quite large quantities without losing\n\nmuch of their effectiveness, so all the aforementioned employers could have a use for an Alchemist of healing. Do not think that these are the only two paths that an Alchemist may follow, however--and certainly no Alchemist sticks only to one branch of\n\nthe science--think of it more as a specialization. I, for example, specialize in incendiary and explosive concoctions. Alchemist Fire, if you will. This means that I am often asked to work for militaries of small offensive guilds… even research companies.\n\nIn conclusion, the lifestyle in terms of business, for an Alchemist, is much dependent upon what they specialize in, and regardless of their business opportunities the life of an Alchemist is rarely full, and in my opinion, very fulfilling.\n\nThe Morality of an Alchemist.\n\nMany jobs seem to have a set \"morality.\" Soldiers are expected to be lawful and trustworthy, Mages to be intellectual and neutral... the Morality of an Alchemist is much the same as that of a Mage, and is, much like\n\none's business opportunities dictated by the Alchemist's specialization. To use the same examples as before, it would be more likely for an Alchemist specializing in poisons to fall into a darker, more \"evil\" morality, as they would likely find their work\n\nwith small groups of assassins of the like. Whereas an Alchemist specializing in healing, would be much more likely to fall into a \"good\" morality, as by nature, their job of choice is to help people. There are not set rules, of course, a healing\n\nAlchemist may very well choose to assist an unlawful organization, and an Alchemist of poison may choose to supply a small vigilante group with his poisons. In essence, the Morality of an Alchemist is neutral, and is dictated completely by the individual.\n\nThe Living Conditions of an Alchemist\n\nThis section will be somewhat small, as there is very little that can be written about this. An Alchemist's abode will generally have only one constant: a lab, usually located in a basement. This lab would contain\n\nan Alchemist's supplies, equipment, and is generally kept locked, as much inside would be fragile or dangerous. As for why it is usually found in a basement… Well… The earth seems to be a bit more resistant to explosions than wooden or cobblestone walls.\n\nFarewell:\nI thank you, reader, for taking the time to read my small introduction to the Alchemist. I bid you good ever, good day, and farewell.\n\nAn Introduction to the Alchemist\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Books Sold", "§bLorena Faeliel", "STORE RECORDS\n\nDiary of Books sold, prices and to whom.\n\n*The book you open would be a diary like layout, containing all the books sold after a current date.\n\nThat date being the 21st of The Deep Cold, 1520\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/ofz3g4y", ""),
        StaticBook("In Sheep's Wool", "§bNafis Yar", "On Wolves in Sheep's Wool\n\nAn Informative Pamphlet on the Adrian Dog and Others Associated to the Breed.\n-------------------\n\nWhen training man’s companion, one must start from an early age. You are to drill the sort of conduct you wish to see into them, much like you would do with a new soldier under your command or your own toddler once they begin to walk. If left alone, the\n\ndog becomes wild growing up. It will run amok in your household and eventually it will bite the master’s hand. While usually there re ways to remedy this after it has passed the threshold, this is perhaps the exemption where there is only one route to\n\ntake.\n\nReader, I ask you pay heed to the words I write in these darkest of times. Look to this particular breed of Canis that has long sincebeen allowed to run wild by humanity’s predecessor’s : The Adrian Dog. Do not put blame on those men who live on\n\nthrough the archives, for they had only shown mercy as taught by the Orenic Faith. But understand their mistake. I urge all readers to learn from it and do not repeat it or else the dreaded cycle of Crow continues.\n\nMy words mean nothing without evidence,\n\nand this I can provide, dear reader. The Adrian Dog is a carnivorous beast hell bent on the destruction of others for mere amusement. It is the thrill of the hunt that gives them activity.  If they have nothing to hunt, they grow restless. Cranky, much\n\nlike a baby whose sleep is disturbed. But this is no mere infant! It is a monster of a beast that will bite the master’s hand when least expected.\n\nThe Adrian Dog is one who subjugates the unwilling. Looking through the archives of Athera,\n\nwe witness this in practice with the genocide of the Waldenian people where my grandfather once hailed from. After the forefathers of the Adrians had robbed the throne from House Chivay, they proceeded to eliminate all those that opposed. Wishing to\n\nmaintain their vows to the overthrown Chivay, the Waldenian people refused to follow suit with the other Orenian vassals. This was never out of greed as it was  portrayed by Crow nor was the Konigreich of Aesterwald ever meant to be. It was through sheer\n\nloyalty to their vows that the Waldenian people refused to back down until the supposed “Protector of Humanity” Emperor Tuvya Carrion mobilized his armies alongside Uruks and threatened to bring Aesterwald down. Only then, to protect his people from the\n\ndestruction that would have came, did Konig Voron Rovin I (may he rest in peace) swear fealty. But how can one trust humanity to Crow when Tuvya rejected all peace talks and his only wish was to either subjugate or destroy the Waldenian people? When\n\n rebellion came and the forces of Renatus and Aesterwald defeated the Crow, the latter rolled on its back in submission. In turn, the forces of Renatus and Aesterwald spared the dogand allowed it to scamper off and lick its wounds. A mistake that haunts\n\nus today. Where are the Waldenian people now? Nearly all dead with few scattered about the realm. Men who wished to be free were hunted down and slaughtered after unholy forces wreaked havoc upon Vanderfell - obliterated by hell fire from cultist work.\n\nThese “protectors of humanity” did not come to the aid of men against this hell fire. Now why allow the dog to regain the reins of humanity?\n\nNow reader, you might bring up three questions. Are the Adrians not the same as the Waldenians and only wish to\n\nrule themselves? Why should we wage war on a people when we all carry the curses and sins of Iblees, is this not just a product of such? What makes the loyalists so different from the Adrians? I shall answer all these as well.\n\n1.) While both the Adrian\n\nDog and the Waldenians sought to rule themselves, the Waldenians had never tried making claim to the Orenian throne. In fact, they had pushed for talks of an alliance to answer Tuvya’s arguments of the need for a unified humanity.\n\nThe Crow is gluttonous however, and pecks at anything it finds edible. Even that of rotten flesh. Today, the Adrian Dog wishes to usurp its former master and seek the throne themselves. And the Adrian Dog will not stop there.\n\n2.) While it is true that we as mortals carry the affliction given by the fallen one, Iblees, the Adrians have surpassed any of its limits and have grasped the sins Iblees instilled in us as the norm. Something to be proud of. The Adrians side with\n\nbandits contrary to their faith and for too long all walks of life have cowered at the barbarism demonstrated by these untamed beasts. A unified front is the only answer to subduing the beast that has been created overtime.\n\n3.) Under Olivier I Ashford de Savoie, the realm of mortals has seen order and stability absent during the rule of Crow. To allow a just man to be usurped by the Adrian Dog is not only allowing a plague on to humanity, but on to all races across the land.\n\nAnd you, reader, ask why this is a plague on all? Before I continue, I admit I am not Orenian. I fight for Savoie though because should he be left alone in his just fight, we will all be next. There is a young lady I know back home who cannot fight and\n\nonly wishes to fish in peace and live modestly. A shepherd who is soon to be married to a woman born with no eyes at birth. Despite his economic status and her affliction, they seek happiness too. There are plenty more innocent people back in my home, but\n\nthe Adrian Dog is one with poor eyesight. It does not see soldier or child, elderly or woman. It sees prey. And it will rip the throats of any that is not them.\n\nRemember the Waldenians, who tried living just lives in peace but were near annihilated by the Crow. Remember the attempted genocide on Dwed by King Heinrik Carrion in the old lands of Anthos. Remember the raids you have all faced at the hands of the\n\nAdrian Dog teamed among banditry.\n\nAdrian Dog whispers ‘Mina-Mina’ to you like a dumb brain and jingles coin before you. But they will claim this back for war reparations in conquests they start against YOU.\n\nAnd we will fall one by one to the predator if we do not take a stand now. They will hide among your people disguised and take control from the inside. They assault holy men and seek blood for coin.\n\nTo those who answer this call to fight alongside me, then let me be the first to say it will be an honor to fight alongside you. The words I write are true, backed up by evidence in the history of the Adrian Dog. The enemies are snakes in the grass,\n\nand we must cut the grass to reveal their slither. They are dogs who have been disobedient for far too long and must be dealt with before they bite the hand that once fed them. They will not stop until they are the last in the realm.\n\nAnd the only way to deal with Adrian Dog is to put them down.\n \n-NY\n\n“To never to turn the back upon a foe” - Vander Code", ""),
        StaticBook("Storm Evocation", "§bHeruza", "The following is a compilation of the following books made by Heruza to save bookshelf space.\n\n1. Hydromancy\n2. Tome: Air Evoc\n\nBOOK ONE: HYDROMANCY\nWater: Seemingly the simplest of elements, and yet incredibly complex. Water is a necessity of life, needed by all living things, plants and beasts alike. Just as it is the patron of life, water can also pose as the harbringer of\n\neradication. Despite our best attempts; we are mortal. A single wave can take everything we own. A flood can contaminate food. A particularly harsh winter can be inescapable. Water contains raw power, a power that a hydromancer yearns to wield.\n\nA hydromancer's training stems from the evocation and control of water itself but not the water that we know. This water can only be found in the void and some say it is not water at all. As all evocationists know, their power comes from their ability to\n\ncontrol \"mana\", but I'll leave that topic for others to discuss. After much dedication and training, a hydromancer is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is difficult\n\nto put into words, as connecting to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained. As a mage's training progresses, connecting to the void and evoking the mana within it becomes a much simpler task. Many mages use a staff when\n\nevoking the elements, but the truth is that the staff is not necessary. I, for example, use a staff topped in mage-gold and carved from elderly jungle wood. This staff is fitting for me because of some of the properties that it posesses, and also because\n\nit has been personalized for me. The purpose of my use of a staff is to create a simple, close point for me to concentrate on and evoke water from. When the water is pulled forth, it creates a stream at the end of my staff that maintains itself midair.\n\nFrom here, I can move it, project it somewhere, or allow it to dissipate. One thing about water evocation that differs from other branches of evocation is that water can change states in our world. Novice hydromancers start by controlling water in its\n\npure liquid form. As a hydromancer becomes more skilled, they can transform the water into ice. Ice is much more suited for battle and defense than liquid water is, as it can be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, and block projectiles. I have\n\npersonally mastered a technique involving blasting an opponent with water, and then freezing them in their tracks should they be hit. Magical ice is not like that which can be found in our world; void ice does not melt from heat. To break the ice, the\n\nhydromancer must either completely lose concentration, or another mage must do something to break the ice. Water is not often formed into the vapor state, as water vapor is difficult for even the most trained evocationist to control. Water, being able to\n\nbe formed into almost any conceivable shape, is only limited by the caster's imagination and fatigue. Water can be suited for almost any purpose with proper training.\n\nBOOK TWO: TOME: AIR EVOC\nAccording to research and study, the void is a place of infinite plane of pure thought and energy surrounded by complete darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvass.\n\nHypothetically, anything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. The first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and its 'blank' concept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found. Learn\n\nto blanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to create your canvas. Wind and Air are essences to life from all around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self. With the art of air evocation, you manipulate it. Wind is\n\nunpredictable and one of the best studied branches of arcane magic. You must experience the element in its true form before you can even think about summoning it. In order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a place of high altitude and feeling the wind\n\nrush over your very body. Experience how pressure seeps through the cracks of every substance. Taste it. Feel it. Smell it. Another useful experiment is placing something in the air which can float. Watch how the wind cradles the item and gently lowers it\n\nback to the earth or carries it away. After you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; You may begin your best attempts at summoning your element from the void. Firstly, you must find a place of peace.\n\nNext, use your blank canvas to imagine air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very blood. Through combining all of this, a small amount of wind may be conjured. You may pass out a few times upon first\n\nconnection. After you have mastered basic connection, you can move onto some of the key spells in an air evocationist's arsenal. The first and most obvious is the force push. Essentialy, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one\n\nforceful push at his or her enemy. Secondly, and slightly more defensive, is the air tornado. A skilled air evocationist could create a spiraling current of wind that could keep most objects out of your sphere.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nether Star", "§bCloven", "Nether Star\n    Research notes\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      Written by Elvi\n        Terryal\n\n *A detailed drawing of the object is on this             page*\n\nWhat is the object?\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe object appears to be a type of gem, rather purplish and resembling much like a heart. According to a few people, this gem is found within a foul creature wielding three heads, most likely one of Iblee's servants or\n\npart of his undead army. Could this possibly be the heart of this creature?\nFrom observance, the gem appears to be fairly normal, aside from resembling a little bit of a heart. However, I do feel a strange yet eerie aura radicating from it. Could there\n\nbe something within the gem or is it something used to store the creature's energy in? This energy, or perhaps the gem itself, could be used within Alchemy, magic and perhaps further. Hence why I am studying this object.\n\nResearch 1#\n~~~~~~~~~\nFrom what I know, this gem is from a creature with three heads, mostly known as a 'Wither', a dark creature that is said to be in league with Iblees. This gem comes from the Wither whenever someone would defeat it.\n\nHowever, it is unsure on what this item is used for. Could it be used as an Alchemy symbol (then what would it represent? What element would it be?)? Would this be used as part of magic, either light or dark magic? Or does it dive much deeper into\n\nsomething that perhaps we do not understand. That is something I am hoping to find out during my time researching it.\nFor the time been, I shall refer to the gem as the 'NetherStar' as it would be likely that the Wither is from the Nether and the gem does\n\nvagely resembles a star from some angles.\n\n\n-Written by Elvi Terryal\n\nDate: 12th of Sun's smile 1484\n\nTheory number one\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe energy theory\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nOne of the few theories I have came up with about this gem is about a potental energy hidden within.\nNow, think about the Wither. This gem can supposedly be its heart, what keeps it\n\nalive. That energy within can be a type of life source, something that keeps the wither alive. If we can somehow extract this energy from this gem, then we may be able to use this energy for either good or bad intentions, depending on who wants to use it\n\nand why. I believe a way of extracting this supposed energy can be through the use of magic, or someone who can extract energy from things and possibly can transfer the energy from the gem into something else.\nHowever, judging that the energy is from a\n\nwither, I cannot guarentee that this energy can be used for good purposes as it is from a very dark creature.\nI am planning on asking a mage of some sorts about this theory. However, I just need to know where one is and ask. Hopefully they will  explain\n\nabout the process and whenever or not it can be possible. I suppose only time will know.\n\n- Written by Elvi Terryal\n\nDate: 11th of Grand Harvest 1485", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elves I", "§bFreyr Mantisuku", "Investigations into The ancient ones. Volume I\n\n*There is a drawing here of a seven foot tall elf clad in heavy armor and elfs lay near death around its feet its blade covered in blood and arrows sticking out from its neck and joints*\nThe scene is bloody and gory.\n\nArthur: Freyr Mantisuku\nCo-Author: Crineas Acosta\n[Forewarning: Do not confront the Ancient Ones unprepared]\n[Always Bring a Paladin or war cleric with you during hunts]\n\nA Short Introduction\n\nThe Ancient ones are elves that once lived in this land long before we arrive.Their civilisation ended long before the descendents arrived.\n\n They have now been reawakened apparently by necromancers  and roam the elven lands looking mortals to slay. The creature is near unkillable with nearly no weakness apart from the Holy magic of Xan or Tahariae.\n\nAppearance\n\nThey stand around seven foot tall clad in heavy armor and wielding two handed weapons  the armor they have is normally dark and we are yet to see what lays inside apart from an ‘elf’.\n\nThey are always hostile towards life and they are cold to the touch.\n\nBehavior\n\nThey roam the Elven lands and never out of them hunting any and all mortals to send to the grave. They are extremely hostile to living creatures and when they fight they have little care for their bodies.\n\nThey will label the descendents as ‘malieir’, which means traitor in the old elven tongue.\n\nStrengths\n\nThey are extremely resistant to all damage apart from holy, A sword into the skull will do little but make it swing at you.\n\nThe strength they have is unmatched quickly bending shields and breaking swords of their foes with it.\n\nThe armor whether by magic or form it's made of is extremely durable and able to withstand almost all projectiles and melee weapons\n\nIt seems to be impervious to arcane voidic spells, having a significant resistance for it.More investigation is needed in this area.\n\nHas Great magical power, being able to summon transportation portals and a large array of spells.\n\nWeakness.\n\nThe only known weakness is the Paladins of Xan or the War Clerics of Tahariae. In other words, holy magic.\n\nOrigins and Additional details\n\nNote: Theoretical\n\nThe Origins of the ancients ones laid in a tomb that the Elves ventured into stealing the relics from within and awaken the ancient ones . \nNote: The relics are now held by The Laureh'lin Archaeology And Artisanal Organization\n\nEntering ruins of the Ancient Ones is extremely warned against, as expeditions previously done had found hundreds of feral and hostile elves harbouring within.\n\nWe also know that the creatures are thralls of powerful necromancers but are unsure if the necromancers awoke with the ancient ones or if they are dead and the ancient ones are the last of their power.\n\nAncient Elven Guidenote.\nAnd Elven the creatures are known to speak.\n\nMalieir: traitor\nAme: Forest\nIgnere: Burn\nHileia: peace\n\nNotes:\nAny extra, Corrections or confirmations on information can be\nSent to Either Freyr, or Crineas (( samsan99, Sharkali ))\nFurther Volumes will be compiled as more information is made available.", ""),
        StaticBook("Viceroy Edict", "§bSiri", "Edict of Viceroy\n1514\n\nRecorded by Siri Ihelia\n\nBy decree of His Majesty, King Olivier de Savoie, the office of Viceroy has hereby been established. The position, along with a seat on the Privy Council, grants the Viceroy authority over all the provinces in the Reformed Kingdom of Oren, and grants\n\nthese following duties:\n\n1. The responsibility, entrusted by the King, to act as his chief liaison and representative in all provincial matters.\n\n2. The right to govern the provinces in a manner that best reflects the well-being of the Kingdom.\n\n3. The duty to ensure a loyal and law-abiding populace within the governed provinces.\n\n4. The responsibility to represent all the provinces during crucial matters of state.\n\n5. The responsibility to represent all the provinces in any foreign affair or domestic affair.\n\nReaffirming these duties, the Viceroy will have authority over the Province of Laurehlin, the Protectorate of Haelun’or, and the Ancillary of Ker’nor\n\n for an indefinite period. The office of the Viceroy is to be held by Lord Helton Chivay.\n\nSigned,\n\nHis Majesty, King Olivier de Savoie\n\nHis Excellency, Viceroy Helton Chivay\n\nAuthors notes: While Helton Chivay was appointed Viceroy for all 3 subsidiary states, he has never once wielded his power, save for one incident of a small rebellion in Haelun'or over some dispute for the position of Sohaer. One must ask themselves is non\n\naction is the correct way of governance for the elder races, or if a more active hand would have brought the mali-kinded up to the expected size of a duchy in Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Zeliek's Journal", "§bZeliek", "Zeliek's Journal§0\n§0\n§0I'm writing this journal out of personal boredom aswell as to keep track of the progess I have done not only as a Paladin but towards my own personal goal too.\n\n-------------------§0\n§0Today was somewhat of a strange day, I've strolled upon two people in conflict with a supposed murderious girl. Sadly despite my efforts to halt the conflict and help said girl. . . She died. I. . . Perhaps was a little too harsh in my\n\nAccusations and what I said to the duo that ended the girl, saying things like \"You are no better than her.\" And \"What grants you the right to shorten a life?\" I'm sadned by what I've done there. Yet what was stranger is after the male of the two followed\n\nMe and spoke with me of the situation and surprisingly, that I was noble. We exchanged names and words and in the end I learned he was becoming a Cleric. I am happy and at the same time sad. Yet in time I'm sure he will learn of Tah's nature. I do hope I-\n\nSpeak with him soon though. Hallot Belal.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 2.§0\n§0\n§0Today I've met two women who had came to me asking for information on necromancers, after a while of talking they-\n\nTold me that they themselves wished to become necromancers themselves all to resurect their dead sister and see her smile again. I told them that doing that would be meaningless and only produce a mindless corpse puppet. After a while I'm glad to say that\n\nit would seem atleast they changed their mindset and instead are now set to becoming Void mages. I still don't know if this is true, yet I'm happy to know I may have changed their path for the better, even if it was in a small way.\n\n-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 3.§0\n§0\n§0Today me and my friend Archibald found something strange in the woods, so we began to gather others to hunt said creature. Yet the sight we came to find was rather insane.\n\nA gigantic plant like creature with a large multitude of tendrils stood before us. As soon as we came a large tendril came to greet us, I somehow managed to slash at the thing and slice it in half. I then, considering the the fact we had two mages with-\n\nus, began to walk and circle the creature to draw it's attention untill I was met with a hole in my arm by the beast. I manged to heal my arm through the mists of Xan as the others dealt with it through a massive exploasion and fire. I still don't know-\n\nWhat the creature might have been though I know it is dead and I have it's head in my posession.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0Entry 4.§0\n§0\n§0Today I was met by one who needed assistence from a cleric or Paladin-\n\nIt seemed that their base was tainted by the likes of a necromancer and him and three others were wounded. I went to the place to try and clense the taint yet to no effect, sadly I do hope they get it clensed soon. Much later on I met a really nice Cleric\n\nBy the name of Meiko, she seemed to have a really livily personilty and in all honesty truly brighted my day. We had a long chat on many topics, mainly clerical and Paladin topics however. Our conversation sadly had to be cut in the middle as she had to-\n\nDepart, though I do hope I meet her again sometime soon.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 5.§0\n§0\n§0Today I had a chat with Meiko before a girl who seemed to love performing showed up-\n\nShe gave us a little show of dancing and singing. Afterwards we were met by a child covered in wounds and bruises. The terrible sight made me pitty the child, yet everything is alright as I managed to heal all of his injuries. I'm now just waiting for-\n\nMeiko to return so we may go explore lands.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0We just went on an adventure about the island and even though not much has happend she seemed to have a great time. We even seemed to had a philisophical moment where she seemed-\n\nSad by the fact her adoptive father was gone. Yet we spoke about how even though they are gone, they still live in our memories and all that. I suppose I just wait till the next time we can speak and  adventure.\n\n-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 6.§0\n§0\n§0Today me and a group of friends went off into the woods and were met by a large phoenix, we had a grand battle with it were I managed to slash off a bit of it's flesh before I was met-\n\nBy embers upon my atire, someone crashing into me and gusts of wind blowing onto me. Overall it was a terrible experience. . . Yet after that it flew off towards the city where it was delt with, or so we think. Someone had one of it's eggs which I can-\n\nonly assume hatached and became it's child.§0\n§0After a long period of time the child seemed to quickly grow to the size of it's parent before flying away somewhere random. All I am left with now are some minor burns and a piece of it's flesh. Aswell the-\n\nmemories that follow.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 7.§0\n§0\n§0Today I attended Ramza's wedding and I must say I wasn't all impressed. From what I saw someone slaped Ramza with a fish, cake rained from the skies-\n\nThere were bunnies on the red carpet and someone punched Ramza in the nose. Overall I feel this 'wedding' was more of a comedy act if anything else. Though I still am glad that Ramza and Elvi are now officaly together and I hope they stay that way happily\n\n-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 8.§0\n§0\n§0Today I was called by Sam to head to a city known as Adria, upon my arvial I fond Sam having two arrows in his shoulder and calf, after healing him with the assitence of Xan, he granted me some extreamly-\n\nSoft cloth. We parted ways afterwards and I headed to the Mali'ame city where I was met with a specter apprently attacking the city. Despite my efforts to try and free the creature from it's torment, it was taken down soon by some golden dust. I'm but sad\n\nI was unable to provide any assitence in the matter.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 9. §0\n§0\n§0Considering the recent lack of excitment in my life, I think it may be better to write this entry on the past, perhaps a way for\n\nThose that read this book in the future to understand what has occured in my life and why I have these morals. §0\n§0\n§0In the past I lived carefree with my brother, he was more of the deliquent type while I the well behaved I suppose-\n\nWe lived in a noble home the two of us and all was well untill one day we decided to go on a walk. From there a bandit came and attacked us both while still little, I was fine yet my brother was stabbed in the gut. I quickly treated his wounds but after-\n\nHe had a strange look in his eye, his fingers clutching into a fist as blood ran from his palm. I could tell he wished for revenge. I never saw him again after that, even now we haven't stayed in touch. But from that experience I now wish to be the one to\n\nGuide him back to us, him and all who are lost. It is from this that I created three self rules for myself.§0\n§0\n§01. To never kill, solve conflict without bloodshed.§0\n§0\n§02. To guide others that have fallen back onto the right path.\n\n3. To protect everyone, no matter what.§0\n§0\n§0These are the three rules I have created and perhaps the true reason I became a Paladin, to better uphold these rules.\n\n-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 10.§0\n§0\n§0I am but angered today at not the specter but myself. Today the specter returned and decided to grant us a \"Demonstration\" of our idoicy. And to my suprise, it was me.\n\nThe being shot out a golden blade into my back and I was treated by a cleric. I am not mad at the creature but myself. . . to know this being made a mockery of me not once, but twice. Afterwards I heard the being whisper into my ear \"You will die.\" I-\n\nShall be the one to make this being vanish. . . You can be sure of that.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 11.§0\n§0\n§0Recently there has been a wyren attack at the city, however it seems to have been dealt with.\n\nThis beast created a scene of slight pure chaos by all the guards and others fighting it with bows and arrows, I would assume atleast twenty or more guards were invovled. Aswell as a large number of injuried afterwards. Atleast it is gone however.\n\n-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 12.§0\n§0\n§0Been awhile since I made an entry, however today an army of undead visted the wood elf city and I helped, it was a bloodbath but in the end we won. Afterwords I had to use the mists of Xan\n\nTo heal a girl's arm, I can only hope the rest of the wounded are okay aswell.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 13.§0\n§0\n§0Today me and a group of friends went out to fight a witch within the woods, this witch has been-\n\nKnown for her dark practicing and sacraficing of animals. Once we arivied I was slashed by a bear across the chest before managing to end it with flames and a sword, from there me and another rushed towards the home and up the stairs untill they went out-\n\nAnd both of us fell downwards. A wolf then bite itself into my shoulder before we dealt with it aswell. Surprisingly after that we managed to end the witch and now we await the mina reward. I believe I was even able to see one of Xan's keepers in the-\n\nBattlefield, I but wonder who that could be.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 14.§0\n§0\n§0Today I am sad to say I have spoken with a friend known as Arelin on why she is a frost witch. When I first brought it up she-\n\nSeemed hesitent, frightend even. She then began to speak saying that she became one to be imortal, in order to escape the fear of death. Her worst fear is dying and because of that she has turned her body into one of the witches. She then questioned on-\n\nWhat I thought happends when you die. Obviously I said what most say, \"I believe there is a life of death, one never just stops existing, they but are sent to the creator when they die.\" I am unsure of weither or not that stayed in her mind though-\n\nStrangely after speaking with them about it, they offer me a favor. So I gave it. . . \"My favor is even if your kin order you to harm others. My wish is but that you not kill a soul.\" Perhaps I was asking too much of a dark being. . . Though part of me-\n\nWishes they she will keep the promise. Not for my own stastfaction but for her own sake. As a friend I just don't want to see her fear consume her and turn her into a murderer. No one. . . No one should ever be forced to kill another.\n\n-------------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 15.§0\n§0\n§0Today was a rather eventfull day, Meiko returned and learned that I actually loved her from Ramza. . . The emberassment she must have felt was probably too much though when she exited the tavern with\n\nRamza she kissed me upon the lips. This. . . Shocked me to say the least but Meiko thought of it as a wrong thing to do, so I quickly went to comfort her. Now it would seem that me and Meiko are begining to start dating. Though at the same time I still-\n\nHave my duties to work on. . . The ancient elves, Undru, frost witches and Arelin. . . And recently Necromancers. Dispite my feelings to Meiko my own duties come first, otherwise what kind of man am I that neglates his work and his own self goals. I can-\n\nOnly pray that I shall get through these dark times.§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Theorem of Wisom", "§bAerxuis", "Theorem of Wisdom\nBy Godwein Stafyr\nCopied By Aerx\nWhat is wisdom?\n        Wisdom is not easy to define, likely similar to eternity. Every person has its own views of wisdom. To elaborate this further, a row of examples.\n        Is knowledge\n\nwisdom? Perhaps.\n        Is knowing the right thing to do wisdom? Perhaps.\n        Is doing something good wisdom? Perhaps.\n        Is learning wisdom? Perhaps.\n      \nAs aforementioned you cannot simply define wisdom.\n\nWisdom is a multitude, colorful, differently shaped. Wisdom can and does exist in many of us. To different degrees, in different shapes. A forester can have the wisdom of knowing how to treat his plants and trees properly, when to grow what to\n\nreach the best result. As can the farmer. A sorcerer or wizard can know a lot about the divine art of magic and has through this his very own wisdom.\n        Still, one would say, that in these example wisdom turns out to be rather knowledge, which\n\nis only partially right, if it’s right at all.\n         Wisdom requires more than simply having knowledge. Wisdom requires understanding the spirit, the being, the living and many things more. The inner peace and silence may bring wisdom.\n\nOn the other side, a warrior may achieve a new level of combat by finding his inner stability in combat. To be calm in the face of the storm and evil.\n        As we now scratch the evil, the darkness, I wish to bring in a small part of my very own\n\nopinion. Wisdom doesn’t exist in people who are simply evil and work for their very own profit. Wisdom requires selflessness as well.\n        You may now think I am taking the side of the good here, solely. It is right. I do align myself to the\n\ngood and the light, but must say, that I may be completely wrong with my statement about wisdom and the evilness here. Perhaps the other side may have their own kind of wisdom, being evil as it is.\n        Is it wisdom to write a book about\n\nwisdom? No.\n        Is it wisdom to explain what wisdom can be? Perhaps.\n      \nWhy perhaps? Because wisdom is wisdom. Colorful and different. Not definable. That is wisdom.", ""),
