        StaticBook("Allahs Creation", "§bFaiz Ibn Qhuhafah", "The first creations of Allah - a book by Faiz Ibn Qhuhafah. A shortened version of the greater scripts by the first prophet.\n\nThe great allah was as the first prophet stated in his first scripts not born into the world. Allah have neither mother nor father as Allah has always been in this world. Allah was always and will always be but only allah have always been.\n\nAllah was surrounded by darkness with him being the only light in the darkness - the only light that had ever been. In Allahs infinite wisdom he decided to create other lights in the world. He then decided to create the heavens and earth in his wisdom.\n\nA day passed as Allah decided that his creation had to be seperated from himself as to not overshadow it. He created the sky above the earth beneath the heaven deciding this too was fit to be in the world he made it stay.\n\nWhen Allah looked down on his creation from heaven he was dismayed by the lack of dry land and by his grace the land was created seperating the hard from the wet forming continents on the great earth.\n\nIn the wisdom of Allahs mind the world lacked diversity and he created the night sky with stars and moon and the day with the sun shining brightly on earth creating a great light but still insignificant compared to the light of Allah.\n\nYet the beauty he had created was not enough for the mighty Allah. He breathed at a sea as a mighty fountain erupted with fishes and other seacreatures swimming out by the will of Allah. With the seacreatures he made the birds to sing for him as pleased.\n\nThe next day Allah thought of the bare dirt that covered the planet and decided in his infinite wisdom to breathe life into dirt creating what is known today as animals. Looking into the water he saw his own reflection and decided to create man.\n\nMan was by Allahs divine will created in the image of Allah. Over all the animals man should stand and by Allahs will the first of man was named Âdam for that was the will of allah.\n\nBy his divine grace Allah decided that âdam should name all the animals as Allah rested on the seventh day after he had started the creation. Allah rested for as was his will that noone should work if he had not the full energy to do so.\n\nAllah had degreed peace in his realm and that all should bow to the pinacle of his creation - man. Not all his servants was willing to do this as ïblis decided that he was above protasting to another beign,\n\nThis was directly defying the will of Allah and should have been punished by death but in his eternal mercy Allah decided to let ïblis live for the price of banishment to watch all other souls banished from his realm.\n\nïblis was vengefull after his banishment and decided to act revenge. Revenge was towards the one he was supposed to bow to - man.\n\nIn the mean time god had in his wisdom granted Ädam a companion Hawwâ was her name and she was the first woman to be created by Allahs mercy. Formed by a rib taken from Adam she was formed but still under the first creation Ädam.\n\nThe ïblis saw the weakness in the woman as he transformed into a snake and snook into the garden and up into one of Allahs holy trees. ïblis gazed upon Ädam and Hawwâ for days untill he decieded that it was time to enact revenge.\n\nHawwâ walked past the tree as ïblis disguised as a snake spoke to her. He tempted her to eat the fruit of the tree and even though god had told her not to the ïblis was as manipulative as his form and she ended up eating the fruit.\n\nFurious god saw as the ïblis made her eat the fruit and he decended from his heavenly throne. The light was so strong that ïblis fled and was hurt for eternity and to this day the light can still be seen when igniting the descendants of the trees that\n\nwitnessed the greatness of Allahs descendence. Allah opened his mouth as his heavenly voice ran across the world of his banishment of Hawwâ and Adam to the mortal and deadly world beyond his realm. now they are mortal forever.\nSubhanallah.", ""),
