ame, they created walls that were 50 meters in height over night.\n\nDuring Inadgo’s shock, Iblees stabbed Inadgo in the heart, ending the corrupt king’s life.\n*A drawing of Inadgo being stabbed brutally is here. It looks as though the artist put a little bit too much detail into it.* \nщ (*ㅇ△ Φ☆)ノ\n私は何を見たのですか？\n\nThey even lost their digestive systems. They were only driven by three things: gold, booze, and the extermination of all other races, especially humans. Most ranged in height at around fifteen meters.\n\nAll dwarves: Male and female, old and young, short and not as short, began to grow in epic proportions. But at a cost. They lost all of their reproductive organs and lost their ability to think freely.\n\n*A drawing of Iblees with big Kawaii eyes is talking to a large fat dwarf, supposedly Inadgo.*\nＯ(≧∇≦)Ｏ\nDESU DESU DESU DESU DESU!\n\nIn exchange, Inadgo had to give up his soul to Iblees when he died. Inadgo, being the greedy heretic dwarf he was, accepted without hesitation. So Iblees conjured a curse.\n\nThe Grand King Inadgo Stormhammer of the Dwarves made a pact with Iblees, the Fallen One. As part of their heretical plan, Iblees would give the Kingdom of Urugan an unstoppable army that would destroy his enemies (all of the other nations).\n\nThe dread that was a life under their rule…The humiliation of being caged like birds. On that day, Humanity remembered the terror of being ruled by them.\n\nIt was 107 years ago in the year 1450 when they first gave rise. \n｡゜(｀Д´)゜｡\n\n[OOC DISCLAIMER: This is based off the Manga/Anime Attack on Titan. Any likeness to IRL people is completely coincidental. This is for IC propaganda only. Spuller does NOT really make deals with Iblees.]\n\n*A picture of a young Heinrik Carrion is seen slaying many Giant Dwarves on the cover of the book. Heinrik appears very kawaii desu with big bright eyes. These eyes appear strong though, showing he is major badassuru!*\n\n“Attack on Dwarfu!” \nThe Manga!\n Issue #1\nBy Raigeki Kato", ""),
        StaticBook("Peace", "§bJack", "Peace is a state of mind. A achievement of the soul at comfort within its own body, content with the world around them.\n\nBut the mortal races is bound by the desires of flesh and the materialistic world. Nothing is ever enough.\n\nThe world is unfair, people dont always get what they want. But it also makes us mortal. We fight for survival, we live for the future. \nPeace will never come. Because in your attempts to be content, you will hurt someone else in the process", ""),
        StaticBook("Humble Beginning", "§bShayne789", "17th of Snow's Maiden\n1449\n\nSo far in my year of serving my liege Vectis Vekon, I've fought rebels, fought Scourge, and have learned many new things. On thing in particular would be how to evoke the elements.\n\nMy interest began when I discovered the books in the castle library. From there, I read and read, and I discovered that with enough meditation, one can connect with the Void. And thus I did. After months of thought, and reading, I did it.\n\nWe were hiding in the dungeons, William and I. We heard a dragon across the river, and sought cover. It was there in the dark, dank dungeons that I cast out all thoughts, and meditated on the Void. I felt it, and I cried. It was amazing. I felt the\n\nfingers of the Void caressing me, as if I were its child. From there on I know I was to be an arcanist. Not some lowly servant. Since then I concentrated, and tried to evoke, and for some time I had no success.\n\nThen, one day, whilst everyone was chattering, I sat at the fire, gazing into the flames. My thoughts once more wandered to the Void, as if I was called to it. I once again tried to evoke fire, and a flame appeared in my hand.\n\nMy liege Vectis looked to me in surprise. The flame dissapated, and I fell back exhausted. He named me Court Mage there and then, and since that day I wore the silver pauldrons of the Vekonic uniform. I am proud of my\n\nsuccess, and am happy to serve my liege who took me in from the cold, wet outside, and into a home of warmth, and love. Long live the Vekons!\n\n-Rory Bishop", ""),
        StaticBook("a", "§bJack", "Malin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forest of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless,\n\nhe was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of the first men. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves. \n\nSoon the first Man and Woman created by\n\nGod departed Aegis  and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their Creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken with grief at the loss of their parents, seeking to fill the chasm of\n\nemotion inside them they began to create civilization. \n\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither the valour not the charisma of their forefathers, they did carry their forefathers look and traits. The Elves with\n\nMalin at their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\n\nAt this time, Malin, Urguan, Krug and Horen were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan had red. They were all close companions, friends and had much\n\nlove for each other and each others people. Urguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethern. \n\nKrug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and\n\nstrength against the harsh enviroment of Aegis. And Horen married his Queen Julia, as they both began building the first squalid huts and villages in the valleys, giving rise to humanity. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace.\n\nHoren I was encouraged by the Aenguls Tession and Artifai to write down the Holy Scrolls, or the Scrolls of Relevation, as it was the Creator’s will to see the Faith of the One God spread throughout the lands. \nHoren I was encouraged by the\n\nAenguls Tession and Artifai to write down the Holy Scrolls, or the Scrolls of Relevation, as it was the Creator’s will to see the Faith of the One God spread throughout the lands. \n\nUntil the day where one of the great Daemons,\n\n great worshipers and squalid protectors of the Void, kin spirits to the Aengul, defected. Iblees, who was once the greatest of all of Gods worshippers was cast down into the mortal world, he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever.\n\nHe came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things delicate, he was quickly befriend by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\n\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great Gods plan to test the descendants Of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil\n\n in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient History", "§bJack", "Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\n\nIbleeses soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of Skeletons and Zombies burst into flames and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by The Aengul and Daemon.\n\n A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparition stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shied down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be\n\nkilled, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment. \n\nBut,\n\nBefore they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time.\n\n\"You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls that inhabit it.\n\nMalin, I curse you with sterility, you and your kin shall forever lack the children they need. May your forest halls forever be silent, and your hearts heavy with sadness.\n\nUrguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you,\n\n you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in the deep underground of the earth, your hunger never satisfied.\n\nHoren, you wish immortality? I will curse you with the opposite,early death for you and your kin. You shall age quickly and die before you experience the fruits of your useless labour.\n\nAnd you Krug, the most hated of\n\nThe Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your lust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.\"\n\nAs soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Ibleeses mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n\"There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\n\nMalinor, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\n\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the\n\nSeven Skies. \n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.\n\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons\n\ndisappeared into thin wisps in the air.\n\nVolume IV Ancient History", ""),
        StaticBook("*A Tablet*", "§bSprat", "*A worn slab of stone lay before you in the wall, reading as follows.* \n\nH\n\nO", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient History", "§bJack", "In the beginning, there was nothing. Just the Grey Void. But all that changed when a spark of light bursted forth, creating disparity. Dark and light both came about, wrought forth by actions of the Creator\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty\n\nof the Creator, the One and only. The merciful Creator of the Seven Skies. With his intent,  and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. THe rolling seas, proud mountains and vast\n\nlandscapes, all in a second, created by God. \n\nThe first mortal being created was man. This man was sculpted with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the ther immortal beings to see. The Aengul and the\n\nDaemon, the two spirits created before the mortal beingsand before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existence into the hollow shell\n\nand the Man lived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all Aegis, the same spot where the Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple\n\nbeings could not talk, nor did they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of\n\nAegis.\n\nVolume I of Ancient History", ""),
        StaticBook("To Theodoric", "§bShady_Tales", "Dear Theodoric,\n\nI pray that your recovery is going well. Haven't seen a beating as bad as yours since\nMarcus was oathed two years ago. Initiation does that. As I've told you before I am most proud of you and you've finally proven yourself to become a\n\nbrother. Keep up the good work. Inside this chest is a golden sword. Use it if you ever go on trips to slay undead beasts. \n\nDeus Magnus,\nHoly Ser Raigeki Kato", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient History", "§bJack", "To Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content. Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to occupy\n\nbarren forests. \n\nTo Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguans greed failed him.\n\nHoren, was anxious he would not live long enough to see\n\n his city completed and his lands increased, he did not know he had the gift of immortality and was tricked by Iblees. He thought he needed more time, and Iblees struck the cord and promised immortality.\n\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury. \nThe whole world witnessed Iblees’s transformation into a hideous\n\nbeast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals\n\n fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand infront of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood infront of the apparation.\n\nIn Iblees’s right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed\n\ncharged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury,\n\n flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful\n\nwere the arms that carried Krugs Axe and strong was Horens heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malins sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor thirty years The Descendants\n\n fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’s mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Iblees’s armys grew.  It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis,\n\nthe brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast.\n\nUrguan grew greedy, he fought valorously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. Horen was too ambitious, too weak of a leader, many of his people\n\nfought for Iblees and many of them died of recklessness. The Holy Scrolls too, were lost in the sea of time.\n\nIt seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and The Descendents weakened. \nUntil one day\n\nVolume III Ancient History", ""),
        StaticBook("Urgent note", "§bVarstivus", "To Gestahl Vonschlichten,\nWe need to speak, immediatly. I have recieved a document from my old Master, Ambros.\nIt spells the ressurection of the Mage's College and order. By the number of people that have signed, it is certain.\n\nI would consider it to be a top priority to get them to move from Wyverwyn hold to Dul' Barad Citadel. We cannot let this chance pass us by.\n\n-Varstivus, Battlemage, Master Mage, Minister of Alchemy, and Delver Artificer", ""),
        StaticBook("AoD Manga #1", "§bthanndreli", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe End!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~KONBONWA! \nSilly Gaijin, you read book backwards! Easterner race is master race! See next issue soon! To be continued…\n\n*A drawing is on this page of a derpy looking drunk dwarf at heights of over fifty meters. It lacks skin, showing the muscles on the behemoth.*\n｡゜(｀Д´)゜｡\nドワーフ異端は、私たちすべてを殺す！\n\nMankind had softened up, believing they were simply a myth. But when Young, charming Heinrik Carrion looked up to the top of the fifty meter wall, A dwarf’s head popped up. And mankind remembered who they were ruled by.\n\n*A picture of orcs being eaten by Giant Dwarves is here. Most grotesque!*\n(ノಠ益ಠ)ノ\nオークは私の親友だった！\n\nWall Malin fell in just a few days and the Abresi Civilization became further encroached by the Giant Dwarves. Then there was a 107 years of peace with no sight of the Giant Dwarves.\n\nThe orcs enthusiastically went to Wall Malin but little did the ruling Dark Elves know that the orcs would open up the gates of Wall Malin to fight the Giant Dwarves, which lead to the demise of their race.\n\n*A drawing of the Abresian Civilization is here. The historical city is at the middle surrounded by Wall Horen. The other walls surround the historical city, creating layers.*\n\nファンシー！\n＼(☆o◎)／\n\nThese walls circled around their respective civilizations. Up until the Dark elves took control of Wall Horen. They pushed the humans into Wall Krug and told the orcs that there was more “glomp” with the giant dwarves in Wall Malin.\n\nThe people of Abresi created three walls: Wall Malin was the outer wall, Wall Krug was in the middle, and at the center, there was Wall Horen.\n\nNo one knows how they were created. This city was and still is known as Abresi, though now it was much bigger to encompass all of Anthos’ survivors.\n\nHe sent forth the giant dwarves, wiping out the lands of the elves, orcs, and humans. Only one city stood firm. Having had time before the giant dwarves came, they created walls that were 50 meters in height over night.\n\nDuring Inadgo’s shock, Iblees stabbed Inadgo in the heart, ending the corrupt king’s life.\n*A drawing of Inadgo being stabbed brutally is here. It looks as though the artist put a little bit too much detail into it.* \nщ (*ㅇ△ Φ☆)ノ\n私は何を見たのですか？\n\nThey even lost their digestive systems. They were only driven by three things: gold, booze, and the extermination of all other races, especially humans. Most ranged in height at around fifteen meters.\n\nAll dwarves: Male and female, old and young, short and not as short, began to grow in epic proportions. But at a cost. They lost all of their reproductive organs and lost their ability to think freely.\n\n*A drawing of Iblees with big Kawaii eyes is talking to a large fat dwarf, supposedly Inadgo.*\nＯ(≧∇≦)Ｏ\nDESU DESU DESU DESU DESU!\n\nIn exchange, Inadgo had to give up his soul to Iblees when he died. Inadgo, being the greedy heretic dwarf he was, accepted without hesitation. So Iblees conjured a curse.\n\nThe Grand King Inadgo Stormhammer of the Dwarves made a pact with Iblees, the Fallen One. As part of their heretical plan, Iblees would give the Kingdom of Urugan an unstoppable army that would destroy his enemies (all of the other nations).\n\nThe dread that was a life under their rule…The humiliation of being caged like birds. On that day, Humanity remembered the terror of being ruled by them.\n\nIt was 107 years ago in the year 1450 when they first gave rise. \n｡゜(｀Д´)゜｡\n\n[OOC DISCLAIMER: This is based off the Manga/Anime Attack on Titan. Any likeness to IRL people is completely coincidental. This is for IC propaganda only. Spuller does NOT really make deals with Iblees.]\n\n*A picture of a young Heinrik Carrion is seen slaying many Giant Dwarves on the cover of the book. Heinrik appears very kawaii desu with big bright eyes. These eyes appear strong though, showing he is major badassuru!*\n\n“Attack on Dwarfu!” \nThe Manga!\n Issue #1\nBy Raigeki Kato", ""),
        StaticBook("Phoenix Reb. II", "§bJosef and Kernith Timothee", "A History\n         of the\n   Phoenix Rebellion\n\n      Vol. II of II\n\n\n\n\n\nJosef and Kernith Timothee\n\nKing Enor somehow became aware of rising opposition to his rule. It is still unknown if he was tipped off by someone who overheard the plans of the Revolution, perhaps when the revolutionaries excitedly discussed their goals on the White Road.\n\nThere were various times when the Revolutionaries were overheard, once by the Orcish Rex. Perhaps one of the revolutionaries betrayed the others and told the King directly. At any rate, he decided that the best decision for him and for the nation of Oren\n\nwas to step down as King and pass on the crown. It was his chosen successor that drew a considerable amount of controversy – the leader of the Teutonic Order, Gaius Marius.\n\nEnor claimed that Marius was a strong ruler who would be able to counter the Undead threat and save Oren. The Black Cross would now be used to protect Galahar and the other scattered towns that composed the nation. The Phoenix Revolution was outraged.\n\nAs the Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order, Marius had been in direct opposition to Oren in the past and had invaded Al’Khazar several times. The revolutionaries declared him an unfit ruler who was an enemy of Oren,\n\nwhich at this point had been reduced almost solely to the feudal town of Galahar. Others welcomed Marius as the King of Oren, who would be able to defeat the Undead and restore Oren to former glory. The Humans were more than ever\n\n at this point as to who they thought should lead Oren. Enor still retained support, as did Marius, but so did the Revolution and other popular figures. The Phoenix Revolution agreed to listen to Marius, but he was unable to convince them that he would\n\n rule in Orens best interests during a series of meetings in Galahar.\n\nThe revolutionaries had many reasons why they did not want Marius as their new king. The main argument was that as the Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order Marius\n\nhad marched on Al’Khazar and the Kingdom of Oren in the past, proving that he was an enemy of the nation. Others declared that for Enor to give up the throne so easily proved there was some sort of agreement between them,\n\nand the fact that Enor had lost the support of the people meant that anyone he willingly gave the crown to should be treated with suspicion. Others said that the Black Cross was a military organization, and Marius was nothing more than a military leader\n\nwho was not fit to be king. At this point, there was not even agreement among the revolutionaries about what to do next. Some wanted to end the Revolution and accept Marius as their new king, while others wanted to overthrow him as well\n\nfor reasons mentioned, with a long range of opinions in between. There was enough support among the revolutionaries that an agreement was made to resort to drastic action. The revolutionaries hooded themselves\n\nand seized the fort in Galahar. With the city effectively in the hands of the revolutionaries, they could easily demand that their voices be heard. At this point, Marius officially held the crown of Oren, but Tarus retained the support of the Revolution.\n\nWith Galahar effectively under the control of Tarus and the Revolution and Oren under the control of Marius, an agreement had to be reached. Talks were held in the fort between the Phoenix Revolution, the Teutonic Order and Ascended.\n\nA few things were decided.\n\nOriginally, the decision was for Marius and Tarus to rule Oren as a biumvirate. Features of the decision included that citizens of both halves of the kingdom had to respect each other,\n\nboth sides would assist each other militarily, neutrality was to be upheld in the event the Dwarves and Orcs went to war and Zibaen Vivyaen was declared the emissary between the two halves of Oren. This decision meant that both those who supported\n\nTarus and those who supported Marius would have their opinions heard, and those who wanted peace would also be appealed to. Tarus would rule from Galahar and have control over the western lands. Marius’ capital would be Konigsberg,\n\nand would rule the eastern lands that were held by the Teutonic Order. However, it quickly became apparent that this arrangement would not last, and so the Realm of Hanseti was formed by Marius and the Kingdom of Renatus by Tarus.\n\nThe dissolution of Oren and the creation of Renatus and Hanseti is commonly thought to be the end of the Revolution. The revolutionaries had gotten what they wanted, a new form of government. The former king had avoided bloodshed.\n\nThere were more pressing issues to deal with, such as bolstering the defenses of the cities against potential threats from other nations and the Undead. New systems and institutions had to be created in both new nations. Of course, the effects\n\nof the Phoenix Revolution would be felt for years to come. Soon after the creation of the nations, Enor Sheffield and Dawn Perea declared that the peaceful nation of Salvus created. With this, there were three Human nations\n\nspread throughout Aegis. With the Human population split, it has been argued that the defenses of Galahar were far less than they could have been. Although Galahar was never officially conquered by the Undead, it was abandoned after being tainted,\n\n and it can be argued that with no city on the King’s Road to stop further aggression it was then only a matter of time before Kal'Urguan fell, the Orcs were attacked and Laurelin burned. In Asulon, the three human nations conducted relations\n\n best described as volatile, with war and distrust common. Renatus was frequently attacked by Hanseti and allies, before deals were arranged to stop the constant violence. Salvus came under assault soon afterwards, eventually\n\nsuccumbing to the constant barrage. When Godfrey I arrived in Arethor, he declared his intentions to be a consolidation of all Human nations. Seventis, a nation initially established as an alternative to the constant in-fighting\n\nof the other Human nations, was struck with Plague and annexed by Renatus. Salvus was conquered through war. Facing overwhelming military might Hanseti agreed to submit rather quietly, hoping to avoid the destruction Solace had faced.\n\nWhat would the world be like, had those revolutionaries never sought to overthrow King Enor? Had Al’Khazar not fallen to the Undead, would the great distrust of Enor have been bolstered when he was in the Nether for so long?\n\nWhat if he had not given the crown to Marius, prompting fighting and the need for two nations? Had Salvus never been created, would Renatus and Hanseti have been locked in war in Asulon with no third nation to help tip the balance?\n\nDid Dawn Perea have to die at the hands of a mob screaming for the blood of the witch? Nothing is certain.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elves", "Minuscule_Evil", "The Ancient Elves\n\n§§       by, Aedan\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nOnce upon a time, long before the beginning of written history, the lands of the wilderness were inhabited by a single race: The Ancient Elves. This race was the first to love in the lands of Aegis.\n\nThey built incredible structures in the lands of the Niben bay, and its surroundings.\n\nThe Niben bay was a large body of water lying in the Niben Basin, largely east of the city of Hawkhaven. It lies across the Niben River, splitting it into two parts, and so is technically a lake rather than a bay.\n\nThe Niben was once occupied by their capital: Garlas Malathar, also known as Nirn Weye vas Cyrod: The White Gold City.\n\nThis city was, according to the ancient books, the biggest capital in Aegis. The city was filled with complex tunnels and districts with different ambience.\n\nThey say you could feel one with the city, it was filled with statues of nature, exotic birds and wonderful animals… including Dragons…\n\nThe Ancient Elves learned how to befriend a Dragon, instead of taming them like most races did. They knew that friendship was stronger than any force in the world.\n\nThese Dragons shared their knowledge with them, they showed them the basics of energy manipulation that are still used now-a-days.\n\nThey soon found how to store energy in crystals and use them for many things. They used them to power their entire civilization, giving power and light to their cities.\n\nOne day, a new Dragonlord took power of the empire. His name was Akron. He was foolish and always wished to have more power. He hated other races and considered them inferior. He soon tried to power stronger crystals for war.\n\nThe Dragons refused and prevented him from doing so.\n\nAkron then called upon the forces of Iblees to drain the dragons’ power. The dragons, foreseeing their end, created the varla stone and powered it with The Dragonfires, sealing the gates to The Nether, and killing themselves…\n\nSome dragons remained as statues, petrified, and waiting to be awakened. They will wake up when the right time comes.\n\nAfter the beginning of the First Era, Akron began to damage nature and attempted to enslave other races. This marked the beginning of the Great War which lasted decades.\n\nAkron was finally defeated. To the fall of their Empire, humans took the power of the crystals.\n\nTheir power turned them blind and foolish. They began to kill all survivors of the Ancient Elves and burned their cities to the ground. Some of the managed to escape and survived.\n\nMany kings tried to restore their old glory but failed. Without the power of the Dragonfires, they weren’t able to do such thing.\n\nThey say that if you look closely to the sunrise, you can still see the ruins of Garlas Malathar, waiting to be discovered, and raised once again…", ""),
        StaticBook("Ghorash", "§bThurak'Yar", "`... -n Uruk by the name of Ghorash. Stumbling into my blarg, she pleaded for my help. No Feuruk would find a mate as a cripple, and without her arm there was no hope for the youngest of her cubs. Reluctantly, and without promise, I agreed to the attempt.\n\nHer own limb had been lost in the klomp, so I improvised with that of a dead Feuruk I’d preserved from last moon. Despite my doubts, with the aid of Akezo the torn flesh of the woman stitched and fused back together; accepting the new limb no doubt\n\nwith thanks to the prompting of the well-meaning spirit. The attachment was simple, however several more precise blessings were required to aid Ghorash in her finer motor controls.\nUnfortunately, I forgot my limits. Nothing may last forever,\n\nand to change and warp flesh is to take control of the fate of nature. The blessing Akezo gave was only temporary, and weeks later the limb grew fetid, and the Feuruk died.", ""),
        StaticBook("Navitas I", "§b[Child] Silus Hightower", "The Book of Nativitas\n\nThere were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either\n\n but it would be the only way to explain the existence of such a Deity in contrast to the emptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of the Seven Skys. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created.\n\nAll he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\n\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? Well, that is for us to speculate.\n\nThough I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and how clean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see.\n\nThe Aengul and the Daemon, the two spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and the Man lived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands.\n\n God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings could not talk, nor did they know much about the World. They roamed the world,\n\n enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\n\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis\n\n fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\n\nWe do not know how they fathered sons and how their lines continued but perhaps God created a partner for each Son to continue their lines? Soon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis\n\nand climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken with grief at the loss of their parents,\n\n seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\n\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour,\n\nthey did carry their forefathers looks and traits. The Elves with Malin at their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue\n\nand began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\n\nAt this time, Malin, Urguan, Krug and Horen were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build\n\nMalin had blonde hair and Urguan had red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for each other and each others people.\n\nUrguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of Aegis, and Horen began building\n\nthe first squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace. Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the Void, kin spirits to the Aengul, defected.\n\nIblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man.\n\n A gentle being who loved things delicate, he was quickly befriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\n\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's plan to test the descendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created,\n\n still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\n\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children.\n\nHe promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content. Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to occupy the barren forests.\n\nTo Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him.\n\nHoren, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased. He needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality.\n\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire.\n\n All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror.\n\nIn Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed,\n\nbecoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted.\n\nAnd Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis\n\n Malin’s sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor the thirty years the Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess\n\nThe dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Iblees’ armys grew.\n\nIt was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred.\n\nWoe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew greedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground.\n\nMalin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers.\n\nAn army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east\n\nIblees’ soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon.\n\nA robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before Iblees,\n\nknowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment.\n\nBut..\nBefore they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time.\n\n\n“You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last?\n\n I have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls that inhabit it.\n\nMalin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in\n\nthe distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of your own. Even you have done my work, if you realize it or not.\n\nUrguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you,\n\nHoren, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and die before you ever taste the fruits of your pointless labors.\n\nAnd you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder!\n\nYour lust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.”", ""),
        StaticBook("Great Collapse", "§bBazian Grandaxe", "The Great Collapse\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBazian Grandaxe\n\nIn my findings through various old texts of dwarven and non- dwarven nature, I have successfully abridged the forgotten time before King Simmpa to the time of his reign. To the best of my knowlage, there are no living dwarves\n\nhat have survived through the days before King Simmpa. To this account, my findings will be based of the old texts.\nAs you all well know, the reign of King Simmpa came into being in the most unknown circumstances.\n\nThat which you do not know is the event that took place before King Simmpa came into power, an even of most devious and dishonorable context. Let it be known, that this horrific event, forgotten, will be called, \"The Great Collapse.\"\n\nThe times before the Great Collapse where of a king named Thorgarn's reign. For what I have read so far, his reign was nothing out of the ordinary. It was an uneventful reign, which the only interesting part that I could find was some mess\n\nabout subterranean potatoes that where found. It was only until I found this journal that gave me the most shock. This old, broken journal has but a few legible pages (As most old literature had)  but it had the most revealing facts amongst these pages.\n\nI will share the legible pieces of that journal with you and let you cast judgement upon them before I depict my own.\n\"Something ov this day was off. I cannae feel the the hard hitting anvils amongst the stone. As I hit the stone with my pick,\n\nshe shook in fear, a sort of fear not dawned by natural causes…\n…mines shake. Our crew ascends the tunnels as we do when the stone shakes with anger. The crew leader takes our headcount before we enter the main hall.\n\nThe ascent was strange, the stone shook even stronger which did not make sense. We where farther away from it's hammer crashing on an anvil heart. How could such a quake intensify, such a precise hit that it felt as if the forge god Yemkar was hard at\n\nwork...\n…adness, everywhere! The iron-born protectors of the king where slaughtering the crafting and elder dwarves alike. They burn our works, dwarven books cast into the fiery magma of the freshly chiseled moat of the king's subterranean castle.\n\nMe closest kin 'n I have taken refuge with the clans, Goldhand and Frostbeard, 'n the forests outside Kal'Urgu…\n…must be on the move, no more time. Let it be known on this day that Thorgarn is no king of dwarves.‍ Urguan‍ be with us al…\"\n\nAlbeit, it was broken with missing sections, it gives us insight. To my own discontent, I was unable to deuce the clan of which Thorgarn belonged to. For this, his dishonorable kin have been sharing their burden with the rest of us,\n\nwhether they realize it or not. Regardless, much history was lost in the Great Collapse as well as the throne. Until, of course, King Simmpa rallied the dwarves back to Kal'Urguan, once again making it a haven for all dwarven kind.\n\nAs I read the last of this dusty, broken diary, I fear as our past may be forever lost. Let us never forget the deeds of Thorgarn. For when the day comes that the clan of the dishonorable be brought to the light\n\nof Yemkar's glowing anvil, may they answer for every life lost at the hands of this slaughterer of kin!\nMay we be ever knowing, through the knowledge of Ogradhad, Bazian Grandaxe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Laurelin's Story", "§bHigh Prince Native", "High Prince Native\n        and the\n   Story of Laurelin\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nHigh Prince Native\n\nA powerful Arch Druid from one of Malinor's eldest cities in the first age came to Aegis to help the Monks of The cloud Temple and a few surviving families at the coming of the Second Age. An aspirational wood-elf refereed to as \"Native\"\n\nwas among a surviving colony of wood-elves during this time and he sought to use his knowledge of creating homes within treetops to protect those who were hoped to return to their soulstones at the Aegis Temple after the great war.\n\nThe wood-elf sought the Druid, and found him near the cobblestone spires to the west of the Aegis Temple. They set off on foot to a mountain gorge he had come across that would act as a natural barrier to potential foe's. Once they arrived,\n\nthe Druid wandered around in the valley reaching into a pouch on his hip every so often and scratching his head before dropping a seed. He showed Native the seeds within the pouch and they had tiny, intricate vines woven around them -\n\n with a shine very similar to glow stone. Whilst Native's guild of builders were creating the cities wall and pathways, the old druid continued to walk along and casually drop the seeds in areas with his gnarled crook in-hand. In a matter of moments,\n\ntrees began to grow exponentially! It seemed as though the tree's grew faster the taller they got and soon the canopy raised hundreds of feet above them. A wonderful sight, the leaves sprung out of the branches with a burst of the similar glowstone glow.\n\nBits of dust swirled down from the tree tops and faded away as they neared the forest floor.\nThere was still however, a large clearing in the center of the grove. \"This of course is for the Mother Tree\" The druid exclaimed.\n\nHe then grabbed a bit of parchment from his satchel and looked over at me reassuringly. The Arch Druid walked to the center of the clearing, and began to cast a powerful spell upon one of the seeds. Leaves suddenly whirled around him for a short moment\n\nand fell to the ground. The tree's trunk sprouted around him, and he was no longer in view. Native was rather frightened when he saw this, hoping the druid hadn't casted the spell incorrectly. As The Mother Tree grew to its final height,\n\nhe saw a small opening halfway up the tree. Low and behold, the Arch Druid stood in the opening proclaiming \"This is where a stone alter shall lay\".\n\nOnce the rest of the smaller tree's were done growing, The builders guild & Native climbed up the trees with packs of wooden planks and began setting down the first few platforms. In time, Laurelin had become one\n\nof the Finest Cities of Malinor and to think it had all begun with just a pouch of seeds and a pinch of Druid Magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Research I", "§bArchmage Crumena", "Fourth of the Sun's Smile, 1497\nCrumena Ilwindior \n\nAn extreme oddity this is. The transporting closets, whatever they are, are beyond mind boggling. Elindor and myself sat down and attempted to unravel the enchantments\n\n\nthat create them. It is safe to say we were unsuccessful. By the title of Rasmot it is no surprise that this entire compound would be so sporadic and deranged. Although everything, even the tiles, are imbued with magics that have never\n\n\nto the likes of myself or even Elindor. For the transports we are still questionable of them. Possibly they have another purpose? Is it possibly some side effects occur from usage? I still recall the first time we used the closets. It\n\n\nto another one in the same closest. Both Elindor and myself felt a daunting pain in our stomachs. While the feeling has passed whenever I use the transporters it does make me wonder. What if on the first attempt Rasmot’s\n\n\nfrom the both of us?", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegis Destroyed", "§bUnknown", "The Destruction\n        of Aegis\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nUnknown\n\nThe Falling of Our World\n\nAegis. It became an unholy world. The Undead reached their evil hands across it, conquering and destroying all that was before them. They corrupted each of of the cities, one by one. First, Al'Khazar fell, and then Alras.\n\nProceeding onward into the realm, they claimed Kal'Urguan as their own, as well. The many souls of Aegis tried to push back, but the powerful miasma the Undead created would fill their lungs, killing them, with every attempt. It seemed hope was lost,\n\nas constant storms raged on, and the souls of Aegis stood back praying that the last three foot-holds of Aegis, Krugmar, The Cloud Temple, and Laurelin would not fall. The children would cry, while the adults would try to look for the greener side.\n\nTime passed, and the Undead ceased their attacks. Instead, they claimed the world as their own, and walked it freely. Visiting each of the footholds, they would simply look down upon the poor souls of Aegis, as they knew they couldn’t do much to stop it.\n\nThis continued for some time, until an Undead named Vardak was beaten down by Native. After the beating, directly outside Laurelin, Mogroka felt more was necessary. Mogroka banished Vardak and his Wife to the Spirit World.\n\nHis death created an explosion, leaving a large crater. From this crater, a portal appeared, linking the forsaken realm of Iblees to our own. Aegis was left in shock, no one sure of what to do.\n\nEntering Drauchriem\n\nLaurelin, in shambles from the death of Vardak, the darkness contaminating the grounds opened a portal to the forsaken lands. This portal, the only thing separating the forsaken city of Drauchriem from Aegis,\n\nnow stands open for all to fear. The nations, shocked with the event, raised their most fierce champions to enter the portal with the greatest equipment of the realm. Equipment that was blessed with the holy signs of Aeriel.\n\nAs the cities around Aegis fell, Al'Khazar, Alras, Galahar, New Terriko, the nations united and sent their Champions into the Portal, in hopes of destroying the forsaken realm.\nAnd so the Champions entered the portal. Upon arriving in the forsaken city,\n\nthe Champions did not falter. They began their ever-long quest to destroy the Nether. As the heroes traversed the course to get to the Axe of Krug, they were battered with endless waves of hell-spawn and traps.\n\nMany died, fathers, brothers, friends, all lost in the realm. The Undead, watching as the Heroes continue to fight against all odds, move back into the Nexus, waiting for them.\n\nAfter many long hours, the Heroes fought their way through the forsaken realm, until on champion reached the Axe and began to race into the Nexus, knowing his goal, and what it would mean to him. As the Champions find their way back out of the Nether,\n\nthe Hero with the Axe must travel to the Nexus, and finish the taint that has been spreading. Battling his way through hoards of tainted creatures, he finally made his way to the heart of the Nexus. The heart of the nexus, a pool of lava,\n\nthe heat and the corruption pulsating throughout it. The hero, knowing what he had to do, sacrificed himself, as well as the Axe, and jumped into the Pool. Instantly the Realm of Iblees was shut off, and broken.\n\nThe hero who sacrificed himself died, saving the realm of Aegis from Iblees and his puppets. The hero was named Urir Ire'heart. The Champions who escaped the Nether to bring news of the victory were later known as Legends,\n\nand the ones who died were the bravest souls, giving up their lives to save Aegis and its people.\n\nA Final Escape\n\nUpon the escape of those remaining, there came forth a man named Blundermore. He had pieced together parts of a map, collected from each Nation. He followed the map and found the remnants of an ancient portal,\n\nand the diaries of those that had passed through long ago. Inside, he read that the Verge was the only way out. Some listened to this, and they traveled to the Verge, and began to build boats, wanting to get as far away from Aegis as possible.\n\nThose who remained in Aegis were given a rude awakening. Iblees came into the land, summoning his pets from the Void: Dragons. They destroyed all and killed all. Aegis was lost. All retreated to the Verge,\n\nin hope of finding new land. The construction of the boats was completed soon after, as many sat there, in hopes the weather would be clear enough to set sail.\n\nTime passed, and with it, the storms. On the perfect day, the souls set out, hoping to find a sanctuary. They sailed for weeks, and after much time, they arrived in an unfamiliar land… a land called Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("The White Ravens", "§bSilv'ar Vanguard", "A guide to the History\nOf the White Ravens\n\n-The Grey Wardens\n\n-The Reform\n\n-The Golden Days\n\n-The Founding\n\n-The Clipping\n\n-The Grey Wardens-\nIn the earily days of\naegis a old elf who\nlived in a church between the city\nof Malinor and Ravenhold created a church. This Church was where he safed many people but once they left his church\n\nThey were beyond his help and to combat this he created the Grey Wardens a small guild that lived close to the church. They started out with few members. They spend there days watching the roads between the two citys.\n\nThough the Wardens of Mailnor heard there name and became angered over the name. So the leader of the grey wardens turned the page and Reformed the grey wardens.\n\n  -The Reform-\nThe whole grey wardens was reworked into the White Ravens.\nLed by Alavaska. The White Raven grew to a massive size and led many to safety. It wasn't till the creation of the Council till the numbers swell to massive size.\n\n-The Golden Days-\nIt was a breif time when the white ravens fought the undead and won several attacks and led two seiges on there fortress and won them! but these days were short. The leader of the White Ravens Vanished and the end of Aegis had come.\n\n-The Founding-\nThe people of Aegis found a new land where the White Ravens founded and created a wonderful city and created a prosperous nation.\n\n-The Clipping-\nThis was the end.\nThe Specters\n\n*The page would end there clearly torn out. A small mark would be left of a tree on a cliff and a number.\n'1501'.", ""),
        StaticBook("Uruk Records- I", "§bThurak'Yar", "Uruk Records\n----------------\nForeword-\n\nThe following is to be a record of all notable events of the Uruk people, going on from the 1’st of The Amber Cold, 1501. Although these records\n\nfocus solely on events after this date, other relevant information will be included for past context.\n\n\n~Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, of the Yar Clan.\n\n-First of The Amber Cold, 1501.\nThe population of the Uruks has flourished in recent months; some say even to the point where we could once again be held as a major force in the workings of the realm, and yet to what we\n\nhave to thank for this one cannot rightly say. Some, quite fairly, claim this spike to be attributed to the migration of the Trog (This is the name given to the village situated by the Main Atherian Road) from our capital San'vitar (Fittingly, \"Old City\"\n\nIn Old Blah). Although there might be some truth in this, one can find Uruks openly mumbling dissent about the move; even as we’re at our most powerful, we’re at our most vulnerable, for here we have no forts or battlements to\n\nmake war from, and the looming threat of the Azogs and Oren is something we’re all too aware of. Others say that it is in fact our new Rex that we owe our activity to. Zogrocka’Rax, a Latauman and indeed a turned Dark Shamanism\n\nuser, took up Rexdom from Rix’Rax, who he killed in single combat. He’s taken to a somewhat neutral stance to the war, however he’s actively encouraged brutal combat with those Orcs of the Azog clan, who were banished and are\n\nnow raiding and assaulting our Trog Camp on a daily level. With this, however, comes an issue when we note that Oren has taken up an alliance with these Azogs. Although Zogrocka has not openly declared war, many battles and counter attacks\n\nhave been had involving both Azogs and the men of Oren’s ever growing army. \nOn a less offensive front, the Shamans have been growing in population as the Orcs have, and many new apprentices have been taken on in recent weeks.\n\n The past Wood Elven commander Phaedrus was recently indicted as an honorary Uruk, and has now begun training as the only other Farseer of the Uzg save for myself. Some take this with offense, however I believe with the\n\ncorrect training the Elf may just be a great Farseer and guide to the Uruk people. \nThe Spirit Realm has been mostly quiet recently, however Ehnrok, the spirit of War, is gaining prevalence once more as his ideals spread through the\n\nUzg and indeed the realm. A dispute has arisen between the spirit Arwa one one of the minor spirits under her control- Laklul. With a whole clan supporting him, the Spirit of Swamps seeks to break off from his overruling spirit of\n\nfertility, and commanded his followers to effectively neuter themselves as a show of violation to their pact. The Clan is led by none other than Shreck’Lak, and fittingly it is the first clan to be in full worship of a single spirit. If their\n\nprogress continues, no doubt the spirit will soon rise to a fully fledged Greater Spirit in the Immortal Realm.\n\n-Fourteenth of The Amber Cold, 1501.\nThe Uruk Hu-Din has been declared Pug in the Rex Zogrocka’s latest preaching to the Uruks of the War Uzg. Hu-Din’Lak was once the most avid supporter of Rex and Farseer Rusk’Dom, and\n\never since the Doms’ disbandment and the death of Rusk Hu-Din has striven to impeach his own values on the Uzg. Even should these values be honourable and in the best interest of the Uzg, Zogrocka’s leadership has been challenged by them,\n\nand as such Hu-Din’Lak has been demoted until such time as he desists. Meanwhile, the Rex has openly declared the Uruk’s opposition to the humans of Oren, stating, “The Humans have decided to fight with our Azog enemy,\n\ntherefore they are treated like an Azog. No mercy will be given to them whatsoever.”\nHe has also condemned the attack of the Druids in response to a recent incident with the Wolf Druid Ouity. In thanks, the Druids have agreed\n\nto take care of the wildlife of the Uruk savanna, which has been growing ever since the destruction of San’Vitar, and may soon be attractive poaching grounds for nearby human settlements.\n\nIn other events, Zar’roc’Yar has been appointed as a temporary Targoth, and both Shreck’Lak and Grazadh'Gorkil were promoted to Warbosses in response to the Laks’ growing population, which now stands as the most populous clan of the\n\nUzg. The Uruks are currently neutral to the Dwarves, Dunamis, the Kharajyr, and the Caliphate, and this isn’t looking to change any time soon with the Rex set in his position on the war.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic History", "§bThe Druidic Order", "Druidic History\n         in Aegis\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Druidic Order\n\nHistory - Pre-Dream\n\nThe Age Of Founding And The Before Times\n\nThe records of these times are currently being fully deciphered. Although we know of some of the first druids in Malinor, such as Respiren, Swifthide, and Native,\n\nbut very few details are known. Hopefully the past regarding these times will be cleared up in the near future. Recently a interview was done with Respiren to shed light on this early days. It can be found here.\n\nThe First Age of Reconstruction\n\nThe First Age of Reconstruction was ushered in by the initiation of Dragon Druid Apollan into the order. Apollan was the first to express interest in joining the order after reading the Myth of the Great War and spend long hours in the Druid Grotto\n\nafter he was famously murdered outside the gates of Laurelin by a bandit. Apollan quickly moved up the ranks. Meanwhile, the order grew. After initiating Apollan, Respiren expressed interest in 'rebuilding the order'. Every day, new citizens of Aegis\n\nwould show up in the grove wanting to become Druids. Most were immediately initiated. As the Order grew so did a number of things including property and knowledge. During this time the order gained a lodge in Ravenhold, as well as one in the Laurelin\n\ndocks. Additional, two stalls were bought at the Laurelin Marketplace and hundreds of books were added to the orders library.\n\nThe Age of Abandonment\n\nUnfortunately, due to extremely\n\ncasual and non-uniform initiation rites of the Wayward Druid, people were joining the circle, only to wander into the wilderness never to be seen again. With no established Hierarchy, the Order lacked organization and purpose.\n\nThis was made apparent when an elf named Rowan arrived. Archdruid Rowan, arrived from a far off forest, seeking to reestablish his lost circle the 'Druids of Mother Aegis'. Rowan is most likely the only citizen to have argued with the orders ways.\n\nHis only backing for title of Druid was that he 'had a love of nature'. When Rowan became annoyed by the fact that he had to be initiated in order be allowed into the inner library he stormed off claiming he would start his own order somewhere else.\n\nRowan was last seen entering the wilds outside his home in the Ravenlodge, and was never heard from or seen from again. Fortunately the dark Age of Abandonment was brought to an end by the light of the Dawn Druid Maiavel.\n\nThe Age of Reformation\n\nThe Age of Reformation was brought on by the ideas and drive of one Maiavel. With her determination, she was able to rally the remaining Druid to create an official; lore, Hierarchy, rules, and sense of order.\n\nThe Second Age of Reconstruction\n\nDuring the second age of Reconstruction many more books were written and a Grand Tree in the Laurelin Grove was planted. New Dedicants were brought in byt less frequently than in the first age, and the initiation\n\nprocess was more careful and uniform. During this age, the current Hierarchy was established with Apollan as Arch Druid.\n\nThe Age of Knowledge\n\nThe Age of Knowledge was ushered in by the Petyr, the Salmon Druid.\n\nHis creation of the Dedicant's Vows and the Attunement Ceremony greatly helped the order as well as his order ideas including spearheading the wiki.\n\nThe Age of Mushroom Transgressions\n\nThis age was brought about by the conflict caused by the differing ideals in the order. Some Druids were becoming increasingly annoyed at the restriction that came with having a grove in the city (where trees/mushrooms could or could not be planted\n\nand the structure of the druid tree). Other Druids argued that it was their duty to promote balance, and that the runway growth of mushrooms flowing from the grove was nowhere near natural. Some Druids wanted a new grove tobe created outside the city and\n\nfaraway. Others wanted the grove to be close. Still others did not want a new grove at all. But, it is important to note that most of these arguments were caused by misunderstandings, which is why this age is sometimes called the Age of Misunderstanding\n\nor the Age of Confusion.\n\nThe Age of Renovation\n\nIn the end most mushrooms were removed from the grove when Maiavel stamped her foot and the muchrooms instantly broke\n\n (but were unthoughtfully left on the ground, only to be swept up by Deltaro). A new, secret grove was set up in the wilderness outside Ravenhold, (notable work from Mahten and Aeaira whom spent days working on the road leading to civilization).\n\n The Laurelin Grove continued to be renovated and improved on, with notable work contributed by Lunar Druid Bircalin and Dedicant Deltaro.\n\nHistory - Post-Dream\nThe First Age of Dreaming\n\nFor a long time it seemed that Nature was silent. For a great length of time, none had seen any feats spoken about in the ancient druid tales. But then, as if a seed was planted,\n\nNature began to speak, and each Druid began to dream mysterious dreams. It was the Aspects of Nature, Cerridwen and Cernunnos, calling to their newly found children. Wayward Druid Respiren called a Moot to discuss these dreams, leading into…\n\nThe Age of the Aspects\n\nThe Moot decided to embrace these aspects as their primary deities.\n\nThe Age of Little Occurrence\n\nNothing happened for a while, except for a few little things\n\nThere was a small Hierarchy change; The Archdruid position was given to three people and the Grand Druid's description was changed. John and Maiavel were promoted to Archdruids but Maiavel soon retired. Her spot was filled by Petyr. Cleric Druid Mahten\n\nwas also promoted to the rank of Guide. A small little recruiting strategy was initiated.\n\nThe Second Age of Renovations\n\nDuring this age the Laurelin Grove experienced a number of additions.\n\n A wall was created around the grove with a retractable gate. This was done to keep out a number of citizens that were harassing the druids. In addition, all the entrances were cover up so that one must always  use the front gate.\n\nMore additions to the grove were a kitchen, a melon and pumpkin farm, the cultivation of the Grand Tree's roots deeper into the ground, a tree farm, an elevator system and druid dwellings at the top of the Grand Tree.\n\nThe Age of Poor Judgement\n\nA lot of inter-order augments and bad feelings culminated in this Age. Multiple parties were involved and no side was completely right. The end result was the leaving of Seeker Druid Deltaro from the order.\n\nThe bad taste left in the mouth of many Druids caused Apollan to create the Druid Code.\n\nThe Second Age of Little Occurrence\n\nDuring this age, as its name would imply, not many things happened.\n\nThe grove as given another renovation, mostly for aesthetic purposes. In addition, a Druid Order Forum account was created as well as a blog. Unfortunately during this time, Archdruid John's mental health was also starting to slide.\n\nThe Second Age of Dreaming\n\nDuring this age Salmon Druid Petyr had a vision in which the creation myth was shown to him by the Aspects. It foretold of the time before the four races and a great exodus to come.\n\n A second Moot was called and all in attendance agreed to accept the vision as truth.\n\nThe Age of Mourning\n\nUnfortunately during this time, John's mental state grew worse. One day, John snapped.\n\nAmong a number of thing he attacked the Dusk Druid. He then fled to his soul tree (Which he named Marcus) located in the pond outside the Laurelin Grove. There he made his last stand. The Druids present at the time were Dusk, Mahten, Apollan, Respiren,\n\nSaviticus and Thork the Betrayer (Thork the Blood Druid). In addition several princes and bystanders were also there. John stood on the roots of his soul tree and attacked anyone who came near. There was a standoff for some time until all at once\n\nthe Druids charged the tree. All some traded blows with John, Apollan worked to purify the water around the tree for he sensed that there was a taint at work. Suddeny the Dusk Druid produced and axe and chopped at the soul tree until only\n\none column was left. It was then that; with that ability to see inside the tree, Apollan discovered the taint in the form of a block of netherrack. Before Apollan could share his discovery, Thork went into a blood lust. He cut down the last column of the\n\n tree rendering John unconscious. Then Thork stabbed John's body killing him. In the days followed Thork was shunned for violating Druid Code. John's tree was turned into the place of his burial where his body was burned and the ashes scattered around\n\nLaurelin. His will named Mahten as his replacement as Archdruid.\n\nThe Age of Expansion\n\nDuring this age, the Nature's Bounty chain was expanded by one new store on the King's Road.\n\nThe order was also expanded by one new member. Zannith [to be added later], the 10 year old son of the Dusk Druid and an unknown elf moved into the grove. Much to the dismay of one Bircalin. Zannith later left the Druid grove to join the Wardens and later\n\ncommitted suicide by jumping from the Grant Tree.\n\nThe Age of Knowledge\n\nDuring this age the Druid took control of the library of the Cloud Temple of Aegis. Petyr also retired from his position\n\nas Archdruid and became a Hierophant. Dusk Druid Aeaira was elected to fill the spot and Saviticus became Head teacher.\n\nThe Second Age of Mourning\n\nDuring this age Archdruid Mahten transformed\n\n his entire being into a tree in the grove. As a result of his sacrifice, Druid Dusk was named(in his will) as successor to the position of Arch Druid. In this time she has began to bring new life to the Druids Tree; ushering forth growth and spread\n\n of new branches, and brought a new generation of druids into the Dedicant rank.\n\nThe Second Age of Expansion\n\nDuring this age the Druid Order and Grand tree grew exponentially.\n\nThe Third Age of Mourning\n\nDuring this age Archdruid Apollan and Dusk we killed under mysterious circumstances. Apollan's position was given to his close freind Horizon Druid Makia and Dusk's position was given to\n\n Fox Druid Valas.\n\nThe Age of Poor Logic\n\nDuring this age, everything the druids knew was proven to be incorrect. Petyr proved that wood doesn't exist, then proved that it does.\n\nHe also proved that magic isn't real, and that water is fake. Unable to hold all this nonsense, Archdruid Darrian was convinced that he had gone crazy and was only dreaming. After jumping to his death from the top of the Grand Tree,\n\nFey Druid Vanyariel took his position as Archdruid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life of Urguan", "§bBrindle Ironstick", "The Life of Urguan\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBrindle Ironstick\n\nFor as the tensions of the war grew, so did the bond between Urguan and the human lord. Though he began to become more tentative in the war, surely, none can doubt that Branden Heigh helped persuade him to take a more active combat role.\n\nIndeed, were fate left up to Horen only, we may have been overwhelmed by our earthly greed, never peeking out of the safe cavernous city.\nHow Horen viewed Heigh is unclear, but evidence seems to show a rather rocky relationship.\n\nThis is to be expected, as great minds rarely cooperate, it seems. The eventual outcome of the human power stru……………………………………………..lucky that the dwarves were coaxed out into battle before Horen was proclaimed ruler. And……….", ""),
        StaticBook("Phoenix Reb. I", "§bJosef and Kernith Timothee", "A History\n        of the\n   Phoenix Rebellion\n\n      Vol. I of II\n\n\n\n\n\nJosef and Kernith Timothee\n\nThe Phoenix Revolution has proven to be one of the greatest upsets in modern times. A group of Humans, angry with the rule of their legitimate monarch, banded together to overthrow the established political order. In the process,\n\none nation was destroyed, three were created and the world was never to be the same. Had there been no revolution would there have been a Salvus, Renatus or Hanseti? If the Humans had managed to stay strong and united, would the Undead have been able to\n\n take over Aegis? Would Seventis have sought the need to exist? Would Godfrey I have appeared and reunited the Human lands into the Holy Oren Empire? Without a united Human nation, would other races have been able to\n\ntake advantage of the weakened position of the Humans? It is impossible to know what Asulon would look like today if the Phoenix Revolution had not occurred or if at key moments certain scenes had not unfolded exactly the way they did.\n\nThe very start of the Phoenix Revolution began in Oren, under the rule of the Sheffield’s. Following the death of the King Pampo Perea to the Undead, his Seneschal Edmund Sheffield took the throne. The rule of Sheffield proved to be polarizing.\n\nRight from the start of his rule his legitimacy as king was questioned, as following tradition the throne should have gone to the eldest son of Pampo Perea, Rhonin. Sheffield was, however, applauded in his efforts to fight the Undead that advanced on Oren\n\nthe north. He was also seen to be very supportive of the Oren military and used them wisely to fight the Undead. Other nations depended on the Humans of Oren to defend against the Undead threat in the north, given that should Oren fall the\n\nUndead could easily attack south down the King's Road. It was argued by some that his popularity was bolstered by his wife, Ivrae, and their three children, popular among citizens of Al'Khazar. Sheffield also retained support by those who wished\n\nto bolster their own ambitions, or because they viewed the monarchy as irrefutable. The Undead threat grew steadily during the rule of Sheffield, eventually culminating in his own corruption to the Undead and subsequent murder of his wife.\n\nAs an Undead he was known to have attacked Alras and other places.\n\nFollowing the fall of Edmund Sheffield there was an internal struggle in Oren regarding who should take over the throne.\n\nHis son Enor eventually emerged as the clear and legitimate choice. Just like with his father, Enor’s rule also drew supporters and detractors. His supporters claimed that being young and new to the throne meant he would make mistakes,\n\nbut only needed experience. He was also declared to be upholding the throne’s legitimacy. His wife Luna Wildewyn likely helped increase his popularity. Over time, opposition increased. He was accused of using tax money meant to fight the Undead\n\nto pay the guards to stifle dissent to his rule, creating a vicious circle. Others said he was paranoid in trying to defend his rule. Some of the more frivolous complaints included the housing costs in Al’Khazar. Many grew to consider Enor a weak and\n\nspineless leader who relied on his military to protect his own interests.\n\nIn 1338 Al’Khazar fell to the Undead, marking the first major Undead victory in many years and the start of the Human diaspora. During the attack Enor was kidnapped by\n\nthe Undead and taken to the Nether for a year. During this time concerns were raised that he may have been tainted like his father and become a pawn of the Undead, perhaps even at the hands of Edmund himself. Upon his return to Aegis Enor claimed\n\nthe Council that had formed in his absence to be illegitimate and once more declared himself to be the sole ruler of Oren. For those who already saw him as a near dictator, these claims only made him appear less appealing as king\n\nIn the chaotic aftermath of the Fall of Al’Khazar, the Phoenix Revolution began.\n\nThe Phoenix Revolution was initially formed in response to the rule of the Sheffield’s, the losing of the war against the Undead and the threat posed by the Human diaspora.\n\nThe Revolution quickly attracted many important figures within Oren, including leading military and political men. Out of the ten members of the Council that was established following the disappearance of Enor to rule in his absence at least half\n\nwere avid supporters of the Revolution. Also notable was that support came from all levels of Human society. Peasants to nobility all had reason as to why Enor should be removed from the throne. Amid other nations, support was strong as well. Many\n\nof those who lived on the King’s Road thought that the Humans were the best chance to stop the Undead from advancing south, which Enor failed to do. Although very little explicit support was given to the supporters of the Revolution,\n\nmost nations seemed to indicate that they would not try and stop it.\n\nEnor was widely seen as inefficient, corrupt and unfit as king. As the northern towns of Crimson Vale, New Alstion, Winterfell and Celestine fell to the Undead\n\nin 1340, opposition only increased. With more people attracted to the idea of the Revolution, a formal headquarters was established on the White Road. Planning was cautious, and only those who were trusted enough to both take part\n\nin the Revolution and not give it away were told about it. It was imperative that anyone who could oppose the Revolution be left in the dark. In the earliest stages, there were numerous leaders suggested to guide the Revolution.\n\nThe two most prominent choices that emerged were Eze'kiel Tarus and Zibaen Vivyaen. There were concerns about the potential for Tarus to follow in the footsteps of his sister Atriana, who had been the High Constable of Oren before betraying it to the\n\nUndead and becoming one herself. Others expressed doubt that either man was well known enough among ordinary people of Oren, and other men were suggested as potential leaders, including Throdo Therving. In the end, Tarus emerged as the favourite\n\nchoice among the revolutionaries and he was chosen to lead the Revolution.\n\nLevels of support for the Revolution were varied, and included gathering items and food for potential conflict, swaying others to join and creating propaganda.\n\nThe symbol of the Phoenix was chosen to represent the Revolution, as a sign of a new Oren rising from the ashes of Enors rule. At this time, the goal of the revolutionaries was not to cause major change, but to dethrone Enor in what they\n\nhoped would be a move to restore and invigorate Oren against the Undead threat. Although they clearly had a leader in mind for the new Oren, many expressed that they would be willing to negotiate with Enor to find a leader suitable to all parties.\n\nAs the final stages of the Revolution drew closer, it was commonly agreed among Revolutionaries that the goal was peace. Violence would only be used against those who opposed the Revolution with force, and it was hoped Enor would peacefully\n\nstep off the throne. The Revolutionaries knew that Enor retained considerable popularity, despite the support they themselves had attracted, and they would have to tread carefully in dethroning him. What happened next shocked the revolutionaries.", ""),
        StaticBook("Clerical Healing", "§b[Child] Silus Hightower", "A guide to Creator Clerical healing\n\nby Lady Sarah Hightower.\n\n\nDedicated to my dutiful students.\n\nAssessment.\n\nThe first step in treating a patient is to assess his or her injuries. Ask yourself the following questions before you attempt to treat the injury.\n\n1 Where is the wound located?\n\n2 What is the severity of the wound.\n\n3 Am I able to treat this wound.\n\nStart by locating the wound, sometimes you'll have to cut away clothing to properly access it.\n\nThen classify the\n\nwound using the following scale\n\nI Light cuts and bruises, no severe bleeding.\n\nII Cuts with bleeding, at risk of infection, no internal damage. Burns that leave skin intact.\n\nIII Broken bones in the limbs. Major burns and arrow wounds in the limbs or ones that did not damage major organs.\n\nIV Broken ribs, Internal injuries, broken skulls arrow and crossbow bolt wounds that pierced major organs.\n\nV Loss of limb, defects in the lungs or heart.\n\n\nAttempt the find the classification that fits the scale best and then decide if Your clerical abilities are prudent to use, or perhaps the patient can be better treated with\n\nmundane healing. In the early stages of your clerical career you will often have to combine both Clerical and mundane healing.\n\nConnecting\n\nThe second step one must take to heal a patient through clerical magic is to connect to the Creator, this must be done through prayer.\n\nYou begin by clearing your mind of all woes\n\ntry and think of a place or memory that fills you with joy, then you will have to say or think of a prayer, asking the creator to bestow his Holy gifts upon you. for the newer clerics this is an exhausting process, but the more talented can summon\n\nHoly light in a matter of seconds.\n\nYou must be a devout follower of the creator to use his holy light, one who kills or injures without good cause will not be able to do so.\n\nGuiding the light\n\nThe next step is to bring the holy light onto the injury, staves may be used although using your hands is most likely the more practical solution. \n\nIf you concentrate enough you will find\n\nthat the light will obey your commands and goes where you want it, in theory you could heal a patient without using your hands, but this will be severely exhausting and even Class I wounds will prove a challenge to fix for the advanced cleric.\n\nHealing\n\nWhen you've guided the light to the injury, you may start the healing, this is not done automatically, you must know how the injury works before you are able to heal it. \nFor instance if you cannot set a bone\n\nproperly, you cannot use the holy light to do it, the results will most likely be unpleasant, so educate yourself in mundane healing before attempting to treat the more difficult wounds. \n\nTo heal the wound you simply imagine how the\n\nwound mends, think of the procedure and guide the light so that it does thus, you will find that the light will mend the injury you are faced with, granted it is within your abilities to heal it.\n\nProgressing your abilities.\n\n§ § Clerical magic differs from other schools of magic in one aspect. A cleric can draw on more power than he or she can handle this is fairly common and in light doses harmless\nhowever there are\nside effects\n\nI Fatigue\nII Light shaking.\nIII Headache.\nIV Light coughing.\nV Danger of falling in an unconscious state.\nVI Coughing up of blood.\nVII Long term weakness, damage to the lungs.\nVIII Death.\n\nYou will often have to push yourself to stage V or even VI\nto advance your abilities. this will mean you advance faster, but comes at risk of long term weakness, if you treat wounds that are at your level of experience you will also grow\n\nin power, but you will rarely find wounds that match your experience exactly.\n\nMindsoothing.\n\nA cleric also has the ability to calm the minds of others, to achieve this you must be in a calm state yourself. If you are not then you will not be able to succeed, however you can calm yourself through a quick prayer\n\nor a short meditation session.\n\n§PDistress Scale.\n\nA: Normal state of mind.\n\nB: Light panic, nervous eye movement, soft speech, cautious movement.\n\nC: Total panic, crying, heavy shaking, difficulty speaking.\n\nD: Catatonic state, generally inable to move or speak, will sit or remain still, as if frozen. Some patients may repeat phrases or motions until treated.\n\nAs with the healing of wounds, you must first assess the condition of the patient, if there is a physical injury as well you must decide which to treat first. \n\nThen you must clear your mind of woes and connect to the creator.\n\nThen you must guide the light to either your eyes or your hands. and look at the patient directly, or in the latter case, move your hands to touch his body, then you simply project your own calmness unto the patient.\n\nLimb regereneration.\n\nIn the final stages of your abilities you will be able to regrow limbs using the creator's blessing, however this is not to be taken lightly and will take a great physical cost and depending on the severity\n\nmay require several Clerics. However fingers and hands can be regrown over multiple sessions at a lesser physical cost.\n\nYou MUST § do the proper research before attempting this procedure, every vein, bone and muscle must be regrown\n\nperfectly or the limb will not be of much use, or worse the patient may suffer internal bleeding and die.\n\nIn theory one could regenerate a vital organ such as a lung or liver, but this will leave you at a severe risk of dying.\n\nNever attempt to regrow a heart or brain, you will most likely die of the side effects before you generate a working heart, the brain is simply impossible.\n\nI hope that this guide has helped you in understanding Holy magic.\n\nMay you heal many people.\n\n~Sarah Hightower\n\n10th of Sun's Smile\n                  1456", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature's Break", "§bMonk Scribe", "Nature's Break\n\nAs the sun arises,\nthe moon falls,\nas the warmth starts,\nthe cold fades,\nas the leaves are bore,\nthe frost thaws,\nAegis rotates.\n\n- Written by LaTerre Amant in Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Abjurist", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "Wards & Abjuration\n^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^              a\n         study by\n\n  Gallidron Elindrow\n\nAbjuration is a facinating branch of voidal magic, and perhaps the most difficult. I say this because the most knowledge is required to be a succesfull abjurist or warder.\nTo cast a mighty evocation, one need only understand the element that will be their\n\nmedium and the art of evocating. To transmute water into ice one needs to understand the intricasies of the freezing process, to conjur one must know what they wish to make in exact detail before they can begin to even form the creature or item in the\n\nvoid. But to ward against these things, to abjure them into non-exsistance, one must not only understand how to cast protective magic, but they must also understand in detail the magic they wish stop.\n\nIt is for this reason that I say, the successful abjurist should be lauded above all other mage kind for they are at once massively powerfull and a dutiful student of all forms of magic. I would admonish any who seek to ward or abjure to learn all they\n\ncould of magic that they might not be caught unprepared. It would even be prudent to learn what one could of the dark arts, within the bounds of reason and safety, that they are not caught off guard by these most sinister magics.\n\nAn Abjuration is a more offensive style of protecting one's self or others from magic. Suppose that an enemy mage has cast a fire spell at you and a veritable flood of flame is headed in your direction. Now, you are somewhat knowledgable in the department\n\nof evocation and so you realize that the spell itself is functioning on the premise of converted energy. Fire is after all just energy moving from one form into another. In this case that energy is the mana of the mage and the form it has taken is shaped\n\nin the void. There are several ways to go about this, as is the beauty of abjuration (one is only limited by their resevoir of power and their imagination). You could try to disrupt the flow of mana from the mage to the spell, or you could break its\n\nconnection to the void. All in all, the most effective, fool proof, and easiest way is likely to break the connection to the void. This is called disrupting the mana anchor. The Mana Anchor is the metaphorical place where the spell and the energy for it\n\nmeet and create its effect. It is also what keeps the spell active in our world and not just a figment of a thought in the void. Knowing these things you craft your abjuration and destory the spell before it gets to you. Assuming of course that you are\n\nas powerful or more so than the mage who is trying to fry your skin off.\n\nA ward is more deffensive and takes more time to make. They are also potentially more versitile and usefull, this is the cause for the increased time of casting.\n\nA ward is stationary and is used like a shield against one or various forms of magic. Where as an Abjuration can be cast in the moment, it can only defend from one kind of magic. A ward can be crafted with care and forethought and thus be made to\n\ncounteract various kinds of magic at once. They can last for a long time, given that they have a steady supply of mana to draw upon. The larger and more intricate the ward, the more energy will be required. A ward that is crafted and placed on an object\n\nor in a place can be thought of much like an enchantment. In fact many enchantments are wards of one kind or another. These spells require the use of a mana gem, a kind of magical battery, to continue to function after the mage has left, and even then\n\nthe mana gem will only last for so long.\n\nA working knowledge of the magic to be blocked by the ward is still required to create the spell.\n\nPower is of tantamount importance. If you are a beginning abjurist, you cannot block the fire ball of a master evocationist. They will simply overwhelm you with the might of their spell. One must be at least equal to their opponent to bring their casting\n\nto a stand still.\n\nOne does not need to be a master evocationist, or even be able to cast evocation, to create wards or abjurations against it. But you will need at least a working knowledge of the element used.  Of course the more experience you have\n\nthe better you will fare as an abjurist.\n\nI hope that this book has been enlightening to you as a reader and that you will put this knowledge to good use.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\npublishing date 6th of\nGrand Harvest, 1519\n\nPlease look for my next study on the Arcane!\n\nLightning and fire and frost, oh my!\n\na study on Evocation", ""),
        StaticBook("Jokes for Humans", "§bVykk Volaren", "In Petrus, a young woman, somewhat of a simpleton was on the point of delivering a baby. she had been having long enduring pains, and the midwife, candle in hand, inspected her wizard sleeve, in order to see if the baby was coming. \"Look also on the other\n\nside.\" The woman said, \"My husband sometimes takes that road as well.\"\n\n          JOKE 2\nThree men were conversing in Alras, each wishing for things that would make them happy. One wanted to be the King, the second wanted to be the Pope, the third man said \"I think I would rather like to be a melon.\" shocked, the other men\n\ninquired why. \"Because.\" said the man \"then everyone would have to smell me.\"\n\n         Joke 3\nA man from Vanderfell was worried that his wife was having intamate moments with another man. he racked his brain to figure a way to know for sure. without a second thought he emasculated himself, \"If my wife becomes pregnant, I will know\n\nfor sure if she is an adulterer or not!\" He proudly exclaimed.\n\n          Joke 4\nWhile working in the fields, a peasant man from Petrus measured his sons to those of a prominant noble. \"Why,\" he exclaimed, \"Do his sons get to join the military, while mine must toil away in the farms?\" his neighbor turned to him,\n\nBecause, they will have to leave their wives during war to... take care of other men as they say.\n\n          Joke 5\nA man from Polaris went down to the river to catch his family a meal. Along came a youth, \"Where are you going inquired the man?\" The boy smiled and retorted \"I am going to the brothel to cast my line and catch your mother.\" The man from\n\nPolaris just laughed, \"Be careful, where you cast your line.\" Said the man \"Or you will be sure to catch yours as well.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Cook's Assistant", "§bthanndreli", "Difficulty: Varies. Easy to Medium.\n\nFeeding the Lucienist order is a difficult job since the rise in recruits. \n\nContact Raigeki Kato to assist him in jobs. Fair warning, not everything is cooking.\nRewards vary on type\n\nof success.\n\nDEUS MAGNUS!", ""),
        StaticBook("Magical Unctions", "§bAmbros", "Magical Unctions\n\nBy Ambros\n\nUNGUENTS, or unctions, collyries, philters, &c., conveying the virtues of things natural to our spirits, do multiply, transform, transfigure, and transmute it accordingly; they also transpose those virtues, which are in them, into it, so that it not only\n\nacts upon its own body, but also upon that which is near it, and affects that (by visible rays, charms, and by touching it) with some agreeable quality like to itself. For, because our spirit is the pure, subtil, lucid, airy, and unctuous vapour of the\n\nblood, nothing, therefore, is better adapted for collyriums than the like vapour, which are more suitable to our spirit in substance; for then, by reason of their likeness, they do more stir up, attract, and transform the spirit. The same virtue have\n\nother ointments, and confections. Hence, by the touch, often plague, sickness, faintings, poisoning, and love, is induced, either by the hands or clothes being anointed; and often by kissing, things been held in the mouth, love is likewise excited.\n\nNow the sight, as it perceives more purely and clearer than the other senses, seals in us the marks of things more acutely, and does, most of all, and before all others, agree with our fantastic spirit; as is apparent in dreams, when things seen do more\n\noften present themselves to us than things heard, or any thin coming under the other senses. Therefore, when collyriums transform the visual spirits, that spirit easily affects the imagination, which, being affected with divers species and forms,\n\ntransmits the same, by the same spirit, unto the outward sense of sight, by which there is formed in it a perception of such species and forms, in that manner, as if it were moved by external objects, that there appear to be seen terrible images, spirits,\n\nand the like. There are some collyriums which make us see the of images of spirits of the air, or elsewhere; which I can make of thegall of a man, and the eyes of a black cat, and some other things. The same is made, likewise, of the blood of a lapwing,\n\nbat, and a goat; and if a smooth shining piece of steel be smeared over with the juice of mugwort, and be made to fume, it causes invocated spirits to appear. There are some perfumes, or suffumigations and unctions, which make men speak in their sleep,\n\nwalk, and do those things that are done by men that are awake, and often what, when awake, they cannot, or dare not do; others, again, make men hear horrid or delightful sounds, noises, and the like.\n\nAnd, in some measure, this is the cause why mad and melancholy men believe they hear and see things equally false and improbable, falling into most gross and pitiful delusions, fearing where no fear is, and angry where there is none to contend. Such\n\npassions as these we can induce bymagical vapours, confections, perfumes, collyries, unguents, potions, poisons, lamps, lights, etc.; likewise by mirrors, images, enchantments, charms, sounds, and music; also by divers rites, observations, ceremonies,\n\nreligion, etc.\n\nABRACADABRA\nBRACADABRA\nRACADABRA\nACADABRA\nCADABRA\nADABRA\nDABRA\nABRA\nBRA\nRA\nA", ""),
        StaticBook("Scourge Guide 1", "§bKnyghtfalcon", "Information on the\nScourge and Harbingers.\n\nTOC -\nMembers and Names\nTainted Creatures\nMagical Abilities and Combat Tactics\nCultist Names\nThe Use of Thanic Ore\n\nWithin the Scourge, there are many members of both Harbinger and other creatures alike. The list is as follows.\n\n Harbingers -\nShae'tan - Shaela\nFemale\nFavours Deception\n\nAbsolution\nMale\nFavours Combat\n\nXort\nMale\nFavours Combat\n\nNihil\nMale\nNeutal - Peaceful\nTreasures Knowledge\n\nDumamis\nMale\nFavours Combat\n\nKalgeryas\nMale\nExtremely Violent\n\nMarak\nMale\nSecluded and Devious\n\nMortum'Vherzix\nMale\nSecluded, EXTREMELY HOSTILE, DO NOT APPROACH.\n\nSitri'aim - Deceased\nMale\nFavoured Manipulation\n\nKav'Zoras - Deceased\nMale\nFavoured Violence\n\nEudihr - Kaos\nMale\nViolent and Deceitful\n\nCreatures -\n\nVithquar\nFemale\nViolent and Childish\n\nCreated by the Masked Judge - Rosso. A half-dragon female.\n\nIt is hostile, dangerous, and believes herself to be the wife of Iblees, queen over the nether realm. Advise approaching with caution, although she is easily manipulated.\n\nMittens\nApparition\nEXTREMELY DANGEROUS\n\nMittens is an apparition created from hundreds of tormented and damned souls, of those who have died in the harsh terrain of the north.\nIt is extremely violent and almost\n\ncompletely unstoppable without a strong dose of holy or spiritual magic. Advise not to approach, turn the other way if you see it. It is dangerous. It will not hesitate to kill you.\n\nKaar'thul the Snake\nUnknown\n\nThis being is a snake-like creature which can assume an almost completely invisible state, and possesses powers alike the Harbingers, with the ability to breath frostfire.\n\nIt is a long segmented serpent when visible, with blood red eyes and a shredded and torn body. It was created to serve the Harbingers although its current alignment is unknown. Advise caution when dealing with the beast, it is very deadly.\n\nCorrupted Drakes\n\nSetherien is in command of many drakes and other serpentine beasts of the north.  When dealing with these creatures, it is advised that you do not face them alone and stay out of tight groups.\n\nThey attack with fire, claws and biting, along with physically slamming their body down on structures and opponents. The best way to kill them is to hit the joints of their wings, strike their eyes, or strike in their mouth when they roar or breath fire.\n\nBohra\n\nLarge pig-like humanoid beings who used to inhabit the northern lands. These creatures are tainted to serve Setherien. They are brutes, yet stupid in most cases, the best course of action is to have someone distract\n\nthem while another attacks, or to simply take them out from a distance. A few arrows in their skull should end the beasts. Aim for the spine or eyes in the case of the corrupted ones, only severing the head or spinal cord can truly end them.\n\nServants of Setherien\n\nSkeletal creatures, the past mortals who have fought against Setherien. Every time a body is taken from the battlefield by Setherien's minions, these are created from the remains. Formerly known as Kambasors\n\nThey usually arrive in groups of two to five from the rifts created by Harbingers or other creatures. In groups they are quite deadly, but singled out are easy to remove. They inflict a sickness on contact, so beware hand to hand combat. The sickness is\n\nknown as taint poisoning, and will sap away your life force and weaken you severely. Aim for the spine or skull, as it is the only way to defeat the creatures.\n\nDrudges of Setherien\n\nThese creatures are the brutish and more armored version of the Servants. They usually possess better equipment and armor, and are slightly more strategic. They inflict a stronger form of the taint sickness.\n\nThey are killed in the same way, spine or skull. It is best to avoid these and remove them from a distance, they usually arrive through rifts in groups of three at a time.\n\nThe Riders of Setherien\n\nConquest\nWar\nFamine\nDeath\n\nThese creatures are spectral beings which ride on the backs of undead steeds.\n\nNot much is known about them by me at least, they were created close to my removal, and thus I had not much time to learn. They are deadly, swift, and masters at combat and war. They possess the ability to open rifts as the Harbingers do.\n\nCombat - \nThe Harbingers in combat are quite weak to melee abilities and require their distance and magic to compete. In order to vanquish one, you must severely damage its armor to force it away.\n\nThey are weak to lightning, and typically do not appreciate fire. They are cold beings, and attacks of ice have no affect. They can not suffer from sickness or wounds, burns nor freezing. They are spectral creatures, and only solid physical strikes will\n\ntruly affect their form. Harbingers can be sentenced to destruction and removed from the realm permenantly if enough clerics can focus holy magic on the creature. Holy magic is their ultimate weakness, use it to your advantage.\n\nAbilities -\nDrakaar's boon\n- This is the basic of magic for the spectral beings, and other dark creatures. This is the gift of the dark one, Setherien, which grants them their abilities and the skill of drawing power from him.\n\nThis is the key, and gives access to all other abilities one might possess. This is what powers the harbingers, keeps the alive. This allows them to hover, and use a specialized form of illusion which allows them to disguise themselves.\n\nFrost Fire, the Northern Breath.\nThis is a specific form of dark, unholy fire, which freezes instead of burns. It is very deadly, and gives highly painful and deadly frostbite on contact, and coats objects with ice. A single blast contains enough\n\nmagical energy to kill a man, and armor seems to have no affect against this.\n\nThe Taint of Setherien, Setherien's Wrath.\n\nA cloud of pure sickness cast out from the forms of the spectral beings, other creatures possess the ability to breathe this out as well. It infects those within the cloud with a\n\nhorrendous desiese which has the ability to spread between multiple hosts upon mere contact. It weakens the victim, induces sickness, vomiting, hallucinations and saps their life from them. Tainted Bohra also can spread this desiese.\n\nSetherien's Call, the Ballista of Drakes.\n\nA large, explosive ball of corruptive energy, cast out to cause mass destruction on an area. It is capable of destroying walls and other structures in a single condensed blast. Only Harbingers are capable of this\n\nThe Rift of the Drakaar Realm, Call of the Servants.\n\nUsable by the Horsemen and the Harbingers, as currently known, along with Corrupted Drakes. This magical rift through dimensions can call forth Servants and\n\nDrudges of Setherien into Combat. A dark ball of pure dark energy is cast to the ground, which begins to spread in a large wave of taint as a rift opens between worlds, dragging the beasts out to fight. Do not step in the rift, it is very toxic.\n\nThe Ritual, Summoner of the Damned.\n\nA ritual performed by the Harbingers, which calls down a large Skeletal Servant simply known as 'The Prophet' which takes the form of a large Drudge. It is extremely hostile, capable of taking down\n\nplatoons of soldiers on its own. It is not often used, as it takes much of their energy to summon. But beware, this creature is extremely deadly, fast, and possesses magical abilities beyond all others. Some believe it is Setherien himself in disguise.\n\nThe Summoning of the Tokens, Call of the Sword.\n\nThe Harbingers possess the ability to call forth their weapons from the same realm of the Kambasor creatures. They can do this at will, in mere moments. They are never unarmed.\n\nIn order to defeat the creatures, beyond their magical abilities, you must kill them as quickly as possible. The longer they exist, the more rituals they may perform and the more kambasors are brought forth. It is important they are dispatched as soon as\n\nyou can get within striking distance. Without their leaders, the rest of the creatures will panic, and they will fall. Just the same, the creatures are without hope if they do not have their servents to defend them. Get them seperated and kill them.\n\nCult Members Known -\nVithquar\nAsher 'Latue' Acosta\nRin\nHaadi Mumbdee\nKelsey Von Craw\nCombo'Breaka'lur\n(Descriptions match each name)\n\nThanic Ore -\nThanic ore is important to the scourge. All bloodshards are made of thanic ore, as are the Harbinger's weapons and armor. While poisonous to void magic users, theirs is enchanted and thus does not kill on contact. They possess large\n\nquantities. It is vital to them, as their armor can not be made of anything but the material.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v3", "§bBishop Cordal", "A History of Humanity From Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume III: The Second Age of Kings\n\nThe Second Age of Kings\n1422-1431\nOn the Continent of Anthos\nKings from the Houses of Horen, Carrion, Hightower, Elendil, Flay-Silverblade\nAlso known as: The Fractured Era, the Age of Five Kings, the Second Unrest, the First Dark Ages, the\n\nFirst Papal Intercession\n\nFollowing Salvus's betrayal and the disbanding of the empire, High Pontiff Goddard I claimed the dissolution of the empire had freed his territories from royal fealty, as they had been granted autonomy from direct\n\nrule when William took the throne. He claimed the Salvian-affiliated territory of Emperor's Forest (later formalized as the County of Kvaz in the second empire), and the Prince-Archbishopric of Savoie (composed of the County of Norfolk, Barony of\n\nAldersberg, Viscounty of Bar, and other minor territories) as independent of the Orenian crown. In a matter of months, the Dukes Charles Greymane of Corpathia and Siegmund Carrion of Raev also swore under the High Pontiff, who took the title Apostolic\n\nKing and subbed his realm the Holy Kingdom of Savoie. \n\nIn the east, the newly seceded Flay-Silverblade island Kingdom of Galahar was not as successful, and it dwindled in relevance as it faced government inefficiency, brutality, and mass emigration\n\nresulting from its disconnect with the Orenian mainland. It was soon forced to wild banditry in order to fund its expenditures. During this period, the Kings of Savoie, Adunia, and Oren took protectorate status under the Grand-King Thorin of the dwarven\n\nGrand Kingdom of Urguan in an effort to try and protect their borders from incursions by one another and the dwarven state. Despites this, Galahar continued its heavy raids until the Duke Siegmund Carrion brought the bandit-state under his command.\n\nThe Savoyard state was around this time then abdicated to Siegmund Carrion, who had been named heir apparent to the pontiff of Carrion blood, and the pontiff returned to matters of the faith.\n\nWhen the Grand-King of Urguan died, the human states were\n\nreleased from their protectorate status and were quickly at odds with one another. Renatus readied for war against Savoie's growing state, which had recently negotiated the absorption of Salvus and hte pagan nation of Adunia into its borders. The King of\n\nSavoie redubbed his state the Kingdom of Ruska, in reference to the culture of his people, the Raevirs.\n\nThreatened by the growth in land and power of Savoie, the King William III of Oren declared High Pontiff Goddard I excommunicated (citing the\n\ncaesareopapist reign of Horen V as legal precedent for state over church supremacy) in an effort to diminish the authority of the kingdom, and brought the nations of Ruska and Oren to the brink of war.\n\nThe Lord High Steward of Oren, Edward\n\nWinter II, met in secret with Goddard I, and the two negotirated terms contingent upon Edward's deposition of William and his gathering the support of other leading advisors and nobles. Goddard I and Edward II led a peaceful exchange of power from William\n\nIII to his cousin, Lord High Treasurer Silus I, who agreed to back the Ruskan-Winter agreement. Silus quickly assumed the throne and appointed countless Ruskan nobility in court positions. In thanks for his services, Edward was created King of Herendul,\n\nand given control of his former liege's, Duke Codrik Green of Hanseti, territories as his kingdom. Herendul, the Crownlands of Oren (now renamed Renatus), Ruska, and the weakened state of Salvus then combined into a loose confederacy governed by a\n\nconstitutional monarchy. King Silus then stepped down and abdicated to Otto Carrion, resulting in an imbalance of of the constitutional monarchy that ensured the election of Siegmund Carrion as Emperor of the Second Empire of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Servants' Conf.", "§bThird Elder Monk", "The Servants’\n         Conflict\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThird Elder Monk, 109\n\n…..the female Aengul proceeded to leave, Aeriel and the Wizard were indeed distraught. The system collapsing before their own eyes…… Odion was called for guidance. It is reported that the Daemon’s stone\n\nhalls spat flames like a baneslither when he heard of this dissent. They rushed to find that the portal had already closed, making it impossible to trace the followers of the Dark Lady, as Monk John was apt to call her.\n\nAeriel decreed that the ethereal spirits must refrain from the constant contact with the Descendant Races as to avoid further mishaps such as this. Some of the Daemons who had befri…..d mortals were angered and left the realm as well,\n\nwhile the remaining Daemons and the majority of Aenguls decided to abide by thi….., each in their own way.\nIt did seem that Aeriel, as well as the Wiz……………….which some did not……… ……and throughout Aegis, the monks destroyed all tomes other than\n\n……much to his dismay. The Wizard was quite upset with the actio………. though it was all for a grand cause, indeed. He later came to be glad for Aeriel’s decision, for………… efforts were certainly successful for the most part,\n\nas is apparent in society, and the account o…………not fully untrue, naturally, yet th………… only to be preserved within this room by the Scarlet Monks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v1", "§bBishop Cordal", "A History of Humanity, From Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume I: Introduction and The First Age of Kings\n\nAuthor's Note: The states of the modern realm were formed in a time of civic unrest caused by militarized cultural differences\n\nwithin the Fourth Empire. However, while these nations differ in culture, they retain a simple heritage of governing states, so that the modern man may understand the liegestate to which he pays homage. While my cousin Cordal Winter sought to chronicle\n\nthe timeline of humanity and my fellow writer Procopius sought to color them with his heart, I seek to establish a coherent and continuous history connecting the modern nations to those of the past, and documenting the states through which humanity\n\nprogressed, to allow the modern man to draw parallels between this time and the times before.\n\n-Edward Winter II\n\nThe First Age of Kings\n600s-mid 1300s\nOn the Continent of Aegis and Asulon\nKings from the houses of Perea, Sheffield, Tarus, Horen, Marius, de Nurem\nAlso known as: Aegisian Ages, the First Unrest\n\nIn the first years of recorded history, there was one Oren\n\nformed by the conquering lords of the House Horen, who united many smaller sovereign feudatories into one nation. The last reigning king from the first regnal dynasty was King Daniel Horen, whose seneschal took the crown in a coup, and styled himself King\n\nPampo Perea. Upon his death, his own seneschal, King Edmund Sheffield, took power. King Edmund was then corrupted by the Undead and tried to eat the flesh of his wife and himself died. He was succeeded by his son, King Enor Sheffield.\n\nThe Sheffield\n\nDynasty was fraught with inaction and sloth, and in a coup known as the Phoenix Rebellion, Zibaen Vivayean and Eze'kiel Tarus split from the kingdom and formed their own, called Renatus, with Eze'kiel as king. King Enor Sheffield granted the remainder of\n\nOren to the Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order, Gaius Marius, who named it Hanseti.\n\nHochmeister Gaius Marius died, and he was succeeded by Hochmeister Samuel Bealcrest. The King Eze'kiel Tarus, fearing the military threat of the Teutons,\n\ndemanded their disbandment. The resolution of the ensuing war occurred when King Eze'kiel met a sariant, a soldier of the Teutonic Order, in a duel and was defeated.\n\nThe Kingdom of Salvus was formed on a nearby island by the dethroned Enor\n\nSheffield, alongside his wife Dawn Perea. They lived apart from the warfare of the human realm for a short while. On the mainland, King Eze'kiel left his governance to his regent, Reynard Lycian.\n\nThe kingdoms' citizens moved to a new continent when an\n\nundead plague threatened their survival on Aegis, and were joined by the newly founded Kingdom of Seventis. This new kingdom joined Renatus in defending against an assault by the Realm of Hanseti, the dwarven Kingdom of Urguan, the Kingdom of Salvus, the\n\nmulti-racial Kingdom of Alras, and the Orcish war-state.\n\nUrguan, Salvus, and Hanseti then aligned themselves against Renatus, Seventis, Alras, the Orcs, and a dissident faction within Salvus led by Lorethos Basileus called the Twilight Army. Salvus was\n\ndefeated, and was absorbed into Renatus. The noble House of Hightower was given control of the Salvian realm. Seventis was shortly after stricken with plague and devastated, and its lands too were absorbed into Renatus. The then-Hochmeister Mirtok de\n\nNurem, following a conflict with Renatus and an internal dissident faction called the Wolverines, surrendered his lands too to Godfrey Horen, a politician who had been handed control of Renatus and later was crowned Emperor of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v2", "§bBishop Cordal", "A History of Humanity, From Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume II: The First Empire\n\nThe First Empire\nmid 1300s-1430s\nOn the Continents of Asulon and Anthos and the land of Elysium\nEmperors Godfrey Horen I, Horen V, William Horen III\nAlso known as: The Era of Godfrey, the Golden Age, the Imperium Primus\n\nThe first empire grew\n\nand diversified. Many noble houses emerged, and the empire was broken down into more than twenty smaller feudatories. Notable among these was the House Chivay of Rivia, who formed a military larger than any ever seen before called the Order of the White\n\nRose. \n\nA rebellion against the new Horen dynasty was led by the House Tarus, but was defeated with the help of intelligence gathered by the Hochmeister de Nurem, who then left on an expedition to distant lands and abdicated to Hochmeister Dain\n\nFarhammer. In an intra-imperial conflict, the noble House of Flay made war with the Teutons, and left only tatters of the Teutonic Order in their wake.\n\nSoon rising waters threatened the lowlands of Asulon, and the Empire's citizens sailed across\n\nthe sea to the better-positioned continent of Anthos. There, Hochmeister Mirtok reunited with the remaining Teutons and reformed the order. There the Empire subdivided into the Kingdom of Salvus to the south, the Kingdom of Hanseti to the North, and the\n\nImperial Crownlands of Renatus to the East, but all remained ruled by the Emperor Godfrey Horen.\n\nThe Princedom of Malinor, of the elves, lay to the west. It was conquered by the Empire of Oren, and its country-land was given to Peter Chivay of the Rose,\n\nwho styled himself King of Kaedrin, while the capital of Malinor was made a city-state subservient to the empire.\n\nThe House Flay, renamed Blackmont, married into the royal House Chivay. Their two militaries became allies and frequently came into\n\nconflict with the Teutonic Order. In a series of three battles, the House Flay and their vassal House Carrion, the auvergnian House Valois, and the House Chivay and the Rose defeated the Teutonic Order and the Houses of Baelish, Ishikawa, the royal House\n\nHightower of Salvus, and an organization of mages called the Arcane Delvers. The Emperor then disbands the Teutonic Order, its fortress of Greywyn lying dormant. The Emperor Godfrey Horen then died, and his son Horen V took the throne.\n\nFeeling threatened\n\nby the growing might of humanity, the southern foreign powers of the orcs, elves, kharajyr, and dwarves banded together and launched an attack on the southernmost crossroads into Oren. They were soundly defeated and survivors were routed deeply back into\n\nthe lands of the dwarves.\n\nThe Emperor Horn V was then divinely inspired to travel with his court and the Rose to the distant continent of Aeldin, and abdicated the throne to his son William III. However, the Kingdom of Salvus saw this change of power as\n\nan opportunity, and broke oaths to side with the foreign powers, resulting in a chain of collapses within the Empire ending in Emperor William III styling himself King William III of Oren, over the much diminished remaining land.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v4", "§bBishop Cordal", "The History of Humanity from Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume IV: The Second Empire\n\nThe Second Empire\n1431-1447\nOn the Continent of Anthos\nEmperor Siegmund Carrion\nAlso known as: The Time of Crows, the Imperium Secundus\n\nThe Carrions emerged from the Second Age of Kings in command of humanity, and did so\n\nwithout interruption for several years. Siegmund's rule began with the systematic execution and seizure of property by Otto and Tuv Carrion from all of the first empire nobles that remained loyal to House Horen, wiping the slate clean for a new\n\nRaevir-dominated nobility. His reign was a quiet one, and primarily foccused on rebuilding a unified state after the Second Age of Kings. There was a short rebellion by Empress-claimant Sophia Horen, who was backed by several disenfranchised nobles of the\n\nFirst Empire, but it fell into disorder after a year. \n\nAnother rebellion followed, led by descendants of Eze'kiel Tarus, the Teutonic Order, and dwarves who challenged the Carrion's right-to-throne in open rebellion.\n\nSeveral prominent families of the First Empire also joined Horen and Tarus. The House Stafyre was almost pushed into joining when then-High Pontiff, who styled himself High Ecclesiarch Radomir I, nearly flogged a Stafyr for defending a heretic. However,\n\nthe Stafyrs were persuaded to back the empire, and their castle was used to garrison Orenian troops bolstered by the Church's Order of Saint Lucien in a victorious defense against the rebel coalition.\n\nIt was not too many years later that the\n\nEmperor Siegmund Carrion died of age, and in his will dissolved the second empire into its constituent states of the Kingdom of Oren and the Kingdom of Herendul.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "SapphireShard", "Greetings, Rosanna.\n\nI am delighted by your interest in our order.\n\nCurrently we have very few members since we got purged by the now-deceased 'Holy Oren Empire', so we're lacking in numbers - hence my slow reply - I have\n\n  extremely busy as of late.\n\nIf you wish to come to the Temple soon, please reply with a date and time and I will endeavour to be there.\n\n - Neri", ""),
        StaticBook("Rebirth of Evil", "§bLily Enrique", "She awoke in dire pain and confusion as the livelihood of the Crimson Fist’s purpose and existence, literally, weighed heavily upon her. The Champion's mind sporadically showed images of a battle that just collapsed the temple containing most, if not all,\n\nof the Crimson Fist, sending them to an early demise. Shouts meant to be full of victory turned into blood curdling screams of pain and death as they were overrun by their adversaries, the Holy Vanguard. As she clawed at the gravel and dirt that trapped\n\nher, she tried listening to her surroundings for others survivors calling out to her, their Champion. But all her ears could hear were the cracking, sliding, and grinding of the stone walls collapsing inward on her and the others. She could see the\n\nlook of horror and death in the eyes of her brethren as stone collaped on them, toruting her mind. Forcing her bloody and gashed hands to sift quicker through the rubble in an attempt to escape. Her hands, digging and sifting faster, trying to escape the\n\nmemories of her life that was quickly collapsing around her. But the images and sounds only seemed to come faster as she struggled, keeping in tempo with her movements.§0\n§0\n§0With a heavy grunt and thrust, she forced her arm through a\n\nsmall lift opening, finally feeling the cool air wrap itself around her skin. This simple thing volstered her will, giving her the strength to push herself through the small opening and back into the outside world. The Elven woman lay there in the cool\n\nmorning fog for what seemed like an eternity, time completely lost to her, breathing in deep the fresh moist air. Slowly, from the dense fog, a shadowy figure approaches her exhausted self and shoves a bow and arrow into her face. Panting, the woman looks\n\nup at the figure as he pulls back his hood, revealing the rugged features of a worn huntsman. The man pulled back the weapon slightly and asked for her name.§0\n§0\n§0\"M-My name...\" the Elven woman spoke between labored breaths, \" is Cora.\"\n\nSeeing her state, the huntsman took pity on Cora and led her to his dwelling in the forest, far from the rubble and ashes of the tower. There, he fed and dressed her wounds, nursing her back to health. Cora slowly came around to the man, however knew all\n\ntoo well how easy it is for one to lower their guard around those they trust, but she made sure never to speak about the Crimson Fist. When he questioned her about her past, she simply said that she was a servant to the people that owned the, now, pile of\n\nrubble and ash that he found her at, not entirely a lie but only a partial truth. The man nodded, knowing it rude to question a person's past from his own experiences, and went about his business. However, no matter how hard he tried to focus on his tasks\n\nhe was mesmerized by Cora's beauty and soon felt for her. Cora, knowing that the Crimson Fist was either utterly destroyed or scattered to the winds, accepted the huntsman's affection with open arms and soon gave birth to a child of a rare complexion. The\n\nchild's skin was pale like snow, his hair like fine straws of white gold, and his eyes...crimson like blood. Because of his defining eyes, Cora named him Haemon, the Blood Child.\n\nHaemon's features were the most exciting thing about his dull life in the\n\nforest. His father taught him how to string a bow, to catch a fish, to chop wood, and skin a kill. He promised to take him hunting when he was rightfully a man and left Haemon in charge of keeping order at home when he left on his numerous hunting trips.\n\nSurprisingly, Cora took to motherhood quite well. Her swift and accurate hands that once sliced a man's throat before they could blink now directed a needle and thread through cloth; her strength and determination that kept her alive during fights with\n\narmed guards during assasinations now carried in loads of firewood and clean wash. She watched over Haemon throughout the years grow in to a fine young man, but also watched herself age. She knew that with her death, the Crimson Fist and all of its\n\nunfinished work died as well. So, as her husband left on one of his hunting trips, Cora brought Haemon into the cellar of their small home. There, she had him swear to keep this information privy, even from his father, and showed him the history of her\n\npeople, his people. Haemon was fascinated with the rituals, chants, stories, and tales of the infamous Crimson Fist. He begged his mother to know all of there was, and so, every time the huntsman left, Cora took her son to the cellar and taught him.\n\nThis continued for many years until the night before Haemon's eighteenth birthday. The huntsman returned home early, carrying a finely crafted bow to gift his maturing son. However, he approached a dark and still home. Quickly entering the home he noticed\n\nthe fire and candles had been recently snuffed. The darkness of the home, however, did allow the light from under the cellar door to draw his attention. The room filled with light as he pulled it open, and his earsd were met with the voices of his family.\n\nAs he descended the stairs he found his family, naked with painted symbols on their bodies, dancing around an animal's carcass that sat next to a blue flame. Haemon was the first to notice his father, quickly dropping his arms and backing away in shame.\n\nCora noticed her son's change and turned, meeting the horrified gaze of her husband. He softly questioned her, but she remained silent, afraid to unveil the lies they had been keeping. The huntsman became angry, gripping his wife by the arms and shouting,\n\ndemanding anwers, begging her to explain to him why she lied to him. But it was Haemon that noticed the fire in the center of the room growing larger, and only Haemon that heard the flame commanding him to stop his father. Haemon covered his ears, trying\n\nto escape the raspy voice in his head, demanding the boy to act! Haemon shut his eyes and screamed, and then suddenly, silence filled the room. His slowly opening eyes found his hand around a bloody knife, thrusted deeply into his father's back. Blood\n\nleaked from the innocent man, darting to the fire at the center of the room, eventually reaching the firey claws of the flame. With an immense heat and power, the flame jumped high and turned crimson. Haemon now became drawn to the fire, walking to it.\n\nCora reached out and screamed silently as the flames enveloped her son. Haemon did not feel the flame burn his skin, but felt it burn his insides, as if it reached into his heart and soul and turned them to ash. He could not scream, nor react to the pain\n\nhis mind felt. His vision slowly became dark and blurred, his sense of feeling seemed to numb away, and his mind began to close in on itself. The flames danced high and the heat reached Cora, causing her to become dazed by the light until she fainted.\n\nWhen Cora woke the next morning in her bed she quickly wretched onto the floor. The nightmare was so real to her, the heat of the fire, the smell of blood, the image of her son being consumed by the fire, all shook her deeply. She struggled out of bed and\n\nwalked down to the kitchen, finding it cold and dark as it was every morning. She started a fire and hung a pot of water to biol as she called out to Haemon to wake. However, he did not return her call. When she checked his bed, she found it vacant and\n\nundisturbed from the previous morning's making. Fear struck at her as she turned to look at the closed cellar door. Slowly approaching it and wrapping her hand round the latch, she closed her eyes as she opened it and was greeted by nothing but darkness\n\nand the smell of burnt flesh. At the bottom of the staircase she could see her husband's burnt skeleton in the same spot it laid in her nightmare. She cried out and slammed the cellar shut, turning to run from the house.\n\nBut a figure stood in the doorway, blocking her escape. It stood still, shadowed from the sun coming up behind it. Its glowing, deep crimson eyes were its only distinguishable characteristic. The figure spoke to her with two voices, both familiar but from\n\ndifferent times of her past, different lives. She covered her mouth and screamed into her hand as it spoke to her.\n\n\n\"Hello, Mother\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ of Passage", "§bTuvya", "*Seal of House Carrion*\n------------------\nThe Company of the Raven is given the right of passage of Emperor Tuvya Sigismundovic Carrion; to be unaccosted wherever their members may travel.\n\n*Tuv's signature*", ""),
        StaticBook("Jemila", "§bAyita", "If you need me to return the stuff \n3 iron blocks\none song disk\nI will return them", ""),
        StaticBook("Menu", "§bKetiley Strong-Heart", "The Hall of The\n       Hundred Meadhall\n\n\n           Item Menu\n\nDrinks (Alcohol)\nSoft Drinks\nFood\nDeserts\nSpecial Drinks\n\nThe Hundred Sons' Golden-\nA very smooth, heavenly, but hard, mead that's like tasting the Bledssed Isle.\n10 Minas\nBloodborne Ale-\nA heavy, red, dark ale, that'll most likely knock you on your arse.\n7 Minas\nBlackberry Spiced Wine-\nA smooth, light, and\n\ncrisp wine that will coat your throat and tastebuds in a good time.\n7 Minas\nKetiley's Secret-\nA Mixture of premade Jagermiester, Goldschlager, and peach snops.\n8 Minas\n\nSoft Drinks:\nMilk - 2 Minas\nWater - Free\nApple Juice - 2 Minas\nOrange Juice - 2 Minas\nHot Apple Cider - 3 Minas\nLemonade - 3 Minas\n\nTea:\nRosemary and Cinnamon -\n1 Mina\nLavendar and Peppermint -\n2 Minas\n\nPassionfruit and Rasberry\n3 Minas\n\nFoods:\nSweet Delight:\nGolden roasted bread baked in with Lavendar, cinnamon, and Peppermint.\n0.5 Minas\nThe Isle's Toast:\nA slice of Sweet Delight topped with 'peanut butter', Cinnamon, and 'powdered' sugar.\n0.5 Minas\n\nGrilled Chicken -\nChicken grilled to perfection and marinated in lemon slices, carrots, mixed herbs, butter, and lime juice and cooked over oak to offer a hickery taste.\n3 Minas\nSalior's Delight -\nSavoury boiled fish chopped into bits to float in harmony\n\nlemon, crushed pepper, mixed herbs, and chicken broth.\n5 Minas\nGrilled Fish -\nDeliciously grilled salmon or cod preboiled in water, lemon, cinnamon, basil, mixed herbs, tamatoes, garlic, and scallions then put into a low flamed oven to grill.\n2 Minas\n\nFilet Mignon -\nPan-seared steak cut to precise messurments, topped with a secret garlic sauce and merinated in carrots, chicken broth, meat seasonings, and egg whites.\n5 Minas\nThe Pig's Gift -\nA lovely porkchop topped with melted pepperjack and marinated\n\nwith carrots, onions, grilled mushrooms, chicken broth, and mixed herbs.\n5 Minas\nChicken Soup -\nSavoury grilled chicken diced and set to boil with light and fluffy Chiocciole noodles, carrots, onions, scallions, basil, black crushed pepper,\n\nand diced potatoes.\n5 Minas\nFrozen Ice 'cream' -\nLusciously milky frozen cream with fruit blends diced into small bits included with banana, pineapple, apple, and pomegranate.\n\nDesserts:\nPumpkin Pie -\nA light and fluffy pie with a mashed pumpkin center added with Cinnamon and a crust made with peppermint, vanilla, and lavendar.\n6 Minas\nApple Tarts -\nHeart sliced apples baked into small tartlets with lavendar, cinnamon,\n\nvanilla, and crushed almonds added with a creamy apple center.\n4 Minas\nHazelnut Pudding -\nRich and fluffy pudding with cinnamon, vanilla, hazelnut, and small bits of bananas added into the gooey goodness.\n3 Minas\n\nSugar Cookies -\nLush and velvety cookies mixed in with lavendar and sugar; golden on the outside and soft on the inside to melt deliciously in your mouth.\n\nFrozen Ice 'Cream' -\nLuciously milky frozen cream with blends of diced up fruits like banana, raspberry, passionfruit, dragonfruit, strawberry, pineapple, orange, blueberry, chocolate, and vanilla.\n3 Minas\n\nSpecial Drinks:\nGrog -\nA dark drink that will jumpstart your body to work when it's weary. Rather bitter with a sweet tinge. ((Coffee))\n0.2 Minas\nChilled Wtermelon & Sterberry Tea -\nA lovely blend of watermelon and strawberry\n\nchunks in the watered-down juices of the fruit, chilled.\n0.5 Minas\nSparkling Elderberry -\nA chilled elderberry drink that seems to bubble and 'sparkle' with sodium, making the drink rather fun.\n0.7 Minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Drink Menu", "§bKetiley Strong-Heart", "The Hall of The Hundred\n             Meadhall\n\nAlcoholic Drinks selection:\n\nThe Hundred Sons' Golden\n\nBloodborne Ale\n\nBlackberry Spiced Wine\n\nKetiley's Secret\n\nThe Hundred Sons' Golden:\n\nA very smooth, heavenly, golden, but hard mead that tastes like sipping the Blessed Isle. This is a Gorundyr special and can only be found in Anthos, though a very select few Gorundyr still know it.\n\n25 Minas for 5 Gallons\n\nBloodeborne Ale:\n\nA heavy, red, dark ale that will most lightly knock you on your arse. It has a heavy liquor scent and taste, but slides smoothly down the throat.\n\n18 Minas for 5 Gallons\n\nBlackberry Spiced Wine:\n\nA smooth, light, and crisp wine that will coat the throat and tastebuds in a relaxing good time. This wine is great for parties or a get-to-gether involving alcohol.\n\n18 Minas for 5 Gallons\n\nKetiley's Secret:\n\nA mixture of premade alcoholic drinks listed -\nJagermiester, Goldschlager, and Peach Schnopps.\nThis drink is quite hard but offers a peppermint and licorice scent and taste with a small bit of peach.\n\n19 Minas for 5 Gallons", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy", "§bLemik Rextiureus", "Dear Roopak,\n\nI wish to place a very specific order. I am going to create an area where you or your company shall be gavering Alchemecila ingredients. We shall have an are where you break the grass and till the land continously. This is the fastest-\n\n-way to find alchemical ingredients as many are buried jus underground. \n\n-Lemik Rextiureus", ""),
        StaticBook("Unknown", "§bRilkor Niwarsay", "It's been 3 hours since her departure, my emotions are fully intact. It's before and after I felt the breath of lonliness reach down ny back. The quickest you'll read this is 3 days after and i assure I'm fine on this day. But what I express is only a\n\nmoment. The before times were different then, this. She had to change her skin, a simple task indeed. It was there I awaited for hours on end for her return. I was feeling lost hope, hoping for the best on that day. It was then when she had returned, that\n\nI was filled with glee, but there was crushed dreams and I awaited her again. It was then I awakened, and awaited for her once again. This, time there were no distractions of work, so I stayed in this realm, doing little tasks. I could not tell what I\n\nfelt. I was waiting for hours and hours on end losing all hope for a second time. It was then that you did return for long times I awaited and now I was happy to see you here. However it was very short-lived you leaved ever so soon it was then you gave me\n\na poem showing many things for our second-life alike. It was as I read that poem that I noticed what I had felt. As I read that poem I started to tear up seeing everything in perspective. I lay there reading only hearing the sounds of the earth and water\n\nand flames and distant monsters that hid being my fortress which once you were in. I felt many feelings of unexplained I felt a need to tell you this. But the only one way I could dream of that hope is the green letters that would show. I felt a strange\n\ntype of lonliness after that, a strange one yes indeed. I knew that I was alone with the sounds I usually heard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Blue Moon Inn", "§bDaycia Polyian", "*Menu*\nSailor’s Delight Stew 8 minas\n\n\nA delightful stew containing the freshest fish in town and cooked vegetables  that's pleasurable to eat while on the high seas!\n\nWhole Wheat Bread\n5 Minas\n\nA warm, soft bread made out of the finest dough made out of the finest wheat.\n\nBlackberry Spiced Wine\n8 minas\n\nA dark, shimmering, purple wine that smells of blackberries. It is smooth, crisp, and refreshing.\n\nBloodbourne Ale\n8 minas\n\nA blood-red ale with a heavy liquor scent and taste, but is very smooth and smells of cherries and raspberries.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Macecatcher", "§bGoobly Fancyhat", "-+-         \n\n       Macecatcher,\n         The Play\n\n         -+-\n\n        Written By\n    Vaerus Varaadul\n\n         -+-\n       C a s t\n\nHigh King Lachlan Mor\nAdunian Bannerman 1\nAdunian Bannerman 2\nKilted War Elephant\nKing Carrion\nKraltan Militia 1\nKraltan Militia 2\n\n         -+-\n\n\n\n         -+-\n\n \n        ACT I\n\n\n         -+-\n\nunfinished play, found by Faiz but written by Vaerus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sudden Valley", "§bthanndreli", "Difficulty: ET required.\n\nSudden Valley Mausoleum. Its current appearance masks the conflict between the clergy that took place leading up to its current state. Now the undead rise within the catacombs, devouring all those who venture in.\n\nLucienists, purge the undead from the Sudden Valley Mausoleum and discover what had happened. GOD WILLS IT!\n\nDEUS MAGNUS!", ""),
        StaticBook("Criminal Sketch", "§bIsabella Deathsbane", "*A sketch of a man is here. He has brown hair, brown eyes, and a beard. He appears to be human, with a sturdy, strong build. \n\nThe face is drawn in great detail, the nose long, the lips thin behind his beard. \n\nHe wears light armor.*\n\n*Overall, the drawing is a shockingly close likeness to Calvin Headsted. Even with some ink lines crossing each other he's quite easy to recognize.*\n\nThis man abuses children he falsely adopted. He goes by the name 'John'.\n\nHe supposedly lives with the\n\nvictim's mother, a blonde haired green eyed woman who is 'slightly' pale, a Mali'aheral or perhaps Mali'ame.\nThe child says she is called Lauirinia.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Retirement", "§bHigh Prince Haelphon", "The Resignation\n            of\n High Prince Haelphon\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTranscribed by Ebs\n\nFriends if I may have your eyes for a small moment~\nTimes have come and gone, like night and day. I grow old now, only seeing a few timely years left on my life, and I believe it be in our best interests for me to retire\n\nfrom our holy position as High Prince of the Council and Nation of Malinor.\n'Tis painful for myself to depart from the position in which the majority of my life was dedicated to reaching.\n\nRegardless decisions, I started my life as a young boy in Oren. The capitol city of Al'Khazar housed me for years, until I departed after the untimely death of my father in the first undead raids of New-Aegis.\n\nAt that time, I was just a young man in my teen-years.\nTwenty long years after this event, I felt my Elvish routes calling me to Laurelin, a place in which both my parents kept me from seeing, as I was to success my father as I grew up. Upon my return\n\nto Aegis, I was quickly prompted by my new and dear friends Bircalin, Aedan, Romanen, and Verigan to head to Al'Khazar once more, to pursue the duties of a guard at the front gates of the majestic city. There I met my second closest friend\n\n(brother by law), and my Lieutenant at the time, Eze'kiel Tarus.\nFrom there, I returned from Oren to start learning in the druidic arts of trees, in which I was educated by the High Prince Native upon my first few years in Malinor.\n\nI lost contact with Bircalin at that point, and the grand \"Tree-Growing Competition\" in which the most fantastic arts were ever bestowed before my eyes! This began my first dependency on the Elvish Council of Malinor.\n\nI was inducted into the realm as the 'Tree-Lord'; one who maintains trees for Malinor, as well as grew them for the uprising Sister City. 'Twas the best moments of my life whilst I was with my love. My love Felore, was a lovely Warden\n\nin the Elvish military. My dear friends Aedan and Indelwehn introduced me to her, as they felt I was lonely. *chuckles* Oh my, how I was! Those were some of the best years in my life. Post marriage, we happily celebrated our two twin children~ Our daughtr\n\n Draera and our son, Polcari the III. Life continued on, as I frequented Malinor's different cities working as the 'Tree-Lord.'\nAs life progressed, the threat of the undead was rising. I met my fiance, Valer D'Avore and lived in peace\n\nwith her for years, until our split after four years time. Malin bless her for putting up with my insolence. Recent happenings had caused urgent business for our High Prince Native, who was needed elsewhere in Aegis, and could no longer continue\n\nhis duties as the High Prince. It was a troubling scene for us all, who most had known Native their entire lives. The council, then was short on members, inducted Princess Indelwehn into the council as the illustrious High Princess.\n\nMalinor was overjoyed with this selection, and Malinor once again began to prosper.\nA few months after Indelwehn's election, I was added into the Holy Council of Malinor as a Prince, a duty in which I served up to the last breaths of Aegis.\n\nUpon exactly six moons before the destruction of Aegis, as well as my closest friend Bircalin (Whom I grieve for every night of my further existence) I was voted into the Council as the High Prince of Malinor. The duty, I have held for almost\n\n thirty years now, at this current time.\nAs I state, I do indeed grow old~ The allocations of the High Elven thought of me as being \"half-breed\" is of course true, yet my nation refused to disbelieve this in Laurelin. My age grows short,\n\nas my remainder of my days will be happily spent farming in Renatus, with my brother Eze'kiel. He in-fact requested I become a member of the Tarus family! I could not turn down a family once again.\n\nFor those who wish to know my final words as High Prince of Malinor:\nAll elves, I beseech you to coincide as you once did in Laurelin, under the backing of High Prince Native, High Princess Indelwehn, and I; High Prince Haelphon.\n\n It has been a fascinating journey of the times, to participate in a life long event to hold true to the last moments. Serve your nations well, and appreciate everything you see in life, regardless your beliefs. For those who ever seek my blade,\n\nI remain for you. I shall continue to serve Malinor as a diplomatic holder, for relations.\nAnd the time has come, my friends~ at last: a new leader for Malinor.\n\"I, High Prince Haelphon Addechio, leader of the illustrious Malinor:\n\nDo solemnly give my remaining powers to the successor of my self.\nThe two votes I have in my power to select, I give to thee~\n-One for my new friend, Prince Bravepaw of Malinor\n\n-One for my dear sister in the council, Princess Sythra Duskwind of Malinor.\nChoose wisely, Elves; as it will impact your futures to the greatest beholder.\nWith that, I bid you a kind farewell,\n\nAnd a wonderful future in Asulon.\nWarmest Regards,\n~High Prince Haelphon Addechio (Polcari Addechio the II) of Malinor", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidology", "§bRespiren", "~Druidology~\n\nDruids are the druii, the dryw, the druwid.\n\nNature's sorcerer, the seer, the oak-knower.\n\nFor those that know the oak, the trēow is both the tree and the truth.\n\n\n\nMysterious guardian of a sacred grove, wise counselor to monarchs, cunning master of many shapes, friend of animals, and terrible defender of unspoiled Nature.\n\n\n\nThe Druid revere Nature, wielding power over plants, animals, the weather, and the elements.\n\nAll druids are of neutral alignment and share an ethos devoted to protecting the wilderness and maintaining natural cycles and a balance between good and evil.\n\n~Scribed by Wayward\nDruid Respiren", ""),
        StaticBook("Book o' Regents", "§bRilkor Niwarsay", "Rilkor's Great Big Book of Regents\n-------------------This is a Botany and Regent Book\n-------------------In the great big lands of Athera, there are many different assortments of plants and possible regents in alchemy.\n\nUpon my travels I have found and discovered many. In here, I will list how to acquire said ingredients and their affiliated symbol.\n-------------------\n\n-------------------M", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grand Drake", "Matthew_Hollis", "His power is unmatched by any force in Anthos, and he offers it to those he deems worthy, and those who assist his cause. Setherien, the great one, has already infiltrated several nations at high ranking levels and will continue to assault, all will fall.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Stormhammers", "§b[Saviour][Dungrimm Preacher] Clan Elder Odin Ireheart", "_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_    The Stormhammers\n           And\n      The Irehearts\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\n\nThe Clan of the stormhammers is a slection of Dwarven folk who come from a military background, or a dwarven background of some other sort to\n\nit mining or trade. Their numbers often are found to be soldiers of the Legion who hve served within the order under the Clan Father Kjell Stormhammer formerly know as Kjell Ireheart clan father of the Irehearts.\n\n-------------------  Founding Lord's Tale\n-------------------\nThe paragon Kjell Ireheart is a dwarf of remarkable feats of which have been committed during the great wars of the races nearing the end of the second age, The Ireheart clan the same Kjell\n\neheart was the\nfather of faded from history and over all existance mainly due to conflict with\nthe undead threats of the north along with conflicts against the Orcish hoards as during these times turmoil drove the Dwarves to rapidly thinning numbers\n\nwhich the Starbreakers and Irehearts suffered the worst of. Kjell being the\nlast of his kind began a quest to unite the clanless Dwarves after witnessing the dark ages of the Dwarves, hopefully with one day with the aid of the\n\nBrathmordakin the clanned ones as well under one banner. \n\n-------------------       Third Age\n-------------------The Origin of the clan was first conceived under a peculiar name the Grim Brotherhood during the third age when the time the\n\n Clans fought and conflicted with one another over power, land and\nrights to riches of the Kingdom. This spurred the Grim Brotherhood to be made\nduring the reign of the Boneless King Hiebe Irongut whom at the time widely\nbelieved by Dwarves\n\nwas conspiring with the other races to seize a tyrannical\ncontrol over \"his\" people and due to these claims a hidden revolution\nwas born starting with three Dwarves each blessed by the Brathmordakin through\ndiscovering hidden and ancient armour with\n\noutstanding capabilities, these three\nDwarves Gorum and Goruk Frostbeard along with Paragon Kjell Ireheart combined\ntheir efforts to fuel a hidden rebellion, this was until a conflict between the Paragon and a elven\n\ncommander whom worked under the favor of the Boneless King.\nDuring this time Kjell exposed the elf of his crimes against himself and his\nkin the Dwarves thus creating a grudge against the elf but after refusal from the King Hiebe to allow\n\nthe elf to be punished under the constitution the\nParagon Kjell began to aim his efforts to further fuel his rebellion towards\nthe royalty slandering the King's folk the Ironguts for the heinous acts they have committed.\n\nThis feuding between King and Paragon was brought to the halls\nof the city and the council's court with outbursts of rage coming from both\nsides all of which where accompanied by threats, after discovering the attempt of Dun Irongut's\n\ndenouncing of the Paragon's holy title with the aid of Hiebe\nIrongut the rebellion finally began as the Tyrant attempted to arrest the\nParagon for treason in which a agreement was made on both behalves that the King and Paragon would answer for their\n\ncrimes towards one another. This did\nnot come to pass as the nearing end of the third age was closed by a darkness\nonly the Paragon and the elders of the Dwarves themselves where familiar with, the evil forces of Khovard pushed the people of Asulon\n\nfrom their homes and\nhalls including the Dwarves and due to this the Paragon along with the King\nmade amends to fight for their Kingdom's survival to reach the new lands.\n\n-------------------       Fourth Age\n-------------------\nDuring this time the clan Stormhammer was truly created\nafter the Boneless King Hiebe was removed of throne by the True Grand King Thorik who was recovered from the volcano after\n\nhaving believed to have been\nassassinated by the Grimhall clan's Dwarves a selection of Architects who for\nreasons unknown went Stark Raving Mad. With the crowning of the Grand King Thorik, plans within the Paragon's head to unite the Dwarves\n\nbegan to run as he\nbegan his negotiations with the Goldhands to bind his clan the Irehearts with\ntheir folk, this first coined the clan's true name Stormhammer and provided for\nit's first members. But after discovering the leader of the Goldhands Thoak\n\nSludgefist intoxicated himself far beyond his capability to understand words\nthe drunken Clan Lord mistook the Paragon's sayings believe the Goldhands would merely aid in the creation of the clan thus causing a predicament for the clan lord of the\n\nStormhammers.\n-------------------          Trials\n-------------------To become an Ireheart within the Ireheart clan you must complete the trials. \n\nThey are slaying the raw hides of three different colours of Orc.\n\nCutting off the ear of different skinned elves and trying it to a rople to form a necklace. \n\nClaiming the bark of a dryad's life tree. \n\nOnce the tests are completed the individual must hand them to the clan father. At this point\n\nthe Ire blooding ceremony will begin. After the ceremony is done. The Individual will become an Ireheart. \n\n-------------------         Religion\n-------------------The stormhammers are strict followers of the Brathmordahkin and are mostly\n\nfollowers of their patron god Dungrimm, many Stormhammers are known to be very zealous and have on multiple occasions killed in the name of Dungrimm. The Ireheart rite actually involves being within the Clergy district and standing in front of the\n\nDungrimm Shrine.\n\n-------------------          Values\n-------------------\nHonour is a great value for any dwarf and for the Stormhammer’s inparticular. They devote their lives to obtaining a strict code  of honour and work\n\nvery hard in keeping to this code. The Stormhammer’s are known to battle with honour and are known across the land for their honourable deeds. \n\nThe Stormhammers are known to be a very loyal clan and have stuck by the Kingdom\n\nsince their creation. They never think twice before thinking about the betterment of their Kingdom and always do things that will have a good effect on the Kingdom and their clan. \n\nThe clan is one of the most devoted clans in dwarven history,\n\nthey have worked tirelessly for their Kingdom and have built many structures for the Kingdom in the past. Alot of their members have held high positions in dwarven society and are known for having done an amazing job while having them.\n\nhe Stormhammer’s are very well known for their religious zealotry and have often been found killing in the name of their patron god Dungrimm. All of their members are devoted to Dungrimm and would die if their god commanded such. They have followed him\n\nsince the birth of the clan. \n\nThe Stormhammer’s are known for their bravery on and off the battlefield and some of their members have killed thousands upon thousands of enemies. The clan is known to not fear anything\n\nand have sometimes gone into battle with nothing but a sword dressed in war paint and slaying hundreds of enemies. \n\nThe Stormhammers were originally founded as “The Grim Brotherhood” and held those values very high, they are known\n\nfor their great respect for eachother no matter each members past. They have always and will always have great respect for eachother and dwarves alike.\n\nThere are many other traditions, holds and artifacts yet that can be obtained by asking\n\na Ireaheart or Stormhammer!", ""),
        StaticBook("Abominations", "§bVarkid", "Abominations\n  An observation of\nthe lesser succubus.\n@=---------------=@\n\nThe lesser succubus, name varying between regions but typically following the theme of, \"Frost Demon,\" is a magic-oriented abomination found to exploit the weakness of men. \n\nVarying in form but always female, these creatures are of blue-ish almost\n\ngrey skin, have edged teeth and are occasionally depicted as having claws. This said, the creatures frequently hide their forms behind a relatively weak magic and by taking preemptive action, most issues with these creatures can be curbed.\n\nCombating  the  Threat -------------------\n\nStep One:\n  Identify the threat.\n\nWhen in the company of a strange woman or suspected atrocity, a physical check of the figure is required.\n\nAsk to see the teeth of the figure. Should they be blatantly abnormal and sharp, outcome is obvious. \n\nThe creature is deathly cold to the touch. As if made of ice and snow. \n\n- Nothing like a room cooled moist cloth.\n\nStep two\n  Assault.\n\nShould you be unfortunate enough to have your hand near it's mouth, well, hope for the best. Immediately retract your hand and put space between yourself and the target.\n\nShould you be a bystander, immediately notify the local guardsmen.\n\nShould you be alone, well, a judgement call is absolutely needed. Do you think yourself capable of killing a mage or any form? Can you kill it quickly?\n\nStep Three:\n   Aftermath.\n\nDue to the abnormal nature of the creatures, immediate purging by fire is suggested. Should a cleric or priest be within range, request their hand in the matter.\n\nFinal Notes:\n\n\nThe creatures attempt to come across as helpless and may request escort to isolated sections of a city.  - Never escort a female stranger alone.\n\nThe creatures are mages. - If untrained in dealing with these sorts of enemies, simply run. Do not risk your in the name of pointless glory.\n\nKeep it away. - They take advantage of the desires of men. Take precautions when dealing with strangers.\n\nLastly, always travel with a group. We live in a dangerous world. Play it safe, never go it alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Yelbegkhai", "§bBahadir Abd Timuroğul al-Subudai", "The Yelbegkhai\n\n\n   recollections of a\n        lost tribe\n\n\n\n\n\n\n             by\n      Bahadir Abd\n        Timuroğul\n\n  To the common man of Athera, the word Subudai may evoke thoughts of barbarism, of backwards religion, and of savage culture.  Over time the Subudai Confederacy has lent to this image through its terrifyingly effective military campaigns and through\n\nits affiliation to the violent Uruks.  These fierce nomadic riders made their marks on history, despite how brief their tenure may have been.\n\n  The Subudai Confederacy was essentially a loose union of many different tribes. These tribes were united by\n\ncommon culture and by strong rule.  The Subudai were all equestrian people, seasonally nomadic, totemistic and shamanistic.  But it was the harsh nature of established human civilization that drove these tribes together, in order that they could preserve\n\ntheir ways.\n\n  However, these tribes were never always unified.  In ancient times, war was common and necessary among the tribes.  Slavery drove what industry there was among the nomadic camps.  Violence and death was a part of everyday life.  Boys\n\nand girls alike were expected to ride only a few years out of the womb, shoot a bow not a few months later, and take another’s life if it came to it.  Battle was as natural as the seasons to these tribes.  Honor was valued more than life.\n\nReligion was also a divider of the tribes.  Though every tribe had mystics and believed in the spirits, some preferred certain spirits, or worshipped different aspects of nature.  These differences may have been minor, but they were often enough to cause\n\nconflict.\n\nOne of these tribes, situated in the lands near the edge of the steppes, bordered by a dense and massive forest, was fundamentally different from the other tribes.  This forest tribe descended into the\n\nsteppe relatively late, but acquired the penchant for horseback nomadism to no lesser a degree than the other tribes.  It was from this remote corner of steppe lands that this tribe cultivated its culture apart from the other tribes.\n\nThese were the Yelbegkhai.\n\n  The Yelbegkhai came from a colder region compared to the other Subudai tribes, and their skin tones were slightly lighter to show that.    Their hair colors ranged from the dark brown and black of the common Subudai, to\n\ndirty-blonde and stunning silver hues.  There was even said to be an honorable, and noble-if that were a notion of their people-bloodline of Yelbegkhai with pale-blue eyes.  The common Subudai tribes often referred to the Yelbegkhai as radiant,\n\nbut not out of reverence, for the Yelbegkhai were hated and perceived as foreigners.\n\n  The Yelbegkhai culture differed in more than just their looks, however.  While the other tribes worshipped all the spirits, the Yelbegkhai\n\nworshipped the celestial bodies, their ancestors, a winged serpent deity, and the deity’s children, known as “Drulkai” in their tongue.  What we know now to be dragons are what were thought to roam the lands the ancient Yelbegkhai occupied.  It is said\n\nthat the most honorable Yelbegkhai riders wore mail made of dragon scales and wielded blades crafted from dragon teeth.  Some Yelbegkhai folk stories tell of wise mystics who could communicate with the dragons and who would live with them in\n\ntheir mountainous lairs.\n\n  Though these all are just stories, and none of the dragon scale or teeth artifacts have been recovered, it is well known that the Yelbegkhai tend to have mutualist relationships with the Vourukhai.  While many\n\nof the Subudai tribes participated in falconry for sport and sustenance, the most strong-willed of the Yelbegkhai often bonded with members of a nearby Vourukhai flock.  The flock that originally lived within the territory of the Yelbegkhai often\n\nrelocated over time, following the Yelbegkhai as they travelled throughout the lands of old.  It is thought that this flock remained with the Yelbegkhai when they joined the Subudai Confederacy, but it is not known if the Vourukhai continued on with the\n\nConfederacy or the united Subudai people through to Athera.\n\n  While the other tribes were focused on appeasing all the spirits, the Yelbegkhai were more concerned with appeasing their ancestors.  The Yelbegkhai believed after an honorable\n\nlife, the souls of the deceased passed into another realm where they could hunt and battle to their heart’s content, while also looking down into the realm of the living to watch their relatives.  Looking up to the night sky, the Yelbegkhai thought of\n\nevery star as an honorable rider or warrior who was looking down from the realm beyond.  Constellations were the sites of glorious battles, shooting stars were fearless lancers charging across the night sky towards the enemy, and the moon was the home of\n\nthe winged serpent god and all the honorable ancestors, where they would return to after a long night of battle.  Celebrations, rituals, sacrifices, and the likes were often held on a monthly cycle, dependent of the phase of the moon.\n\nEven with all the ancestor worship and the belief in the dragon deity, the Yelbegkhai acknowledged the spirits, and on some rare occasions would communicate with them through the mystics.\n\n  Through all these fundamental differences, the\n\nYelbegkhai remained hated and despised among the Subudai tribes.  War was constant between them.  This perpetual war crafted the Yelbegkhai into a battle-hardened tribe.  Though their horse-archers were not superior to the other Subudai tribes',\n\nthe Yelbegkhai had the most feared lancers and skirmishers among all the tribes.  The Yelbegkhai first employed the strict battlefield discipline and advanced maneuvers that is commonly thought of as Subudai today.  They would break their\n\nlines and separate, pulling the enemy apart, and then rally and concentrate a strong lancer offensive on the point where the enemy’s commander was located, while horse archers followed close behind picking off enemies on the flank.  It was through\n\ntheir military prowess that the Yelbegkhai were able to be absorbed into the Subudai Confederacy, despite their cultural differences.\n\n  It was in the Subudai Confederacy that the Yelbegkhai began to lose their tribal values.  Inter-tribal\n\nunions within the Confederacy led to a breaking down of Yelbegkhai culture.  Over time, the Yelbegkhai came to adopt the blanket moniker of Subudai, along with all the other similar Subudain tribes.  Assimilation melded the dragon-worshipping,\n\nradiant nomadic tribe in with the rest of the Subudai people, to be lost mostly to history.\n\n  It is said, however, that a great Yelbegkhai bloodline still remains, hardly tainted by the bloodlines of the other tribes.  Though the bloodline bears\n\nthe name Subudai, it still has a sliver of the fair silver-haired and blue-eyed lineage known to the ancients that descended from the woodlands to ride with dragons.\n\n§§``Xypa azh Zerenc bayuk Uunazhan ya tui Drylkai-dsan''\n\n-Yelbegkhai blessing said in the ancient tongue, carried on through oral tradition.\n\n\"Speed and fortune to the Riders of the Dragon.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Unknown", "§bRilkor Niwarsay", "Here in is written an account of encounters with a being known as \"The Pumpkin Lord\"\n\nEre I returned from a trip to the wilds to the keep of Gwydir.  When I went below the keep to the forge the presence made itself known.\n\nAbove doors slammed. The howling of wolves grew and all lights were dimmed but the fires of the forge. All was cast into shadow.\n\nFearing what this unknown was i drew my blade and cast my eyes about. A figure appeard. Though I know not if i can believe\n\nmine own eyes. He was hood and cloaked in dark robes. But for a moment he stood there. Then he vanished. A voice filled the air.\n\"Do You Fear.....Death\"\n\nMy reply was that of any man of honor.\n\"No\"\n\nAgain it spoke. Though its words were cryptic. It spoke of \"Redemtion\"\nIt demande the slaying of the one whom I next saw. Promising riches. Loath was I for such a task. Yet I knew i could not appose this being.\n\nIt was my own Captain whom i first saw.\n\nLoath was I to do the task. Yet the voice was in my ear. He could not be denied. So i confronted my Captain. Yet I was overcome. And seeing not what drove me he sought understanding.\n\nLaughter echoed over the bridge. My Captain brough me inside.\n\nBade me sit at the fire and stood guard. The being came again. Its voice echoing. Light died in the keep. All was dark.\n\nYet its purpose was foiled. It departed. Promising to watch us. And so it dose. Still it watches me.\n\nHalf an Elven day passed. While in the wilds he came again. A great pumpkin bearing a sign. I called out for him to reveal himself. The Pumpkin burst asunder and out spawned many Bats. The voice echoed and was gone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cryptography", "Tristanm1", "Basic Cryptography\nFirst Edition\n\nBy Yana Stafyr\n\nIntroduction\n\nIf you want to pass messages, making sure only the person you're giving the message to can read it can be important. In this book, we will go over a couple simple ways to encrypt your messages.\n\nHoren Cipher\n\nThe Horen Cipher the most basic method of encrypting a message. It works by shifting a letter down the alphabet a set number. If the end of the alphabet is passed, it wraps back around to the beginning again.\n\nFor instance, with a shift of 3, \"message\" would be written \"phvvdjh\" To translate back, simply shift back the same amount.\n\nVigenere Cipher\n\nThe Vigenere Cipher is similar to the Horen Cipher, but a bit more sophisticated. Instead of a fixed shift value, you get a keyword. The keyword is repeated over the length of the message,\n\nand each letter of the keyword corresponding to it's own shift value for that letter, going from A=0 to Z=25. \"message\" with a keyword of \"key\" would map the keyword to message in the repeating pattern of \"keykeyk\".\n\nThe encrypted message would then be written \"wiqceeo\" Once again, the message can be decoded if you have the key by reversing the process.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Brotherhood", "§bJistuma", "Introduction:\nMany Aegeans now are sheltered. They know nothing of this world and what is happening. For instance, today I saw the Temple of Aegis in trouble. Slimes had started a siege on recently resurrected player, and sending them back to the\n\nCrypt. It was mayhem. And what troubles me even more, as a traveler, is that very few people know about the Dark Brotherhood. This evil guild is intent on the destruction of this world’s inhabitants. And needs to be stopped at all costs. This is why I\n\nwrite this book, so that you may learn to defend yourself against this, this taint… Let me begin on the history of the guild.\n\nThe History of the Brotherhood.\nIt is said they started off as… well… assasins with perfectly harmless intentions. This soon changed with the arrival of one known only as “The Stranger”. This “Stranger” as he is known, is responsible\n\nfor the deaths of many, and is rumored to be the Grand Master of the guild. It has been this way for many years now. If his true identity is found, report it to me immediately! It must be shared!\n\nThe Guild Itself.\nThe Guild is mostly assasins, with a few bandits mixed in. This makes it hard to track down members, commonly referred to as “Danalus’”. These appear to be the average rank, with half the guild seemingly comprised of it…\n\nThere is also the recruit variety of Danalus it seems. Koloth is apparently the next rank. Only two have reached this rank so far to my knowledge. This is the final rank. Only higher is the “unique” ranks. These ranks are only availible to those who\n\nThere is also the recruit variety of Danalus it seems. Koloth is apparently the next rank. Only two have reached this rank so far to my knowledge. This is the final rank. Only higher is the “unique” ranks. These ranks are only availible to those who\n\nhave proven their worth to the Grand Master, lesser councel and High Councillor. This is the Silencer rank. This rank is only available to those select few, and it is limited space. How it works is each high ranking member has one or two silencers, who\n\ncarry out personal contracts for the high ranking members. There is one more rank within the Brotherhood, and it is by far the most terrifying of the assassin ranks. It is “Iblees Champion”, a seemingly obscure term used to describe the best member.\n\nIt terrifies me, but thankfully, there is not a Champion yet.\n\nHigh Ranks\nThe highest ranks available are now closed it seems. These are namely the Lesser councel, High Councillor and Grand Master.\n\nThe Dark Brotherhood\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Blood of Many", "§bRosso", "With great might and ideals men have raised themselves to fight. Throughout the sands of time we have seen gigantic armies fall and tyrant kings still stand. And yet, where do these ideals, these admittedly impressive albeit unsuccessful ventures lead?\n\nDeath and destruction. The decay of rebellions, and the downfall of freedom. And yet where many have failed, it takes but one to succeed. Need one be reminded of any of the ancient kings and rules who have come to an, shall we say abrupt end? Indeed,\n\nAssassins shape the tide of history more than you know. And here you arem reading, seeking, learning. What is it that you wish to know I wonder?\nIt is true that we have our governments, it is true that they are what hold us together- And yet! It is also\n\nthat we have the power to sway the tide! Move the battlefield to our advantage! And even, end the rule of the horrendous” The power in the minority is greater than we think. And it is why today we live in a world DEFINED by the assassinations of\n\nyesterday! And were these the greatest historic decisions? Perhaps not. But while some were not the best, others changed history for the better, bringing Aegis to the place it is today-or was yesterday rather. Grand armies once again amass in a hopeless\n\neffort to combat the Undead forces.\nIt makes one question where the world will be left, with such meek enemies yet so strong.\nIt is high time we accept our history’s motive and ally ourselves with Iblees to bring salvation to our world. This is where our\n\npowers are tested. We must remain resolute in the times to come if we are to become united. Otherwise we might as well let our blood spatter against the stone.\n\nThe Blood of Many, the Heart of One\n\nRewritten by Leyu’Maehr\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Frum'Staaz", "§bThurak'Yar", "``. . . All forms one could imagine. They gathered about the great Traf accompanied by their Shamans as Frum'staaz; they obeyed, but only in companionship, for these beasts were never to be controlled. By one Uruk's side\n\nOnly a flat, grey shadow could be seen, trailing from his feet and blinking back at those that glared. . .\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Alch Notebook I", "§bLaerden", "The Alchemist's Notebook\n\nForeword\nThe Realm of Anthos is filled with all types of herbs, creatures and phenomena to which are the delight of the many alchemists which fill it.\n\nSwamps and plains; hills and deserts can be found all around the continent, and in each of them a plethora of regents await to be found. With that being said and done, I welcome you, reader; to the Alchemist's Notebook on each (though not every) of\n\nthese very regents in their corresponding habitats.\n\nThe Southern Desert\n\nGoblin's Ivy\nKnown for its hardiness and abundance, Goblin’s Ivy covers dunes, caves, buildings and trees seemingly without preference or deterrence of any of the nearby inhabitants. The sludgy,\n\nOrc-Hide hue that colours the vine is, to be blunt, abhorrent, and its lack of appeal is only increased by its near uselessness in alchemy. With that being said, though, every regent has its function, and Goblin’s Ivy’s would be as an obvious\n\nsymbol Earth, resilience, and life. It can be used somewhat effectively in Stoneskin Potions, Potions of Fortitude, and even Potions of Strength. It’s been seen to have been used in poisons too, strangely, though any such are\n\nuseless in practicality and cause no more than mild nausea. Finding it isn’t a challenge, even in the vast expanse of the Badlands, and harvesting it is done simply enough by cutting off a length of the vine with a\n\nmachete or a similar knife, and keeping it in your satchel with all the other regents you have collected. When used in potions it can be extracted into water through boiling, or crushed finely in a mortar and pestle, though the second is advised in oils.\n\nBlood Lotus\nWith a blood like colouring and a blood like taste, the aptly named Blood Lotus is a desert crawler considered to be a valuable regent when traversing the dunes in search of a symbol of Fire. It’s widely accepted that heat and\n\nstrength are the two main things the plant represents in alchemy, and can be used in many potions in need of a more (And I use this lightly) calm portrayal of fire. It has been said that Blood Lotus can be brewed into an invigourating ale\n\nor even eaten crushed as a nutritional spice, and is commonly fed to people weak with sickness to help keep up their strength. It can be easily found in the mouths of caves and caverns and harvested by bottling the plant and\n\nkeeping it alive until use. It wilts and becomes useless quickly; as is the tendency for flame-related flora.\n\nThe Northern Icelands\n\nFrost Vine\nFound in the deepest cold of the North, it is only natural that Frost Vine be known as a symbol of Water- But more importantly so of ice, calmness and release.\n\nIt blends well into its chilly landscape with a light blue, and almost grey skin, and would seem to prefer to live in the shade of a tree, sheltered from the North gales. It can be used well in Oils of Frost and Potions of Mending,\n\nas one of its more useful attributes is a handy numbing agent that can be observed simply by a few minutes touch. After being crushed and extracted into water it becomes more potent, and is as quick and powerful at numbing\n\nas any alchemist or healer would need it to be. Harvesting can be done by bottling the vines and perhaps keeping them cold, and it should be said that growing Frost Vine away from the North or any other cold ecosystem\n\nis nearly impossible due to its fragile nature.\n\nElrow Berries\nA strange plant to say the least, Elrow berries are one of the only symbols of Fire that can be grown naturally in cold climates such as the North. One would seem to ask why when first told this fact, though by only a simple taste\n\nof the Devils of the North would they find out. Similar to chilli’s in nature, the berries burn the eater’s tastebuds and dry his throat nigh instantly upon consumption; leaving you craving for water or some other release from the aching\n\nElrow Berries bring. A mouth full of snow is a common enough cure for ‘berry burn’, and any nearby Frost Vine or Serpent’s Stalk would work just as well in the case of any snowless expanse. It can be used in potions and poisons alike\n\nas a symbol of power, anger and destruction, as that is simply what follows after eating the Berries of Elrow. They can be harvested without worry from any bush found in a cranny in a rock up North, though tend to lose some\n\npotency once dried. To dry and crush the berries is the best way to use them in a potion, though ample warnings should be given for any ignorant lab assistants; as even after processing they possess the same spice as they would naturally.\n\nElf's Hair\nAs rare as any growable regent can get, and as hard to spot as a Signus in a snowstorm, the Elf’s Hair Vine may only be seen once or twice in a whole year of searching, as many Alchemists find out to their dismay.\n\nFound atop mountains or hanging precariously over cavern edges, these wisps of vine and blossom are rivalled only in their potency by their beauty. The petals of the plant are of a soft, creamy white, and are indeed the most useful part of\n\nthe plant- In an alchemical sense, at the least. They hang loosely off the vine they grow on, and with any strong gust of wind are blown off and away; drifting over the air to populate some sparse piece of land far away. It is undeniable that\n\nElf’s Hair is a symbol of Air, speed, and grace, and it has been said that it an essential in any potent Potion of Swiftness. To harvest it one must be very careful- a stray bump could mean losing your rarity to the winds. It is the petals\n\nand the nectar that are most potent part of the plant, so plucking the whole blossom would be the simplest and easiest way. The nectar can be infused slowly with a potion, drop by drop, and the petals crushed; which\n\nis the most unfortunate part of using this reagent. Commonly, after the blossoms have been used, the vines wilt, die, and succumb to the winter winds.\n\nThe Midland Marshes\n\nDwarven Pumpkin\nAs swampy a plant as one could rightly get, Dwarven Pumpkin is a valuable symbol of Fire, power, and destruction. It can be easily spotted amongst the swamps and bogs by\n\nthe murky orange leaves that surround it; these being the main part of the plant you will want to use- and the brighter, the more potent, in this case. It’s usually found basking in sunlight in a rare clearing in the Marshes, which indeed\n\n is a great need of most herbs representing fire. Though commonly used for its potency in potions revolving entirely around fire, Dwarven Pumpkin also has a use in many other potions such as ones of fortitude, in which\n\nits representation of power grants a concentration boost to your armour-for-your-armour. Harvesting it is done by pruning off the leaves of brightest orange, and keeping them uncrushed in your satchel. They should be used soon after\n\nharvesting, in potions, by crushing them thoroughly and pouring the juice slowly into your concoction. It’s not a naturally toxic plant- but neither is it particularly pleasant to eat; with a bitter, clinging aftertaste.\n\nSaffvil\nThis plant, looking more like some clump of dilapidated weed-grass than a useful ingredient, is one of the few regents in the Marshes which is more repugnant to harvest than Mandragora. Found among the rotting carcasses\n\nof recently deceased swamp beasts, or sprouting from beneath decomposing mushrooms, Saffvil is a vile floral parasite and decomposer with a very handy use in potions needing a strong symbol of Earth, resilience, and decay.\n\nPoisons are the strong suite of this lacklustre herb; it has long been known to be a critical component in some of the more deadly brews, and indeed induces a blood clotting effect in most potions it is used in- though this can be\n\nremedied by including the nectar of the swamp blossom plant in your concoction, or any other strong symbol of air and speed. Harvesting it can be done by a simple uprooting of the whole, grassy mound, and washing it clean\n\nof any contaminations, to avoid impure potions (the bane of any alchemist intent on keeping their eyebrows). The easiest way Saffvil can be used in potions is to infuse it by a process similar to tea making.\n\nLeave the regent in a pouch soaking in your base ingredient until most of the plant has lost its colour, and dispose of it afterwards.\n\nSwamp Blossom \nFound growing in the crowded treetops above the Midland Marshes, this purple stemmed perennial produces strange, transparent nectar known well for its interesting properties, and its use as a symbol of Air, speed, and motion.\n\nThe liquid will not diffuse into water in great quantities without great heat and effort, and seems to refuse to behave as anything aqueous should. It glides across skin, and most any other surface it comes into contact with,\n\nand only seems to be interested in sticking to itself- Quite the opposite of water, in fact. Growing naturally on the branches of high-reaching swamp trees, Swamp Blossom can be spotted by its curved purple-green petals and the\n\npreviously mentioned burly, mauve-hued stem. Swiftness Potions and Potions of Mending are what this plant is of most use in, as both require a powerful symbol for speed. To harvest this plant this plant is difficult-\n\nOne must wait for first the plant to be producing its nectar, before slowly letting it collect it a water skin, or a vial. Consumption is practically harmless, though not advised- As Swamp Blossom is much more valuable\n\nas an alchemical regent than it is a barely nutritional, foul tasting pallet cleanser.\n\nMandragora\nOne of the more deadly plants inhabiting the swamps of Anthos, Mandragora is quite the prize of any herbalist; and is rather impressive on display. In several stages of its lifecycle, this parsnip shaped fungi releases toxic spores\n\nwith a hallucinogenic and eventually fatal effect on most creatures when inhaled. The meat of this plant is the most useful in potions involving clarity and regeneration, and is a somewhat strong symbol of Water\n\nwhen properly harvested. The plant’s brown coloured leaves can be used in soups, brews, or a rather nice tea- Though all have a chance of fatality or intoxication if boiled or cooked incorrectly. Harvesting this plant, as would be expected,\n\nis nigh impossible for any unknowing alchemist; two to three weeks after the Mandragora’s spores are released is the safe time to harvest, eat, and use it in potions. This can be done by simply uprooting the wholething, and separating the leaves\n\nand ‘meat’ later on at your alchemical workstation. The best way to brew Mandragora into a potion is to grind it up with a Mortar and Pestle, sprinkle it through your base, and later filter out the chunks.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Riddle", "§bKalameet", "I am the ultimate, destination of all...\n\nMore wicked than Daemons, I make Aenguls fall...\n\nOwned by the poor, needed by the wealthy...\n\nDo not eat me, if you wish to stay health. What am I?", ""),
        StaticBook("From the Depths", "§bthanndreli", "Difficulty: ET Required.\n\nIn recent months, the fishermen of the Barrowmarsh and Herendul have been plagued with the annoyance of large whale. So far, there have been several casualties and many damaged fishing trawlers since it\n\nhas made its home near our coast.\n\nLucienists, get your ships ready and arm yourselves with harpoons. It is our duty to ensure the survival of all mankind, including the livelihood of the locals.\n\nDEUS MAGNUS!", ""),
        StaticBook("[!] A Note", "§bAmbros", "Exercitatio Magica Nobilissima\n\nBy Ambros\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nVirgula divina\n\nSome Sorcerers do boast they have a Rod,\nGather’d with Vowes and Sacrifice,\nAnd borne about will strangely nod,\nTo hidden Treasure where it lies;\nMankind is sure that Rod divine,\nFor to the Wealthiest ever they incline.", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic The Basics", "ventus2", "Magic The basics\n\nMagic is the art of using magical energies from the void and bringing them to life, forming them into what most people call spells or magic. Now this book shall state the very basics of magic. What the energy is and some other facts\n\n     Magical Energy\n\nMagical energy or in other words “Mana” is what mages use to perform their spells, How mana is found is through the void, the void is the realm that supports all mana inside, There is a everlasting amount of mana inside the void,\n\n         The Void\n\nThe void is everything and nothing at the same time, An everlasting is inside the void and is where mages connect to perform their spells, Connecting to the void is a process that is easy in a sense but at the –\n\nSame time extremely dangerous, and the reason for this is being that the mana inside the void is what we call stamina, or in other words life energy, The main way of connecting to the void is through one’s mind, And how to do this? One must find out for-\n\nThemselves, Also considering that mana is life energy there may or not be a way for a mage to use this in order to grant themselves eternal life, But I leave that to you as well as how to perform spells and use mana.\n\n-Corvo", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "{!} The front cover of this book would be trimmed in gold vines with the name \"Kaia Kharadeen's Diary\" written in bronze of the middle §0\n§0-------------------Summer month of Sun's Smile, 1565§0\n§0\n§0Can't help but think of life when it's a stormy night. Sitting in\n\na huge white tree located in the main home of my family's arch enemy. No, not Oren. The Welfs- Mali'ame. Twenty. No friends, lover, just.. Kaia. Just the life of Kaia. Except for Tepah. He's my pet Kha or well, not a \"pet\" for he has feelings just like me\n\nand every other being in Vailor. §0\n§0\n§0{!} A rain stain would be here§0\n§0\n§0I wonder, now, that the rebellion has begun if I am able to freely go places without having to sneak out of the palace.\n\nAuntie warned me about the Uruks and the montrosities of Oren, but I can't help to be... curious. §0\n§0\n§0Who doesn't think about the unknown?§0\n§0\n§0A Princess. Doesn't seem like the life some peasant dreams of. It's more of a\n\nblack hole of lonesome hope. Hope that one day a rafiqi.. a friend could be more than just one person.§0\n§0\n§0~ Princess Kaia K.§0\n§0OOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO§0\n§0                            In this place, Vandoria, Athermoor. It's a shaggy tavern, but it'll do I\n\nsuppose. Just hope that my tiara isn't a dead give away of unuse of status. §0\n§0\n§0The Blushing Sun.. smells more of Blushing Ale if you'd ask me. I wonder how anyone could manage to sit in here properly and exchange conversation. Just a life of a\n\nperson who looks through different eyes, I suppose. §0\n§0\n§0No one's talking to me. Haha, what's new. §0\n§0\n§0-------------------It's now winter and as the seasons changed, so have I. A man, a noble of Vandoria by the name of Edwin Sarino has made such\n\nan impact on my life. My brother Yusef seems to like him as well. He told us tales about how he went monster hunting in the mountains. Well, he wasn't lying for we took a journey there today.§0\n§0\n§0Not only was it amazing.. so was he. The way he grabbed\n\nmy waist and placed a peck against my cheek.. It was something I couldn't even fathom. Of course it was inappropriate for me to let it happen still, but a part of me couldn't help it. He's such a handsome man.  §0\n§0Not only did that change, I brought back a\n\ngift for my younger brother Yusef! A leaf the size of my bed spread from Laurelin! It's magnificent! Oh, how I wish I could repay Mister Sarino for all of the kind things he's done for us. He's truly showed me a whole new world. §0\n§0I wonder when's the next\n\nwe will meet again. I hope, no, I pray that it is soon. §0\n§0\n§0He's just brought me back home and I already miss him so dearly.§0\n§0\n§0I shouldn't be having these thoughts of leaving home, but I do. I always do. Just to\n\ntake this adventure outside of the palace. And I have, truly found myself a rafiqi. A friend named Edwin.§0\n§0\n§0~ Princess Kaia K.§0\n§0------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "\"Law name, number and etc.\"§0\n§0\n§0If bound by marriage, that person is only allowed to bed his or hers' partner.§0\n§0\n§0Should a citizen find herself with child by the result of bedding outside of marriage, the father of the child and the mother -\n\nwill marry to ensure the child to be raised in a complete household.§0\n§0\n§0Draft I.\n\nDraft II§0\n§0\n§0-Citizens is disallowed to bed others.§0\n§0\n§0-Only married couples are allowed to bed and only with their mate/partner/spouse.", ""),
