        StaticBook("Illusion 1 (ART)", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "/\\\n       /\\ \\ \\\n   /\\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n   \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n    \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n     \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n      \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n       \\ \\ \\/  \\ \\\n        \\ \\/   / /\n         \\      \\ \\\n          \\  /\\ \\ \\ \n           \\/ /\\/_/\n            \\/\n~By Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Waterlogged Tome", "§bMifris Ghilain", "[!] The book is tattered and waterlogged. Only a very minute few of the pages are discernable.\n\nThus is it that we have tamed the djinn found in the northern hinterlands. We cannot bring it to the Temple, for should it break free of its bindings it would wreak havoc upon our home. Our ailer'tanya may keep it bound.\n\nEntry I\n\n[!] The page is undiscernable.\n\n[!] The page is undiscernable.\n\n[!]The page is undiscernable.\n\nWe have received news that shadows of ages yore have pursued us to our new home. I cannot say what is to come, but the half-men do not come with the laurel of peace in display. They come with fire and steel, and our numbers cannot hope to stave the tide.\n\n[!] The page is undiscernable.\n\n[!] The page is undiscernable.\n\n[!] The page is undiscernable.\n\nWe have erected murals in memory of our fallen. Contact with the other enclaves has ceased entirely, and we are cut off. The tides grow higher and higher with each day, and I fear we may be required\nto abandon our home.\n\nThe Djinn has become unruly as of late. Our ailer'tanya can no longer keep it bound. Let us pray that --..\n\n[!] The page is undiscernable.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tome of the Wolf", "§bWolf Druid Ouity", "I. Power\n\nThe soul attracts that which it secretly harbors- that which it loves, and also that which it fears. Thus, circumstances do not make the Druid; they only reveal him to himself. It means that blessedness, and not wealth, is the measure of right\n\nthought; misery, not poverty or lack of family is the measure of wrong thought. A Druid will find that as he alters his thoughts towards Nature and the Aspects, Nature and Aspects will alter towards him. For you will always draw near toward that which you\n\nsecretly most love. The Races surge with uncontrolled passion, are tumultuous with ungoverned grief, and are blown about by anxiety, doubt, and the wars and wills of Aenguls and Daemons. Only the wise Druid, only he whose thoughts are controlled and\n\npurified, can make the winds and storm of the soul, and indeed the world, obey him. The greatest achievement was at first, and for a time, only a dream. Just as the oak sleeps in the acorn, and the bird waits in the egg, so dreams are the seedlings of\n\nrealities. Beware therefore of what you dream of. For some dreams are given by the Aspects to inspire us by what may yet be. Others are planted within us by others, foul seeds that we harvest to our destruction.\n\nII. Pride\n\nThere is but one way to truly gain mastery over nature, and that is to realize you cannot truly master it at all. It masyers you. When one attempts to force it, compel it, command it, or otherwise exercise dominion over it- the power flees like\n\na timid bird. This is because the Aspects know our innermost thoughts. They know how we intend to use Nature's Gift. Man may decieve other men, but one simply does not decieve the Aspects. If their will is sought, they will come. If we emulate the\n\nprincipals by which they thrive, they flourish in us. Pride is poison to them. In reality, there is perhaps not one of our natural passions so hard to subdue as our pride. Disguise it, struggle with it, beat it down, stifle it, mortify it as much as you\n\nplease. It is still alive, and will every now and then peep out and show itself. You will see it perhaps, even within the most sacred grottos of the realm. For even I, the Arch Druid, could not concieve that I had completely overcome it. If I had, I\n\nshould probably be proud of my humility. A desire to be observed, considered, esteemed, praised, beloved, and admired by his fellows is one of the earliest, as well as the keenest dispositions discovered in the hearts of the Races. My advice to new\n\nDedicants is to squelch it all their days, for those desires lead to ruin.\n\nIII. Doubt\n\nMany Dedicants arrive at the Groves with passion already instilled in them. They yearn to learn, they carry drive, and zest, and youth, and curiosity. When they enter our great tree, they have nothing, and leave with everything,\n\nHowever, a few lose what they have. The rigorous trials of Dedicancy begin to take their toll on them, or they submit their thoughts to the subtle poison of doubt. Not even an Arch Druid's power can cure it, for these students do harm to themselves. The\n\nmind, like the body, can be moved from sunshine into shade. They submit themselves to the slews of miriad ways of the Aenguls and Daemons, and the trickery of man, and they yield before this great power to sway one's faith in the Aspects' might. Those of\n\nyou who would stay and train inasmuch as you strip yourself from jealousies and fears, and humble yourself before the Aspects, for you are not sufficiently humble, the veil over your eyes shall be torn and you will see. See all their glory and power, and\n\nknow you are beloved. A servant of the earth, and wild. Having concieved of their attunement, a Druid should mentally makr out a straight pathway to service, looking neither to the right nor left. Doubts and fears should be zealously starved. They are\n\ndisintergrating elements which break up the straight path, rendering it crooked, ineffectual, and useless. Thoughts of doubt and fear can never accomplish anything. They always lead to failure. Purpose, energy, power to do, and all strong thoughts cease\n\nwhenever doubt and fear creep in. The will to do springs from the knowledge that we can do. He who has conquered doubt and fear has conquored failure in all his endeavors, both as a Druid, and a person.\n\nIV. Blight\n\nIn every era there comes a moment when the collective thoughts, whims, and motivations of arcane delvers become so self-absorbed, so malignant, so unheeding that nature itself revolts. Man scars the land such that it finally rebels\n\nagainst him. As thoughts can spread despair and death like seedlings of weeds strewn by the wind, so they must eventually draw the Druids to pluck them out. The vetches must be pulled, roots and all. When this happens, the Aspects cease to bless, and\n\ninstead they curse. Instead of healing, they spew poison. It happens so swiftly and terribly. The ancients of the Wayward's time gave it a name, this culling process that blackens the world. They named it after a wasting disease that occurs in once\n\nhealthy groves of trees. They called it the Blight, and the first of these, the Great War.\n\nI put this quill to paper here now so that others do not make the mistakes I did in my youth. Blinded by war and hate, my transgressions were many, and hard to earn penance for. Though I served the Aspects diligently for many lifetimes, I fear that in my\n\nheart, I have failed them. May the Aspects look kindly on me in the Afterlife-\n\nXal ussta stath xunde mir dosst elamshinae, Nemiisae.\n\nWolf Druid Ouity, retired Arch Druid of the Order\n\nElandriel Grove", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "hex37", "__Mundane Healing: The treatment of minor wounds with common herbs.__\n\nNienna’s Foreword: When I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients for the\n\ntreatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien. One or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery or internal organs with\n\nnothing but rose thorns and petals. In the interest of not wasting precious paper, I’ve recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one or two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n\n-Minor Cut (Nienna)\nSimply apply a dose of  deceased Sentient-Slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it.  The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n\n-Headache (Aleya)\nBoil milk. Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n\n-Stomach Ache (Nienna)\nBoil water. Once it hits a full broil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber color. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n\n-Soreness (Aleya)\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax the muscles, and rest a lot.\n\n-Burns (Nienna)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere. The important thing about\n\nburns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist, and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check and clean the burn wound daily until the\n\nskin can finally reform.\n\n-Fever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim’s body cool using cold water. Give him hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off the disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apekha: A plague", "§bUho'Yuzira", "A Metzli-Worshipper's Guide to Apekha\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nINTRODUCTION\nApekha are smelly, dirty, and traitorious, shadows of a Kha who's minds have been taken over by apes. Never trust one of these heretical creatures and always try to avoid\n\nthem.\n\nWHAT TO DO WHEN AN APEKHA APPROACHES YOU\nIf an Apekha has discovered you outside the temple, he may try to convince you to join it. DO NOT listen to its words and attempt to imprison it. If the ape is armed, you may send a bird for assistance.\n\nVARIOUS WAYS A APEKHA HAS BEEN PUNISHED\nsacrifice\nsacrifice\nsacrifice\nsacrifice\nsacrifice\nand finally, sacrifice.\nWHY NOT TO BECOME AN APEKHA\nIf you are doubting Metzli or the Tla's authority, contact a local preist. If you\n\njust think you can pull off being an apekha....your horribly wrong. Preists have hunted Apekha down and most times they did so, they came back with an Apekha. Remember, Metzli is the deity that created you, not a foreign ape's myth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary 2", "§bGreenfingers", "*The top half of the entry is ripped off*\n\ngrow several, deadly plants in various locations around the land.\n\nI keep seeing strange symbols and phrases dotted about the walls of the house and all over these notes.\n\nThey say things such as \"...Filthy Tree huggers...\", \"...Vicious felines...\" and \"...Stupid long-ears...\"\n\nPerhaps these are clues as to who he means to inflict these plants of his upon...or perhaps they are merely the crazed writings of a madman...\n\nEntry 5600\n\nThese notes are unlike anything I have ever seen...\n\nI have been studying them for a while now and these plants he plans to create are horrific.\n\nThey seem to be bred\n\nto do nothing but fight. The Master really has lost the plot...\n\nThere is something else about these plants...they are incredibly tough. He seems to want to have them posess a thick skin that, in his words, \"Will deflect an axe as easily as a troll\n\ncan throw a feather.\"\n\nI managed to find the section upon how to get past their deadly hides...\n\nIt involves using a blade imbued with\n\n*The entry is torn apart here...*", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day 1-§0\n§0Got this little journal yesterday. Thought it would be worth writing stuff down, as therapy. It's very relaxing.§0\n§0As you can see, I finally learned to read and write. So, that's a good thing.§0\n§0I've also been accepted into the Felsen military!\n\n(I'm actually cheating and writing this at night, but that's ok)§0\n§0I also managed to get myself into a date with a man of importance, which §0is...alright§0, I suppose. He's awfully sweet, but naive.§0\n§0Also met some vampireish character who goes by 'Bram'\n\nHe's §0odd...rather§0 harrasing, and he can't speak properly.\"§0\n§0Pretty nice though, for a vamp.§0\n§0I stand corrected.§0\n§0\n§0Anyway, I discovered there is a man nearby that terrifies me...§0\n§0Oh, Auzredh is here now. good. I like him. He's nice.\n\nI feel §0funny...Blood§0, just...\n\nRudi hasn't been around lately...I worry...\n\nKILL HIM§0\n§0KILL HIM§0\n§0KILL HIM§0\n§0KILL HIM§0\n§0KILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIMKILLHIM\n\nKILLKILLKILLKILLKOLLKILLHIMKILLHIM\n\nKILL\n\nKILL\n\nKILL\n\nKILL\n\nKILL HIM§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Journal of Dreveni Gilvani. If you are /not/ Dreveni (me) Do respect my privacy and do not read. Unless I'm dead, then please do read.§0\n§0\n§0I will be writing this in entry form, as I cannot be bothered keeping track of the days as they go by.\n\nEntry 1: Finally have \"borrowed\" enough supplies of Dre'nor to forge this journal. Things are going swell, with the banishment of Dram I feel safe with my people here, and we've begun to gather some decent numbers as well, Mali'ker, of course. Things are\n\ngoing rather swell... except for a number of problems. Firstly, I don't know who I am going to make priestess, I have a number of options, mainly Leyu, but I don't know where her loyalty lies. Secondly, I am ill. Sick, whether this will infact kill me or\n\nnot, I cannot say. Something feels.. wrong deep inside me, I feel weaker, yet my head is putting me through agony, I am beginning to.. hear thoughts that are not my own. Thoughts of aggresiveness, hunger, vulgarity. I must find out what is happening to me\n\nBut, as long as Drenor stands I feel confident that I will be able to pull through this. Here's hoping we can gather more numbers, and my situation can improve. Only time will tell. [End.]§0\n§0\n§0Entry 2: Amongst other things, like a minor run in with a\n\nhalf-elf showing me how the Mali'ker of our settlement feel. It has been rather quiet in.. Dre'nor? If we'll keep calling it that. My.. illness has not been getting any better, and has driven me to quite some lengths to contain myself. Regardless, that is\n\nnot why I write this entry. Recently, some big elven figure who is now some scholar in a library, has sent me a letter asking for contact to talk about our history, and maybe  even get the Mali'ker out there again, get some attention for our species.\n\nThis is the best news I have heard in quite some time. And he even referred to me as leader of the Mali'ker, at last finally someone regards me with some respect. Each day I spend speaking with our Mali'ker, the more I realise.. a council will not work.\n\nI'm not surrounded by fellow Mali'ker, I'm surrounded by idiots! They defend half elves, BLOODY HALF ELVES. How?! They are impure, and disgusting. The very thought that this child was the offspring of a valah and a Mali, blegh!\n\nI hope that little wretch doesn't get in the way of my plans for the Mali'ker, and with Faendral, I very much look forward to meeting this... Ashur. And I hope it will bring some much needed attention for the Mali'ker.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Crazed Ice", "Adam_barnett", "_-_§0\n§0    /~~   ~~\\§0\n§0 /~~         ~~\\§0\n§0{               }§0\n§0 \\  _-     -_  /§0\n§0   ~  \\\\ //  ~§0\n§0_- -   | | _- _§0\n§0  _ -  | |   -_§0\n§0      // \\\\§0\n§0\n§0=================== The crazed Ice§0\n§0===================\n\nA long time ago when Mukar was under lead of Temporary Tlatlanni, Rameethar, in the large temple of Karak'Vylthawl, we were hunting just outside our walls.§0\n§0\n§0It turned out we were being stalked outselves.\n\nA creature in pure gray and hard armour stood behind us as he caught a Bokolo or two, the details are sketchy.§0\n§0\n§0He spoke in an odd and monotone voice. All around it began to freeze. It claimed it followed an entity\n\nknown as Azdromoth.§0\n§0After a brief discussion we commenced our attack, it was a foolish decision to make. Our forces were low and the only moon fire wielders were Mukar at the time. Two Kharajyr retreated to the grand temple and brought back\n\na large group of priests and other kha warriors, each attempting to battle the horrid creature.§0\n§0\n§0The priests fire worked but then spikes of ice drew up from the ground, destroying Ja'Ketzawls feet.§0\n§0He was pulled away from the scene.\n\nThough a large and mixed group arrived to our aid, a group of paladin, Ascended, Magi and Clerics arrived. With their aid and our fire it was defeated for now. It vanished in a puff of white ash. Leaving only behind a barren patch of ice, unmelting.\n\nIt left shards which some orders have. §0\n§0\n§0What ever it is, lets hope we do not meet again.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sages entry.", "§bSage Ju'Mukar", "----------------------------------------\nThe diary of Mukar\n---------------------------\nFor Mukars eyes only, should non-mukar eyes lay upon this book, close your eyes and return to Mukar or may Metztlis wrath be upon you.\n========================\n=======\n\n- 22nd of The deep cold, 1530.\n----------------------------------------This was a strange day that Metztli provided for Mukar. For rumours spread of a sky-rock falling onto the druidic grove many years ago. But the foolish druids never informed the Fylax.\n\nThey hidden it from us, for this could be the event we forsaw. \n\nMukar sent Ja'Ketzawl to investigate these rumours. Though they were true the druids refused to give any detailed explanations of the event that transpired there on that moon. The Fylax will\n\ncontinue to investigate these events, for they could be the bringer of something gravely evil.\n\nSa'vi Metztli.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elem. Alchemy", "Jistuma", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n------------\nElements of Alchemy\n\nVolume I-2 of V\n\nThe Elements:\n--------\nFire\n--\nEarth\n--\nWater\n--\nAir\n\nSkeptics often approach me with a wholly ignorant conundrum, and that is “how can you trace every spell and element back to these four basic elements.” But what they do not realize is that an understanding of what is meant by these four elements is\n\nrequired before that question can be answered and in fact, if that understanding is acquired then this question will never be asked.\n\nThese four basic, rudimentary elements, Fire, Earth, Water, and Air, are what every potion, oil, elixir, and\n\nconcept, in Alchemy of course, is based upon. An ignorant outlook on this statement is that what is meant is the physical, literal meaning behind these elements but one must look into the symbolism, they must look deeper than the surface. I shall go into\n\neach of these elements in detail, so that you, and budding alchemist or simply a well-read individual, may understand how Air may both aid someone’s speed, as well as their perception of their surroundings.\n\nFire\n===\nThe Destroyer, the Unmaker, the Cleanser.\n\nWe will begin with one of the most rudimentary and used element, Fire. Fire can represent many a feeling, action, and state and because of this, it is often one of the most useful elements of the Alchemist’s arsenal. Fire can represent rage, anger,\n\nhatred, as well as bravery, courage, and gusto. Through this a brew can be crafted to make someone unquestionably and savagely furious, but it could also craft a brew to strengthen one’s will, and allow them to do what other men would shrink away in fear\n\nat. These feelings, these emotions can be invoked by the element of Fire within a potion, but feelings are not the only thing that fire can produce, actions are another.\nActions are often the most recognized aspect of fire, and by this I mean the action\n\nof burning, consuming, and destroying. Alchemist’s Fire, a handy inferno in a bottle, is an example of this aspect of Fire, for within it is the action of destruction. This action can be further expanded upon with burning oil placed upon a weapon, but if\n\none were to use this example they would also have to include the element of pain, another feeling that fire an invoke. State is aspect that Fire can take one within an alchemist’s potion and this is often represented as Chaos.\nIt is true that Chaos is\n\noften something alchemist’s fear, for it is something athat often ruins a potion, but it is yet another aspect of Fire that must be recognized. Chaos, being the state that it is, may seem like it has little place in a potion but brilliant minds and\n\npowerful reason can bring it to use just the same as the first farmer realized a stone and a stick, two completely different objects, could help them till their fields by putting them together. As this is not a book on the philosophy of alchemy, or\n\nsolely on the element of fire, I will not go into depth on how Chaos can be used. The teacher must leave something for the student to ponder.\n\nEarth\n===\nThe Enduring, the Lifegiver, the Fortifying\n\nWith the conclusion of Fire, the other elements will not have as long as description for most of the fundamentals of the elements are covered in how they can represent different things, I will simply go over what they may represent, starting with Earth.\n\nEarth is a truly powerful element for it may represent metals, strength, the notion of being stalwart, solidity, firmness, flora, animals, and countless other, quite obvious, subjects. Earth is often used for potions that increase one’s endurance, or\n\nstrength, and it is a must in potions that toughen one’s skin. In fact, a strong series of representations of Earth are required to perfect a barksin, or stoneskin potion. Protecting oneself is not the only use for the element of Earth, for it is also\n\nused in antidote potions, disease-curing potions, and, of course, fertilizers. Antidotes use this element for it can represent animals, and among those elements are snakes and spiders, often associated with poison. Of course a symbol of Water is also\n\nrequired for a proper antidote, but this will be addressed later on. Many of the uses of the element of Earth are quite obvious, but a always, if one wishes to master the field of Alchemy they must learn creativity is their greatest friend, and using\n\nelements in odd and interesting ways can be useful, and quite detrimental, in numerous ways. A final note on the element of Earth is how it is associated with the fable of Transmutation. Now, as a scholarly and skeptic individual, I have doubts upon\n\ntransmutation, its existence, and possibility. This will be described more in depth, but know that the element of Earth is the greatly represented by metals, for metals are merely ores in their purest forms.\n\nWater\n===\nThe Base, the Purifier, the Healer.\n\nWater is the element that seems to get the most amount of use due to how it is a base for many a potion and it is true, for if someone wants a liquid spell they want to use the Element of Water. Often known as the “base” element, it truly lives up to its\n\nname for observations, and personal experience, lead all to believe it is necessary for life. This base element, is often associated with flowing, liquids, balance, peace, calm, order, life, and rebirth. One requires water for any potion that one plans on\n\ndrinking, and any oil that one plans on applying for to have a liquid, one must use the Element of Water. Now that and understanding on how Water is a base, we must go into how it is used beyond simply supporting the other elements.\n\nWater’s uses are varied, for it can be used both in antidote as well as poisons, showing that it is quite the versatile element. One may also use it to create a potion of calmness, or perhaps a potion of healing due to its association with life. But one\n\ncan also use this beautiful element in the creation of an oil to coat a weapon, or to coat and strengthen armor. This is not the same as enchanting armor or weaponry, mind you, for doing that is often permanent and requires magic. Through oils, one may\n\nreap similar benefits of enchantment but instead it is only temporary and anyone with basic sense can apply them. The purest base, and often representation of water, is Aqua Vitae or “Water of Life,” which is best made by distilling wine or other liquors.\n\nAir\n===\nThe Nimble, the Traveller, the All-Seeing.\n\nOur final element, the element of Air, is not the least by any stretch of imagination but is often the hardest one to put into representation and use in a potion. Now this element is often associated with agility, quickness, travel, feet, perception, and\n\neven flight, it can be quite difficult to embody the element of Air into a physical item due to our basic fault of lacking understanding of what we cannot see. But with reason and the opening of one’s eyes, the ways in which to represent Air are quite\n\nobvious in our everyday world.\nItems that can be used to represent air, and subsequently put through your tools to produce a potion, are rather easy to find during your average day but of course, as with all the elements, purer ingredients are often quite\n\nrarer. One representation that you may have already thought of is a mere feather, which is often the most common representation of Air. This, of course, is not the purest representation of the element but it will often due for your more basic potions\n\ncentered around this element. Another, more outlandish representation, are rabbits’ feet. Rabbits are often seen as quick and agile critters, and as Air takes on the aspect of agility and quickness, it becomes quite obvious how the feet of a rabbit and\n\nAir intermingle. With that said, it becomes rather easy to find out representations of Air through simply looking and observing the world around you. But do not fret if you are still hard-pressed to find these symbols, the next chapter will explain\n\nherbs that will best aid you in the process of finding symbols for all the elements.\n\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I-2\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers*\n((13/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Gronkkston", "§bDo'tepah", "Chapter 1. \n  The fleet of the kharajyr had no choice but to head to the mainland, but to their rejoice the orcs took them in with open arms. Rex Gronkk and the Krughai council granted the group of Kharajyr to build and set up a\n\ncamp just out side of Gronkkston. They tended to the fields and once again thrived in the camp. But the kharajyr and other races were taken through a gateway known as the Fringe. Soon a mighty battle arose in the fringe which resulted in the\n\ndeath of setherien. The death of Setherien caused the frozen norths to melt. which in turn, began to flood Anthos. The Fringe now their only hope of survival", ""),
        StaticBook("Va'Khajra:Asulon", "§bDo'tepah", "Chapter 1.\n Akha' name of Miian was kidnapped in the 'Mainland' by unknown force to the Kharajyr. Tla'Xerdun brings all kharajyr that can fight, sealed to the location to where the kidnappers were. When the Kharajyr\n\nfinally arrived, wandering the lands of unknown they encountered the first creatures o fthe mainland. The Orcs, they made a deal for a fight and sadly the kharajyr lost. Tla'Xerdun had to make a deal with the Orcs to prevent\n\nKharajyr death but could not find a way to take Miian along with them, it was a term of which no Kha knew of.\n          ~*~    \nAfter months, scouts of Kharajyr were sent to mainland to search for more answers on these\n\nnew creatures and the Kharajyr reacted violently because of the other races reactions towards kharajyr. It was by now the Kharajyr Empire was fully constructed and the Karakatuan Empire would rise to glory..\n\nChapter 2.\n  Slowly the numbers of Kharajyr decreased after Tla'Xerdun's self inflicted death. A few kharajyr lost faith, died or just simply went missing after this happened. After a short period of\n\nbeing leaderless their goddess metztli had stepped in, and from the supposed moon-lit heavens aboce bestowed her perfect white fur upon a new emeror. An unexpecting Tigrasi, Tiazar had been chosen to be the next Tlantanni\n\nnumbers still decrease and the kharajyr were threatened by the Dwarves, Elves and Orcs. Kharajyr continue their annoyance and violence towards the races, until the orcs decided to strike due to the Kharajyr not\n\nbeing loyal and carrying out the terms they had once agreed under Tla'Xerdun's reign. From small parties trying to take on the kharajyr, Kharajyr were successful twice. But the final blow was coming, and\n\nKharajyr scouts sent warning that the orcs were about to release a full on strike at the kharajyr whilst the were weak. Tla'Tiazer order to all of the Kharajyr to leave the island in fear of Metztli's children being slaughtered.\n\nonly a small number of the  Kharajyr survived and soon took shelter with the High Elves of Haelun'Or whom respected Tla'Tiazar highly for granting them insight to knowledge about the sacred Blood moon's tha Metztli\n\nshowed her people. Va'khajra was left in ruins, and the orcs now had complete control of it..\n\nThey call it 'The fall of V'khajra and Karatuan Empire' this was around the year 48 but is not exactly known", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry v1", "§bUho'Yuzira", "Poetry, by Uho'Yuzira\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nIntroduction-Poetry is an art here in Karakatua. Its what we do when we feast, when we do our chores, and even when we go to war. We should respect our Poetry as we do other texts.\n\nTable of Contents\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nLove Poems\nWar Poems\nChore Poems\n\nThe Tale of Two Kittens, by an unknown author\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nThere were once two kittens. They played day to day, enjoying life. When one went to farm, the other worked with her yarn. They fell in love and made a den, but it was only then they knew\n\nwhat they were missing. So they had kittens, 2 kittens. \n\nStorming the Castle of Love-by an anonymous author\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-I shall take my sword of roses and my trident of caring to storm this castle of love. Oh I love you my dear but you stand\n\ndefiant. I put on my helm of laurels, remembering my morals, and my chestplate of linen, made with the love I have for you. I put on my cloth of loin and my iron boots forged with friendship. All of this, I shall use to storm your castle of love.\n\nDo' The Drums are Sounding-by an unkown author\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nCome on soldiers of Metzli! Their flags fly in kharajyr wind! Do' the drums are sounding! The bounding of your lazy feet is so not terrifying! Fight with the might of your elders! Fight\n\nbecause the drums are sounding!\n\nMemorial to the Fallen\n-by Ju'Mukar\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Let us not remember them as the dead. Let us not remember US as the living! Let us simply remember ourselves as the kharajyr that stand defiant and gallant!\n\nWhat Shall we do With the Lazy Baker?-by Uho'Zhikar\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Shove them in their pies! Make them cook their eyes! Sacrifice is not needed for thee as long as you can provide what we need! We need no lazy bakers, because theyre no better then\n\ntraitors!\n\nThe Breadloaf March\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nDrums of ovens, sticks of bread lets sound the Breadloaf march! Pastries on the floor, we all shall not be bored!", ""),
        StaticBook("Stone of Metztli", "§bTli'Mukar", "The Stone of Metztli.\n\n\n\n              [!]\n A crude drawing of the holy relic, suspended in the air, sits here.\n\n\nThe stone of Metztli is that of pure power. It provides every kharajyr\n\ntheir connection to Metztli herself. Without it such would falter, the magic she had gifted render null as they would no longer be able to access the power gained from the ancient relic.\n\nThe stone is a pure crystal of empowered lapis. Pure energy swirls\n\nwithin the stone, the energy the priesthood/Fylax use to master the art of\nMuun'trivazja.\n\nThoughout history everybody but the kharajyr who stood infront of the stone was forced to their knees infront of the stone. The voice of Metztli filling their\n\nears, turning them insane. It would be a fools errand to try to damage or touch it.\n\nBut throughout history there has been doccumented incidents where, for unknown reasons, they were able to get close enough to cause damage or even explode the holy\n\nrelic. The outburst of the explosion being catastrophic. In one incident the blast was so large it consumed a whole island. Though such was forseen and evacuation was already complete before the relic exploded.\n\nThe stone is also, though there has\n\nnever actually been any incidents so far, employable to corruption and taint. Such is prevented by the many barriers and defences that lay in wait for unsuspecting vandals or dark art users.\n\nThe crystal is also able to be damaged by\nmana\n\nleeches. The mana leech was able to absorb all of the energy residing within the empowered stone. Killing the leech only made it near impossible to gain the power of the energy again. A searing pain engulfed those attuned to the stone.\n\nThough while the\n\nstone is able to be destroyed. They may also be re-created. The majority of the time Metztli creates new ones in underground tombs.\n\nIt is the icon of power and a direct connection to the goddess Metztli.", ""),
        StaticBook("Val'Korsa:Asulon", "§bDo'tepah", "chapter 1.\n  Once Va'khajra had fallen some of the Kharajyr began to question their faith, for they were not really sure if metztli was still with them. How could their goddess have let their island paradise be take from them, why\n\nhadn't she done anything.Whilst that remained a mystery, many Kharajyr had begon to wander aimlessly though desperation some of them integrated within other cultures, mainly human cultures, and these Kharajyr were\n\nlooked down upon and called the 'Ape Kha' by still loyal Kharajyr. Though Tla'Tiazar held his head high and proud, making a call to arms for any kharajyr still loyal to Metztli and Karakatuan Empire to assemble upon the island nation\n\nof Holm. A good few gathered, all suited for battle that was supposedly to come. They swiftly charged upon and conquered a new island North of Holm, an island that they would build their new home upon, and island\n\nthey name Val'Korsa", ""),
        StaticBook("Kha history", "§bSo'Zinawr", "Kha History\n\n\n\nObservations made by Zinawr, during a lesson held by sage Mukar\n\nThe first Tlatlanni was was Tla'Xerdun, yet that seems to be but a myth, created by the kha while he was not the first he was the first true Tla. The first actual Tlatlaani  was Tla'jhaan, the ruler of the Karatukan empire. Xerdun was the tla's son making\n\nhim of the Tlatlaani bloodline, his empire fell. when the empire fell Tla'Jhaan went with it, he became a heathen, he outlawed the worshipping of metztli in the empire. The majority of the kha disagreed with Jhaan, including his own son, this led to\n\nXerdun assassinating his patta, Xerdun then replaced him as Tla, it was serene in the empire for years though Metztli still enraged by Jhaan's heathenous actions and the people who willingly followed him, she was distraught as her people began to forget\n\n\nher. Metztli enacted her wrath through a nearby volcano forcing it to errupt and pour over her people's empire, many heathens were killed during this eruption. Xerdun then set out to rebuild the empire, he unfourtunately died soon after\n\nleaving his people without a leader, Metztli chose a new Tla herself gifting him with the white fur of a Tlatlaani, Tiazar was his name. Though orcs soon attacked, conquering the kha, Tiazar soon led the kha to a new island which they claimed though force\n\nAfter tens year peace on this island Tla'Tiazar passed away, His son morthawl became tla, Morthawl took his people to the Mori'Quessir, they gifted the Tla a cavern and the kha had the druid grow a beautiful jungle inside. Shortly after this\n\nOne of the main races triggered the undead minions of Abbysal forcing the kha to move from Asulon to anthos where the kha lived happilly for years. at some point the Oren emperor wished to obtain karatuka, but that was the only incident. The kha had to\n\nLeave karatuka as sage Natayshi forsaw the black scourge. The draagur Setherin and his minion attacked karatuka, while a harmbringer attacked the sonte of metztli destroying it, the kha fleed to the orcs in Gronkkston, under the current rex at the time\n\nThere were many disagreements over the sacrafice of an orc who attempted to assassinate Tla'Morthawl. The kha then took up the druid on an offer for a grove near the cloud temple, unfourtunately the black scourge struck again forcing the kha into the\n\nFringe along with the other main races, In the fringe the kha took harbourage with the High elves In tahn'siol, setherin was presumed dead this was not the case, soon after a huge battle took place in the red realm Setherin's realm in which he was defeat-\n\n-ed. Once again a disaster stuck the fringe Drought and Plague forced them out and led them fleeing to Thales, In thales still under the high elves the kha constructed a small settlement called Karak'tuum the settlement was breath of fresh air for the kha\n\nfeeling homely. To the kha's terror a vision of eternal winter over thales was shown to the wife of Tla'Morthawl the races once again fleed to the athera to the island of Ohlokar, they lived there in peace though with a few false threats from Uragan,\n\nlater the island was raided by orcs the kha chose to defend upon orders by Tla'Morthawl under the guidance of Ja'Lorie seeing the islands destruction as important in terms of the greater cause. Two grand warriors stayed Qi'Quatl and Do'Kreshawl they took\n\nout half the orc force before fleeing for their own survival. The Ordium replaced the old island and Tla'Vyallu the daughter of Morthawl became Tla she died shortly after however in a conflict with the Va'kha. The Ordium was destroyed by the Amyas and\n\nDaro took over as Tlatlaani, Daro was later outlawed for his crimes against Vyallu, and Rameether took over, He led the Kha to caliphate soon after though he disappeared, the kha then transitioned between three Tlatlaani's Tla'atl, Tla'Kaharal and\n\nTla'Lunaw then the kha moved to their current island under the guidance of Tla'Rokhan, Though soon after our arrival here Rokhan went missing rewarding Rameether for his long servitude to the kha. This Brings us up to the present day. Written on the 4th\n\nof the grand harvest 1559.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creation", "§bDo'tepah", "Spanning generations, the history of Asulon and Aegis is catalogued in ancient tomes and holy texts throughout the lands, the knowledge tightly guarded by religious priesthoods  and avid collectors\n\nalike. However, the tale of the Kharajyr is one not written in any ancient tome; It is a tale unknown to all, save for a few privileged scholars, denounced as madmen.\n\nChapter 1.\n  Inthe dark times, during the worlds infancy, when Aenguls and daemons roamed freely; in a time of myth and legend;in a time that few believe ever existed, there was an old wives tale, told between the ancient settlemen-\n\nts, of a particular Daemon - a Daemon with an affinity for stealing babies in the night, leaving no trace of its coming. The tale was widespreadacross the land in the wake of a wave of unexplained infant disappearances.\n\nthere were those who debunked the rumour as fear mongering and heresy. What no one knew, however, was the truth. Under the cover of the stars, the Daemon Metztli would visit lonely farmsteads, driven by the sent of infant's blood,\n\nand in the depths of the night, steal the infants from the safety of their cribs. In the wake of several \"accidents\" surrounding the disappearances, it was said that Metztli's form was so beutiful, that those adults who looked upon her\n\nform would be driven mad and tear their own eyes from their sockets. Through fear of the truth, the village elders would often attribute this phenomenon to intense grief the parents' experienced rather than anything otherworlly\n\nChapter 2.\n  The truth behind the child disappearances does not end with Metztli however, the after math of the abductions only becomes more chilling. The children were taken far away, to an undiscovered land in the mists of\n\nthe oceans. this island was of untold beauty, giving life to many varieties of flora and fauna not yet discovered by the rest of the world. this paradise was of metztli's own creation, and all that was missign was her master race. The ocelots\n\nthat called the islands their home were taken by Metztli, and in a series of horrifying, magic infused experiments, their blood was combined with that of the infants. after generations of perfecting and tweaking and\n\nafter hundreds of hideous failures were discarded into the ocean, Metztli at last created a single white humanoid ocelot. This was the first of the Kharajyr - of the purest Descent. Instantly after beholding her new creation Metztli\n\nwas filled with the love of a mother - she had atlast succeeded in creating a race she deemed to be perfection. Desperately Metztli attempted to replicate her creation, but could never acgieve the same level of beauty of her\n\nfirst creation. Nonetheless, She embraced her new creations, the Kharajyr race, with all the love a mother could muster. After nurturing her children to a state of maturity she decided, as any caring mother would, that her\n\ntime had come to leave her creations to their own devices, to stop nurturing them and to depart the island paradise\n\nChapter 3.\n  Metztli's true intentions for the creation of the Kharajyr were never revealed. It has been speculated that she wished to recreate the for of a creature she once fell in love with, but who was\n\nstolen away from her. Others say that she wished to bestow the world with a race of sentient beings, created in her own image. still others suggest that Metztli wished only to play god and nurture other living beings\n\nGenerations passed and the Kharajyr thrived in their jungle paradise. Yet Metztli felt neglected by her children and wished for them to show their gratitude. Feeling pity towards them she gifted them signs,\n\nwishing to guide them in the knowledge of their own creation. These signs were unravelled and interpreted by the kharajyr sages, and her people accepted her as their creator and divine ruler, constructing great Temples in her\n\nname and sparking the order of Priests and Priestesses, devoted to her worship.\n\nYet relatively recently, the last Emperor, Xerdun's father, deemed his dominance to be absolute and he\n\nrefused to bow befor any deity, believing himself greater even than a Daemon. His laziness and arrogance drove his Metz'al Natayshi, the only remaining Kharajyr sage, away from her own people and was\n\nultimately to be the downfall of the Kalenwyr Empire. Despire the Emperor's assassination by his son, Metztli chose to teach her creations a harsh lesson. Unbeknownst to the kharajyr, the moutain around which their capital\n\ncity had been constructed was a dormant volcano. In a torrent of fire and multen mub, the civilisation was all but buried and the Kharajyr desperately scrambled to their ships. Fleeing their homes with what little they could salvage the\n\nkharajyr set sail West, to the land of Asulon, the knowledge of their Goddess firmly ingrained into their hearts once more. Under the new Emeror's leadership, so as to avoid similar disasters Metztli, religious\n\nsacrifice and ceremony is to become an integral part of society once again. The latest Emperor, Tla' Xerdun, views the volcano as a personal warning to him to not follow in his father's footsteps....", ""),
        StaticBook("Kha who kills", "§bKoruk", "Wawnce upon a tym, thewre was a kharajyr knawn aws Zeek. Zeek was a Qi, or hawnter een the veelage. Zeek waws wawn awf tah beest Qi's een all of the kharajyr. He cawnstantly gawt meals feet fawr a Tlannti.\n\nBut thawr was sawmtheeawng Zeek deed nawt hawve. A mate. Zeek awbsessed abawt a female Ja' een thaw veelage. She waws beawtifeel awnd smat awnd all thawt. Bawt her Patta waws very peeky abawt wu cawld be her mate.\n\nZeek hawnted hawrd bawt culd nawt fynd gud enawf trophies. He tryed crocs, tygers, awnd awpes. evawn awrcs. Bawt Zeek cawld nawt impress the patta enawf. Saw Zeek tuk the mawst drawsteek mesure pawssible. \nMawrder.\n\nDa patta leeved een tah rum weeth the Ja'\nSaw Zeek wawld hawf tu be cawreful, eef the Ja' notcied, she wawld neevawr luv heem. Hees brawther waws a Do', or soldiers awf thaw kharajyr. Saw Zeek tuk hees unifawm yle he waws away.\n\nNaw thawt naw wawn wuld suspect heem, he walked thruw the Ja' rums awnd tu teh one Ja's rum. Bawt sawm real Do's cawm frawm the corner, Zeek hid een the dark shadow seence eet was nyte.\nHe deed eet bcawse the Do's myte awsk heem where hees station ees.\n\nWen tha coast was cler Zeek cunneengly snuck taw the door. HE awpened eet up a crack tah see whawt was gawng awn. Eet seemed tah Ja waws sleeping awnd teh patta ws makeeang stew. Zeek quytly opeened le dawr awnd took hees Per'tas blade awnd\n\nRawn eet throw the patta's thrawt. Tha Patta cawld nawt scream cawse awf the thrawt, all he cawld du was cawlf awt blud awnd mawr blood. He leeft thaw blawde stawk een thaw thrawt awnd wyped awf bludstains awnd made hees way awt.\n\nThaw Per'ta hawd hees nawme carved awn the blawde saw wen eet was recarvered, u cawld beet everyawn thawt eet waws the Per'ta. Da Per'ta was away colleecteeawng herbs alawn saw he hawd no alibi, awnd everyawn thawt Zeek was sleepawng.\n\nSaw the Per'ta was sentawnced taw deth awnd weethawt the Patta Zeek cawld marry thaw Ja', wu was already charmed by hees skeel befawr the murdawr, wheech she deed nawt knaw the turh abawt.\n\nTey gawt marreed. Awnd saw they plawned ta hawve mawny keetawns awnd lyf wuld be normawl fawr Zeek. Awnly thawt eet waseent. Ya see the Ja' kept a scrawl weeth her everywher she weent. Zeek deed nawt knuw whawt was een the scrawl\n\nawnly thawt eet was ther. Awnd eet bugged him, bawt he deed nawt tell the Ja'. HE deed nawt want the Patta's deth taw be een vain. \nSaw he kept hees mawth quyt awnd he hawd 3 keetawns. Dey wuld awl pass their tests of maturity awnd geet awp hy een the so-\n\ncial ladder. THe 1st becawm a Qi jawst lyk Zeek. Tah 2nd being a Ja'. Awnd thaw awther wanc becawming a munblade. He was abawt 195 yers awld. The scrawl dreev heem eensane. He lawved hees Met'zal. Bawt he deed nawt want ta die knaweeng he\n\ndeed nawt see whawt was een thaw scrawl.\nSaw he feexed awp sawm herbs fawr thaw Ja'. He put poison een the dreenk awnd so they drank.\n\nBawt the ja felt a slyt pain, awnd theen next theeawng ya knaw she was falleawng tu tha ground in pain. Zeek theen snatched thaw scrawl and red eet.\nAwnyways.. this ees whawt eet said.\n\n\"Justeece haws ben served.\" \nZeek pondered what it mant for a yle. BAwt theen he relized. Ther was nawtheeawng special abawt tah scrawl. Eet was awl a trawps to get Zeek taw luse everytheeawng he killed 4.\n\nHe hawd no Met'zal. AWnd chance awre hees keeds weel knaw he deed eet. Wheech meant he wald have nawthing. Wem tah Do's cawm Zeek sayd he accidently peeked poisonous herbs. Tey beleeved heem. Hees keeds deedant awnd he leeved ot hees\n\nlife alown. Naw wun knows wu wrote le scrawl. Rumawrs as eet thawt eet was a son. ANawrhter wun was eet was the moonblades. Anawther rumawr was thawt Metzil Herseelf plawnted the scrawl tu shaw the kharajyr ya cawnt fawrsake her.\n\nMoral awth the stawry, \nDAW NAWT MURDAWR PEAWPLE!\n\n(BTW IM SORRY I DIDNT KNOW YOU DONT USE THE ACCENT. I HOPE YOU COULD UNDERSTAND IT)", ""),
        StaticBook("Bloody note", "§bPetyr Redlock", "[!] The writing is bloody and drips down the page.\n\n\"Bad...Skyshog...\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A last goodbye?", "samler", "*A finely written letter, folded neatly with dark blue ink for letters, on the front it says. \"For Miss Lanavia.\"*\n\nDear Lanavia.\n\nI, Seth Calith, write this letter as it might potentialy be our last contact.\n\nIn your story about the dragon you claimed you had no friends, in that case I am sorry to not make it clear enough I saw a friend in you.\n\nBut just as most lives can't survive a sword in the back, friendships too can break if pulled too far.\n\nUnder the tyranny of Laethis Izalith, I lived in fear, was banished for pointing out our Tilruir'tir (Elwyn Izalith) was illigaly chosen for the title.\n\nI have been aimed at with crossbows for living in the city I chose to stay in because of family.\n\nI do not claim the current Kalenz'or is much better as a friend of mine has been assaulted by the mercenaries known as The Vigil, but I don't compare two\n\norcs together for such would be pointless. Both of them hurt our kin.\n\nWhile in power, he taught the princip of Kalenz' teachings. Decit and manipulation for gain of power.\n\nThese is the teachings which plagues our kin, a corrupted\n\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya. While I can't blame Laethis only for these teachings to run rampart amoung the shadowy elite, he is at large, part of it being widespread.\n\nThis is also a plead for you to turn away from the path you have stumbled upon.\n\nIf a home is needed I can provide such.\nIf food is needed I can gather such.\n\nAll it takes is one letter and I would come to your aid. Fear keeps me of writing the current location I call home. Fear that should Laethis read this, my life would be cut\n\nshort by a blade of a stranger or jaws of an ice cold being.\n\nThe letter is not written out of jealosy but in desperate hope that you would not go down a path which leads to corruption of your being, and for the fear of losing a friend dear to me.\n-S. C.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Gregory and Alys", "§bLeuvina Zytiaear", "Gregory's trip was long. His bare feet trotted through a dirt path that parted down the center of flowing wheat ripe for harvest. His gaze was low to keep away from the sharp rocks that threaten his feet. He took a moment to raise his head. The sea of\n\nof wheat was vast to the young man.\n\nTheir golden heads sway in waves with a peaceful hum of wind. He would not know it but he was one with the place. With features delicate as a young maiden's and skin in common with the hue of the harvest,\n\nhe looked many years younger. He looked less of a young man than a boy. \n\nHe was a boy coveted by most maidens who happened on him. There was not one attention given to any of them by Gregory as he hadn't felt the need. He was still\n\neager to play and to learn as a boy.\n\nUp ahead, only about two minutes from him lay the only break from the endless wheat. A tiny pond sits against the path with encircled trees. The pond could dry at any drought and was barely good for\n\nfor fishing, but the trees offered shade and the water made the air humid and cool. \n\nThrough the leaves, he could see a young woman at the water's edge trying her line in the water. It was Alys, he was sure, who was the single friend he had so far from\n\ntown. She wore a simple white dress, barefooted as him, and she sported a crown of flowers. She enjoyed making such simple crafts, and like Gregory, Alys was not ashamed of her girlhood. \n\nGregory made his way through the branches. Alys turned her head\n\nto see him approaching. She smiled, like she always does, when he revealed himself in the thicket. Her line tugged, but she couldn't be bothered by it. She had a flutter of womanhood when she was about him. She was aware of her feelings, but unlike others\n\nthat covet him, hers was a gentle longing rather than a desire. Gregory never used her gender against her. He always allowed her to speak and spoke freely himself. They shared their childhood together and she trusted no boy more than Gregory. She fretted\n\nwhat his manhood would do to his manners, so she did not try and arouse the man in him. She'd keep him a boy forever if she could.\n\n\"Gregory, I am glad you finished your work.\"\n\n\"There was no work for me today.\"\n\n\"Then why did you not come earlier, if I may ask?\"\n\n\"The lord's criers delivered a decree, Alys, there is to be a levy.\"\n\nAlys sat still and gazed onto the boy. Her features were much like his. Her skin was fairer, but was kissed by the sun on her shoulders and face. Her gaze persisted as she was not satisfied with his answer, and sought to provoke him to elaborate and so he\n\ndid.\n\n\"It is a matter of the Creator, a holy war in his name.\"\n\nThe girl lifts her brows. Her fifteen and him sixteen, they both understood the reality of any war. The girl began to fret before him, and deep behind his brave\n\neyes, she saw that he did too. \n\n\"He...The Creator has demanded that I participate.\"\n\nThe girl's lifted brows fall. \n\n\"Oh?\"\n\nThe boy nods half-surely.\n\n\"Then please tell me, what does the Creator look like?\" She asks.\n\n\"I...I haven't seen him, Alys.\"\n\n\"But you said the Creator demanded you to participate, didn't he tell you?\"\n\n\"He did, Alys.\"\n\n\"Then surely he has told you in person, as he would tell you himself!\"\n\n\"No, Alys!\" He shouts her name at her. She was not offended, as she appreciates when he is honest with her.\n\n\"Those in the church told you, did they?\" She asks rhetorically. Her merely can nod.\n\n\"Aren't you curious what they stand to profit? Gregory, everything the Creator does is good, but certainly a holy war will only bring suffering, how can it be truely for\n\nthe Creator?\"\n\nGregory exhales a harsh breath at her words. He doesn't offer an argument other than silence. His fair consideration of her words leaves his sweet, but simple mind with no answer. \n\n\"Alys, I am going to fight this year,\" he\n\nstates after several moments.\n\n\"Gregory, I want you to stay here.\" She retorts quickly.\n\n\"I'll come back, and I'll make good with you,\" he states, \"then it will be a truely holy war.\"\n\nThe girl shifts where she sits while she pulls her line from the water. She'd say nothing as she stood along with him. She insisted that they share a hug, which they did. \n\nThe boy went to war as he said he would. Somewhere in the war\n\n, and no man knows which battle, he was felled. He had achieved little in his short campaign and was forgoten by the king's men. \n\nThe girl waited for him to return for five years. When, at twenty, her father felt that she was spreading\n\nrumors about her family for being single at such an old age. He arranged for her marriage, and so she married. Her husband was cruel and nothing he did was good to her. She lost her first labor and soon followed her departed newborn.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem", "§bIturi Vanrya.", "Coveted be the crown and chain\n\n-=-\n\nTo leave wrists without a blister\n\nand never more fear a neighbor's whisper\n\nbut forever more the chains still hold\n\nthe man cries \"if only I were more bold!\"\n\n-=-\n\nbut the king still gives his order\n\nand his domain expands its border\n\nbut the earth opens for the soilder to lie\n\nthe woman cries \"If only my son were alive!\"\n\n-=-\n\nBoth find loathing for the crown\n\nand grow ill to their chains\n\nthe man's cowardice begins to drown\n\nthe woman's love feels it's pains\n\n-=-\n\nMan and woman come united\n\nand find the king and his brow divided\n\nin song and dance they find glee\n\nfor from their chains they are free\n\n-=-\n\nbetween the homes of man and woman\n\na great tree stands proudly without omen\n\nbut here comes the winds of winter\n\nand man and woman want the tree to splinter\n\n-=-\n\nneither has want for the cold\n\nbut which property does the tree hold?\n\nthe woman claims, by right of writ, the tree is hers\n\nbut the man retorts, \"Never has this tree ever been yours.\"\n\n-=-\n\nMan and woman agree for a simple plan\n\nthat all they need is a rightious man\n\nand raise this authority to be vehement\n\nso that he may settle their petty disagreement\n\n-=-\n\n-=-\n\nThey found a man with desired tone\n\nand lifted him together on his throne \n\nman and woman properly begin his reign\n\nand returned to their crown and chain", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "If you're reading this, I'm probably dead (which is no big surprise to be honest). Anyways, all the things that are written in this book must be done as followed, in other words these are my death wishes (or will, I mean)...\n\nTo Miche Tisharu...§0\n§0\n§0Miche, you've been a wonderful student and loving friend of mine since the beginging (aside from your arrogance and bluntness, both of us can look over those flaws either way). Anyways, I appreciate that you've been with me through\n\nthick and thin. Makes an old man happy knowing that someone is always there for them. Before I say anything else, I want to apologize for any trouble I've caused you or Kuro. All I've ever really done for you is cause you trouble and annoy you. So I'd\n\nlike to apologize; hopefully you can forgive me... Being my closet friend and being like a daughter to me, I'll hand you down all my belongings and my property. You can do anything you want with it as long as it's in your possesion and yu must spend at\n\nleast one night within my property (depending on how many houses or land I own).§0\n§0\n§0To Shiloh Ellis Atatis...§0\n§0\n§0Shiloh, you've also been a great friend of mine. Even though our friendship is very neutral, I'm still glad we've been friends\n\nfor such a long time. I'd also like to apologize to you if I've been a bother to you; all I've done to you is be a bother, an annoyance, and a major setback. All I've ever done is cause you trouble these many years. I honestly don't think I can ever\n\nforgive myself for all the trouble and stress I've caused you... Being one of my second closest friends, I will hand you down my self portrait so you can keep as a memory (or use it as a dart board or whatever. Heck, you'd probably burn it so why am I\n\neven asking you to keep it as a memory of me).§0\n§0\n§0To everyone else that I've known and cared for...§0\n§0\n§0You've all been very wonderful and great friends of mine. I could've never thought asked for any better friends than you\n\nguys. You've shown this old man what it means to live happy and prosper in life. Although we've been through thick and thin, I'd like to thank you all for being the best friends an old man can ever have...\n\n(there are several scribbles on this page that you can barely make out, due to the terrible handwriting.)\n\n\"Why do I bother even having this page..\"§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\"I don't have a wife nor anyone like that..\"§0\n§0\n§0\"I've wasted my life, haven't I\"§0\n§0\n§0(The rest is illegible and a bunch of doodles and scribbles.)\n\nFuneral arrangements...§0\n§0\n§0First off, I'd like my funeral to be held somewhere quiet and peacful (anything works as long as it fits the description). I'd also like for my body to be burnt to ashes rather than having it buried in some random place.\n\nFinally, I'd like Miche or Shiloh (both work perfectly fine) to say a few words of honor or a speech of any sort at my funeral. I would also like Naz or any bard really to play this song at my funeral. §0https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-jvf41LksxU\n\nI would also appretiate the funeral to consist of a small list of close friends and guests, those being:§0\n§0\n§0Xhaguar: sakSLK§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Combat Theory", "§bLilja Edrick", "This is a personal book on combating a mage without using any mana of your own. Steward of Skyfall; Dunstan Zytiaear told me his thoughts on combating mages. If you're reading this, you must be me years from now, or a possible student.\n\nThe entire concept is based around draining mana. As anyone who's ever connected to the Void would know, running dry of mana usually ends with fainting. The vomiting afterwards really depends on the strength of your stomach, however.\n\nDunstan's theory on combating a mage without using magic yourself is to attempt to trick them into wasting mana willy-nilly. \nAs an aspiring alterationist I find this method would come in handy should I ever get into a fight with an evocationist.\n\nAlthough I myself am not one for conflict, I figured I'd write this down instead of letting it go unsaid by our resident muscle-mountain.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asher's Guide", "§bKatari Stirling", "Beginning lessons -\n\nThe first lesson would consist of teaching said student about the void. The void is a place that consists of everything yet is nothing- a definition that has been spoken countless times throughout time. However if you're teaching a -\n\n- magic to a student it's incredibly likely that you're already aware of the void and how it works. Thefore, we'll move on to the more important teachings of actual fire evocation.\n\nA fire evocation teacher's first lesson should be simple. Incredibly simple. They would need to teach their student how to evoke a simple flame, a flame the size of a candle light; if not smaller. If necessary, the teacher could begin with a spark.\n\nThe teacher would of course explain how this process is done. The student would need to focus on their goal and their goal only- creating a small flame. They'd clear their mind of any distractions and imagine a small ember, wavering and acting just as -\n\n- any other flame would. They'd practice this act until they were capable of performing it without much of an issue.\n\nAfter that lesson would be complete, the teacher would have a bit more freedom. They would be allowed to teach their student how to direct flames in certain directions, or they could teach said student how to sustain a larger flame. The process begins -\n\n- the same way, the student creating a small ember in the void and withdrawling it into the mortal plain. If they were being taught how to create and sustain a larger flame, all they'd have to do is simply imagine their ember slowly swelling and growing -\n\n- in size. This would be quite a tiring process for a beginner of course, and they'd have to practice it for a short while just as they had to practice the sustaining of the ember. If they were learning how to direct their ember, it would also take -\n\n- a good amount of practice to complete. They'd simply imagine the movement of the flame, making sure it acts just as any other normal flame within the realworld, otherwise it would diminish into nothingness.\n\nIt would be best if the student becomes proficent in both of these tasks, as it will make the more advanced things much easier. A good size would be things such as a medium sized ball, and being able to toss the flame at a reasonabley fast speed without -\n\n- it diminishing before it reached its destination.\n\nAfter these tasks are complete, the teacher would begin teaching the more advanced parts of fire evocation. Things such as the temperature of their flame, the speed it is thrown at and even how many balls of flame are created at once; or even creating-\n\n-a torrent of flame and controlling it in different ways. There's something I feel I forgot that was important...\n\n[!] A few things are scribbled here and crossed out.\n\nOh, yes! I forgot that there's a step before all of this you have to take, that step being actually teaching your student the properties of fire. You know, things such as the way it acts, the way it reacts to other things, etc. Here, I'll give a few -\n\n- starters:\n\n- Fire is hot. What a surprise.\n-It can't be controlled to a fine degree, since it's.. fire.\n-Fire wavers and flows, it won't stay still and will always rise upward, so don't be silly and try to create a fire under your hand. Unless you're-\n\n-asking to be burnt.\n-I don't think I mentioned this yet, but fire is hot.\n-Fire is hot.\n-Super hot.\n-Fire will burn you.\n-I'm not kidding.\n\nAlso, white fire will probably kill you. Just a heads up. That's assuming-\n\n-you don't pass out first.\n\nTime between teachings and such- \n\nWe'll go off of a sort of tier system. \n\nTier one would last for about 1-2 weeks.\n\nTier two would last for about 3 more weeks until you reach tier three.\n\nTier three would last for about 1-1 1/2 elven months until tier four is achieved.\n\nTier four would last for a long while. Perhaps 2-3 months until the student masters the magic.\n\nWhat to teach at each tier-\n\nTier one- Begin with the basics. Things as simple as how to create and sustain an ember. Perhaps practicing how to grow it to a slightly larger size. Nothing else should really be-\n\n-practiced however at this stage, as that might be a bit too much for the student.\n\nTier two- Begin teaching your student how to continue the growth of their flame, and also how to start controlling its direction. Once again, nothing-\n\n-too fancy should be taught at this point, only more advanced versions of the basics. (If that makes sense.)\n\nTier three- At this tier the student would obviously continue learning how to further the movement and growth of their flame but-\n\n-they should also begin learning how to launch the flame at high velocities, ones the size of a medium sized ball. They could also begin experimenting with things such as multiple balls of flame the size of apples. Two at once, rather.\n\nTier four- At this tier the teacher should once again continue teaching their student how to increase their size and fluent movement of flames, though it becomes less of a priority. They should teach them about things more advanced. Things  such as-\n\n-evoking larger sized balls of flames at once, tossing it at quicker speeds, using fire in different forms; such as torrents and larger explosions.\n\nAt tier five, the student should be able to create their own usage for the magic and have -\n\n- essentially mastered the art.\n\n          -----\n\nThe teacher should also teach their student at about tier three how they're capable of deciding if the flame is explosive or not, though it takes a longer-\n\n- amount of time to evoke.", ""),
        StaticBook("Skyfall : Fealty", "§bSarrion Zytiaear", "“I, Sarrion Zytiaear, humble subject of the Lord Protector, the Kingdom of Vandoria, and to the future king should one fitting be found, hereby swear the following oaths...\n\n I swear to uphold the Lord Protector’s law and word.\n\nI swear to defend the Lord Protector against his enemies.\n\nI swear to protect all lawful citizens of Vandoria.\n\n I swear that my family and those under me will serve the Lord Protector as well as I.\n\nI swear to speak truth and nothing but truth to the Lord Protector, and shall not tell lies.\n\nI swear to honor and uphold the Vander Code.\n\nBy these words I and those under me swear loyalty to the Lord Protector until the end of days or until relieved of my vows by the Lord Protector. May GOD judge my soul truthfully and punish me for my faults.\n\nSigned,\nSarrion Zytiear\n\nThe Guild Master of the Society of Skyfall", ""),
        StaticBook("Report", "§bTevor Softfoot", "Place of incident: Nyrhold.§0\n§0\n§0In command: Saradunan Ivan Ulfricson.\n\nVictim was tied to a tree by her legs with many other corpses hanging from it. She was then taken to the stockade where she was made to endure public shaming with rotten produce\n\nthrown at her. The men who had taken her then proceeded to smear her face with a white narcotic substance and Cactus green thus intoxicating her. They then ripped open the back of her coat and branded her. She was then taken into a house and guards\n\non it to stop unruly peasents from injuring her further. After being sure she was safe a message was taken to Lord Sarrion of Skyfall by Tever Softfoot informing him of said events.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Sarrion", "§bBelegar Irongrinder", "Hello Sarrion, I seek more knowledge about the homunculi, specifically regarding the effects of thanhium on them. Be sure to contact me as soon as possible. \n\nSincerely, Belegar.", ""),
