        StaticBook("Study of Magic", "Toxzero", "Foreword:§0\n§0It’s really no question that our world was forged in the ways of a greater ancient magic through voidal influence as we’re so tightly tethered to the void in which those who dedicate their lives to the study of the arcane draw their powers\n\nfrom can even feel any massive differences in the void. It is in my studies of recent times that everything was created and shaped by will, which brings life to the world with such an influx of mana,\n\nallowing people who study the arts of transfiguration to be able to shift the world as they please so long it follows equivalent exchange of course.§0\n\n“Voidal Tethering”§0\n§0Our world is so heavily influenced by the void that a lot of people don’t realize it, every action leaves a shift in the void. Our realm is tethered closely to the voidal realm, everything having dormant mana and the\n\ndescendants having the scar which acts as our gateway to the voidal influence goes to show such. Mana is simply our bridges to influence the void and summon forth powers that don’t even come close to match the ancient magic before our time,\n\nand all of this sums up to a fact of voidal tethering.§0\n\nMana’s Influence:§0\n§0Every action from walking, to cooking, sword play and especially casting spells let them be voidal or deity, mana is consumed. Once we discovered how much influence we have over our mana we were able to create bridges\n\nto the void with them, and summon forth anything we could imagine, so long it followed equivalent exchange of course. Deity subjects summon the powers of the gods through a bridge created through the soul using mana,\n\nallowing them to summon forth the spell so long their bridge is held. Voidal users are able to summon forth arcane spells through the tear in their soul into the void rift, the bridge created and sustained by mana as they draw forth\n\n the endless powers of nothingness. This goes to show that anything and everything has mana that influences us, infact without such there would be no life.§0\n\nOn Deity Users:§0\n§0Deity users are people who devote their lives to the gods, or as many call them aungles or daemons. It is proven fact that these gods have direct influence on our realm, with powers unbelievable to very thought,\n\nand as every god is they are greedy for more. Subjects under these gods are considered Deity users, who summon forth the ability of their deity through a bond created by being synced to your deity,\n\nthis bond is embedded into the soul and becomes your gateway for summoning those powers. Like all spells there is a bridge formed through mana in which allows them to draw forth the powers to our realm, so long that bridge is held.\n\nOn Voidal Users:§0\n§0Every descendant has a scar inside of their soul that tethers us to the void, once tapped into and synced with the void they gain the ability to see aura and the like. Voidal users are actually little to no different to those\n\nwho worship gods, only they summon forth power through self will and imagination, knowledge purely and it’s not handed down to them. They create a bridge from themselves to the voidal realm,\n\nin which they influence the power in that realm to create the spell they so wish to desire to summon dependent on the school of magic they study, and bring forth the spell to our realm to cast such spell.\n\nWritten by Sarrion Di'Pascali.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The§0\n§0   Pen of Calligraphy§0\n§0\n§0             By§0\n§0       Lilja Acosta\n\nI acquired the Pen of Calligraphy many years ago at a travelling magic shop of sorts.§0\n§0To this day I still don't know exactly how it works. As a matter of fact, from what I can tell it shouldn't.\n\nThe pen makes the holder's penmanship look downright beautiful. It doesn't hold a mana gem, yet the enchantment works nonetheless. §0\n§0Speaking of the enchantment, I've attempted to recreate it, to no avail.", ""),
        StaticBook("Revised Chivalry", "§bFrançois \"L'Iconodule\" d'Ibelin", "The Code of Chivalry\n\nBy Ser Maric, transcribed by Ser Akal, transcribed, reworded and translated into Auverginian by Francois d'Ibelin.\n\n(Written in Auverginian, turn the page for Common translation.)\n\nLive par l'honneur, la gloire, et de garder l'honneur de votre compagnon de chevalier.\n\nHonorez le Créateur; maintenir son église.\n\nGardez la foi; agir en justice.\n\nServez votre Liège avec vaillance, de la diligence et de la conviction.\n\nPersévérez toujours; ne jamais tourner le dos à l'ennemi.\n\nNe pas donner ou prendre infraction pour des choses insignifiantes.\n\nPorter secours aux veuves et aux orphelins et considérer l'honneur des femmes.\n\nOffrir aux nécessiteux; sauvegarder l'impuissant et faible.\n\nRespecter ceux qui sont placés en situation d'autorité; lutter pour le bien-être de tous les peuples.\n\nAbstenez-vous de ce qui est injuste, cruelle ou malhonnête.\n\nPreuve de courage; être vigilant, même dans le visage du mal.\n\nMais jamais remplir votre langue avec la tromperie, même sous peine de mort.\n\nCommon Translation: \n\nLive by honour, for glory, and guard the honour of your fellow knight. \n\nHonour the Creator; maintain his church.\n\nKeep the Faith; act in righteousness.\n\nServe your liege with valour, diligence and conviction.\n\nPersevere always; never turn your back to the foe. \n\nDo not give or take offense for trivial things.\n\nGive succour to widows and orphans and regard the honour of women.\n\nOffer to the needy; safeguard the helpless and weak. \n\nRespect those placed in authority; fight for the welfare of all people.\n\nAbstain from that which is unjust, cruel or dishonest.\n\nShow courage; be vigilant, even in the face of evil.\n\nResolve not with arms that which can be resolved with swords.\n\nBut never fill your tongue with deceit, even on pain of death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Drink Menu", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Sofetios's§0\n§0       Restaurant§0\n§0\n§0      ===========§0\n§0           Drink§0\n§0           Menu§0\n§0     =============§0\n\n        Alcoholic§0\n§0       Beverages\n\nPale Ale§0\n§0\n§0Your run of the mill ale. Made with boiled then cooled water, then put through the brewing process. It has a moderate amount of alcohol.§0\n§0\n§04 Minas\n\nRed Wine§0\n§0\n§0Red wine made with boiled then cooled water, then put through the wine making process. It has a high content of alcohol. Best to drink slowly.§0\n§0\n§06 Minas§0\n\n           Tea\n\nRose petal tea§0\n§0\n§0Tea made mainly from rose petals and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel more relaxed and rejuvenated. §0\n§0\n§02 Minas§0\n\nWake Up Herbal Tea§0\n§0\n§0Tea made mainly from Herbs, made to help the drinker more alert. Caution as it is very bitter.§0\n§0\n§02 Minas§0\n\nPine leaf tea§0\n§0\n§0Tea made mainly from Pine leaves and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel more relaxed and rejuvenated it has a crisp taste. §0\n§0\n§03 Minas§0\n\nBirch leaf tea§0\n§0\n§0Tea made mainly from Birch leafs and other herbs, made to help the drinker gain more awareness of their surroundings. §0\n§0\n§03 Minas §0\n\nDandelion Petal Tea§0\n§0\n§0Tea made mainly from Dandelion petals and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel more full and at ease. It goes great with a small meal.§0\n§0\n§04 Minas§0\n\nPoppy Tea§0\n§0\n§0Tea made mainly from Poppy petals and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel more Healthy and helps relieve stress.§0\n§0\n§04 Minas§0\n\nChamomile Tea§0\n§0\n§0Tea made mainly from Oxeye daisy petals and other herbs, made to help the drinker feel more calm and breath better.§0\n§0\n§04 Minas§0\n\n         Juices\n\nPumpkin Juice§0\n§0\n§0Juice made from pumpkins, it helps keep you cool when in hot climates.§0\n§0\n§05 Minas§0\n\nMelon Juice§0\n§0\n§0Juice made from Sweet Melons, it is VERY sweet. Not for people who can’t handle too much sweetness.§0\n§0\n§05 Minas§0\n\nCarrot Juice§0\n§0\n§0Juice made from Carrots, it helps keep you cool when in humid climates.§0\n§0\n§05 Minas§0\n\n         Other\n\nEggnog§0\n§0\n§0A drink made with creamy and sweet goodness. Makes you filled with energy!§0\n§0\n§06 Minas\n\nPlease return The Menus to the waiter. Thank you!§0\n§0\n§0~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("I am a' witness", "§bJentos Blackwood", "Thas here is what happened tha' me, for A' am witness O' what happened to tha' lord Arthur Roswell.\n\n\nFor tha's man has did nothin'! Tha Falkenrath paied me' ta' spread tha' rumor that Arthur joined tha' Dunamis! They said they would feud with me' and tha\n\nStauntons. \n\n\nSigned: Jentos Adam", ""),
        StaticBook("ballad of the", "§bCroesus Letholdus", "in me school on the menu they hav fish with a ricecake\n\nawfully cold day hur en glasgae me toes er gedden a bit frosty n i can heer me mum callen me tu put sum warm socks on\n\nim writen this from inside me gym i m @ me gym tedeh liften sum\n\nw8s treyn tu ged mi muscles bak ye knu i used 2 hav big musles they used ta call me tha scottish stallion ma8\n\nme car battrey died last nite on me way home from tha pub su im sitten on tha trolly next tu some homless fella with dark skin an he's askin me\n\nall surts uf ?'s n im like wot m8 this mate askin me if im luukin 2 nab an eight ball wotever that is\n\nturns out tha fockah was a bloody cop su im here spendin me nite in th jailhouse oim prepared tho ma8 iv seen me sum jailhouse cinema at the thee atre.\n\nwot a bloddy supris m8 fish an ricecake is all these fokn cunts hav whos nan du i hav tu dropkick in tha face tuh ged meself a fockn candy in this fokckn place\n\nits been three deys iv been in tha jailhouse now ma8 nd im missin tha outside blad im missin\n\ntha trees n lakes n mountains ma9\n\nnever ged locked up in tha dog pound ma8", ""),
        StaticBook("My Confession", "§bUlfrith Hammerbane", "I Ulfrith Hammerbane§0\n§0am writing my confession of being part of a plot to frame Count Roswell.§0\n§0\n§0They recruited me while I was wrongfully imprisoned by them and forced under torture and by threat of death so spread lies about the count and to speak to\n\nthe dunamis on count Falkenraths behalf.  He plans on having the Dunamis assassinate him and then plans to overthrow the Duchy§0\n§0of Istria,§0\n§0I have seen enough blood spilled, I don't want to be cause for Roswell to lose both titles AND life because of me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Zei Grie", "§bAvenel Synalli", "I\n            III\n           IIIII\n          IIIIIII\n        II       II\n      IIII       IIII\n   IIIIIII       IIIIIII\n      IIIIIIIIIIIIIII\n       III  III  III\n      III   III   III\n      III   III   III\n      ＺＥＩ  ＧＲＩＭＯＩ\n            III\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nThe mind. One of the most powerful tools one can have, given they understand how it works. The mind holds all that is dear, all that one sees, all that one has heard, remembers and has forgotten; the mind is an infinite platform for\ncountless things.\n\nThe mind however, has a major vulnerability that being the tricky archetype of the arcane known as Illusion. While our mind can play tricks on itself, it is generally more vulnerable for being played around by an outsider. Not so many realize that\n\nthe mind generates and projects various\nillusions on itself naturally. This is what the commonfolk call 'Dreams' and if the illusions have negative themes they are 'Nightmares'. While they are considered commonplace in the community that actually sleeps,\n\npeople hardly come into conclusion that they are actually naturally occuring illusions; they are so real and genuine sensations until the dreamer realizes it is nothing but a dream. That means the key to illusion is managing to keep it realistic. Making\n\nsomeone paralyzed without any kind of contact simply doesn't add up, thus a diversion must be put in place for such an exemplary illusion to actually work. The illusions are vital for the mind mages; the Mentalists.\n\nIn no way are illusions the only thing a talented mentalist can master in their collection of spells.\nThe most common spells in a mentalists' array are telepathy, imaginary projection, means to pass barriers and melding, not to mention illusions.\n\nMore talented mentalists on the other hand have knowledge of wiping memories and cataleptic illusions, but in addition to them\n\n.\n\n.\n\n.\n\n.\n\n.\n\n..\n\n.\n\n.\n\n..\n\n.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Sorcery", "§bAmbros", "A Guide to Sorcery\n\n\n      By Ambros\n\nIn this book you will find a very simple guide on being a proper mage, this would include  your supplies you need as well as the proper training you need to become a decent mage.\n\nWhat is Arcane Magic?\nAll magic uses the same power source, although what varies from magical user to magical is dependent on how the user goes about manipulating his/her powers. Arcane magic is often considered to be a more modern version\n\nof magic compared to the ancient druids ot the gifted Ascended or Undead, although none the less Arcane magic can be considered to be the most complex of magical manipulation.\n\nHow To Manipulate Arcane Magic.\nArcane magic can be manipulated in a number of ways, although most scholars believe the best way to go about doing this is creating an image in your mind of what you want the final effect of your spell to be.\n\nSome scholars believe that the best way to use the most powerful form of magic is through emotion Of course this is quite wrong and this form of magic is hard to control and should never be done. Many mages claim that their powers are akin\n\nto keys-necessary to unlock the final effect of a spell-another, new theory has begun to gain ground among younger mages.  These energetic mages assert that components aren't keys, but rather locks, suggesting that even the most learned of\n\narcanists don't fully control their own powers, and that components are necessary intruments to keep the spells in check. Whether these locks were placed by the deities themselves or are simply such an old conention that\n\nno one today questions their utility is anyone's guess.\n\nDiffrent Types Of Magic\nMages are mostly a combat and \"trick\" type magic.  Rarely do they have access to many of the necromany and healing magic that the Undead, Ascended, or druids might have.\n\nAlthough they can often achieve a number of other magical feats that the other magical orders can not.  Since arcane magic is a magic of the mind its power is based off of your intelligence then more often than not you will see a mage locking a door with\n\na spell, shooting fire from his staff, or moving blocks of stone about.  This is due to the fact that arcane magic is not a spiritual form of magic so any form of \"spiritual\" attributes about it are gone.\n\nA healer mage is a very rare sight as well, healing magic is a form of \"spiritual\" magic helping the mind cleanse and wash away pain and injury. Now of course you might see an unorthodox way of healing from a mage such as sealing a wound with fire\n\nor easing pain with a numbing spell.  Whatever the case is arcane magic is a magic of the mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human Anatomy", "§bIoannis", "-= Body Anatomy =-§0\n§0\n§0The face is covered with lots of nerves. An injury there would cause a lot of bleeding. Best way to treat the injury would be to locate it , clean it with some water or vodka and use a bandage.\n\nEyes are rather too complicated. An injury there would mean a loss of an eye since it cant be treated, not with the current tools.§0\n§0\n§0The neck has too many nerves and muscles. Trying to find and clean the wound as fast as possible. Use§0\n§0cauterise and bandage\n\nChest:§0\n§0By studing the body, i came to the conclusion that the best way to treat a wound or major injury is by locating the it as fast as possible , use a cloth to stop the bleeding and then clean it , using vodka to prevent any infection.\n\nLegs:§0\n§0Cleaning the wound and covering it with a bandage will suffice.§0\n§0For deeper cuts , locating the wound to stop bleeding and using cauterise on the main artire to cauterise it and stop bleeding is required.\n\nArms:§0\n§0Arms are covered by more muscle than feet , especialy in warriors. To treat a wound , treat it with extreme caution in order not to damage any nerve. Use bandages and vodka , cauterise only if needed.\n\nRemoving of dead tissue:§0\n§0\n§0Use a sharp dagger or a schapel. Clean before removing and after with vodka. Cauterise after and keep an eye on the patient.\n\nInfections:§0\n§0Many do die from them. Use a schapel , dived in vodka for few minutes before usage. Make a cut on one side of the infection and remove any liquids with a cloth. Later remove all of the infection and pour vodka. Cauterising suggested.\n\nDrawings of the human anatomy can be seen on this page with small notes beneath them.§0\n§0\n§0Each body part , drawn with every detail.", ""),
        StaticBook("My broken Soul", "§b[Edict] Nephor Fortza", "-=-§0\n§0Erik has tortured his own brother... Joto... he refuses to speak with us so he just ignores us like the asshole he is. Erik and I were a couple, were. He asked me after we've gained friendship. I said yes with no hesitation. I loved Erik...\n\nBut did he love me? I thought he did for the reason he asked me to be with him... I thought he loved me just as much as I loved him. We were together for a few years, two or three... Until someone in Edict told him I was flirting with other guys. I WASN'T\n\nHe brought me to the balcony outside of the barracks, I knew it was bad when he needed to speak with me. §0\n§0\n§0When he brought me out there, he told me that he was told that I was flirting with other guys... I denited it with my life, hoping for his trust...\n\nafter a good five minutes of denial and convincing, §0\n§0   \"Nephor, I can't do this anymore...\" §0\n§0\n§0At that point my heart shattered. It felt like I was swallowing acid, I could practically feel my heart breaking. So I croaked \"Okay\" and walked away...\n\nWe haven't really spoke to eachother at all. Just glaring to eachother like strangers, clueless as to why he left me. I still loved him, I still cared for him. §0\n§0\n§0Did he not feel that to me?§0\n§0\n§0I guess not...\n\nSoon after the Edict left the Princedom, We all went to an island. We didn't stay there long though. For the time we WERE there, Joto acted different towards me. He acted more fragile. I appreciated it, No more insults, no more bumps to my shoulder...\n\nJoto had asked me to be with him, he'd asked me if we could be a couple. I simply nodded on the outside, on the inside, I was dancing my life away, knowing i'd be with someone for a long time. §0\n§0\n§0*a picture of a well drawn tree with a rose at the roots*\n\nJoto and I were together for a long time, not as long that Erik and I... nevermind him. Joto and I were together for about a year and a half, I loved him and I felt like he loved me. I only prayed that he wouldn't break my heart like Erik had...\n\nI stood at the tree. Looking in horror at Jotos mangled body. No eyelids, no teeth, no claws, only a lump of fur, meat, and blood. Vulthur had already ran back to the grove shouting for Erik. I ran after him, hoping for the revenge Vulthur wanted...\n\nWe found Erik at the docks. He was sitting on a wagon with a cocky grin slapped on his face, it was disgusting. It gives him pleasure when he murders his brother. He refused to speak to us, ignoring our threats and requests little by little...\n\nSomehow a dark elf and I got into an argument, she hegan to lecture me on why Erik left me in such a painful way. §0\n§0 \"He never cared,\"§0\n§0      \"He didn't love you\"§0\n§0         \"He didn't give a fuck\"\n\nAt that point I couldn't stant it... I tried to ignore her, but her words pierced me like knives and glass. At that point I just left. It was unbearable to listen to her horrifying words. It's because I've never heard them before in my life...\n\n            -=-\n\n\n\n\n            End\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n            -=-", ""),
        StaticBook("Unfortunate End", "§bZenro", "Day 3: I was following some old man through Felsen when he came to the Felsen Grove. He started shouting at the Druids gathered there, demanding they tear it down. I am unsure what to think, all I know is that when I moved into Felsen, this grove was\n\nalready here, so I assume they got proper permission.\n\n***\nThe Journal ends abruptly here, many pages are ripped out ahead, and the next page is stained a crimson red. You may assume, the Halfling has, sadly, died.\n***\n\nRunning away, through the woods, can't stop to write more, large, green men with clubs. \n\nI have made it behind a tree, I think I am safe from them! Oh no... I hea them coming back, it's only a matter of time before they s *** The Journal ends here ***", ""),
        StaticBook("Z's Journal #1", "§bZenro", "Day 1: Met a nice lady in Felsen! She had a black eye, though. She said she ran into a wall! I don't believe her, I hope she's okay at home.\n\n   Met some nice man in a large scarf! We enjoyed some ale! Alot of ale, actually! I had to go buy a new keg!\n\n  I met a wonderfully nice lady. Her name is Avelon! She was being flocked by all the boys in Felsen! They are disgusting! I took her to my little abode, and gave her a place to stay for a bit, while the boys stopped looking for her. She said they were\n\ngoing to rape her, how despicable! I'm glad she's safe now, and I gave her a key incase she needs to ever run back here to hide from them.\n   \n   I met a nice Felsen Guard! How special! He told me where to refill my keg of ale. I sure hope the\n\nFelsen Inn's ale is tasty! Mmm... I can taste it now.\n\n   I met a nice, young man that told me how to get to the Inn! I'll be sure to return the favor for him some day! Perhaps he'd be thirsty for some ale one day, after a long days work.\n\n   I witnessed some Felseners trying to do things to a poor girl! They took turns on her! How awful! I wish I could have helped her.\n\n   I found an old friend wandering through  the streets! She was approached by the same nasty, nasty man! She was\n\nable to get away, however! I am sure glad for that. The men in Felsen need to learn how to keep their hands off of every woman they see! Honestly, it is so terrible.\n\n   I met a void magic user! He uses telekinesis! He floated my dirk around me, and\n\nthen set it into my hand! How interesting! He said he would be my partner in adventuring, this I am very much interested in! He seems like a good lad. His name is Gredge.\n\n   I met a nice lady named Ixtara! She welcomed me to Felsen. I've known her\n\nbefore this actual meeting, though! I met her while trying to get into Felsen with her, we were both trapped at the gate and she called a guard over, and he opened the gate for us!\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nDay 2: I was sitting in the Felsen square when somebody said a rug was walking around! How weird! When I turned around there was just a bunch of Felseners, and a Kharayjr. That man lied to me... why'd he do that? I really wanted a rug...\n\n   I was shown\n\nthe head of a Elf! He looks like a High Elf! Or perhaps a Snow Elf... I was told he was a prince. Dumb Elves, very weak... very... very weak.\n\n   I met someone named Luna, she was crying in the Tavern! I went and tried to calm her down. It worked!\n\nWe went to the docks, and sat there. I made her feel better. She has a bunch of nasty scars, but I don't want to ask about them. That'd be rude! She fell asleep on me as I'm writing this, so I'll probably be here awhile. That's fine, though! I enjoy\n\ntalking to her, and it appears I'm making her feel better with this.\n\n*The Pages ahead were torn out, and the Journal ends here. The Reader would perhaps see faint traces of something red on the pages. Perhaps someone or something bled onto the pages?*", ""),
        StaticBook("StuffForMuildir", "§bAnthron", "To you, Muildir, I leave you my minas((there would be 10 minas in the chest)) \nMay they be of more use to you as they were to me.\n\nFarewell - Anthron", ""),
        StaticBook("Karma", "§bIsengar Brockfall", "The breeze flew into the deserted inn.\nThe doors slammed shut every minute, whilst the inn keeper kept his elbow onto the counter and his hand pushed onto his face people were looking in and running off.\n\n\"COM' 'N 'ERE\" he would shout.\nBut they got too scared and ran off into the distance.\n\nHe would glance out the dirty window, looking at the sky until it fades dark.\nHe would then blow out the candles, put on his brown coat and walk\n\nhome.\nHe would always hide the key under the inn mat.\n\n\"'Lo Isengar\" they would say when he stumbled into Gimblewood.\nIsengar was never the social person so he often grumbled or moaned and kept to\n\nhimself.\nAs he jammed in his silver key into his burrow he would sit down on his hand made wooden chair.\nYou could count his personal items in a matter of seconds.t\n\n1) 2 wooden spoons\none for eating and the other one for stiring stew.\n\n2) A small handmade wooden chair with a tied on cotton pillow.\n\n3) A dusty desk with old books on it stacked Alphebetically.\n\n4) An old mattress that has yellow stains on it.\n\n5) A bucket full of dirty water with old socks in it.\n\n6) A small wardrobe\n\n7) Knives and forks\n\nAs much as Isengar seemed like he was poor from the way his house was, he was actually very rich.\nHe was very tight with his money.\n\nHe always seemed to have money in his pockets or in the bank.\nPeople teased him saying \"Yer go' 'ny dust 'n t'em notes?\"\n\nHe would sit on his chair smoking a pipe looking out his window.\nHe would then prepare his favourite food:\n\nA roast pork stew with some seasoning.\nHe would stir the stew until it is brown, thick and gooey.\nWhere the meat is soft and tender.\nAfter his large meal he would wash it down with some Carrot juice that he squishes with a circular cutted log.\n\nThen he would go straight to his wardrobe and pull out his Light blue PJ's.\n\nThen he would go bed.\n\nOne day Isengar got up at about 5:30 which gives him time to prepare the meals for his inn.\n\nAs Isengar slowly got out his bed stretching his arms and yawning with a glum look on his face he would get changed into his coffe stained shirt.\n\nHe would then then put on his black trousers and head to work.\n\nIsengar glanced out\n\nhis window, and noticed it was pouring with rain.\n\"Hmph\" he grumbled.\n\nHe would slip on his coat and wander outside.\nHe would take a right to head out of Gimblewood.\n\n\"Mornin' Mr Brockfall\" one of the Halflings smiled.\nIsengar gave him a fake smile and headed out.\n\"Feckin' humbug\" he whispered as he passed him.\n\nHe arrived at the inn at last the rain started to quieten down Isengar started to relax.\nHe made himself a mug of Vincenzo Ale slurping at every sip.\n\nSoon an odd man walked in with a red robe and had a strange look on his\n\nface.\n\n\"What ca' a'h get yer?\"\n\n\"Nothing\" he replied\n\nIsengar looked at him with a confused and solid look on his face.\n\n\"T'en ge' out yer stuped feck\" he shouted.\n\n\"Now. Now no need to get feisty little one\" he smirked.\n\nIsengar started to calm.\n\n\"Yer obviously 'ave a'h reason ter com' 'ere a'h s'pose?\"\n\n\"Aye\" the man said.\n\n\"T'en tell me'h or ah'll...\"\nIsengar threatened but was interupted by the man.\n\n\"You should learn to give your money away young man!\"\nhe smiled.\n\n\"A'h can do what a'h w'unt wit' me money yer cunt\" arthur growled.\n\n\"Aye, you can but perhaps you should learn to give some away to your fellow Halflings.\"\n\n\"'o do yer t'ink ye ar' tellin' me wot ter do wit' me mon'eh?\"\n\n\"I am Karma\" he smiles.\n\n\"Pfft, yer bullshites catchin' up wit' yer.\"\nHe grins an evil smile.\n\n\"Get ready Isengar for bad things to happen to you!\"\n\nIsengar ignored his pathetic speech, and carried on cleaning his counter with a ragged cloth.\n\nLater on when Isengar finished work he noticed a man sitting on the side of the road.\nWhen Isengar passed the man gripped his\n\ntrousers and asked for money, Isengar refused to give his money away to a peasant.\n\n\"Ge'h a'h job yer pesant\" he shouted.\n\nThe man looked down at the dirty pavement in sorrow.\n\nIsengar walked off to Gimblewood.\nAs he came in he noticed his house had a big sign out front, as he read the sign aloud it said:\n\n\"Dear Mr.Isengar, a'hm afrai' we'h kickin' yer out. Yer see Gimblewood 's a'h community, we'h shar'\n\nour stoof, so be packed by tomorro'.\"\n\nIsengar was furious, he kicked the sign over in rage.\nAnd went over to Milo's house.\n\"Yer feckin' cunt, yer can't kic' ma'h out!!!\"\n\nMilo chuckled \n\"Isengar calm dow'\" he said in a calm voice.\n\"CALM DOW' EY? YER FECKIN' KICKIN' MA'H OU'!!!!\"\n\"A'h can see why yer angr'eh, but unti' yer learn ter shar' yer shite t'en yer ain't comin' back!\"\n\nAs Isengar stomped back into his house grabbing and throwing things about.\nHe packed anything important like food etc.\n\nSo as Isengar was knocking things off the shelf into his small handmade bag he panicked of where he was going to stay.\n\n\"'n inn perhaps\" he muttered.\nIsengar peeked under his chair and grabbed his bag of 200 minas.\n\nIsengar opened his burrow door and slung his bag's over his shoulder.\nHe took the silver key out his pocket and looked at it for a\n\nmoment, then he extended his arm back and threw it forward letting go of the key it plopped into the lake and sunk into the soil.\n\nIsengar had his head down with a glum look on his face, the other Halflings giggled as he stumbled out of Gimblewood.\n\nIsengar walked down the road to Petrus.\nHe was blinded by the light when he was out of the trees.\nSquinting his eyes he made out a figure on the end of the bridge.\nIsengar Huffed realising who it was!\n\nIt was the Old man, he smiled at Isengar laughing.\nA sudden voice came to Isengar's head.\n\"Had enough yet, small one?\" The voice giggled.\nIsengar did not reply but instead shook his head.\n\nThe man smiled with an evil grin.\n\nSuddenly the rain started to fall from the clouds!\n\n\"'S t'is Karma too yer cunt!?\"\nThe man started to chuckle.\n\n\"No, That's just the weather\" he says politley.\n\n((PART 2 WILL COME OUT SOON))", ""),
        StaticBook("Song Of Roses", "§bLentos", "*The words of the poem are written neatly, yet artfully in a way*\n\n Oh tweety bird what is your sorrow.\n\n Of love or hate-\n Or petty quarrel.\n\n Up there you sit atop your tree.\n\n You choose to sing-\n Yet not for me.\n\n Your song is for the  Wayward Vagabond.\n \n The sickyly brother.\n\n And all those who wither.\n\n You sing to them-\n Of the trees.\n\n Their gnarled roots.\n \n And joyful leaves.\n\n Yet they do not listen.\n\n No not to you.\n \n You singing bird atop your stoop.\n \n Instead they listen-\n To the flowers.\n\n Who's words are encrypted.\n\n Behind their petals.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Lur's Journal§0\n§0Day 1§0\n§0Drunk§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0This is def not a dairy, ok mabey a little.\n\nDay 2§0\n§0Drunk\n\nDay 3§0\n§0Drunk\n\nDay 4 §0\n§0Drunk\n\nDay 5§0\n§0Drunk\n\nDay 6 §0\n§0Kon stole me ale§0\n§0he shall pay§0\n§0Drunk\n\nDay 7§0\n§0Drunk\n\nDay 8§0\n§0I'm a cunt drinking Ale", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Unknown Topics V1: The Fylax§0\n§0written by: Makai§0\n§0Researched by: Makai and Demo\n\nIntroduction:§0\n§0In these books I shall be discussing topics that are vastly unknown by the vast majority of the people in our world. These topics often take many, many days, months or perhaps even years to research. Me and my partner will often have\n\nmore people helping us research these topics than we name. Also we won't name many people we talk with out of respect for their privacy. In this volume we shall discuss something called \"The Fylax\".\n\nBackground:§0\n§0Me and my partner were in the Library of Dragur when we came upon a book in the Kharajyr section. This was a book called \"Sage's Entry\". It seems to be some sort of guild, order, or organization that is researching something of it's own.\n\nWe are unsure as to what this Fylax is researching, but we intend to find out.", ""),
