        StaticBook("autograph", "§bMand'ani Volani", "To my number 1\n    fan, Adel suka\n\n   From your pal,\n   Mand'ani Volani", ""),
        StaticBook("Govt. I.D. [005]", "§bGoseph Joebbelstein", "===Heil Vandaloria===§0\n§0\n§0Name: §0\n§0Adil ibn Athir§0\n§0MCName: kincaid_§0\n§0\n§0Position: Council Member of Hallowvale.\n\nClearance:\nLevel 5\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nlol\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nasdsa", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "=================== Captain's log of Edward Thatch. §0\n§0===================It all began with a dream, a dream to become the greatest sailors the world would know, and we knew exactly how we were going to get there. I, and my brother Thomas came from humble\n\norigins, forced to make our own living from the tender time of adolescence, having to fish across the Orenian provinces just to make ends meet, this is where we found... Him.§0\n§0\n§0T'was a stormy day, the sea hammered out at the Felsen docks, threatening to\n\nrise up and swallow us in, but it was a risk we had to bear; for that was a day one of fine angling, Tythersharks as big as Orcs came about the docks, being tossed about by the hot Khalestinian foam into nets reach, first came one, then two, then ten...\n\nAnd that's where we found him... Or rather, he found us. After a good amount of success realing in the tackle, we found something, about the size of a Halfing's head, but much hairier, and without a body... A coconut. Maybe it was just coincidence, or\n\nperhaps destiny, but one thing I do remember for sure about that chance encounter, is that Coconut was nothing ordinary- For it spoke to me, and me alone. Upon observing it with curiousity and asking myself \"What is this?\" I heard it- No. I FELT it... One\n\nword singed into my very mind, a word of purity, hope, power.§0\n§0\n§0\"Kieth.\"\n\n===================Part two:§0\n§0Keith, he who I serve.§0\n§0===================Things seemed much better after that, I kept Keith at my side, kept him safe, in return Keith gave me his knowledge, his wisdom, his blessing. As we lay beneath the stars at\n\nnight he would speak to me, only after Tom was asleep he'd enlighten me with his brilliant teachings and tales of who and what he was before he was imprisoned within his wooden cage, though this is perhaps something for another book entirely.§0\n§0\n§0After some\n\ntime, Tom grew curious, as any man would having seen his brother carry a coconut at all times for most of his teenage years; I had kept Keith to myself until this point, for fear of Thomas trying to take him away from me, or not understanding the forces\n\nat work, Tom was after all, the stupid one. At first I kept quiet, mulling over the best way to explain the hallowed seed which I carried, that's when he grew impatient. He looked to me, with that stupid look upon his face, and then started grabbing Keith\n\n\"It's just a coconut! Why wont you show me?\" he'd jeer, all the while getting more and more physical, trying to tear Keith from my grasp- and then I lost control... First it was a punch to the gut, trying to keep him away. Then he hit back, and I followed\n\nwith a kick in his shin, then a punch in the throat, then a stamp upon his toe, sending him to the ground. I climbed atop him and with a snarl I asked \"You want me to show you? I'll show you!\" and here is where things got dark. First it was just a few\n\npunches in his face, to show him a lesson, a cut lip, a bleeding nose, a black eye- nothing too serious... Then something came over me... Something cold. I raised Keith above my head, high into the sun, then brought him down into Thomas' face, right in\n\nhis eye. One. Two. Three. Thomas was out cold after the first, the others were sheer aggression.§0\n§0\n§0About an hour passed before Thomas came to his senses, I was about to leave him for dead but forced myself to stay, he was my brother after all-\n\n\"Look after your brother\" I remember mother saying as we left home. He seemed alright, sure, covered in blood and bruises, but he would live, hopefully. \"What happened?\" he asked me, barely moving. Remember this, dear reader, if I wasn't granted that time\n\nwhilst he slept to plan out a response, I would've killed him before he had a chance to speak. I craftily responded \"Fishing accident; You reeled in a big one, it came at your face, knocked you out cold... You hit your eye on a rock, is it okay?\" To this\n\nday I regret such a question, as the answer I had received was \"Edward, my eye, it's gone! It's popped! I can't see with it!\" my heart sank \"You still have half your vision, be grateful brother.\" I responded leaving little else on the matter. He\n\nwanted to see a monk and try to have it fixed, but I feel like somehow... They'd know. I told him it would heal on its own, not to waste the Monk's time. Not to waste my time. From what I've observed, he doesn't remember the fight we had, or what it was\n\nabout, though I have my doubts. To this day he has yet to ask about Keith. Thomas' eye never healed.\n\n===================Part three:§0\n§0The Broken Toe.§0\n§0===================A few years later we found ourselves in the Cloud Temple, not to allow Thomas time with a monk, for he did request it, but simply to find one capable in the magical arts, for a week\n\nprior, during a conversation with Keith he had told me that in order to help him, and myself, I would need to grow stronger, not only physically, but mentally, in order to fulfill that which he had planned I would need to become masterful in the arts of\n\nmagic, though which arts he did not specify, as they would present themselves to me eventually.§0\n§0\n§0It is here that we first encountered Avos, a Highlander, though of Heartlandish appearance, bearded and shaggy haired like myself, looking around the same age\n\nthough with much fairer hair, and paler, softer skin. He wore a silken shirt and weaved trousers, he also seemed to speak with less of an edge than my brother and myself, from my observations I deduced him to be a much less seasoned character than I and\n\nThomas. He seemed awfully trusting of others, vulnerable even, he asked us to join him on his quest to Felsen, in search of a Clergy. After some private discussion with Thomas, and establishing that Avos was in fact NOT a homosexual, we decided to join\n\nhim, seeing an opportunity to safely return to Felsen following the end of the Duke's war, in search of work amongst their Anglers.§0\n§0\n§0It seemed once again Keith had delivered his blessing unto us, for rather than a mediocre fishmongers job in the Felsen\n\ndocks like we had hoped, we were instead lead by a group of crusaders to the New Port Vydrik, there we discussed an interesting agreement with the Count, Percival Staunton, whom offered us a private ship, with which we would bring cargo and trade to the\n\nport. Around a year went past and things were good, we established a fish trade with the local tavern, a lumber supply to (the now late) Lord George and a crop trade with the local farmspeople, keeping our ship forever stocked in a cargo of Sugar and Hay.\n\nEventually we christened the ship \"The Broken Toe.\" for its shoddy appearance, receiving the blessing of both Father Piers and Keith, who seemed especially pleased with our step up in the world. I established an altar of sorts behind the helm for Keith,\n\nso that in my absence he would pilot the ship for me.§0\n§0\n§0Despite this busy time, I still retained my goal of becoming stronger, in order to serve him in whatever his divine scheme would entail, using my new vessal to search the far corners of Vailor in\n\nsearch of one who could enlighten me in the magical arts. §0\n§0After a few Saints days, I found myself at the Caliphate, here I first encountered the owner of the Eastin Dia trading company, Captain Ayche Raven'Kor, who just so happened to be a mage\n\nhimself. Upon discovery of me and my brother's youthful admiration of his work, and my own tradeship which I had offered to collaborate with his fleet, he informed me that he already had two students of his own and could not take another, though did teach\n\nme a summary of the different types of magic, namely two which Keith himself instructed me to seek, having explained to him their uses; Electrical Evocation, an art in which one would channel magic from something called 'The Void' and use it to form their\n\nown Lightning as a weapon with which they could destroy their opponents. The other being what was called \"Contract Magic\" a form of 'Rune Smithing' in which one could create a document of sorts, binding those who sign to the contract holder's will, for\n\nthreat of magical punishment.§0\n§0\n§0I, and Keith saw both of these magics as potentially fit to aid our cause, though it seemed that teachers of which were in small supply, apparently.§0\n§0\n§0A few weeks passed, I went in search for a teacher in the High\n\nElven capital of Haelun'or, though whilst there I did come into contact with a gentleman by the name of 'Galahad', a rather well spoken businessman of sorts, whom attempted to insult me, I would've physically taken him on there and then if it wasn't for\n\nKeith instructing me otherwise.§0\n§0\n§0Upon my return to Port Vydrik I encountered a woman by the name of May Scarlett speaking with Count Percival. When I approached I was informed by Percival that miss Scarlett wished to join my crew, at first I was hesistant\n\n\"A woman should have no place on a tradeship\" I would explain, though Count Percival persisted, for his influence alone I allowed May to become a Scout for the Broken Toe, on the condition she would also aid our attempts to supply the tavern with Fish.\n\nWhilst Thomas showed May about the ship and I consulted her presence with Keith, a chance encounter occurred; Galahad happened to arrive, claiming to have been in search of my vessal, he had a trade offer for me, a potion of his he refered to as Ruibrium.\n\nThough somewhat illegal in most of the Orenian provinces, I accepted the offer due to the amounts offered for shipping out his drug, which Keith suggested would be a perfect time in which to continue searching for magical practitioners, travelling the far\n\ncorners of Vailor to sell this product, hopefully finding a master of Electrical Evocation or Contractual Magic along the way.\n\n===================Part Four:§0\n§0Dirty Deeds.§0\n§0===================Now I, dear reader, am no fool. I am well aware of the dangers about", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Ser Orgmar (Org_The_Robo)§0\n§0Garsto Leaf§0\n§0(LevitatedPotato.)§0\n§0George Staunton§0\n§0(WoodenApples)§0\n§0Babad Ooks§0\n§0(Babadooks)§0\n§0Ysolda-Aria Endoriel§0\n§0Johanna", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dear Arty,§0\n§0\n§0Ye butt 'tis so smelly Iblees woul' refuse ye arse entry inte the nether.§0\n§0\n§0Love§0\n§0Pikel B.§0\n§0\n§0Ps. Ye feet stink too.", ""),
        StaticBook("Besti", "§bAudbjørn Fáóláin", "General Beastiary\n- Discoveries during my travels.\n   - Vivianne Verdigris\n\nNote- This was written by Vivianne Verdigris, I just happened to find it after she left.\n\n\n\n\n\n     The Boar\n\nThe boar is so fierce a beast, and also so cruel, that for his fierceness and his cruelness, he despiseth and setteth nought by death, and he reseth full piteously against the point of a spear of the hunter. And though it be so that he be smitten or\n\nsticked with a spear through the body, yet for the greater ire and cruelness in heart that he hath, he reseth on his enemy, and taketh comfort and heart and strength for to wreak himself on his adversary with his tusks, and putteth himself in peril of\n\ndeath with a wonder fierceness against the weapon of his enemy, and hath in his mouth two crooked tusks right strong and sharp, and breaketh and rendeth cruelly with them those which he withstandeth. And useth the tusks instead of a sword.\n\nAnd hath a hard shield, broad and thick in the right side, and putteth that always against his weapon that pursueth him, and useth that brawn instead of a shield to defend himself. And when he spieth peril that should befall, he whetteth his\n\nAnd hath a hard shield, broad and thick in the right side, and putteth that always against his weapon that pursueth him, and useth that brawn instead of a shield to defend himself. And when he spieth peril that should befall, he whetteth his\n\ncomforteth the roots of his teeth therewith by vertue thereof.\n\n\n\n\n\n  The Eagle\n\nWhen an eagle is corky, its eyesight dims and its feathers and wings become heavy. to rejuvinate itself, the eagle flies up to the climature of the sun, which burns aroint the humour ov'r its eyes and burns off its corky feathers. the eagle then plunges\n\nthree times into water, and its youth is restor'd. also as a result of age, the eagle's beak grows until it can nay longer englut; by striking it against a rock, the eagle breaks its beak which then grows back. the eagle's eyes art very sharp and can\n\nsee gudgeon when the bird flies ov'r water. the eagle can look directly into the sun. as a test of the worthiness of its young, the eagle holds them up facing the sun. the birds that cannot stare into the sun and turn their eyes aroint art cast out of\n\nthe aery.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  The Fox\n\nA fox is called Vulpes, and hath that name as it were wallowing feet aside, and goeth never forthright, but always aslant and with fraud. And is a false beast and deceiving, for when him lacketh meat, he feigneth himself dead, and then fowls\n\ncome to him, as it were to a carrion, and anon he catcheth one and devoureth it. The fox halteth always, for the right legs are shorter than the left legs. His skin is right hairy rough and hot, his tail is great and rough; and when an hound weeneth\n\ntake him by the tail, he taketh his mouth full of hair and stoppeth it. The fox doth fight with the brock for dens, and defileth the brock's den, and hath so the mastery over him with fraud and deceit, and not by strength.... The fox feigneth himself\n\ntame in time of need, but by night he waiteth his time and doeth shrewd deeds. And though he be right guileful in himself and malicious, yet he is good and profitable in use of medicine.\n\n\n\n\n\n The White Hare\n\nthe white hares of the alps art thought to englut snow in the winter, f'r they turn col'r when the snow melts. some say that the hare is as many years corky as it hath folds in its bowels, and that 'tis a hermaphrodite that can\n\nreproduce without a mate.\n\n\n\n\n\n    The Hedgehog\n\nThe hedgehog has the appearance of a young pig, but is entirely covered with sharp spines or quills, which protect it from danger. When it is time for the harvest, the hedgehog goes into a vineyard, and climbing up a vine, shakes the grapes\n\noff onto the ground. It then rolls around on the fallen grapes to spear them with its quills, so it can carry the fruit home to feed its young. (Some say that the fruit the hedgehog carries away is the apple or fig.) A cooked hedgehog can be used to make\n\nmedicine. When the hedgehog notices the approach of a man, it rolls itself into a ball so its spines protect it, and creaks like a cart to fool the man. Hedgehogs can detect the direction the wind is blowing from; when the wind comes from the\n\nnorth, the hedgehog closes the north hole of its lair.\n\n\n\n\n\n The Jay, or Jackdaw\n\nThe jay 'r jackdaw is a noisy bird. it lives in forests and flies from tree to tree, singing noisily. a captur'd jackdaw can be kept in a cage and can be taught to talk. if such a bird escapes back to the forest, 'tis yea noisier than 'ere.\n\n\n\n\n\n The Nightingale\n\nNightingales sing continuously for fifteen days and nights when leaves first appear in the spring. This bird has a remarkable knowledge of music, and uses all of the arts that human science has developed in the mechanism of the\n\nflute. Each bird knows several songs, with the songs differing beween birds. There is great competition and rivalry between them; the one who loses the competition often dies, her breath giving out before her song. Young\n\nnightingales are taught music by their elders; they are given verses to practice, and improve their singing under the criticism of the instructor.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n   The Owl\n\nThe bird of the night haunts ruins and flies only at night; preferring to live in darkness it hides from the light. 'tis a dirty, slothful bird that pollutes its own aery with its dung. 'tis oft found near tombs and lives in anters. some\n\nsay it flies backwards. when other birds see it hiding during the day, they noisily attack it to betray its hiding place. birds of the night caterwauling out when they sense that someone is about to die. there art several kinds of birds of the\n\nnight describ'd in the bestiaries: noctua, the night-owl, that lives in the walls of ruin'd houses and shuns the light; nicticorax, the night-raven; and the bubo, the ingraft bird of the night, a dirty bird that pollutes its aery.\n\n\n\n\n\n  The Raven\n\nThe raven beholdeth the mouths of her birds when they yawn. But she giveth them no meat ere she know and see the likeness of her own blackness, and of her own colour and feathers. And when they begin to wax black, then afterward she\n\nfeedeth them with all her might and strength. It is said that ravens' birds are fed with dew of heaven all the time that they have no black feathers by benefit of age. Among fowls, only the raven hath four and sixty changings of voice.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Proposal", "§bRoland Graeme", "With my utmost respect, I am writing to who'm ever this may concern in the topic of recruiting. I am a young and abled body who wishes to join your mighty empire in the feilds of battle, where the sparks fly from perfectly crafted mettle,\n\n\nAnd to be a loyal guard who will watch over your city with pride, and gratitude knowing \"Thy leaders have trusted me to protect their great lands.\" The honor in standing with your spirit is profoundly my most cherished dream.  Nonetheless,\n\nIf all else fails... And I am not able to be a knight of thy hold, I am perfectly willing to to use my other expertise for the greater good. As you may well now know, I have broke into your castle recently, asking to join you on your noble cause. So I\n\nHave aquired some skills in the steath, and speed arts. I have also started to train myself in Breeding, and Smithing. May anything I offer be of use, please do so consider my proposal.       With my deepest Gratitude\n    -Roland", ""),
        StaticBook("Misfortune Hunt", "§bMisfortune Teller", "The land is small and full of lore.\n\nThe pumpkins grow around your hoe.\n\nThe King of all is next to me, but huge to all that are in his fee.\n\nRoad Down to the giant Tree where people laugh and drink with me.\n\nStraight into the moon at night, lowering down onto the road.\n\nInto the Holy flame and water, Ying and Yang.\n\nRun through the never ending vines and fields.\n\nTowards the doors of young and into the water of smelly tears.\n\nYou see the grand one resting on his throne, surrounded by his minions and watching over the town.", ""),
        StaticBook("Question 1", "§b[Child] Kloxin Jayamen", "Please answer to the §mBestest§r best of your ability! \n\n1. If I am you and you are he then who are you if he is me? \n(a) He \n(b) Me \n(c) You \n(d) That other guy", ""),
        StaticBook("A Hundred Years", "§bDeven", "A hundred years is a very long time!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nA hundred years is a very long time!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nThey used to think that pigs could fly!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nI don't believe it, no, not I!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nThey thought the moon was made of cheese!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nYou can believe it if\n\nyou please!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nThey thought the stars were set a-light!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nBy some good Angle every night!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nThey hung a man for making steam, they cast his body in the stream!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nA hundred years is a very long time!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nA hundred years is a\n\nvery long time!\n\nA hundred years ago!", ""),
        StaticBook("Evelina's Diary", "§bEvelina Rovin", "20th of the Grand Harvest 1502~\n\nTonight was pretty hectic, since I was invited to a masquerade! Well, I wasn't directly invited since House Rovin wasn't visible on the guest list, but I used Klara's invitation to get in. She was unable to attend,\n\nseeing that she's still in this 'Lady School', which seems like absolute torture by the several letters I've recieved from her. Such a shame that she was unable to attend though. She would've loved the flamboyant masks pasted upon these people's\n\nfaces, and the mystery that they held. I expected for Rhosyn to attend too, but due some unfortunate reasons with her son, she was unable to arrive whilst the ball started. She came later that night, though I haven't heard much from her since, because she\n\nwas dancing all night with this.. baron? Hmrph, seems like she has another man courting her. I wasn't expecting for Athelstan to attend too. From what I know, I wouldn't think that Athelstan would go to these parties pure out of fun, and excitement.\n\nHe'd probably attend them for political reasons, which is.. smart, I guess. But really though, after our marriage, I really have to pump some more joy into his body, and maybe drag him away from his desk. He's barely around, and is always buried\n\ndeep down, where his office is. Well, the masquerade wasn't quite what I've expected, as people were just screaming around, as they were children playing in the garden outside. The only one keeping me company, was Ceto Kharadeen, really. She had the same\n\nexact thoughts I had when she stood there at the party, as my ears could've exploded if it wasn't for Lady Horen starting her first dance. To my great surprise, I saw Karl at the party. I expected Lorin to come too, but good thing she didn't. I might have\n\nborrowed her blue corset and dress for this masquerade, as Karl wouldn't even notice that I was wearing his sister's attire. Lorin would've been furious if she knew that I was wearing her party gown, as she's so over possessive about her clothing, like I\n\nam. Things went well at this masquerade, until the endless amounts of screaming occured, when there was a dragon flying above our heads. Tessa rescued both me and Ceto, as she strapped her armor on in a rather fast pace. I think Tessa would be a good\n\nand responsible Paladin, as she proceeded her endless amounts of quests. After the dragon flew away, everyone started dancing with their partner. You saw many men seeking for a woman to dance with, as there were only a couple. I had the chance to dance\n\nwith Adrian de Bar, Klara's uncle, if I'm correct. He was a charming man, and certainly did make me feel comfortable at this party, while Ceto left hours ago. The ball went great, and it was a rather pleasant relief after my horrid illness I've had, as\n\nI've been locked inside my room for days.\n\n24th of Sun's Smile 1502~\n\nI don't think that I can ever escape out of this nightmare father placed me in. It's truly horrifying to know that he's willing to push me off the Hiebenhall tower, simply because of my decisions. I'm happy, and father can\n\nsimply ruin my fortune pure out of despite for House Stafyr. Perhaps I see something else in House Stafyr than father, though I definitely see a whole other person in Athelstan than everyone else does. The only person I've talked to about this yet was\n\nTessa, who's currently staying in Al-Dirakh. The city itself is absolutely magnificent. It would probably be prettier than Ayr, if I do say so myself. Though, that's my opinion. I've packed several things with me on my journey to Al-Dirakh the night\n\nbefore, and left the next morning to simply have a chat with Tessa. The carriage ride that I took at the Cloud Temple must've been the most relaxing thing I've ever experienced at the time being. I had the chance to actually draw again, and create these\n\nsupernatural creatures. Heh, my imagination's big, I guess. Upon arrival, I felt the air immediately fall upon me, and the sand crawling between my toes in my shoes. Tessa seemed the most comfortable from us two, as she was only wearing a thin orange\n\ndress, with only slippers to embrace her feet. The carriage was unable to stop at the village itself, so we had to walk another part through the desert, to finally sit down, and have tea together. While Tessa would've been my greatest nemesis, she's\n\nthe only person, besides Rhosyn and Athelstan, that I can fully trust. You really need a friend who can purely just listen to you, and where you can tell everything to. Since Klara was this person before, I was locked with these secrets that I was unable\n\nto carry alone, and needed a person who I can talk to, and feel safe.\n\n10th of Malin's Welcome 1503~\n\nOh dear, today I've seen Athelstan again. It must've been over a year since we had our last conversation occuring, and our last sight of eachother. Though his beard may have grown longer, he hasn't changed a\n\nsingle hair, as for his personality. His polite, and charming voice chanting behind me, calling my name. The feeling of me seeing him again was like seeing Klara again, after she got back from her Lady boarding school. This may sound dramatic and all,\n\nand it certainly is, but it was absolutely a delight to see him again. He wanted to have a small chat, about our future, and such things. He gave me his permission to actually steward the new visitors, whom are in the need of housing. As I will become\n\n'Countess Evelina Marie Stafyr Rovin', he told me that he'd  share his titles equally with me, and that I won't become an accessory for him. Again, Athelstan is very kind, and I desire to never leave him for my father. I do wish for us to plan our wedding\n\ndate soon, as Athelstan's cousin, Margaery will already have her marriage occuring soon. If I see Rhosyn and Farley, I really desire to have a child one day. Having a little youngling following you around, perhaps helping you with a few things. Though\n\nfather may throw me off the Hiebenhall tower for this, I'm still willing to carry Athelstan's child. I cannot imagine our children to look like. A young, flamboyant redhead, with eyes so grey as Athelstan's eyes. Oh, I'm filled with joy already!", ""),
        StaticBook("Stage 1", "§bCederick de Bolbec", "[!] The offical wax seal of House de Bolbec is stamped here.\n\n\"Places of interest.\"\n\nTo keep pressure upon Ayr. Constant patrols. Series of raids.\n\nBranaford of Cavarn,\nC.O.K\n\nGuy de Bar\nC.O.K\n\nOliver de Savoie\n---", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "§bNemir", "Dear Elves of Haelun'or,\n\n   I feel that I should do what's right in my life and open my eyes.  My path has been set and I walk down it feeling free, spiritually clean, and truly pure.  I thank those who understood me, though I shall not say names for-\n\ntheir safety.  I thank you guys.\n   I am writing this letter because I am leaving Haelun'or, forever, I am not running to Oren, that would be a too much of an obvious place to do to.  I am not going to the Dwarven kingdom, you might look there too. -\n\nI am going to a place where I feel safe.\n\n\n\n   -Farewell\n\n  ~ Nemir.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crimson Heart.", "§b[The Loyal] Mordew", "Mordew's Report, First Incident-§0\n§0Stood watch upon the gates and saw Master Draethar head off into the woods, I followed, keeping myself hidden as I deemed this behaviour suspicious. I remained undetected as he entered a seemingly abandoned barn in the\n\nmiddle of the woods, From there I heard voices, Notably Draethar's but also some others, I caught drips of a conversation and am assured I heard speak of Necromancy and Betrayal. I returned to the City and reported this information to Medi'ir Avern.\n\nMordew's report, Second Incident- After some controversy involving a goblin sighting within the city, Lady Avern and myself went to visit the barn, The doors were locked and we had to force our way in. Upon entry we were 'greeted' by two people, One that\n\nAppeared to look like a wood elf, the second a human. The wood elf was armed but I was wearing my newly forged suit of armour and commanded him to drop his weapon, Lady Avern was also equipped with her staff and magic, they then decided to begin obeying.\n\nAfter Avern requested them to stand against the back wall I examined the inside of the barn, it was dark, too dark for any real functioning barn, with no ventilation. There was a smell of damp and some obvious moulding of the wooden floorboards. Whilst\n\nI kept the men against the wall, Lady Avern began to search a cellar entrance to the right hand side of the floor, inside of which she found a hidden switch, though pretended to be ignorant of this information for the time as we had come without the-\n\ncorrect force to aprehend both men. During her time searching the cellar I questioned the men, they claimed to be \"Hay salesmen\" though they had no field in sight and the barn was not suited for proper storage I can confirm there was a significant amount\n\nof hay present. When questioning where they got the wheat to make the hay they simply claimed to buy it, though a source for purchase was not given. They also claimed to have the Sohaer's permission to be working on Haelun'or's land, this has yet to be\n\nconfirmed as the Sohaer could not be found upon our return to the city.\n\nMordew's report, third incident-§0\n§0After returning to the city Lady Avern said we would need to gather forces before returning, during this time I went back to the barn alone, hiding in the trees I managed to listen to some further conversations from within\n\nTwo voices (not those of the 'famers' I should add) seemed to be discussing the \"Fame and fortune\" they would receive for their schemes (unspecified) it seemed one was attempting to recruit the other to their cause as I heard one eventually request to be\n\njoining whilst the other mentioned a presentation of \"Elf paperwork.\"\n\nMordew's report, fourth incident-§0\n§0A party approached the gate, requesting myself and Avern to follow them for their council in their barn, I recognised the voice of their leader from within, he was the one offering a contract earlier. A dark elf, by\n\nthe name \"Sonoren\". Him and lady Avern spoke in the garden alone, upon my approach Sonoren hastily asked me to leave, I remained until Avern informed me that he was no threat and that I could leave. I could a brief snippit of the conversation mentioning\n\nslave armies from Sonoren, this appeared to be a slip of the tongue as he then requested to leave and after some controversy he was allowed to go, leaving by diving from the garden into the lake.§0\n§0I inquired with Lady Avern about their discussion afterward\n\nshe told me that I needn't worry about the barn anymore and that they were no threat to Haelun'or and that Elsohaer and Elmodi'ir were already aware of the situation. When I questioned the necromancy she did not give me a definate answer but I can confirm\n\nit was not discussed at their meeting, I have doubts of how well informed people are about the necromancy too, though Lady Avern assured me that \"They are no threat to us, especially considering who they are.\" When I asked who exactly they were I was told\n\n\"It is not needed to be known\" at this my enquires came to an end as it is not my place to question a Medi'ir, only to serve.\n\nMordew's report, fifth incident-§0\n§0After speaking with Lady Avern I decided to continue the investigation alone, returning to the barn and listening once more to the conversations within, though I could be mistaken it seems they have increase in numbers\n\nsince earlier, I could hear a minimum of ten voices if not more from within, this therefore was awkward to report on as there was a lot of sound going on at once. After some time observing I noticed Master Braxus approach the Barn, he came alone with no\n\nweapons or armour and knocked upon the door, at which point two men (the same that had pretended to be farmers.) approached him and continually asked him to leave the area, caliming it to be 'theirs'. After some time watching Braxus try and explain that\n\nthe land was under Haelun'or's control one of the men pulled a blade to him and from what I observed he intended to attack. Therefore I then rushed from my hiding position, clad in my armour and with my blade ready, instantly the two backed off, the one\n\nthat had drawn his sword seemed significantly scared and instantly backed against the barn whilst the other began shouting into the barn that \"Lord Mordew is here!\" I feel as though I may have unintentionally earned myself a bad reputation of killing.\n\nMaster Braxus seemed thankful for my intervention and proceeded to warn those who emerged from the barn that should he or another citizen of Haelun'or be threatened by them again then they would have me to deal with. Many of them seemed honestly concerned\n\nby this and stepped away, forming a loose circle around us. Sonoren eventually stepped from the barn, clearly being established as their leader and at the sight of Mine and Braxus' blades suggested that we return to our city and they would return within\n\ntheir barn without any violence. After some talking Braxus eventually went to leave and as I went to follow Sonoren approached me, asking who my master was, I simply responded \"The Medi'ir\" and he appeared familiar with who I was referncing, he then told\n\nme that The Medi'ir was a former member of what he called 'The Crimson Hearts' and that I should relay a message for him to contact Sonoren as soon as possible.§0\n§0Upon return to the city Master Braxus also mentioned that he wishes to speak with The Medi'ir\n\nas soon as possible.\n\nMordew's report, sixth's incident-§0\n§0A few hours following the last incident I decided to investigate the seemingly deserted barn, the doors were still damaged from being kicked in by myself and Avern earlier so entry was simple, I made my way to the cellar\n\nand found the lever Avern was speaking of, it triggered some sort of mechanical passageway and then I was allowed entry into the underground complex I had suspected. The complex at the time of my visit was still under construction, it consisted of three\n\nfloors, the first consisting a notice board with no relevant information other than \"No magic until I return\" which leads me to assume those practicing there are under Sonoren's strict rule. I decended to the second floor and found two rooms, one was a\n\nstorage room that I could not access, the other was a bunk/ housing room, at the time of my visit it consisted of 12 beds, with room for four more, I beleive this is the approximate number of 'Crimson Hearts' currently on the island. The bottom floor\n\nconsisted of many rooms, each seemingly under construction with the acception of what appeared to be a classroom, fit to house at least 20 students, I imagine this is where they pass on lessons in necromancy to the members on the island. I could not find\n\nmuch else as I heard the door to the barn above me slam shut as someone returned, I fortunately had my soulstone prepared and made my escape before being caught.\n\nMordew's report, seventh incident- Sonoren and five of his hearts entered the city, requesting to speak in the gardens with the Okarir's present at the time. He again persisted that I was not to be allowed presence at the meeting, I kept watch at the\n\ngarden's gates and observed their conversation. Sonoren mostly seemed to be informing the Okarir's of his groups intentions to \"Protect Haelun'or if they are in need of aid, in exchange for use of it's land.\" None of the Okarir's protested. After the\n\nconversation came to a close I approached and brought up the incident with Braxus, Sonoren openly insulted him, calling him a moronic fool and none of the Okarir's present seemed to care much about the assault, one even said that \"It has already been\n\ndealt with.\" though they had not discussed the incident there or then and from what I am aware Sonoren or his men have received no discipline following the incident, though I am not omnipresent and can not assume such things.§0\n§0Upon the Heart's leave I\n\nInquired with Okarir Suliin'thill about if the hearts were to be trusted, he responded with \"For now.\" and then continued with \"Nothing is permanent, this is a life lesson, Mordew.\" I shall lower my guard against the Crimson hearts for now unless they\n\napproach armed or with ill seeming intentions. I fear that the Okarir's may be unaware of what I have learned on my scouting efforts though I do not question their judgements and remain loyal to their requests unless the master wishes otherwise.", ""),
        StaticBook("To You  [ .CB]", "§bColette Blake", "Dear,\n\nI am not the first person you loved. You are not the first person I looked at with a mouthful of forevers. We have both known loss like the sharp edges of a  knife. We have both lived with lips more scar tissue than skin.\n\nOur love came unannounced in the middle of the night.\nOur love came when we'd given up on asking love to come.\nI think that has to be part of the miracle.\n\nThis is how we heal.\nI will kiss you like forgiveness.\nYou will hold me like i'm hope.\n\nOur arms will bandage and we will press promises between us like flowers in a book.\n\nI will write sonnets to the salt of sweat on your skin. I will write novels to the scar of your nose. I will write a dictionary of all the words I have used trying to\n\ndescribe the way it feels to have finally found you.\n\nAnd I will not be afraid of who you are, and your scars.\n\nI know sometimes\nIt's still hard to let me see you\nin all your cracked perfection,\n\nbut please know:\n\nwhether its the days you burn more brilliant than the sun\n\nor the nights you collapse into my lap\nyour body broken into a thousand questions,\nyou are the most beautiful thing i have ever seen.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n\n\nI will love you when you are a still day.\n\nI will love you when you are a hurricane.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Hard Test!", "§b[Child] Kloxin Jayamen", "Kloxin Jayamen's hard test!§0\n§0\n§01. If I am you and you are he then who are you if he is me? §0\n§0(a) He §0\n§0(b) Me §0\n§0(c) You §0\n§0(d) The guy there!§0\n\n2. How many enclosed spaces are in one circle? §0\n§0(a) 1 §0\n§0(b) 2 §0\n§0(c) 3 §0\n§0(d) 4 §0\n\n3. If red minus 2 = yellow and red plus 3 = green then what is red plus 1? §0\n§0(a) 5 §0\n§0(b) Orange §0\n§0(c) 1 §0\n§0(d) Purple §0\n\n4. Hey! Are you there? §0\n§0(a) Yes , I’m here §0\n§0(b) Where? §0\n§0(c) No, I’m over there §0\n§0(d) Yes, I am over there §0\n\n5. Sassalass §0\n§0(a) Sasperella §0\n§0(b) That would be rude §0\n§0(c) Root beer? §0\n§0(d) Ssalassas §0\n\n6.  If 2 + 2 = two pairs of shoes then what is 8 plus 4? §0\n§0(a) 8 pairs of shoes §0\n§0(b) An octagon §0\n§0(c) Would it equal four more? §0\n§0(d) 4 more shoes §0\n\n7. Which word is the same as ZWOMIWHO §0\n§0(a) MIOWWHZO §0\n§0(b) OHWIMOWZ §0\n§0(c) OHMIWOMZ §0\n§0(d) None of them\n\n8. Directions §0\n§0Left = right §0\n§0right = down §0\n§0Down = up §0\n§0up = Right §0\n§0down = Left §0\n§0Left = Down §0\n§0Right = Up §0\n§0Which word that means a direction has nothing equal to it? §0\n\n9. How do you think you did on this test? §0\n§0(a) Perfect (all right!)§0\n§0(b) Well (half or more right§0\n§0(c) Poor (one to half right)§0\n§0(d) Horrible (none except this one right.)§0\n\nThat is all, thank you!", ""),
