        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alchemy ~§0\n§0\n§0Page 1-5: Juice/Tea§0\n§0Page 6-10: Alcohol§0\n§0Page 10-15: Potions/Poisons§0\n\nApple Juice -§0\n§0Water Bottle§0\n§0Apple§0\n§0\n§0Dandelion Tea - §0\n§0Water Bottle§0\n§0Dandelion§0\n§0\n§0Poppy Tea -§0\n§0Water Bottle§0\n§0Poppy§0\n\nMulled Wine -§0\n§0Water Bottle§0\n§0Dark Resin§0\n§0\n§0Pale Ale - §0\n§0Water Bottle§0\n§0Wheat§0\n\nHealing Potion -§0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Tippens Root§0\n§0\n§0Numbing Potion - §0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Blissfoil§0\n§0\n§0Healing + Numbing - §0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Blissfoil§0\n§0Tippens Root\n\nPoison (Flaky Skin) -§0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Goblin's Ivy§0\n§0\n§0Sky High Potion - §0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Halflings Grass§0\n§0\n§0Poisoned Blood - §0\n§0Water Bottle§0\n§0Rotten Flesh\n\nserpents stalk§0\n§0blissfoil§0\n§0tippens root", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Judas Windsor, Adept farmer§0\n§0\n§0Nemir, Masterful Lumberjack (UnBaed) 25 stacks per week quota§0\n§0\n§0Org_The_Robo (Rengar) Caravan Guard/enforcer§0\n§0\n§0Eagles2910 (Helene Aquilla) Miner *Hired*\n\nValuum (Joeker396)§0\n§0Adept Woodcutter", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter To Arial", "tuslwmonster", "Hello, Grandmother.\n\nI have recently purchased a home in\nSalvus. Its a small home and I am still making improvements on it, but I'd love for you and Mother to come live with me. Like I mentioned before, it is small, but it has an alright sized farm.\n\nI feel we can make a living here. There are no taxes, and I am soon paying the house off. I will take care of the weekly taxes and the needs of you and mother. Please respond when you can with your location and I will come and lead you here. ~Edward", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I've arrived in Iralis, or Idalis. I forget the name. The first man I met introduced me to the Duke, Aleksander Staunton. They signed me up for the military, and gave me a house. It's not too cold, or small- I fit a desk in, and my carpenters table. I\n\neven fit a double bed in. Some building here and there and it was a home indeed.§0\n§0The Duke is a good man. He drinks with the men, pays for the drinks too. He offered me materials for my house aswell. And his officers, Percy and Phylip, are both great. I\n\nsparred with Phylip, and lost, but it's progress. §0\n§0\n§0\n§0Today, I met some new people. They had strange accents, and wanted to open a clinic, so I helped them. The rest of the day was guard duty, or home building.\n\nToday, Percy and I got into a fight with Dagr, some upjumped nobleman. We broke off after a while, and Percy and Dagr dueled. Percy lost. I had a mind to enter and fight with Percy, but I didn't want to spark off the Vanirs.§0\n§0\n§0The Duke talks of killing\n\ntrolls as part of his Gentleman's club. He's got some squire with him. §0\n§0\n§0We are visiting the elven capital, Laureh'lin. It's got tight security, and we had to leave the dark elf behind. They gave us a tour of the place- and as I said before\n\n- their architecture is astounding. One of them, a smith, said he could forge us weapons. He never did show the forge, but he started rambling about gods and aspects and druids. §0\n§0\n§0I took the Duke's sister off to the library, and then we had a look around\n\nat other things, like the flowers. When we got back, I learnt that the festival is fast approaching! I can't wait to fight in the melee. Theres plenty of important people coming to attend, like some holy church man. Not like I'm part of his faith.§0\n\nI've met both the Duke's right hand and two snarky children. They're all cunts. They keep judging Eve, and I can't help but put them in their place. §0\n§0\n§0However, Eve is very strange. She says she woke up with blue hair and purple eyes.\n\nIt's strange to believe her. I might have to dig deeper.§0\n§0\n§0I just learn't being faithless is illegal. The Duke made me endure a session with the Father. It actually wasn't as bad as I would have thought. I learnt some useful things, and I see why he'd do\n\nit. Still, probably wont convert.§0\n§0\n§0I've began digging a tunnel under the city. Theres an empty plot of land on the opposite end. If I need to make an escape, that'll be my route.§0\n§0\n§0Caught Arcus smooching his girl on the wall. I told him not\n\nto fall. He's probably fallen head over heels for her. Good for him.§0\n§0\n§0The tourney is today!§0\n§0I mean to fight in the melee, jousts and other competitions. If I can win, I'll be well known, maybe even liable for promotion.§0\n§0\n§0I've arrived at Leone.§0\n\nThe tourney starts very soon. It was a bugger to find, but the hardest part is over. I swear, the melee is mine!§0\n§0\n§0Nevermind. Lost the melee, first bracket. Some arrogant ass stole beat me. Should've eaten before the fight.\n\n[!] The page is scribbled out vigorously, no words visible.\n\nHaven't written in here in a while. Winter is coming on.", ""),
        StaticBook("Autograph, Clegg", "§bSer Aymer Fournier", "To my juicy peasant, I write you to tell you, that you are a delicious man. Signed, Cleggtrain", ""),
        StaticBook("Carrot Man", "CCCP_Zhulik", "King Crab: The Tale\nKing Crab was best friends with Carrot Man. Carrot Man was a man who loved carrots.\nThe end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rule of Lucia", "§bSister Lucia", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~ §0\n§0             I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0  I--------------I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0             I§0\n§0  The Rule of Lucia§0\n§0~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\nThese are the vows that the nuns of my convent shall take:§0\n§0\n§0Poverty:§0\n§0  +The nuns shall own      nothing besides:§0\n§0       A cloak(armor)§0\n§0       A form of §0\n§0       defense§0\n§0       A journal§0\n§0       Monk bread§0\n§0       Bread for the §0\n§0       poor\n\n        Tools for §0\n§0        working§0\n§0        Prayer book§0\n§0  +Anything else owned    by the convent will §0\n§0   be property of the     community, not of an    individual.§0\n§0\n§0Chastity:§0\n§0   +As Brides of the        Church, nuns are §0\n§0\n\n     prohibited to §0\n§0     practice §0\n§0     polygamy, nor §0\n§0     may they partake§0\n§0     in any romantic or §0\n§0     sexual relations.§0\n§0   +Chastity, not only§0\n§0    being a physical §0\n§0    thing, condones §0\n§0    also impure §0\n§0    thoughts. It is§0\n§0    against the rule to§0\n§0\n\n    not have a §0\n§0    shield protecting§0\n§0    one's thoughts §0\n§0    from temptation.§0\n§0\n§0Obedience:§0\n§0   +All nuns must have      obedience to their       superior.§0\n§0   +If you are told by      a priest or monk §0\n§0    to do something§0\n§0    against your\n\n     Abess' wishes, §0\n§0     you must follow §0\n§0     their orders, for§0\n§0     according to the§0\n§0     Holy Scrolls, men §0\n§0     shall have§0\n§0     religious §0\n§0     dominance over§0\n§0     women.§0\n§0    +If this does §0\n§0     happen, against §0\n§0     one's morals, do §0\n§0     not be\n\n     disobedient; §0\n§0     however, you §0\n§0     must report the§0\n§0     events to Abbess§0\n§0     or Confessor so§0\n§0     that they may §0\n§0     resolve the §0\n§0     situation.\n\n\n§0      How a Nun's§0\n§0       Day Shall§0\n§0           Go§0\n§0\n§03:00 AM§0\n§0   The nuns shall §0\n§0   begin their day by§0\n§0   studying the Holy §0\n§0   Scrolls, and §0\n§0   praying for the §0\n§0   sinners. This may§0\n§0   include penances\n\n    or mortifications. §0\n§0\n§06:00 AM§0\n§0    At this time, the §0\n§0    nuns shall have§0\n§0    their morning mass,      and after this they     will eat breakfast.§0\n§0\n§09:00 AM§0\n§0    The nuns will then§0\n§0    go out onto the§0\n§0    fields and collect\n\n     harvest. It will §0\n§0     then be brought§0\n§0     to the abbey's§0\n§0     bakery. These§0\n§0     crops will be used       in order to make§0\n§0     money for the §0\n§0     Church.§0\n§0\n§012:00 PM§0\n§0     The nuns will now §0\n§0     go to their daily§0\n§0     jobs. This\n\n     includes, but is §0\n§0     not limited to:§0\n§0         Baking§0\n§0         Teaching§0\n§0         Farming§0\n§0         Preaching\n\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~§0\n§0\n§0        Code of§0\n§0          Law§0\n§0\n§0The nuns shall wear a simple and humble grey habit. They shall /never/ wear normal civilian clothing, for they are set apart as the Brides of the Church.\n\nBesides the grey habit, they must wear a black headress to cover their hair. Vanity is extremely looked down upon, and therefore if a nun is found with a mirror, or looking at themselves in a reflection, they will be severely punished. The punishment will\n\nbe based on their Confessor, not their Abbess. The preferred punishment is seclusion to a cloistered enviroment.§0\n§0\n§0Punishments for breaking their vows are:§0\n§0 Chastity-Defrocking§0\n§0 Obedience-Seclusion§0\n§0 Poverty-Seclusion\n\nOf course, all punishments will be based on the degree of the offence.§0\n§0~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~§0\n§0\n§0        Steps of§0\n§0        Initiation§0\n§0    ((Time is IRL))§0\n§0\n§0Postulancy:§0\n§0   The Postulant will §0\n§0   spend 1 week in §0\n§0   this stage.\n\n    They will spend §0\n§0    their time studying§0\n§0    the scriptures, §0\n§0    and they shall §0\n§0    make residence in§0\n§0    the convent, §0\n§0    examining the §0\n§0    nuns.§0\n§0\n§0Novitiate:§0\n§0    The Novice will §0\n§0    then receive the §0\n§0    habit, and\n\n     her first prayer§0\n§0     book. This period §0\n§0     lasts for half a §0\n§0     week. The Abbess\n     or Mentor will \n     assign the novice        7 tasks. This will\n     reveal both if\n     they call from \n     the Lord is true,\n     and if the\n\n     novice has a \n     strong will.\n\nTemporary-Vows:\n     The novice will \n     then take tempo-\n     rary vows, of \n     poverty, \n     chastity, and\n     obedience. This\n     stage will last \n     half a week. It\n     is meant as a\n\n     test to see if the\n     woman can \n     endure the vows\n     of the Sisterhood. \n\nPermanent-Vows:\n     With the consent\n     of both the \n     Abbess, Mentor,\n     Pontiff, and the\n     candidate's\n     Confessor, they \n     will be\n\n     consecrated to\n     the Sisterhood.\n     Because they are\n     a new nun, they\n     are not allowed\n     to go on a \n     preaching or\n     teaching mission\n     for half a week.\n\n          Signed,\n             Sister Lucia", ""),
        StaticBook("Thesis on Canon", "§bSister Lucia", "I will be writing my new thesis on how all Canonists should act, both the laity and religious alike. There are specific duties we must fulfill, and specific ways we must act. First, I shall elaborate on what Canonists must do. First, I will speak of how\n\nthey must treat themselves. We are God's creation, beautiful in his eyes. We must treat our bodies and spirits with secure states of mind. But what is more important, the body or the spirit? I say the latter, for any man may destroy the\n\nbody, but the spirit is eternal, and may only be destroyed by the Most High. In order to keep your spirit in good health, you must both feed your soul, and give it drink. One would ask, 'That is impossible, how might you give drink or food to the Spirit?'\n\nThe Word of God is the food of the spirit. You must feed your soul properly, so therefore keep His Word close to your heart. To give your spirit drink, you must pray. Prayer is the Divine Relationship that has been established between Man and God.\n\nPray constantly, and your heart shall be protected from all tempation. Do these two things and you shall become pure and in the Light of God.§0\n§0\n§0I shall now elaborate on what you must do for others than oneself. As a follower\n\nof the One True God, you must act as a representative of Himself. Thus, in order to act Holy and Just, as He is, you must always practice these acts:§0\n§0   Feed the hungry§0\n§0   Give drink to the §0\n§0   thirsty§0\n§0   Clothe the naked§0\n§0\n\n   Shelter the §0\n§0   homeless§0\n§0   Visit the sick and§0\n§0   old§0\n§0   Bring hope to the§0\n§0   imprisoned§0\n§0   Bury and pray§0\n§0   for the dead§0\nBesides these physical acts of mercy, you must provide spiritual aide to all believers and\n\nunbelievers:\n   Instruct the \n   ignorant\n   Counsel the \n   doubtful\n   Admonish sinners\n   Bear wrongs \n   patiently\n   Forgive willingly\n   Comfort the \n   afflicted\n   Pray for ALL", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "One long lasting sourse of high quality heat.§0\n§0Sufficient amount of Tungsten, for conduction of heat.§0\n§0one large sphere of hollow obsidion, with many 1/2Inch holes in it.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0W\n\nFill obsidion sphere with heat sourse.§0\n§0Forge Tungsten into 1/2Inch rods and place into holes of obsidion shard.§0\n§0Place entire piece into location of water firmly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seth's Case", "§bAlyn Aylanir", "*The writing seems to be copied in childish handwriting*\n\n\nThe Case Of\nPrimrose/Mediliyur\n\n\n\n\nSummary:\n\nPrimrose, Mali'Ahreal.\nFormer Sillumiran\nSuspected of impure acts\n\n\n\n\nObjective:\n\nFind her ties to the Clerical Order and find out where she currently resides.\n\nInvestigation:\n\nCassiel went undercover and successfully infiltrated. There he discovered her ties with the Clerical Order. She mastered the healing arts, but was in no formal position.\n\nHe had discovered this by conversing with Jakir, a member of the Order. Furthermore, Cassiel discovered was getting married to an unknown impure. These facts were uncovered back in the Fringe.\n\nAfter re-opening the case inn Athera, Cassiel got reconfirmation by Lenniel'on. I quote: \"She was crazy and definitely impure by Mali'Aheral standards.\" Furthermore, a Valah by the name of Heather Hartwarm confirmed she knew Primrose.\n\nHer ties were with the Druidic Order as well as the Clerical Order. Cassiel then went on an investigation and discovered there was indeed a Primrose who goes by Raven Druid. Cassiel then got confirmation of different Drui.\n\nEarendur, known as Mist Druid and Guide of the Druidic Order has confirmed he has guided her before and perfectly described Primrose/Mediliyur in detail. We are certain he speaks of the same person.\n\nPrimrose/Mediliyur is often spotted in elcihi. Her purity is still questionable due to her disappearance back in the Fringe.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n~Alyn", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "§bPercy \"The Loyal Man\" Staunton", "2nd of The First Seed, 1513.\n\nWe are soon to depart Athera.\n\nThat is all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Petrusian Men", "§bCederick de Bolbec", "Orenian Support\n\n[!] The Wax seal of House de Bolbec is Stamped at the top of the document.\n\n\"It is on this day, that I shall speak to my allies, as follows in Petrusia.\"\n\nList of Formal Allies.\n\nProfound Clergyman.\nFarmer A.\nAymas A.\nAymas B.\nAymas C.\nAymas D.\nAymas E.\nAymas F.\nAymas G.\nGuard A.\nGuard B.\n\nGuard C.\nGuard D.\nOffical A.\nOffical B.\nOffical C.\nMerchant of Status A.\nTavarn A.\n\nFamily FAO\nFamily Gre\nFamily Vis\n\n-His Grace,\n\nCederick Augustus William Hanover Gregory de Bolbec Winchester", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C1", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n \n             -By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n\n     Chapter One\n A Walk in the Woods\n\n“Mom!” I yelled as I went out the back door. “I’m going out to the woods!”\n\n“Fine Honey!” My mom yelled back. “Just be back before dusk ok?”\n\n“Sure Mom!” I answered. I put on my sword, closed the back door, and headed out. Knowing exactly where I was going as I ventured more into the woods. As I walked I couldn’t help but notice how nice everything was today.\n\nFrom the glistening emerald green leaves leaving a slight greenish tint on the ground, to the random scuttles and noises coming from the woods, it just seemed like it was going to be a good day. I approached the usual spot I hung out at near dusk.\n\nA small opening with a flat rock and a small clear pool in the middle. It wasn’t much but I always thought better here. I laid down on the rock looking up into the trees and begin to wander off in my head.\n\nI was about to dose off when I heard something. I sat up quickly. It wasn’t a normal sound. It sounded like the song that Linink played on the piano at the Festival, only it was on a flute. Cautiously, I got up and went in the direction of the sound.\n\nIt got louder and louder as I went along through the trees and bushes until I reached another larger clearing. I looked amazingly at what I saw. There was a Statue in the middle of the clearing with multiple statues around the clearing.\n\nThey all looked just like the one in the middle of town, except in different poses. The one in the middle had his arms outstretched in front of him.\n\nI went closer and saw that in it’s his hands outstretched was a Bow, Arrows, A sword, a dagger, and a scroll. Cautiously I went up closer to the statue and was about to take the scroll when suddenly the music stopped and a voice said,\n\n“Hey! Boy! What are you doing here” Startled I jumped back and turned to face an old man.\n\n“I’m sorry!” I said shocked. “I was just going to look at it! I swear!” The Old man had a frown on but then smiled and said.\n\n“Well why didn’t you say so? Go ahead and take a look.”\n\n“Wait… what?” I said surprised.\n\n“Go on, take a look.” Said the old man again still smiling.\n\n“Um… ok…” I said confused, turning to face the statue. I slowly took the scroll and opened it. Written on it was… nothing.  I frowned and looked back but the old man was gone. Only in his place was a flute.\n\nI scratched my head, went to it, and picked it up. As I touched it I heard the music start again but this time, it was in my head. Shocked again I dropped the flute, the scroll, and the music stopped.\n\nCuriously I picked up the flute and tried to play the notes I had heard. I had played the flute many times before but this time felt different somehow. As I finished playing the notes nothing seemed to happen.\n\nI wondered what I was expecting to happen. Once I waited about a minute I bent down and picked up the scroll. Only this time there was something written on it. Curiously I examined the scroll.\n\n It had a few lines of music notes on it and the title of it was called “Song of the Rain”. The music notes where different from the ones I had just played, so I began to play these ones.\n\nAs I played it sounded like a stormy night at sea. When I completed it, nothing seemed to happen. After a minute I walked to the statue, wondering if it would be a good idea to take the sword. Suddenly a Voice behind me said,\n\n“Would you look at that! You’re a natural at the flute.”\n\nShocked, I turned to see the old man again, this time he had a bird on his shoulder. He had the same smile on his face. \n\n“Where do you keep coming from?” I said.\n\nSeeming to ignore the question the old man looked at the weapons the statue had.\n\n“I see you like those weapons?” Said the old man. \n\n“Yea. They look amazing.” I said turning to the statue.\n\n Then looked at the face and said,” But… where they his?”\n\n“What do you mean?” Said the old man. “You’re the one wearing them.”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said turning to the old man again.\n\nBut he was gone. I turned back to the statue that had the weapons but they were gone. Suddenly I saw something on myself. I looked down and there was a sword on my belt, but it wasn’t my sword, it was the statues.\n\nI looked to the other side of my belt and there was the dagger. I slowly reached up and touched my shoulder. As I did I felt the feathers of an arrow and the string of a bow.\n\n I then realized it was dusk, my mom would be annoyed if I wasn’t home soon. I took off the weapons, put them back on the statues hands, and began to walk home.\n\n As I walked home I noticed the air began to feel denser and the wind began to pick up a little bit. Suddenly. I felt a raindrop. I looked up and one hit me on my forehead. I started running as fast as I could toward the house.\n\nAs I got in the back door my mom was standing there with her arms crossed. \n\n“Where have you been?” She said sternly. “You’re late and your soaked head to toe!”  All I could say was,\n\n“I don’t know.”\n\n“Jaya.” Said my mom in a warning voice. \n\nI sighed and recounted the whole story about the old man, the weapons, the flute and the scroll. As I finished my mom looked pale.\n\n“Are you alright?” I said. She walked slowly to a kitchen chair and sat down.\n\n“Jaya.” My mom began. “I’m going to have you see Linink.”\n\nLinink was the best doctor around and also the leader of the adventurer’s guild, a guild that helps people and goes on quests. My friends Sofetios and Sofia go there.\n\n\n“Wait, why?” I said concerned. “Do you think I’m sick?”\n\n“No Jaya.” My mom said. “It’s about something else. I think it’s time you went to bed.” Confused and concerned, I went to bed.\n\nEND OF CHAPTER ONE\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "/\\/\\ Fantasy Novelties /\\/\\§0\n§0  §0\n§0 Tis That Which the Winds §0\n§0                    Sow§0\n§0\n§0     by - Korius Highwatch§0\n\n   Sickles would flash underneath the glaring sunlight, as men unjustified and undivided by any martial law, would hack away at the golden strands of wheat. Their sweat, like fertilizer to the soil, would trinkle from their body's and moisten the crop. §0\n§0\n\nAvast, the beams from the Creator's sun would give us meaning in our toils, as it rained pillar upon pillar of light unto us. Labor during the Sun's presence and rest during that of the Moon's. Yes, these golden fields, the verdent green waves of hills --\n\n   --with everlong arrays of towering trees and vibrant fields of soft flowers. We sought peace in such lands, to be free from the war mongering Kings who considered themselves Gods. This island, it is the cottage that any farmer would rest his soul with-\n\n-within, where the winged creatures would perch upon the shoulders of men and where the flames of war would not conflagerate. Our time here, will be eternal, our lives will expire upon this land, and our souls will wander it's premise for the rest of time\n\nTo bear a pitchfork and a sickle, is the way of the farmer. Bear a hammer and clamp, the way of the blacksmith. A hatchet of the lumberjack. Tis the way of labouring men seeking peace from their endevours. But to toss it all and bear the sword in the name\n\nOf a God King, for his purpose, is an outrage. No, we will never bear arms for any King, so long as they continue their schemes toward God hood.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "oh yes daddy said eyad von dinkleberry", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Vanir Castle§0\n§0\n§0-Near The hideout.§0\n§0\n§0Saltstone keep§0\n§0\n§0-North of Iralis§0\n§0-Rapier located there", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I was walking about one day, doing to usual thing, when I came across two bridges that appear to have fallen into ruin. I made it across these consecutive bridges, getting a little wet. At the end of the second bridge, was a scorching hot desert. And when\n\nI came upon the sand, I got an edgy feeling, not one of fear, or sudden constipation, nor a instant sun burn, which I had expeceted. It was a sense of danger, a sense that your every move was watched and judged. That got me curious, so I then strolled\n\ndeeper into the desert.  In this feet blistering desert, I came upon a large city, it's foundation relying upon the strength of the enormous pillars it sits on. Inside was a pathetic hobgoblin, he was attempting to create  a novel, but everytime he tried\n\nto write, he'd make a mistake and rip out the page. I entered and he immediatlyclosed the journal and stared at as a man would a dog, I noticed he salivated but then attempted to hide it. I told him that I was new to these lands and wished to learn, so he\n\nshowed me the place. He pointed here and there, about the huts and the Rex, and then about the fighting ring, this and that. An interesting thing was this creature appered very young, and then at the ring, he looked me over as if I was meat. He salivated\n\nsome more, and then pushed pass me rudly. He took me into the Rex's castle, which then had a spot below the throne. He asked me to stand there as he pretended to be the Rex, since he had been gracious  to teach me. Then he tried a evil laugh and pulled a\n\nswitch. It took a moment when the ground beneath me opened and I fell into a pit. This little monster had tricked me. He then made his way down a passage to where I was. Here he thought he'd get to kill me. But the pit was blocked at the bottom, requiring\n\na key. He then ran off to find others. He hadn't returned after afew minutes, which was when I had finnaly managed to climb out of the pit. The bit was about six mters deep, and two meeters across, so I managed to lift myself out. He then charged in for\n\na tackle whne I stepped to the side and he fell in. I climbed up onto the throne and pulled the switch again, now closing the roof to the pit. I gracefully walked out of there, only happy not be another skewed peice of meat. -Tasslehoff, The Orc Capital\n\nA Mysterious Beast,§0\n§0I was walking out ofDour's Watch, a small fort I had been assigned to weeks back that lies on the road between the Monk Temple and the city of Oren. I had just had a little chat with one of the people managing the gate, whom had\n\ndecided to be a douche today and not let me in. So as I continued on I saw something very unqiuem something I had never seen before in my life. It was a creature, half deer half human. It was prancing about, and I decided, the heck with it and followed\n\nthe best one could.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The art of economic structure is not based merely on the immediate effects a choice of resource may have on the populace, but the long lasting effects on any act or policy. One may describe a food distortion as being an immediate function, where as\n\nsmithing and armor would be secondary to an immediate state. Economy is the definition of not only survival, but thriving. To evaluate the structure of once settlements function as a whole, one must find the needs, before the luxury. A well built fountain\n\nwould be invalid compared to the more integral ration supplies, as well as shelter. People subjective to an administrators rule must be of willpower, and stability in order for an economy to function properly. The diplomatic factor would also be\n\nprinciple in detaining another faction from holding hostilities to said settlement\n\nCatherine \"Vulf\" Unterstein is better than you are.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "N.Everheart - Iron Tools§0\n§0R.Divine - Arms & Armour§0\n§0J.Sano - Animal Products§0\n§0R.Torena - Iron Tools§0\n§0S.Artenin - Res+WarStuffs§0\n§0P.Idate - Logs§0\n§0Rwonda - Tailor§0\n§0Tybalt - WarStuffs§0\n§0A.Burchoff - Enchantment§0\n§0R.Windsor - Logs\n\nBlacksmiths;§0\n§0Rose Divine - A&A, 200M, N) Deposit Box§0\n§0R) Security, Thaumic Ice", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dedicant name: Atlas§0\n§0\n§0Teacher Name: Ryn Chirr§0\n§0\n§0Dedicant date:§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n\nTask One: Ode to Nature§0\n§0\n§0Assignment: Write a poem about nature, four pages long. It cannot be about a tree.§0\n§0\n§0*Ryn's signature is here showing task complete*\n\nTask Two: To be a Tree§0\n§0\n§0Assignment: Dress as a tree and stand as one for a full Elven hour in a populated area to learn how it feels to be a tree.§0\n§0\n§0*Ryn's signature is here showing task complete*\n\nTask Three; The Hunt§0\n§0\n§0Assignment: Go hunting for an animal of any kind. Use every part of the animal in some way and return the bones to me.§0\n§0\n§0*Ryn's signature is here showing task complete*\n\nTask Four: Intro to the Aspects§0\n§0\n§0Assignment: Read about the Aspects and return with three items, one to represent each Aspect.§0\n§0\n§0*Ryn's signature is here showing task complete*\n\nTask Five: A Time to Grow§0\n§0\n§0Assignment: Plant and grow a tree. Tend and care for the tree, bond with it.§0\n§0\n§0*Ryn's signature is here showing task complete*\n\nTask Six: A Staff§0\n§0\n§0Assignment: Take the branch gifted to you by your tree and carve your Druidic staff.§0\n§0\n§0*Ryn's signature is here showing task complete*\n\nTask Seven: The Ranks of the Order§0\n§0\n§0Assignment: Read and research the different ranks within the Order, then seek out three members of different ranks and do a task for them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Journal§0\n§0            Of§0\n§0      Viscar Van'Eer§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~§0\n§0Guard of Astfield, Guard of Hotchen Merchant Group, and Footman of the Gold Corp.§0\n§0-------------------I currently live in Astfield.....", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "How to be seductive.§0\n§0The journal of Miss Von.§0\n§0\n§0* A bunch of scribbles of lusty stick figures surround a stick figure who appears to be \"posing\" would be seen here.*\n\nJournal Entry one:§0\n§0\n§0First time I was trying to be seductive I failed. Turns out the person already had a lover. §0\n§0\n§0TIP NUMBER ONE!§0\n§0\n§0Don't seduce someone who already likes another person.", ""),
