        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Wonders Of The World§0\n§0By Erendiel Thoren§0\n§0\n§0[!] There'd be a beautifull map of the islands drawn here.\n\nFelsen§0\n§0As the Capital of Oren it is one of the largest cities around, home to many humans. Its dwindling alleys and such are home to great buildings, and it's protected by a strong wall.§0\n§0[!] A drawing of the front gate is made here.\n\nDuchy of Istria\n\nDuchy Of Carnatia§0\n§0The duchy of Montefort's surroundings are that of scorched lands, caused by fires and such. It's capital is named Montefort, and is guarded by a magnificent castle on the top of the mountain.\n\nDuchy of Courland§0\n§0Also know as the duchy of the north, this duchy is located in a relatively more cold area of the Holy Orenian Empire§0\n§0It's capital is Riga, a reasonably large city.\n\nDuchy Of Lorraine§0\n§0The Duchy of Lorraine is a more southern one, with warm pleasant breezes, all around. It has a lot of farmland. It's capital, Summerhall, is a small village. It is home to beautifull scenery, making it a great place for married folks\n\nshmud was here PS gruk'ku has a small", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Crash And Burn.§0\n§0-------------------  Sailing though the blue sea of the sky is a mighty ship. The hull is tied to a massive thick balloon tied with ropes that stretch and strain on the verge of snapping!§0\n§0 A man steps onto the helm of the ship.\n\nClothed with a red shirt and black leather pants he stands tall looking over the lands as he flys high above. He closes his eyes and takes in a deep breath. §0\n§0  As the man takes in a deep breath his eyes suddenly widen as his nose is met with the smell....\n\nof smoke. \"HONEYDEW!\"  Shouted the man as he turns to see the hull of the ship that has bursted into flames. §0\n§0  A young dwarf with firey red hair burst onto the deck of the ship. He held in his hands a flint and steel. \"Were goin down! take cover!\"\n\nShouted the dwarf as he ran around the ship in a panic. The man  and the dwarf both run to grab onto whatever they possibly can. Grapsing for safty and sucurity. The ship dips it's front end as it dives into the earth into the side of a hill.\n\nThe two rise from the hull as fire covers the land. Sand covers the newly made crator that hath destoryed the land around it. §0\n§0 The man the dwarf climb out from the reck and infront of them stands a small cave. The cave has a tall dark frame made of the\n\nblackest of stone. Covered in torches at the top of a stone stairway. The two look around. The man climbs from the reck looking at the portal. \"Whats with all the sand? where did this all come from?\" He could not help but ask himself. \"Honeydew!\"\n\nThe man shouted once more as the dwarf step up looking sheepish. \"It's not my fault! I didn't do any of this! Wait. Were are the other two?\"§0\n§0  From the hull of the ship climbs a old man and a younger man. The elder in old wron tatterd rags.\n\nThe younger one in more upkept well groomed cloths. §0\n§0  \"Lewis do you remember where we are?\" The dawrf asked the man.§0\n§0  \"Yea this is near the yogcave. Our old home.\"§0\n§0 Suddenly an old and weak voide is heard as the old man steps up.\n\n\"Hero's! follow me through the portal when you are ready!\"    The old man shouts out to the man and dawrf only to be ignored. The man and dwarf had already started looting the chest.§0\n§0  \"Honedew you want to take the tnt?\"\n\nLew the man in red looked to the dwarf already tossing the red sticks to his friend. §0\n§0  \"Are you sure that's a good idea? Seeing as how the ship well you know.\"§0\n§0 \"You've proven to know what you are doing better then me you best have it\"\n\nThe old man shouts at the once more \"Daisy awaits us! We need to save her!\"§0\n§0  The two hero's heads snap looking as the old man. \"Oh right we need to saver her! Top priority!\" Exclaimed the dwarf as he stood up making his way to the portal.\n\nLewis Honeydew the old man and young man all look at each other as they walk up the stairs and through the portal. The darf shreaks in fear as he passes through only to come out the other side. \"What just happened? We are still here.\" The dwarf looked\n\nto the old man. §0\n§0 The old man shakes his head with a solum sigh. \"He has sealed the portal. Alas we must find another way.\" The old man looks around at all the sand and takes a moment of thinking. §0\n§0\"This sand? Could it be?\" The old man seems worried.\n\nThe younger male steps over to him. \"What Peculier? What is it?\" §0\n§0 Peculier shouts out \"NO! The portal must be destoryed!\"§0\n§0Once more the younger male questions Peculier. \"What about Dasiy?\"§0\n§0Abruptly the dwarf interupts the two.\n\n\"Wait a moment. First you want us to go through it now we need to destory it? How can we follow Israphel without the portal?\"§0\n§0  \"There are other portals in this world. We must find them. At times like this I fear the world is in peril.\"§0\n\n\"Quickly hero's! Act with haste and destor the portal! Lest it corrupts the land even more!\"§0\n§0Shouted the younger male as the dwarf grabs his pick and swings at the portal portal frame. \"Worry not olod man i'll destroy the operol!\"§0\n\nThe old man watched as the dawrf took swings at the black stone. \"Are you drunk?\" Asked Peculier.§0\n§0   Peculier clutches his hand over his chest suddenly and the other three turn to look at him in worry.\n\nThe three men crowd around him. \"I'm so tired... But I can't rest.\" The old man said with a weak voice.§0\n§0  \"We need to get you to Mistral city! You are sick!\" Said Lysander the younger male.§0\n§0 \"we can conintue our search there.\" Lysander continued.\n\nWith a voice weak and desperate the old man calls out. \"Daisy!\"§0\n§0  Lewis stands in the back as he watches Lysander hold Peculier. \"Where is Mistral city? We have to get there now.\"§0\n§0 Lysander stands tall after setting his old friend down.\n\n\"The trip to Mistral city is not a short one. It's a day travel at lest. Gather all supplies you can carry.\" The man and the dwar look at each other with a nod as they run to the reck once more. They start looting the chest in the burning hull.\n\nSoon the two look around. The man, Lewis. The Dwarf, Honeydew. Glancing at each other they look to the cake that they had just left and near it rose a mound of smoke. §0\n§0  Without Hesitation they run to the cave finding a tunnel.\n\nThe tunnel is long and deep. It quickly fades into a thick veil of darkness. §0\n§0  With a farm grip on the hand of a torch the man Travels down the tunnel. Honeydew follows closely behind as their friends Peculier and Lysander....\n\nFollow behind the two.     As Lewis come to the end of the tunnel he stops. His eyes widen as he gasp a look of terror floods over his face.§0\n§0  The Dwarf falls to his knees with a cry of anguish and defeat. In front of the hero's stand what once was their\n\nhome.§0\n§0  Fire covers the lands as all has been burrned to ash. The floor is ripped up and the walls are nowhere to be seen. All that remains is the stone that the structer was carved into. §0\n§0  Craters and fire is all that remain.\n\nYet that brought up only more questions. §0\n§0  How recent was this? The fire still burns so it had to be recent.§0\n§0  \"The smoke from this place. Seems to clogged the ship and caused it to fall to the ground!\" Lysander suddenly exclaimed as Lewis\n\nglanced over to Honeydew.§0\n§0  \"It was not my fault! See! Lysander said it himself\"§0\n§0  Honeydew stated seemingly cured of his sadness. \"Well we can't be here forever\"§0\n§0 The dwarf wipes tears to from face as he stands tall.\n\nWell as tall as a dwarf can get. \"Hurry hero's get to Mistral City!\"§0\n§0  Old peculier started to get restless trying to urge the heros on their journy.§0\n§0  \"Come on hero's we need to get moving now. I'll lead the way\"§0\n§0 Without hesitation Lysander\n\ntook the lead drawing his sword. He was ready for the dangers that lie ahead on the road to Mistral city.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Naffog's Journal§0\n§0\n§0This is not so much a journal as it is a logbook of all the things I've done in my life, good and bad. This is a record of my thoughts, my ideals and philosophies.\n\nA thought occured to me today whilst I sat alone in the hall. I have seen the deaths of thousands. I have heard their screams, their pleas for mercy and help. Yet have I ever batted an eye? Have I ever flinched? Does that absence make me a monster?\n\nThis may be slightly unorthodox compared to my other entries, but I have to get this out; why in the bleeding nether do assassins these days feel the need to wear unbelievably obvious clothing? Why do they make their weapons blatantly obvious? Why robes?\n\nThis seems slightly similar to my last entry... But, years ago, I also used to see so many Elves in green tunics and caps. Usually a leather belt. It annoyed me terribly, but what happened to all those Elves? Perhaps the White Rose purged them on Anthos?\n\nMy thoughts drifted back to Tyler today, and I wept... Could I have saved him, I wonder? Could I have cured his illness? I sometimes wonder if I could have died in his place, but it /was/ an illness. Wasn't it? Forgive me my dear old friend, I failed you.\n\nToday my mind brought me back to Ventus, or at least thinking of him. Had I been there, I wonder if I could have taken that killing blow for him... But no, I was probably in a tavern somewhere drinking my worries away. Forgive me, brother.\n\nMy bloodlust sometimes drives me mad. I really do wonder if I am losing my mind. I medidate, and tell myself 'restist, resist, rest'. For years I have done that. It may have dulled that old urge, but by no means does it quench it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day 1§0\n§0\n§0It's been said around town that a volcano errupted and there is a dragon on the loose. I cannot see the sun as there is a cloud of ash covering a good proportion of the sky, making it nearly impossible to see.\n\nDay 2§0\n§0\n§0Bits of ash have begun to fall from the clouds. I at first assumed it to be snow, however it's not. The air smells of smoke, and a dense bog conceals most of the land. The ash is on and off, but the cloud is constant, taking over most of the sky.\n\nDay 3§0\n§0\n§0Almost no ash for most of the day. Or what we call day. I wouldn't know because we cannot see the sun. I sleep when I feel tired.\n\nDay 4§0\n§0\n§0Things have gotten much worse. Since I woke up the ash has not stopped falling. Small grey piles are beginning to pile up on the rooftops, and the sky, if possible, is even darker than yesterday. The ground is hot and I can hear the magma boiling\n\nunderneath me. No crops are growing,\n\nso we have little food. We must rely on our stocks, for our livestock is not yet efficiently developed.\n\nDay 5§0\n§0\n§0The ash is still falling. The ground is rumbling and I fear what is to come.\n\nDay 6§0\n§0\n§0The ground is almost ankle deep with ash. It's like snow, but not as bright. And it smells. And I'm alergic to it. Anyways.§0\n§0\n§0The  dragon attacked Port Vydrick today. I was away as this happened, but it was supposedly terrifying.\n\nDay 9§0\n§0\n§0I'm currently standing in Laureh'lin, watching as a storm occurs. The lightning is bright, and all striking in one specific spot. The wind is making it difficult to write but I am trying to keep track. More in a few minutes. §0\n\nDay 9 pt 2§0\n§0\n§0The lightning is heavy, I've been hit at least 3 times now.§0\n§0\n§0Pt3§0\n§0\n§0I'm slouched underneath a tree. I fear for my life and question coming out here to investigate.\n\nPt4§0\n§0\n§0I blacked out. I don't remember what happened, but I woke up today with scars on my back shaped almost identically as the lightning bolts that struck.", ""),
