        StaticBook("Fishidex", "§bCir'dian", "The Fishidex\n\n\n\nThe #1 information book for fish and fisherpeople.\n\nBy Sen Nymphea\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n       -Bonefish-\n\nThis fish has skin so thin that its bones are visible, and there are so many that I can't even count them ( I lost count at 420, couldn't be bothered to start again ). I don't think there's enough meat on the entire body of\n\nthis thing, other than bone, to even justify trying to eat it. Any volounteers are welcome to try, but I cannot be held responsible if they choke...\n\nTends to weigh around 1lb and 6oz and is found virtually everywhere. Doesn't\n\nseem to give any unusual effects after consumption, but my husband, after volounteering to try some, still managed to cough up a bone even after I spent fourty minutes making sure there were none left.\n\n      -Ghostfish-\n\nThis fish is very odd. It's practically weightless and I can almost see straight through it. In fact, I'm not entirely convinced it's actually here. It could just be my imagination and perhaps I never even caught the fish in the\n\nfirst place.\n\nI can't even get an accurate measurement of its weight, but it weighs less than 1oz. I've only ( barely ) seen these swim about in swampy areas. My husband told me it tasted and felt like paper, and that for a moment, he felt dead.\n\n       -Sunfish-\n\nThis variety of fish has very shiny, yellow scales. They're a very common sight, especially around dawn, but always swims toward shelter when night falls. It hates Mooneye fish with a passion and viciously attacks them\n\nwhenever they see them.\n\nThese fish tend to weigh around 4lbs 4oz and are found in literally every location. Some people actually throw these back after catching them. My husband says it tastes very nice, but is a hint too spicey for him.\n\n       -Mooneye-\n\nThe Sunfish's nocturnal rival. These fish bare a large contrast compared to the Sunfish, donning pale blue scales that glow under moonlight. They are just as common as Sunfish, and why they fight so often I have no idea,\n\nbut I've heard that if the two varieties of fish are ever seen swimming together in a friendly manner, an eclipse is going to occur soon.\n\nFound everywhere, just like Sunfish, and weighs around 2lbs 5oz. Apparently lovely texture, but tastes\n\nbland, so my husband suggested that I find something to serve with it to give it some flavour.\n\n     -Weaverfish-\n\nThis fish tends to bury itself on the bottom of lakes and snatch small animals as they venture past, including smaller fish. It has a sand-like colour to its scales with a fairly black tail and dorsal fins.\n\nI've only found these in thick jungle forests, where many other dangerous varieties of fish tend to live, and usually weighs around 5lbz 7oz. My husband nearly collapsed after I had him try eating some, and said he was almost paralyzed. I'm not sure what\n\nexactly caused this, but I'm considering finding other volounteers...\n\n       -Monkfish-\n\nThese beasts are huge and very greedy, its teeth are also very sharp, which has allowed them to bite through many of my nets in the past. They're also quite difficult to cook because of its size.\n\n\nPretty difficult to weigh, but on average they size up around 14lbs 10oz. They're found in several locations, usually rivers and thick wooded areas. After convincing my husband to try some of this fish, he said that it was quite chewy, but made\n\nhis entire body feel like it'd spent a year on the most comfortable mattress and it definately made up for the last fish I'd made him try.\n\n      -Cactusfish-\n\nThis prickly feller is covered head to tail in grey needles, which makes it very difficult to cook, catch and prepare. Their scales are normally dark green and the teeth are surprisingly blunt. Sometimes other fish get stuck to the\n\nspines along its body, which is a bonus if you're willing to try and peel them off.\n\nFound in dry, desert areas and weighs on average 6lbs 2oz. After very carefully removing all of the needles, my husband said the fish tasted similar to steamed\n\nvegetables and that the texture was delicate. Nevermind, he still managed to find a needle with his tongue...\n\n       -Hagfish-\n\nThis thing is actually pretty creepy. It looks shriveled and aged like an old Human lady and it even has a bit of hair growing on it. It also smells like mouldy wood. To be honest, it probably is just a really old fish of another variety\n\nthat has somehow found a way to take refuge away from the rest of fish society. They hate venturing far from their homes and hate anything that ventures too close to their homes even more. \nOnly found in murky swamplands and usually weighs\n\naround 3lbs 9oz. It smelled disgusting, even when cooked, and my husband agreed, but after finally trying some ( and struggling not to vomit ) he told me that he could somehow see everything much better and that he could see my beauty even better than\n\nusual. I'm considering serving this to my husband more often.\n\n      -Silverfish-\n\nThis fish is very interesting... Because I don't think it's a fish at all. In fact, I'm pretty sure that it's a bug, but whatever it is, I found it swimming about like any other fish. The only reason I'm making an entry for it is\n\nbecause I accidently squished it on to the page...\n\nI find these things swimming about near large mountains, but its too small to weigh.\n\n     \\ \\ / /\n-->]}}}}}}}}|===\n     / / \\ \\\n\n       -Knifefish-\n\nAs the name probably suggests, this fish is notably dangerous because of its knife-like shape. The entire head is like one long blade, varying in length from 2 - 5 inches, about as hard as a rock, and so sharp it could\n\nprobably be used as a weapon. The body is rather light blue whereas the head blends in to a more subtle white.\n\nTends to roam around thick jungle areas with an average weight of 1lb 2oz. My husband said it tasted quite nice, and he kept the\n\nhead as a spare knife, but felt nothing strange.\n\n       -Toadfish-\n\nThe round, fat body of this fish makes it difficult to distinguish from other animals that roam aqautic habitats, such as frogs. Actually, it looks so much like a frog that it might actualls just be a legless one with an\n\nunusually fish like tail. Whichever it actually is, it certainly likes to croak.\n\nOnly found quite occasionally in swamp and marsh regions, where other similar animals live and, on average, weighs around 2lbs 2oz. My husband had a\n\nsevere stomach ache that lasted several hours. I've decided that I won't be asking him to try anymore fish. I'll just have to find some volounteers instead.\n\n        -Alefish-\n\nI despise this fish because it smells distinctly of alcohol, and the smell gets even stronger when it's cooked. I don't have any clue why it smells like this. It's mostly white with a faint hint of amber.\nmaybe this is where\n\nale actually comes from? I really don't know, but one thing I do know is that this is probably the fish I've never been more dissapointed to find.\n\nI found this fish swimming around Vaerhaven, which is far too cold for most fish to survive, and\n\nit weighs just 1lb 2oz. My husband volounteered to try this fish as soon as he could smell it coming from the kitchen, and said it had that Halfling brew taste. It took me an hour to get him to stop acting drunk.\n\n        -Mullet-\n\nThis fish is rather dull, and doesn't seem to possess any 'unique' properties. The scales are grey and the fins wash to a colour fairly similar to cooked beef, which only puts me off even more. It can easily be distinguished because\n\nof its exceptionally long body and the 2 dorsal fins on both its back and belly.\n\nThese are quite commonly found around mountainous areas and weighs around 5lbs 11oz on average. A friend of mine volounteered to try this one, and\n\nactually quite enjoyed it, claiming it had a very unique taste that she would expect from an expensive restaurant, but said she didn't feel anything unusual after consumption.\n\n      -Snakefish-\n\nFor some reason, I wasn't very happy with catching this fish, probably because it reminds me of my childhood obsession with snakes. Everything about this fish is remniscent of a snake, even the tail somewhat. It can be\n\ndistinguished by the pale pink scales across the body and the long fins that stretch by its sides. In fact, if it weren't for its fins, I'd say I really had caught a snake.\n\nFound in a river very close to a jungle and weighs around 5lbz 4oz.\n\napparently tastes like mutton with a much finer texture, but didn't have any unusual effects.\n\n        -Salmon-\n\nThis fish is apparently popular among deepsea fishermen due to its high demand. It has an appearance similar to Mullet, but normally with a dark spotty texture along its back with a very subtle hint of red. The meat itself however is\n\nvery distinguishable because of its unmistakable salmon pink colour when raw.\n\nFound quite commonly near or in the Ocean, with an average weight of 7lbs 8oz. My friend said she loved the taste and would happily try more if I needed her to. No\n\nunusual effects were reported.\n\n       -Lakefish-\n\nThese fish are slick and very oily, and also have a strong tail which they flail about madly when startled. This makes them fairly difficult to handle, especially with nets. The scales shine a variety of blues, usually lightest from\n\nthe back and gradually shading darker until it reaches the belly.\n\nFound very commonly in lakes and sometimes near thick wooded areas. Usually weighs around 5lbs 2oz, apparently tastes quite bland and has no unusual properties.\n\n       -Magikarp-\n\nI really don't have much to say about this one. It's probably the most boring fish I've ever seen, despite how ridiculous it looks. The scales are very vibrant orange and the fins are equally as vibrant yellow. The eyes are very large\n\nand don't even look like they belong to a fish.\n\nI find these quite scarcely just about everywhere, and they weigh around 2.2lbs on average, depsite their average size. My friend told me it was the most boring thing she'd ever eaten and\n\nnothing even slightly unusual happened. The only thing slightly interesting about this fish is that it splashes around madly when pulled to land.", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 3", "§bLucion Sullas", "-------------------\n            The\n        Maehr'sae\n        Hiylun'ehya\n\n        Chapter 3\n-------------------\n\nAs interpreted by Lucion Sullas. Former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun'or.\n\nAs with any ideology, there are misconceptions amongst the uninitiated. Mainly upon the desires of its adherants, the reasons behind their actions, or perhaps even mere differences in personality. It is difficult to write a truly concise list,\n\nbut one hopes the ones he lists are relevant to the reader.\n\n   1. On Racism and\n        Seclusion\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support illogical hatreds of other peoples. Rather, it supports rational wariness of dangerous outsiders--such as Orcs, goblins, and suspicious\n\nstrangers. The Orc and goblin are beings with a natural aversion to elven thought and philosophy. Though there can be exceptions, they are often ignored or destroyed, should they be in the presence of the Pure. They cannot be\n\ntrusted under any circumstances.\n\nIn regards to the other races, it is most certainly dependant on the high elf in question. I am yet to meet a High Elf aside from Uradir who truly despised all peoples equally.\n\nIt is for these\n\nreasons adherants separate themselves from contemporary society.\n\n  2. On Insults and\n      the Insulted\n-------------------The Maehr'sae hiylun'ehya does not support arbitrary personal attacks. It does, however, support learning, advising, and truth.\n\nShould an individual speak without\n\nmerit or evidence upon an individual with the purpose of cruel amusement, then they are a poor adherant, and have provided nothing to anyone.\n\nHowever, advise can often be misinterpreted as insult. Adherants are taught to\n\ndespise falsehood, therefore should something be perceived as incorrect they rightly feel the need to amend it.\n\nIf an individual has their feelings hurt during the process, it is their issue, and not the adherant's.\n\n  3. On Violence and\n       Aggression\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support physical violence of any kind. It does support safeguarding the purity of its people. Often, death to those who would sully the purity of the\n\nadherants is the first and foremost answer to such crimes. However, violent actions belong to beasts, and are beneath us. Ours is an order built upon the mind, not on the passions of raised fists.\n\n  4. On 'Purges' and\n         Murder.\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support 'Purges,' or murder. It does, however, support the exaction of justice to craven monsters.\n\nSome individuals are so profane in their\n\nexistance that they insult and endanger our way. Such people are more often-than-not loathed throughout all civilised lands. Such individuals are few and far between, but if by the act of living they injure us, then they must be destroyed for the good\n\nof all. Exile ought to be the first and foremost method of drastic punishment in any case.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n5. On Experimentation\n     and Learning\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support unethical and cruel experiments. It does support the vigorous aquisition of knowledge. Those that would perform any experiment on a living,\n\nsentient, non-consenting individuals are performing a disgusting act that harms their own purity through reckless and untethered curiosity, as well as harming the reputation of their own people. It is bizarre, cruel, unethical, and the findings never\n\noutweigh the cost.\n\n  6. On Emotion and\n     Aversion to it.\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not support an emotionless state in the individual. Rather, it encourages logic, foresight, and wisdom over passionate outbursts.\n\nIt is wiser to think before feeling. In public, it is beneath an adherant to act by the whims of emotion--it shows a lack of self-control and would likely offend those around yourself.\n\n  7. On Superiority\n    and Arrogance\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya does not declare high elves to be superior to other races. It does, however, support that those who follow its path closely are greater than others, as they seek\n\nenlightenment through the unravelling of truth, rather than the mundanities of life.\n\nIdentifying adherants as 'arrogant' is simply an innocent misinterpretation on the side of the uninititated. Should one encounter an adherant that claims\n\nthemselves to be 'superior' generally speaking, one would advise you to ask them of their current academic projects. Should they refuse to answer, it is safe to say their ego speaks, and not the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya.\n\n 8. On Adherants and\n     Their Qualities\n-------------------The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya supports that only the Mali'aheral, with their inherant blessings, can successfully follow the Pure Way. But this is only true in theory.\n\nThe Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya encourages community cohesion and the search for truth. Theoretically, any race (with the exception of perhaps the orcish peoples) may adopt and follow the path to enlightenment. No other race has attempted\n\nto adhere to it, thus perhaps it will never be known for certain.\n\nOne hopes that this series has been illuminating. Seek out L. Sullas, if you can, should questions be sought. Otherwise, good luck on your own twisting path.\n\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Tower of Heroes§0\n§0\n§0((Originally written by TehLulu))", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Bryophite. Affected by plant-like parasite. Glows in the dark. Verdigris Moss account on her. Bryophites have natural sedatives that neutralize large amounts of pain, not consciously controllable. Bryophites have a small, cordoned-off\n\nsection of their minds controlled by the parasite, controlling the plant functions of body. Made of plants, weak to fire and cold. No sunlight-- can't sleep, headaches, becomes hard to move. Hallucinations. Eventually, death. Can practice deity magic,\n\nmore subject to the repurcussions of voidal magics. Using dark magic physically sickens them. No repurcussions from deific magics. Plants grow on them, not actually part of them. If uprooted, grow back. Plants and herbs that grow on Bryophites\n\nare of a higher quality than natural-grown ones. Leads to undesirable situations.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Ghouls-undead, require life-force, burned by Ascended flame, weak to aurum, is hungrier each time it rises, soulless shell of man. becomes calm with life-force. drains from people and beasts. Immortal. Soul shadows deny death.\n\nCannot die whatsoever, efforts of common/holy men futile. Puts into rage upon awakening from death. without souls, rather have soul shadows, compararble to  flames vs. embers.§0\n§0ghouls can 'master' themselves, and retain some semblance of humanity, but\n\nthose who don't only live to get lifeforce. Husks and shells.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "crowning; apparition/wight saturating mystic with ectoplasm, allowing them to generate it. saps of energy. §0\n§0KEEP THIS BOOK SAFE", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "menhir- conducts ectoplasm. gives off ripples of it. mana + ectoplasm put through a soul. thus, all extoplasm is unique, as souls are. deadbreath-- only on-the-go spell of mysticism. useful. physical manifestation of ectoplasm. blinding thick milky fog\n\nsubtly disorientates. air evocation/holy magic gets rid of it ez. mystics/phantoms unnaffected due to already being marinated. lingers for hours to days. useful in enclosed spaces-- globe around user. very persistent. bring ectoplasm from place in body\n\nto skin, envision it. Saturation; complicated, saturating a weapon with ectoplasm. contained ectoplasm in item, usually used to create a Graven or Ghost. ghost of an animal, as they can't make gravens. when it comes to people, they chose between ghost or\n\ngraven OOCly. they wll be linked with creator due to his ectoplasm being around. must land killing blow. Only cast when next attack will be fatal. often to skull/throat. soul unable to go to soul stream, anchored to ectoplasm in body. ectoplasm no longer\n\nbelongs to you and belongs to newborn phantom. ectoplasm from then on produced from mystic's original. phantom will always follow orders, not harm you. don't abuse it, phantoms are still people. obedience fades in a year.\n\nphantoms can be forced to do something with different liturgy. time until ghost/graven is formed related to prowess of user. takes full year with no practice, shorter as it goes. for cosi, instantaneously to an hour.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Black mist from shoulders. abnormally fast. armored. taught by ashkeeper of the flames. black miasmas.§0\n§0Known as Darkstalkers. Collect life force, incredibly strong. Weak to holy magic. keep coming back to life; like liches. capable of speech and\n\nreason. necrotic undead; raised by necromancer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Remriel; golden, odd entity.§0\n§0\"communes\" with Yeh Rhthulu§0\n§0Calls himself an \"Augur\". born descendant. Became an augur through Yeu Rhthulu's grace. used to be a high elf. became so by following yeu and her thirty §0scriptures.\n\ndiet: none. similiar to spectres. Is immortal.§0\n§0obscure process. feels like mercury. refused to be poked with gold sword. floats. Lefkos Glowsbane, second augur.  became augurn through yeu rhthulu. can change back. is a high elf. also feels like\n\nmercury, sort of. wears golden-plated armor, part of his body. feels 'refreshed'. does not require food. can float up to three feet high temporarily. armor is attached to body. augurs of blue, pink, and without helmets?!!\n\nYeu Rhthulu: aengul, depicted with white skin, black hair, blue eyes. large and peasant-like nose. No place of worship: worshipped with life and heart. forgives.§0\n§0color of augur may be augur's fav color? yeu not into symbolism or deep meanings. simple.\n\njust wanting to follow yeu is enoug, quite accepting. loves all followers. doesn't care about no soul.§0\n§0Doesn't seem to get angry. Immune to fire and electricity. descendant can use magic. Totally sterile. same process of becoming an augur as becoming\n\ndescendant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "climbed out of a woman's body§0\n§0emotional capacity for laughter still there§0\n§0desdemona. can wear corpses, suits of armor, humanoid forms, necrotic amalgations/skeletonsweaker magic when husked. more weight, weaker magic.\n\nInvisibility. Kozilek, Barrowlord of the Tide, Herald of the Nameless. Wight. Gifted with 'unlife'. Necrotic undead; liches, darkstalkers, ghosts, wraiths. anomalous; iblees' undead, harbingers. spectral undead: gravens, apparitions, wights.§0\n§0*ghouls for\n\nghost. Wights not entirely natural. Wights created through mysticism without godly intervention. invisibility natural, as is without weakness of the flesh, no physical body. telepath, telekinesis, better mystic, manifestation control. is intangible.\n\naurum conducts lifeforce and does bad shit to undead. he's le only wight. being forced out of a body is really bad yo.§0\n§0feels metaphorical death. mysticism started by Kozilek. ((totally wack yo))§0\n§0Wights composed of ectoplasm mostly", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "nearby the caliphate, beside the road. seen in the evening. were talking, scattered when seen. one woman who was unarmored; basic, ragged clothing. human. no insignias. burgundy to dark gray.\n\nFjarriauga/Frost Witches", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "===================Archery by Ashur§0\n§0VOL IV: Individual Archery Warfare§0\n§0===================§0\n§0\n§0*This illustration depicts an assault on Wrath's Clutch, a common battleground of Aegis lore, with a young Dark Elf nervously clutching at his bow.*\n\nI am Ashur Uilosson of Laurelin, once Prince of the Holy Princedom of Malinor. My eyes have seen the rise and fall of kingdoms, races, and entire worlds. I can tell you from experience that life as we know it has few constants. Archery is one of them.\n\nUnsurprisingly, so is warfare.§0\n§0\n§0Preparing for war is complex beyond measure, and even after centuries of experience, I wince when I try to convey it to the layman. Nonetheless, I will educate you as best I can.\n\nThe archer's style largely draws upon their race and particular inclinations. For example, as a young Warden of Malinor, I was educated on subjects such as guerilla warfare, striking without being seen, the importance of mobility, and such.\n\nOther races, such as most human factions, are more open and aggresive with their bow support, sometimes openly riding into battle with a pike as their secondary should archery prove ill-suited. All in all, however, there is only one /correct/ form:\n\nThe best style of archery is the style that kills your enemy in that time and place. §0\n§0\n§0That said, before we touch on tactics, you should familiarize yourself with the types of bows and arrows used in combat. Your equipment is the main priority.\n\n--=TYPES OF BOWS=--§0\n§0\n§0-COMPOSITE§0\n§0The composite bow is constructed of multiple types of material, working in tandem to produce a more efficient usage of force. One common style of composite, made popular in Hanseti culture, uses\n\nhorn and sinew, laminated upon the belly and back respectively. While composite bows provide a smaller, stronger weapon, maintenance and upkeep is a pain. The animal glues used to laminate are quickly ruined by rain and humid temperatures.\n\nIn addition, the creation of a composite bow takes far more time than the typical self-bow. If you plan to use this tool, I'd advise restricting it to dry climates, and to carry it in a waterproofed leather case.\n\n-COMPOUND§0\n§0A more recent invention, the compound bow uses levers and pulleys to provide the archer with a mechanical advantage. I've only experimented with one of these tools, so my experience here is a little slim. They are made of metal,\n\nand take several weeks to properly manufacture. While the concept of a scientific bow is fascinating to me, it is nearly impossible to make one without a professional, and the rigors of warfare have a way of breaking little bits and parts. Be wise.\n\n-FLATBOW§0\n§0My heritage. The flatbow was pioneered within mali'ker society as far back as Aegis, and while few are able to trace its impact on archery as a whole, I can say for a fact that this style of bow has saved my life countless times.\n\nThe limbs of the flatbow are rectangular, narrowing in the middle for the grip of the bow - the complete opposite of a traditional bow, where the limbs are narrower than the grip. The limbs are non-recurved, and distribute stress evenly.\n\nWhat I personally enjoy about the flatbow is its versatility: you can adapt the limb lengths to create a small hunting bow or a long warbow, and the style remains effective. They take more time to fashion and create, but are well worth the effort.\n\n-LONGBOW§0\n§0This is the seige weapon of old, and you will find it amongst the heavy artillery and mounted archers. These bows are long, usually matching the height of the archer themselves, and require a trememdous amount of strength to operate.\n\nPersonally, during some \"land disputes\" with the nation of Renatus of Asulon, I carried a longbow of yew that had a draw strength of 180lbs. Given arrows worthy of its might, it could easily punch through lesser metals at a reasonable distance.\n\nLongbows are the common bow of warfare because they can fire for long distances, and are absolutely devastating up close. They are cumbersome, however, and are heavily exhausting to operate repeatedly. I'd advise against charging into the fray with one.\n\n-RECURVE§0\n§0What makes a recurve bow special is its limb tips. As the limbs near their terminus on either end, the wood curves back around to angle the tips in the opposite direction, facing the enemy. A rough design to maintain over time, but effective.\n\nArchers on horseback or within thick underbrush will find relief in the recurve, since it allows more force for less weight and size. Most rangers and unrelated edgy hood-wearing shadow figures swear by its capacity for destruction on short notice.\n\nNote, however, that the recurve design in wood is highly unnatural, and will slowly deform over time. In closing, this style of bow is excellent for the quiet professional, or as an auxillary weapon for someone more versed in a different style of combat.\n\n-REFLEX§0\n§0In this style, the limbs of the bow don't curve back towards the archer, but /forwards/, curving forward in a C shape when unstrung. To prepare, you pull the limbs back into shape, using the bowstring to maintain it.\n\nI've seen this design favored in Orc culture from time to time, but never really grew fond of it. They require premium materials and constant babying to maintain, but are extremely compact when unstrung. They simply aren't my style, but they may be yours.\n\n-SELF§0\n§0The common bow, made of one piece of wood. No fancy bells and whistles, no recurves or styles of thicknesses, this is the primal, raw bow. Useful to create in a pinch, but horrid in combat. The Orcs will certainly piss in your skull if you try.\n\n-==PROPER ARMOR==-§0\n§0\n§0By now, you should have an idea of what style of archer you'd prefer to be. Just as no single style of bow fills all tasks, no single suit of armor will be best for the job at hand. This is also dependant on your strength.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Daddy, that looks silly on you§0\n§0\n§0No, daddy, it's a surprise§0\n§0\n§0Daddy, don't go tonight, I'm, I'm scared§0\n§0\n§0It's snowing, I told you it would\n\nDaddy, daddy where are you, where are you going, daddy§0\n§0\n§0Today I drew a picture of a rabbit, daddy§0\n§0\n§0No, I don't like that story§0\n§0\n§0But daddy, you promised\n\nDaddy, come back, you said you would come back§0\n§0\n§0One last trip! One last trip! You always come back! Always!§0\n§0\n§0Why did you lock the door, daddy, you said you'd come back, you promised.\n\nI hate you, daddy, you promised me, you promised me§0\n§0\n§0I'm so hungry, come back daddy, why did you lock the door", "")
    )

    private fun _VAILOR_13(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-§0\n§0\n§0\n§0     THE LIBRARY                 OF DRAGUR        §0\n§0\n§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-§0\n§0\n§0*Here lies an illustration of a Harbinger's helmet, hollow and empty*\n\nI am Ashur Uilosson. Those familar with the name know that I need no introduction. If you haven't heard of me, I would encourage you to read more history, do more push-ups, and laugh once in awhile. §0\n§0\n§0We suffered greatly to ensure your current liberties.\n\nDuring the cusp of the new year 1539, in the realm of Vailor, I found myself wandering the Cloud Temple docks. Even in my older age, I've found small ways to bribe myself aboard vessels, exchanging labor for free transport. One of my favorite hobbies.\n\nI departed from a Dwarven whaling fleet with some little handmade candles of blubber. The shuttles across this space of land are inexpensive, you see, and I was able to elect transport from a red-robed stranger with two candles as payment.\n\nHis carriage took me to the Library of Dragur, a newer establishment I'd heard in passing while acting as a stagehand for an Elven playwright some time back. The building is rectangular, with towering sphere dormitories of blue along its roof.\n\nSitting behind the reception's desk was an Inquisitor.§0\n§0\n§0Their threat is dimished since Anthos, but it still caught of off-guard. His pale-blue helm regarded me with a silent nod as I entered the wings of waiting knowledge.\n\nNaturally, the section on Elven history is tragically small and inaccurate. Ebs' anthology on Malinor is there, and despite its way of glossing over my homeland's most proud achievements and culture (and me, namely - we never got along), it provides the-\n\n-layperson with a glimpse into Laurelin. Much of Aegis' Elven literature was destroyed in its final weeks. But that's a subject for another volume.§0\n§0\n§0Despite this one flaw, the library had an excellent selection. Superior to most.\n\nI found \"residency\" squatting in an overgrown farm barn a few miles beyond the place, and became a regular visitor. Books have become a fabulous pleasure of mine in the past two centuries, since much writing focuses on past history, which I am bound to.\n\nA notion occured to me one day while passing the Elven shelves:§0\n§0\n§0Why can't /I/ write?§0\n§0\n§0In the past, I'd shyed away from pulling all memories to the forefront for fear of recalling things that ought be forgotten. But the idea lingered.\n\nI approached the Harbinger (Orithur, pale blue helm), and requested a blank tome. He offered one after brief conversation on what I'd be writing on. §0\n§0\n§0I selected an easy-enough topic: parts and construction of a bow.\n\nThe book appeared faster that I'd have ever thought possible. I filled the pages with illustration and bullet-point on everything I'd learned since I was a whelp in Laurelin's limbs, focusing merely on how to make a fine bow and arrow.\n\nUpon creation of the book, I left it on Orithur's desk with a request for employment.§0\n§0\n§0A week later, I was given the key to one of the blue sphere towers, and a set of red robes. At that moment, I began as a Scholar of Dragur.\n\nDuties were painfully simple, so the act of tidying up the shelves or taking inventory were nothing but an afterthought. True exertion came from writing, re-writing, illustrating, and binding several novels of my own. I wrote on anything I could think of:\n\n-archery, rangerhood, camoflauge, guarding authorities, construction of wild and fanciful bows. A wonderful release of my energy.§0\n§0\n§0Few others worked as Scholars, and for a time, everything was peaceful, something I didn't expect to last.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Essie's Diary§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=*The page is covered in small drawings of what seems to look like Riga in Felsen, a large house and a smaller one conjoined together with a small barn where farms animals rest*\n\nDear diary, §0\n§0Today I found out that Lady Roswell is expecting, I was ecstastic but for her, not so much. She is very worried that we shall be attacked and she won't be able to help her people. I have been through it so I can help.\n\nDear Diary,§0\n§0I am confused as to what this is between me and Tenaka, I think we are engaged but holding off the wedding for a long time, he is a very nice man, am I ready to stay I love you to him yet? Or have children?\n\nDear diary,§0\n§0Today I asked Tenaka to move in with me, it was awkward for a while until he said yes and now we're happily living together. Although he'd love to sell his old house so we must do it secretly. Oh the worry.\n\nDear Diary, §0\n§0I am currently battling with two high elves and a ghoul, I have slayed one and I am now hidden. It is time I work up the strength to kill the other high elf. My sword is at the ready in it's leather sheath, I will serve justice.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Josiah Mallister's notes and thoughts.§0\n§0_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_*_§0\n§0\n§0Baron Aymer Fournier has been attacked by an unknown assailant, the main suspects are as follows;§0\n§0\n§0Dwarves (likely Dunamis) Which I find to be quite plausible, as Dunamis has raided\n\nNyrhold on numerous occasions over the past few Saint's days§0\n§0\n§0As I cannot pursue my lead with the dwarves, as my death will ensue (probably torture before death) I will pursue the secondary lead with the masterly house of Roke.\n\nHughes Fournier, the heir to the Barony of Rivervyn listed a few minor grievances with the Roke's, such as a whipping. Adriana Fournier, daughter of Aymer Fournier, was assaulted at an unspecified date and a n unknown Roke stood and observed.\n\nI shall now pursue the lead and head to the Roke ruled barony of Nessevelt.§0\n§0\n§0-14th of First Seed 1544.\n\n\"Ser Aymer decided to mock my father's death and my deceased wife, so I flogged him\" - Ser Rhys Roke§0\n§0(Deceased wife; Ellerette Roswell)§0\n§0\n§0\"I saw the odd creature choking Adriana to death and throw her into a well\"\n\n\"I then proceeded to fend it off, it hasn't been seen since\" - Rhys Roke§0\n§0\n§0He spoke of the duel and explained what happened, saying Fournier servants had spat on the area and assaulted Prince Elias de Savoie.§0\n\n- No land Disputes§0\n§0- No Monetary Disputes", ""),
        StaticBook("Hymms of Canon", "§bCarleton Cassius", "Sanctus\n \n \nSanctus, Sanctus, Sanctus, Dominus Deus Sabaoth.\n \nPleni sunt caeli et terra gloria tua.\n \nHosanna in excelsis.\n\nBenedictus, qui venit in nomine Domini.\n \nHosanna in excelsis.\n \nAmen.\n\nLuceat Eis Lux Invicta, Luceat Eis,\nCum tui gratia, Sancte Domine\nLux vestra.\nac ostende eis via tua.\nSanctum sanctorum viam\nAmen\n\nPater Noster,\n \nBenedictum sit nomen tuum.\nR.Amen\n \nBenedictum sit nomen tuum\nR.Amen\n\nEt dabit, nobis Messiarum\n \nHoren, Owyn, Godfrey, Seigmund.\nR.Benedicatur nomen eorum\n\n\nVenerunt omnes in nomine tuo,\nR.Amen, Amen, Amen.\n \nEt expanderunt verbum tuum et pro illo rogamus, ut pro nobis orent.\nR.Ita faciemus.\n\nAtque ponant omnes beatos et angelos nostre pietatis testimonium.\nR.Nos permanebunt pio modis.\n \nAmen.\nR.Amen\n\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nAd te Rex summe,\noculos nostros\nsublevamus flentes:\nexaudi et exaltabitur,\nsupplicantum preces.\n\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nDextera Patris,\nlapis angularis,\nvia salutis,\nianua caelestis,\nablue nostri\nmaculas delicti.\n\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nRogamus, Deus,\ntuam maiestatem:\nauribus sacris\ngemitus exaudi:\ncrimina nostra\nplacidus indulge.\n\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nTibi fatemur\ncrimina admissa:\ncontrito corde\npandimus occulta:\ntua, Redemptor,\npietas ignoscat.\n\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n\nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\n \nFiat pax in virtute tua: et abundantia in turribus tuis.\n\nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\n \nPropter fratres meos et proximos meos loquebar pacem de te:\n\nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\n \nPropter domum Domini Dei nostri quaesivi bona tibi\n\nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\n\nRogate quae ad pacem sunt Palatinus:et abundantia diligentibus te.\n \nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\n\nGloria Deus, sicut erat in principio et nunc et semper, et in saecula saeculorum. Amen\n\nDominus regnavit,\ndecorem indutus est:\nIndutus est Dominus fortitudinem,\net praecinxit se.\nEtenim firmavit orbem terrae,\nqui non commovebitur.\nParata sedes tua ex tunc;\nA saeculo tu es.\n\nElevaverunt flumina, Domine,\nElevaverunt flumina vocem suam,\nElevaverunt flumina fluctus suos,\nA vocibus aquarum multarum.\n\nMirabiles elationes maris;\nMirabilis in altis Dominus.\nTestimonia tua\ncredibilia facta sunt nimis;\nDomum tuam decet sanctitudo,\nDomine, in longitudinem dierum\n\nGloria Deus,\net Spiritui Sancto.\nSicut erat in principio,\net nunc, et semper,\net in saecula saeculorum, Amen.\n\nHosanna Filio Horen,\nBenedictus qui venit\nIn nomine Domini\nRex Oren\nHosanna in excelsis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of TheBald", "§bCharles \"The Bald\" Irongrinder", "I am the deputy,\nI am a piece of history.\nIf you meet me in PVP\nGet down on your Knees.", ""),
