        StaticBook("Goodbye", "§bThalia", "Dearest Toren,\n\nThis is very hard to write, so here it goes.\n\nI have just become a Dedicant in the grove so i will be studying there for about 3 years or so before i become a Druid. \n\nThis means i will have to move out into an\n\napartment in the Grove. \n\nI am extremly sorry about this matter and it also means we cannot date anymore as i will be too busy.\n\nI feel terrible about this but  have to tell you somehow.\n\nI have made extras of everything so you may keep things n the kitchen, and i will be halfing the things in storage.\n\nI will come back and vist in between tasks and studys, so we may be able to fit a date in then.\n\nSorry, Toren.\n\nLove from Thalia.\n\np.s Thank you, for everything.", ""),
        StaticBook("PC News #1", "§bFawynn Sorbus", "Penith Caverns Official News\n  Writer: A. Dalter\n\nThe township of Penith Caverns. A friendly community nestled underground, cut off from civilization. Founded once in the year 1274, and once again in 1804 after a long series of accidents. May our\n\nchildren be saved when that happens.\n\nThere has been discussion of a newspaper being issued, and if you are reading this you have not been slain by the newspaper men and know the rumors are true.\n\nWe all know how\n\nevasive the council can be about answering questions.\n\nAnyways, on to the news. Annilyn’s bakery has been carved out, and with it a strange discovery. A small child was found in a small bubble in the rock. In his arms he had a worn tome, which the guards\n\npromptly threw into a fire and began to pray over. He appears to be male, and stares blankly head, occasionally blinking. When he encountered a raw potato, he ate it in small, rapid bites.\n\nIf you have lost a male child who enjoys potatoes, please come\n\nretrieve him at Annalyn’s bakery. According to reports he has started singing quiet hymns and rocking back and forth.\n\nThe guards would also like me to remind everyone: dwarves are not real. They are a fictional creature only children should\n\nbelieve in. Do not try to talk to any dwarves. If you believe you have seen a dwarf, please turn yourself in at the mines for reeducation.\n\nA message from Annalyn's Bakery:\nHave you ever felt a void in your life? In your heart? In your thoughts?\n\nAre your thoughts real? Consume, destroy, obey. Annalyn’s Bakery.\n\nWe are accepting advertisements in the future, so you will be hearing from the editors if you own a buisiness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sirame in Short", "§bLindrael Torena", "The Order of Sirame§0\n§0\n§0This order, known commonly as the Sirame are the great protectors of the Wood Elves. They often do many things which the Wood Elven citizens are ungrateful for, such as keeping our lands bandit-and-creature free, bringing honour to\n\nour culture, and giving shelter and work for those who are otherwise depraved in the form of recruiting them. The Sirame is a brotherhood as much as a military, as much as it is an important pillar of our community. Many take this for granted, often\n\nnot contributing themselves, but yet the Sirame still regard them with respect, as they live under a basic code of decency and honour. Oftentimes, many who find the Sirame disagreeable are infidels themselves, untrusting of us because they have something\n\nto hide from the eye of the Law, but we, ever-vigilantly, often root out such evils. A perfect example is the evil contained within one known as Llywellyn, who, as a disgraceful member of the Sirame (using us as a cover for evil doing), did commit many\n\natrocities such as stocking armour and weapons which are believed to be aquired through illicit means, harbouring a human who attempted to assault a true member, and digging out a large segment of the ground under Laurelin. He was rooted out quite quickly\n\nas when his burrow was sacked and evicted, his armoury was rather bare, though it was clear plans for much more wrongdoing was in effect. The moral of this tale?\n\nJOIN THE SIRAME AND BECOME HONOURABLE IN ALL SENSES OF THE WORD.\n\nNOT ONLY ARE YOU HELPING YOUR PROVINCE, YOUR FELLOW MALI'I, YOU'RE ALSO HELPING ANY LOVED ONES YOU HAVE AND YOUR HOME. CONTACT YOUR LOCAL GUARD TO FIND OUT HOW YOU MAY JOIN TODAY!", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidism", "§bLibrarian Azkel Frostbeard", "This book was written by Remembrancer Azkel Frostbeard. All content in this book is first hand information passed on from the druids themselves.\n\nDruid Beliefs:\n\nDruid beliefs are based off of the the two aspects: Cerridwen and Cernunnos. Cerridwen represents birth and growth, while Cernunnos represents hunting and animals. With both of the aspects together, they represent nature and balance\n\nof all wildlife and nature. Druidism bases themselves around everything natural, and choose to not allow anything \"unnatural\" into their groves or homes. In the eyes of druids any form of void magic is considered to be unnatural, and are not allowed\n\nlearn it.\n\nDruid Code of Conduct: \nDruids are very anti-violence against themselves and others. Druid policies are based on how you are to not hurt fellow druids, or anyone else, unless out of self defence. If any unnessesary force is used, it would be highly looked\n\ndown apon. Even though this is an important rule, many druids dont go by it all the time, and may end up attacking someone with no reason.\n\nDruid Rankings:\n\nWhen you become a druid, you start off as a Dedicant, where you are starting off your learnings as a druid. If you follow the druid policies, and are deemed worthy of becoming a full Druid, then you are made into a druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Families", "§bLibrarian Azkel Frostbeard", "Druids are a wide spread group of people, with many different backgrounds, but this book shows the major families of druids.\n\nCommon Druid Families:\n\n-Winterleafs\n\n-Ibar'kers\n\n-Deathsbanes\n\n-Camoryns\n\n-Callaxons", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy In. V.II", "§bLibrarian Azkel Frostbeard", "Alchemy Ingredients Volume II: Fire Symbols\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Desert Bush Berry:\n\nRepresentations: Empowerment, Overwhelming\n\nLocations: Desert Cactus Forests in full moon days\n\nDescription: withered rose bush with brownish-gray stalks\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Flametongue's Root:\n\nRepresentations:Heat, Anger, Destruction\n\nLocation: Forest hillsides and burnt forests\n\nDescription: Bright. red colored roots\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Dwarf's Pumpkin:\n\nRepresentations: Rage,Envy,Bitterness, Power, Strength\n\nLocations: Swamplands next to muddy waters\n\nDescription: odious orange-leafed shrub\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Blood Lotus:\n\nRepresentations: Hope, Courage\n\nLocation:Entrance of caves in hot desert lands\n\nDescription: rusty- colored vine\n\nElrow Berries:\n\nRepresentations: Rage, Anger, Burning\n\nLocation: Bushes in cold climates\n\nDescription: Unedible Berries\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_\n\nCrimson Vase:\n\nRepresentations: Heat, warmth, love, passion, compassion\n\nLocations: At the base of young trees\n\nDescription: A crimson flower with large petals\n\nDrake's Tail:\n\nRepresentations: Heat, Destruction, Chaos\n\nLocation: In deserts close to  oasis\n\nDescription: A red-dusky colored plant", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Origins", "Finalhazard", "Arlen Teharissa's Compendium on:§0\n§0\n§0The Druids§0\n§0The Creator§0\n§0The Aspects§0\n§0Nature§0\n§0\n§0In Loving Memory Of:§0\n§0\n§0My Teacher: Salhassan§0\n§0My Best Friend: Fawynn§0\n§0My Father: Aphoros\n\nTable of Contents§0\n§0\n§0Chapter 1: Page 5§0\n§0The Creator§0\n§0Chapter 2: Page 17§0\n§0Our Realm§0\n§0Chapter 3: Page 21§0\n§0The Druids\n\nAuthor's Note:§0\n§0\n§0This book isn't for the ignorant. Nor is it for whom believe their God of choice is the only God in existence. This book is for the thinkers, the inventors, and those who wish to seek knowledge. Do not be afraid to interpret the-\n\n- teachings of your Archdruids, Paladins, Preachers, Popes, Kings, Queens, and your parents differently. You're not going against their word. You're expanding your knowledge by proceeding and thinking differently.\n\n\n§0Chapter 1:§0\n§0\n§0The Creator§0\n§0\n§0The start of all lies. While I do not doubt \"The Creator\"'s existence, I doubt his ability to interfere to directly with the mortal realm. That is, if he is even still alive, or-\n\n\"Active.*\"§0\n§0\n§0[*]Active; I'm led to believe that Aenguls and Daemons can, or are forced to enter a dormant state where they are unable to directly influence the world, mortals, or their own patrons. Being 'Active', is when an Aengudaemon is-\n\n- whenever they are not dormant.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0The Creator[Cont.]:§0\n§0\n§0The Creator was the first to breathe life into the world. I believe that The Creator had many failed experiments in order to create-\n\n- some sort of Primordial being similar to himself. With this, I believe he was the first alchemist. §0\n§0\n§0While this may seem trite, I believe The Creator tried to create a wife, or a husband. I really don't know as The Creator may not even have a-\n\n- true gender. Perhaps The Creator was genderless. Anyways, I digress.§0\n§0\n§0The Creator tried to create a companion in order to keep himself company. If his experiment succeeded or not, I do not know. Yet I believe that something tragic occured -\n\n- hence why we hear nothing of a second Creator-tier being.§0\n§0\n§0Then he created nature. By nature, I don't mean the grass, trees, and animals. I mean he invented a complex force (Similar to that of Mana, Life-Force, and Olive Oil) -\n\n- that cannot be governed, or maintained by any Aengul, Daemon, group, or individual.§0\n§0\n§0However, he tried to maintain it. Through this, he created The Aspects. Cerunnos, and Cerrwiden.§0\n§0\n§0The two then began to maintain nature. At -\n\n- the time however, nature was contained within a garden, or a 'Grove' of sorts.§0\n§0\n§0Eventually, nature grew rampant and spread to the nearby lands outside The Grove. The once dry deserts turned into a lushful oasis, and the lifeless tundra sprouted -\n\n- greens and turned into a dense forest.§0\n§0\n§0It was beautiful.§0\n§0\n§0But it all had to die.§0\n§0\n§0The Creator saw all the life that had been created, and decided that there must be a counterweight in order to ensure that nature did not -\n\n- overprogress. §0\n§0\n§0So, he allowed another being to roam the land. Yet, this woman was cursed. Everything she touched that was outside 'The Grove' would perish. The flowers would wilt and turn black and the dirt would lose its fertility faster than an elf.\n\nThis woman would be come to known as Nemiisae.§0\n§0\n§0As time began to pass, Cerunnos, Cerridwen, and Nemiisae knew that the three of them alone could not maintain nature, so instead they passed on the art that they knew onto the ancient descendents, thus -\n\n - creating the 'Second Generation' Druids.§0\n§0\n§0The Aspects themselves, being the 'First [or Primordial] Generation Druids.'§0\n\n\n§0Chapter 2: §0\n§0\n§0Our Realm§0\n§0\n§0\n§0I'm led to believe that the realm we live in cannot be directly touhed by any Aengudaemonic being. The Creator was no fool, I imagine he setup a barrier that is -\n\n- impenetrable to specific beings. This would include the Shamanic Greater Spirits.§0\n§0\n§0Why this barrier was setup, I do not know. I do have my theories, however.§0\n§0\n§0Perhaps The Creator forsaw himself using his powers to -\n\n - directly influence us. §0\n§0\n§0Or maybe, he realized that his future-kin would try to intervene in our mortal affairs. §0\n§0\n§0Whatever the case. I've come to this conclusion due to the fact that if the Gods could truly step down upon this realm they-\n\n - would have a long time ago, and this very land that sit on would be a warzone for the Aenguls and Daemons to fight on. §0\n§0\n§0Instead, they choose to have us follow beliefs, religions, and guided-mindsets in order to speak to them.\n\n\n§0Chapter 3:§0\n§0\n§0The Druids§0\n§0\n§0\n§0I say this as the son of a Druid, and as someone who has switched between the Naelurir and the Mother Circle. §0\n\nA catastrophe is a naturally occuring event that occurs whenever the balance is disrupted to the point of no-return. §0\n§0\n§0The freezing over of Thales.§0\n§0The drought in The Fringe.§0\n§0The Bull Worm of Athera.\n\nAll these moments of loss is a product of our own misconduct.§0\n§0\n§0To be blunt. A Catastrophe is nature's way of resetting itself from the damage that we let occur, whether it be overgrowth, or the entire destruction of nature. Do remember that nature itself-\n\n- is a primordial force that the Aspects do not control, but help maintain nature, and simply represent specific aspects of it.§0\n§0\n§0While I do not believe that the destruction of nature is the way to obtain 'balance', on the contrary I also do not -\n\n - believe in the idealogy that planting trees and having each dedicant create a grove as a Grand Task is optimal for the balance.§0\n§0\n§0A cruel type of irony it is that we as Druids are supposed to aid in maintaining the balance, when a large portion of\n\n- us refuse to change our lives in order to fit the balance we're meant to uphold. §0\n§0\n§0But, I stray from my original topic. §0\n§0\n§0The Druids as a collective whole are a unique group of individuals whom work both tegether and seperately in order-\n\nto serve the Aspects, and therefore nature in order to 'protect the balance'. §0\n\n\n§0Final Notes:§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Vol. 2 Coming Soon[TM]§0\n§0\n§0\n§020th of The Grand Harvest, 1561.§0\n§0\n§0Author:§0\n§0Arlen§0\n§0Teharissa", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Do you ever wake up, from what you assumed would be a short repose, instead groggy as all hell, having no idea where you are or how long you've been napping, ravenous as all hell?§0\n§0\n§0Me neither.\n\n   People have a bad habit of putting animals in cages. I don't very much like circuses for that fact, not that anyone has them anymore. One time I saw a catsnake in a cage. Or was it a mongoose?§0\n§0\n§0It was in there, but a midget let it out.\n\n    Can't imagine how the circuskeeper or head clown or whatever they call themselves felt about that.§0\n§0\n§0I wasn't there, though. So I couldn't say how he reacted. Probably fairly badly.\n\n   I'm curious what happened to the cat.§0\n§0\n§0When they threw it in the pond did it drown the cat, or ruin the pond?§0\n§0\n§0Pretty sure it just pissed him off.\n\n    Am I the only one who hates spiders?§0\n§0\n§0Almost makes me wish the lizard had gotten ahold of it. But it got away, and took the lizard with it. §0Or...something§0.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cigar Designs", "§bNyxxa", "-==Cigar Designs==-\n\n* these designs are just that designs and have no been create.\n\n*reproduction of these cigars is prohibited unless permission is given.\n\nSin Archetype Cigar\n\nLook: A broad black leaf wrapped about fine broad leaf tobacco. Small dark red flecks spot the filler leaves. An ebony band with an inlaid orchid painted aqua circles the rounded end of this cigar. The end of this cigar is blunt.\n\nSmell: The smell would be a hint of chocolate, salty caramel, and the very subtle smell of fine dark tobacco.\n\nTaste when smoked:\nA Subtle dark tobacco coated with the seductive cacao and teased with the salty sweet caramel.\n\nGrape Delight Cigar\n\nLook: Think leaves of light green wrapped over dark purple filler leaves. An ebony band with an inlaid orchid painted aqua circles about the cigar. This cigar is rounded on both ends and it's curcumference is largest in it's center.\n\nSmell: The smell of well ripened purple grapes, slightly fermented and young tobacco.\n\nTaste when smoked:\nThe wondrous prefection of fermented purple grapes miexes well with the young tobacco's sweetness.\n\nSugar Cookie Sweet Cigar\nLook: Leaf green broad tobacco leaves wrapped over crystallized green leaves. An ebony band with an inlaid orchid painted aqua circles about the cigar. This cigar has straight sides and is closed to a round on both sides.\n\nSmell: would smeel the aroma of young sweet tobacco and sugar.\n\nTaste when smoked:\nVery sweet sugar matching to the young tobacco's sweetness is meshed into a prefect mimicry of a sugar cookie.\n\nMint Burst Cigar\n\nLook: Wrapped in light brown borad leaf tobacco around a combination of mint leaves and golden tobacco. An ebony band with an inlaid orchid painted aqua circles about the cigar. This cigar is open on one end and has straight sides.\n\nSmell: An almost overpowering smell of fresh mint with undertones of musty golden tobacco.\n\nTaste when smoked:\nPure unadulterated fresh mint with the hint of musky golden tobacco like a fresh blend of tea with just the smallest dash of honey as an afterta", ""),
        StaticBook("A B C of Vailor", "§bLorena Faeliel", "An A B C of Our World.\n\n\n~A Child Friendly  A B C Book on the World and its Inhabitants.~\n\nA is for Aspects\n\n\"Aenguls of nature, a balance of two faces.\"\n\nB is for Bow\n\n\"A weapon used by all races.\"\n\nC is for Canonist\n\n\"Orens faith since its birth.\"\n\nD is for Dwarves\n\n\"What they lack in height, they make up in girth.\"\n\nE is for Elf\n\n\"Tall, thin, lithe and pointy eared.\"\n\nF is for Ferrum\n\n\"Makes reliable weapons, reputably feared.\"\n\nG is for Gorundyr\n\n\"Pagans and warriors, tough as rocks.\"\n\nH is for Halflings\n\n\"Short little men who worship pumpkin god knox.\"\n\nI is for Ironborn\n\n\"An evil empire of khorvad's desire.\"\n\nJ is for Jailers Moss\n\n\"A swampland moss, used in situations dire.\"\n\nK is for Kharajyr\n\n\"A bipedal race, feline and furry.\"\n\nL is for Leather\n\n\"Dried cow hides, can be tanned in a hurry.\"\n\nM is for Mage\n\n\"Shooting out fire and conjuring flowers.\"\n\nN is for Noble\n\n\"A man of high birth, knee deep in power.\"\n\nO is for Orcs\n\n\"Greenskinned and gruf, blood is their lust.\"\n\nP is for Paladin\n\n\"Servant of Xan, their cause is just.\"\n\nQ is for Qalasheen\n\n\"Brown skinned people who reside in the sands.\"\n\nR is for Raevir\n\n\"Dirty Sovetski, the scourge of the lands.\"\n\nS is for Sword\n\n\"A simple tool of wanton murder.\"\n\nT is for Tahariae\n\n\"A holy stag god who takes purity further.\"\n\nU is for Undru\n\n\"Some spooky masked god who lived in a schism.\"\n\nV is for Vailor\n\n\"Due sooner or later for a big cataclysm .\"\n\nW is for Wood Elf\n\n\"A woodland race who's bows are advanced.\"\n\nX is for Xan\n\n\"The holy diety patron of the golden lance.\"\n\nY is for Yamamoto\n\n\"The ancient homeland of the squinty eyed man.\"\n\nZ is for Zombies\n\n\"A rotting flesh monster, run if you can!\"\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Our world is vast. Our races varying and our stories different. \n\nThere are many different words for each letter. Do not limit yourself to these!\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~((Props to leowarrior14 for taking it on himself to rhyme every description.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0      The princible§0\n§0             of§0\n§0        cuteness§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0        By Zinawr\n\nLooks are a thing that even though people don't wish to admit it are a huge factor on first impressions", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "4th of Sun's Smile 1551 §0\n§0\n§0Upon investigating the coordinates given by Sir Azoth's fieldnotes volume 1, myself (Rai'wyn) and Renn came across the fearsome Dralazar's tomb. How the mighty fall, directly into a cold tomb to be forgotten.\n\nFurther investigation is advised by my novice opinion.\n\n5th of Sun's Smile 1551§0\n§0\n§0Coltaine Wick was detained by the Sirame, tortured and questioned, what about I am unsure due to being under suspecion. Suddenly you cannot trail a known Xionist member with a book and a quill without being looked at\n\nfunny.§0\n§0\n§0Hours pass and they leave the barracks but Coltaine remains inside, they tell me he is being heald over night despite their officer informing me they were executing him. Was hard to not laugh when the guards lied directly to my face.", ""),
        StaticBook("Designing v.2", "§bNyxxa", "- Designing Arcanum \n    Volume 2\n\nWritten by on called Nyxxa in the year of 1541\n\n[!] This entire book is written in an advanced code.\n\nGetting a meeting with Crineas is proving more difficult then excepted... will keep trying...\n\nMeeting with Crineas may not be as fruitful as I had hoped, I may have to locate another void mage.\n\nUpon serveral attempts to locate a shaman, a druid, a mage, and a cleric I have come up with nothing. it has been nearly half a month and the original purpose for this specific research is beginning to suffer. (see diary)\n\nAt this juncture I am going to have to attempt each method of contact myself.\n\nMy first step in this case will be Void magic. I will not as of yet cast anything as I have not enough knowledge of what effects such magic really has though I\n\nhope to prove through this experiment that all magic deity, spirit, natural, or otherwise is drawn from the void and thus accusations of mages corrupting the natural order simply cannot be true.\n\nHave gathered for the first experiment Thurak, Crineas, cerruber a court mage, and one observer Hernaeranin.\n\ntwo new faces joined our table Areni Treni and  Nihil\n\none more joined Vanlor.\n\nafter a long debate and more understand as to the nature of shamanic magic I have come to the conclusion that in fact while the origin of such magics must be the same (see against nature) \n\nThe variety of magics are not as closely connected as I had\n\nintially thought. I will write a book on the creation of this world to explain further on this topic suffice it to say that at the current juncture my project is stalled until such a time as I have further information as to the forming of the various\n\nmagics.\n\nI will continue my project after a journey to see a spirit in the immortal plane and the writing of the book about such. \n\nUntil then I am going to write what I plan to do on this journey\n\nand I will then finish this journal and begin a new addition.\n\nWe those mentioned at the meeting, will be journeying through the assistance of the shaman Thurak to the immortal spirit plane.\n\nThere we hope to contact the greatest\n\nbeing available and ask it about the creation of the world for the purpose to gain further insight into the varieties of magic. \n\nI am leaving this journal on my shelf so that in the case I am not able to return to my research, there\n\nwill be a record of my research.", ""),
        StaticBook("Plebeian Poems", "§bNyxxa", "-= Plebeian Poems =-\n2. Joyful Sleep\n3. Days of Sun\n4. Love Me?\n5. Wishing\n6. The Unready\n\n-==Joyful Sleep==-\n\nWhat a joy is sleep,\n\nDreaming illustroiousness\n\nRestful Always.\n\n-== Days of Sun ==-\n\nSunshine on the head\nSickle in hand\nPlanting roses red\nlaboring for land\n\nHe who smiles so\nsees me working hard\nI smile in return\nat the ever knowing bard.\n\n-== Love Me? ==-\n\nDid you love me,\nas we walked amoung the trees?\n\nDid love you see,\nas on lovely lilies we agree?\n\nDo you love me?\nWe will see...\n\n-== Wishing ==-\n\nWishing you were here\n\nholding onto to me\n\nOr at least near\n\nit's you I wish to see\n\n-== The Unready ==-\n\nOh dear there he goes again\n\nThe horridly unready one\n\nDestruction paramount and Insane\n\nSafety to save for none.", ""),
        StaticBook("Artful War", "§bNyxxa", "-==Artful War==-\n1. Battlefield\n2. Blade Dance\n3. Quietly\n4. The Rack\n5. Within\n\n--BattleField--\n\nLooking in a mirror,\nscene of blood and toil,\npainted ever clearer,\n'cross field's bitter soil.\nGlourious yet tired,\nbattle may be won,\nbut time will make a liar,\nof what can't be undone.\n\n--Blade Dance--\n\nRiver of Steel Dance,\n\nSet free the bird dressed in red\n\nHand, Arm, Body, Soul, Dance.\n\n--Quietly--\n\nQuietly we ride,\nnight as our misty stead,\n\nTown on hill's side,\nUnknowing of the deed,\n\nDeath's wails belied,\nTo the void we lead.\n\n--The Rack--\n\nTwist, crunch, crack,\n\nOne more turn upon the rack.\n\nCrack, red, bled,\n\nanother turn and you'd be dead.\n\n-- Within --\n\nWhat lies Within,\nthe beast of war?\n\nWhat lies Within,\nmen's hearts too sore?\n\nNothing hides the truth of heart,\nThe war within is too fine an art.", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 3", "§bFenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\" Volume One Part Three.\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: Hello once again dear reader! Our story will be taking a slow progression in action, so do be patient with the  frequency of the fighting sequences. Now, onto the story!\n\nChapter Eight: Look Before You Leap.\nAfter walking along the road for some time, an alluring scent caught my attention. It was coming from within the woods to my right. I decided to investigate and see if I could ask someone if there was a nearby town\n\nOr if they were willing to part with some food. I followed the scent of cooking food with my nose… It smelled like… fish! Delicious smelling fish at that. My stomach growled at the same time Shamone did \"I smell food kid, were gettin some of that!\" The\n\nSwath of hair said. “Yeah yeah, I’ll see what I can do with this little bit of money. Hope its enough for at least one fish.” I replied, squinting my eyes and looking through the trees, trying to see any signs of civilization. After walking a little\n\nFurther in the brush of the forest, I spotted what looked to be a clearing with a log cabin in the center. The area seemed to glow in the dimming afternoon sun. My eyes lit up at the prospect of meeting someone new and possibly getting something to eat.\n\nHowever, as I entered the clearing, I stepped on a large net and slipped, landing flat on my face. The trap was quick to activate, as the net snapped around me and hoisted me high in the air below a sturdy tree branch. Me and Shamone thrashed against the\n\nNet, but it was no use. Neither of us had a tool to cut us free. That’s when she burst through the cabin door. She had short, spiky, burnt orange hair, and stunning carrot orange eyes. She bore identical triple clawed scars  on both of her cheeks, and a\n\nLarge scar going all the way around her neck, just above a leather collar with a golden bell. Her skin was tanned and she wore a sleeveless suit. It had a tiny skirt, but left her legs otherwise unbarred. She wore a utility belt around the skirt, with\n\nSeveral pouches attached to it. She wore thick golden looking wrist guards that covered her forearms with a leather pad, not covering her fingers, as well as leg guards covered her feet to her toes, and went up to her upper thighs. The most striking\n\nFeatures about her though, were her strange cat like additions, including high perching chocolate colored cat ears that flicked from time to time, a tail of the same color that looked more sharp than it did fluffy, and long claw like nails on her feet and\n\nHands. She looked triumphantly at me, caught in what I assume was her net. “Ah ha! Like a mouse in a mousetrap! I knew I would catch a bandit sometime!” She said, briskly walking towards my entrapped self. “Nonono! I’m not a bandit! I-I just smelled food\n\nAnd wanted some!\" I said, frightened for my life. She just sneered at me “Oh yeah? How are you gonna prove that!” She said, as she reached behind her and… Pulled off her tail? I looked on in confusion, as she snapped the tail once. It straightened out\n\nInto what looked like a rod of metal with a single bladed edge, looking sharper than that of any steel... How was I gonna get out of this one?\n\nChapter Nine: Fish And Playfulness.\nI held my hands out through the resistant net meshing, \"Please you gotta believe me! I don't even know if I'm from around here! I don't know anything!\" I said, on the verge of a panic attack as the cat lady stood\n\nUnderneath me, the tip of her tail sword poking against my stomach. The woman sighed, before jumping up and slashing the netting above, dropping me to the ground. I smacked into the earth, all the air in my lungs being forced out of me from the harsh\n\nImpact. I gasped for air, closing my eyes and waiting, thinking I was going to be slain by this cat person any second. When I finally opened my eyes hesitantly, I found the cat lady bent over in held in laughter, her tail back where it belonged. She\n\nStarted to laugh uncontrollably, as I looked at her in suprise. \"Y-you aren't going to kill me?\" I asked meagerly. \"Oh my god! The look on your face! Ahahah, that shit is priceless!\" The woman said, now in a lesser fit of giggles, slowly standing back up\n\nTo about 5'8\". \"The names Natalia FoRune! Sorry about that little net of mine, tends to catch more people than it does animals. What's your name miss?\" She says, reaching out one of her clawed hands. I took up the hand and pulled myself up, while I\n\nGrabbed my hat with the other and  tightened  it back on my head \"F-Fuqua... I don't know my last name... But thanks for not killing me.\" I said, as my body unstrung itself from the stressful situation it just went through. \"My pleasure Ms. Fuqua.\"\n\nNatalie said. My stomach growled even louder than before, as I placed a hand on top of it to try and calm it. \"I don't mean to be rude but um... Would you mind if I have some of your food? I can pay for it of cou-\" I said, before Natalie cut me off.\n\n\"Ep ep! That's absolutely fine. You can come join the family for dinner! I'll bet they can't wait to see what the cat dragged in this time!\" She says, laughing joyfully at her terrible cat joke, letting go of my hand and heading towards the cabin,\n\nMotioning for me to follow. \"Well, go on kid! Free food!\" Shamone said, urging me on hungrily. I bopped my hat, startling the parasite. \"Oh be quiet you!\" I said jokingly to Shamone, before following Natalia. The air behind her smelled of... fish and\n\nPlayfulness... If that can even have a smell.\n\nChapter Ten: Meeting The Parents\nNadalie threw open the front door of the cabin, \"I'm back!\" She said in a sing song voice. I followed behind slowly, peeking my head through the door. There was a large table, chock full of food, with the main course\n\nbeing fish and rice. I licked my lips in anticipation of a meal, while Shamone nearly coated my hair in a layer of drool. There were two people sitting at the table, one male human, and one female kharajyr. The female had the same burnt orange hair as\n\nNatalie. I waved shyly at the pair \"Well who's this cute thing you dragged in?\" The kharajyr asked with a giggle. \"This is Fuqua! She fell into one of my hunting traps so I decided to let her eat with us! Hope that ain't too much of an inconvenience!\"\n\nNatalie said loudly, going to promptly take a seat, patting an empty one next to her. \"I'm Sixis FoRune, and this is my husband, Roger FoRune, make yourself at home Fuqua!\" Said the kharajyr, gesturing to the man to signify his name. I was more or less\n\nTransfixed on the swishing of Natalie’s tail than focused on making my way to my seat or replying. So, unsurprisingly, I tripped and stumbled over my own two feet and barely caught myself. I glowed with embarrassment, I shuffled into the chair next to\n\nNatalie \"So... How does your family eat?\" I asked politely. \"Dig in!\" She said, not even using the fork next to her and snatching up a whole fish, then chomping into it with fervor. Her mother did the same, but Roger picked up his fork and ate with a more\n\npreserved manner. I decided I was to hungry for eating normally, and grabbed up an entire loaf of uncut bread, tearing into it hungrily, before reaching out with my left hand to grab one of the grilled salmon, biting off large chunks of delicious fish. I\n\nKept eating like this for a while, alternating between the meager varieties of foods. After eating my fill of food (And Shamones) I leaned back in my chair. The rest of the family at the table stared at me, as I looked around slightly put off by this.\n\nThen Roger started to applaud, the others joining in quickly. I looked around at them, very confused. \"Uh... Why are you guys clapping?\" I asked with a suspicious look on my face. Natalie stood up, giving me a standing ovation, sticking her fingers in her\n\nMouth and whistling loudly, while Sixis laughed. Richard was able to explain to me \"You ate a third of the food!\"  He said in a smooth voice, a grin on his face. I looked down at the table, and discovered the lane of food in front of me was cleared. My\n\nFace grew very flustered, as I apologized in rapid fire succession. Natalie just slapped me on the back laughing \"That was awesome! I haven't been out eatin in a long time! Well played Ms. Fuqua.\" She said, her tail swishing happily. I breathed a\n\nSigh of relief and smiled. It looked like the day was about to go from worse, to ok for me... Maybe tonight wouldn't be so bad.\n\n\n\n\n===================End Of Part Three\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParasites--->\n\nParasites Explained: Parasites are strange creatures, pre dating back to before the beginnings of all the races. They once posed a major threat to the minor gatherings of people, but now, being surrounded by people in major cities, have decided to change\n\nTactics... At least most of them have. They have now adopted to leaching off sentient beings for nutrients, while maintaining their own powers. These powers are partially transferred to the host, giving them superpowers and abilities, whether they were\n\nWanted or not. Attempting to follow the example of natural parasites, people created synthetic parasites, although, they were not at all ethical in any way possible. The host controlling synthetic parasites often were mutilated in order to control them,\n\nand more often than not, end up holding more than on parasite in their body, which leads to soul corruption. Soul corruption occurs when multiple parasites are taking from the body. They begin to leach at the persons soul, instead of the hosts food,\n\nLeading to mental instability and insanity. Synthetics are able to be detached from the body, while most natural parasites cannot.\n\nCurrent Parasites In Novel: Shamone; An unruly mop of black hair, residing on the back of Fuqua's head. His rude attitude and composure usually annoys his host. He is one of the most powerful parasites in brute strength.\n\nFishtail: Manifesting in Kharajyr's only, has taken a special exception to Natalie, as she is half human, half Kharajyr. Her mixed blood had a strange effect on the parasite, giving her near immortality in the way of undying flesh. Natalie still ages and\n\nHas shown no negative effects to the parasites presence. Fishtail himself is unable to speak. He takes the form of Natalies ears and tail, infusing himself into her at a young age. Her orange fur in those areas had turned to a shiny brown.\n\nHis own ability is to be able to sharpen and stiffen, depending on the circumstance. Fishtail may also be detached by the tail only, functioning as a sword at that point. He does not give his host physical buffs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Edgy Alphabet", "§bJJKoshane", "A is for apple which might be poisonous.\n\nB is for blood which you love to spill.\n\nC is for culinary arts which are not your run of the mill...\n\nD is for dark which is a way to explain your past.\n\nE is for eternal which your suffering is.\n\nF is for fire which will turn your enemies to ash.\n\nG is for greed which corrupts us all.\n\nH is for horrible which is one way to describe how you feel.\n\nI is for internal where your pain resides.\n\nJ is for jugular which is an easy target... usually.\n\nK is for killing which you love to do.\n\nL is for luck which those who cross your path and live to tell the tale have.\n\nM is for monster which is how you see yourself.\n\nN is for negative which is what you are often considered.\n\nO is for offense which is the best defense.\n\nP is for pestilence which you pray for everyday.\n\nQ is for questionable which is what some consider your methods.\n\nR is for roaming which is what you do.\n\nS is for strike which you do from behind.\n\nT is for testicles which is a favorite target.\n\nU is for unfit to live which is what you believe most are.\n\nV is for vulture which picks the remains of your prey.\n\nW is for world which you want to destroy.\n\nX is for... I got nothing... moving on.\n\nY is for youth which is a common target.\n\nZ is for... I am at a loss again... damnit.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                       FIN\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nI wonder who want want this book...", ""),
        StaticBook("Creepy Tales V1", "§b[Teen] Mikazuki Mantisuku", "~The Cursed Doll~\n\nThe story begins back in Elysium. A young woman found a doll laying in the dirt. Believing it to be a sign of good fortune she picked it up and took it home.  It was a small beat up porcelain doll with beautiful blue eyes.\n\nThe hair on the doll was something of an oddity. It was filled with strands that were slightly different shade of color and there were some bald patches. Not thinking much of it, she took it home and cleaned its face.\n\nRestoring the doll back to beauty. She sewed new dresses for it and cleaned it thoroughly. That night, she left the doll on a shelf. She went to bed happy and content. The moon slowly rose over the sky and a loud crash was heard.\n\nStartled, the woman bolted up. The wail of her infant daughter in the room brought her attention to the child. Slowly she lit a candle and made her way to the crib. To her shock, she spotted the doll next to the crib on the floor.\n\nShaking the strange feeling she got, she picked up her child and began singing a lullaby. After the child was asleep, she picked up the doll and headed back to the main room. She frowned seeing a vase that had been next to the doll was shattered.\n\nSetting the doll back up, she began cleaning up the shards. Tired and a bit on edge, she took it outside to dispose of later. It was then she looked up, seeing a very ominous red crescent moon.\n\nA cry broke the silence and the woman turned. Hurrying inside she froze in her tracks when the crying stopped. Straining to hear she heard no crying or cooing from her room. Candle in hand, she moved to the crib.\n\nHer scream of terror pierced the air when she looked upon the thing in her crib. Blood stained its clothes and a new patch of hair had been added.\n\nThe doll sat in the crib, no child in sight. Its blue eyes stained with blood as it stared into the eyes of the woman. Slowly they seemed to glow orange and a sinister look fell upon the doll as the room soon lit aflame.\n\nThe woman, too paralyzed to move, went up with the house. The neighbors heard her screams of pain and sorrow, tried to get in the house to save her but to no avail.\n\nWhen the blaze finally died out, the only thing found was bones of the mother, cradling the broken bones of an infant. The doll was found untouched on the shelf where the mother had originally placed it, its clothes singed slightly\n\nand its head of hair nearly full. Blood still stained the clothes. When the people returned to collect the things, the doll was no longer in the home.\n\nRumors are spread that a similar doll was found in the home of the duchess, not long before the orcs claimed her head. Through out the history since that first recorded event, the doll has appeared over and over, death and bloodshed following its wake.\n\nWhen the Fringe opened, the doll seemed to have disappeared, but who knows how long until it resurfaces.", ""),
        StaticBook("Heaven In Hell", "§bDurza Volkihar", "He comes to me every night in my dreams. A figure wrapped in shadows with red eyes. He whispers temptations of power. I admit i was extremely tempted to accept his offer but i have got to many things to stay good for but fear i might give in.\n\nHe sends me visions of myself ruling over the lands. It showed me vanquishing any enemies that stood in my way but i still resist. Theres just to much to stay pure for to go with him. But with each passing night the temptation grows larger,\n\nHe has taken to torturing the people i love instead of useing the temptations of power and wealth. He told me they would all die, i..i tried to remain resistant but my resistance is crumbling. I fear after one more night i will be lost.\n\nI tried to tell my friends but they told my i was being foolish. They have stopped talking and visiting me. I sit here and cry until i fell an hand on my shoulder, I turn around and its him with his hand outstretched so i take it. He smiles opening a\n\nportal in the middle of the room. He puts his hand around my shoulder and leads me into the portal. But before he did he spoke three words \n\"I am Iblees\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Blackfoot Plague", "§bLelien", "Blackfoot Plague\n\n    by Lyuin Avern\n\n22nd of Grand Havest, 1461\nSymptoms:\n- Coughing\n- Blurred vision\n- Inability to clot blood\n- Internal acid burns\n- Haemorrahage of lungs\n\nThis has been dubbed 'Blackfoot plague'.\n\nThe Mali of Than’siol seek a cure, these have come in several forms.\nThe latest of which are thanhium pillars which attempt to kill plague particles.\nThe masls are somewhat effective, but not plague-proof.\n\n1st of Amber Cold, 1461\nIt has been discovered that strands of the plague can latch on to wheat crops, infected them and making ingestion of the infected bread to cause the plague. Furthermore, it has been adivsed and tried to see if this plague can\n\nnfect other food-stuffs.\nIn better news, Clerics have discovered they are able to rid the plague from its host. Thus creating an efficient method to remove plague from a host. However many Clerics are not immune themselves and thus choose not to involve\n\nthemselves in such matters.\n\nThe plague is both transmitted through consumption and through ingestion of air and infected foodstuffs.\n\n20th of Snow's Maiden, 1461\nA cure has been found! Discovered by the Valah withing the Fringe. This is an odd solution made up of several components including milk, carrot, tippen's root and other materials.\nThe filter-masks have proven useful and\n\nwith the cure having cleansed many of the people of their ailments, it is safe once more for our people.\n\n‘Blackfoot’ plague cure\n- A single gound carrot\n- A ground carrot of golden complexion\n- A single unit of Tippen’s root.\n- A measure of plague blood extracted from a victim of the plague\n- A single egg (remove the shell)\n\n- A single bucket of milk (should be fresh)\n- Oddly, a feather plucked from a chicken.\n- Several units of fertilizer", ""),
        StaticBook("Armor-Keeper", "§bWilliam Armor-Keeper", "I was raised as a blacksmith. Sometimes I would even work with my dad on swords and armor. He needed all the help he could get. A war was breaking out, and Supply And Demand was in action. FOr years, my dad and I would make the finest armor pieces you\n\ncould ever emagine. That is why we had the last name of Armor-keeper. But there were more things in my life then forging tools and weapons. My mom was a baker, and a skilled one at it. After we had all the tools and armor we needed for the day, my mom and\n\nI made the finest cake in the kingdom. It was a great time. But soon after the celebration of finishing all the armor we needed, the war approached. The northerners struck first, right at our city. Building were burned, and lots of peoples life hard work\n\nwas gone in a heart beat. We had to evacuate.\n   We packed everything we could and headed out. We raced for the mountains, hoping that the battle didn't stretch that far. The journey took many days, but we finally\n\ngot away from it all. As we thought we ere safe, a patrol came in. But as we looked closer, they had our Harold on it! We raced to them calling for help. Then I went pale. A soldier had unsleashed his word at my mom and impaled here with the mighty blade.\n\nI was so shocked, I couldn't move. But tahts when my dad Jumped at me and shoved me down the mountian with all of his strength. I was rolling, faster than any steed. Then everything went black. \n    I wake up in a home I have never seen befor. An old\n\nhouse. With rotting walls and empty shelvs. The only things there were some food and medicine. An old man walks in from the door on my right. \"You are as good as new now that I fixed you up. Your head will take a few days to heal. Say, why is a young lad\n\nlike you out here by yourself?\" \"Well it is not exactly my falt. I didn't mean to get here you know. I think all 12-year-olds should know not to be out wandering in a middle of a war.\" I exclaimed. \"Just asking. You dont have to make a deal out if it.\"\n\n\"Well I have to go now. I might visit you again.\" \"Good luck!\" He shouted back as I left. Well, I didnt have a forge to make armor to sell or a cooking pot to make bread in, so I found my perfession in stealing things. After a few months I started looking\n\nback at my life. All the way people were helping me, risking there lives and time to help me. To let me live on. And I have been repaying them in a wrong way. So I decided to pay them back. But that didnt work out. Well, you see, I had a 500 minas\n\nbounty on my head. I was chaced out of the city and was on the run for several days. After a week or two, I made it to a place called Athera. I was safe there. I was half starved to death when I got to the cloud temple. The monks there kept me there and\n\neducated me the best they could. And that is how I ended up here. Writing books, selling bread to pay off my house loan. Living in a 3x5 house on a farm. You dont have to take the turn I did. I wrote this book to warn you about the dangers in life.\n\nStealing wont get you anywhere. Frends will be by you in any situation. Money will run out evenually. Choose carefully. There are no retakes. Make your adventure in the LOTC the best you can make it.", ""),
        StaticBook("L1: Mori'Quessir", "§bAthe'lor", "I had known of the existence of the Mori’Quessir in Asulon, yet it was not until after the fact that I was informed of the language they had spoken, unlike any other. As one who delves into Lexicology on a regular basis and prides himself in being-\n\nable to speak many languages, I sought the want to learn their language as well. I found it necessary to learn what I could about the race as a whole, aside from only studying the language.\n\nUpon scouring libraries and shops for tomes on the subject, I managed to find very few, but enough to sate my hunger nonetheless. I learned of a Deity they worshipped called Nemiisae from a poem I had bought, and of the Mori’s affinity-\n\nor closeness with spiders. I am not sure if it is correct for me to use the past tense when speaking of the Mori for they may still be alive, but for the sake of this minor introduction I hope the reader will condone it.\n\nThe Mori’s society was matriarchal, in the way that women had power over men and were allowed to have multiple slaves. After managing to track down a man who was once a slave to the Mori’Quessir, we came to the agreement that he-\n\nwould teach the language to me. I will include very basic words on the following pages, accompanied by three full sentences. If all words are memorized and an individual wishes to learn more, they are welcome to confront the author on the subject.\n\nUsstan = I/myself\nUssta = my\nL' = the\nKaas = name\nZhah = is\nXanalress = language\nTlun = am\nAglla = trying\nUlu = to\nScrea = learn\nY'sik = rather\n\nXull = difficult\nXal = may\nNaut = not\nTelanth = say\nWiles = words\nListrane = properly\nJhal = but\nShlu'ta = can\nInbau = get\nWun = in\nOl = it\n\nSevir = leave\nXuz = end\nElgg = kill\n\nVendui ussta kaas zhah Izier. \n=\nHello, my name is Izier.\n\nL'xanalress Usstan tlun aglla ulu screa zhah y'sik xull.\n=\nThe language I am trying to learn is rather difficult.\n\nUsstan xal naut telanth l'wiles listrane jhal Usstan shlu'ta inbau ol wun l'xuz.\n=\nI may not say the words properly but I can get it in the end.\n\nBy this time the reader may have noticed that the original, seperate words were put into an order very similiar to the sentences themselves. This was the intention. The language of the Mori'Quessir is structured extremely similiarly to common, to the\n\nextent that translated Mori words in the same exact order can probably be read aloud in common as well, retainaing the sentence's integrity. \n\nThis is all I have for you, o' pages of mine. Rest sweetly until you are awoken. \n\n-Athe'lor", ""),
        StaticBook("Trial of Imarssa", "§bAsul'athri Parir'tailyu", "Imarssa Sillonaine is hereby charged with attempted murder, assault and battery, and extreme insubordination in regards to Elsillumiran, as well as letting in the unscrupulant ata and avernan. Pariran'tir include Elwyn, Braxus Ni'leya, and Mediliyur.\n\nElwyn begins questioning. First question: How do you plead to the list of charges?\n\nImarssa: Not guilty, except for that of insubordination.\n\nElwyn asks Ibar Izalith, witness whom alleged that she had made an\n\nattempt to kill him, as to how many witnesses he had. He answered one, being Earendur. She then asked him to recount his story.\n\nIbar: She came to me sword drawn, saying they needed to chat. She advances towards him, but stops when Earendur leaves the\n\ninn. She stops, and says, \"It's a shame he arrived.\" He inquired as to whether she had meant to kill him, to which she said, \"Perhaps next time.\"\n\nElwyn asks Imarssa to make defence. Ibar interrupts, withdraws claim as to the Sohaer having issued the\n\ncommand to Imarssa. Begins directly slandering Elsohaer, Elwyn silences him. Imarssa begins.\n\nImarssa: I approached Ibar, fully armoured, and told him I wished to speak privately. He refused, and I inssisted, and then Earendur came out to\n\nsay he wished to speak with me. Before Ibar left, he stated that he believed me to have intention of killing him. I responded with a sarcastic \"Definitely.\"\n\nElwyn asks her as to what question she wishd to ask. Imarssa replied that she had wished to take\n\nlessons for elmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya. Elwyn asks why this would require the unsheathing of a sword. Imarssa replies that it was the entire time sheathed.\n\nBraxus begins line of questioning.\n\nBraxus: How many\n\ntimes have you been a citizen, and how many times have you been expelled?\n\nImarssa: Three and two respectively.\n\nMediliyur begins interrogation. She asks for a recount of her final crime, insubordination.\n\nImarssa begins recounting story.\n\nImarssa: I allowed Tarlok into elcihi after recieving word that he would exchange information on a possible coming attack in exchange for a chance to go through his purity trials.\n\nBraxus interjects, clarifying that these were against his direct orders. Interrogation continus.\n\nMediliyur: Was this action cleared with any official, such as oem'Medi'ir?\n\nImarssa: Tarlok admitted to having no\n\ntrue information and was hoping that I would play along, as he believes me still his sister. When he entered, I moved to apprehend him against Braxus' orders, as he is a fire evocationist. I was attempting to stop him from connecting to the void in\n\nbreaking his concentration through pain. After an extended amount of warning from Braxus, I removed him from elcihi.\n\nPresider Okarir'tir Asul'athri requests that they reach a verdict. Elwyn request for time for discussion,\n\nrequest was granted. Three Pariran'tir parlay quietly, attempting to reach their verdicts.\n\nVerdict is reached.\n\nBraxus names the accused guilty, as does Mediliyur and Elwyn Punishment is noted to be\n\nbanishment and branding, with no chance of appeal or return.", ""),
        StaticBook("Etiquette Guide", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "A Guide to\n   Proper Social\n     Etiquette\n  \n   by Lucion Sullas\n\nI have been asked on a number of occasions upon the \"proper\" way of acting when in the presence of fellow citizens. Not that I wish to presume my compatriots have terribly poor manners (though many could perhaps use advice) I shall regardless outline\n\nthe proper etiquette taught to me by my family. Should the citizenry be interested in such things, then do please read on.\n\nI shall no offer explanation for \"why\" to do such. Merely that I find it pleasant, as should anyone.\n\n-One's Attire-\nA Mali'aheral's outfit should be clean, devoid of creases, and be of a fine quality. Avoid garish, bright colours that would attract pointless attention. Be a beacon through your words and mind, rather than the hue of your under-shirt.\n\nAlways wear an outfit that is tasteful to the eye. Though there are outfits with smaller amounts of material that compliment its wearer's natural perfection, showing unnecessary skin speaks poorly of your character, and may mark you as one of ill-repute.\n\nWhen wearing a long-coat, always be sure to position the bottom hems carefully when sitting down upon a chair, a stool, or the ground. The material can become easily crushed, and create dreadful creases.\n\nWhen dressed in full robes, be sure to sit straight on your chair. The cloth located upon one's sternum is highly likely to crush when leaning forward, so take special care to smooth the material whilst sitting for long periods.\n\n-One's Posture-\nNever slouch under any circumstance in public. Slouching implies weariness, and looking weary around others may give them the impression that you find their presence tiring. Should I have to explain why such a thing tends to reflect\n\npoorly on your reputation, I feel you should simply close this book now.\n\n-One's Voice-\nAlways speak clearly with precise annunciation. A fiercely exaggerated \"r\" does nothing to endear yourself to you compatriots. \n\nThere is nothing more dismal than a Mali'aheral who mumbles. Worse still,\n\none who speaks with awful colloquialisms (Example, \"Aye,\" \"Nay,\" \"Milord,\" \"Milady,\") is similar to that of a dove braying like a donkey. \n\nRefrain from filthy languages as often as possible. The Uruk tongue, though it may have its uses in\n\ncommunication with those beasts, should be avoided during social gatherings. So too, should any foul words native to the common tongue (I shall no write them here, as it is a public book, after all). Speaking as a brute is but the first step to being a\n\nbrute.\n\n-One's Habits-\nDo not pick at your features when in the presence of your fellows. An itch upon ones ear may be scratched, certainly, but an irritation in the nose must wait until privacy may be found.\n\nAlways cough or sneeze into a handkerchief, or if one is not available, away from the table/direction of your colleagues. Illness spreads in the air, as well as the body, and others may avoid you should you not have a way of keeping your expulsions\n\ncontained. Should you feel the need for flatulence, excuse yourself from the vicinity.\n\nNever smoke or chew tobacco; it dirties the lungs, fouls the air, and stains the robes. Those who do such are naturally filthy, and their stench is\n\ndeplorable. Be mindful of your fellow citizens, and respect their nostrils.\n\nOne should always carry a handkerchief, or at least a clean length of cloth, to wipe away any grime that should get upon your clothes. Better yet, carry a second to\n\noffer a compatriot who is otherwise handkerchief-impaired.\n\n-One's Courtesy-\nShould a citizen be walking towards a gate behind you, be sure to open it for them if they intend to go forth themselves. The same idea extends to that of doorways, however, one should offer entrance to the one behind first.\n\nShould you observe fellow residents caught in the rain, it is polite to offer them sanctuary from the elements until they pass over. You yourself would not wish to be sodden, and thus extending that courtesy is polite.\n\nWhen you have a guest within your home, be sure to first offer them a refreshment of some sort. If none is to be had, then offer food. If there is a lack of both, be sure to apologise for your poor housekeeping.\n\nAlways ask permission to sit at another's table. As a guest in a home, you should never presume that you have any right to be seated in the presence of another. Furthermore, always request permission to leave, once conversation or purpose has been\n\nexhausted. Should you be seated at a public table, then consider the ones seated at it before you the \"owners\" of the space and the rules may be applied appropriately.\n\n-One's Pleasantries-\nWhen greeting a fellow citizen, a simple \"karin'ayla\" is sufficiently polite for strangers. However, those closer to you, or those worthy of praise, should be entitled to more elaborate forms of greetings. A short\n\nbow towards a respectable fellow is reasonable enough, as well as a quick arm gesture (example, touching one's chest, and extending your arm outwards) would be sufficient still. \n\nCombining all three is polite in all situations without any chance\n\nof insult.\n\nWhen retiring from conversation, a simple \"Van'ayla\" combined with the bow and gesture is excellent indeed.\n\nAddressing your fellow citizens by name is tasteful, and it is always best to seek\n\nout their name at the beginning of every conversation. Should you not recall another's name, inquire of it quickly to avoid further embarrassment. \n\nThe statement \"maehr'sae hiylun'ehya\" is in itself a blessing, and may\n\nbe used as both a delightful \"hello,\" or \"goodbye.\" However, to not return this blessing upon receiving it is -extremely- rude. How could you not return such a sentiment? Are you truly so devoid of eloquence that you dare not embarrass others with your\n\nfoul pronunciation? It is truly outrageous.\n\nKnow these words, and use their advice. The people of this city will be far better for it.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fool's diary", "§bFool", "Day 1\nDear diary,\nSo many things have happend in this land ever since i got here. First i was in search of my father, who is a wood elf. i got captured by an orc and i was sold to be a slave. the lady who bought me kind of set me free but im still\n\nher maid. i was looking for work and an elf called Sonoren Klaren recruited me to crimson heart. i got new robes and everything! (still get to keep my old robe hood!) we are preparing to set up a\nhomestead.\n\nDay 2\nMr. Klaren said to explore our new land. I found a little farm house and a little town area. lets hope we can repair it soon... im straving to death! The pain! the pain!\n\nDay 3\ni cannot find anyone and im afraid im lost. for now im heading back to the heart of the forest. I cannot find the sacred pillar any wear... i was starving to death but the pain went away and im now in Crimson Hearth!\n\nDay 4\nIm starting to farm. My guild mates are starting to find the \"Big House\" and more and more people start to join us!\n\nDay 5\n   Im writing this in class beacuse im board. Demons the darkest part of my childhood. They killed my ansestors and my beloved pet crow Nutmeg. Celestia is my hero beacuse she burned the Demon Lords in an endless pit of fire.\n\nDay 6\n   I left Crimson Hearth. I was finding my lifestyle there quite boring. Well time to look for a new nation/town/city/guild.It has been ages of me looking around and i cant find any nation/town/city/guild to join. Ive asked a few weird\n\npeople were a nation/town/city/guild is but they couldnt give me one. one girl said she tasted orc skin. she said it tasted salty. that was very weird. I found the high elf city and joined it! yay!!! I learned llir means friend! so i can kinda talk elven.", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Notebook", "§b-", "*An old notebook of sorts*\n\nDay 8: \nAlas, it seems to be all labor and no fruit! I have experimented with the greatest reagents I could find: Dragon bone, entire fins of Hydra, and the beaks of Hippogryphs! It seems to be a wild goose chase!\n\nEverytime I try to incorporate these greater reagents into anything, I simply end up with overly efficient healing potions. BAH! I’ve taken to simply using these failed attempts at the Panacea for creating more homunculi… strange, alien homunculi.\n\nThey seem to mock me. I fear them, I had my manservant lock them into the basement while they were still confused in the beginning moments of their creations.\n\nDay 14:\n    More and more failed attempts. This is ridiculous. I use more powerful reagents, yet they are so powerful that now I cannot produce potions anymore… just fiends and deviants.\n\nThey cram every single cell and cranny of this blasted mansion. I hear their screams of agony, they mutters and senseless murmurs. I cannot sleep.\n\nDay 20:\n    Finally! A revelation! It turns out that the more organic reagents I use, the more impure the potion is! This is why those pesky homunculi kept on appearing.\n\nIf I perhaps use a different base, I can create potions instead of these blasted fiends. I had a lot of them burned and buried out in the crypts. I kept the deviants.\n\nThey took too much money and too much precious reagents that could have had a better use.\n\nDay 21:\n    Almost immediate success! I could not sleep last night for my anticipation kept on making me get out of bed. I labored all night, and finally got a potion:\n\na beautiful golden liquid that almost pulses with light! It looks angelic… perhaps I have dispelled this myth!\n\nForget getting rich: my name will go down in history as the Alchemist who discovered the Panacea! I will be showered with gifts by every nation!\n\nI will keep this recipe secret, however. Money is not such a bad thing after all… and humans would be thirsting after this potion. Now, only to test it.\n\nDay 23:\n    As I write this, I contemplate on testing this potion out on my manservant. I am worried, however. I am waiting for the tea to finish boiling… and I endeavour with myself to decide whether I should slip some of this brew into the tea or not.\n\nNo, that it preposterous! I cannot afford to harm anyone! What if this potion is just a homunculizing tool? What if it turns Remy into one of those blasted Dopplegangers my colleagues have talked about?!\n\nI need to find something to test this potion on… oh, cursed fate! For every thing I resolve, another problem has to arise!", ""),
        StaticBook("L2: Kharajyr", "§bAthe'lor", "Beneath the alias of Ja’Sirah was one accepted into the Kharajyr community, and became able to learn first-hand about their culture, language, and way of life. As might be assumed, an individual living amongst the Kharajyr would pick up the dialect-\n\nfairly quickly after having heard it spoken throughout the day, day after day. Ergo, I was able to master the Kharajyrian dialect before any other ‘apes’ (What the Kharajyr called non-Kharajyr), and have found myself able to still speak it to-\n\nthis day regardless of body. You may ask how an Elf managed to disguise himself as a Kharajyr and remain under this guise without being discovered, but that is for another book entirely.\n\nAll Kharajyr are born and raised to speak with their natural accent, however it is believed that a Kharajyr can speak the Common tongue properly through mere exercise. Conversely, an Elf can learn to speak with a Kharajyr accent.\n\nThe following page contains simple Kharajyrian words that generally sound the same spoken aloud as they are read.\n\nSa'vi = hello\nMul'ta = thank you\nTra'kul = you're welcome\n\nPatta = father\nMunna = mother\nMetz'al = life mate\nPer = son\nPer'ta = brother\nMaut = daughter\nMau'na = sister\n\nRarely will a Kharajyr speak words more advanced than these, and they will merely speak Common, though accented. However, it is believed the Kharajyr had an entire language to themselves at one point which I will not claim any mastery over.\n\nHowever, I will share what few words and phrases I happen to know.\n\nSo hy'sa ec…\n=\nmy name is…\n\nQuin hy'sa ec?\n=\nwhat is your name?\n\nFre'ma dra feht p'mufc, dra Kha' nasyeh cd'nuhk.\n=\nwhile the wind blows, the Kha stay strong.\n\nThe Kharajyrian accent is what distinguishes how the Kharajyr speak related to other races. Though, put simply, all Kharajyr could speak with slightly different accents, and not many would be able to notice. I will write a few sentences-\n\nin the accent I acquired, and if you are diligent and persistent enough you may give birth to your own. An important note to keep in mind is that all Kharajyr speak in the third-person, and this is quite unique to the language.\n\nHello, how are you today?\n=\nsa’vi, haw awr yu’ssah tu’day?\n\nI am very good, thank you.\n=\nja’sirah ees ver’ray guut, mul’ta.\n\nWhat on Athera do you think you’re doing?\n=\nwhut’tah awn Aw’ther’ah du yoo theenk yu awr du’ang?\n\nDirty humans are everywhere, I wish they would go away.\n=\nder’tay aypes awr ef’ree’way’awr, ja’sirah weeshess thay wood gu aw’ay.\n\nThis book should be detailed enough for any intellectual to comprehend, take the knowledge from, and use to be able to speak with a Kharajyr accent. I now retire this tome to the shelf, to be put to good use.\n\n-Athe’lor", ""),
        StaticBook("Regents o'Anthos", "RedBench", "Common Alchemy Regents of Anthos\n\nBy Gauldrim Irongut\n\nName: Orcs Braid (Stick)\nSymbol: Fire (Weak)\nDescription: A rope like plant that grows in sewers and drains. Easy to obtain but not very useful. Has the characteristics of a rope.\n\nName: Singed Kha (Leaves)\nSymbol: Fire (Medium)\nDescription: A useful regent the Singed Kha has the scent of burning Kha hair as well as the leaves sharing similar texture to that of a Kha's pelt. A large bush like plant of a bright vermillion colour.\n\nName: Blistering Toad (Red Mushroom)\nSymbol: Fire Symbol (strong)\nDesription: An ugly mushroom with a deep red hue it is found in places of great humidity and is very difficult to cultivate. Is a very rare and useful fire regent.\n\nName: Miners Helmet (Brown Mushroom)\nSymbol: Earth (Weak)\nDescripion: A large fleshy mushroom that grows in dark and deep caverns. Is poisonus and if one wishes to eat it must boil it for fifteen minutes before hand.\n\nName: Drilltongue (Vines) \nSymbol: Earth (Medium)\nDescription: A very strong and hardy plant that has been known to ingrain itself into stone. Has narotic effects if ingested, especially the buds.\n\nName: Bronze Dust (Clay)\nSymbol: Earth (Medium)\nDescription: An irritant that can be found in large veins of rock under the Earth. Found in mines it breaks off in chunks making it easy to move. Has a similar look to clay.\n\nName: Opal Scarab (None)\nSymbol: Earth (Strong)\nDescription: A beetle that can be found living and gorging on farmers crop. A pest but extremely useful and common. The beetle does have poison glands but the organs are useful.\n\nName: Wisp Breath (Vine)\nSymbol: Air (Strong)\nDescription: An almost transparent vine that grows from tree branches. This regent can be a substitute for cactus green and is found growing in underground caverns.\n\nName: Jokers Scum (Grass or Vines)\nSymbol: Water (Medium)\nDescription: A flesh eating plant that floats around in the deep sea. Eats fish and men alike and grows in 'colonies' almost. It secrets an acid that can be useful.\n\nName: Aqua Nymph (Glass)\nSymbol: Water (Strong)\nDescription: An extremely rare regent it is almost transparent and cannot be seen in running water. It is very delicate and should be treated with care", ""),
        StaticBook("Lean (Alchemic)", "§bGrim'aeldus", "The origins of Lean or more commonly known as Purple Drink (Purple Drank if you’re of Southeron dialect) precede man himself according to the legend of Lawrence Lean.\n\nBack in the First Era a would-be herbalist was delving far into the reaches of Aegis looking to change the face of the herbal game forever. It was after thirty years of searching that his thirst was quenched, he had discovered the Chrono root.\n\nIt glowed when he unearthed it on accident on a hot day in the wastes. Shocking and magnificent he gently uncovered it without severing it from its host. A perfect extraction was followed by mass excavation.\n\nBefore too long Lawrence Lean had a nice stockpile of Chrono and made preparations to head back to the heartland of Aegis to share his findings.\n\nUpon a relatively short trip back to his lab the herb fiend got to work. Mashing, grinding, and boiling Lean went wild trying to find a use for his life’s work.\n\nIt was in a workplace rage that he discovered the Chrono root actually grew out of root form and created a dense bush of sweetly scented buds and flowers.\n\nWhen a mature plant’s roots are grinded and boiled in cheesecloth Lawrence Lean found himself with a powerful elixir. It’s effects are known to slow down perceived time in the user’s mind and induce an intense warped effect about the user.\n\nWhen dried out the buds made for great pipe tobacco substitute. Chrono’s use as a smokable remedy has recently been made famous by Hansetians, notably avid Chrono user the late Darius “Lion”.\n\nLawrence Lean proclaims his elixir Lean to be the key to immortality. It has been described as a mixture that looks like the deep heavens in color and enthralling nature when staring directly into a fresh mug of Lean.\n\nAfter Note:\n\nTexts recovered from a Human library prior to it's closure. Original texts indicate the author was one Lion III of the Holy Oren Empire from the era of Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Simple Cures", "§bGili Strongbrow", "Basic Healing\n\nCommon cold: Steep tea leaves in boiling water, and add sugar and citrus. The cleansing smell of the tea will purify the throat and lungs.\n\n\n\nMinor cuts: Apply soft damp wool to stop the bleeding, then place clean green slime over the wound. Cover with dry wool to aid healing. Remove after three days.\n\n\n\nBroken bones, especially limbs: Lay the patient flat on the ground. Make a splint using two strong sticks and some wool wrapped tightly around the appendage. If the bone sticks out from the skin, bind it as on page 2.\n\n\n\nHeadache: Brew a strong tea, and add one drop of oil made from poppy seeds. Failing that, inhale steam from boiling water for no longer than fifteen minutes.\n\n\n\nFever: Ensure the patient is in a cool, dry environment. If they become distressed, bathe their forehead with cold water to bring down the temperature. Feed them only apples or other fruit, and make sure they drink water.\n\n\n\nRashes on skin: Apply strong apple beer to the affected area. Cactus juice will also work to prevent spreading and further irritation of the skin.\n\n\n\nPoisoning: To draw out the poison from a cut or bite, suck the blood from it and spit it out immediately. If the poison has been eaten, drink plenty of milk to purify the stomach.\n\n\n\nFainting: If someone has fainted, they will awaken within 5 minutes with no knowledge of what happened. Keep them calm during this time. If someone has been knocked unconscious, treat the headwound with water and ice in a cloth.\n\n\n\nBruising: Apply damp wool on top of the affected area, and press ice onto the wool to cool the skin. Do this every day for 5 days. The bruises should be gone within a week.\n\n\n\nVomiting: If the patient is vomiting profusely, ensure they drink lots of water. Do not allow them to eat rich food or drink milk as this will worsen their condition. Plain bread or potato is suitable. The nausea will fade within a week.", ""),
        StaticBook("Anti-Contagion", "§bLelien", "Anti-Contagion\n  Filtration Mask\n     Guidebook\n\n       by Mirtok\n\nThank you for accepting your very own anti-contagion filtration mask, through this handbook you will learn all the important functions and procedures for operating and effectively using your mask. By the order of the Hochmeister in hopes to combat the\n\nrising infectious ailments, every Hanseti citizen is issued their own filtration mask for safety.\n\nSafety Tips\n\n1) Never misplace or lose your mask, though the Hochmeister cares deeply for your safety, he will not be able to give out spare masks to careless people.\n\n2) Never share your mask, to prevent the spread of the illness the Hochmeister urges all mask users to stay with their own mask no matter the circumstances.\n\n3) Maintain your mask, keeping your mask in proper order at full upkeep will prevent incidences of breaks or breaches in your mask’s special protective filtration and sealant systems.\n\n4) Use filters to their fullest, each few years the Hochmeister will distribute new filters for your masks but until then you must ration off what you have, this will not only test your ability to be responsible of your life, but to prove you have what it\n\ntakes to survive in a hazardous world.\n\nPreparing your Mask\nUpon receiving your mask, it is a good idea to become acquainted with how it works and how to properly use it to fend off infective agents of death.\n\nFirstly, it is a good idea to make sure your filters are in place and secure\n\nalong both sides of the mask.\n\nUnder the eye sockets of the masks should be two metal containers with 3 clip secure locks located on the circumference of each capsule. Inside you can see the several layers of filters and spinning mechanism that make\n\nup the filtration system. Do refrain from tinkering with the delicate parts and only manipulate the filters. Once assured that the filters fit snuggly in their respective areas we can make to making sure there are no cracks in the mask. We are unsure as\n\nto how the infection is spread and therefore it is important to count for all possible biological entries into the body. First examine the two large eye sockets and lenses on the front of the mask. Also scan along the main folds and seams of the mask to\n\nmake sure no loose strings or openings are present. Finally, make sure the center piece where each tube leading from the two filter capsules is not loose or emitting a rattling noise when shook. Be sure to be extra careful when checking for breaches as\n\na single hole can mean the difference between life or death.\n\nReplacing Filters\nTo replace a filter, you must first unlatch the lid to the two filtration capsules. Once the interior is exposed, carefully turn the filter pads until a hard click is heard above the smaller clicking during turning. When heard, the\n\nthe pads should slightly elevate themselves into a popping motion and then should be ready for removal. Replacement works in the opposite fashion, place the new ones in the direction of the painted arrows and turn when the resistance is felt.\n\nSeveral clicks should be heard until a final snap indicates its in place. Close the capsule and move to the next one.\n\nUsing your Mask\nWhen your situation calls for you to use your mask, you must follow a few simple steps to ensure your maximum safety in the face of an infective area. First loosen all of the straps along the back and front of the mask. Then place the\n\nloose mask over your head and position the eye sockets for your preferred viewing.\n\nWhen ready, slowly tighten each strap until the strapped area feels tight and snug over your head. It is very important to maintain a tight fit but also to keep the mask\n\nfrom cutting off blood flow to your mask and face as such will prompt discomfort and compel you to adjust the mask. When all straps have been secured, turn the small dial located on the front of your mask where the capsule tubes meet until you hear a\n\nsmall rush of air., When all these are done, you should have achieved maximum anti-contagion safety.\n\nBreaching/Cracks\nIn the event of a breach or crack in your mask, it is advised by the Hochmeister to quickly remove yourself from the jeopardizing area and seek cover and solitude from any other contact with others. The Hochmeister then urges you to\n\nremove the filter pads from your filtration capsules and attempt to apply them over your nose and mouth if no other repair methods are successful on the damaged mask.\n\nGood luck out there and may Celestia keep this tragedy from our frozen lands.", ""),
        StaticBook("ScientificMethod", "§bAnnabella", "The Basic Scientific Procedure\n\nBy: Arrabella\n\n-Ask a question.\nthere is litterally no point in attempting an experiment if you dont know what you even want.\n\n-Do Background research. Make sure your experiment has not already been done, also find similar things that have been done to base your hypothesis on.\n\n-Construct a Hypothesis. Begin to form what you believe will happen when you do you experiment.\n\n-Analyze your data and draw a conclusion. It is important to fill out every detail at this point.\n\nHelpful tips:\nDo NOT tamper with results because you wanted another result. If you do this, you are not a scientist. You are a liar. \nDo share your results with others so they may also learn. \nMake sure your experiment is a 'Fair test'. A fair test--\n\noccurs when you change only one variable and keep all other conditions the same.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nThis is a simplified way of explaining how to do an experiment properly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lartius' Diary", "§bLartius", "The Diary of:\nJohn Lartius Fredfor\n------------------\nEntry one:\n1st of The Grand Harvest, 1469.\n\nToday I finally got the materials to make my navigation tools for the telescope, a compass and a clock. They look mighty fine.\n\nHowever I'm still uncertain of what the night sky actually does. Aris showed me a crystal which seemed to project the nightsky in it. However it doesn't look familiar. Odd. Looking forward to the Halfling Party.\n-------------------\n\nEntry two: 11th of The Grand Harvest,  1469\n\nToday was quite the day actually. Participated in the Halfling Festival, pig riding occured. Quite the lovely fellas. So light spirited and good at heart. Later on I went on an adventure with Ambros. There\n\nare many secrets to this realm of Athera that we do not yet know of. Something with Druids and Mages working together. Quite odd. Purple circle was it called. There are many mysteries in this. Not sure if I get the opportunity to study it however.\n-------\n\nEntry Three:  4th of Sun's Smile, 1469.\n\nIt seems that I was wrong. Or well. My curiosity took over and I went to visit Gi'Garun. I told him about The Purple Circle and both our memories opened up to old stories we had once read.  Back in\n\nAncient times in Aegis within Laurelin a portal to the Nether had opened. In an effort to close this both Mages and Druids had worked together to close it. However as we started to talk about this Gi'Garun mentioned the Chill giving huge double doors that\n\nare stationed underground in various places across this land. I know of them as I found one when we exited the ships to here. As already knowing to me many have said this land may have been Aegis once and that those doors could contain Ibless. What\n\nGi'Garun however gave the thought of is that the \"Void\" like darkness that is at the edge of this realm could perhaps once have been Aegis. It is indeed odd that corruption spreads throughout the land for many miles and then suddenly stops. Something of\n\nCataclysmic events must have happened there once. This grows odder and odder at every step. Also recently saw both Selina and Blundermore within the same day. Extremely unusual. The Ascendeds must finally have started to reform. -----------\n\nEntry Four:  8th of The Amber Cold, 1469\n\nOnly a couple of days ago Aris and I planned what the field we were going to study should be cataloged under. \"Voidalogy.\" This is before we believe that the night sky formerly known as the Cosmos might indeed be-\n\n-The void. Interesting idea. Furthermore we discussed results of my data and work in the past regarding the shape of the world we live in or on. Haven't seen much from The Swords of Aeriel as of recently. My dear friend Xar seems to have gone missing. I\n\nshould try to relocate him as soon as possible. We need a strong rally guard for the followers of Aeriel should the rumors regarding Ibless being contained under our feet indeed be true. We must wait and see. PS: Finally got a prototype for my telescope\n\nready. It looks magnificent and offers much more control and fine adjusting than my previous telescopes. Can't wait to get it made for real.\n------------------\nEntry Five, 8th of The Deep Cold, 1469.\n\nToday The Adventure Group consisting of\n\nThorogh, Myrddin, Arkan and Linete finally found a proper place to set up their inn. With help from me of course. But it surely is their victory. I look forward to see it finished.\n-------------------Entry Six,  24th of The Snow's Maiden. 1470\n\nThe Weary Travellers Inn at portland is now close to completion. What a ride. It've been tough especially considering The Grand Architect does not like the building. However it is in my head the finest piece of building I've ever participated in making.\n\nFurthermore the idea that this is Aegis is continuing to bloom. The theory Gi'Garun proposed with The Abyss being were Aegis once was seems likely. Furthermore I've discovered that there is up to seven or nine of these chill giving doors. Quite terrifying\n\n!\n------------------\nEntry Seven, 9th of The Grand Harvest. 1472. \n\nTwo years since I last wrote in this old notebook.. Hmm.. But here I am. Well just last night we held the annual Wizards Gathering at the instit\n\nInstitute. Quite the blast actually, but I most say it ended rather abruptly after Mister Ambros decided he needed some sleep. Well that is that. I plan on soon travelling to Avalon once more, my last encounter with Mister Windraker was pleasant enough,\n\neven IF he isn't very talkative. Anyhow, the Scions have moved there you see. And I hear rumors from Naeri she have something big in the works. I hope it will turn out great, anything to help that old Lass. And Windraker and his pals too. Aye. I shall clo\n\nse this book and travel to Avalon. That must be The Adventure for the next few nights then. Farewell The Weary Travellers Inn. For now, at least.\n------------------\nEntry Eight, 2nd of The Deep Cold, 1475.\n\nAnd to Avalon I went, and here I am, sitting\n\njust outside the gates in The Weary Travelers Inn, and no. Avalon did not move to the Freeport, but the Weary Travelers Inn did. It's quite the lovely place, however I must say that I rarely see customers, but more than at the Freeport, so that's always\n\nsomething. The Scion order have broken up, but have been replaced by the KoA, Knights of Aeriel. I like the name better than the Scions to be quite honest, furthermore we're finally following a deity who surely can do good with our assistance. I fear for\n\nthe future. Iblees have been spotted in the Halls of Urguan and it will not take a long time before his minions, The Undead, will return to him.\n\nI hope Aeriel will guide us through this as she always has. Somehow... Evil always tends to find us. Odd.\n\n-------------------\nLast Entry\nThis books pages have steadily, but surely started to fill up.\n\nI'll end this diary here and begin on writing a new as soon as possible. Thanks for all pages and ink, you've helped me through tough times.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven LessonsIII", "§bKalenz Uradir", "New Elven\n     Lessons:\n     Volume 3\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\n\nTo conjugate verbs in elven one must note precisely what person is being referred to in the sentence. Then the verb is conjugated:\n-e - 1st sing\n-a - 2nd sing\n-e - 3rd sing\n-ae - 1st pl\n-an - 2nd pl\n-eyae - 3rd pl\n\nTo create past and future tenses is quite simple in elven. However, it takes specific forms depending on the time of day. For these two tenses the following four words are used:\n\nKarin'ento - Next sunrise\n\nKarin'ante - Last sunrise\n\nKer'ento - Next sunset\n\nKer'ante - Last sunset\n\nIf it is night at the time the elf refers to the past or present the two forms with the 'Ker' are used. If it is day at the time the elf refers to the past or present the two forms with 'Karin' are used. These endings are simply added on to the end\n\nof sentences to designate the tense. \n\nEx.: Kalenz iyathe (Kalenz thinks) becomes Kalenz iyathe ker'ante (Kalenz thought). Assuming the time in which it is spoken is the night.\n\nIn spoken elven, particularly more casual speech these endings are often shortened into the slang of karinto, karinte, keno and kente.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons II", "§bKalenz Uradir", "New Elven\n     Lessons:\n     Volume I\n\n  by Kalenz Uradir\n\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in Elven are as follows:\n\nKae - Me\nNae - You\nLae - He/Him\nHae - She/Her\nLye - We (used to speak of Elves, people or world)\n\nFor example the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (He fared well).\n\nIn addition to this, other good language supplements to anyone learning Elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be added to create further detail of form critical grammatical structures in a sentence.\n\nThe dash denotes location of seed word. Affixes and seed words are separated by an apostrophe.\n\nac- (aca-) - Honorific for accursedness\nah- (ahe-) - Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholar. Ex.: Ah'Lucion\nfi- - New or anew\n\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) - Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of a high military rank. Ex.: Cer'Silir\n-ante (-nte) - Last\n-ento (-nto) - Next\n-onn - From or born\nu- - Or\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive\n-ir - purpose\n\n-sae - The spreading, develpment or management\n-ii - diminuitive form\n\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("Salvus: Part 1", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The History\n     of Salvus:\n       Part 1\n\n      by N. Evitan\n\nThe history of Salvus starts with the Oren town of Winterfell. It was the most northern, recognized settlement of man and always had the reputation of being somewhat indepent. The reign over Winterfell was in the hands of the Perea Family, after the\n\nSheffields had control over all of Oren from them. Since Lord Pampo was mostly absent, his wife Lady Dawn Perea was solely in charge most of the time. She redefined Winterfell from an almost stronghold like town to a welcoming and careful community.\n\nLife was good there, but one fateful day the undead chowed cruelty and strength like never before and tained the capital of Oren, Al’Khazar. Winterfell was now separated from the rest of Oren, not only by state of mind, but also by a belt of death.\n\nSince the Undead claimed the north for themselves, it was only a matter of time until they would reach for winterfell. The citizens of Winterfell lived in this Solitude for nearly half a year. Then they came... Lead by the Undead called Vardak, who\n\nbrought pain and suffering to the many people in the Realm of Aegis, the undead hordes attacked. The citizens fought for their home, but there was nothing to gain, but death. Just as it seemed like every last soul was to be consumed by the evil beings the\n\nAscended Eruza appeared and managed to hold off the undead just long enough for the survivors to escape.\n\nThe loyal subjects, not willing to leave the side of Lady Dawn, were taken in by Dawn and found shelter in her youth home.\n\nThis place was later to be known as the Isle of Salvus.", ""),
        StaticBook("L5: The Blah", "§bAthe'lor", "Despite being an elf, for a long period of time this scholar was accepted in Krugmar and allowed to walk its sand dunes, speak with its people, and eventually become familiar with its language. It is my belief after years of study that the Uruk found-\n\nthemselves unable to speak Common properly (at least without tremendous effort, and those who could were deemed ‘Whitewashes’) and because of this, they found a need to create a more clear form of communication.\n\nWith this need, the Uruk butchered words in Common and created their own words to replace them. Because of their large, barbaric forms with tusks, orcs have difficulty saying most words and consequently they are mispronounced. The following pages-\n\nwill include all necessary words one must know to speak ‘Blah’ (another name for orc-speak) properly. All things aside, one could always argue that Blah is not proper in the first place but I digress.\n\nUg = hello\nThrom’ka = respectful greeting\nYub = yes\nNub = no\nGug’ye = goodbye\nLat = you\nMi = me\nRulg = thank you\nBlah = talk, speak\nGruk = understand\n\nBubhosh = great, large\nSnaga = slave\nNubhosh = small, bad\nKlomp = attack\nFlat = dead\nBlarg = home\nBruddah = friend, war nation orc\nSkah = curse word\nNubded = undead\n\nStowt = dwarf\nTwiggie = elf\nShara = human\nKitty = kharajyr\nAgh = and\nMojo = magic\nGoi = city\nAsh = one\nDub = two\nGahk = three\n\nUsing these words, all one has to do is speak with an Uruk accent which in truth is not all that difficult; it is probably easier to speak with an orc accent than a Kharajyr accent. When one of the prior words on the list is necessary in conversation, -\n\nall an individual has to do is substitute the orc word in (and there are not that many). Chances are learning the language will be rather useless to the reader regardless of mastery, as orcs will probably grow upset if you speak it.\n\nThe final and perhaps most useless book of my volumed language collection is finished. May it sit happily with its brothers and sisters, until the day comes when one can make use of it.\n\n-Athe’lor", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Bezerkers", "§bDurza Volkihar", "The Orcs of the desert are bezerking abominations.They crave war and fighting. the majority of fights i have been in and have witnessed have been created by orcs.They do not speak a normal tounge.Their tounge isnt as elegant as the elfs or a simple as the\n\nmen of oren or the dwarves.Their language is called the blah.The blah shouldnt even be considered a language at all, it is just a series of grunts and guttaral sounds.They often resort to eating people to stop there endless hunger for meat and blood.\n\nThere are three types of Orcs:\n\nThe Uruk: The Uruk is the most common of the orcish blood.They have a very limited volcabulary and a limted brain size.They are very skilled in combat though.\n\nThe Goblin: The goblin is considered the smartest of the race of orcs but the weakest and smallest. What they lack in braun they make up for in brain size and wit.\n\nThe Olog: The Olog is the strongest and powerful of all the orc's. They are the dumbest of all the orc's. They do not possess the ability to think. They are mindless beasts built for one pupose, war\n\nIt is obvious that the orcs are a race that only cares about war. The only execption for that is the goblins who would rather tinker with devices than fight every creature they come across. The word negotiate is not in their vocabulary.\n\nIf you share these views come find me.\n\n\n[!] A red eagle is drawn here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Punishment II", "§bArchmage Crumena", "The Punishment of Hubris II\n\nWhat Nemiisae did not realize was that the portal had only been closed to prevent their leaving. The portal within the Verge to this new land was still open to anyone who could discover it. And discovered it was. The Dwarves were first to uncover\n\nthe portal into the Verge, as the first group to find it mined into the cavern it had been hidden in. Seeing the notes left behind by Nemiisae, they sent one dwarf ahead to try and locate the portal inside the Verge. He returned shortly, proclaiming\n\nthe glory of the land he saw reflected in the portal’s visage! Mountains, gold, diamonds, as far as the eye could see! It was right there, a short walk away! A world of their own, which they could run as they like, without having to share it with\n\nanyone! The Dwarves quickly made a decision to gather their families and things and venture through. Within the day, they were ready to venture to the Verge and then towards their new land. Greedily, they decided they had to prevent others\n\nfrom discovering this mystical, resource rich land. Using good, old fashioned Dwarven ingenuity, they collapsed the tunnel they had accidentally discovered the portal via, then quickly passed through. They quickly found the portal\n\ninside the Verge leading to this mystical new land and pass through that as well. And again, another group had fallen for the trap. The portal was closed behind them, so there was no place left to go but forward. They ventured into the\n\nland, ready to settle it and hoping to thrive. But within the next half of a millenia, they had all perished to the cursed land and it’s terrors…creatures or otherwise. All they left behind was skeletons, of their homes and of themselves.\n\n\nAbove ground, as the tunnel to the cavern shifted and collapsed, a huge crevice formed in the landscape. It had not been there the day before and as a Human merchant group passed the area they began to wonder what had caused such a\n\ncrevice. One of them suggested it may have been a tomb, full of riches. Eager to investigate, the Humans spent the next month digging down into the ground, following the slant of the crevice and eventually discovering the cavern which\n\nhoused the portal to the Verge. The Humans too spied the notes and messages Nemiisae had left behind, promising them a land free from Iblees’ curse, free for the taking! Their short lifespans would be gone and they would be immortal like their cousins!\n\nThe merchants quickly climbed back to the surface, cutting down the branches of nearby trees to cover the entrance to the land. They all quickly traveled to their homes, to fetch their families and supplies in order to settle this new land. The came\n\nback less than a week later, descending into the Cavern, through the Verge and into the new world. But they too fell into the trap. The Portal was closed behind them and they had no place left to go but forward. They ventured out to settle these new\n\nlands with their families. But within the next half of a Millenia, the majority of them had perished to the cursed land and it’s terrors. They were not made immortal as they had hoped, but rather had even shorter lifespans than usual. They became\n\ninbred, sick, ill, and in the end all they left behind were shadows of their former selves, a slow, stupid race incapable of complex thought and cursed by maladies and deformities.\nAfter the Humans had placed tree branches to cover the entrance to\n\nthe Cavern, a group of Elves ventured into that area, hearing the call of the wounded trees. They discovered the branches and removed them, wondering what foul creature had despoiled the trees in such a way and for what cause. Into\n\nthe cavern they ventured, discovering the notes from Nemiisae and the portal to the Verge. This group did not go back for more, though more would come later, as they were immediately forced through. Running from a threat, they\n\nentered the Verge and discovered the portal to the new world. Fleeing still, they had no choice but to enter. They too fell into this trap, the portal closed behind them, no way back, though they would only find this out after returning later to\n\ninvestigate. For now, they still had running to do. Immortal though they were, this land was still rife with danger. Forced to settle in it, the Elves would follow in the footsteps of their cousins, perishing within this strange lands within half a\n\nMillenia. In these lands they were susceptible not just to the terrors, but also their own curse. Far more infertile than they were in their original lands, they died out merely due to a lack of numbers. While some of them eventually interbred with\n\nNemiisae’s children, those who refused would only gain numbers through other poor fools coming through the portal. In this way the Elves too, were trapped.\nWhen the Elves first found the broken and disturbed trees as well as the secret\n\nthey hid, they did not realize they were being hunted. Following them from Malinor had been an Orc hunting party, searching for slaves, meat, or just a bit of violent fun. The Orcs assaulted the Elves at the entrance to the crevice, and\n\nhaving no other way to go, the Elves immediately fled into the Crevice and down into the Cavern. The Orcs gave chase, of course, following them through the Verge and the next portal, into the new world. The Elves had gotten ahead, fleeing to the\n\nnearest forests they could find. In the thick cover, the Orcs lost sight of them. They began to investigate the land as their cousins had. They settled, adventured, and fought. Fighting was what they were good at and they were much better\n\nequipped for the trip into this new world, to face the terrors that haunted it. But their own aggression killed them in the end. They perished at the hands of beasts, monsters they should have known they would never defeat, at least not in totality.\n\nWithin a half of a Millenia, the Orcs too were extinct, leaving behind only the skeletal ruins of their previous homes and their old enemies they had died out battling.\n\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed, 1473.\nTo be continued in the third volume.\n[Credit to TehLulu for the writing itself.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C6", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n\n      Chapter Six\n     The Lore Book\n\n“Wait.” I said. “How can you be part of the Omira. They died long ago.” \n\n“Not all of them.” Said Cloak.\n\n “My mother escaped the temple where your headed before the incident happened.”\n\n“What happened at the temple?” I said.\n\n“Something my mother made me swear never to speak of.” Said Cloak looking slightly away.\n\n“I hope you can respect that. You will know what it is when the time comes.”\n\n“Can you at least tell me something?” I said. “Seeing as I’m headed there.”\n\n“Let’s just say it’s beyond dangerous.” Said Cloak.\n\n “You will make it through alive with the weapons though. But the weapons you possess alone will not get you through. You will need to know how to use them. Which is why I’m coming with you in your travels.”\n\n“I’m not sure how that will go through with Sofetios and Sofia, especially Sofia.”  I said.\n\n“I’m sure we’ll figure something out.” Said Cloak. Then he paused and said,\n\n“ I guess ill have to follow you in the shadows when your traveling. Go ahead down and watch your friend in the competition. I’ll be down  there in a minute or two.”\n\n“How will I know your there?” I said.\n\n“I will be there in person.” Said Cloak.\n\n“I thought the Omira were supposed to be stealthy.” I said.\n\n“Who ever said I can’t walk around like a normal person.” Said Cloak with a slight smile.\n\n I got up, burning with questions and left out the door. I looked back at the waitress who nodded to me. I went down the stairs and sat back at the table with Sofetios.”\n\n“Where have you been?” Said Sofetios a bit concerned.\n\n“Oh I just went to use the restroom.” I lied\n\n“Ok.” Said Sofetios as he watched Sofia slam another guys arm down. I decided to take this time to look at my lore book. I opened it up and got to the first page.\n\nThere was a picture of the sun. In the middle of the sun was a small poem. It read,\n\nThe Prophecy, Part 1,\n\nOne day in the future,\nThe sun dims.\nThe Night will come up ever faster.\nAgainst every one of our wims.\n\nOne will come,\nOne bold and bright.\nTo stop the ever\nComing of the night.\n\nWith shining weapons,\nForged of light,\nThis hero will vanquish\nThe evils delight.\n\nBut the greatest weapon of all,\nThe Heart Indeed.\nWill determine how well,\nThe hero does succeed.\n\nI thought about this for a moment. So It was all up to me whether I succeed? Were the days really getting shorter?\n\nWhat is this evil it talks about? I turned the page. There was a note that said,\n\n‘Hello, If you are reading my book, that means you are either me or the Hero that the prophecy tells of. This also means I was lucky enough to find you.\n\nI’m just writing here to tell you of some pages in this book that you might find helpful, If you don’t already know the content of them. The pages are, 4, 7, 8, 14, 17, 20, and the last page. –Linink’\n\nI turned the page and found the table of contents. Page 4 said ‘The Lin Flute’. Page 7 said ‘The Lin Orb’. Page 8 said ‘The Temple of the Omira’. Page 14 said ‘Companions’. Page 17 said… Nothing. I turned the page to 17.\n\nIt was just a blank page. I turned back to page 4.   It said,\n\n‘The Lin Flute\n\nThe Lin flute is said to contain the ability to control the elements.\n\nIt is said to be able to make rain pore in a matter of seconds in a desert, make the most withering plant grow, or even teleport you places.’\n\nThat must have been what happened when I played The Song of Rain. I thought. I turned to page seven. It said,\n\n‘The Lin Orb\n\nThis artifact is said to be a ball of pure Lin that grows infinitely.\n\n No one knows how big or small it is. The fact that this is commonly known has caused many people to go looking for it, in which not many people return. Those who do return are empty handed.’\n\nNext I turned to page 8 and it said,\n\n‘The Temple of the Omira\n\nThis place is said to house The Alter of the Sun which is said to control how the sun acts. This is also headquarters of the Omira.’\n\nI turned the page to 14 and it said,\n\n‘Companions\n\nIt has been said that people have a type of spiritual animal familiar living within them. This companion is said to reflect ones self or inner being.\n\nI know this because I myself have one. To get yours to appear, simply will it out. If you are not practiced in Lin then yours might be harder to get out.\n\nThis passage scared me. The fact that there was some type of spirit inside me wasn’t exactly a pleasant one. I wondered what it was.\n\nI turned to page twenty. It read,\n\n‘The Great Monsters of Edrot\n\nEdger\n\nThis monster is said to be a giant spider and as large as a small cottage. It lives in the Dark woods on the side of Ridgewood.\n\nRumor has it knows how to defeat most all the other monsters as it is known to be the oldest and wisest monster.\n\nTifantis\n\nThis is a water spirit said to live in the water of lake Edrot. It is known to guard treasure of great magnitude as People passing by the lake can see a treasure chest at the bottom of the lake.\n\nThe trouble in getting it is that there is a current going away from the chest at all sides. Some people don’t believe Tifantis is real, and that the current is natural. But after all, what you believe is up to you.\n\nWenden\n\nWendon is said to be a wolf-man that roams the Dark woods. The simple fact that there are no others like him lead me to believe that he is not a wolf-man, but just a man who has the capability to use Lin to transform his body.\n\n Though why he would choose a wolfish form, I do not know.’\n\nThat is all there was, the bottom portion of the page was ripped out. Was there something that Linink didn’t want me to see?  I turned to the last page.\n\nThere was nothing put a picture of glasses with a dot above the nose rim. Sofetios poked me and I looked up. \n\nA larger crowd had gathered. Sofia got to the last person. It was a muscle like tan guy.\n\nI could tell Sofia’s arm was hurting Because she was stretching it. The muscle guy sat down. Sofia then said.\n\n“Wait, before this last round. Let me have a drink.” There were dissatisfied awws from the crowd. “You guys have Honeylinn?”\n\n“Of course!” said the waitress as she brought her one. Sofia took the drink and put it on the table. She then reached in her jacket pocket to get a coin when the waitress said, “On the house.”\n\nSofia smiled and brought her hand to the glass. The weird thing was her thumb was wet without it getting into the drink. She put her thumb over the glass quickly and took it out so fast that nobody seemed to notice that a drop fell in.\n\n“Cheers!” Said Sofia. Everyone raised their glass and said Cheers too. When Sofia drank her drink she gave the cup to the waitress and said, “Alright, lets do this!” It seemed as though her arm didn’t hurt as much anymore.\n\n The whole restaurant yelled, “THREE”, “TWO”, “ONE!”. There was a slight struggle, but in the end Sofia managed to get his arm to the side of the table. The place exploded with applause.\n\nAs if on queue, Someone walked into the room, dressed all in purple robes. It was Cloak.\n\n“Thank you everyone for coming to this event!” Said Cloak as he made his way toward Sofia. “And Congratulations to you!”\n\nCloak reached in his robes and gave Sofia a bag of gold. \n\n“Who are you?” Said Sofia taking the gold.\n\n“Why, the owner of this Café of course!” Said Cloak. “Now everyone. A round on me!” Everyone started rushing to the bar.\n\nSofia walked toward us and said, “well that was fun.” \n\n“Yea especially the Lin you put in your drink in the end.” Said Sofetios. Sofia elbowed Sofetios in the ribs .\n\n“Someone could hear us.” Said Sofia.\n\n“You don’t want us thrown out, do you?”\n\n“Ok, Ok.” Said Sofetios. “I was just kidding.”\n\n“Any way, lets get going.” Said Sofia. “We’re already behind schedule.”\n\n“Where’s our next stop?” I asked still looking at Cloak. \n\n“Sadzten.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“What kind of town is that.” I asked looking at Sofia.\n\n“It’s a fishing town.” Said Sofia.\n\n“So they are by the sea?” I asked.\n\n“No.” said Sofetios. “They are at Lake Edrot.” I remembered what the book said about Tifantus.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C1", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n\n      Chapter One\n\n  A Walk in the Woods\n\n“Mom!” I yelled as I went out the back door. “I’m going out to the woods!”\n\n“Fine Honey!” My mom yelled back. “Just be back before dusk ok?”\n\n“Sure Mom!” I answered. I put on my sword, closed the back door, and headed out. Knowing exactly where I was going as I ventured more into the woods. As I walked I couldn’t help but notice how nice everything was today.\n\nFrom the glistening emerald green leaves leaving a slight greenish tint on the ground, to the random scuttles and noises coming from the woods, it just seemed like it was going to be a good day. I approached the usual spot I hung out at near dusk.\n\nA small opening with a flat rock and a small clear pool in the middle. It wasn’t much but I always thought better here. I laid down on the rock looking up into the trees and begin to wander off in my head.\n\nI was about to dose off when I heard something. I sat up quickly. It wasn’t a normal sound. It sounded like the song that Linink played on the piano at the Festival, only it was on a flute. Cautiously, I got up and went in the direction of the sound.\n\nIt got louder and louder as I went along through the trees and bushes until I reached another larger clearing. I looked amazingly at what I saw. There was a Statue in the middle of the clearing with multiple statues around the clearing.\n\nThey all looked just like the one in the middle of town, except in different poses. The one in the middle had his arms outstretched in front of him.\n\nI went closer and saw that in it’s his hands outstretched was a Bow, Arrows, A sword, a dagger, and a scroll. Cautiously I went up closer to the statue and was about to take the scroll when suddenly the music stopped and a voice said,\n\n“Hey! Boy! What are you doing here” Startled I jumped back and turned to face an old man.\n\n“I’m sorry!” I said shocked. “I was just going to look at it! I swear!” The Old man had a frown on but then smiled and said.\n\n“Well why didn’t you say so? Go ahead and take a look.”\n\n“Wait… what?” I said surprised.\n\n“Go on, take a look.” Said the old man again still smiling.\n\n“Um… ok…” I said confused, turning to face the statue. I slowly took the scroll and opened it. Written on it was… nothing.  I frowned and looked back but the old man was gone. Only in his place was a flute.\n\nI scratched my head, went to it, and picked it up. As I touched it I heard the music start again but this time, it was in my head. Shocked again I dropped the flute, the scroll, and the music stopped.\n\nCuriously I picked up the flute and tried to play the notes I had heard. I had played the flute many times before but this time felt different somehow. As I finished playing the notes nothing seemed to happen.\n\nI wondered what I was expecting to happen. Once I waited about a minute I bent down and picked up the scroll. Only this time there was something written on it. Curiously I examined the scroll.\n\n It had a few lines of music notes on it and the title of it was called “Song of the Rain”. The music notes where different from the ones I had just played, so I began to play these ones.\n\nAs I played it sounded like a stormy night at sea. When I completed it, nothing seemed to happen. After a minute I walked to the statue, wondering if it would be a good idea to take the sword. Suddenly a Voice behind me said,\n\n“Would you look at that! You’re a natural at the flute.”\n\nShocked, I turned to see the old man again, this time he had a bird on his shoulder. He had the same smile on his face. \n“Where do you keep coming from?” I said.\n\nSeeming to ignore the question the old man looked at the weapons the statue had.\n\n“I see you like those weapons?” Said the old man. \n\n“Yea. They look amazing.” I said turning to the statue.\n\nThen looked at the face and said,” But… where they his?”\n\n“What do you mean?” Said the old man. “You’re the one wearing them.”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said turning to the old man again.\n\nBut he was gone. I turned back to the statue that had the weapons but they were gone. Suddenly I saw something on myself. I looked down and there was a sword on my belt, but it wasn’t my sword, it was the statues.\n\nI looked to the other side of my belt and there was the dagger. I slowly reached up and touched my shoulder. As I did I felt the feathers of an arrow and the string of a bow.\n\n I then realized it was dusk, my mom would be annoyed if I wasn’t home soon. I took off the weapons, put them back on the statues hands, and began to walk home.\n\n As I walked home I noticed the air began to feel denser and the wind began to pick up a little bit. Suddenly. I felt a raindrop. I looked up and one hit me on my forehead. I started running as fast as I could toward the house.\n\nAs I got in the back door my mom was standing there with her arms crossed. \n\n“Where have you been?” She said sternly. “You’re late and your soaked head to toe!”  All I could say was,\n\n“I don’t know.”\n\n“Jaya.” Said my mom in a warning voice. \n\nI sighed and recounted the whole story about the old man, the weapons, the flute and the scroll. As I finished my mom looked pale.\n\n“Are you alright?” I said. She walked slowly to a kitchen chair and sat down.\n\n“Jaya.” My mom began. “I’m going to have you see Linink.”\n\nLinink was the best doctor around and also the leader of the adventurer’s guild, a guild that helps people and goes on quests. My friends Sofetios and Sofia go there.\n\n“Wait, why?” I said concerned. “Do you think I’m sick?”\n\n“No Jaya.” My mom said. “It’s about something else. I think it’s time you went to bed.” Confused and concerned, I went to bed.\n\nEnd of Chapter One\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Treatise", "§bAluuvia", "When we are born we are placed on one side of the divide or the other.\n    Only the Creator's first were in the grey and not all still are.\n    We feel ourselves pulled towards one side or another. And if not pulled we are pushed away from one, by\n\nit's own inhabitants.\n    It is wearisome to be alone on one side of imbrication. To think that that above us may be lurking in the murky in-between.\n    And so we pull our Gods over as well, giving them places and powers and loves and hates,\n\nand all the mortal fallacies and things Gods care nothing for.\n    When we make our Gods more like us, do we make them less like Gods? But what many refer to as such are merely the Creator's First.\n    His first Creations.\n\n    But perhaps they do not mind so much.\n\n\nBeing named Gods.\n\n    There are reasons not to wander towards either horizon.\n    To the East it is bright and distanct. Pleasant to be sure, a luminescence that works it's way under the skin, into the being.\n    One can make no objections to this and wonders who could.\n\n    To the West it is dark and silent. \nComforting to be certain, a gentle stillness that calms the bones, the mind.\n   Another can make no objections to this and wonders who could.\n    Then there stands those who have crossed the border.\n\n    Those who have been both East and West, seen the sun rise and the sun set, and settled upon one or the other.\n    Then there are those who have crossed the border.\n    Those who have been both East and West, seen the sun rise and the sun set.\n\n    And settled upon neither.\n    We sat ourselves down in the grey in-between, where the sun never rises and the sun never sets.\n    But it's rays are not of light nor of coming dark, in the middle where we lurk.\n\n    I have watched people come and people go. Some have stayed to linger, others left too soon.\n    Many more simply walk right over me, never looking down as to them I make no sound, no noise nor purpose to be heeded.\n\n    I cannot say I blame them. It is loneliness in the place where two things meet but neither be. Sometimes it feels there is no one here but me.\n    No one wants to be alone and so no one wants to linger here.\n\n    If others embrace the light, you may too.\n\n    If others seek the dark, you may too.\n\n   For some the light blinds, wherein the dark they find solace.\n\n    For some the dark frightens, where in the light they find safety.\n\n    But the light blinds me and I find no solace in the dark.\n\n    The dark frightens me and I find no guardian in the light.\n\n    I was not born here, in the middle grey in-between.\n\n    Here I shall stay.\n\n    It is easy to find excuse, a circumstance of birth. Sunrise or Sunset, a preference is a choice.\n\n    Not an affliction.\n\n    Not a disease.\n\n    We just make us in-between.\n\n    Then there is North and South. Still and shifting. They are neither East nor West, sunrise nor sunset.\n    For the few that pass from East to West, South and North is a horizon all must cross between.\n    But there are those who don't.\n\n    There are those who linger.\n\n    Those who cling to the South refusing to pass the border, relishing the warmth of the sun and the cool breeze.\n    Those who wander the North, walking though all else around is still and silent.\n\n    At the very center there is that and in and of that are they. We pass through but do not linger for as we pass we are not even cognizant of doing so for the sake of never really being there.\n\n    And of those some may push against the veil that cloaks that center, pressing this way or that, North and South meaning nothing to them, but East and West of significance, for that is where we are always regardless of all else.\n\n    Some seek those by sunrise, others those by sunset. They reach out and they reach through, invisible to all, without a face or flesh or bone. They set us about, against the other one's, pick us up and drop us down.\n\n    We are reflections of them, in our search for power. Some of us in our judgement.\nOthers in our reach across the horizon, ever searching for companionship to join us, on our side of the divide.\n   Here I benefit, in the in-between.\n\n    For here I may simply stretch my arms out to either side and offer my hands.\n\n\n\n    And I know in time someone will always place their hand in mine.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Brass Teapot", "§bIsengar Brockfall", "Our story begins with two very unwealthy people that were known as John and Alice.\n\n\"If I were rich honey, I would stay in bed with you all day\"\nhe smiled with a glistening look on his face.\n\n\"But! I have to get to work.\"\nHis smile faded into a depressed saddened expression.\n\nJohn got out of the bed that was originally made for one, it squeaked when they got up as one of the springs were broke.\n\nJohn tucked Alice in nice and warm and gave her a quick kiss before he got dressed into his coffee stained suit.\n\nJohn reached for the wooden handle and opened his wardrobe pulling out the grey suit.\n\nHe smelt it and made a *it's okay to wear again* look.\n\nJohn took his bucket of dirty water with flies floating around in it, and poured it over his head.\nIt drenched his suit but atleast he was clean! He thought.\n\nJohn got a small rag with yellow stains glued onto it and wiped himself down, although it didn't do much to get him dry.\n\"Hmph\" he grumbled, as he grasped for his silver inn key for work.\n\nAs he kicked open his stiff door it swung open and a heavy breeze hit johns face.\nHe slammed the door shut and headed to work.\n\n\"Good Morning Mr. Caulfield\" he waved as he left Petrus.\n\nJohn ran out onto the graveled path in a hurry to get to work.\n\nAs john arrived he was shouted at by his boss Vinnie! ((Read his lines in an Italian accent))\n\"Ey Johnny what do you think your doin' turnin' up this late?\"\n\nJohn put a fake smile and apologised, he started to mumble curse words about Vinnie as he hung his suit jacket up on the hook.\n\nAlice groaned as she got out of bed and reached for glass of water.\nShe chugged it down and stumbled out of her bed.\n\nShe grabbed her pink robe and put it on. She ran her fingers down the silk and smiled whilst doing so.\nA knock at the the hollow wooden door startled her.\nShe shuffled to the door and opened it wide, shivering at the coldness from outside.\n\n\"A'hm 'ere fer te'h rent!\" Their landlord (Albert) asked impaitently.\nAlice had a slight worried look on her face.\n\"I'm sorry Albert we can't afford this months rent!\"\n\nAlbert laughed with a sense of angryness in it.\n\"Wel' t'en what yer goin' ter do 'bout et?\" he snapped!\n\n\"I...\" before she could answer Albert pushed passed her knocking her into the door.\n\n\"What's te'h mos' Valuable t'ing yer go'?\" he examined the living room suspicously.\n\nAlice cried \"Pleas' Albert!\"\nHe looked at her with an imtimidating expression.\n\nShe pointed in the kitchen and told him.\n\"My mums Jewerly, but the gold is fake\" she cried.\n\nAlbert grabbed the jewerly and shoved it into his pocket a penny fell out and rolled under the cupboard.\n\nHe huffed in anger and stomped out.\nAlice slammed the door shut and screamed into a handmade cotton pillow that was rough when you touched it.\n\nShe glanced to the cupboard and dived onto the ground, she rummaged her hand into the narrow space\n\ntrying to find the 1 mina that rolled under.\nShe grabbed something circular and pulled it out.\nShe opened her palm and a nickel was covered in dust.\nHer eyes widened in amazement.\nShe put it in her and John's jar of savings.\n\nWhich contained\nA long piece of string, 4 minas including the one she found, and some screwed up denied job applications for the local barbers.\n\nJohn opened the door smiling.\n\n\"Why are YOU smiling\" she groaned.\n\nJohn reached into his pockets pulling out a free drink coupon at the deathbanes inn.\nAlice giggled and kissed him on the lips she whispered \"I love it when you spoil me!\"\n\nThe next day John woke up to his normal routine.\nHe used his quarter in his pocket to get a carriage to the inn.\n\n\"Ey Johnny you're late!\"\n\"Err sorry Vinnie I was...\"\n\nVinnie had interuppted him.\n\"You're fired!!!\"\n\"What?! are yer talking about Vinnie\" he smiled worrying.\n\"We have another Inn keeper who wants the job, and you always fuck up so...\" He snapped.\n\n\"You...You're firing me\" John felt a tear coming down his eye.\n\"But I have a wife!\"\n\"Find another job, and err oh I need the key back.\"\nJohn was full of rage, anger and despair.\nHe threw the key outside and stomped outside crying.\n\n\"WHY!!!, HAVEN'T YOU HAD ENOUGH FUN?\" he shouted to the sky.\nHe scraped a pebble up and thew it into the bushes.\nHe slowly strolled back to Petrus!\n\nAs he turned the key into his front door he saw that there was fresh blood on the floor and a bloody hammer.\n\"ALICE!\" he shouted in the living room.\nHe ran towards the bed, She was covered in thick red blood as if it were a murder.\n\nHe grasped his hands on her arms and shook her with a tear rolling down his cheek.\nShe slowly opened her eyes and blinked, \"Alice!\" he smiled.\n\"What the heck happened?\"\nShe laughed and told him the story!", ""),
        StaticBook("On Orcs", "§bLelien", "On Orcs\n\n    by Leyu'Maehr\n\nNo race is more adapted to the harsh deserts than the muscular Orcs. Masters of combat and wrestling these 7ft high Goliaths can destroy most prey with their bare hands. To an Orc the most important thing is the hunt and the protection of his\n\ntribe and clan. For that reason, they do not intermix with other races much. They have a mutual hatred and respect for the Dwarves of Kal’Urguan because of their ferocity and strength. However they disdain other races simply because they’re not big\n\nenough. Where other races establish cities and build monuments to their predecessors, Orcs establish tribes and build strong clans around the mythic figures of their ancestors. Orcs tend toward nomadic life, but what villages they do choose to establish\n\nare usually built from the ruins of other cities, swallowed and spat forth again by the drifting dunes of the desert.\n\nAlthough Orcs can naturally live longer than humans, this rarely becomes a point of debate. The oldest Orc to ever live was Karguk\n\nof Caln Pyrathon, who died in glourious battle on the turning of his two hundredth year (Eight hundred Orcish seasons). Orcs are just as prolific as Dwarves and Humans, but their children have the shortest period of puberty, sometimes reaching full\n\nadulthood in only fifteen years. Orcs are also the race in Aegis most likely to cull their own, whether purposefully leaving the incapable behind in the desert, or removing the weak through ritual trials. However, the strength of the clan is paramount in\n\nan Orc’s eyes, and they will defend their young and wise to their very last breath – even if it is only to give enough time for the wise to show the young how to best attack after their elder clansmen have fallen.\n\nOrcs are usually brown skinned with green tints, varying from sandy to dark green and rarely black, and their hair is usually very dark, with brown and black the most common. Most Orcs follow the practice of coloring their hair with the blood of their\n\nenemies. Because their hair is so dark, this coloring rarely shows until many dousings, and it is considered a sign of a great warrior for your hair to glow red with the blood of your enemies: Orcs of the Shaman bloodline tend more toward green skin and\n\nblack hair, usually distinguished from other Orcs by size.\n\nSize and musculature set them apart from all other races on Aegis, sometimes considered giants at two and a half meters tall. Orcs of the goblin bloodline, are most notably smaller than\n\nother Orcs, usually only reaching a meter and a half. Goblins are the most likely of all Orcs to have black skin and fairer hair. Orc eyes are usually brown or black, with a rare few blessed with blood-red.", ""),
        StaticBook("Punishment I", "§bArchmage Crumena", "The Punishment of Hubris I\n\nLet me tell you a story of the children of Malin, Horen, Urguan and Krug; A tale from the time when God’s melting pot became a cauldron. And many wondered about his beneficence.\nA tale from when God was first questioned and his mortal children cried\n\nout in anguish.\nOur story takes us back to the beginning, when the Four Brother’s children were coming of age in this world known as Aegis. One stood out among the sons of Malin. Born beneath the shade of the canopy on under the pale light of a\n\nfull moon, his father named him Zanunder. Proud and strong was his stature, Zanunder stood tall among his brothers and sisters, resembling their Father in many ways. His hair was the color of the noon-day sun and his eyes a vibrant shade of\n\nforest green.\nIblees came, then, as Zanunder grew. Corrupted his father and uncles, in the end unleashing upon the world a devastating curse. They said that Iblees had been a Daemon, a servant of God. Zanunder began to question this. If God was\n\nomnipotent, surely he would not allow evil to exist. Nor would he do so were he kind, benevolent or even compassionate. But he was not the only being to begin to question the ways of the world. There was also her…she stood tall, her presence unlike\n\nanything he had laid eyes upon before. Hair black as night, lips green as ivy, but the strangest thing about her visage was surely her eyes. The whites of her eyes were a deep, steel blue, and inside they were a light blue, like the clean waters of a\n\ngently flowing stream. He came to know her as Nemiisae, a kindred spirit in this world he viewed as cruel. In short time they fell in love, relishing in each other’s ideals and presence. They came to the conclusion quickly that they should escape\n\nthese lands, hoping that in doing so they would also be able to break free of Iblees’ curse upon the lands. They retreated deep underground in order to begin their plans, for Zanunder did not wish others to know what they had planned, lest they\n\nbe branded heretics.\nDeep beneath the ground, in a large cavern, Nemiisae created a portal to a world known as the Verge. From there it would be easier for her powers to stretch across the lands, locating a fit place for her,\n\nZanunder, and their soon-to-be abundant children to settle. It would also protect them from the scourge Iblees unleashed across the lands. Inside the Verge the two thrived, and quickly multiplied, first growing to three, then four, then\n\nsix, eight, ten, and continuing on. Nearly a hundred years after they first arrived in that place, Nemiisae had finally found a suitable place to settle. However, during those hundred years, Kings had risen and fallen. The Brothers had all\n\npassed away. Kingdoms and Guilds began to rise to power throughout the lands. The curse seemed to barely affect people’s lives. These events had gone unnoticed by Nemiisae and Zanunder, so wrapped up in raising their young and\n\nfinding a place to flee to from Iblees’ curse. Inside the Verge, Nemiisae created another portal. It reflected the green, verdant lands they planned to settle…but not the dangers lurking within. Before they went through with their children,\n\nZanunder stopped his love. He requested that the portal be closed behind them, as well as the portal out of the Verge that they had entered through. Zanunder did not wish for their children to be followed, believing that Iblees’ curse\n\nbeing, feeling love for all the races of Aegis. She believed they could all escape Iblees’ curse and did not wish to deny them the chance to do so. Little did she know that in the end, all who sought her same refuge would be lead to their dooms by it.\n\nbeing, feeling love for all the races of Aegis. She believed they could all escape Iblees’ curse and did not wish to deny them the chance to do so. Little did she know that in the end, all who sought her same refuge would be lead to their dooms by it.\n\nAs soon as Zanunder, Nemiisae and their children stepped through the portal, they realized it had slammed shut behind them; They could no longer return to the land they came from. At first, this was not a problem to them. They were confident\n\nthis land would be their Paradise, the savior of their children. But their children had spent decades cut off from the light of sun, while living and thriving within the Verge. They set out immediately for the thickest forest they could find, in hopes\n\nof slowly acclimating their children to the light. But this was not to be. This land was rife with dangers, of all shapes and sizes, lurking behind corners, within the trees, in the skies, the oceans, the rivers…There was no escaping it. The very least\n\nof these dangers were the skittering, venomous spiders of the caverns. Their children began dying off, one by one, then two by two, then five by five, then by the droves. Finally, Nemiisae chose the least of the threats of this world and blessed her\n\nchildren with that creature’s aspects. Her children became a mix of her blood, Zanunder’s, and that of the spiders that lurked the caverns. They migrated into these same caverns, living amongst and as the Spiders did, save from the beasts and terrors\n\nlurking on the surface. Vicious, cruel, the children shifted and changed into horrible beasts, preying and feeding upon one another.\nNemiisae knew she had to bless them in this way so that they may survive, yet still she grieved for their corruption.\n\nAs well, no matter how hard they tried, Nemiisae and Zanunder could no longer procreate. Horrified, they began to believe it had been a trap all along. A trick by God to punish them for acting out, perhaps?! Or was it just for His own amusement?!\n\nZanunder refused. They argued at length, until finally he threatened to take the children and go elsewhere. He firmly believed if they traveled far enough they could survive, thrive, beat God and the Curse. Frustrated and exhausted,\n\nNemiisae knew she had to stop him somehow, or their children would all perish. She remembered the blessing she had given her children and as Zanunder turned to leave, she changed her form to that of a giant Spider. She put him to sleep with her\n\nNemiisae knew she had to stop him somehow, or their children would all perish. She remembered the blessing she had given her children and as Zanunder turned to leave, she changed her form to that of a giant Spider. She put him to sleep with her\n\nvenom and wrapped him within a cocoon. Then, she bade the eldest and closest of her Daughters to watch over the others, before retreating into the deep with Zanunder, to try and find a way to force open the portal and escape this horrid place.\n\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed, 1473.\nTo be continued in the second volume.\n[Credit to TehLulu for the writing itself.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Scourge Members", "§bUnsigned", "There is a cult in Anthos that has the purpose of following the commands of the Black Scourge. In a way, they are considered part of it.\n\nIn this book there is information on their past members, and some of their current ones.\n\nVithquar\n\nAn experiment created by some of the members of the Scourge, particularly the Judge and the Shadowed alchemist, with aid of one of the Harbinger, Shae'Tan. Physically strong, and slightly sexy, she is not really that smart.\n\nTo identify her is easy, she has horns, a tail, black wings, and black and yellow eyes. She also wears very little slothing.\nShe believes she is a goddess that has lost her powers, and that she should be treated as such. If you actually treat her like\n\nshe wants to be treated, you get on her good side.\nWhile she is part of the cult, she does not worship Setherien. She is only in it because she was created by them, and because she has received power from them.\n\nThe Listener\n\nLeader of the cult, not much is known about him. A warrior, always armored when meeting the cultists. He is in direct contact with the Harbingers, and takes orders from them.\nHe is one of those who recruits.\n\nThe Judge\n\nOne of the higher ups in the cult, a more calm person. He hides his identity through black robes and a skull mask, having a straight posture and speaking in an unnatural voice. Not a fighter himself, he used to stand behind others he\n\ncommanded, or make more use of tricks.\nFrom those captured he would be normally the cause for it to happen. He would interegate them, question them, before deciding what to be done. Some he releaced, some only after torture, some he killed fast, but when\n\nhe didn't like the answers or the person, he usually did something else. It would be a sort of ritual, before he carved symbols into someone's back and skinned them. Why he did so was never known.\nHe was a true believer of the word of Setherien,\n\nmostly the part about adquiring peace by force, yet this soon turned out to be false when he betrayed the Scourge, and destroyed a Harbinger.\nHe is wanted by the Scourge, and as such, he is in hiding.\n\nQa'darath\n\nBefore a higher up of the cult, he too betrayed it, the reasons for the betrayal known. An elf which had quite a few powers. He could tap into the mind of people, and he was a necromancer. If you have not known until\n\nnow, the Scourge and the necromancers are against eachother. The reason for his betrayal is simple, he sided with the necromancers instead of the cult.\nHis description is as simply described as white haired high elf, thin, and with purple robes.\n\nBurzumkil\n\nOne of the stronger warriors in the Scourge. A human with a thick accent. Very powerful in war. Merciless as well, he was one of those who lead raids against towns and villages. He has not been seen for a while.\n\nPrince Ebs\n\nOne of the best spies in the cult, prince Ebs is said to be the one responsible for the information required to access the lands of Old Malinor with the power corruption. He would also keep the Scourge updated with movements of the\n\nelves, and information about politics of Anthos.\nA Prince of Malinor, he has the perfect cover, and would only meet with the Scourge in designated times and places. He would bring great information that would keep the Scourge up to date. While as a spy,\n\nHe never really attacked anyone, and he has great skill in lying. He was commanded to never show himself as a cultist, even to those of the cult, nor to help them. He is a pure spy, one which has not even been given much information on the Scourge, as for\n\nhim to do his job as best he could. If captured, he has nothing to tell, even if tortured. Giving away his position as spy, would only result in his execution, he knows that if he says he worships Setherien, even in torture, he will lose his life, be it\n\nby those who captured him, or by those under Setherien’s will.\n\nThe Oogie Boogie Man\n\nA twisted being, corrupted so much that neither his mind or body is anything good. Black robes and skull mask like the Judge, but the way he behaves is quite different.\nBugs of various kinds seem to be what he is\n\nmade of. Spiders crall from his eyes, ears, and hands.\nOne that enjoys te pain of others, and the bringing of destruction. If he does worship Setherien, it would be because Setherien brings those things. Knowledged in the arts of weird dark magics,\n\nhe was the one that was able to bring a strong ghost into the rule of the Scourge, and he was the one which discovered a way to destroy Old Malinor.\nPowerful in knowledge… weak physically. He is one of those weaker in the Scourge, using tricks and dark\n\nmagic to capture and torment the people of Anthos.\nHe likes to tell stories, and normally just walks unprotected through the lands, with his black robes and skill mask.\n\nThe Shadow Alchemist\n\nAnother one to take intellect over power, this old man is an alchemist that focuses on the dark and twisted sides of it. Experimenting and taking to the Judge were some of the things he did best. Also a great friend of the\n\nOogie Boogie Man, for the same reasons, knowledge.\nExtremelly smart, and twisted to the point of not caring of the life of those he experiments on.\nUnlike the other two, this one can still swing an axe once or twice before he gets tired.\n\nThe Mistress\n\nA twisted elf, which collects heads. Only in the cult to gain more power.\nA fighter and a spy, she also collected relics and information when not killing.\nNothing much is known about her appearance, as she wore masks.\n\nKaos\n\nA human or elf, not known. He is another powerful warrior, leading charges and raids with Burzumkil.\nHe made good use of armor, and hid his identity quite well.\n\nThere are more but I do not know enough details to write about them. This information has been given from a member on the inside, so the informer will remain anonymous as well.\n\n*The book is left unsigned.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Blood", "§bDurza Volkihar", "Dark elfs are the most elegant but strong of all the races. everything that a dark elf does come from the heart. Whether it be the way they fight, the way they speak or the way they dress everything comes from the heart. Dark Elfs do not view each other\n\ndepending on someones wealth they view each other depending on someones accomplishments. Dark elfs walk with a certain look of confidence. They are taught to belong in any situation and in any enviroment.\n\nDark elfs are very proficient in combat. They are not trained to be fierce or bezerking warriors, They are trained to be elegant and graceful in their movement. Unlike their wood elf cousins, the dark elfs prefer to use swords instead of bows although\n\nwhen a dark elf chooses the path of the bow they are highly sought after as archers and rangers. Dark elfs have a great love of theater and poetry. They also love to paint often depicting one of their legends or a great battle.\n\nDark elfs are common victims of racial attacks due to the colour of their skin or the unusual colour of their eyes. Dark elfs do not give in though they will fight until they die. Instead of chargeing head on into a situation they think before attacking.\n\nUnfortunatly Dark elfs are extremely unfertile which means it is very rare for a dark elf child to be born. But when they are born parents treasure and are extremely protective of their children but they also encourage them to do everything they can do.\n\nIf you agree with my views seek out my emblem.\n\n\n\n\n[!] A red eagle can be see here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of the Mori", "§bArchmage Crumena", "When the murder and attacks upon the city occurred, many speculations arose within the city itself of whom was to blame and should be slaughtered for such acts against their kind -- many claimed it was the work of surfacers, others believed\n\nthat such things were only possible by those within the city.\nIt was declared and enforced that all living mori were to return to the bosom of Nemiisae and remain within the sanctum of Menorcress: behind these stragglers to return the\n\nhorror unfolded, each path and passage they journeyed through only hours before could be heard crumbling under the weight of explosives. The people were brought each in turn to the Temple of the Mother to be cleansed of their\n\ntaint, the sickness of the surface that had infested them. The final act of the Valsharess and her yathrins before the war broke out.\nMany that had broken loose from such rigid traditions fought against this cleansing and became quickly enraged,\n\nspitting in the faces of the priestess' whom dared demand their obedience and silence. It was not long before two factions emerged, the devote and the rebels.\nBeneath the surface of the world, sealed off from the blinding damnation of suns\n\nlight, the Caverns of Menorcress. Its streets littered with crude barricades, strewn with the deceased and wounded -- the one marvelled city now rots with death and destruction... crumbling under civil war. Bathed in life blood of their kith\n\nand kin, the rebellion breach upon the Yathrins' sacred enclave; banners raised in revolt, their armour and bodies marked by their treason. Once considered mere common rabble; these denizens now slaughter blessed noble born and\n\ntheir ilk standing guard at the doors of the Temple. From behind the sealed doors both rothe and mori alike stand in un-ease union against the treat of taint of its own city -- this seeded by those turned to the hubris of their Ilharn Zanunder.\n\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed 1473.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C3", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n\n    Chapter Three\n The Melonko Festival\n\nI went to the town’s center where everyone was gathered, People where playing music and everyone was seemingly having a good time.\n\nThe mayor, Jedjory, appeared and walked to the center and everyone quieted down.  Then Jedjory said, \n\n“Good morning everyone, this is the 10th Melonko festival, Celebrating good fortune and peace.\n\nNow  everyone please stop and listen to the Adventurers guild orchestra!” Everyone turned to the front of the Adventurers guild where there where about 50 teenagers with all kinds of different instruments. Linink was on an instrument and started to play.\n\nThen others joined in and more until everyone was playing.  I had heard Sofetios speak of this kind of thing before, where everyone joined in when they felt it was right. I think he called it free playing.\n\nThe sound was great. When they all finished there was a round of applause and Jedjory spoke again when they all quieted down.\n\n“Let the Melonko festival begin!”\n\nI met with Sofia and Sofetios a bit later in front of one of the games tents. \n\n“So, chosen one, how did you like the performance?” Said Sofia sarcastically. \n\n“Don’t call me that.” I said angrily.\n\n“Come on.” Said Sofia smiling. “Everyone is going to start calling you that once they realize what you found.”\n\n“Hopefully that won’t be soon” I said worried. I noticed that Sofetios was looking behind the tent. “What is it Sofetios?”\n\n“I think I just saw a black hooded figure behind the tent.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“Not possible.” Said Sofia. “I already know what you’re thinking and it’s not possible. They died out years ago.”\n\n“Yea, your right.” Said Sofetios turning to me. “I guess I’m just worried about the Journey.”\n\n“Wait, what died out years ago?” I said.\n\n“Jeez Jaya.” Said Sofia. “You really should pay more attention to lore.” I then remembered the Lore book that Linink gave me and pulled it out of my bag.\n\n“I see Linink gave you his lore book.” Said Sofetios.\n\n“That will probably help in times to come. “Look up the word ‘Omira’.”  I skimmed the book until I found the word. I then said,\n\n“ ‘The Omira are a clan of people dedicated to protecting the Land from any evil. They commonly wear black robes with hoods and are practiced in concealing themselves.\n\nThey are said to be mainly of the rouge class, but there were rumors of some being mages. They are said to have died out long ago. ‘ “ \n\n“That about covers it.” Said Sofetios. “Did Linink give you anything else?”\n\nI pulled out the water sphere Linink gave me. At this Sofetios’s mouth hung slightly ajar.\n\n“He gave you a water sphere?” Sofetios said in amazement. “How much did he say was in there?”\n\n“A weeks worth for three people he said.” I said.\n\n“Well then I guess we won’t need to worry about water.” Said Sofia. “Come on, let’s go to the fortune stall.” Sofia went to the fortune stall every year.\n\n The weird thing about the lady who runs it is that all her predictions seem to come true.\n\nAs we approached the purple tent. I couldn’t help but be worried. I was about to have my future laid out for me. Maybe I just wouldn’t get my fortune read.\n\nWe entered the tent. The old lady was sitting behind the usual crystal ball.\n\n“Come in.” She said as she looked up. “Ah Sofia. Come to see your fortune again I see?”\n\n“Yes Maim.” Said Sofia.\n\nThis is pretty much the only time she gets enthusiastic or manner full about anything except fighting.\n\n“Ok then.” Said the Lady. “Please take a seat. I will need your two friends to step outside.” Sofia looked at us and both Sofetios and I left.\n\nAfter 15 minutes, Sofia left the tent looking slightly uneasy. She was also holding a fortune cookie in her hand. The old lady also gives those out so people can have a little extra info.\n\n“She wants you to come in next Sofetios.” Said Sofia. Sofetios went inside the tent without saying a word.\n\n“What did she tell you?” I said.\n\n“None of your business.” Said Sofia right back.\n\n After another 15 minutes Sofetios exited the tent looking a bit down. \n\n“Well your next.” Said Sofetios to me. I nervously entered the tent. \n\n“Take a seat.” Said the lady. I went over and took a seat.\n\n“Your friends certainly had interesting fates. Now let’s see yours.” She pulled out her famous set of fortune cards and spread them out face down. “Choose four.\" I picked the ones in the beginning, end, and two in the middle.\n\n“Now flip them over in the order you choose. One by one.” I flipped the first one. It had a picture of someone about to be shot by and arrow but there was someone behind the person who was the real one about to be shot with a dagger raised.\n\nThere were words printed around the sides. It said, ‘Saved by a Friend’. “It seems you have more friends then you realize.” Said the old lady. “Now the second.”\n\nI flipped over the second one. It showed a book with worlds spewing out of it with the word ‘Skill’. “It also seams that you will excel at learning. Now the third.”\n\nI flipped over the third one and it had a picture of a blanket over a bizarre shaped object with jagged edges and then a picture of a bird in a cage with the blanket on the ground, the words on this one said ‘Doubt then Understanding’.\n\nThe old lady seemed a little worrisome on this card. \n\n“Is something wrong?” I said nervously.\n\n“No, no.” said the old lady.\n\n “This card means that you will doubt something or be undecided, but then see the truth. Now the Fourth.” I flipped the fourth card and it showed two paths going separate from each other.\n\nOn one side there was what looked like woods, on the other it looked like a plain. The words on it said ‘The Choice’  “That’s the toughest one of all.” Said the lady.\n\n“You will have a tough choice in the future. Now for your final fortune with me. Please place your hands on the side of the crystal ball and you will see your future.” I hesitated, then was about to place my hands on the crystal ball.\n\nWhen I touched it, it exploded with light. The old lady stood up quickly and gasped and then I realized I was standing up too. As soon as my hand left the ball the light went away immediately.\n\n“You…” Said the lady slowly. Then she calmed down. “So the prophecy is coming true. “ \n\n“What does this all mean?” I said.\n\n“It means you have a long journey ahead of you.” Said the old lady.\n\n“Here.” She reached in a jar at the side of the table and pulled out two cookies. “Only Break and eat one. The other you are to give to a friend.”\n\n“Is that all you have to say?” I said hoping for more.\n\n“That is all.” Said the old lady. I exited the tent, sure that I looked worried.\n\n“What happened in there?” Said Sofia.\n\n“Yea.” Said Sofetios. “We saw a flash of light.”\n\nI was about to tell them when I remembered its bad luck to tell your fortunes. I needed all the luck I could get.\n\n“Sorry I don’t know myself.” I said with some truth.\n\nAfter some hours had passed, we went to the entrance of the village. Sofia and Sofetios had huge packs on. \n\n“Should I have brought anything?” I asked.\n\n“No we have everything here.” Said Sofetios.\n\nThen I remembered my mom.\n\n“But we can’t go yet, I need to say goodbye to my mom!” \n\n“Relax Jaya.” Said Sofetios. “Linink probably already told your mother.”\n\n“Yea, I guess your right.” I said a little down. Then it occurred to me that I didn’t even know where we were going.\n\n“Wait, where are we going?” I said.\n\n“To the temple of the Omira” Said Sofia. “You should really take a look at that lore book.” As we left I dug into my pocket and got the two fortune cookies. I picked one at random and opened it. The paper inside said one word. ‘Believe’.\n\nEnd of Chapter Three\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elder Seed", "Eenhoornheid", "Journey of the Elder Seed: Normandor\n\n\n\nChronicled by Ithri\nSourced by Bravepaw\nTranscribed by Elorna Avern\n\nThis is the story of how the Great Elder Tree of Normandor formed. For generations, a powerful dynasty of Elves held the seed. However this was no ordinary seed, this was an Elder Seed. It is said that of all the great trees in Aegis, only the Elder Seeds\n\ncould produce the finest and most magical entities. These seeds were tainted by borht light and dark magic and would yearn to reside in the heavens but also in the void.\n\nThe last known holder of this seed was Bravepaw, now chief of Normandor, founder of the Elder Tree. Having little understanding of the seed's power, the gods truly had guided him to unleashing its full potential. Over the long elvish years and with the\n\nconsiderable gaps between generations, the purpose for the seed had been somewhat lost. All that survived was the tradition to pass the seed on to the new eldest son with the simple words,\n\"Light conquers evil, consumes darkness, embraces life and\n\ntakes root even in the most darkened of places.\"\nBravepaw had indeed always been baff;ed bu these wprds, but wore the seed around his neck, instilling in him the protection and guidance of his ancestors.\n\nOn his father's deathbed, Bravepaw was told, \"When the Void surrounds you, look to our greatest source of light.\", with those words passing him into the beyond. The Elder Seed became incredibly sentimental to Bravepaw, he clutched it in remembrance of\n\nhis fathers before him; it guided him and comforted him, leading him to the beyond.\n\nSeasons passed, Bravepaw grew mature and wise. He became very close to his Elvish comapnion Genriel, and formed a strong pact with two Elves named Orlanden\n\nand Travathian. They eventually came to settle south of Laurelin, in a place called Valenwood. For a while Bravepaw found peace there, but the seed would alwats distract him and push him, he was never truly at home. Following a peace treaty struck\n\nbetween the Elves and the Orcs, the four companions were given the opportunity to run as Elvish Outpost and have much autonomy. Bravepaw accepted this position in order to expand the frontier of the Elvish power. He always remained suspicious and vigilant\n\nof the new Orcish landlords. A price of 50 000 minas was put on the land, Bravepaw set about to gather the necessary finds, the Orcs giving him one week to do so. However, the Orcs in their treachery, arrived earlier than this to collect it.\n\nThey wanted a reason to ransack the place and remove the Elvish presence. On arrival, Bravepaw had managed to raise the necessary amount and offered it willingly. The Orcs, defeated in their dim-witted plan, turned it down and retreated, attempting to\n\nsalvage what they would call Orcish pride. Bravepaw decided to take a hunting party to gather food for the outpost. He left two younger Elves to pay the Orcs on their return. Supplies were running low and this hunt would be critical for their survival.\n\nFate, it would seem, has a wicked sense of irony.\n\nThe Orcs were watching; they watched Bravepaw lead his people into the wilds to hunt. They watched the two Elves that were left behind and they watched the sun dip behind the mountains\n\nuntil it was day no more. That night the Orcs charged the outpost, slaughtering the two Elves, taking the money and setting the place on fire. The outpost had no hope and was scorched from the very surface of Aegis. When Bravepaw returned with his\n\ncompanions, they were met with smouldering ruins, the air thick with smoke, the ground covered in ash. The Orcs there told Bravepaw this was the action taken for not paying. Bravepaw used his Elvish wisdom to try and reason with them, he had given the\n\nopportunity of payment and even left the money.\n\"Cunsidda it compens... compen... compen-\nsation.\", the Orc growled; looking very pleased with himself for mustering the necessary vocabulary.\n\nBravepaw felt a rage build inside of him; he wanted to strike these foulish Orcs down now where they stood. He reached for his bow, but something stopped him. He felt the seed beating, beating as if it were his own heart.\nIt calmed him, it filled him with\n\nwarmth, a vision flew into his head, the void, an island, a distant land, unlike anywhere he had seen in Aegis. Was this to be his home, was his father calling him or was this the magic of the seed driving him insane? He pondered on this for a moment.\n\nAn Orc seeing that his hand had reached for his bow, lunged forward, piercing his dagger into Bravepaw's chest. His companions gasped, reaching for their swords, fearing the worst. However, Bravepaw had not been harmed.\n\nThe dagger struck the seed and the seed ad erupted. The Orcish metal dissolved into nothing, corruption spread through the body of the Orc, he squirmed and screamed as he turned into ash, a breeze rolled past, taking with it the Orish ash.\n\nThe Elder Seed had awoken! The rest of the Orcs, seeing the raw power of whatever this was, rushed away, leaving Bravepaw and his companions in awe of the events that had just transpired. The Elder Seed was glowing now, it had been given its sacrifice.\n\nThe flow of the Seed was pulling them, leading them, guiding them. The group would follow its light, to the very end of Aegis if they needed to. They made a pact that day, to never rest until they had found the home the seed was leading them to.\n\nThe group played their part in the evil times to come, the rise of the Undead and the Torment of Iblees. But this, like many things, is a different story.\n\nThe companions boarded an Elven ship on the shores of the verge. The Seed had brought them here,\n\nevil had driven them here. Throughout all they had suffered the Seed still shone bright. It was drawing them across the perilous ocean; it was calling them to Asulon. On reaching the shores of tis new land the Seed seemed to glow brighter than ever.\n\nThey knew after all these years, they were close. Bravepaw and his companions were loyal to the Elves. They stayed with them to protect their people until the Elves stopped in what later would become Malinor and where the Elvish city of Elandriel named\n\nthe Mother Tree, Bravepaw buried the Seed here, not understanding what he should do. They remained there fro many Elven weeks, a busy bustling city sprung up around them as the Elves settled into their new home and an Elven prince oversaw\n\nthe creation of a new Elven safehaven. Bravepaw never left the site where he planted the Seed at the foor of the Mother Tree. Until one fateful night he awoke.\n\nA blinding light erupted from where he planted the Seed. The light send sparks far to\n\nthe south and he heard a distant explosion. Bravepaw ripped the Seed from the earth. To his amazement, it had sprouted! (The mages of Normandor believe this to be a simple explanation: The Seed had somply forgotten how to be a tree.\n\nThe Mother Tree reminded it of this, however this will be explained in another Chronicle.) Bravepaw woke his comanions and they ran in the direction of the sparks. The Elder Seed glowing brighter than ever before emitting a single melodic tone the\n\ncloser they got to the site the sparks had landed.\n\nThey came to the sea;\nacross they saw a shorline, the top smouldering, glistening in the darkness, surely the site of the explosion. They swam across the shore, they were close now,\n\nand they knew it. They came to the top of the smouldering mass and stared down into the abyss. There a temple lay, surrounded by the darkness of the Voic. (The mages of Normandor believe this to have been the site of Mori ritual and sacrifice to the Void)\n\nDarkness filled their hearts, evil filled their minds; they all dropped to the floor, and the Void was consuming their very souls. As Bravepaw's mind became dark, his vision blurred and his warmth removed, he clutched the Seed tight.\n\nIn his head he heard the saying of his family he had always kept true, \"Light conquers evil, consumes darkness, embraces life and takes root even in the most darkened of places.\" Bravepaw's mind cleared, he saw... the impossible...\n\nThe ghost of his father and his dying words, \"When the Void surrounds you, look to our greatest source of light.\" Bravepaw's mind cleared, only for an instant, he knew what he must do. He mustered the last of his strength, and casted the Elder Seed into\n\nthe depths of the Void. Darkness filled him. Bravepaw and his companions were but lifeless corpses on the fringes of this foul temple and her Void.\n\nAs they lay there, something never seen before happened.\n\nShoots, roots, branches, leaves and vines sprouted from the all consuming darkness of the Void. Several of the vines carried Bravepaw and his comanions upwards, beneath them a tree like no other was growing. The Elder Tree had been born in Asulon!\n\nBravepaw and his companions awoke, gasping for air. They were astonished; they had awoken to find themselves on top of the world. Beneath them the Elder Tree creaked in the Asulonian winds and the leaves roared. It is not know how long the tree took to\n\nsprout, but Bravepaw and his comanions were sustained by its light and had been released from the clutches of the Void. They began to climb down its branches and sed her vines as ladders. When they reached the foot of the tree, they looked at eachother.\n\nThey had been given their home Travathian look to his comapnions, \"Normandor... Above sacred land.\"\n\nThe Elder Tree was visible from much of Malinor.\n\nMany journeyed to its shores, drawn by its light. Bravepaw, Genriel, Orlanded and Travathian appointed themselves as the Chiefs and Chiefesses of all of Normandor, founders, protectors, and rulers. They created the first High Council of Normandor\n\nto oversee its development. High Magister Kyrenn, High Commander Ithil, and High Lord Thrase now sit on the Council and oversee many different aspects of its development. They work with the Chiefs to ensure harmony and prosperity across all of Normandor\n\nand the Elder Tree. The inside of the Elder Tree and indeed the very top became space for many home and building and is home to some of the finest Elven architecture in the the lands.\n\nOn one fateful day the High Prince of the Elven lands of Malinor decided to journey to Normandor. He had heard the many tales of its beauty and tranquility. He had been busy securing the future of Malinor and it was not until now he found the time to\n\nobserve the Elder Tree in all her glory. On arriving at the bridhe and meeting Bravepaw, he could not believe his eyes. This truly was the place of Elven might and power. Its beauty and nature overwhelmed him. He consulted the High Elven Council and\n\ntalked to the Princess of Malinor. In his wisdom he dedcreed that the Elder Tree City of Normandor was to become Capital of all Malinor. The city of Elves, a bastion of Elvish power, home to the High Council Chambers and would house the Malinor's central\n\ngovernment. The citizens of Normandor rejoiced and celebrated. Bravepaw was appointed Pronce of Malinor and joined the other Princes and Princesses in the Malinorian Government.\nHis loyal companions and rulers of Normandor were declared as Lords\n\nand Lady of the Elven realm. The Elder Tree, reborn, reviyalised and rejoiced.\n\nOver the years as the Elder Tree has grown, its roots plunging ever deeper into the Void and its branches ever further into the heavens.\n\nThe Tree's arcane aura had expanded significantly. Many mages have been drawn to this raw arcane infusion and believe tremendous power can be drawn from it. This ultimately led to the establishment of the Normandorian college of mages;\n\nthe activities of which will be continued in a separate Chronicle.\n\nAll this leads us to the current day, as Normandor still stands strong.\nLong may she bring peace, stability and light to the Elves of Malinor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons IV", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "New Elven Lessons:\n     Volume 4\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\n\nIn elven, numbers are formed by the composition of multiple words. Each word representing the magnitude of the number. To note a number between one to ten the simple word in elven to use. To express a multiple of ten, an elven number is placed before\n\na multiple of ten.\n\nFor example: niut'matelu means 200.\n\n1 - oem\n2 - niut\n3 - hael\n4 - vailu\n5 - kulin\n6 - banih\n7 - laier\n8 - esun\n\n9 - moiel\n10 - telu\n100 - matelu\n1000 - marmatelu\n\nAnother particularly useful prefix not mentioned before is 'fer'. Fer is used in combination with seed words to form the names of handheld tools.\n\nSome such examples include those below. However, to those more advanced in elven others may be thought up. \n\nFer'ame - axe\nFer'thuln - pickaxe\nFer'nor - shovel\nFer'sul - torch\nFer'bilok - hammer\nFer'norsae - hoe", ""),
        StaticBook("Savages Of Oren", "§bDurza Volkihar", "The men of oren are vile savages.They attack and kill their own family and friends to seize power.They consider themselves the superior race and they believe all races are beneath them. I have been attacked multiple times by the knights of oren and have\n\nwitnessed my brethern be murdered just because of their race.I recently took part of a defense force for a dwarven city.I am not a dwarf but yet they accepted as one of their own kin.We held steadfast as the men of oren attacked the city.Mind you this was\n\non the coronation day of their new king.Now what does this say about the men of oren? It shows us that they celebrate their festivites by killing people.Now the knights of oren feel as if they have a right to rule the land and its inhabitants but they do\n\nnot have that right. Only a king has that right but their king does not do anything to stop them causeing havok everywhere they go. Knights are bound by a code but these knights do not follow those codes of chivalry. If you share these views come seek me\n\nout. Ill be waiting for you seek this symbol out\n\n\n\n\n[!] A red eagle is drawn at the bottom of the page.", ""),
        StaticBook("JayasJourney C2", "§bSofetios", "Jaya's\n        Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n      Chapter Two\n\n         Linink\n\nAs I woke up the next morning I couldn’t help but feel a bit afraid. Linink was one of the most important people in town and he was never really free.\n\nAlso, why was my Mom so worried last night? I stepped out of bed. Instead of the usual hardwood floor I was used to I was stepped on something lumpy and cold. I looked down and jumped back on my bed.\n\nThe weapons from last night where on the floor right next to my bed. \n\n“Jaya what’s all the racket?” Said my mom’s voice. It sounded like she was coming to my room. Quickly, I covered the weapons with my blanket.\n\nLike that would do anything, but it was worth a shot. My mom came in the door and said,\n\n“Jaya why is your blanket on the floor?” \n\n“Bad dream.” I Lied.\n\nMy mom frowned, bent over, and was about to pick up the blanket. I closed my eyes and cringed from what was about to happen. \n\n“Jaya are you ok?” Said my Mom concerned.\n\nOpening my eyes I saw my mom had folded the blanket and on the floor was nothing.\n\n“Uh, yea.” I said scratching my head. “I think I just must have hit my head.”\n\n“Well it’s a good thing your going to see Linink today.” My mom said. “Come on, breakfast is ready.”\n\nI ate very little breakfast this morning. The taste of it as usual was great, but the stress of what I thought was to come overcame my hunger. After breakfast my mom took me straight to The Adventurers Guild.\n\nAs I approached the massive building I started to get nervous. My mom opened the doors, led me past staring students, rooms that where full of weapons, and many more things.\n\n Finally we reached Linink’s Office. The large green door looked inviting enough but as to what was to happen behind it still worried me.\n\nWithout knocking a voice said, “Come in.” My mom and I entered the triangle shaped room. I saw Linink sitting a table in the middle, but beside the table on both sides where my friends Sofetios and Sofia.\n\nI relaxed a little. At least they would be here with me. “Jaya, would you please take a seat.” Said Linink coolly.  I took a seat, looked back at my mom, and Linink then said,  “I need to speak to Jaya and his friends alone Madam.”\n\nMy mom nodded and left the room quietly. Everyone was quite for a bit until I said, \n\n“What am I here for?” \n\n“I’d like to know that too.” Sofetios added.\n\n“Same here.” Said Sofia. After a moment Linink said,\n\n“We are here to discuss a recent series of events.”\n\n“Like what?” said Sofia. “Other then the Melonko Festival being today all that’s really happened was that Rainstorm last night.\n\n“Exactly my point” said Linink. “A rainstorm now? In the middle of summer? I just don’t really see that as natural. There is also the Prophecy.”\n\n“You mean that old tale everyone listens to at the festival?” Said Sofetios inquiringly.\n\n“Just that.” Said Linink seriously. “From what I’ve seen happening in the last two days I’m inferring that it may be coming true.” At this Sofia laughed and said,\n\n“Like that would happen now. I mean the rain was probably coincidence and it’s not like the weapons have been found.” At this I felt the blood drain from my face.\n\n“Well from what I heard from Jaya’s Mother last night, I think they may have been found.” Said Linink. Sofia and Sofetios look right at me and Sofetios said, “You didn’t really… I mean you couldn’t have…”\n\n“He probably didn’t” Said Sofia, Otherwise he would be wearing them right now. It’s not like he would leave them at his house or something if he found them. Right?” I looked slightly down at this comment.\n\n“The weapons only appear if the owner wants them to.” Said Linink. Sofetios turns to me and said. “Well Jaya? Did you actually find the weapons?” I tell them the whole story of what happened last night and this morning.\n\nWhen I finish, Sofia is staring at me in disbelief, Sofetios is too, and Linink looks the same as he did before. No one said anything for a while until Linink said,\n\n“Well I guess the prophecy is coming true.”\n\n“Should we tell everyone?” Said Sofia.\n\n“No.” said Linink. “That would only raise panic. We should just tell whoever really needs to be told then you three set off after the festival.”\n\n“Us three?” I said.\n\n“Yes.” Said Linink “You know both Sofia and Sofetios pretty well. Except for what each they specialize in.” I didn’t actually know what Linink taught Sofetios and Sofia in the Guild and they had never shown me.\n\nI gave an odd face to all three of them then Linink said, “To put it bluntly Sofetios is a magician and Sofia is a fighter, in class terms that is.” \n\n“A magician?” I repeated while looking at Sofetios.\n\n“Intermediate magician.” Said Sofetios. “Sorry but Linink said we couldn’t tell anyone outside the guild.” \n\n“Wait so what can you do?” I said. “Levitate stuff or something?” Sofetios looked at Linink and Linink nodded.\n\nAll of the sudden everything small in the room started to slowly floated upwards.  I froze and looked around.  Then the things in the air floated down to their original places.\n\n“You see Jaya, Everything we teach at this guild more or less has to do with Lin.”  Said Linink.\n\n“Lin?” I said curiously.\n\n“Yes, it is something that is in everything around us.” Said Linink. “Kind of like a fifth element so to speak. Sofetios will be teaching you about this on your travels.”\n\n“Wait.” I said. “There’s a whole Fifth element?”\n\n“Yes.” Said Linink simply. “Sofetios, Sofia, please get ready for your departure.”\n\n“But sir.” Said Sofetios. “We still-“\n\n“Come on Sofetios.” Said Sofia as he grabbed Sofetios on the shoulder and had him follow her. When they closed the door, Linink turned to me and Said. \n\n“You have a long journey ahead of you.”\n\n“Yes sir…” I said tentatively.\n\n“I just need to make sure you really have the weapons.” Said Linink concerned.\n\n“I would sir but I don’t know how to get them to appear.” I said.\n\n“Just hold your hand as you would your sword and try to will them there.” Said Linink. I did so and in a second a white sword materialized there. It felt warm in my hand. Linink seemed was taken aback a little, so I asked,\n\n“Sir, why me?” Linink seemed back as himself and said after a moment,\n\n“Because He chose you. At least that’s what the Prophecy sais.” Linink got up and went to his bookshelf.\n\nHe picked up two books and put them both on the desk. He opened one and the inside of it was hollowed out. All there was, was a semi-clear sphere about an inch long.\n\nHe handed it to me and said. “This is something I’ve been working on for a long time. Use it well.”  I sheathed the sword and took the sphere and said,\n\n“Sir, what is this?”\n\n“Don’t you recognize it?” Linink said surprised. “It is object from part of the lore they tell at the Melonko festival. Well, my version of it anyway.”\n\n“I’m sorry sir, I don’t really listen to the tales they tell.” I said a little embaraced.\n\n“Well then I should probably tell you.” Said Linink. “It is my version of a water sphere. This one I would say holds about 1 week worth of water for 3 people.” Unbelieving, I stared at the sphere.\n\n“All you need to do is heat it in something and water will come out.”\n\n“Sir?” I said. “What did you mean by ‘your version’?”\n\n“You’ll find out soon enough.” Said Linink. Suddenly there was music outside. “The festival is starting.”\n\n“Sir, what now?” I said.\n\n“Now, you go enjoy the festival.” Said Linink. “But before you go,” Linink picked up the other book and handed it to me. “This is a book on lore of Edrot. You may want to study it.”\n\n I turned to leave when Linink said, “and Jaya, two words of advice. First, with the powers you will soon possess, Make sure you use them the right way.\n\nSecondly, I need you to will away that sword for now. The people in town don’t need to see it.”\n\n“Is that all sir?” I said.\n\n“That’s all” Said Linink.\n\nEnd of Chapter Two\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C7", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                 Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n\n     Chapter Seven\n        Sadzten\n\nAs we got to Sadzten I couldn’t help but feel how dry it was. I looked at the caked ground and asked Sofetios,\n\n“Hey Sofetios, why is it so dry here?”\n\nSofetios looked around and said,\n\n“I think there could be a drought in this region. Let’s ask someone what is going on.”\n\n“Guys remember this is just a stop on the way.” Said Sofia.\n\n“We can’t stop for too long.” \n\nWe walked a while until we got to a great fountain. The disturbing thing was that no water was coming through it. There was a plaque on the fountain. It said,\n\n‘Tifantus’s Fountain\n-\nMay you always treasure the life in water’\n\n“Is someone there?” A voice from behind said. We turned around to see an old looking man.\n\n“Who are you.” Sofia Asked.\n\n“I’m the last person in this town.” The old man said. “At least I’m pretty sure.”\n\n“What happened here?” Asked Sofetios concerned. The man sighed and said motioning to a nearby house,\n\n“Please come in.” We followed him into the house. The old man sat down slowly and said, “Please, sit.” So we sat down.\n\n“I’m afraid its my son that happened.” Said the man.\n\n“About a month ago, My son Roth found a way to steal the treasure from the bottom of the lake.”\n\n“What!?” said Sofetios and Sofia together. “But, that’s impossible.” Said Sofetios.\n\n“Oh, its possible all right.” Said the old man. “It just takes someone willing enough to do it.” He got up and moved to the window. “You see out there?” He said. We got up and looked.\n\nThere was what looked like used to be a waterfall going into a empty crater. “That is Lake Edrot. Run dry.”\n\n“Dry?” Said Sofia. “What happened to make the water stop running?”\n\n“I guess its my fault on two accounts.” Said the old man. “You see, when I was a young boy about your age. I found a way to steal the treasure.\n\nThe current around the treasure was unbreakable, So I figured the only way to get the treasure would be from on top on it.” \n\n“The waterfall.” I said\n\n“Correct.” Said the old man. “At night, I climbed the waterfall, jumped, and landed straight on top of the treasure. Before the water swept me away, though I grabbed a gold coin.\n\n Next thing I knew a wave had risen in the water which washed me back to shore. Then to get worse the water spirit Tifantus appeared before me in the water. At first he was furious, but then suddenly amused.\n\nHe told me that as a token of my wit, I was allowed to keep the gold coin, But if anyone ever took from his treasure again, he’d cause a drought so bad that everyone would leave so no one would touch his treasure again.\n\nSo I thanked him fearfully and went off home.”\n\n“But how did your son steal from the treasure?” Asked Sofetios.\n\n“I told him how I did it as a bed time story when he was a youngster.” Said the old man. “I thought he thought that it wasn’t real. Little did I know my son had taken it to heart. I saw an entry in his journal saying he would go after it.\n\nAnd I think you could probably tell the rest of the story.”\n\n“So where is your son now?” I asked.\n\n“Well as soon I had realized what he was doing, I went out looking for him at the lake.\n\nI saw him take the dive and as he took a coin there was a great rumble and water rushed inward into the cave behind the waterfall, taking him and the treasure with it.”\n\n“How have you survived this long without water?” I asked. \n\n“Well surprisingly to me the water flows from the fountain for me.” Said the old man.\n\n“I guess it’s Tifantus’s way of telling me he still likes my wit, or maybe he’s making fun of me by giving only me water. Either way, Everyone is gone, and I’m without my son.” \n\n“I’ll get your son back.” I said.\n\n“You won’t be able to.” Said the old man. “That cavern is sealed shut. Only clue I had to the entry were the music notes on it.”\n\n“Music notes?” Said Sofetios.\n\n“Yes.” Said the old man. “I’ll show you.”\n\nWhen we arrived at the waterfall cavern entrance, we went down into a crevice in the floor where the water probably washed through into the cavern and Sofia lit a torch.\n\n“There it is.” Said the old man pointing to a door. We went closer until I stared in disbelief. The notes on the wall where not any notes. These were the beginning to The Song of Rain.\n\n“What is it Jaya?” Said Sofia\n\n“I’ve seen these notes before.” I said.\n\n“Young man!” said the old man. “The inside of your bag is on fire!” Startled I flung my bag off. When I realized it wasn’t on fire, but light was coming out of it.\n\nI walked to it and carefully unbuckled the buckle and some of my stuff fell out. One of them being a flute. The Flute. I picked it up and the light from it faded away.\n\n“You…” Said the man. “Your… the one from the prophecy.” \n\n“Yea…” I said still looking at the flute. I walked up to the stone and started to play The Song of Rain. Suddenly, at the end of it, I heard drops.\n\nI looked behind me and rain drops where starting to fall slowly, then they picked up pace.\n\n“Jaya!” Said Sofia. “What did you play?”\n\n“The Song of Rain.” I said.\n\nSuddenly water started trickling down the crevice we were in toward the door. There was a loud rumble and the boulder opened up a little bit, as if to just let the water through.\n\n Then more and more water began to build up. There was a loud roar like thunder. Suddenly the door raised itself fully and water rushed out. Just as this happened, Sofia grabbed the old man and threw him above the crevice.\n\nThe water slammed against us and then receded back into the cave, us with it.\n\nEnd of Chapter Seven\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Punishment III", "§bArchmage Crumena", "The Punishment of Hubris III\n\nIn the course of the first two-hundred and fifty years, as Nemiisae searched for a way to open the portal and leave this place, Zanunder aged within his sleep, eventually dying. Bereaved of her husband she fell into a great remorse for having\n\naccidentally killed him. Her mind became clouded, muddled, perhaps even mad. Then her children came to her with reports of these strangers in their lands. She realized then what had happened…The portal only shut on their side. It must\n\nhave been an act of God, she believed. Then she realized, it was a test! As God had tested the Four Brothers, surely he was testing her and these others to become stronger. But her compassion would not allow her to let others fall victim to this trap\n\nshe had unwittingly played a part in. She could not reopen the portal, but she could close it from her side, sealing off both the portal to the Verge and the portal within it to the new world. Then she retreated back into her Caverns, encouraging her\n\nchildren to live, breath, fight, grow stronger. Punish and perish the weak and live for themselves and for her, for it was the only way to gain God’s favor. Then she left them to their own devices, her wishes for their future made clear.\nIt was in this\n\nway that hubris was punished, that the sins of those who came before was tested and they were proven guilty. Had these people physically gone to these lands, surely the curse would not have killed them all. But by passing through the\n\nportal of Hubris which Nemiisae had created, they doomed themselves and their kin. Other groups found the portals between the time Nemiisae realized what had happened and closed it off, but anyone who came through was doomed to suffer and die.\n\nThere was no hope for them as soon as they had passed through those portals into that world. But it is far enough removed that between the first settling of it and our time, no one has ever discovered it again. Beyond churning, whirling seas,\n\ndeadly islands, leagues and weeks away from the lands settled by the Four Brothers, it would be impossible to reach without the assistance of a very strong force indeed. But perhaps it is for the best, that these ruins remain ruins, and the skeletons\n\ngo undisturbed, lest we awaken old evils...", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elves.", "§bGarsto Leaf", "Those of the High Elf bloodline can usually be pointed out for their very long ears, platinum hair, and the golden tint to their fair skin. This tint is complemented by their hair, which is usually \nblonde, though silver and light brown hair is not\n\nunheard of. Their eyes range from hues of green to blue, occasionally even purple. It is also not uncommon for an High Elve's eye color to become darker as they age, revealing the accumulation of wisdom. They are the tallest of elves, and are usually\n\nquite thin, making them the sub-race worst suited for physical combat.\n\nDespite this they often excel at the use of arcane magic. They often have a strict code which governs their lives, and have a distinct hate for impurity and half-breeds.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of Aegis", "§bLelien", "Fall of Aegis\n \n       by Native\n\nThe miasma in the North lingered ever more so. Galahar was evacuated and the Cloud Temple became our final stand. From the Temple I shouted out into the crowds, summoning those who were chosen by the Nations as their champions. Upon arriving in\n\nLaurelin, I called all of the champions into Dawn’s Bakery, where a secret entrance lay.\n\nThe High Priestess handed out blessed armour pieces enchanted in Aeriel’s grace to each of the champions. We then took a small passage, into what was once the\n\nLaurelin Gauntlet. Entombed in a massive oak tree, lay Vardak’s portal from the Nether.\n\nThe champions gaze into the portal and grip the hilts of their weapons tightly.\n\nI step out of the way of the portal, clenching my soulstone in my hand tightly and wish them good lucl. As I vanish, the brave few enter head first.\n\nSpoken by Native the Elf in the Deep Cold, 1351", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lone Tree", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "=======()======\n ===-=- ========\n ======/\\ ===-=-\n =====/__\\ =====\n =====/   \\ =====\n ====/____\\ ====\n ===== _U_======\n ===,_/     \\_====\n ==/_______ \\===\n “The Lone Tree” \n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Sun's Yellow Gaz", "§bWilburn Ellingworth", "Sun's Yellow Gaze\nBy: Wilburn Ellingworth\n\nThe sun's yellow gaze shines up on the horizon,\nBirds sing along with this soft melody,\nDespite what they think, they don't know just where I've been,\nSo don't sing along 'til you understand me. There was once a time when my life was just average,\n\nLiving apart from those children's stories,\nBut then things did change when I sat up on that ridge. When to that new world something gave me the keys. I found myself bearing a cold suit of armor, Fighting a beast of immense strength and speed.\n\nEyes wide in awe at how I'd become stronger,\nI suddenly found myself fall to my knees. I stood now in darkness, a cave black as midnight,\nTrembling in fear, what would come from within? But what I saw next was not quite such a great sight,\n\nThe horror I felt then stabbed me like a pin. On the floor there lay a corpse of quite great size,\nCoated with crimson that shone in the night, The same kind of beast I'd just seen with my own eyes,\nBut this one had children curled up by its side.\n\nRight at this moment I chose to stop fighting,\nThe sword I had wielded fell down to my feet,\nNot caring if the beast chose to keep biting,\nAn ending of death I would not let it meet. The sun's yellow gaze shines up on the horizon.\n\nBirds sing along with this soft melody,\nDespite what they think, they don't know just where I've been,\nSo don't sing along 'til you understand me", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem of Nature", "§bEndrai Denthrular", "A poem of nature\nBy Endrai Denthrular.\n\nOh great tree and forest amongst the main circle       How strong your bond must be with the druids that co-exist with you\nYour leaves are as beautiful maybe even more beautiful than the ones at the Spring Circle near Haelun'or\n\nAnd your roots, deeper than any grove in all this world\nHow great your bond must be with the druids that reside with you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eloluern'ne II", "§bDio Astóre", "Further study confirms that the mana required to sustain Eloluer’ne is prodigious. Mana fed into it will diminish passively, disappearing entirely within moments unless anchored or linked to suitable shielding.\n\nEven so, such protective measures must be actively maintained. Modification to the Gate component could reduce the required frequency of re-entering.\n\nDue to its intermediary nature, certain artefacts evoked within Eloluer’ne can be sustained even by unshaped mana, so long as the artefact was initially engineered to work at various stages of damage.\n\nOnly highly skilled practitioners could feasibly arrange such a thing, but the range of applicable disciplines is not limited.\n\nI theorise that apart from utilisation of the soulstone itself, the most effective alternative would be any magic that has a nullifying effect on mana or which actively feeds on it.\n\nGreat care must be taken and precision exercised to avoid accidental damage to any of the constructs. Diligence too should be afforded to ensuring their continued operation.\n\nThe effect of the passive diminishment does not seem to take place from a fixed point or direction, but rather occurs at all positions simultaneously. Anyone introducing or maintaining constructs within must therefore take this phenomenon into account.\n\nFollowing the design logic of the Golden Pools and the water conduits of old Haelun’or, the redirection of mage-gold and seamless integration of discrete water features could allow for a slow yet progressive siphoning of mana to power Eloluer’ne.\n\nShowers, fountains and bathing areas are all viable for connecting to Eloluer’ne. Heated water is recommended to mask any fatigue that may be noticeable after a prolonged session of immersion.\n\nIt is advised that children are prevented from entering such areas and instead be directed to any that are unconnected.\n\nIntroduction of a sanitation policy would compliment progress, however whether foreigners too should be used is a matter of discretion. In the positive case, such facilities are to be kept to the exterior of the city proper.\n\nCorrupted beings may yield unpredictable results, though the purification of Eloluer’ne shall indubitably cleanse those parts it deems unfit.\n\nWith regular attention it should be possible the construct a device within Eloluer’ne that operates in a similar manner to a portal, delivering those that are worthy to the promised lands.\n\n§o§6Lye’sae ito celian.\n\n§lOOC Notes:\n§rNo positive or negative effects need to be roleplayed.\n\nAlmost everything disappears inside the pocket dimension of Eloluer’ne. Exceptions include soulstones, people and anything with mana.\n\nHow fast something disappears depends mostly on mana levels, intellect and willpower. Any devices built inside need to be protected and fixed regularly.\n\nSiphoning is mild and could make a character tired or hungry, depending on how energetic / healthy / rested they are. If a character is sickly, optional prolonged weakness is possible if they choose.\n\nA character staying too long inside Eloluer’ne will feel pain when returning, but this is never fatal. Absent-mindedness, drowsiness, forgetfulness and emotional changes would scale with time, but are all optional and effects vary from person to person.\n\nThe portal - if completed - would be powered by a soulstone. If used, an imperfect copy of the persona would be made in another universe.\n\nThis either has no effect on the current character or perma-kills them and destroys the soulstone used. Visual effects depend on personality and aura colours.\n\nIf you want a part of your character’s story to continue in another game / world, feel free to use this to link them together.\n\nThe dream goes on...", ""),
        StaticBook("H: Aegis-Asulon", "§bDio Astóre", "Haelun’or - the ancestral home of the Mali’aheral - has a recorded history which is incomplete due to various causes, omission, destruction, as well as challenges posed by gaps in time and space, considerable to even the Mali themselves.\n\nThe following describes credible events regarding the formation and history of Haelun'or.\n\nAncient tomes of lore make mention of a point in time where little difference existed between the progenitors of the many diverse races that now live within the realm.\n\nWhilst the facticity of this is disputed, as time progressed the years that saw Malin’s children separate into distinctness drew closer.\n\nRegarded as the beginning of this timeline was the birth of its most esteemed individual: the daughter scholars came to know as Larihei Lohmanih and the one the Mali’aheral came to revere as the mother of their kind and its culture.\n\nThought to have been conceived by a member of Malinor’s High Council - largely on account of her influence with the populace - she would eventually become a controversial figure at odds with the prevailing traditions of Mali culture.\n\nTheories suggesting the causes for this vary; views that the aggressiveness of the younger races threatened Mali way of life, disapproval of Mali complacency in regards to worldly affairs or that immortality heightened the status of Mali.\n\nWhilst the original ideals are left for future generations to interpret via the remnants of the culture, it may be said that her influence had powerful matriotic qualities.\n\nUltimately Larihei and a portion of her supporters segregated from the main body of Mali society.\n\nMoving on to build a private settlement, the contents of nearby water sources would become a vital part of Mali'aheral cultural development and in turn influence the distinct physical features of the people.\n\nThis process is recognised as both natural and magical; from the exclusiveness of bloodlines to the activities which they partook in ritualistically, the gold-laden water itself later becoming an important symbol of the ideology: maehr’sae hiylun’ehya.\n\nIn the cradle of their newfound home the search for more prosperous futures begun anew and once more the Mali’aheral would take steps to exempt themselves from a world that they viewed to be riddled with danger, guided by Larihei Lohmanih.\n\nThose families known to be reluctant in their adoption of the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya electing to stay behind, the great majority would trust in the wisdom of their leader and so would begin upon a path that would bring them to the realm of Asulon.\n\nRecords of this period become scarce, however after arriving to Asulon their efforts at establishing a sanctuary succeeded and culminated in at least the south-western portions of the Emerald Isle falling within the boundary of ancient Haelun’or.\n\nLittle evidence exists to suggest expansions were made. Historical items remain a focal point for some present-day Mali’aheral scholars. For reasons not yet understood the civilisation diminished and the structures left decayed, turning to ruins.\n\nMany years later those Mali’aheral that had chosen to remain behind in Aegis were forced to flee from their own forthcoming doom, brought by the scourge of Iblees and the Daemon’s undead servants.\n\nTraversing the Verge - a hostile land reached through a portal near the Aegisian Cloud Temple - they would sail across its waters to find the shores of Asulon.\n\nDiscovering the ruins of Haelun'or College, these Mali'aheral would make their home there, separate from their woodland and dusken kin.\n\nOriginally little more than a scholar's camp situated at the base of the College, an ever increasing need for more elaborate forms of organisation became apparent whilst translations progressed on those documents that were intact in the library.\n\nIt would not be long before land-claim disputes would be brought forth. Their history threatened, a gathering of various pathfinders and researchers took place, among them Mali'aheral seeking to reclaim the home of their forebears.\n\nOpinions were mixed and numerous challenges were presented for the right to the future of Haelun’or. Pathfinders vouched for their priorities of finding, scholars would advocate preservation of the site, nobility fought for control of more estate.\n\nThe lore within the College bolstered support that Haelun'or was appropriately Mali'aheral inheritance.\n\nDeciding through majority vote that they would follow in their ancestors footsteps by reinstating the Heial’thilln - the Silver Council comprised of seven governing seats - new persons were elected to fill six of these positions.\n\nThe role of Okarir’Tayna - the most esoteric role of governance - fails to find a successor.\n\nIndependent now, the ruined city saw an influx of visitors which the resources of the land were not equipped to provide for. A decision not made lightly, colonising the island became a priority for the modest yet growing population.\n\nAgriculture begun to sustain the residents, refurbishments to the structures made, shelters were erected and oft revised as Haelun’or became the image of a fledgling city-state, one without substantial military resources or engineered protection.\n\nPolitically neutral, some official exceptions existed. A mutually defensive arrangement made with the neighbouring nation of Malinor - itself annulled at a future date for a violation of terms.\n\nThere was also a brief period of asylum provided to the Kharajyr - with whom they maintained good relations.\n\nThe Valah had shown themselves willing to aid Haelun'or in dire times, though no official stance was ever taken.\n\nDespite their insistence on avoiding violent affairs, the Mali’aheral suffered multiple assaults upon Haelun’or.\n\nAll grievances resulted in further fortification and eventually decreased tolerance towards outsiders, forming a violent cycle that strengthened the more radical interpretations of the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya.\n\nDevelopment of the Silver City continued and among the creations made were agricultural islands, apothecaries, astronomy towers, aviaries, bookstores, dockyards, laboratories, markets, medical practices, taverns, theaters and workshops.\n\nThe original structure known as Haelun'or College serving as the central hub for fulfilling the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fishing Song", "§bMelodystar", "Katie's Fishing Song\n\nOne, Two, Three, Four, Five!\n\nOnce I caught a fish alive!\n\nSix, Seven, Eight, Nine, Ten!\n\nThen I let it go again!\n\nWhy did you let it go?\n\nBecause it bit my finger so!\n\nWhich finger did it bite?\n\nThis little finger on my right!", ""),
        StaticBook("An Old Note", "§bCeruberr Asul'Ailer", "~*~*~\n   A Silent Admiration\n\nIt began years ago, when I first laid eyes upon her in the grand city of Lin'everal. There she sat, under a willow, transfixed in a book. Her hair seemed to be an endless stream of gold, laying down upon her simple\n\nyet beautiful dress of blue. My heart seemed to skip a beat as she glanced up towards me, her eyes almost seemed to shimmer with a brilliant teal. I found myself for the first time in my life, speechless...\n\nMonths went by and every day, I continued to admire her beauty. Although it was not only her beauty that had me spellbound. She was the keeper of the Eternal Library, intelligent, witty and studied the arcane.\n\nEventually the months turned to years, and\n\nthe years to decades. \n\nI couldn't act upon my feelings. I was too young. But I didn't know if I'd ever have the courage to act upon them.\n\n*The note seems to have ended here. It appears to be very old and a name can\n\nbe seen faintly at the bottom of the page*\n\nCeruberr Asul'Ailer", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem to Kalenz", "§bIkur Seregon", "*A letter is delivered, sealed with wax.*\n\nDearest Kalenz Uradir,\nI do think it is time to tell you that you are dear\n\nCertain am I of your purity,\n\nYet of your love for me, there is an insecurity\n\nWe could progess as fortold in the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya\n\nEnding at a butterfly, and beginning as gastraea.\n\nI do hope your love will be reciprocated\n\nYour response is anticipated\n\n\n(Do so by planting a poppy in front of the entrance of the clinic)", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "Pinsir99", "Mundane Healing\nBy Unknown\n\nCopied by Aerius Adurond.\n\nMatron’s Foreword:\nWhen I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange Dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients for the treatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien.\n\nOne or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery or internal organs with nothing but rose thorns and petals.\n\nIn the interest of not wasting precious paper, I’ve recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one of two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n\n\nMinor Cut (Matron)\nSimply apply a dose of deceased sentient slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it. The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n\n\nHeadache (Aleya)\nBoil milk, Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n\n\nStomach Ache (Matron)\nBoil water. Once it hits a full boil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber colour. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n\nSoreness (Aleya)\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax he muscles, and rest a lot.\n\nBurns (Matron)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere.\n\nThe important thing about burns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist and not evaporate as water would.\n\nBe sure to check the burn wound daily until the skin can finally reform.\n\nFever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim’s body cool using cold water. Give him hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sci Method", "§bFinris'ta ovl Haterin", "-------------------          SCIENCE\n        --------\n\nScience the very word that is used by those who pursue knowledge of all kinds. This also would imply that Science is another word for knowledge in the common tongue.\n\nScience itself being the pursuit of knowledge in either a physical or philosophical mannerism. Though science is also the method of putting knowledge together to shape an answer.\n\nThis however can be done in many different ways, depending on the acceptance of the population at large. However for those of higher intelligence science is mostly regarded as organizing testable explanations and predictions.\n\n This meaning that even if something seems logical to assume this is not an answer but rather part of the Hypothesis.\n\nThose who pursue science are more commonly known as scientists, however this is not always what they are called.\n\nBecause of the broad term of who is a practitioner of science for people at large. Therefore some that are practitioners of science go by other names but in the end they are still scientists.\n\n Those who follow science all commonly share a mentality, this being the acceptance of failure. One should always critique oneself, as a scientist who is unable to make mistakes is not a scientist.\n\n This is what could be referred to as pseudo-science, as they do not accomplish actual science but a fake reality of it. This is very important as not to corrupt your own scientific research.\n\n If you are someone who does this type of science, know that when you are proven to be a liar it is highly possible your science will forever be questioned.\n\nTherefore i digress further, do not attempt this pseudo-science as it’s the very taint of our scientific society.\n\nIt’s also known well that within science it’s very much expected that you keep documentation of your work in the form of text.\n\nThis is a vital step in making sure that discovered science is not lost and can be reproduced for future generations. However it’s also widely known that this is not a mindset that all agree with.\n\nThere are people who would rather have their finds die with them or groups who find secrets and keep them to please their greed. This is also something that makes Mali’aheral different from many other scientific practitioners.\n\nWe work as a group to find solutions and maehr’sae within our community. This makes us the prime example of actual science and therefore we should always strive to fulfill our maehr’sae hiylun’ehya.\n\n-------------------       METHODOLOGY\n     ------------\n\nMethodology not a word to be confused with method as it is not something that is supposed to answer a question or provide solutions.\n\n Methodology can in many ways be compared to ideology as it is more a way of thinking or a process that may or may not result in better results.\n\n It is more the way you perceive your scientific study and how it is from your perspective supposed to be shaped. Therefor a theoretical analysis of the methods applied to a field of study.\n\n Methodology therefore strives more to provide you a way to find what set of methods you wish to use. This essentially being a way to lay the framework, for the possible best way to go about your research.\n\n In a shorter way of explaining Methodology is the entire framework of your research, and all the things you have done within it. If you decide to use mathematics or a witness as your first step then this is the first step in your methodology.\n\n-------------------      EPISTEMOLOGY\n    -------------\n\nEpistemology is understanding of knowledge in every sense very philosophical in origin.\n\nIt concerns itself with the nature and scope of knowledge at large and can be recognized as ‘’the theory of knowledge’’.\n\nIt questions what knowledge is and how it can be acquired, and the extent to which knowledge pertinent to any given subject or entity can be acquired. This meaning that if you were to become ill you might assume you will recover quickly.\n\nHowever this does not mean that you are infact going to recover quickly. Therefor this is not a good way of acquiring knowledge. However in the eyes of those who use logic only this can be a way of acquiring knowledge.\n\nThis is why Epistemology looks upon the nature of acquiring knowledge rather than what works and what does not\n\n-------------------        RATIONALISM\n      -----------\n\nRationalism the belief in reason, logic and rational and the very concept that everything can be found through logical thinking.\n\nThey see reason as the main source and test of knowledge. In rationalism the criterion of the truth is not sensory but instead intellectual and deductive.\n\nThose who follow rationalism is what is called rationalists and they believe reality has a intrinsically logical structure. Because of this belief rationalists argue that certain truths exists and that the intellect can directly grasp these truths.\n\nThe rationalists assert that certain rational principles exist in logic, mathematics, ethics and metaphysics that are so fundamentally true that denying them causes one to fall into contradiction.\n\nThe rationalists have such a high confidence in reason that proof and physical evidence are unnecessary to ascertain truth. They believe there are significant ways in which our concept and knowledge are gained independently of sense experience.\n\n-------------------         EMPIRICISM\n       ----------\n\nEmpiricism the belief in evidence and what one can physically see and touch. They believe strongly that science is only that which can be proven and reproduced and not miracles.\n\nIf something happens it does so for a reason, and because of a chain of events which can be reproduced.\n\nThey are also the scientific communities pen and paper figures, as they document all of their findings and exact descriptions as to accomplish reproduction.\n\nIf someone approaches a Empiricist without evidence when presenting something, it is highly unlikely that they will care as much contrary to if you did.\n\nThey also believe that knowledge is based on experience and that knowledge is a tentative and probabilistic, subject to continued revision and falsification.\n\nThe mindset of the empiricist also makes them more keen to do a lot of experiments towards their scientific research. Their great tenant being that sensory experience creates knowledge.\n\nThe scientific method, including experiments and validated measurement tools, guides empirical research.\n\n-------------------           COMMON\n\n        SCIENTIFIC\n\n       METHODOLOGY\n\n-------------------\n      ------------\n\n------------------- -------------------\n\n      Observations\n      -----------\n\nObservations are simply to observe something and then studying this in various ways. This can all be different depending on the scientist though a example will be provided:\n\nIf you observe what you believe is a new species of butterflies were you a empiricist, Then the first step one would start with is collecting a physical sample to ensure validity.\n\nThen afterwards you would start observing this sample. This is the very nature of observation and a very good example though there are many ways to go about observation.\n\n        QUESTION\n       ---------\nQuestion the very thing you start doing after you have acquired something or are in the midsts of observing. This is a step towards building your own perspective and stepping stones towards your hypothesis.\n\nYou question the objects functions or eventual attributes and other subjects depending on the scientist.\n\n       HYPOTHESIS\n      -----------\n\nHypothesis the very fragment of belief you have in what can come to happen and what you think is correct.\n\nIt is your assumption of something what you are striving to test to see if it is correct. This ties in with prediction however they are both very much entwined.\n\n       PREDICTION\n      -----------\n\nThe prediction state is very much like the Hypothesis however this step is a much more expansive one. This is where you quickly test things to confirm or deny your eventual predictions.\n\nIn the end if the hypothesis is correct you move back to predicting more possible outcomes. This is also a very vital part that plays into testing.\n\n           TEST\n           ----\n\nTesting this is what you do last after you have done all the necessary steps and precautions. This is where you test your hypothesis and prediction from earlier.\n\nWhen you get a result of some sort you note it down and document it. Now if the test is positive then you move into the phase of predicting more possible outcomes or possibilities.\n\nHowever if the test is negative then you move back and make a new hypothesis.\n\n\n-Finris'ta ovl Haterin", ""),
        StaticBook("In Aurum Alchima", "§bVaclav Pascal", "//In Aurum Alchimia\\\\\n\nItaque ut aurum Alchemist historiae mutare propositum, et memoria ejus, et in cognatione sua. Salve Pascal.\n\n-Vaclav Pascal\n\n-> Chapitre I\n\nThe alchemist stand is a fine and packable device. It's easier packed depending on the size. The alchemist stand is an iron stand with three clips for bottles, under the bottles will be stone oil burners.\n\nEach stone burner is a small square sized stone slab, grooves dug in for the oil to be burned, and heat the potion. The clamps must be tight to hold the bottles exactly three inches over the burner.\n->.. aurum et Alchemist stetit.<-\n\n->Chapitre II\n\nThe Bottles. A brew can be different by even the bottle used to brew the potion. Neck Bottles, Screw Bottles, and even the special Alchemist Fire Bottle. An alchemist is to be able to blow their own bottles.\n\neach bottle must have a neck, so its able to be clamped onto an alchemist stand easily, and heated. Each bottle will also have its own cork, make sure each cork blocks air, and liquid alike, keeping the bottle safe.\n\n->Chapitre III\n\n    Alchemist Bases\n\nWater> Low Tier potions, weak brews.\n\nDistilled Water> Medium Tier potions, greater brews.\n\nAqua Vitae> High Tier Potions.\n\n-> Water\nWater must be clean, and fresh from a flowing source of water, and bottled cold.\n\n-> Distilled Water\nThe water must be boiled into a glass tube, and cooled until it drips back into pure water Using a distill.\n\n->Aqua Vitae\ndistilled liquor or wine. It is to be boiled into a glass tube, and the spirits must be collected clean.\n\n->Chapitre IV\n       The Elements.\n\n  Each element has its own special effects to a brew. Fire, allows the destruction, burning, effects. Water, allows cooling, Healing, Createing effects. Earth allows Healing, and life affects. Air\n\nbrings affects of rapid, spreading, and speed. \n\n->Earth\n>Goblin's Ivy(Vine)\n>Alabaster Leaf (Oak Leaf)\n>Tippen's Root(Dead Shrub)\n>Saffvil(Grass)\n\n->Air\n>Crouching Feather(Feather)\n>Swamp Blossom(Vine)\n>Elf's Hair Vine(String)\n->Water\n>Serpant's Stalk(Lily Pad)\n>Frost Vine(Vine)\n>Athin(Cactus Green)\n>Zawabate(Yellow Folower)\n\n->Fire\n>The Dwarf's Pumpkin\n(Pumkin)\n>Elrow Berries\n(Rose Red)\n>Drake's Tail\n(Dead Shrub)\n>Blood Lotus\n(Red Flower)\n\n->Other Ingredience\n>Lard\n(Porkchop)\n>Yak Liver\n(Beef)\n>Seaweed\n(Vine)\n>Fish Parts\n(Fish)\n>Blood\n(Redstone Dust)\n>Liver\n(Fermented Spidereye\n\n>Lungs, Flesh\n(Rotten Flesh)\n-------------------\n\n  Ita expedito Alchemist aurum, et qui sequebantur succedant..", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elven Curse", "§bAsul'athri Parir'taliyu", "Conjectures On the Subject of the Aged Elven Mind\n-----------------\nI write this now to you, dear elven reader, to forewarn you of the curses bestowed upon our elven race.\n\nFor it is as the Bronze say, that the elves were not cursed once,\n\nbut by twice. The second elven curse is that of inevitable insanity, stemming from our long lives.\n\nThis insanity is common to all elves and every elf whom lives with pure blood - I say not in the fashion that we high elves have made it, but I say it in\n\nthe looser terms of the wood and dark elves below us, whom distinguish not between silver, bronze, and onyx - only between the children of Malin and those whom are not.\n\nAll whom live too long ages and bearing pure elven blood shall be\n\nsubject to the weight of thought and experience, and their minds shall fold like a piece of parchment in the water.\n\nNow, if a life is lived twice as fast, twice as strong, it shall be lived like a flame, which burns twice as bright but dies twice as\n\nquick. And so the mind folds.\n\nMany of us display this insanity even now, in violence, irrationality, psychopathy, and all sorts.\n\nIn most elves, the signs begin to display themselves in the ages of 500 to the thousandth year,\n\nwherein it should first manifest as incredible stubbornness, rigidity, and volatility and/or depression, or other neuroses.\n\nIn time, these symptoms shall continue to the point that the individual can no longer take active part in society, either due to\n\nbeing highly dangerous or just incapable of actively providing to the community. \n\nRegardless, the insanity besets itself on any elf, and can beset itself at the age of 100 and all the way until the thousandth year, depending on the given elf's lifestyle\n\nand personal experiences. The elf should thus take great care to live life slowly, rationally, and emotionally full, without neglecting either mind or emotional response. When life is lived in balance, then balance shall be in the elf, and this is what\n\nall elves should strive for and is encompassed in every philosophy - in the Bronze Codes of the Wood Elves, the Druidic Laws of the Druian, the ancestral ways of elmali'ker, and elmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya of my own people.\n\nBy Asul'athri Parir'taliyu\n\nWritten on the 12th of Malin's Welcome, 1506", ""),
        StaticBook("Ryker's Research", "§bAntonious", "Hair changes from its natarual color and progressivly turn lighter and lighter until silver-white.\nEye color seems to change colors lighter, than sporadically, than the lightest form of the original color. Skin color progressivly spreads and spreads -\n\nbecoming a blueish hue. Memory seems to slowly lack in random areas, long-term and short-term.\nNo nausea, and rare peircing migraines.\nLoss of balance occurs during the migraines.\n\nBedrest helps memory partially, but is not very effective. Facepaint can cover the afflicted facial skin to prevent people like Miriel calling you an ugly monster.\n\nIf Thanhium Poisoning afflicts the brain, it should be absorbed into the blood. Siphoning out the blood and filtering it is a valid option. The only other treatment option you could try is decapitation, or eating more Thanhium until you die.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pigmen", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "A Brief History\n     of Pigmen:\n   Aegis - Kalos\n\n  by Sunshine Druid\n         Verden\n\nThe appearance of Zombie Pigmen was first documented during the Second Iblees Invasion, several hundred years ago. These unnatural monsters were used by the Fallen Daemon as powerful soldiers during his war of conquest against the mortal races of\n\nAegis, where their group mentality and shear ferocity was crippling to the defenders. Unlike other lesser Undead, the Zombie Pigmen possessed an intellect far superior to any common Zombie or Skeleton. THey would always be seen in possession of\n\njagged, golden swords and very rarely were encountered alone.\n\nTheir speed was almost on par with that of the living, a trait that allowed few the luxury of escaping. After the invasion was ended and the Dark One had been sealed away for good, many\n\nstrange things were observed by the population of Aegis. While the mindless Zombies and Skeletons continued to attack anyone on sight, the Pigmen did not. They had become passive, almost completely indifferent to the world around them.\n\nInstead of mindlessly killing, they began to aimlessly roam the world, staring blindly at the things around them as if they weren’t truly there. After Aegis had crumbled and sank into the sea, many thought they would never see the creatures again.\n\nAnd, indeed, they didn’t. For a time. But, again, the Pigmen emerged from the unknown, and they were furious. For many years the Pigmen were found roaming the darkest corners of Asulon and attached anyone foolish enough to get close. The reason for this\n\nis not clear, an many theories have arisen to explain. However none have been proven. Yet another strange event was observed on the island of Elysium.\n\nA large volcano near the temporary Elven settlement erupted and spewed lava over the\n\nMalinor farms; and the Pigmen rode it down the slope. They were, thankfully, peaceful this time; but they appeared in numbers never seen before. Hundreds of them began to blindly wander from their lair, spilling over the border into the Orcish deserts.\n\nThere they were destroyed not by men, nor by beast, but by cacti. The creatures tore themselves to shreds over the next few months as they walked through the cacti farms, and they would still if it wasn’t for the piles of their dead brethren impeding\n\ntheir movement.\n\nSince arriving in Anthos there has only been one reported case of Pigmen. This was a very small issue, where only three or four Pigmen would wander around a border wall in the Wilds. A logical fpi,tao, was placed at this\n\nsite, and all has been quiet since then.\n\nIf the Pigmen are here on Anthos, they are hiding very well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sullasian Stack", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The Sullasian Stack\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\n\nOne of many old technological marvels I have created in my century of habitation with the exalted mali'aheral is the device by which one can create small amounts of artificial lighting (or \"sub-lightning\" as is the proper term). One would usually go\n\non to explain the methods by which he created such a device, but this tome is but a guide for its creation, and not so much its uses. Let us end, then, this frivolous banter, and begin the instruction.\n\nIngredients\nFirst, one advises you to retrieve the items required for the stack's creation prior to reading the instructions (the reader may appreciate the logic in such a decision). Firstly, you will need a smith to smelt and shape metallic \"discs\"\n\nor \"plates\" of a flat variety. The size of said plates is not especially important, but they must be uniform in their appearance and diameter. The plates themselves are made of two metals often mixed together for use in brass implements - copper, and\n\nspelter (One would suggest inquiring about the material at your local smithery). There must be equal numbers of said plates for use in the device. Note that the more plates that are available, the more powerful the device's effect will be.\n\nSecondly, a number of other metallic parts will be required for the device's construction--namely two strips of copper (no thicker than the width of a finger) and two iron prongs roughly of the same width. The prongs will need to be joined at the end of\n\neach copper strip. One suggests leather strips to be best for binding the two. Thirdly, one will require lengths of cloth (preferably wool or cotton) as well as a bottle of brine water. The cloth must be ripped into smaller lengths approximately the size\n\nof the copper and spelter plates. Optionally, one may create an upright \"stand\" for these plates to be housed in. It is not necessary, but it makes moving the device and holding it in place far more simple.\n\nMethod\nFirstly (provided you have built the stand), place the (non-pronged) end of a copper strip upon the bottom of the stand. After this, place the first of your copper plates upon it, and then place a spelter plate atop the copper one. You shall\n\nthen take one of your pre-organised lengths of cloth, and douse it liberally with the brine-water. Once it is thoroughly drenched, place this upon the spelter plate. This copper-spelter-brine rag is referred to by myself as a \"unit.\" The effect of the\n\nstack increases as you add further units. One suggests at least ten before performing the final step. After you have placed the appropriate number of units, place the second copper-prong between the final copper and spelter plates. This is out of\n\npracticality rather than garnering the best effect, as you would doubtlessly desire to keep the strip from moving around. The stack is now ready for use.\n\nOperation\nNever, under any circumstances, touch both prongs with your bare hands, nor should you attempt to hold the stack with more than one bare hand. The stack is a fascinating device, but the pain of accidentally shocking oneself is not\n\nparticularly pleasant. Always wear proper protection at all times while operating it. This includes: clamps to hold the prongs, thick leather gloves for your hands, and at least a leather apron to protect yourself from any other accidents. Always apply\n\nthe two prongs directly to your target, or there will be no effect.", ""),
        StaticBook("Brown Fungi", "§bUnknown", "Brown Fungi\n\n       by Unknown\n\nThese fungi seem to sprout a lot slowly although grow with a top cap not bent over, this cap follows the sun blocking it out as mushrooms smaller would grow underneath and spout out, although the brown mushroom would decay quicker than the toadstools\n\nthey will kill or decay a lot more of their surroundings, helping nature’s peace. These mushrooms are handy although not efficient in hot or cold climates, since the stem would be too weak and break or burn in any hot or cold climate.\n\nThese mushrooms are also used for mushroom soup to counter the toadstools drugged effect and give a very tasteful and filling meal. These mushrooms are great for around people, although try not to breathe in most of the spores as they will endanger\n\nyour life span or your life in general.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poisons", "Teerz", "Posions\n\nPlant name\n\nPart\n\nSymptoms\n\nHyacinth\n\nBulb\n\nNausea, vomiting, diarrhea. May be fatal.\n\nNarcissus\n\nBulb\n\nNausea, vomiting, diarrhea. May be fatal.\n\nDaffodil\n\nBulbs\n\nNausea, vomiting, diarrhea. May be fatal.\n\nOleander\n\nLeaves, branches\n\nExtremely poisonous. Affects the heart, produces severe digestive upset and has caused death.\n\nDieffenbachia \n\nAll parts\n\nIntense burning and irritation of the mouth and tongue. Death can occur if base of the tongue swells enough to block the air passage of the throat.\n\nElephant Ear\n\nAll Parts\n\nIntense burning and irritation of the mouth and tongue. Death can occur if base of the tongue swells enough to block the air passage of the throat.\n\nRosary Pea\n\nSeeds\n\nFatal. A single Rosary Pea seed has caused death.\n\nCastor Bean\n\nSeeds\n\nOne or two Castor Bean seeds are near the lethal dose for adults.\n\nLarkspur\n\nYoung plant, seeds\n\nDigestive upset, nervous excitement, depression. May be fatal.\n\nMonkshood\n\nFleshy roots\n\nDigestive upset and nervous excitement.\n\nAutumn Crocus\n\nBulbs\n\nVomiting and nervous excitement.\n\nStar of Bethlehem\n\nBulbs\n\nVomiting and nervous excitement.\n\nLily-of-the-Valley\n\nLeaves, flowers\n\nIrregular heart beat and pulse, usually accompanied by digestive upset and mental confusion.\n\nIris\n\nUnderground stems\n\nSevere-but not usually serious-digestive upset.\n\nFoxglove\n\nLeaves\n\nLarge amounts cause dangerously irregular heartbeat and pulse, usually digestive upset and mental confusion. May be fatal.\n\nBleeding Heart\n\nFoliage, roots\n\nMay be poisonous in large amounts. Has proved fatal to cattle.\n\nRhubarb\n\nLeaf Blade\n\nFatal. Large amounts of raw or cooked leaves can cause convulsions, coma, followed rapidly by death.\n\nDaphne\n\nBerries\n\nFatal. A few berries can kill a child.\n\nWisteria\n\nSeeds, pods\n\nMild to severe digestive upset. Many children are poisoned by this plant.\n\nGolden Chain\n\nBean-like capsules in which the seeds are suspended\n\nSevere poisoning. Excitement, staggering, convulsions and coma. May be fatal.\n\nLaurels\n\nAll parts\n\nFatal. Produces nausea and vomiting, depression, difficult breathing, prostration and coma.\n\nRhododendrons\n\nAll Parts\n\nFatal. Produces nausea and vomiting, depression, difficult breathing, prostration and coma.\n\nAzaleas\n\nAll parts\n\nFatal. Produces nausea and vomiting, depression, difficult breathing, prostration and coma.\n\nJasmine\n\nBerries\n\nFatal. Digestive disturbance and nervous symptoms.\n\nLantana Camara \n\nGreen berries\n\nFatal. Affects lungs, kidneys, heart and nervous system.\n\nYew\n\nBerries, foliage\n\nFatal. Foliage more toxic than berries. Death is usually sudden without warning symptoms.\n\nWild and cultivated cherries\n\nTwigs, foliage\n\nFatal.   Gasping, excitement and prostration are common symptoms.\n\nOaks\n\nFoliage, acorns\n\nSymptoms appear only after several days or weeks. Takes a large amount for poisoning.\n\nElderberry\n\nAll parts, especially roots\n\nChildren have been poisoned by using pieces of the pithy stems for blowguns. Nausea and digestive upset.\n\nBlack Locust\n\nBark, sprouts, foliage\n\nChildren have suffered nausea, weakness and depression after chewing the bark and seeds.\n\nJack-in-the-Pulpit\n\nAll parts, especially roots\n\nIntense burning and irritation of the mouth and tongue. Death can occur if base of the tongue swells enough to block the air passage of the throat.\n\nMoonseed\n\nBerries\n\nBlue, purple color, resembling wild grapes. May be fatal.\n\nMayapple\n\nApple, foliage, roots\n\n Children often eat the apple with no ill effects, but several apples may cause diarrhea.\n\nMistletoe\n\nBerries\n\nFatal. Both children and adults have died from eating the berries.\n\nWater Hemlock\n\nAll parts\n\nFatal. Violent and painful convulsions. A number of people have died from hemlock.\n\nButtercups\n\nAll parts\n\nIrritant juices may severely injure the digestive system.\n\nNightshade\n\nAll parts, especially the unripened berry\n\nFatal. Intense digestive disturbance and nervous symptoms.\n\nPoison Hemlock\n\nAll parts\n\nFatal. Resembles a large wild carrot.\n\nThorn Apple\n\nAll parts\n\nAbnormal thirst, distorted sight, delirium, incoherence and coma. Common cause of poisoning. Has proved fatal.\n\n Lords-and-Ladies\n\nAll parts\n\nBurning and swelling of the lips, mouth, tongue, and throat. Skin irritation after contact with root juices. Stomach pains, dizziness, and cramping after ingestion of berries.\n\nBlood lily\n\nBulbs\n\nSalivation, nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.\n\nBlue Lily\n\nPlant sap in leaves.\n\nIrritation of skin and eyes from cell sap. Irritation and ulceration of mouth if ingested.\n\nBottlebrush buckeye\n\nSeeds\n\nMuscle weakness and paralysis, dilated pupils, vomiting, diarrhea, depression, paralysis, and stupor.  Possible Death.\n\nBurning bush\n\nAll Parts\n\nVomiting, diarrhea, weakness, chills, coma, and convulsions.\n\nLeucothoe\n\nLeaves and nectar from flowers.\n\nSalivation and nasal discharge, sweating, tingling sensation, headache, depression, weakness, abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting, diarrhea, possible death.\n\nChlorine Lepidella\n\nMushroom \n \nNausea, vomiting, dizziness, abdominal pains, etc. Symptoms occur 30 minutes to several hours after ingesting.  Possible death.\n\nGround cherry\n\nUnripe berries and leaves.\n\nStomach pain, lowered temperature, dilated pupils, vomiting, diarrhea, circulatory and respiratory depression, loss of sensation; may be fatal.\n\nTrumpet flower\n\nLeaves and flowers\n\nHeadache, incoordination, excitability, stomach pain, lowered temperature, respiratory depression; may be fatal.\n\nCelandine\n\nRoots\n\nNausea, vomiting, bloody diarrhea, numbness, fainting, and coma.  Possibly death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hot Air Rises", "§bThurdan Orathon", "Hot Air Rises\n\nHow can this be proven scientifically? For example, when water is boiled to a high level of heat, it will change to its gaseous form. Once steam appears, it will begin to ascend. It will continue to ascend until the heat\n\nof the steam starts to diminish. At this moment, the steam will change back to its former state, and form water droplets.\n\nDue to these results, one can confirm that hot air rises.\n\nOriginal text by Thurdan Orathon\n\n*a pile of paper has been neatly stacked*", ""),
        StaticBook("Butterflies.", "§bThe Scribe.", "The Progress of the Lives of Butterflies.\n\n\n\nThe majority of Butterflies live their full life of four months. These four months are divided into three stages, where the most prominent and well known stage is the last one.\n\nStage One; Pupae to Larvae. \n\nWhen butterflies are birthed, they are not birthed as creatures of the spring air, flapping their iridescent wings. Instead, they are born as maggots, or 'pupae'. In this state\n\nthe butterfly has no natural defenses. It grows slowly as it consumes in small amounts the foliage around its body. As it continues to grow, the pupae slowly becomes a caterpillar. This stage lasts a month. During the caterpillar's time\n\nas well, a caterpillar, it consumes as much food as it can find.\nThis is in preparation for its next stage of life.\n\nStage Two; Caterpillar to Crysallis.\n\nThis is the beginning of the end for our friend the caterpillar. The caterpillar stocks up on food by devouring ravenously a multitude of plants and leaves. After doing so, the caterpillar changes\n\nroles from tree-top destroyer, to spider-like home spinner. The caterpillar secrets a thick strand of webbing, and wraps its body from tip to end.\nFrom here, the wrapping hardens, and the caterpillar prepares itself for the\n\njourney ahead. This stage lasts two weeks.\n\nStage Three; Crysallis to Butterfly, and the time after.\n\nInside the crysallis, the caterpillar's anatomy wildly changes. It becomes shortened, and wings develop. The butterfly emerges from the crysallis two weeks\n\nafter its formation. Here, the butterfly spends some time preparing its wings for flight. The butterfly will live on its own for up to two more months, harvesting what it can gather from flowers using an elongated probiscus.\n\nThe butterfly will lay its own larvae during a migration to either the north or the south. The cycle begins again, with the formation of new caterpillars marked by the death of the old butterflies.\n\n*a detailed description of butterfly anatomy lies here*\n\n*a drawing labels and guides the reader through the visual steps of growth*\n\n~penned; The Scribe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aisilnn Log", "§bDomainoft", "Aislinn's Medical Log\n===================\n\n*A crude drawing of Jex lies here, various parts labelled, and a few injuries also drawn on as well.*\n\nSubject took multiple puncture wounds to the side, lower chest, and shoulder. A slashing blow to the back of the head and piercing of the temple was the cause of death.\n\nI opened up his chest and cut open the large bone in front of the heart. It was difficult, but expected. After all, the heart is extremely important, and should be protected.\n\nI examined the heart and lungs closely.\n\nFrom what I already know, it /is/ possible to repair a punctured lung. When a lung is pierced, I suppose blood and other fluids fill up, causing the person to 'drown'.\n\nAnother thing I noticed is that arteries and veins, which obviously transport blood\n\nthroughout the body, are quite elastic and stretchy. If one was cut, it /may/ be possible to sew or cauterize it shut, preventing rapid blood loss. \n\nMaybe if it could be pressed or squeezed somehow, blood loss could be migitated\n\non severed limbs and the like. Although now that I think about it, it would be preferable to bring the person to the monks, to save the limb.\n\nAs for the eyes, I have seen dozens of eye injuries. Despite my careful work, I cannot understand\n\nnor comprehend how the eyes work, or how they could possibly be worked on or fixed. \n\nA shame, really.\n\n*Another drawing, better this time, is made of a large, muscular Valah*\n\nSubject died due to severed throat. Too much blood loss, artery cut.\n\nI checked the heart and lungs carefully, noting the position. \n\nA note on the stomach - I found that it holds food, as the throat appears to lead to\n\nit. However.. once the stomach branched off into the long, spiraling organ, I became stumped. I'm not even going to attempt to fathom how food is digested.", ""),
        StaticBook("Deadly Diseases", "§bdaelaris", "A collection of my limited knowledges in the medical field of infectious diseases.\n\nBo'dank is an extremely contagious disease. It is a bacterial infection of the respiratory tract. It is airborne and spread by inhalation. The symptons are the worst -\n\n- part of Bo'dank.  Those with Ki'katta are more susceptible to the disease. The symptons are as follows:\n\nFever\nChills\nCoughing\nItchy throat\nBuild-up of mucus\nEye pain\nConfusion\n\nThis disease is so widespread, that it will typically happen once to every person.\n\nKi'katta is another contagious disease, a key denoter is that people infected are more susceptible to Bo'dank. Doctors have little idea on the origins of the disease, but it typically is not fatal. It will leave those inflicted in pain for up to weeks.\n\nSymptoms are as follows:\n\nFever\nAbdominal Pain\nRedness of the eyes\nDehydration\nCramps\nWeakened Bones\nDiarrhea\n\nGrish is one of the nastier diseases, caused by poisoning from raw or rotton meat. The devestating part of this ailment is the extremely high mortality rate, a massive seventy percent. Those who do survive will have to deal with many side-effects, such -\n\n- as mental impairment, vision loss and numbess of digits or tongue. This is a result of little blood flow to the nerves. Symptons are as follows: Constriction of blood vessels,\nanxiety\nvertigo\nstrange vissions, dreams, hallucinations\nBlackened skin.\n\nEasily the deadliest disease in all of the realms, the plague strikes quickly and it hits hard. It has a high fatality rate and was first recording in year Thirty-seven of Asulon, in Seventis. The infected began to die in mass numbers, quickly spreading -\n\n- spreading to nearby settlement. All attempted cures have failed, the monk's magics unable to cure it. Many nations implemented quarentines, and, with time, the disease subsided. There are several variations of the disease.\n\nGreen-spot variation:\n\nGreen dots that cause itching.\nNumbness.\nWeakness, Fatigue.\nMemory loss and bi-polar mood swings.\nVomiting, typically with blood.\nCoughing up blood.\n\nBlack-Spot Variation:\n\nShivers, tremors and muscle spasms.\n\nExtreme Paranoia.\n\nCoughing up blood.\n\nHemophobia.\n\nInternal hemorrhage, fatal.\n\nWheat was also infected by this disease, and all types of beasts suffered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Technomancy", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Technomancy:\n   Origins, and\n   Explanations\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\n\nShould the reader be mislead by the name of the tome, the writer shall forgive your confusion. The study of \"technomancy\" is not one of the recognised magical arts, but merely a simplified term for the combined usage of magic and mechanical devices.\n\nThe writer finds the term far more agreeable and efficient to speak, rather than the official title of this study known as \"Orrery-derived magically-infused mechanical engineering.\" This work is more of a recountment and\n\nexplanation than actual instructions for construction. That said, do allow yourself to turn the page, and we shall begin.\n\nMagic used with technology is not an entirely obscure concept.  Rumoured during Asulon, the Valah \"Teutonic Order\" created advanced, magically-enhanced armours to survive the haze of deadly air within the frozen lands of Hanseti. One can barely fathom\n\nthe work this Valah order must have undertaken to achieve such an end. Strangely enough, their order was disbanded shortly after the destruction of their keep via the claws of the Northern beasts, and their technology was lost. A most interesting\n\ndevelopment, which makes one wonder why they abandoned such pursuits when in their prime. Such things will likely remain a mystery. The mali'aheral are now the next to attempt such grand technological advances, so let us begin with the most important\n\ndetail--\"Where did this inspiration come from?\" One shall explain.\n\nI, Lucion Sullas, as a then-member of the guild of Mages, was ordered by the archmage Ambros to study and operate an ancient relic found beneath the Wyvern Hold, known simply as \"The Orrery.\" One had originally presumed that the device would be a\n\nsmall thing, as a \"relic\" usually is. However, one was was surprised to find this \"orrery\" to be the height of twenty feet within a grand, underground chamber. As the reader might understand, one was rather enthralled.\n\nThe machine's complexities were extraordinary--I was dumbfounded by the magnificent detail and nigh-perfection of almost every \"cog\" placed within it.\n\nThe \"cogs\" themselves are not uncommon--our own city gate has multiple of them. However, never had they been used to such a numerous and creative degree. A cog, for those who are unfamiliar with them, is a wheel surrounded by segmented \"ridges\"\n\nn its edges. The ridges intertwined with those of another cog, allowing for physical energies (for more information on theoretical logic, see K. Uradir's \"Weightology and Kinesiology\") to be transported between cogs, while only one itself is being moved.\n\nIf one can now imagine this process to an enormous degree, then they can comprehend the orrery.\n\nWhat one did not understand at the outset of the study was how this machine moved in the first place. There was no crank, or levers, or even a system of pulleys. It was only through months of study did I finally make the connection -- powerful\n\nenchantments were used upon a single wheel hidden behind the stone base that allowed it to move without need of whole teams of servants to pull or push. Having performed some enchantments myself by this time, my work continued until one's ideas expanded\n\nto what it is today. \n\nAnd that, reader, is what \"Technomancy\" is--the art of creating engineered mechanical devices that are operated independently by magical enchantments. \n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya", ""),
        StaticBook("Death Potions V2", "§bJistuma", "*~Death\n\n          Potions~*\n\n\n\n\n\nVolume II – Pain\n\nIn the clutches of the underground rivers of the realms of the end, the drinks of the shadow ones, they make you closer to join them. Their tendrils and teeth suck the soul from your very being, dragging you onto their lands by chains.\n\nPain\n\nLow fires torment and blacken the bodies of the filth. Only through pain shall they know the reasons of the malevolence.\n\nGoblin’s Ivy to start up the brew, add it to water and let it heat. Green it will become, not the color to hold, the Night sap much then be added, to make it sweet and taste good. The more you add the more they’ll like the taste.\n\nThe Nether fires shall then come, Blazing powder to bring it forth. From the beasts of the lands of heat you must gather their rods, and grown them into thin powder without harm. Slowly the powder is mixed, slowly the sulfur combines.\n\nIt is strong, magical of the lands. Blessed by the darker flames of below, their skin shall breathe fire. Their heart shall only feel pain for the sins they have not done.\n\nFire Skin poison ingredients:\n\n- Blaze Powder \n- Cactus\n- Glistering Melon", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal of F.H.C", "§bFenris Cross", "~Journal of Fenris C.\n\n*The entries are short. Written in small neat handwriting*\n\n-Witnessed a trial. Accussed kissed another publicly, out of marriage, and of same sex. Accussed was executed.\n\n-Spiders attacked. Many wounded, myself included.\n\n-A party happened, many were entertained. Alot of people joined in dancing.\n\n-Body of Accused cremated. Ashes collected for parents.\n\n-Alfred Steam is wounded and cared for.\n\n-A jester appears in the square. Quite the character. He was infact entertaining.\n\n-Ikur seems to have a secret of some kind. He is very defensive of it.\n\n-I have returned to the city. Many changes have been made.\n\n-Boredom seems to be my number one enemy in life. I need to find a job to occupy me.\n\n-I saw a golem, quite the constructs.\n\n-Alfred Steam exiled,\n\npossible impure.\n\n-I have been looking for Ikur so I may take up a job in the city. So far he eludes me.\n\n-I heard a group conversing on alchemy. The topic interests me, I will look into it.\n\n-I have returned to find the city in ruins and the people spread. I will seek a new place to reside.\n\n-Many new prospects, so far a town in the North holds my interest.\n\n-Mountain ruins, sealed off but the view from\n\nthe peak made up for it.\n\n-I made it inside the mountain ruins. They may infact be inhabited. I will look around.\n\n-Nothing of note in the ruins. Moving out.\n\n-The Fragments of Silver, this should be\n\ninteresting. I will apply the knowledge I have gathered to further myself and perhaps give the order an edge.\n\n-The uniform is rather...out there. Not very good at blending in but still nice and with a filtering mask and chainmail weaved in.\n\n-So long spent away from my comrades, I have become out of touch travelling around. I will seek them out.\n\n-Met back up with my comrades. New city, new things to learn.\n\n-Raiders, patrol sent out to look.\n\n-Giraffe taming mission? Inturrupted by Uruk. He was escorted out\n\n-Commander of \"The Vanguard\" allowed into the city. He request aid against a Lord Powell\n\n-The Commander was turned away peacefully, he may\n\nreturn again with the same offer.\n\n-Disturbance in the tavern. Red electricity, crackling and loud. Red light seems to signal something. Figures appear from it\n\n-Adventure, we destroyed an alter. Many injured. First\n\nkilled. Artifacts retrieved and all returned to city.\n\n-Licia the Paladin passes out after healing wounded. Brought to inn to rest and recover.\n\n-Spirit showed up and offered Ikur advice on feelings. A tea cup\n\nalso took up arms against us. (?) We defeated it in combat.\n\n-Stood for what seemed like hours as a meeting took place. My body feels sore from the standing.\n\n-A ball in the city, quite the event. Had to search and sieze\n\nweapons at the gates.\n\n-Ball was a disaster at first. It got better after fighting at the gates.\n\n-Got caught up in a homosexual dispute in a dwarven family.\n\n-Hit on by said dwarf. Stange ball...\n\n-Gave an elf molten gold eyes. Threw him out of city.\n\n-Undead besiege city, Ikur saves the day with help from the Sill.\n\n-Strange dark elf, had to kick her out twice before she got the message.\n\n-City is being expanded, perhaps I can get a house finally?\n\n-Large abandoned fortress in the swamp. Chest locked under a tree, will need to bash open.\n\n-Fortress has green and red banner. It\n\nmay have belong to one house or another. Seems abandoned.\n\n-Blood rituals and an alter, this swamp hides something dark.\n\n-Found an outpost close to the fort, entrace in through graveyard. No idea if inhabited\n\n-Dark magic pit under this outpost. Way blocked by gate and strange symbols.\n\n-Destroyed city, there may be useful things here still. No sign of life. Red and yellow banners.\n\n-Underground ruins hidden in the cliffs.\n\n-New city, seems inhabited. Crosses with elven bodies dispute the hospility this place has.\n\n-Treated as Olivier de Savoie's guest. We talked for hours and he granted me a book. We travelled back to the Silver City together.\n\n-Sort of robbed by orcs on the way to turn in the book lent by Duke Savoie. The where attacked and I managed to make up for the food they stole by getting from the free food chest they passed. I left them as they where attacked by a monster. Pray they die\n\n-Met the King of Oren as a pact was made for the coming war.\n\n-War is coming. Already witnessed combatants outside the gates early today.\n\n-A dwarf arrived with a crystal. It was recieved and the dwarf sent on his way.\n\n-Witnessed my first major battle. Manned the siege works till we decended down into the town. Manage to kill one of the enemy and aquire new gear.\n\n-Skirmishes, little battles outside the gate. Hope they are stopped before reaching here.\n\n-Interesting thing looking around, seeind plate and chain covering everyone. At least war seems to bring people together.\n\n-Hellfire on the city! Right when I was watching a man juggle swords...\n\n-Delievered scroll\n\nback to Olivier's keep.\n\n-Troops brought back a strange quartz artefact. It is placed in the library.\n\n-An Archmage shows up for Silir accompanied by two Golden Lance Paladins. Something important.\n\n-Phillips also comes to me. The damn thing talks every now and then, but not as much as he used to with my father and Grendor. The other skull is not with him, destoryed perhaps? I hope.\n\n-I have started expirementing with alchemy. There are a\n\nfew book dedicated to the topic in the library that are quite helpful.\n\n-Ikur, Azorella, and I inspect and an underground door. Phillips believes the door to be dwarven, but conciedes possible Elvish origin. Ikur uses anti-magic to try and open it.\n\nblackness leaked out. We left Ikur to work safely.\n\n-Creature of darkness appeared. He gave a cryptic message and allowed us to leave. Promised in time we would return.\n\n-Ventured to around\n\ntill we located Kalameet's home. We were invited inside.\n\n-Viewed a Lexicon, able to store vast quantities of knowledge.\n\n-Guarding the gate. Interesting creatures and people pass by it regularly.\n\n-Rouge mage attacks, blasts through gate. Kills himself with a meteor.\n\n-Gave Ikur the object found during the battle in the wood elf city.\n\n-Scouting out a dwarven outpost. Sent my report in for review.\n\n-Dwarves outside the city, something about a battle with the Kha? They robbed me of my sword an bow, gave me back my bow, then sent me off without murdering me. Strange.\n\n*The book ends with the drawing of an island.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dark Past", "§bNetphreak", "[!] A story, that never ends.. Everyday more words added to this series and everyday his own words come to life. [!]\n\nA lone Necromancer scans the tree tops for any sign that the 'one of the night' would be there, smiling down upon him with that\n\n-face that melts the roughest of hearts. Behind her mask, something dark and mysterious, something the lone Necromancer himself has come to witness.\n\n\"She wanders within the shadows, and upon the trees, searching.. For what though..?\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer.. A man of many faces, a man of many names.. So known to the world yet.. All they see is a vessel, the darkness that haunts him day and night.. Remain concealed within his mind.   \"The curse, will forever stay with me until my death.-\n\n-I've come to accept the fact, I can no longer offer my heart, for the rare times I have.. Heartache comes in return.\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer himself, sits within the tree tops of Lenniel, writing the story you read now, while watching the stars-\n\n-roll on by, looking to the soft sounds below, the insect life, sound of the water, even the echoes of the wind seem to tell tales of past times.\n\n\"The stars are beautiful, each one so unique, yet a sight we take for granted.. I've found myself many a-\n\n-time just, watching.. Beauty just outside of my reach, for a Beast cannot tame such beauty.\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer, once again scarred by another with a blind mission. To find the other Necromancers and destroy them. A hole in his right-\n\n-hand gives detail of the pain he took, to protect those who don't even acknowledge his existance.\n\n\"Bound by blood, although I loathe it, I must protect my bretheren, even if it costs me my life.\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer sits at his desk, next to the room of his precious and delicate Flower, to write down the events and continue the story.\n\n\"My heart aches, I long to seek her, although I've made promise... I must keep it, for her sake.\"\n\nA promise, something that should be soul bound, yet so easily broken, although this lone Necromancer takes promises seriously.\n\n\"A man of trust, although trust I've broken in the past.. I've still yet to fix, I'm only a mortal.. I can -\n\n-only do so much.. They expect much from me.\"\n\nWithin the shadows of his safe haven, he rests, he ponders, he weeps, he listens.. What questions come to mind.. Will that noose take him today? Will that Rosary Pea stop his heart? -\n\n- \"Many times, I've pondered how I would end my life, to keep the Monks from reforming my body, around a soul that should have never been created..\nI wanted to, I tried to even.. I have to stay strong.. For my little Flower...\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer calls out her name in the midnight hour, although no words escape his mouth, his curse keeps him still.\n\n\"This thing, this monster in my brain.. I can see their faces, eyes like a sea of emerald, combined with the 'one of the night'\n\n- A motherly figure, embracing the Flower as if her own.. How I wish for such a dream to become truth..\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer creeps through the night, without a purpose, wandering aimlessly.. Will there ever be light to this darkened soul?\n\n\"As a Necromancer, I find myself.. Around beings of the dark, but.. Sometimes I wonder.. If the dark beings are really the evil ones.. All we want is to be left alone.. And these people of 'light' scream theirs diety's name and slash us with their blades-\n\n-I can't see how we are the evil ones, when we do what we do to survive.. Yet, the ones of 'light' slaughter us on sight because of some false sense of pride, or perhaps... Fear.\"\n\nWithin the Necromancers humble abode, a room of-\n\n-steam, books and iron.. A room to simulate the very nature that a Necromancer steals, life..\n\n\"This room was never meant for one person, but to be shared, to have filled with laughter and tales of happiness, this..-\n\n-Will not come to pass.\"\n\nAs the lone Necromancer climbs into the pool, many scars exposed, some of ink.. A skull within a rose.\n\n\"Each scar, tells a story. Whether it be a hooded Elf-\n\n- using claws to cut the left cheek and forearms, or it be a lover impaling a shovel in the stomach.. A hole in the right hand, to try and expose the secrets never to be spoken.. Although, the scars that tell the best or the worst stories.. Are the ones -\n\n-unseen by the naked eye.\"\n\nA flip of a lever, the Necromancers' hand did manipulate, as the sound of a thousand horses come crashing down with a final 'clank!' To isolate, and keep safe the Necromancer within the steel cage. -\n\n- \"Visitors are rare these days, though it seems my kind of visitors are generally hostile.. Precautions have been taken.. Gates are needed.\"\n\nWalking through the forest of frost, the lone Necromancer unites with the Inferno-\n\n- A mission they both have, to gather the power of a nation of frost, such a thought seems impossible.. Although, the combination of Death and Inferno proves too much for any political power.\n\n\"We, have influence in a nation of frost-\n\n-it wasn't too hard, although I can't help but feel a bit of loyalty for them.. The thought crosses my mind, can I find purpose here?\"\n\nFrom above, a creature of darkness screeches down amongst the living.-\n\nA predator, watchful and swift flies through the air, with a letter in its husk.. The last to be sent with meaning and promise, a ring lay inside to signify the last promise.\n\n\"It was.. A day of confusion, I found myself in a situation that I could not-\n\n-comprehend.. The 'one of the night' stood there in front of me, hand extended.. Her face was cold.. It was empty, almost... As if Death itself was manipulating her actions.. Someone succumbed by the pain and loss of loved ones.. I cannot blame her..\"\n\nThe daylight shines upon the ground, yet the lone Necromancers face remains a shadow, a pair of bloodshard eyes watching, scanning, manipulating.. \nA face once filled with joy and peace.. Now cold and dark. -\n\n- \"It wasn't always like this, the days were like any other, sunny, rainy, hot or cold.. The obscure side, that only very few know about.. Remain concealed, some things the rain cannot wash away.\"\n\nWithin the walls of a newly built Conclave the lone Necromancer rests upon a tree, writing down the story..\n\n\"Some areas are peaceful, and quiet.. Whilst others, even with silence speak horrible stories..\"\n\nAnother day, another mystery, another adventure, even though for the lone Necromancer that adventure is of domestic grounds. Although he has run into 'the one of the night' to see the Oceans of turquoise and emerald.\n\n\"She was... Different today, we held an embrace and I couldn't turn away, to invest whatever of my heart I have left.. It seems like something I've missed my entire life. Love is something that I've never fully understood, it's something people speak of-\n\n-all the time but yet.. It's power is beyond that of the gods. Should a Necromancer like myself feel this emotion? It's so intoxicating.. I find myself wanting to just please her, make her happy.. I wish I can.\"\n\nAt the humble abode, the lone Necromancer readies his new tactics against any possible form of attack.\n\n\"For security reasons, I'm sure you know I cannot write down my exact measures, I'm sure you would understand.\"\n\nAt the City of Walls the lone Necromancer spots an unusual child, silent, brave, tough. Her eyes almost screamed for attention yet, she remained quiet and attentive.\n\n\"This child was... Interesting I should add, it was an unusual-\n\n-encounter, I've never had such with a child before.. She actually reminded me of myself when I was a young boy, my mother would always tell me to stay silenced when being spoken to.. I saw this in that little girl, she finally spoke after we've had the-\n\n-battle of the stares.. She said to me, 'Those who I care about deeply.. Are my family.'\n\nHow I can relate to this little girl.. As the only one's I have left as family, are the closest to my heart..\"\n\nThe lone Necromancer sits aside a warm fire, the 'one of the night' across from his view as he writes. She is soothing someone in a very calming manner..\n\n\"I myself would have not used such measures.. But I think I should change for the better.\"\n\n-------------------\"I fear I don't have much time left, Battou has gotten stronger whilst myself weaker.. I fear, those I love will outlive me, and my absence will cause them pain.. I would love to say I lived a good life, but I would be lying..... -\n\n- I have come to find joy within my life, I consider myself extrememly lucky that Poppy and Lilith found it worth their while to know me.. I think it's safe to say we brought a little joy to one anothers lives...\n\nI guess... This story will have to end-\n\n- As we all have an expiration date set.. I didn't think my time would be so short, but I love the ones in my life.. Lilith, Poppy.. Heck even Joe..\n\nSo, my final chapter.. Until Death Do Us Part..\n\n[!] Pherak's Signature [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity", "§bZeus Ith'ael", "Series One of Three\n          PURITY\n--------------------------------------\n\n     Scribed on the\nSeventh of the Grand Harvest. The year, 1496\n\n       Second Revision\n          First Edition\n\n      Printed by Lazul\n          Literature\n\nPurity. Progression. Superiority. These are the qualities of a tried and true high elf. Through impeccable purity we gain progression. Through progression we gain superiority over the lesser, the impures and the mongrel dogs that call themselves men.\n\nPurity. Symbolized by silver and white. It is our most important quality. Without purity we are no more than mutated savages. Purity runs not only in the blood of our people, but the attitude they possess.\n\nAcceptance of lessers and impures will damn those who hold our qualities. Those that sympathize with any cause but our own are to be considered stark raving mad like a dwarf and condemned to the brand.\n\nThose without silver hair should make you wary, but blonde counterparts can be tolerated upon showing worth. Most notably Kalenz Uradir, our most illustrious leader.\n\nThose that stray into the dirty colours of blonde are NOT to be trusted, tolerated or accepted in anyway. Their mere existence is a farce of high elven culture. This brings us to the tone of skin.\n\nIt is well known that blacks, browns, ashes and reds are an irrefutable sign of impurity, but that is not to say that purebloods can’t gain a tan. There are those among us that do diligent work inside dark rooms surrounded by tomes and inventions.\n\nWe respect them. However, there are those among us that prefer to spend their time training their minds and bodies in the light of the sun. They are our protectors and the unavoidable tanning of their skin is to be respected\n\nat the same level as their scholarly compatriots. We do not tolerate anything more than a simple tan. Those touched by night are thieving rats. Most often greedy and violent. Simple dogs that are only to be used and abused for the progression of our\n\npeople. The simple notion that we allow them into our city in this day and age is revolting. The blood that creates our appearance is not the only sign of purity.\n\n\n           \n\n            =O=\n\nThe toleration, acceptance and communication with the lessers, the impures and the mutants shocks me. Communication is the only form of interaction that can be somewhat acceptable as we live in a diplomatic era.\n\nAt its current state we cannot simply liquify the muts outside our walls, but a day will come. Those that are found outside of the Silver City without a diplomatic reason for interacting with the abominations outside of our pristine zone of control\n\nare to be reported immediately. At that point they have shown clear signs of an impure mindset. Rehabilitation is an option, but the only real solution is liquefying their bodies and hoping their souls do not re-manifest\n\nin an even more disgusting form of life. By allowing co-mingling among our people and the lessers we are damning our progression as one. The chaotic ways of the others will twist and contort our brothers and sisters\n\ninto hideous beasts unfit to walk among our gardens, halls and places of knowledge. They shan’t speak the beautiful tongue of our ancestors.\n\nI hope you hold the words written to heart. Impurity is not only measured in skin tone, hair colour and irises, but in the mindset and attitude of a true elf. There are those among us that we should impose an inherent distrust\n\nof such as those that mix elven and common. Those that sympathize with the ideals of the chaotic savages. Through only purity can we find progression.\n\n\n\n             =O=\n          THE END\n\nLook for the the next book in the series, Progression.\n\nThank you for reading and I can only hope you take these words to heart. For only the people of today can shape the future of tomorrow.\n\n   Viligance is diligence.\n\n\n                Zeus Ith'ael\n\nOther works worth reading:\n\n*Racism by Sullas\n*Perfection and Purity by Vellulaie'thillin Vul'athri", ""),
        StaticBook("Excerpts", "§bDio Astóre", "In peace, creation. In war, protection. In destruction, forethought.\n\n===\n\nWithout life, the edict of the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya cannot be fulfilled.\n\n===\n\nGreed and false prides find themselves in detestable abundance; to blindly place faith in their own convictions; forgotten will truth be in those shrouded pits, only torments and anguish for the mind lie there. Old bonds shattered or strained, fear and\n\nambition rules the lands, breakers of oaths; climbers of the mountain of bone. For their own gain and own fame; shame to them those who seek to sit, atop the graveyard throne!\n\nLoathe the seekers of glory in graves!\n\nLoathe the speakers for honour in pain!\n\nLoathe the meager who lie in chains!\n\nCast and bound, to death and blame!\n\n===\n\nMisunderstanding and ignorance births wars.\n\nThey that detest conflict show wisdom in their disposition, however to permit truths to be hidden behind falsehoods or to deprive them opportunity to be free of dissent and violence is an affront to wisdom. \n\n===\n\nTo fight against destruction may seem hypocrisy, however the validity of this does not penetrate the surface; reasoning in mortal affairs is of horrid complexity.\n\nIn striving to affirm themselves, commit to identifying their values, and how best they may be served. Should they be threatened, one cannot hesitate in their defense.\n\n===\n\nThe flesh of the unaware is not their own. Seek the questions which lie within prior to the answers that lie without. The one that does not understand themselves shall never be able to understand that which is external to them.\n\nTime for solitude; where one finds naught but thoughts for company, there will great minds be born, for in creating a bond between its faculties does the individual earn a rewarding relationship.\n\n===\n\nThe hourglass brings with it deserts the likes of which no mortal eye may behold; such perfect emptiness in the falling of each grain, lost to oblivion each pain, and triumph.\n\nThat which is Eternal offers to the endurant a simple lesson: there are but more than a single way in which one can experience death and dying.\n\n===\n\nA hand in favour to the loyal, an eye of suspicion upon masks.\n\nTo maintain trust is as noble a cause as any, though wary one must be, and critical in judgements, for you may find the ambitious oft have a cause greater than nobility and honourable sentiment.\n\n===\n\nRegarding those that take it upon themselves to earnestly pursue truth, they must firstly possess the ability to discard that which does not lend itself to the task. Much knowledge is unique to a given time and place - it constantly acquires new forms,\n\nborn of the various interacting elements of the world. The destruction of these elements is an affront to the art of learning, though destructive elements pose the greatest risk to the acquisition of wisdom. Be prudent in acting upon these words.\n\n===\n\nWould there a scale be that measured the weight of the mind and the heart, wherever would we see them both taken to?\n\nShould we see a heavy heart heave thoughts into lofty places, far removed from the tangible\n\nor a mentality with such gravity that would rob us of our care of it? Imbalance will lead to immorality, but not all immoral behaviour is committed to satisfy ill ends.\n\n===\n\nSharp words have no intrinsic ability to draw blood, though they may very well be the cause of such when met with a dull entity. Those that wield the hammer of blunt statements will inevitably meet an opponent that tests the efficacy of a lexical shield.\n\nA barbarous mind is ill accustomed to defending itself with anything but the primitive tools which it can master.\n\n===\n\nLogic may seem chilling as the winter frosts, though one should not mind so much the bite of an arctic wolf upon learning it is merely a hunger that is being satiated; caution does wisdom prescribe however in seeking to appease the appetite of curiosity.\n\nThe purest of things are also those which tarnish with the greatest haste.\n\n===\nEND", ""),
        StaticBook("Salvus: Part 2", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The History\n     of Salvus:\n       Part 2\n\n      by N. Evitan\n\nThe survivors of Winterfell lived in relative peace for a while on the Isle of Salvus, unnoticed by the rest of Oren, which was in the process of getting ripped in half. It was around that time, when former Oren King Enor Sheffield joined forces with\n\nDawn Perea in hope of creating an idyll for everybody, who wanted a peaceful life. But this easygoing days would not last forever, as the Undead continued to spread their reign of terror further south with every passing day.\n\nThe Isle seemed not inflected, as the rest of the world started to perish in the flames, but it was soon clear that Aegis as a whole was lost. The nations started evacuating into the Verge and prepared boats for the departure of everything they ever\n\nknew and likewise did the citizens of Salvus.\n\nAlongside the other nations they waited for the final day and set sail into uncertainty, when Iblees raged in fury over what was once called Aegis. The boat of Salvus was not the biggest by any means,\n\nbut it was certainly one of the fastest and so it was one of the first to wash ashore Asulon.\n\nAfter a torturing long time on the boat, nothing could hold the people on it, once they saw the new land. Thus they set out into the night, following their\n\nQueen Dawn Perea and their King Enor Sheffield in the search for food and shelter. What they found was two stone structures, sitting on top of a wooded hill hinting mysterious stories from long forgotten kingdoms.\n\nThus the people of Salvus seeked shelter in the building, which is known today as the Palace of Solace. Day by Day, Month by Month, the citizens started the first rebuild the palace and the Keep, then building up homes for themselves and the new\n\npeople joining them with the wish to share a peaceful life.", ""),
        StaticBook("L3: Cervitaur", "§bAthe'lor", "I was first introduced to the Cervitaur language rather recently, today being 16th of The Deep Cold, 1491, by a Cervitaur nonetheless. For some reason, Plazea (The Cervitaur) was within Haelun’or but unable to speak Common, only another-\n\nlanguage foreign to me. I then took it upon myself to teach the half-man, half-deer how to speak Common, at least enough to be able to translate words for me.\n\nThis sparked our ‘friendship’ as I encouraged Plazea to translate words from Common into Cervitaur, although clearly after a few days the creature no longer wished to translate and would avoid the topic. Even still, I believe with the words I was-\n\ngiven are enough to for me to finish translating, and I shall explain why. Not only is Cervitaur similar to Mori’Quessir in the manner that the sentence structure is nearly identical to Common, but there is a pattern to the letters.\n\nMany times did I hear Plazea say the word ‘good’, or as it translates into Cervitaur, ‘Ruun’. Yet, on more than one occasion, did I hear Plazea say ‘Guun’. Was this mispronunciation? My question was answered-\n\nafter Plazea told me the word for language, ‘Relriera’. However, in another sentence the creature used the same word, but said ‘Lelriera’. Do you notice the pattern, reader?\n\nLanguage, Lelriera; language, relriera. Good, Guun; good, ruun. I believed the key to unlocking this language was in the difference between capital and lowercase letters, and my hypothesis was correct. When a letter is capitalized, it remains the same.\n\nHowever, in Cervitaur when a letter is lower-case, it may turn into a variety of things (or may also stay the same). The next few pages will include capitalized words, and lowercase words I have translated.\n\nIrrar = yes [] Yar\nLu = no [] Nu\nHarru = hello/Hello\nRuunfirra = goodbye [] Guunfirra\nFirra = bye [] Birra\n\nRserr = grass [] Gserr\nLlruwas = flower [] Fruwas\nWedas = water/Water\nSil = run [] Ril\n\nRunadainar = sometimes [] Sunadainar\nAir = is [] Ir\nIlnasrdeln = understand [] Ulnasrdeln\nRelriera = language [] Lelriera\nErru = also [] Arru\nEln = and [] Aln\nRdillll = stuff [] Sdillll\nFuuc = book [] Buuc\n\nRuun = good [] Guun\nFen = bad [] Ben\nCairr = kill [] Kairr\nAyair = evil [] Eyair\n\nAs the reader may be able to tell, translating from Cervitaur to Common is not all that difficult, you must merely know which letters replace which (and only lowercase letters are replaced). If you were to write a sentence in Cervitaur in all capital-\n\nletters, yes, it would seemingly translate into the exact same thing; the trick solely lies in being able to replace lowercase letters with other lowercase letters. If one seeks conversation in Cervitaur, you are encouraged to speak with the author.\n\nI now tuck my words to sleep, and pull the blanketed leather cover over them. Sweet dreams; may you find yourselves in the hands of those who pursue knowledge. \n\n-Athe’lor", ""),
        StaticBook("Avern'ne", "§bDio Astóre", "A copy of a tome from the archaeology site of Haelun’or, Asulon.\n\nThe original being found underneath the Black Seat*, the short volume pertains to an iteration of the ancient Heial’thilln, its seven Okariran and the titular Avernne’an or ‘Seekers’ that carried out its will.\n\nFor how long this social structure prevailed remains unclear. Study of the Heial’thilln is advised prior to perusal of this text. Simplification is provided, due to much of the necessary contextual objects being no longer available for study.\n\nTranslation of the primary lore item along with appended notes is included, as well as text on objects of power purported to be associated with each colour. Only the Miruel variant is known to have existed, now lost.\n\n*The Black Seat refers to the center-most section of a large throne-like structure found within the oldest known council chambers of Haelun’or.\n\n===\n\nEach one of seven councillors - known as an Okarir - existed as an embodiment of a certain aspect of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. The Avern’ne would operate similarly to the Okarir they represented, though the Okarir had authority as a teacher and exemplar.\n\nThese duties were archetypal and became symbolized by certain colours, which were widely integrated in society. How an Avern’ne was selected remains uncertain. Listed below are said archetypes.\n\nBarbu Avern'ne [Black Seeker]: The Mirror\n\nMirror that reflects scenes in an endless pattern though never shows the beholder within them.\n\nShadows of the light. Where perfection exists, there the black does not. Teachers of obscure lessons. Let them guide others, that they might fly toward the radiance of wisdom. As moonlit lakes at dusk, they offer a chance for reflection.\n\nWhen all has been completed and the hues are unified in a pure white illumination the shade shall shrink into a fulfilled nothingness.\n\nLittle is known of the way this type of Avern’ne functioned or whether it existed as a coherent group with a shared ideology.\n\nIt could be inferred that the Maheral belonged to this archetype - regarded as a unifying figure, however this unification might not have been achieved via wholly virtuous means.\n\nSpeculation is that the Black represents those that have deviated from maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, acting as inverted paragons.\n\nVallel Avern'ne [Blue Seeker]: The Wheel\n\nGyroscope that spins in accordance with the strength of nearby emotions.\n\nObservers and analysts of the natural world and its workings. Perceptive minds as well as critical thinkers, the blue is seeing the frost covered lands, the depth of the seas, the tempest of the winds through the eye of logic.\n\nSouls that are methodical and instructive, they prescribe to forms even as they subject such forms to their machinations. Keepers of memory and knowledge, they protect what has been and what always will be.\n\nPrimarily involved in scholastic and scientific pursuits, this Avern’ne archetype committed most strongly to maehr’sae and were among the most able academics, usually being individuals which valued things that could be subjected to reason.\n\nProne to political ambivalence and internal contestation. Their contributions were a keystone of Mali’aheral society and earned them favour.\n\nLentos Avern'ne [Brown Seeker]: The Flute\n\nMusical instrument that has the ability to hasten plant maturation and compel lesser creatures.\n\nEndurant presences upon the earth, abundance becomes not only their own benefit but others. Bastions of quiet grace and strength.\n\nVoids become whole; the truth of self becomes realised in the sanctuary they provide. Crowned by browns life was. By its law, they live.\n\nA rarer multi-disciplined Avern’ne. Closely aligned with hiylun’ehya, their activities tended towards those of a creative or restorative nature.\n\nLeading in matters of infrastructure, community welfare and culture, they ensured daily life was stimulating and prosperous. An Avern’ne changing paradigms to the Brown after service with another was acceptable practice.\n\nFilental Avern'ne [Green Seeker]: The Key\n\nKey with an uncut blade and a sphere bow. Effects vary.\n\nKeepers of balance and vanguards of harmony. Openers of doors and cultivators of opportunity. With persistence the green will persevere; adaptive, growing; assuming a wide spectrum of forms as diverse as they are numerous.\n\nCapable of enduring or creating change, they find themselves at comfort amidst what others think strange.\n\nPossessing a heightened affinity for forethought and often of an adaptive persuasion, these Avernne’an had a greater potential for compromise and mediation, which at times put them at odds with other Mali’aheral, especially those of the Yellow.\n\nMany of them were involved in extra-political affairs and cases of dissent are associated with them. Whilst less orthodox they provided opportunity for development.\n\nValmuel Avern'ne [Purple Seeker]: The Crystal\n\nPrism which changes colour chaotically, depicting broken glimpses of memories.\n\nStudents and practitioners of the ancient artforms. Manipulators of force and creatures of mystery. Upon the border of reality will they pluck their threads and ply their craft.\n\nEsotericism is where the purple mind dwells, upon the farplanes with no names; places that thought, spirit and aspect cast their spell; dream that is never the same.\n\nThose Avernne’an that were highly learned in magic and had the greatest understanding of the incorporeal. Lore implies they had a propensity for secrecy and were frequently the most disconnected with Mali’aheral culture.\n\nThey specialized in applying their expertise to augment or supplement conventional activities and research, yet were oddly vulnerable to idiosyncratic behaviours.\n\nMiruel Avern'ne [Red Seeker]: The Sword\n\nWeapon with two forms. It uses flames against things dark or aggressive in nature.\n\nEnd-bringers and accomplishers. Through trials of fire will the true order be birthed. By the path of a sword will the way be carved and through a closure of the heart shall the passage to truth be opened.\n\nPurging illuminators, reds are a blazing inferno that leave ash in their wake. From ruins are their purpose born. Upon crumbled foundations will the glorious monuments be placed.\n\nWhether these Avernne’an were the most loyal or the furthest removed from hiylun’ehya is a matter of perspective. They tasked themselves with securing favorable conditions for the Mali’aheral and minimising circumstances that posed danger.\n\nTheir aversion to defeat made them formidable, suitable to the militant and strategic activities that defined them.\n\nAyal Avern'ne [Yellow Seeker]: The Scale\n\nGolden cloth. Any item it touches feels heavier the less worth it has to the holder.\n\nDiscerning spirits whose talent lies in their ability to embody the qualities of what they persue.\n\nThey cultivate what is valuable, in the hands of their hue a seed buds into an existence greater and more glorious than itself. In hands held to the sun, all is balanced.\n\nOrganized and collected, with a focus on maintaining order and performing administrative duties.\n\nMost Avern’ne belonging to the Yellow were seen to co-operate with the Red and had sway in the interpretation of law and oversaw the disposition of resources, which included the assets of their information network.\n\nThey possessed links to other Avern’ne and generally took a neutral stance in affairs that did not concern civil stability.\n\nEND", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Wizard Foam- A thick harsh ale which perpetually foams.§0\n§0\n§0Ambrosia - A subtle golden colored drink which puts the drinker into a deep ecstasy.\n\nVitriol- A highly potent liqeur, clear in nature and mildly §0acidic...It§0 comes in three colors, Blue, Green and white. Alcohol content increasing with each.§0\n§0\n§0Aqua Fortis - A clear white liqueur which will eat through one's skin if consumed.\n\nAlcheseltzer - Dry liqueur, pink grapefruit liqueur, orange flower water, and lemon juice and some magic.§0\n§0\n§0Celestial Riesling -§0\n§0A soft white sparking wine.  §0\n§0And now, the order of the Alphabet. ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\n\nSome people say that dragons aren't real. Well that's impossible because I am a dragon.\n\nTo make rotten flesh you simply murder someone, preferably an innocent child they have the best taste. And then you just let them sit in a dirty pit or something for a few days.\n\nMy name is Tom, if you're reading this, I am dead. Please avenge me.§0\n§0\n§0The High Elves exterminated my family, burned them all in front of me. And now me.§0\n§0\n§0Do not let them get away with torture. Remove them from existence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Field Notes VL.1", "§bAzoth Hawksong", "19th of Sun's Smile§0\n§01550§0\n§0\n§0Grungron and Ian Waveharp meet in the Ascended Keep for a meeting. Ian seems concerned of Aeriel's stance towards Xion matching Hers towards Iblees.§0\n§0\n§0Grun agrees and says that even Xionist are\n\noffered the chance of salvation. Xan, too, agrees to this degree, though it is revealed that Leric spared one willingly.§0\n§0\n§0Grun claims he is the one to have found the names first. Ironic. Heial and I were the first long ago. But meh, you win some you\n\nlose some. Oh whale.§0\n§0\n§0[FURTHER UNRECORDED]§0\n§0\n§012 of the Amber Cold§0\n§01550§0\n§0\n§0New names of Xionist cultists are being delivered from two people passing by the Keep. They are as follows:\n\n1.) Selrick (aka John the Friendly) is a lich.§0\n§02.) Rathel (aka Hauxir and Eziel) is with Acerbus.§0\n§0\n§0[FINISHED]\n\n18th of Amber Cold§0\n§01550§0\n§0\n§0A base for spooks is located here:§0\n§0\n§0X: -183§0\n§0Z: -3,837§0\n§0\n§0We found a Lich by the name of Artius. He is a kind fellow with a good heart. Or so it seems.\n\nGrungron is fully against sparing or even attempting to cleanse the Lich who could be of great aid. Rather strange when one considers how many users of the dark arts he has let thrive in the past.§0\n§0\n§0But it is not my place to say.\n\n13th of First Seed§0\n§01551§0\n§0\n§0Some new names to keep an eye onto:§0\n§0\n§01. Silvos§0\n§02. Coltaine§0\n§03. Thatch§0\n§04. Zaviel§0\n§0\n§0Rumored necromancers and cultists associated\n\nwith the cult. Further developments at a later date... maybe. Probably. Shut up.§0\n\n18th of First Seed§0\n§01551§0\n§0\n§0I'm sat in the tavern in Sanctuary. I notice Coltaine sitting down a level. I am going to approach. Wish me luck!§0\n§0\n§0He moves towards the exit. I follow.§0\n§0\n§0He enters the Cloud Temple. He then goes\n\nto the Caliphate. Straight forward from the cart lies a fort. I believe this to be a lead to the Necromancers.§0\n§0\n§0The fort seems active. I hear voices. Perhaps five inside. It is fortified and difficult to assess. Further investigations are probably needed.\n\nI overhear them. Sarrion and the Sultan are present. They speak of new Flays from the remnants of Dunamemes. They speak of revolution in Oren.§0\n§0\n§0This is highly questionable. So, of course, I am going to enter the fort. Walk in, of course.\n\nI enter. Sarrion seems awkward around me and this meeting. I assume he is attempting to hide something. Look into this further.§0\n§0\n§0It seems this meeting was first meant to discuss the death of the Emperor by the hand of an assassin. Interesting.\n\n19th Grand Harvest§0\n§01551§0\n§0\n§0Sarrion discloses to me in my visit to Skyfall that Coltaine is indeed a Xionist. He met with their 'leader' once who wore a mask. Perhaps an Acerbus or the actual leader. Purple robes is what Sarrion tells me acted\n\nlike a hood, as well.§0\n§0\n§0He claims to have seen him at the Library. Perhaps a lead?§0\n§0\n§0Possible Xionist Members:§0\n§0\n§01.)\n\nCONCLUSION\n\nThis is Issue 1 of Azoth Hawksong's notes in the field. I am starting my new notes soon to free more space.\n\nAeriel Bless your path.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Eloquent Note", "§bAenor Calithil", "To the one known as Janus:§0\n§0\n§0Karin'ayla,§0\n§0\n§0My name is Aenor Calithil, El'Chirr of the Order of Sirame. My brothers and I have heard some tidbits of information about you, and are rather interested in what\n\nyou have to offer. Should you wish to, we would very much like you to join our ranks. Should you have any questions or concerns, please feel free to contact me either by letter, or in person. I usually tend to frequent my forge, which is right next to the\n\nbarracks, or the main square by the gates. I look forward to hearing a response.§0\n§0\n§0Ame nae evareh,§0\n§0Aenor Calithil", ""),
        StaticBook("A mad man Vol.II", "§bHileia Sythaerin", "§0§lThe Ramblings§0\n§0§l       of a§0\n§0§l     Mad Man   §0V. II§0\n§0\n§0\n§0He's been alright lately. He has lost his desire to study tremendous amounts, instead he's spending his time in the library reading literature and taking things slow.\n\nPerhaps he realizes how quickly he's aging. He doesn't appear to care about the elections whatsoever. One way or the other, another will sit on the Sohaer's seat and pretend to rule this society. Perhaps things will change for the better.\n\nThe other day he came home and started singing. It has been such a long time since I've heard him sing. In his low, yet slightly baritone voice he recited:§0\n§0\n§0§oPrayer is the bell jar, we put over this goodbye. I'd rather leave this embrace\n\n§obetween you and I. Let's lock out the bearded old man in the night gown, he can tap against the glass but I'm not coming out. I built bridges with these arms I will not build a fortress. In the circle around the kitchen table I say my amen because I\n\n§ofeel blessed. Secretly §0 §0§ohoping while joining hands that you can't feel my trembling fingertips... If I sign this piece of paper do I sell my soul along with my duties and we won't put our money where your catholic mouth is. Even though the teeth\n\n§oare long gone, there's still bone beneath the gums and there's a lot of potential in a mighty mighty organ. I want trees instead of gravestones, nothing to confess. I've got a soft spot for your ancient books and horror stories. I get a music in my ears\n\n§ofrom long long ago and far far away, and I'll still hum its tune.§0\n§0§oHow could I ever believe every word it says to me...§0\n§0\n§0§oWe follow our own steps, while our shadows keep watching us.\n\n§oThe wrong step, would be not to start this exodus...§0\n§0\n§0And that's where he stopped. Suddenly halted, frozen in place, staring out the window with glazy eyes. I didn't know what to do, I just sat down and read the lyrics\n\nhe'd sang to me. At first glance they looked like nonsense but there was a certain element to it that I could not get my head around. Like there was a story hidden within this odd, odd song that for some reason he sang.\n\nHe sang it a few more times the upcoming days, allowing me to complete the lyrics I drafted from his recital. Still, an odd story but there was something so soothing about hearing him sing it so I let him continue. Now, he looks brighter. Clearer. Purer,\n\nalmost. He is barely using his magic, not doing much with his hands, I believe he is even working on a mechanical version of his protheses so he might not have to use telekinesis anymore. I do not know why but it feels right this way.\n\nA few days past and back he came, with new hands. Ones made of an odd material, seemingly a mixture of green, blue and black fragments. He wears his gloves over them so they do not look quite as odd, thank Larihei. And then a poem emerged from his mouth.\n\n§oOh how I'd like to feel again. Feel things and hands and so much more. To be able to sit and simply touch, anything made by elf or man. §0\n§0\n§0§oBut alas, my touch, has long ago past. As I was not careful, and I paid a price.\n\n§oA powerful substance I created, yellow and swift, thick like mist. It attacked me, and although I was fine, for my hands that day was their last.§0\n§0\n§0Another flashback it appears, to our days in Anthos. I cannot blame him for missing his senses, he\n\nalways did love texture. And I too, miss his non-magical touch, but now it might have returned.§0\n§0\n§0He seemed happy today. He came home smiling like a little child, telling me \"Look Vio, look what I can do!\"\n\nHe held out his arm, pointed to the flesh, and as I watched a small spot turned blue. Then red and green, and lilac and orange. Then finally blue, and pale white again. \"Nifty, isn't it?\"§0\n§0I simply chuckled, it looked quite amusing.\n\nNow, he's singing again. A different song, however, and I am struggling to write it down. I will do my best:§0\n§0\n§0§oWhen once upon a time was real, we'd paint upon the walls with words. And call upon our doubts to kneel,\n\n§othen fall upon their tongues with swords.§0\n§0\n§0§oIf I might suggest to you, that all the dreams we ever knew, were more than real and more than true. They were stories we could tell.\n\n§oIn broken rythms, busted rhymes, and all good turns in all good time, of primal pulls and passions, and parables and primes.\n\nSo dance with shadows, paint with flames, and cast as far as far can feel. Cause once upon a time's today...\n\n§oAnd once upon a time is real.\n\n§rHe just fell asleep. It sounds so calming, almost hypnotic. I think things might be alright for now.\n\n§o-H. V. Sythaerin", ""),
        StaticBook("Eloluer'ne", "§bDio Astóre", "Excavation and research within Haelun’or continued alongside restoration efforts up until migration became necessary. Prior to this many discoveries and translations enabled us to fulfill our cultural re-envisioning.\n\nPoetic and prosaic texts offered glimpses into our way of life, whilst a collection of cryptic texts located within the dark depths of the land riddled something of complexity. For the sake of preservation, the dig-site was made restricted.\n\nFollowing the remains of the subterranean water conduits allowed us to happen upon a stairwell leading to a cavern, containing rocky islands partially submerged in water, all linked by bridges.\n\nThe wall furthest from the stairwell had hewn out of it a hollow stone shell, within which stood a freestanding archway.\n\nWater flowed through the shell and the archway caught the stream in such a way as to create an aquatic curtain, which itself drained through a crack in the floor barely a finger-width across.\n\nThe entire surface of the archway was covered in symbols and meticulously wrought, each deeply etched into the stone and encrusted with an assortment of gemstones and metals, of mostly purple and gold varieties.\n\nA haze shrouded thoughts and made wakefulness a seemingly difficult task when in proximity to this unnatural edifice.\n\nReferences to this Gate stored around rooms of the subterranean network provided the confidence required to proceed with more elaborate interactions.\n\nLucidity changed in a linear manner that matched distance to the archway. Moving under the curtain of water induced a brief mental oblivion, upon the conclusion of which an awakening would occur and one would find oneself placed in a dreamlike scene.\n\nProlonged exposure loosened notions of selfhood and induced a disconnect with tangibility. Remaining longer within would increase the likelihood of feeling pain upon returning, the means for that being submersion in water.\n\nOnce safety procedures were established for exploration, I invited a select few to experience immersion and their proceedings helped shape the conclusions drawn.\n\nWitnessing each of them enter produced the same result: the water would appear to carry their corporeal form away as rain does to clay. Returning saw the process similarly reversed.\n\nFeatures within the dreamscape appeared to be influenced by thoughts, memories and emotions - stronger by those of the subjects entering.\n\nObjects both found and brought lacked substance, constantly shifting toward and away from definition, possessing amorphous qualities that lent themselves to manipulation. An exception was the soulstone, which proved resilient to the effects.\n\nOur early observations showed things primal in nature, with mortality and fertility as dominating themes.\n\nIntroducing various animals produced scenes that reflected their habits, however they often would not survive returning and the simpler life-forms would become translucent before fading away entirely.\n\nRemnants of exposed personalities would very briefly linger and continue to give shape to the surroundings. A conclusion drawn from my observations is that strength of will corresponds to longevity, and shared intent accomplishes this exponentially.\n\nSigns of Mali’aheral influence pre-dating our own remained for observation; shadowy images of immense regal structures, monuments with celestial and aquatic motifs, figures of proud stature attending to their noble works - all like murky apparitions.\n\nThose that had entered before us strived greatly to preserve our legacy; the magnitude of willpower required to endure that plane befits only our ancestors.\n\nTheir genius birthed constructs that reflected their memories, but time had diminished their potency. The immensity of energy required to enact such creation suggested a great sacrifice and a constant link to a formidable source of power.\n\nNevertheless, none of the things produced within could be withdrawn for application elsewhere, narrowing the possible intentions for its construction.\n\nMere historical preservation remains an unsatisfactory explanation, for it is too close to vanity for our kind and the medium has a nature of brevity. The possibility of a contraption having been built inside the Gate is a promising theory.\n\nAmong my conclusions regarding the Gate is that the Golden Pools had the additional function of acting as a primary mechanism in the preparation of the body for the Gate, whilst offering a way to passively channel mana into it.\n\nSeveral agents capable of manipulating said mana would nevertheless be necessary - the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya surely cultivated the appropriate qualities of mind.\n\nSuccessive generations of purity would certainly compound this, however the process is long and all too easy to interrupt.\n\nImpurity is a great hinderance and death must be avoided. Corruption too must be kept at bay. Without life, the edict of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya cannot be fulfilled.\n\nReplication of the Gate is possible, however a location with the requisite qualities must be established, as the Nodes or Pools. Each realm varies in its properties and migrations act as a setback.\n\nThe time necessary for a sole person to proceed with the undertaking is not negligible, however I am certain that the ascension of our race is tied to its principles.\n\n\n<<The following page appears to have belonged to another book.>>\n\n§oIt transcends flesh and doubt; not faith is it, nor reasoned conviction. \nCast yourself within the exalted device and behold!\nWhole and meticulous are these constructs rendered.\nEndlessly does the dream unfold ‘fore your stellar awakening.\n\n§l- Dio Astóre", ""),
        StaticBook("Oppression", "ElectrcWizard", "Songs of Oppression\n\n     These songs are in their text form, in my interpretation. They are only words, yet hearing these men sing as if they have no pleasure in life. Geraldes, a young fellow I met in the swamps of Renatus. He was dirtied and tattered to the threads\n\ntrousers were soaked and tattered to the threads. He spoke with a thick accent I could not help recognize, the common language of the servants and workers of my land as a young boy.\nGeraldes told me of his story, and his brothers and sisters in the chains\n\nbrought on by their master's hands.  Geraldes was taken from his wife and young girl, to work on the sugar farms.\n\nThese are their songs, in the written form, but to hear it sung by the men who have carried it for generations, is much more haunting.\n\n   Early in the Mornin'\n\nWell, it's early in the mornin'\nBaby, when I rise, Lordy mama\nWell, its early ever mornin'\nA-baby when I rise well-a\nWella-a when I rise, it's a early in the mornin'\n\nWell-a, whosonever told it\nThat he told a dirty lie, babe\nWell-a, whosonever told it\nThat he told a dirty lie, babe\nHe gonna rise and fly, sugar\nWell-a He gonna rise and fly, well-a\n\nWell-a! Rocks 'n gravel make a solid road, sugar, well-a\nIt takes a-rocks-a,\ngravel to make a solid road\nIt takes a good-lookin' woman to make a good lookin' whore\nO takes a good-lookin' woman to make a good-lookin' whore\n\n      Po Lazarus\n\nWell, the high sheriff\n   He told his deputy\n\nWant you to go out and     bring me Lazarus\n\nWell, the high sheriff\n     Told his deputy\n\n  I want you to bring me Lazarus\nBring him dead or alive\n        Lord, Lord\n\nWell the deputy he told       the high sheriff\nI ain't gonna mess with         Lazarus\nWell the deputy told \n     the high sheri\n\n   Says I ain't gonna mess with no Lazarus\n\n       Well he's a\n     dangerous man\n        Lord, Lord\n          He's a\n      dangerous man\n\n  Well then the high\n   sheriff found\n      Lazarus\n\n   He was hidin'\n   in the chill of a\n       mountain\n   With his head\n      hung low\n\nSays I come to arrest     you, Lazarus\nTold the high sheriff\n   And bring you\n     dead or alive\n\n   Well then Lazarus told the sheriff, I ain't never been arrested\n\nWell Lazarus told\n  he sheriff,\n Says I ain't never\n    been arrested\n       by no man!\n        Lord, Lord\n        No man\n\n And then the sheriff,\n      he stabbed\n       Lazarus\n\n     Well the sheriff\n   stab Lazarus,\nwit a might big sword\n      Four feet\n       Oh Lord,\n      Four feet!\n\nWeeell, 'dey take ol' \n          Lazarus\n\n Yes they laid him on\nthe grasy plain,\n  Well the taken poor\n   poor ol' him\n And laid him on the\n    grassy plain.\n\nHe said, \n    My wounded side\n        Oh, Lord.\n    My wounded side.\n\n        O' Death\n\n O, Death\nO, Death\nWon't you spare me over til another year\n\nWell what is this\nI can't see\nWith ice cold hands takin' hold of me\n\nWhoa, death someone would pray\nCould you wait to call me another day\n\nThe children prayed, the preacher preached\nTime and mercy is out of your reach\n\nI'll fix your feet til you cant walk\nI'll lock your jaw so you can't talk\n\nI'll close your eyes so you can't see\nThis very air, come and go with me\n\nI'm death and I come to take the soul\nLeave the body and leave it cold\n\nTo draw up the flesh off the frame\nDirt and worm both have a claim\n\nO, death\nO, death\n\nWon't you spare me over till \nanother year\n\nMy mother came to my bed\nPlaced a cold towel upon my head\n\nMy head is warm my feet are cold\nDeath is-amovin upon my soul\n\nOh, death how you're treatin' me\nYou've closed my eyes so I can't see\n\nWell you're hurtin' my body\n\nYou're makin' me cold\nYou run the life right out of my soul\n\nOh death, please consider my age\nPlease don't take me at this stage\n\nMy wealth is all at your command\nIf you will move your icy hand\n\nOh the young, rich and poor\n\nThey hunger like me\nyou know\n\nNo wealth, no ruin, no silver or gold\nNothing satisfies me but your soul\n\nO, Death\nO, Death\n\nWon't you spare me over til another year\n\n   Geraldes wished for me to include this short one, not a song, yet I hear him often working away just singing the three same lines.\n\n\n\n\n\n Oh freedom, freedom\n    Freedom over me\n    And before\n  I'd be a slave,\n  I'd be buried\n  in my grave\nAnd go home to my Lord, and be free\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nRecorded & Arranged\nby\n       Alexander\n     de Stolistes", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "§bFrederick Thyrite", "1st of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================Our group has established a focus point in the southern region of the dwarven mountains. We are currently hunting something that has been plaguing the countryside. No idea as to what it is currently\n\n\n===================, , but I believe it has been a pack of wolves located somewhere near, as the tundra is quite the location to house wolf packs.\n\nThis scouting should hopefully be successful.\n==================\n\n5th of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================So currently our hunt has shown very little evidence of what beasts actually reside around this area. We have been getting attacked by various bands of cultists. Quite the nuisance I must say. Nothing has-\n\n===================actually developed apart from a few corpses of animals strewn about the area. We have scavenged them and used them for food, but rather than that. It has become quite... Quiet\n===================\n\n6th of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================Our band grows ever smaller, as our Orcish mercenary has fallen ill to some sort of fever. He awoke with various cuts along his body, with a trail of blood leading towards the rivers, nearby the mountains. He -\n\n===================claims to not remember anything, but I believe he attacked a beast and nearly died, too afraid to admit that. Perhaps we shall save this orc, or perhaps he shall be our downfall. Only the Creator knows.\n===================\n\n9th of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================We were awoken to a corpse outside our camp, apart from the orc which passed a day before. Our band of four found a wolf corpse, torn apart. It's jaw snapped in two with various bones protruding out of it. -\n\n===================And it was covered in Frost?! This confuses me, because only the mountains appear to be cold enough to give water, a shape. Well, I am starting to think that something is trying to lure us. There is one thing though. This is the -\n\n===================creature that we have been hunting for, and we shall capture it and skin it for our reward!\n===================\n\n11th of Sun's Smile, 1479\n===================We have found a cavern up to the north of our camp, it being the exit point of a stream which flows into the river below. As we approached it yesterday, it smelt, disgusting. Bones were strewn about the -\n\n===================entrance and blood stained the nearby stone. I am afraid for the rest of our band that we will not be able to make it, but I have a fair idea of what has been plaguing these mountains. I have only heard of these creatures in legends. -\n\n===================None I have known to have appeared in Athera. \nI guess it is time to try and test judgement, Creator give me strength, for the one that resides in the mountain is stronger than us all.\n\n===================-Frederick Thyrite, Leader of the 4th Band of the Green Pawed Hunters.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Lelien", "§bMithradites", "To the One for\n      Whom I Yearn\n\nEyes of striking emeralds,\n\nbroken heart, soon to be mended.\n\nOne can give only his love,\n\nto earn your own, currently suspended.\n\nWhen in this Tomb, the light touched naught,\n\nluminescence came from only our fires.\n\nBut when I saw you approach that day,\n\nthe chamber lit as if strewn with a thousand pyres.\n\nOne cannot take without permission,\n\nand you shan't give without desire.\n\nI shall not push, nor take your love,\n\nbut without you with me, my emotions expire.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOne is not a poet.", ""),
        StaticBook("SnowMan", "§bVioletoin", "Lyrics\n\nDo You Wanna Build A Snow Man:\n2-6\n\nDo You Wanna Build A Snowman.\n--\nDo you wanna build a snowman?\nCome on let's go and play\nI never see you anymore\nCome out the door\nIt's like you've gone away\nWe used to be best\n\nbuddies\nAnd now we're not\nI wish you would tell me why\nDo you wanna build a snowman\nIt doesn't have to be a snowman\n*go away Anna*\nOkay bye\n*knock*\nDo you wanna build a snowman?\n\nOr ride our bikes around the halls\nI think some company is overdue\nI started talking to the pictures on the walls\nIt gets a little lonely\nAll these empty rooms\nJust watching the hours tick by\n*tick tock tick tock*\n\nElsa, please, I know you're in there\nPeople are asking where you've been\nThey say have courage\nAnd I'm trying to\nI'm right out here for you\nJust let me in\nWe only have each other\nIt's just you and me\n\nWhat are we gonna do?\nDo you wanna build a snowman? *insert cry\n\n- xoxo\nNOW U DONT HAVE AN EXCUSE ANYMORE IF YOU FORGET LYRICS.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bird.", "§bflyingpanda2799", "The tree sways gently in the air,\nLimbs swinging about without a care,\nThe bird stays deeply in its cover,\nIts feathers such a wonderful color.\n\nBut when the wind stops,\nthe bird shall start to fly,\nover the human shops and up to the tree tops,\nbefore he lands on a branch with a sigh.\n\nThen the rain starts to fall,\nand the bird sings out with a sad little call,\nfor he has nowhere to go and call home,\nfor all he does is roam.\n\nHe lives where he sleeps.\nand sleeps where he can.\nbut for all the ones he keeps,\nhe always has to give it up to man.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spirit Realm", "§bShel'Yar", "The Spirit Realm, spoken as Frum’Stroh by Shamans, was created by the Daemon Apohet. Within the realm are three planes. The Ancestral Plane, the Elemental Plane, and the Immortal Plane. The Three planes in order of creation go EIA. Elemental, Immortal,\n\nthen Ancestral.\n\nThe First Plane is the Elemental plane, spoken as Voga’Stroh. It was created by Apohet to suit himself.  The Realm itself is difficult if not impossible for Shamans to map out. This is due to the fact that elementals are able to mold the\n\nrealm to their liking. Meaning that they can live anywhere, within any structure.\n\nThe next plane being the Immortal Plane, was created whenever powerful elementals requested a plane of their own. The Immortal Plane is at constant war bewteen the\n\nimmortals. This is mostly because each immortal represents an aspect of culture, emotion, and society. The Shamans said it is no place for rest, and is always difficult to carve a path through. It usually takes multiple Shamans working together.\n\nThe Ancestral Plane, spoken Stargush’Stroh by the Shamans. The Ancestral Plane is a resting place for the most powerful and honorable Uruks. Shamans say that the Ancestral Plan is heavily based on the mortal world. More experienced Shamans explained that\n\nwhen visiting, the sound is very much like a quiet constant noise. However, as you grow more experience as a Shaman, you can extrapolate from the noise to filter perceptions of senses. Thus allowing the Shaman to hear and see.", ""),
        StaticBook("Learning of Fire", "§b[Sillumir] Zaniil Tinuvriel", "Understanding the process behind Fire.§0\n§0\n§0As you are likely aware, a crucial aspect in learning to utilise fire, is in understanding how it shapes the world, and how it may be born of certain physical stimulation; as is the case with fire and\n\nlightning. §0\n§0\n§0A good practice at any stage, but certainly in the beginning of your journey, is to meditate within close proximity to real-world fire. As you connect to the void, feel the warmth against your skin and the crackling of the wood beneath\n\nflames.§0\n§0\n§0It is imperative that you gain a great deal of understanding if you wish to progress. It is also important to note that despite what many will tell you, the art of Fire evocation is not only a boon for violence.\n\nIt is responsible for your warmth in the winter, for the shaping of ores and stones that aid your city, and in feeding your kin. §0\n§0\n§0Without fire, civilisation would not have advanced to its current state. It is truly the element of the modern day.\n\nUtilising the element of Fire.§0\n§0\n§0You are now at the stage where you understand the complexities of your chosen element. You have connected to the void, and you wish to bring forth -for whatever reason- this element into the world.\n\nBe aware of how fire is born. It is far easier to summon an ember and add to it, than it is to summon a colossal inferno.\n\nJust as the passing of time feeds fire, so too will it aid your ability if you harbour the patience.\n\nOf all evocation, it is truly noted that Fire is most interesting, when pertaining to the subject of shaping the world.§0\n§0\n§0For it is the only element that can continue to thrive in the world without your direct influence. It is capable of feeding\n\non a source of fuel, and quite likely sparks the ember of a real flame that replaces it.§0\n§0\n§0This will serve as a great boon to you, as unlike other evocationists, you will spend less mana utilising it. Once you have summoned a flame, it is only\n\nnecessary for you to add to its intensity if you wish to hasten a natural reaction; or create an unusually large flame.§0\n§0\n§0A word of caution:\n\nI do hope that in reading this text, you have gained an understanding in how to utilise\n\nevocation. However, I can only hope that your intention is to utilise this element for the good of your nation, and not for mindless violence.§0\n§0\n§0It is with a heavy heart that I have been forced to use this upon those that would wish harm against me.\n\nLet us hope that you do not suffer the same ill fate. In light of this, may your studies continue to aid the progression of your mind and your people as you advance.\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya \n\n- Zaniil Tinuvriel", ""),
        StaticBook("A request", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "Okarir'Indor,\n\nI formally request that I may withdraw my book, \"An Encyclopedic Arcanum\" (Arcane Magic) That I may make a few copies of the work.\n\nThank you,\nGallidron Elindrow", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation", "§bEnedor Pastly", "Elemental Evocation§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0Elemental Evocation is the art of drawing a  temporary form of an element from the void using mana. §0\n§0This sounds simple however it is much harder to do in practice. This is because you cannot actually\n\npull an element from the void, you actually pull a substance that mimics the properties of a chosen element. §0\n§0This means when learning magic one must study their element in order to understand how it works.§0\n§0It is worth noting that evocationists have §0\n\nNO power over existing elements.§0\n§0\n§0The Void§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0The void is said to be an infinate plane of potential thought surrounded by darkness. §0\n§0Since we find complete darkness very hard to imagine, the first step\n\nto learning any arcane magic is to meditate in order to try and get an understanding of the void.§0\n§0\n§0It is believed that the creator pulled everything to existence from the void and therefore it is possible for us to use some of the void's energy\n\nto cause changes to the world around us.§0\n§0\n§0Mana§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0Mana is like an invisible liquid. It flows around the world and exists in all living things, including us.§0\n§0\n§0Mages use mana to draw their spells from the\n\nvoid. §0\n§0\n§0The term 'Mana Pool' is used to describe how much mana an individual has. Your mana pool determines the strength and duration of spells that a mage can cast. The more experienced a mage is, the better they can§0\n§0manipulate mana.\n\nTypes of Elemental Evocation.§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0Each evocable element is treated as a subtype of magic as each element has specific properties that have to be studied before one can perform the magic.\n\nFire Evocation§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0Fire Evocation is perhaps the most widely used Evocation as it has many uses.§0\n§0One can create fireballs that can be used in combat or can simply use fire as a heat and light source when traveling.\n\nFire evocation is said to be one of the easiest elements to evoke but one of the hardest to control.\n\nEarth Evocation§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0Earth evocation, like fire evocation has many uses aside from combat. The art of summoning rocks and minerals found in the earth is quite usefull for defensive and brute force combat although the art of\n\ncreating and using materials found in the earth has many more uses.§0\n§0\n§0Earth is a harder element to evoc as it is a more solid element then, for example water.\n\nWater Evocation§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0Water is a very diverse element. Water can be found as liquid, solid and gas, all of which can be evoked. §0\n§0Ice is normally used in combat.§0\n§0Water can be used for more day to day tasks like cleaning. §0\n\nSteam isn't evoked much as it has little use and is hard to learn.§0\n§0\n§0Water evocationists also have control over the temprature of their water.\n\nAir Evocation§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0Air evocation is certainly one of the least used evocation. It generally has less uses then the other evocations.  §0\n§0Air evocation can be used mostly for defensive combat as one can use it to push back enemies\n\nand even block some magical attacks. §0\n§0\n§0Air can also be used for some simpler tasks such as cleaning and cooling oneself  down with a breeze. §0\n§0Air evocation is hard to study as the element is invisible to our eyes. Instead a mage must feel it to learn how\n\nit works.§0\n§0\n§0Electrial Evocation§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0Electrial Evocation is one of the most powerfull evocable elements however it is very hard to control and consumes a lot of energy.§0\n§0Commonly Electrial evocationists create\n\nbolts of electricity to combat their enemies. Though they have to be careful because just like electricity the element is easily attracted to metal.§0\n§0\n§0It also takes longer to summon electricity then the other elements because it uses more energy and\n\nmore mana then, for example, summoning a small ball of water.§0\n§0\n§0Dangers/side effects of evocation.§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0The side effects of  Elemental Evocation are  similar to other arcane magics and should certainly be looked into beforet\n\ndeciding to learn the magic.§0\n§0\n§0Side effects include:§0\n§0\n§0-Decreased life span.§0\n§0\n§0-Becoming physically weaker and frail. (This is why many mages use staffs)§0\n§0-On some occasions mages have been driven mad by the lust\n\nfor power.§0\n§0\n§0Most of these problems are caused by the fact that magic isn't a natural task for our bodies to carry out and therefore it damages us.\n\nLearning magic§0\n§0___________________§0\n§0\n§0If you do decide you want to learn the art of evocation, the best way to go about it would be to find a teacher. This is a hard and lengthy process that can take many years, however the way you do this is up\n\nto you.§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("~\\ Wheat Poem /~", "§bRenn Stirling", "-=o=-   Wheat  -=o=-\n         ~~~~~~\nA Golden Glisten of Summer Sea,\nGraceful Arms Wave to and fro.\nA Warm Sensation Runs Through,\nA Feeling of Protect and Peace Bestow.\n\nSoft Movements from a Gentle Breeze,\n\nGrace, Prosperity is of Nature's Own.\nThin Straws of Vigor and Strength,\nA Sense of Light Against the Unknown.\n\nLand's Children of Grain,\nTreated as a Gift that Provides Life.\nA Gift of Quelling Formidable Hunger,\n\nA Mighty Savior of Times of Strife.\n\nLife of Giving, a Seed to a Stalk,\nO' Nature, Grant me Day and Week.\nThat the Grains Retain their Numbers,\nFor a Life Without Wheat Shows Bleak.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tasks: Lesson", "§bLillith Winterleaf", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n\n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nVerbal Lesson on Natural Resources: This should directly follow a gathering of a variety of natural resources. Take the Dedicant aside to a quiet place so you will avoid interruption. Take each item the Dedicant has brought you and explain,\n\nin your own words and opinion, the purpose of the item, its uses, its place in nature, and anything else you feel worth mentioning about it. Return each item afterwards for the Dedicant to study further on their own if they so desire.\n\nAsk them questions about what you have told them to ensure they have paid attention and learned from you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Unknown Origins", "§bVellulaei'thill Vul'athri", "The Dark Arts.\n\nChapter 1: Lifeforce.\n\nIt is said that a necromancer uses that of life force to bring others back to life or to drain and tain the land around them. Life force in a sense is basically the life energy of others in-\n\nOur world, Like mana life force flows about within us. However life force and mana are two seprate things entirly. When life force is brought out of the body it apears in a blackish mist of sorts. When a necromancer uses such mist they use their own life-\n\nForce and in return slowly kill themselves in the process.\n\n\n       The Taint\n\nTaint is what is known as the residue left behind by lifeforce, When life force is used in the world it creates taint which is-\n\nLet out by the life force. Taint is said to be used for many things in Necromancy. From tainting large ammounts of land to that of tainting an object to increase it's power. It is said that by even being near taint is drains those that are near it. Slowly\n\nCausing sharp needle like pains to tear across their joints and the like. However if one were to consume said taint the tain's effect would double.\n\n[!] The rest of the pages seem to be riped out. Perhaps lost within the vast regions of the fringe [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Tasks: Poetry", "§bLillith Winterleaf", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn.\n\n~The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Winterleaf\n\nPoetry: A poem is an excellent way to judge one's particular affinity towards nature, and what specific aspect of Nature they are drawn to. This also can help the Dedicant get an idea what Totem they may wish to choose if they reach attunement,\n\nfor they will usually write about that which they are drawn to.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electrical Evo", "§bLelien", "Electrical\n     Evocation\n\n   §\n\n*Once you flip to the second page, a current, about the strength of a electrical fence, would jolt through you. Most likely rendering you unconcious.*\n\nWith magical love,\nSilvos and Lelien.\n*A small heart is drawn at the bottom*", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Witches", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "An\n       Encounter\n           With\n      Frost Witches\n/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\\n\n            By\n   Gallidron Elindrow\n\nI first learned of the dreaded creatures known as Frost Witches from one of the tomes of the grand libraries of old Haelun'or. I remember the fear that gripped me as a child when I learned of their macabre ways. Though as an adult of more mature\n\nconstitution and greater understanding, I revisted the subject of \"monsters\" and relearned the available details of the Frost Witch.\nThay are exclusivly women, so far as any adventurer who's survived an encounter with them can tell. They are grotesque and\n\nunnatural to look upon. Grey skinned and with eyes like ice they appear in their true form. But it is not so easy to spot them, for Ice Witches are masters of disguise and employ illusion to hide their nature. In fact, as the story goes, they will adopt\n\nthe guise of a young woman and sit and cry in the midst of a snowy glade to lure in unsuspecting men. The clever frost witch will attract the unwitting male and take him to the rest of her coven. There to be devoured by these fiends. They are, without\n\nexception, powerful magic users, though the older ones are the more dangerous and adept. In fact, every frost witch draws her power from a \"Witch Mother\" who is the head of her particular coven. Like unto a queen bee she will build her nest and gather\n\n\\    \"   `  I  '   \"     /\n  \\   \"   ` I '  \"     /\n    \\  O  {X}  O   /\n    /\\ , O II O ,  /\\ \n^ / % \\  ! I !   / % \\ ^\nl/ ``~'' \\  %  / ``~'' \\l\n\\ * X *  \\  /  * X * /\n  \\ i i,.,{   x   },.,i i /\n    \\     /  \\     /\n      \\ / `  ' \\  /\n            %\nG1\n\nworkers who rely upon her, and she them to some extent. When another frost witch is of sufficient power and experience she may set out to create her own coven. They begin by searching for women who are depressed or sadened. The frost witch will then mark\n\nwoman with a curse that will appear as little more than a bruise upon the back of the woman's neck. If the marked female succombs to her sadness and grief, she will become a frost witch herself. Thus do their numbers swell. It is reportedly a favorite\n\ntactic of the frost witches to eat a married man and then mark his grieving widow. Thus they gain both a meal and a potential coven member. The woman who is marked may not become a frost witch \"if her faith is strong and she resist her sadness to seek\n\nafter joy\", as the old tomes say. Though it should be noted that there is no known way to remove the curse once it is applied. The woman in question will most likely live with the mark for the rest of her days.\n\nIn order to destroy a frost witch coven one must destroy the witch mother. In some cases this alone is enough to cause the coven to whither and die over time. In other cases, however, another witch may be of sufficient strength to rise up and assume the\n\nrole of witch mother and the coven can limp on. If one is a \"monster hunter\" of sorts, then you will likely want to exterminate as many of the witches as possible to reduce the chances of this occuring.\n\nIt is important to note that frost witches are not rabid animals. They are clever and capable of reasoning. It is possible to treat with them, but the humor of the witch can change quickly and every moment you stand in their pressence you are in grave\n\ndanger. In truth they are fickle and there is no telling what a frost witch might do, should you seek to speak with them. It is said, however, that if one finds a frost witch in disguise and calls them out, the frost witch is bound by her curse to offer\n\nthe clever mortal one favor. But this is only rumor and would prove dangerous to study.\n\nA great deal of the knowledge I possess has come from the reading of books. But I have done some field research as well. The following pages will detail my, albeit brief, encounter with the frost witches.\n\nI was told of a coven of frost witches to be found far in the north, by a man of the nation of Salvas. His name was Archrim Elmoran and he had encoutered these witches himself. How the man survived I do not know, for it seems that the witches were intent\n\non eating him. I told me that there was an ancient ruin that the witches called home, upon a lonely and frozen peak. The coordinates were as follows.\n{X 153, Y -3762}\n\nI, being curious, set out to see this for myself. I traveled far into the north from\n\nmy home in the warm waters of New Haelun'or and traversed the mountains of the north.\n\nThere, I found a most curious set of ruins which seemed to at one point have been a church or temple of some sort. They were in a valley to the south of the\n\nreported witches lair. It is there that I found the symbols marked G1 (glyph 1) which you saw earlier in this book.  What ever ancient civilization left these ruins, I would be most interested to learn more about them. Whilst searching about I had the\n\ngood fortune to happen upon another Mali'aheral, a High Elf woman named Allona. After ensuring that she was not one of the dreaded frost witches I asked what she was doing in those parts. Apparently she was a mage and had sought solitude to meditate and\n\nincrease her skills. The ruins that we were in had provided such solitude until I had interrupted it. She warned me that the frost witches where still about, though further up the mountain range, and she advised me against going to investigate the area.\n\nWe spoke for a while longer before she showed me a cavern that she had discovered just north of the ruins. It held an ancient library of sorts and had evidently been of some importance to whatever people had left it behind. The books were too ruined to\n\nread, but the very exsistance of such a place is highly facinating. However, I digress.\n\nAfter parting ways I decided to go on and look in on the frost witches. It was not my intention to actually interact with them or get close enough to do so.\n\nWhen I approached their lonely peak an icey wind blew past me and seemed to steal the very warmth of my blood away. An ancient and imposing structure sat atop the peak and looked for all the world to be abandoned. Using some wit and no small amount of\n\ndexterity I climbed the peak, agianst my better judgment and explored the old fortress.\n\nIt was empty as I suspected, though the air was somehow even colder within. After looking around a bit I thought I saw foot prints in the snow, or at the very least\n\nimpressions of where something had been. They were by an alcove under the main floor of the ruin. As I approached I heard something moving on the other side of the alcove and quickly hid. A wall moved out and one of the menacing creatures emerged\n\ncautiosly from the hole. The frost witch looked about as though she knew I was there and crept forward. For all the world I thought I was doomed. Doomed for my curiosity and for my foolish assumption that the keep was empty. Only then did I realize. They\n\ndid not live in the delapidated structure atop the mountain, they lived beneith it. A man from Salvas had told me that those mountains were full of caverns and tunnels.\n\nThe witch moved forward and I could have sworn she could smell me. Then, just before\n\nshe reached my hiding place, she turned and went up the stairs to the main floor. I took no more chances and I ran for my life. I was out of the keep and down the mountain as quickly as gravity and semi-safe desent would permit.\n\nIn closing. Frost Witches are a dangerous facination and one should not seek them lightly. They are still there, so far as I know, lurking in the tunnels beneath that frozen mountian. \nI hope this book has been interesting at least and helpful at best.\n\nI hope that you remember what you have read should you ever have....\n\nAn encounter with Frost Witches.\n\nPublishing date\n18th of Deep cold, 1516\n\nby Gallidron Elindrow\n\nDedicated to Archrim Elmoran, the human who risked life and limb to discover the hold of the Frost Witches and told me about it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wilds Task", "§bArinislia", "For this simple task, I left from my Guide Lillith's Grove and set off into the southern wilds nearby. I ventured here before with another task of collecting the different plants and found this area quite enjoyable to walk through.\n\nDay 1\n\nI found a suitable clearing where I quickly set up camp. I find it humorous that my guide think I would find this unpleasant to do. She seem to forget that I had been travelling for a time and although I do find this quite demeaning,\n\nI am rather used to it now. I laid out the items she has given me. Three jungle saplings, 3 seeds, 8 bonemeal, 6 dough, the tent set up behind me of course, 1 dandelion, 4 empty bottles, and one water bottle. Given how much bonemeal I was given, I assumed\n\nit was meant for the seeds rather than the saplings itself. \n\nDay 2\n\nI set about planting the seeds into the ground near the tent and moved alittle further out to plant the jungle saplings. I am not familiar with\n\nthis plant so I have given it as much space as possible. Keeping them watered, I preceded to plant the dandelion into the ground just outside the flap of my tent. The dough provided is serving well, only making small amounts of bread and taking little\n\n bites as possible while filling the bottles up with water at a nearby stream. \n\nDay 3 \n\nIt is quite peaceful out here. I always found nature to be so. Though I do love the magical structures and buildings of my\n\nkind more, this will do as well. I am been pondering this Grand Task for awhile. I have a few ideas and will take them in motion once I am done here. The seeds have started to spout, showing life within the plant as it grows. I sprinkled just a small\n\namount of bonemeal on the plants, helping them along while I went to tend to the saplings. The saplings themselves seemingly larger now as well. \n\nDay 4\n\nI awoke to find the seeds turned into small strands of wheat.\n\nThey are still quite green and not yet ready to be harvested, though I think I shall leave them be and let them stay grown. The saplings have grown larger as well, already taller than my own form with a few branches sprouted here and there. This task\n\nseems simple enough, doing what I already do, observe. I do recall standing in the fairy ring, feeling the life around me. I heard the song once more, I seek to hear it again. \n\nDay 5\n\nI bathe in the nearby spring to make my\n\nappearance presentable to a passerby that happens to come across me. The saplings now turned into small jungle trees. I sprinkled some bonemeal on them so they can grow alittle more faster. The wheat now fully grown and quite full of life.\n\nI feel that my time here is coming to an end. I have already packed up the tent and put away the supplies that was given to me. The trees now grown even more than when I have last seen them. The dandelion's petals bloomed fully and resting near where I\n\nhave slept. Prehaps I shall return here after I am attuned. Though I do think there are more tasks ahead.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Formal Request", "§bMajystur Laurenzo", "*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*       A Formal Request\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*          Dedicated To:\n\n      The Courtship of\n      Lelien Aeléyèlsa\n&       Zeus Ith'ael\n\n\n\n\nUpon the birth of your precious offspring, I request permission to sacrafice it to an unnamed god, or unseen evil presence at the peak of Dun'Suldur.\n\n\n\n\nAt the completion of the sacrificial ceremony, I plan to promptly dedicate a song upon the forsaken organ to the bonding of your child's soul, and that of the unquenchable lust for chaos of the iniquitous phantom.\n\n\n\n\nDo you accept this proposal?\n\n[] Yes.\n\n[] No.\n\n\n\n\nI patiently await your response, and hope that you find my proposition reasonable and acceptable.\n\n\n\n\n*The message would be left without a closing signature, nor any other signs of who initially wrote it.*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Anonymous", "*The pages seem to be written in a near-illegible scrawl*\n\nBark of iron, deep in the south. The rip in the world that we must embrace! It gives gifts! It gives wonderful gifts to those who serve!\n\nA blade most perfect! So perfect that it does not belong in our world!\n\nAll it takes is a few drops of blood! A few drips from your wrist, and it shall awaken! And when it does, it will look upon you with\n\nsuch favour! The sweetest favour! It is an impossible thing, but it is a wonderful thing! Seek it out, brothers and sisters!\n\nSeek it seek it seek it deep in the south, for amongst the Islands of the\n\nAnkulos Peninsula, it waits for others to appreciate its luminescence!\n\n*A second piece of writing by a different hand is scribbled below the first*\n\nDo not trust it. The tree is evil in a\n\nway that I cannot comprehend. Take only its first gift, and then never return.\n\n*A third piece of writing by yet another hand is scrawled at the very bottom of the page*\n\nTake nothing from it! It wants only to consume! It consumes everything! It will consume you! I can't get it off me I can't get it off me I can't get it out of me only flame will end it\nBurN th TrEE\n\n*The writing trails off to nothing*", ""),
        StaticBook("Op. Watershead", "§bGrigor Grandaxe", "Operation Watershead\nOffical Plan Documented and coined by Grigor Grandaxe of Oren.\n\nThis plan will ensure that Oren has all of the bargening power when it comes to the undead\n\nPhase One: Gather a number of men together, preferably between 5 and 10 men.\n\nDistribute cloaks to each of them, which they will put on.\n\nMeet outside of the Front Gate of Petrus.\n\nPhase 2: With inside help navigate through Kal Agnar, attempting to be undetected. (Orders surrounding this will be established at the time.)\n\nLocate Velkan Ironborn the Second when he is on his own.\n\nPhase 3: With Velkan alone, Grigor will distract him. In the mean time Farhorn, aided by the others will knock him out, gag him and tie him in chains. He will then be escorted to Petrus.\n\nPhase 4: Velkan will be placed in the Torture chamber of Petrus, bound by Iron bars.\n\nPetrus is then entitled to extract info from Velkan, to capture an officals in Kal Agnar and use all of it as barganing power.\n\nPhase 5: Establish the demands Petrus would like.\n\nPetrus now has info, and important people of the Undead.\n\nKey Phrases in time of emergancy:\n\nGreen Apples: Run back to Petrus Now\n\nRed Potato: Come over ehre so I can whisper\n\nBlue Shakr: We have been Spotted\n\nPlan Mark I\nby Grigor Grandaxe\n\nFor the Eyes of Tuvya, Edmund, Nicholas Blackwell and Grigor Grandaxe only.", ""),
        StaticBook("Navitas II", "§b[Child] Silus Hightower", "As soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World. The Descendants stood still for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees.\n\nMalin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to corrupt their souls,\n\n the brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\n\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\n\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\n\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into thin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("AUTOGRAPH", "§bHannah Tosscobble", "Don't spend it\n      all at once\n\n            ;)\n\n\n\n                 -love,\n                    M\n                 E\n         K   E", ""),
        StaticBook("Ender Eyes", "§bSalamandra", "Pearl Eyes of Ender\n\nWoe was the poor elf, tricked by two humans, who asked him to show them the way to Galahar. Yet along the way, they said they heard something in the brush, and so the elf followed. They quickly turned on him, stole his belongings\n\nand gouged out his eyes, though why is not known. Though he feigned to be dead, once the humans had left, he dragged himself back towards Laurelin. Found by the Elves: weak, lowly, and grunting he was, and he was taken to the Druid's Grove. There a Druid\n\nnamed Dante took pity on the poor Elf, and commanded him merely rest on the floor. He could not give the Elf his old eyes, that much of he was sure. But taking two enderpearls, the Druid heated them with fire, then coated them with something unknown. He\n\nplaced them in the Elf's eyesockets and the Elf could see, though we imagine all the colors were warped. The eyes lasted over a century, before the Elf found others, and we imagine they would have lasted much longer. \n\nThe Druid's name was Dante Flormai.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fun Poems", "Tantaparo", "If you are a dreamer, come in,\nIf you are a dreamer,\nA wisher, a liar,\nA hope-er, a pray-er,\nA magic bean buyer,\ncome in,\nIf you are a looker, A lover, A helper, A dancer, A worker, A kisser,\ncome in,\nIf you hate, leave.\n\nMillie McDeevit screamed a scream\nSo loud it made her eyebrows steam.\nShe screamed so loud\nHer jawbone broke,\nHer tongue caught fire,\nHer nostrils smoked...\n\nA spider lives inside my head\nWho weaves a strange and wondrous web\nOf silken threads and silver strings\nTo catch all sorts of flying things, Like crumbs of thought and bits of smiles\nAnd specks of dried-up tears,\n------Continue on--\n\nAnd dust of dreams that catch and cling\nFor years and years and years . . .", ""),
        StaticBook("Bundle of poems", "§bthomas20101997", "In Ithilien \n----------------The leaves of the beeches breathe the sparkling air of day's awakening.\n\nThe birches spread the buds of leaves for small singing birds to linger there. \n---------------\n\n\n----------------In Ithilien, land of the tunefull waterfalls wandering together heals my beloved.\n\n\n\n\n\n---------------\n\n      Galadriel\n----------------In joy thou hast lived. Beware of the sea!\n\nIf thou hearest the cry of the gull on the shore Thy heart shall rest in the forest no more\n\n---------------\n\n    Vi Dyr Ennui\n----------------In western lands beneath the sun. \nIn spring, flowers rise, the trees bud, waters run, and the merry little birds sing. \n\nThere it is cloudles night and-\n---------------\n\n\n----------------shuddering beechs hold the starry host, the white jewels, on their branching hair.\n\nHere at my path's end I am lingering in deep darkness buried. Beyond-\n---------------\n\n----------------towers strong and high. Beyond all mountains steep.\n\nAbove all shadows rides the sun. And stars always dwell. I will not say \n'The day is done'\nOr to the stars \n'Farewell'\n---------------\n\n     Thinnuel\n----------------At starfade a time comes. When you see one brilliant star left behind. When the starry host ha departed. The star fades, the world does not wait.\n\nWhy do I linger-\n---------------\n\n\n----------------and sing under this fading light.\n\nThere is a daisy among the elanor blossems. \nTo me it is fair.\n\nThere is a birch tree under the-\n---------------\n\n\n----------------mallorn trees.\nTo me it is fair.\n\nThere is a butterfly above the swan.\nTo me it is fair.\n\nA small star follows sirius. \n---------------\n\n\n----------------\nTo me it is fair.\n\nThe leaves of the mallorn are numberless. One tiny leaf, one fading leaf holds my eye. When will it fall?\n\nThe brilliant star-\n---------------\n\n\n----------------iis fading. Now it departs to the heavens. \n\nNow I will depart the world holding a leaf in my hand.\n\n\n\n---------------", ""),
        StaticBook("What is magic?", "§bElenthor Mithri", "What is magic?\nNot litteraly, no, figurativley. What is the arcane? Many are born with it, and can consider its power a blessing or a curse. Those who choose to seek it out either get more than they bargined for, or come up empty handed. It is two sides\n\nof a coin realy. Many become consumed by the power of the void for example, the 9 scourge members, who destroyed our home Anthos. And the undead who long passed still remain in the minds of men. These are all examples of the coruption of magic.\n\nThose that persue good and kindness have a more powerfull magic that is hard to channel but far more powerfull. Dark magic is easy to channel but is reckless and hard to controll. There are few out there that can handle the power of strong magic before it\n\nconsumes you. A great example of a once great warlock was the White Wizard. He lived for many a year and survived all the transitions into the new worlds. Some say he grew corupt, others say he was killed. But the majority say he is alive and still pure\n\nof heart. It is hard to find good teachers in magic, the white wizard or the \"white one\" is known to have taught most of the powerfull sorcerers in this land today. Though this is just mith and fantasy.", ""),
        StaticBook("A mad man Vol. I", "§bHileia Sythaerin", "§l   The Ramblings§0\n§0§l        of a§0\n§0§l      Mad Man§0\n§0\n§0 §0§oBy Hileia'Vione Sythaerin, his wife and§0\n§0§opeacekeeper in days of trouble.§0\n§0\n§0§oTo any that may read this, let it be known that he is not a bad person. His intentions have always been\n\n§opure, and he would§0\n§0§onever harm another§0\n§0§opure mali'aheral by§0\n§0§ochoice. Any words I write in these volumes are his, quoted directly and unchanged. Please read with caution.\n\n\"Vio, get me a glass of wine.\" He called coming home late once again, his skin whithered and blackened, his hair wild and loose. His ankles were sounding especially worn out. He immediatly went upstairs and sat down in his chair again. His staff in hand,\n\nhis ramblings continued. §0\n§0\n§0\"Great work today. Progress. Maehr'sae. Suliin'thill is still quiet. The dog barks. The owl sits upon his pole, observing. My ankles ache, he tells me to take off my feet but I can't. The gold is locked. I am in pain.\"\n\nHe coughs. His fits have been getting worse. I am afraid for his health but there's nothing I can do. I give him his wine. §0\n§0\n§0\"Ahern ito nae'leh, Vio.\" He says, immediatly acting as if nothing was wrong. He takes a sip. The ramblings continue.\n\n\"I am three centuries old. My wife brings me my wine. I am a noble, I live in Kal'Alras, I started as a guard, I ended up a King. I don't remember how. Or I do. I don't know. Aislin came, Aislin left. I have his eye. Dwarves came, Dwarves left. I took\n\ntheir gold. Kyral came, Kyral left. I took her nation. The Basilisk sat§0\n§0upon the throne, minding his daily business until an odd one came to my city in search of gems. He looked similar to me. Pale, bright haired, long ears. A high elf, yes. Mali'aheral,\n\nhe taught me. From Haelun'or, he said he was. Yes, Haelun'or, a city of Mali'aheral far away on the isle of Malinor of Asulon. Vio packed my bag. I went with him. The basilisk's wife was on the throne. I was on a boat. It took days for us to arrive.\n\nAnd there I was. This odd island, filled with luscious, giant forests and populated by elves. We travelled on. Walked, through forests, a long path. In the distance, there it stood. An immense city, guarded by a bridge and surrounded by a steep cliffside.\n\nHaelun'or. I was only three centuries old when I- No. I was already three centuries old when I found my home. It took me three centuries after the fire to find my family again. I rapidly forgot about the throne, gave up my palace for a hall in this city\n\nof Silver. Vio joined me a few weeks later. We left Alras to the rats. Told the citizens they should move to their old queen Kyral, to Salvus. They did. I didn't care. I had met the High Elves. I was home.\"§0\n§0\n§0He fell asleep in his chair again.\n\nHe woke up two days later. The ebony marks on his skin had faded again, he appeared ready to leave the house once more. I did his ponytail as I do every morning and kissed him goodbye. But as he left the house, he twitched, and I feared him.\n\nThat evening the rambling continued once more.§0\n§0\n§0\"Elvulnir, Uradir, playful little trickster. Always playing games on people, well not this time mister. Falling objects we observed, studied all, even the way they curved.\n\nNow into a force we've summarized it, a force like magic, isn't that splendid? You tried to teach me illusion, tried to make me a mage like Lucion, tried to make me join your guild, now look at the empire I've built. A magic we did create, and master it I\n\nsoon did. A power so great I lost control, and started becoming less fit. With my physique my mind too failed, for the years were catching up to me. Then one day when I was minding my work, I was gruesomely maimed. And so began, 'tis not a joke, the story\n\nof Professor Silverhands.\"§0\n§0\n§0He smiled. I'm not sure what to do. I just wrote down his words and walked away. I was afraid. Bad things happen when he digs into his past, and it appears that thing inside him is forcing him to.\n\nA few days later I came to visit him in the labs, he hadn't come home last night. I found him sitting in this odd, insanely bright white chamber behind his chair, talking to himself again.\n\n\"I am not impure. I have not, nor will I ever taint my blood with an action any less pure than studying and reading. I am good. \nI am not impure.\nI am not.\nI am.\nI might be.\nI don't know anymore.\n\nI fear it sometimes.\nAlthough I shouldn't.\nMaybe I should.\nIt gives me power.\nNo, that's wrong.\nPerhaps strenght?\nAnyway, where was I?\nI don't recall.\nNeed to sleep.\"\n\nThere he stopped again, and blacked out against the ever so bright walls of his little room of purity. \n\nI can't stand writing this anymore for now, perhaps I will continue another day.\n\n-Vol. I, H'V Sythaerin", ""),
        StaticBook("The book", "§bEnedor Pastly", "I want to learn magic because I am fascinated with it. But eventually fascination leads to anticipation. §0\n§0Its very hard to say why you want to learn evocation without just saying \"because I want to\" but I will do my best.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Next page...\n\nI am physically quite weak and not able to defend myself or others around me, I would like to learn evocation in order to defend myself and others around me. Normally if I or someone I know is confronted I can do little as I'm not good with the sword or\n\nbow. Evocation could give me a boost and help me fight back, or at the least defend myself.§0\n§0\n§0Magic is capable of destruction but does not have to be used in combat. I would want to learn evocation for much simpler tasks. Fire can be used to\n\ncreate a light in darkeness and air could be used to clean surfaces of dust and small objects.§0\n§0\n§0These smaller uses could prove handy for me as a traveler. §0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Just a little more...\n\nSo in short:§0\n§0\n§0-I have been facinated in how evocation magic works and this has lead me to wanting to do it myself. §0\n§0-I want to learn it to help defend myself and others as I am weak at most combats.§0\n§0-The simpler tasks you can do with magic would be very\n\nhandy for my life style. §0\n§0\n§0Sorry for making it a little long, I wanted to try and explain it as best as I can.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Child Poems One", "§bAthri'narncael'onn", "Elves§0\n§0-------------------        A Poem by Athri'narncael'onn§0\n§0-------------------      Inteh desert, in the sea, in the woods of a bar-o-ny the Elves always seem to show. §0\n§0       In the mud in the snow, The Elves can make do with things.§0\n§0\n\n      But in the sky no§0\n§0race can guide the Elves are yet to prevail. Oh my, Oh my what a beautiful sky only if we could reach it.§0\n§0   But in The First Seed, Nanrainia'maehr flew her kite in the night. But when a large gale hit the kite the girl came off\n\nthe ground! The first elf to fly, the first race to fly, what a race the Elves are!§0\n§0\n§0\n§0        Maehr'sae§0\n§0        Industries§0\n§0-------------------       Maehr'sae, Maehr'sae what a wonderful name, one of the most wonderful labs!\n\n   Maehr'sae, Maehr'sae, finds the facts! If it's animals, redstone, it doesn't matter!§0\n§0      Maehr'sae finds the facts.§0\n§0       §0\n§0         Mining§0\n§0-------------------    Dwarves, dwarves, dwarves. Mining because they're dwarves! Redstone,\n\n Coal, even some stones, dwarves will mine for days!§0\n§0\n§0        Vines\n-------------------     Vines, vines, vines. You can learn all about vines!\n          Going up trees! Creeping across fields, vines will never stop! In the desert,\n\n in the rain, In the night in the day, in the woods, even in Haelun'or!\n \n         An Apple\n-------------------     An apple, a steak, a lemon, a melon, it's all the same!\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Shade of Desire", "§bAnonymous", "One§0\n§0           Shade§0\n§0         Of Desire§0\n§0\n§0\n§0by Anonymous\n\nOnce a young and handsome guard of the city was on patrol. He had lived his life in honor and glory as a soldier of Haelun'or, though he was terribly lonely. He had never found a woman to love.§0\n§0\n§0Though on this night, he would meet someone who would change\n\nhis life forever. She was beautiful and fair and he knew she was special.§0\n§0\n§0She didn't seem to know him but she could sense the connection to him, the tension that could only be released in one way.\n\nAs they lock eyes they both knew that they would surrender to passion that night. As they drifted into the shadows together, her true nature as a SHADE became evidents and her tentacles shot forward to bind him. §0\n§0Fade to black.....", ""),
        StaticBook("Wood elves.", "§bEnedor Pastly", "Wood elves:§0\n§0Appearance:§0\n§0Shorter then other elves, often have red or brown hair.§0\n§0\n§0Their smaller size makes them agile and fast. They are good at suprise attacks and ascapes in their favoured woodlands.§0\n§0\n\nLocation: §0\n§0Wood elves live usually in woody, natural unspoilt environments as the name suggests. Laureh lin is a common place to find wood elves.§0\n§0Magic:§0\n§0Many wood elves take up druid magic. Much of this  involves healing and controll over nature.\n\nAging:§0\n§0Like other elves wood elves can live for a long time. It is said that some elves have lived up to 1200 although this is quite unusual as many die of disease, murder and physical harm.", ""),
        StaticBook("Potions", "§bJeffwise Sadget", "Regen\nNormal Water\nLilypad/Vine and tippens root\n\nHaste\nNormal Water\nPoisonous potato and egg\nStrength\nNormal Water\nRed mushroom, cactus, brown mushroom", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes IV", "§bArchmage Crumena", "Second of the Deep Cold, 1498 \nCrumena Ilwindior\n\nNote to self, Elindor demands Elven yak milk. Cannot be human grown. Forbids it to be Druid grown. Says he will know instantly if it is. What even is 'Elven' yak milk?", ""),
        StaticBook("*an old scroll*", "§bThurak'Yar", "*as you unfurl the length of the tattered, yellowing scroll before you, you would find that instead of runes or notes, pictures adorn the aged reed paper. It would seem to be the retelling of an event, or, perhaps, a prophecy*\n\n*the first scrawling depicts a small, hunched figure warming himself by a crude fire. Around him is a scribbled, complete blackness, broken only by the light from his meagre flames*\n ////////////\n////// O////////\n//// # |-| //////\n\n*the campfire has grown to a bonfire, and around it figures dance and drink. The black of the night is all but gone in the presence of the light and merryment*\n  //////////////\n  //// # ////////\n //// ## {O} O| ///\n /// #### ||   |  ///\n\n*a hush seems to have fallen over the camp as the night grows longer, and the fire has withered significantly. The black creeps in once again as the weary rest*\n  ///////////\n/////////////\n///// # //////\n//// ### __o //\n\n*blackness covers the next page; unbroken and unfaltering*\n\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~ \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n*a sunrise is pictured further down, illuminating a flat, bleak landscape. The remains of a fire have been scattered, and corpses mingle among the dirt*\n///////////////// ((\n//////~///////////\n______#__ x__ x__\n\n*at the bottom of the scroll a small verse is scribbled- the only writing on the whole piece. It seems to be in some strange, dead language*\n\nFiith slaium az dhog az zamal amut ângh- slaium;", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations", "wardog4445", "I stand before a field that has seen its share of corruption of many sorts. Years ago it was the site where one of the bloodiest battles in an Orenian civil war. However most recently it is where the corruption of void magics can be easily observed.\n\nBefore me is a tree with branches as brittle as sedimentary stone, bark long eroded by the heat from unearthly fires. This is an extreme example of what void magics can do to nature, However it is important to recognize the so called boundaries, how far\n\nvoid magic can corrupt our own world, so that we may recognize its danger and act accordingly.\n\n    Field observations,\n      From Dedicant\n            Avern'len", ""),
        StaticBook("These Words", "birdwhisperer", "Foreword\n\nThis book is originally from Asulon, and was first found on the Island of Armaluna, in the Bards College’s Library. It was rest- ored and brought to Anthos by Elorna Avern.\n\n ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nThese Words, My Love\n        \n           ~~~\n\nThis song was written for my beloved wife, Kyra. Though we will never have children... It matters not. We are rich in happiness. Words are my children, and you my inspiration.\n\nMy pen pierces the page and\n\nImpregnates her with my thoughts.\n\nShe nurtures my mind in\n\nA womb of poetry,\n\nKept deep inside her,\n\nThose memories I'd long forgot.\n\nA preservation of distant,\n\nYet vivid imagery,\n\nNested within the warmth\n\nOf her embrace,\n\nAre the comforts of\n\nMelancholic, younger days\n\nTh wind on my back,\n\nThe sun in my face,\n\nRereading my past in\n\nNew yet nostalgic ways,\n\nThe precious moments that\n\nI can't replace,\n\nThese words, my children,\n\nBring my back, to that special place.\n\n\n~Griffith du Mont, Grand Maestro and Husband", ""),
        StaticBook("The Architect", "§bGrim'aeldus", "Discovered in a more remote part of the Hansetian Underground, “The Architect” was unearthed by a small debris clearing team dispatched to clear away a collapsed portion of a tunnel sub-network.\n\nThe first recorded contact with a living being was when Sariant Vicar Dimitri had just finished blasting away a particularity hardened fallen wall and was preparing to return to the surface for debriefing.\n\nHe had toppled a large blackened material to discover a room that appeared to go on forever.\n\nEstimated 4 meters away from his position sat four large metallic rings suspended around a single platform. The rings showed extreme signs of neglect and disrepair. In the center of the rings was a single podium with an object being held up by three pins.\n\nDimitri recovered the artifact and brought it back to the librarium for further investigation by the stationed personnel. The object was taken and stored in a 1x2 wooden chest along with a few other items of interest.\n\nThe object was recorded to have been left untouched for 2 weeks while other items were analyzed.\n\nUpon retrieval, the chest had a noticeably increased storage capacity and the once packed items were able to have ample space between each other.\n\nA research and recovery team was dispatched to the original location of discovery to find that what was once an endless room had collapsed.\n\n Further efforts to unearth parts of the endless room were uneventful as it appeared the drilling personnel punctured into a tunnel that was recorded to have been 6 meters from the freshly cleared tunnel by the original debris clearing group.\n\nHowever, the four rings that hung suspended were recovered and replicated at the Order librarium.\n\nThe Architect (As dubbed by Hochmeister Mirtok) is not to be contained in any structure. It is to be attached to powered rings at all times.\n\nShould they once more fail, agents are to report to the containment area and prevent access to all unauthorized personnel until the containment rings are repaired and power is restored.\n\n The containment area for The Architect is currently configured to resemble a large eating hall with the artifact and its containment rings disguised as a statue of the Hochmeister. Any and all visitors are to be monitored.\n\nAny structures affected by The Architect are to be demolished after review by the Hochmeister. Final demolition approval or inclusion into the librarium vaults will also be determined by this body.\n\nNo investigation is to be done into affected structures without approval and a rescue team on standby.\n\nThe Architect is a small, smooth metallic object, 10 cm tall and 10 cm wide, in the shape of a dodecahedron. Each face of the figure has a circular hole in the center, and a small sphere is attached to each vertex.\n\n The object is made of an unknown, but highly attractive, alloy about as hard as brass. The object appears to stick onto certain metals with extreme force, keep away from the listed attractive substances to prevent any accidents regarding the object.\n\nWhen inside an enclosed structure and uncontained by the rings, The Architect expands the structure's inner volume without altering its outer area.\n\nThe artifact will increase the inner dimensions of any enclosed structure by .5x its original squared volume each day, beginning one hour after entry into the structure.\n\n Initially, The Architect only extends the walls out, causing the spaces to become much larger without adjusting the height of the room. This expansion continues until the original square footage has been tripled.\n\nAfter the space has reached the tripled squared volume a drastic change begins to occur.\n\nAt this point, the object starts creating wholly new rooms. It is apparently able to copy items from inside the structure, creating furnished rooms consistent with the rest of the structure.\n\nAfter a period of time, however, the expansion process appears to break down. For example, items will be made from inappropriate materials (glass books, a wooden anvil),\n\nrooms will be oddly-shaped, doors will open into blank walls, and hallways will be tiny or twist back around in long mazes. The new inside structures continue to be more and more odd, while the outside remains unchanged.\n\nThe effects of the object remains in the enclosed space until it is both removed and or a new entry way is breached from the outside of the contained space.\n\nNo large scale tests have been conducted on this possible remedy for the sake of unknown consequences. Rooms that are filled with items are marked under the strictly do not test category.\n\n*The rest of the book appears to have a few pages torn out and the rest of the written text is heavily blackened out and without any indication of what was written before.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mental Barriers", "§bThurak", "Rescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 10th of Sun's Smile, 1484.\n\nRecognising the Backgrounds of Mental Barriers\n\n1. Birthright\n\n2. Learnt- Emotional\n\n3. Learnt- Intellect\n\n4. Self Aware.\n\nWhether conscious of the fact or not, all who are of mental capacity for independent thought operate with mental barriers. An avoidance of certain foods, sentimentalities for or against an individual based on previous experiences, a shudder at rain\n\ndropped upon the bridge of the nose. Whether they serve a point or not is beside the point, but all with functioning minds should also have functioning mental barriers. Granted, some are more useful than others, but none should be ignored.\n\nConsideration One\n\nWhile minds are capable of being moulded, as in the case of a particular experiment where a disadvantaged goblin child is given the intellectual upbringing of a noble elven child (For scientific experiments only)\n\nand it is observed that the matter of its circumstance of birth played little consequence in its mental abilities after the experiments completion; however there is equal quantity of proof to suggest the opposite; that particulars\n\nof birth can suggest better or worse mental ability. So if all with mental function possess mental barriers at some level, then it can also be agreed that some individuals may have naturally more intentional barriers resulting from the\n\nparticulars of their birth.\n\nConsideration Two\n\nEmotional experiences are an inevitable by-product of experiencing the company of others. What is not certain is whether the usefulness of such can be realised. It has been observed through various\n\ntrials in which test subjects experienced the same situation that a similar emotional outcome in each subject came forth. The results were conclusive that the female subjects were more capable of becoming emotionally guarded against a similar circumstance\n\nwhen the same tests were repeated (and with more definitive results in the older subjects). The outcome of said experiments showed that aged women are more capable of producing emotional based barriers than are young men. Of course this\n\ndoes not mean it is only the aged woman’s’ game to create emotional barriers, but that their past experiences before commencing tests rendered them more prepared to react in an emotionally defensive manner.\n\nBut whether young or old, and possessing of either of the genitalia, emotionally driven mental barriers prove to be an easily formed barrier that many people demonstrate. It is the experience that heat means danger, or that a wanting\n\nlook from the opposite sex means trouble. And such learning becomes the basis of these most simple barriers with the intent to better our future course from further danger.\n\nConsideration Three \n\nLearning needs by necessity of adapted barriers (the terminology “Adapted” used to refer to any barriers that are reactive in nature) is not limited to that of emotional education, though\n\nit is certainly the easier and more likely to occur in individuals who have no conscious recognition of mental barriers than those of the next type: intellectual . Mentally capable individuals, typically of a higher learning, are more aware of\n\nof themselves and the commencement and termination of their own thoughts, such that they might be able to deduce that the outcomes of something will be of ill consequence, and thus establish an intellectual barrier against\n\nit without requiring the emotional experience of it to draw such a conclusion. Anyone with such an ability would be considered of a more valuable intellectual worth than those who remain unconscious of their circumstance until they experience\n\nit first hand, because they demonstrate a conscious control over adapted barriers,, knowing the beginnings of danger before the danger is present. As is the results of tests among children in which one observes another\n\nexperiencing pain and assumes the outcome of the test implement used will result in pain, without having to experience it for themselves. Individuals with intellectual adapted barriers can become conscious of a problem before the problem manifests, and\n\nthus one who intends to expose them to mental danger will find their defence against it pre-emptive from the first.\n\nConsideration Four\n\nThe last is definitively the most complicated. Tests on such subjects still remain inconclusive as the data is often to broad an array to speculate commonalities; suggesting that great caution be taken in anticipating\n\nthe adaptive and individualistic reaction to provocation. \nIf the proposed individual be of such mental awareness as to acknowledge their own thoughts and recognise the thoughts of others within their own murmurings, then any mental intrusion will be\n\ndetected from the first by these clever adaptive barriers that prevent further intrusion of outside stimuli.\nUnderstanding such mental barriers can only be done on an individual basis, for without\n\nforeknowledge of the mental, emotional and experiential past of the individual, one has no way of interoperating or supposing their reaction. And no one route will have conclusive success in all cases.\n\nThe Boldest Conclusion\n\nIf, in any of the previous cases and most cunning of the latter one, an individual were to acknowledge their own conscious existence with relation to a broader knowledge of the universe\n\nand/or deities, and at the same time comprehends themselves in reference to The Void, then their mental resoluteness may account for intentional barriers of not just emotional and intellectual stimuli, but of all mental stimuli.\n\nSuch an individual is capable of constructing a deliberate blockade that utilises their own experiences and acknowledging their own experiential or anticipated reaction, mould it into that will require a specifically, and equally intentional, attempt to\n\nremove it. Of anticipating and overcoming any barriers that the source of which that has been suggested in the previous pages, this book will do no work towards. For the effort to remove a barrier is to discredit the worth\n\nof it, while the intent of this book has been to acknowledge and more clearly define the circumstance from which mental barriers may have been constructed.", ""),
        StaticBook("EMERALD Vol. 2", "§bAemyn Verde", "The EMERALD\n         COLLECTION\n                of\n          STORY and\n              SONG\n\n*-*-*-*-]}X{[-*-*-*-*\n\nWritten and Compiled by\n       Aemyn Verde\n            of the\n   Emerald Company\n\nVOLUME TWO:\n-*-*-*-*-*-\n- O! Sweet Maiden of Flotsam-town!\n- Lord Extortion, or, The Flight of the Emerald Company\n\nO! Sweet Maiden of Flotsam-town!\n-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-\nThere once danced a maiden sweet\nFrom Flotsam-town on dainty feet\nFar along the Anthos Highway,\nEach graceful step did bring her my way.\n\nIt was such that I did glance\nUpon the horizon 'cross which she pranced,\nHer golden hair the wind caressed,\nAnd tugged at silken skirt, exposin'\nLegs with which she'd been quite bless'd,\n\nNevertheless! T'was not her clothin'\nThat caught my eye,\n'Twas the allure of her fair eyes!\n\nUpon the lute I played for her;\nShe spun upon her feet - a blur!\nAnd then, as the tune slowly faded,\nShe stopped, panting, in the mud.\n'Twas then that fair complexion,\nShimmering, shaking, took on perfection,\n\nThe shell of that poor peasant lass,\nDid break and fall like shatter'd glass;\nAnd where she once wore woolen rags;\nIn silken white, held an Aengul's flag!\n'Pon golden wings she then ascended,\nAnd there, she sang, her voice so splendid:\n\n\"My thanks for your song,\" she sighs,\n\"The tune so sweet it made me rise,\n\"Back t'wards the heavens gold!\"\nI sat there, shiv'ring in the cold,\nAnd watched her fade right out of sigh,\nOnce upon a lonely night...\n- A.V., 20 TGH 1457\n\nLord Extortion, or,\nThe Flight of the\nEmerald Company\n-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-\nThe situation had sprung up on a night as ordinary as any other; crowds began to flock as the Emerald Company primed for another night of music and merriment. Aemyn, backstage,\n\nplucked the strings of his lute, tuning its strings to perfection. Devon muttered something about how awfully large the crowd was, as Aregon stood upon the stage, calling passersby in to join the already-assembled audience. Laughter filled the crossroads\n\nVekaro and Kvaz as this Master of Ceremonies employed his stand-up charm.\n\nThis atmosphere of mirth swiftly dissipated as a grim-looking figure pushed through the suddenly silent onlookers. From behind his scraggly beard, his curled lips and cold\n\neyes marked him as an oppressor of the poor in spirit; a noble seeking to extort those he deemed 'beneath him' , and, with their taxes, vassalage, and very lives, he sought to pad his stone-cold throne.\n\nFrom between those desiccated, lustful lips\n\nof Ivan Ruthern were spat the egregious words, inquiring,\n\"What are you doing on my land!?\"\nThe members of the Company blinked, turning to each other in confusion. Of what did he speak? Surely we aren't on land that belongs to that horrid, towering keep?\n\nThis was Aemyn's mentality as he descended from the stage... He slapped a hand to the old codger's shoulder, proposing that they take this business elsewhere, that bureaucracy would not disturb their positive energy - their 'vibe'.\n\nAnd so, in the frigid halls of the nest where crows do sleep, the selfish lord did regard, with contempt, the entertainers at his feet. They begged why, at all, there need be such rivalry; why not let them carry on?\n\nNO! The laws of feudalism do provide me with the cause to extort from you taxes, just like any other under my blessed 'protection'! If you wish to remain (living) on that knoll, you will give to me yearly... Three-hundred Minas - Nay! Five-hundred!\n\nBy the end of his tirade, he had settled on three-thousand!\n\nAemyn looked to Aregon; unsure, at first, but swiftly resolution came to the pair. Aemyn cleared his throat, and defiantly stated that they would not bow to his unjust demands; they would\n\nmove elsewhere!\n\n\"Hah! Very well, you poor fools, but hear this! If you have not rid me of your presence by midnight, you will find yourself just that - fools! My steward; go fetch the jester hats; I sense they will soon have someone to entertain!\n\nThe sinister, wrinkled lord cackled as his 'guests' stormed from his lair; but, underestimating the value of brave Aemyn's word, he began compiling a list of lullabies - songs that his mother used to sing to him 'til the very day she died. Not strange in\n\nitself, apart from the odd fact - that she had died just last week, at the criminal hands - or pants, rather, of her son - his noxious gas had killed her in her sleep!\n\nBut the valiant, determined men of the Emerald Company had no intention of\n\nstaying under the oppression of that maniacal twit; they prepared, post-haste, to be, of him, rid. The wagon rumbled far away, behind the graveyard hill, where Aemyn had drunkenly piddled on King Heinrik's grave. The wagon wobbled as it passed the spot\n\nwhere Aemyn had then vomited on Lord Tuvya's chestplate. It was a long time before the wagon stopped in peaceful lands - at least a hundred metres away!\n\nAnd so, now, the merry band entertains beside the walls of grand Vekaro, with the\n\nproud patronage of the great leader Tuvya, who does honour to the cause of song, story, and of mirth. Let his joyous name be extolled as we entertain upon his earth!\n\nBut cursed shall be the House of Ruthern - let it be trampled in the dirt!\n\n- Aemyn Verde\n\n17th T.G.H. 1457", ""),
        StaticBook("Tasks: Specimens", "§bLillith Winterleaf", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n\n~The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Winterleaf\n\nOne of Every Specimen: This is not as straightforward as it may sound. This task is meant to familiarize a Dedicant with a variety of nature's creations. Some choose to have the Dedicant bring them 'one of everything that grows'\n\nif they are not particularly knowledgeable about plant life, while others choose to have them bring all of one or two particular varieties of natural things, like flowers, logs and leaves, ores, mushrooms\n\nand grasses, fish meat and bones, or any variety of such things. All of the chosen items are turned in together, and should be followed by a verbal lesson, which I will explain as a Task of its own.", ""),
        StaticBook("Example Record", "§bHileia'elr", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatient's Name:\n\nAge:\n\nRace:\n\nGender:\n\nCondition / Injury:\n\nTreatment plan:\n\nDoctor who treated the patient:\n\nCost for treatment:\n\nDate ((From the date patient was admitted to the date patient was released))\n\nEnd result:\n\n-Have the doctors signature on a blank page-", ""),
