        StaticBook("Journal Amoss", "§bGrigor Grandaxe", "Journal Of\n        Amoss\n\nJeffwise sadget - suspects my corruption\n\nJacob Chapel- Believes Grigors Lies\n\nZaviel- Threat to my position\n\nGrigor- Ruined reputations\n\nAllies-\n\nTuvya- Close Friend and Emperor\n\nMark- Close friend \n\nEraborn- Leader of rangers\n\nFaramith- Noble brother of eraborn\n\nBalek Irongut- Dwarf and good friend\n\nVjek Grandaxe- Close Friend\n\nName Unknown- Lord and strong ally got me my position!\n\nAssasinations Required-\n\nZaviel\nGrigor\nJeffwise Sadget\nJacob Chapel\nFaramith Greymane\nYakov\nEdmund", ""),
        StaticBook("Evelynn Diary", "§bVioletoin", "John Vilcan    1\n-------------------He's a nice guy. I dont know if i still have feelings for him. Havent spoke him in a while. John is friendly and kind. But i dont know if he's still special to me. Last time i saw him, he lost some stuff and wandered\n\nWilliam Jacknife 1\n-------------------He seems a very good friend. Nice and looks pretty too.((Wink :3))\nDont know if he's special or if he's going to be more then a friend. I'll know it soon i guess.\n\nSeiya    1\n-------------------I feel like feelings are coming up for him. Although im not sure if he likes me, or if he's free or if some other girl likes him. I heard someone was trying to rape him. Anyway, he's really kind. And looks cute too :3\n\nRagnar Faolain  1\n-------------------He's very strong, which makes him look hot. Ragnar is a Northerner, which does not bother me. He lives together with his bro's in a house. I heard he has a fiancee. But he hasnt spoke to her in quite a while.\n\nJohn Vilcan    2\n-------------------off. There was a book inside and i looked in it. Apparently he has been seeing other women. I dont feel so happy right now. I even had to lie to him i didnt touch anything. I feel so bad right now. He asked me several\n\nJohn Vilcan    3\n-------------------questions like, what i would do if he married another woman, or if i like him.\n\nArthur Caulfield  1\n-------------------\n\n       --      --  /\n      I    \\_/   /I\n      I          / I\n       \\       /  /\n         \\   /   / \n           \\/   /\n          / \\_/\n        /\n[!] Unreadable words are written down\n\nDeckard Ironcrown 1\n-------------------He's a very nice guy. I like him. Deckard gives me lots of advice, which is useful. He's a great guy. Lately he said, good luck on finding the true one. I think i might've found him already, with him.\n\nAepholis   1\n-------------------He's very kind, and looks nice. I find his orange eyes special. They're beautiful.\nAnd his hair too, it's so cute :3 He's friendly, but i dont know if i should pick him. He's not liked by a few of my friends.\n\nZaviel    1\n-------------------He's so hot! With his white shirt, and his black hair. Its great to talk with him. He's pretty nice. I've had this little talk with him. I dont care he's not 'Nobel', he's a good person to me. Nothing is wrong with him.\n\nHi", ""),
        StaticBook("On \"Racism\"", "§bLelien", "On \"Racism\"\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\n\nDuring my initial days of Haelun'or, I took great care in writing a treatise upon the more common questions critical of Mali'aheral society. This book contained rebuttals to these questions for the sake of education, and the sake of the ignorant\n\npeoples beyond our community. This is a reprint of sorts (though not truly, as the original manuscript was lost in Asulon) that contains more ignorant questions, extended arguments, and superior literacy. That said, this introduction is long enough. Let\n\nus begin.\n\nA human once told me,\n\n\"Purity is of the heart, not of the mind and body.\"\n\nLet us ignore the obvious conclusion that a heart is merely a muscle that pumps blood through the\n\nbody, with no importance to purity other than filling its mandatory biological role. The human presumably refers to the heart as the beholder of an abstract concept of \"goodness,\" so we shall argue that point. \n\n\"Goodness,\" the act\n\nof being \"good,\" is a fundamentally flawed concept. There are things that are innately evil, such as the dread-demon Iblees, profligates of Dark Magics, and other varying monsters who tout goals of domination and destruction. These are certainly cruel.\n\nBut what can truly be considered \"good?\" Good (and at times \"evil\") are subjective in their very nature. Even the words of the much-revered Aenguls are only a matter of perspective. Let us say that in a Valah village, a family is taxed heavily by their\n\nlocal Lord. This lord treats them the same as any other family, but this one is particularly poor, and can barely survive the long winters. One day, the father in desperation robs a nobleman, and kills him. The pauper did not take pleasure in the act, and\n\nhad not intended the nobleman to die. This allows him to feed his long-suffering children. Would this act be good, or evil? If one situation can be skewed in such a way, then, logically, others must also be flawed.\n\nThe maehr'sae hiylun'ehya teaches\n\nthat purity is a combination of mind, and body. It is something only mali'aheral are capable of, and can never be allowed to fester beneath the guidance of the ignorant. To advance our people, Mali'aheral must enhance and strengthen their\n\nminds. To understand nature's workings is to understand our existence and its natural place in the true-world. To this end, our people are gifted with extraordinary intelligence, and it allows us a greater capacity to absord information, and\n\ncreate our own.\n\nIn advancing our people, we complete the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya. The heart has no purpose in true purity.\n\nA wood elf once asked me, \n\n\"If you are not racist, why do you not allow\n\nintermarriage between your people and other races?\"\n\nThe other races are, as commonly said, \"lesser\" than true, pure mali'aheral. This is not a malicious slur aimed at them for amusement or as an emotion-fueled outburst of hatred.\n\nThis is simply observable fact. Traits that commonly bring the ruin of other societies, for example; greed and violence, are barely prevalent within our community. Furthermore, our aforementioned heightened mental faculties make such traits almost\n\nnon-existent. Our blood ensures this superiority, and every muddying of our family lines with inferior specimens dulls preferred Mali'aheral traits. This makes the completion of the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya more difficult with every corrupted generation.\n\nWere we to allow rampant, foolish breeding, then the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya would never be completed, and our kind would languish in the mediocrity of the other Mali.\n\nA Dwarf once asked me,\n\n\"If you have no\n\nprejudices, why do you allow so few outsiders within your society?\"\n\nOutsiders are difficult to trust. There are a worthy few of them accepted into our number, but these have proven their compliance and worthiness to our people. To why we\n\nbar outsiders in general, will be answered in an allegory--one that will be far simpler to grasp for those not of our people.\nImagine yourself the owner of a fabulous dwelling, filled with delights unknown to your envious neighbours. You\n\nenjoy your life amongst the trinkets and comfort items that you gathered, and rest in a fine wicker chair in the sitting room. Suddenly, a person you have never met walks through your door, without so much as a knock, and begins to walk about \"Ooh\"ing and\n\n\"Ahh\"ing at the many delights and placing her dirty fingers upon your property. Confused and concerned, you ask the obvious question of \"What are you doing?\" The stranger, with a smile, explains that she thinks your home beautiful, and is looking around.\n\nYou, in turn, explain to her that you don't want unannounced people in your home. With that, she becomes angered, and declares that you're \"greedy\" for keeping your property to yourself. Such things should be for everyone to see! You explain to her that\n\nshe is free to do as she pleases with her own home, but that you prefer your privacy, thank you very much. \n\nThe stranger disappears, and begins spreading rumours amongst your fellow neigbours of your greed, and how you \"hate people.\"\n\nSuddenly these neighbours also begin to barge their way in, and look about. Sometimes, things go missing. You in turn build a high wall around your home, and though they continue to voice their anger at your actions, they are no longer a nuisance. It\n\nshould not be a necessity to do this, but the nature of your neighbours makes it so.\n\nA dark elf once asked me,\n\n\"Your people insult ours so viciously! Why would you be so cruel?\"\n\nMisinterpretation on the part of those whom we \"insult.\" If this occurs so commonly, why have these victims not re-evaluated the reasons behind our words? What we say always has merit. This is what they do not understand. They choose defensiveness over\n\nrecognising their faults, and therefore never adapt and improve themselves. Thusly, our people will \"insult\" them again, and will likely continue to do so until their missteps are recognised. Such is only befitting a proper Mali, and for their own good.\n\nA Goblin once asked me (version interpreted from orcish babble),\n\n\"If you are superior, how is it we orcs have slaughtered you in battle countless times?\"\n\nActs of combat and physical strength do not imply superiority.\n\nViolence is one of the basest and most simplistic natural urges that any animal is capable. It can stem from any dark emotional outburst, and those that practice them commonly cannot be fully trusted. To use yet another example -- were a giant spider to\n\nto attack and kill an Uruk, would the spider therefore be superior to the orc?\n\nSuch as it is, these questions irk me so, especially when my associates cannot answer them. May you be further enlightened, my reader.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to get magic", "§bJoe", "In these series of words, you will be informed on how to gain a teacher. No, this doesn't involve torture methods, magic itself or any other bizzare operations.\n\nI'll tell you now, back when I was an embryonic mage, I\n\nthought of multiple ways which I thought would give me an arcane teacher. However, I never did such. All I did was  stalk famous arcane mages, stand outside where they often reside and ask commoners and plebians where I can find a teacher of the\n\nArcane Arts. Of course, this didn't get me anywhere. But, one day, a powerful conjurer, like me, but a lot more powerful than I, named Almora Grandaxe was benign enough to give me a chance at magic. Sadly, I did not manage to have one lesson one. Well, I\n\ndid have one lesson with Almora, but it was unfinished. But, enough about me! This book is for and about you, my wannabe mage!\n\nSo, let's start, my friend.\n\nFirstly, you may want to act sophisticated before the mage you want teaching you. Why? Well, going by stereotypes, mages are supposedly wise beings that hold vast amounts of knowledge. Rarely, you will find a mage teaching a nonchalant and uncaring\n\nstudent. First impressions are key to any individual you meet most of the time. \n\nSecondly, you will want to know the mage and let the mage know you. This is brutally important, a teacher of magic who bears a student they are not\n\nexactly fond with will not be as dedicated to the student and may pay no attention to them at all. Try to develop a bond with your desired teacher, they may end up teaching you. However, don't be attached to the mage. The mage may just find you irksome.\n\nThirdly, you will want to have a good reputation. Why? Well, if you were known as a man who slays children for a living or a woman who sleeps with a lot of men, then ends up killing them, you will not get far with your desired mage. That mage may know\n\nabout your doings and may want avoid you. The mage may see you as a problem if he/she were to ever take you in as a student. However, ifyou were a man or woman that constantly seeks to save those in danger  or in grave issues, then the mage you seek\n\nteaching you may also view you as a nusiance and might not consider taking you in as a student. So, keep your reputation neutral, try not to be well known among those in this realm. Make sure your views and your ways of executing actions are similar\n\nto the mage you want teaching you.\n\nMake sure that you don't anger the wrong individuals, you may never know if those that you enrage may be a friend of the mage you want teaching you, I don't need to go into detail on the possible\n\noutcomes of such events taking place.\n\nAnd lastly, be yourself. Don't force a change in who you really are just to obtain magic, act normal. If the mage you want to to teach you takes notice of you drastically changing your\n\ntemperament around him/her, then it will be painfully obvious to them that you only treat them differently due to the fact that you want them to share their arcane knowledge with you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Phsycology Bases", "§bAthri'narncael'onn", "Phsycology is a very confusing study. The first step is to evaluate the patient's mental health.§0\n§0             To get people to follow laws, have many sectors. If criminals go to one sector, then tell them they can do some of the things they usually\n\ndo, at a HIGH cost.§0\n§0          The second group would be good citizens, which mean you have to tell them specifically what they CAN'T do.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~            When evaluating a patient's mental health put them on survailance for an amount of\n\n time. Remember to hide in a place where they can't see you. Give them rules to follow. When they get hungry give them a roll, but tell them if they don't eat it by the time you get back, they can have two.§0\n§0        That will show you the amount of\n\npacience the patient has. If they don't follow rules you had earlier put them in the criminal group. The criminal group will have sub division based upon if they ate the roll or not.§0\n§0               The same goes for teh people who did follow the rules.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~         If a patient is mentally derranged, it's best to isolate them with people of similar nature.§0\n§0              If murderers are in the sector, isolate them in a cell with dim light, a locked iron door and a gaurd in their sector.\n\n       Patient care and§0\n§0needs is important, too because you don't want them to die. Provide a toilet, food chute and other neccecities.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        People breaking out of wards is a problem. To ensure this doesn't happen, provide maximum\n\nsecurity UNDERGROUND.        In the rare case a person randomly passes away, put them in a cemetary based on their beliefs. You should always respect your patients.§0\n§0             Create jobs to keep people busy. Appropriate jobs include, baking,\n\nfarming, alchemy, leatherworking and science.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        Torture is a method of punishment.§0\n§0I personally suggust breaking peoples fingers and toes until they give you the answer or, say sorry.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n      Phsyciatric drugs can be found in the Herbs section of teh Eternal Library in Haelun'or. Herbs can be used to sedate a patient, heal a patient, wake a patient and more. Herbs should be obtained by professional herb suppliers.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        Animals are important to keep in patients cells and sectors but you should always put them in a place they are safe.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~          Treats should be rewarded to patients when they are good and\n\nbad things should happen when they are bad§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~         Your sector(s) should have daily appointments with prisoners but the prisoner should stay in the cell and you should stay out.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       Security should have at least\n\n five stations. The cell, the Hall, the Sub-sector, the Sector and the front door.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~§0\n§0        Visits should always be allowed. A bar should be placed between the people. The visitation room should be secure. There should be no door from one\n\nside to the other and visitation time should be very limited and strict.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        If prisoners, swear, perform a violent action or is disrespectful punish them. You should break a finger for each offense. If you run out of fingers just hit\n\nthe prisoner.§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        If you cannot handle a patient, give him to the town or state. If a prisoner tries to kill you, get gaurds and beat him so hard that you have to put him in a clinic.§0\n§0People with powers should be isolated.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~          If a patient has committed too many crimes, execute them in fron of teh victims families.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~        If you have more Problem, contact Doctor Athri'narncael'onn (colinizer.) This book is Doctors Edition.", ""),
        StaticBook("For you, sir.", "§bJoe Orman", "Ah, Conjuration; the rarest Arcane Art known... Well, he won't be rare anytime soon. Of course, once you begin to learn the art, you will be referred to as a \"Conjurer\". A conjurer is an individual who access the Void and construct living organisms which\n\nare fueled wholly by the mana of their creator. Through the depths of the void, a Conjuration user will be bale to summon almighty creatures and pretty flowers into reality. Alas, as a conjurer you will be constantly delivering your mana for virtually\n\nevery second your ersatz summon exists. You will soon come to a realisation that Conjuration uses the most of your mana unlike any other Arcane Science. In order to uphold the existance of your faux creature, you must feed it precisely\n\na great portion of mana to flow within it. As the creature you summon will be downright complex, the process of building it within the Void will be rather tiresome and there is a good chance you may be drained completely of your mana until you reach\n\nunconsciousness, as tha thappens, your beast will be removed from the physical realm and be sent back to the Void. Yes, you can decide to desist the flow of mana beforehand, in which case the fauna will vanish to no consequence.\n\nNow, for you to construct an organism within the Void, you must first have a sharp and great nderstanding of both the interior and exterior of the living entity you wish to formulate. This can be achieve dby oftently killing and dissecting the creature\n\nyou wish to summon. However, it is also best to keep very detailed anatomical diagrams of the beast you wish to conjure. Remember to have notes on the animal's exterior and interior and bone structure if you want to have an accurate understanding of it,\n\nsmell it, taste, feel it. How does it react to certain physical actions?\n\nIn the opaque Void, the fabrics which generate the entity are smmoned bone by bone, layer by layer and organ by organ the Conjurer crafts and sculpts their being into an\n\ncopy of their previously existing self. As a result of poor research, the Conjurer may fail at this point, producing a being unlike that of its true and real form. This will result in an uneven and revolting entity which would certainly turn to sludge\n\nonce conjured. After a while of practice, the Conjurer would be able to summon creatures exactly how it was before it was slain and have it formed with sheer stability. As it will behave akin to the life form it represents, it will follow its creator's\n\ncommands.\n\n\nAs a Conjurer myself, I would highly reccomend you commence to study roses, then petite insects until you grow stronger enough to move on to study and conjure anything larger.\n\nThink of Conjuration as art. You are the painter and the Void is the frame. What you paint in the frame will need to look beautiful and make sens ein the judge's eyes. Bea rin mind that the \"judge\" is the physical realm. If the judge thinks tour work of\n\nart is good, it will be accepted and become brought into reality. However, if it's horrible, it will be stamped on and crushed and it will appear as an abomination in the mortal plane and you will be smacked in the face for your poor effort. That smack\n\nwill tire you. Keep practising and your artistic skills will improve and the judge will continue to accept your art.\n\nOvertime, your frame will expand and leave you open to produce larger paintings which the judge can view. Be warned though, the\n\nlarger, the harder.\n\nAnd yes, you can produce hybrid fauna. I'll leave that for you to grasp the concept of alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Redstone Studies", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "Day 1§0\n§0\n§0I, Gallidron Elindrow, have begun my study of Redstone. I intend to gain greater understanding of this substance that I may learn to manipulate it to more fascinating purpose, perhaps even that of an arcane one.§0\n\nTo this end I am beginning with basic observations of the material in question. Redstone is found in the earth as an ore much like iron, however it is fragile in nature and breaks down into a dust when extracted. Not unlike Thanhium when it is extracted,\n\nwhich causes me to think the two might have a connection, but this is just a musing of mine.§0\n\n The dust is coarse to the touch and grainy, but gives off a slight shine. It is capable of being compressed into a block and then seems to be much more durable than in its natural form as an ore. Hence it does not break apart when struck.§0\n\nThe compressed block is decidedly smoother than the dust or the ore, but this is just a product of the refinement process.§0\n§0\n§0This concludes my observations of its physical nature.\n\nday 2§0\n§0Redstone is primarily used for its conductive nature. My experiments today are centered around this aspect. Redstone is so conductive that it can be laid in a line as a powder and still hold an electrical current.§0\n§0This is a common way to use the\n\nmaterial, as it is not necessary to enclose redstone while transferring power through it. §0\n§0The current will eventually taper off however, thus showing that while uninsulated some of the power is indeed lost in transfer.\n\nA compressed block of redstone can obviously hold more energy and act as a greater conduit due to its increased mass. More water flows through a bigger pipe, the same is true of energy it would seem.§0\n\nRedstone is used for transferring electrical energy and can be used as a conduit for errant electrical static, especially if one has a large quantity of it available in the open air.§0\n§0\n§0More will be studied on this tomorrow.\n\nDay 3§0\n§0\n§0This third day of observation finally includes some actual experimentation. I had to wait untill I could find an electrical evocationist of at least some skill.§0\n§0To this end I contacted the okrarir'indor Lelien§0\n§0Lazul\n\nThe experiment is intended to test the conductivity of redstone to arcane lightning. I wished to see whether or not it can negate or at least affect the course and accuracy of the electrical energy in question.\n\nExperiment Setup§0\n§0\n§0I sought an area outside in the open air, as I felt that it would be more condusive to the conjuring of electrical energy. After gaining express permission from the Okarir'tayna, Silvos Sythaerin (who would sit in on the experiment)\n\nI set up a stone target as to not introduce more conductive material than neccesary. I then set up a block of redstone five paces away and one pace out, as to be just to the side of the \"firing range\" as it were.\n\nAt fifteen paces away I set up a platform for our talented mage to stand upon.§0\n§0\n§0The first test was simple enough as I asked for her to fire a bolt of lower voltage toward the target. The result was very promissing, as the bolt traveled toward the\n\ntarget only to veer off as it neared the redstone. The restone did not attract the bolt so completely as to pull it into itself, but the energy did miss the target and set some bushes aflame, as well as a chicken who met sudden and explosive end.\n\nThe next test involved removing the redstone block and setting up four interconnected lines of redstone dust. These lines were placed between the mage and the target and a current was sent through them. I then instructed the mage to fire again.\n\nThe results were most interesting as the lighting, almost immediately, shot down into the redstone and was utterly consumed. The redstone itself was burnt up into almost nothing and ruined. The possible application of this in magical defense is intriguing\n\nAfterward we performed one final test, in which the redstone lines were replaced just as they were before though this time no current was run through them. Again a bolt of lightning was fired at the target and, much as in the first test, the redstone\n\npulled the energy toward it and it struck the base of the target.\n\nMore tests are to be run in the future but for now I will close this research journal with this conclusion.§0\n§0\n§0Redstone makes an excellent conductor of electrical energies, arcane or otherwise. It is concievable that one might be able to defend themselves\n\nfrom electrical evocation by making use of the substance. Though the research is new and possible, practical application has yet to be tested in this manner.§0\n§0Also, Redstone, with a current running through it, seems a more powerful conductor to electrical\n\nenergies. But if it is not possessed of enough mass to diffuse the energy, it will be burned up and wasted utterly.§0\n§0\n§0Published 8th of the §0\n§0First Seed, 1523\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow", ""),
        StaticBook("Ode to Nature", "§bDedicant Gi'Gárun", "An Ode to Nature\n   By Gi'Gárun\n\nWe walk upon her soil,\nWe gaze upon her trees.\n\nWe're surrounded by all kinds of things,\nThat sprouted from her seeds.\n\nWhen one steps out of one's front foor,\nOne will see her work.\n\nHer prowess great and beautiful,\nNo dark or evil mirk.\n\nWhat is it that,\nI speak about.\n\nWhat is it that I praise?\n\nThe land we roam,\nThe streams that foam.\n\nThe trees so tall,\nThe rain that falls.\n\nAll of these are of her make, for they are her and her alone. The make of two of love and great.\n\nThat be nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tasks: Salve", "§bLillith Winterleaf", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n\n~The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Winterleaf\n\nMake A Salve: There are a variety of salves able to be made from various herbs and mixtures, which can be found documented in other books, I will not clutter this book with them. Choose a salve, be it for burns, wounds, pain relief, antivenom, or whatever\n\nyou feel there will be ingredients readily available for. Have the Dedicant bring you the finished mixture to inspect it, then have them apply it to a relevant affliction or wound if such is available.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tea", "§bIyath the Toymaker", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Elise's Drink Recipes§0\n§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Teas:§0\n§0\n§0Cactus Tea§0\n§0\n§0Poppy Tea§0\n§0\n§0Blue Orchid Tea§0\n§0\n§0Dandelion Tea§0\n\nBrowncap Mushroom Tea§0\n§0\n§0Rose Tea§0\n§0\n§0Juices:§0\n§0\n§0Orange Juice§0\n§0\n§0Apple Juice§0\n§0\n§0Pumpkin Juice§0\n§0\n§0Melon Juice\n\nCarrot Juice§0\n§0\n§0Alcohol:§0\n§0\n§0Mulled Wine: Dark Resin§0\n§0\n§0Pale Ale: Wheat§0\n§0\n§0Vodka: Poisonous Potato§0\n§0\n\nOther:§0\n§0\n§0Blood: Rotten Flesh§0\n§0\n§0Distilled Water: Coal\n\nOther Teas:§0\n§0\n§0Chamomile Tea: Ox Eyed Daisies§0\n§0\n§0Herbal Tea: Grass§0\n§0\n§0Birch Tea: Birch Leaves§0\n§0\n§0Pine Tea: Pine Leaves\n\nPotion of Halfling's      Grass§0\n§0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Halfling's Grass\n\nPotion of Serpent's Stalk§0\n§0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Serpent's Stalk\n\nPotion of Tippen's Root§0\n§0\n§0Distilled Water§0\n§0Tippen's Root", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0elven language basics §0\n§0\n§0          VL. II\n\nThese words make up the brunt of the Elven language, and may be modified by various affixes to create new words.§0\n\nacal: valuable, golden, cursed §0\n§0acalin: shop§0\n§0acaln: gold§0\n§0(a)chikr: (without the a:) ***** - §0\n§0(a)dil: needy, desiring, wanton - When one forfeits the 'a' it becomes as of a vice§0\n\n(a)dont: requesting, awaiting - Without the 'a' it becomes 'demanding', -er makes verb as always§0\n§0adri: evil, immoral, hate§0\n§0(a)elor: abomination, faithless, demon. §0\n§0Aengul: Aengul - race of semi-divine beings affiliated with light.§0\n\naetah: age§0\n§0aeth: aether§0\n§0aher: to bless.§0\n§0ahern: blessing.§0\n§0akal: valuable, golden - less ominous§0\n§0akaleh: wealth, money, valuables§0\n§0akalin: shop§0\n\nakaln: gold - less ominous way to speak of gold.§0\n§0allim: sin  - allimar: to sin; alliman: sinful§0\n§0andria: hope§0\n§0annyer: to dance§0\n§0Asul: sun§0\n§0ata: ugly, tainted§0\n§0athri: serpent, snake§0\n\n(a)iler: Wizard, conjurer, heretic -Any wizard or spiritual humanoid that's not a druid. §0\n§0alor: salmon -aloronn/alonn: salty§0\n§0ame: forest§0\n§0annil: guiding -anniler: to guide, direct§0\n§0ante: Last§0\n§0arche: infrequent, sporadic, rare§0\n\n(a)rhil: just fair (without the a:) vengeful, scorned.§0\n§0asimulum: sanctuary, glade, asylum, dedicated place (esp. one of nature)§0\n§0aver: to wander, to roam around aimlessly, to be confused§0\n§0avern: wanderer, confused person§0\n§0ayal: yellow§0\n\nay(i)lu: liked, likable§0\n§0ayla: good§0\n\n\n§0barbu: dark, black, hedgehog§0\n§0berr: bow§0\n§0belou: pink§0\n§0beloun: pig§0\n§0bilok: to create, to make§0\n§0Bortu: dwarf§0\n\n(a)caele: sky. §0\n§0celia: star§0\n§0ceru: strong, mighty§0\n§0chirr: wolf§0\n§0chul: to must§0\n§0cihi: city§0\n§0cinh: to stop, to cease§0\n§0ciw: to sleep§0\n§0crua: hurting, suffering - which makes cruan: pain§0\n\nDaemon: Daemon - race of semi-divines affiliated with smoke and fire.§0\n§0dion: long - dionne: short§0\n§0divtilru; lit. \"devoid of servitude.\"§0\n§0divu: empty§0\n§0drui: Druid§0\n§0draoi: Evil/corrupted druid. Warlock. Sorcerer.§0\n\nehier: to find§0\n§0enaer: guest§0\n§0ento: next§0\n§0ern: to can, to be able to§0\n§0eth: end, to end, to die -word can be a noun, passive verb and active verb depending on usage§0\n§0evar: to protect, preserve§0\n§0eyr: to use, apply§0\n\nfaesu: horse§0\n§0fer: tool - This word creates a wide array of words for various tools, such as torches and pickaxes. They are discussed further in 'curious words'.§0\n§0fenn: ice§0\n§0feta: cold§0\n§0fih: to eat, to feed§0\n§0fin: region§0\n\nfiyem: reborn, renewed, revitalized§0\n§0fyu: full§0\n§0\n§0\n\nhae: her§0\n§0haelun: mother§0\n§0haler: to promise, to pledge§0\n§0harriel: square§0\n§0heial: circle, council§0\n§0hier: near§0\n§0hileia: Peace. - Has no plural§0\n§0hiuw: to twitch, to move§0\n§0hiylu: Healthy / spirited§0\n\n\n§0ibar: white, owl§0\n§0igne: flame, fire - igne'sae: destruction, war§0\n§0iheiuh: wind§0\n§0iheiuhii: voice, breath§0\n§0ihn: stick§0\n§0ihnsil: spear§0\n§0ikur: wrought, cold, gray§0\n§0ikurn: iron§0\n§0ikru: foolish§0\n\niller: to give, to grand§0\n§0ilum: glowing §0\n§0inder: to read§0\n§0indor: book§0\n§0irrin: glass§0\n§0ito: to, here, within§0\n§0iyat: thought§0\n§0iyath: to think§0\n§0iylanh: to place§0\n\n §0\n§0kae: me§0\n§0kalem: Malin's year, - Roughly 26 Anthos years, denotes the length of a High Prince's reign.§0\n§0kaliri: Event, party§0\n§0karim: Fortday, - The measure of time from one Dwarven sleeping cycle to the next, roughly 24 Anthos days.§0\n\nkarin(ah): sunrise, - Also used to speak of day§0\n§0kathir: foe§0\n§0ker: dark, sunset - Also used to speak of night§0\n§0khel: darkness - Strictly a noun§0\n§0kina: murdered, killed, death, in mortal danger§0\n§0krafeh: corpse§0\n§0krey: single. kreyn - pair.§0\n\nlae: him§0\n§0lar: sturdy, steadfast.§0\n§0lareh: boulder, mountain, rock§0\n§0larebil: anvil§0\n§0larueth: netherrack§0\n§0laureh: chosen, favored, noble§0\n§0laurir: Noble§0\n§0len: song§0\n§0lenaern: inn§0\n§0lenniel: melody§0\n\nlenti: growth, moss.§0\n§0lentos: brown§0\n§0leyu: graceful, beautiful.§0\n§0liewyn: smile - liewynh: to smile, liewyn'saer: to entertain, to amuse; maliewynh: to laugh§0\n§0lle: kindness, good intention§0\n\nlie: dishonest, untrue, false, deceitful -lien: lie , liear: to lie; maliear: to betray (malieir: traitor)§0\n§0llir: friend§0\n§0lin: home, place -linan'sae: town§0\n§0llum: sorrowful, mourning - llum'saer: to sadden§0\n\nllyt: aggressive, intimidating, -llyth: to strike§0\n§0lom: to fragment, to splinter§0\n§0lomi: fragment, splinter, pebble§0\n§0lomal: flint§0\n§0luci: grape - lucionn: sour§0\n§0luer:  to imprison, to cage §0\n§0luerlent: flowerpot§0\n\nlye: we§0\n§0lyu: silent - leads to the words lyun: silence; lyuer: to silence and lyu'saer: to censor §0\n§0maehr: wisdom, knowledge§0\n§0maelu: to know§0\n§0mahnih: wall§0\n§0Mali: elf/elven §0\n§0maln: father§0\n§0marn: more§0\n§0marenne: less§0\n§0masuleh: anvil§0\n\nmedi: helping, helpful§0\n§0meracahe: balance§0\n§0miar: lava miar'sae: griefing, harming, spiting§0\n§0mira: warm§0\n§0miruel: red§0\n§0myumier: to carry, to bring§0\n\nnae: you§0\n§0naeri: devout one, cleric§0\n§0narn: to walk, travel through§0\n§0nealu: to teach§0\n§0nor: land - nor'sae: farming§0\n\no: why§0\n§0ohn: like - Either a prefix or stand-alone§0\n§0oment: to meet§0\n§0okar: to safeguard§0\n§0okarn: oasis§0\n§0orrar: to hunt§0\n§0othelu: sharp§0\n\nparir: harbinger§0\n§0pern: potato§0\n§0parsaer: to conceive, to kindle. \"to have an idea\". §0\n§0perith: to remember§0\n§0puer: to write, to draw, to scribble.§0\n§0puerith: to write down (of books), to memorize. to record (more formal than 'puer')§0\n\nriv: claw §0\n§0riurn: swamp§0\n§0raell: carrot, root, herb. (refers to subterranean parts of plants possessing healing or nourishing properties)§0\n\nsan: word, news - saner: to speak§0\n§0saneyr: to debate, discuss. - saneyir: debater, public speaker, orator.§0\n§0salum: to feel, to sense§0\n§0seth: void§0\n§0sew: soup, stew§0\n§0siimah: tower§0\n§0sil: sword§0\n§0siol: lone, lonely§0\n\nsirame: Honor; connection to the forest. - Has no plural§0\n§0siru: mushroom -siruonn: bitter§0\n§0siyuer: to play§0\n§0sohae: devout one, cleric -In a militant or executive sense. sohaer: ruler §0\n§0suika: sugar -§0\n§0sul: light - strictly a noun.§0\n§0sulier: to see§0\n§0sulii: eye§0\n\nsulirrin: glowstone§0\n§0\n§0taeleh: mind§0\n§0taelu: to learn§0\n§0tahorran: hawk§0\n§0tahu: high§0\n§0tahn: peak, height§0\n§0talar: horizon§0\n§0talareh: stone §0\n§0taliyna: body, living being, aspect §0\n§0taliiyh: to bleed§0\n§0taliyu: secret§0\n\nTalonnii: family, blood(line) - always capped§0\n§0tarem: Elven week -Equivalent to 7 'karim'§0\n§0tayna: life, energy of living§0\n§0taynei: green§0\n§0taynuel: vitality, energetic, alive§0\n§0tenna: until§0\n§0tennallar: ocean§0\n§0terh: to grind, process, churn\n\ntiuth: triangle §0\n§0thruer: to explode§0\n§0thrur: explosive, volatile§0\n§0thrurn: explosive, dynamite§0\n§0thill: pure, refined, delicate§0\n§0thilln: silver§0\n§0thul: raw, unrefined, brusque§0\n§0thulith: metal§0\n§0thuln: ore, raw material§0\n§0tilru: serving, submissive§0\n§0tir: law§0\n\ntos: desert, wasteland, barren ground - tos'sae: razing§0\n§0tufer: to construct, to prop§0\n§0tur: bone§0\n§0turr: sheep§0\n§0tuva: everything, all§0\n§0tuveh: wool, something soft§0\n§0\n§0ueth: nether§0\n§0uhier: to seek§0\n§0ulln: rot, withering - strictly a noun.§0\n\nullr: rot, decay, wither - Often of dead flora.§0\n§0ullral: monster, undead §0\n§0uradh: to scowl. - uradir: naysayer§0\n§0uriar: to shout§0\n§0urth: to rule - negative connotation to this word. urthir: ruler; maruthir: tyrant§0\n§0Uruk: Orc§0\n§0ut: because§0\n§0uvul: powder§0\n\nValah: human§0\n§0vallei: water§0\n§0valein: milk§0\n§0vallel: blue§0\n§0vallum: crying, griefin§0\n§0valmir: artist §0\n§0valmuel: purple§0\n§0van: to fare§0\n§0Velulaei: moon §0\n§0vihai: whisper§0\n§0vilut: cow§0\n§0vira: vigilant, mournful\n\nvularale: bat§0\n§0vull: to deceive, to trick§0\n§0vuln: fox§0\n§0\n§0waleh: to heal§0\n§0wehn:  grass, grain.§0\n§0welier: to listen, to hear - rewelier: to repeat, to echo§0\n§0wy: appendage§0\n§0wyl: while§0\n§0wyn: happy§0\n\ny: upon§0\n§0yallr: to live.§0\n§0yuln: gemstone - Used as the seed for many words, including maleyuln: diamond§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0       The Story§0\n§0            of§0\n§0     Larry Shortoak\n\nThe story begins at the halfling village of Goodborough! Larry stepped off the small boat, his hairy feet touching the oak docks. He stretched upwards to limber up after his long voyage. The first halfling he met was Rupert Herbwallow, the man that gave\n\nhim the name of Larry. He was originally named as Laorin as he grew up in an old forgotten town consisted mostly of elves. Rupert allowed Larry to move into the first burrow on the path, just across the small bridge. The burrow was used for a guide for\n\nnew halflings. Weeks passed, Larry started meeting the locals, started to farm, become reasonably known, even made some biggun friends. However, due to the location of his burrow, he was often raided an attacked, tortured and beaten senseless. This was a\n\nconstant thing, every second elven day, stolen from almost every day, his hopes were down, his knees had received so much damage he struggled to walk properly. That is when Larry became to travel, his ideas of Goodborough one of sadness and nerves. On his\n\ntravels through the human settlements, he was often looked at oddly, a short man that most people were shocked by. Most people had forgotten about halflings, however, this also made him yet another§0\n§0target due to his size. Larry was attacked one day just\n\noutside the clinic in the Caliphate. This is where he would meet Dahlia Floreck, a human that lived in Dour Watch who he would end up marrying in secret. This was improper and as such Larry didnt tell anyone until a few months later, not because he was\n\nhappy about it, but because she had died, along with the child she was bearing. Larry and Dahlia were captured by a biggun named Marcy that Larry had befriended years earlier. She kidnapped them both with the help of an Orc that I forget the name of. They\n\nwere both enslaved, the brand still scarred into my leg. It is a reminder of what happened that day. The Orc made me clean while I heard the silence from the room where they kept her. They had killed her, chopped her up and cooked her in a stew.§0\n\n[!] A few tears would be scattered along the page.§0\n§0\n§0The Orc and Marcy forced me to eat the stew. I couldnt bare to eat it, I spat it out and threw up onto the floor I had just cleaned. I watched as they ate the stew. When I escaped\n\nI wanted to jump off a cliff, to just die, end the suffering. I didnt even know she was pregnant at the time. §0\n§0\n§0Skipping past this depressing part of my life, we move onto the time when Goodborough was destroyed by the Skygods, the town turned to ruin and\n\nwe all had to flee. Andwise, my best friend was given the title of Mayor before we moved. He and I decided that we should move below the Dwarven mountain surrounding a lake at the foot of it. Not many halflings came with us, we were few in number and here\n\nI was appointed the position of Sheriff. The Sheriff of Petyrborough. We gradually gained numbers, the Crison Edict continuing to assist us as they did when we were at Goodborough.§0\n§0Years had passed before Marcy came to visit me.\n\n[!] This page appears to be torn out, I wonder what it could have said about this encounter.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0I just couldnt kill her, I didnt have the strength.\n\nThe attacks continued, the scars continued stacking up on his body. My burrow was burned, stolen from and blown up. We had to move again due to safety issues, a group of racist dwarves forced us out by threatening every halfling and no one seemed to care.\n\nI also decided to leave out the time I was turned into a person made of plants, the time I was burnt as well as the time I was tied up and tortured in my burrow left to die. §0\n§0All these incidents happened in both Petyrborough and Goodborough.\n\nThis brings us to the part of the story where Andwise and I decided to move the halflings behind the wood elves to the village of Willow Hollow. I was still Sheriff when this happened and was for another fifteen years or so. I was Sheriff for about§0\n\ntwenty-five years.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Ug name: Xbaz§0\n§0s", ""),
        StaticBook("A Piece of Paper", "§bOuity Deathsbane", "Bang.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Neo-Druidism", "§bKyrah", "Neo-Druidism§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Written by the Salmon Druid, Petyr Brandybuck, this book describes two forces which encompass the field of druidism in it's entirety, a balance if you will, of action, and non-action. The state of non-action\n\ndetails the passive acts that a druid commits in their lives, such as meditation and silence, better known as invisible motions.§0\n§0Action, however, is the state of one's restoration of balance, and being the hand of nature itself. With these philosophies\n\nrevealed to the reader, it then goes into deeper depths...§0\n§0\n§0SEC.1 - Unity of Nature -------------------To make distinctions about anything merely by sight is detailed as foolish, titling things so simply as life and death, good and evil, light and dark,\n\nand so on. There is no true distinction between anything as it is all nature, and druids are simply beings who understand the truth of such a logic. What this details simply, is that all things natural, are not separate, but are simply pieces of nature,\n\nthat form that which is known as 'The Way'. Or, the path in which nature leads that which is comprised of.§0\n§0\n§0SEC.II§0 Way of Nature§0\n§0-------------------Nature is, as described in the book, a river of life, in which we flow along. Balance shifts eternally as\n\nthe tides, something in which Druids merely partake in, serving as the hands of Balance, and the Flow of Nature, also known as the 'Way'. To act, is simply not enough to be a druid. One must also 'not' act. They must focus on levels both physical and\n\nmetaphysical, as detailed in the first section, otherwise they are not embracing their powers to their fullest extent, and not acheiving their goal in doing so.§0\n§0\nSEC.III - The Druid\n-------------------Despite the overall enigmatic text of this\n\nsection of the book, it is quite easy to understand when put into simplistic perspective. What it details is that a Druid is a hand in which nature uses to govern itself, and despite how one may attempt, they will never fully be able to grasp what it is\n\nnature has planned. There is no entirety, as no person, nor even nature itself understands every thing about themselves, or it. Asymmetry is a natural part of existence. Perfection is unnecessary. With these theories in mind, and the perfect\n\nmixture of action and non-action practices, one may at last grasp what the phrase 'All is One' truly means.\n\nThough I myself, indeed have.", ""),
        StaticBook("What I Love", "§bArbor Druid Thudrin", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~§0\n§0\n§0What I love about nature§0\n§0\n§0~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~§0\n§0\n§0~ Written by Arbor Druid          Thudrin\n\nThe trees be wise§0\n§0The trees be old§0\n§0The trees be tall§0\n§0The trees be bold§0\n§0\n§0The water be crisp§0\n§0The water be clear§0\n§0The water be fresh§0\n§0The water be near\n\nThe grass be soft§0\n§0The grass be green§0\n§0The grass be long§0\n§0The grass be clean§0\n§0\n§0The flowers be nice§0\n§0The flowers be pretty§0\n§0The flowers be soft§0\n§0The flowers be witty\n\nThese be me favorites§0\n§0I love them the most§0\n§0I hold them so dear§0\n§0So I raise a toast§0\n§0\n§0To you, nature§0\n§0You, above all§0\n§0You keep us alive§0\n§0So we will not fall", ""),
        StaticBook("Withering Flower", "§bSolstice Druid Callax", "Withering flower, upbraid me not!§0\n§0Why cast on me that look so pale?§0\n§0Why bow thy head?§0\n§0Why bend thy neck?§0\n§0Why look so drooping, wan and cold?\n\nGiving my careless thoughts a check,§0\n§0And tell me I am getting old!§0\n§0Fading flower, upbraid me not!§0\n§0Still nodding in the gentle breeze...§0\n§0Or dost thou think I have forgot?§0\n§0I too am wasting by lives?\n\nFor scarce can I believe my sight,§0\n§0Who lately saw thee flesh and gay;§0\n§0That beauty could so early blight,§0\n§0Or such colors fade away.", ""),
        StaticBook("Natural Poem", "§bDedicant Virella", "Natural Poem§0\n§0By Dedicant Virella\n\nNature's Poem§0\n§0\n§0The peaceful grass.§0\n§0The blowing wind.§0\n§0Blooming flowers.§0\n§0And the tall trees.§0\n§0The matters of them connect to one.§0\n§0Nature, its nature, for all of us.\n\nLinked Together§0\n§0\n§0A Druid serves nature.§0\n§0Linked to one.§0\n§0Same as roots with trees.§0\n§0The sun with plants.§0\n§0A family with support.§0\n§0All is linked together.\n\nDandelion Fuzz§0\n§0\n§0Blooming in the wind§0\n§0Nothing is sinned.§0\n§0The Fuzz flies and plants.§0\n§0Newcomers come to sprout and dance.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haikus by Ana", "§bDedicant Anarane", "Haikus by Ana§0\n§0By Dedicant Anarane\n\n*There is a sketching of a fox*§0\n§0\n§0Your coat is pretty,§0\n§0Colors of orange, black and white,§0\n§0Your cuteness hides strength.\n\n*There is a sketch of a tree*§0\n§0\n§0Your hands are green§0\n§0You wave hello and goodbye§0\n§0Your roots are endless\n\n*There is a sketch of an owl*§0\n§0\n§0You are large and wise§0\n§0Sleep at day, hunt in the night§0\n§0You don't give a hoot", ""),
        StaticBook("On Nature", "§bDedicant Elorlas", "On Nature§0\n§0By Dedicant Elorlas\n\nTake some time to sit and notice.§0\n§0The beauty of the trees.§0\n§0Take a moment to admire, the dancing of the leaves.§0\n§0Note, Mali'i, playing with your toys, so full of joyous hunger.§0\n§0Not to crush insects, who are a thousandth of your weight.\n\nYou may be a tenant of nature, but do not seal their fate.§0\n§0Life is about enjoyment, not creating storms.§0\n§0\n§0So head this warning now, before all Anthos is torn.", ""),
        StaticBook("Balance", "§bDedicant Arial Meadowbloom", "Balance§0\n§0By Dedicant Arial Meadowbloom\n\nBalance is responsibility,§0\n§0Balance is helping gain,§0\n§0Balance is keeping nature§0\n§0in step and free of pain.§0\n§0\n§0Whether it must be stopped,§0\n§0Or the cycle must be helped,§0\n§0Nothing more can be done§0\n§0unless something is felt.\n\nThe unbalance will continue,§0\n§0Unless something is learned,§0\n§0Unless everyone realizes that§0\n§0people scream but cannot be heard.§0\n§0\n§0That sometimes the worst choice§0\n§0Can be the greatest one of all.§0\n§0That sometimes to meet someone,§0\n§0They must break down a wall.\n\nThe balance in nature§0\n§0Is clear to everyone.§0\n§0Whether Druid or Mage,§0\n§0Welcome or shunned.§0\n§0\n§0(Un)balance goes on its way,§0\n§0Through day and night,§0\n§0Without one whimper, one cry,§0\n§0Without one branch giving a fight.\n\nWhich is why we must help§0\n§0In nature's time of need,§0\n§0For when it calls to us,§0\n§0To its voice we must heed.§0\n§0\n§0We must be greatful for all,§0\n§0For the life which we work for,§0\n§0For the things of which we own,§0\n§0And our greatest thing at our core.\n\nWe must that nature no matter where,§0\n§0No matter who and no matter how faulty,§0\n§0We must thank nature for being§0\n§0So utter sweet, yet so salty.§0\n§0\n§0Like the fire may destroy§0\n§0And yet help a forest grow,§0\n§0How a book can ruin a life§0\n§0And yet help someone to know.\n\nThis balance goes on,§0\n§0Forever and forever more,§0\n§0For however long that must be,§0\n§0No one knows for sure.§0\n§0\n§0But for now we continue§0\n§0To give thanks each, every day§0\n§0And to help nature and its parts§0\n§0In every single way.\n\nBecause...§0\n§0\n§0Balance is responsibility,§0\n§0Balance is staying in time,§0\n§0Yet it is also keeping§0\n§0Nature in its prime.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cycle", "§bDedicant Daneard", "A deer's frozen breath in winter§0\n§0Hunter crouching low in snow§0\n§0Hungry family waiting at home§0\n§0Blood seeps into the ground§0\n§0Returned to nature\n\nA calming breeze of a spring's day§0\n§0Flowers shyly blooming after a long sleep§0\n§0Young fawn nibbling at the soft grass§0\n§0Reborn", ""),
        StaticBook("Pine Trees", "§bThe Pine Druid", "Pine Trees§0\n§0~By The Pine Druid\n\nWhen one be walking bout thee lands.§0\n§0One may wander dunes of sand.§0\n§0\n§0Or maybe even caverns deep,§0\n§0And view the beauty found beneath.§0\n§0\n§0When one begins to feel cold,§0\n§0They start to miss the sands of gold.\n\nBut when one things to open eye,§0\n§0They see the beauty way up high.§0\n§0\n§0True beauty lies above you see,§0\n§0It stands as such, a mighty tree§0\n§0\n§0A towering canopy tall and fine,§0\n§0The tree I speak of is the Pine.\n\nWhen the time is right and the tree is sound.§0\n§0It drops its pinecones to the ground.§0\n§0\n§0The needles that it holds above,§0\n§0Are there not to be grabbed or shoved.§0\n§0\n§0But rather be a tool to use,§0\n§0Not a weapon to abuse.\n\nThe tree I speak of is no quarry,§0\n§0So harm it and you shall be sorry.§0\n§0\n§0So when thou next go near a Pine,§0\n§0Be sure to heed these words of mine.§0\n§0\n§0Respect the tree so tall and firm,§0\n§0And feel the kindness of the Pine.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Watcher", "§bDedicant Thickfeet", "The Watcher§0\n§0By Dedicant Thickfeet\n\nNight falls and the Watcher awakens§0\n§0\n§0For soon she will find one to be taken§0\n§0\n§0Time always manages to find its toll§0\n§0\n§0But for the Watcher, it merely plays a roll\n\nHow can a creature be so ancient?§0\n§0\n§0It must be very careful, forever patient§0\n§0\n§0There is no protection, not even for kings§0\n§0\n§0For those who scurry beneath the raptor's wings\n\nThroughout the world there is so much clatter§0\n§0\n§0But the Watchers wait for a very specific patter§0\n§0\n§0Eyes of gold sweet through the trees§0\n§0\n§0Seeking out the creatues, that which they will seize\n\nThere are many possibilities, but it must be right§0\n§0\n§0Before this hunter can truly take flight§0\n§0\n§0A very light stirring, and then an exposure§0\n§0\n§0The Watcher will soon have in its grasp full closure\n\nA push and lift, she takes to the air§0\n§0\n§0A target is found, they left themselves bare§0\n§0\n§0She swoops forth, like a flash of lightning§0\n§0\n§0A sight so elegant, but ever so frightening\n\nThe distance shrinks as she glides almost to totter§0\n§0\n§0Moving so quickly, on a mission of slaughter§0\n§0\n§0Without a sound, claws snatch it away§0\n§0\n§0Success is achieved, the Watcher took its prey\n\nReturning to the branches, a home so secure§0\n§0\n§0She feasts on her victim, a reaping so pure§0\n§0\n§0Night after night the Watchers ever prowl§0\n§0\n§0Flying up to high fame, of the Great Horned Owl.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant Poem", "§bDedicant Veren", "The leaves rustle as the wind blows strong,§0\n§0Flowers blossom and trees grow tall.§0\n§0The Druids protect the beautiful place,§0\n§0While the Aspects guide with strength and grace.\n\nThe Druids watch the void grow strong,§0\n§0Trying to protect the things we love.§0\n§0As nature listens so subtle and quiet,§0\n§0The world grows on, forever strong.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0~By Dedicant Veren", ""),
        StaticBook("Test", "§bCalius Terin-Aureon", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "§bAeran", "To Calius§0\n§0\n§0I've messed up a lot in my life. In many things, and I hope I can learn from all the recent stuff better than I have in the past. I'm sorry for wasting your time with my juvenile actions, and hope that I can be the Druid that I always knew I\n\ncould be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note: Tax Reguar", "§bShinku", "I will be absent and unable to pay so I have posted 2 elven weeks worth of tax.\n-with consideration\nShinku\nP.S.\nI hope you dont mind the paying before \n;3", "")
    )

    private fun _VAILOR_16(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-----------------------The Lantern-----§0\n§0\n§0       Written By§0\n§0 §0\n§0         Azuline§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§09th of The Grand Harvest 1566\n\n  Once upon a time, there was a girl who had a small white paper lantern. The girl cared for it and it for her as it would light up the night and keep darkness at bay.  §0\n§0\n\n[!] There was a drawing of a small child holding onto a lantern in the darkness. In the darkness there was tiny specks of red as if eyes were looming over the child. [!]\n\n One day, a fox came to the girl and said, \"There are wonders in the darkness that one can see without light.\" He gestured at the lantern and the girl frowned at him.§0\n§0 \"I rather not see those wonders, but rest well in the darkness of the night with my\n\nlantern by my side.\" She explains.§0\n§0 \"Oh? Do you not want to see the dancing figures and join them on their parade?\" The fox grinned from ear to ear.§0\n§0 \"No, now let me be!\" The girl said and wondered off to avoid him.\n\n[!] There was a picture of the girl who promptly walked away from the fox who was about twice her size. The fox looked mad at her. [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Transcribed by Crineas Acosta§0\n§0\n§0Year 1541. §0\n§0\n§01st of The Deep Cold.\n\nThy blessings we do receive and give thanks for,§0\n§0\n§0The beauty of the springs and forest beasts§0\n§0\n§0Enlighten us as we stroll the peaceful fortitude\n\nIn which we are guarded by four;§0\n§0\n§0The four presided by one more", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[The pages would have smudges of charcoal, and be slightly crinkled as if someone tried to throw away these peices a few times, the later pages fresher as if the writer was filled with some sort of... determination to finish]\n\nI've never made good choices. That's something I came to accept as life went on, I always messed up.§0\n§0Bad desicions followed me even when they seemed the right choice, at the time atleast...§0\n§0I can't pretend I'm anything less than a failure anymore.\n\nAbandoning my child, I stupidly thought it was right, that it'd be better for him. I still think it was, he's grown into a better man than I could've raised.§0\n§0Far from his shit father.§0\n§0But it's good he found the Des'nox, and that they've taken him in.\n\nBut me, I don't deserve to be with them. I'm a coward and I'd rather run away than face things. I can't do it I just... I've tried. And all my attempts at happiness just lead to pain.§0\n§0\n§0I feel I have no place among the ancestors. And that's... crushing.\n\nEverything just hurts. My failures, and my own lack of... wanting to try. I don't think I could ever sucseed even if given the chance.§0\n§0And I was given a chance, but I'm to frightened to fail- it freezes me in place and I just... I don't know if I can...\n\nYpres saved my life once, and I'm indepted to him for that.§0\n§0But of course I fail at that too, and I just want to go away- Away from this all.§0\n§0When I think of myself all I see still is a cripple, crippled physically, emotionally, a failure without worth.\n\nI'm going to let them down again... and again and again, I'm a smudge against the Des'Nox name ruining its glory.§0\n§0\n§0Today, Dakel takes his last breaths.§0\n§0\n§0I'm sorry, Arveldir, I couldnt be there. I do love you, I tried even if I failed.\n\nI wasnt a good father to you. I tried in the time that we were together, but I doubt you remember. I worked a lot, to keep you fed and in a bed, but when the offer came up for the inkeep's family to take care of you... I took it. I thought I'd be safer.\n\nI could take more jobs, and send money back to you. I did for a long time, until I got word that you were adopted by Ker, I didnt know where you lived so I couldnt send anymore.§0\n§0\n§0When I met you in Athera I tried to hide who I was.\n\nI recognised you so quickly though, as soon as I saw your eyes. I tried to avoid it because I thought coming back into your life would mess things up. You were adopted by my cousin, which was great. I knew what would happen though and... well. It did.\n\nI deserved it.§0\n§0\n§0I'm still sorry.§0\n§0\n§0I don't even know if you'll be getting this, I'm probobly throwing this in the fire like all the rest.§0\n§0\n§0But no, if I'm going to do one last brave act it'll be apologizing for all my wrongs.", ""),
        StaticBook("<3", "§bGrungron Irongut", "Madde, I love you. Thought about it for a while, and I know I've said it a lot. You're special to me, and you're a really beautiful person. Honestly I'm so happy I met you, nothing in the world could ever make me as happy as I've been these last couple\n\nof months. I just want you to know that I'll always be here for you, and that I care about you a lot :) So take care. You're a wonderful person, so never feel down, ok? It means a lot that your willing to spend time with me~ Hopefully we'll catch up on\n\nanimu. I'll always remember the times we've shared, and that false faces was our first anime! :D\n\nLove you~", ""),
        StaticBook("<3", "§bAdaril", "I love you Maddy. I can say that I've never felt this way about anyone else before. You're special to me, and I want to give you the world. I don't care about anyone else, I wake up every morning with a smile because of you. Your kindness, your\n\npervy side and your teasing. Your sense of humor, your beautiful personality. And I have to say, its not just your personality that's beautiful. You're gorgeous, princess. I can't describe how wonderful you are. I really wish I could it into words. I\n\nlove you, beautiful. \n\nYes, I had to re-write this. I tried to put it in your inventory and it disappeared. GG.... also here's your items. Enjoy your day, ok? See you later~", ""),
        StaticBook("Forget", "§bSalamandra", "The Mind of Madness\n\nThe wind's arms tore against my chest, trying to hold me back. I resisted, and continued flying across the rooftops.  This was my domain. They would never catch me here. The guards were below, in the street, but stood no chance of\n\nkeeping sight on me as I quickly dashed to the right, leaping to the next building. In their clunky armor they were far too slow, and were now forced to fight their ways through narrow alleys. Poor sods. Taking the rock from my pocket in-hand, I leapt to\n\nthe next building, my destination. Throwing the rock a building ahead, I quickly ducked inside the trapdoor in the roof, shutting it as silently as possible. With a quick disrobing as I heard the guards run through the alley, I left the building and went\n\non my way. The guards were so jumpy about people on the rooftops, I wonder why?\n\nI now had the map I needed scribed in my head, and the contacts information about the guards was good, not great. Arriving undetected during the ceremony was easy: just had\n\nto act like everybody else and dress for the occasion. Once inside I had to wait until no guards were looking at me before sneaking through the tower door, waiting a few extra minutes was no hinderance on the operation, so I was still on schedule.\n\nI didn't feel nervous at all. Shouldn't I be? I asked myself these things as I took off the annoying dressy clothes and put on my Brotherhood robes. This would be my first /real/ kill, so I was surprised that my nerves were perfectly fine. I climbed the\n\nsteps with my bow in hand, and only the single arrow that I would need; the less equipment the better, but I did take a dagger just in case. I walked across the roof, mindful of my footsteps. The goal was that nobody would hear me from below, as I snuck\n\nto the planks I had loosened a few days before, so I could slip through them and into the rafters of the large church, undetected. This is what transpired. The priest had just started his service, and I rested the bow across my knee with the arrow in\n\nhand. All I had to do was remain perfectly still and wait. This is what I did, listening in to the priest. He'd obviously put some effort into what he was saying, and looked like a man who enjoyed sharing his beliefs with the crowd. I waited until he\n\nwas back, standing before the altar, before raising the bow and arrow up to my chin. My nerves suddenly lost all control, and I began to shake. I was going to end this man's life, his very existance if I simply let the string....go. All sensations left me\n\nall but one that was the rapid, pounding beating of my own heart. My vision blurred, and I began to take louder, ragged breaths. Faster and faster my heart continued to throb, tearing away at my flesh until each beat was an agonizing dagger, rending at\n\nme from the inside. I glared down the arrow and the priest, and forced myself to pull the arrow from the string. Quickly turning I reached up for the wooden planks, dropping the bow into the crowd below.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nThe first time was so difficult. I remember it clearly, branded there into my head. The priest's face is as clear as day,, and I watch the blood pour from his eyes and mouth every night in my dreams. Forgetting is the hardest part, they've told me. I want\n\nto forget this pain, this guilt. Is it right to forget every soul you've sent to the void? Every person you've killed. Every existance you've destroyed.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nContracts after contracts find their ways to me, and they only seem to get easier and easier. My body moves in tandem with my will. Running across rooftops was never so enjoyable before, as now when the guard is in the street just below, ready to take\n\nyour life. Only you and your body limit yourself. If you don't want to get caught, don't. Keep moving, and never keep still.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nThe faces pass me by as I sleep, only to fade into nothingness. So easy, now. Blood. \n\nCutting flesh is simple, and watching the blood pour out is the prize. More will replace who /they/ were, and I will always have purpose.\n\nThey will die. They will know my face. The avatar of death. The golden skull forces them into the afterlife, holding their faces beneath the water as the bubbles rise. They shake violently, as if begging me to stop, yet my hands are true and I let them\n\nresist, knowing that they will \n\n...\n\nstop.\n\nI am a predator, and they are prey. I consume. They are consumed.\n\nForgetting is simple.\n\nRemembering is hard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Phaedrus", "§bTurin", "*the letter is written in dark green ink, probably concocted of some forest plant.*\n\"Phaedrus,\nI joined this force with eager eyes and a hopeful disposition. I feel I have done my duty as a guard well, be it patrolling the Elven lands or marching behind\n\nyou in battle. \nI have been with you for nearly four years now, and I have seen a shift in you, an unpleasant one. I obeyed your each and every command, but I am done. I see now that we are no different from the Silver... The Bronze is merely just a new\n\nhead fit poorly upon the same chicken. I fought for freedom, yet I see Elvenkind slaughtered for their beliefs. Revenge was not what I thought your leadership would bring. We were treated as lesser by the Aheral, but what do we treat them as now?\n\nMalin would frown upon this \"Era of the Chosen.\" I frown upon it as well. \nI do see that you will remain leader, perhaps for many years. Think upon what I have written, I hope it will point out flaws that I see. Maybe you will pay them heed, maybe you\n\nwill not. But remember why my brothers have died in battle, remember what they fought for so that YOU might be in power. Do not make their spilt blood be for nothing.\n-Turin\"\n*a badge is laid on the paper, as well as a shiny leaf\n\nmade of metal. It seems to be cracked in half, with red paint flowing from the cracks, \"I hope you see what I see from this, llir.\" is written by it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lenniel's Task", "§bLenniel'onn", "Art Camoryn: Situation- practicing lighting evocation. Shot down spark of lighting, harming himslef, and one other, the other being an innocent, simply watching the display. Art was seriously charred, and unable to speak or move, the other individual was\n\ncharred as well, but not to the extent of Art.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alirya's Letter", "§bElorna", "\"The people remain together because they fear persecution, these splinter groups as you say do not. There is no patriotism, simply strict order. Haelun'or will be nothing unless elves will put themselves in harms way for the sake of other elves they do-\n\n\"-not even know, these cultures that have been invented within the century counteract such progress. A tree must bend in a storm to survive and a create must evolve to thrive. -Alirya Khen'aum.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy of Xan", "§bHilan the First", "YSEKIETAAAOZWVVDECFUJPLVDXSOHBXIAKST,CWEKGSETISOTQWZFVLUGPLRHICQXHAXKRMQUSZTUGXWQWW.GBOGAZQKFENWDEEXY,ZVPUIJTLYDILCFUUTSLWQLRXNMKIEHRNYTF.TCEXUPUCVHWYJIEDDYZEKIZNRUHSQRVRTUGQ. ZOYUIRKTUGHNOORA,YYTGVBHTUGHXSLGIQ,SOWJLBFRAXNSGVNVE,HOWUSTTUGJSXRR.\n\nZVPBJTLYFXSLNVYTBXNSIVVYGR,GBOXUPYYMRZISENEVLKZEWVOINPVCCWEYTBSVSY.YSEKIETAALGGDPJLYFAGBEHHEOESTEFHVLNPGOSYWYLNQ,GBOZMGSTUGQUCYUMFTNTVLKHTPIVDNVIL.\n\nUBWBJSEALOGGEEVYKIAHPQEAESCVKVLPYPD,CWWOGSEISRRPQPNYCRFKLEPRTBOOZWXUPONEIYZCEX.YHZSUTM,HSQRVRHRSVSYVNPNVLZCEKIJZRYFANSCHEQLEZQRNCWGWUZSGCKK\n\n\n-Hilan Athna, Prophet of Xan", ""),
        StaticBook("A Gift", "birdwhisperer", "Avern'len, kae'mayilu...\nmy words do not come in the form of skillful rhymes and rhythms, for I am no poet.\nYou have woven many delightful verses for me, and I wish to give the same gift to you.\nSo here is my attempt at poetry, through prose,\n\nThe mellow sweetness\nof your voice as it fills the forest thrills my ears more than even the sighing breeze or singing brook.\n\nYour arms are like the great branches of a sheltering tree, and when you hold me I lose all fear...\n\n...for I know that in your arms, I am safe.\n\nThe grace and delicacy you display as you play upon your lute gives all the world pause, and the birds themselves soften their melody-making to hear your song.\n\nI smile to touch the silken stream of sunlight that is your soft hair.\n\nAnd the heat that radiates from your passionate soul warms me to the heart, and I know that you are, and will forever be, my beloved.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n~Elorna, nae'mayilu.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal VI", "§bElorna", "Aspects help me it's happening all over again.\nThe druids and high elves are at war, or nearly. So many things have caused it. Everyone is acting like children and violent fools.\nI thought we could have peace, we nearly did. But today\n\neverything escalated and Ouity attacked Kalenz. Now Lucion give us their terms for peace...\n\nMilo and Ouity will be turned over to the Mali'aheral. Neither of them can die anyway, so that doesn't matter. They must be shunned. That might be difficult\n\nto get the Order to accept, but both endangered the Order and every druid's life with their actions. Ouity, at least, I understand what he did and why. Perhaps he would be willing to be shunned for the Order's sake.\nAnd lastly, the three druids who are\n\ninfluential residents of Haelun'or... Oropher, Earendur, and myself must be shunned. To ensure our loyalty to Haelun'or over the Order.\n\nThese are the terms for peace. My order or peace. My order or sanity. My order ot the high elves. I know\n\nwhat Callax, Dover, all of them already think of me. That I've shirked my duties to nature, abandoned my vows. This would only strengthen that belief. Earendur at least said he doesn't care. That's not surprising, he's always been more Mali'aheral than\n\ndruid. Oropher was shot and I can't find him...\n\nThey probably won't accept even this, but they might... I would be sacrificing my reputation, my Order, the friends in the Order - few as they may be now - in order to stop more\n\nbloodshed and lives lost. For peace.\n\nPeace and life.\n\nThe last promise I made to Avery was that I would live. I would survive. I want to live. I want others to live.\n\nI don't seem to have much choice. The\n\nultimate thing I must consider... will this help nature? Would the Aspects approve?\n\nI would abandon my Order to save it. I would abandoned my Order to keep them from abusing their gifts to bring war and plague on Tahn'siol. I would abandon my\n\nOrder to keep the high elves from burning the grove and killing every druid they find.\n\n\nLet us hope they accept.\n\nWell, it has been quite a busy few days. We've had so many moots, trips between Haelun'or and the grove. I'm exhausted. But they are finally terms that both Kalenz and the druids can agree to. So, in order to end this conflict, the druids must leave\n\nHaelun'or alone, turn in Milo and Ouity, and shun two of the five Kalenz originally asked. I thought they were going to shun me and either Earendur or Oropher, but Milo and Ouity actually volunteered. They've not turned themselves over yet, but they said\n\n\n\n*a few pages appear damaged by water and\ndust. The words are smeared into the page and impossible to read.*\n\nlove his company. I even called him mayilu.\n\nI'm not sure how to know when you are ready to move on. Have I already? Or will I never be. Little things still remind me of Avery, but I don't know that I would ever not remember him, or want to. Does one have\n\nto forget to move on? I believe Phaedrus will propose soon. He strongly suggested it, anyway. If I'm not ready to remarry now, will I ever be? I do believe I love him. Yet I don't believe I no longer love Avery. How long is long enough? Would it be unfair\n\nto Phaedrus to marry him while I still love the memory of Avery? I'm also worried that if I wanted to wait longer I would simply lose Phaedrus.\n\n\nI suppose I have until he proposes to think on it.\n\n*the next few pages are blank, smeared with grime and dust. The entire book seems rather musty and damaged by water or time.*\n\nWell. Hello once again. It's been several years now since I last picked up one of you. I've somehow managed to keep all my journals together despite all this hopping from place to place. I'm not sure I have the heart to read through them all again, but\n\nperhaps soon. This one seems to be the last place I left off, which was... in the Fringe, just before Phaedrus proposed. Well, now we're about two worlds away and we've been married for over a year! I'm not quite sure where to start but I suppose I'll\n\ntry to summarize the last few years.\n\nPhaedrus proposed and of course I said yes. We were very nearly robbed in the middle of it, but after all that was cleared up it was pleasant. We were planning to have the wedding in the ballroom but\n\nsomething happened that made us wait... I don't remember what.\n\nOh, I believe it was a drought. Or was that before? I don't remember. The drought was after the plague though, and I'm fairly certain I wrote about the plague already. Anyway, there was a\n\nvery bad drought near the end of the conflict between the high elves and druids, and other things that made us start to consider finally leaving the Fringe. Something happened during a council meeting and several of us were somehow teleported or had a\n\nvision about an altar. Something about how the elven language was too powerful and being misused by Larihei. It's rather hazy now. Anyway, we left the Fringe and settled on a little island called Thales. Every year the winters would get longer and colder,\n\nuntil it seemed to be perputually winter all the time. I fell very sick for a long while, I'm still not quite sure what was wrong with me. Anyway, partially because of that Lin'ame was off to a very bad start, hardly anything got done and the population\n\nnearly dissapeared. There was that monstrous high elf, Durion, who threatened to kill Lenniel and Naaliya several times. I believe he murdered a druid in the grove in order to start another war between us and tried to get Kalenz or Lucion to exile him,\n\nbut nothing came of that. At least not then, but I'll get to that part.\n\nDue to the harsh winters we left Thales, and arrived on a beautiful new content called Athera. The landscapes here are gorgeous, though there seems to be a\n\nlot of arcane corruption in the wildlife. The forest of Fiandria is almost completely unresponsive to any druid's attempt to commune with it, and the entire forest, trees and spiders and all, attack anyone who goes near the ruins there. Its tied in with\n\nthe vision we had about the alter.\n\nSo anyway, Phaedrus and I were finally married. In the middle of it some vile humans tried to push off the grove tree, and we were once again teleported by whatever beings guard the ruins in Fiandria\n\nand they said something about protectin the altar.\n\nWhen they returned us to the real world we fell in a mud puddle and had to walk back to the grove to finish the ceremony. But thankfully we were able to complete the wedding that same day\n\nand the rest of the evening was spent trying to get away from one ridiculous elf or another. Katona, one of the guards, wanted to give us a severed head as a wedding gift while we were washing off. He's quite an interesting person, though I see a lot of\n\npromise in him.\n\nMore recently, things have gotten tense between the Mali'aheral and other elves. The Beru'cinhir is currently the only really functional guard force in the city, and the high elves show no respect as always. Kalenz even\n\ninterrogated Phaedrus because he was too 'efficient' or high-elf like. Now there is a plot of some kind to simply overthrow the Mali'aheral. Phaedrus is going to present a list of demands, including making him the new Sohaer. He's gathering support from\n\nthe other nations, and the high elves themselves are debating what to do about it. I listened in one of their meetings, and they seem to be quite threatened by all this, but don't plan to do much.\n\nHonestly I'm simply worried something will\n\nhappen to him if he takes this course of action. The high elves are in a very vulnerable position right now, yet Durion, as I mentioned, attempted to take over as well and he was executed by Oren. I'm not sure who Oren will side with. The Rose have\n\nreturned, this time as the Flaming Rose and a different tabard, but they are the same order. They are still allied with the high elves as well.\n\nI simply don't want this to come to war. And I don't want Phaedrus hurt. I don't think I'd be able to survive\n\nthat again. Hopefully it won't come to that. If he succeeds I believe the Mali as a whole will be able to truly thrive.\n\n\nI cannot help but be reminded of Avery, and when he wanted to do something similar. He didn't really want to, but he felt he had to.\n\nPhaedrus seems to truly want to, I think. Even so it might be best to go away somewhere and live quietly. If Avery and I had done that he may never had died. I'm stronger now than I was then, and perhaps I could protect Phaedrus if something like that\n\nwere to happen. Because I won't let it happen again.\n\nI've read over the beginning of this journal and I seemed to be asking if I truly loved Phaedrus as I had Avery. I can answer now with yes. I can be confident in myself again knowing\n\nthat he'll be there for me whenever I need him, and I want to be there for him on whatever path he chooses to take. So I'll support him in this current path. However it may end, we'll end it together.\n\nWell.\n\nI am once again writing while bedridden. Earlier today, while I was talking with Shadow after not having seen him in some time, a child that we've had trouble with before ran up to huge me. Meanwhile, he sister came up behind me and stabbed me in\n\nthe back. Probably one of my more painful injuries so far, which wasn't helped when a mage cauterized it to stop the bleeding.\nI was taken to the grove and thankfully Leyun was there. One of the herbs she used though - beardweed - has added side effects..\n\nI have grown a beard.\n\nI'm not sure if I should laugh or cry, really. I suppose all in all it's not the worst thing that's ever happened to me, but it's very embarassing. My back is feeling a little better, at least, though I'm a bit afraid to try moving\n\ntoo much.\n\nSomething is going on in the city so Phaedrus has gone to check.\n\nI suppose I'm going to be hear for a while. I don't have many pages left, but I suppose I can summarize recent events. We've finally\n\noverthrown the high elves. It had been planned for a long while, but when Iatrilemar was elected Sohaer it seemed he would be more progssive and let the wood and dark elves have more representation. Camernor was planning to assassinate him,\n\nbut Phaedrus killed him in Fiandria. Some time afterwards, he was found frozen in a crystal, so Phaedrus declared martial law. The Mali'aheral didn't like that, so Kalenz tried to make Kalameet Sohaer. Ah, and I've since heard from Jakir that Kalameet is\n\na shade. After that Phaedrus began to hear from the dwarves, Aesterwald, the orcs, and some others that they would support him as the new leader of Haelun'or, and finally there was a battle. Before the army even arrived the high elves burned the library\n\nand left the city, but in place of a battle for the city Iblees attacked. He did quite a bit of damage, and the 'golden pools' under the city are tainted now. I'm planning to gather a large group of clerics, druids, and Ascended to heal them.\n\nThere's not much to do right now. I suppose my back is feeling better but I'd rather not wander around in public with a beard. I'll need a new journal soon, too.\n\nPhaedrus and I have been married for a while, and want children, but still\n\nnothing. I know the elves are cursed, byt with Avery I became a pregnant after... five or ten years, maybe a little more. I know it's been longer than that by now for Phaedrus and I. And it's been over half a century since I had Lenniel, so it can't be\n\nanything about that.\n\nAh well, I suppose it will happen when the Aspects will it to. I've been leaving offerings at Cerridwen's shrine in the grove.\n\nAnd I'll be holding classes to teach new druids how to harness their gifts. I should\n\nstart working on the curriculum for that...\n\nWell, it seems I'm on the last page. This journal was a bit more neglected than my others, and I probably missed a lot. But all in all... it has not been a bad passage of my life. Until next time, Elorna.", ""),
        StaticBook("Copy of Journal", "§bDwyn Tinuvial", "Year 1402\n\nEntry 1\n\nI just arrived at Normandor. It looks like a nice place. Hopefully everything will go alright. This is the first time I've ever been this far away from home. I wish my  dad could be here to see\n\nme. I really hope that that he would be proud of me...\nOn a hopefully happier note, I passed by another wood elf on the bridge here. He kept looking at me. Checking me out maybe? Probably not.\n\nEntry 2\n\nI'm thinking about joining the guard here. They're called the Sentinals. I want to be able to help and protect people. I'll have to look into it and see how I can join. My dad was a guard for our village when he was alive. He was\n\neverything to our village...\n\n\nEntry 3\n\nThe wood elf from the bridge to Normandor... He actually talked to me today. I saw him around town a couple of times, but hadn't run into him again. I found\n\nout that his name is Dwyn. I was in the tavern, sitting at the bar when I heard someone speak to me. I turned around, and there he was. He kept flirting with me, telling me how pretty my hair was. How pretty I was. My stomach wouldn't stop doing\n\nflip-flops.\nHe was off duty and when he saw me, he decided to talk to me. He's in the Sentinals, and he said he could help me apply to be a part of it when I told him I wanted to be a guard.\n\nEntry 4\n\nI was accepted into the Sentinals! Thankfully, Dwyn told me what it would be like beforehand. What they were expecting and all of that. He wants to take me out for drinks to celebrate. Is it bad that I'm feeling more excited about that\n\nthan being accepted into the Sentinals? I mean, I'm really happy about getting in, but my heart is racing at the thought of going out with Dwyn.\n\nEntry 5\n\nI can't believe it. He kissed me. My face has never felt so hot before. And he said he'd like to keep seeing me outside of the Sentinals. I'd really like to keep seeing him too, so of course I agreed to it.\n\nEntry 6\n\nIt's been a while since I've written in here. But I've just been so preoccupied with being in the Sentinals and being with Dwyn. We've been officially together for a couple of weeks now. He asked me not long after I joined the Sentinals.\n\nI've never felt this way about anyone before. I think I'm really falling for him.\n\n\nEntry 7\n\nI'm really enjoying being a part of the guard. I feel like I'm not as skilled at the other members, but\n\nDwyn reassures me that I'm just as good as the others. He keeps getting promoted, so I'm really happy for him. I'm fine with the rank I am. I just want to be able to help people, and I'm getting to do that no matter what my rank is.\n\nEntry 8\n\nI really have no excuse for not writing in here. I just keep forgetting about it. I'm spending as much free time as I can with Dwyn when we're not on duty. We get to see each other while on duty,  but obviously since we're on duty,\n\nwe can't really do much besides talk a little.\n\n\nEntry 9\n\nOrcs were attacking the city, and I was nearly attacked by three of them. They told me to take off all of my armor and to\n\njump into the water or they'd kill me. They clearly had the upper hand since there were three of them and only one of me. Using a sword isn't my best skill, so I wouldn't e able to take them all on at the same time. I had no choice but to do what they\n\nasked. Thankfully, I was able to swim to shore to get back into Normandor. The guard was able to push them back without anyone really getting hurt, so that's good at least. I don't think I've ever felt so shaken though.\n\nEntry 10\n\nEver since I got cornered by those orcs, Dwyn hasn't let me go out alone if he can help it. Sometimes he has to, because he'd on duty and I'm not. But for the most part, he hasn't left my side. It feels good to have him worrying\n\nabout me. I know I worry about him when he's on duty, even if I am there. What if something happened?\n\nYear 1403\n\nEntry 11\n\nMe and Dwyn moved in together a while ago, hence my lack of writing in here. We fully moved in a couple of weeks ago. He's so silly though. Someone knocked on the door, and I answered it.\n\nWhat does he do? He walks out naked, completely horrifying them. I had to scold him to at least wear something around the house.\nHard to believe we've been together seven months already. But they've been amazing. I hope we're together for a really long\n\ntime to come.\n\n\nEntry 12\n\nHe said he loved me. My heart is soaring. I wasn't expecting that when he took me out for dinner tonight. But it was a nice surprise. I love him too. So much. I really do think that\n\nhe's the one.\n\n\nEntry 13\n\nMy thoughts about him being the one were just confirmed. He proposed to me, and I said yes. I've never been so happy in my life. I can't wait for rest of our lives\n\ntogether.\n\n\nEntry 14\n\nWe just got married yesterday. We don't really have anything planned for a honeymoon. Probably just spend a couple of days together. I really wish my dad was alive\n\nto be able to meet him... I think they would have liked each other.\n\n\nEntry 15\n\nWe both retired from the Sentinals since we got married. We discussed it, and we felt that it was the right thing to do, so\n\nwe could settle down and start our lives together. We've even talked about having a full family someday. I'd really like that. I've always wanted one.\n\nEntry 16\n\nToday was really hard. It was the anniversary of my dad's death. It doesn't normally hit me so hard. But it just hit me really hard that he's never going to see my husband. Or our famil. He's never going to be able to meet any of them.\n\nDwyn made it easier to get through though. He just held me the whole day and let me cry into his shoulder. I don't know what I would do without him.\n\nEntry 17\n\nI asked Dwyn if we could visit my home village, because I want my Uncle Elessar to meet my husband. Okay, he's not actually my Uncle. But he was my dad's best friend. He might as well be my Uncle. Anyways, he said that we could, but it\n\nwas obvious that he wasn't really comfortable with it. So, I won't make him go. We can always go at a later time.\n\nYear 1408\n\nEntry 18\n\nSomething's off. Things haven't been the same in a while. But I'm not sure what it is that's off. We spend a lot of time together, but... Something's just... Off. I'm not really sure how to explain it.\n\nHopefully this is just a temporary thing... We can work it out. I know we can.\n\n\nEntry 19\n\nWe've been together over seven years now. What changed...?\n\nEntry 20\n\nI really thought we'd be able to work it out. We've worked out things before, so I just figured that we'd be able to again like we always have. That's part of being in a relationship and being married. Working things out... But apparently\n\nwe can't. Dwyn talked to me today about splitting up, saying that things just weren't the same as they were before and that he doesn't know what happened. There's still time, isn't there? For things to work out? There's still time...\n\nEntry 21\n\nThere wasn't time... Dwyn packed up all of his things this morning. He took off his wedding ring and gave it to me. He told me that I should sell it, and then he left. He took all of his things and left. I can't sell it... There's no way I'd be\n\nable to sell it. I really wanted us to work out... What happened? Why couldn't things work out...?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Craftsman", "§b[Dove Druid] Elorna", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nThe craftsman sets his fire burning,\nLighting up the night.\nHeat to melt the strongest iron\nTo rivers of sunlight.\n\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nThe craftsman strikes upon the anvil,\nHis hammer's music rings.\nStrong of arm and sure in action,\nHe makes his anvil sing.\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nThe craftsman molds gold, silver, and steel.\nHis calloused hands are deft.\nForging tools of strength and works of art,\nNot one imperfection left.\n\n =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nThe craftsman has a fire burning,\nBurning in his chest\nTo craft his weapons, rings, and armor\nAnd make them at their best.\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nThe craftsman sets a fire burning\nBright within my heart.\nI watch him ply his craft with skill,\nHe is truly set apart.\n\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n~Elorna Lle'hileia\n\n\n*the rest of the page contains a simple sketch of a blacksmith's hammer.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal II", "birdwhisperer", "I have run out of space in my old journal... it is fitting that I would begin a new one at this time of my life. I can feel my baby preparing to be born. It should be any day now.\nI'm afraid... both of the pain, and of letting my child out into the\n\ndangerous and unpredictable world. While I yet carry him, or her, he's safe from that.\nBut on the other hand, this has been a long journey. One I am eager to be done with.\n\n*rather clumsy drawings of tiny hands, dispersed with a few butterflies and designs for baby clothes fill the page.*\n\n\n\nLenniel'onn. Healthy, green-eyed, red-haired boy. Our son.\n\nGavin may be taking over as my guide... I've already cut a branch from our birch to make a staff.\n\nOz and Lenniel seem to get along quite well. He enjoys caring for him.\n\nGavin says, and I fear it may be true, that Oz is only acting like that\n\nbecause he still has feelings for me. I don't know what I'm supposed to do about that, it's not as though I've done anything to encourage him. And he has done nothing aside from being a pleasant friend.\n\nI miss Avery, though... he needs to return.\n\nIt would seem I've been robbed. I'm not sure when, exactly, I only just now noticed. I found a note in one of the drawers about a donation to the guild, and locks, and another one of those gold coins.\nAnd the necklaces Avery got me were gone.\n\nThe opal ones, at least, were left alone, which I'm thankful for because those were my favorite. But the ruby one, and the white crystal necklace have both been stolen. None of the books seem to have been bothered, at least...\n\nI learned a bit about healing from Gavin. It seems most of it just has to do with common sense and being prepared. He also said I may be attuned soon. And I need to work on my staff.\n\nAvern'len returned some time ago, and Lenniel'onn is walking now.\n\nOz showed me to a ruin he and Gavin have taken over. There was a lovely beach on the way there, and we saw Bravepaw's new Elder tree.\n\nCallax has given me the task of finding objects in the forest that represent Ceridwen and Cernunnos.\n\nI've decided on a piece of a spider's web from the Western forests, and an apple. And my staff is now complete.\n\n*a few sketched birch leaves float across the page, accompanied by a single apple, a badly-drawn horse, and varying patterns for what appear to be stuffed toys in the shapes of small animals.*\n\nLenniel'onn is a year old now.\n\nThere has been a strange attack... the same creatures that Avery was having visions of all those years ago. And this time I don't know where he is.\n\nBut Lenniel'onn is safe.\n\nSo now I'm waiting for Callax...\n\n*a few more idle sketches of grass, mushrooms, and moths adorn the page*\n\nI'm not quite sure what to do about Oz. He's a good friend. I like his company. Lenniel'onn seems to like him. But\n\nthat might be the problem. I certainly hope Oz has gotten past things, it's been several years after all. But lately it's been hard to tell.\nNot that he's said anything of course. Simply the way he acts. Gavin may be right, and the wisest course is to\n\nsimply ease out of each others lives.\n\nI can't really justify that, though. As I said, he hasn't said or done anything.\n\nAlthough. With Avery's absence, Oz has spent more time with Lenniel'onn. As much as I like him, I don't want\n\nLenniel to regard Oz as more of a father than Avery. I'm not sure if he does.\n\nBut if he does. That would be a problem...\n\nIt would be simpler if Avery weren't away so much. And if Oz weren't so vague.\n\nLast night was odd.\nA strange Valah, Ebs, and I buried a nameless corpse the Valah found. I hope it is a not of sign of things to come... and I hope whoever it was, did not suffer. It is quite a sad thought, to die without a name.\n\nWhen we had finished\n\nthat, there was a loud explosion and something fell from the sky and landed near the bridge to Lin'everal. It was mostly stone, but also ice, and was somehow on fire. We put the fires out, and took some pieces of the stone. The Valah said it must have\n\nlaunched as an attack from somewhere, but I believe it is a fallen star of some kind.\n\n*a basic sketch of the fallen comet is here, as well as smaller sketches of a strange geode encrusted with gemstones*\n\nBrother Shadow suggested I name my staff. I've no idea where to even start.\n\nHe also said to think on a Grand Task. After a few days, it sort of struck me that Malinor doesn't have anywhere to honor their dead. Not that we have many dead, but in times of\n\nviolence... anyway, so I am considering growing a sort of cemetary. Though this would be more like a small grove where people can remember their loved ones. Perhaps burry them, if they wish. But a place of remembering and honoring the dead.\n\nThings I'll need:\nSeedlings, bonemeal, logs, leaves, glow stone, mushrooms, flowers, gravel....\n\nTo do: get permission for space.\nGet supplies.\nStart building.\n\nAvern'len is showing up less frequently... I'm worried about him.\n\n\nI occupy myself with my child. Lenniel'onn is two years old now.\nAnd with little bits of work. Sewing, my grand task... I want to write something, but it is difficult.\n\nLenniel'onn is nearly three now, and running around more than ever. Today has been a long day, though. I don't remember ever being so frightened before, except perhaps during Oceas's wedding...\n\nThat was a very different event. I\n\nwent with Lenniel to the Delver's base. I knew it was a terrible idea at the time, yet there we were. He and Nienna's daughter started playing a game, and I lost sight of him. I must of searched around those tunnels for hours. It felt as though I was\n\ngoing to lose my mind, I was so sick with worry.\n\nIn the end, he was fine of course. But there's no knowing when he'll wander off again, and in a less friendly place.\n\nAnd Avern has not been seen in...\n         almost a year.\n\n*a few small sketches of roses and flowers fill the page, appearing to have been rather half-heartedly.*\n\nThe druid's grove is gone. The creatures from the north overtook it. I'm not sure where they've gone, but I can't have Lenniel so close.\n\nSo we returned to the Delvers. They've taken us in, set us up with a room. I don't want to be here but there's\n\nno other choice. Our room is very close to the entrance, though, so it's not so bad. And Lenniel seems to enjoy playing with Nienna's daughter, Eventa. He wanted to come here.\nI only hope the rest of the druids are alright.\n\n\nI need Avery to come back. He's been gone nearly a year or maybe more. I need him. I need you kae'mayilu. I don't want to raise Lenniel alone, and now Gavin is trying to have his own input. I can't do this on my own. I need you, love.\n\nI spent most of the day waiting by the shores near the Mali'aheral with the druids. Lenniel has gotten it into his head that Gavin is his Maln. This is exactly what I feared would happen with Oz, and it seems that through Gavin's meddling and Lenniel's...\n\nneed for a father, it's happened despite anything I may have tried.\n\nAnd now Lenniel wants me to love him, and Gavin was saying absurd things I don't even want to think about...\n\nI just need Avery.\n\n*the outline of a beach and small hill, covered in trees fills the page.*\n\n\n\n*a single birch leaf is pressed between the pages.*\n\nI have been attuned with nature and am now a full druid! Saviticus oversaw, and my totem is the Dove. It isn't quite what I was expecting, though I'm not sure what I did expect. But it seems fitting.\n\nAvery is back!\n\nThe past few days have been rather interesting...\n\n\nGavin and Avery apparently got into a fight. Then later Gavin apologised and gave Avery his sword as a token of his sincerity. And there was a moot held, and it seemed as\n\nthough Gavin would be removed from his seat as Arch Druid, but he was not. Instead, Kefi was made a second Arch Druid.\n\n*wheat sheaves, birch leaves, owls, sparrows, and simple, curling flowers are sketched on this page*\n\nI don't remember how long it's been since I picked this up last...\n\nQuite a bit has been happening, all worrisome. It seems we cannot have but a few days of peace.\n\nLet's see, where to start.\n\nSome time ago, I met two strange men just outside the gate of Malinor. They were both wearing hoods, but one said his name was Torian, and the other may have been a mali'ker. They told me a man had been watching Lenniel'onn, and was probably a danger to\n\nhim. They wanted me to come with them to Adunia to confront this man. Then one of the Delver mages, Richard Tarus, walked past and said they were wearing undead robes, with the eye of Iblees. So I left to check on Lenniel, who was asleep on Samuel. Meta\n\nfollowed me, apparently, and warned me of the men.\n\nLater that night Art got into a fight with them, and one of the men was captured. I don't believe much was learned from him.\n\nThey knew my name, and Lenniel's, and of\n\nour home in the Delver's village.\n\nSome time after that, I saw one of the hooded men on Samuel. He didn't do or say anything, but he pointed to my tree. I found on my bed... a severed finger, and a bit of cloth with a line from the poem I wrote\n\nfor Avern'len. I thought I'd lost between moving all my things so often.\n\nSomehow those men got a hold of it... I'm not sure what they're trying to accomplish, though. Lenniel had wandered off, so I paniced and thought he had been taken by\n\nthem, and went running over Malinor and Samuel looking for him.\n\nHe was fine, but while I was in the tree trying to clean up the scene, a raving ikruan kicked him for no reason and broke his ribs. Thankfully we are right next to the Cloud Temple, so Avery\n\nand I took him to the monks to heal.\n\nAvery and I spoke after that, and decided we needed to move again, where those men can't find us.\n\nNot long after, Avery returned from one of his trips to Abresi, saying he'd been\n\nhired by some knightly order in Oren to be their personal bard. He seems very happy being in Abresi...\n\nAnyway, he also got us a house there, and everything was set up.\nSo we showed Lenniel. He seemed to not mind it too much, but he's very young and it's\n\nquite different from what he's used to.\n\nBut the next morning when I return to the house, I find his leg had been cut open. He'd gotten out of the house somehow\n\n*the next few lines look very shaky, many are scratched out*\n\nHe was taken from the middle of the city\nand tortured by several men.\n\nThey told him not to speak, and they'd be finding him again.\n\nI don't know if it's connected to the others. I don't know what to do. Nowhere\n\nwe have gone is ever safe. There is no home for the three of us that is both safe, and happy...\nI've run out of pages again, it seems. This one has lasted nearly six years, but it does not seem that long.\nHopefully in my next book, I'll have better news.", ""),
        StaticBook("Trials", "§bElorna", "I have roamed the south, the snowy regions around the dwarves, and the jungles at the outskirts of the wilds. So far no luck, however I can now see how few large swathes of wilderness remain in Athera, which is quite concerning.\n\nI've come to a pine forest in a valley, with a huge elder tree at the center.\n\nNow I've reached the ridge above the valley, to a sparse forest of pine and oak trees. On the other side of the ridge is another valley filled with orchids. This feels\n\nlike the right place...\n\nI've found it. I came accross a fox in the valley and experienced... well, it's hard to describe. A sign from Cernunnos when our eyes met.\n\nThe fox is an older vixen, who lives with a family of foxes in this valley. The family\n\nincludes the mating pair and their little of cubs, and some of their grown cubs from last year's litter that stay to help with the hunting and tending to the young ones. The first fox that I met, though, is older than the parents, a grandmother, perhaps\n\nyou could say. Her mate died and the new male chose her cub. Most of the other male offspring have gone off to find their own territory, but it seems like the females tend to stick together and take care of the newest litters.\n\nI've helped them hunt tonight. They'll eat anything from mice, to crickets, to berries. I fear I sometimes neglect the aspect of nature that Cernunnos oversees in favor of gentler things. The second trial may come hard for me, but I will do what I must to\n\nfinally give Cernunnos his due service.\n\nIt is done. The oldest of the vixens took me hunting, she seemed to want me to prove that I was capable of it. I wasn't even sure myself, but apparently I am. After that there was an odd moment, and we both seemed\n\nto know what would happen next. We fought. She drew first blood and gave me quiet a few scratches, but I won in the end. I killed her. It's an odd feeling. Yet, if I'm to believe the tome Thudrin gave me, her spirit will merged with mine. She will live on\n\nin me. And I've proven to myself and to Cernunnos that I can fulfill the duties of the hunt.\n\nNow to return to the grove with the pelt.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keeping a Vow", "wardog4445", "When you close your eyes, I wonder what your dreams are, as we rest beneath the onyx skies, glancing over each star,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=The world is changing as it always does, but my dear let me tell you something, my love will remain like it always was,\n\nLike the stars it's never faltering,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Such simple gestures carry such great weight, like your touch upon my cheek, A kiss will always quicken my heart rate, carrying feelings that I could never speak,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nI realize my mind may descend, to depths I cannot climb, but do not be saddened by this news, I only needed a verse that would rhyme,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=I love how you softly laugh, I love how your skin turns crimson, you are my other kindhearted half,\n\nOne that cannot be replaced by nation, cause or other women,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=I love how your eyes follow mine, I love how you distract me from troubled times, I love how our fingers intertwine, and I love our spontaneous tree climbs,\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nElorna, on the day that we were married, I promised you, I would always call you...\n\nKae'mayilu...\nI... Love... You.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal III", "§bElorna Lle'hileia", "It seems odd to find that I need a third book to use as a journal. It also odd to think that it's been nearly fifteen or more years since I began my first journal. \nAvery and I hadn't yet married, Lenniel of course was not born. My worries were those of\n\nMalinor, and the problems of the world. Now, my worries are not so heavy, but closer and sharper.\nNo... my troubles now are much more personal.\n\nMalinor is probably doing alright. I have distanced myself from it quite a bit these\n\nrecent years. But those hooded men came to Samuel a few days ago. This time with armor and crossbows.\nThey demanded that I be handed over to them, lest they hurt someone. I dont' understand why they are targetting me, but when Gavin asked they said I had\n\nattacked and insulted one of them. Obviously this is absurd, but it still doesn't explain their actions. I can't fathom it.\n\nThey said they would continue to hunt me down...\n\nWell, today has been rather unpleasant. Lenniel has come down some of kind of awful flu, and has been stuck in bed for the past few days.\nAnd in the temple, two uruks were talking to a simple-minded man about slaves, and I tried to warn him about them.\n\nAnd one of the orcs kicked me in the stomach. I suppose I'm gratefully that's all that happened...\n\nI tried to commune with Samuel, as well. His presence is so... overwhelming, and I somehow lost consciousness. I wasn't expecting it to\n\nbe such a strain, I suppose.\n\n*a sketch of an apple, feathers, and moths fill this page*\n\n*the following is written in very shaky handwriting*\n\nI was taken. I don't remember much at all, but those hooded men took me. I'm told they came to Samuel, and I vaguely remember being in some kind of boat with Leyun... then nothing. And after\n\nthat, just darkness... a lot of pain in my head. And a cell.\n\nThe next thing I knew I was wandering through the temple ground, and Avery found me.\n\nIt's been a few days, and I think I remember a few things more clearly.\nI was standing on Samuel, and two men approached. A human, and a dark elf. Then it gets blurry, and I remember again, hiding on a boat with Leyun. And the dark elf found us... After\n\nthat, I awoke in a cell, with my hands and legs bound. Strangely, there was light within the cell, but darkness without. So I couldn't see, but I could be seen...\n\nBeyond the bars were hooded figures standing in shadow. They spoke of\n\nchanging me, of my faith in the Aspects. Then I was taken to another room and chained to a chair, and that same dark elf was speaking to me. I don't recall what he said, or did... only that I was terrified.\nBeyon that, nothing makes sense. I felt cold.\n\nI found myself wandering through the Cloud Temple grounds in a daze. I was alone, my mind was muddled, and my body was weak and shaking. I couldn't walk back to Samuel, so I collapsed in a corner, until Avery found me. He was crying, and said he tried to\n\nfind me, but couldn't. He found my captor, but I wasn't there.\n\nI don't want to think on this any more, but I can't stop going over what little I remember in my mind, acting it out again and again like a scene on a stage. Every time I close my eyes.\n\n\n*a few clumsy, mostly crossed out sketches fill this page*\n\n\n*a small, timid rose is sketched in the bottom corner*\n\nIt has been several days, and I feel a bit better. Not as shaking, a bit stronger.\n\n*several sketched patterns for fine ball gowns and suits take up several pages. Masks, like those for a masquerade party, can also be seen.*\n\n*two larger and more defined patterns for very formal clothes fill this page*\n\n\n\n\nI made a patch of carrots grow today.\nAnd had a beautiful time with Avery in Malinor.\n\nAvery and I went to a masquerade ball Malinor held. And the creatures from the north attacked.\n\nWe're both alright, though.\n\n*a sketch of two masks fill the majority of this page. The rest is taken up by a potted fern.*\n\nI've been having the same nightmare quite a lot recently. I'm in a small circle of light, surrounded by darkness. There are people in the shadows. I can't see them, but they can see me.\n\nOf course, I've always had trouble with nightmares.\n\n\n\n\n\n*this page has been torn out.*\n\n\n\n\n\n*this page has been torn out.*\n\n\n\n\n\n*this page has been torn out.*\n\n\n\n\n\n*this page has been torn out.*\n\nAvern'len has become a dedicant now. I'm not quite a guide, but Leyun had me give him his first task. He needs to do two things in service of Cerridwen and Cernnunnos, so he'll be farming and helping fish for Samuel.\n\nIt's been quite some time since I picked this up.. I can't remeber what's happened that I've missed. I have a dedicant now. He's very enthusiastic...\n\nI read back on some of the last few pages... and am dissapointed. There is no reason to sink so far into\n\ndespair. Life is good again. I have a devoted husband, a healthy son, a strengthening connection to nature, and I feel more confident than I have ever before. I believe I owe it Avery. If he had not been with me, I don't think I could have gained so much\n\nstrength. I'm not sure how to show what he means to me, though... he is always so thoughtful. I'll think on it.\n\nApparently Avern'len has been teaching Lenniel how to fight with a dagger, and while they were practicing on Samuel, he slipped and cut Lenniel across the face. The poor child's cheek is scared, he could have easily lost his eye. I truly do not understand\n\nhow Avery could have been so careless.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWell then. It's been several days, and it's just now come out that Lenniel wasn't hurt while they were\n\ntraining. Those men who took me found him. And they took him and gave him that scare. Avery had him lie so I wouldn't worry. I just\n\n\nI'm afraid. For my son. And that they lied.\n\n\n*a few blank pages seem to have gone unused.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal IV", "§bElorna", "It would appear that my third journal has gone missing... I truly don't remember where I left off, or what has happened since then.\n\nAh... looking through the last entries in my old journal, I remember what happened last. None of it good. Thankfully,\n\nthose times have passed for now and the days are long and pleasant again. I am a Guide, I don't remember if that was mentioned. Lenniel'onn is nearly twelve years old... which amazes me. He's been wanting to be a dedicant, but now he says he is unsure.\n\nThe issue with mages and the void confuses him, and he doesn't want to lose his friends in the Delvers. \nHe's been targeted by that same cult. One of them apparently took him straight from Malinor, cut his face, and left him on Samuel. Avery found him,\n\nand they both lied and told me he had simply been injured while they were sparring. I was livid at Avery, of course...\nThen the truth came out. I don't believe I've actually discussed that lie with Avery, yet.\n\nAh yes. I suppose my last journal left off\n\njust before... that other mess. Those hooded men, part of an Iblees worshipping cult, came onto Samuel and took me from it. I don't remember much at all from that. I was hit on the head several times, I think.\n\nI just remember talking to Leyun, then a\n\ndark, underground place. Voices and figures in the shadows. Threats. He said he wanted to 'change' me.\n\nThen I found myself walking about the Cloud Temple in a daze I could barely function at all after that. Avery helped, though. He stayed\n\nclose by for months, and with time I felt stronger. I feel stronger now than I can remember feeling.\n\nThose men... I'm not sure if I can say they still trouble us, as we haven't had actualy trouble from them. Aside from Lenniel being hurt. But they\n\nhave been following and appearing around us often.\n\nThe dark elf... the same one that took me, I now think, helped Avery in a fight against mages. We didn't know who he was at the time. And a short while ago, while I was growing a tree on the mountainside\n\nits roots broke through the stone and caved in a small hole, which I fell through. I found myself in a large, underground complex, with a garden at the center. A very evil looking place, disregarding the garden. And that man was there. He claimed to be\n\nlost as well, and together we found a way. Then we simply parted ways, as friends.\n\nI shudder to think of what could have happened down there... his actions make no sense to me now.\n\nAh yes, and he\n\nappeared again more recently.\nAvery and I were trying to help a young boy who had seemingly fallen and broken his legs. It was awful. There was no way to help him aside from remove his legs...\nbut he did not survive, regardless. It was awful....\n\nAnd then that dark elf appeared there. He and Art seemed to get into some kind of conversation, then they left. I watched from a tree, as he and Avery spoke. He spoke in riddles, and wouldn't explain why he kept following us. Avery warned him to stay away\n\nand I have not seen him since. Yet.\n\nWell, it has been quite some time since I picked this up last, hasn't it... much has happened, and I have not found the time to write about it.\n\nLet us see...\n\nThe Order has split into three. Gavin left his Arch position and\n\nmade his own circle. I was nearly made an Arch in his place, but such duties do not appeal to me, nor did I feel I was ready for them.\n\nRegardless, tensions between Avery and the other druids were just as bad as before, and seemed to be getting\n\nworse. Apparently Ouity somehow transformed into a bear in front of him, then tried to force him to eat a golden apple and forget the encounter. I'm still not sure how either of those things works. Almost immediately after, we decided to leave for Gavin's\n\ncircle, and have had much more peace since. Ouity did make some odd threats that certain higher ups in the Order would try to kill us if we spoke of his transformation. I find that idea ridiculous, however concerning.\n\nI'm not sure if this\n\nwas before or after we joined Gavin's circle... however I was taken, again. It was some time ago now, so it is not as difficult to write about, but I do not feel I can go into too much...\n\nIt was that same cult that is somehow connected to the\n\nNorthern creatures, and have been demanding a sacrifice from Malinor and leaving heads when they are denied.\n\nI thought I was going to die. I felt I was willing to do or say anything just to be let out alive... but it didn't matter to them. When\n\nthey said I would be let out alive... I didn't care what happened after that. And they did. But my face is scarred now. I didn't think myself to be vain before, but I feel so disfigured now... it is shaming.\n\nAvery is encouraging as ever. I don't know\n\nhow I would have survived these last few years without him. I truly could not imagine a better husband. My love, kae'mayilu.\n\n\n\nThat was not the last of the trouble I had with them, though. A few Elven days ago\n\nthey sent me a letter demanding three animals to be given to them for a sacrifice. If not, they would kidnap, torture, and sacrifice three druids in their place. I spoke to Avery and Callax about this, and Callax brought it to the Order's attention.  He\n\nand Ouity, and Milo decided to go willingly as a sacrifice in place of the animals. The way Callax and Ouity spoke, it seemed as though they did not believe they would truly 'die', and would remember the encounter. \nStrange secrets, though I have not seen\n\nthem since.\n\n*a few drips of ink spot the page, half way down are a few blotted out words.*\n\n\nWe went to their meeting place, a sandstone arch between Malinor and the Cloud Temple. No\n\none was there, then we heard shouting from underground. Some delver man, apparently, was being held there. I thought he was part of the trap at the time, but it seems he was a genuine victim as well.\n\nA door in the side of the mountain opened, and Callax,\n\nOuity, and Milo entered. Avery, Verden and myself stayed outside...\n\nThey were killed. I'm not sure exactly how, but it was very fast. The door opened again, Avery said he saw Ouity, not dead but nearly so, and shot him so he would not suffer... a mouse\n\nescaped and confirmed they had all died.\n\nI led them there. They knew what was going to happen, that's why they went, but those people used me and I don't know why.\nThey sent another letter, telling me as much. Avery ripped it up.\n\nAnd so far, well, that is all that has come of that. They said they would contact me again... and Iler has said that they are demanding animals from the grove each elven day. They know we will not comply, the ullral. I cannot fathom how twisted their\n\nminds must be to be so evil and cruel. They speak of 'Him' and their Master. Aspects protect us.\n\nFor somewhat less heavy news... Gavin's circle the Equinox circle as it is called, is on that lovely island that I grew my grand task upon. It is even\n\nmore beauitufl than before, and lush with animal life. The waters are bursting with fish, there's a healthy population of sheep, and quite a few native rabbits and cats roam the island. A few have taken to coming along with me on trips to Malinor. The\n\nhigh elves have proven troublesome as always. Apparently they did not know or approve of us settling on the island, and before Callax talked it over with Kalenz, they may have thrown us out or burned the island out of spite.\nKalenz also told me we have\n\npermission to tend to their farms and livestock, though I haven't actually been able to follow up on that because of their ridiculous gate.\n\n\nAvery has been much calmer since we moved here, though. He's been meditating, and I\n\nthink is fully on his way to becoming a druid. I don't believe he's gotten into any fights lately, aside from all that with those Northern cultists. If it weren't for them, life would be quite pleasant now.\n\nThings I need to do:\nSpeak to Kefi and the other blight healers about cleaning the taint from Lin'evaral.\n\nMake more living spaces in the grove.\n\nCollect cuttings from a berry bush to be planted on the island.\n\nI think it's about time I replaced my staff. I've thought on it, and considered simply another branch from the same tree, but I just had a thought. There's more than one birch tree that holds important memories for me now. So, why not make a staff from a\n\nbit of all of them. There's the one in Malinor of course. Then the tree Avery and I planted for our wedding in the field near the Mali'aheral. The one by our old home in Oren. And the birch at 'Lover's Leap'. And then perhaps the one that I planted for my\n\nGrand Task. That makes five trees in all. I'm not sure how I would combine a branch from them all into a staff. Perhaps if I grew the branches together. Or took a seed from each and grew the staff right out of the ground. That would be worth trying.\n\nOh dear, it's been a while.\nSo much has happened. So much unpleasantness. As it happens, I'm writing this while sitting in Aislinn's after having an arrow removed from my leg. I don't think I've ever been shot before, or had to have surgery...\n\nThis time it was because a group of Mali'ker was fighting with the wolves that have settled near Malinor. I tried to get everyone to stop, and stepped in front of one of the wolves as she was being shot at. And the reason there are elves camped so close\n\nto the den, is because Malinor has been tainted by some corruption from the North, and rather than try to fix it, the entire city has evacuated and set up tents and new buildings in the forest near the river mouth and Haelun'or. At the same time as that\n\nstarted, the Northern beasts took over the island grove. It was filled with corrupted spiders and had a huge red stone floating above it. I tried talking to them, and they said that if Titania made peace with them they would return the grove. Well, of\n\ncourse that didn't happen, and a battle was fought for it. They were driven out, but all the trees died or burned down - except for my little grove, it seemed to have been far enough from the center that it was spared.\n\nI find little time to write now. The island grove has been reclaimed and healed. Avery has returned from his long absence.\nLenniel seemed to be interested in learning wind magic from some ikru Valah... I'm not sure what I'd have done to that man if he did\n\nteach him. Somehow Avery got Resia to teach Lenniel clerical healing instead. Which is more acceptable... in a way. I wonder sometimes, if it was right to not let him be a dedicant at a younger age. But still, he's at least choosing for himself as mostly\n\nan adult. He is still so very young, though. I think back, and can only vaguely remember my first three decades... my childhood is especially hazy. I suppose, with time, Lenniel will experienc the same... but I'll be around for him, unlike my parents.\n\n*several pages have been skipped over and left empty.*\n\n*the next few pages have large, black blotches of charcoal, some ripping through the page as though they had been stabbed at repeatedly with a blunted pencil.*\n\n*the handwriting is uneven and in some places illegible. The paper crinkles in many spots as though it were wet, then dried.*\n          am\nG- a...     |',      n\n      Av       '.,    \n |,'       er y      .,\n*more dark charcoal splotches mark the page.*\n\nMy mayilu    .'|,  *,.\n    why    I cannot\nPlease no      Avery\n   Please Cerridwen `.\n*incomrehensible writing fills the page.*\n.. ' |'   He's dead\nHe died       how do I go on    how   *|,  . ' ,\n\nI need him. My love. Please Cerridwen bring him back.\n\nMy love- my Avern'len kae'mayilu. He looks so pale, feels so cold. I cannot bear to look away, he is still so lovely. My beautiful husband, why did I let this happen.  Aspects\n  I need you Avery! You cannot leave me!\nCerridwen return him to me. I can't go\n\non. I cannot live without him. He's all that's left, all others are gone, dead. I could live with only him, with the rest of the world dead. I cannot live without him. He is gone, gone. Only Lenniel is left. I cannot live to lose him. I cannot live...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal VIII", "§bElorna", "Journal number eight.§0\n§0\n§0I've been writing these on and off since Anthos... I remember the first entry of the first book. I was sitting beneath my birch tree in Malinor, Avery was asleep beside me. I wasn't even a druid then. What a strange thought,\n\nthat there was a time when I couldn't hear the voices of nature around me...§0\n§0\n§0I reached my second century last year. Two-hundred... I was just fifty when I began my first journal. And so self-concious about my age. I didn't want anyone to know I\n\nwas so young. I've been keeping these journals for one-hundred and fifty years.. and been a druid for nearly all of that time. One-hundred and fifty years since I met Avery... over a hundred years since I bore my first child...§0\n§0\n§0Strange thoughts...\n\nWell... the races have fled Athera. The new land is called Vailor. It's quite vast, and most of its wilderness has been left untouched.§0\n§0\n§0Shortly after we arrived the Shape Circle had a small meeting. It looks like I'm the first woman added to their ranks.\n\nAn honor indeed.§0\n§0\n§0Since the voyage here I've been spending more time with Mark. He admitted straight out he may have feelings for me, or at least... likes me and would like to see what happens. §0\n§0I figured it would do no harm to see. I enjoy his company,\n\nthough he is odd. A mage, of all things. But he's passionate about what he does, which is mostly design and build boats and siege equipment...§0\n§0After spending all that time with him, I realized there's really not much we have in common, or any real\n\nconnection. I'm also not... entirely ready to move on yet... so I told him that, and he seemed to take it well. He actually laughed and seemed relieved.§0\n§0\n§0Then he told me about his past relationships and... well... I'm a bit glad I there was no 'spark'. He\n\ntalked about one of his lovers who kept a slave, that he helped to beat. And that he kidnapped a cleric, who fell in love with him while he was still with the first woman. Arrow dodged, is the expression I believe.§0\n§0\n§0I was also talking to him last night,\n\nhe brought up some giant octopus creature that is being hunted. It apparently destroyed five ships. I may try to commune with it, though there's the difficulty of communicating with something under water, and the possibility that it cannot even be\n\ncommuned with at all. A risk, certainly. After that Mark said I always seemed sad, and gave me a gem. Perhaps he does not think what I said before still stands... I don't look forward to dealing with that, if it comes up again.§0\n§0\n§0I suppose I am sad,\n\nthough. It seems to be the perpetual state I am in. Perhaps not sad, just... melancholy. I've seen a lot of pain over the years. And I'm lonely. Still very lonely... Avery is gone, Phaedrus betrayed me... it still hurts. I want it to stop hurting. I'm a\n\ntwo-hundred year old woman, it should not still be bothering me. But it does. And both my children have left me. I'm in constant communion with all of nature and yet I am lonely. I don't want to be alone forever, without a partner. I'm not ready to move\n\non yet, but I do hope that someday I may find someone else. I don't want to spend my days and nights alone.§0\n§0\n§0It's a perfectly natural need. Every creature in this world wants a partner. Some creaturs only mate long enough to bring about offspring. Some\n\nstay with each other for a season, then part. Some stay together for life. I would say that elves are the sort of creature that bonds for life, but experience suggests every couple only manages a few seasons. Perhaps if we accept that, it will hurt less.\n\nIt's perfectly natural that I want a partner. Someone to hold me close and protect me. Yet I fear there is no one out there who could meet those needs. That I am destined to be alone forever now. If Avery had not died, it would have been different...\n\nNo. I am a druid, a servant of the Aspects. I have wasted too much energy on these matters. I have brought two children into the world, and that is enough. §0\n§0\n§0The family of foxes I met on my trial was composed of only one mating pair. The others were older\n\ncubs from the pair's previous litters. They helped take care of the newest litter of cubs, and brought food to the mother. There was also an older vixen. The one I have merged with. She did not have a mate, but she helped the other foxes. That is my role\n\nnow. An elder, a helper. I am married to nature, and need no other mate. I will focus on this union as penance for my past mistakes and unfaithfulness. I am a druid, and that is all I need to be.\n\n*several pages have been left blank*\n\nHow negligent I've become in keeping these. Perhaps it is time to pen the final page, at least for a while. I have been spending more time... in the forest, and it is becoming hard to come back. This no longer feels like home. I belong out there.\n\nPerhaps, on my next venture I will not come back.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0It has been quite a journey.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Elorna", ""),
        StaticBook("Scars", "§bElorna Lle'hileia", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nMy heart has scars,\nThey're old but deep\nAnd form a faded line.\n\nLong healed by now,\nThe pain is dim,\nYet I still count them mine.\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nA loving word,\nA sweet embrace,\nWill soothe them like a balm.\n\nSo pull me close\nAnd hold my hand\nGently within your palm.\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nI feel the scars\nUpon your hands,\nThough you don't let them show.\n\nAnd now I see\nThey're deeper than\nYou want the world to know.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nI cannot change\nThe things you saw\nThat happened in your past.\n\nBut I can kiss\nThe pain away,\nWe need not let it last.\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nDon't be ashamed,\nDon't cover up,\nThough we need not revive...\n\nThe scars are proof\nOf inner strength\nAnd that we both survived.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nSo pull me close\nAnd hold my hand,\nKiss away my fears.\n\nI'll do the same,\nFor you, my love,\nForever through the years.\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nOur two scarred hearts\nIn warm embrace\nWill beat a vibrant tone.\n\nFor now that I\nAm with you, love,\nYou'll never be alone.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo Phaedrus, my fire.\n\n~Elorna", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal I", "birdwhisperer", "*a few idle scribles fill the page, images of trees, detailed sketching of leaves and flowers petals.*\n\n*several pages seem to have been torn out*\n\n*the rest of the book seems to contain notes\nquickly jotted down*\n\nI had another nightmare. They only seem to happen when he's away... I don't want to worry him though.\n\n*some simple sketches of arrows and bows spread across the page, gradually changing to blades of grass farther down.*\n\nWatching Mirlene's baby, Miri. She's a sweet child. I remember many years ago, going through a period of longing. My arms felt empty, and I yearned to hold a child of my own. I am more content with life now, yet I feel that old longing return again. Yet..\n\nTo be a mother. What an incredible, and at the same time terrifying thought.\n\n*the rest of the page is filled with idle drawings of moths and budding flowers. The outline of a looping ribbon winds its way around the page.*\n\nI wish that the world would pause in all its busyness, and let moments like these go on without any interruptions, from either dawn, or duties, or any other troubles. We have an eternity to spend our lifetimes together, yet these quiet moments are so\n\nshort, so fleeting. What would it be to simply hold each other in quietness by this peaceful birch, still and silent, for a year? What is a year, when held against endless youth? Let the world continue on in its frantic noise without us, let us have these\n\nquiet moments of peace. We do not need the world, when all it has to offer could never bring as much joy as simply holding him to my heart.\n\n*the rest of the page containts different combinations of elven words, many crossed out.*\n\nkae'oem, kae'tuva, iyatmaraheral'eyha kae'mayilu.\n\nMy one, my everything, most blessed thought and my beloved.\n\nelame aher lae'leh\n ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n\nkae'evarir\n\n\n*a sprig of lavender is pressed between the pages. Though it is dry and fragile, it still holds its vibrant green and purple hue.*\n\nI don't want to leave.\nBut he's unhappy here.\n\nI don't want to be the only reason he stays, because that means there's nothing else keeping him from leaving. I don't want him to be unhappy. I don't want to be without him.\n\nOrganize all the houses.\nTalk to Arch Druid Arum.\nGather up things to take:\nBooks, clothes, sewing supplies, writing material, carrot and melon seeds, cuttings from a blueberry bush. Furnishings.\nSay goodbyes.\n\nOrlanden wants to meet Avern at the tavern, send him a bird later.\n\n~~~~~~\nI'm now a Druid Dedicant!\nIsabella is my guide, and my first task is to make a hat from things I find in a forest.\n\n*a few basic sketches of a small cottage, a waterfall, a tree on a cliff's edge, and tiny blueberries fill this page. Each drawing is very dark, and appears to have been made with a very heavy hand.*\n\nI am just over half of a century old. Just old enough that I have begun to notice patterns in life. For a time, all is pleasant and happy. Then comes conflict, suffering, pain, and loss. But that does not last, and eventually the world seems joyful again.\n\nNeither does the joy last forever, and once again times of suffering return. It is like the seasons. Always changing, but always in the same cycle, the same old and predictable pattern. I remember my early childhood as being enjoyable. My mother was an\n\nexcellent teacher, and cared for me greatly, though I remember her seeming sad very often.\nThe she died, and father began to drink more.\nAnd that was painful. But when I moved to Malinor, befriended Brave, Orlanden, life became pleasant.\n\nMuch of that time blurs together now...\nThen I met Scicle. That was more confusing than anything else... but there was a single day of happiness, which was quickly ended. It is for the best.... *the writing trails off here*\nAnd of course there was having\n\nto leave Asulon, and settle upon a mountaintop. But that was turned into a happy time with Walehir and Bravepaw.\n\n\nThat ended as well...\n\n\nThen came war.\n\nBut I met Avery, and the war ended. Our engagement and the years following our marriage are the happiest, most beautiful years of my life that I can recall.\nAnd I am still happy with him. Yet times have changed once again. We live in a tiny house on a\n\ncliff in some Valah town next to the White Rose.\nYet these times, too, will come to an end. History has shown that nothing will last. And so, I can wait out our time here, content in knowing that the seasons will turn as they always do. Perhaps this next\n\nseason will be the one that brings a child...\n\n\n*the remainder of the page is filled with idle drawings of flower petals, blades of grase, an ant, and several attempts at moths in flight.*\n\nAvern is going to take back Malinor... and make himself king.\n\nIt feels like betrayal somehow. I know that he will be able to finally bring prosperity to the Mali, that Malinor has the chance to become great again. He would be an incredible king.\n\nYet I cannot shake this feeling.\n\n\n\n*the  remainder of the page is left devoid of markings*\n\n*sketched patterns for various types of clothing fill the page. Dominating the drawings are confident outlines of a long coat, and tentative designs for what appears to be a straw hat.*\n\nHe's asking me to choose. I can't choose. How can I choose between such a thing...\n\nOn the one hand, we could stay in Oren. Or travel, most likey in Oren. I have not encountered anything too distasteful here, but the only being I've actually spoken to\n\nat length has been the Bortu Lord, I forget his name. Edgehand, perhaps. The other, I think it has been two, Orenians I have met were either aloof or mad, and some White Rose man who was spying on me from a rooftop for who knows why. It has not been\n\nexactly unpleasant - yet - but it has certainly not been anything that would make me want to stay. It's uncomfortable being on the ground so long, I've found myself more easily agitated recently...\nBut that's not the point. We can either stay...\n\nOr we can return to Malinor. My home. The home I have been so faithful to for nearly all of my fifty years.\nBut he refuses to return unless he rules it, unless he can make Malinor great and something to be proud of again.\nAnd he can do it. He can help. He\n\ncan do so much to help. But at such a high price...\nHe said himself he doesn't want it. He doesn't want to be a king, he would simply do it to make me happy, make our home safe. But he is convinced that when he does it will alter him. And of course put\n\nboth our lives at risk. I'm not so sure that I could not keep him from being so heavily affected... but it is a risk.\n\nAnd this choice he has laid on my shoulders.\n\nThe choice is do I sacrifice him, to save my race...\n\nDo I give up the bard for the king...\n\nOr do I let Malinor continue in it's ruined state, live in Oren, but keep him...\n\n\n\n\nI will speak to a drui.\n\n*small sketches of fish flit about the page, as well as the usual flowers, blades of grass, and moth wings.*\n\n*three leaves from a birch tree are pressed between the pages.*\n\nRose Hips: Used by sailors to prevent scurvey.\nLavender: oil is potent, can be used to make tea. Found in plains.\n\nTrying to change who I am for someone I love.\n\nBrother Shadow has given my next task. I need to find a struggling sapling and nurture it back to health.\n\n\nAnd Avern said he may wish to become a dedicant as well.\n\n*this page is filled with idle sketches of butterflies, cookies, cake, apples, small flowers, and blueberries.*\n\n\n\n\nI am with child.\nI'm going to have a baby.\n\nI'm pregnant.\n\n\n\nI don't know what else to say...\n\nMalinor has new books, I will need to make copies for my own collection.\n\n\"Ancient Elves\"\n\"Cloud Temple\"\n\"History of Magic\"\n\nAnd Isabella has as my next task, making a cake and singing to the animals I collect the\n\ningredients from. There's a book here on making cakes... I think I can remember the steps well enough. I need eggs, milk, and flour, mainly. And I need to sing to the cows and chickens.\n\nI wonder if I should sing to the wheat too...\n\nI am most definitely pregnant! I beleive it has been two or three months now, and I am significantly... larger.\n\nThe worst seems to have passed, though. I can keep down my food and read without falling asleep, though the simplest tasks are rather tiring.\n\nWhich will make my continueing pursuit of dedicancy more interesting... I currently have two tasks, to make a cake for Isabella and grow a tree for the Shadow Druid. \n\nThen, of course, there's the matter of names. Avery and I\n\ndiscussed Illera and Talar. I'm not really sure what I would want to name a child...\nSome of my early ideas, from years ago, were Cerulen or Leyulen, but I'm not sure I like those anymore. Perhaps Talar'onn...\nI should probably start making clothes, too.\n\n*this page is filled with sketches and designs for tiny coats, dresses, gloves, hats, and all manner of baby-related clothing items.*\n\nEltalar, Talar'onn, Talarii, Elahern, Ahern'lente, Elleniel, Filenniel, Eltalarii, Lenniel'onn.\n\nI feel as though we're not preparing well enough. I'm not sure when the baby will come, but I feel as though we are nearing the end. We need to make clothes, and blankets, perhaps a bed, books, toys, other things... that a baby may need. I'm not even sure\n\nwhat we need. But I definitely need to begin making blankets and clothes. Perhaps some new clothes for myself, as well. This dress was loose even before I altered it, and it's already beginning to feel snug.\nI have enough free time now, I'll work on that.\n\nIt seems no matter what happens, our conversation eventually returns to this issue of living in Malinor or not. How many times has he told me that he is a wanderer with no home, and is happy wherever we are, so long as he's by my side? Many, many times.\n\nAnd how many times has he mentioned how much he hates to live here? Just as many times...\nAnd he may be right. I may just be living in an illusion of what I want Malinor to be... but this is my home. This is where I, a mali'ame, am supposed to be...\n\nAnd it is not as though I haven't tried it. I gave up so much, simply because he asked. I've given him everything, and didn't complain. At least I don't think I complained, much. Perhaps it has not been enough, and I'm selfish to keep him here...\n\nI don't want to stay on that cliff, though. My heart tightens at the thought of it. I don't know what else to do... \n\nWe can try, this, at least for a time. I tried the place he chose for a time, we can try this. If it is necessary, I'll give it up again.\n\nI just don't know how to work out this glaring difference with him... I grow weary of the subject. I just want the baby to be here, then perhaps things will change.\n\nThis journal is old, and nearly out of pages. I'll need a new book, soon...", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal V", "§b[Dove Druid] Elorna", "What have I done. How can I do this. I want him back... but is this too high a price...\n\nI cannot honestly say.\n\nThe most valuable things in my life are Avery, Lenniel, and my connection to nature. Could I choose my son over my husband, or\n\nmy husband over my son? Yet I must choose between my attunement and my love...\n\nThough I fear it is o longer a choice. The ullran, that foul monster *the writing becomes illegible* cursed me. I can feel it in my mind...\n\nPerhaps the choice is no longer mine, then. I am absolved of responsibility.\n\nYet, I chose to pursue this as far as it has gone... I have denied the reality of death at every turn.\n\nTo die is natural. It is\n\npainful, but we all suffer loss. All things must die... there is a harvest and a hunt. There is balance.\n\nI don't even listen to what I'm saying. They are good words, but not when applied to someone I love. I am a false druid. If I cannot accept death,\n\nhow can I consider myself worthy of the Aspects' blessing? Yet I cling to it. I want both. I want a necromancer to return my love to me, and I want to keep my connection to nature. I am breaking apart. Everything is breaking apart. I wish I could die so\n\nthat I would no longer have to face this.\n\nYet, I am alive. Perhaps everything will be beter when he is back. Perhaps it will be worse. Perhaps he will hate me for bringing him back... perhaps I will hate myself. But what else can I do?\n\nIf I cannot bring him back, what point is there in living... for fifty years I've lived for him. Everything I've done has been with him. My life was his. His was mine. Now half of my life is gone.\n\nI was prepared to die. I wanted to die. I was going to.\n\nI should. It would be easier. Yet I still burn for him. For the chance of bringing him back, the chance at life again. I don't want to die. I don't want him to be dead.\n\n\nBut I do not want to lose what little I have left...\n\nI am not worthy of the Aspects' gifts. I am not worthy of being counted among their followers. I have fallen so far already. There is nothing left to do but keep on falling. Even if I tried to climb back up, he would drag me down again... it is of no use.\n\nI have no other choice. I am false. But I will have my love. I will have my love, or I will die.\n\n*three blackened and withered birch leaves are pressed between the pages.*\n\nIt's been a year and a half seen Avery died. It's been a year since that necromancer, the same man who murdered him and promised to bring him back, cursed me. He says I will have him soon.\n\nI try convince myself he's just wandering\n\nlike he used to. I've gone a year without him before... I tell myself the monks found him, and brought him back, but instead of coming home he's been travelling the roads. But he'll come back, just like he always does. He'll make his way back eventually.\n\nBut then I check... and he's still there.\n\nIt's an awful sight...\n\nBut he IS coming back. Eventually. And I've come too far to give up now. I feel so cold all the time, even farther south. I've grown so pale and thin... and people keep\n\nbringing it up. It's not anyone's business anyway. And no one has suspected anything, until recently. Gavin jumped to conclusions...\n\nthough I suppose they were correct...\n\nhe tried to kill me. I think, perhaps, I'm not\n\nsure, I might have killed him instead if I had been able to. I've tried to act normal, not let anyone suspect anything. The fool has grown harsher, and he's tell others. I'm not sure what I can do, besides get to people first. I could kill him, perhaps.\n\nWhat am I saying... why would I kill him.\n\nHe's getting in the way. He wouldn't listen, wouldn't leave me alone. He doesn't understand. He won't stop me from getting what I've been suffering for this past year. I won't allow it.\n\n*the writing skips a few pages. The ones before appear dusty and old.*\n\nAh me. It has been a long time...\n\nYou've been collective dust on the Equinox Island for some time. I'm not sure if it's been years, but it\n\nfeels like it could have been a decade. \n\nI'm not even sure where to start. So much has happened...\n\n\nAvery is back. Mostly.\nI did try to stop it toward the end, but the wraith took him. After torturing me.\n\nBut now he is back. As a lich. It is not so bad, perhaps... we can still talk with each other. It is still difficult, though. But I feel as thought I have moved past it.\n\nMalinor formed a town for the Mali'ame. Then a rebellion rose up, the Conclave, and\n\ntook Malinor. Our town, Leanniel, tried to remain neutral during the war, and seperate after. We held on quite well for a while. But recently we signed an alliance with them. It was that or war.\n\n\nThis Conclave, though. A hive of mages. And\n\nduplicitous and deceitful, as you'd expect. It doesn't help when I have to work with a mage on my side, Artimec of all people.\n\nBut it is done. There's a good chance that I'll be the one having to join the Conclave's council as an Adjusticar or some\n\nsuch absurd name like that. I truly do hate all these politics by now.\n\nBut for good news, the druids are moving to Leanniel's grove. That is something to look forward to, at least.\n\nAnd Lenniel'onn...\n\nHe has been taken in by the Scourge... I can only believe that he was corrupted, which is terrible, but better than accepting that he joined them willingly and with a sound mind.\n\nI've not seen him lately either, but I plan to have  a cleric cleanse him.\n\nAnd so far that would seem to the basics of what has happened since... there was much more along the way.\n\n*several pages have been skipped over, and seem stained with dirt and dust.*\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nIt's been a while. Again, so much has happened.\n\n\nAvery is gone... I don't know where, he simply left and said he won't be coming back. He does not want his sanity to fade away, and cause me pain by remaining...\nMy throat still closes\n\nwhen I think on it, yet it has been so long since I first truly lost him. I would give anything to have him back, yet... I must continue living. It is what he wanted. I have to live.\nI suppose I'm the leader of the organized Mali'ame now. The Conclave is\n\ntruly dead now, and the remaining Mali have gathered to the high elves. We are building a district just beyond their walls.\nAnthos has fallen, as well, but the Scourge are gone.\nI went to our birch just before... we had left for the Fringe, but I didn't\n\nknow we would never be able to go back. I was going to return it to its seed and carry it with me. Yet I didn't. I realized I was clinging to things so fiercely that I was hurting them myself. That was I did to Avery.\n*a few ink spatters fill the page.*\n\nOh Aspects how I hurt him. I left that tree on its hill, healthy and happy. I suppose I'll never see it again. I suppose it is fitting, it was our tree, and now I have lost both. If it survived the flooding, it should do well, though.\n\nI did keep a seed\n\nfrom it. I have it on a necklace for now. Perhaps I will grow it into a new staff, or simply keep it close. I really have never been able to let go of anything, have I... I think I have grown, though. I left the tree.\n\nLenniel has been living on his own\n\nfor many years now. He is with Meta and Resia's daughter, Naaliya, and I don't see them very often.\nHe is a cleric now.\n\nAnd so I find this journal has been collecting dust for some time.\n\nInterestingly, I'm writing this from a jail cell of my own making, but I suppose I must get to that later.\n\nLin'ame is complete. It's rather nice now,\n\nperhaps a bit more stone than I would prefer, but we had ot make allowances for Asthil's Bronze ideas. Aside from the Acius, nothing has really come of it, which is rather annoying.\n\nI've discovered that my mother had a sister, and that through her\n\nI have some living family. I do not recall if I mentioned that already, and I am too tired to read through the past pages. Hera Acius, was the first cousin I discovered. It is strange, finding you have relatives... yet nothing has truly changed from it.\n\nI am also... I suppose - in a relationship with a new man now. We met in the grove at first, he is a craftsman and I had him make a few things for the dedicant rooms. He was pleasant to converse with. And pleasant to look at, I admit.\n\nThere are still\n\ntimes when I feel guilty for it. Avery is out there somewhere, and my heart aches for him still. Yet, he had said he wishes for me to be happy, and move on, even find someone else. And spending time with Phaedrus does make me happy.\nI have thought on it\n\nbefore, and decided then that I need to pursue at least one thing that will make me happy. I have few friends, in truth, yet many people I am responsible for. Having someone I can take comfort in... is a blessing.\n\nI suppose I should go\n\ninto what is happening currently, and why I am in a cell.\nA vile plague has taken hold of the Fringe. We've tried to keep it out of Lin'ame, and with- *the writing scratches off the page as though the pen had suddenly been jerked around.*\n It    hurts   I\n\nhave been infected by it. As I sit here I \n  find I have barely\nthe    strength to \nwrite.   Ouity    taught    me    how     to  \nheal... caught it\n   trying to help a \ndark elf.  It seems to\ncome   in fits    and \nwaves   - these symp\ntoms.\n\n*the writing smudges again*\n\nAspects  it  hurts. I've locked myself   in   the    cells to    keep from\n   infecting   others...\n\nI will rest. Try to heal   myself now...\n\nKae'haelun died of plague...\n\n\n*the page is filled with\nsmall, casual sketches of leaves, mushrooms, and dragonflies.*\n\nWell, it seems all that has passed.\n\nThere are many more things I could write on, but I feel it is time to retire this book and start on the next new journal.\n\nIt has been a long and difficult journey.\n          Elorna", ""),
        StaticBook("A Strange Letter", "§bOuity Deathsbane", "In the heart of the first home, so long ignored\n\nRests a doorway which time has decored\n\nWith vines and a waterfall,\n\nThe skeleton key reveals our true past.\n\nHave ye what it takes to join in this rite?\n\nThat ascent or descent depend on your plight,\n\nGo now, seek quickly, for ye hear the call.\n\n*A diagram of the massive mother tree\n\ndecorates the rest of the page, while the sun shines brightly over the main section, the trunk and canopy, the underside of it is shroued in shadow, and barely discernable. A few simple diagrams of a femur bone rests beneath.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal VII", "§bElorna", "Well, it seems I lost my most recent journal again. The last one left off as I was bedridden in Lin'ame. I was writing about how much I wanted a child. Well, very shortly after that I had one! A lovely girl we named Miruel Isabella. She's nearly a grown\n\nwoman by now.\n\nSince then, though, the high elves took back Haelun'or and the wood elves moved to a new town in Fiandria. There was quite a bit of warring between them, and the high elves forced the wood elves to sign a treaty declaring both\n\nPhaedrus and myself banished.\nSome time after that, the high elves murdered the king of Oren, and as you can imagine that put an end to their alliance. But Oren also vassalized the wood elves and dark elves. The terms weren't terrible, but it did include\n\ngiving up worship of anything other than the Creator, so all in all it was quite fortunate that we moved back to the Grove. I feel that the Aspects were looking out for us through all of this.\nPhaedrus had been interested in druidism for a while, then\n\ndecided to take up Thurak's offer to pursue shamanism. Now he's a farseer making journeys to the spirit world. He spends most of his time in the desert, and we have a h...\n\n*the writing trails off.\n\n*dark lines scratch across the page, the paper ripping through in some areas.*\n\n*the rest of the page is taken up with a dark but sloppy sketch of a lizard and snake stalking a moth. Small, wilting flowers fill the bottom of the page.*\n\nI\n\n*the writing devolves into more scratch marks.*\n\nPhaedrus has\n\n*the writing trails off again, and it seems 'Phaedrus' has been written a few times then harshly crossed out.*\n\n\n\n  he left me\n\nHe came to me in the grove, and began saying that he had no reason to return here. I thought he just meant to this place, that I could find somewhere else to live and still be closer to him.\nThen he said he wanted to dissolve our marriage vows.\n\nHe had changed. He wasn't good for me anymore. I had no place in his new life.\n\nHe said many things.\n\nHe said as a shaman he made sacrifices\n   \n          innocent lives\n\nHe's not who I knew.\n\nWe both said many things, I don't remember now. I said I would forgive him if he ever changed his mind and wanted to come back.\n\nHe said he wouldn't, and I shouldn't.\n\nAnd he left.\n\nI went to Dak'ir... he has a stone that will show the faces of your lost loved ones.\n\nI needed to see Avery, Avery would never have done this. He made... many mistakes but he would never have done this to me.\n\nPerhaps I never did move past losing him.\n\nOr perhaps now that this has happened I've just gone back all those years... I did love Phaedrus. Maybe at first I pursued him because I needed someone to be there with me, and I was afraid if I tried to go slowly with him I would lose any chance with\n\nhim and be alone.\n\nI didn't want to be alone. I've never wanted to be alone. I don't want to be alone now. But he's gone.\n\nThey're both gone.\n\nAnd perhaps he never\n    \n     loved me at all\n\nI talked with Lielle before Dak'ir returned to their home. She already knew... Phaedrus had been there just a little before. He bought something from Dak'ir, a necklace. They thought it was for me.\nA green pendant, a spider.\n\nHe ordered it a few days before.\n\nHe said so many things\n\nBut now I don't know if any of them are true\n\nThere's someone else\n  \n         someone else\n\nHe's changed.\n\nI did love him. Maybe I needed him more than I loved him, but I loved him. I still love him.\n\nEven after all this\n\n    no...\n\nYes, I would...\nEven after all this I would take him back.\nI'm a big enough fool, I would.\n\nHe played me for a fool...\n\n\n\n\n*the remainder of the page, and a few pages after, are left blank.*\n\nIt's been a few months...\n\nI calmed down, and I wrote to him, and we talked in the cloud temple.\n\nI don't really want to write about that.\n\nHe's changed. I don't know how I never noticed it before.\n\nAnyway...\n\nNo, I am going to write about it. He's cold and callous. For all the things I selflessly gave up for him he's turned into a selfish man too stuck in his own pride to notice anything else.\n\n*The next few pages are sparily used, occasionally occupied with sketches of cats and differing species of leaves.*\n\nI'm a terrible woman.\n\nThat must be it.\n\nI was a terrible wife. To Avery, to Phaedrus. I let both of them get into things they never should have. If I'd been more faithful in training each of them in druidism things would have turned out so differently.\n\nAvery may not have died. Phaedrus wouldn't have gotten tangled in with the orcs. As strange as it is to say, I was too supportive of him. How could I have ever thought it would be alright to let him strive to become one of those beasts? Encourage him,\n\neven. I thought I was being enlightened, open minded, loving, supportive.\n\nIt's turned out the same way for the both of them. Because of my choices or inaction or foolishness, they both became something they shouldn't have been, and tarnished the memory\n\nof who they really are. Or were. No one remembers Avery as the bard, the prince, the diploment. Just 'the lich'. A monster. And now Phaedrus has become a monster. More so than Avery had ever been.\n\nAnd I'm a terrible druid. If I hadn't been, Avery never\n\nwould have been brought back. I never would have supported Phaedrus in the things he did in Haelun'or, or the things he began to lean toward with the orcs. I never would have tolerated Kalenz for as long as I did.\n\nI've made so many homes. They were all\n\nbeautiful homes. I kept Bravepaw's in Malinor. It was always clean and befitting a High Prince. I made a little home for myself in Anthos, and was happy there. It was sweet, and I was happy living there with just myself. Then Avery moved in, we had a baby\n\nand the home changed to suit our needs. It was perfect. Then there were the chambers in the druid tree, cozy and pleasant. That was perfect too.\n\nI'm not sure where we lived after that... on Samuel, we had a little tree. It was small, but we didn't need\n\nmuch space. Then the one on the Equinox island. We didn't get much use out of that before the Scourge burned it all down...\n\nBy the time I could rebuild Lenniel had grown, moved out.. we didn't need as much space anymore, it was just us.\n\nThen Avery... and it was just me. In a tiny little burrow under a rosebush. Though the whole island came to by home.\nIt was always cold there... I don't like the cold. And those memories will always be tainted.\nThen the grotto in Leanniel. I made a little\n\npassage through the mountain so Avery could come in without being seen.\n\nI made the home in the Fringe grove large... I suppose I was expecting more than I should have. I thought we could find a way to restore Avery. That Lenniel might come back. It was\n\nusually only me, though. All by myself again.\n\nAnd then Phaedrus. I made three homes for us. One for the two of us, the second for the three of us. And finally this last one. It has a room for Miruel, but she's grown and gone just like Lenniel.\n\nI made them all to be perfect for my family. For the perfect vision of what my family should be. But they fell flat. I'm alone again, rattling around in a house two people too large. If I had been a good wife, a good mother, I wouldn't be alone.\n\nI suppose I'm being melodramatic. But these are the things I feel when I look around. See empty rooms, empty beds. It pulls at me. I don't usually say it, or even think it, but it's there.\n\nA new opportunity has come about... \n\nThudrin has offered me shapeshifting. He said I'm a worthy druid of the gift.\n\nI don't know if I am, but I will take it as a sign from the Aspects that I am forgiven, and being given a second chance.\n\nHe asked me to keep a journal of the trials, and I'll be starting a new one for that, because apparently others will be reading it. No need for anyone else to read my dramatics...\n\nI'll finish up some things about today before starting all of that.\n\nLast night I helped Alirya decorate the Cerulin ballroom, and had a long and strange conversation with an orc during that. He mentioned Phaedrus, and another druid woman.\nAnyway, after that Artimec and his significant other Ash'ya asked me to marry the\n\ntwo of them. When I asked when, they said that day. So we went to the grove and had a wedding in front of the the attunement pool. It was actually very nice. \nThe festival was today, and both Phaedrus and Siri were there. That was... uncomfortable. I\n\ntalked to Siri for a while after though. I'm not really sure what that accomplished.\n\nSo, yes...\n\nI think it is time to retire this journal.\n\n\nMay the next one recount events that are a bit more pleasant.\n\n*a few dozen pages are left blank. The last page of the book contains a sketch of a fox curled up in sleep, with a dove flying above it.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Items and Aspect", "§bDwyn Tinuvial", "Items that represent the aspects\n\nCerridwen- Pomegranate. Specifically the tree- Pomegranates grow from the tree and then once they die they grow more of eachother. The shell of the pomegranate keeps the seeds safe\n\nCerrunos- A bow, the hunters weapon. This was an easy pick as he's the father of the hunt- but it goes deeper than that. While hunting is a sport for many people it must be done respectfully. With skill a bow will kill much quicker than a blade or snare.", ""),
        StaticBook("Discovery", "§bR.H. Robertson", "It Was All For Naught\n\nWritten by Illumin Fox\n\n\"It was truly all for naught as I looked into my close lliran's eyes, and I knew what he intended to do. I warned him, I tried to tell him the creature was\n\n too strong. It cut off here for quite a bit, the runes scratched out. - Ralen\n\n\"It was alas, the power of the sorc that struck him up with green eyes illuminate.\"\n\nMore confusion.\nRalen Haled Robertson", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Journal", "§bDwyn Tinuvial", "Average Prices\n\nVendor Product Price\n___________________\nArveldir-Iron-10~12uArveldir-Coal-25s\nOther Shops\nIron- 18 to 30 mina\nCoal - crate ~ 70m\nHaybales 50 per cart\n-The note on Arveldir's prices is crossed out-\n\nNaeri Maltac\n170 Mina\nWants 2 stacks of Coal\n1 of Iron\nHaybales to cover the extra expenses\n\n170 would cover the Coal, and some iron.\nCoal 140\n30m would buy 2 iron at 15m lowered price.\n930 - 19 carts hay\n\nTo do:\nOrganize Chests\nContact all Gatherers and Crafters\nSold 2 Cows for 300m\n\nOn hold, War.\n\nFind out housing cost for new settlement\nNote: Free\n\nCows in good condition. Thank Xyra for those.\nSold two of them for 300m. Will advertise selling more, perhaps. Get a butcher going, or do it myself.\n\n6 Bookshelves to finish bottom floor\n52 per floor\nx2 + 6\n100\n4\n104\n110\nHow much paper?\n3paper 1book\n3book 1shelf\n330book=110shelf\n990paper 15.5bundle\n\nFlowers - Orchid Bluet and sunflower?\ncandles\nfood - sweets, cookies+cake? peirogi\nneed to find a place\n\nAndria: Orange Eyed Highelf and a Darkelf caused trouble. Darkelf had brownish skin, red eyes, had to be killed\n\nInform people of blue-tattooed nearly naked man in golden mask- Mental mage. Harrassed Briar with images from his past.\n\nBriar has a golden apple. Talked him out of using it.\nHe gave me his word\nThat won't matter if\nhis memory vanishes.\n\nGet a Auctioneer and Banker in town\n\nAethos Tyberian - Insane.  Remove from town?\nMassive fucking cave home burrow thing\nEvicted. He can sign up and wait in the waiting list like everyone else.\n\nLittle doodles of flowers and a young Mali'ame are on this page- Aswell as some scribbles done by a much younger hand. What looks like juice is spilled on the page, staining it a light pink.\n\nKatona's misconduct:\n\nBullcrap training reason.\n\nBullcrap reason to not critique training.\n\nKha guard bullcrap.\n\nPunched me (Quav)\n\nFind: \nLibrarian\nBlacksmith\nRancher\n\nAllynial attacked someone she belived to be Savet, trying to follow Art's orders to kill him.\nShe found and him and he admitted he was Savet, but as she tried to strike said it was a 'Illusionary Form'\nAllynial describes this as him not physically being\n\nthere. Her strike went right through him as if air.\n\nWhen I questioned him he said he was named Psohdon and was there 'waiting for a friend' and motioned to Eliza's home.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Final Note", "§bR.H. Robertson", "Translation:\n\nMany of the swords that appear to be shattered were found above, as if a grand battle occured. I found them clasped in skeletal hands, but the remains were gone.\n\nIt is worse than I feared, there really is a necromancer of some sort here... I saw a figure the other day, his eyes glowing green as the skeletal hands clawed at the earth, seeming to be digging something...\n\nI fear my days are numbered, but hopefully my works won't go unnoticed. \nI am glad to have served the King through this research.\n\nSigned, Ralen Haled Robertson, archaeologist.\n\nThe writing ended there, you notice. But blood lies on the pages, as a single word is left on this final page. [!]\n\nHis works will be kept in my personal study, Reginald. For now, keep them where you found them and I will pick them up when I have\n\nspare time. Sincerely, \n\nVulenas Navaris", ""),
        StaticBook("Translation", "§bR.H. Robertson", "\"A beauty to behold,\nthe world trembled with envy, finding naught but inhuman frenzy.\n\nBorn blood of lust,\nfoe of the truth to be discerned, it was only he who yearned still once he had been spurned. \n\nTranslation Notes:\n\nIt is surprising what I have found down here, it surpasses my greatest expectations for such a small ruin.\n\nElven in appearance, many words of the Ancient Dialect are upon these walls and in the graves, including odd runic symbols.\n\nIt has been very enjoyable to continue to engage in these studies, but a looming question still haunts me.\n\nMany of the corpses are missing from the tombs, but this place cannot be over two to three hundred years old.\n\nA skeleton I like to refer as the 'Big Bastard' disappeared two moons ago, I looked outside and I could see it walking away... a haunting, pulsating green light radiating from the sockets of its skull.\n\nThe name issue however is that Necromancy is not only a taboo art, it is impossible to commit to.\n\nThere can't have been necromancers here, it's illogical.\n\nThis is dangerous, it might be best to leave soon.\n\nR.H. Robertson", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid History I", "§bBriar Ophiuchus", "Druidic Studies:\n       History\n\n         AEGIS\nThe Age Of Founding And The Before Times: During this time, Druids were brought together and the Druidic Order was founded by Wayward Druid\n\nRespiren Knox. The records of this time may never be fully deciphered, however. Although we know of some of the first Druids in Malinor, such as Respiren, Swifthide, and Native, very few details are known. Perhaps someday the past\n\nregarding these times will be revealed.\nThe First Age Of Reconstruction: The First Age of Reconstruction was ushered in by the initiation of Dragon Druid Apollan into the order. Apollan was the first to express interest\n\nin joining the order after reading the Myth of the Great War and spent long hours in the Druid Grotto after he was famously murdered outside the gates of Laurelin by a bandit. Apollan quickly moved up the ranks. Meanwhile, the\n\norder grew. After initiating Apollan, Respiren expressed interest in 'rebuilding the order.' Every day, new citizens of Aegis would show up in the grove, wanting to become Druids. Most were immediately initiated. As the order grew,\n\nso did a number of things including property and knowledge. During this time the order gained a lodge in Ravenhold, as well as one in the Laurelin docks. Additionally, two stalls were bought in the Laurelin marketplace and\n\nhundreds of books were added to the order's library.\nThe Age Of Abandonment: Unfortunately, due to extremely casual and non-uniform initiation rites of the Wayward Druid, people were joining the circle, only to wander into the\n\nwilderness never to be seen again. With no established hierarchy, the Order lacked organization and purpose. This was made apparent when an Elf named Rowan arrived. Archdruid Rowan arrived from a far off forest, seeking to\n\nreestablish his lost circle, \"The Druids of Mother Aegis.\" Rowan is most likely the only citizen to have argued with the Order's ways. His only backing for the title of Druid was that he 'had a love of nature.' Rowan became annoyed by the\n\nfact that he had to be initiated in order to be allowed into the inner library. He stormed off, claiming that he would start his own order somewhere else. Rowan was last seen entering the wilds outside his home in the Ravenlodge, and\n\nwas never heard from or seen from again. Fortunately, the dark Age of Abandonment was brought to an end by the light of Dawn Druid Maiavel.\nThe Age Of Reformation: The Age of Reformation was brought on by the ideas and\n\ndrive of one Maiavel. With her determination, she was able to rally the remaining Druids to create official lore, hierarchy, and a sense of order.\nThe Second Age of Reconstruction: During the Second Age of\n\nReconstruction, many more books were written, and a Grand Tree was planted in the Laurelin Grove. New Dedicants were brought in, but less frequently than in the first age, and the initiation process was more careful and\n\nuniform. During this age, the current hierarchy was established, with Apollan as Archdruid.\nThe Age Of Knowledge: The Age of Knowledge was ushered in by Petyr, the Salmon Druid. His creation of the Dedicant's\n\nVows and the Attunement Ceremony greatly helped the order, as well as his Order ideas.\nThe Age Of Mushroom Transgressions: This age was brought about by the conflict caused by differing ideals\n\nwithin the Order. Some Druids were increasingly annoyed at the restriction that came with having a Grove in a city (where trees and mushrooms could or could not be planted and the structure of the Druid Tree). Other\n\nDruids argued that it was their duty to promote balance, and that the runaway growth of mushrooms flowing from the Grove was nowhere near natural. Some Druids wanted a new Grove to be created faraway outside the city.\n\nOthers wanted the Grove to be close. Still others did not want a new grove at all. But, it is important to note that most of these arguments were caused by misunderstandings, which is why this age is sometimes called the Age of\n\nMisunderstanding or the Age of Confusion.\nThe Age Of Renovation: In the end, most mushrooms were removed from the Grove when Maiavel stamped her foot and the mushrooms instantly broke (but were\n\nthoughtlessly left on the ground, only to be swept up by Deltaro). A new, secret Grove was set up in the wilderness outside Ravenhold, (notable work from Mahten and Aeaira, who spent days working on the road to civilization). The\n\nLaurelin Grove continued to be renovated and improved on, with notable work contributed by Lunar Druid Bircalin and Dedicant Deltaro.\n\nAEGIS POST-DREAM\nThe First Age of Dreaming: For a log time, it seemed that Nature was silent. For a length of time, none had seen any feats spoken about in the ancient Druid tales. But then, as if a seed was planted, Nature began to speak,\n\nand each Druid began to dream mysterious dreams. It was the Aspects of Nature, Cerridwen and Cernunnos, calling to their newly found children. Wayward Druid Respiren called a Moot to discuss these dreams,\n\nleading into the next age.\nThe Age Of The Aspects: The Moot decided to embrace these Aspects as their primary deities.\nThe Age Of Little Occurence: Nothing happened for a while, except a few little things. There\n\nwas a small Hierarchy change; the Archdruid position was given to three people, and the Grand Druid's description was changed. John and Maiavel were promoted to Archdruids, but Maiavel soon retired. Her spot\n\nwas filled by Petyr. Cleric Druid Mahten was also promoted to the rank of Guide. A simple, new recruiting strategy was initiated.\nThe Second Age Of Renovations: During this age, the Laurelin Grove experianced a number of\n\nadditions. A wall was created around the Grove, with a retractable gate. This was done to keep out a number of citizens that were harassing the Druids. In addition, all entrances were  covered up, so that one must always use the\n\nfront gate. More additions to the Grove were a kitchen, a melon and pumpkin farm, the cultivation of the Grand Tree's roots deeper into the ground, a tree farm, an elevator system, and Druid dwellings at the top of the Grand Tree.\n\nThe Age Of Poor Judgement: A lot of inner-Order bad feelings culminated in this age. Multiple parties were involved, and no side was completely right. The end result was the leaving of Seeker Druid Deltaro from the Order. The bad\n\ntaste left in the mouths of many  Druids lead Apollan to create the Druid Code.\nThe Second Age Of Little Occurance: During this age, as its name would imply, not many things happened. The Grove was given another\n\nrenovation, mostly for aesthetic purposes. (In addition, a Druid Order Forum account was created, as well as a blog.) Unfortunately, during this time, Archdruid John's mental health was also starting to\n\nslide.\nThe Second Age Of Dreaming: During this age, Salmon Druid Petyr had a vision in which the creation myth was shown to him by the Aspects. It fortold of a time before the four races, and of a great exodus to come. A second\n\nMoot was called and all in attendance agreed to accept the vision as truth. The Age Of Mourning: Unfortunately, during this time, Archdruid John's mental state grew worse. One day, John snapped. Among a number of\n\nthings, he attacked the Dusk Druid. He then fled to his soul tree (which he named Marcus), located by the pond in the Laurelin Grove. There, he made his last stand. The Druids present at the time were Dusk, Mahten, Apollan, Respiren,\n\nSaviticus, and Thork the Betrayer (Thork the Blood Druid). In addition, several princes and bystanders were there. John stood on the roots of his soul tree and attacked anyone who came near. There was a standoff for some\n\ntime, until all at once the Druids charged the tree. While some traded blows with John, Apollan worked to purify the water around the tree for he sensed that there was a taint at work. Suddenly the Dusk Druid produced an axe\n\nand chopped at the soul tree until only one column was left. It was then, with the ability to see inside the tree, that Apollan discovered the taint in the form of a block of netherrack. Before Apollan could share his discovery,\n\nThork went into a blood lust. He cut down the last column of the tree, rendering John unconscious. Then Thork stabbed John's body, killing him. In the days that followed, Thork was shunned for violating the Druid Code. John's tree\n\nwas turned into the place of his burial, where his body was burned and his ashes scattered around Laurelin. His will named Mahten as his replacement as Archdruid.\nThe Age Of Expansion: During this age, the\n\nNature's Bounty chain was by one new store on the King's Road. The Order was also expanded by one new member. Zannith, the 10 year old son of the Dusk Druid and an unknown Elf moved into the Grove. Much to the dismay\n\nof one Bircalin. Zannith later left the Druid Grove to join the Wardens, and later committed suicide by jumping from the Grand Tree.\nThe Age Of Knowledge: During this age, the Druids took control of the library of the\n\nCloud Temple of Aegis. Petyr also retired from his position as Archdruid and became a Hierophant. Dusk Druid Aeaira was elected to fill the spot and Saviticus became Head Teacher.\nThe Second Age Of\n\nMourning: During this age, Archdruid Mahten transformed his entire being into a tree in the Grove. As a result of his sacrifice, Druid Dusk was named (in his will) as successor to the position of Archdruid. In this time, she had\n\nbegun to bring new life to the Druid Tree; ushering forth the growth and spread of new branches, and bringing in a new generation of Dedicants.\nThe Second Age Of Expansion: During this age, the Druid Order and Grand\n\nTree both grew exponentially.\nThe Third Age Of Mourning: During this age, Archdruids Apollan and Dusk were both killed under mysterious circumstances. Apollan's position was given to his close friend,\n\nHorizon Druid Makia, and Dusk's position was given to Fox Druid Valas.\nThe Age Of Poor Logic: During this age, everything the Druids knew was proven to be incorrect. Petyr proved that wood doesn't exist, and then proved that\n\nit does. He also proved that magic isn't real and water is fake. Unable to hold all this nonsense, Archdruid Darrin was convinced that he had gone crazy and was only dreaming. After jumping to his death from the top\n\nof the Grand Tree, Fey Druid Vanyariel took his position as Archdruid.\nThe Age Of Activism: During this age, many Druids had visions fortelling a coming distruction of all of Aegis. The Druids took it upon themselves to find and recover all\n\nancient artifacts of Aegis so that they might be saved from the end and brought with them to a new land. With the help of High Princess Indelwehn, the Druids were lead to the Druid Tree at the docks. There, she showed them the Shadow\n\nCircle, an underground compound created beneath the tree by Apollan and Respiren, to house the First Staff, Seed, and Sapling. \n\n\n\n[END VOLUME ONE]", ""),
        StaticBook("Ever Higher", "§bSalamandra", "Ever Higher\n\nBefore the boy could remember, he was climbing. He had been born in the great forests of Old Laurelin, his mother and father both slain at the hands of the Undead. Every day activities had never fascinated the boy, nor had speaking to the\n\nother children, few as there were. Long he would reflect on his parents and what little time he had with them, and how he longed for his mother's embrace. He would sit atop the tallest tree he could climb, and look ever higher towards his goal; a lone, -\n\ngigantic tree stood tall above all the rest. When mortals die, their souls rise, or so he had been taught. Perhaps if he could climb the tallest tree, he could speak to his parents again. The boy continued climbing for many years, until the branches\n\nwould heed themselves to his footsteps: his body moved arhythm with the trees for where his foot went, a branch was, and where his arms stretched, a helping hand would reach out to support him. The boy became like the wind: rising and ducking below every\n\nbranch, rising higher and higher until he reached his destination, and in a sense the boy knew he could fly. \n\nThe boy challenged the tree, and scaled its trunk 'till the branches finally beckoned. He flipped and flittered amongst its branches, dancing\n\nhis way to the top until he was there, above the world. He looked down upon all things below, and then raised his head and looked higher, and knew he was not high enough. His spirit could not rise high enough to meet his parents.\n\nAnd then the boy fell, his frame plummeting to the ground, carried on the wind itself, until the boy's spirit rose ever higher.", ""),
        StaticBook("~*The Beast*~", "§bEdwarf Ember", "It was one horrific creature. But we made it and we locked it into the prison.\n\nIt was such a long journey, the floating islands.\n\nIt will never escape the prison we made.\n\nIf that happens...\nWe need to kill it this time, it's weak from it. \n\nIt hates the fire more than itself.\n\n\n*~Edwarf Ember~*", ""),
        StaticBook("Order.", "§bPierré Ceux les Sombres", "I, Pierré Ceux les Sombres, would like to order a slender staff.\n\nI 'ave no idea what it would cost. I'll stay in town for a while and probaly have enough minas!", ""),
        StaticBook("Aspect Poems", "§bDwyn Tinuvial", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\n\n      Dwyn Tinuvial\n  \n\n    Dedicancy Poetry\n\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Nestled in the ground it waits, drinking in the light from the sky and nursing from soil. The branches far above sway, keeping the harsh winds away. \nThe roots of the grass and flowers cradle the child\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-and shield it from hoof and boot.  \nShe holds it close with her far-reaching touch, tending to all of her children as they grow and blossom. \nIt grows well-loved, stretching its arms towards the skies and \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-twisting its fingers to scatter its harvest as its own blessing for others to flourish.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-He stood on four hooves in the morning.\nWatching over his family, he gazes from the top of his hill as they frolic, the  children running through the grass and the mothers watching quietly. \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-With a snap and a growl, everyone scatters.\nHe ran on four paws in the afternoon.\nDragging the elk along with him, he makes a small growl of effort as he pulls the days hunt home. \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Crying out in excitement his children rush out to greet him, almost trampling each other as they leap onto  him, questioning what’s to eat until the woods go silent.\nHe walked on two feet in the evening.\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Fur rippling as he strides indoors, closing the door behind him. His children look up, shivering close to the waning fire and sagging in relief as the soft warmth is wrapped around their\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-shoulders, the man holding them within the furs.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-", ""),
        StaticBook("Syviis' Journal", "§bSyviis Galaos", "((If you are reading this, you have stumbled across Syviis' journal, please refer to PMing Nightmare260 for a link to the actual journal, as I cannot write all I want too in these menacing books.  Thank you!))", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Deity Magic§0\n§0-------------------Deity-based magics borrow the power of higher beings to perform a set list of spells, as defined within each deity subtype.\n\nThe amount of people who can learn it is more restricted than other forms of magic because the deities will only acknowledge an individual’s desire for magic under certain circumstances.\n\nDeities can be very sensitive about whom they bestow powers onto, and this can limit the other types of magic that one may pursue in tandem.\n\nIndividual spells must also be taught, either by the deity directly or through a more experienced Follower.\n\nOnly some types actually use mana, like Arcane Magic, but all are bound by the same restriction of only having a limited ability to call upon that specific deity before becoming too exhausted to continue.\n\nDeity Magic Types§0\n§0-------------------Shamanism [Typically an Orc Magic]:§0\n§0Druid§0\n§0Cleric§0\n§0Frost Witch [All the magic used by a frost witch]§0\n§0Muun'Trivazja [Kharajyr magic from healing to rituals, moongazing and chronomancy]\n\nShamanism [Typically an Orc Magic]:§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Witchdoctor [Stranger and oddity rituals and experimenting. Delve in potion making and other]\n\n\n§0\n§0Farseer [Work with the Immortal Spirits, can travel to the spiritual plane and converse with spirits on a neutral field.]\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0Elementalist [Work with the elemental spirits, masters of changing and shaping the physical world.]\n\n\n§0\n§0Lutauman [Avatars of the ancestors. Converse with the spirits of people themselves and invoke their power and blessing.]", ""),
        StaticBook("X P", "§bSarrion Zytiaear", "X P\n   The Experienced", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[Connor has apparently been searching through the logs each time 'Kalenz has been mentioned. Typing in this book leaves absolutely no logs on the server.]§0\n§0\n§0I trust in your intelligence, your majesty. I am certain you can already deduce the\n\nnature of this visit.§0\n§0\n§0I overheard your exchange with Avern. I do not wish to be pessimistic but I doubt the rate of success your operation yields at this moment. Avern is an imbecile. She fled from the dungeon out of fear instead\n\nof assessing the situation and considering the long-term consequence of her actions. Namely the issuing of marshal law within the Silver City. Whilst I doubt I am in the right to plead for such but I would like to request my name to be purged\n\nas aassociate who conspired against Sohaer Osino. I am still a paladin of Xan and still retain my attunement to the deity. If I truly was an aid in the conspiracy my tether would have been terminated. I would be laid to rot in a trench in the frozen North\n\n. Slain my by fellow compatriots. §0\n§0\n§0I believe I may offer a safer alternative in the operation to locate and restrain Kalenz Uradir but I would require your assistance personally. The Mali'ker are the key and you are the sole custodian of their kin.\n\nKalenz is a snake. We are both aware of his powess in terms of manipulating a state. In his situation his power is limited. Looking to the past he turned to his distant brethren in times of aid. 'Uniting' them when in all reality he merely recruited them\n\nto his  side and outfitted them with a snug blindfold. Seeing as how the Mali'ker are vassels of your empire you do hold a secure connection to their inner council, do you not?§0\n§0\n§0>>I do. What do you propose, then?\n\nSpeak with the Mali'ker council. Assess the level of trust you capable of holding to the Dark Elven kin. Inquire who held positive relations with Kalenz. Through that request they aid in this operation to apprehend Kalenz.\n\nHave them state that they wish to join Kalenz and seek assistance in detaching from the Orenian state. Assuming as goes well I will have a sect of individuals I trust aid in the capture of this traitorous Mali'aheral. Of course you will be pirvy to these\n\ncompanions of mine and be spear-heading this operation.§0\n§0\n§0>>Your name shall be cleared amongst what channels it was pinned as being wanted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Creme in the streets, Memes in the sheets.§0\n§0\n§0I am Han, with no family, lonely but glad, grateful for his comrades. The sewer rats move swiftly among Vailor, hunt and pillaging all the stands within there way.§0\n§0\n§0-Day 1, 19th of the Amber Cold", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Lich created - §0\n§016th of the Sun's Smile 1544. Selrik is now a Transcendant.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "§bGregory Donovan", "The house is merely the start, \n\nThe debt has yet to be paid, \n\nThe future would seem quite dim,\n\nFor the Donovons you promised and failed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Cheesy Love!", "§bElayne", "You hold my hand, I caress your lips,\nYou look into my eyes and my heart beat skips.\nI stroke your cheek so soft and smooth,\nI admire your face, every line, every groove.\nWe move in a little closer, our bodies entwine.\n\nYou touch my neck, it sends shivers down my spine.\nYou whisper that you love me and I know it's true, because I feel it in my heart and I love you too.\n\n\n\n\n-=Lain=-", ""),
        StaticBook("Pick Up Line", "§bElayne", "I wake up to your warmth of breath,\n\nRealising you're with me.\n\nI feel your arms tighten around,\n\nAnd draw a smile onto me.\n\nI turn around to face your front,\n\nFeeling blessed a millionth time.\n\nI stare at your sleeping self,\n\nAs I murmur a thankful pray.\n\nWhen I needed, you were there,\n\nTo help me up and walk me through.\n\nI held on tight to your hands,\n\nAs you pull me closer to you.\n\nI found something that I had lost,\n\nA love so pure and so serene.\n\nI kiss your brow slow and soft,\n\nIn my arms I hold you close.\n\nTears would form when you're close,\n\nA clear smile to change the means.\n\nI see your eyes open up,\n\nAnd gaze into mine.\n\nI feel your hands brush my cheeks,\n\nAnd pull me closer under the sheets.\n\nWe both grin at a sync,\n\nToss this poem and let's pass time.\n\n-=Lain=- <3 <3 <3", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Last Will", "§bRobert Ellstrom", "I, Robert Ellstrom, born 1st of The Grand Harvest in the year 1526, and my wife Aayat Ellstrom, born 23rd of Winter's Cold in the year 1518 hereby declare that this is our shared last will and testament regarding whatever is left to the small nobility of-\n\n-House Ellstrom, be it property or wealth.§0\n§0\n§0We hereby revoke, annul and cancel all wills and codicils previously made by me or my wife, either jointly or severally. We declare that we suffer no kinds of mental illnesses during the writing of this-\n\n-will, and that we are sound of mind. This last will expresses our wishes without undue influence or duress.§0\n§0\n§0I, Robert Ellstrom, am married to Aayat Ellstrom hereafter reffered to as my spouce, whom will live and die beside me-\n\n-as is her choice. I father our only child, Robinet, born 15th of Winter's Cold in the year 1541, whom will not adopt the family name. We hereby revoke all claims our son would have of Ellstrom, be it property, wealth, lands or even the name itself, for-\n\n-we had thought long and hard on this matter, and decided it would be better for him to experience the hardships and punishes of life, and allow him to shape himself into a man, without the shortcuts that would have eased his life.\n\nWe bequeath all of Ellstrom's properties, lands and wealth to the local Bishop, in which after receiving this letter, it would have been done.§0\n§0\n§0We hope that a man of faith receiving this by Robinet himself would accept our son as an Altar servant, in-\n\n-hopes of him better understanding our faith far deeper than our own, and aspire to become a holy knight in the name of the Creator and the religion. Otherwise may he know of our disappointment, yet encouragement he become what he wishes.\n\nTo our local church, we direct that on our deaths, our remains are to be cremated, and our ashes carried by the wind until nothing is left, yet becoming one with our land. May our names be forever forgotten, and Ellstrom removed from history, so that our-\n\n-son would make a name of himself, achieve for himself and his children.§0\n§0\n§0Signed,§0\n§0-Robert Ellstrom.§0\n§0-Aayat Ellstrom.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mother", "§bDak'ir Des'Nox", "Delilah De'laronge§0\n§0       The Mother§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Dark Elven Ancestors§0\n§0       Volume 1.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0By Dak'ir Des'Nox\n\nDelilah, or Della as those who knew her referred to her as, was a kind hearted mali'ker with a heart as big as her belly. She was no warrior, nor was she a doer of great deeds.§0\n§0\n§0Della was a champion of another kind. One of the home. Kind words were her\n\nweapons and a warm meal her shield. Born in Asulon, she and her family traveled from city to city for work. All the while, Della honed her cooking skills through out the years. §0\n§0\n§0In Anthos, the Mother encountered one of the few things you'd hear her say\n\nshe detested, The Black Scourge. Della cared for all and seeing the Scourge ruin village after village, city after city. It racked her heart with grief. So it was not uncommon for her to grab her frying pan and fly into action if she suspected someone of\n\nbeing associated with the dark order. §0\n§0\n§0But it was in the cold lands of Thales that she came to settle with kin. The short and rather round woman found herself at the gates of Ker'lomi. Within days she had settled into the tavern and made our\n\ncold cavern into a warm home, full of laughs and small comforts. Sweets to hearty stews, or even a knitted scarf. §0\n§0\n§0Della remained with our kin for a long time, until the elven civil war of Athera. Not long after those events she departed the land and\n\nhas not been since. But she remains in the hearts of those who knew her.\n\nThough her fate was never known, we honour Delilah as 'The Mother' for her deeds of love and kindness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Lazarus", "§bPatriarch Laos Salondil", "Dear Lazarus of Clan DeNurem.§0\n§0\n§0It has come to my attention we have no personal alliance with each other, and continue to squabble over needless arguements, many instigated by your\n\n'Grimwald' and a few of my followers. I seek and jest we put the meaningless squabble behind us. Let our gladiators fight, rather than ourselves.§0\n§0\n§0I hope you come to sense rather than to irrational thought.§0\n§0\n§0Sincerly, Laos Salondil", ""),
        StaticBook("Orgon Shrine", "§bWargoth Malog'Yar", "Orgon Shrine\n\nMound: Pile earth a few feet high, with mycellium to grow on it.\n\nTotem: Made of materials of the nature of Orgon, such as mossey stone, soulsand, stone, cracked stone brick, dark wood.\n\nA paper containing a drawing of the shrine is glued here.\n\nNote: Offering of rotten flesh, pigs, and bats are appropriate for Orgon.\n\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/OrgonShrine", ""),
        StaticBook("Love", "§bLielle Des'nox", "Though the parting was far too soon,\nNothing can change the love held.\nOne glance at him shows everything.\nThey were made perfectly to be together. \n\nLove that burned as passionately as the sun,\nSo strong that I only\n\nhad to hear\nThe way he spoke of her to understand\nJust how deep his love for her ran.\n\nA parting that was far too soon,\nBut a love that will carry on even in death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sweet Memories", "§bLielle", "Though it hasn't been long at all\nIt seems like it's been an eternity\nTogether, we'll make sweet memories\n\nAnd what sweet memories they will be\nEven if we proceed with uncertainty\nThrough the good and even the bad\nThere is so much\n\nhappiness to be had\n\nMay the Ancestors guide and through and through\nTo you, I will always be true", ""),
        StaticBook("Looking Stone", "§bDak'ir Des'Nox", "The Looking Stone of       The Ancestors\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAn artifact summary by Dak'ir Des'Nox\n\n   Found within the mali'ker ruins in the far north, the Looking Stone is a palm sized and rather mundane looking smoothed rock. When held, the stone gives off a faint cyan glow.\n\n   Should the holder gaze into the stone, they would see the\n\nfaces of loved ones lost. Upon further examination, the faces would be seen mouthing the name of it's holder. Their ghostly images would also be seen smiling, seemingly at peace. \n\n   The figures that appear in the stone seem to always be\n\nfamily but on occasion, those who were incredibly close to the holder, regardless of blood, can be seen as well if their bonds were strong in life.\n\n   What give this stone it's unnatural ability is still unknown. But as of now, the mali'ker believe it is\n\nconnected to their fabled 'Pools of Remembrance Lost' judging by the it's cyan glow.\n\nFurther documentation will be recorded when more information is discovered.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oussana", "§bSeraphine Drake-Flormai", "The Dark Elves have been born an enigma, since their very first steps into this realm. They’re various and varied in both body and mindset. In them is the potential of the most tenacious warrior or wisest of seers.\n\nTheir eyes can be of crimson fire, or sapphire water. Among these dark skinned sons and daughters of Malin are the Oussanas.\n\nThe Oussana family describe the birth of the dark elves as part of the first insurrection against Iblees. Their tale of their origin provides an in-depth insight into their beliefs and mannerism, even though the tale is left as simply a myth or\n\nstory among themselves  During this first war between benevolence and a absolute evil, Malin needed children who would have more will and might than his first group of children, the wood elves, in order to decimate the servants of iblees.\n\nHe needed children who can handle the atrocities of war and the evils Iblees could deal. To create this chidl, he reached up into the night sky and took parts of the darkness itself, leaving stars and celestial bodies in place of the darkness he took.\n\nHe then reached into the ground and took a strong, sturdy root from a tree. He then cut the palm of his hand, allowing blood to pool in the center. When he combined himself, nature, and darkness he created the first Dark Elf, a creature born for conflict.\n\nAfter the war, the Dark Elves began to look for where they would dwell. Some sought refuge with their wood elven brothers in what would be malinor while others looked to the roots of trees for their home, far from other elves.\n\nAmong the ones who sought their own destiny aside from their brothers were the Oussanas.\n\nAppearance\n\nAt the adulthood of an Oussana their eyes are typically solid black; however, at birth their eyes are a lighter blue-red color. As they age, the dual blue-red eye color begins to darken until their body fully matures at twenty.\n\nlthough in youth it usually starts off as the dual color, it's possible to see a set of red or blue eyes to begin with At twenty years old, their eyes stop darkening and remain black while the whites of their eyes turn into a light grey color.\n\nHowever, the eye color can take more than twenty years to darken, although it is rare. The typical skin color of an Oussana is a Darker Grey, a shale color. However, if they diverge from the typical, they tend to be paler than more charcoal.\n\nTheir hair is always of long, straight, and white\n\nCustoms\n \nGender Roles\n\nAmong the Oussanas there is no such thing as a gender role. The females are taught the exact same things as any male in the family. A child, if raised by an Oussana, will experience\n\nno gender socialisation that distinguishes male and female. They are both expected to meet the same expectations throughout their life and will not held back because of gender.\n\nClothing\n\nTo express strength, family members will wear less clothing. Like most elves, they do not see a lack of clothing being extremely strange or scandelous. This is only to express physical dominance and prowess.\n\nA family member will believe that both clothing and armor are for individuals who are hiding a particular weakness.  However, they’re not running around in underwear either. They will wear what an environment requires them to wear.\n\nYet when an Oussana shows skin, it’s not meant to be a means of attracting others, it’s how they express their strength.\n\nTattoos\n \nOften times, accomplishments and achievements throughout a family member’s life are marked on their skin in the form of a tattoo. Before in Aegis, this tradition was required,\n\nyet since the disunion of the Oussana it’s a more of a choice, although strongly suggested. To represent these events, a symbol should be designed by  the one desiring the tattoo that would provide insight to the event. If a tattoo is\n\ngiven yet it carries no meaning, it’s often celtic in design. At the age of ten, an Oussana is required to get a tattoo on their skin. It’s often given given by one of the parents. The child however, chooses who gives them the tattoo and where the\n\ntattoo will go. Consciousness at the time of the marking is not required, given that it’s fairly painful.  This tattoo is of the family seal which is a  triquetra(celtic knot) with a moon in the center. One way an Oussana shows true devotion\n\nto a lover is marking themselves with a tattoo. This is only for an individual that has been decided to spend the rest of their near-immortal elfen life with. If there is any doubt, an Oussana raised by their traditions\n\nwill not mark themselves to the other. Symbols engraved onto their body can only be the truth, they will not willingly write a lie on their chest.\n\nValues\n \nDominance and strength:\n\nOussana both male and female are raised to believe they were created to be the strongest . They do not fear flaunting their strength and if given\n\nthe chance they will go to extreme lengths to show dominace. At a very young age, children are taught to fight, usually with swords, to achieve this strength. They are raised to believe the only way to be successful in life is to be feared.\n\nA good example of this would be how animals act when asserting dominance. If challenged they try to prove themselves better. Nearly at all times they would be flaunting their strength, which is the reason for them often having less\n\nlothing when compared to your average elf. Since they enforce strength so adamantly, the exact opposite, weakness, is despised. Oussana were raised to surround themselves around strong individuals and cast away the weak. In the past,\n\nthose that were weak among the family were cast out to malinor to live among the weaker elves. An Oussana will go to any  lengths to not appear weak.\n\nBeauty:\n\nThe idea of perfection is engraved into every child’s mind; however, it’s not just the perfection of physical strength that is sought after. Beauty and maintaining beauty is almost as highly pressed as ones ability in combat.\n\nTechniques and secrets in beautifying both the male and female body is passed down, generation by generation. In the past, if an Oussana did not at least try to maintain physical beauty they would of been deemed lazy and\n\ncould've been cast out from the family because they’re lazy.\n\nOussana Code of Honor\n\n*Oussana protect the weak and do not bring harm to them.\n*The Oussana value family, loyal to the members of their clan above others.\n*The Oussana do not bow to those inferior, but bend.\n\n*The Oussana do not allow Pride to be destroyed by minor things.\n*The Oussana are proud, strong and honorable at all times.\n*The Oussana do not tolerate weakness in the family.\n\n*To show emotion is not weakness, but to control it shows strength.", ""),
        StaticBook("Void Translocat.", "§bHaadi Mubdee", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=                 Void\n        Translocation\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n\n             *< 'O'\n\nThe Void is a realm of pure energy. Simultaneously nothing exists while everything exists. It was from this energy that the Creator formed our world as we know it. The Creator alone has the power to wield  the mana and energy of the Void to create\n\nsomething new. Not much is known about the Void and its elusiveness has made it near impossible to study. Yet the existence of 'nothing' within the Void that can become 'something' in the instant that a being with enough power willed it to be so provides\n\na potential to lesser beings. Evocationists borrow the energy from the Void in the form of a basic element, however what they summon must always return to the Void as it is distinctly different from anything 'real' in that it cannot exist seperate from\n\nthe void. Some users of magic would claim to journey into the void themselves and be able to emerge some time later. Just as much as one being can disappear from our realm, be converted into pure energy and mana, and emerge again seemingly unharmed; so\n\ntoo can objects pass from this world and exist within the Void. If an object's amount of mana can be balanced by the mana of a sorcerer who has a connection to the Void, that object can be removed from being 'real' and exist instead in the void. What does\n\nthis mean? Entities can be sent to the Void  They can be brought back from the Void at another time in another place. But how does one understand this energy? All things are made of small particles that exist as pure energy in the void. The larger and\n\nmore complex an object is, the more energy it contains. All things contain mana. The combination of energy and mana forms the 'DNA' of that object that defines size, mass, consistency, etc. Energy must not be thought of in a linear fashion. If x were to\n\nbe separated from xyz then x does not exist as independent from xyz because its entirety is defined through the combination of mana and energy, so by removing a single part you do not get a part of the whole because the information is fragmented.\n\nIf the leaf of a sapling were to be sent to the void while still attached to the rest of the sapling, then the combination of mana and energy has been disconnected from the whole entity and the leaf fails to exist, becoming meaningless energy in the void.\n\nIf the leaf were to be disconnected from the flow of mana then sent to the void, the mana and energy is able to recombine in the leaf to create an individual entity that can exist separate from the sapling. This may sound complex, but it simply means that\n\na part of something cannot be sent to the void and then reassembled again. The object must be sent and reassembled as a whole. It is possible to partially disassemble something, though it will be converted into generic energies in the void and remain\n\nunretrieveable. Any object that has a fluctuating form likewise has constantly shifting energy and mana. Water that is not in a solid container continually redefines itself and therefore risks becoming nonexistent if sent to the Void because it is\n\nseparated from a part of its' whole. Fire is also not at any instance 'solid' enough for its form to be understood. Larger living animals are highly complicated entities and within every second become vastly redefined in terms of mana and energy as blood\n\nquickly pumps around their large bodies. It would not be possible to read as a whole and understand a large living being as it is almost immediately shifting, therefore the larger the being the more impossible it becomes to discern their form enough to\n\nsend to the Void at all. Natural objects that remain in the form that they were at the hand of the Creator have a much higher levelof mana than those that are reformed at the hand of man. When the form of an object is changed so too is the combination of\n\nenergy and mana that defines it. A plank of wood has less mana but a more complex energy signature than a tree branch. Because the energy is no longer in its natural form when it is within the Void this energy is more distinct than others. A steel sword,\n\nfor example, contains highly complicated energies that would be more difficult to define in the natural world but easy to discover in the Void. In the moment that something dies or is changed in some way (like melting iron) its mana begins to shift and be\n\nused up as the energy particles are redefined. Humans as an entity have constantly shifting mana because of the complexity of the soul. Depending on mood, the connection to magic, physical health and many other attributes, the human body undergoes\n\nconstant changes in mana that makes it impossible to define. How does one perform this magic you ask? A sorcerer must first understand the object that they wish to send. To begin with the object or entity will need to be physically studied, then mentally\n\nstudied, then magically studied. The entity in question must remain unchanging in form and mana while it is being studied, otherwise the shifting energy will make the entity too difficult to understand. Once a sorcerer adequately understands the entity\n\nthey must use their own mana to match that amount of mana. Then, once a connection to the Void is established just as any Evocationist would, the object slips into the nothing and ceases to exist in this world. Now that the entity floats around as pure\n\nenergy in the Void the Sorcerer can get on with their day until such time as they would like to summon it back. Obviously the longer something is left in the void the easier it will be for the Sorcerer to forget the DNA of that entity. If such information\n\ncannot be recalled then the object will never again be seen in this world. However if such time has passed that they can remember the entity's combination of mana and energy, they simply establish a connection with the void again and imagine the entity in\n\nits original form, connecting with the energy and using the same amount of their own mana that it originally contained.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dessert Menu", "§bXusyne", "*A menu with a list of various dishes and their prices are written here*\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/NightLionSweets", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Topical Index:§0\n§0\n§0Introduction: 2§0\n§0Author' Comments: 8§0\n§0Great Houses:§0\n§0   Des'Nox: 9\n\nIntroduction:§0\n§0\n§0    The culture and people of Malinor's children are many and varied. This is quite true for the lesser known of Malinor's children, the Mali'Ker.§0\n§0\n§0Meaning quite literally, \"Dark Elf\" or \"Night Elf\" in the tongue of men, Mali'ker most\n\nnotably differ from their fellow Elves in complexion. Ranging from deep onyx to ashen grays to deeper violet and blue hues, their skin blends in with the Mali'Ker's favored habitats, Darkwood Forests and Mines.§0\n§0\n§0Culturally, the Mali'Ker are a passionate -\n\n- people. They excel in their masonry work, hewing finely crafted homes and furniture from their mines. If any, their mines are second only to the Dwarven folk.§0\n§0\n§0The Mali'Ker, above all else, are most passionate in the veneration of their ancestors, and\n\nmaintain an honor-driven, family based lifestyle.§0\n§0\n§0Built upon this culture of family, the Mali'Ker have developed large familiar groups called Clans. There are many smaller clans, which are offshoots of clans as gruops have intermingled over the years.\n\nPresiding over these smaller clans are the Great Houses, Great Clans, or Great Tribes (all versions are acceptable).§0\n§0\n§0Within these Great Houses have developed the most noteworthy traditions and practices of the Mali'Ker people. This is an investigation of\n\nthese traditions as they differ between the Great Houses. I will also be providing short histories, as told by the living House elders.§0\n§0\n§0To avoid insulting the clans and Great Houses, I make this clear: order is dictaed merely alphabetically, nothing more\n\nAuthor's Comments:§0\n§0\n§0I, Tend'el, am writing this to log the history of my people as I learn of it. An outsider raised in the wild lands, I hope to provide a text which may acclimate travelers to the Mali'Ker as a people, and reduce tensions by sympathy.\n\nHouse Des'Nox:", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Love you <3-Alirya", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "9th of Snow's Maiden, 1535§0\n§0\n§0Dear Diary, §0\n§0This is my first entry, of many in the future...§0\n§0Today, Nothing really happend... Haymin and I went§0\n§0out hunting and I talked to Sam Norwick, The Steward§0\n§0... Five days until Tax, maybe I will survive!§0\n§0Sincerely, ---\n\nFitonor Elmpool§0\n§0_______________________§0\n§03rd of The Grand Harvest, 1537§0\n§0Dear Diary, §0\n§0It has been about 2 years since the last time I wrote in you, Over that period of time, Pompourelia hasnt been doing to well... We have gotten raided many times--\n\nand lost some of our citizens.§0\n§0We have a war claim coming up at 4pm today. Wish me luck!§0\n§0Sincerely,§0\n§0Fitonor Elmpool§0\n§0_______________________\n\nHaymin was here", ""),
