        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-------------------        Gus' Journal§0\n§0-------------------[!]The book would appear to be torn and battered, several loose pages creeping from it's bounds.§0\n§0[!]The handwriting within the book gradually progresses and becomes neater as the book continues.\n\n12th of Deep Cold, 1543§0\n§0\n§0Today I was inducted into the Order of Magi, and given a unique task. Ambros wishes for me to discover Greg of Gregory Inc's aims. What he wants to achieve with his comapny. Hopefully it shall go well.\n\n13th of Deep Cold, 1543§0\n§0\n§0I've finally got a house within Sanctuary - I've suited it to my needs; benches, books to practice my writing, shelves, chairs.. everything.§0\n§0Hopefully Sanctuary will bring around some good opportunities.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§lLie With me ~§0\n§0§l   §0A Short Poem by;§0\n§0 Princess Siil'crux of    the City-State of        Celein.§0\n§0\n§4~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0§o11th of§0\n§0§oSnow's Maiden,§0\n§0§l1558.\n\n\n§0If days go by;§0\n§0and the full moon;§0\n§0flutters a pale glow;§0\n§0\n§0If on this night, §0\n§0I lie awake,§0\n§0with pride and distinction;", ""),
        StaticBook("Torture Devices", "Eenhoornheid", "Torture Devices\n\n     by Unknown\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nJudas Cradle\n\nThe victim would be place on top of a pyramid-like seat. Where they would be slowly impaled.\n\nCoffin Torture\n\nThe victim was placed inside the ‘coffin’. Torturers were well-known for forcing overweight victims into the device, or even making the ‘coffin’ slightly larger than normal to make the victims more uncomfortable.\n\nThe Brazen Bull\n\nWhen a victim is placed inside the brazen bull, he or she is slowly burned to death. It has a complex system of tubes in order to make the victim’s screams sound like an infuriated ox.\n\nThe Rack\n\nThe rack is commonly considered the most painful form of torture. The torturer turned the handle causing the ropes to pull the victim’s arms. Eventually, the victim’s bones were dislocated with a loud crack. This method was mostly\n\nused to extract confessions, as not confessing meant that the torturer could stretch more. Sometimes, torturers forced their victim to watch other people be tortured with this device to implant psychological fear. They often had spikes that penetrated the\n\nvictim’s back  - as the limbs were pulled apart, so was his spinal cord increasing not only the physical pain, but the psychological one of being handicapped at best, too.\n\nDunking\n\nThe victim was tied to a chair which was elevated or lowered by the torturer. If he noticed that the victim was going to pass out, he elevated the chair. If they didn’t reveal information the chair was lowered. This could take hours.\n\nDrops of Water\n\nA very painful method of torture consisted of fixing a victim’s head under a small tube that constantly filtered drops of water. These fell on the same spot of the victim’s head leading to, in prolonged periods of time, death.\n\nFreezing with Water\n\nPouring water on someone in cold areas. Eventually causing them to freeze to death.\n\nForce Drinking\n\nThe effect is this: the victim is forced to drink much water until his confession or death.\n\nExposure\n\nAs its name implies, this method consists of exposing a victim to the elements. The victim could be buried up to his neck, letting any animals, insects or other people kill him slowly.\n\nChair of Torture\n\nThere are many variants of the chair. They all have one thing in common: spikes cover the back, arm-rests, seat, leg-rests and foot-rests. The number of spikes in one of these chairs ranges from 500 to\n\n1,500. To avoid movement, the victim’s wrists were tied to the chair or, in one version, two bars pushed the arms against arm-rests for the spikes to penetrate the flesh even further. In some versions a hole under the seat.\n\nThe Tickler\n\nIt’s a very simple instrument that was used to tear a victim’s skin apart. Due to its shape, neither bones nor muscles were spared. The tool had claws on it sharp enough to tear anything.\n\nThe Maiden\n\nIt stands 7 feet tall and is able to accommodate a man. The victim was tied inside the Maiden and one of the two doors was shut, penetrating the victim’s flesh with the strategically-placed spikes that didn’t\n\npenetrate any vital organs. When completely closed, the screams from the victim could not be heard outside, nor could the victim see any light or hear anything.\n\nThe Head Crusher\n\nWith the chin placed over the bottom bar and the head under the upper cap, the torturer slowly turned the screw pressing the bar against the cap. This resulted in the head being slowly compressed.\n\nRats\n\nThe victim was completely restrained and tied to the ground or any horizontal surface. A rat was then placed on his stomach covered by a metallic container. As the container was gradually heated, the rat began to look for\n\na way out through the victim’s body. Digging a hole usually took a few hours of agonizing pain for the victim. The almost invariantly resulted in death.\n\nThe Wheel Torture\n\nThe device consists of a large wooden wheel with many spokes. The victim’s limbs were tied to the spokes and the wheel itself was slowly revolved. Through the openings between the spokes, the torturer usually hit the victim's hones.\n\nOnce his bones were broken he was left on the wheel to die, sometimes placed on a tall pole so the birds could feed from the still-living human.\n\nFoot Roasting\n\nThe victim’s feet were imprisoned in the stocks and then red-hot coal was placed right under the,. When the subject was interrogated a screen was put between the heat and his feet acting as relief. If he refused\n\nto confess, his bare feet were exposed to the flames. The torture progressed until the victim’s feet were charred to the bone.\n\nThumbscrew Torture\n\nThe victim’s fingers were placed inside the instrument and slowly crushed as the torturer turned the handle on top. This method was used to extract confessions as it was both painful and lasting.\n\nThe Heretic's Fork\n\nThe instrument consists of two forks set against each other that penetrated the flesh under the chin in one end and the upper chest in the other. As usual, this instrument didn’t harm any vital points; thus avoiding death.\n\nLead Sprinkler\n\nAt first sight, it looks like a holy water sprinkler, but in reality it’s a bit more complex. The torturer poured molten metals in one end and its contents slowly rushed to the other side where they fell on any part of the body.\n\nFlaying\n\nThe victim’s arms were tied to a pole above his head while his feet were feet were tied below. His body now completely exposed and the torturer, with the help of a small knife, peeled off the victim’s skin slowly.\n\nKnee Splitter\n\nAs the torturer turned the handle, the claws slowly slammed against each other mutilating any skin in between. The number of spikes the knee splitter contained varied from three to more than twenty.\n\nCrocodile Tube\n\nThe victim was fixed inside a tube just big enough for the victim’s entrance. The tube, having crocodile teeth-like spikes, was slowly compressed leaving the victim totally immobilized. The torturer could only see his face and\n\nfeet. With the help of carbon and fire underneath the tube until he extracted a confession or killed the victim.\n\nThe Brank\n\nThe device was a metal cage or mask that enclosed the head, often with ridiculous adornments designed to humiliate its victim. Commonly attached with bell to warn people of their approach.\n\nCrocodile Shears\n\nThe interior design closely resembles a tube containing numerous spikes on both ends. Although it was sometimes used to mutilate the fingers, its most common purpose was to cut arteries.\n\nThe Copper Boot\n\nFirst, the torturer placed the victim’s feet inside the boot and secured them with chains inside the device. Depending on the crime, the victim could be tortured in many different ways: Molten metals, boiling water, beating it.\n\nThe Pendulum\n\nWith the help of a rope, the victim’s wrists were tied behind his back. As the torturer turned the handle, the rope slowly elevated eventually dislocating the victim’s shoulders.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sirame Docs.", "§bThe Sirame", "http://tinyurl.com/Sirame\n\nThe Full Documents of the Sirame.\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/SirameHandbook\n\nThe Conduct of a Sirame.\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/Vel15\n\nThe Format for Your Gate Forms.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Old Missive", "§bUnknown", "Elves of Malinor,\n\nIt is on this day that your centuries long watch must come to an end. The Betrayer grows in might with each day and our forests, no doubt, will soon be host to his poisonous minions. It is thus that our greatest defence must be\n\nshattered, lest it become an even greater adversary.\n\nDo not hesitate, Guardians. Do not mourn the loss of the Ancient Altar. You do what you must for the continuation of our lines.\n\nThe forest walks\n\nhere. Do not forget this.\n\n— The High Council", ""),
        StaticBook("Fi'Hiiran'tanya", "§bVirion'annil Elibar'acal", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       Fi'hiiran'tanya§0\n§0\n§0     The Magic of§0\n§0\n§0   Blessed Elibar'acal§0\n§0\n§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~_\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Long ago, the pure halls of the Silver State were filled with the impurity of the void. Users of the void§0\n§0which spread their scandulous lies across blessed Haelun'or. Their lies corrupted the minds of the pure and the minds of the true.§0\n§0~~\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~However, there were those who opposed such lies. Blessed Elibar'acal, the true servants of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, the Golden Owls. These blessed souls bathed in pools of Gold, controling a majority of Haelun'or from the underground.§0\n§0~~\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~And so, these blessed Elibar'acal could not defend themselves against the power of the void. They made their own way of curing Haelun'or of such impurity. Fi'hiiran'tanya was empowered by souls binded by ritual. These souls were put into§0\n§0~\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~what is called an 'Umbra Stone'. The power enstowed into the Umbra Stone would then go through further process to be made into a 'mist form', which must be put into a 'mist stone' to be properly used.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Fi' has two variants. Fi'hiiran'seth, and Fi'hiiran'acaele. Fi'hiiran'seth targets the Arcane abilities of a mage, cutting off their connection to the void, or their mana pool. Fi'hiiran'acaele targets the Deitic abilities of a mage.§0\n§0~~~~~\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The Effects of Fi'hiiran'tanya:§0\n§0\n§0~Physical and Mental strain§0\n§0\n§0~Loss of weight§0\n§0\n§0~Incredibly realistic lucid dreams§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("An introduction", "§b'Richard'", "A man laves his home every morning to walk to work and passes a dark shamanism encampment surrounded by a wooden wall. \n\nEvery morning the shamans are out in the yard and he cna hear them saying in unison,\n\n\"10, 10, 10, 10\".-\n\nOne day, he gets curious and looks through a hole in the wall. Suddenly, a stick shoots out and pokes him in the eye.\n\n\"FUCK! He says to himself.\"\n\nWhile walking away pissed off he can hear the patients saying, -\n\n\"11, 11, 11, 11, 11\".\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe end, lore for dank shamanism.", ""),
        StaticBook("Time Warping", "Minuscule_Evil", "Time Warping\n\n      by, Tahjeet\n   Asul'mira Mubdee\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nIf the theory of time as an illusion is correct then it is possible that time itself can be warped, molded or shaped, by the will of a person.\n\nTime, although a perception, an illusion is viewed as reality anymoment where the perception of time\n\nis changed, it is in the eyes of all, truly changed as a reality.\n\nBut to be able to learn to warp the perception of time, an illusion, a person must know how to create and mold illusions.This can be done with, perhaps, one’s mana alike how\n\nevocationists can create and change the arcane through the casting of mana.\n\nTo make a comparison, time is like a piece of iron and the one who can mold this piece of iron is the blacksmith, in this case an illusionist.\n\nTo shape and mold the iron, it requires the iron to be heated., the casting of ones mana, then to shape the piece of iron it requires a hammer, this will be the illusionist’s ability to mold and shape the illusion or perception.\n\nFor example, if the blacksmith hammers the iron flat it become elongated- lengthening time-if the blacksmith hammers the iron into a smaller length it becomes shorter – shortening time– if the blacksmith hammers the iron from a different angle,\n\n becomes bent - perhaps stopping time.\n\nWhat may be that separates simple illusions and the warping of the time illusion, which may be the reason no illusionist, is that time is an illusion seen by all and perceived as a reality.\n\nThis changes what that iron is. The piece of iron the blacksmith had been shaping was just a small piece of a large statue.\n\nThe illusion of time surrounds us, we are immersed in it, fragments of the illusion can be shaped, changing what we see and feel. It is impossible for anyone to truly see time as an illusion even though it is known to be so.\n\nLiving beings are designed to perceive time as a reality, to see old and new, growth and withering, life and death.\n\nTo understand time is to not see through its illusion.\n\nTo warp time is left in the hands of the curious.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pyromancy,AGuide", "§b[In Costume] Archibald Cyrion", "Pyromancy, A Guide.\n\nFire Evocation, otherwise known as pyromancy, is the art of creating flames from the  very essence of the Void itself.\n\nGetting Started:\n\nKnow you may ask\"How do I even get to the Void?!\"\n\nWell ask no further.\n\nA simple week or two of meditation will hopefull get you along the lines of connecting to the void.\n\nImagine the void as a\n\nwindow within your mind, and through that window is energy (of sorts). To keep that window open there needs to be something holding it open, in other words: your energy, call it mana if you will.\n\nAfter connecting to the Void:\n\nAfter managing to connect to the void, a mage simply has to get better, through the means of meditation and practice. \n\nOnce a mage has formed a sort of \"bond\" with the void, they may now begin to summon flames.\n\nHow do you\n\nask? Well all you need to do is know how a flame is, how it is made, how it not only destroys but purify, how it burns, basically BE THE FLAME.\n\nOkay, I Managed With the Void and How Fire Works, Now What?\n\nNow you get to the fun part.\nWith the connection of the void and the knowing of how fire works, you probably know how to do it, somehow.\n\nAt first a mage in there first week or two will barely\n\nmanage to get a spark going, much less a ball of fire. However after continues effort and meditation, a mage can achieve their goal of mastering fire evocation over the course of around five elven months.\n\nFire:\n\nNow you may be asking how are you going to actually use it in the terms of combat. Well obviously you, with some practice, mold the flame into that of a sphere and condense it. The stronger larger the flame, the greater the energy. \n\nAs of this,\n\nyou can also cause an explosion of the fire as it contact with a surface, the size of the explosion depending on the strength of the mage.\n\nNow after reading this, you may or may not want to be a mage. But good luck!\n\n- Archibald Cyrion, Head of the Cyrion Bloodline", ""),
        StaticBook("Golem Issues", "§bJared Blackfoot", "One of my Golems has become slightly sporadic. It seems my design is slightly flawed, they must be shut down or maintained regularly to prevent their logical functions from deteriorating to an unworkable state. Just another chore for Enas, I suppose.\n\nStill, I should keep an eye on him, things would be bad if they went rampant.\n\n-Jared Blackfoot", ""),
        StaticBook("A Guide on Mages", "§bLerin Hrak", "A rough guide to hunting mages, by Lerin Hrak\n\nForeword, This is only a rough guide and the first book I have written in many years, it will eventually be refined by me in the future.\n\nChapted One, Identifying mages\n\nWhile a mage can be just about anyone, they often will stick to light clothing and carry only basic weapons if any on them, they also tend to favor staffs both to help them focus on spells and to aid them\n\nin walking. Almost never will you see a mage wearing armor as it encumbers them too much and they need as much energy as possible to create their spells.\n\nChapter Two, A Overview of mages\n\nMages are indivduals who have spent many years in learning the ability to harness the void to create spells, which are in a way, altering the physical realm to create something, truthfully I am not learned in that\n\nparticular subject. In this pursuit their bodies are often left physically weaker then average members of their race and they have little time to learn much else to become skilled in it, such as swordsmanship. Mages also rely on their on energy and focus\n\nin order to create their spells, creating a weakness for if they can not focus, then they are next to helpless and only skilled mages can create magic that can actually kill instead of only wounding.\n\nChapter Three, Tactics against Mages\n\nIn my years of experience, I have figured out one of the best tactics to use against a mage is to disrupt their focus, pain is a excellent way to do this, and it is also wise to keep close to them so you can\n\ndisrupt their focus more so as they will not be able to focus without letting their guard down for you  to attack. Another favoured tactic of mine is stealth, for a mage can not attack with a spell if they can not see or hear you, and you can quickly kill\n\nor disable one with a single blow.\n\nChapter Four, A guide to types of mages.\n\nWhile for now the last chapter, this is also one of the most useful as you must be aware of the dangers the different types of mages present. The most basic and common would be a Evocation mage, one who can\n\ncreate things such as fireballs and spikes of ice to use as weapons, they can be deadly both up close and at range if they are skilled enough and clever enough. Next is the summoners, while slightly rare from what I've seen, they can be quite deadly as\n\nthey can summon or create creatures using their spells to fight for them, the beasts themselves are not real in a sense, but they can still injure and only persist while the mage can focus on it.\nNext is the Illusion mages, they are capable of using\n\nspells to confuse and muddle the mind by creating false images and other such things, in the end all they create is false, though they can still be dangerous as many illusions can still appear and feel to quite real.\n\nEpilogue\n\nFor now that is all I shall write of, though they are several other types of mages, I shall expand upon this book in other editions and other entire books, eventually I shall cover abominations aswell.\n\nUntil I get around to writing another, I wish you luck and may the Creator guide you against the Undead threat and others who go against him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Investigation", "§bPrince Laethis Izalith", "Merlin and Orsino,\n\nPlease see to it that Faenor and Riondil are investigated for their assault upon Velulaei. Irhamir may have been involved as well.\n\nDearest Regards,\nPrince Laethis Izalith", ""),
        StaticBook("Div'eth Fiyem", "§bLaethis Izalith", "((https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ld7yuasn90fgOINxgQ0BcqVXJQEqoX1Ktbl6uoog9nk/edit?usp=sharing))", ""),
        StaticBook("Aneurin Llywelyn", "§bLaethis Izalith", "((https://docs.google.com/document/d/1F_Egx8VTBbtddsvj3JG2vTjBLzxdnzlGsxJThCj1Z3g/edit?usp=sharing))", ""),
        StaticBook("Frantic Note", "§bPatrick 'Paddy' Garrett", "*the writing is hurried and desperate*\n\nAodhan, my name is Patrick Garrett. Marked Man, we spoke not two elven weeks ago. I have found what fits your description of the Dragaar or Drakaar. The Embermoor Swamps, there is a trench\n\nI was searching for Vodnik and I found this huge beast. I escaped without it seeing me fortunately, I can lead you if you get into contact with me, I hope this is of help. \n- P.Garrett\n\n((coords x 1113 z 1113", ""),
        StaticBook("Salazar", "§bLaethis Izalith", "((https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_eB2rgFuefARWPY4MsgKy-ukli8QyGbxj3BJbHWbvsM/edit?usp=sharing))", ""),
        StaticBook("[!] A Note", "§bSerpen", "I am the one with a battle of souls.\n\nTwo became one.\n\nOpposing desires collide within, leaving me susceptible to either.\n\nMy salvation can only come from those who are garbed in light\n\nand led by the keeper of souls.\n\nMy time is limited.\n\nMalice and destruction are beomcing the prominent desires.\n\nDeliverance into the light shall be either the end, or the return of one pure.\n\nThe green soul fades.\n_\n            _.;_'-._\n           {`--.-'_,}\n          {; \\,__.-'/}\n          {.'-`._;-';\n           `'--._.-'\n              .-\\\\,-.\n              ._..\\\\._\n                  \\\\\n                   \\\\\n                    \\\n-C.A\n\n[!] A drawing of a black rose seems to be at the bottom of the note?", ""),
        StaticBook("A Silver Memior", "§bAndria", "Purity isn’t a lie, but Haelun’or has made it a lie.\n\n  If you’re reading this, I have departed for I hold no hope in the Silver State, nor have I for decades. In fact I recall speaking to Kalameet Izalith about it many years ago in Cerulin, he's a prime\n\nexample of how our state has betrayed its history.\n\n  What gives you the right to call a leader like him an impure when he’s done more than you could ever hope to achieve? He might’ve had a shade, but he was more of a Mali'aheral than Taeleh or Avern\n\ncould ever be. Purity has become a weapon, and the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya a mere saying, if Dio ever saw what you have built, he would weep. Yes, weep. You have become decadent, convoluted, degenerate, and impure.\n\nDon't try to say that\n\nCelelin is all of those things, for blaming another state does nothing. If you remain obstinate like this, your names will be forgotten, and your legacy ash.\n\n  Call me impure all you like, though I have found that family is above purity. If I had learnt\n\nthis earlier my nephew might still be alive. If you don’t know who my nephew is, you should be ashamed, for you have forgotten our history and its many heroes and even greater amount of villains.\n\n  You’re all villains, you use purity as a way to\n\nsteadfast your agenda; your mouths reek with vile words once considered unacceptable; you remove people for decadence yet cuddle up to it’s cold, addictive, embrace; you spurt sayings of progress and health yet you watch contently as the walls around you\n\nyou crumble; but worst of all: you blame everyone but yourselves.\n\n~ A leader long forgotten", ""),
        StaticBook("Fresh Crops", "§bLilliana", "-=+=-Fresh Apples-=+=-\nJuicy and tasty, the apples carry the full flavor of their grown. Grown with tender love and care, these apples are plucked in the prime, making your mouth water by sight alone.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per apple\n\n-=+=-Fresh Carrots-=+=-\nFreshly plucked from fertile soil, these carrots are carefully cleaned and cut to increase the taste and crunch of each bit.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per Carrot\n\n-=+=-Cool Melon-=+=-\nEach slice will bring you bright joy as you bite deep into the juicy red innards of our melons.\n\nPrice :: 1 mina per slice", ""),
        StaticBook("DOmInUZ KhARaK", "§bDominus Kharak'Raguk", "To th leadership of this town, I, Dominus Kharak'Raguk propose a 'tribudhe'. (A pay to stay alive.) As you must be aware, the Uruk have been consistently come to these lands and have been taking slaves. We imagine this is quite troublesome for you. The\n\nnature of a slave's short life is rife with pain and gruelling labour. And with the rise of the Krug-hai, assuming some form of military or force, you can expect a very good threat to your way of life. Every Uruk serves as a soldier. If you want to\n\npreserve your town from the fury of the Uruk forces, you will the supply of iron and a crate of wood as tribute. In return, you will not have the looming threat of the Uruk, and they will help your people when in need.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sirame Notebook", "§bLorus", "14th of Sun's Smile, 1540.\n\nNeph assaulted by a wraith, lacking a name. He fed on her for lifeforce, her skin decayed and horrid. The interrogated is named Archembalt, and he claims that the wraith resides by the dwarven isles.\n\n15th of Sun's Smile, 1540. Interrogation of Ciri'lla.\n\nAn arresting of Avenel was discussed, and how it should be executed. The Sirame will loot his room in the vacant Citadel of Haelun'or, and hopefully set up a meeting at an area.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Members In The Crew§0\n§0\n§0[Captain]Delvin Ghostwood§0\n§0\n§0[First Hand] Liandir§0\n§0\n§0[Alchemist] Warin\n\nNietbas: Aka Faelond§0\n§0Eowulf§0\n§0\n§0By order of Eadune§0\n§0Revitar", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "§bUnknown", "Latsi,§0\n§0Not very likely you'll get this since I sent it off with an owl without his wits, but we're still looking.§0\n§0\n§0Still worried.§0\n§0\n§0Give us a clue.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Varak Notes", "§bArchmage Crumena", "Research notes on the Kal'Varak by the enlightened Magi Auvreaeath in Asulon. No date available.\nRescribed by Arch-Mage V. Illwindior on the 2nd of the First Seed, 1473.\n\nThe Kal'Varak is an ancient, crystalline artifact dug up by the dwarves of Karik. J ust prior to their unearthing of the hibernating dragons. The properties of the c rystal are strange, it seems to be nexus of the magic, but no mage has so far\n\nmanged to manipulate it. The remebrancers studied the artifact at great length, stori ng it in their enclave in Karik. They never managed to find out exactly what the Ka l'Varak does, but they did mange to get it to transmute pieces of gold into strange\n\nelixir that gave the user resistance to fire.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mental Sense", "§bElindor", "Mental Sensitivity\n\nA short depiction of such things and how one may endeavour to experience it.\n\nFeaturing an example.\n\nOur senses are really only the beginning of perception. The simpleton perceives mostly with vision and uses little else of their other senses, and few actually recognise a higher perceptive nature within themselves. But be not fooled by the majority, for\n\nthe mind shall see far more than what comes before the eyes, if one can but forfeit their pre-conceived ideas that only the seen and experienced can exist, as well as pinpoint their place within an almighty expanse of universes in which knowledge is\n\nbut a fraction of the truth, and then dive into the opportunities for them whose mind is self actualised, and whose existence is both infinitely small, and omnipotently all.\n\nLet us embark upon this journey outside of the material things. Let us learn to apprecciate the placement of all things within the universe and begin perceiving without the senses.\nLet us discover ourselves amidst a world that exists just beyond our eyes.\n\nTo begin with. Ignore your senses. Block out the information that your eyes, ears and skin are attempting to bombard you with at all times. Discover within yourself that small safe place in which dwells just your thoughts, and your sense of self.\n\nSome people find this a confronting experience as the immediate outcome is an objective view of the being from which you spend all your time trapped within and, in being so, are unable to adequately examine. You may experience a sense of resentment\n\ninadequacy towards faults. This is not a bad thing, for it means that you have discovered your true nature without the inflated pride that usually skews this view. This is the first most important step towards understanding the world around from\n\na liberated consciousness. In trying to discover this place, do not allow yourself to slip into such blankness of thought that you discover The Void. Immunity from the sensory overload that is our waking existence is required for locating both\n\nones self and The Void that sits in wait behind our reality, yet that much emptiness of mind is not required. Thoughts are a good thing in this circumstance. Your thoughts are what will guide you to view yourself from without your eye sockets.\n\nNow, assuming that you have indeed come to realise yourself objectively; seen your existential being as it were, you may already havcommenced viewing our world from a new viewpoint. Let us take some time before continuing onwards to apprecciate all the\n\nwonders that surround us that we so eagerly allow to slip by under the weight of our own self importance. Let us aclimatise to this expanding of the mind before we carry on.\n\nHave we acclimatised?\n\nGood.\n\nNow. Again, block out all the sensory garbage. Cease seeing, feeling, smelling, hearing and tasting your surroundings and again return to the place of just you and your mind in the quiet.\n\nObviously you cannot also be reading this. So read this first, and then do it. Have you read the rest?\n\nOk, let us continue.\n\nFrom this place of mental freedom, now look beyond yourself. It may be of value to envision an\n\nappropriate illustration to better comprehend the surrounding reality. For the sake of clarity an example will be used to more accurately define what one is attempting to do.\nOnce you have discovered your place in the universe, allow the universe to\n\nreveal its place to you. This isn't supernatural druid bollocks but simply the easiest way to explain that you must oepn your mind enough to discover your surroundings for what they are and no longer what they look, feel and seem to be.\n\nThe Illustration Begins\nYou exist alone. There is nothing. But your eyes are closed, so how can you know that there is nothing? Breath. Allow your mind to drift, it knows what it is doing.\nNow open your mind's eye. See.\n\nWhat you beleived to be darkness is quite the opposite. For you exist surrounded by endless white. There is no distinctive end. You cannot perceive a difference between land or sky. You know yourself to be sitting, yet there is no surface below.\n\nNow examine more closely. What is it that takes shape? There is indeed a surface but it is not solid. You can feel it beneath you, perhaps even see it as your eyes focus. There are stones. Smooth stones that fit nicely in the palm. You might pick one up\n\nso that you can better examine. It seems too perfect to be real. You glance around and see that they are all too perfect. And with each returned glance there are more. Thousands. Countless. The endless white is as an ocean of small white stones.\n\nYou should look more closely now at the one in your hand, for a detail you missed before now seems more obvious. It is not perfectly smooth afterall, there is one small part that is slightly flatter. You gather another stone, there is an imperfection to\n\nits colouring. And another, with a small indentation like a dimple. Even as you look about at the stones far in the distance you become aware that they are not all alike. They are each their own, each in its right place, all together creating an expanse\n\nof white that stretches out beyond the recognition of sight. Further, even, beyond recognition of the mind. You hold tightly the first stone, with its flat side against the skin of your hand. An unexpected feeling as the awakening from a deep slumber\n\nbeckons you outward. You know not how to give in to it, so you clench your eyes and grip onto the small stone.\n\nBack in the room where you were meditating. All is still. But you feel an odd attraction to a candle upon the desk (or\n\nsome other inanimate object as is appropriate to your situation). Perhaps you reach out to touch it, though it does already feel like you have it within your grasp, and as your hand rises the thing appears to wobble. For a single instant. So easy to miss.\n\nConcluding Remarks Such is the beginning. Humble, as most are. \n\nThere is more in store, but self discovery is the only way towards progress from here. Understanding where and how one object exists can bloom into a working appreciation\n\nfor the placement of all things around. And an ability to realise when something is not in the way that it should. When a stone is overturned, misplaced, or unsettled by something new.\n\nThere are other sensitivites that are not just mental based. Sensing auras and magical disturbances have proven highly useful, as was the case with an old mage who had lost use of his sight and was able to perceive as though with eyes from sensing\n\nthe proximity of things emitting aura. \nNoticing magical disturbances is a bit more common, particularly for Void Mages in sensing when something has majorly shifted in the balance of Void energy.\nThe druids too have some connection to the right placement\n\nof nature from their communion with the aspects, which, in all relativity, is highly likely to operate similarly to the mental sensitivity suggested in the former pages.\n\nI will write no more upon the uses of such a thing, as any who struggle to see the usefulness therein are blinded by a love of their sight.\nIn fact, I will write no more at this time upon this subject at all.\n\n    ~ - | END | - ~", ""),
        StaticBook("Soul Gems", "§bRosso", "Soul Gem\n\nIt is theorized that when a vessel or body is compromised, it’s soul escapes into the Existing Plane (The plane which all life exists) for a brief moment before dissipating into the void.\n\nIf such a theory is true, then could it not be possible that the soul is captured?\n\nHowever to capture a soul requires a vessel for the soul to remain.\n\nThere arises the theory of Soul Gems.\n\nSoul Gems are not necessarily gems or precious minerals, but hollow objects made of glass, stone, or gold.\n\nAlthough a simple design, it represents the void- A center of Nothingness surounded by a barrier separating it from the Existing Plane.\n\nWhen a soul escapes it’s vessel, instead of dissipating into the true void, it enters into the Soul Gem- A representation of such.\n\nAlike a living body, a gem may be compromised. The barrier between the soul and the Existing\n\nPlane broken.\n\nIt is hypothesized that a Soul Gem alone can do nothing, it remains a simple hollow object, but if it is commanded, perhaps by symbols or markings, the mana of the soul within the Gem may be used to harness the void’s power.\n\nBut to understand which marking a soul will react to requires the knowledge of the Arcane and the Soul itself.\n\nAs the universe progresses, more will understood of souls and how they react.\n\nThis theory ends with a final thought: Does a soul’s thoughts remain? The inference is no, as one’s thoughts are developed through life, not the void. \n\n-Tahjeet Mubdee\n\nSoul Gems\n\nWritten by Tahjeet Mubdee\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Little Red Bird", "§bKikira", "-=:@:=-\n  The Little Red Bird\n          -=:@:=-\n\n\n\n\n      A short poem.\n\n\n\n\nby: K.I.\n\n  The Little Red Bird\n__________________ \n\nThe little red bird was left behind.\n\nThe little red bird stayed and died.\n\n He died in the snow where the cruelest winds blow.\n\nBut his spirit still flies up high in the skies.\n\nDon't worry it's not all bad, but really it's quite sad.\n\nThat he lies where no man goes in the coldest of snows.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "§b[Elder] Thurak'Yar", "Water\n\nWater appears of one of the simplest elements that inhabit our world, but it is in fact incomprehensively more complex that most people think it is. To fully understand it, one must practice large\n\n amounts of time meditating, and indeed spending their time around said element- be it by lounging around by a pond, or studying its properties profusely in laboratories. Water is a necessity of life, needed by all living and sentient things,\n\nfor example Humans, Orcs, Dwarves, Kharajyr, Elves and also various other animals or plants. Water, also appearing as such a calm element, is also one of the more dangerous; out in the seas, a storm can take out a fleet of ships within moments.\n\nOne can never fully control water that isn’t evocated, unless of course one is a shaman- In which case the Spirits control the element, and in-avertedly the shaman controls the water too. Despite out best attempts, we are\n\nall mortal; we do not live forever, nor do we have amazing power like the ascended or the undead back in Aegis. As said before, water can be a very dangerous element; a single flood can wipe out a village just as easily as it might cause it to flourish.\n\nThe element water contains raw power; a power that all Hydromancers would wish to wield. A Hydromancer’s training consists of learning about the Void, being able to evocate from it, and learning about their element so they can properly evocate it.\n\n. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a single element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the same as the water we have around us, however it is completely different. The water that us Hydromancers evocate can only\n\nbe created in the void and can brought forth into this world by ourselves. Mana, or life-force, is the power we use to create and transport water from the void, and is vital in most, if not every known magic. If one uses too much of this mana,\n\n, then they would simply fall unconscious or even die before they complete their task due to overuse or too much exerted force after large amounts of dedication and training; such as learning about the void and Hydromancy, and shaping and creating\n\ntheir mana into an interpretation of water. The connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however; though once one has learnt about Hydromancy itself then they should be able to understand where we are coming from. One’s\n\nconnection to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained- Like feeling happy, or in love. As a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and evocating elements becomes a simpler task. As one would possibly notice, many\n\nmages use a staff when they’re casting their magic- This however, is not necessary at all, and only aids the magician by giving them something to focus on while evocating. Water can be evocated in various forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water,\n\nan orb of ice, and other things I have not generally experimented on yet. Hydromancers which have been learning for a long time will be able to use more things and will be able to explore completely different aspects of the element.\n\nIce is more suitable for offence in a battle, rather than defence, however, generally water evocation itself is more useful to protect the caster, as walls of water or ice can be willed to block a projectile or a strike, or simply to\n\nintercept and deflect one, though such must be done at short distance. Ice that we evoke isn’t the same that we find in our world naturally; it cannot be melted by the heat of the sun or a torch, but it can be melted with the use of Pyromancy.\n\nTo break the ice, the Hydromancy must both lose connection to the void and have their creation dissipate, or have a Pyromancer melt it with their fire, or, in the later stages of their training, with steam.\n\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited to the caster’s imagination and fatigue, and with proper training it can be suited for any purpose.\n~Adorellan", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dragons", "§bKypris'dionne Thylsealaes", "On Dragons\nLife and Death\n\n\nBy Sam King\n\nChapter 1: Birth\nDragons are known by most everyone, born by egg like our domesticated and less dangerous, Chicken. Once the egg is laid it goes on a one month incubation period. The mother dragon will warm her eggs with her belly,\n\nlaying next to it, gently murmuring away, like a loud rumbling purr, as she increases her internal heat. She would do this for hours at a time for about a month, or until it's time for the eggs to hatch, where they begin their lives as hatchlings.\n\nChapter 2: Hatchling\nAfter the egg hatches and if all goes well it will begin to stand on all four legs, stretching it's wings for the first time. It is important to note that the young dragon will not be able to fly at this age, and won't be able to\n\nfor quite some time. Dragons at this age are about size of a wolf, and thought to be relativly tame and kind, much like a puppy. For its first week a hatchling will wander around its nesting sight, never traveling out of eye sight of it's mother.\n\nIt is during the second week of a hatchlings life that is left alone, as the mother goes to hunt to provide for both her and her hatchling's hunger. The hatchling is then left to its own accord, and begins to hunt small rodents and animals. The third\n\nmonth is when the hatchling is now able to hunt on its own, under normal circumstances, and when the fires within begin to bubble up, though not able to breathe its deadly fire, it is good to note, smoke can be seen from their nostrols and mouths. When\n\nthe hatchling reaches a year of age, is when it is left alone and now considered a Drake or 'Teenager'.\n\nChapter 3: Drake\nDrake are still unable to use its deadly fire, but its bow a fierce and dangerous hunter, around the size of a horse and rather grumpy. This age is often considered to be their 'Awkward' phase in their life, as they are prone to explore\n\ngreat distances for no apperent reason, which is why they were said to be the most commonly sighted age of a Dragon. They hae also been said to have caused the most havoc, as they are for some reason, really aggressive and prone to attack anyone nearby.\n\nChapter 4: Adult\nLittle is known about adult dragons, as they were rarley ever said to be sighted. What is known however is at this stage is when a dragon is now able to 1-Breathe Fire\n2-Fly\n3-Mate\nAdult dragons are thought to be rather\n\nunaggresive, except for a few circumstances which I will get to soon, as they have been rarley sighted and don't attack often, if at all. Now the mating rituals of dragon is, ofcourse, unknown, most likely lost in time. What is known is, they\n\nbecome very aggressive and is one of the few times they are said to be. During their mating season, time is also unknown, is when they are said to attack towns, as when they adult has its nesting sight picked, nothing will stop it from nesting there, even\n\nif it is already occupied. It is also worthy to note that the legend and myth that dragons have an affinity to treasures, is neither proven or disproven, though most likely false. As to why and what purpose a dragon would horde treasure is unknown, except\n\nto possibly attract potentional mates?\n\n[!] Here is where the ink would change color, the previous was a lighter less heavy pressed black, the next passage would be much deeper and harder pressed.\n\nChapter 5: Wyrm's\nAlmost nothing is known about Wyrms, other than they are some of the oldest and ancient dragons ever to 'Exist'. When an adult becomes a Wyrm is unknown, what is known though is that they are to be feared, extremely feared.\n\nChapter 6: Death\nNatural deaths have never been known or speaken of for dragons. The only few deaths of dragons spoken of is by furious knights/wizards, even then this legend and stories have no real reason to be thought of as fact\n\nin nearly all occasions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Copied Transfig.", "§bKypris'dionne Thylsealaes", "As I had guessed the art of Transifiguration is seems to be just as easy as telekinesis, though this time it requires thorough understanding of Equivalent Exchange and alteration. Every object no matter how large or small has dormant mana.\n\nThis mana controls the alchemical makeup of every and such is where alchemy by taping such and creating elixirs of the likes. This time the idea is to trap the mana using your own, not just to change the velocity of this object but to change the the whole\n\nmakeup in your own way.. to alter the material is how /you/ chose, though the law of equivalent exchange must be followed, so no turning Ferum to Aurum anytime soon. My first connection seemed to be more easy than when I had first connected to control\n\nan object velocity when I had learned about telekinesis, but this time instead of using my connection to the void to 'grip' and object by this dormant mana, I was actively using my own mana to tap into this mana, and activate it! It was incredible, it\n\nfelt like I was one with the object. Even with my fairly low training with the magic I understand vastly on how this whole concept can be used in the most complex scenarios. For now I am to stick to heating this ball up, or cool it down.\n\nA simple task as tempurature is a mere thought, though because of how new I am to this spell it seems to take a toll on my body as if I was a student once more, an odd feeling. Avenel after our first lesson has provided me with a metal ball. I will be\n\nusing such to practice with my first and many attempts of Transmutation, as it's one of the most easiest matters to understand, especially for a blacksmith such as myself or rather ex-blacksmith. It was simple, I had understood the weight of the ball\n\nwhen I had first held it, and I knew the makeup of the Ferrum. So it was merely just /thinking/ of the reaction.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fi'hirran'tanya", "§bValia'laure Faeifeth", "The Smile of Larihei Heals the Mind Like Milk Heals the Body.\n\nThe Lifting— Sacrifice\n\nThe Ritual of the Lifting is different from that of Untempered Fi, for it is the stringent conditions which make for the true, Tempered Fi's creation.\n\nThe ritual of the Elibar'acal follows, and yet it is sufficient but not necessary to create a Tempered soul.\n\nThe sacrifice is tied to the Altar, imbued with the magic of Fi. The room is lit only by the light of a Fi' orb in a specially made lamp.\n\nGold dust is scattered upon the sacrifice as the following is read. Each in attendance may bless themselves as they so desire.\n\nElibar’acal, elkhel ito narne\nil’cruan ay’thilln kaean taliiyh\nadri’leh, ullral, ata— narne’ne ito\nkaean evarn’lar\n\n(Translation on next page --->)\n\nThe Golden Owl, darkness is upon us,\nWith pain and for silver, we bleed,\nApparitions, beasts and the wretched walk amongst us,\nWe are the shield.\n\nliewyn'Larihei eltaeleh walehe ohn vallein eltaliyna walehe,\n\nThe smile of Larihei heals the mind like milk heals the body\n\nMilk is passed between those in attendance in a Silver Chalice. It is drunk by each in turn, symbolising they are worthy of the Milk of Larihei, and therefore her smile.\n\n \nYour body unfit for the milk, Your mind unfit for the smile of Larihei,\nYour very essence forefeit.\n\nThe Milk is refused to the sacrifice, symbolising they are unworthy of it. A blade imbued with Fi' energy (read: Fi'chant, just as the altar is)\n\n is used to cut the sacrifice's throat and as this is done droplets of blue will pool on the blade's tip.\n\nBlood is collected in a clay pot. The droplets will spin and form an orb of blue light which will become stable (PK)\n\nor will explode in a flash of light (no PK, soul escapes). It is required an orb be present to power both the altar and the blade.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFi'hiiran'seth\n\nThis subtype of the magic focuses on the negation of Arcane Magic. Whether Evocation, Conjuration, Illusion, Runes, or Alteration, it can either send a forming spell back to the void or eat away at a created spell.\n\nThe magic will also steal the aura needed for Shade magic, but has no affect on existing tendrils.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFi'hiiran'acaele\n\nThe second subtype of the magic can stop all Deity Magic. (For example: Clerical, Druidism, Shamanism, Monk, Muun'Trivazja, and Ascended). Unlike its brother subtype, which funnels mana away into the void,\n\nFi'hiiran'acaele disrupts a connection, interfering with someone's ability to connect with their chosen deity. This can be small, when they cast a spell, or large, severing a connection for a time.\n\nStrangely, neither Fi'hiiran'acaele or Fi'hiiran'seth affect Necromancy.\n\nThe mage must be a first-time magic user, never having connected to anything, Deity, Void, or otherwise.\n\nThe mage must be of good physical condition. Fi'hiiran'tanya corrupts the body twice as much as a normal magic, and the mage's increased metabolism may wither them away without proper care.\n\nThe mage must perform the Ritual.\n\nThis Ritual, developed by the Elibar'acals, is the source of the mage's power. They must find a sacrifice (a character willing to be permanently killed) that they know well, and kill them on the altar.\n\nIt is in this moment, when the soul is leaving, that the mage will connect to the Void for the first time. The soul will be returning to The Cloud Temple,\n\nand the mage will grab it, trapping it in a state of Limbo. A state of half-death, forever caught in the mage's grasp. The soul will become a tool,\n\nand will eventually forget its old self, becoming more and more compliant. There is a small chance, in the beginning years, that the soul will attempt to wrest control, though no soul has ever gained full control.\n\nPhysical and mental strain\n\nLoss of weight and muscle mass\n\nIncredibly realistic lucid dreams and nightmares, leading to a confusion on what is real and what is imagined.\n\nEnchanted areas will leave a Fi'hiiran'tanya user fatigued if they stay in there for too long a time period.\n\nProblems with breathing, blood loss, internal bleeding, and the rate at which wounds heal.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Who knows\"", "§bJan C. Karlowicz", "FALL'S NOTES\n(life story is in these words throughout the book, but it is hard for anyone to understand unless they were there..)\n\nWarrior\n------------------\nYou fascinated me,\ncloaked in shadows and secrecy \nThe beauty of a broken angel\n\nI ventured carefully,\nafraid of what you thought I'd be, but pretty soon I was entangled\n\nYou take me by the hand\n\nI question who I am\nTeach me how to fight, I'll show you how to win\nYou're my mortal flaw, and I'm you fatal sin\nLet me feel the sting, the pain, the burn under my skin\nPut me to the test\n\nI'll prove that I am strong, Won't let myself believe, that what we feel is wrong.\nI finally see what you knew was inside me all along\nThat behind this soft exterior,\nLies a warrior.\n\nMy memory refused\n\nTo separate the lies from truth\nAnd search the past\nMy mind created\n\nI kept on pushing through\nStanding resolute which you\nIn equal measure\nLoved and hated\n\nYou take me by the\n\nhand\nI'm seeing who I am\n\nTeach me how to fight \nI'll show you how to win\nYou're my mortal flaw\nAnd I'm your fatal sin\nLet me feel the sting\nThe pain\nThe burn\nUnder my skin\n\nPut me to the test\nI'll prove that I'm strong\nWon't let myself believe\nThat what we feel is wrong\nI Finally see what\nYou know was inside me\nAll along\n\nThat behind this soft exterior\n\nLies a warrior\n\nLies a warrior....\n\nYou take me by the hand\nI'm sure of who I am\n\nTeach me how to fight\nI'll show you how to win\nYou're my mortal flaw\nAnd I'm you're fatal sin\n\nLet me feel the stong\nthe pain\nthe burn\nUnder my skin\n\nPut me to the test\nI'll prove that I'm strong\nWon't let myself believe\nThat what we feel is wrong\nI finally see what\n\nYou knew was inside me All along\n\nThat behind this soft exterior\nLies a warrior\n\nThe pictures come to life\nWake in the dead of night\nOpen my eyes\nI must be dreaming\n\nClutch my pillow tight\nBrace myself for the fight\nI've heard that seeing\nIs believing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Strange Code", "Jistuma", "From a note written by a friend in code, of many pages, she had no memory of writing it, or what it did mean.\n\nI decided to try and decipher it as if it were a secret note between armies, and I came with results. The code is copied first, then the\n\nmeaning of the code is told, then the translation.\n\nCode\n\n{t, ƒ:ªº£ ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, ñ.nü| ƒ'ª t, u':ô .nô t, ,ñö£:n,ºº d,i'û t, u':ô û,ª, e:º £' c'ññ.nô]\n[t,ü û,ª, ô\"º£ .nô e, û.º .º . º\"nd,.ñ| ô,ƒ:n:nø .£ i.º£ t,:ª ê.ö,]\n\n[.º û.º d,ƒ'ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, .ø.:n| û:t t, º'ªª'û 'ƒ º\"ni:øe£ ª,ñ.:n:nø \"n£ª,.£,ô .nô \"nû,ic'ñ, £' t, ô,,ö c\"ªª,n£º 'ƒ t, º,.]\n[º\"ç ô:ª,c£:'ni,ººn,ºº :º .n.t,ñ. £' e:ñ| ûe' :º i:n,.ª]\n[t,º, .ª, £' d, E:º £ª:\"ñöeº .nô E:º ƒ.:i:nøº| ñ.nü £:ñ,º 'u,ª]\n\n{t, º,c‘nô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.c£:‘nº ‘ƒ t.£ ûe:ç :º e, .ª, d.ªª,ô ƒª‘ñ ,n£ªü]\n[t, ‘t,ªº e.u, t,:ª ô,u:c,º ‘ƒ û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n| ô,ƒ:n:æ t,ñ .º ûe.£ t,ü .iû.üº e.u, d,,n| t, c.ª,£.*,ªº ‘ƒ t,:ª ƒ.£,]\n\n[t,ü ê‘“£ .nô öi,.ô .nô ‘ƒƒ,ª t,:ª u‘:c,º £‘ t, e,.u,nº| d“£ t,ü .ª, .º t, ô,,ö c.u,º d,øø:æ ƒ‘ª º“ni:øe£]\n[t, û.ü :º ê“£]\n\n{t, t:ªô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[. ‘n, £,.ªº ƒª,, t, di:nôƒ‘iô ‘ƒ t, .düºº ƒª‘ñ t, ,ü,º ‘ƒ t, ö.ª£º]\n[:£ :º .º :£ û.º]\n[t, i:øe£ .nô i:øe£º .nô i:øe£:æ ‘ƒ t,:ª êª:n,º ƒª,, t,:ª º:øe£| t.£ t,ü ñ.ü di:nô ‘t,ªº]\n\n[û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n .ø.:n º“øø,º£º :£º,iƒ| .nô t, i:n, :º ñ.ô, .º .n “nc‘“n£.di, º,ª:,º ‘ƒ ö‘:n£º| .ii :n c‘nƒi:c£ û:t t,:ª ƒ,ii‘ûº]\n[.ii û:,iô:æ t,:ª i.û]\n\n{t, ƒ‘“ªt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t,:ª i.û :º t, ö‘û,ª ‘ƒ t, ñ.nü]\n[ºi‘ûiü t, i:øe£º .ª, ,æª.u,ô û:t t, ºüñd‘iº ‘ƒ t, ,nº,ñdi,º ‘ƒ t, ñ.nü]\n[t, º:øe£º ‘ƒ n,û ç.:nº .ª, ƒ.ñ:i:.ª]\n\n{t, ƒ:ƒt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.øñ,n£º .ª, ñ.ô, .º £‘ø,t,ª .º û.º d,ƒ‘ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e,]\n[t, ñ.nü ç‘‘º, t,:ª ö.t| £‘ t, ª,ö,£:£:‘n .º t, º“n ª:º,º .nô ƒ.iiº ‘ª £‘ t, dª,.*:æ ‘ƒ :£| t.£ t, º“n ê.ii º£.nô º£:ii]\n\n{t, º:xt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ñ.nü d,c‘ñ, .º ‘n, .º û.º t.£ ûe:ç :º e,]\n\n{t, º,u,nt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[.º û.º d,ƒ‘ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º ñ.nü ñ.ô, .ø.:n]\n\nMeaning\n\n. - a\n, - e\n: - i\n‘ - o\n“ - u\n\nt - th\nƒ - f\nª - r\nº - s\n£ - t\nñ - m\nc - c\n\nø - g\nû - w\ne - h\nç - ch\nô - d\nn - n\nü - y\nu - v\nö - p\nd - b\ni - l\nê - sh\n* - k\n\næ - ng\n\n| - ,\n\n[] - sentance\n{} - title\n\nTranslation\n\nThe first mathic age.\nThat which is He made many, for the void and the emptiness below the void were His to command.\nThey were dust and He was as a sunbeam, defining at last their shape.\n\nAs was before, that which is He made again, with the sorrow of sunlight remaining untreated and unwelcome to the deep currents of the sea.\nSuch directionless is anathema to Him, who is linear.\n\nThese are to be His triumphs and His failings, many times over.\n\nThe second Mathic age\n\nThe fractions of that which is he are barred from entry.\nThe others have their devices of war and disunion, defining them as what they always have been, the caretakers of their fate.\n\nThey shout and plead and offer their voices to the heavens, but they are as the deep caves begging for sunlight.\nThe way is shut.\n\nThe third Mathic age\n\nA one tears free the blindfold of the abyss from the eyes of the parts.\nIt is as it was.\nThe light and lights and lighting of their shrines free their sight, that they may blind others.\n\nWar and disunion again suggests itself, and the line is made as an uncountable series of points, all in conflict with their fellows.\nAll wielding their law.\n\nThe Fourth Mathic Age\n\nTheir law is the power of the many.\nSlowly the lights are engraved with the symbols of the ensembles of the many.\nThe sights of new chains are familiar\n\nThe Fifth Mathic Age\n\nThe fragments are made as together as was before, that which is he.\nThe many choose their path, to the repetition as the sun rises and falls or to the breaking of it, the sun shall stand still.\n\nThe Sixth Mathic Age\n\nThe many become as one as was that which is he.\n\nThe Seventh Mathic Age\n\nAs was before, that which is he many made again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The leatherbound sketchbook has an ornate cover and heavy, high-quality paper within.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0There are a few pages within that have been carefully cut out and cannot be found in this book.\n\n\n§bBaby names - §0\n§0\n§bGirl§0\n§bTamara§0\n§bEloise§0\n§0\n§bBoy§0\n§bSimeon§0\n§bJon§0\n§0\n§b(Keep names. Just in case? <3)\n\nWe named him Jon.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0   ~*~Jon Atatis~*~§0\n§0\n§0\n§0The little sunspark of my life.\n\nASPECTS§0\n§0\n§0Cerridwen - Life, birth, fertility, growth, and peace.§0\n§0\n§0Cernunnos - The hunt, strength, the forest, the animals.§0\n§0\n§0Father and Mother of Nature and Balance.\n\nDon't talk about Nemiisae.§0\n§0\n§0She is important, but not well-liked because she is the embodiment of death.§0\n§0\n§0It's dangerous to speak about her.§0\n§0\n\nShun - \"Much wind pours from your mouth.\" §0\n§0\n§0Those who committed crimes against the druids. Never to be spoken to.§0\n§0\n§0Forgotten/Lost Druids- AWOL Druids. If they give a valid reason, they don't incur a punishment.\n\nDruidic Rankings §0\n§0\n§0Dedicants - Students (like me!)§0\n§0\n§0Druids - Carry out duties as servants of the Aspects and protect nature's balance. (There's more than them??)§0\n§0\n§0Guides - Teachers. Okay fair enough.\n\nMoot - A druidic meeting. (Za didn't know what \"moot\" means though.)§0\n§0\n§0Arch Druids - Keep the Order in line. Can call for a Moot or Shun.§0\n§0\n§0Heirophants - Retired druids that are so well-respected they earn their title. ...\n\n...Advisors§0 of Arch Druids.§0\n§0\n§0CURRENT HEIROPHANTS- §0\n§0Brothers Pine, Tortoise, Wolf and Song. (Time to be the first Sister.)§0\n§0\n§0Notable Druids - Famous druids who've done big deeds for the Order. ...\n\nPetyr, Respiren, Callax and Maiavel.\n\n\n§0\n§0TWINS!§0\n§0\n§0~*~Eloise and Théogène~*~§0\n§0\n§0Blessed by precious sunsparks, all three. I couldn't be happier.§0\n§0[A drawing of the little babies has been sketched here.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Hands", "§bLemik Rextiureus", "-------------------Account entry of Lemik Rextiureus\n-------------------\nI was faction leader for four years these were the dark ages, knowledge was lacking population was lacking. I hope that you can learn from my mistakes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Of the Hand", "§bShynys Itesti", "Disciples of the Hand\n\nFaction Skills:\n\n-Alchemist\n-Blacksmith\n-Chef\n-Enchanter\n-Leatherworker\n-Stonemason\n-Tinker\n-Woodworker\n\nDisciples of the Hand\n\nFaction Discription:\n\n- Individuals that work raw materials into fine armor, ancient enchants, and funny gadgets.\n\nDisciples of the Hand\n\n- These individuals work long hours, perfecting their crafts, training their skills, and trying to make a name for themselves by paying great attention to detail on singular items.\n\nDisciples of the Hand\n\n-These workers use raw materials to create and manufacture expensive products that can be sold throughout the world.\n\nDisciple of the Hand\n§\\\n\nFaction Speaker:\n\n-These individuals represent their faction at meetings with the leader.\n\n-They inform the leader of any pressing matters or concerns within their faction.\n\nDisciple of the Hand\n\nFaction Speaker:\n\n- These individuals negotiate things with the town leader.\n\n- These individuals are elected by their faction. Elections take place once a month.\n\nDisciple of the Hand\n\nFaction Speaker:\n\n- Should this position become vacant, or the individual become disposed for over a week, emergency election will be held.\n\nDisciple of the Hand\n\nSpeakers to Date:\n\n- Shynys Itesti 8/24", ""),
        StaticBook("Govt. I.D. [104]", "§bAdulfin Ehrlichmann", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\nName:\nPyotr Nicodemus\nMCName: Abeam1\n\nPosition: Legend\n\nClearance:\nLevel 3", ""),
        StaticBook("Govt. I.D. [001]", "§bGoseph Joebbelstein", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\nName:\nDecimus Rovin\nMCName: Zhulik\n\nPosition:\nKaiser\n\nClearance Level:\n100", ""),
        StaticBook("Merry Christmas", "§bNicolas Headsted", "Hey man, its Nick, or NicktheRed20. I'm your secret santa and I wanted to give you this gift. I wanted to make it a little more personal because christmas slowly loses its value when you get older and older. For me, it barley feels like christmas ---\n\nanymore. And that really sucks. When I was younger, the only thing I loved was christmas. Getting older sucks, my man. You really don't want it. I know the last thing you want is a lecture. I'm sure you're thinking \"Hey, this really cool guy have me a-\n\nsword that has enchants, and is modreator approved. Why is he blabbering about christmas?\" Correct me if Im wrong :) \n\nBut for now, enjoy minecraft, enjoy your 8th grade year (I listened to you in ts) and enjoy being a kid.\n\nHave a very Merry Christmas, Owl.\n\nYour friend, Nick Pechersky.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "§bJudas Agnarsson", "Dear whomever reading this letter.§0\n§0\n§0Perhaps to you I remain unidentified, I am a man of various crimes and yet I have been sentenced to death by one I have not committed.\n\nI'd like for you as a being to concern the following people I am dead:§0\n§0\n§0Jeffwise ((Billy5691))§0\n§0Location: Sutica§0\n§0\n§0Richard Staunton ((Kosherzombie))§0\n§0Location: Courland\n\nNathan Everheart ((GamerCrimson))§0\n§0Location: Felsen§0\n§0\n§0Richard Windsor§0\n§0((TotallyNotAudun))§0\n§0Location: Courland§0\n§0\nI sincerely apologise for what I am doing, this may cause trauma upon some of you.\n\nRichard, a cousin, a comrade and a brother at arms.\n\n-sincerely \n\nJudas Agnarsson.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0            O§0\n§0          /  \\§0\n§0        /      \\§0\n§0        l        l§0\n§0         \\     /§0\n§0           \\_/§0\n§0\n§0fig. 1: watch diagram§0\n§0A small gold watch crafted by my own hands.\n\n  /\\                   /\\§0\n§0  \\ \\_              _/ /§0\n§0   \\_  \\          /  _/§0\n§0      \\  \\_____/  /§0\n§0       \\            / §0\n§0        l            l§0\n§0        l  {}  {}   l§0\n§0        \\          /§0\n§0         l          l §0\n§0         \\        /§0\n§0Fig. 2    \\^_^/", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0Runhithron§0\n§0Reason For Visitng: §0\n§0Chief Commander Trying to test the guards? §0\n§0Seems like a human, doubt this is his real name, has been insulting us.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sea", "§bElluna Koortova", "The Sea\n\n*The writing would be beautifully written in script.*\n\nThe Sea.\n\nMystery. We all recognize the sea, but what do we know of her? All I know is that her visage captivates me so. She..\n\nHas a gentle appearance with harmonious waves that run across her surface.. The pervading warmth from the glimmering rays that run off the essence that is her beauty. However, what captivates me most is her endless depth. What lies beneath the sea?\n\nWhat secrets doth she hold? Well.. All I can do is gaze into her shimmering eyes, and wonder. What thoughts run through her flowing mind? Indeed, I’d wonder if her radiant beauty has ever paid much heed to me, a bystander.. -Ink drip-\n\nNonetheless, she is the one I hold feelings for. The person who is my sea, you, Gaelyn. \n\n\n*There would be a few fancy squiggles here.*\n\n\n    ~A Bystander~\n*Cough, Cough, A Cassius,*\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "§bElluna Koortova", "Treating Wounds\n  \n    By Anonymous\n\n\nMy time in the Order of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. \nLet’s start using steps,\n\n\nStep I - Cleaning the Wound\n\nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or deeper wounds you'll need something with alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sorts. Of course you need to wash the dirt out\n\nfirst should it have dirt in it. Remember to clean thoroughly!\n\n\nStep II -  Suturing the Wound\n\nFor that you'll need a needle and some thread. Sounds easy right? Well not really, you need a steady hand and you also need to do it by these.. Let’s call them sub steps.\n\n\nSub Step I - Heating the Needle\n\nYou need to do that to burn away any remaining illness covering the needle, should it have had any.\n\nSub Step II - Clean the Thread\n\nYou surely need to do so, as you do not want a single speck dirt in your wound!\n\nSub Step III - Starting the Suture\n\nYou start at, well, the start of the gash or deep wound. (Warning! this does NOT apply for small wounds!)\n\nYou then sew it closed like you’re sewing a tear in a rag, a messy and bloody rag that screams like a little girl. Nonetheless, a rag. \n\nSub Step IV - Bandaging the Wound\n\nA bandage could be just about anything,\n\nan old rag (As long as it's clean, obviously!), bed sheets, anything of cloth material. Then you simply wrap it around the wound. Done!\n\nNote: If there's any sign of infection before or after you’ve gone through this process you'll be\n\nbetter off cutting off the leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "§bElluna Koortova", "Electric \n         Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  By Gauldrim Irongut\n\n\nChapter 1, Uses of Electromancy:\n\nElectromancy is a very volatile form of arcane evocation, is just as likely to veer off it’s course or shock the user. A source of incredible heat and force, electromancy is a formidable tool. Slow to conjure\n\nand is a lifelong commitment electromancy can be used in survival situations. Able to create fires when need be through the burning of wood or other flammable materials. Another property that can be found in electromancy is  the extreme attraction\n\nto large amounts of metal. An anvil, a suit plate of armour, or a large iron gate can cause the electricity to be attracted towards it and then channeled inside of it. If one is to touch a piece of metal charged with electricity they will be hurt or burnt\n\nas the electricity discharges. The most obvious use of electric evocation is the use of it in combat. A deadly force to be reckoned with once the user has achieved a high enough power to use it. Slow to conjure, though fast once released, electric\n\nevocation is one of the most powerful forms of arcane evocation. Able to kill a large man in full plate mail in a single bolt, if large enough this just lends perspective to the raw power. Electric evocationists also have the ability to summon forth\n\nlightning from the heavens in the event of a storm with very good accuracy.\n\n\n\nChapter 2, Properties of Electromancy:\n\nAttracted to metal, can be conducted through metal, has the force to shatter stone and the ability to travel through water. Electromancy is as versatile as it is powerful. Electric\n\ncurrents can be sent through water enabling one to shock someone that is in contact with the said body of water. This practice also applies to metal and if one is in contact with a suit of plate mail when the electric current is sent towards the bearer\n\nthey will experience not only the force of the bolt but the current of the electricity as well. The current of the electricity will also cause muscle seizure and the dulling of senses. The shattering of stone occurs when an extremely powerful bolt is sent\n\nhurtling towards the stone, resulting in flying rubble and scorched rock. As well as being able to scorch rock, Electromancy can set wood, paper, and any other flammable materials alight causing fire and burns.\n\n\n\nChapter 3, Conclusion: \n\nElectromancy is an almighty power to be reckoned with and those that perform it should be regarded with extreme caution. Slow to cast into immense power yet still dangerous even at short range.\n\nIt is advised that when in combat against such a mage, that large amounts of metal and or armour are unadvised to have and even steel or iron greatswords. So to wrap this short informative text up, one would be wise to heed the words of an electromancer\n\nand to regard the raw power and wisdom of those that wield it.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCopied by Elluna Koortova", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This sketchbook belongs to the Wood Elf named Penelope Clover.§0\n§0\n§0If found. Please return to her via messenger bird. Thank you!§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0(PandaaGirl13)\n\n[!] On this page would be a beautifully and skilled drawing of a snowy mountain side with a cozy cabin. Smoke curls from the cabins chimney. The sun setting behind the mountain peck [!]§0\n§0\n§0~Signed by §0\n§0Penelope C.~\n\n[!] This page would have many random doodles on it, one is a small sketch of her new home. Another sketch would fill half the page. It's a very neat drawing of the giant white tree found in Laureh'lin. [!]§0\n§0\n§0~Penelope C.~\n\n\n§0[!] A lot of time and effort would appear to have been put into this drawing. It's of the Lion statue found in Aethermoore. It's very well drawn and also colored. [!]§0\n§0\n§0\n§0~Penelope C.~\n\n[!] A sketch of a man with gray-blue eyes. A look of confidence within them. He would have medium-length curly auburn hair that would just barely reach past his ears. [!]§0\n§0\n§0\n§0~Penelope C.~\n\n[!] This Sketch is Titled   \"Unpredictable Fox\"§0\n§0\n§0A young elf with long blonde hair with captivating blues smiles at you on this page with an adorable crooked grin. On her arm is a tattoo of many roses. [!]§0\n§0\n§0~Penelope C.~", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "K§0\n§0              O§0\n§0              S             ===================Page three, For Rules,\n\nThese are the rules a Strider Knight must follow to keep balance within our blades.§0\n§0\n§0Rule One, Never turn down a chance to help someone,§0\n§0\n§0Rule Two, If you become a personal guard you must speak with An Elder, Or (->)\n\nAnyone of Rank IIIII", ""),
